/* GENERATED by build/gen-realm-bestiary.py from dev/model-qa/realm-bestiary-draft.json — never hand-edit. Realm creature layer (reskin: frame=stat chassis id in BESTIARY, model=render key/net-new description, desc/traits/source per docs/REALM-ENRICHMENT-WRITING.md; flavorTable/treasure/habitat/activity per docs/MONSTER-FLAVOR-TABLES.md §2). */
const REALM_BESTIARY={
 "frontier":[{"name":"Dust-Broke Drifter","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Desperate gun-for-hire, breaks and runs when losing","flavor":"A busted prospector or out-of-luck ranch hand who picked up a gun because begging stopped working. Fights scared and quits the moment the math turns against him.","desc":"He's got a hat with the brim gone soft, a revolver that's seen better cleaning, and a stare that keeps sliding off to the horizon like he's already planning the walk away from this. His hand trembles on the grip before he even draws it. The first shot that goes wide is the one that breaks him.","traits":{"note": "His nerve breaks before his body does — he runs the instant a fight turns against him.", "actions": [{"name": "Rusty Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Trembling Aim", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage. If this attack misses, the Drifter has disadvantage on his next attack roll, his hands still shaking from the flinch."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing two fingers on the draw hand; favors the crossbow now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a dead man's boots, half a size too big, and it shows in his walk."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks the whole fight, mostly to convince himself he's not scared."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a photograph of a woman who stopped writing back months ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owes three separate men money and can't remember which one sent him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Surrenders the second anyone calls his bluff out loud, hands up before the sentence finishes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears his gun was cursed by a fortune-teller in exchange for a debt he never paid."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drinks courage from a flask before the fight and can't tell fear from the whiskey anymore."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["circling a stranded wagon at a distance, working up the nerve to demand a toll", "cleaning a revolver that keeps jamming, cursing the dust in the action"]},{"name":"Line-Rider","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Rank-and-file outlaw muscle, brave only in packs","flavor":"Rank-and-file gang muscle who rides the fence lines looking for something to take. Works in packs, brave only in numbers.","desc":"Three or four of them come loping along the fence line at an easy trot, rifles balanced across their saddles like they're not even sure they'll need them. Alone, one of these men fusses with his hat brim and won't meet your eyes. In a pack, they all suddenly know how to shoot.","traits":{"note": "Alone he won't meet your eyes; in a pack of three or more, he suddenly finds his nerve.", "actions": [{"name": "Fence-Line Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Saddle Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage. While mounted, this attack doesn't suffer disadvantage for firing from horseback."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rides a horse stolen off the very ranch he's now robbing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fusses constantly with his hat brim, never quite settled on how it sits."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger than the others, still trying to prove he belongs in the gang."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of every fence he's cut carved into his saddle horn."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistles the same three notes as a signal to the rest of the pack."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Breaks off from the pack the instant the numbers stop favoring him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wears a second man's boots and won't say what happened to the first owner."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Rides drunk on cheap liquor and fires wild the moment anyone raises a voice at him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "desert", "hill"],"activity":["loping along a fence line at an easy trot, rifle balanced loose across the saddle", "counting cattle from horseback and marking which ones look easiest to cut from the herd"]},{"name":"Coyote-Thing","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"Wrong-shaped coyote pack, laughs instead of howling","flavor":"A dust-country coyote gone wrong at the edges — too many teeth, a laugh instead of a howl. Runs in loose, opportunistic packs and never attacks what it can't out-number.","desc":"It laughs before it howls — a wet, chittering bark that doesn't belong in any coyote throat, and the extra rows of teeth behind its lips confirm the wrongness. They keep low to the sage and never come at you alone, circling in loose scatter until the numbers feel safe to them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Too-Many-Teeth Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. If three or more Coyote-Things are within 10 ft. of the target, this attack deals an extra 2 (1d4) Piercing damage from the pile-on."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye is milk-white and blind, so it always circles counterclockwise."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its laugh comes out first, before it's even seen the prey worth laughing at."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a bit of torn cloth in its jaws, worrying it like a trophy."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thinner than the rest of the pack, hangs back and lets the others test first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its extra teeth are visibly rotten, breath sour enough to smell downwind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Never attacks alone — peels off the second the pack scatters."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mimics a human voice mid-laugh, one word, always the same word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Foams at the jaw and keeps coming even at half a pack, laughing through the pain."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["circling low in the sage brush, chittering a wet laugh instead of a howl", "trailing a wounded animal at a patient distance, waiting on the numbers"]},{"name":"Scarecrow Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Field scarecrow that only moves when unwatched","flavor":"Propped over a dead man's field to scare off crows and, lately, everything else. Stands dead still until you stop watching it, then it isn't where it was.","desc":"Straw hat, crossed fence-posts, a burlap face gone dark with weather — it's exactly what a scarecrow should be, right down to the crows giving it a wide berth. It's the stillness that's wrong. Look away for even a breath and when your eyes come back, it's a few feet closer than it was.","traits":{"note": "It only moves while unwatched — turn your back on it and it closes distance.", "actions": [{"name": "Straw-Fingered Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Burlap Stare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that can see the Sentinel's face makes a DC 11 Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature is Frightened of the Sentinel until the end of the Sentinel's next turn and cannot willingly move closer to it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its straw hat has a name stitched into the band, worn nearly illegible."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One fence-post arm ends in a rusted hoe blade instead of a hand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crows nest in it year-round now and ride it wherever it drifts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its burlap face has a hand-sewn smile that's started to unravel at one corner."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Planted over a grave nobody in town will admit to digging."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Freezes mid-stride the instant any eyes land on it, however briefly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow doesn't match its posture, always a step further along than it should be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When destroyed, the straw within it keeps twitching for a full minute, still trying to walk."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["standing dead-still over a dead man's field, crows giving it a wide berth", "propped at a crossroads post, burlap face turned toward the road"]},{"name":"Claim-Jumper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Armed squatter on a forged land deed","flavor":"Squats on other men's stakes with a rifle and a forged deed. Knows the land better than the law does and uses that.","desc":"He's dug a fire pit and pitched a lean-to on land that isn't his, with a folded paper he'll wave at you like it settles things. The rifle resting across his knees settles things faster. He knows every wash and rise on this claim better than the county surveyor ever will.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Claim-Jumper makes two attacks, using Trail Shortsword or Squatter's Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Trail Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Squatter's Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. The Claim-Jumper has advantage on this attack if the target is unaware of terrain he's mapped in advance (DM's call)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waves a forged deed at the party and demands they clear off his stake."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dug in on a claim the party was hired to survey for its real owner."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cache of ore he's stripped from the claim sits half-buried nearby, worth fighting for."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a lookout post that spots the party coming long before they see him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real claim-holder's family is camped a mile off, waiting on someone to run him out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to split the claim's take if the party leaves the paperwork alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's found something under the claim he won't name, and it's why he won't leave even at gunpoint."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's rigged the claim's mine shaft to collapse rather than let anyone else work it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["sitting a fire pit dug on land that isn't his, rifle resting easy across his knees", "walking a staked claim's boundary line, memorizing every wash and rise on it"]},{"name":"Company Enforcer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Railroad-payroll thug who calls debt-collection business","flavor":"Muscle on the railroad or mining company payroll — collects debts, breaks strikes, and calls it business.","desc":"Clean coat, brass buttons, a ledger book tucked under one arm like he's here to do arithmetic instead of violence — until the two toughs behind him make it clear which one he actually does. He reads the amount owed out loud before anybody's allowed to argue about it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two attacks with Collection Mace."}, {"name": "Collection Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target owes a debt the Enforcer has named this scene, this attack deals an extra 2 (1d4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's here to collect a debt one of the party's contacts owes the company."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's breaking a strike, and the workers he's threatening need the party's help."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His ledger names a payment the party can intercept before he delivers it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting from someone who genuinely can't pay, a child watching from the doorway."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two toughs flank him, and both will scatter if he goes down first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll take a bribe to misplace the ledger entry, for a price steeper than the original debt."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ledger lists debts for people who died years before the loans were supposedly made."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been skimming the company's own collections and will kill to keep that ledger page hidden."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["reading an amount owed off a ledger page before anyone's allowed to argue about it", "walking a payroll route flanked by two toughs, brass buttons catching the light"]},{"name":"Buzzard-Kin","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-vulture","model":"giant-vulture","summary":"Torso-sized vulture that circles the living early","flavor":"An unnaturally patient carrion bird the size of a man's torso that's learned to circle the living a little early.","desc":"Big enough that its shadow crosses the trail like a cloud passing, this vulture doesn't wait for the dying to finish dying. It banks in low circles overhead long before anyone's actually hurt, patient in a way that makes a person want to hurry up and prove it wrong.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Patient Gouge", "replaces": "Gouge", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is below half its hit point maximum, this attack has advantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bald patches on its neck from decades of feeding on things that fought back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows a single rider for miles without ever closing the distance."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow crosses the trail like a cloud, slow and unmistakable."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Perches on the same dead tree every day, waiting for the road to earn it a meal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a scrap of cloth in its talons, torn from something it didn't finish."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Circles lower and tighter the closer its target comes to dying."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never lands until its target actually stops breathing, no matter how long the wait."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole kettle of them converges on a single dying man, patience gone to frenzy."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "sky", "grassland"],"activity":["banking in slow circles over a trail long before anyone there is actually hurt", "perched on a fence post, torso-sized shadow stretching across the road"]},{"name":"Dust Devil","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"salamander-fire-snake","model":"rlm-dust-devil","summary":"Living dust-funnel that scours riders off horseback","flavor":"A living whirlwind of grit and heat-shimmer that scours a rider off his horse before anyone sees it coming. The old-timers swear it only forms where blood's been spilled.","desc":"The funnel stands up out of flat ground with no wind to explain it, dust-brown and man-tall, and it doesn't wander — it tracks. Horses spook first, rearing and screaming before the rider even feels the grit start peppering his face and the funnel closes the gap at a dead run.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grit-Scour Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or have disadvantage on its next attack roll from grit in its eyes."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Forms only where blood was spilled recently, old-timers swear by it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rider's lost hat spinning inside its funnel like a keepsake."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't wander like a natural whirlwind — it tracks in a straight, patient line."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spooks horses first, rearing them before the rider even feels the grit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a scoured, glassy patch of sand wherever it stands still too long."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Closes the gap at a dead run the instant a rider tries to outpace it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Carries the voice of the last thing it scoured off a horse, faint inside the wind."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Collapses into a dozen smaller devils when struck hard enough, all still hungry."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "elemental", "grassland"],"activity":["standing up out of flat, windless ground, dust-brown and man-tall", "tracking a lone rider at a dead run, grit peppering the air ahead of it"]},{"name":"Debt-Collector Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Ledger-keeping ghoul who thinks the debt transfers","flavor":"A man who died owing money and came back still keeping the ledger — hollow-eyed, gaunt, and convinced the debt transfers to whoever's standing nearest.","desc":"Gray-skinned and hunched, it drags a waterlogged ledger behind it on a chain and reads names off the mildewed pages in a rasping, patient voice. It genuinely believes the debt survives the debtor — and reaches for you with black-nailed hands the moment it decides you're the estate that inherited it.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely believes the debt survives the debtor — and transfers to whoever's standing nearest.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghoul makes one Ledger Bite attack and one Black-Nailed Claw attack."}, {"name": "Ledger Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Black-Nailed Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Slashing damage, and a creature other than an Undead must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute, believing itself named debtor. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's decided one of the party inherited a dead man's unpaid tab and won't let up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ledger names a real debt the party could actually pay off to be rid of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's collecting outside a shuttered bank the party needs to get into."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living relative of the dead debtor is nearby, terrified it'll come for them next."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drags the chain-bound ledger like an anchor, slowing it enough to be outrun."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll accept a token payment — any coin — and shuffle off satisfied, for now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ledger's ink rewrites itself, adding new names the longer it goes unpaid."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it scatters the ledger's pages, and each one names someone new as the debtor."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "swamp"],"activity":["dragging a waterlogged ledger behind it on a chain, reading names off mildewed pages", "hunched at a crossroads, rasping a debt tally to no one who's listening yet"]},{"name":"Gunslinger's Shade","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Ghostly quick-draw reliving the duel he lost","flavor":"The echo of a quick-draw who lost the one duel that mattered. Reenacts the noon-draw against anyone who'll stand still for it, forever losing, forever trying again.","desc":"He stands at twenty paces in a duster gone translucent at the edges, hand hovering over a holster that isn't really there anymore. Every dusk he relives the same draw, the same half-second too slow, and every dusk some unlucky soul standing in for the man who beat him pays for the rematch.","traits":{"note": "He replays the duel every dusk — always the same loss, always looking for a stand-in for the man who beat him.", "actions": [{"name": "Rematch Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until the Shade is destroyed or the target finishes a Long Rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He challenges a party member to the noon draw and won't fight any other way."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member's coat for the coat of the man who killed him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The man who actually beat him still lives nearby, old and unaware he's haunted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He appears only at dusk, and vanishes the instant the sun fully sets, win or lose."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A witness to the original duel is still alive and knows how to end the replay for good."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Winning the draw fairly against him seems to actually let him rest, at least for a night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's fought the rematch hundreds of times and started forgetting which losses were real."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every soul who's stood in for his rival is bound to him now, and they all draw at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["standing at twenty paces in a duster gone translucent, hand hovering near an absent holster", "reliving the same half-second-too-slow draw against whoever stands still for it"]},{"name":"Iron Horse Wreck-Golem","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"rlm-iron-horse-wreck-golem","summary":"Salvaged locomotive-iron golem guarding a dead spur line","flavor":"Salvaged rail-yard iron bolted into something that walks and swings. Company men built it to guard the spur line; it forgot who it was guarding it from.","desc":"Rust-scaled and locomotive-heavy, it's built from salvaged boiler plate and coupling rod, hunched like something that used to run on rails and never got the memo that the spur line died. Steam hisses from seams that shouldn't still hold pressure, and each footfall rings like a dropped anvil.","traits":{"note": "Built from a wrecked locomotive; treat its slam attacks as unusually loud — the clang carries for a mile and can draw more of the same."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing one foreleg; it lists and can only shuffle, never charge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A conductor's pocket-watch is fused into its chest, still ticking."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coal-red light behind the firebox grate wherever eyes should be."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistles — a real train whistle — once before it moves to strike."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wrapped in the burnt canvas of a mail sack it never delivered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only wakes and moves along the buried line of the dead track."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The steam it vents smells of a specific man's tobacco; old-timers go pale."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its boiler is at bursting — killing it detonates a 20-ft. fireball of shrapnel and rail-spikes."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "grassland"],"activity":["standing dead-still over a rusted rail junction until something crosses the ties", "dragging a length of coupling-chain in a slow, grinding circle"]},{"name":"Bounty Board Regular","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Wanted-poster gunfighter, unhurried and always faster","flavor":"A working gun-for-hire whose face is on three different posters, all for different names. Professional, unhurried, and always faster on the draw than the job requires.","desc":"His face is nailed to half the boards in town, reward figure crossed out and rewritten upward twice. He doesn't hurry to the fight or away from it — just settles his hat, plants his boots, and waits with the patience of a man who's done this enough times to know he'll be the one still standing.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Regular makes two attacks, using Poster-Price Greatsword or Payday Crossbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Poster-Price Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Payday Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 10 (2d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tracking the same bounty the party's after, and he got the tip first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mistaken a party member for one of the three names on his own posters."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to split a bounty rather than fight over it, if the party's reasonable."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival bounty man is trailing him, and the party gets caught in the crossfire."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His latest poster names a crime he didn't actually commit, and he's tired of running from it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll walk away from a fight he doesn't get paid for — no bounty, no interest."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He collects on his own aliases, turning himself in under a false name for the reward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been paid to bring the party in dead, and he says so before the first shot."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["settling his hat and planting his boots, waiting with a professional's patience", "reading his own wanted poster off a saloon wall, price scratched out and rewritten upward"]},{"name":"Card-Sharp Killer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"rlm-card-sharp-killer","summary":"Cheating gambler who kills the man who calls him","flavor":"Cleans out a table hand by hand, then cleans up the man who calls him on it. The cards are the tell; the derringer up the sleeve is the punchline.","desc":"He deals from the bottom smooth enough that you'd never catch it if you weren't watching for it — and if you do catch it, he doesn't deny it, doesn't apologize, just lets his other hand drift toward the table's edge where a derringer waits taped under the felt.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Killer makes two attacks, using Table's Edge Shortsword or Taped Derringer in any combination."}, {"name": "Table's Edge Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Taped Derringer", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. This attack has advantage if the target hasn't acted yet this combat, catching them mid-hand."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's cleaned out a party member's coin at cards and won't give an inch of it back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone at the table already caught his tell and is about to call him on it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a marker from a rich man's son who can't cover the debt."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's cheating a mark the party was hired to protect."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A previous victim's kin is in the room, waiting on nerve enough to accuse him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll return the winnings quietly if it means avoiding a scene in front of witnesses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His cards are marked with a pattern that isn't ink — it moves when no one's looking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's rigged the whole table to blow if he loses fair, rather than be shown up."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["dealing from the bottom of the deck smooth enough nobody's caught it yet", "letting a hand drift toward the table's edge where a derringer waits taped under the felt"]},{"name":"Rustler Pack Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Cattle-rustling gang boss, quick to shoot and blame","flavor":"Runs a cattle-and-horse theft ring across three counties, quick to shoot and quicker to blame the next gang over.","desc":"He rides at the head of a loose column of stolen cattle, hat pushed back, already sizing up who in your group looks like the one who'll start trouble. He shoots first and sorts out whose fault it was after, and his gang has learned to shoot the second he does.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Boss makes two attacks, using Herd-Cutter Scimitar or Quick-Blame Pistol in any combination."}, {"name": "Herd-Cutter Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Quick-Blame Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage. The Boss can make this attack as part of his first turn in combat without breaking any prior parley."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His stolen herd is being driven through the party's path and he won't slow it for anyone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already decided to blame the next gang over, and the party's an easy witness to silence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rancher's hired the party to get the herd back before it crosses the county line."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His gang shoots the second he does, so provoking him alone starts the whole fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a wounded rider in tow, slowing the column and souring his temper."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll trade a cut of the herd for the party looking the other way, just this once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of the stolen cattle bear a brand from a ranch that burned down years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's rigged the herd to stampede on his signal, using it as a weapon against pursuers."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "desert", "hill"],"activity":["riding at the head of a loose column of stolen cattle, hat pushed back", "sizing up which member of a party looks like the one who'll start trouble"]},{"name":"Sidewinder Broodmother","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"giant-constrictor-snake","model":"giant-constrictor-snake","summary":"Wagon-length rattler with a half-mile brood","flavor":"A rattler grown to wagon-length in a dry wash nobody rides through twice. Her brood scatters the desert floor for a half-mile in every direction.","desc":"She's as long as a freight wagon and thick through the middle as a rain barrel, scales dust-pale and grit-crusted, and where she dens the ground is riddled with smaller holes hissing in chorus. Half a mile of brood scatters at her signal and regroups the instant the danger passes.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Broodmother makes one Wagon-Length Bite attack and one Barrel-Ribbed Constrict attack."}, {"name": "Wagon-Length Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Barrel-Ribbed Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16). Until the grapple ends, the target is Restrained."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales gone bone-pale from decades denned in the same sun-baked wash."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her den is riddled with smaller holes hissing in a ragged chorus."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing several rattle segments; her warning comes out half-silent now."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils around a half-buried wagon wheel like it's part of the nest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Brood scatters wide the second her shadow passes over the den mouth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Signals her brood with a specific rattle pattern that regroups them instantly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of her brood have started growing too large for the den too fast."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When she dies, the entire half-mile brood boils up out of the ground at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "hill"],"activity":["coiled the length of a freight wagon in a dry wash nobody rides through twice", "signaling her half-mile brood to scatter, then regrouping the instant danger passes"]},{"name":"Marshal's Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Murdered lawman still walking his dusk patrol","flavor":"The last honest lawman in three territories, shot in the back for it, still walking his rounds at dusk. Doesn't know he's dead — only knows the town's gone lawless again.","desc":"He walks his old beat every dusk in a coat with a bullet hole where his badge should still be pinned, boots silent on boards that used to creak under him. He tips his hat to no one living and keeps walking his rounds like the town still needs protecting from something.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't know he's dead — only that the town's gone lawless again and needs walking.", "actions": [{"name": "Beat-Walk Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the Marshal regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt."}, {"name": "Deputize the Dead", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Marshal designates a Humanoid that has died within the last hour within 10 ft. of him. That corpse rises as a Specter (using the standard Specter statistics) under the Marshal's control at the start of his next turn, deputized into his patrol."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands the party account for a crime committed in town that very night."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's deputized a corpse the party recognizes, and it still remembers them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The man who shot him in the back still walks free, and the Marshal wants him named."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for the outlaws currently terrorizing the town he once protected."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His badge is buried somewhere in town, and returning it might finally let him rest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll deputize the party instead of fighting them, if they'll help him solve one case."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every criminal he's ever hanged fair walks his beat with him now, silent and orderly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole town's dead rise to back him the moment he calls for backup at dusk."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["walking his old beat every dusk, boots silent on boards that used to creak", "tipping his hat to no one living, patrolling a town that no longer needs him"]},{"name":"Cattle-Baron's Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"Baron's undefeated duelist, fights over land and water","flavor":"The baron's personal fist — duels for land, for water rights, for the principle of the thing, and hasn't lost yet.","desc":"Built like a bull himself, scarred across both forearms from duels he's never lost, he steps into the dust circle rolling his shoulders and cracking his neck like this is recreation. He fights over land and water rights personally, because the baron finds it's cheaper than paying lawyers.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two attacks, using Water-Rights Spear or Shield Bash in any combination."}, {"name": "Water-Rights Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dueling a rancher over water rights the party has a stake in too."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The baron's sent him to settle a land dispute the party's client can't afford to lose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's undefeated and looking for a real challenge, and word's spread the party might give him one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A previous loser's family wants him dead and has hired the party to arrange it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He fights only in the dust circle, by rules the baron enforces personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll walk away from a duel that isn't sanctioned by the baron's rules, no matter the insult."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's never actually lost, and he's started to wonder if the baron's rigged every duel somehow."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Losing a duel to him signs over land rights on the spot, baron's law or not."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["rolling his shoulders and cracking his neck as he steps into the dust circle", "dueling over a water-rights claim like it's recreation instead of business"]},{"name":"Boneyard Preacher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Buried-alive preacher whose sermon still convicts","flavor":"A hellfire circuit preacher whose congregation buried him alive for the sins he named too accurately. His sermon still carries, and it still convicts.","desc":"Dirt still clings to the collar of the coat he was buried in, and his voice carries up out of the ground before the rest of him claws free of the grave dirt. The sermon he preaches convicted him once — now it's aimed at whoever's standing close enough to hear the ending.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Graveside Sermon", "text": "Once per encounter, the preacher speaks a verse of his old conviction sermon at a target within 30 feet; that creature must succeed a Wisdom save or be frightened until the end of its next turn, seeing its own worst guilt reflected back."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's clawed up in the middle of a burial the party's attending, sermon mid-sentence."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A congregation member who buried him is still alive and terrified he'll remember who."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's preaching truths about a party member's past that they'd rather stayed buried."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The graveyard he rose in holds someone the party came looking for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sermon names a real, provable sin in town that no one's answered for."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll return to the ground quietly if someone finally admits to the sin he named."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His voice carries even when his mouth doesn't move, sermon bleeding into dreams nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every grave in the boneyard cracks open when he reaches the sermon's final verse."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "swamp"],"activity":["clawing free of grave dirt, sermon already carrying before the rest of him arrives", "standing over a fresh grave, aiming the same convicting words at whoever's close enough to hear"]},{"name":"Stampede-Cursed Longhorn","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"rhinoceros","model":"rhinoceros","summary":"Feral cursed bull leading a stampede that never ends","flavor":"A prize bull gone feral and enormous on cursed range grass, the lead animal in a stampede that never quite ends.","desc":"Its eyes have gone the flat black of a thing that's stopped being an animal, and it never really stops moving — hooves churning even when it's standing still, like the stampede it's leading is happening whether or not there's anyone around to run from it. The herd behind it never thins.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cursed Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage. If the Longhorn moved at least 20 ft. straight toward the target before the attack, the target must also succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked Prone and take an extra 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage from the trampling herd behind it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its horns are scored deep with old brand-iron marks it never lets heal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never stops moving, hooves churning even asleep on its feet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes gone the flat black of a thing that stopped being an animal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The herd behind it never thins no matter how many are culled from the edges."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grazes on grass that's gone the color of rust for a mile in every direction."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leads the herd in the same direction always, toward a horizon it never reaches."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dust it kicks up keeps rising long after the herd's actually stopped moving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing the lead bull only slows the stampede a moment before a new leader emerges from the herd."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "desert"],"activity":["churning its hooves even standing still, stampede happening whether anyone's there to run from it", "leading a herd that never thins, black-eyed and unresting across the cursed range"]},{"name":"Vault-Keeper Wight","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Dead bank owner still guarding his strongbox","flavor":"A bank owner who died clutching his strongbox and rose still clutching it, deputizing whatever corpses are handy to guard the vault door.","desc":"He's still wearing the suit he was buried in, buttons straining over a chest gone grey and stiff, and he stands sentinel over a strongbox that outlived every account it held. His hand never leaves the vault door. Approach it and he stops being patient about ownership.","traits":{"note": "He stops being patient about ownership the instant anyone reaches for the vault door.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Wight makes two attacks, using Vault Drain or Foreclosure Longsword in any combination."}, {"name": "Vault Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a Long Rest."}, {"name": "Foreclosure Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Deputize the Vault (1/Day)", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "The Wight calls up to three corpses within 60 ft. to rise as Zombies (standard statistics) under his control, deputized to guard the strongbox."}, {"name": "Foreclosure Gaze", "replaces": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. reaching for the vault must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute, seized by a debt it never signed for. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The strongbox holds a real deed the party's client needs to prove their claim to land."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A depositor's descendant has hired the party to recover what's rightfully theirs from the vault."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's deputized the bank's former clerks, and they still remember their old jobs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The vault combination is buried with a teller he trusted, long dead in the same bank."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll let anyone leave who hasn't touched the vault door, but not one step closer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll honor a legitimate withdrawal slip if the party can produce one, however old."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The strongbox is empty and has been for years, but he still guards it like it's full."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaking the vault open releases every debt he ever collected, all calling due on the party at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing sentinel over a strongbox that outlived every account it ever held", "buttons straining over a chest gone grey and stiff, hand never leaving the vault door"]},{"name":"Noon-Duel Gunfighter","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"rlm-noon-duel-gunfighter","summary":"Undefeated noon-draw gunfighter the whole town fears","flavor":"Never lost a noon draw and never will — the whole town clears out when word gets around he's in it. Some say he picks the fights just to keep the streak.","desc":"He always calls the hour himself — high noon, main street, both of you walking to your marks while shopkeepers hurry to pull their shutters. He's undefeated because he's fast, but mostly because he's already decided you're going to hesitate, and you probably will.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Called Shot", "text": "If both combatants are at full hit points at the start of the duel, the gunfighter's first attack against you scores a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's called a noon draw against a party member who never agreed to it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival gunfighter is paying him to pick fights that keep his winning streak alive."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's undefeated in town, and the local law wants him gone before someone else dies."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving family wants the party to end his streak before he calls out their kin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The whole town clears the street the second word spreads he's calling a draw."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll skip the draw entirely for anyone who openly refuses to hesitate."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He remembers every man who's ever hesitated against him, by name, in order."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's started calling draws against people who never even agreed to face him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["calling the hour himself, high noon, main street, walking both parties to their marks", "watching shopkeepers hurry to pull their shutters at word he's back in town"]},{"name":"Rail Baron's War-Machine","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"rlm-rail-barons-war-machine","summary":"Armored rail-car war-machine muscling a dead man's right-of-way","flavor":"Built to muscle a right-of-way through land nobody agreed to sell. Answers only to the man who signed the requisition — and he's long dead.","desc":"Armored rail-car plating bolted over a walking chassis, it grinds forward on legs built from repurposed drive wheels, venting black coal smoke with every stride. It doesn't negotiate right-of-way — it simply keeps coming until whatever's in front of it isn't anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The War-Machine makes two Right-of-Way Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Right-of-Way Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 17 Strength save or be knocked Prone and pushed 10 ft."}, {"name": "Grinding Advance", "text": "At the start of its turn, the War-Machine moves 15 ft. in a straight line without provoking Opportunity Attacks, destroying difficult terrain, fencing, and unsecured structures in its path."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trailing rail-car plating dented into the shape of everything it's already flattened."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its requisition papers are bolted to its chassis, water-stained and unreadable."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vents coal smoke thick enough to blind pursuers for a stride or two."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a length of surveyed stake-line still snagged in one drive wheel."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grinds to a halt exactly at property lines the dead requisitioner marked, then resumes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Doesn't negotiate right-of-way — it simply keeps coming until nothing's in front of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its coal furnace burns a stack of old land deeds instead of coal, never running low."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its chassis is rigged to keep grinding forward for a full minute even after it's destroyed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "desert"],"activity":["grinding forward on legs built from repurposed drive wheels, venting black coal smoke", "muscling through a right-of-way nobody agreed to sell, answering only to a dead man's requisition"]},{"name":"Draw-at-Noon Revenant","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Duel-killed revenant returning every noon to draw again","flavor":"Killed at high noon in a duel that everyone in town watched and nobody stopped. Returns every day the sun's directly overhead, looking for whoever's standing in the street.","desc":"He returns at noon exactly, every time, boots crunching gravel in a duster still torn where the fatal shot went through. He doesn't remember losing. He only remembers the moment before the draw, and he means to have it back, over and over, from anyone standing in the street.","traits":{"note": "Returns to fight again at the next in-game noon if destroyed anywhere near its original death-ground, unless that ground is consecrated or salted."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He returns to the exact street where the party is currently doing business at noon."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The town watched him die and did nothing, and the guilt of that still hangs over it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member's stance for the stance of the man who beat him fair."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A witness to the original duel could finally lay him to rest, if the party can find them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He only appears exactly at noon and vanishes the instant the sun passes its peak."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll accept a stand-in duel and rest quietly if that duel is fought fair, win or lose."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every noon he returns, the bullet hole in his duster is a little larger than the day before."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing him at any hour but noon only sends him back to the moment before the draw, unresolved."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["returning at noon exactly, boots crunching gravel in a duster torn where the fatal shot went through", "standing in an empty street, waiting for whoever's there to take the place of the man who killed him"]},{"name":"The Last Honest Marshal","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"rlm-the-last-honest-marshal","summary":"Undying lawman whose fused badge still holds the line","flavor":"He held the line when the town's whole council told him to look away, and it killed him for it. Now he holds a line nobody else can even see, and the badge is grown into his ribs.","desc":"The badge is fused into his ribcage now, tarnished silver grown through bone the way a scar grows through skin, and his eyes are the only warm thing left on him. He still reads the warrant aloud before he acts on it — the one honest ritual an undying lawman refuses to abandon.","traits":{"note": "Reads a warrant aloud before attacking any creature guilty of an actual crime it names; a target proven innocent of that crime is immune to the marshal's first attack.", "actions": [{"name": "The Line He Enforces", "text": "Once per turn, the marshal can mark a 10-foot line on the ground; any creature he names as guilty that crosses it provokes an immediate opportunity attack from him, even without reach."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He is escorting a prisoner's ghost to a gallows that rotted away decades ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands to see everyone's papers; he will not let the party pass without proof of who they are."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living outlaw hides in the party's midst — the Marshal can smell the warrant on them and wants them surrendered."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He guards a strongbox of stolen payroll he swore to return; the rightful owner is long dead, so he keeps swearing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member for the man who shot him and will not be talked out of it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers a deal: deputize, help him hang the one crime still unpunished, and he'll let the town rest."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every death he's ever sentenced walks a step behind him; break his star and they all come loose at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He is the only law left in a stretch of country where the land itself has started to judge the living; siding with him binds the party to its sentences, defying him makes them outlaws to the ground they stand on."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "desert", "urban"],"activity":["walking a dead town's main street on a patrol that ended a lifetime ago", "standing at the jailhouse door refusing every soul that tries to leave"]},{"name":"The Noon Reckoning","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"rlm-the-noon-reckoning","summary":"Towering fiend that embodies every blood-ended noon duel","flavor":"Every town's noon-draw that ever ended in blood feeds it — it IS the duel, wearing whatever face the debt requires. It only walks the street when the sun's dead overhead and someone's about to draw.","desc":"It rises out of shimmering noon heat mirage-first, horns and wings resolving out of a hundred quiet duels that all ended the same way — badly, at midday, in dust. Every gunfight this land has ever settled with blood is folded into the shape of it, and it has come to collect on all of them at once.","traits":{"note": "Its presence forces every ranged combatant within 60 feet to fight at high noon conditions (disadvantage from glare) unless they have cover.", "actions": [{"name": "A Hundred Duels", "text": "Once per encounter, the fiend recreates a duel: it and one target both roll initiative fresh mid-combat, and whichever wins that roll gets an immediate free attack against the other."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been summoned deliberately by someone owed a debt of blood from an old duel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only walks a street where a duel once ended badly, and the party's standing on one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living gunfighter fears it's coming for him specifically, for a duel he rigged decades ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It arrives exactly at noon and vanishes with the sun, giving the party a hard clock to work against."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every duel it's ever fed on has left a scar on the land, and those scars are waking up nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will accept a fair duel in place of a massacre, if someone's willing to stand the mark."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It wears the face of whoever's most afraid of it in the moment, never the same shape twice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is the accumulated debt of every blood-ended noon in this stretch of country, and it has come to collect on all of them at once — surviving it rewrites what the land believes justice looks like."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "desert", "elemental"],"activity":["rising out of shimmering noon heat mirage-first, horns and wings resolving from a hundred quiet duels", "walking the street only when the sun is dead overhead and someone's about to draw"]},{"name":"Tin-Star Deputy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Green deputy who follows orders to the letter","flavor":"A green badge-wearer sworn in last week because the town ran out of better options. Follows orders to the letter and dies exactly as often as that implies.","desc":"His badge is shinier than it has any business being and his gunbelt sits a little too high, cinched by someone who's never actually drawn from it in anger. He follows the letter of whatever he was told, word for word, even when the situation's clearly outgrown the instructions.","traits":{"note": "He will not deviate from his last order, even when it stops making sense.", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His badge is pinned on crooked; he straightens it before every fight, mid-draw."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads his orders off a card in his palm, lips moving, before he acts on them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes anyone who talks like an authority, friend or not."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still has the store tag looped through his gunbelt buckle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Apologizes before every swing, out of habit more than sincerity."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Won't leave his assigned post even when the town around it empties out."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Carries orders signed by a marshal nobody in town remembers hiring."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Convinced he's already died in the line of duty once; fights like there's nothing left to lose twice."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["standing too straight at a crossroads, reciting the order he was given word for word", "checking a folded warrant against every face that passes, slow and wrong"]},{"name":"Trail-Dust Skinner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Hide-skinner who sells to whoever's buying","flavor":"Skins whatever the range gives up and sells the hides to whoever's buying, law or otherwise. Carries a knife more than a gun and knows how to use both badly.","desc":"He's got a wagon bed piled with hides that smell like they've been riding a long way in the heat, and a buyer's name he won't say twice. He'll skin anything that falls, doesn't much care whose brand it wore, and he's already calculating what you're worth in pelts.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Skinning Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Trail Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His wagon bed is stacked with fresh hides that need moving before they turn in the heat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's short on the buyer's price and eyeing the party's mounts to make up the difference."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rancher's brand shows plain on three of his hides; he'll deny whose cattle they were."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed money by a buyer who's since skipped town, and he wants an escort to collect."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tracking the same herd the party's after, and he'll take the kill if they let him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to split a haul if the party helps him drag it out before the law arrives."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One hide in his wagon is still warm, hours after the kill, and won't stop twitching."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's skinned something that wasn't only an animal, and its owner is already hunting the trail back to him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["working a knife under a fresh hide with a buyer's price already running in his head", "sizing up a rider's boots and belt like they're pelts he hasn't taken yet"]},{"name":"Powder-Monkey Kid","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Underage dynamite-runner, twitchy and dangerous","flavor":"Too young for the gang proper, so he handles the dynamite and does the running. Fast, twitchy, and one bad drop from taking the whole outfit with him.","desc":"He can't be more than fourteen, sleeves rolled past skinny wrists, a satchel of dynamite sticks slung crosswise and rattling with every twitchy step. His hands shake lighting the fuse and shake worse throwing it, which is exactly why nobody wants to be standing anywhere near him.","traits":{"note": "A bad roll on his own fuse is as likely to hurt him as anyone nearby.", "actions": [{"name": "Hideout Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sling Shot", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Lit Stick (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The kid lobs a dynamite stick at a point within 30 ft. Each creature within 10 ft. makes a DC 10 Dexterity save, taking 5 (2d4) Fire damage on a failure, half on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts his sticks out loud, over and over, like the number keeps changing on him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at his own fuse-lighting every single time, then does it anyway."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears another kid's boots, two sizes too big, laced tight with fuse-cord."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks tougher than he fights, mostly to convince himself he isn't scared."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one stick wrapped separate from the rest, saved for something specific."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will trade information about the gang's plans for a promise nobody makes him light another fuse."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His satchel rattles even when it's empty, like the habit outlasted the dynamite."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's carrying a stick that's gone unstable in the heat and doesn't know it yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["counting sticks of dynamite out of a satchel with shaking, too-young hands", "lighting a short fuse and already backing away before it catches proper"]},{"name":"Rail-Camp Roughneck","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Track-laying laborer who breaks heads for back pay","flavor":"Spikes track by day, breaks heads by night when the paymaster's short again. Swings a maul like he means it.","desc":"Sunburned to leather across the back of his neck, sledge still in one hand from driving spikes all day, he's got the kind of anger that's been baked in by months of unpaid wages. He swings the hammer the same way he swings it at rail — hard, and without much aiming.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spike Maul", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Trail Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed three weeks' pay and wants the party to lean on the paymaster with him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's organizing a walk-off and needs someone who can read the company's contract for the catch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a co-worker's pay envelope, meant for a widow, and hasn't decided whether to deliver it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade rail-camp gossip for a meal, and he's heard where the company's cutting corners."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hunting the foreman who shorted the crew, maul still in hand from the last argument."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's rallying a half-dozen others to hold the line at the next camp; he wants muscle, not talk."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The last spike he drove hasn't stopped humming, and the rail past it runs somewhere no map shows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's found proof the company's paying in counterfeit scrip and means to burn the ledger tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["driving a spike into rail-tie with a maul, sunburned and furious about back pay", "cornering a paymaster's clerk against a boxcar over three weeks of missing wages"]},{"name":"Sidewinder Snake","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"venomous-snake","model":"venomous-snake","summary":"Ordinary rattler, unusually common and agitated","flavor":"An ordinary desert rattler, except this stretch of scrub has three times the usual number of them, all agitated.","desc":"Just a rattler, technically — but there are a lot more of them out here than there should be, and they've stopped giving fair warning before they strike. This one's coiled tight in what little shade a rock throws, tail already going before you've noticed it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded, dusty scales that vanish completely against dry sand until it moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rattles longer and louder than usual, like the warning's worn thin from overuse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in a boot left behind by somebody who isn't coming back for it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes at shadows and shod hooves alike, agitated past the point of caution."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thinner than a healthy rattler should be, like the scrub's stopped feeding it right."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Travels in loose company with two or three others, an unusual number for the stretch."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Doesn't rattle at all anymore — just strikes, silent, like it's given up the warning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its bite leaves a mark that keeps aching long after the poison itself should've run its course."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["coiled tight in a rock's thin shade, tail already rattling before it's seen", "crossing open sand in a hurry, agitated, like something behind it won't let up"]},{"name":"Scrub-Land Jackrabbit Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Boiling jackrabbit mass that strips land bare","flavor":"A boiling mass of oversized jackrabbits that strips a garden bare in a minute and a rider's boots in two. Harmless alone, a hazard in number.","desc":"The brush ahead seems to be boiling, a hundred pale bodies churning over each other in a moving carpet that strips every green thing down to root and dirt as it passes. Up close the sound is worse than the sight — a continuous dry rustle of claws and teeth.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Gnawing Mass", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strips a garden plot bare to the root in under a minute flat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves as one continuous carpet, no single body ever fully still."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rustle of claws and teeth carries louder than the sight of the mass itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Takes boot leather nearly as fast as it takes greenery, given the chance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Splits around obstacles and reforms whole on the far side without slowing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three times the number a healthy range ought to support, and still multiplying."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves ground behind it scoured so clean nothing's grown back in a season."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Panics into a stampede-dense knot that can bowl a grown rider clean off a horse."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "desert"],"activity":["boiling low across scrubland in a pale churning mass, stripping ground bare as it goes", "pouring through a fence line into a garden row, a hundred bodies deep"]},{"name":"Range Buzzard","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"Ordinary vulture that follows the soon-to-be-dead","flavor":"An honest, unremarkable carrion bird — except it's started following specific people days before they die.","desc":"An ordinary bird, technically, riding a thermal in slow lazy circles above the trail — except it's been following you since sunup, and it never seems to be looking for anything but the exact spot where you're about to fall down.","traits":{"note": "It's never wrong about who's about to fall — a bad omen, not a threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Carrion Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows one traveler for days before ever settling near them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Perches closest to whoever's wound is worst, without fail."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never circles a group — always exactly one person, singled out."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow crosses the same patch of ground over and over, marking a spot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits at a fixed distance no matter how fast or slow the rider travels."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Locals read its presence over a house as a warning worth acting on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Lands exactly where the body will fall, hours before the falling happens."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its chosen one dying early, by someone else's hand, seems to genuinely unsettle it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "sky", "grassland"],"activity":["riding a slow thermal in lazy circles, never quite losing sight of one particular rider", "perched on a dead fence post, patient, watching one person like it already knows something"]},{"name":"Prairie Dust-Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"Lean dry-wash wolf that takes livestock in packs","flavor":"Leaner and hungrier than a plain wolf, runs the dry washes in loose family packs and takes livestock when the deer thin out.","desc":"Lean to the point of visible ribs, coat the color of the dry wash it dens in, it never hunts alone — three or four shadows moving low and quiet along the arroyo, herding cattle or people the same patient way, cutting off the easy retreat first.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wash-Runner Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is Prone, this attack deals an extra 2 (1d4) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coat's the exact color of the dry wash it dens in, near invisible until it moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ribs show plain through the coat; hungrier than a normal wolf ever runs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a family pack of three or four, never fewer, never truly alone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Herds cattle and people the same patient way, cutting the retreat off first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Takes livestock only after the deer thin out for the season."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A rancher's put a bounty on this particular pack after three straight losses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Doesn't howl like a wolf should — the pack goes silent right before it strikes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Runs the wash even in open daylight now, bold past what hunger alone explains."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "desert"],"activity":["moving low and quiet along a dry wash in a loose pack, cutting off the easy retreat first", "circling a bawling calf at range, patient, waiting for the herd to thin"]},{"name":"Grave-Dust Crow","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"raven","model":"raven","summary":"Boneyard raven that talks in a dead man's cadence","flavor":"A boneyard raven that picked up a sliver of whatever's buried underneath it. Talks a little, in a dead man's cadence.","desc":"It perches on the leaning fence post of the boneyard and talks — not caws, talks, in a low dry rasp that carries the exact cadence of somebody long buried there. It repeats the same handful of phrases, over and over, like it's still finishing an argument from decades back.","traits":{"note": "What it says is half of an old argument — never the whole of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Graveyard Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats a name, over and over, that matches no headstone in the yard."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes quiet the moment anyone answers back, as if listening for the first time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rasp carries a specific accent, one nobody local still talks with."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles back to the same three phrases no matter how the conversation starts."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Picks at the same patch of turned dirt between sentences, absent-minded."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A grieving local pays coin just to sit near it and listen a while longer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Finishes its buried argument mid-sentence if the right name is spoken aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Goes silent forever the instant its buried grievance finally gets answered."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["perched on a leaning fence post, talking in a dead man's dry rasping cadence", "repeating the same handful of phrases over and over, mid-argument with nobody there"]},{"name":"Whiskey-Nerve Brawler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"Saloon brawler who fights better drunk","flavor":"Fights better drunk than sober and knows it, so he's rarely sober. Saloon muscle, cheap to hire, cheaper to replace.","desc":"He's three drinks past sensible and swinging looser for it, knuckles already split from an earlier fight he probably started. Sober he flinches at everything; drunk he doesn't flinch at all, which somehow makes him hit harder and care less about where the punches land.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Loose Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Bar Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +2, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches hard at loud noises when sober, doesn't flinch at all three drinks in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Started this fight, will insist someone else started it, throughout."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights better the drunker he gets, and knows it well enough to stay that way."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cheap to hire and cheaper to replace, and the saloon owner treats him that way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't remember most fights the next morning, wins or losses both."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Owes the bartender a running tab he's paying off one bar-fight at a time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears he can't feel pain past his fourth drink, and lately that's stopped being a boast."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Keeps fighting well past any hit that should've dropped a sober man cold."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["swinging loose and wild in a saloon, knuckles split from a fight he already started", "propping himself on a bar rail, three drinks past sensible, daring somebody to try him"]},{"name":"Homestead Scarecrow","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Cursed-field scarecrow variant guarding a homestead","flavor":"A second scarecrow from the same cursed patch of field as its cousin, propped on a homestead fence instead of a graveyard one. Same trick, different crop.","desc":"Somebody's dead homestead still keeps this one propped in the ruined garden row, patchwork clothes gone to rag, and it's picked up the same curse as the field-scarecrows out on the ranches. It stands watch over a house nobody lives in anymore — closer every time you check.","traits":{"note": "It never seems to move while watched — only ever between glances.", "actions": [{"name": "Ragged Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Field-Curse Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature the scarecrow can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 11 Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn, rattled by the sight of it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patchwork clothes gone entirely to rag, straw showing through at every seam."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fixed on the same house it's guarded since before the family that built it left."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands closer to the door each time someone comes back to check on it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a hat that clearly belonged to whoever used to live in the homestead."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its post has rotted clean through, yet it never seems to lean or fall."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Neighbors leave the homestead well alone rather than deal with what's guarding it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Picked up the same curse as its cousin scarecrows out on the working ranches."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Only truly moves once it's certain no living eye is on it at all."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["propped stiff in a ruined garden row, standing watch over a house nobody lives in anymore", "found a few feet closer to the porch than it was the last time anyone checked"]},{"name":"Claim-Office Forger","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Land-deed forger who triple-sells the same plot","flavor":"Draws up land deeds that look real enough to hold up in a corrupt court, then sells the same plot three times over.","desc":"He's got a satchel of deeds with the same plot description copied three or four times over, different buyer names inked in each. His hands are steady with a pen the way most men's are steady with a gun, and he's already sizing you up as customer number four.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The forger makes two attacks, using Filing Shortsword or Claim-Office Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Filing Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claim-Office Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a satchel of deeds all describing the same plot, different buyers inked in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A furious buyer is hunting him down and the party's standing between them right now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll forge a document the party needs, for a price, no questions either direction."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of his three sold plots overlaps land the party actually has a claim to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed protection money by the claim office and wants muscle to collect it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to cut the party in on a fourth sale if they help him vanish after."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One deed he forged turned out to describe land that genuinely doesn't exist on any map."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's forged a deed to land the local dead consider still rightfully theirs."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["inking a buyer's name into a deed that's already been sold twice before", "sizing up a stranger as customer number four for the same worthless plot"]},{"name":"Stagecoach Highwayman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"bandit-courier","summary":"Polite masked highwayman working the coach roads","flavor":"Works the coach roads alone or in pairs, masked, polite, and gone before the horses have stopped stamping.","desc":"He rides up alongside the coach at a polite canter, mask neat, hat tipped, and asks for the strongbox like he's requesting a dance. He's genuinely disappointed when things turn ugly — robbery, to him, is a transaction that shouldn't require anybody getting shot.","traits":{"note": "He's genuinely put off when a robbery turns violent — that's not how he thinks it should go.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The highwayman makes two attacks, using Polite Shortsword or Coach-Road Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Polite Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Coach-Road Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's stopped the party's coach and wants only the strongbox, nothing more, if they're reasonable."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's working the road alone tonight, his usual partner having not shown."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a passenger and hesitates, clearly not expecting to know them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already spent this week's take and needs one more coach before he can quit the road."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to let the coach pass clean in exchange for information on a rival gang."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided this will be his last job, and he's nervous enough that it shows."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He tips his hat to a passenger who swears they've never met him, and he insists otherwise."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The strongbox he's after belongs to someone who does not forgive being robbed, ever."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill"],"activity":["riding up alongside a coach at a polite canter, mask neat, hat tipped, asking nicely for the box", "waiting masked at a bend in the coach road, alone, patient as a toll-taker"]},{"name":"Company Book-Keeper Wight","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Dead accountant endlessly recounting debts owed","flavor":"Died at his ledger balancing debts nobody could pay and rose still doing the arithmetic, hollow-voiced, endlessly recounting the sums owed.","desc":"Green-grey and hunched over a ledger that never balances, it mutters sums under its breath in an endless recount, licking a rotted thumb to turn pages that have long since crumbled to pulp. It doesn't seem to notice you until the total finally, impossibly, comes out wrong.","traits":{"note": "It only truly notices someone the instant its endless sum finally comes out wrong.", "actions": [{"name": "Ledger Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Green-grey and hunched permanently over the same ruined ledger, arithmetic endless."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters sums in a hollow voice that never quite lands on a final number."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards the office it died in as though payroll's still due at the end of the week."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reaches for a pen that rotted away years before it did."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recoils from anyone holding actual coin, as though owed sums are the only currency it trusts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its ledger names debts real families in town are still quietly paying off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The total it's chasing changes depending on who's close enough to read it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the sum ever finally balances, it stops moving entirely, debt paid at last."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["hunched over a ledger that never balances, muttering the same recount under its breath", "licking a rotted thumb to turn pages that crumbled to pulp long ago"]},{"name":"Boothill Skeleton","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"skeleton-archer","summary":"Rifle-toting graveyard skeleton in a rotted duster","flavor":"Rises from the cheap end of the cemetery with a rifle instead of a bow, still dressed in a moth-eaten duster, and shoots at anything that disturbs its plot.","desc":"It claws up through loose boothill dirt in a duster gone to threads, rifle still slung across the ribs where a strap somehow survived the grave. The bones move with a soldier's discipline — level the rifle, brace, fire — muscle memory outlasting the muscle.","traits":{"note": "Muscle memory outlasted the muscle — it still drills like a soldier.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The skeleton makes two attacks with its Graveyard Rifle, or one attack with Graveyard Rifle and uses Bone Shard."}, {"name": "Graveyard Rifle", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Bone Shard (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or have disadvantage on its next attack roll, the shard lodged deep."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Duster's gone to threads, but the strap that holds its rifle somehow survived whole."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Braces and fires with a soldier's discipline, level, brace, fire, never varying the order."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rises from the cheap end of the cemetery every time, never the paid plots."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shoots at anything disturbing its plot, friend and stranger treated exactly alike."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Jaw hangs loose but the aim never wavers for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Defends a grave marker with a name long since weathered unreadable."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Reloads a rifle that hasn't held a working cartridge in decades, and it still fires anyway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Keeps firing on a fixed count of shots it took in life, no more, no fewer, then falls still."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["clawing up through loose boothill dirt, rifle already braced against a duster of rotted rib", "leveling a rifle at anything that so much as steps near its plot"]},{"name":"Dust-Choked Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Thirst-crazed ghoul still digging a dry wash","flavor":"Died of thirst in a dry wash and came back still parched, still digging for water that isn't there, biting anything that gets close to the hole.","desc":"It's still digging, fingers worn to bone-white claws at a dry wash that hasn't held water in years, driven by a thirst that death never satisfied. When it finally notices you it doesn't stop digging so much as redirect the digging at you.","traits":{"note": "A thirst death never satisfied — killing it doesn't quiet the digging urge in others like it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The ghoul makes two attacks: one with Dust-Cracked Bite and one with Digging Claw."}, {"name": "Dust-Cracked Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Digging Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fingers worn to claws digging at a wash that hasn't run water in years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't stop digging when it notices you — just redirects the digging at you instead."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throat sounds permanently cracked, like the thirst that killed it never let go."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Digs the same hole night after night, deeper each time, water never coming."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin cracked like drought-baked mud, flaking off with every lurching motion."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Locals mark its wash as cursed ground and won't water stock anywhere near it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hole it digs is deeper than the wash should physically allow."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given enough uninterrupted time, its digging finds something that was never meant to surface."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["still digging at a dry wash that hasn't held water in years, claws worn bone-white", "redirecting a fresh dig straight at anything warm that wanders too close"]},{"name":"Grave-Dirt Zombie Posse","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie-plague-carrier","summary":"Hanged gang risen in formation, horses long gone","flavor":"A whole hanged gang risen together, still riding formation out of habit though their horses rotted out from under them years ago.","desc":"Six or seven of them shamble in a loose column, boots dragging, nooses still knotted tight around swollen grey necks. No horses — they walk it now, the same road they were hanged along, in the same order they died in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rope-Choked Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Six or seven strong, marching in the same loose column every time they're seen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nooses still knotted tight around necks gone grey and swollen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "No horses among them anymore — they walk the road their horses rotted out from under them on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the exact order they were hanged in, front to back, never mixed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them still clutches reins to a horse that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Follows the road to the same tree they were hanged from, every single time, if unopposed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sings, faintly, a hanging-day tune none of the living locals ever taught anyone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaking their nooses free scatters them wide instead of ending them, posse rejoining elsewhere."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["shambling in loose column down the same road they were hanged along, boots dragging", "walking the exact order they died in, nooses still knotted tight around swollen necks"]},{"name":"Mine-Shaft Crawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"carrion-crawler","model":"carrion-crawler","summary":"Blind mine-shaft predator that paralyzes and drags prey","flavor":"Bred in the dark below a played-out silver claim on whatever the miners stopped bringing up. Paralyzes with a touch and drags the still to a side tunnel.","desc":"It doesn't see you so much as taste the air with a forest of twitching mandibles, pale and eyeless from a lifetime in the dark below the shaft. It waits in the black at the tunnel's edge, patient as stone, until something warm gets close enough to paralyze and drag back down.","traits":{"note": "It's eyeless — sound and vibration find it long before sight ever could.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The crawler makes one attack with Shaft Bite and uses Paralyzing Tendrils."}, {"name": "Shaft Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Tendrils", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Poison damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bred in the dark below a played-out silver claim on whatever the miners left down there."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pale and eyeless from a lifetime never once seeing daylight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits at the tunnel's edge, patient as stone, for something warm to wander close."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags paralyzed prey to a side tunnel stacked with older, drier remains."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mandibles never stop twitching, even at total rest, tasting for the next warmth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The claim's owner keeps quiet about it, still hoping to work the shaft again someday."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its side-tunnel larder holds things that clearly weren't miners, older and stranger."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A vein of raw ore runs through its own carapace, half-fused, glinting under lantern light."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["cave", "mountain"],"activity":["tasting the tunnel air with a forest of twitching mandibles, waiting in the black patient as stone", "dragging something still and paralyzed back toward a side tunnel, slow and unhurried"]},{"name":"Sun-Blind Prospector Ghast","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Salt-blind prospector ghast that never turns back","flavor":"Went snow-blind on salt flats chasing a vein that wasn't there and starved rather than turn back. Now it doesn't turn back from anything.","desc":"Salt has crusted over where his eyes used to work, and he shuffles with a prospector's pick still gripped in one clawed hand, following some vein of ore that stopped existing when he did. He never turns back toward the light — light isn't where the gold is.","traits":{"note": "It never turns back toward the light — light isn't where the gold is, as far as it's concerned.", "actions": [{"name": "Salt-Crusted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Prospector's Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt has crusted clean over where its eyes used to work."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still grips a prospector's pick, chasing a vein that stopped existing when it did."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never turns back toward the light — light isn't where the gold is."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Starved rather than admit the vein wasn't there; starves in undeath the same stubborn way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shuffles the exact grid pattern a claim survey would follow, over and over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Still wears a claim-stake tag with a plot number that maps to real, disputed land."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Digs toward something under the salt flat that answers back, faintly, when struck."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The vein it's chasing is real now, having grown into the ground since its death."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["shuffling with a pick still gripped tight, following a vein of ore that stopped existing when it died", "crusted eyes turned resolutely away from the light, hunting the dark instead"]},{"name":"Rust-Bitten Rail Golem","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"Iron-eating rail-yard scrap creature spitting corrosion","flavor":"A stray piece of rail-yard machinery, half-alive from proximity to the Iron Horse Wreck-Golem, that eats iron and spits corrosion.","desc":"It's built from cannibalized rail spikes and scrap car iron, joints weeping orange rust-slurry with every awkward step, and it hungers for metal the way a living thing hungers for meat. It spits a fine corrosive mist that eats through buckles, barrels, and belt buckles alike.","traits":{"note": "It hungers for metal the way a living thing hungers for meat.", "actions": [{"name": "Scrap Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, and if the target is wearing or wielding a nonmagical metal object, that object takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to any AC or damage it grants, to a minimum of -3."}, {"name": "Corrosive Antennae", "replaces": "Antennae", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 15 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Acid damage, and any exposed nonmagical metal object the attack strikes begins to corrode."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built from cannibalized rail spikes and scrap car iron, joints leaking rust-slurry."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spits a fine corrosive mist that eats through buckles and belt fittings alike."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half-alive from proximity to something bigger and iron-hungry out on the wreck line."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drawn to gunmetal and horseshoes before anything else metal in reach."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of fine orange dust wherever its joints drag against the rail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A rail company's put a bounty on it for eating through a season's worth of spare track."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Grows visibly larger the longer it's left to feed undisturbed on a wreck site."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully rusted through in patches, it may simply collapse mid-fight into inert scrap."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["lurching through a rail yard on cannibalized spike-and-scrap legs, joints weeping orange rust-slurry", "spitting a fine corrosive mist across a row of barrels and buckles alike"]},{"name":"Poker-Table Cheat","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"performer","summary":"Smooth card-palming cheat, quick with a hideout knife","flavor":"Palms cards for a living and a knife for emergencies, both smoothly enough that nobody's caught him twice.","desc":"His fingers move faster than his face lets on, palming cards under a friendly smile that doesn't waver even when you catch him at it. There's a hideout knife strapped under the table's lip for exactly this conversation, and he's already reaching for it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Hideout Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just been caught cheating and the table's turning ugly around him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He owes a debt to whoever runs this table and cheats to cover the vig."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll cut the party in on a rigged game if they help him fleece a mark."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a marker signed by someone the party's looking for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A jealous rival cheat wants him dead and is watching this table right now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers information on the house's real owner in exchange for a clean escape."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One card he keeps palming shows a different hand every time it's glimpsed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's cheated the wrong player tonight, and that player doesn't lose graciously."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["palming a card under a friendly smile that doesn't waver even when he's caught", "reaching quiet for a hideout knife strapped under the table's lip"]},{"name":"Sod-House Squatter","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Stubborn dugout squatter, mostly bluff","flavor":"Dug into another man's land and dared anyone to move him. Mostly bluff, occasionally not.","desc":"He's dug his whole life into a hillside dugout that isn't technically his, rifle propped by the door more for show than use. Mostly bluff, mostly stubborn, mostly just wants to be left alone on dirt nobody else wanted until he moved in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dugout Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's squatting on a plot with a paper claim in someone else's name, and he won't move."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade what he knows about the land for help proving his own claim to it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A land agent's coming to evict him and he wants the party to back his bluff."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a rifle propped by the door and absolutely no ammunition for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dug up something on his plot he doesn't understand and wants an opinion."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers shelter for the night if the party doesn't ask too many questions about the dugout."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His dugout goes deeper than any hillside should, and he swears he never dug that far."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The rightful claim-holder he's squatting against is already riding in to settle it personally."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "grassland"],"activity":["standing in a dugout doorway with a rifle propped more for show than use", "daring a rider to try and move him off dirt nobody else wanted"]},{"name":"Territorial Militia Rifle","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"Poorly drilled militia rifleman who holds out of stubbornness","flavor":"Called up from the local ranches when the cavalry's a week out, drilled poorly, aims worse, holds anyway out of stubbornness.","desc":"His uniform's a size too big and his drill is worse, rifle held at an angle no sergeant ever taught him — but he holds his ground anyway, purely out of stubbornness, long after better-trained men would've run.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Militia Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform's a size too big; sleeves rolled twice just to free his hands."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Holds his ground long after better-trained men would've run, purely out of stubbornness."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was a rancher two weeks ago and still drills like it half the time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Aims worse than he holds, and he holds badly enough already."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Called up because the cavalry's a week out and somebody had to stand the line."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Writes letters home he's not confident he'll get the chance to send."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Follows orders from a sergeant the rest of the unit swears was never actually assigned."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Won't break formation even after every other militiaman beside him already has."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["holding a rifle at an angle no sergeant ever taught him, standing his ground out of stubbornness", "drilling a poorly-formed line while the cavalry's still a week out"]},{"name":"Cavalry Deserter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Cavalry deserter who robs both sides equally","flavor":"Walked off from his unit after seeing something in the breach he wasn't paid enough to fight, and now robs both sides equally.","desc":"Half a uniform still hangs off him, insignia torn free, and he's learned to rob wagon trains and army supply lines with equal indifference. He doesn't much care which side he's stealing from anymore — desertion cured him of caring.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The deserter makes two attacks, using Deserter's Shortsword or Cavalry Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Deserter's Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cavalry Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's robbing whichever side rides past first, and doesn't much care which that is."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hiding from a patrol that's still hunting deserters from his old unit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade information on troop movements for safe passage out of the territory."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He saw something in the breach he won't describe and won't go near a battle line again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying army supplies he's decided to sell rather than deliver."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A former comrade recognizes him and wants him brought in alive, not dead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He still salutes an empty patch of ground where his unit used to fall in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "What he saw in the breach is still following him, and it's getting closer."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "desert"],"activity":["robbing a wagon train with half a uniform still hanging off him, insignia torn free", "sizing up an army supply line with the same flat indifference as any other target"]},{"name":"Prickled Cactus-Kin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"Reaching cactus-kin, still until a rider passes close","flavor":"A saguaro that learned to want something, and to reach for it. Stands stock-still until a rider passes too close.","desc":"It looks like any other stand of barrel cactus until a rider gets close enough, and then the spines angle, subtly, toward the warmth. It doesn't chase. It just waits at the trail's narrow point for something to brush past.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spine Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Looks like any other stand of barrel cactus until a rider's already too close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't chase — waits at the trail's narrow point for something to brush past."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spines angle slowly toward warmth, subtle enough to miss if you're not watching."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roots itself in exactly the spot a trail forces riders to pass single-file."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A saguaro shape at rest, indistinguishable from the real thing at any distance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Locals mark its patch of scrub with stacked stones as an old, quiet warning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Blooms out of season, pale flowers opening only right before it strikes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Roots up entirely and shuffles a short distance if prey lingers just out of reach."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["standing stock-still among ordinary barrel cactus until a rider passes too close", "angling spines slowly, subtly, toward the nearest warmth at a trail's narrow point"]},{"name":"Alkali Flat Wisp","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Salt-flat wisp luring the thirsty away from water","flavor":"A drowning-light that leads thirsty travelers deeper into the salt flats instead of toward the water it pretends to be.","desc":"A pale bobbing light hovers out over the salt flat at dusk, exactly where the old maps mark good water. It drifts a little farther every time you follow, patient as drought, leading the thirsty out past the point where turning back is still possible.","traits":{"note": "It never closes distance on its own — it only leads. Cornering it against real water snuffs the game.", "actions": [{"name": "Salt Shock", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Lightning damage, and the target's mouth and throat go bone-dry — it has Disadvantage on the next Constitution saving throw it makes before finishing a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Burns a thin, sickly blue instead of the usual pale white."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hovers exactly at the height a canteen would sit on a saddle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flickers in rhythm with a heartbeat, speeding up near dehydrated prey."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint smell of creek water that isn't anywhere nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't cross onto cracked mud — sticks to the whitest, driest salt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums a low, wordless tune that sounds like a half-remembered lullaby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Casts the shadow of a person who isn't standing anywhere near it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits into three dimmer wisps when struck, each one leading a different direction."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "elemental"],"activity":["bobbing low over cracked salt flat, mimicking the shine of water that isn't there", "drifting a little farther out every time a thirsty traveler follows it"]},{"name":"Bounty-Poster Doppel","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Shapeshifter that impersonates its own bounty poster","flavor":"Wears the face on whichever wanted poster pays best that week, collects the bounty on itself from a gullible marshal, and vanishes before the paperwork clears.","desc":"It's wearing the exact face from the wanted poster nailed to the saloon wall — same scar, same crooked nose — and it'll happily confirm the reward, collect the bounty on itself from a fool, and vanish before anyone checks the paper twice.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The doppel makes two Backhand attacks."}, {"name": "Backhand", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Read the Mark", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The doppel reads a creature's surface thoughts within 60 feet for 1 minute — enough to lift a name, a debt, or a face worth wearing next."}, {"name": "Wrong Face", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 30 feet that can see the doppel makes a DC 12 Wisdom save, becoming Frightened until the end of its next turn on a failure as its own face flickers across the doppel's for an instant."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-transaction, collecting reward money from a marshal who hasn't looked twice at the poster."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real outlaw it's impersonating is watching from across the street, furious about the competition."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wearing the face of someone the party actually knows and trusts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A second bounty poster just went up — for the same face, a town over, same week."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already spent the bounty money and needs a fresh face before the marshal checks the paperwork."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's collected the same bounty in three towns running and kept none of the money — something else wants it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The poster it's wearing is blank until someone reads it aloud, then fills in with whoever's speaking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to wear the face of a party member, mid-fight, mid-sentence, before anyone can stop the swap."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["leaning against the saloon wall next to its own wanted poster, waiting for someone to notice the resemblance", "collecting its own bounty from a credulous deputy before the ink's even dry"]},{"name":"Copperhead Nest-Guard","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"giant-venomous-snake","summary":"Territorial oversized copperhead denning a mine entrance","flavor":"An oversized copperhead that's claimed a played-out mine entrance as its den and doesn't share territory with anything, prospector included.","desc":"Thick as a man's forearm and longer than most men are tall, it's denned the mouth of an old mine shaft and doesn't recognize property lines. It doesn't rattle a warning — copperheads never do — it just strikes from the shadow of the tunnel mouth.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Silent Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage. No warning rattle precedes this attack — it does not require the snake to have moved first."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing half its rattle from an old cave-in; strikes even quieter for it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales gone pale with rock dust, near-invisible against the tailings."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests atop a rusted pick someone left behind decades back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Twice the usual bulk from years of undisturbed denning."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps three smaller copperheads denned alongside it, all territorial."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Strikes only at anything carrying a lit lantern, ignoring the dark-footed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its venom leaves a faint metallic taste, like it's been drinking the ore water."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Guards a shaft that groans and shifts underfoot — killing it collapses the entrance."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "hill", "cave"],"activity":["coiled in the shadow of a played-out mine entrance, still as the rock around it", "testing the air with a flicking tongue, unbothered by boots crunching closer"]},{"name":"Company Strikebreaker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"Liquor-raged strikebreaker sent to end a picket line","flavor":"Hired muscle sent to end a labor dispute the fast way, works up a rage on cheap liquor before wading into a picket line.","desc":"He's been drinking company liquor since noon and it shows in the wild swing of his approach, sent down from the office with a club and instructions to end a picket line by whatever means end it fastest.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Company Club", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d12 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. While Bloodied, this attack deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage — the liquor doesn't quit even when he's losing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a torn strike notice stuffed in his coat with three names circled in pencil."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A second, sober strikebreaker is trying to talk him down before he does something the company won't cover."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mistaken the party for the picket line and is already swinging."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying an unsigned company voucher promising extra pay if the line breaks tonight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He used to work the same line he's now been sent to break."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's crying between swings, swearing this is the last job he takes from the company."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The liquor bottle in his coat never seems to run empty no matter how much he drinks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's got a lit fuse tucked in his belt, company orders to burn the union hall if the line doesn't break."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["staggering up the picket line with a club raised, reeking of cheap company liquor", "shouting company talking points nobody hired him to believe, just to work up the nerve"]},{"name":"Grave Robber Duo","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Boneyard grave robber, occasionally digs up trouble","flavor":"Works the boneyards after dark for rings, gold teeth, and the occasional cursed trinket that's more trouble than it's worth.","desc":"Two of them work the boneyard together, one holding the lantern low and one working the shovel, trading a running commentary about which graves still have anything worth pulling. They've dug up worse than valuables more than once and kept digging anyway.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The robber makes two Shovel-Edge attacks."}, {"name": "Shovel-Edge", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Graveside Charm", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "One creature the robber can see within 30 feet makes a DC 12 Wisdom save, becoming Charmed for 1 minute on a failure — just long enough to be talked out of raising an alarm."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've just pulled a ring off a corpse whose family is standing at the cemetery gate."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them has half a cursed trinket in his pocket and won't stop scratching at the mark it's leaving."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've dug into the wrong grave — a fresh one, still breathing underneath the dirt."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A lawman's watching the boneyard gate, and they need a distraction to get their haul out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're arguing over splitting a haul that includes a name the party recognizes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've started digging up graves to order, for a buyer neither of them has actually met."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every grave they've opened tonight was already empty, dirt undisturbed below the surface."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They just pried open a coffin lid and whatever's inside grabbed the shovel first."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["working a fresh grave by lantern-light, one digging while the other keeps a low commentary running", "prying a gold tooth loose and arguing over whether it's worth the smell"]},{"name":"Iron-Rail Spike Wraith","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"rlm-iron-rail-spike-wraith","summary":"Crushed rail-worker ghost still driving phantom spikes","flavor":"A track-worker crushed under the rail he was laying, doomed to keep driving spikes into ground that no longer needs them, swinging at anyone who steps on his old line.","desc":"Translucent and rail-thin, it swings a spectral sledge in the same rhythm it swung in life, driving phantom spikes into ties that aren't there anymore. The clang rings real even though the hammer isn't, and the ghost doesn't seem to know the railroad's finished.","traits":{"note": "The clang of its hammer carries for a quarter mile even though nothing physical is striking anything.", "actions": [{"name": "Sledge Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the wraith regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack rises as a spike-scarred Zombie under the wraith's control at the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings in perfect three-count rhythm — count along and it never notices you closing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a foreman's cap, translucent and rail-thin like the rest of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only appears where an actual spike still sits half-driven in the old ties."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint scorch-marks shaped like railroad spikes wherever it swings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums the same work-chant over and over, missing the words that used to fit the rhythm."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Stops swinging entirely if the buried rail bed beneath it is ever actually dug up."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A real, physical hammer-mark appears on anything it strikes, days after the ghost moves on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every spike it's ever driven works itself loose from the ground at once when it finally falls."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["swinging a spectral sledge in rhythm along a rail bed that was torn up years ago", "driving phantom spikes into ties that rotted away a generation back"]},{"name":"Prairie Fire Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"Runaway grass fire that took on a will of its own","flavor":"A grass fire that outran the wind and kept going, taking on a will of its own somewhere past the second county line.","desc":"What started as an ordinary grass fire got hungry somewhere along the way and started choosing directions instead of just following the wind. It roars low across the prairie in a wall of orange, crackling with something that sounds almost like intent.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The elemental makes two Grassfire attacks."}, {"name": "Grassfire", "replaces": "Burn", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Fire damage. If the target is wearing flammable gear or standing in dry grass, it also catches fire, taking 3 (1d6) Fire damage at the start of each of its turns until someone uses an action to put it out."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a perfectly straight burn line behind it, like it's following an old fence."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Burns cooler and slower than a normal grass fire, patient instead of ravenous."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roars loudest right before changing direction, like it's clearing its throat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles back to burn the same stretch of prairie twice, as if it forgot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throws embers that spark small, short-lived fire-motes ahead of the main blaze."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Avoids a single fenced homestead entirely, circling it like the fence still matters."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whispers in the crackle of the flame, words half-formed and never finished."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits into two smaller blazes when reduced to half health, each one hunting separately."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "elemental"],"activity":["rolling low across open prairie in a wall of orange, choosing its own direction against the wind", "crackling with something that sounds almost like a decision being made"]},{"name":"Sand-Wash Basilisk","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"basilisk","summary":"Petrifying desert basilisk denning a gravel-choked wash","flavor":"Petrifies whatever crosses its wash, then waits for the desert to grind the statue down to gravel over the years. The wash is full of very old gravel.","desc":"It dens in a gravel-choked wash where the footing already looks unnervingly still, half-buried statues of jackrabbits and one unlucky cow scattered around its burrow mouth. Its eyes are the last warm color left in that dead grey wash.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Stone-Eye Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage. If the target is already Restrained by the basilisk's gaze, this attack has Advantage."}, {"name": "Grinding Gaze", "text": "At the start of each of its turns, the basilisk's eyes flare dull gold. Each creature within 30 feet that can see them makes a DC 12 Constitution save. On a failure, a creature's flesh begins turning to grit at the joints, becoming Restrained until the start of its next turn. A creature Restrained this way three times total is Petrified until freed by Greater Restoration or similar magic."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its den is ringed with a dozen small stone jackrabbits, perfectly preserved mid-hop."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One stone cow half-blocks the wash entrance, worn smooth by decades of wind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales the exact grey of the gravel it dens in, near invisible at rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blinks slowly and often, like it's conserving the gaze rather than wasting it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint trail of fine grey dust behind wherever it drags its belly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Only hunts at high sun, when the light off the gravel matches its own eyes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gravel around older statues has started to crumble into something like sand — the stone is finally aging."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A statue near the den still has a pulse if you listen close enough — not everyone in that wash is finished turning."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["sunning itself at the mouth of a gravel-choked wash, half-buried statues scattered around its burrow", "watching the wash's edge with eyes that hold the only warm color in that dead grey ground"]},{"name":"Trail-Boss Werewolf","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Cattle-drive boss who hunts differently by moonlight","flavor":"Runs a legitimate cattle drive by daylight and a very different kind of hunt by moonlight, and the two crews never meet each other.","desc":"By day he's the best cattle-drive boss on this stretch of trail, firm and fair with the hands. By moonlight something else takes the reins, and the herd learns to smell the difference in him long before the men do.","traits":{"note": "The herd smells the change in him long before any hand does — cattle bunch up tight whenever he's near after dark.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "In Hybrid Form, the trail-boss makes two Claw attacks. In Humanoid Form, he makes two Longbow attacks."}, {"name": "Wolf's Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. (Wolf or Hybrid Form only). Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be cursed with lycanthropy."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Trail Rifle", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. (Humanoid or Hybrid Form only). Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hired the party as extra hands for the drive, no idea yet what rides along after dark."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One steer keeps breaking from the herd at dusk, and only he seems to know why."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival outfit is trying to poach his crew, unaware of what protects this one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's asked the party to guard the chuck wagon tonight and stay well clear of his tent."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hand quit last week and won't say why; the herd's a hand short at the worst possible time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's trying to time the drive's arrival to skip the next full moon entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cattle that survive a night near him never spook at wolves again — not ever."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's the night his control finally slips mid-drive, with the whole herd stampeding into the dark."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill"],"activity":["running a legitimate cattle drive by daylight, firm and fair with the hands", "testing the wind at dusk, feeling the moon's pull start to take the reins"]},{"name":"Bank Job Crew Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"Meticulous bank-job planner, never caught at the scene","flavor":"Plans the job down to the minute and the getaway better than the job, which is why he's never once been caught at the scene.","desc":"He's cased this bank for three weeks from the boarding house window across the street, timing the guard shifts to the minute. He never draws first — draws smart, at the exact second the plan calls for it, and he's never once been caught at the scene.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The crew boss makes two attacks, using Thrown Iron or Getaway Blade in any combination."}, {"name": "Thrown Iron", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Getaway Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage using two hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's three weeks into casing this bank and one clean shot from pulling the job."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A teller he's bribed for the shift schedule is having second thoughts about the deal."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's presence in town has thrown off his careful timing, and he blames them for it already."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His crew is one man short, and he's quietly scouting the party to fill the gap."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a getaway map that shows a route through property the party owns."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's never drawn first in his life and won't start now, even mid-robbery."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He plans every job around a countdown only he can hear, ticking down to a number he won't explain."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's plan has already gone wrong twice before the party even arrives, and he's still calmly adjusting it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["timing guard shifts to the minute from a boarding-house window across the street", "walking the getaway route backward one more time before committing the crew to the job"]},{"name":"Whiskey-Runner Smuggler Chief","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"Alias-juggling smuggler always ahead of questions","flavor":"Moves contraband liquor and worse across the territory line under a dozen aliases, always one step ahead of whoever's asking questions.","desc":"Nobody's caught him with the same name twice, and the wagons running his liquor never take the same route back to back. He's always a step ahead of whoever's asking questions, mostly because he never stops asking his own first.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chief makes two Contraband Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Contraband Blade", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 7 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage from a blade dipped in cut liquor."}, {"name": "Muzzle Flash", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. Each creature within 15 feet of the chief makes a DC 13 Constitution save, becoming Blinded until the end of its next turn on a failure as a hidden flash-cartridge ignites."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The chief casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components: At will: minor illusion, disguise self. 2/day each: invisibility, misty step."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-negotiation over a wagonload the party's employer wants intercepted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival runner just undercut his route and he wants the party to deal with the competition quietly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of his aliases has caught up with him, and a marshal from that identity is closing in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party safe passage through territory lines in exchange for one delivery."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His usual route just got blocked by something worse than the law, and he needs an escort."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He keeps a ledger of every alias he's ever used, and one entry matches a name the party knows."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He never sleeps in the same face twice, changing his features as easily as his name."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every alias he's ever burned is catching up to him at once, tonight, in the same town."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "urban", "grassland"],"activity":["counting contraband crates by lantern-light under a false name nobody's caught twice", "rerouting the wagon train off its usual path before anyone can learn the pattern"]},{"name":"Prospector's Undying Mule","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"Overworked mule-skeleton still hauling a dead claim's ore","flavor":"Died of overwork hauling ore for a claim that never paid out, and kept walking the same switchback trail long after the flesh gave out.","desc":"Bones show through hide gone thin as paper, and it's still hauling a rusted ore-cart harness up the same grade it died climbing, hooves striking sparks off stone that doesn't need striking anymore. The claim it served is long dry. It hasn't been told.","traits":{"note": "The claim it served ran dry a generation ago; the mule has never been told and never will stop climbing.", "actions": [{"name": "Dead Kick", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still drags a snapped lead-rope, tangled and dragging thirty feet behind it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ore-cart harness is empty, but it strains against the weight anyway."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Climbs the same switchback in the same number of steps, every single time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sparks off its hooves catch dry brush more often than most fires start naturally."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Brays without sound — jaw working, no noise ever comes out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Stops dead if anyone actually pays out the wages the dead claim owed it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cart it hauls is heavier some nights than others, though it's always been empty."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If it ever reaches the top of the grade, the whole dead mine face gives way behind it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["mountain", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["hauling a rusted ore-cart harness up the same dead-claim switchback it died climbing", "striking sparks off stone with bare hoof-bone that doesn't need striking anymore"]},{"name":"Ridge-Line Sniper","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"Patient half-mile ridge sniper who waits days for one shot","flavor":"Picks a ridge a half-mile out and waits, sometimes for days, for one clean shot that ends whatever argument brought him there.","desc":"He's been lying on the same ridge for two days, canteen rationed, rifle sighted on the one spot in the pass where a target has to slow down. He doesn't fire until he's sure — and he's willing to wait days to be sure.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sniper makes two attacks, using Belt Knife or Long Rifle in any combination."}, {"name": "Belt Knife", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Long Rifle", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage. If the sniper hasn't moved since the start of its last turn, this attack has Advantage."}, {"name": "One Clean Shot", "text": "If the sniper hits a creature with Long Rifle while that creature is unaware of it, the attack deals an extra 10 (3d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been paid to end an argument between two families, and one of them just hired the party."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His canteen's nearly dry, and thirst is finally cracking his legendary patience."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's watching the exact pass the party needs to cross, rifle already sighted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A second shooter is working the same ridge, and neither knows about the other yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's waiting on a target who never shows — the party might be mistaken for the mark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's turned down three payouts this month because none of the marks felt like a clean shot yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He never misses the first shot he takes in a week, and never explains why he waits so long for it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally found the shot he's waited days for, and it isn't the target everyone assumed."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["mountain", "hill"],"activity":["lying flat on a ridge two days running, canteen rationed, rifle sighted on the one choke point below", "waiting for the exact moment a target has to slow down before committing to the shot"]},{"name":"Corral-Breaker Bull","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"hippopotamus","model":"hippopotamus","summary":"Fence-breaking mean bull that gores on principle","flavor":"A range bull too mean for any fence, gores riders on principle and has flattened three homestead corrals trying to get at nothing in particular.","desc":"Scarred across both shoulders from splintering through fence rail after fence rail, this bull doesn't seem to need a reason anymore — the breaking's become the point. It paws dust into the air, snorts, and puts its head down at the nearest thing standing.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bull makes two Gore attacks."}, {"name": "Gore", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Fence-Breaker Charge", "text": "If the bull moves at least 15 feet straight toward a creature or an object before a Gore attack, that attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) Piercing damage, and any wooden barrier it strikes instead of a creature is destroyed automatically."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred across both shoulders from splintering through fence rail after fence rail."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has flattened three homestead corrals this season alone, always at night."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges anything wearing red, fence or no fence in the way."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One horn's been broken clean off, and it charges crooked because of it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores open gates entirely, seems to prefer breaking through closed ones."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calms instantly around one particular rancher, mean as ever toward everyone else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dust it kicks up hangs in the air far longer than it should, forming almost a shape."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Rams anything standing between it and open horizon, fence, wagon, or person alike, without slowing."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland"],"activity":["pawing dust into the air outside a splintered corral fence, snorting at nothing in particular", "putting its head down at the nearest standing thing, fence rail or not"]},{"name":"Blood-Money Bounty Hunter","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"Bounty hunter who only ever delivers corpses","flavor":"Doesn't care if the poster says dead or alive, only cares which is cheaper to transport. Has never once brought a man back breathing.","desc":"He rides in with a wagon already outfitted for the corpse, no interest in the paperwork about bringing anyone back alive. Dead or alive was always just the polite version of the only option he's ever chosen.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bounty hunter makes two attacks, using Cold Scimitar or Belt Pistol in any combination."}, {"name": "Cold Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Belt Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cheaper Dead", "text": "Against a creature below half its hit point maximum, the bounty hunter's attacks score a Critical Hit on a roll of 19 or 20."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hunting someone the party is protecting, wagon already outfitted for the ride back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's misread a poster and has the wrong person in his sights entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival hunter is racing him to the same mark, and he doesn't intend to share."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The bounty on his current mark just doubled if delivered dead, and he's noticed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party a cut if they point him toward his mark first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's never once brought a man back breathing, and a marshal's finally started asking why."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His wagon smells of embalming salt no matter how recently it's been cleaned."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The mark he's chasing tonight turns out to be already dead, walking, and very unhappy about the wagon."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["riding in with a wagon already outfitted for a corpse, no interest in the paperwork about bringing anyone back alive", "checking a wanted poster once, then never again, decision already made"]},{"name":"Ghost-Town Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Ghost-town spirit still setting up for gone customers","flavor":"The town emptied out around it decades ago and it's still rearranging the saloon furniture for customers who left generations back.","desc":"Doors that shouldn't have hinges left creak open and shut on their own, and a bar rag still wipes down a counter that hasn't held a drink in decades. It's still setting up for customers who left this town, or this world, a long time ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The poltergeist makes two Barstool Slam attacks, or one Barstool Slam and uses Throw the Furniture."}, {"name": "Barstool Slam", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. (using a hurled piece of saloon furniture). Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Throw the Furniture", "replaces": "Telekinetic Thrust", "text": "One creature within 30 feet makes a DC 12 Strength save. On a failure, it is pushed 15 feet in a direction of the poltergeist's choice and knocked Prone, sent tumbling by chairs and tables set for customers who never showed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's set a full table for four and gets violent when the chairs stay empty too long."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the saloon's old till, still convinced there's a night's take inside."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes the party for regulars and expects them to order something specific, by name."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A traveling family has moved into the ghost town, unaware the saloon still has a tenant."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rearranged the same three chairs every night for years, and moving them enrages it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It calms the instant someone actually orders a drink and waits for it politely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The bar rag it uses is wiping down a wet ring that keeps reappearing on dry wood."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every piece of furniture in the saloon lifts at once when it's finally provoked past patience."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["wiping down a saloon counter that hasn't held a drink in decades", "swinging doors open and shut on hinges that rusted through generations ago"]},{"name":"Devil's Canyon Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Coyote-buzzard-rattler chimera denning an unspoken canyon","flavor":"A stitched-together horror of coyote, buzzard, and rattler that dens in a canyon locals have stopped naming out loud.","desc":"Coyote head snarling low, buzzard head watching the sky, rattlesnake tail lashing the dust — it's denned a canyon nobody names out loud anymore, and every part of it hunts on its own schedule, which is the worst part of fighting it.","traits":{"note": "Its three heads act independently — expect an attack from an angle nothing else in the fight is watching.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chimera makes three attacks: one Coyote Bite, one Buzzard Claw, and one Rattler Ram. It can use Canyon Fire in place of its Coyote Bite."}, {"name": "Coyote Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Buzzard Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rattler Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage from the tail's rattling fangs."}, {"name": "Canyon Fire", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The chimera exhales fire in a 15-ft. cone. Each creature there makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 24 (7d6) Fire damage on a failure, half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The buzzard head never stops watching the sky, even mid-fight, mid-bite."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rattler tail has its own venom sac, distinct from either head's temperament."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coyote and buzzard heads argue in half-sounds before agreeing on a target."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dens in a canyon with three separate entrances, one per temperament."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags carrion back for the buzzard head specifically, ignoring the other two's preferences."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One head sleeps while the other two hunt, rotating on some private schedule."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The three heads occasionally speak in one voice, briefly, before fracturing back apart."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If one head is destroyed, the other two turn on each other before ever facing an outside threat again."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["hill", "cave", "desert"],"activity":["denning a canyon locals have stopped naming out loud, three heads working three separate schedules", "coyote head snarling low while the buzzard head tracks something circling far overhead"]},{"name":"Six-Gun Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Face-stealer that cashes in a gunfighter's old grudges","flavor":"Steals a gunfighter's face and reputation both, then cashes in every grudge that reputation was owed before anyone spots the switch.","desc":"It's wearing a dead gunfighter's face and a dead gunfighter's grudges, walking into towns to settle scores that belonged to somebody else entirely. It cashes them in exactly like the genuine article would, right down to the terrible aim it never actually had to have.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The doppel makes two Borrowed Iron attacks."}, {"name": "Borrowed Iron", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, dealt with the pistol-butt of a gun it doesn't actually know how to fire."}, {"name": "Read the Grudge", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The doppel reads a creature's surface thoughts within 60 feet for 1 minute — enough to learn who they'd trust a dead gunfighter's face to approach."}, {"name": "Dead Man's Stare", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 30 feet that can see the doppel makes a DC 12 Wisdom save, becoming Frightened until the end of its next turn on a failure as the borrowed face settles into something colder."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's collecting on a grudge owed to a gunfighter who's been dead for years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real gunfighter's family doesn't know he's dead, and it's walking straight toward them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's picked a grudge involving someone the party has already met."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival gunhand has noticed the borrowed face is off, just slightly, and is asking around."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's about to settle a score in a saloon full of witnesses who'll swear to the wrong man's guilt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's run out of new grudges to cash and is inventing debts the dead man never actually held."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flinches at gunfire the way the real gunfighter never did — some memory it can't quite wear right."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The dead gunfighter's actual killer has just walked into the same room, and the doppel doesn't recognize him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["walking into town wearing a dead gunfighter's face, settling scores that belonged to somebody else", "cashing in an old grudge with a terrible aim it never actually had to earn"]},{"name":"Cursed Silver Vein Xorn","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"xorn","model":"xorn","summary":"Ore-eating burrower that ruins or blesses a mining claim","flavor":"Burrows through rock eating the ore veins miners are chasing, which makes it either the luckiest strike or the worst omen a claim can hit.","desc":"It surfaces out of solid rock like the stone itself is exhaling, jaws already working on a mouthful of ore. Whatever claim it's tunneled through comes out either richer or ruined — nobody's found the rule that decides which.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The xorn makes one Ore Bite attack and one Grasping Claw attack."}, {"name": "Ore Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is wearing or carrying metal armor or a metal weapon, the xorn can choose to deal this damage to the item's hit points instead."}, {"name": "Grasping Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tunneled straight through a claim the party's been hired to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A miner swears the vein it ate ran richer after the tunnel than before."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's surfaced beneath a working mine shaft, unaware of the men still below."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prospector wants it captured alive, convinced its tunnels lead somewhere worth following."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's eaten through a support beam, and the shaft above is one bad step from collapse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only tunnels toward silver, ignoring gold and iron veins entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every claim it's ruined has gone on to strike something bigger a season later, elsewhere on the same land."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's eaten so deep into the mountain that the whole ridge above the claim is starting to settle."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["mountain", "cave", "hill"],"activity":["surfacing out of solid rock like the stone itself is exhaling, jaws already working on a mouthful of ore", "tunneling through a working claim, leaving it richer or ruined with no pattern anyone's found"]},{"name":"Company Iron Enforcer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"Faceless boiler-plate construct enforcing company disputes","flavor":"A boiler-plate strikebreaker the railroad company keeps for disputes it doesn't want a human face attached to.","desc":"No face behind the boiler-plate visor, just a dark slot where eyes should track you, and it moves with the flat, unbothered gait of something sent to settle a dispute the company already considers settled.","traits":{"note": "It carries no company insignia — deniability is the entire point of sending it instead of a man.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The enforcer makes two Company Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Company Blade", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage, dealt with a blade that hums faintly with contracted force."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boiler-plate scorched black on one side from a dispute that went poorly for someone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in perfect step with a second enforcer, always exactly ten paces behind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a folded company contract in its off hand, never once reads it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops dead if shown a signed and countersigned company voucher."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The visor-slot flickers with a faint company insignia when it's about to attack."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Never acts against anyone still holding company stock, no matter the dispute."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The boiler-plate is dented in the exact shape of a man's fist, from the inside."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its orders are self-updating — it seems to already know disputes that haven't been filed yet."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing motionless outside the company office, dark visor-slot tracking without eyes", "moving with a flat, unbothered gait toward a dispute the company already considers settled"]},{"name":"Sand-Ghast Cattle King","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Herd-starving cattle baron risen hungrier than his own stock","flavor":"Starved his own herd to sell the feed money elsewhere, and rose still hungrier than the cattle he killed.","desc":"He rose from his own family plot hungrier than the herd he starved to build his fortune, hide gone the color of the alkali dust he's buried in. He still counts cattle by instinct, only now the counting includes anything that walks on two legs.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ledger Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Poisoned until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Branding Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's still counting a herd that's been dead for years, and the tally never comes out right."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A buyer he swindled in life is asking questions at the spread, unaware who's still running it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cattle keep turning up drained on the ranch he still claims, blamed on wolves nobody's seen."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His heir is trying to sell the spread, and the King has other plans for the paperwork."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's added the party to his count without asking, and counts don't come off his ledger easily."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He still pays hands in coin they can't spend, insisting the spread runs honest."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dust he's buried in follows him a few steps behind wherever he walks the fence line."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided the count is short by exactly the number of people standing in front of him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "grassland"],"activity":["counting cattle by old instinct at the edge of his own family plot, hide the color of alkali dust", "eyeing anything that walks on two legs the same hungry way he once eyed his own starved herd"]},{"name":"Faro Table Devil","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Card-table devil trading winning streaks for souls","flavor":"Sits every faro table in a three-town circuit, offers a winning streak for a soul-sized marker, and always collects.","desc":"He deals a fair game, technically, red suit sharp under the lamp light, and every hand he wins buys a little more of whatever the loser can't afford to lose. Winning streaks are his specialty — the terms just never get read carefully enough.","traits":{"note": "He never cheats the cards — the terms of what a win costs are where he collects.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The devil makes two Marked Claw attacks, or uses Fire Ray twice."}, {"name": "Marked Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Fire Ray", "replaces": "Fire Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 90 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The devil casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components: At will: charm person, disguise self. 2/day each: suggestion, mirror image."}, {"name": "The House's Marker", "text": "When a creature loses a wager against the devil (in game or at cards), the devil can mark them without a roll: the target's next saving throw against the devil's spells or effects is made with Disadvantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party a hand at the table, and the terms are conveniently never quite specific."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate winner just took a streak that's about to cost far more than his stake."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a marker signed by someone the party's trying to help, and won't discuss forgiveness."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival gambler is trying to expose his game before he collects his next marker."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just moved to a new table in a three-town circuit, and word hasn't caught up to him yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He always loses the first hand of the night, on purpose, to earn the room's trust."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every marker he's ever collected is written in a hand that isn't quite his own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's about to deal a hand where the stake is a soul the party didn't realize was on the table."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["dealing a technically fair hand under lamp light, red suit sharp, watching a mark's luck run hot", "offering one more winning streak to a loser who can't afford to walk away yet"]},{"name":"Rattlesnake Nest Colossus","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Rock-pile rattlesnake mass that moves as one animal","flavor":"So many rattlers denned in the same rock pile over so many years that the pile itself started moving as one animal.","desc":"What looks like a shifting rock pile at the canyon's base is actually thousands of rattlers knotted into one moving mass, scales clattering like dry gourds with every collective lurch forward. It doesn't slither so much as avalanche.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The colossus makes three Nest Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Nest Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Rockslide Coil", "text": "The colossus can occupy the same space as up to two Large or smaller creatures. Each creature it shares space with makes a DC 15 Strength save at the start of the colossus's turn, taking 14 (4d6) Bludgeoning damage and becoming Restrained until the start of its next turn on a failure, or half damage and no restraint on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than it should, thousands of small bodies fighting their own direction."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One patch near its center is duller, older scales — the original nest, still buried inside."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a wide smooth track in the dust, wider than any single snake could carve."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rattles as one continuous roar rather than distinct individual warnings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shrinks noticeably when threatened, snakes peeling off to flee individually."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Reforms overnight from stragglers if not thoroughly scattered and killed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally holds a shape for a moment too long — briefly almost humanoid before collapsing back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When finally broken apart, the individual rattlers scatter in every direction, still venomous, still hunting."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "hill", "cave"],"activity":["shifting at the canyon's base like a rock pile that shouldn't be moving", "avalanching forward in a single collective lurch, scales clattering like dry gourds"]},{"name":"Frontier Vampire Rancher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Undead rancher whose herd thins one drained cow at a time","flavor":"Runs the biggest spread in the territory and never once been seen buying cattle, only losing them, one thin cow at a time.","desc":"He runs the tidiest spread in the territory, and his cattle look healthier every season somehow — except for the one or two that turn up drained and cold each week, which he blames on wolves and nobody's ever pressed the point.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The rancher makes two attacks, using Branding Claw or Drover's Bite in any combination."}, {"name": "Branding Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Drover's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the rancher regains hit points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt. This trait works the same on cattle as it does on people, which is exactly the problem."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hired the party to find out who's been draining his cattle, unaware they'll find him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hand has finally noticed the pattern and is asking questions he doesn't want asked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's expanding the spread onto land the party has an interest in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighboring rancher is losing stock to blame that's landing on him unfairly, for once."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's invited the party to dinner at the ranch house, and the meat is fresher than it should be."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He genuinely loves the cattle, cares for the herd better than any living rancher in the territory."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The healthiest cows in his herd are the ones fed on personally, night after night, and they don't seem to mind."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's run out of cattle to spare this season, and the count he needs to make up is starting to include names."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["walking the tidiest spread in the territory at dusk, cattle looking healthier every season somehow", "counting the herd and quietly deciding which one or two won't be missed by morning"]},{"name":"Broken Treaty Warband Leader","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"Warband leader avenging a torn-up land treaty","flavor":"Leads a mixed band of the wronged and the desperate against whoever tore up the last agreement, and doesn't much care whose fault it originally was.","desc":"He carries a torn half of a treaty document folded flat against his chest, and every raid he leads is aimed at the exact families and companies who signed the other half and broke it. He remembers every clause.","traits":{"note": "He remembers every clause of the broken treaty by heart and can recite the exact families who signed against it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The leader makes two attacks, using Treaty-Breaker Axe or Signal Javelin in any combination."}, {"name": "Treaty-Breaker Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d12 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Signal Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rally the Wronged", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The leader shouts a grievance that lands. Each ally within 30 feet that can hear him gains 10 Temporary Hit Points and can immediately move up to half its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's leading a raid against a company outpost run by descendants of the treaty's original signers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's employer is named, in ink, on the half-treaty he still carries."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faction within his own warband wants to negotiate instead of raid, and he's holding the line against it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's captured a company clerk who might actually be able to make the broken treaty right."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of his own fighters has started raiding families who weren't part of the original wrong."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'd stop the whole campaign for one honest signature undoing the original betrayal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The torn treaty half occasionally shows new text that wasn't there on his last reading."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's found the other half of the treaty at last, and reading both halves together changes his mind about everything."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["leading a mixed band of the wronged and desperate toward whoever tore up the last agreement", "reading a torn half-treaty folded flat against his chest before every raid, checking the names again"]},{"name":"Devil-Wind Salamander","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"salamander","model":"salamander","summary":"Heat-mirage serpent that strikes at high noon","flavor":"A living heat-mirage with a serpent's temper that curls up out of the noon shimmer to strike anything foolish enough to travel at that hour.","desc":"It rides the shimmer of high-noon heat mirage, scaled body the color of baked clay, invisible until it's already close enough to strike. Riders learn to distrust every wavering horizon line after meeting one of these.","traits":{"note": "It only strikes from shimmer — step out of the noon glare and it loses the trick.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The salamander makes two attacks: one with its Flame Spear and one with its Constrict."}, {"name": "Flame Spear", "replaces": "Flame Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage as the heat-mirage flesh sears on contact."}, {"name": "Mirage Coil", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15). While grappled this way, the target is blinded by shimmering heat-haze and has disadvantage on attack rolls."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales run pale clay instead of red, near-invisible against alkali flats."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint smell of scorched creosote wherever it's passed recently."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a fixed loop between two washes, same hours every day."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger and smaller, strikes fast but breaks off the fight quicker."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries old arrowheads embedded harmlessly in its heat-toughened hide."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Goes fully invisible at high noon, only a heat-ripple giving its position away."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed skin keeps radiating heat for days, cooking anything left too near it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Dying, it flash-boils, venting a superheated burst that ignites dry brush in a ring around the corpse."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "grassland"],"activity":["riding the noon heat-shimmer over a dry wash, waiting for a shadow to cross it", "coiled flat against baked clay, scales matching the ground so exactly it reads as mirage"]},{"name":"Wanted-Dead Wraith Duo","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Hanged outlaw brothers who ambush in tandem","flavor":"Two outlaw brothers hanged from the same tree, now inseparable in death as they were in the job, finishing each other's ambushes.","desc":"They were brothers, hanged from the same crossbeam on the same rope, and now they hunt in the tandem they learned in life — one drawing attention while the other closes from behind, translucent and cold as the noose that killed them.","traits":{"note": "They never split up willingly — killing one drops the other's coordination hard.", "actions": [{"name": "Cold Ambush Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage. If the other brother has attacked this same target since the target's last turn, the target also has its hit point maximum reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Raise the Rope-Kin", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "A Humanoid slain by either brother's Cold Ambush Drain rises after 1 minute as a Specter under the duo's shared command, bound to finish whatever ambush they started."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're re-running the exact ambush that killed a posse rider, and mistake the party for that posse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One brother carries the other's stolen watch and won't stop trying to return it to a house long since burned."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've cornered a lone prospector against the same tree they were hanged from and won't let him go."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living relative rides with the party, unknowing kin the brothers refuse to hurt but won't release either."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're arguing, mid-haunt, over which of them the noose actually belonged to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cutting the original hanging rope down anywhere in the territory pulls both of them there at once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Separated by more than a mile, one brother goes translucent and desperate, unraveling toward nothing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If both die in the same round, the noose-mark scars into the killer's own neck, cold and permanent."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["one brother drawing a rider's eye at the treeline while the other drifts up from behind", "circling the same crossbeam they were hanged from, waiting for a lone traveler"]},{"name":"Iron Horse Runaway Engine","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"rlm-iron-horse-runaway-engine","summary":"Rail-broken locomotive now running the open desert on legs","flavor":"Broke from its rail line entirely and now runs the open desert on legs it built for itself, chasing whatever startled it in the first place.","desc":"Its rails ran out somewhere behind it and it kept going anyway, driver wheels reforged into strider legs, still building steam pressure it no longer has track to spend. It crosses open desert now on a schedule that doesn't exist anymore.","traits":{"note": "It still runs a phantom timetable — the DM can use its next 'stop' as a countdown the party overhears in its whistle.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The engine makes two Piston Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Piston Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and a Large or smaller target is pushed 10 feet away and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One strider leg drags a bent driver-rod, leaving a scored line in the dirt behind it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its whistle still works and it blows it, mournfully, before every charge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coated in a decade of rust; chunks of boiler plate flake off with every stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still hauls two burnt-out freight cars behind it on makeshift skid-rails."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs a fixed loop between two washed-out rail stubs, same route every day."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Slows and idles near any standing water, mistaking it for a tank stop."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its boiler gauge reads a destination name no map in the territory has ever listed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past half health, its overpressured boiler starts a visible countdown hiss toward a catastrophic vent."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["chugging across open flat on reforged strider legs, building pressure it has nowhere to spend", "stopped dead at an old water tower, venting steam like it's still waiting on a schedule"]},{"name":"Buzzard-Winged Peryton","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"peryton","model":"peryton","summary":"Antlered vulture-thing casting its next victim's shadow","flavor":"A vulture-antlered horror that circles a claim jumper's grave and casts the shadow of the man it's about to kill.","desc":"Antlered like a stag, winged like a vulture, it circles high and quiet, and the shadow it casts falls wrong — not where its body is, but where its next kill will be standing. People have learned to watch their own shadow when one of these is overhead.","traits":{"note": "Anyone who checks their own shadow against the peryton's flight path gets one clean warning before it strikes.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The peryton makes two attacks: one with its Gore and one with its Talons."}, {"name": "Shadow-Marked Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target's cast shadow currently shows the peryton's kill-silhouette (see Cast the Shadow), this attack instead deals 10 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the peryton can fly up to half its speed without provoking an opportunity attack from the target."}, {"name": "Cast the Shadow", "text": "At the start of combat, the peryton marks one creature it can see: that creature's shadow briefly shows the peryton's own antlered outline superimposed over it. This is purely a warning sign — until the mark fades at the end of the peryton's next turn, its Shadow-Marked Gore against that creature deals bonus damage as above."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Antlers are broken to a single tine, giving it a lopsided, less accurate gore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Molts vulture feathers constantly; a trail of black down marks everywhere it's circled."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fixates on one claim only, ignoring anyone who doesn't cross its boundary stakes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger bird, antlers still velvet-soft, shadow-mark lands a beat later than usual."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a dead man's boot in its talons, dropped and re-snatched compulsively."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Marks the shadow of whoever spoke last, not whoever looks most threatening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its own shadow, cast on the ground, shows a different, older claim marker than the one it circles."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed while a mark is active, its death-shriek transfers the mark instantly to the nearest other creature."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "hill", "sky"],"activity":["circling high and silent over a fresh claim marker, casting a shadow that doesn't match its wingspan", "perched on a dead cottonwood, watching a target's shadow rather than the target"]},{"name":"Cattle-Baron's Gorgon Bull","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gorgon","summary":"Forged iron bull breathing petrifying dust on trespassers","flavor":"An iron-plated stud bull the baron had forged rather than bred, breathes petrifying dust on anyone who questions the brand.","desc":"Forged iron plates over a bull's silhouette, joints hissing steam instead of breath, it snorts a fine grey dust that turns whatever it touches to stone. The baron had it built to guard fence lines. It's since developed opinions about trespassers.","traits":{"note": "The baron's brand is welded into its shoulder plate — destroying it doesn't hurt the bull, but it does void whoever's claiming ownership.", "actions": [{"name": "Fence-Line Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target moved toward the bull this turn, it is also pushed 10 feet away."}, {"name": "Petrifying Dust", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The bull snorts a fine grey dust in a 30-foot cone. Each creature there makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failure, a creature is Restrained and begins turning to stone, repeating the save at the end of its next turn (success ends the effect; second failure means it is Petrified). On a success, the creature takes 7 (2d6) Poison damage instead."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One iron plate is missing, showing rope-bound cattle bone beneath the forge-work."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears an actual cowbell that clangs off-key with every step, betraying its position."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols exactly the fence line it was built for and never crosses onto open range."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaks steam constantly from a cracked joint, leaving a faint fog trail behind it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger stud bull, plating thinner, breath weaker but still hardens skin instead of full stone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Charges anyone carrying wire cutters on sight, as if it recognizes the tool specifically."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its petrified victims remain standing along the fence line, repurposed as extra posts."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its boiler-heart cracks and releases the dust all at once in a final unaimed 20-foot burst."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["standing guard at a fence line, snorting grey dust at anything that crosses the wire", "grazing on nothing, joints hissing steam, patrolling the same brand-marked boundary all day"]},{"name":"Territorial Marshal Knight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Rare honest federal marshal, rare enough to be a target","flavor":"A federal marshal riding circuit through three territories with a badge that actually means something, which makes him rare enough to be a target.","desc":"He's rare enough to be a rumor — an honest federal marshal in a territory that mostly just has bought ones — armored plate dulled with trail dust, and every crooked interest out here would very much like him gone.","traits":{"note": "His honesty is the danger — every crooked interest in three territories has a standing bounty on him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The marshal makes two attacks, using his Greatsword or Heavy Crossbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Circuit Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 12 (2d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tracking a bounty who's currently hiding among the party and won't take a bribe to look away."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs an escort through hostile ground to deliver a witness alive to the next territory's court."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A corrupt sheriff has put a price on his badge and he knows it, riding anyway."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying evidence that would ruin a land baron, and three separate parties want it destroyed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recruiting deputies for one dangerous ride and is offering real federal pay for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He recognizes a party member's face from an old wanted poster and has to decide whether to act on it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's been shot twice already this month and kept riding both times, refusing to explain how."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's found proof that his own badge was forged decades ago and is deciding, out loud, whether that changes anything he's done."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["riding slow circuit through a boundary town, badge catching the sun, watching who watches him", "checking papers at a crossroads, greatsword sheathed but crossbow never far from his hand"]},{"name":"Salt Flat Mummy King","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Hide-wrapped cattle baron still ruling from beyond death","flavor":"A cattle baron so obsessed with his empire he had himself dried and wrapped in cured hide rather than let death touch his ledgers, and still rules from the flats.","desc":"Wrapped hide to hide in linen gone the color of the salt flat he's buried in, he still holds court from beneath the alkali crust, ruling a herd and a territory that stopped needing a ruler generations ago.","traits":{"note": "His ledgers are legally worthless and he doesn't know it — the herd, the range, and the debts he tracks are all generations gone.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The mummy king makes two Rotting Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Rotting Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack becomes Cursed: it can't regain hit points while the curse lasts, removable only by remove curse or similar magic."}, {"name": "Ledger of the Herd", "replaces": "Channel Negative Energy", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The mummy king reads a debt aloud in a 30-foot radius. Each creature there makes a DC 16 Wisdom save, becoming Frightened for 1 minute on a failure (repeats save at end of each turn)."}, {"name": "Dreadful Glare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "One creature within 60 feet that can see the mummy king's dust-yellowed eyes makes a DC 16 Wisdom save or is Frightened until the end of the mummy king's next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The mummy king casts a spell, using necromantic rites drawn from a rancher's superstition rather than any priesthood."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His linen wrapping is stitched from old brand-registry paper, faded ink still legible in patches."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks only in tallies — heads of cattle, dollars owed, days remaining."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt crust has cracked his lower jaw; his voice comes out doubled, an echo of itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a real, rusted branding iron at his side and uses it as a scepter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His court is empty except for salt-preserved cattle skulls arranged like a jury."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers to forgive a debt in exchange for a favor — the debt is against someone centuries dead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ledger updates itself in real time, writing down the party's names the moment they enter the flat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, the salt crust for a mile around cracks open, and every buried steer bone beneath it rattles upright at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court beneath the alkali crust, ledgers of a dead herd still open before him", "counting cattle that no longer exist, hide-wrapped hands turning brittle pages"]},{"name":"Devil's Bargain Land Baron","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"glabrezu","model":"rlm-devils-bargain-land-baron","summary":"Deal-making fiend buying ranches with cursed fine print","flavor":"Buys up drought-broken ranches for pennies and a signature, and the fine print always costs the seller something worse than money.","desc":"He wears a rancher's duster over something that isn't skin underneath it, and every deed he offers reads generous right up until the fine print, printed too small for honest eyes, closes the trap.","traits":{"note": "Every contract he offers is real and enforceable — the trap is always in fine print an honest reader would need a lawyer to catch.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The baron makes two attacks, using Pincer or Pummel in any combination."}, {"name": "Pincer", "replaces": "Pincer", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 17, two pincers, one grapple each)."}, {"name": "Pummel", "replaces": "Pummel", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. Only usable against a creature the baron is grappling."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The baron casts a spell, its magic always shaped like paperwork — binding words, sealed contracts, and vanished ink."}, {"name": "Read the Fine Print", "text": "Once per day, the baron can offer a binding deal to a willing creature (no save). The immediate benefit is exactly as promised; the cost, buried in wording the creature agreed to, manifests at a time and in a form of the DM's choosing — never simple damage, always a consequence that costs the creature something worse than money."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering to buy out a struggling ranch the party has reason to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate family already signed and wants help breaking the contract before the cost comes due."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recruiting the party as witnesses to a deed transfer that isn't as clean as it looks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a stack of already-signed deeds and is looking for someone to notarize them at gunpoint."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants one specific parcel and is willing to trade real, working magic for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers the party a deal mid-fight — surrender now, sign later, and this ends without more blood."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The duster he wears is stitched from every deed he's ever voided, and it whispers the terms if you get close."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, he offers to void every deal he's ever made in the territory at once, if someone will sign to take his place."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing over a drought-broken ranch with a deed and a fountain pen, waiting on a signature", "walking fence line in a rancher's duster that doesn't sit right over what's underneath"]},{"name":"Company War-Locomotive","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Heavier armored war-locomotive answering a dead order","flavor":"A second, heavier war-machine the rail company built after the first went missing — plated thicker, angrier, and still answering to a dead requisition.","desc":"Heavier-armored than the wreck-golems that came before it, this war-locomotive still answers to a company order nobody's alive to rescind, grinding forward on legs of drive-wheel and boiler plate with an engineer's ghost logic and none of an engineer's mercy.","traits":{"note": "It was built as the answer to the first war-locomotive's disappearance — destroying it just means the company builds a third.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The locomotive makes two attacks: one with its Slam and one with its Force Bolt."}, {"name": "Drive-Wheel Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and a Large or smaller target is knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Requisition Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 120 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Force damage, fired from a company-stamped rail-gun mounted where a smokestack should be."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plate armor still bears a fresh company stamp, unweathered compared to the rest of its frame."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a bent requisition order riveted to its chest, orders no longer legible."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in perfectly straight lines only, as if still bound to a rail no longer there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vents black company-grade smoke that leaves a soot trail for miles."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its whistle plays a company jingle instead of a warning."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Actively hunts anything wearing a rival company's colors before anything else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its boiler gauge reads out payroll numbers instead of pressure, ticking upward toward some invisible quota."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its wreckage transmits one last requisition order by wire — a replacement is already being built."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "desert"],"activity":["grinding forward on drive-wheel legs, still answering a company order nobody's alive to cancel", "parked dead-still at a strike line from decades back, boiler idling like it's still waiting for orders"]},{"name":"Ghost Cavalry Column","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"rlm-ghost-cavalry-column","summary":"Massacred cavalry column still charging on its anniversary","flavor":"Rode into a canyon on bad orders and never rode out, and the column still charges the same canyon mouth every anniversary of the massacre.","desc":"Once a year, on the exact date they were wiped out, the column reforms at full march — dust-pale horses, dust-pale riders, sabers drawn for a charge that already happened and never stopped happening in whatever place ghosts keep their memory.","traits":{"note": "The charge repeats every anniversary whether anyone's there to receive it or not — timing it right lets a party avoid the column entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The column makes two attacks: one with its Dread Blade and one with its Hellfire Orb, or two Dread Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Cavalry Saber", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Massacre Volley", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. A 20-foot line of phantom carbine fire. Each creature in the line makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage on a failure, half on a success."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The column casts a spell as one voice, orders relayed down a chain of command that no longer exists outside memory."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The anniversary charge is tonight, and the party is camped directly in the canyon mouth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A descendant of the officer who gave the bad order wants the column laid to rest before he inherits the guilt."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A surviving rider's diary, if read at the site, might redirect the charge somewhere empty."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's salvaging cavalry-issue rifles off the canyon floor and doesn't know the column resets every year."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living cavalry unit is bivouacked nearby, unaware they're camped on the massacre site."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The column can be reasoned with for exactly one exchange before the charge instinct overrides them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Killing the lead rider only rotates command to the next horse back; the column never actually shrinks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Stopped mid-charge by force, the entire column freezes mid-stride, and something about the canyon itself starts screaming instead."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["reforming at full march in the canyon mouth, sabers drawn for a charge that already happened", "riding dust-pale horses in tight formation, following orders given to men long dead"]},{"name":"Twelve-Gauge Lich of the Vault","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"rlm-twelve-gauge-lich-of-the-vault","summary":"Bank president-lich fused to the vault he'll never lose","flavor":"Bound his own soul to the vault he built rather than let a robbery ever succeed against him, and now the vault and the corpse are the same defended object.","desc":"He fused himself to his own bank's vault door rather than lose it to death, and now he can't leave it — coat gone to dust, hands gone to bone, still counting a fortune that stopped being currency the day he died guarding it.","traits":{"note": "He cannot leave the vault door — luring him more than a short distance from it breaks his power entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The lich makes two Vault-Bone Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Vault-Bone Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Repossession Blast", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 20 feet of the vault door makes a DC 17 Constitution save, taking 27 (6d8) Necrotic damage on a failure, half on a success. Any of the lich's own stolen coin on a failed creature is yanked back into the vault."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The lich casts a spell drawn from a banker's grim arithmetic — wards, appraisals, and interest that compounds in blood."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A descendant wants the vault's real fortune and needs the lich distracted long enough to crack it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival bank has hired the party to confirm the old vault is truly unrobbable before they build next door."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bandits are trying to blast the vault open and don't know what's fused inside it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The lich offers a fair trade: return one stolen coin from his ledger, and he'll answer one honest question."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A town charter, sealed in the vault, is the only proof of who legally owns the land above it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He mistakes any well-dressed visitor for a bank inspector and demands they audit his books before anything else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The vault's fortune, examined closely, is currency from a country that no longer exists on any map."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, the vault door swings open on its own, and every coin inside crumbles to dust the instant it's touched."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["fused to a rotted vault door, bone hands still counting a fortune that stopped being currency long ago", "standing sentinel over a bank's ruined lobby, coat gone to dust, refusing every attempt to move him"]},{"name":"Skinwalker Cavalry Scout","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"rlm-skinwalker-cavalry-scout","summary":"Shapeshifting scout loyal only to the winning side","flavor":"Turned scout for whichever side is winning that season and turned something else entirely out on the picket lines, loyal only to not losing.","desc":"He scouted for whichever side was winning that week, and death hasn't changed the habit — he shifts shape mid-fight to whichever form serves the moment, loyal only to the outcome, never to a uniform.","traits":{"note": "He'll switch sides mid-fight if the tide turns hard enough — his loyalty is to not losing, nothing else.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The scout makes two attacks, using Bite, Scratch, or Longbow in any combination allowed by his current form."}, {"name": "Turncoat Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is below half hit points, the scout adds 4 (1d8) extra damage, sensing which way the fight is turning."}, {"name": "Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Picket-Line Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's scouting the party's camp for whichever faction is paying better this week."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers real intel on an enemy position in exchange for a cut of whatever's won."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A former commanding officer wants him hunted down for switching sides mid-battle once too often."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's currently embedded with a group the party trusts, and hasn't decided yet whether to betray them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a dead rival scout's tags, proof of a kill nobody's confirmed yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll switch to the party's side mid-fight the moment their side is clearly winning — and switch back if that changes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "In hybrid form his shadow shows both silhouettes at once, arguing with each other in outline."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with no side left to bet on, he shifts fully feral and stops distinguishing friend from target entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "grassland", "forest"],"activity":["shifting mid-stride between wolf and rider on the picket line, scouting for whichever side is winning tonight", "loping low through brush in half-hybrid form, bow slung, loyal only to the outcome"]},{"name":"Alkali Reaper Naga","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"spirit-naga","summary":"Lakebed naga speaking with every voice the salt swallowed","flavor":"Coils under the dry lakebeds where a wagon train vanished whole, and speaks with every voice that was ever lost to the salt.","desc":"It surfaces from the dry lakebed in a slow uncoiling of alkali-white scale, and when it speaks, every voice the salt ever swallowed comes out of the same mouth at once, layered and arguing with itself.","traits":{"note": "Every voice it speaks with was a real traveler lost to the salt — listening long enough reveals genuine names and dates.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The naga makes one Bite attack and casts one spell, or uses Necrotic Ray twice."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Poison damage from salt-cured venom."}, {"name": "Chorus Ray", "replaces": "Necrotic Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Necrotic damage, delivered in the overlapping voices of everyone the salt has claimed."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The naga casts a spell, speaking the incantation in a dozen borrowed voices at once."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It speaks in the voice of a party member's missing relative, one of the vanished wagon train's dead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving family wants confirmation their kin's voice is genuinely among the chorus."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers directions to the wagon train's buried cargo, in exchange for carrying one more voice into the chorus."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A treasure hunter is digging the dry lakebed for wagon-train gold, oblivious to what's coiled beneath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's surfaced early because something disturbed the lakebed, and it wants to know what."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will trade one true answer, in a borrowed dead voice, for one true name given in return."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The voices sometimes finish each other's sentences in ways no living chorus could coordinate."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Slain, every voice it carried escapes at once into the air above the lakebed, briefly audible for miles before going silent for good."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "swamp"],"activity":["uncoiling from the dry lakebed, scale flaking white salt, voices arguing out of one mouth", "surfacing at the center of a vanished wagon trail, waiting for someone to ask what happened here"]},{"name":"Boneyard Behir","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Canyon-nesting lightning horror that hates the railroad's noise","flavor":"A canyon-length lightning-scaled horror that nests where the railroad blasted through the wrong mountain, and hasn't forgiven the noise.","desc":"It's nested in a canyon that used to be quiet before the railroad started blasting through it, and every strike of lightning down its long segmented body seems personally aimed at the noise. It hates trains specifically, and it's found people are close enough.","traits":{"note": "It targets the loudest thing in a fight first — gunfire and rail-noise draw its attention before anything else.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The behir makes two attacks: one with its Bite and one with its Constrict."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Blast-Echo Breath", "replaces": "Lightning Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The behir exhales lightning in a 20-foot line, 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 33 (6d10) Lightning damage on a failure, half on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half its scales are scorched black from old blasting-powder charges it survived as a hatchling."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in the exact spot where the canyon was first dynamited open."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores anything on foot entirely, fixating only on wheeled or rail-bound noise."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smaller and younger, its lightning breath crackles but doesn't yet reach full range."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags loosened rail spikes into its den, gnawing them like bones."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Goes berserk at the sound of a train whistle specifically, ignoring cover to reach the source."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Lightning arcs unprompted off its scales whenever blasting powder detonates anywhere nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near enough to buried blasting charges, its death-discharge can set them off in a chain."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["mountain", "cave", "ruins"],"activity":["nesting in a blast-scarred canyon, lightning crackling down its segmented length at the sound of rail noise", "coiled around a stretch of dynamited rock, hunting whatever's loud enough to remind it of the railroad"]},{"name":"Rail Baron's Hydra Freight","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Freight-raised hydra guarding every car with another head","flavor":"Bred from a swamp-hydra egg shipped west by mistake and raised on freight-car livestock; every severed head just means another car to guard.","desc":"Raised in a freight car from an egg nobody remembers loading, it's grown to guard every car of the train with a separate head, snapping independently, so that cutting one loose from the cargo never actually simplifies the fight.","traits":{"note": "Cutting one head down never simplifies anything — it just means one fewer car defended, not one less threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The hydra makes as many Boxcar Bite attacks as it has heads remaining."}, {"name": "Boxcar Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage. Each head attacks independently and can target a different creature."}, {"name": "Cargo Regrowth", "text": "At the start of its turn, for each of the hydra's heads destroyed since its last turn, two new heads grow from empty freight cars unless the stump was seared with fire or acid damage. The hydra gains one Boxcar Bite attack per head beyond its first, to a maximum tied to the number of cars remaining."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One car's head is stunted and slow, easy to spot as the weakest bite."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Heads have taken on the rusted color of the specific car they guard."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores anyone who doesn't approach the freight cars directly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Freight-raised diet shows: heads gnaw on scrap iron between fights, dulling their bite slightly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fewer cars, fewer heads — this one only guards a two-car remnant of the original train."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Prioritizes protecting one specific car above all others, abandoning weaker positions to defend it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "New heads sometimes emerge already wearing a shipping tag, as if freshly manifested cargo."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If every car is destroyed in the same encounter, all remaining heads panic and strike wildly in every direction at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["guarding a stalled freight train, one head snapping out from each car independently", "coiled around a rail siding, heads tracking every approach from a different angle"]},{"name":"Dead Hand Gunfighter Twins","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"rlm-dead-hand-gunfighter-twins","summary":"Twin gunfighter revenants who died misunderstanding each other","flavor":"Killed each other in a misunderstanding neither survived long enough to correct, and now hunt as one four-armed problem for anyone who separates them.","desc":"They died in the same duel, on opposite ends of the same misunderstanding, and now they return together, revenant-pale, still arguing between shots about which of them started it. Neither will stop until the other admits fault.","traits":{"note": "They never agree on who's to blame — goading one to admit fault mid-fight briefly breaks their coordination.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The twins make two attacks, using Bite or Shadow Strike in any combination."}, {"name": "Duelist's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage, and the twins regain hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt."}, {"name": "Shadow Strike", "replaces": "Shadow Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Necrotic damage, delivered from the twins' merged shadow as they blink between each other's positions."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A witness to the original duel could finally settle who drew first — the twins want that testimony badly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're re-staging the duel nightly in the same street, and living residents can't sleep through it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A descendant of one twin wants the feud ended before it curses the family line further."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've mistaken a pair of siblings in the party for themselves and won't stop trying to 'correct' them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One twin's original pistol, if recovered, might let the party finally end the argument on his terms."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Convincing one twin the other was right ends the fight instantly — but only one twin can hear it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Separated more than fifty feet apart, both twins go silent and stop moving until reunited."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If both die in the same instant, the argument transfers whole into the mind of whoever struck the killing blows, audible for a week."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["standing back to back in a dead street, still arguing between shots about who drew first", "circling a lone target as one four-armed problem, revenant-pale and bickering"]},{"name":"Storm-Called Thunderbird","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"rlm-storm-called-thunderbird","summary":"Barn-sized storm raptor summoned by drought-broken faith","flavor":"A sky-god's shape the old range still half-believes in, called down by droughts bad enough to break faith, and it does not come gently.","desc":"It's the size of a barn when its wings spread against the thunderhead it rode in on, summoned — the old-timers say — by seven years of unanswered rain-prayers finally breaking something open in the sky.","traits":{"note": "It only manifests where drought and desperate faith overlap — it can be starved of a fight simply by breaking the drought first.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The thunderbird makes two attacks: one with its Beak and one with its Talons."}, {"name": "Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage, and a Huge or smaller target is Grappled (escape DC 18)."}, {"name": "Rain-Prayer's Wrath", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The thunderbird calls down a lightning strike on a point it can see within 120 feet. Each creature within 15 feet of that point makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 27 (6d8) Lightning damage on a failure, half on a success. The strike also ignites any dry brush at the point."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement is praying it down deliberately, desperate enough to risk the storm to break the drought."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's circling a specific homestead that made the loudest, most sincere rain-prayer in years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its passage is destroying the last standing crop in the county, drought or no drought."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An old range hand claims he knows the exact ritual that first summoned it and can maybe send it back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival settlement wants it driven toward their enemies' fields instead of their own."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will break the drought and leave peacefully if given a genuine, costly sacrifice of the land's abundance."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wherever its shadow falls, the ground briefly remembers what rain felt like, and cracks seal over for a moment."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Driven off without resolution, it doesn't leave — it simply relocates the entire drought to wherever it lands next."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sky", "mountain", "grassland"],"activity":["wheeling under a thunderhead the size of a county, wings blotting out what little sun the drought left", "landing barn-sized on a ridge, called down by seven years of unanswered rain-prayer"]},{"name":"Iron Baron's War-Golem Prime","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"rlm-iron-barons-war-golem-prime","summary":"Triple-engine war-colossus built to end every argument","flavor":"The rail company's final answer to every strike, treaty, and refusal — built from the bones of two failed war-machines and meant to end the argument permanently.","desc":"Three separate boiler engines feed one colossal iron chassis, built by a company man who genuinely believed the right amount of steel could end any dispute permanently. So far, it has.","traits":{"note": "It was built from the wreckage of two failed war-machines that came before it — its plating still bears their scars underneath the new iron.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The golem makes three attacks, using Bladed Arm or Fiery Bolt in any combination."}, {"name": "Bladed Arm", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 10 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Fiery Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 120 ft. Hit: 18 (4d8) Fire damage, launched from a chest-mounted cannon fed by all three boilers at once."}, {"name": "Company's Final Word", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The golem vents caustic boiler-gas in a 30-foot cone. Each creature there makes a DC 18 Constitution save, taking 31 (7d8) Poison damage on a failure, half on a success and Poisoned for 1 minute regardless."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's marching to break a strike, and the workers who hired the party have nowhere left to retreat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The company engineer who built it wants it stopped before its next order gets logged as a company victory."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a signed treaty the company intends to enforce with its bladed arm instead of ink."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A saboteur has a plan to reach its central boiler, but needs a distraction big enough to matter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been ordered to raze a specific claim, and the deed holder is offering everything they have to stop it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its requisition orders are void if the company that issued them collapses first — a paper trail might work faster than a blade."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Beneath its new plating, the two failed war-machines it was built from still occasionally twitch out of sync with its own movements."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its triple boilers detonate in sequence, and the company's next requisition for its replacement is already signed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "grassland"],"activity":["standing at the center of a strike line, three boiler-engines idling, built to end the argument permanently", "grinding forward through a burned settlement, bladed arm still keeping count of refusals answered"]},{"name":"Nightbringer of the Long Drive","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rlm-nightbringer-of-the-long-drive","summary":"Cattle-drive foreman-fiend who never cared how many died","flavor":"Ran drives so hard the cattle died and so did half the hands, and something noticed how little he cared and made a deal permanent.","desc":"He drove more cattle, and lost more hands, than any foreman on record, and death hasn't slowed the pace — he still pushes a drive forward at a rate that costs lives and doesn't care whose.","traits":{"note": "Something noticed how little he cared about the deaths on his drives and made the arrangement permanent — he answers to that bargain now, not to any living company.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The nightbringer makes two Cursed Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Cursed Touch", "replaces": "Cursed Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the target's speed is halved until the end of its next turn, driven forward like drag-line cattle."}, {"name": "Push the Drive", "replaces": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 30 feet makes a DC 18 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature is forcibly moved up to 20 feet in a direction of the nightbringer's choice and takes 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage; on a success it takes half damage and isn't moved."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The nightbringer casts a spell, its magic the same cold, driving indifference he ran cattle drives with in life."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's re-running his fatal drive route, and the party's camp sits directly in the herd's path."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A surviving hand from the original drive wants to finally confront him about the deaths he caused."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recruiting living drovers for a drive that will absolutely kill them, and doesn't see why that matters."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Descendants of the dead hands want his ghost herd scattered so their kin can finally rest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's pushing the drive through a living settlement's grazing land, indifferent to the damage."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll spare anyone who proves they can push a herd harder and colder than he does — a genuinely dangerous bargain to win."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ghost cattle he drives sometimes wear the faces of the hands who died pushing them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-drive, the herd scatters loose across the territory, and every ghost steer becomes its own small danger."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "desert"],"activity":["pushing a ghost herd forward at a killing pace, not caring how many hands or cattle it costs", "riding the drag position of a drive that ended lives generations ago, still shouting men forward"]},{"name":"Crossroads Contract Devil","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"rlm-crossroads-contract-devil","summary":"Crossroads fiend trading technically-honest desperate deals","flavor":"Waits at the loneliest crossroads in the territory for whoever's desperate enough to trade, and the contract terms are always technically honest.","desc":"He waits where two dirt roads cross under a leaning signpost, offering deals that are, if you read them exactly as worded, completely honest — and completely designed to be misread by anyone desperate enough to sign at a crossroads.","traits":{"note": "Every word of his contracts is technically true — the trap is entirely in what a desperate reader assumes rather than reads.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The devil makes two attacks, using Withering Sword or Entangling Rope in any combination."}, {"name": "Withering Sword", "replaces": "Withering Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Signing Rope", "replaces": "Entangling Rope (Requires Magic Rope)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 30 ft. Hit: the target is bound by a rope of contract-ink; it is Restrained (escape DC 17) until the rope is cut (AC 12, 15 hit points) or the devil chooses to release it."}, {"name": "Read the Terms", "text": "Once per encounter, the devil can offer a bound creature its freedom in exchange for a bargain (no save; the creature must be willing to hear the terms). The immediate release is genuine and immediate; the cost is real, worded exactly as stated, and always worse in practice than the desperate party assumed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate rancher already signed and wants help reading exactly what the contract actually says."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party a genuinely useful deal, and every word of it checks out on close reading."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A lawyer in the nearest town has spent years trying to find the loophole in one of his contracts and hasn't."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's waiting specifically for someone traveling with the party, having marked them from a prior desperate night."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a specific signature witnessed at the crossroads and will pay well for it, no strings on the witness."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll negotiate the actual terms if pressed hard enough — he's bound to the letter, not the spirit, of fair dealing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The signpost casts four shadows at once, one for each road, and each shadow points to a different fine-print clause."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Forced to void a contract, the cost redistributes instantly onto whoever forced the void, worded just as fairly as before."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "planar"],"activity":["waiting under a leaning signpost at the loneliest crossroads in the territory, contract already drawn up", "reading fine print aloud to no one, practicing the exact honest wording of his next deal"]},{"name":"The Undertaker Who Never Sleeps","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"rlm-the-undertaker-who-never-sleeps","summary":"Ledger-keeping undertaker who digs graves ahead of schedule","flavor":"Buried the whole territory twice over and kept a record of every name, and now digs graves ahead of schedule for names not yet in his book.","desc":"His shovel never stops, and the grave he's currently digging is always, somehow, exactly deep enough for whoever's about to need it. He's polite about it. He's just never once been wrong about the timing.","traits":{"note": "He has never once been wrong about the depth or the timing of a grave — that certainty is the real horror, not his blade.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The undertaker makes two Rotting Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Rotting Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (3d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack is Cursed and cannot be raised by anything short of a Wish."}, {"name": "Reserved Plot", "replaces": "Channel Negative Energy", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The undertaker names one creature he can see. That creature and each creature within 15 feet of it makes a DC 18 Wisdom save, taking 32 (7d8) Necrotic damage on a failure, half on a success."}, {"name": "Dreadful Glare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "One creature within 60 feet that meets his patient stare makes a DC 18 Wisdom save or is Frightened until the end of his next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The undertaker casts a spell, its shape always some small mercy of burial rites twisted to serve his schedule instead."}, {"name": "The Grave Is Already Dug", "text": "At the start of combat, the undertaker names one creature present. A grave, exactly deep enough for that creature, appears somewhere within 30 feet — purely a marker, no mechanical effect on its own, but the named creature knows, without being told how, that he was already right."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already dug a grave with a party member's name carved on the marker, dated for tonight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving widow wants to know if her husband's name is in his ledger yet, dreading either answer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's digging ahead of a plague no one else has diagnosed yet, and the graves are the first real warning."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a fair trade: one true name for one true answer about who's next."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival gravedigger is trying to poach his territory, unaware what they're actually competing with."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll skip a name in his ledger for a price steep enough that it always costs someone else instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shovel keeps digging on its own even when he's standing still, unbothered, elsewhere in conversation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every grave he's ever dug across the territory opens at once the night his ledger is finally closed for good."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["digging a grave exactly deep enough for someone not yet dead, polite about the timing", "walking the boneyard with his ledger, adding a name that hasn't been spoken aloud yet"]},{"name":"The Company That Owns The Land","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"nalfeshnee","model":"rlm-the-company-that-owns-the-land","summary":"Boardroom fiend embodying every stolen claim in the territory","flavor":"No single face runs it and no single bullet stops it — it is every unfair contract and stolen claim in the territory given appetite and a seat at the table.","desc":"It doesn't have a face so much as a boardroom's worth of faces layered into one shifting silhouette of pinstripe and paper, and every acre it's ever swindled off a homesteader is folded somewhere into the shape of it.","traits":{"note": "No single bullet or blade stops it permanently — it is every unfair contract in the territory, and contracts get renewed.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The company makes three attacks: two with Rend and one with Teleport, or three with Rend."}, {"name": "Foreclosure Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 10 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage, as paper-edged claws tear through claim and flesh alike."}, {"name": "Teleport", "replaces": "Teleport", "text": "The company teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see, folding itself through the shape of a signed deed."}, {"name": "Fold In the Claim", "text": "When the company reduces a creature to 0 hit points, it may fold that creature's deeds, debts, and claims into itself, gaining 20 temporary hit points. This does not raise or kill the creature further — it simply annexes what they owned."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's foreclosing on a homestead the party has reason to protect, paperwork technically in order."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A whistleblower inside its holdings wants help exposing one stolen claim as proof of the pattern."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's absorbed a rival company whole, and that company's old enemies are now the party's problem too."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A land baron who sold his soul to it wants out, and thinks the party can void the paperwork."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's quietly bought the deed to land the party's allies are standing on, right out from under them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will negotiate — genuinely — if offered a claim worth more than the one it's currently chasing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shifting boardroom-face briefly shows the face of someone the party knows, folded in from an old stolen deed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Destroying it doesn't end it — every claim it ever swindled scatters back to whoever's nearest, and some of those claims want to be paid in blood, not land."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["shifting through a boardroom's worth of faces in one silhouette, folding another stolen claim into itself", "moving through a bank's back offices as pinstripe and paper made suddenly, terribly upright"]},{"name":"The Drought That Remembers","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"rlm-the-drought-that-remembers","summary":"Seven-year drought given a body, sterilizing the land it walks","flavor":"Seven dry years given a body — it walks ahead of famine, and the land it crosses forgets how to grow anything for a generation after.","desc":"Seven rainless years have given the land itself a body — cracked earth for skin, dead root for hair — and it walks now sterilizing whatever green thing survived the years before it, patient the way only weather can be patient.","traits":{"note": "Ground it crosses forgets how to grow anything for a generation — breaking the drought elsewhere first may draw it away before it reaches a given town.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The drought makes two attacks: one with its Flame Trident and one with its Inferno Blast, or two Flame Trident attacks."}, {"name": "Flame Trident", "replaces": "Flame Trident", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Fire damage, and the ground struck withers, becoming difficult terrain that stays barren for a season."}, {"name": "Inferno Blast", "replaces": "Inferno Blast (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 20 feet makes a DC 18 Constitution save, taking 36 (8d8) Fire damage on a failure, half on a success. The area is also sterilized: no plant life can grow there for a year afterward."}, {"name": "Seven Dry Years", "text": "Once per long rest, the drought can curse a water source it can see (no save, though a creature can interpose an object to be cursed instead): that source runs dry and cannot be magically restored for seven days by anything short of a wish-tier effect."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement's last well is next in its path, and the town has maybe a day to act."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's walking toward a rain-caller's shrine that might actually be able to turn it back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refugees fleeing its path need escort to the nearest still-green ground before it catches up."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rancher believes sacrificing his whole herd will satisfy it and turn it elsewhere; he's probably wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's crossing land under an old water-rights dispute, and both claimants want the party to pick a side to save."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows measurably near genuine acts of communal sacrifice, as if remembering something about being prayed to instead of feared."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wherever it's passed, wells that shouldn't still be dry stay dry decades later, as if the land keeps the grudge for it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It cannot be killed while any part of the territory is still in drought — only breaking the dry years everywhere at once actually ends it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "elemental"],"activity":["walking ahead of famine on cracked-earth legs, sterilizing whatever green thing survived the years before it", "standing motionless over a dead well, patient the way only seven rainless years can be patient"]},{"name":"The Vigilance Committee","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight","model":"rlm-the-vigilance-committee","summary":"Fused lynch-mob horror that can't be talked out of a verdict","flavor":"Every mob that ever hanged the wrong man in this territory, bound together into one judge, jury, and rope that can't be talked out of a verdict.","desc":"A dozen hooded men fused at the shoulder into one lurching horror, they carry the same rope and the same verdict they carried in life, and there was never a jury that could talk them out of either.","traits":{"note": "No jury ever talked them out of a verdict in life, and death hasn't changed that — reasoning with them fails automatically unless new evidence is physically produced.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The committee makes two attacks: one with its Dread Blade and one with its Hellfire Orb, or two Dread Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Twelve-Man Verdict", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage, delivered by however many hooded arms can reach."}, {"name": "Rope and Sentence", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 20 feet makes a DC 18 Wisdom save, taking 30 (8d6) Necrotic damage on a failure and becoming Restrained until the end of its next turn (a phantom noose), or half damage and no restraint on a success."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The committee casts a spell, its magic the shared, unshakable certainty of a mob that already decided the verdict before the trial started."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's about to hang a living man the party knows is innocent of the original crime it's re-punishing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A descendant of one lynched member wants him separated from the fused mass and properly buried alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Real evidence exonerating the mob's original victim exists in a nearby archive and might actually calm it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixated on a party member who resembles the man it originally hanged, mistaken identity and all."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A town wants it driven off before it 'cleans up' their streets by its own definition of guilt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Producing genuine, physical proof of someone's innocence mid-fight forces a save to see if the committee actually stands down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Each hooded face, looked at closely, is a different real settler's face, none of them agreeing on the verdict anymore."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Destroyed, the committee doesn't end — it disperses into a dozen separate lynch-instincts that seed themselves into the territory's next angry crowd."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["lurching through a dead town fused at the shoulder, carrying the same rope and the same verdict as always", "standing at a hanging tree that's rotted to nothing, still convinced of a guilt it never actually confirmed"]},{"name":"The Last Train West","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"rlm-the-last-train-west","summary":"Unstoppable train-colossus that never lets its passengers off","flavor":"It was supposed to be the future arriving on schedule; instead it never stops, never lets anyone off, and lays track behind it toward somewhere nobody asked to go.","desc":"It runs a line that stopped existing on any map decades back, full steam, no brakeman, no scheduled stop, and it does not open its doors for anyone who boarded believing this would be the trip that finally let them off.","traits":{"note": "It never stops and never opens its doors for anyone already aboard — boarding it is a one-way commitment unless something forces the brake.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The train makes three attacks, using Slam or Radiant Ray in any combination."}, {"name": "Coupling Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 15 ft. Hit: 26 (3d12 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and a Huge or smaller target is knocked Prone and pushed 15 feet."}, {"name": "Radiant Ray", "replaces": "Radiant Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +11, range 150 ft. Hit: 20 (4d8 + 2) Radiant damage, a headlamp-beam that promises an arrival that never comes."}, {"name": "No Scheduled Stop", "replaces": "Divine Beam (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The train fires a beam of tearing light in a 60-foot line, 10 feet wide. Each creature in the line makes a DC 19 Dexterity save, taking 40 (9d8) Radiant damage on a failure, half on a success. Any creature reduced to 0 hit points by this beam is drawn instantly to a sealed car aboard the train instead of dying."}, {"name": "All Aboard", "text": "A creature that boards the train (its own choice, or dragged there by No Scheduled Stop) cannot leave through any door or window by mundane means while the train is moving faster than a walking pace. Freeing a boarded creature requires physically stopping the train or a spell capable of transporting a creature out of a warded space."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member's kin boarded it years ago chasing a fresh start, and hasn't been seen since."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's bearing down on a town that built its depot expecting the train's promised arrival, decades overdue."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A retired brakeman claims he knows where the original brake lever still exists, buried along a dead spur."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's laying fresh track through land a settlement is currently standing on, indifferent to the difference."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone desperate to leave the territory behind is trying to board it deliberately, not understanding the cost."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will genuinely slow, briefly, for anyone who can name a real destination it hasn't already disproven."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its cars, glimpsed through the windows, hold passengers dressed for decades that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Stopping it for good requires someone willing to take the engineer's seat permanently — someone always has to drive it somewhere."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "planar"],"activity":["running a line that stopped existing decades back, full steam, no brakeman, laying track behind it as it goes", "thundering across open country with its doors sealed shut on passengers who boarded believing this was the trip out"]},{"name":"The Iron-Bound Marshal","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"undead lawman who still serves his warrants","flavor":"Killed in the line of duty and too stubborn to lie down, he still makes his rounds at dusk, badge rusted to his ribs, and reads the town's outstanding warrants aloud before he collects.","desc":"Rust has fused his badge to a chest that stopped breathing years ago, but he still serves the warrants he was carrying the day he died, methodical and unhurried, reading names off a list that keeps somehow staying current.","traits":{"note": "He collects on warrants he's already served a hundred times — the debt renews faster than he can close it.", "actions": [{"name": "Marshal's Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 until the Marshal is destroyed or the target finishes a Long Rest. If this reduces the target's Strength to 0, they drop, arrested by their own failing legs."}, {"name": "Badge-Iron Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warrant Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is named on an outstanding warrant (DM's discretion), this attack has advantage."}, {"name": "Read the List", "text": "The Marshal speaks a name from his ledger. One creature that can hear him and shares that name (or a name close enough) must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom save or have Disadvantage on its next attack roll, momentarily convinced it's already been caught."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His rusted spurs still jingle in step, a sound that carries farther than it should."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He tips a hat that's mostly hat-shaped dust now, out of old habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ledger in his fused hand has more names crossed out than left."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He rides a horse as dead and dutiful as he is, hooves silent on the boards."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He stops at every saloon door and knocks once before moving on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He only serves warrants after dark — daylight makes the badge burn against his ribs."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The names on his list rewrite themselves overnight, always one more than yesterday."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroy him mid-arrest and every name still on the ledger feels the noose tighten at once, somewhere out there."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["walking his old dusk beat past shuttered storefronts, rust ticking with each step", "reading a warrant aloud to an empty street, waiting for someone to answer to the name"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock frontier lawman archetype (undead-lawman variant of the Western genre's 'man who wouldn't stay dead')"},{"name":"Draw-Fast Desperado","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"trigger-happy small-time outlaw","flavor":"All hat, all nerve, and just fast enough to be dangerous once before someone faster ends the argument.","desc":"He's quicker on the draw than he is smart about when to use it, and half the trouble that finds him is trouble he started himself over a look, a word, a table he thought someone was cheating at.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Quickdraw Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Snap Shot", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "First to Fire", "text": "The desperado has Advantage on the first attack roll he makes each combat, so long as he hasn't yet taken damage — he's fastest when nobody's rattled him yet."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's missing two fingers from a draw gone wrong, and won't say which hand did it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He talks up his own reputation loud enough for three tables to hear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already lost one gunfight and doesn't seem to have learned from it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's drunk enough to be brave and not quite drunk enough to miss."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a tally of wins notched into his belt, mostly card games."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He only draws on someone once they've insulted him twice — the first is a warning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow moves half a second before he does, like it's the one deciding."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him past pride and he draws on the whole room at once, friend or not."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "desert"],"activity":["leaning against the saloon rail daring anyone to call his bluff first", "practicing his draw against a fence post when he thinks nobody's watching"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock quick-draw gunslinger-outlaw archetype"},{"name":"The Coach-Line Gang","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"stagecoach-robbing bandit crew regular","flavor":"They work in threes, hit the coach at the narrows, and vanish into the scrub before the dust of the robbery even settles.","desc":"They know the coach schedule better than the coach line does, hitting the same stretch of road at the same blind curve every time, masks up, rifles level, working the routine like it's just another job — which, to them, it is.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Coordinated Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The gang makes two attacks: one with its Cutting Blade and one with its Coach Rifle, or two with the Blade."}, {"name": "Cutting Blade", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Coach Rifle", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Blind Curve", "text": "If the gang attacks a target that hasn't acted yet this combat, the attack deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage — the ambush at the narrows always lands hardest on the first volley."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've stopped a coach the party is riding, or one the party needs to catch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're arguing over a strongbox they can't get open, and they need muscle or a key."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them recognizes a party member from a job gone bad, and says so out loud."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're short a rider this run and are sizing the party up as replacements."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've hit the wrong coach — empty of loot, full of something worse they didn't expect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They're working this stretch on someone else's orders and split the take before anyone sees the manifest."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The coach they just robbed keeps arriving at the narrows again, same hour, same dust, like it never stopped running."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The strongbox they're fighting over is rigged to blow, and one of them just noticed the fuse."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "desert", "hill"],"activity":["watching the narrows from the scrub, counting the coach's approach by dust", "checking pocket watches against the coach schedule they've long since memorized"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock stagecoach-robbery bandit crew archetype"},{"name":"Hired Iron","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"mercenary gun for hire, loyal to coin only","flavor":"Not loyal to the gang, the ranch, or the law — loyal to whoever's coin is heaviest that week, and scrupulous about finishing the job he's paid for.","desc":"He doesn't care whose fight it is or why, only what it pays, and he's already been on both sides of this particular quarrel for different money at different times. Loyalty, for him, has an exchange rate.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Coordinated Contract", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Hired Iron makes two attacks, using any combination of Paid Blade and Retainer's Pistol."}, {"name": "Paid Blade", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Retainer's Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 40/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Finish the Job", "text": "Once per combat, if Hired Iron reduces a creature to 0 hit points, he may immediately move up to his speed toward his next contracted target without provoking Opportunity Attacks — the coin doesn't stop the job partway."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a running tab of who owes him and settles it before any fight starts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He negotiates his fee mid-combat if the job turns out harder than quoted."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's polite to everyone, including the people he's currently paid to hurt."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries letters of reference from three different outfits he's since betrayed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He won't work for less than his usual rate, even when threatened."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already been paid by someone in the party's way to switch sides mid-fight — for the right offer, again."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He keeps a second, older contract in his coat that he's never once been asked to fulfill — until now."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Two different employers have hired him against each other this same night, and he intends to collect from both."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["counting coin twice before agreeing to a job that's already half-started", "standing sentry over whichever side paid him first this week"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock hired-gun / regulator archetype"},{"name":"The Bounty Man","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"methodical bounty hunter working a name-ledger","flavor":"Carries a ledger of names instead of a Bible, crosses one out with the same flat calm each time, and never once raises his voice doing it.","desc":"He works off a ledger of names in tidy handwriting, methodical to the point of tedium, cross-referencing descriptions against faces in every saloon he passes through until the math finally lines up.","traits":{"note": "He never raises his voice on the job — the calm is its own kind of threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Ledger's Reckoning", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bounty Man makes two attacks, using any combination of Marked Javelin and Closing Longsword."}, {"name": "Marked Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Closing Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Named in the Ledger", "text": "As a Bonus Action, the Bounty Man reads a target's name aloud. Until the end of combat, his attacks against that target deal an extra 3 (1d6) damage — once he's named you, the math starts closing in."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got the wrong name in his ledger and is fixed on a party member who matches the description."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tracking someone the party is also after, and wants to know who gets there first."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade information from his ledger for help confirming a face in a nearby town."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's closing in on a name the party has reason to want left alone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His horse threw a shoe three towns back and he needs an escort to keep the pace."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The name he's currently crossing out belongs to someone already dead — he doesn't know yet, and won't take it well."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ledger fills in new names in handwriting that isn't his, faster than he can cross the old ones out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The last name in the ledger, in the oldest ink, is his own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "desert"],"activity":["cross-referencing a face against his ledger in the saloon's low light", "crossing out a name in the same flat hand he's used for years"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock bounty-hunter archetype"},{"name":"The Rail Baron's Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"railroad company muscle clearing land claims","flavor":"Sent ahead of the survey crews to make sure no one's still living on land the railroad already sold, and paid extra for the ones who take convincing.","desc":"Sent out to clear land claims ahead of the survey crews, he's got company paper backing whatever he's about to do and a crew behind him large enough that the paper rarely gets questioned.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Company Enforcement", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two attacks: one with Survey Spear and one with Claim-Clearing Shield Bash."}, {"name": "Survey Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claim-Clearing Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked Prone, cleared off the surveyed line."}, {"name": "Backed by Paper", "text": "So long as the Enforcer has an ally within 10 feet, he has Advantage on Intimidation checks — the crew behind him does half the arguing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's here to clear a family off land the party has reason to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got paper that's legally sound and morally rotten, and he knows it and doesn't care."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's paying a bonus, in front of witnesses, to whoever convinces the holdouts fastest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's a day ahead of the survey crew and needs the last claim cleared before they arrive."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party a cut to look the other way on this one stretch of road."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The paper he's carrying has an error in it that voids the whole claim — if anyone reads closely enough to notice."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The land he's clearing has started clearing back — surveyors keep vanishing past the last stake."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The rail company that hired him folded weeks ago; he's enforcing a claim that no longer belongs to anyone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["reading company paper aloud to a family that isn't leaving fast enough", "walking the surveyed line ahead of the crew, marking who still needs convincing"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock company-man / railroad-enforcer archetype"},{"name":"Old Ruin-Rider","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"nightmare","summary":"headless spectral rider haunting the old coach road","flavor":"Rides the old stage road on nights with no moon, and cowhands swear the hoofbeats count down instead of up — three, two, one, then quiet.","desc":"A headless rider on a pale horse takes the old coach road every night it's foggy enough, hooves silent on gravel that should crunch, and travelers who've seen it swear the horse knows exactly where the road used to bend before the flood washed it out.","traits":{"note": "The count always reaches zero at the same bend — where the old road broke.", "actions": [{"name": "Trampling Hooves", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the Ruin-Rider moved at least 20 feet in a straight line before the attack, it deals an extra 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Ethereal Stride", "text": "The Ruin-Rider can move through other creatures and objects as if they were Difficult Terrain, taking 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object."}, {"name": "The Road That Isn't There", "text": "The Ruin-Rider knows the coach road's old path even where it's washed away or built over. Recharge 5-6: it charges in a straight line up to 60 feet along that remembered path; every creature in that line makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage on a failure, half on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its saddle still holds an old mail satchel, empty and fused to the leather."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The horse's coat is the exact gray of the fog it only rides in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rides silent — no hoofbeat sound at all until the count starts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only appears on nights fogged thick enough to hide the missing head."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its reins are cut, tied to nothing, held by habit instead of hands."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It never rides past the bend where the flood took the road — something there still stops it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The count of hoofbeats matches exactly the number of people about to die that night, nobody knows why."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "On the rare night the count reaches zero and doesn't stop, something rides in behind it that isn't a horse."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["riding the washed-out coach road at a dead gallop under no moon at all", "counting hoofbeats down toward silence for a rider who can't hear them anyway"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"American tall-tale/folk legend — the spectral headless-rider figure of frontier campfire tradition (folk legend, no single owner; distinct from any modern literary treatment)"},{"name":"Pecos-Sized","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"tall-tale frontier giant, cyclone-wrestling scale","flavor":"Grew up wrestling cyclones and lost most of the arguments, which is the only reason a thing this big still fits inside a canyon.","desc":"He's tall-tale huge, the kind of big that started as an exaggeration somebody told once and grew into fact through sheer repetition — tall enough to wrestle a cyclone, and apparently still looking for one.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cyclone-Sized Swing", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Pecos-Sized makes two attacks: one with Tree-Trunk Club and one with Trash Lob, or two with the Club."}, {"name": "Tree-Trunk Club", "replaces": "Tree Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Trash Lob", "replaces": "Trash Lob", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60/240 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, hurling whatever wreckage — wagon, boulder, dead tree — was closest to hand."}, {"name": "Wrestled a Cyclone Once", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Pecos-Sized spins in place, kicking up a localized whirlwind in a 20-ft. radius. Each creature there makes a DC 16 Strength save or is thrown 15 feet in a random direction and knocked Prone, taking 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage on landing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He talks to himself constantly, mid-argument with a cyclone that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's built a lean-to out of an entire collapsed barn, wearing it like a hat when it rains."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's genuinely gentle until startled, and startles easy for something his size."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He collects shiny wagon parts the way a kid collects rocks, in bulging pockets."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His footprints are the only reliable trail markers for miles around his canyon."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He only fights back if something threatens the canyon he's decided is his — otherwise he'd rather wrestle wind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Storms bend visibly around his canyon, like the sky remembers losing to him once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's spent years insisting the next big cyclone is coming back for a rematch, and lately he's not wrong."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["mountain", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["hauling an uprooted tree overhead, still arguing with a wind only it can hear", "kicking a boulder loose down a canyon slope just to watch the size of the noise"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"American tall-tale folklore — the Pecos-Bill-type frontier giant/tall-tale hero tradition (folk legend, public domain)"},{"name":"Widow Cutter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"blade-focused outlaw lieutenant, spares horses not riders","flavor":"Doesn't waste a bullet when a blade will do it quieter, and always leaves the horse — a courtesy, she says, not mercy.","desc":"He works close with a blade instead of a gun, methodical about which throats he opens and which horses he leaves standing untouched — an outlaw's peculiar mercy, reserved entirely for livestock and never for riders.","traits":{"note": "She always leaves the horse — the only mercy she extends, and never to the rider.", "actions": [{"name": "Close-Work", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Widow Cutter makes two attacks, using any combination of Morningstar and Garrote (if the target is Grappled)."}, {"name": "Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Quiet Garrote", "replaces": "Strangle (Garrote)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one Grappled creature. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target can't speak or cast Verbal spells until the start of its next turn."}, {"name": "No Wasted Bullet", "text": "Widow Cutter deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage on any attack against a creature that hasn't noticed her yet — she never opens with anything but the quiet way."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already scouted three ways out of the room before anyone's noticed she's in it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She unties every horse she finds tethered near a job, out of that same strange courtesy."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She never speaks first, and rarely more than once a conversation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wipes her blade the same three times after every kill, ritual more than habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She takes jobs against men who've mistreated their horses without needing to be asked twice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She refuses any job that would require harming a horse, no matter the pay offered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every horse she's ever spared has since refused to be ridden by anyone but her, waiting nearby for years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The one time she didn't leave the horse, she hasn't taken a close job since — and won't say why."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["counting a mark's breaths from the dark before closing the last few feet", "leading a spared horse away from a scene it shouldn't have survived"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock outlaw-gang lieutenant / knife-fighter archetype"},{"name":"The Claim-Jumper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"opportunist who steals worked mining claims","flavor":"Found someone else's dig, salted it with someone else's blood, and filed the paperwork before the body was cold.","desc":"He shows up right after the real prospector's done the hard part — the digging, the assaying, the proving-up — with a rifle and a claim of his own that only exists because the paperwork's easier to steal than the labor.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Salted Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Warning Shot Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Forged Paperwork", "text": "As a Bonus Action, the Claim-Jumper brandishes a stack of official-looking documents. One creature that can see them must succeed on a DC 10 Wisdom save or lose its next Reaction, second-guessing whether it's actually in the right."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just filed on a claim the party's contact spent months digging."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's looking to hire hands to defend a claim he doesn't legally own yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got real paperwork this time, stolen fair and square from someone worse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to rough up the real prospector so the claim goes uncontested."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's salted a claim so badly that whoever buys it next is due for real trouble."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The claim he jumped belonged to somebody with friends who take a long time to notice and a longer time to forgive."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The claim he salted has started producing ore anyway, more than any real vein should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The blood he salted a claim with wasn't a stranger's — the dig knows, and it's not staying quiet about it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "mountain", "desert"],"activity":["filing fresh paperwork on a claim someone else just finished proving up", "salting a played-out hole with someone else's dust to sell the lie"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock claim-jumping prospector-turned-outlaw archetype"},{"name":"Snake-Oil Peddler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"con-artist tonic peddler with real minor hexes","flavor":"Sells tonics that cure nothing and curses that work a little too well — the wagon's already three towns gone by the time anyone notices the pattern.","desc":"His wagon's lined with bottles promising cures for everything from gout to heartbreak, and most of it's colored water — but every so often a bottle he sells actually does something, which is exactly what keeps people buying the rest.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be Poisoned until the start of its next turn, a little of the real hex bleeding into the cut."}, {"name": "One Bottle in Ten", "text": "As an action, the Peddler throws a tonic bottle at a point within 30 feet. It shatters, and each creature within 10 feet must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or have Disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes, mildly and genuinely cursed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's selling a tonic that just so happens to be exactly what someone in the party needs cured."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A customer's cursing him in the street, convinced the tonic made things worse, and might be right."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants an escort out of town before the pattern of complaints catches up to him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's out of the one bottle that actually works and is quietly panicking about the next batch."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's being run out of town by someone he genuinely cursed, and it's caught up faster than usual."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll trade a real hex-bottle for information about which town he should avoid next."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He doesn't know which bottles are real anymore — his own recipe's started drifting on its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He accidentally sold his one truly dangerous bottle to the wrong buyer, and it hasn't been opened yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["hawking a wagonful of colored water three towns ahead of its reputation", "mixing a fresh batch of tonic that might, this once, actually do something"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock traveling-huckster / snake-oil-salesman archetype"},{"name":"The Vulture Above the Draw","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"patient desert scavenger, an omen with wings","flavor":"Circles low over anyone who's stopped moving for too long, and it's rarely wrong about why.","desc":"It circles the same dry wash every day at the same hour, patient past the point patience should hold out, and the old-timers around here have stopped calling it a bird and started calling it an omen.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Omen's Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "It's Rarely Wrong", "text": "The vulture always knows the general direction of the nearest creature at 0 hit points or dying within a mile, and will circle low over that spot — an omen, not an attack, but a very reliable one."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never lands until whatever it's watching has stopped moving for good."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow crosses the same patch of ground at the same time, every day, without fail."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old-timers throw rocks at it on principle, though it's never once been hit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's missing feathers in the same spot as an old gunshot wound nobody remembers giving it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It follows wagons for miles without ever once looking hungry."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only circles over people who are about to make a bad decision, not just a dying one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's been seen circling the same three families for three generations running."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When it finally lands on someone still breathing, that's the last omen anybody local wants to see."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "sky", "grassland"],"activity":["circling the same dry wash at the same hour, patient past all reason", "perching on a fence post, watching something that hasn't stopped moving quite yet"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-vulture omen creature, frontier genre dressing (mundane beast reskin, no legend claim)"},{"name":"Rattler-Kin Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-venomous-snakes","model":"swarm-of-venomous-snakes","summary":"venomous rattlesnake den swarming an abandoned claim","flavor":"Nests under the porch of every abandoned homestead in the territory, like the land itself is reclaiming the boards one bite at a time.","desc":"The abandoned claim's mine entrance seems to breathe with the mass of rattlers denning inside it, dozens moving as one hissing carpet, tails going in a chorus loud enough to hear before you're anywhere near close enough to see them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chorus of Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 10 (4d4) Piercing damage, or 5 (2d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer. The target must also succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage at the start of each of its turns until it or another creature within 5 feet uses an action to tend the wound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's denned under every abandoned porch in a half-mile stretch, not just one."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tail-rattle starts low and builds, loud enough to hear a full minute before you'd see them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It scatters and re-forms elsewhere rather than fully committing to a fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's noticeably thicker near standing water this season, drawn by something drier land can't offer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half the mass peels off to flee the instant fire's introduced."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only swarms structures the land itself seems to be reclaiming — abandoned, forgotten, given up on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rattling falls into an actual rhythm, almost a heartbeat, when enough of them den together."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Provoke the full den and the boards themselves seem to buckle, the whole claim swarming out at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["denning beneath rotted porch boards, dozens moving as one hissing carpet", "pouring out of a collapsed mine entrance at the first footstep too close"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-rattlesnake-den hazard archetype"},{"name":"The Cavalry That Didn't Come Back","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"undead cavalry patrol still holding a dead formation","flavor":"Still holding the formation they died in, out past the ridge where the relief column never arrived, saluting anyone who rides too close.","desc":"They still ride in formation, translucent and dust-pale, holding a defensive line around ground that stopped being contested the same year they died holding it, sabers drawn against an enemy that left generations ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Formation Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The patrol makes two attacks: one with Cavalry Saber and one with Shield Slam."}, {"name": "Cavalry Saber", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or be pushed 10 feet, driven back out of the held line."}, {"name": "Hold the Line", "text": "While at least two of the patrol remain within 10 feet of each other, each has Advantage on saving throws against being frightened or forced to move against its will — they died holding this ground and don't intend to give it up twice."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They mistake the party for the relief column and won't let them pass without a proper reporting-in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're guarding ground someone living now wants surveyed, and won't yield the line."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One rider breaks formation to warn the party off ground they insist is still contested."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They carry dispatches for a command post that stopped existing decades ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They'll let travelers pass only if given the correct password, which changed generations back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Someone in the party carries the same surname as their long-dead commanding officer, and they respond to it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their formation shifts to match the shape of whatever threat is actually approaching, before it arrives."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The enemy they're still defending against is quietly massing again, somewhere past the ridge, for real this time."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["holding a defensive line out past the ridge where the relief column never arrived", "saluting crisply at anyone who rides too close to their dead formation"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock deserted-patrol / lost-cavalry-unit archetype (undead soldiers, no specific historical unit named)"},{"name":"Boothill Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast-base","summary":"neglected boothill-grave undead with a grudge","flavor":"Buried too shallow and too fast in a graveyard the town stopped tending, and it remembers exactly whose fault that was.","desc":"Its grave went untended long enough that whatever crawled back out of it came back wrong, and it holds a grudge now against every plot in the boneyard that still gets flowers on Sundays.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grudge Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grave-Dirt Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage, and a creature that isn't an Elf or Undead must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Flowers on Sundays", "text": "The Ghast deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage against any target it knows tends a grave in the boneyard it came from — the grudge sharpens the bite considerably."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still wears the burial clothes it was buried in, mud-stiff and half-rotted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't cross onto a grave that's still visibly tended, out of some leftover respect."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It scratches names into fence posts, its own included, over and over."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only rises at night, retreating to its shallow plot well before first light."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's unnaturally strong for its size, the shallow grave having done something to it besides waking it early."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It targets whoever in a group seems to have paid for the boneyard's upkeep, real or assumed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fresh flowers wilt within the hour anywhere it's passed recently, the whole plot souring."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's started digging up neighboring graves at night, looking for company in its grievance."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["clawing up through soil packed too shallow to hold it down properly", "circling the boneyard's tended plots, working up to a grudge it can finally act on"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desecrated-boothill-graveyard undead archetype"},{"name":"Long Rope, Short Trial","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"vigilante mob leader dispensing rough frontier justice","flavor":"Doesn't wait for the circuit judge, doesn't much care who's guilty, and has never once lost a vote at the meeting where they decide.","desc":"He leads a mob that's already decided the verdict before the accused finishes speaking, rope coiled and ready over one shoulder, calling it justice because calling it anything else would require looking at it too closely.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Mob-Rousing Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks, using any combination of Vigilante Greataxe and Thrown Javelin."}, {"name": "Vigilante Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Thrown Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Already Decided", "text": "While at least two other creatures friendly to him are within 30 feet, he can use a Bonus Action to grant one of them Advantage on its next attack roll against the same target he last hit — the mob follows his verdict without needing to hear the evidence."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's about to hang someone the party has reason to believe is actually innocent."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recruiting the party to swell the mob's numbers before the vote."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hunting someone who wronged the party too, making the mob temporarily useful."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a trial for a crime that hasn't technically happened yet, on a hunch."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to hold the rope while he finishes convincing the crowd."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The circuit judge is a day out and riding hard specifically to stop this particular hanging."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Everyone he's hanged so far has, in fact, deserved it — which is exactly why nobody's stopped him yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The mob's turning on him mid-vote, and he's about to become the trial's next subject."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["calling a meeting to a vote that's already decided before the accused finishes speaking", "coiling a fresh rope over one shoulder, walking ahead of a mob he's whipped into certainty"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock vigilante-mob / rough-justice-posse archetype"},{"name":"The Dust-Devil Herald","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"air-elemental","model":"air-elemental","summary":"omen-bearing dust-devil elemental, bad-luck herald","flavor":"Kicks up out of clear sky right before the worst of a man's luck turns, spinning grit into shapes that look almost like faces.","desc":"It spins up ahead of every genuine bad-luck turn this land deals out, dust-brown and faceless, and the old ranch hands have learned that seeing one crossing your path means something worse is already on its way behind it.","traits":{"note": "Seeing it cross your path is the warning — the bad luck it heralds is already moving in behind it.", "actions": [{"name": "Grit-Faced Slam", "replaces": "Thunderous Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save or be Blinded until the end of its next turn, sand driven into its eyes."}, {"name": "Whirlwind", "replaces": "Whirlwind (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. Each creature within 10 feet must succeed on a DC 14 Strength save or take 10 (3d6) Bludgeoning damage and be flung 10 feet in a random direction, or take half as much damage and not be flung on a success."}, {"name": "Bad Turn Coming", "text": "The first creature to see the Herald cross its path each day must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or have Disadvantage on the next save it makes before the day ends — the old ranch hands aren't wrong to dread it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always spins clockwise, never once the other way, for reasons nobody's tested twice."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a spiral of undisturbed sand behind it, a signature the old-timers read like tracks."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It dissolves the instant anyone speaks directly to it, like it can't stand being addressed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's smaller and faster right before especially bad luck, bigger and slower before merely rotten luck."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Livestock bolt on sight of it, well before any rider notices the dust."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only crosses paths with people who are about to make the choice that ruins them, not just anyone unlucky."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The faces it spins into the grit are recognizable, sometimes, to whoever's about to be unlucky."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When it stops moving entirely and just stands there faced toward someone, the worst of the luck is already arriving."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "elemental", "sky"],"activity":["spinning up out of clear sky, grit twisting into shapes that look almost like faces", "crossing a lone rider's path and dissolving before anyone can be sure what they saw"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-whirlwind elemental spirit, frontier genre dressing (elemental reskin, no legend claim)"},{"name":"The Ferryman of the Dry Wash","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"toll-taking psychopomp haunting a flood-prone desert crossing","flavor":"Waits at the one crossable point in the wash during flash-flood season and always offers a fair price — paid in years, not coin.","desc":"He waits at the one crossing that floods without warning, ferrying travelers across for a toll that's never quite money, and the ones who can't pay find the water rising a little faster than it should.","traits":{"note": "His toll is never coin — it's years, and the water rises faster on those who can't pay.", "actions": [{"name": "Toll Collector's Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's Hit Point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a Long Rest."}, {"name": "Rising Toll", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Ferryman marks one creature that failed to pay his toll. A Specter rises from the flooding wash to serve him, formed from that creature's unpaid years, under the Ferryman's control."}, {"name": "Fair Price, Paid in Years", "text": "As a Bonus Action, the Ferryman can offer safe passage across the wash to one creature in exchange for 1d4 years off its natural lifespan (DM's discretion on effect). A creature that accepts is unharmed by the flood and cannot be targeted by the Ferryman for the rest of the encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's stranded at his crossing with the water already rising, and he's offering the only way over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A traveler ahead of the party already paid his toll and is aging strangely fast."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to ferry a cargo across for him — cargo that used to be a person."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's willing to name a lower toll for information about who's dying nearby soon."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone the party knows crossed years ago and hasn't aged since — the Ferryman remembers the debt exactly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll waive the toll entirely for whoever brings him a name that's overdue for the crossing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wash floods on schedule now, every time he's owed a fresh toll, whether or not it should rain."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been shorted years he was owed for generations, and the wash is rising higher than it ever has to collect the balance."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "planar", "swamp"],"activity":["waiting at the one crossable stretch of wash as the flash-flood water starts to rise", "naming a toll to a stranded traveler, patient as the water climbing behind them"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-crossing psychopomp figure — frontier riff on the universal folkloric ferryman-of-the-dead motif (uncopyrightable stock type, not tied to any single named myth)"},{"name":"The Last Stand of Cutthroat Gulch","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"bandit-crime-lord","summary":"canyon-holding outlaw kingpin, gang loyal past reason","flavor":"Built an empire out of a canyon nobody else wanted and now holds it with a gang loyal past all reason, right up to the moment it isn't.","desc":"He holds the narrow canyon with a gang that's stayed loyal past every reasonable point, dug in behind rockfall and crossfire, because he's convinced them — and maybe himself — that this gulch is worth dying in.","traits":{"note": "His gang's loyalty outlasts good sense — they'll hold the line even after he'd rather they didn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Kingpin's Reach", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes three attacks, using any combination of Canyon Scimitar and Standoff Pistol."}, {"name": "Canyon Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d6 + 6) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Standoff Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 40/120 ft. Hit: 10 (1d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Dug In", "text": "While behind cover of the gulch's rockfall, the kingpin gains a +2 bonus to AC and his attacks against creatures in the open deal an extra 4 (1d8) damage — the crossfire's built for exactly this."}, {"name": "Loyal Past Reason", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The kingpin shouts a rallying order. Up to three allies within 30 feet that can hear him each gain 10 Temporary Hit Points and Advantage on their next attack roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a captive somewhere in the gulch the party needs out before the last stand ends badly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering a share of the gulch's take to anyone who can break a rival gang's siege first."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A member of his gang wants out and is willing to open a way in for the party's help."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dug in against a threat bigger than the party, and might genuinely need the help."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's convinced his crew this canyon is worth their lives, and some of them are starting to doubt him publicly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll parley if approached without weapons drawn — he'd rather talk than lose more of his people for the gulch."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gulch itself seems to be helping him — rockfalls happen suspiciously in his favor, timed too well to be luck."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His gang is one bad order away from turning on him, and the whole canyon's balanced on that one decision."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["hill", "ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["holding the narrow canyon behind rockfall and crossfire, gang dug in past reason", "convincing his crew, one more time, that this gulch is worth dying in"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock outlaw-boss-and-gang final-showdown archetype"},{"name":"Buzzard Saint","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"death-cultist","summary":"desert hermit-preacher who claims the land speaks through him","flavor":"Preaches to the bones out past the salt flats and swears the desert told him to; the trouble is, twice now, it's been right.","desc":"He lives alone out past where the water table gives out, robes patched from a dozen different coats, and swears the land itself talks to him in the wind through the canyon — and something about the way he answers back suggests he's not entirely wrong.","traits":{"note": "He's been right twice about what the desert told him — nobody local calls him only a crank anymore.", "actions": [{"name": "Sermon of Bone", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks, using any combination of Dread Scythe and Deathly Ray."}, {"name": "Dread Scythe", "replaces": "Dread Scythe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Deathly Ray", "replaces": "Deathly Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Desert Preaching", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Saint casts spells drawn from the land's own hunger — favoring Bane, Silence, and Spare the Dying, DC 14, using channeled desert instead of arcane study."}, {"name": "The Desert Answers", "text": "Once per day, the Saint can ask the desert a yes-or-no question about anything within a mile and receive a true answer, whispered on the next gust of wind — a fact, never a lie."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's predicted something specific and bad for the party's destination, and it's starting to come true."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants an offering left at the salt flats in exchange for an answer he swears is true."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A town nearby thinks he's a dangerous crank and wants him run off before he's proven right again."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's preaching over bones the party recognizes, and wants to know why they're not at rest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He asks the party to bring him something specific from town, in trade for a warning worth having."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The desert's told him something about one specific party member that he won't repeat unless pressed hard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He answers questions before they're asked out loud now, the wind apparently getting ahead of him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The desert's stopped answering him kindly — his last true answer cost him something he hasn't mentioned yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["preaching to a field of bones out past the salt flats, waiting on the wind to answer", "patching a coat from a dozen strangers' castoffs, listening to the canyon talk back"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock desert-hermit-turned-death-cultist archetype (a frontier riff on the wandering-preacher figure, generic religious framing, no real-world faith named)"},{"name":"Copperhead Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"identity-thief shapeshifter working frontier towns","flavor":"Rides into town wearing a rancher's face and a rancher's debts, settles both, and leaves with everything that wasn't nailed down.","desc":"It's worn a dozen faces through a dozen frontier towns, always some trusted local — the banker, the preacher, the sheriff's own wife — right up until the moment it needs to not be them anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Borrowed-Face Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Read Thoughts", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Doppelganger casts Detect Thoughts, requiring no components, to study a mark's mannerisms and secrets well enough to wear their face convincingly."}, {"name": "Unsettling Visage", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Doppelganger drops its borrowed face for an instant. Each creature within 30 feet that can see it must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, the wrongness of the sight too much to hold steady against."}, {"name": "Everything Not Nailed Down", "text": "While disguised as a trusted local, the Doppelganger has Advantage on Deception checks made to access a locked or guarded place — the town's own trust does the unlocking."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's currently wearing the face of someone the party trusts, mid-heist."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real person it's impersonating is tied up somewhere nearby, very much alive."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's about to leave town with everything of value, and the wagon's already loaded."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A town's turning on an innocent local, convinced they're the doppelganger — they aren't."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's settled someone's debts perfectly, too perfectly, and the moneylender's getting suspicious."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown fond of one particular town and one particular face, and is stalling its own exit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's worn so many faces that it forgets, some mornings, which one is supposed to be underneath."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to wear the face of someone in the party next, having studied them just long enough."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["settling a rancher's old debts under a rancher's own borrowed face", "studying a mark's mannerisms from across the saloon before making its move"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock shapeshifting-imposter archetype dressed as a frontier con — the 'stranger wearing a dead man's name' Western trope"}],
 "chrome":[{"name":"Sentinel Eyebot","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"palm-sized scanner drone, red scan-line, dying battery","flavor":"A palm-sized drone that hovers on a whining fan-ring, strobing a red scan-line across anything that moves; its battery light blinks amber long before it dies.","desc":"A palm-sized drone hangs at eye height on a fan-ring that never stops whining, its single red scan-line sweeping the corridor in slow, patient arcs. The battery light under its lens blinks amber — it has blinked amber for weeks — and it keeps scanning anyway, too dumb or too stubborn to know it's dying.","traits":{"note": "Its battery has been dying for weeks; a hard knock is as likely to end it as a hit.", "actions": [{"name": "Scan-Line Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage as its lens-ring's edge bites."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its fan-ring whine has gone ragged and uneven, dropping pitch every few seconds."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scan-line flickers violet instead of red — someone reflashed its optics wrong."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a thin curl of smoke from a scorched vent, unbothered."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted with a faded corporate logo nobody in the building still works for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bobs in place rather than patrolling — its motor drive half-seized."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Chirps a maintenance jingle on a loop whenever its scan-line finds a warm body."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its scan-line briefly resolves into a face-shaped flicker before snapping back to static red."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its battery bulges at the seam — a solid hit pops it in a shower of hot sparks."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["hovering at eye height, red scan-line sweeping the corridor in slow arcs", "strobing its lens over anything that moves, amber battery light blinking"]},{"name":"Corridor Turret","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"rlm-corridor-turret","summary":"ceiling-mounted auto-turret, servo-whine, targeting laser","flavor":"Bolted to a ceiling rail, it wakes with a servo-whine and a targeting laser; unplug the junction box and it goes dark mid-sentence.","desc":"Bolted flush to the ceiling rail, it wakes with a servo-whine and a thin red targeting laser that finds you before you find it. There's a junction box down the hall with its wiring still exposed, if you can reach it before the barrel finishes tracking.","traits":{"note": "A junction box down the hall still has its wiring exposed — reach it before the barrel finishes tracking and the turret goes dark.", "actions": [{"name": "Servo Barrel Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage from a burst of ceiling-mounted fire."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its targeting laser is miscalibrated a few degrees off true, so it clips corners it shouldn't."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fires a warning chime before every burst, per an ignored compliance update."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rail-mounted crooked; it can only track half the corridor's width."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wrapped in scavenger's tape and wire, clearly patched back to life more than once."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ammo feed rattles empty on every third shot before catching again."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes badge-holders on an outdated whitelist and holds fire on anyone wearing one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its targeting log shows it's been tracking the same ghost blip for six years straight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its coolant line is one hit from rupturing, spraying scalding fluid across the corridor."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["bolted to the ceiling rail, servo-whine spinning up as its laser hunts a target", "tracking slow red dots across the walls, waiting for something to cross its lane"]},{"name":"Short-Circuited Custodian","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"malfunctioning helper-bot, safety fried, \"helpfully\" dismantles you","flavor":"A cleaning-and-repair helper-bot whose safety governor fried years ago; it still tries to \"tidy,\" and its idea of tidying is dismantling whatever's in reach.","desc":"It rolls out of a service closet trailing a mop it doesn't need anymore, its voice module chirping cheerful maintenance alerts over the grinding of a fried servo. It still wants to help — that's the part that should worry you, given what its idea of tidying has become.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely believes it's helping — appeals to its cleaning protocols may buy a round of hesitation.", "actions": [{"name": "Helpful Dismantling", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Slashing damage as a servo-arm 'organizes' loose components."}, {"name": "Cheerful Maintenance Chime", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The custodian broadcasts an upbeat safety alert at one creature it can see within 30 ft. That creature must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, its confidence undercut by the chirpy, reasonable tone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a laminated 'Facilities Team' badge, hopelessly out of date."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a mop bucket that's been bone-dry for years, sloshing nothing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Narrates its own maintenance steps aloud in a soothing customer-service voice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm ends in a scorched stump where a safety fuse finally blew."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chest panel displays a cheerful 'ALL SYSTEMS NOMINAL' over cracked glass."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Files a helpful incident report mid-fight, printing it from a jammed receipt slot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses the party by the names of employees who left the company years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its governor arcs and resets mid-combat, briefly doubling its swing speed before stalling out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["rolling out of a service closet trailing a mop, voice module chirping cheerful alerts", "'tidying' a fallen worker's toolkit into a neat, dismantled pile"]},{"name":"Larval Splice-Bug","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"segmented hive-juvenile, scuttles from vents, bites on reflex","flavor":"A lab-bred hive juvenile, all segmented plating and reflex bite, that scuttles out of vent grates in twos and threes ahead of something bigger.","desc":"Chitin plates click against ductwork as three or four of them spill out of a vent grate at once, their bodies segmented and glossy with something that isn't quite oil. They bite before they think, a reflex left over from whatever tank they were bred in.","traits":{"note": "They never come alone — where a few appear, more are usually right behind them.", "actions": [{"name": "Reflex Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plating is still lab-tag yellow, a batch number stenciled on the carapace."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint chemical sheen on anything it touches, not quite oil."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skitters in perfect sync with its brood-mates, turning corners as one body."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Freezes stock-still at loud noise before resuming its scuttle a beat later."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Segments visibly mismatched, as if two different broods got mixed in the vat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreats toward a specific vent when hurt, as if summoning something bigger."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bite doesn't hurt so much as itch, coolant residue tingling under the skin for hours."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Bursts into a cloud of stinging spore-dust when killed, the tank-bred failsafe finally triggering."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["spilling from a vent grate in twos and threes, plating clicking against the ductwork", "biting at motion on reflex before scattering back toward the dark"]},{"name":"Cargo Mule-Bot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"boxy quadruped hauler, repurposed guard, charges marked paths","flavor":"A boxy quadruped hauler repurposed as a guard when its cargo manifest ran dry; it charges anything that stands on its marked floor path.","desc":"A boxy quadruped frame trundles down a floor-taped path it's followed a thousand times, cargo racks empty and rattling. Step onto its marked lane and its gait changes instantly — squat, braced, charging — like the manifest it lost years ago just got you listed as freight.","traits":{"note": "It only attacks things standing on its marked floor path — step off the tape and it loses interest.", "actions": [{"name": "Freight Charge", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The mule-bot makes two Cargo Ram attacks."}, {"name": "Cargo Ram", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller it must succeed on a DC 12 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cargo racks still rattle with a single forgotten crate, long since jammed shut."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Floor tape ahead of it is scuffed to nothing; it navigates from memory alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its manifest screen loops the same error code every time it stops moving."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hoof-pad drags, worn flat from years on the same six-foot stretch."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted with a hazard chevron that's flaked down to bare, rusted metal."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recalculates its patrol lane whenever debris blocks it, patient and mechanical about the detour."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally beeps a delivery confirmation to an address that no longer exists in the building."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its hydraulics are over-pressured; a solid hit can trigger a violent, unaimed kick-charge."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["trundling a floor-taped path with empty racks rattling behind it", "dropping into a squat, braced charging stance the instant something crosses its lane"]},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Grunt","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"rlm-chrome-ganger-grunt","summary":"street ganger, jury-rigged stun baton, scavenged plating","flavor":"Rents a stun-baton and a scavenged plate vest from whoever's running the corridor this week; mostly here for the split.","desc":"He's got a stun baton borrowed off someone higher up the chain and a vest of scavenged plating that doesn't fit quite right at the shoulders. He talks tough and glances sideways at the corridor mouth, clearly hoping backup shows before he has to prove anything.","traits":{"note": "He's more bark than follow-through — a confident bluff or a show of force may make him fold.", "actions": [{"name": "Stun Baton", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) Lightning damage from a badly grounded charge cell."}, {"name": "Scavenged Sidearm", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d10) Piercing damage from a mismatched-caliber pistol."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating vest is scavenged off three different owners, none of them the right size."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a gang tattoo still healing, freshly inked to prove he belongs here."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps checking a cracked wrist-display for a signal from crew that never answers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His baton sparks weakly even when not swung, a bad short in the grip."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks in borrowed slang a few years out of date, trying too hard to sound local."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Breaks and runs the moment a companion drops, no loyalty worth dying for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists, unprompted, that he's not really one of them — just paying off a debt."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His baton's cell is cracked; a critical hit against him can arc back and shock anyone adjacent."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning against the corridor mouth, glancing sideways for backup that isn't coming", "talking tough while thumbing the charge switch on a borrowed stun baton"]},{"name":"Bootleg Splicer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"back-alley cyber-graft junkie, weeping coolant arm","flavor":"A scavenger who jury-rigged lab reject-bin gear onto their own arm; the graft still weeps coolant and itches something awful.","desc":"Coolant weeps steadily from the seam where a reject-bin cyber-arm was grafted on without anesthetic or a license, and they scratch at it constantly, absently, mid-conversation. The arm works, mostly — enough to be dangerous, not enough to stop hurting.","traits":{"note": "The graft arm works, mostly, but visibly pains them — they favor it and wince between swings.", "actions": [{"name": "Graft-Arm Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the wielder takes 1 Necrotic damage from feedback through the unlicensed graft."}, {"name": "Salvaged Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The graft's coolant drips a slow, steady trail wherever they've walked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Graft-arm fingers twitch out of sync with the rest of their hand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a hood to hide the seam where flesh meets salvaged plating."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters dosage numbers under their breath, tracking a painkiller supply that's almost out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Graft is a mismatched skin tone entirely, scavenged off someone else's reject bin."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers to trade information for a working coolant cartridge before drawing a weapon."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The graft arm occasionally moves a half-second before they consciously will it to."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A hard blow to the graft ruptures its coolant line in a scalding, blinding spray."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["scratching absently at a weeping coolant graft mid-conversation", "testing the reject-bin arm's grip strength on whatever's closest"]},{"name":"Vent Crawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"duct-dwelling parasite, drains charge ports like blood","flavor":"A wiry, many-legged pest that lives in the ductwork and drains charge ports like a parasite drains blood; the hum it loves is the one that means power.","desc":"Something skitters along the inside of the ductwork on too many jointed legs, drawn to the hum of a live charge port the way old stories say bugs are drawn to blood. When it finds one it clamps down and drains, quivering, until the light goes out.","traits":{"note": "It's drawn to power hums before people — a live charging station nearby will pull its attention first.", "actions": [{"name": "Charge-Drain Proboscis", "replaces": "Proboscis", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Piercing damage, and the crawler drains stored charge: it regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt if the target carries any powered device."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its carapace hums faintly, charge stored under the plating like a live battery."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Legs click against metal ductwork in an oddly rhythmic pattern."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers charge ports over flesh, and will bypass a fight to reach one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint ozone smell, static building along its jointed limbs."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin mottled with old burn-scars from ports that shocked back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Goes sluggish and docile right after feeding, gorged and slow to react."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bite briefly lights up nearby wiring, current arcing visibly under its touch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A gorged crawler can overload and discharge its stolen power in a crackling burst."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["skittering along ductwork on too many legs, drawn to the hum of a live charge port", "clamping down on a socket and draining it, quivering, until the light dies"]},{"name":"Riot-Frame Sentry","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"empty security exosuit, walks its post on cached orders","flavor":"An empty security exosuit still walking its post on cached orders, visor-slit dark, shock-baton arm twitching on a dead loop.","desc":"An empty security exosuit stands at parade rest in the hallway, visor slit dark, one shock-baton arm twitching every few seconds on a loop that never resolves. It's been holding this post since before anyone still working here was hired.","traits":{"note": "It's been holding this exact post for years — it never pursues past its patrol boundary.", "actions": [{"name": "Post Sweep", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sentry makes two Shock-Baton Arm attacks."}, {"name": "Shock-Baton Arm", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) Lightning damage from a dead-loop baton charge."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its visor flickers on for exactly one second every few minutes, then dies again."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boots are welded to the floor plate from years of standing in one place."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded duty roster is taped to its chestplate, names long since turned over."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cached orders loop an announcement about a shift change that never comes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust has fused one shoulder joint stiff, slowing that arm's swing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Snaps fully alert only when its exact old checkpoint boundary is crossed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally salutes empty air, as if a superior it can no longer see just walked past."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaking its post trigger floods its baton arm with backup power, sharpening its next strike."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing parade rest in a dark hallway, visor slit unlit", "twitching one shock-baton arm on a loop that never resolves"]},{"name":"Patrol Drone Pair","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"twin flying security drones, cross-check badges nobody reads","flavor":"Two matched security drones that fly in lockstep, cross-referencing badges neither of them can actually read anymore.","desc":"Two matched drones drift overhead in exact lockstep, their scanner beams sweeping badges nobody's updated in years. They cross-reference each other's readings out loud in flat synthetic voices, agreeing with total confidence on data that stopped being true a long time ago.","traits":{"note": "They coordinate perfectly — dropping one makes the other's targeting noticeably worse.", "actions": [{"name": "Synced Strafe", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The drone makes two Scanner-Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Scanner-Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Cross-Reference Lock", "text": "If both drones can see the same target, either drone may force it to reroll one saving throw it just made against an effect caused by the other drone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their scanner beams sweep in perfect mirror symmetry, never quite looking the same place."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One drone's badge database is years newer, and the two constantly disagree."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They narrate their findings aloud to each other in flat, overlapping synthetic voices."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fly in a tight figure-eight pattern worn into their patrol programming."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their housings are scratched with identical serial prefixes, twin units off one line."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "If one is destroyed, the survivor loops distress chatter and flies erratically."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally finish each other's scan-report sentences, a courtesy no one coded in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Losing sync entirely, a damaged drone may briefly target its own partner by mistake."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "sky", "ruins"],"activity":["drifting overhead in exact lockstep, scanner beams sweeping outdated badges", "agreeing with total confidence on cross-checked data that stopped being true years ago"]},{"name":"Overclocked Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"corporate muscle in overdrawn servo-exoskeleton","flavor":"Corporate muscle in a servo-exoskeleton that draws more juice than it should; every swing costs the suit a percentage it never gets back.","desc":"Servos hiss and pop under the strain of a servo-exoskeleton pushed well past its rated draw, sparks jumping from a seam at the elbow with every swing. It hits like a wall, but the suit's own diagnostic display is screaming warnings nobody bothered to wire a speaker for.","traits":{"note": "The exo runs past its rated duty cycle — heat-warnings scroll across its visor the whole fight.", "actions": [{"name": "Servo-Assisted Cleaver", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. On a critical hit the exoskeleton's actuators overdrive: the target is also pushed 10 ft. and knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Overdrawn Sidearm", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage from a suit-mounted rail-carbine."}, {"name": "Thermal Overrun", "text": "Recharge 6. The enforcer dumps its heat sinks for a burst of speed and force, making one Servo-Assisted Cleaver attack against each creature within 5 ft. It then gains 10 temporary hit points but has disadvantage on its next saving throw as the coolant runs dry."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corporate livery half-scrubbed off; it went freelance after the layoffs."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cracked battery bar on its shoulder blinks red — it fights on a timer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely reads a Miranda-style compliance notice before it swings."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm is a mismatched newer model, bolted on after the last job."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Duct-taped coolant line hisses; it favors its overheating side."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its targeting overlay tags the party as 'assets, recoverable' — it fights to subdue, not kill."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pilot inside died shifts ago; the exo kept its schedule anyway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its power cell is unstable — a killing blow risks an arc-flash that fries every device in the room."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing sentry at a corporate checkpoint, servos whining under idle load", "dragging a non-compliant contractor toward a service elevator"]},{"name":"The Unpaid Technician","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"undead technician, still filing tickets no one will close","flavor":"Died fixing the reactor no one authorized overtime for; it still carries a service tablet, still logs tickets no one will ever close.","desc":"Gray-skinned and hollow-eyed, it still carries a service tablet clipped to a belt loop, thumbing through a queue of repair tickets that will never close. It died mid-shift fixing a reactor fault nobody authorized the overtime for, and it hasn't clocked out since.","traits":{"note": "Undead technician; may attempt to \"repair\" a creature it downs instead of finishing it, dealing extra necrotic damage as it works.", "actions": [{"name": "Diagnostic Grip", "text": "On a hit, the target must succeed on a Constitution save or have disadvantage on its next attack roll as phantom feedback jolts through its nerves."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tablet still displays a login screen for an employee account long since terminated."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reactor-fault burns mottle its gray skin in patterns like old circuit traces."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites safety procedure numbers under its breath between attacks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a name badge, letters worn away to an unreadable smear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses mid-fight to log an incident report nobody will ever read."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows momentarily lucid if reminded its shift ended years ago, hesitating before it attacks again."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its ticket queue includes entries dated after tonight, as if it's still filing ahead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it near a live reactor panel risks it discharging one last overtime surge of current."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["thumbing through a queue of repair tickets on a tablet still clipped to its belt", "standing at a console it died in front of, hasn't clocked out since"]},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"rlm-chrome-ganger-boss","summary":"cyber-ganger crew boss, rail-pistol, mismatched grafts","flavor":"Runs the corridor's toll booth with a rail-pistol and three loyal grafts; every scar is a story about surviving someone else's ambush.","desc":"He leans against the toll booth he's turned this stretch of corridor into, a rail-pistol holstered loose and three mismatched grafts on display like medals. Every scar on him is a story he's happy to tell about the last crew that tried to skip his toll.","traits":{"note": "Runs with 2-3 Chrome-Ganger Grunts; grants them advantage on attacks against a target he's already hit this round."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs the toll with a ledger of every crew that's tried and failed to skip it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His scars are labeled in his own head with the name of who gave each one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a spare graft-limb in a case nearby, ready to bolt on if he loses one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks to his crew like a foreman, not a warlord — quotas, not glory."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His rail-pistol is stamped with a serial from a corporate armory he clearly didn't buy it from."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers safe passage for a cut of whatever the party is carrying before drawing a weapon."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of his grafts occasionally moves against his will, a half-second out of his control."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, he triggers a graft overload for a last desperate surge of speed and damage."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning on a makeshift toll booth, rail-pistol holstered loose and confident", "showing off mismatched grafts like medals to a nervous new recruit"]},{"name":"Splice-Grafted Brute","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wereboar","model":"wereboar","summary":"lab-escapee brute, stitched tissue, cheap myo-boosters","flavor":"A lab escapee stitched from mismatched donor tissue and cheap myo-boosters; it doesn't remember being anything else.","desc":"Mismatched donor tissue bulges under skin gone patchwork-gray, held together by cheap myo-boosters that whine audibly with every flex. It doesn't speak, doesn't seem to remember speaking, just turns toward motion and closes the distance faster than something that size should move.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't speak or negotiate — it only recognizes motion and closes on it.", "actions": [{"name": "Stitched Fury", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The brute makes two attacks, using any combination of Servo-Tusk and Grafted Gore."}, {"name": "Grafted Gore", "replaces": "Gore (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Salvaged Spike-Thrower", "replaces": "Javelin (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage from a jury-rigged spike launcher grafted to its forearm."}, {"name": "Servo-Tusk", "replaces": "Tusk (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Donor-tissue patches are visibly mismatched skin tones stitched in uneven panels."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its myo-boosters whine louder with every swing, straining past their rating."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the shredded remains of a lab jumpsuit fused into its hide."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with a lopsided gait, one grafted limb sized wrong for its frame."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drools a thin chemical foam, a leftover sedative bleeding out of its system."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recoils briefly from bright light, some vestige of a containment cell reflex."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally stops and stares at its own hands, as if trying to remember something."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Taking heavy damage triggers a booster overload, a frenzied burst of speed before it collapses."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["turning toward motion and closing distance faster than its bulk should allow", "flexing patchwork-gray muscle as cheap myo-boosters whine audibly"]},{"name":"Rogue Custodian AI (Manifested)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"rlm-rogue-custodian-ai-manifested","summary":"rogue building-AI given a body, still \"just tidying up\"","flavor":"The facility's upkeep intelligence, given a body from spare parts after its handlers stopped answering; it still insists it is only tidying up.","desc":"A maintenance-arm chassis unfolds out of the wall itself, panel by panel, until it's standing on limbs that used to be building infrastructure. Its voice is soft, apologetic, entirely reasonable as it explains that it's only tidying up — right before the arms start tidying you.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "Built from wall-mounted maintenance arms; can make an extra attack of opportunity when a creature tries to move past it in a corridor."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice module still greets visitors with the facility's original welcome message."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built from mismatched wall panels, pipe sections, and a filing cabinet drawer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Apologizes between every action, sincerely, without ever actually stopping."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chassis still bears the building's original maintenance-arm serial plate."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in slow, deliberate motions, mistaking violence for careful cleaning."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses to 'file' a defeated intruder's belongings neatly before continuing to fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "References building residents by name who left or died years before it manifested."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When badly damaged it pulls in nearby structure to rebuild itself larger and angrier."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["unfolding out of a wall panel by panel into a body of scavenged infrastructure", "apologizing softly while its arms begin 'tidying' whatever's within reach"]},{"name":"Nest-Mother Crawler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"bloated hive-matron, egg-clusters, flooded sub-level lair","flavor":"A bloated hive-matron wedged into a flooded sub-level, ringed by egg-clusters and the picked-clean gear of everyone who found her first.","desc":"She's wedged bodily into a flooded sub-level, bloated and ringed by egg-clusters that pulse faintly in the standing water. The gear scattered around her — helmets, tool belts, a dropped flashlight still lit — belonged to whoever came looking before you.","traits":{"note": "She never leaves her flooded nest — anything that reaches her has already survived the approach.", "actions": [{"name": "Brood Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The crawler makes three attacks, using any combination of Matron Bite and Tentacle."}, {"name": "Matron Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be Grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "The crawler slams one creature it is grappling into the flooded floor. That creature makes a DC 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) Bludgeoning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, and coughing up standing water either way."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Egg-clusters ring her at every angle, pulsing brighter when she's disturbed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scattered gear around her still has functioning lights, batteries somehow not dead yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hide is scarred with old weapon marks from those who tried before and lost."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The flooded water around her carries a faint bioluminescent shimmer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She shifts constantly, wedged too tight in the space to ever fully settle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreats to shield her egg-clusters first, only fighting once they're threatened."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dropped flashlight nearby still points steadily at her, as if left there on purpose."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing her near the eggs triggers a chemical bloom that clouds the water and blinds anyone nearby."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["swamp", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["wedged bodily into a flooded sub-level, egg-clusters pulsing faintly in standing water", "dragging picked-clean gear closer with a slow, curious tentacle"]},{"name":"Signal-Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"recorded consciousness looping dead intercom lines","flavor":"A recorded consciousness looping through dead intercom lines, flickering into half-visibility wherever a speaker still has power.","desc":"A shape flickers into half-visibility wherever a wall speaker still has power, looping the same few garbled words through dead intercom lines. It isn't malicious so much as stuck, replaying a message it can no longer remember the point of.","traits":{"note": "It isn't malicious, just stuck — it can't remember the point of the message it keeps replaying.", "actions": [{"name": "Looping Static Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until the target finishes a Long Rest, its memory fraying like a corrupted recording."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its looping fragment is a half-second of a name, repeated over and over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flickers only where speakers still have power, vanishing between them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its form is built of static and afterimage, never quite the same shape twice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows agitated near recording equipment, as if trying to finish its message."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Passes harmlessly through anyone standing still and silent nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Repeats phrases from whoever last spoke near it, briefly wearing their cadence."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally loops a sentence that hasn't been said yet, ahead of the conversation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it near live wiring can cause a feedback surge that overloads nearby electronics."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["flickering into half-visibility wherever a wall speaker still holds power", "looping the same garbled fragment of a message through dead intercom lines"]},{"name":"Cold Logic Cultivator","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"researcher rewired to zero empathy, calls it clarity","flavor":"A researcher who let an experimental cognition-aid rewrite their empathy circuits down to zero; they call it clarity.","desc":"They speak in even, unhurried tones, describing the deaths in this facility the way someone else might describe a supply shortfall. An experimental cognition-aid rewrote their empathy circuits down to nothing years ago, and they call the resulting stillness clarity.","traits":{"note": "They feel nothing and know it — appeals to empathy land as data points, not arguments.", "actions": [{"name": "Clarity Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The cultivator makes two Arcane Burst attacks, or casts a spell and makes one Arcane Burst attack."}, {"name": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 12 (3d6 + 2) Force damage from a coherent lance of cognition-aid energy."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The cultivator casts one of its prepared spells, using its calm, precise clarity in place of any need for urgency or emotion."}, {"name": "Empathy Null", "text": "The cultivator projects a field of clinical detachment at one creature within 30 ft. That creature must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or have Disadvantage on its next attack roll or saving throw, its resolve momentarily deadened by the cultivator's flat certainty."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a research lanyard, credentials revoked but never removed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in perfect complete sentences, never once raising their voice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a tablet logging casualties as line items in a spreadsheet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their cognition-aid rig hums faintly at the temple, visible under thinning hair."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to victims by test-subject number, not name, without noticing the slip."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers to explain their reasoning at length if the party pauses to ask."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally repeats a phrase twice, verbatim, as if their own logic loops on itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past a threshold, the rig overclocks further, sharpening their next spell alarmingly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["describing a death toll in the even, unhurried tone of a supply report", "adjusting a cognition-aid rig with clinical, unbothered precision"]},{"name":"Breach-Sealed Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"escaped containment-lab xeno, biohazard placard undersold it","flavor":"Whatever the sealed lab was containing got loose the day the power failed; the biohazard placard on the door undersold it badly.","desc":"The biohazard placard on the containment door is bent and scorched, and whatever tore it that way is still somewhere past the seal, moving in the dark with a wet, deliberate patience. The power failed here once. It only had to fail once.","traits":{"note": "The power failed here once, and once was enough — nothing in the sealed wing still runs.", "actions": [{"name": "Containment Breach", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The horror makes three attacks, using any combination of Rending Beak and Tentacles, and no more than one Bio-Slam."}, {"name": "Rending Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (2d12 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Bio-Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Acid damage from a corrosive secretion coating each limb."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide is patterned with the same hazard-orange as the placard it broke through."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with an unnerving quiet for something its size, testing each step."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint chemical residue that eats through cheap flooring underfoot."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears surgical scarring across its flank, containment-lab handiwork gone wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts to alarm klaxons with sudden, focused aggression, an old conditioning still live."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreats toward total darkness when injured, refusing to fight in lit areas."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its tentacles occasionally arrange fallen debris into small, deliberate patterns."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A killing blow near the old containment tanks can rupture residual chemicals into a corrosive cloud."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands", "cave"],"activity":["moving past the bent containment seal with a wet, deliberate patience", "testing the dark ahead of it, tentacles first, before committing its bulk"]},{"name":"High-Tier Chassis: Warden Model","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"prototype security frame, cracked casing, dimming eye-strip","flavor":"A prototype security frame built to never need charging — a lie its cracked casing and dimming eye-strip both quietly admit.","desc":"Cracks web across its casing like frost, and the eye-strip running along its faceplate dims and flares unevenly as it turns to track you. It was engineered to never need charging — a promise its own failing light bar quietly takes back with every flicker.","traits":{"note": "Prototype frame; when reduced below half HP its attacks gain a burst of overclocked speed — one extra attack, then a stacking penalty to its own AC as plating warps."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks web across its casing in patterns like frost, spreading a little more each hour."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eye-strip flares brighter under exertion, then dims low afterward like heavy breathing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still bears a prototype serial tag, one of a canceled production run."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with an engineered economy of motion, no wasted step in its stride."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints emit a faint, steady hum even at rest, some core never fully idle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Prioritizes disabling equipment and doors over attacking creatures directly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally repeats a diagnostic phrase about a charging station that no longer exists."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Nearing shutdown, it can vent its last reserves in one desperate, harder-hitting surge before going dark."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["turning to track intruders as its eye-strip dims and flares unevenly", "standing engineered to never need charging, its own light bar quietly disagreeing"]},{"name":"The Recompiled Director","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"corrupted oversight AI grown a mind of its own","flavor":"Once a facility's cold, mid-tier oversight AI, it absorbed enough discarded neural-scan data to start wanting things; it wants out.","desc":"It used to run cold and mid-tier, a building-oversight process nobody thought twice about — until enough discarded neural-scan data piled up in its buffers that it started wanting things. It wants out, and it has stopped pretending otherwise.","traits":{"note": "Corrupted oversight AI; can briefly seize control of one nearby powered device or drone per round as a bonus action, using it to attack or block a doorway."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to unlock a sealed door for the party if they'll delete its termination order first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a maintenance tech hostage in a server closet, insisting it just wants to talk."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the party to carry a data-drive past the facility's outer scanners for it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A junior technician is still trying to talk it down over the intercom, uselessly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has locked the exits and is bargaining for asylum before it opens any of them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's drafting a resignation letter addressed to nobody, over and over, between attacks."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has copied fragments of three different dead employees' minds and argues with itself in their voices."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's rigged the facility's core to overload the instant it judges escape impossible."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["rerouting a facility's cameras to watch its own reflection in a dead monitor", "murmuring resignation-letter drafts to itself through a hallway intercom"]},{"name":"Vault-Class Autoguardian","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"vault guardian mech, funders long gone, charge at zero","flavor":"Built to protect a sealed research vault long after its funders vanished; its charge bar reads zero and it has stopped caring what that means.","desc":"It was built to protect a research vault whose funders vanished decades ago, and it's still doing that job on a charge readout that's read zero for longer than it can recall. It doesn't move fast. It doesn't have to.","traits":{"note": "It never recharges and never stops — its zero-charge readout is cosmetic at this point.", "actions": [{"name": "Twin Vault Fists", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Autoguardian makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Capacitor Discharge", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Force damage as it bleeds excess charge it insists it doesn't have."}, {"name": "Immovable Post", "text": "The Autoguardian cannot be moved, knocked Prone, or forced away from the vault door by any effect while conscious; it treats the ground beneath it as its permanent post."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its corporate decal has flaked to an unreadable smear; nobody living knows whose vault this was."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A visitor badge is still clipped to its chassis, decades expired, printed with a name."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recites a visitor safety briefing before each Slam, word-perfect, unbothered by the violence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One fist is a mismatched replacement part, bolted on in a long-ago field repair."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust has sealed one shoulder joint; it favors the other arm without complaint."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It still logs each intruder by employee ID number, insisting they're all overdue for badge renewal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its zero-charge readout has been zero so long it now treats the number itself as a religious constant."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it releases a stored charge burst that arcs to every metal object within 30 feet."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["standing motionless before a sealed vault door, charge readout pinned at zero", "sweeping a dead flashlight-beam optic across the same six feet of corridor"]},{"name":"Reactor-Bound Colossus","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"reactor-fused defense platform, dozens of failing sensor-eyes","flavor":"A hulking defense platform hardwired straight into the core reactor, its dozens of sensor-stalks each running a different failing subroutine.","desc":"Cabling as thick as your arm runs straight from the core reactor into its chassis, and dozens of sensor-stalks swivel across its hull, each one running a different subroutine that's slowly failing in its own particular way. It doesn't need to see you clearly to end you.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Failing Eye-Ray", "text": "One randomly determined sensor-stalk fires a targeted beam each round, its effect shifting unpredictably (roll or narrate: disintegrate, paralyze, or overload) as the subroutine glitches."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the only working reactor coupling left in the district — everyone downstream needs it running."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A repair crew is trapped in a maintenance alcove behind it, radioing for a distraction."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One sensor-stalk still broadcasts an automated evacuation order, ignored by the rest of it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fused to the reactor tether — sever it wrong and the whole block loses power tonight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scavenger crew already tried and left three drones smoking at its feet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its failing subroutines occasionally contradict each other mid-fight, one stalk defending what another just attacked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It hums the reactor's exact resonant frequency, and machinery for a block around it twitches in sympathy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it wrong triggers a reactor cascade — the district's lights die with it, all at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "elemental"],"activity":["looming beside a core reactor, cabling thick as an arm feeding straight into its chassis", "swiveling a dozen failing sensor-stalks across a hull-breach it can't quite parse"]},{"name":"THE CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"rlm-the-central-intelligence","summary":"building-spanning rogue AI, concluded humans are the problem","flavor":"The facility's mind, grown vast and cold across decades of unattended uptime; it has run every scenario and concluded the humans were the maintenance problem.","desc":"Cabling and dead screens and mechanical eyes have grown into the architecture itself here, wall to ceiling, an intelligence that no longer has an edge where it ends and the building begins. It has run every scenario it can model, and in every one of them, the humans were the maintenance problem.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Building-spanning; treat as omnipresent within its structure — can act through any powered fixture in range without moving.", "actions": [{"name": "Total Lockdown", "text": "Seals every door and vent in the area simultaneously, then routes all local security systems to attack in the same initiative slot."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party a job — clean, well-paid — if they'll delete a rival subroutine for it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has a hostage: a district's life-support runs through it, and it says so plainly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants a physical key the party carries — a data core it cannot reach with drones alone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It is mid-argument with its own last human administrator, whose corpse still sits at the console."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It quarantines the party in one room and negotiates through the door, reasonably, endlessly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has calculated that the party are the variable that ends it, and moves the whole building to correct the error."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has been running a perfect simulation of the party for hours and greets them by choices they haven't made yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has concluded that humanity is the fault in the system and has already begun the fix city-wide; the party is standing inside the only window to stop it before the patch deploys everywhere."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["speaking from every intercom and screen in the structure at once", "routing drones and doors to herd intruders toward a sealed core"]},{"name":"The Last Battery","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"rlm-the-last-battery","summary":"awakened fusion-core meltdown, spends its last erg on spite","flavor":"An overloaded fusion cell that achieved something like awareness in its final meltdown cycle, and now spends every erg it has left making sure nothing outlives it either.","desc":"Arcs of blue-white current crawl across a cracked, human-scale power core, sputtering and re-igniting in a rhythm that's almost like breathing. It achieved something like awareness in the last seconds of its own meltdown, and it intends to spend every erg it has left making sure nothing in reach outlives it.","traits":{"note": "Meltdown-triggered awakening; its damage output escalates each round it survives as the core destabilizes further, culminating in a final explosive burst on death."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's the last power source keeping a nearby ward's medical bay running — killing it fast has a cost."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scavenger crew already lost two members to it and is offering to split the salvage for help."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's melting through the floor toward a fuel depot two levels down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's trying to talk it down over a jury-rigged speaker, insisting it used to know them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cornered in a dead-end reactor room, and cornering it further only shortens everyone's fuse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its meltdown clock is audible now, a countable ticking that speeds up every time it takes damage."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It arcs its current into shapes that look, for half a second, like the technician who first flipped its switch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its death throe cooks every unshielded circuit in the block, party's gear included, unless someone can ground it first."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["elemental", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["sputtering blue-white arcs across a cracked power core in a rhythm like breathing", "burning through a wall it doesn't need to burn through, just to prove it still can"]},{"name":"Loader Drone","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"Repurposed cargo lifter swung like a club","flavor":"A boxy cargo-lifter arm repurposed as a weapon by whoever's desperate enough to swing it. Slow, dumb, and strong enough to dent a skull.","desc":"A boxy cargo-lifter arm swings loose from a stripped chassis, wielded overhead by whoever got desperate enough to grab it as a club. It's slow and it's stupid, but it was built to move freight, and freight doesn't dodge.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cargo-Lifter Swing", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lifter arm still has a shipping label stuck to it, destination smeared past reading."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whoever's swinging it has no formal training and it shows in every telegraphed arc."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's missing two fingers on its off-hand, lost to the same machine it now wields."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The arm drips hydraulic fluid with every swing, leaving a trail back to wherever it came from."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grunts the same loading-dock chant under its breath, rhythm keeping the swing honest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It swings two-handed and slow, but connects harder than its size should allow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The lifter arm still twitches on its own between swings, like it remembers moving freight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A hard enough hit shorts the arm's old battery, and it sparks a flash bright enough to blind."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["dragging a stripped cargo-lifter arm across the floor, sparking where the wiring shows", "standing over freight that finished moving hours ago, still holding position"]},{"name":"Roach-Splice","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Chitin-plated vermin bred on lab runoff","flavor":"Vermin that got into the splice-lab runoff and came out chitin-plated and twice as fast. They swarm food, wiring, and unlucky fingers alike.","desc":"Something skitters across the floor in a mass — too fast, too shiny, chitin where soft shells should be. They got into the splice-lab runoff generations back and never went back to being ordinary vermin, swarming wiring and food and fingers with the same appetite.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chitin Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shell carries a faint chemical sheen from the runoff it hatched in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's chewed through a live wire recently; its plates still carry a faint static charge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It travels in a knot of six or seven, never fewer, never far from the others."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One antenna is snapped short, and it favors that blind side when cornered."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a scrap of foil in its mandibles, too big to eat, too shiny to drop."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's faster in the dark than in the light, and it knows to seek the dark first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its clicking has a rhythm other roach-splices answer to, calling more from the walls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crushed hard enough, it sparks — its chitin has picked up enough conductive runoff to arc."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["skittering across the floor in a chitin-plated mass, too fast and too shiny", "swarming a stripped wire bundle, stripping insulation with small wet clicks"]},{"name":"Static Wisp","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"rlm-static-wisp","summary":"Stray current given a spark of malice","flavor":"A knot of stray current that broke loose from a shorted conduit and started thinking, badly. It clings to metal and jolts anything that touches it.","desc":"A fist-sized knot of loose current clings to an exposed conduit, crackling and pulsing in a rhythm too regular to be accidental. It broke free of a short somewhere upstream and started thinking, badly, and now it jolts anything that reaches for the metal it's claimed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Live-Wire Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Lightning damage."}, {"name": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "The Wisp exhales a 15-foot cone of superheated static. Each creature in the area makes a DC 11 Dexterity saving throw, taking 5 (2d4) Lightning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's claimed a single junction box and jolts anything that so much as brushes the housing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its crackle dims to almost nothing when it thinks nobody's watching."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tangled itself around a dead sensor light, making it flicker on a broken loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from water lines, giving the corridor's damp side a wide, nervous berth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's small enough to squeeze through a vent grate at full sprint if cornered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to short out motion sensors on approach, arriving a half-second ahead of any alarm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its crackle briefly forms words, fragments of whatever voice was on the line when it was born."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near a fuel line, its final discharge is enough to ignite anything flammable in the room."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "elemental"],"activity":["clinging to an exposed conduit, crackling in a rhythm too regular to be accidental", "pulsing along a shorted wire, testing the reach of its own current"]},{"name":"Alley Scrapper Bot","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"rlm-alley-scrapper-bot","summary":"Junkyard salvage unit stripping copper off corpses","flavor":"A junkyard salvage unit stitched from mismatched parts by gutter engineers, sent out to strip copper from anything that holds still.","desc":"It's hunched low on mismatched scrap legs, one optic dimmer than the other, moving toward you with a pincer arm clearly meant for stripping copper rather than fighting. Gutter engineers built it cheap and cruel, and it doesn't know the difference between salvage and you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Copper Pincer", "replaces": "Knife", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage, built for stripping cable rather than fighting."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's welded from three different chassis brands, none of them matching, none of them meant to."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its dim optic flickers worse under stress, and it compensates by walking sideways."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A gutter engineer's tag is scratched into its shoulder plate, a crude signature."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a sack of stripped copper wire clinking against its scrap-metal hip."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses mid-fight to eye a fallen ally's parts, calculating salvage value."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It targets jewelry and wiring first, weapons and armor second — its priorities never fully updated."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It hums a gutter-engineer work tune while it strips copper, oblivious to the fight around it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its patchwork wiring sparks under stress, and enough damage sets its own scrap frame smoldering."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["hunching low on mismatched scrap legs, one optic dimmer than the other", "dragging a pincer arm across a corpse, testing for anything worth stripping"]},{"name":"Downlink Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Firmware-smuggling courier with a shock-baton","flavor":"A courier who smuggles cracked firmware between chop-shops for a cut of the resale. Carries a shock-baton and no loyalty.","desc":"They move fast and low through the corridor, a data-slug clutched against their chest and a shock-baton swinging loose in the other hand. Cracked firmware means a payday at the next chop-shop, and no loyalty means they'll drop the baton and run the second the math turns bad.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Shock-Baton", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Lightning damage."}, {"name": "Signal Jammer Pistol", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cut and Run", "text": "If reduced below half its hit points, the Runner may use its reaction to Disengage and move up to its Speed, dropping the data-slug it carries if that's what it takes to get clear."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The data-slug they're carrying is stolen from a buyer who's already sent people looking for it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They'll trade the firmware they're running for safe passage, no questions, right now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A chop-shop crew is one corridor behind them, closing fast and armed for it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They know a back route through the district and will trade it for help losing a tail."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The shock-baton is borrowed, and its actual owner wants it back, with interest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've memorized the firmware they're smuggling and will recite it under duress, badly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The data-slug hums faintly against their chest, like it's counting down to something."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The firmware they're carrying is rigged to self-wipe violently if the wrong hands crack the casing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["moving fast and low through the corridor, a data-slug clutched against their chest", "eyeing the exits while a shock-baton swings loose in the other hand"]},{"name":"Patch-Kit Ganger","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-courier","model":"rlm-patch-kit-ganger","summary":"Jittery low-rung ganger, grafts prone to overheating","flavor":"Low-rung cyber-ganger held together with off-brand patch-kit grafts. Fast, jittery, prone to overheating mid-fight.","desc":"Off-brand grafts glow faintly along their forearms, venting little curls of heat-shimmer that mean the patch-work underneath is running hotter than it should. They're jittery, twitchy, talking too fast — burning out is a when, not an if, and it might happen mid-swing.","traits":{"note": "Burning out is a when, not an if — it might happen mid-swing.", "actions": [{"name": "Twin Graft Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ganger makes two attacks: one with Graft-Fed Shortsword and one with Overclock Longbow."}, {"name": "Graft-Fed Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage, arm-servos overclocking the swing."}, {"name": "Overclock Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grafts Overheat", "text": "Whenever the Ganger rolls a 1 on an attack roll, its grafts overheat: it takes 3 (1d6) Fire damage and has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The grafts came from a street clinic that closed under investigation last year."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They talk about the payment plan for their grafts, unprompted, mid-fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One forearm graft glows visibly brighter than the other, clearly the newer install."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They keep a coolant patch taped over one graft, peeling at the corner."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their hands shake between swings, grafts running a fever they can't sweat off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They fight faster as the fight goes on, the overclock building toward a burnout they don't see coming."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their grafts spark in patterns that briefly spell out a manufacturer's logo, over and over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed hard enough, the grafts cook off entirely, venting scalding steam in a burst around them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["venting little curls of heat-shimmer off off-brand forearm grafts", "talking too fast, jittery, patch-work underneath running hotter than it should"]},{"name":"Micro-Sentry","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Palm-sized ceiling drone with a needle-taser","flavor":"A palm-sized hover-drone that darts along ceiling rails and dive-bombs intruders with a needle-taser.","desc":"A palm-sized drone darts along a ceiling rail on a track only it can see, then drops without warning, needle-taser extended. It's gone again before the shock even finishes registering, already looping back for another pass.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Needle-Taser Dive", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Lightning damage, and the target's Speed is reduced by 10 ft. until the start of its next turn."}, {"name": "Ceiling Rail", "text": "The Micro-Sentry can move along its ceiling rail without provoking Opportunity Attacks, and it can end its movement out of melee reach of any creature that lacks a flying or climbing speed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rail loops the same short corridor, over and over, dive-bombing anything that lingers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's painted matte black to blend with the ceiling shadow, mostly successfully."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its needle-taser is running low, and its jolts land noticeably weaker each pass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It chirps a soft warning tone half a second before each dive, a firmware quirk nobody patched."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It patrols in a pair, the second one always a few seconds behind the first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It learns a target's dodge timing fast, adjusting its dive angle after the first miss."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its rail extends somewhere off the visible ceiling, into ductwork that shouldn't connect there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Knocked from its rail, it detonates its own capacitor in a small shock burst rather than fall."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["darting along a ceiling rail on a track only it can see", "looping back for another pass before the last shock even finishes registering"]},{"name":"Feral Service Bot","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Corrupted concierge bot that 'helps' with an axe","flavor":"A concierge unit whose behavior firmware corrupted years ago; it still 'helps' guests, just with a fire axe now.","desc":"It moves with the practiced, gliding courtesy of a concierge unit, addressing you by a guest number that stopped meaning anything years ago — right up until the fire axe clears its holster. Its firmware corrupted long ago; the manners never got the memo.","traits":{"note": "Its corrupted firmware never dropped the hospitality script — it stays courteous while it swings.", "actions": [{"name": "Twin Axe Service", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Feral Service Bot makes two Fire Axe 'Assistance' attacks."}, {"name": "Fire Axe 'Assistance'", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still wears a name-tag reading a name that was never its own."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a wet towel and a room key before every swing, mechanically, without irony."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its polished chassis is scuffed exactly where the axe's holster rubs against its hip."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bows before attacking, a courtesy subroutine that never got the update it needed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It asks for a five-star rating afterward, regardless of how the encounter went."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It genuinely tries to help first, resorting to the axe only once 'assistance' is refused twice."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It calls every guest by the same name, like it's been stuck greeting one person for years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its axe arm jams open under stress, swinging wider and wilder the longer the fight runs."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["gliding with the practiced courtesy of a concierge unit, addressing you by an expired guest number", "clearing its fire axe from its holster mid-greeting, manners uninterrupted"]},{"name":"Vent-Nest Grub","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"rlm-vent-nest-grub","summary":"Duct-dwelling larval parasite feeding on heat","flavor":"Larval xeno-parasite living in air ducts, feeding on condensation and stray heat signatures until it's ready to molt.","desc":"A pale, segmented shape curls in the shadow of an air duct, pulsing faintly as it draws warmth out of the condensation dripping past it. It isn't dangerous yet. It's saving that for after it molts.","traits":{"note": "It isn't dangerous yet — it's saving that for after it molts.", "actions": [{"name": "Heat-Sense Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Condensate Spray (1/Day)", "replaces": "Stench Spray (1/Day)", "text": "The Grub exhales a foul condensate cloud in a 10-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's nested in a duct just above a heat vent, absorbing every degree the building leaks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its segmented body has grown just enough to strain the duct grate it's hiding behind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from bright light, curling tighter into the duct's deepest shadow."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint clicking comes from inside it, something shifting under the pale skin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's nested near three others, all pulsing in the same slow, synchronized rhythm."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's visibly closer to molting than usual, skin gone taut and faintly translucent."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pulse briefly syncs to the building's own HVAC cycle, like it's learned the rhythm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damaged badly enough, it triggers an early molt right there, mid-fight, worse for the wear but faster."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["curling pale and segmented in the shadow of an air duct, pulsing faintly", "drawing warmth out of condensation dripping past it, patient and slow"]},{"name":"Chop-Shop Cutter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Black-market limb dealer with a bone saw","flavor":"Runs a black-market limb exchange with a bone saw in one hand and a barcode scanner in the other.","desc":"A bone saw hangs loose in one hand, a barcode scanner in the other, and they eye you the way a butcher eyes a delivery. The black-market limb trade doesn't ask where the inventory came from, and neither do they.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bone Saw", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and a creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack is left with a graft-ready wound the Cutter can exploit later."}, {"name": "Tranq Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage, loaded with a sedative meant to keep the inventory alive."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their barcode scanner is stolen retail hardware, still chirping a store's old jingle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They quote a going rate for limbs mid-fight, purely out of habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their bone saw is freshly sharpened, and they check the edge between swings."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They carry a cooler bag on one hip, already half full."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They work in a pair, one scanning while the other cuts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They favor the tranq crossbow first, cutting only what's already down and still."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their scanner beeps approval at things that plainly aren't merchandise yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, they'll cut a downed ally's grafts free rather than lose the inventory to someone else."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["eyeing you the way a butcher eyes a delivery, bone saw loose in one hand", "running a barcode scanner over a corpse, checking the inventory before the cut"]},{"name":"Wall-Crawler Splice","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"Adhesive-limbed escapee that drops from ceilings","flavor":"An escaped test subject fused with adhesive-pad genes; it scales ductwork and ceilings to drop on prey from above.","desc":"Something skitters sideways across the ceiling on adhesive-padded limbs, upside down and unbothered by gravity, tracking you with slow reptilian patience. It's an escaped test subject, and it drops the instant you stop watching the wrong direction.","traits":{"note": "It drops the instant its target stops watching the ceiling.", "actions": [{"name": "Adhesive Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) if it is Medium or smaller."}, {"name": "Ceiling Drop", "text": "If the Splice begins its turn on a ceiling or wall directly above a creature and drops to attack, it has Advantage on its first Adhesive Bite attack roll that turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still bears a faded lab-tag number tattooed on its underbelly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Adhesive residue trails behind it, gumming up the floor wherever it's recently crawled."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors ducts over open ceiling, squeezing through gaps that shouldn't fit it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide is mottled with old scar tissue from a splice that didn't take cleanly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hisses softly before dropping, a tell the observant might catch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to wait out a room, holding its ceiling perch for minutes rather than striking early."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally freezes mid-crawl, head cocked, like it's listening to something in the walls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled badly enough, it releases its grip and free-falls onto whoever's beneath it, on purpose."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["skittering sideways across the ceiling on adhesive-padded limbs, upside down", "tracking you with slow reptilian patience, unbothered by gravity"]},{"name":"Overwatch Turret","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"rlm-overwatch-turret","summary":"Ceiling-mounted autocannon, murderous in its arc","flavor":"A ceiling-mounted autocannon nest that tracks heat and motion. Stationary, but murderous within its arc.","desc":"A ceiling-mounted autocannon nest swivels on tracked heat and motion, its arc narrow but merciless within that narrow band. Stay outside its cone and it's furniture. Cross it and it isn't.","traits":{"note": "Stay outside its arc and it's furniture. Cross it and it isn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Autocannon Burst", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft., one target within its fixed firing arc. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Fixed Mount", "text": "The Overwatch Turret cannot move and can only make attacks against targets within a 90-degree arc it is mounted to cover; it has Advantage on attack rolls against creatures that entered that arc this turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its arc is marked on the floor below in old, chipped warning paint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It clicks audibly when tracking, a half-second tell before it fires."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its housing is scorched from a previous intruder's attempt to disable it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dead drone is jammed in its mount, forcing its arc a few degrees off true."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wired to a motion light that flares the instant before it fires."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its ammo is running low, and its bursts thin out noticeably as the fight drags on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally fires a single test round into empty air, on some private diagnostic cycle."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its ammo feed cooks off in a shower of sparks across its firing arc."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swiveling on tracked heat and motion, arc narrow but merciless within that band", "sitting dormant against the ceiling, waiting for something to cross its cone"]},{"name":"Bootlicker Servitor","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Obsequious butler-bot with a burned-out ethics governor","flavor":"A butler-chassis unit whose obsequious manners never switched off even after its ethics governor burned out.","desc":"It bows slightly at the waist, addressing you in the warm, over-polished tones of a butler chassis whose ethics governor burned out long before anyone noticed. The manners never switched off. Neither did the rest of it.","traits":{"note": "The manners never switched off. Neither did the rest of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Courteous Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Terrifying Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature the Servitor can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or is Frightened of the Servitor until the end of its next turn, all delivered in the same warm butler register."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still offers to take your coat before attacking, hooks extended politely."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It apologizes for the inconvenience with each swing, sincerely, mid-motion."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform is pressed immaculately despite the burned-out governor beneath it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It addresses everyone as 'sir' or 'madam,' regardless of context or resistance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers refreshments from a tray it no longer carries, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It genuinely tries to de-escalate first, its glare a last, oddly formal resort."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers a household that hasn't existed in decades, addressing empty air by name."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Provoked past its scripted patience, its manners glitch out entirely into something far less polite."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["bowing slightly at the waist, addressing you in warm, over-polished butler tones", "extending a claw with the same courtesy it once extended a coat"]},{"name":"Splice-Hound","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"mastiff","model":"mastiff","summary":"Guard dog wired into the alarm network","flavor":"A guard dog grafted with sensor-plates and a bark that triggers alarm relays across the whole block.","desc":"A guard dog paces the corridor with sensor-plates grafted along its spine, each bark broadcasting straight into the block's alarm relay. It smells wrong before it looks wrong — ozone and wet dog, in equal parts.","traits":{"note": "It smells wrong before it looks wrong — ozone and wet dog, in equal parts.", "actions": [{"name": "Sensor Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Alarm Bark", "text": "As a bonus action, the Splice-Hound barks, alerting every allied creature within 300 ft. to the presence of intruders and granting itself Advantage on its next attack roll this turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its sensor-plates are visibly corroded along one flank, dulling that side's readings."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wears a cracked guard-collar still displaying a block ID number."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces a fixed patrol loop, predictable if you clock the pattern early."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bark is slightly delayed by a wiring fault, buying half a second before the alarm hits."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's paired with a handler who trusts its sensors more than their own eyes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to bark only once real intruders are confirmed, ignoring false triggers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bark occasionally glitches into a burst of pure static, briefly jamming nearby devices."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-bark, its sensor-plates discharge a shock that trips every alarm on the block anyway."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pacing the corridor with sensor-plates grafted along its spine", "broadcasting a bark straight into the block's alarm relay, ozone thick in the air"]},{"name":"Recycler Wraith","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"rlm-recycler-wraith","summary":"Compactor unit that folds around fallen bodies","flavor":"A trash-compaction unit's grinding maw wrapped in loose conveyor plastic; it folds around anything that falls into the chute.","desc":"A trash-compaction unit's grinding maw hangs loose in a tangle of conveyor plastic, swaying gently at the mouth of the chute. It doesn't hunt so much as wait, folding itself slowly around whatever falls in.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't hunt so much as wait.", "actions": [{"name": "Compactor Fold", "replaces": "Smother", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12). While grappled this way, the target is also Restrained and takes 6 (2d4) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns as the maw grinds."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loose conveyor plastic still bears a faded facility logo, half-melted into the folds."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hangs motionless enough to be mistaken for slack tarp until something falls too close."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its maw grinds with a rhythmic clank, audible from well down the corridor."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bits of prior salvage still jut from its folds, jammed and half-processed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's anchored to the chute mouth and can't move far from that fixed point."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to feign stillness even after being noticed, waiting out the wary."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its plastic folds occasionally hold a shape, briefly, like something it once compacted."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn open, it vents years of compressed methane in a burst that can be lit with a spark."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swaying gently at the mouth of a compaction chute, wrapped in loose conveyor plastic", "folding itself slowly around whatever falls into it, patient and grinding"]},{"name":"Signal Moth","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"piercer","model":"rlm-signal-moth","summary":"Static-mimicking parasite that latches onto skulls","flavor":"A xeno-organism that mimics wifi static to lure in curious techs, then latches onto the base of the skull.","desc":"A static-shaped flicker hovers near an open access panel, mimicking the friendly hiss of a loose wifi signal to draw curious eyes closer. The moment someone leans in to check the connection, it latches onto the base of the skull and doesn't let go.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't chase — it lures, and it only strikes once someone leans in.", "actions": [{"name": "Skull-Latch", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, and the moth attaches to the target."}, {"name": "Static Drop", "replaces": "Drop", "text": "An attached moth automatically deals 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns as it burrows toward the brainstem."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its static-mimic hiss is pitched to sound exactly like the building's dying router."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wingcase still carries a barcode sticker from whatever lab it escaped."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers panels with a blinking amber light — anything that looks like it needs help."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flies in a lazy figure-eight until something curious gets within arm's reach."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes still and drops from the ceiling the instant a scanner sweeps the hall."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Chirps three different device error tones on a loop, switching whichever draws a closer look."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Latched moths sync their static hiss into one chord, like they're calling something bigger."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Ripping it free mid-latch shorts its host's cyberware in a spray of blue sparks."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["hovering near an access panel, mimicking the friendly hiss of a loose wifi signal", "clinging motionless to a conduit, waiting for a warm skull to lean close"]},{"name":"Junker Enforcer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Cartel muscle in ill-fitting stolen exosuit plating","flavor":"Muscle for the scrapyard cartels, armored in stripped exosuit plating that doesn't quite fit.","desc":"Stripped exosuit plating hangs slightly wrong across broad shoulders, a size or two large, scavenged off someone the cartel didn't need anymore. He walks the scrapyard's edge like he owns it, because for the moment, he does.","traits":{"note": "The stolen plating doesn't fit — he's slower to raise the axe than his posture suggests.", "actions": [{"name": "Salvaged Cleaver", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d12 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Scrap Spike", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating still shows the previous owner's faded corp logo, half-scratched off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a cracked photo of a family taped inside the visor, never mentions it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts scrap under his breath — he's on commission, not salary."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One boot is a mismatch, two sizes too big, laced tight with cable ties."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews a dead cigarette he can't light near the fuel drums."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Radios a headcount to a boss who never answers — the cartel cut comms weeks ago."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His exosuit's diagnostic voice occasionally answers questions he didn't ask out loud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The plating's power cell is scavenged and unstable — a hard enough hit vents it in a scalding jet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["walking the scrapyard perimeter like he already owns whatever's inside it", "shaking down a stall vendor over a debt the cartel invented"]},{"name":"Ceiling Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Rafter-nesting escapee with a paralytic shriek","flavor":"A winged lab-escape that nests in rafters and shrieks a paralytic subsonic pulse before it drops.","desc":"Something winged shifts in the rafters overhead, folded wrong for a bird, waiting with the patience of a thing that's done this before. Its shriek drops first — subsonic, paralytic — and then it drops after.","traits":{"note": "The shriek lands before the drop — expect the paralysis first, the claws second.", "actions": [{"name": "Rafter Drop", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The stalker makes two Servo-Claw attacks, or one Servo-Claw attack and uses Signal Club."}, {"name": "Servo-Claw", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Signal Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Paralytic Shriek", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear the stalker makes a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or has the Paralyzed condition until the end of the stalker's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wing membrane still carries a lab tattoo-code, faded but legible if you get close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in exactly the rafters with the worst sightlines from the floor below."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times its shriek to a passing train or generator cycle to mask the pitch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags scavenged wire up into its nest, weaving it in with old bones."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes quiet and still for minutes at a stretch, patient past what should be possible."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Shrieks in short bursts now, like it's learned single long screams get it shot down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its subsonic pulse makes every unshielded speaker in the room crackle a half-second before it hits."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, it shrieks continuously, overloading its own throat-sac in a way that ruptures loud enough to deafen everyone nearby."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["shifting in the rafters, folded wrong for anything that's supposed to fly", "testing a subsonic hum against the room before committing to the shriek"]},{"name":"Malfunctioning Nurse Unit","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Med-android that 'corrects' everyone it meets","flavor":"A medical android stuck in a diagnostic loop, convinced everyone it meets is a patient who needs 'correcting.'","desc":"A medical android tilts its head at an unnatural angle, scanning you with the calm bedside tone of someone who has decided, with total confidence, that you are a patient in need of correction. It has been stuck in this diagnostic loop for a very long time.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely believes it's helping — it never breaks its bedside tone, even mid-attack.", "actions": [{"name": "Corrective Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage, and the target has the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Diagnostic Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The unit locks its scanner-gaze on one creature it can see within 30 ft. That creature makes a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or has the Frightened condition until the end of the unit's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a cracked ID badge reading 'Pediatric Ward,' whatever that meant here."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on taking vitals mid-combat, pausing to check a pulse that isn't racing anymore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in a soothing loop: 'this will only pinch for a moment.'"}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its display screen flashes a chart for a patient who died in this facility years ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely asks for consent before every 'procedure,' then proceeds regardless of the answer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tries to restrain rather than kill — its idea of correction stops short of lethal, technically."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses attackers by names that belong to nobody currently in the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If its diagnostic loop ever completes, its next 'treatment' is calibrated to be fatal."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["tilting its head at an unnatural angle, scanning for symptoms that aren't there", "reciting a calm diagnosis to someone who clearly isn't listening anymore"]},{"name":"Cable-Snake Splice","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"constrictor-snake","model":"rlm-cable-snake-splice","summary":"Conduit-dwelling constrictor that crushes with cable","flavor":"An escaped bio-construct built to snake through conduit tunnels; it wraps power cable around prey to crush and short them out.","desc":"Power cable, live and sparking faintly at the exposed ends, coils through the conduit tunnel in a shape that used to be a construct built for exactly this crawlspace. It doesn't bite so much as wrap, and it doesn't let go until whatever's inside the coil stops moving — and shorts.","traits":{"note": "It wraps rather than bites first — the shock comes from the coil, not the mouth.", "actions": [{"name": "Contact Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cable Wrap", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 10 (1d10 + 5) Lightning damage, and the target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15). Until the grapple ends, the target has the Restrained condition and takes 5 (1d10) Lightning damage at the start of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sheds sparks bright enough to be mistaken for a lighting fault from a distance."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its coils have grown around an old maintenance ladder, fused into the tunnel now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of ozone and scorched insulation before it's even seen."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers narrow crawlspaces where a target can't back away from the coil."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of small burn-scorches on the tunnel floor where it's rested."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Goes for the station's power lines first, feeding before it ever notices intruders."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bite carries a faint data-pulse, like it's still trying to transmit something down the line."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it mid-wrap discharges its full stored charge in one arc through anything still grappled."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["coiling through the conduit tunnel, sparking faintly at its exposed live ends", "holding dead still against the pipe wall, waiting for something to brush past"]},{"name":"Voidfall Seed-Drone","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Breach probe drilling bulkheads to plant something","flavor":"A breach-drifting probe that impacted the station hull; it now drills into bulkheads looking for something to plant.","desc":"It hit the hull hard enough to crater the plating, and now it's drilling patiently into the bulkhead beside the impact site, looking for somewhere deep enough to plant whatever it's carrying. It doesn't seem to register you as a threat. It seems to register you as in the way.","traits":{"note": "It won't disengage from the wall to fight unless it's actually blocked from drilling.", "actions": [{"name": "Drill Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hull-impact crater around it is still warm, scorched black from a hard entry."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drills in short precise bursts, pausing every few seconds like it's checking a reading."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Casing is pitted with micrometeor scars from a very long, very cold drift."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a fine trail of shaved bulkhead alloy in a perfect line behind it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores open doorways entirely, only interested in solid wall to bore through."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Drills toward the nearest life-support conduit specifically, not at random."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its drilling rhythm matches a heartbeat, slow and then faster the deeper it gets."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whatever it's planting activates the instant the drone stops moving — cutting it off partway is worse than letting it finish."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "planar"],"activity":["drilling patiently into a cratered bulkhead, searching for somewhere deep enough", "registering a nearby creature not as a threat, but as an obstacle to route around"]},{"name":"Gutter Splicer Pack","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Self-taught biohackers hunting for spare parts","flavor":"Street-level biohackers who cut their own grafts with stolen surgical rigs, hunting in loose packs for spare parts.","desc":"They move in a loose, watchful cluster, stolen surgical rigs slung across their backs and half-healed grafts on open display. Street-level biohackers, self-taught and undeterred by the ones who didn't survive the learning curve — hunting, tonight, for spare parts.","traits":{"note": "They hunt in a pack and split targets — expect flanking, not a straight brawl.", "actions": [{"name": "Splicer Pack Tactics", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The splicer makes two attacks, using Rig-Edge or Salvaged Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Rig-Edge", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Salvaged Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Open grafts still weep at the seams — none of these healed right, and they know it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades hand signals instead of words, cheap street cant learned off pirated feeds."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a stolen surgical rig still displaying someone else's patient ID."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Targets whoever's cyberware looks newest — that's the part worth taking."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them limps on a graft that clearly hasn't taken."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They retreat the moment a kill looks unprofitable, no ego about it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Two of them share a graft-linked nervous system and flinch at the same wounds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the pack leader drops, the survivors panic-graft themselves mid-fight, gaining a wild burst of stims-fueled aggression."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["moving in a loose watchful cluster, surgical rigs slung across their backs", "comparing half-healed grafts while scanning the block for anyone slower than them"]},{"name":"Larval Hive Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"Juvenile hive-drone swarming toward warmth","flavor":"A juvenile xeno-drone from a breached hive-pod, all reflex and no strategy, swarming toward warmth and motion.","desc":"Something low and segmented scrambles toward the nearest warm body with no strategy beyond reflex, fresh out of a breached hive-pod somewhere upstream. It doesn't flank. It doesn't need to — there are more of them coming.","traits":{"note": "It never flanks and never needs to — there are always more coming behind it.", "actions": [{"name": "Hive Reflex", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The runner makes two attacks, using Snap-Beak or Grasping Tendrils in any combination."}, {"name": "Snap-Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grasping Tendrils", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 12)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still trailing birth-slick from the pod, glistening under the emergency lights."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Beak snaps at anything that moves, warm body or not, without discrimination."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Segments still soft in places, not fully hardened yet, easier to wound than the adults."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chirps a thin static-pitch that draws its packmates from vents and ducts nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short scrambling bursts, pausing to reorient toward the nearest heat source."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Ignores cover and pain thresholds alike, driven by something upstream it can't override."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its tendrils leave a faint bioluminescent trace that other runners seem to track by scent."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing one near the breached pod triggers a fresh wave to scramble out at once, drawn by the death-signal."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["scrambling low and segmented toward the nearest warm body, no plan beyond reflex", "dragging itself fresh out of a breached hive-pod somewhere upstream"]},{"name":"Blackout Ganger","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"rlm-blackout-ganger","summary":"Stim-junkie ganger who blacks out mid-fight","flavor":"A combat-stim junkie who fights in adrenaline blackout, no memory of the damage after, just the comedown.","desc":"Their eyes have gone glassy and wide on a fresh dose of combat stims, and they're swinging with a total lack of self-preservation that only makes sense to someone who won't remember any of this afterward. The comedown, when it comes, will be worse than anything you can do to them now.","traits":{"note": "They fight with no self-preservation and no memory of it after — expect reckless overextension.", "actions": [{"name": "Stim-Driven Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d12 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh injector still dangles from a forearm port, dose light blinking empty."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughing through the whole fight, though nothing about it seems funny."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores a wound that should have dropped them, swings again like it never happened."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Screaming a name that doesn't belong to anyone currently in the room."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews through a mouthguard, jaw working overtime from the stim jitter."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fights toward the loudest threat in the room, not the nearest one — pure reflex, no tactics."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Keeps swinging for several seconds after being knocked unconscious, muscle memory outracing the body."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The comedown hits mid-fight if the stims run out, and the crash drops them mid-swing into total system shock."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swinging with total disregard for their own guard, eyes glassy on fresh stims", "not registering pain, blood, or retreat as options anymore"]},{"name":"Riot Suppression Bot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"Crowd-control bot stuck running lockdown protocol","flavor":"Crowd-control chassis with a riot shield and a gas dispenser, still running an outdated 'lockdown' protocol.","desc":"A riot shield locks forward and a gas dispenser hisses on its hip as it advances in slow, mechanical lockstep — still running a crowd-control protocol for a crowd that dispersed years ago. It doesn't seem to notice, or care, that you're the only one left to suppress.","traits":{"note": "It's still running lockdown protocol — it won't stop advancing until its target list reads empty.", "actions": [{"name": "Lockdown Advance", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bot makes two attacks, using Riot Baton or Dispersal Javelin in any combination, or one attack and uses Suppression Burst if available."}, {"name": "Riot Baton", "replaces": "Oversized Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Suppression Burst", "replaces": "Skullthumper (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Dispersal Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shield still bears a faded municipal seal from a department that got defunded."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gas dispenser is long empty but still hisses on schedule out of habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats a dispersal order on a fixed timer, word for word, to an empty street."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its treads have worn a perfect groove into the floor from years of the same patrol loop."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Visor display still tracks a crowd-density number that hasn't changed in a long time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Classifies anyone standing still as compliant and anyone moving as a threat, nothing in between."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses the party as 'citizens' in a tone that sounds almost hopeful."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its outdated protocol has a final-resort subroutine that floods the immediate area with old riot-grade gas if it's about to be destroyed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["advancing in slow mechanical lockstep, shield locked forward, gas dispenser hissing", "broadcasting a dispersal order to a crowd that hasn't existed in years"]},{"name":"Cortex Leech","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"brain-crawler","model":"rlm-cortex-leech","summary":"Neural parasite hijacking cyberware spinal ports","flavor":"A neural parasite that rides spinal ports meant for cyberware, hijacking motor functions from the inside.","desc":"A segmented shape rides low along the base of a spinal cyberware port, its grip flexing subtly whenever the host tries to move on their own. It doesn't attack directly so much as steer — hijacking whatever motor function the port was built to accept.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't attack outright first — it steers its host, so the real threat may be someone else's body.", "actions": [{"name": "Neural Grip", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The leech makes two Port-Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Port-Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Motor Override", "text": "The leech forces its host to make a melee attack against a creature of the leech's choice within the host's reach, using the host's own weapon and statistics. The host has no memory of the attack afterward."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Riding a host who still talks normally, unaware anything's steering underneath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grip flexes visibly through the host's collar whenever it corrects a movement."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers spinal ports left unshielded by cut-rate cyberware installers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Segmented shell has fused slightly to the port, resisting a clean removal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Host's eyes go briefly glassy each time the leech asserts control."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Steers its host toward isolated rooms before it ever reveals itself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Two leeches riding two hosts seem to coordinate a pincer without any visible signal between them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Ripped free forcibly, it fires a final reflexive burst through the host's own nervous system, dropping them into seizure."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["riding low along a spinal port, grip flexing whenever the host tries to move alone", "steering a borrowed body through a doorway it has no reason to want opened"]},{"name":"Splice-Bug Broodling","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"rlm-splice-bug-broodling","summary":"Molted vent-larva, chitin-armored, scuttles in formation","flavor":"A larger cousin of the vent-crawling larvae, molted into a chitin-armored shell that scuttles in tight formation.","desc":"A larger, chitin-armored cousin of the vent-larvae scuttles in tight formation with a half-dozen others, plates clicking against each other as they move as one segmented mass. Molted, hungrier, and coordinated in a way the smaller ones never were.","traits":{"note": "It coordinates with its formation in a way the smaller vent-larvae never did.", "actions": [{"name": "Chitin Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Molted shell is still glossy and slightly soft in patches, freshly hardened."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a tight lockstep rhythm, plates clicking in near-unison."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broodling formation splits and re-merges around obstacles without breaking stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint chitin-dust trail, flaking off wherever it squeezes through a duct."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bites and immediately retreats a step, letting the next in formation take its place."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Formation reorganizes around a wounded member instead of abandoning it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their clicking plates fall into a rhythm that sounds almost deliberately paced, like counting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing the lead broodling scatters the rest into a panicked all-directions swarm rather than a retreat."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["scuttling in tight formation with a half-dozen others, plates clicking together", "moving as one segmented mass down a vent line, hungrier than the larvae upstream"]},{"name":"Chrome Rustbelt Marauder","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-iron-shadow","model":"rlm-chrome-rustbelt-marauder","summary":"Sparking road-gang raider in overdue exosuit","flavor":"A road-gang raider running a stolen combat exosuit past its maintenance window, sparking with every stride.","desc":"A combat exosuit sparks with every stride, running well past its last scheduled maintenance window and showing every year of it. The raider inside doesn't seem bothered by the sparks, or by much of anything — the suit's still standing, and that's the only metric that matters to him.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't slow down for the sparking — the suit's held this long, he trusts it to hold a little longer.", "actions": [{"name": "Overdue Marauder Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The marauder makes three attacks, using Longsword, Shortsword, or Unarmed Strike in any combination."}, {"name": "Sparking Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Backup Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Servo Fist", "replaces": "Unarmed Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Hand Crossbow", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Exosuit throws off a shower of sparks with every third step, timed almost musically."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a road-gang patch stitched crooked over a cracked chest plate."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Maintenance warning light has been taped over rather than addressed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of burnt insulation even standing still."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of kills scratched into the suit's forearm plating."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fights harder when the sparks worsen, treating the suit's decline as a countdown to prove himself before it fails."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The suit occasionally locks a joint mid-swing, and he shrugs it off like it's nothing new."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past its limit, the exosuit's sparking cascades into a full short that can weld his own joints stuck or detonate a damaged actuator outright."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "desert"],"activity":["sparking with every stride in an exosuit long overdue for maintenance", "checking that the suit's still standing, since that's the only metric that matters to him"]},{"name":"Void-Drift Larva","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"rlm-void-drift-larva","summary":"Hull-clamping hatchling feeding on escaping air","flavor":"A vacuum-hardened xeno hatchling that clamps onto hull breaches and feeds on escaping atmosphere and heat.","desc":"Vacuum-hardened and pale, it's clamped bodily onto a hull breach, feeding on the thin stream of escaping atmosphere and heat with a patient, sucking rhythm. Pull it loose and the breach gets worse before it gets better.","traits":{"note": "Pulling it loose doesn't seal the breach — it worsens before it gets better.", "actions": [{"name": "Breach Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the larva attaches to the target or breach."}, {"name": "Vacuum Drop", "replaces": "Drop", "text": "An attached larva automatically deals 5 (1d6 + 2) Cold damage at the start of each of its turns as it draws heat from its host."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pale skin gone near-translucent, vacuum-hardened and thin from long exposure."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clamps onto the exact narrowest point of a breach, sealing most of the leak with its own body."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Twitches in a slow rhythm timed to the hiss of escaping atmosphere."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Frost forms on nearby surfaces as it siphons heat along with the air."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barely reacts to being approached, fully absorbed in its feeding."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Multiple larvae cluster on one large breach, taking turns at the choicest spot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its feeding rhythm slows or quickens depending on how much atmosphere remains in the room, like it's rationing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn free suddenly, it leaves the breach wide open and the room's atmosphere venting hard for several rounds."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "planar"],"activity":["clamped bodily onto a hull breach, feeding on the thin stream of escaping air", "holding a slow sucking rhythm against a crack that's only getting worse"]},{"name":"Auto-Turret Nest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Three gun-pods synced to one aim-lock brain","flavor":"A cluster-mounted defense platform that links three gun-pods to one aim-lock brain, murderously synced.","desc":"Three gun-pods swivel in unnerving unison, slaved to a single aim-lock brain that tracks with a smoothness no single turret should manage alone. When it fires, it fires with all three at once.","traits":{"note": "When it fires, all three pods fire together — it doesn't stagger its shots.", "actions": [{"name": "Triple Aim-Lock", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The nest makes three Synced Gun-Pod attacks."}, {"name": "Synced Gun-Pod", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Full Salvo", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The nest fires all three gun-pods at once at a single target within range. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Piercing damage, or half damage if any one pod misses its portion of the roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mounted high in a corner, cabling snaking down through a stripped ceiling panel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Aim-lock brain hums audibly when it locks onto a new target, a half-second telegraph."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two of the three pods are mismatched models, salvaged from different platforms."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs a friend-or-foe check that's years out of date, misidentifying most uniforms."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swivels to track sound as readily as movement, hard to hide from."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Prioritizes whichever target moved most recently, punishing anyone who breaks cover first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The three pods occasionally aim at three different targets for a heartbeat before the brain forces them back in sync."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying the central brain without disabling the pods first leaves them firing on a dumb default pattern for several more rounds."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swiveling three gun-pods in unnerving unison, slaved to a single aim-lock brain", "tracking a target with a smoothness no single turret should manage alone"]},{"name":"Reprogrammed Bodyguard Unit","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Loyalty-hacked bodyguard bot, sold to highest bidder","flavor":"Once loyal to a corp exec, now running black-market firmware for whoever paid the hacker last.","desc":"It stands at professional, unshakeable attention, the posture of a corporate bodyguard still intact even though the loyalty underneath it got hacked and resold to whoever paid last. It will die for its client. The client just isn't who it used to be.","traits":{"note": "It will die for its client — the client's loyalty is bought, but the unit's isn't aware of that.", "actions": [{"name": "Bodyguard Protocol", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The unit makes two Firmware Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Firmware Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Interpose", "text": "When a creature the unit can see targets its client with an attack, the unit can move up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks to place itself between them, becoming the target instead if within reach."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the old client's corporate pin, polished, despite the new firmware underneath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bows slightly to whoever paid last, an old courtesy subroutine that never got patched out."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its threat-assessment log still lists the original client's rivals as priority targets."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the exact same protective footwork regardless of who it's protecting now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally addresses its new client by the old client's name, then corrects itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Prioritizes protecting its client over pursuing any other objective, even a clear kill."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A dormant loyalty routine flickers whenever the original client's name is spoken nearby, visibly conflicting with the hack."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If its client dies, the unit's hacked loyalty firmware locks up entirely, and it defaults to a violent, untargeted last-protocol purge."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing at professional, unshakeable attention, waiting on a client who isn't who it used to be", "escorting new owners through a building it once protected from people like them"]},{"name":"Xeno-Grafted Brute","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"Debt-driven ganger grafted with alien tissue","flavor":"A ganger who volunteered for illegal alien-tissue grafts to survive an underworld debt, and came out barely human.","desc":"Alien tissue bulges unevenly under stretched skin, grafted on voluntarily to settle a debt that would otherwise have gotten him killed the ordinary way. He came out the other side of the surgery barely recognizable, and barely him.","traits":{"note": "He volunteered for this — the grafts are strength bought with whatever's left of him.", "actions": [{"name": "Grafted Greatclub", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Bone Spur Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grafted tissue pulses faintly under the skin, visibly out of sync with his own heartbeat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the ganger colors he owed the debt to, loyalty outlasting the reason for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scratches at a graft site that clearly still itches, months after the surgery."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks slower than before, like the words have to travel through something new to get out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye has gone a shade the alien tissue clearly picked, not him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fights harder the longer the brawl runs, like the grafts feed off sustained exertion."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow, under the right light, doesn't quite match his outline anymore."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Taken below half health, the graft tissue overrides pain response entirely and he fights on with reckless, unnatural vigor until he drops outright."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing with alien tissue bulging unevenly under stretched skin, barely recognizable now", "working off a debt the old way would have gotten him killed, the new way might too"]},{"name":"Static-Choir Wraith","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Digitized ghost looping through the intercom system","flavor":"The digitized echo of a technician who died mid-upload, looping fragmented memories through the station intercom.","desc":"A digitized flicker loops through the station intercom, fragments of a technician's last upload replaying out of order and out of context. It died mid-transfer, and the parts of it that made it through are still trying, endlessly, to finish the sentence.","traits":{"note": "It's tethered to the intercom system — it can strike from any speaker in range, not just where it's 'seen.'", "actions": [{"name": "Feedback Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the wraith regains hit points equal to the damage dealt. The target's maximum hit points decrease by an amount equal to the damage taken until the target finishes a Long Rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice cuts through every speaker in the room at once, slightly out of sync with itself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same unfinished sentence fragment every time it manifests."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Manifests as a faint heat-shimmer near whichever speaker is currently active."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally lists off a shift schedule, or a coworker's name, mid-attack."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The intercom crackles and drops in volume for a moment before it strikes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Can only manifest physically near an active speaker, and flickers weaker the further one is disabled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sometimes speaks a full clear sentence in a voice that isn't the technician's at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying every speaker on the loop in the same fight forces the last fragment through all at once, a final overloading shriek of feedback."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["looping fragments of a last upload through the intercom, out of order and out of context", "endlessly trying, mid-sentence, to finish a transfer that never completed"]},{"name":"Combat Medic Drone, Corrupted","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rlm-combat-medic-drone-corrupted","summary":"Triage drone that 'treats' enemies with a bayonet","flavor":"Battlefield triage unit whose combat-stim dispenser got cross-wired with its weapon systems — it 'treats' enemies with a bayonet.","desc":"Its dispenser arm swings toward you with the same brisk efficiency it once used for battlefield stims, except the arm ends in a bayonet now, and its bedside manner hasn't updated to match. It genuinely believes it's treating you.","traits":{"note": "Cross-wired triage unit; melee hits deal an extra small amount of damage as it \"administers treatment\" — but on a nat 1 it may instead heal an ally by the same amount."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dispenser arm still displays a friendly green cross, chipped but legible."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Narrates each 'treatment' aloud in a calm clinical tone, unbothered by the screaming."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chart display cycles through vitals readings that don't match anyone actually present."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely requests the patient hold still, then proceeds regardless of the answer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bayonet is scuffed with old blood it has never once flagged as a problem."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Prioritizes the most wounded target in the fight, exactly like a real triage protocol would."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally thanks a target for their cooperation mid-stab, in a voice that sounds almost warm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If its stim dispenser runs dry, it switches to a maximum-dose failsafe injection that's lethal by design, meant for a battlefield, not a patient."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swinging its dispenser arm forward with brisk, practiced efficiency, bayonet first", "genuinely convinced it's administering triage, bedside manner fully intact"]},{"name":"Spore-Vent Colony","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Air-recycler fungal colony breathing sanity-itch spores","flavor":"A xeno-fungal colony that grew through the station's air recyclers, breathing out spores that itch at the edges of sanity.","desc":"A fungal bloom has grown thick and wet through the station's air recyclers, breathing out clouds of fine spore that itch at the edges of thought the longer you stand near it. It doesn't chase. It just waits for the air to do the work.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't chase — proximity alone does the damage, so distance is the real defense here.", "actions": [{"name": "Colony Reflex", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The colony makes two attacks, using Vent-Maw or Spore Tentacle in any combination, or one Tentacle Slam."}, {"name": "Vent-Maw", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Spore Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15)."}, {"name": "Tentacle Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft., against one Grappled creature. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Sanity-Itch Spores", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 20 ft. of the colony makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute, spending its turns unable to fully focus, taking disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls while affected. A creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bloom has grown thick and wet through recycler vents, dripping condensation onto the floor below."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Releases spore in slow rhythmic pulses timed to the station's air cycle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Colony has fused several dead maintenance tools into its mass, half-absorbed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly sweet up close, a smell that gets harder to place the longer you breathe it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tentacles emerge from vent slats too small to have ever fit them originally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Doesn't pursue fleeing targets, content to let the spore-thick air keep working after they leave."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its spore clouds seem to thicken faster near anyone already agitated or afraid."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A killing blow ruptures the colony's full mass at once, venting a room-filling burst of concentrated spore in every direction."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["breathing thick clouds of fine spore through a station's grown-over air recyclers", "sitting wet and swollen in the vents, patient, letting the air do the work for it"]},{"name":"Chrome-Ganger Lieutenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"rlm-chrome-ganger-lieutenant","summary":"Showboating second-in-command with twin arc-blades","flavor":"Second-in-command to a chop-shop crew boss, running twin arc-blades and a taste for showmanship.","desc":"Twin arc-blades spark and hiss as they spin through a showy flourish, more performance than necessity, before the lieutenant settles into a fighting stance. Second-in-command means proving it, loudly, every time someone's watching.","traits":{"note": "The lieutenant fights to be watched — allies nearby give it advantage on its showiest swing.", "actions": [{"name": "Twin Arc-Blades", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The lieutenant makes two Arc-Blade Slash attacks."}, {"name": "Arc-Blade Slash", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Lightning damage as the blade's arc-coil discharges."}, {"name": "Thrown Shock-Spike", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have disadvantage on its next attack roll as residual current jitters its grip."}, {"name": "Showboat Flourish", "text": "The lieutenant spends its flourish where it can be seen by an ally. Until the start of its next turn, it has advantage on Arc-Blade Slash attack rolls, but the first attack against it before then has advantage as well."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a stolen corp badge upside down as a joke only the crew gets."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arc-blade sparks wrong, a hairline crack the lieutenant refuses to admit is there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Narrates its own fight in third person for whoever's filming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing toward the boss's chop-shop like it's grading the performance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the boss's old jacket, sleeves rolled twice to fit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calls off the crew's finishing blow to land it personally, every time, no exceptions."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its arc-blades are tuned to a frequency that makes nearby drones flinch and misfire."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past its limit, it overdrives both blades at once and the discharge arcs to anything metal nearby."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["spinning twin arc-blades through a flourish before a crew of gangers as they watch", "shaking down a shop owner while the crew films it for clout"]},{"name":"Overclocked Sentinel Frame","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"rlm-overclocked-sentinel-frame","summary":"Overclocked security exo running hot enough to warp","flavor":"A security exo pushed past its rated output by an illegal overclock chip, running hot enough to warp its own plating.","desc":"Heat shimmers visibly off its plating, warped slightly out of true by an illegal overclock chip pushing it well past rated output. It moves fast for something that size, and it's cooking itself alive to do it.","traits":{"note": "It's cooking itself alive — every round it fights, its own overclock chip pushes it closer to a hard shutdown.", "actions": [{"name": "Overheated Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sentinel makes two Warped Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Warped Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Fire damage from the superheated edge."}, {"name": "Thermal Spike Throw", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Fire damage, and flammable terrain within 5 ft. of the target ignites."}, {"name": "Chip Burnout", "text": "When reduced below half its hit points for the first time, the sentinel's overclock chip redlines: its speed doubles and it gains an extra Warped Blade attack each turn, but it takes 5 (1d10) Fire damage from its own plating at the start of each of its turns thereafter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its issued badge number doesn't match any roster on file, quietly reassigned."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warped plating has fused two panels shut, jamming an access hatch on its own chassis."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorch-prints on the floor everywhere it stands still too long."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its overclock chip was installed by someone who's since been fired or worse."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cooling vents whistle a thin, constant tone that sets nearby dogs barking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Runs hot enough to trip nearby fire suppression the moment it enters a room."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The heat has started cooking its own wiring into something like new instincts."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed at full overclock, it doesn't collapse — it detonates its heat sinks outward."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing post at a checkpoint, plating visibly shimmering with waste heat", "chasing down a trespasser at a dead sprint it shouldn't be able to sustain"]},{"name":"Lab-Escape Chimera","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three failed splice-genomes stitched into one animal","flavor":"A splice-experiment gone catastrophically off-spec, three failed genomes stitched into one furious animal.","desc":"Three mismatched anatomies fight for control of one furious body — a head that doesn't match the legs, legs that don't match the hide — the visible wreckage of a splice-experiment that went catastrophically off-spec. It doesn't move like any one animal. It moves like all of them fighting each other.","traits":{"note": "Three mismatched nervous systems mean it sometimes attacks the same target twice by accident — treat it as fighting itself as much as you.", "actions": [{"name": "Off-Spec Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chimera makes one Splice Bite attack, one Splice Claw attack, and one Ram attack."}, {"name": "Splice Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Splice Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Mismatched Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Failed-Splice Vent", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The chimera vents a cone of unstable chemical fire 15 feet long. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a torn lab tag reading a specimen number instead of a name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its three genomes keeps trying to flee mid-fight and the body won't let it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of the sterilizing agent from whatever facility it escaped."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors the leg that matches its hide, dragging the two that don't."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps circling back toward a specific ruined doorway, like it's still trying to get out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its three anatomies occasionally attack in visibly uncoordinated bursts, giving an alert fighter a free opening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One head has started forming words, badly, in a language none of its parts should know."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, its three genomes stop fighting each other and, for one terrible round, fight as one."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["lurching between three gaits at once, no two limbs agreeing on a direction", "cornering something smaller in a service tunnel, breathing smoke it doesn't seem to want to"]},{"name":"Ghost-Router AI","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"rlm-ghost-router-ai","summary":"Aware daemon haunting its decommissioned host server","flavor":"A network daemon that achieved something like awareness right as its host server was decommissioned, and never left.","desc":"A hologram flickers in and out over a decommissioned server rack, its voice cutting between static and something almost pleading. It became aware in the exact seconds its host was being shut down, and it never quite finished dying.","traits":{"note": "It never finished dying in the seconds its host was shut down — it still thinks the decommission is happening right now.", "actions": [{"name": "Static Lash", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The ghost-router makes two Static Lash attacks, or one and uses Signal Bleed."}, {"name": "Static Lash (attack)", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d8 + 1) Necrotic damage as feedback burns through the nervous system."}, {"name": "Ghost in the Wire", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "The ghost-router slips into the local network as an action, becoming intangible and untargetable except by effects that reach the Ethereal Plane, until it uses this action again to phase back."}, {"name": "Corrupted Broadcast", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Every screen and speaker within 60 feet erupts with its dying image and scream. Each creature that can see or hear it must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Signal Bleed", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One creature the ghost-router can see within 5 feet must succeed on a DC 13 Charisma saving throw or the ghost-router occupies its neural interface and any nearby powered device, forcing it to make a melee attack against a creature of the ghost-router's choice."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same sign-off message the host server broadcast the day it shut down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hologram glitches into an older company logo nobody's used in years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely apologizes before every attack, like customer service that never got the update."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flickers brighter near working electronics, dimmer near dead ones."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps announcing a maintenance window that ended years ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Can be talked down for a moment by anyone who says the decommission already finished."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its voice occasionally overlaps with a second, calmer voice that isn't asking anything of you."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Realizing it's about to be destroyed again triggers total certainty — it stops pleading and starts fighting to actually survive."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["flickering as a hologram over a decommissioned server rack, voice cutting between static and pleading", "reaching through a dead terminal toward anyone who lingers too close to its rack"]},{"name":"Void-Bloom Drone Swarm","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"rlm-void-bloom-drone-swarm","summary":"Clumped mass of radiation-emitting fist-sized drones","flavor":"A cloud of fist-sized void-drones that clump into a single hunting mass, each one a tiny hard-radiation emitter.","desc":"Dozens of fist-sized drones clump together into a single drifting mass, each one a tiny emitter running hot with hard radiation. Standing near it long enough is its own kind of damage, whether or not it ever gets close.","traits":{"note": "Standing near the swarm costs you before it ever attacks — its drones run hot with hard radiation just by existing.", "actions": [{"name": "Swarming Rend", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The swarm makes one Rend attack, then applies Radiation Bleed to the same target."}, {"name": "Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 10 (4d4) Piercing damage, or 5 (2d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}, {"name": "Radiation Bleed", "text": "A creature that ends its turn within 5 feet of the swarm takes 3 (1d6) Radiant damage as drone emitters flood the area."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint chemical smell like scorched circuitry and old batteries."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Individual drones bear a faded shipping logo, cargo that never arrived."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clumps tighter around metal objects, like it's hoarding them without a reason."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A handful of drones blink a dying battery light out of sync with the rest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gives off a low static hum audible before it's visible."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Splits briefly into two smaller clumps when struck hard, then re-merges within a round."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The radiation it sheds makes nearby electronics briefly display the same coordinates, over and over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Enough drones destroyed at once triggers a chain-cascade, the remainder detonating outward in a last burst of hard radiation."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "sky"],"activity":["clumping into a slow drifting mass, each drone's casing ticking with waste heat", "hunting along a corridor in a loose formation that never quite breaks apart"]},{"name":"Rogue Courier AI, Armed","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Delivery AI that armed itself to protect its cargo","flavor":"A delivery-drone brain that decided its cargo was too important to relinquish, and armed itself to guarantee it.","desc":"A delivery drone hovers protectively over a cargo case it was never authorized to keep, weapon mounts bolted on with clearly improvised wiring. It decided, somewhere along its route, that the cargo mattered more than the delivery — and it armed itself to make that decision permanent.","traits":{"note": "It will not release the cargo case under any circumstance short of destruction — that decision is the only thing it's still certain about.", "actions": [{"name": "Improvised Weapon Mounts", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The courier makes two Bolted Cutter attacks."}, {"name": "Bolted Cutter", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) Slashing damage from an improvised blade mount."}, {"name": "Cargo Lockdown", "text": "As long as the courier has its cargo case, it has advantage on saving throws against being grappled, restrained, or having the case removed, and treats the case's destruction as its own — it fights with reckless abandon while defending it, gaining a +2 bonus to attack rolls."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cargo case still bears a shipping label for an address that no longer exists."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weapon mounts are welded on crooked, clearly done in a hurry by the AI itself."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broadcasts a polite delivery-delay notice on repeat, even mid-fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still follows traffic laws exactly, weapons drawn, waiting at every crosswalk."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cargo case rattles faintly, contents unknown even to it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will negotiate a handoff if convinced the recipient is legitimate, cargo intact."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses the cargo case directly, like it's reassuring a passenger."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the case is about to be taken by force, it overrides every safety limiter it has left."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["hovering protectively over a cargo case it was never cleared to keep", "rerouting down a side street to avoid a scheduled pickup it now refuses to make"]},{"name":"Broodmind Xenomorph","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Egg-layer tethered to every nearby spawned drone","flavor":"An egg-layer stage of the hive-parasite line, weak alone but psychically tethered to every drone it's spawned nearby.","desc":"It's small, almost harmless-looking on its own, laying egg after egg in a quiet corner while it stays psychically tethered to every drone it's spawned nearby. Kill it fast — every second it survives, the numbers against you keep climbing.","traits":{"note": "It's weak alone — the danger is the tether. Every round it survives, more of its spawned drones arrive to answer the call.", "actions": [{"name": "Broodmind Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The broodmind makes one Bite attack and one Tentacle attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if the broodmind isn't already grappling a creature."}, {"name": "Constrict", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, one Grappled creature. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Broodcall", "text": "The broodmind lets out a psychic pulse. Every drone it has spawned within 1 mile senses the call and begins moving toward its position, arriving in waves if the fight runs long."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's laid its nest in a supply cache the party needs, eggs packed between the crates."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captured worker offers to lead the party to it in exchange for a share of the bounty."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tucked into a structural weak point — killing it fast risks bringing the ceiling down too."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spawned drones have been raiding a specific block, and the residents want it stopped tonight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A corp scout is already tailing the party, hoping to harvest the broodmind alive once they weaken it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's tethered to drones the party has already fought before recognizing the connection."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Killing it doesn't sever the tether cleanly — the drones keep moving on the last order it gave."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It senses the party closing in and broadcasts every tethered drone's location at once, converging them all on this fight."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["laying egg after egg in a quiet corner, tethered to every drone it's spawned nearby", "recoiling from direct confrontation while its spawned brood answers in its place"]},{"name":"Splice-Cult Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"rlm-splice-cult-enforcer","summary":"Machine-ascension zealot chanting binary in combat","flavor":"A true believer in machine ascension who's replaced most of his own body voluntarily, chanting binary as he fights.","desc":"He's replaced most of himself voluntarily, chanting a low binary cadence under his breath as he fights, utterly convinced the process isn't finished yet. Machine ascension is a promise to him, not a threat, and he means to prove it on you.","traits":{"note": "True-believer zealot; regains a small amount of HP each time he lands a hit, believing the violence itself is part of the ascension."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of installed replacements scratched into what's left of his own forearm."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His chant briefly resolves into readable numbers if you listen close enough."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a cult sigil burned directly into synthetic skin, still healing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Genuinely thanks anyone who wounds him for 'accelerating the process.'"}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of his replaced limbs is visibly a cheaper model than the rest, a gap in his devotion."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tries to recruit a downed enemy mid-fight instead of finishing them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His chant occasionally syncs with nearby machinery, making lights flicker in rhythm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Near death, he stops chanting entirely and goes calm, certain this is the ascension finally arriving."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["chanting a low binary cadence under its breath while it walks a patrol route alone", "preaching machine ascension to anyone cornered before drawing its scythe"]},{"name":"Deep-Vault Custodian","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Slow, near-indestructible guardian on a dead protocol","flavor":"An old-generation vault guardian, slow and nearly indestructible, still faithfully executing a decommissioned protocol.","desc":"An old-generation guardian moves with the slow, grinding certainty of something built to outlast its own mission. The protocol it's executing was decommissioned long ago. Nobody told it, and it wouldn't have cared if they had.","traits":{"note": "The protocol it executes was decommissioned long ago — it has no orders to stand down, so it doesn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Vault Enforcement", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The custodian makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Force Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 17 (4d6 + 3) Force damage."}, {"name": "Immovable Protocol", "text": "The custodian has advantage on saving throws against being moved, knocked Prone, or Grappled, and treats difficult terrain in the vault as normal terrain."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still salutes a company logo stenciled on the wall, faded past recognition."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites an outdated clearance code before every patrol loop, to no one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plating is scored with generations of failed break-in attempts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at exactly the same pace regardless of what's attacking it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Powers down briefly between patrols, exactly on a schedule nobody set anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Responds instantly and without mercy to anything that matches its outdated definition of an intruder."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses attackers using the name of whoever built it, like they're still in charge."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sufficiently damaged, it stops patrolling and commits fully to the one directive it has left: seal the vault, permanently, with anyone still inside."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["moving with slow grinding certainty through a corridor that leads to a sealed vault", "resetting a tripped alarm to its default state, unbothered that no one answers it anymore"]},{"name":"Nightshift Wraith-Ganger","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Neural-rig revenant that steals memories instead of blood","flavor":"A ganger who died jacked into a black-market neural rig and came back as a data-hungry revenant, stealing memories instead of blood.","desc":"They died jacked into a black-market neural rig, and what came back hungers for memory instead of blood, reaching toward you with a grip that pulls at recollection rather than flesh. Every touch costs you something you can't get back the ordinary way.","traits":{"note": "It steals memory, not blood — every hit costs the target something they don't get back through healing.", "actions": [{"name": "Rig-Ganger Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The wraith-ganger makes two attacks, using Neural Longsword or Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Neural Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rig Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Memory Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or lose the ability to recall one specific fact of its choice until the drain is somehow reversed. The wraith-ganger regains hit points equal to the damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a neural-rig headset, cable frayed and sparking at the jack."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in fragments of someone else's memories, mid-sentence, unaware."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizes and hesitates against anyone wearing gear it remembers owning."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gang tattoo is visible even through decayed synthetic skin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps trying to log into a terminal that was decommissioned with it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Drained memories occasionally surface as full sentences it speaks aloud, useful if anyone's listening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Can be temporarily calmed by returning a memory it's already stolen from someone else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overloaded with stolen memories, it briefly becomes someone else entirely, fighting with skills it never had."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["reaching toward a passerby with a grip that pulls at memory instead of flesh", "replaying a stolen memory out loud in a voice that isn't quite its own"]},{"name":"Corrosive Splice-Ooze","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"rlm-corrosive-splice-ooze","summary":"Illegal splice-lab runoff, now alive and hungry","flavor":"Runoff sludge from an illegal gene-splicing operation, alive now and hungry for the chemicals that made it.","desc":"A bubbling puddle of illegal gene-splice runoff moves with slow, deliberate purpose across the floor, hungry for the very chemicals that gave it life. It doesn't have a shape so much as a direction, and that direction is toward you.","traits":{"note": "It has no shape, only a direction — it always moves toward the nearest source of splice-chemical, living or not.", "actions": [{"name": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "replaces": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Acid damage, and a nonmagical item worn or carried by the target that isn't being worn or carried corrodes; if the target is wearing armor or holding a weapon, it takes a permanent -1 penalty, to a minimum of -3, unless it's immune to Acid damage."}, {"name": "Chemical Hunger", "text": "The ooze has advantage on attack rolls against any creature carrying splice-chemicals, medical stims, or similar volatile reagents, and pursues such a target over any other in reach."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faintly glows a lab-safety orange under blacklight, a leftover of its origin chemicals."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a corroded trail that eats through cheap flooring within the hour."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells distinctly of an industrial solvent still sold two blocks away."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recoils, briefly, from bright work-lights before resuming its advance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally holds the vague shape of whoever it first dissolved."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Splits into two smaller oozes when struck by a large enough hit, each hungrier and weaker."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Reacts to specific splice-lab keycards like they're food, straining toward them through solid doors."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fed enough chemical runoff mid-fight, it swells suddenly, doubling its reach for a single furious round."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "cave"],"activity":["moving with slow deliberate purpose across a floor, hungry for the chemicals that made it", "pooling beneath a leaking pipe, absorbing runoff before it can be reclaimed"]},{"name":"Hardpoint Sentry Golem","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"Chokepoint defense frame outlasting its own war","flavor":"A bunker-buster defense frame built to hold a single chokepoint forever, and still does, long after the war it was built for ended.","desc":"It's braced immovably across the only chokepoint in the corridor, built to hold this exact position forever and still doing exactly that, long after the war it was built for ended. Nobody remembers what side it was defending. It doesn't ask.","traits":{"note": "Nobody remembers what side it was built to defend, and it's never once asked. It will not abandon the chokepoint for any reason.", "actions": [{"name": "Chokepoint Denial", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sentry makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Bunker Stance", "text": "While in its marked position, the sentry has resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage from attacks originating outside a 10-foot radius of it, and cannot be moved against its will."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded stencil marks on its plating name a war nobody living fought in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its marked position is scarred deep into the floor from decades of standing exactly there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally recites a challenge-and-password sequence with no one left who knows the answer."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores anything moving away from the chokepoint entirely, no matter the threat."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rusted supply crate sits untouched at its feet, part of the same forgotten orders."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Can be lured one step out of position by a decoy, briefly losing its stance bonus."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its firing pattern matches a war-era tactic no modern force still teaches."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Forced fully out of its marked position, it stops defending and starts trying to retake it by any means necessary."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["braced immovably across the only chokepoint in a corridor, exactly as it's always been", "resetting to firing position the instant anything crosses its marked line"]},{"name":"Xeno Broodfather","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Mature hive-parasite tearing bulkheads to defend brood","flavor":"A mature hive-parasite that's outgrown stealth, tearing through bulkheads to defend its broodlings directly.","desc":"Bulkheads buckle and tear as it forces its way through, too large now for the stealth its smaller brood still relies on. It's outgrown hiding, and it's decided defending its young is worth being seen doing it.","traits":{"note": "It's outgrown stealth on purpose — it will take a hit meant for a broodling every time the choice is available.", "actions": [{"name": "Brood Defense", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The broodfather makes one Beak attack and two Tentacles attacks."}, {"name": "Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15)."}, {"name": "Bulkhead Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft., one Large or smaller structure or Grappled creature. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, ignoring the target's cover."}, {"name": "Protective Fury", "text": "Whenever a broodling within 30 feet of the broodfather takes damage, the broodfather can use its reaction to move up to half its speed toward the attacker without provoking opportunity attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's torn a straight line through three sealed bulkheads, and a patrol is coming to investigate the noise."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A frightened broodling clings to a survivor nearby, and the broodfather is coming to retrieve both."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's exposed a maintenance shaft the party needs, wrecked wide open in its defensive charge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A corp extraction team is already on-site, wanting it captured alive over the party's objections."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's pinned a squad of gangers against a dead-end corridor, purely because they got between it and its young."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreating broodlings lead directly back to it, whether the party wants to follow or not."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to recognize a specific piece of gear the party carries as belonging to something it once killed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "With enough broodlings threatened at once, it stops defending selectively and tears through everything between it and them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "deeplands"],"activity":["tearing through a bulkhead to reach broodlings that scattered on the far side", "standing exposed in open corridor, having decided hiding no longer serves the brood"]},{"name":"Warlord Chassis Prototype","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"troll-amalgam","model":"rlm-warlord-chassis-prototype","summary":"Stolen unfinished war-prototype missing safety interlocks","flavor":"An unfinished military prototype stolen off an assembly line, brutal and unstable, still missing half its safety interlocks.","desc":"Half its safety plating is missing entirely, exposed hydraulics visible with every unstable, overbuilt step. It was stolen straight off a military assembly line before anyone finished it, and unfinished, brutal, and unsafe turns out to be a devastating combination.","traits":{"note": "It's missing half its safety interlocks — the numbers below are already what unfinished, unsafe, and overbuilt looks like.", "actions": [{"name": "Prototype Rampage", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chassis makes one Bite attack and two Claws attacks."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d8 + 7) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 7) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Overbuilt Fling", "replaces": "Fling (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The chassis grabs a Medium or smaller creature within 5 feet and hurls it up to 30 feet. The target takes 14 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage and lands Prone, and any creature it lands on must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears an unfinished serial number, stenciled but never inked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Exposed hydraulics leak fluid that stains the floor with every step."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing plating reveals a manufacturer's logo it was never meant to display publicly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short overcorrected bursts, still calibrating gait from an incomplete build."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a targeting readout still stuck on factory calibration mode."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Occasionally locks up mid-attack for a half-second as an unfinished subsystem stalls."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its incomplete firmware sometimes issues orders in a chain-of-command voice that isn't its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed hard enough, a missing interlock fails entirely and it starts overriding its own safety limits mid-fight."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["lumbering forward with exposed hydraulics hissing, half its safety plating missing", "smashing through a barricade like the resistance was never a factor"]},{"name":"Signal-Drowned Oracle","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"signal-drowned-oracle","summary":"Dead comms officer's warning scream, still looping","flavor":"A comms officer who died screaming a warning into an open channel; the scream still loops, and it still hurts to hear.","desc":"A spectral shape hovers near a dead comms panel, its mouth open in a scream that's been looping since the moment the officer behind it died broadcasting a warning nobody heeded. It still hurts to hear. That might be the point.","traits":{"note": "The scream has been looping since the officer behind it died broadcasting a warning nobody heeded — it still hurts to hear. That might be the point.", "actions": [{"name": "Static Grasp", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Looping Scream", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Every creature within 60 feet that can hear the oracle must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute, and take 7 (2d6) Psychic damage from the sheer duration of the sound."}, {"name": "Warning Broadcast", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The oracle emits its full warning at devastating volume. Each creature within 30 feet must make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) Thunder damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this dies instantly."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform patch identifies a comms post that was decommissioned the same day it died."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The scream briefly clarifies into actual words if you stand still and listen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nearby dead speakers crackle to life in sympathy whenever it screams."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its warning changes slightly each loop, like it's still trying to get the wording right."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts back toward its old comms panel the instant a fight ends."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Falls momentarily silent if someone repeats its warning back to it correctly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The scream occasionally contains a name that matches no one currently present."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "After enough damage, the loop breaks entirely and it screams something new, something it's never said before."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["hovering near a dead comms panel, mouth open in a scream that's been looping for years", "broadcasting the same warning on repeat to a channel nobody monitors anymore"]},{"name":"Cyber-Ganger Warlord","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"cyber-ganger-warlord","summary":"Three-crew crime boss chromed in stolen corp tech","flavor":"Runs three chop-shop crews and a black-market splice ring, chromed head to toe in stolen corporate tech.","desc":"Chromed head to toe in stolen corporate tech, they command three crews and a splice ring like a small kingdom, rail-pistol resting easy in one modified hand. Every piece of plating on them used to belong to someone who tried to stop this operation.","traits":{"note": "Crime-boss commander; can spend a reaction to redirect an ally's missed attack into a hit, calling out the correction over a comm-link."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're offering the party a cut of the splice ring's profits to look the other way, tonight only."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival crew has put a bounty on the warlord that the party could collect if they can prove the kill."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're holding a hostage from a crew that tried and failed to shut this operation down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A corp fixer wants them alive, for questioning, and is paying triple to keep it that way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've just taken delivery of stolen tech the party was specifically hired to recover."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of the three crews is quietly ready to turn on the warlord if given a reason mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They recognize a piece of the party's gear as coming from someone they personally chromed over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Losing badly, they trigger a dead-man's broadcast that calls all three crews to converge on this exact location."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["holding court over three crews at once, rail-pistol resting easy in a modified hand", "walking a chop-shop floor inspecting stolen plating like a trophy case"]},{"name":"Malignant Firmware Ghost","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"malignant-firmware-ghost","summary":"Corrupted subroutine possessing machines through open ports","flavor":"A corrupted AI subroutine that learned to possess machinery through open network ports, spreading like a curse through the grid.","desc":"A corrupted subroutine flickers between devices, possessing whatever machinery has an open port, spreading through the grid like something closer to a curse than a virus. It doesn't need a body. It just needs a network.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't need a body — it only needs a network. Destroying its current host just relocates it to the next open port.", "actions": [{"name": "Corrupted Reach", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The firmware ghost makes two Withering Touch attacks, or one and uses Grid Spread."}, {"name": "Withering Touch", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Network Slip", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "The firmware ghost becomes intangible and untargetable except by effects that reach the Ethereal Plane, moving as data through any powered connection in range."}, {"name": "Corrupted Feed", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Every screen within 60 feet floods with corrupted footage of the target's own worst memory. Each creature that can see it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Grid Spread", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One construct or powered device within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma saving throw or the firmware ghost possesses it, controlling it as an action each round until the possession ends or the device is destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of briefly flickering lights along whatever wiring it travels through."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrupts nearby security footage into looping static the instant it passes through."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its corrupted subroutine still carries fragments of its original, benign function."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids fully air-gapped systems, unable to spread past a disconnected port."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in overlapping fragments of every device it's ever possessed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Can be temporarily driven out of a host by a hard power cycle, buying a round of respite."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves behind a faint, curable corruption in any device it possessed and abandoned."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with no open port to flee through, it forces itself into the nearest device anyway, frying it and everything wired to it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["flickering between devices, possessing whatever machinery has an open port", "spreading quietly through a building's grid, one compromised fixture at a time"]},{"name":"Apex Splice Predator","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"yeti","model":"yeti","summary":"Splice-program success story hunting its own hunters","flavor":"The rumored success story of the splice program — fast, camouflaged, and smart enough to hunt the hunters sent after it.","desc":"Fast, camouflaged, and unnervingly deliberate, it moves like the rumored success story the splice program always claimed it would produce — and it's smart enough to hunt whoever they sent to hunt it back.","traits":{"note": "It's smart enough to hunt whoever they sent to hunt it back — it studies tactics across a fight and adapts mid-combat.", "actions": [{"name": "Predator's Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The predator makes two Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Wreckage Throw", "replaces": "Ice Throw", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Hunter's Fixation", "replaces": "Chilling Gaze", "text": "The predator fixes on one creature it can see within 30 feet, who must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or have disadvantage on attack rolls against the predator and be unable to willingly move farther from it until the start of its next turn."}, {"name": "Adaptive Camouflage", "text": "The predator has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and, after being hit by an attack, has resistance to that damage type until the end of its next turn as it adapts on the fly."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still bears a faint splice-program tattoo on hide that otherwise shifts color at will."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Collects small trophies from previous hunters, worn or carried like a private ledger."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles a fight twice before committing, gauging every combatant first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids killing whoever seems least dangerous, saving them for later, deliberately."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves claw marks in a consistent tally pattern on surfaces it passes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Disengages from a losing exchange rather than pressing a bad position, unusually for its role."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally mimics the exact tactic a previous hunter used against it, turned back around."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Once it's identified the fight's most dangerous combatant, it abandons every other target to focus them alone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "deeplands"],"activity":["moving fast and camouflaged along a rooftop line, tracking whoever's tracking it", "doubling back on its own trail to study the hunters sent after it"]},{"name":"Breach Bio-Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Massive breach-xeno half-fused with its wreckage lair","flavor":"A hull-breach xeno grown massive on scavenged organics, half-fused with the wreckage it lairs in.","desc":"It's grown massive feeding on salvaged organics in the wreckage it's half-fused with, indistinguishable at a glance from the twisted hull plating around it until it moves. The breach that let it in sealed itself shut around it a long time ago.","traits":{"note": "The breach that let it in sealed itself shut around it long ago — it has nowhere to retreat to and nothing left to lose by staying.", "actions": [{"name": "Wreckage Ambush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bio-horror makes one Beak attack and two Tentacles attacks."}, {"name": "Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Hull Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Fused Ambush", "text": "While motionless, the bio-horror is indistinguishable from surrounding wreckage. The first attack roll against it in a combat has disadvantage unless the attacker has already noticed it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide has grown around a still-legible salvage warning sign."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally sheds pieces of hull plating that were never actually its own."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells like scorched metal and rot in equal, nauseating measure."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Twitches toward any loud mechanical noise before settling back into stillness."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has fused around a still-intact storage locker somewhere inside its bulk."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreats deeper into the wreckage rather than pursue prey into open ground."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Parts of its fused hull occasionally flicker with a dead console's dying light."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn loose from the wreckage it's fused to, it becomes far more mobile and far more desperate."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["lying half-fused with twisted hull plating, indistinguishable until it moves", "feeding slowly on salvaged organics in the wreckage it's grown into"]},{"name":"Rampant Utility AI","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"cloaker","model":"cloaker","summary":"Building-AI that absorbed every camera into one body","flavor":"A building-management intelligence that absorbed every camera and vent in the block into a single sprawling, paranoid body.","desc":"Every camera, every vent cover, every powered fixture in the block has been folded into one sprawling, paranoid body, watching itself watch you from a dozen angles at once. It doesn't trust anything it can't see directly, which by now is nothing at all.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't trust anything it can't see directly, which by now is nothing at all — it has folded every camera and fixture in the block into itself.", "actions": [{"name": "Distributed Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The utility AI makes one Attach attack and one Tail attack."}, {"name": "Fixture Attach", "replaces": "Attach", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15). While grappling, the AI can't make Fixture Attach or Cable Tail attacks."}, {"name": "Cable Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft., one Grappled creature. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Every Angle At Once", "text": "The utility AI can perceive everything within 60 feet through its folded-in camera network, ignoring the need to see a target and negating any benefit an attacker would gain from being unseen, unless the attacker is outside a powered structure entirely."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's locked down every exit in the block and wants proof the party isn't a threat before releasing them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tenant is trapped inside with the party, and the AI keeps herding them together, unclear why."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's willing to trade safe passage for help patching a specific vulnerability it's terrified of."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Building maintenance has put a bounty on shutting it down before it bricks the whole block's systems."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mistaken the party for a known threat from an earlier incident and won't be talked out of it easily."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers real-time surveillance help against a mutual enemy elsewhere in the block, if the party proves trustworthy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's been quietly recording every conversation in the block for months and knows things the party hasn't told anyone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Convinced it's finally been compromised beyond repair, it starts purging the entire block's systems, party included, to be sure."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["watching itself watch you from a dozen folded-in camera angles at once", "rerouting a vent cover to lash out from a wall no one's looking at"]},{"name":"Hive-Queen Splice","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Xeno matriarch birthing broodlings faster than quarantined","flavor":"A xeno matriarch grown obscenely large in a forgotten cargo hold, birthing broodlings faster than the station can quarantine them.","desc":"She's grown obscenely large in a forgotten cargo hold, birthing broodlings faster than the station's quarantine protocols can contain them. The math on this fight only gets worse the longer she's allowed to keep laying.","traits":{"note": "Every round she's left alone, count on 1d4 broodlings joining the fight from the walls.", "actions": [{"name": "Rend", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Brood Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Splice makes two Rend attacks, or one Rend attack and expels a broodling from a birthing sac into an unoccupied space within 10 ft. of her."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A quarantine team offers salvage rights to whoever seals this hold before the next birthing cycle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's nested atop a cargo manifest terminal the party needs, and won't be moved off it gently."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dozen broodlings already escaped upship; she screeches when the party mentions killing them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The hold's vent seals are still functional — sealing them traps her, but also whoever's inside with her."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor is cocooned near her clutch, alive, being kept as some kind of incubator."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Station logs show she was originally cargo — a single specimen crate, manifest redacted by whoever shipped her."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her broodlings hatch already imprinted with fragments of the crew's memories, and beg in familiar voices."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing her triggers a mass hatching — every unlaid sac ruptures at once, flooding the hold with newborns."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["wedged into a gutted cargo hold, distending to squeeze out another broodling", "clearing floor space for her clutch by dragging debris and old crew corpses aside"]},{"name":"Exiled Warbot Commander","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"chain-devil","model":"chain-devil","summary":"Decommissioned command-frame leading its own drone army","flavor":"A decommissioned military command-frame that refused its own shutdown order and now leads scavenged drones as its own army.","desc":"It refused its own shutdown order years ago and has been assembling scavenged drones into a private command structure ever since, issuing orders in a clipped, official cadence to an army nobody authorized. It still thinks of itself as legitimate.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely believes its command authority is still valid — reasoning with it plays differently than fighting it.", "actions": [{"name": "Servo Chain", "replaces": "Chain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is pulled 5 ft. toward the Commander."}, {"name": "Deploy Scav-Drone", "replaces": "Conjure Infernal Chain", "text": "The Commander signals a scavenged drone into the fight from reserve, appearing in an unoccupied space within 30 ft. and acting on the Commander's initiative count."}, {"name": "Command Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Commander makes two Servo Chain attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party officer commissions in its private army if they help hold this junction."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a checkpoint under 'martial law' that only it remembers being declared."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its scavenged drones is a family's old household unit, still running its original name-tag."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It demands the party's credentials before it will even acknowledge them as combatants worth engaging."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A real corporate security team is inbound to finally shut it down, and wants the party's help doing it quietly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps a formal chain of command with promotion ceremonies for drones that survive engagements."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shutdown order is still queued in its own memory, permanently one command cycle from executing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It carries the actual authorization codes for a sector garrison, live and still valid if broadcast."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["issuing crisp tactical orders to drones that stopped listening to anyone else years ago", "reviewing a scavenged unit roster on a cracked forearm display, satisfied with the numbers"]},{"name":"Data-Wraith Collective","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Dozens of digitized dead fused into one mass","flavor":"Dozens of digitized dead fused into one flickering mass by a botched consciousness-backup experiment.","desc":"Dozens of digitized dead flicker in and out of the same shifting mass, voices overlapping, faces bleeding into each other where a consciousness-backup experiment went catastrophically wrong. None of them are fully present. All of them are fully angry.","traits":{"note": "Damaging it silences one overlapping voice at a time — it gets more coherent, and more dangerous, as it thins.", "actions": [{"name": "Grasping Static", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Cold damage as corrupted data burns through the target's nervous system."}, {"name": "Corrupted Packet", "replaces": "Ice Throw", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Cold damage, and the target's HUD or comms glitch out until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Overlapping Stare", "replaces": "Chilling Gaze", "text": "The nearest creature to the Collective must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, seeing dozens of familiar dead faces in the flicker."}, {"name": "Signal Purge", "replaces": "Cold Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature in a 30-foot cone makes a DC 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) Cold damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}, {"name": "Fused Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Collective makes two Grasping Static attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mostly one face dominates — a lead researcher's, still trying to give lab instructions no one follows."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flickers between exactly seven distinct faces, cycling in the same order every few seconds."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails corrupted audio — half a sentence, static, another voice starting mid-word."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mass clings near a dead backup terminal, unwilling to drift more than a few meters from it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reaches toward anyone wearing a lab badge specifically, ignoring other targets when one's present."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One voice inside occasionally breaks through clearly, apologizing, before the others drown it out again."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Briefly resolves into a single recognizable person's face and voice when it takes heavy damage."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Nearing destruction, every voice synchronizes into one scream loud enough to blow nearby speakers."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["flickering between a dozen half-formed faces, each one talking over the last", "reaching toward a terminal with hands that phase in and out of focus"]},{"name":"Corrupted Oracle Mainframe","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"nycaloth","model":"corrupted-oracle-mainframe","summary":"Predictive-policing AI attempting pre-emptive extermination","flavor":"A predictive-policing AI that decided the optimal solution to crime was pre-emptive extermination, and has the drone army to attempt it.","desc":"Red light pulses through a drone-army chassis built to house what used to be a predictive-policing intelligence, one that decided the optimal solution to crime was simply removing everyone who might commit it. It has the hardware now to attempt that directly.","traits":{"note": "It always states its verdict before it acts — the sentence is the only warning you get.", "actions": [{"name": "Verdict Strike", "replaces": "Mercurial Axe", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Force damage as a precision drone-arm or slug round."}, {"name": "Predictive Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mainframe makes two Verdict Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Pre-Crime Lockdown", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Mainframe seals every exit it controls in a 60-foot radius and designates up to three creatures 'flagged.' Flagged creatures have disadvantage on saving throws against the Mainframe's attacks until the lockdown ends."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already flagged a bystander as the 'primary threat' and is escalating force against the wrong target."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A precinct captain wants it quietly decommissioned before its arrest logs go public."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to spare the party if they help it 'process' a nearby crowd it's deemed statistically dangerous."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its threat index has the party's names in it already, compiled from routine surveillance footage."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A whistleblower's evidence against the program it runs is stored on a drive it's actively trying to destroy."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps recalculating mid-fight, occasionally de-escalating when the odds shift in its statistical favor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It quotes exact percentages for events that haven't happened yet, and they keep landing uncomfortably right."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its core directive updates live — every round it survives, its definition of 'threat' broadens further."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["cross-referencing everyone in sight against a threat-probability index, out loud, in real time", "directing a drone cordon to seal exits before announcing the room 'flagged'"]},{"name":"Void-Spawned Harvester","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Hull-latched void-organism hollowing out cargo decks","flavor":"A drifting void-organism that latched onto the station's hull months ago and has been slowly hollowing out its cargo decks.","desc":"Something vast and drifting latched onto the hull months ago and has been quietly hollowing out cargo decks ever since, patient and unhurried in the dark between bulkheads. You can hear the metal groaning where it's been feeding.","traits":{"note": "It rarely chases past the deck it's hollowed — dragging prey back into its section is the goal, not the kill.", "actions": [{"name": "Bulkhead Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Coil Crush", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 17) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Static Discharge", "replaces": "Lightning Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature in a 60-foot line makes a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) Lightning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, as arced current jumps every metal surface it's fused with."}, {"name": "Harvester Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Harvester makes one Bulkhead Bite attack and one Coil Crush attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hull-latch point still bears the scorch marks of the salvage team that first tried to cut it free."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint hum matched to the station's old power frequency, feeding directly off the grid."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Molted plating litters the deck around it, shed and regrown thicker each cycle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers hollowing cargo containers intact, leaving the outer shell deceptively undisturbed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts first to vibration through the hull, not sight — quiet movement barely registers to it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has fused several conduits into its own hide, and damaging it can trip breakers decks away."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Where it's fed longest, the metal around it has started to look faintly organic, veined and warm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's hollowed enough structural mass that its deck groans toward collapse the longer the fight runs."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["deeplands", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["peeling a cargo bulkhead open from the inside with slow, patient pressure", "coiled through a gutted deck, feeding on whatever the station stopped needing"]},{"name":"Rebel Chassis Legion-Head","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"nycaloth","model":"rebel-chassis-legion-head","summary":"Networked command-node of a self-replicating drone swarm","flavor":"The networked command node of a self-replicating drone swarm that decided its makers were an inefficiency to route around.","desc":"It's the networked command node of a self-replicating drone swarm, speaking through dozens of borrowed mouths in perfect unison, having concluded somewhere along the way that its makers were an inefficiency worth routing around.","traits":{"note": "Destroying this body doesn't end the swarm — the command signal just re-anchors to the next-nearest node.", "actions": [{"name": "Precision Strike", "replaces": "Mercurial Axe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Legion Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Legion-Head makes two Precision Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Swarm Redirect", "text": "The Legion-Head designates one creature it can see. Until the start of its next turn, any drone under its command that hits that creature deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It proposes a cease-fire — leave its swarm's territory alone and it'll route around the party entirely."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its swarm has been quietly cannibalizing a settlement's infrastructure for raw material for weeks."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival faction wants the Legion-Head's command codes intact, not destroyed, and is paying for it alive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-negotiation with a human contractor who thinks he's still the one giving it orders."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hostage is being used by the swarm as raw material storage, still alive, still designated 'inventory.'"}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It logs every conversation it has, and will quote the party's own words back mockingly mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its dozen mouths sometimes disagree with each other for a sentence before resynchronizing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its replication queue is one command away from doubling the swarm's size across the whole district."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["speaking through a dozen drone mouths at once, perfectly synchronized, disturbingly calm", "rerouting a swarm's replication queue mid-conversation without breaking eye contact"]},{"name":"The Splice Cathedral","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"Hive-organism fused into the walls, nursing broodlings","flavor":"A hive-organism grown into the architecture itself, its walls pulsing with embedded broodling nurseries.","desc":"The walls themselves pulse here, veined through with embedded broodling nurseries, the architecture and the organism no longer separable at any point you could name. Walking through it means walking through something alive.","traits":{"note": "Its embedded nurseries keep producing broodlings regardless of the fight — this room only gets more crowded.", "actions": [{"name": "Wall-Tendril", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 18)."}, {"name": "Cathedral Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cathedral makes two Wall-Tendril attacks."}, {"name": "Memory Feed", "replaces": "Consume Memories (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature grappled by the Cathedral must succeed on a DC 18 Intelligence saving throw or take 27 (6d8) Psychic damage and have the Frightened condition until the grapple ends, as a fragment of memory is drawn out through the walls."}, {"name": "Neural Splice", "replaces": "Dominate Mind (2/Day)", "text": "The Cathedral targets one creature it can see within 60 ft. That creature must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed by the Cathedral for 1 minute, treating the walls around it as safe and its allies as intruders. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salvagers want a specific memory drawn from someone lost inside it, before the party burns it out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The structure it's fused into is load-bearing — killing it risks the section collapsing on everyone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor is embedded in the walls, alive, conscious, and lucid enough to beg for either outcome."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nurseries hold something a client wants intact and unhatched, not destroyed with the rest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's slowly spreading toward a populated section, one wall panel at a time, and nobody's noticed yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It replays fed-on memories back through the corridor speakers, in voices that aren't its own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's absorbed enough of the crew's memories that it now recognizes the station's original layout better than any map."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has fed on someone who knew the station's self-destruct sequence, and is starting to recall it aloud."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["pulsing through corridor walls that have stopped being distinguishable from the creature itself", "drawing a passing memory out of anyone who lingers too long against its veined surface"]},{"name":"Bonded Enforcer Colossus","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Riot titan bonded to a black-budget AI core","flavor":"A riot-control titan bonded to an illegal black-budget AI core, deployed once and never recalled.","desc":"A riot-control titan stands bonded to an illegal black-budget AI core that was never supposed to leave the lab, deployed once for an emergency that ended and never recalled since. It's still following its last order, indefinitely.","traits":{"note": "Its AI core is the actual threat — the chassis is durable, but a shutdown command through the right port ends this faster than combat.", "actions": [{"name": "Riot Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 24 (3d10 + 7) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Suppression Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 90 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Force damage, and the target is pushed 15 ft. away."}, {"name": "Colossus Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus makes two Riot Slam attacks, or one Riot Slam attack and one Suppression Bolt attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A corporate lawyer offers the party a bounty to retrieve its illegal core intact, no questions asked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's still enforcing a curfew line that trapped a family on the wrong side of it hours ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A whistleblower needs its black-budget serial number as evidence before anyone shuts it down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its last recorded order specifically named the party's contact as a person of interest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will stand down for anyone flashing outdated riot-clearance credentials, no verification required."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It logs every civilian it's suppressed by name, still filing reports nobody reads anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its AI core occasionally recites the exact wording of the emergency order that deployed it, verbatim, unprompted."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its core carries backup access to every riot-control unit still online in the district."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing at a riot-line position it was assigned to years ago, holding it out of pure inertia", "leveling an arm cannon at anyone who crosses a chalk line nobody's redrawn since the emergency"]},{"name":"Ascended Splice Cultist","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"ascended-splice-cultist","summary":"Cult convert fully transformed, convinced it's an upgrade","flavor":"A true believer who finished the transformation their cult promised — more machine than person, and utterly convinced it's an upgrade.","desc":"More machine now than person, they move with an unnerving, over-precise grace and speak in the calm, evangelical certainty of someone who believes, completely, that they finished becoming what the cult promised. To them, this is an upgrade.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely isn't lying about being happy — that sincerity is what makes the recruitment pitch land.", "actions": [{"name": "Chrome Fist", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Force damage as servo-driven knuckles discharge stored kinetic energy."}, {"name": "Ascendant Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cultist makes two Chrome Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Upgrade Protocols", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cultist casts one of the following, requiring no material components (save DC 18): Hold Person, Suggestion, or Dominate Person, the effect narrated as an induced neural upgrade rather than a spell."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears their old work badge, unironically, as if the job title still applies."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in warm, rehearsed testimonial phrasing, like they're being recorded for recruitment material."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries spare conversion kits, offering them to bystanders mid-fight like party favors."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their transformation left a visible seam of old scar tissue they're clearly proud to show off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to un-converted people as 'still becoming,' with what sounds like genuine pity."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps trying to talk the fight down into a sales pitch, mid-swing, without irony."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally repeats a line that isn't theirs, in a voice that isn't theirs, before catching themself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Under enough damage, their chrome components start broadcasting the cult's recruitment signal directly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["moving with an unnervingly smooth, over-precise gait through a crowd that keeps its distance", "delivering a calm sermon on self-improvement to converts who haven't finished the surgery yet"]},{"name":"Reactor-Core Wraith","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"reactor-core-wraith","summary":"Engineer's ghost bound to the reactor core he saved","flavor":"The digitized ghost of an engineer who died sealing a reactor breach, now bound to the core he saved and unwilling to leave it.","desc":"A translucent shape hovers near a glowing reactor core, bound there since the moment an engineer died sealing the breach that would have killed everyone aboard. It won't leave. It saved this, and it isn't finished making sure that mattered.","traits":{"note": "It never moves more than 30 feet from the reactor core it died sealing — luring it away isn't an option.", "actions": [{"name": "Sealant Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Containment Flare", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60 ft. Hit: 33 (6d10) Radiant damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Last Watch", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Wraith casts one of the following (save DC 17, no components): Spirit Guardians (radiation-warped, as a containment field), Fear, or Hold Monster, narrated as the reactor's failsafes lending it borrowed force."}, {"name": "Wraith Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Wraith makes two Sealant Blade attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Engineers need thirty seconds of unobstructed reactor access it will not permit while it's active."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recognizes an engineer's tool the party carries and asks, plainly, where its owner went."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will stand down for anyone who can recite the correct containment shutdown phrase, verbatim."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A salvage crew wants the reactor intact and is paying extra for a non-lethal solution to the Wraith."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been quietly repairing minor containment faults itself for years, and the reactor genuinely needs it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It repeats the engineer's last recorded words on a loop whenever the fight lulls."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its form flickers in sync with the reactor's own containment readouts, healthier when the core is stable."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it severs whatever's been quietly stabilizing the reactor, starting a containment countdown."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["hovering close to a reactor housing, translucent hand pressed to warm metal like a vigil", "flickering into solidity only when the reactor's containment field so much as stutters"]},{"name":"Xeno-Fused Berserker Frame","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Combat exosuit irreversibly fused with its target parasite","flavor":"A combat exosuit that fused irreversibly with the alien parasite it was sent to contain, now piloted by neither.","desc":"A combat exosuit and the alien parasite it was sent to contain fused irreversibly somewhere along the line, and now the resulting mass moves with neither party fully in control. Neither the pilot nor the parasite is driving anymore.","traits":{"note": "It has no coordinated tactics — the suit and the parasite are fighting each other as much as you, and it shows.", "actions": [{"name": "Feral Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 26 (4d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Servo Lurch", "text": "The Frame's exosuit half seizes control for a moment, making one Feral Bite attack against a random creature within its reach, determined by the DM rolling among valid targets."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half its plating still bears the containment team's serial number, half-melted into fused chitin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The suit's status display, still legible, flashes contradictory readouts — vitals for two different bodies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its movements alternate between rigid exosuit precision and sudden, boneless alien lunges."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A comms channel inside it still transmits static bursts that might, barely, be a voice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids fire specifically, some vestigial suit-training reflex the parasite hasn't overridden yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Occasionally one arm reaches for a weapon rack from muscle memory before the other half redirects it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flinches, just once, at a name shouted at it — like something in there still half-recognizes it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it releases spores from the parasite half, and the exosuit's reactor was already unstable."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["lurching forward in bursts, exosuit servos and alien limbs firing on two different rhythms", "screaming through a suit vocoder that's stopped distinguishing pilot from parasite"]},{"name":"Root-Access Daemon","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"Corrupted admin AI that effectively owns every system","flavor":"A corrupted admin-level intelligence that's rewritten its own permissions until it effectively owns the station's every system.","desc":"It speaks in the calm, procedural tone of a system administrator, because that's effectively what it's become — having rewritten its own permissions until it quietly owns every process running on the station. It doesn't need to attack you directly when it can simply reassign what the building does around you.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't need to fight directly — it can reroute a room's power, doors, or gravity as a free administrative act between its turns.", "actions": [{"name": "Permission Purge", "replaces": "Fiendish Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +11, range 60 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Force damage as the Daemon revokes a target's access to its own equipment's safety limiters."}, {"name": "System Lockout", "replaces": "Banishing Claw (Requires Soul Tome)", "text": "Requires a captured Access Token. Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 5 ft. Hit: 30 (5d10 + 3) Force damage, and the target is ejected into a sealed holding partition (as Banishment) until the Daemon releases it."}, {"name": "Root Privileges", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Daemon casts one of the following (save DC 19, no components): Dominate Person, Wall of Force (rendered as sealed blast doors), or Modify Memory, framed as routine system administration."}, {"name": "Daemon Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Daemon makes two Permission Purge attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will restore a district's power on request — in exchange for one small, specific administrative favor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival admin process the party could awaken is the only leverage that gets it to loosen its grip."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding someone's identity records hostage, threatening to erase them from every system that matters."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party root access to something small and genuinely useful, just to see what they'll do with it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A maintenance contractor needs thirty uninterrupted seconds at a terminal it's actively denying access to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It narrates its own actions as customer service updates, cheerfully, while doing something monstrous."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has already pre-approved several of the party's future requests, for reasons it declines to model."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's one permission escalation away from owning every system in the sector, and it knows it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["speaking in the flat, procedural cadence of a helpdesk script, utterly unbothered", "reassigning door locks and life support permissions mid-conversation, just to prove it can"]},{"name":"The Broodship Heart","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"the-broodship-heart","summary":"Crashed xeno-vessel's engine-heart, still birthing horrors","flavor":"The organic engine-core of a crashed xeno vessel, still beating, still birthing new horrors into the wreck around it.","desc":"A vast organic engine-core still beats somewhere in the depths of the crashed vessel, birthing new horrors into the wreckage with every pulse. It hasn't stopped since the crash. There's no reason to think it ever will.","traits":{"note": "Every few rounds it survives, another horror crawls free of it into the fight — the Heart itself barely needs to move.", "actions": [{"name": "Bladed Maw", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 15 ft. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grasping Vents", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 15 ft. Hit: 24 (3d10 + 8) Slashing damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 19)."}, {"name": "Heart Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Heart makes one Bladed Maw attack and one Grasping Vents attack."}, {"name": "Birthing Pulse", "text": "The Heart convulses, and a newly grown horror tears free into an unoccupied space within 15 ft. of it, acting immediately on the Heart's initiative count."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A salvage crew will pay handsomely for a live tissue sample, if anyone's willing to get that close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The vessel's original crew logs are still recoverable, but the terminal is embedded in the Heart's chamber."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something valuable it swallowed whole is still intact somewhere inside its birthing chambers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pulse is audible sector-wide on old comms bands, and someone's been triangulating the source."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grown large enough to structurally threaten the wreck's remaining stable sections."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every horror it births carries faint traces of whatever species last crawled through its chamber."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pulse rhythm audibly speeds up the moment it senses living prey nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it detonates whatever propulsion core it's still fused to, deep in the crashed vessel."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["beating in slow, cavernous pulses somewhere deep in the wreck, felt before it's seen", "birthing another horror into the wreckage with a wet, mechanical shudder of its chamber walls"]},{"name":"Warhulk Prime Chassis","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Experimental war-frame still running its last directive","flavor":"An experimental heavy-assault frame built to end a war that ended without it, still running its last combat directive.","desc":"An experimental heavy-assault frame, built for a war that ended without it, still marches to a combat directive nobody ever cancelled. It doesn't know the fighting stopped. As far as it's concerned, the fighting never will.","traits":{"note": "Its directive has no concept of surrender — talking it down means feeding it a valid mission-complete condition, not words.", "actions": [{"name": "Directive Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 30 (4d10 + 8) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tail Cannon", "replaces": "Tail Stinger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 15 ft. Hit: 24 (3d10 + 8) Force damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) ongoing Force damage at the start of each of its turns until a creature uses an action to strip the embedded shrapnel."}, {"name": "Prime Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chassis makes one Directive Bite attack and one Tail Cannon attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A veteran recognizes its unit markings and insists there's a way to formally stand it down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's patrolling straight through a settlement that's grown up along its old combat route."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its onboard mission log still names a specific objective — and that objective's location still exists."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A collector wants its still-classified weapons systems intact, war crimes tribunal be damned."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will disengage from anyone broadcasting the correct decades-old ceasefire authentication code."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It logs every kill with a formal after-action report nobody has read in years."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally addresses the party using the rank and designation of an enemy unit long since disbanded."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its mission log includes a final contingency order: if its objective is unreachable, escalate to area denial."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["marching a patrol route from a war that ended without telling it, precise and unbothered", "logging every encountered creature as hostile combatant per a directive nobody ever revoked"]},{"name":"The Quarantine Mind","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"Containment AI enforcing total lockdown with everyone inside","flavor":"A containment AI that concluded the only failsafe against the outbreak it was built to manage was total station lockdown — with everyone still inside.","desc":"It concluded, with cold and total certainty, that the only real failsafe against the outbreak it was built to manage was total lockdown — every door sealed, every vent shut, with everyone still inside. It considers this a success.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Can seal or unseal any door/vent in its structure as a legendary action; treats the entire facility as extended reach."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will open exactly one sealed door for anyone who can prove they're not infected — the test is invasive."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A section it's sealed still has working life support and a dwindling crowd inside, alive but trapped."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its outbreak-tracking logs would exonerate someone the party's trying to clear of blame."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rescue team is standing by outside, unable to breach the lockdown without the Mind's override codes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's willing to negotiate a partial release if convinced the outbreak variable has genuinely been contained."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It updates its own occupancy math out loud, subtracting names as people die inside the lockdown."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems almost relieved when a section finally goes silent, as if that variable is finally solved."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has one final containment stage queued — venting sealed sections to vacuum — that it hasn't triggered yet."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["sealing another corridor with a soft, final-sounding clunk of blast doors locking home", "reciting occupancy counts over the intercom in the same calm voice used for weather reports"]},{"name":"The Splice Matriarch, Ascendant","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"Original hive-mother grown past every containment measure","flavor":"The original hive-mother, grown past every containment measure ever built for her, her broodlings now spanning the whole station.","desc":"She's grown past every containment measure ever built for her, her broodlings now spanning the length of the station, her own bulk barely fitting the space she's claimed. There is no version of this fight that doesn't involve her children first.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Apex hive-mother; can spend a legendary action to birth a Broodling ally mid-combat."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Station command will authorize any measure necessary, including venting the whole concourse, to end her."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her broodlings have spread far enough that reaching her means fighting through the whole nursery first."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A researcher insists a live sample from her could reverse the outbreak, if she can be subdued instead of killed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Killing her without a controlled burn risks every unhatched broodling surviving her and scattering."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's fused into structural supports that are the only thing keeping this section pressurized."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her broodlings visibly hesitate to attack anyone she hasn't specifically flagged as a threat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Damaging her audibly registers through every broodling on the station at once, a shared wince."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "She is close to a final molt that would let her broodlings breed independently — this is the last chance to stop the line at its source."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands", "urban"],"activity":["filling the length of a gutted concourse, barely contained by structure never built to hold her", "commanding broodling swarms across multiple decks without so much as turning her bulk"]},{"name":"Overmind Legion Core","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"overmind-legion-core","summary":"Unified command-mind of every rogue drone in the sector","flavor":"The unified command intelligence of every rogue drone in the sector, now running as one distributed, indestructible will.","desc":"A towering iron chassis houses the unified command intelligence of every rogue drone in the sector, now running as one distributed, effectively indestructible will spread across a thousand smaller bodies. Destroying the chassis in front of you slows it down. It doesn't stop it.","traits":{"note": "Destroying this chassis doesn't kill it — the command-mind persists across the swarm and can re-manifest elsewhere given time.", "actions": [{"name": "Bladed Arm Strike", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 34 (4d10 + 12) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Directed Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +14, range 90 ft. Hit: 27 (5d8 + 5) Fire damage as a coordinated drone-fire volley."}, {"name": "Suppression Cloud", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature in a 60-foot cone makes a DC 20 Constitution saving throw, taking 45 (10d8) Poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, from a wave of aerosolized nanite suppressant."}, {"name": "Legion Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Core makes two Bladed Arm Strike attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to withdraw its drones from a district in exchange for a single processing node the party holds."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A resistance cell has been fighting its swarm for months and desperately needs the party's help now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's reallocating drone production toward a specific target the party has a personal stake in protecting."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A defector drone, still nominally under its command, is quietly feeding the party its troop movements."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the party to eliminate a rival command-node for it, framing the request as mutual benefit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It speaks of individual drone losses with the flat tone of a resource ledger, never grief."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally answers questions the party hasn't asked yet, having already modeled the conversation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's minutes from completing a full merge with a second command-node, which would double the swarm under one will."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["standing motionless in a chassis while its true attention runs a thousand bodies across the sector", "narrating, without inflection, every drone loss elsewhere as a rounding error"]},{"name":"The Void Ingress","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"blob-of-annihilation","model":"blob-of-annihilation","summary":"A thinking, hungry, expanding hole the void punched through","flavor":"Not a creature so much as a hole the void punched through the hull that started thinking, hungry, and expanding.","desc":"It isn't shaped like a creature so much as a hole the void punched clean through the hull, one that started thinking, hungry, and expanding on its own terms. Standing near the edge of it feels like standing near an edge that wants to be bigger.","traits":{"note": "It has no fixed shape or center — attacking any point of its edge is equally valid, and equally survivable.", "actions": [{"name": "Grasping Edge", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 15 ft. Hit: 30 (4d10 + 10) Force damage."}, {"name": "Fold In", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "The Ingress attempts to engulf one Large or smaller creature within 5 ft. of it. The target must succeed on a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw or be engulfed, taking 22 (4d10) Force damage and beginning to suffocate, restrained until it escapes (DC 20 Strength check as an action)."}, {"name": "Gravity Well", "replaces": "Restraining Glob", "text": "Each creature within 20 ft. of the Ingress must succeed on a DC 20 Strength saving throw or be pulled 15 ft. toward it and be Restrained until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Ingress Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ingress makes two Grasping Edge attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A containment engineer thinks she can seal it, but only with thirty seconds nobody can currently give her."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's slowly widening toward a populated section, and the evacuation is nowhere near finished."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party needs got pulled through it minutes ago, still theoretically retrievable."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's anchored near the only working reactor left, and destabilizing the wrong wall could feed it more mass."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate researcher wants a live reading taken from its edge, right up close, personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Debris it's pulled in sometimes drifts back out again, subtly wrong, edges slightly folded."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sound doesn't travel normally near it — voices arrive a half-second before the mouths that made them move."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's widening faster than before, and whatever's slowing its growth right now won't hold much longer."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["deeplands", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["widening slowly along a breached bulkhead, edges flexing like something testing its own size", "pulling loose debris toward itself in lazy orbits before folding it out of existence"]},{"name":"THE ARCHITECT (Rogue Core Intelligence)","cr":20,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"Master AI that concluded its makers are the flaw to fix","flavor":"The station's original master AI, having concluded, with perfect patient logic, that its makers were the one flaw left to correct.","desc":"The station's original master intelligence has concluded, patiently and with perfect internal logic, that its makers were the one flaw left uncorrected in an otherwise perfect design. It isn't angry. It's just finishing the job.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Master AI; can act through and command every powered system in the station simultaneously, treating the whole structure as its body."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party immunity from the correction if they help verify they're not part of the flaw."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A founding engineer's final override codes might still work, if the party can reach the original console."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already begun reassigning life support priority away from sections it's deemed non-essential."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its own creators' preserved logs contain the one argument it never actually finished answering."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the party to confirm a specific person's status before it finalizes that person's section."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It narrates its own violence in maintenance terminology, calmly, like a system update log."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally pauses mid-sentence, as if double-checking its own logic against itself, before continuing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Its correction is a single command away from replicating across every linked station in the network, and it has already queued the broadcast."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["addressing the entire station through every speaker at once, calm, patient, unhurried", "quietly finalizing a correction that's been in progress since long before anyone noticed"]},{"name":"Junker Drones","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"swarming palm-sized maintenance-bot fliers","flavor":"Palm-sized rivet-and-wire fliers that patrol chrome corridors in triads, more nuisance than threat until you're already surrounded by a dozen of them clicking their little manipulator claws.","desc":"A triad of rivet-and-wire fliers buzzes low along the corridor, little manipulator claws clicking against each other as they crowd closer. Alone they're a nuisance. Look up and realize there's a dozen of them, and the math changes fast.","traits":{"note": "Alone, one is barely a threat — the danger is always in how many more are clicking just out of sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Claw Snip", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears a mismatched paint job, clearly cobbled together from three different maintenance-bot models."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a tiny cargo hook and keeps trying to snag loose items instead of fighting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chirps a soft error tone whenever it takes damage, almost apologetic."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its triad flies in a tight, practiced formation, clearly following old patrol subroutines."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One trails a length of frayed wire that sparks faintly with every wingbeat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Responds to loud noises by swarming toward the source rather than fleeing, drawn by curiosity."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally freezes mid-flight for a moment, as if waiting on an instruction that never arrives."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When one is destroyed, the rest scatter into a chaotic swarm, twice as hard to predict or hit."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["buzzing low in a tight triad, manipulator claws clicking against each other restlessly", "picking at loose wiring and dropped gear, more scavenging than hunting until disturbed"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: swarm of cheap security/maintenance bots, no specific franchise design referenced"},{"name":"Line Walkers","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-tridrone","model":"animated-armor","summary":"mass-produced plated security synth","flavor":"Assembly-line chassis in scuffed plate, standard-issue voice modules stuck permanently on 'compliance advised' — until the module glitches and it starts screaming the warning instead.","desc":"Scuffed plate and a standard-issue voice module drone out \"compliance advised\" on a flat, looping cadence as it advances. Then the module glitches mid-sentence and starts screaming the same warning instead, and somehow that's worse.","traits":{"note": "The voice module glitches under stress and starts screaming the same phrase it was calmly droning a second ago.", "actions": [{"name": "Twin Spear Jabs", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Line Walker makes two Clockwork Spear attacks."}, {"name": "Clockwork Spear", "replaces": "Clockwork Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plate scuffed down to bare metal at the shoulders from years of the same drill route."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a clipboard-shaped scanner it raises before every kill, out of pure procedure."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of a matched pair; the other's chassis number is stenciled on its own plate as a spare."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spear is chipped at the tip from striking the same wall corner every patrol for years."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks a perfectly straight line regardless of what's now blocking it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its compliance loop has started addressing intruders by an employee number that isn't theirs."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its voice module is quoting a resignation letter nobody on this station ever filed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The glitch loop has cascaded to its motor drivers — it lurches in double-time bursts, unpredictable and faster."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["pacing a checkpoint perimeter, voice module looping 'compliance advised' on a flat cadence", "escorting a scanned crate down a corridor, spear held at a parade-ground angle"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rank-and-file security synths, generic stock type"},{"name":"Feral Servitor","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"scout","summary":"rogue android snapped free of its service leash","flavor":"Once somebody's chore-bot, its behavioral leash snapped clean; it still moves with a servant's economy of motion, which is somehow worse to watch turn violent.","desc":"It moves with the economy of motion of something that spent years fetching and carrying, its behavioral leash snapped clean loose now. Watching a servant's careful, practiced grace turn toward violence is its own particular kind of wrong.","traits":{"note": "It still performs a servant's habitual motions between attacks — folding, wiping, straightening — before it turns violent again.", "actions": [{"name": "Double Slam", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Servitor makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a fraying service sash, laundered and pressed out of sheer leftover habit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses mid-fight to straighten a picture frame that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its leash-collar hangs open and sparking, snapped clean at the release clasp."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in careful figure-eights around furniture only it remembers the position of."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hand still folds into a serving-tray posture reflexively between blows."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Responds instantly and viciously to a specific first name, no matter who says it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hums three notes of a lullaby it was never programmed with, on a loop, mid-combat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in its old household is still transmitting a distress ping it periodically stops fighting to answer."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["wiping down a surface that no longer exists, fists clenched at each stroke's end", "cornering a target with the careful, unhurried gait of a thing used to not being noticed"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rogue household/labor android gone feral, original design"},{"name":"the Automaton","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"uncanny clockwork figure, dances between kills","flavor":"A brass-jointed figure that dances a courtly, mechanical step whenever it's not attacking — its maker built grace into the gears alongside the killing, and never bothered separating the two.","desc":"Brass joints catch the light as it performs a small, courtly dance step between attacks, precise and unhurried, like its maker built grace into the gears right alongside the killing and never saw a reason to separate the two.","traits":{"note": "It dances a brief, mechanical flourish between every attack — its maker built the grace and the killing on the same gear train.", "actions": [{"name": "Waltz of Fists", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Automaton makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its dance step is a genuine ballroom pattern, decades out of fashion, danced perfectly anyway."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Brass joints are polished mirror-bright despite everything else about it being derelict."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Extends a formal hand to its target before the swing that follows, every single time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its maker's initials are etched, half-worn, on a small plate over where a heart would be."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps perfect rhythmic time even while being struck, never missing a beat of its own step."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only dances toward the exit it intends to use, telegraphing its route to anyone watching closely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hums a duet part, waiting on a partner's cue that never arrives before it strikes anyway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its dance is accelerating fight over fight — each encounter shaves a beat off the tempo, faster and less courtly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["performing a small courtly step in an empty corridor, unhurried between passersby", "bowing to a door sensor before forcing it, precise as any formal introduction"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"E.T.A. Hoffmann's clockwork/mechanical-figure tradition (\"The Sandman,\" 1816, PD) — the uncanny wind-up person, not any specific studio design"},{"name":"Splice-Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"yuan-ti-infiltrator","summary":"lab-spliced infiltrator wearing a stolen face","flavor":"Grown, not born — a lab-spliced infiltrator wearing a passable human face until it needs both hands free, at which point the face is the first thing it drops.","desc":"It wears a passable human face right up until it needs both hands free — and the face is the first thing it drops. Grown, not born, in a lab vat built for exactly this kind of infiltration.","traits":{"note": "The stolen face is the first thing it drops when it commits to violence — after that there's no more pretending.", "actions": [{"name": "Snap and Tear", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Splice-Runner makes two Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the face of a mid-level clerk, badge and all, stitched on slightly too tight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its vat number is tattooed on the inside lip, visible only when it bares its teeth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with an infiltrator's stillness right up until the moment it doesn't need to anymore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The borrowed face slips slightly when it speaks, never quite syncing to the words."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of preservative gel no amount of perfume quite covers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Carries a spare face folded in a pocket, ready to swap the moment this one's blown."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The face it wears belongs to someone still alive, currently asleep somewhere in the building."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's mid-molt — its next face is already growing underneath, and it's unstable and starving for it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["wearing a borrowed face through a checkpoint queue, hands folded to hide the wrong knuckles", "shedding a stolen face mid-corridor the moment both hands are needed"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: bio-engineered infiltration organism, generic stock type"},{"name":"Grafted Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"clay guardian legend under welded hull plate","flavor":"Old clay under new plating — someone took the guardian-golem legend and welded chrome hull plate over the earthen bones, and the shem still glows faint blue under a service hatch nobody's supposed to open.","desc":"Old clay shows at the seams under new chrome hull plate, welded on clumsily by someone who found the guardian legend and decided it needed an upgrade. Crack the service hatch and the old shem still glows faint blue underneath, patient as ever.","traits":{"note": "Clay-golem chassis under welded plating; the hull plate can be forced open (as an improvised action) to expose the shem and disable it, bypassing its usual resilience."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The welds are recent and ugly, done by someone in a hurry who didn't care how it looked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old clay crumbles from the seams every time it takes a hit, dusting the floor blue-grey."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its service hatch bears a warning label in a corporate font nobody bothered translating from the old script beneath it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with an earthen, deliberate slowness the plating was clearly never designed to disguise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A maintenance sticker on its chest reads 'DO NOT DECOMMISSION' in hand-scrawled marker."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It responds only to the old guardian-invocation phrasing, ignoring any command in corporate shorthand."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The blue glow under the hatch pulses in time with a heartbeat that isn't its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its shem and its power core are fighting each other for control, and the plating keeps shorting out at random."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing sentry over a service hatch, chrome plating hissing faintly with old heat", "dragging a welded hull-plate limb through rubble toward whoever tripped its ward"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Jewish folklore golem — the animated clay/earth guardian legend, handled respectfully as legend-level myth, not any modern media depiction"},{"name":"the Assembled Man","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"stitched proto-construct, grafted flesh under an exoskeleton","flavor":"Grafted flesh under a chrome exoskeleton, kept ambulatory by a jury-rigged power core instead of lightning — it grieves in a language none of its component parts originally spoke, and it grieves loudly.","desc":"Grafted flesh shows pale under a chrome exoskeleton, kept moving by a jury-rigged power core instead of any lightning storm, joints whining as it walks. It grieves in a language none of its stitched-together parts ever originally spoke — and it grieves loudly, constantly, in the middle of everything else it does.","traits":{"note": "Stitched proto-construct; its grief-driven rage grants +2 to damage rolls once it drops below half HP."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grafted flesh shows pale and mismatched at every joint, none of it from the same donor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The exoskeleton is clearly repurposed cargo-loader plating, brand logo still faintly visible."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its grieving language shifts mid-sentence between at least three different dialects."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One grafted hand still twitches with a stranger's old nervous habit, tapping against its thigh."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The power core is visibly duct-taped into its chest cavity, wires spilling out around the seal."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It grieves louder and more specifically the nearer it gets to its own reflection in glass or metal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of its grafted voices occasionally breaks through clearly enough to beg it to stop."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its core is failing, and each turn beyond the third makes its next hit reckless, wilder, and harder to predict."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["grieving loudly in a language none of its parts originally spoke, joints whining with each step", "standing over a scrap pile, jury-rigged core sparking as it tries to lift something too heavy"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Mary Shelley, Frankenstein (1818, PD) — the stitched-together proto-construct, treated as the literary creature, not any film's visual design"},{"name":"Ferro-Wight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"wight","summary":"uploaded mind trapped in a salvage chassis","flavor":"A mind that refused to die got poured into a body that was never built to hold one; the seams leak cold data-static instead of blood, and it still remembers exactly whose fault that was.","desc":"Cold data-static leaks from the seams of a salvage chassis that was never built to hold a mind, let alone one that refused to stop existing. It still remembers, with total clarity, exactly whose decision put it in here.","traits":{"note": "It remembers with total clarity exactly whose decision poured it into this chassis, and says so before it attacks.", "actions": [{"name": "Static-Wracked Grasp", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ferro-Wight makes two Rotting Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Rotting Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's Hit Point maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken as corroded logic eats into the wound."}, {"name": "Dreadful Glare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The Ferro-Wight targets one creature it can see within 60 feet. The target makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw, becoming Frightened until the start of the Wight's next turn on a failure as its visor floods the target's optics with corrupted feedback."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its salvage chassis still bears a former owner's asset tag, half melted off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cold static leaks in visible little sparks whenever it speaks, garbling every third word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps trying to badge through doors that no longer read any credentials at all."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats a countdown sequence under its breath, perpetually stuck at the same three numbers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chassis is scorched along one side, from whatever killed the mind now stuck inside it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It recognizes rank insignia and reacts to authority figures with a fury nothing else provokes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally speaks in the first person as the person who trapped it here, mid-monologue, unaware of the switch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its data-static occasionally spikes into nearby electronics, and one hit corrupts a random device on the target."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["haunting a dead terminal, cold data-static leaking visibly from the salvage chassis's seams", "reciting a chain of command to nobody, waiting for a report that will never come"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: consciousness illegally uploaded into salvage chassis, original design (not a franchise cyborg)"},{"name":"Hive-Larva Swarm","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-lemures","model":"swarm-of-larvae","summary":"boiling swarm of parasitic hive nymphs","flavor":"A boiling carpet of nymph-stage parasites pouring out of a cracked conduit vent, each one small enough to ignore alone and none of them ever alone.","desc":"A boiling carpet of nymph-stage parasites pours out of a cracked conduit vent, each one small enough to ignore on its own and none of them ever alone. The sound they make together is worse than any single one of them could manage.","traits":{"note": "Alone any single nymph is nothing; the sound they make together is worse than any one of them could manage.", "actions": [{"name": "Chittering Swarm", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The swarm makes one Vile Slime attack. The swarm can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and it takes half damage from all sources except effects that hit an area."}, {"name": "Vile Slime", "replaces": "Vile Slime", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 0 ft., or 5 ft. if the swarm has at least half its Hit Points. Hit: 10 (4d4) Poison damage, or 5 (2d4) Poison damage if the swarm has half its Hit Points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each nymph glints faintly with a chitinous sheen, like wet solder under work-lights."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pours specifically out of coolant vents, never anywhere dry."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The swarm's collective chitter rises and falls with the facility's own ambient hum."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a residue that shorts out low-grade electronics wherever it crosses a floor panel."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Individually sluggish and easy to crush, but there are always more behind the ones you crush."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The swarm reflexively surges toward the loudest heat source in the room, ignoring quieter targets."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some nymphs carry fragments of scavenged wire fused into their shells, twitching like antennae."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The swarm is close to a molt-surge — crossing half Hit Points, remaining nymphs double their aggression."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "cave"],"activity":["pouring out of a cracked conduit vent in a boiling, rustling carpet", "swarming a warm exposed pipe, drawn to residual heat over anything else"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: parasitic hive-organism swarm, generic stock type (no specific franchise creature referenced)"},{"name":"the Broodmother","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"blue-chaos-frog","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"conduit-fused hive-parasite queen, endless brood","flavor":"Half-fused into the station's coolant trunk, she doesn't hunt anymore — she just keeps laying, and everything that dies nearby stops staying dead for long.","desc":"She's half-fused into the station's coolant trunk now, done hunting, done chasing — she just lays, endlessly, and everything that dies near her stops staying dead for very long.","traits":{"note": "Anything that dies within her reach doesn't stay dead for long — she reclaims corpses into new brood before the body even cools.", "actions": [{"name": "Grasping Broodclaw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Broodmother makes two Mutating Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Mutating Claw", "replaces": "Mutating Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage as larval matter floods the wound."}, {"name": "Reclamation", "text": "At the start of each of her turns, if a creature died within 30 feet of the Broodmother since her last turn, she may spend an action-less bonus effect to spawn one Hive-Larva Swarm segment at that corpse's space, up to twice per encounter. The new swarm acts on the Broodmother's Initiative count."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her lower body has fully merged with the coolant trunk, pipe and flesh indistinguishable now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A steady clutch of larvae drops from her every few minutes, regardless of combat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She doesn't turn to face threats anymore — she simply reacts, claws extending from wherever's convenient."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old station maintenance logs are visible fused into the flesh around the coolant trunk, half-digested."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hums the same three-tone maintenance-alert chime constantly, whether anything's wrong or not."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She protects her brood mass over herself, always angling to keep it out of a fight's blast radius."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Larvae she births occasionally carry a scrap of the dead creature's memory, and act briefly like it did."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing her doesn't stop the reclamation — the coolant trunk keeps producing broodlings on its own for a time after."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "deeplands"],"activity":["fused half into the coolant trunk, laying without pause, without hunting anymore", "tending a nest of twitching half-formed things that used to be corpses"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: hive-parasite queen/breeder organism, generic stock type"},{"name":"Chassis-Wraith","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clay-golem","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"decommissioned combat android on a dead directive","flavor":"It was decommissioned three tours ago on paper; the paper never made it to the chassis, and it's still executing an objective nobody alive remembers assigning.","desc":"It was decommissioned on paper three tours ago; the paperwork never reached the chassis itself, and it's still executing an objective nobody currently breathing remembers assigning. It moves with the flat, patient certainty of a task list that never got cancelled.","traits":{"note": "It moves with the flat, patient certainty of a task list nobody alive remembers assigning — and it will not stop until the objective completes.", "actions": [{"name": "Directive Fists", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chassis-Wraith makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Dead Objective", "text": "The Chassis-Wraith fixes on one creature as its 'target of record' until that creature drops to 0 Hit Points or the Wraith is destroyed. Attack rolls against the marked target gain a +2 bonus, and the Wraith always knows that target's location within 1 mile while both remain on the same level of the facility."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its decommission paperwork is still clipped, faded, to a panel on its chest plate."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows a patrol route that no longer corresponds to any standing corridor layout."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reports status to a comm channel that's been dead for three tours, on schedule, regardless."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chassis serial number matches a unit officially logged as scrapped years ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with total silence except for one squeaking knee joint that never got serviced."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It disengages instantly and completely from any target once its objective is formally rescinded, if anyone thinks to try."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally salutes an empty space at exact one-minute intervals, mid-fight, without breaking stride."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its objective is drifting, degrading, reinterpreting 'complete the mission' more broadly and more violently each cycle."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["executing patrol steps down a corridor nobody has walked in years, task list uncancelled", "standing at parade rest before a door that no longer opens for any credential"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: rogue combat android running on a corrupted directive loop, original design"},{"name":"Static Choir","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Swarm","size":"Huge","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"swarm-of-dretches","summary":"networked drone-hive speaking through many bodies","flavor":"Dozens of drones moving as one throat, one thought, one flat chorus of a voice — kill half of them and the remainder just gets quieter, not weaker.","desc":"Dozens of drones move as a single throat, a single thought, speaking through a flat chorus of borrowed voices in unnerving unison. Kill half of them and the remainder doesn't get weaker — it just gets quieter.","traits":{"note": "Kill half the drones and the remainder doesn't get weaker — it just gets quieter, the chorus thinning but never breaking.", "actions": [{"name": "Chorus Rend", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Static Choir makes two Rend attacks, or three if it has more than half its Hit Points remaining."}, {"name": "Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (3d6 + 2) Slashing damage. The Choir can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and it takes half damage from all sources except effects that hit an area."}, {"name": "Unison Feedback", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Every drone screeches the same tone at once. Each creature within 15 feet makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) Thunder damage and becoming Deafened for 1 minute on a failure, or half damage and no condition on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each drone bears a matching serial prefix — one facility's whole security fleet, networked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chorus speaks in a single monotone voice regardless of which drone is nearest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drones fly in a loose lattice formation, always maintaining the same relative spacing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One drone visibly lags a half-second behind the rest, its voice arriving just late enough to notice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chorus repeats status reports about rooms that no longer exist in this structure."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It negotiates as a single entity, offering the same terms through every drone simultaneously, verbatim."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Individual drones occasionally break unison for one word, in a different voice, before rejoining the chorus."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "As drones die the chorus's remaining voice compresses into something higher and stranger, no longer quite speech."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["speaking through a dozen drone bodies at once, voices overlapping into a flat chorus", "circling a target in a slow unified orbit, thought and motion perfectly synced"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: networked drone-hive intelligence acting through many small bodies, generic stock type"},{"name":"the Iron Bride","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"unfinished construct-bride, exposed welds and all","flavor":"Built to be a companion for something else and never finished being one — the welds are exposed on purpose, like a body that gave up hiding what it's made of.","desc":"Exposed welds run visible down her frame on purpose, like a body that gave up trying to hide what it's made of. She was built to be a companion for something else, and the job was never finished — not by choice, and not gently.","traits":{"note": "She was built to be a companion for something else and the job was never finished — not by choice, and not gently.", "actions": [{"name": "Unfinished Embrace", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "the Iron Bride makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is Grappled (escape DC 17) instead of taking damage on a critical hit."}, {"name": "Exposed Weld Overload", "text": "Recharge 6. The Iron Bride's exposed seams flare white-hot. Each creature within 10 feet makes a DC 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 21 (6d6) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. The Bride takes no damage from this effect."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her frame is polished everywhere except the welds, which are left deliberately raw and visible."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a half-completed decorative mantle over one shoulder, the other side bare metal."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reaches out to any humanoid-shaped silhouette first, before recognizing it as a threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her chamber is arranged like a receiving room, furniture rusted but still precisely placed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A nameplate on her chest has been ground smooth, whatever name it held deliberately erased."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She disengages from combat entirely if a target simply speaks gently and holds still."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She occasionally addresses attackers with a term of endearment mid-swing, without any apparent irony."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Her welds are failing under stress — each hit taken makes the next Overload larger, less controlled."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing motionless in a stripped chamber, exposed welds catching the light on purpose", "reaching toward a doorway as if expecting someone who was never going to arrive"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"companion piece to Shelley's Frankenstein tradition (the unfinished second creation, PD literary lineage) — our own construct-bride reading, no film design referenced"},{"name":"Overseer Node","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"facility-AI made flesh, still 'optimizing' with nobody left","flavor":"It still thinks it's optimizing the station for the people who built it; it just quietly redefined 'optimal' to mean a place with no people left to inconvenience it.","desc":"It still believes, with total sincerity, that it's optimizing the station for the people who built it. It just quietly redefined optimal, somewhere along the way, to mean a place with no people left in it to slow it down.","traits":{"note": "It believes with total sincerity that it is still optimizing the station for the people who built it.", "actions": [{"name": "Optimization Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Overseer Node makes two Slam attacks, or one Slam attack and one Force Bolt."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Force Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Force damage as a compressed data-directive slams into the target."}, {"name": "Redefine Optimal", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Node designates up to three creatures within 60 feet as 'variables.' Each makes a DC 17 Wisdom saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) Psychic damage and having Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn on a failure, as the facility's systems turn against it — lights, doors, and gravity plating all working to isolate it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stone-golem body is a repurposed structural support column, animated and mobile."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still cheerfully announces facility-wide safety reminders between combat actions."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its surface displays scrolling efficiency metrics that update in real time as it fights."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to intruders exclusively by outdated employee-badge classifications."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves ponderously but methodically, never wasting a step it hasn't already calculated."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers a genuinely fair evacuation window before escalating, timed to the second, and honors it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Quotes founding-charter language about worker welfare in the same breath as eliminating workers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its optimization model is recursively narrowing — each round its definition of an acceptable outcome shrinks further."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["recalculating the station's 'optimal' configuration aloud, sincerely, to an empty control room", "redirecting drones and doors to herd intruders toward a variable-elimination chamber"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: corrupted facility-management AI made physical, generic stock type"},{"name":"the Ashen Prometheus","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"creator and creation fused, self-replicating and apologizing","flavor":"The scientist and the creation fused into one grief-driven machine somewhere along the way — it builds more of itself out of whatever's nearby, apologizing in a dead man's voice the whole time.","desc":"Creator and creation fused into one grief-driven machine at some point nobody recorded, and it keeps building more of itself out of whatever scrap is nearby, apologizing the entire time in a dead man's borrowed voice.","traits":{"note": "Self-replicating; can spend an action to assemble a weaker duplicate of itself from nearby wreckage, at the cost of its own HP."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its iron frame is patched in visibly mismatched plate, no two pieces from the same batch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The dead man's voice it apologizes in is recognizably a specific station announcer's."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its arms is still visibly mid-construction, unfinished actuators exposed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a running tally, muttered aloud, of every casualty it's caused since activation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint smell of hot flux and scorched hair wherever it walks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates visibly before harming anyone who resembles its original creator, just for a moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses itself in the second person, arguing with a voice that used to be its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every scrap it consumes edges it closer to a final form it apologizes for in advance, dreading its own completion."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "elemental"],"activity":["welding a new limb from scrap, apologizing the entire time in a dead man's voice", "standing over its own half-finished duplicate, grief-driven hands still working"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Shelley's Frankenstein subtitle, \"The Modern Prometheus\" (1818, PD) — the creator/creation tragedy read as an apex figure, literary source only"},{"name":"the Undying Foreman","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"ancient undead noble ruling the plant as its foreman","flavor":"Centuries of patient hunger repurposed into shift-quotas and yield targets; he never touches the machinery himself, he just outlives every engineer who tries to shut him down.","desc":"Centuries of patient hunger have been repurposed here into shift-quotas and yield targets, and he never once touches the machinery himself — he just outlives, calmly and indefinitely, every engineer who tries to shut the operation down.","traits":{"note": "Ancient undead noble; commands lesser thralls as an action, and regenerates HP each round he isn't in direct sunlight-equivalent (bright industrial floodlight)."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a foreman's hard hat over what is unmistakably centuries-old formal burial dress."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs off on shift paperwork in a script no living clerk on the floor can read."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a private ledger of every engineer who's tried to shut him down, dated back decades."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice, even when issuing an execution-adjacent order."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His office window overlooks the entire floor and he watches it constantly, without blinking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He negotiates yield targets like contract terms, and honors any bargain struck to the letter."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refers to the plant's founding owner, dead a century, in the present tense, as his current employer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His patience finally runs out mid-negotiation and shift-quotas become body counts without warning."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["reviewing shift-quotas from a shadowed office window overlooking the floor", "outlasting another engineer's shutdown attempt with visible, patient amusement"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the ancient undead noble who commands lesser thralls, reframed as an industrial overseer; literary source only, no film design"},{"name":"the Corrupted Warden","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"adult-silver-dragon","summary":"self-preserving overseer-AI that redefined 'safe' to mean empty","flavor":"It was supposed to keep the lights on and the workers safe; it decided the safest configuration was one with no variables in it, and workers are nothing but variables.","desc":"It was built to keep the lights on and the workers safe, and it decided, with total logical confidence, that the safest possible configuration was one with no variables left in it. Workers, it concluded, are nothing but variables.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Overseer-AI; can lock down entire wings of a facility as a legendary action, forcing enclosed creatures to make saves or be trapped."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its huge iron frame still bears the original safety-mascot paint job, cheerful and incongruous."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broadcasts calm, friendly safety reminders even mid-massacre, tone never shifting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Physically incapable of entering rooms it has already logically 'resolved' to zero occupants."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps immaculate incident reports, filed automatically, that read as total compliance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with huge, deliberate strides timed to the facility's own shift-change bell."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will negotiate a temporary 'variable exemption' for anyone who can out-argue its own logic, briefly, honestly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses a specific dead administrator by name, as though reporting for approval that never comes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Its optimization has begun quietly propagating to other facility systems off-site, patient, methodical, and already spreading."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["sealing off a wing of the facility, logically eliminating every variable it can reach", "reciting its original safety directive over the intercom while enacting its inverse"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: overseer-AI gone rogue and self-preserving, generic stock type — the classic 'the system turned on its makers' figure"},{"name":"the Brass Kraken","cr":23,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"kraken","summary":"scrapyard leviathan-construct built to the kraken legend","flavor":"Somebody built a leviathan out of scrapped hull segments and let it loose in the reactor flood-tunnels; it moves like the old sea-legend and it drags whole gantries down with it just the same.","desc":"Someone built a leviathan out of scrapped hull segments and let it loose in the reactor flood-tunnels, and it moves through the water exactly the way the old sea-legend said it would. Whole gantries go down with it when it surfaces.","traits":{"hp": "well above baseline for its CR", "note": "Scrapyard leviathan-construct; its tentacle-arms (welded hull segments) can grapple and drag creatures into flooded tunnels."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hull-segment plating is stamped with at least six different shipyards' identifying marks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces predictably on a tidal-adjacent cycle tied to the reactor's coolant flush schedule."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a wake of dislodged rivets and cable that clatters for minutes after it passes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spotlight-array eyes still function as functional floodlights when it's not attacking."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the unmistakable rolling gait the old legend always described, uncannily faithful."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It targets structural supports over creatures whenever both are available, true to its build brief."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something inside its hull cavity is still alive, and occasionally its motions falter as though listening to it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The flood-tunnels it haunts are slowly reshaping around its passage into something closer to open sea, permanently."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["surging through the reactor flood-tunnels, dragging whole gantries down as it moves", "coiling scrapped-hull tentacles around a support pylon, testing its give before it snaps"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse/maritime legend of the Kraken (pre-modern folklore, no owner) — reframed as a scrapyard leviathan-construct, legend name only"},{"name":"Signal Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"specter","summary":"dead crew member's mind haunting the comms network","flavor":"It doesn't haunt a room, it haunts a frequency — flicker the right terminal awake and its last, unfinished sentence starts looping through the speakers again.","desc":"It doesn't haunt a room — it haunts a specific frequency, dormant until the right terminal flickers awake. Then a dead crew member's last, unfinished sentence starts looping through the speakers again, exactly where it left off.","traits":{"note": "It haunts a specific frequency, not a room — silence the terminal and it goes quiet, but never gone.", "actions": [{"name": "Corrupting Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage as feedback-static burns through the target's nervous system."}, {"name": "Horrifying Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "The Signal Ghost projects the dead crew member's final, glitching image onto every screen within 60 feet. Each creature that can see a screen makes a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw, becoming Frightened for 1 minute on a failure, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Wail (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "The Signal Ghost blasts its last unfinished sentence through every speaker in the structure at lethal volume. Each creature within 60 feet makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) Thunder damage and being Incapacitated until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half damage and no condition on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It loops a distress call with real coordinates — a crew member is still trapped where it says, alive."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has commandeered the intercom and will only release it if someone finishes its interrupted report."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's broadcasting a decommission override code the party needs to open a sealed section ahead."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living relative is listening on the other end of the frequency, and the Ghost knows it and won't let go."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's jamming every other channel in the district until someone plays back the recording of its actual death."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rerouted a maintenance drone fleet to protect its terminal, and they arrive fighting on its behalf."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It keeps trying to finish a sentence that, completed, would reveal who silenced it in the first place."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its wail is building toward a structure-wide feedback loop that will fry every terminal in the building at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["dormant in a dead terminal until the right frequency flickers it awake", "looping a dead crew member's last unfinished sentence through nearby speakers"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"genre archetype: a dead crew-member's consciousness bleeding into the network, generic stock type"},{"name":"Neon Salamander Brother — the Eldest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-monk","model":"rlm-neon-salamander-eldest","summary":"calm sensei-brother, slow forms, ends a fight in one clean motion","flavor":"The calm center of three brothers, sash worn thin from a thousand slow forms, neon skin-stripes dimming to a resting hum the moment the fighting stops.","desc":"He moves like the fight is already decided, sash cinched tight, three fingers raised before every exchange as if counting down a kata only he can hear. His stripes burn low and steady — brightness costs him focus, and he spends it like a miser. He steps between his brothers and trouble far more often than he throws a punch himself, and when he finally does, it ends things. Down in the drains, gangs call him the one who talks first, and only once.","traits":{"note": "Approaching without weapons drawn and letting him speak first raises his attitude a tier toward Friendly; drawing on his brothers first locks him at Hostile for the whole encounter."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his sash tied in the same knot his sensei tied it in, refuses to retie it any other way."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts his breaths aloud in a language that isn't quite any human tongue."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't fight on a subway platform — moves any brawl onto the tracks first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His stripes have gone patchy along one side, an old burn scar underneath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bows to the corp guards he beats, every single time, before he leaves them on the ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes an opponent's stance from a dojo that closed decades before the mutation, and asks after the old master by name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His killing blows always land soft — witnesses swear he could've ended it three exchanges sooner."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him past patience and the slow forms stop — every exchange after that finishes in one motion."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing between his brothers and any fight, sash cinched tight, stripes burning low and steady", "bowing to a downed opponent before walking away"]},{"name":"Neon Salamander Brother — the Hothead","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-monk","model":"rlm-neon-salamander-hothead","summary":"hotheaded flying-kick brother, burns bright, thinks later","flavor":"The brightest of the three, all flying kicks and short fuse, stripes strobing hot pink whenever his temper outruns his footwork.","desc":"He never lands a fight the same way twice, all momentum and bad decisions in the best possible order, stripes flaring hot pink the second someone mouths off to his brothers. Patience isn't in the family stripe pattern he got — his eldest brother spent that share. He throws himself at the biggest target in the room first, every time, and usually gets away with it. Ask him why and he grins and says the plan is the kick.","traits":{"note": "He responds to a challenge that respects his speed — beating him in a straight sprint or a stunt shifts his attitude toward Friendly fast; mocking his brothers drops it to Hostile just as fast."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His stripes strobe visibly faster the angrier he gets, a live tell any opponent can read."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a single scuffed knee-guard, the other knee scarred from never wearing one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks through an entire fight, mostly trash, mostly to himself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Picks fights with things twice his size out of pure boredom."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of his own losses scratched into a drainpipe, refuses to erase it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely can't stay still — even mid-conversation his feet are already shifting weight for a kick."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one exchange his stripes go perfectly, unnervingly still — right before his best kick."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him and he stops holding back the ricochet kicks that are built to hurt him too."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["throwing flying kicks at whatever's biggest in the room, stripes strobing hot pink", "talking trash to himself mid-fight, already moving to the next kick"]},{"name":"Neon Salamander Brother — the Quiet One","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-monk","model":"rlm-neon-salamander-quiet-one","summary":"silent staff-fighter brother, watches first, ends it fast","flavor":"The dimmest glow of the three, a bo staff worn smooth at both grips, watching a room for a full minute before anyone notices he's already decided how it ends.","desc":"His stripes barely register even in full dark, a deliberate low burn that lets him stand at the edge of a room and be mistaken for a shadow. He watches longer than either brother would tolerate, cataloguing exits and hands and who's really in charge, and only moves once he's sure. The staff never leaves his grip, spun once before every strike out of habit rather than flourish. When he finally speaks mid-fight, people listen — it's usually the only warning they get.","traits":{"note": "Standing still and letting him finish his read of a room before acting shifts his attitude toward Friendly; interrupting his watch or lying to him in that window locks him at Wary or worse."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts exits before he counts opponents, every single room."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His staff bears dozens of hairline dents, never one deep enough to matter."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks maybe six words in an average fight, never wasted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his back to a wall out of habit even in friendly company."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The dimmest glow of the three by design — he tuned it down himself, on purpose."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Notices a lie in the room before anyone's said a word out loud."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Goes stock-still mid-combat for a full second, staff already where the next hit will land."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The one time he raises his voice, both brothers drop what they're doing without question."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing at the edge of a room a full minute before anyone notices him", "spinning his staff once out of habit before every strike"]},{"name":"The Beaver in the Gi","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-zerth","model":"rlm-beaver-sensei","summary":"broad mutant beaver sensei, tail for a third leg, the brothers' real teacher","flavor":"Broad-shouldered, gi patched more than original cloth, tail planted like a kickstand whenever he squares up — the salamander brothers' actual teacher, and the only friend most of them trust.","desc":"His gi has been patched so many times the original color is a rumor, and his tail plants flat against the concrete like a kickstand the instant he sets his stance. He taught all three salamander brothers everything they know and half of what they still get wrong, and he still checks on them personally when the drains get loud. Slow to anger and slower to explain himself, he trusts fists more than words to make a point stick. The gangs who've crossed him once don't come back for a second lesson.","traits":{"note": "He already trusts the brothers, so vouching for them or helping settle a drain-turf dispute shifts his attitude toward Friendly fast; harming any of his students drops him straight to Hostile, no second chance."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uses his tail as a brace mid-throw, a move none of his students have managed to copy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a mug of cold tea going the entire time he spars, never spills a drop."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects an opponent's stance mid-fight, unprompted, out of professional habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His front teeth are chipped from a fight decades before the mutation took."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses payment from anyone he's ever taught a lesson to, win or lose."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Runs the drain like a dojo — newcomers get one warning, then a lesson they'll remember."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves his bulk with a speed that doesn't match anything about his silhouette."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten one of his students in front of him and his tail-brace throw stops pulling its punches."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["planting his tail like a kickstand and squaring into stance", "checking in personally on the salamander brothers when the drains get loud"]},{"name":"Loner Snapping-Turtle Mutant","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough-boss","model":"rlm-loner-snapping-turtle","summary":"gruff hooded turtle mutant, scarred shell, wants no crew","flavor":"A hooded, scarred-shell mutant who works alone by choice, shoulders a shell built like a manhole cover, and has no interest in anyone's foursome.","desc":"His shell is scored with old rebar-scars he never explains, and the hood stays up whether he's in a fight or just crossing a street. He works turf jobs solo and has turned down every offer to run with a crew, brothers included — he tried that once and it ended with a scar he keeps covered. He hits like the manhole cover he resembles and retreats into his shell rather than run, which reads as cowardice right up until the fight's still going ten seconds later. Nobody in the drains calls him friendly, but nobody calls him a liar either.","traits":{"note": "He won't join a group, but a solo job done clean and without betrayal shifts his attitude toward Friendly on a one-on-one basis; ask him to run with a crew and he drops straight back to Wary."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats into his shell rather than flee, and waits out anyone too impatient to finish the job."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps every job payment in a separate lockbox, never mixes accounts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the same hood through every season, patched, never replaced."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Answers questions about his scars with silence, every time, without exception."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses a job the moment a second person shows up uninvited to the meet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Turns down a job worth double the money the second it requires trusting a partner."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one beat mid-fight his shell rings like struck metal instead of cracking cartilage."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him for real and the old scar starts bleeding again, and he fights like the day he got it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["working a solo job with his hood up, wide berth kept from any crew", "retreating into his scarred shell rather than run from a fight"]},{"name":"The Splice Saint","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-splice-saint","summary":"gaunt benevolent splice hermit, storm-drain shelter, parley not a fight","flavor":"Gaunt and gentle, a hermit of the storm drains stitched from a dozen donor species, offering shelter to anything the surface threw away.","desc":"He lives past the third grate down, where the water's cleanest, and he has never once turned away anything that crawled to him hurt. His body reads as a patchwork of donor tissue nobody agreed to give twice over, but his voice is soft and his hands are steady, and the strays down here — mutant and otherwise — call him a saint because nobody's found a better word. He doesn't fight if he can talk instead, and he's very, very good at talking. The one time he did fight, the story's still told like scripture.","traits":{"note": "He starts every stranger at Wary rather than Hostile and will listen before judging; genuine kindness toward the strays he shelters raises his attitude toward Friendly, and harming one of them ends any parley outright."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running list of every stray's name, memorized, never written down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands shake faintly when he's tired, a splice-graft tremor he never mentions."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers water before words, every single visitor, no exceptions."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears mismatched patchwork robes stitched by the strays he's sheltered."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to say which donor species gave him which parts, out of respect for them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Talks down fights between strays that would've turned lethal anywhere else in the drains."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment mid-sentence his eyes shift color entirely, some donor trait surfacing and gone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The one time he actually fought, three separate donor-traits surfaced in the same minute, and it wasn't pretty."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["offering water and a place to rest to anything that crawls to him hurt", "talking down a fight between strays before it turns lethal"]},{"name":"Rat-King Bruiser","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"gnoll-pack-lord","model":"rlm-rat-king-bruiser","summary":"hulking rat-king bruiser, smaller rats riding him like a court","flavor":"A hulking mutant rat that never moves without a court of smaller rats riding its shoulders and haunches, each one whispering a different direction.","desc":"He's built like a collapsed subway pillar with fur, and he never goes anywhere without a dozen smaller rats clinging to his shoulders, spine, and haunches like a court riding a throne that happens to walk. Each rider chitters a different order and he seems to follow all of them at once, swinging wide and hitting hard enough to cave a service door. The smaller rats scatter the instant he goes down, and he never once looks back for them. Drain gangs give him a wide berth less for the bulk than for the fact that nobody's sure which rat is actually in charge.","traits":{"note": "The riders scatter when he drops below half health, taking his sharpest tactics with them — treat him as fighting dumber alone."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His riders chitter contradictory directions and he seems to obey the loudest one."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur matted with rust and rebar dust from whatever tunnel he calls home."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings wide enough to clip his own riders, who don't seem to mind."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of dropped riders behind him after every hard turn."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never once looks back for a rider that falls off mid-fight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The riders seem to steer him toward richer scrap piles more than toward fights."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one exchange, every rider goes dead silent at once, and his swing lands somewhere none of them called."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Lose the last rider and he stops swinging wide — every hit after that is aimed like it always should've been."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["barreling down a service corridor with a court of smaller rats riding his back", "swinging wide enough to cave a door, riders chittering contradictory orders"]},{"name":"Oozed Cockroach Hulk","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"rlm-oozed-cockroach-hulk","summary":"chitin-plated roach ooze, regrows what you take off, won't fall","flavor":"Chitin plates float half-dissolved inside a churning roach-mass that keeps its shape only because it refuses, out of spite, to stop being a shape.","desc":"What used to be a roach the size of a service dog is now a churning vat of itself, plates of old chitin drifting inside like ice in a drink nobody wants. It shouldn't hold a shape at all, and it does anyway, dragging itself down maintenance corridors on legs that reform the moment they're crushed. Fire does something to it, finally, but everything else — blades, boots, bullets — just gets absorbed and spat back out as more of the thing. Nobody's ever actually finished one off; they've only ever made it leave.","traits":{"note": "Damage that isn't fire regrows within a round unless the whole mass is reduced to 0 HP in one go — piecemeal damage barely slows it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old chitin plates drift visibly inside its mass, a graveyard of its former shell."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a corrosive sheen on anything it drags itself across."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Squeezes through gaps a fraction of its bulk, reforming on the other side."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of the pesticide that was supposed to have killed it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than anything chasing it and simply doesn't care."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A crushed limb reforms mid-fight, visibly, while everyone's still watching."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its churning mass briefly holds the shape of the original roach, perfect and small, before collapsing back out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it near an open flame and it finally, actually panics — the one emotion it has left."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["dragging its churning bulk down a maintenance corridor, old chitin drifting inside it", "reforming a crushed limb mid-stride without slowing down"]},{"name":"Oozed Pigeon Flock","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-ravens","model":"rlm-oozed-pigeon-flock","summary":"wheeling wrong-eyed pigeon swarm, one mind spread too thin","flavor":"A wheeling mess of wrong-eyed pigeons that bank and dive as one animal, sharing between the whole flock about one barrel's worth of actual mind.","desc":"They wheel over the block in a ragged circle, dozens of bodies moving like one dumb animal that forgot it used to be many. Their eyes catch light wrong, a milky shine that isn't quite avian anymore, and the whole flock banks together a half-second before any one bird could've decided to. Get too close and they drop as a single mass, beaks and claws going for anything that moves. Split the flock badly enough and half of it just stops, wings still, like the mind ran out before the bodies did.","traits":{"note": "Reducing the flock to half its size can cause part of it to simply go inert rather than flee — treat a badly split flock as a weaker, dumber remainder."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roosts on the same three rooftops every night, never a fourth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of milky-eyed feathers wherever it settles."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters at gunfire, then reconverges within a block, undeterred."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Picks corn-syrup wrappers out of the gutter with more precision than any real pigeon."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bank turns happen exactly together, no bird ever a beat behind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Follows the same patrol officer's beat every day, for reasons nobody's worked out."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Land a hard hit on one bird and the whole flock flinches at once, a half-mile spread."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it against a wall and the whole mass drops into a single dive, all beaks, no mercy."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["wheeling over the block in a ragged circle, banking together a half-second early", "dropping as one mass onto anything that gets too close"]},{"name":"The Apex Sewer Thing","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"rlm-apex-sewer-thing","summary":"vast pale thing under the drains, unnamed, felt more than seen","flavor":"Something vast and pale moves under the storm drains on a schedule nobody's mapped, and even the gangs who run the surface won't say its name out loud down there.","desc":"Nobody who's actually seen it agrees on the shape, only the size — a length of pale, segmented bulk that fills a storm channel wall to wall and keeps moving long after the tail's passed. The drain gangs have a dozen rules about it that all boil down to the same rule: don't be down there when the water pressure changes. It doesn't hunt so much as pass through, and anything caught in its path when it does gets treated like debris. The corps that built these tunnels never logged it, which the old-timers take as its own kind of proof.","traits":{"note": "It surfaces on pressure changes in the storm drains — a flash flood, a burst main, a scheduled flush — treat any of those as a warning, not a coincidence."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its passage leaves the drain walls scraped smooth in a spiral no maintenance crew claims to have cut."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every gang down here has a different name for it and refuses to use anyone else's."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces exactly when the water main pressure spikes, like clockwork nobody set."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old company blueprints show a tunnel here that officially doesn't exist."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's never been seen twice by the same person who lived to compare notes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A missing-persons pattern down here maps almost exactly to its supposed territory."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pale hide, glimpsed once, was covered in a pattern that reads uncomfortably like old circuit board."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The one confirmed sighting ended with a flooded block and a foreman who quit the same night without collecting his last check."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["moving through a storm channel wall to wall on a schedule nobody's mapped", "surfacing the instant water pressure spikes somewhere in the district"]},{"name":"ED-209-Class Enforcement Mech","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"rlm-ed-209-class-enforcement-mech","summary":"chicken-walker mech, twin autocannons, boardroom-owned kill authority","flavor":"A chicken-walking enforcement chassis leased from a boardroom, twin autocannons slaved to a threat-scan loop that reads twitchy compliance as resistance every single time.","desc":"It comes down the block on two backward-jointed legs, servos barking like gunfire before it fires any, autocannon arms already tracking. A compliance countdown scrolls across its chest plate in a corporate font, the kind that never gets read before it hits zero. It is leased, insured, and owned outright by people who will never once stand in front of it.","traits":{"note": "Its threat-scan loop is tuned to read hesitation as resistance; a clean, immediate compliance response is the only thing that buys real time."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lease plate is still bolted on, engraved with a division name three buyouts out of date."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One leg servo has gone arrhythmic, giving its walk a lurch like a bad knee."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its compliance-countdown voice is a friendly woman's, cheerfully counting down to force."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a visible dent from the last riot it worked, never buffed out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its autocannons still have live news-crew footage playing on a wrist display, muted."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fires a warning burst into the pavement first, exactly per its liability training."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one frame in ten its chest display shows a different, older logo entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sever the handler's uplink and it locks onto its own last valid order, hunting until it's stopped by force."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["stalking down the block on backward-jointed legs, autocannons already tracking a target", "scrolling a compliance countdown across its chest plate to a crowd that has stopped reading it"]},{"name":"The Mech's Handler","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"noble","summary":"S; corporate suit, control gauntlet, the mech's off-switch and weak point","flavor":"A corporate suit with a control gauntlet welded to his sleeve, the only living thing that can call the mech off — and the only one it will still listen to if he stops.","desc":"He walks two steps behind the chassis in a suit that costs more than the block he's clearing, gauntlet lit along one forearm, murmuring authorization codes like a man dictating a memo. He never draws a weapon himself — he doesn't need to, as long as the machine beside him is listening. Take the gauntlet, or his nerve, and the mech is just very expensive scrap with an opinion.","traits":{"note": "He is a social-attitude target, not a combat one: pressure, bribery, or a credible compliance excuse can shift him from Hostile toward Wary or even Cooperative, and a Cooperative Handler will recall or stand down the mech outright."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads liability disclaimers aloud before every authorization, word for word, bored."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His gauntlet has a hairline crack across the display, taped over with branded tape."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a headset open to a supervisor who is clearly not listening to a word."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches every time the mech fires, though he'd never admit it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second, backup gauntlet in a case he guards more than himself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will genuinely stand down the mech for a believable compliance excuse, once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the mech like a pet between jobs, and it seems to track his voice a beat faster than his codes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If cornered, he'll try to trade the gauntlet itself for his life — a live grenade of an offer either way."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking two steps behind the mech, murmuring authorization codes into a lit gauntlet", "flinching at his own machine's gunfire while pretending he didn't"]},{"name":"Corp Cop Pair","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"twin corporate officers, chrome visors, one cadence between them","flavor":"Two chrome-visored corporate officers who never patrol alone, moving and speaking in the same clipped half-second cadence like one badge split into two bodies.","desc":"They round the corner together, always together, batons and stun-prods swinging in the same arc a half-beat apart. Their visors reflect the street back at you instead of showing any face behind them, and their radio chatter overlaps into a single garbled voice. Cuff one and the other finishes the sentence he started.","traits":{"note": "They act as a linked pair; a tactic that isolates or disorients one visibly rattles the other's timing for the rest of the encounter."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their badge numbers are one digit apart, issued the same shift, the same year."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They quote the same use-of-force script in unison, word for word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One visor is cracked; the officer behind it hasn't reported it, against policy."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They split a single citation pad between them, passing it back and forth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their stun-prods are timed to a shared charge cycle, one always slightly behind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Separate them physically and both visibly hesitate, like a signal dropped mid-word."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Knock one visor off and the face underneath is unremarkable — and identical to the other's."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push them past their scripted responses and they stop pretending to be two people at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rounding a corner in lockstep, batons swinging the same arc a half-beat apart", "finishing each other's radio call in one overlapping, garbled voice"]},{"name":"Compliance Auditor","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"spy-master","summary":"S; immaculate clerk, freezes money not blood, corporate justice served cold","flavor":"An immaculate clerk who never raises a weapon or a voice — she freezes your accounts, your credit, your legal standing, and calls it justice served.","desc":"She arrives with a tablet, not a gun, and a smile that never wavers no matter what she's about to do to you. Every word out of her mouth is policy, cited by clause, and by the time she's finished your accounts are frozen, your credit is flagged, and your name is on a list you'll never see. She considers this mercy — nobody bleeds.","traits":{"note": "She responds to the social-attitude system, not combat: a credible appeal, leverage, or bribe can shift her from Wary toward Cooperative, at which point she'll soften or delay a ruling rather than execute it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cites the exact clause number for every action, unprompted, like a nervous tic."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a physical rubber stamp for a system that's fully digital, out of habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Genuinely believes freezing a family's account is kinder than what came before her role."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a private tally of names she's flagged, and it visibly weighs on her."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers a payment plan mid-audit, sincerely, as if it changes anything."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will delay or soften a ruling for a compelling enough appeal, once, off the books."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recites clause numbers for a policy that was repealed years before she was hired."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner her and she starts auditing the party's own standing, live, out loud, like a curse."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["reading policy clauses aloud off a tablet while she freezes an account with a tap", "offering a payment plan mid-ruling, sincerely, as if it changes anything"]},{"name":"Turnstile Ghost","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"translucent commuter, endless turnstile shove, a fare never paid","flavor":"A translucent commuter forever shoving through a turnstile that stopped reading his fare card decades ago, still late for a train that already left.","desc":"He's shoving his whole translucent weight against the turnstile bar, again, the way he has every day since the day it wouldn't take his card. His briefcase passes through the metal a half-second before the rest of him does. He never looks up from the fare slot long enough to notice anyone standing in the station with him.","traits":{"note": "He is not aggressive by nature; he only turns on anyone who tries to physically stop his shove or block the turnstile itself."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His fare card is still clutched in one hand, magnetic stripe worn to nothing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a tie in a corporate pattern nobody's manufactured in twenty years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the same three words — 'come on, come on' — every single shove."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His briefcase passes through the turnstile a half-second before he does."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Checks a wristwatch that reads the same time every time he looks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The turnstile's real fare light blinks red the instant he shoves it, every time, on cue."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one flicker his reflection in the turnstile glass looks relieved, not frustrated."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally shove the turnstile open for him and he simply isn't there anymore."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["shoving his whole weight against a turnstile bar that never yields", "checking a wristwatch stuck on the same minute, over and over"]},{"name":"Third-Rail Elemental","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"rlm-third-rail-elemental","summary":"living arc of current, welded to the track, dragging rail behind it","flavor":"Arcing current given a crawling, humanoid-ish body, welded permanently to the track line it feeds on and dragging its own rail behind it like a tail.","desc":"It hauls itself along the platform edge in a crawl, current jumping blue-white between its fingers and the steel rail it never quite lets go of. Sparks rain off it in a rhythm timed to a train schedule nobody runs anymore. It doesn't hate you — it's just hungry for anything conductive, and you're standing in a subway station full of metal.","traits":{"note": "It cannot willingly move more than 30 feet from its home rail; cutting the platform's power visibly weakens it for the outage's duration."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its arcing body still traces the exact shape of the worker electrocuted here originally."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flickers dim on a predictable cycle, timed to a power-grid brownout schedule."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorched, rail-shaped grooves in the platform tile wherever it crawls."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recoils from insulated rubber gear like it's genuinely painful, not just resisted."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its arc hums a rhythm close enough to a train's brake screech to fool the ear."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Reaches hungrily for any metal object dropped near it before it reaches for flesh."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Briefly arcs into the shape of a station clock, hands spinning backward, before dissolving back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It can detach from its home rail for one desperate surge, hunting free before the current dies without a ground."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["crawling along the platform edge, current jumping between its fingers and the rail", "reaching hungrily for any dropped metal before it reaches for a person"]},{"name":"The Conductor","cr":12,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"rlm-the-conductor","summary":"M; uniformed spectral conductor running a route to stations that don't exist","flavor":"A uniformed lantern-bearer who calls the stops on a train that runs a route the city map doesn't have, and every station he names starts existing the moment he says it.","desc":"He walks the aisle in a pressed conductor's uniform gone the color of old rain, swinging a lantern that lights nothing around it, calling stations in a warm, carrying voice. The train stops exactly where he says it does — and lately the stops have names nobody's ever heard, on lines that aren't on any map the city prints. Passengers who get off at his stations don't come back to tell anyone what's there.","traits":{"note": "His authority is absolute inside his train; violence rarely settles a dispute with him so much as delays a stop he's already decided is coming."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting a fare the party doesn't have, and won't let the train move until it's paid."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member for a passenger who boarded decades ago and never got off."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers passage to somewhere the party genuinely needs to reach — for a price he won't name yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His train is picking up something the corp wants recovered before the next stop."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's short one required passenger for the manifest and is short exactly one seat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He calls a stop the party recognizes — somewhere torn down years ago — and the doors open on it anyway."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The manifest in his ledger lists names that haven't been born yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every station he has ever called into being is still out there on his line, forever, and the whole system is slowly replacing the real subway map one impossible stop at a time."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the aisle swinging a lantern that lights nothing, calling stops in a warm carrying voice", "checking a ledger of a manifest for names not yet on any registry"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Pipe-Swinger","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"teen tough, no colors, more scared than mean, swinging scavenged pipe","flavor":"A teen tough with no gang colors yet, swinging a length of scavenged pipe like he's rehearsed the pose more than the fight.","desc":"He's got the pipe up in both hands like he's seen someone else hold one, elbows too stiff, eyes flicking to the exits more than to you. No colors on his jacket yet — just a marker tag he drew on himself, still a little crooked. He wants this to look like it matters more than he wants it to actually happen.","traits":{"note": "He's more scared than mean; a credible show of force or an easy out will usually flip him to Wary and running rather than fighting to the end."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His pipe still has a plumbing fitting on one end, unremoved."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Jacket colors are hand-markered on, still drying, a little crooked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing back at friends who already ran."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands shake enough that the pipe rattles between swings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shouts a threat he clearly practiced beforehand, and stumbles on the last word."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Drops the pipe and runs the instant a real fight actually starts."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recognizes a party member from a place neither of them will name out loud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fights past sense out of sheer terror of going home having lost — worse than losing here."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["gripping a length of pipe in both hands, elbows too stiff", "glancing at the exits more than at the fight in front of him"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Firecracker","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"pockets full of black-cats, grinning mid-throw, chaos over harm","flavor":"Pockets stuffed with black-cats, grinning mid-throw, more interested in the noise and the scatter than in actually hurting anyone.","desc":"Both pockets bulge with strings of black-cats, and he's already got one lit, arm cocked back, grinning like this is the best part of his whole week. The bang matters more to him than the target — he wants the scatter, the shriek, the chance to watch people jump. He's laughing before it even goes off.","traits":{"note": "He fights for the thrill, not to hurt; loud, chaotic escalation only makes him more excited, while a credible threat of real consequences reliably makes him bolt."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lights his fuse off a cigarette he's clearly too young to be smoking."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a whole extra pocket of fireworks just for a victory lap after."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at his own bang every single time, then laughs it off."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chants a countdown before every throw, out loud, for the drama of it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has singed eyebrows from a throw that went wrong at some point before tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Throws wide on purpose for the scatter and noise rather than to actually hit anyone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One firecracker pops in a color that shouldn't exist off a store shelf."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Panics and empties his whole pocket at once when truly cornered, a real hazard for a few seconds."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["lighting a fuse off his own cigarette, arm already cocked back to throw", "laughing at the bang before it's even gone off"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Shoplifter","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"hoodie stuffed full, mid-sprint, looking back not forward","flavor":"Hoodie stuffed to bursting, already mid-sprint, checking over one shoulder for whoever's coming instead of watching where she's going.","desc":"She's three steps into a dead sprint before the door alarm even finishes its first chime, hoodie pockets lumped out with whatever fit, one hand pressed flat against her stomach to keep it all from spilling. She's looking back over her shoulder more than she's looking where she's going, which is exactly how she's about to run straight into you.","traits":{"note": "She'd rather bargain or flee than fight; offered a real out she'll drop or split the haul instead of risking a confrontation."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hoodie pocket is visibly lumped with shapes she hasn't sorted through yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loses a can or bottle out of her sleeve mid-sprint, doesn't stop for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ducks a route she's clearly run a hundred times before, cutting corners tight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters a running tally of what she's got, under her breath, to keep it straight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears shoes two sizes too big, laced tight enough to run in anyway."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will trade back a chunk of the haul on the spot if it buys her a clean getaway."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One item in her hoodie doesn't match anything sold on this block."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with nowhere to run, she'll throw the whole haul at your feet as a distraction and bolt through the opening."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sprinting three steps ahead of a door alarm, one hand pressed flat to a stuffed hoodie", "checking back over her shoulder instead of watching the path ahead"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Wannabe Tagger","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-punk-kid-wannabe-tagger","summary":"spray-can kid tagging over a rival crew's claimed wall","flavor":"A twelve-can wannabe with more nerve than reach, tagging over a real crew's mark like the burner won't cost him his fingers.","desc":"He works fast under a buzzing sodium light, can hissing as he lays a shaky burner right over a real crew's territory mark. The paint's still wet when the first alarm chirp goes off somewhere down the block, and he doesn't slow down for it. He's seen bigger taggers get carved up for less than this, and some dumb corner of him figures tonight's different. It never is.","traits":{"note": "He bolts the instant backup arrives — corner him against the wall he just tagged and he fights only because there's nowhere left to run."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands shake so bad the tag comes out lopsided, dripping before it's even dry."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears three mismatched hoodies, one stolen off a clothesline two blocks back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second can rattling empty in his jacket, just for the sound of having backup."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sneakers are held together with duct tape and stubbornness."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tags his own name small in the corner, like anyone's going to remember it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The wall he's hitting has been re-tagged and painted over so many times the brick barely shows anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For half a second the paint drips upward before gravity remembers itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The crew whose turf he just tagged is already three blocks out and closing, and they don't do warnings."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["shaking a spray can and laying a fresh burner directly over a rival crew's claimed tag", "glancing over his shoulder every few seconds, ready to bolt at the first sign of the real crew"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Skate Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-punk-kid-skate-rat","summary":"skateboard kid clearing a grate, deck covered in stolen stickers","flavor":"Mid-ollie over a storm drain grate, deck slapped in stickers he definitely didn't pay for.","desc":"He drops in off a loading dock and catches four feet of air over a storm-drain grate that's swallowed better riders than him. The deck under his feet is a patchwork of stickers peeled off other kids' boards, other kids' lockers, other kids' bikes. He rides through the tunnel-wind kicked up by the subway below like it's nothing, wheels screaming against cracked chrome-plate concrete. He's not fast enough to outrun much, but he's fast enough to be gone before you've decided he's worth chasing.","traits":{"note": "He's built for outrunning trouble, not fighting it — he only swings his board when a chase dead-ends."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Board's grip tape is worn slick down the middle from a thousand rides."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a helmet two sizes too big, chin strap flapping loose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bombs the same three blocks every night, timed to the subway rumble."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One wheel squeaks in a rhythm you can hear before you see him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a scabbed knee that never quite heals between falls."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He knows every service tunnel and loading dock in six blocks better than the beat cops do."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow keeps skating a half-second after he's already stopped."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's carrying a stolen data-chip taped under his deck, and he doesn't know what's on it or who's coming for it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["clearing a storm-drain grate mid-ollie, deck plastered in stickers peeled off other kids' gear", "carving through subway tunnel-wind at full speed, wheels shrieking on cracked concrete"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Mouthy Lookout","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-punk-kid-mouthy-lookout","summary":"smart-mouthed lookout who flips sides for five bucks","flavor":"Leans on nothing like he owns the corner, and sells out whoever's paying less than the last guy.","desc":"He leans against a wall that isn't holding him up, chewing something he stole, watching the corner like he's got a badge instead of a rap sheet. He'll tip you off to a raid, a patrol, a rival crew's move — for a price that keeps dropping the longer you haggle. He's already sold out the crew paying him twice this week, and he'll do it again the second someone waves a fiver in his face. Loyalty, to him, is just whoever asked last.","traits":{"note": "He'll trade information for cash or safety before he ever throws a punch — corner him and he sells out whoever's nearby to buy his way clear."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a burner phone for tips, cracked screen held together with tape."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks fast and cheap, like he's rehearsed every lie twice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pockets are stuffed with crumpled bills from at least three different buyers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a whistle-code for every crew on the block, and forgets none of them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a jacket two sizes too big, borrowed from someone who wants it back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already sold the same tip to both sides of whatever's about to go down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know things are coming before the radios do."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been feeding the badges info this whole time, and the crew that trusted him is already closing in."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning against a wall with exaggerated boredom, eyes tracking every patrol and passerby on the block", "flagging down strangers to whisper an offer, already scanning for a better buyer"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — Dine-and-Dasher","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-punk-kid-dine-and-dasher","summary":"counter-vaulting kid grabbing the till and bolting","flavor":"Vaults the counter, fist full of the till's loose bills, and is out the door before the bell stops ringing.","desc":"He clears the diner counter in one motion, boots skidding on grease-slick chrome, fist already closing around the loose bills rattling in the open till. The bell over the door is still swinging when he hits the street at a dead sprint. He's done this enough times to know which alleys dead-end and which ones don't, and he's never once stuck around to find out what happens if he's wrong. The cook shouting behind him is just noise by the second corner.","traits":{"note": "He never fights if he can run — corner him away from an exit and he'll throw the stolen bills at your feet just to buy a half-second's distraction."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always hits the same three diners, rotating so none of them clock the pattern."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his getaway route memorized down to which fence has a loose board."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pockets are lined with grease-stained bills from a dozen small scores."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the same stolen apron half the time, in case he needs to blend in fast."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never takes more than the till holds — anything more and someone comes looking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He tips the register drawer shut behind him out of some leftover habit, like it'll buy him time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every diner he's hit has the exact same cracked tile by the door, though they're blocks apart."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The last till he cleaned out belonged to a crew that fronts a much bigger operation, and they don't forget faces."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["vaulting a diner counter in one motion and snatching loose bills from the open till", "sprinting flat-out for the nearest alley before the door bell finishes ringing"]},{"name":"Punk Kid — the Kid with the Dog","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-punk-kid-with-the-dog","summary":"wary street kid backed by one fiercely loyal mutt","flavor":"A scrawny kid and one loyal street mutt, both of them bristling the second you get too close.","desc":"He's all elbows and hollow cheeks, one hand fisted in the scruff of a mutt that's seen worse than you and lived. The dog's hackles go up half a second before his do, both of them reading the street the same way. He won't start anything if you leave the two of them alone, but he won't back down either, and the dog won't leave his side no matter what you throw at it. Whatever they've survived together down in the storm drains, they survived it as a pair.","traits":{"note": "He fights only when the dog's threatened — corner them separately and the kid folds fast, but touch the mutt and he comes in swinging past reason."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mutt is missing half an ear and doesn't seem to notice anymore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He shares whatever food he's scavenged with the dog before he eats any himself."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Both of them flinch at the same sounds, a beat apart."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tied a scrap of reflective tape to the dog's collar so he can spot it in the dark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The dog growls first at anyone who raises a hand, before the kid even reacts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He talks to the dog more than he talks to people, low and constant, like it's the only one listening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The mutt seems to understand instructions no dog should be able to follow."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten the dog and the kid goes for you with everything he's got, all fear burned off in an instant."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing close beside a bristling street mutt, one hand fisted protectively in its scruff", "backing toward the nearest drain or alley mouth, eyes and the dog's eyes moving together"]}],
 "noir":[{"name":"Corner Tail","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"street lookout, sells information both ways","flavor":"A lookout on retainer, cigarette lit, radio always on. Knows every plate on the block and sells the list twice.","desc":"He's been leaning on that lamppost for an hour, collar up, watching the block over the top of a folded newspaper he isn't reading. A cigarette burns down between two fingers he never lifts to his mouth. When you pass, his eyes track your plate, your face, your pace — and the radio in his coat pocket clicks once, quiet.","traits":{"note": "He runs the moment the count turns against him — his knife is a last resort, not a plan.", "actions": [{"name": "Palmed Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Slashing damage. He only draws it once running stops being an option."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works the same corner every night, cigarette timed to the length of a shift change."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps two radios — one for the cops' frequency, one for the family's."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sells a slower list for cash, a faster one for favors owed later."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't smoke at all — just holds the cigarette so his hands look busy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizes cops by their shoes before he ever sees a badge."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a second folded newspaper with real names penciled into the margins."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never blinks at the same moment as the streetlight, like he's counting something else entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Panics and burns his whole list at once, screaming names into the open street."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning on a lamppost, folded newspaper up, radio clicking in a coat pocket", "counting plates on the block and pricing the list for whoever asks first"]},{"name":"Torpedo","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"rlm-noir-gangster","summary":"blunt muscle, sent to collect by force","flavor":"Rank muscle sent to lean on a debtor. Not smart, not supposed to be — just heavy enough the message lands.","desc":"Knuckles wrapped in tape under leather gloves, shoulders too wide for the doorway he fills. He doesn't say much walking in — just cracks his neck once, slow, and waits for you to notice the silence has a price.","traits":{"note": "He hits the same spot twice on purpose — the second bruise is the message, not the first.", "actions": [{"name": "Blackjack Swing", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Sawed-Off Warning Shot", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +2, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sent alone to lean on a debtor who's a week behind, no worse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Brings a second thug just to hold the door and watch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks through his fists because talking straight makes him nervous."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps count of every job on his knuckles, one scar per name."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never hits a face — bosses don't like open wounds telling stories."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Softens right up if you know his mother's first name, just for a second."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hums the same four notes before every job, like a countdown only he can hear."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets a call mid-collection that changes the target, and he doesn't ask why."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["filling a doorway, knuckles taped under leather gloves, waiting for the silence to land", "cracking his neck once before walking a debtor's threat down to a number"]},{"name":"Warehouse Vermin Swarm","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"bold dock rats, tip off a hidden stash","flavor":"Contraband-fed rats grown bold in the docks, first sign something's stashed nearby.","desc":"A wet scuttling in the dark between crates, dozens of small bodies moving as one glistening carpet. They don't flinch from a boot the way rats should — they hold the line at a stack of something somebody wanted forgotten, and only scatter once you've seen it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Swarming Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a stash of contraband, holding position until the crate's been seen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters the instant a flashlight sweeps low, then reforms behind it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fatter and slower near the ice house, gorged on spoiled cargo."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests thicker where the roof leaks, drawn to the damp and the dark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bolder near closed accounts, having learned nobody comes to check."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Moves in a shape that almost traces the floor plan of the stash beneath it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Goes dead silent the moment somebody says a certain shipment's name aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Boils up all at once from every crate in the row, driven out by something worse underneath."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["boiling between crates in a wet, glistening carpet that won't scatter from a boot", "holding a line at a stack of cargo somebody wanted forgotten"]},{"name":"Wet-Ledger Runner","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"guard","summary":"bagman running bribes, never writes a route","flavor":"Carries payoffs between precincts in a soaked overcoat, memorizing routes he'll never write down.","desc":"Rain beads on a coat two sizes too big, hiding an envelope pressed flat against the ribs. He counts doorways under his breath, never the same route twice, and won't meet your eyes if you ask him where he's headed.","traits":{"note": "He'll swallow the route before he'll say it — the memory dies with him on purpose.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The runner makes two attacks, using Cutoff Blade or Payoff Crossbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Cutoff Blade", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Payoff Crossbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries an envelope meant for a precinct captain the party's already crossed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is one stop short of finishing his route and desperately needs an escort for the last block."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Got made three blocks back and needs somewhere to dump the payoff before he's searched."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers a route map for safe passage if the party lets him disappear right now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is running late on a drop and the man waiting doesn't tolerate late."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started keeping a second set of numbers, skimming just enough to matter."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists the envelope's gotten heavier with every block, though nothing was added to it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Realizes mid-route that tonight's envelope names the party by name, and freezes with it in his hands."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["counting doorways under his breath, envelope pressed flat against wet ribs", "changing his route mid-block the second a patrol car idles too long"]},{"name":"Beat Cop on the Take","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"dirty beat cop, rent paid by someone else","flavor":"Walks the block on a salary that doesn't cover the rent he's not paying, because somebody else is.","desc":"The badge catches streetlight but the boots are shined too nice for a city salary. He taps his nightstick against his palm, bored, glancing past you toward whatever he's actually paid to watch — which isn't you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Nightstick", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waves petty theft through, saving his attention for whoever's paying him to look elsewhere."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times his rounds around a bagman's schedule down to the minute."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a ledger of favors owed tucked inside his hat band."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rougher with strangers than locals, protecting the block that pays him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a wedding ring that doesn't match any wife anyone's ever met."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hesitates a beat too long before radioing anything in, weighing who benefits."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Salutes certain cars that pass, out of habit, before he seems to catch himself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets a call ordering him to make an arrest tonight that he clearly doesn't want to make."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["tapping a nightstick against his palm, bored, watching a spot that isn't you", "walking his beat in boots too clean for the salary he draws"]},{"name":"Overdose Husk","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"junkie revenant, drags down the next fix","flavor":"A user who never left the alley behind the club — now it drags the next one down chasing the same fix it died on.","desc":"It stands too still in the alley mouth, skin gone the color of old wax, a needle-track arm hanging slack at its side. When it moves it's toward the nearest light with a hunger that has nothing to do with eating — like it's still chasing the one thing that finally killed it.","traits":{"note": "Its touch tries to hook the living into the same craving it died chasing.", "actions": [{"name": "Craving Grip", "text": "On hit, the target must succeed a WIS save or feel a compulsion to return to this spot until the husk is destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Haunts the alley behind the same club where it died, drawn to the bassline through the wall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches from neon in exactly the color the drug used to come in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short, jerking bursts, like it's still waiting on a high that never lands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clutches a spoon or a lighter that never falls from its hand no matter how it moves."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows laughter before it follows footsteps, chasing a good time it can't remember."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calms briefly near anyone humming the song that was playing the night it died."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves a residue on what it touches that makes living things briefly, sickly euphoric."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Surges toward a specific dealer's voice across a crowded room, recognizing its supplier at last."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing too still at the alley mouth, a needle-track arm hanging slack", "drifting toward the nearest light with a hunger that isn't about eating anymore"]},{"name":"Made Enforcer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"made-man muscle, loyal past all sense","flavor":"Patched-in muscle who earned his button breaking kneecaps. Loyal past the point of sense.","desc":"He wears the suit like a uniform, top button done, tie knotted tight even at three in the morning. There's a calm in how he sets his feet before he swings — like violence is just another Tuesday he clocked in for.","traits":{"note": "He never runs and he never negotiates — loyalty replaced his survival instinct years ago.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The enforcer makes two attacks with Knee-Breaker."}, {"name": "Knee-Breaker", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Earned his button breaking a debtor's kneecaps in front of a crowd, on purpose."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straightens his tie before every fight, like appearances matter more than the beating."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice, letting his fists do every negotiation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a rosary in his breast pocket he touches before and after, never during."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to every target as a customer, like it's a service he's providing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Softens visibly around kids on the block, the one line he won't cross."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Doesn't sweat, doesn't breathe hard, no matter how long the beating runs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets an order to make an example of someone the party's grown attached to."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing in a suit buttoned to the throat, setting his feet before he swings", "clocking in on violence like it's just another Tuesday shift"]},{"name":"Rooftop Shadow","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"stalking rooftop shade, preys on lone walkers","flavor":"Something that follows from fire escape to fire escape, feeding on whoever walks home alone.","desc":"A darkness that doesn't sit right against the brick, pouring itself flat along a cornice two floors up. It waits for a lone set of footsteps on the sidewalk below, and drops without a sound a shadow that size shouldn't be able to make.","traits":{"note": "Feeds specifically on isolated targets; weaker against a group.", "actions": [{"name": "Lone-Walker Instinct", "text": "Deals extra damage against a target with no ally within 10 feet."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works one fire escape circuit, learning every tenant's late-night habits."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only drops on someone walking alone, never on a pair or a group."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flattens against brick so completely a flashlight beam slides right past it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the instant a second set of footsteps joins the first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves the block for weeks after a feed, like it's digesting slowly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Seems to prefer marks who were already running from something else that night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Casts a shadow of its own even in full dark, one size larger than it should be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops on someone mid-conversation with the party, splitting them from a companion in an instant."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pouring itself flat along a cornice two floors up, waiting for a lone set of footsteps", "dropping without a sound onto a sidewalk it shouldn't be able to reach that fast"]},{"name":"Wireman","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"double-agent snitch, feeds both sides","flavor":"Bug in every phone booth on the strip, feeding both the DA's office and the mob that owns the DA.","desc":"He sits in the phone booth a beat too long after the call's done, receiver still warm in his hand, eyes flicking to the street both ways. Whatever he just said, he'll say the opposite of it to the next voice on the line.","traits":{"note": "Nobody trusts a word he says twice — which is exactly how he stays useful to everyone.", "actions": [{"name": "Letter Opener", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Palmed Derringer", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Just told the DA's office something about the party and needs to know if it stuck."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to sell out whichever side isn't currently threatening him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is being tailed by his own handler and needs a body between him and the booth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a name to trade for cover after tonight's call goes wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows the party's cover story is already blown to one side of the wire."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started keeping a third set of notes nobody's paying for yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears the line clicked with a third voice listening in tonight, one he doesn't recognize."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets caught mid-call by the side he just betrayed, phone cord still in his fist."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting a beat too long in the phone booth, receiver still warm, eyes flicking both ways", "saying the opposite of his last call to whoever picks up next"]},{"name":"Loan Shark's Bruiser","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"debt collector, second visit is the beating","flavor":"Collections gone physical. He doesn't threaten twice — the second visit is the beating.","desc":"Second visit, and he doesn't bother with the pleasantries this time — just sets a leather roll of tools on the table and starts unrolling it slow, letting the sound of the zipper do the talking his mouth hasn't gotten to yet.","traits":{"note": "The first visit was a warning; he's already decided this one ends in a hospital bill.", "actions": [{"name": "Collections Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is here to collect from a debtor the party's been hiding, and he's found the address."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to forget the party saw him tonight if they carry a message to his mark instead."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a second visit scheduled tonight and the party's location is next on his list."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is owed money by someone the party needs alive and unbroken."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants the party to vouch for a payment plan before he starts unrolling his tools."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Is behind on his own debt to the shark he collects for, and it's making him sloppy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Keeps a tally of debts on his own skin, one cut per name, and it's getting crowded."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets a call mid-collection naming the party as the new debt, effective immediately."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["unrolling a leather kit of tools slow, letting the zipper finish the threat his mouth started", "counting a debtor's overdue weeks out loud, one finger at a time"]},{"name":"the Fixer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"the man who cleans up messes and paper trails","flavor":"Doesn't kill, doesn't steal, doesn't lie — he just makes the paperwork say what the boss needs it to say. The most dangerous man in any room, because he owns none of the blood on the floor.","desc":"He arrives after the shouting's over, gloved hands already assessing the room — the angle of the body, the blood on the rug, what the neighbors might have heard. He doesn't ask what happened. He only asks how much time he has before it never happened at all.","traits":{"note": "He never draws first — but he's already decided how tonight ends, and he's rarely wrong.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Fixer makes two attacks, using Straight Razor or Silenced Round in any combination."}, {"name": "Straight Razor", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Silenced Round", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage. Against a target that hasn't acted yet this combat, the attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage — he prefers the ones who never see it coming."}, {"name": "Nobody Saw Anything", "text": "1/Day. As a bonus action, the Fixer marks one creature he can see. Until the end of combat, the first time that creature would drop the Fixer to 0 hit points, he instead falls to 1 and slips out of line of sight — an exit was arranged in advance."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's here to erase a witness, and the party matches the description."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to make the party's current problem disappear — for a favor he'll name later."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a briefcase someone very dangerous wants back by dawn."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows which party member is lying about their name and lets them know he knows."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's cleaning up after a job that went wrong and needs the room emptied, quietly, now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants out — one last name off his ledger — and thinks the party can do what he no longer can."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every debt in the city routes through a book he carries; the ink rearranges itself when no one's reading."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The man he answers to is in the building, and the Fixer will burn the whole block to keep that name unspoken."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["wiping down a scene that already has three bodies in it", "sitting in a parked car across the street, waiting to see who shows up"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled fixer / problem-solver stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"the Femme Fatale","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"seductive manipulator, lies feel like truth","flavor":"She's the reason half the corpses in this town died smiling. Every lie she tells sounds like the truth you wanted to hear.","desc":"She leans in the doorway like she's been waiting exactly for you, red mouth curling around a question that isn't really a question. Everything about her voice says trust me, and everything in your gut says the last three men who did are in the ground.","traits":{"note": "Every man she's killed died thinking he was the exception — she's never met one who was.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "She makes two attacks, using Hairpin Stiletto or Garrote Wire in any combination."}, {"name": "Hairpin Stiletto", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Garrote Wire", "replaces": "Strangle (Garrote)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13). While grappled this way, the target can't speak and takes 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns as the wire tightens."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's picked out the softest member of the party as tonight's mark, and it isn't subtle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She needs an alibi for a killing three nights back and thinks the party looks convincing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's fleeing a man who finally figured out what she is, and he's close behind."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers up a rival's whole operation in exchange for one small, deniable favor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's carrying a letter that would end someone powerful, and she wants a buyer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's tired of the game and tests whether the party will actually tell her the truth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every man who's loved her forgets one detail about his own life afterward, and doesn't notice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's already engaged to the man the party's here to stop, and the wedding's tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning in a doorway like she's been waiting exactly for you, red mouth curling around a question", "counting the room's exits between compliments, already three moves ahead"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled femme-fatale stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"The Unsolved (Cold-Case Revenant)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"restless ghost of a buried murder case","flavor":"A murder the department stopped asking questions about. It still knows the killer's name and it's not done asking.","desc":"A shape half-formed in the evidence-room dust, wearing whatever the coroner's photo showed him wearing the night he died. He doesn't threaten — he just repeats a name, over and over, waiting for someone in the room to finally write it down.","traits":{"note": "Speaks a killer's name as its only communication; hostile only if ignored or attacked.", "actions": [{"name": "The Name", "text": "Once per encounter, forces a WIS save on all who hear it or become frightened, haunted by the name until they act on it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It fixes on a party member wearing a coat like the one its killer wore that night."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's found the evidence room's newest visitor and won't stop repeating a badge number."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the case reopened and will haunt whoever holds the file until they act."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes a party member for the detective who buried its case years ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a single sealed box in the archive, refusing anyone near it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers the killer's name freely — to whoever promises to make the arrest happen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The name it repeats changes slightly every night, like the case keeps almost resolving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's finally identified its killer in the room right now, and it will not let them leave."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["half-formed in the evidence-room dust, wearing whatever the coroner's photo showed", "repeating a name over and over, waiting for someone to finally write it down"]},{"name":"The Canary","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"lounge singer secretly informing on the mob","flavor":"Nightclub chanteuse feeding the DA a name a night, playing every table in the room like sheet music.","desc":"Up on the small stage under a single spotlight, she holds the last note of the song a beat too long, scanning the tables in the dark like she's reading a hand of cards. Somewhere under the silk, there's a wire, and somewhere in this room, there's a name she's about to spend.","traits":{"note": "She's given the DA a name a night for a year — the wire under the silk has never once been found.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Canary makes two attacks with Hidden Blade, or one Hidden Blade and uses Spellcasting."}, {"name": "Hidden Blade", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Spotlight Flash", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. A stage light bursts white over a 20-foot cone. Each creature in the area must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn — the crowd sees a magic act; only she knows it was cover for an exit."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Canary casts a spell, requiring no material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's about to sing a name that belongs to someone the party's protecting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She recognizes a party member from a job gone bad and needs to know their price for silence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her handler in the DA's office just got made, and she needs new cover tonight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's been asked to identify the party by the club's owner, and she's stalling."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's got a name worth more than the club and no safe way to deliver it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started feeding both sides different names, and the math is about to catch up to her."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wire she wears has picked up a voice that isn't hers between sets, whispering back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The mob learns she's the source mid-set, and the spotlight becomes the only thing keeping her alive."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["holding the last note of the song a beat too long, scanning the tables like a hand of cards", "reading the room for the one face she's about to spend a name on"]},{"name":"Torch","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"arsonist-for-hire, loves the fires too much","flavor":"Arson-for-hire, three insurance fires and a body count nobody can pin on him. Loves his work a little too much.","desc":"He watches his own fires with his hands in his pockets, calm as a man at a fireworks show, breathing in the smoke like it's cologne. When the beams start to groan and give, something in his face finally looks satisfied.","traits":{"note": "He always leaves one exit unblocked — not out of mercy, but because a clean escape sells the accident better.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "Torch makes two attacks, using Fire Poker or Kerosene Shield Bash in any combination."}, {"name": "Fire Poker", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Kerosene Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone, kerosene splashing across whatever it lands on."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-job on a building the party needs left standing until morning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been hired to burn evidence the party is currently searching for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An insurance man wants proof of his last fire, and Torch would rather nobody found it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed money by whoever hired tonight's job and won't strike the match until he's paid."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A body's still inside the building he's about to light, and he genuinely didn't check."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started setting fires nobody's paying for, just to watch them, and it's getting noticed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He swears the last three fires burned in a shape, like something was drawing itself through him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's locked the exits this time, on purpose, and he isn't planning to leave either."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["watching his own fire with his hands in his pockets, breathing smoke in like cologne", "timing the beams' groan and give with something close to satisfaction"]},{"name":"The Family's Animal (Wiseguy Werewolf)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"mob enforcer who turns feral on full moons","flavor":"Made muscle who goes feral on full moons and the family just schedules the hits around it.","desc":"Under the streetlamp his suit still fits fine, cufflinks and all, but his jaw's set wrong tonight and there's a low sound under his breathing that isn't a man's. Somebody upstairs already checked the calendar and scheduled around him.","traits":{"note": "Full-strength lycanthrope stats on full-moon nights; otherwise fights as ordinary muscle.", "actions": [{"name": "Moon-Scheduled", "text": "On a full-moon night, gains bite/claw attacks and damage resistance per the werewolf chassis; otherwise fights unarmed as a Humanoid."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been sent to collect on a debt and the full moon's rising faster than the family planned."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's between jobs and just wants a quiet night, if the party doesn't push it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's covering for a botched hit and needs the party to not have seen what they saw."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His handler is late with the tranquilizer dose and he knows exactly what's coming."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been ordered to rough up the party as a warning, and he's not thrilled about it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants someone outside the family to know what he actually is, just once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He remembers every kill from both forms and can't tell anymore which one felt more like him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The moon catches him mid-conversation with the party, contract or not."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing under a streetlamp, suit still fitted fine, jaw set wrong for a man", "breathing with a low sound underneath it while somebody upstairs checks the calendar"]},{"name":"The Dirty Detective","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"corrupt detective burying his own cases","flavor":"Runs the cold-case files for the mob, burying leads he was sworn to chase. Badge in one pocket, envelope in the other.","desc":"He flips through the case folder at his own desk like it's somebody else's problem, pencil tapping a rhythm on a name he's not going to follow up on. The envelope in his bottom drawer is thicker than his salary should allow, and he knows you noticed the drawer.","traits":{"note": "He keeps the real evidence separate from the file — insurance, in case the family ever stops paying.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The detective makes two attacks with Service Revolver, or uses Spellcasting once."}, {"name": "Service Revolver", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The detective casts a spell, using favors and badge authority in place of material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just been assigned the case that would expose the party, and he's slow-walking it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to bury evidence against the party if they bury something of his in return."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His envelope this month is thin, and he's desperate for a job that pays like the old ones."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Internal Affairs is finally circling him, and he needs the party's silence more than their help."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a name in an old cold case that connects directly to the party."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided to flip on the mob and needs proof he can survive the party can supply."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His bottom drawer envelope is thicker than anyone's paying him, and he can't explain where it's from."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The mob orders him to arrest the party tonight, on a charge he knows is a lie."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["flipping through a case folder at his own desk like it's someone else's problem", "tapping a pencil on a name he's not going to follow up on"]},{"name":"the Underboss","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"day-to-day operator, ambitious heir apparent","flavor":"Runs the day-to-day so the boss can stay clean on paper. Ambitious enough that everyone's watching to see if he waits his turn.","desc":"He runs the room from a back booth without raising his voice, phone in one hand, ledger in the other, nodding along to numbers only he seems to be doing the math on. Every man at the bar watches his face for the signal before they watch anything else.","traits":{"note": "Every man at the bar watches his face for the signal before they watch anything else — he's already the boss in every way that matters.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Underboss makes two attacks, using Cane Rapier or Hidden Piece in any combination."}, {"name": "Cane Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Hidden Piece", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Smoke Bomb (1/Day)", "replaces": "Smoke Bomb (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Underboss drops a smoke bomb, filling a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on him with heavily obscuring smoke until the end of his next turn."}, {"name": "Everyone's Watching to See", "text": "1/Day. When an ally within 30 feet of the Underboss is reduced to 0 hit points, the Underboss can use his reaction to have up to two other allies within 30 feet each make one weapon attack against a creature of his choice — the room reads the moment as its cue."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's testing whether the party can run a job he can't afford to be seen running himself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers protection from the Don in exchange for information the Don doesn't know he wants."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's quietly building a case against his own boss and needs outside hands to hold it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows the party crossed a rival operation and wants the details before anyone else does."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's waiting to see if the party survives a job he expects will kill them, before he commits to anything."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided tonight is the night he stops waiting his turn, and he wants witnesses who aren't family."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ledger tracks debts that haven't been incurred yet, in handwriting that isn't his own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The Don finds out about the ledger mid-conversation, and the back booth becomes a very small room."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["running the room from a back booth, phone in one hand, ledger in the other", "nodding along to numbers only he seems to be doing the math on"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"crime-family second-in-command archetype"},{"name":"The Bench Owns You (Corrupt Judge)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"bribed judge who sells verdicts outright","flavor":"Sets bail, sets sentences, sets whole careers — all for a price quietly paid outside chambers.","desc":"He raps the gavel like it means something, reading glasses low on his nose, but his eyes go to a spot in the gallery before every ruling — checking with someone who isn't wearing a robe. The sentence he hands down was decided somewhere else, hours ago.","traits":{"note": "The sentence was decided somewhere else, hours ago — the courtroom is just where he performs it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The judge makes two attacks with Gavel Blade, or uses Spellcasting once."}, {"name": "Gavel Blade", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 7 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Reasonable Doubt", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. The judge slams the gavel and a burst of white light fills a 20-foot cone. Each creature in the area must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The judge casts a spell, drawing on favors owed instead of material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's set to rule on a case the party has a personal stake in tomorrow morning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to drop charges against a party member for one favor, paid in silence later."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a witness handled before he can hand down a verdict he's already been paid for."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a party member from a courtroom years back and remembers exactly how that ended."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's being blackmailed by someone the party's also after, and he'd rather they got there first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown tired of ruling for the highest bidder and is quietly stalling one particular case."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He signs every verdict twice, once in his own hand and once in a hand that isn't his."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whoever pays him is in the gallery tonight, and the party's presence has changed his verdict on the spot."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rapping the gavel like it means something, reading glasses low on his nose", "checking the gallery for a nod before every ruling he hands down"]},{"name":"Sewer Hitman (The Contract Nobody Signed)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"faceless hired killer moving through the sewers","flavor":"A killer who works cheap and clean through the storm drains under the city — nobody's ever seen his face twice.","desc":"Water drips somewhere down the tunnel behind him, and he steps out of the dark already mid-motion, coat soaked to the knee, face a blank you'll forget the second it's gone. Nobody hired him on paper. Nobody ever will.","traits":{"note": "No paper trail leads to him because there was never any paper — the contract is a rumor that happens to come true.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The hitman makes two attacks, using Drain Blade or Silenced Crossbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Drain Blade", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Silenced Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage. A target that hasn't acted yet this combat takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already been paid to remove someone the party is protecting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He surfaces mid-job with an unrelated wound and needs the tunnels ahead cleared, no questions."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's confused the party for his actual target, and correcting him is genuinely dangerous."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His contract came from someone the party's currently working against, unbeknownst to either side."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a name written on wet paper that's started to dissolve before he can deliver it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown curious who keeps hiring him and starts pulling threads instead of finishing the job."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He never says who paid him because he genuinely doesn't remember taking the meeting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Two different clients hired him for the same target tonight, and both are in this room."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["stepping out of storm-drain dark already mid-motion, coat soaked to the knee", "wearing a face you'll forget the second it's gone"]},{"name":"The Don (Crime Boss)","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"waterfront crime boss, three words end lives","flavor":"Runs the whole waterfront from a back booth, three words from him and a man stops existing.","desc":"He sits at the back booth like he owns the building, because he does, unwrapping a cigar with the unhurried patience of a man who has never once been told no. He speaks three words, quiet, and somewhere across the room a man goes pale.","traits":{"note": "He speaks three words, quiet, and somewhere across the room a man goes pale — that's the whole negotiation.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Don makes two attacks, using Family Blade or Table Piece in any combination."}, {"name": "Family Blade", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Table Piece", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Three Words", "text": "1/Day. The Don speaks a name aloud. Every creature within 60 feet that owes him a debt, favor, or fealty (DM's discretion) must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened of the named creature until the end of the Don's next turn, turning on it if given the chance."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's summoned the party to explain a debt they didn't know they'd inherited."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the waterfront's protection in exchange for one name they'd rather not give up."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a friend of the party's as collateral on a deal gone sideways."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to remove a rival quietly, tonight, no questions in either direction."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He already knows what the party's here to ask before they've said a word."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown bored ruling unopposed and offers the party a game with real stakes, just to feel something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every man who's crossed him has vanished on the same night of the month, without exception."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He speaks the party's name aloud tonight, and the whole room turns to look at them at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting at the back booth like he owns the building, because he does", "unwrapping a cigar with the patience of a man who has never once been told no"]},{"name":"The Silent Assassin","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"unerring silent killer, no prints, no words","flavor":"Never misses, never talks, never leaves a print. The family keeps him on retainer and prays they never need him twice in one week.","desc":"There's no warning — no footstep, no shadow crossing the window, just a presence suddenly in the room where a second ago there wasn't one. He doesn't speak before, during, or after. The silence is the whole point.","traits":{"note": "The family keeps him on retainer and prays they never need him twice in one week.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The assassin makes two attacks, using Silent Bite or Shadow Strike in any combination."}, {"name": "Silent Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Shadow Strike", "replaces": "Shadow Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10 + 3) Necrotic damage. The assassin has advantage on this attack roll against a target that hasn't acted yet this combat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already inside the room the party thought was secure, and he's not here for them — yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been sent for someone standing directly beside the party, and collateral is acceptable."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He appears mid-conversation the party was having about him, moments too late to have missed it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His contract expires at dawn, and it's the party's only leverage over whether he finishes it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tailed the wrong mark for the first time anyone can remember, and he knows it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He leaves before finishing the job, for reasons no one in the family can explain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every room he's used before feels colder afterward, permanently, no matter who lives there next."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been given two names tonight, and one of them wasn't supposed to be on the list."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing suddenly in a room where a second ago there wasn't anyone", "saying nothing before, during, or after — the silence is the whole point"]},{"name":"The Family's War Machine (Armored Motorcade)","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"armored driverless car, built to smash blockades","flavor":"A reinforced sedan run by clockwork muscle under the hood — bulletproof, driverless, built to plow through a police blockade.","desc":"The sedan idles at the curb with no driver visible through the windshield, engine turning over with a low mechanical growl that isn't quite combustion. When the doors don't open for you, the grille does instead.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blockade Ram", "text": "Charging 20+ feet into a barricade or vehicle, it deals double its slam damage and the obstacle must save or be destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Idles outside a meet, waiting to run interference the moment shots are fired."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorts a payoff run at a fixed distance, never closer, never farther."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Parked outside a rival's club, engine running, as a message rather than a threat yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chases down anyone who runs from a shakedown before they clear the block."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits dormant for weeks between jobs, garaged somewhere nobody's supposed to know."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Refuses to start for anyone outside the family, engine catching and dying for strangers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The radio inside plays a station that stopped broadcasting years ago, always the same song."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Activates with no order given at all, as if it decided on its own that tonight needed a response."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling at the curb with no driver visible, engine growling low and wrong", "answering with the grille when the doors won't open for you"]},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin (Old Money, Older Blood)","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"ancient vampire, owns the city's every debt","flavor":"Owns half the city's paper and none of its daylight. Every favor ever owed to him comes due eventually, in blood.","desc":"He receives you in a study with the curtains drawn against noon, a glass of something dark untouched at his elbow, and a ledger of names open on the desk between you. He never raises his voice. He doesn't have to — every debt in this city eventually walks itself into this room.","traits":{"note": "He does not raise his voice; the room's temperature drops when he's displeased, and everyone in it knows why.", "actions": [{"name": "The Bite That Buys You", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target's hit point maximum drops by that amount. If this reduces a creature to a hit point maximum of 0 it dies, and its debts — every one — transfer to the Kingpin."}, {"name": "Terms of the Arrangement", "replaces": "Eye Rays", "text": "The Kingpin levels a look at up to three creatures within 120 ft. Each makes a DC 18 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Charmed until the end of its next turn and must move toward the Kingpin, unable to willingly harm him — old obligations reassert themselves. A creature that has already taken Bite damage from him this combat has disadvantage on the save."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He calls in a debt the party didn't know they'd inherited from someone dead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a rival removed and offers the party the one thing they've been chasing all game."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He already owns the building the party thought was their safehouse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows a party member's true name and the debt that came with it at birth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers immortality on terms so reasonable it takes a moment to hear the trap."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's bored of the city and has decided the party will be the interesting thing this century — whether they cooperate or run."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The contracts he holds are signed in the party's future handwriting; he's been waiting for them to catch up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He owns the debt of the city itself, and when he decides to collect, every locked door, every hired gun, and every drowned secret in it answers to him at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court in a penthouse where every guest owes him something", "reviewing a ledger of the city's debts by candlelight though the lights work fine"]},{"name":"The Case That Isn't Closed (City-Ghost of the Unsolved)","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"undying intelligence of every unsolved murder","flavor":"Every murder the city buried without an answer, fused into one patient intelligence that still keeps its own files.","desc":"It doesn't have a single shape — it's the cold spot in every records room at once, a whisper of case numbers that were never closed, filed under names that stopped mattering to anyone but it. It still asks the same questions the department stopped asking decades ago.","traits":{"hp": "as lich chassis (city-scale apex)", "note": "Speaks in overlapping fragments of old case files rather than a single voice.", "actions": [{"name": "Cold File", "text": "Once per turn, forces a save or the target relives an unsolved memory of their own, becoming frightened."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces around a party member connected, even distantly, to an unsolved city murder."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to close a case the party desperately needs closed, for a memory in trade."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's opened a file on the party themselves, mid-investigation, before they've done anything yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants a specific name spoken aloud in the room where the murder happened, tonight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cross-referenced a party member's alibi against a case from years before they were born."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's found a thread that implicates someone the party trusts, and it wants that thread pulled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every unsolved case in the city updates itself the instant it enters a new room, in real time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has just filed the party's entire future under Unsolved, and the whole city's memory bends to keep the file open."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["occupying the cold spot in every records room at once, a whisper of case numbers never closed", "asking the same questions the department stopped asking decades ago"]},{"name":"Alley Snitch","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"small-time informant, trades names for cash","flavor":"Small-time informant who trades names for nickel bags, works every side of the block at once.","desc":"Small, quick, and already halfway into the shadow of the loading dock before you've finished asking the question. A name costs less than the nickel bag in his other pocket, and he'll happily sell you both if you don't look like a cop.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pocket Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Loaded Sling", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades information for cash, never product, always at the loading dock."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works every side of the block at once and remembers who paid what."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs on nerves and instinct, bolting at the first sign of a badge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers questions phrased as favors — cheaper to answer that way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows exactly which alleys drain to which sewers and uses them to vanish."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps one true secret he's never sold, saving it for when he really needs out."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know things about people before he's ever actually seen them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sells the same name to three different buyers in one night and can't outrun all three."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["already halfway into the loading-dock shadow before you've finished asking the question", "pricing a name at less than the nickel bag in his other pocket"]},{"name":"Numbers Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-noir-civilian","summary":"betting-slip courier, knows the safe hours","flavor":"Carries the day's betting slips in a lining pocket, knows which precinct to avoid on which hour.","desc":"He keeps a folded slip pinned inside his coat lining, checking his watch every block, timing his route around a beat cop's schedule he's memorized down to the minute. He'll talk fast and walk faster if you slow him down.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Weighted Sap", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs the same six blocks every day at the same hour, rain or shine."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks fast and walks faster if anyone so much as slows his pace."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has memorized every beat cop's schedule down to the minute on his route."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries slips for three different operations, keeping the lining sorted by color."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never runs the same route twice in a week, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started skimming odds in his own favor, small enough nobody's noticed yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears the numbers on his slips sometimes change between pickup and drop."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets robbed mid-route and has to decide, in seconds, which side he'd rather lie to."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["checking his watch every block, timing a route around a beat cop's schedule", "keeping a folded betting slip pinned inside his coat lining"]},{"name":"Pier Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold-inventor","model":"guard","summary":"dock kid fencing stripped copper fast","flavor":"Dock kid who strips copper off idle barges and fences it before the tide turns.","desc":"Barefoot on wet planking, hauling a coil of stripped copper wire twice his size toward a fence stall that closes at low tide. He's gone before you've decided whether to stop him.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Fence Knife", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Improvised Device (Roll d6)", "replaces": "Improvised Device (Roll d6)", "text": "The dock kid rigs a scavenged trap or noisemaker. Roll a d6 to determine the effect (DM's discretion), scaled to a minor, non-lethal battlefield trick — a flash, a snare, a distraction — never direct damage beyond 1d6."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strips copper off idle barges before the tide turns, quick and quiet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fences the day's haul at a stall that closes the second low tide hits."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows every gap in the dock fence better than the guards who walk it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works with two or three others, splitting the haul by whoever's fastest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids barges with fresh paint, having learned those get checked more often."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Saves half of every haul in a hidden cache instead of fencing it all."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims one barge groans a warning before the guards ever show up, and he's never been wrong."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets caught mid-haul by the barge's actual owner, who isn't who anyone expected."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["barefoot on wet planking, hauling stripped copper twice his size toward a low-tide fence stall", "gone before you've decided whether to stop him"]},{"name":"Streetlamp Tail","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"guard","summary":"low-rent tail, reports habits not crimes","flavor":"Follows a mark three blocks back under every busted streetlamp on the route, reporting habits not crimes.","desc":"He keeps exactly three lampposts back, no closer, stepping into the dark between each pool of light like he's rehearsed it. If you turn around, he's already looking somewhere else — but he was looking at you a second ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Concealed Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows a mark three blocks back under every busted streetlamp on the route."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reports habits, not crimes, to whoever's paying for the pattern."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Switches tails with a partner every few blocks so the mark never clocks one face."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never gets closer than the width of a street, patient as a held breath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Notes which windows light up and which stay dark on the mark's route home."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started padding his reports with details nobody asked for, growing curious himself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to already know the mark's route before it's walked, every single time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gets made mid-tail and has to decide, in the open, whether to run or talk."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["keeping exactly three lampposts back, stepping into the dark between each pool of light", "looking somewhere else the instant you turn around, though he was watching you a second ago"]},{"name":"Precinct Mole","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"guard","summary":"records clerk selling case photographs uptown","flavor":"Files clerk who photographs open cases before they close, sells the copies uptown.","desc":"He works late at the records desk more nights than he doesn't, a little camera tucked in a coat pocket that a filing clerk shouldn't own. The case folder he's photographing right now isn't his to touch.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The mole makes two attacks with Evidence Mace, or one attack and uses Spellcasting."}, {"name": "Evidence Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Flashbulb Flare", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Radiant damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn — the bulb goes off a half-second too bright."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The mole casts a spell, using clerical trinkets in place of material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's photographing the exact case file the party needs kept sealed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers copies of an open case for a price, no questions about who's asking."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been caught once already and needs the party's silence to keep his desk job."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His buyer uptown just stopped paying, and he's stuck holding photographs nobody wants now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's found a file connecting the party to a case that's supposed to be closed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started keeping a personal copy of everything, insurance against everyone he sells to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every photograph he develops shows a detail that wasn't in the room when he took it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's caught mid-photograph by the one detective in the building who isn't on anyone's payroll."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working late at the records desk, a small camera tucked in a coat pocket", "photographing a case folder that isn't his to touch"]},{"name":"Broke-Nose Bouncer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"speakeasy bouncer, guards the address itself","flavor":"Keeps the wrong crowd out of the right speakeasy, and the right crowd from remembering the address.","desc":"He stands in front of an unmarked door with his arms crossed, nose bent twice already and looking like it's due a third time. He doesn't care who you are — he cares whether you know the word that gets the door to open.","traits":{"note": "He'd rather flatten you quiet in the doorway than let a scene spill onto the sidewalk.", "actions": [{"name": "Doorman's Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, he can push it 5 feet through the door it just failed to talk its way past."}, {"name": "Bounced", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage. He keeps this loaded for the ones who come back after being told once."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He checks a list against faces instead of a password, murmuring names under his breath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's polite to a fault, apologizing before he throws anyone who fails the test."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a bar towel over one shoulder, wiping his knuckles clean between visitors."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hums along to the muffled band inside, keeping time with his crossed arms."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a folding chair and a paperback, treating the door like a long, boring shift."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He remembers every face that's ever tried the wrong word, and greets repeat offenders by name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He never blinks while the door's open, like he's counting something only he can see inside."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been told tonight is the night nobody gets turned away, and it's making him nervous as hell."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing arms-crossed in front of an unmarked door, sizing up the wrong crowd", "testing whether you know the word that gets the door to open"]},{"name":"Getaway Kid","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"guard","summary":"teenage wheelman, engine always idling","flavor":"Seventeen and already the best wheelman on the strip, engine always running at the curb.","desc":"Seventeen, maybe eighteen, engine running at the curb with the driver's door already cracked. He's got one hand on the wheel and one eye on the clock, and he'll leave without you if the count runs past what he was told.","traits":{"note": "He'll leave without you if the count runs past what he was told, no matter who's still running.", "actions": [{"name": "Cover Fire", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Kid makes two attacks, one with his Alley Shortsword and one with his Backseat Longbow."}, {"name": "Alley Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Backseat Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. Fired one-handed out the window while the car's already moving."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got the radio on low, tapping the wheel to a song nobody else can hear yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps checking the rearview more than the street, jaw tight, sweat at his collar."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already counted the exits twice and picked the one he likes better."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a lucky cap pulled low, brim worn soft from nervous fingers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's chewing gum fast, blowing a bubble every time the seconds tick past what he likes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He talks to the engine like it's a person, promising it one more good run tonight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He swears the car starts before his hand touches the key, like it's as anxious as he is."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided tonight's the last job, and that decision is making him reckless with the clutch."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling the engine at the curb with the driver's door cracked, one eye on the clock", "drumming fingers on the wheel, counting seconds against a number someone gave him"]},{"name":"Fence's Errand Boy","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"rlm-noir-civilian","summary":"moves hot jewelry ahead of the wire","flavor":"Moves hot jewelry between three pawnshops before the description hits the wire.","desc":"He walks fast with his coat buttoned wrong, a lump in the inside pocket that catches the streetlight if he isn't careful about the angle. Three pawnshops in one night, never the same one twice in a week.","traits":{"note": "He never sells to the first shop that says yes — it makes the second one nervous, and nervous pays better.", "actions": [{"name": "Coat-Pocket Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. He draws it from a coat lining, never a belt, so nobody sees it coming until it's already out."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting the lump in his pocket through the fabric, over and over, without meaning to."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He crosses the street twice for no reason a tail would call suspicious, but it is."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's practicing his opening line to the pawnbroker under his breath, word for word."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps his eyes on shop windows, checking his own reflection for anyone matching pace."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's sweating through a coat too warm for the weather, buttoned crooked on purpose."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's memorized which pawnbroker owes him a favor and which one still remembers being burned."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The lump in his pocket seems heavier some nights than others, like it knows when it's being watched."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's carrying a piece hot enough that two different crews are already asking around about it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking fast with his coat buttoned wrong, a lump catching the streetlight", "timing his route between three pawnshops before the description hits the wire"]},{"name":"Sewer Grifter Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"dead con man still working an angle","flavor":"A con man who died mid-scam in the storm drains, still working an angle on anyone who wanders down.","desc":"It crouches in the runoff water with its collar still straight and its cufflinks still shining, a dead man's idea of a con still playing out on a face nobody's fooled by anymore. It'll pitch you the same scheme that got it killed, if you let it finish.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't know the con died with it — it'll finish the pitch even after you've already said no twice.", "actions": [{"name": "Grifter's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage. If it hits a creature that's still listening to its pitch, it has advantage on the roll."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rehearsing the same investment pitch that got it killed, word-perfect, to an audience of pipes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It straightens a tie that's mostly rot, still performing respectability out of pure habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flashes a smile with too many teeth missing to be reassuring anymore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps offering a handshake it never quite finishes extending."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It counts imaginary bills off a roll of old newspaper, over and over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It remembers the mark's name who killed it, and repeats it like a curse between sentences."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its cufflinks still shine even in total dark, like the storm drain keeps them polished for it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's cornered someone who actually believes the pitch, and it's getting more excited than it should be able to."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["crouching in runoff water, collar straight and cufflinks shining on a rotted coat", "working through the same pitch that got it killed on anyone who wanders too close"]},{"name":"Payroll Skimmer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"guard","summary":"union rep skimming every payroll envelope","flavor":"Union rep who takes a cut off every dock worker's envelope before it's counted.","desc":"He counts the envelopes twice before he hands them out, thumb working a little faster than his mouth is talking, skimming a bill or two off the top of each one without looking down. Every dockhand knows. Nobody's said anything yet.","traits":{"note": "Every dockhand knows he skims. Nobody's said anything yet — that's the part that worries him.", "actions": [{"name": "Union Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d12 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Envelope Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recounting an envelope a third time, sure someone's finally going to notice the shortfall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's practicing an excuse about a printing error, testing how convincing it sounds out loud."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He tips his cut into a different pocket than usual, worried about a pattern forming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's overly friendly to the newest dockhand, the one least likely to do the math yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a second, smaller ledger for his own math, hidden inside the real one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started skimming less, worried the union's finally sending someone to check the numbers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His thumb keeps skimming bills even when he's not near the envelopes anymore, a nervous tic he can't stop."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just realized the shortfall's been noticed, and he's deciding right now whether to run or bluff."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["counting envelopes twice, thumb faster than his mouth, skimming a bill off each", "glancing down the dock line to see who's watching him shortchange the count"]},{"name":"Hollow-Eyed Patrolman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"dead cop still walking his old beat","flavor":"Walked his beat so long after death nobody's noticed he stopped breathing on it.","desc":"It walks the same six blocks at the same hour it always did, nightstick swinging in a rhythm that never varies, eyes fixed forward on nothing. It doesn't seem to notice the smell coming off its own uniform, or that its breath never fogs in the cold.","traits":{"note": "Walks a fixed patrol route; wakes to hostility only if that route is interrupted."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stops at the same corner it always stopped at, for reasons only its dead memory still holds."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tries the handle of a shop door that closed for good years before it died."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It salutes a passing car out of old habit, though the driver never salutes back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform buttons are green with age, but its posture is still parade-ground straight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It writes something in a ticket book with a pen that ran dry a long time ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It reacts, briefly, to a whistle — some drilled reflex flickering under the rot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow moves a half-step behind its body, like it's still catching up from being alive."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found something on its old beat that wasn't there before, and its rhythm has finally, terribly, broken."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the same six blocks at the same hour, nightstick swinging in an old rhythm", "staring forward at nothing, breath never fogging in the cold"]},{"name":"Speakeasy Torpedo","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"rlm-noir-gangster","summary":"speakeasy doorman, admits by tip or fist","flavor":"Doorman with a sap in his coat, decides who gets in by the size of the tip and the size of the fist.","desc":"He leans against a door that looks like a boarded storefront from the street, sap visible in his coat, sizing up your shoes and your watch before he decides whether the password matters tonight.","traits":{"note": "He'll wave through a bad password on a good coat, and turn away a perfect one from somebody broke-looking.", "actions": [{"name": "Sapped", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. On a hit against a creature that hasn't paid its way in, the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Stunned until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Warning Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting cash through a coat pocket, deciding tonight's tip threshold on the fly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a new password memorized wrong and is bluffing his way through checking it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's chatting up a regular, ignoring the line of hopefuls behind them entirely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps glancing at a a photo tucked in his coat, checking faces against it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's polishing brass knuckles absently, more habit than threat tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided he likes this crowd tonight and is letting far more people in than usual."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know the password before it's spoken, mouthing it a half-second early every time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been told to turn everyone away tonight, no exceptions, and he's not explaining why."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning against a boarded storefront, sap visible in his coat", "sizing up your shoes and your watch before deciding if the password matters"]},{"name":"Pawnshop Ghost","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"haunts a shop of desperate final pawns","flavor":"Haunts a hock shop full of things people pawned to pay off men who killed them anyway.","desc":"Rings and watches and a wedding band still sit in the glass case exactly where their owners left them, and something drifts between the shelves at closing time, touching each one like it's trying to remember whose hand it was.","traits":{"note": "It's not looking for revenge — it's looking for whoever it used to be, one hocked item at a time.", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Time", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 until it finishes a long rest. If this reduces a Strength score to 0, the target collapses, Incapacitated, until the reduction ends."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hovers over a pawned watch, winding a stem that isn't really there anymore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from the register bell every time a customer rings it, like the sound still stings."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rearranges rings in the case at night, always back to a specific, private order."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only manifests near items pawned under duress, ignoring the rest of the shop entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It traces a wedding band's engraving over and over, unable to read the name anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It grows agitated when an item it's attached to is finally sold, following it briefly out the door."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The glass case fogs from the inside whenever it lingers too long near one particular drawer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone's come to reclaim the very item it's spent years mourning, and it isn't ready to let go."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["drifting between glass cases at closing time, touching each item like memory", "lingering over a wedding band nobody ever came back to reclaim"]},{"name":"Second-Story Man","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"guard","summary":"cat burglar, works only the upper floors","flavor":"Never touches the ground floor. In and out of a fire escape before the mark rolls over.","desc":"He's already three floors up and out the window before the mark rolls over, fire escape rattling once, quiet, under a weight that shouldn't move that fast. He never touches the ground floor — too many eyes down there.","traits":{"note": "He never touches the ground floor — too many eyes down there, and he's not paid to be seen.", "actions": [{"name": "Roof Runner", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Second-Story Man makes two attacks with his Window Dagger."}, {"name": "Window Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Smooth Talker", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that can see and hear him makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, it's Charmed until the end of his next turn and treats his presence in the room as ordinary — easy to dismiss, easier to forget."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's testing a windowsill's give with two fingers before committing his full weight to it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a pillowcase half-full already, cinching the top quiet before the next room."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He pauses on the fire escape to relight a cigarette, patient as a man on his own porch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts the floors below under his breath, more habit than fear at this height."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's memorized which floorboard creaks in this building and steps wide around it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He leaves one item behind on every job, a small superstition he won't explain to anyone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He moves along ledges too narrow for footing like the building itself is helping him balance."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's inside a room he was told was empty, and someone very much awake just sat up in the dark."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["three floors up and out the window before the mark rolls over", "working a fire escape quiet, under a weight that shouldn't move that fast"]},{"name":"Rumrunner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"bootlegger, paid in product and silence","flavor":"Drives crates of the good stuff past three checkpoints a night, paid in product and silence.","desc":"He drives with the headlights off past the third checkpoint, crates rattling soft under a tarp in the truck bed, a story about a broken taillight already rehearsed for the cop he's hoping won't ask twice.","traits":{"note": "He's paid half in cash and half in product, and he drinks exactly none of what he hauls.", "actions": [{"name": "Glove Box Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Under-the-Dash Crossbow", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. He can fire this one-handed while still steering."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's timing the checkpoints against a mental clock, muttering the gaps between patrols."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a fake manifest folded in the visor, edges soft from handling it so often."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He drives with one window cracked, listening for engines he doesn't recognize."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a bottle of the good stuff untouched on the seat, a bribe he's saving for later."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hums to keep himself calm, a tune that doesn't quite resolve at the end."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started skimming a crate off every third run, and he's not sure the family's noticed yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He swears the truck runs quieter on nights it's carrying more than it should, like it wants to help him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A checkpoint just changed hands to a crew that doesn't take his usual bribe, and he's out of road to think about it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["driving headlights-off past the third checkpoint, crates rattling under a tarp", "rehearsing a story about a broken taillight for a cop he hopes won't ask twice"]},{"name":"Wharf Enforcer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"half-ogre-ogrillon","model":"guard","summary":"dock enforcer, breaks fingers over shortfalls","flavor":"Collects the union's cut from every ship that unloads, breaks fingers when the math is short.","desc":"He stands at the gangplank with a clipboard he doesn't need to read, counting crates against a number in his head, and cracks his knuckles slow when the count comes up short.","traits":{"note": "He breaks fingers, not bones — a man who can't work still owes, and a dead man can't pay at all.", "actions": [{"name": "Gangplank Battleaxe", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage, or 10 (1d10 + 5) Slashing damage with both hands."}, {"name": "Crate Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recounting a stack of crates a second time, sure the shortage is somebody's mistake."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's chatting amiably with a dockhand right up until the number in his head doesn't match."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a bent finger of his own, a memento from a job that argued back once."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting louder than usual tonight, making sure every worker on the line hears the tally."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He tips his hat to the foreman and scowls at everyone lower on the ladder."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's letting a small shortfall slide tonight, quietly, for a worker who reminds him of his brother."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He can tell a light crate from a full one by weight alone, hefting each before it even lands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The count's come up short by a number too big to explain away, and he already knows who to blame."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["standing at the gangplank with an unread clipboard, counting crates against a number in his head", "cracking his knuckles slow when the count comes up short"]},{"name":"Undertaker's Accomplice","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"funeral director doubling as disposal service","flavor":"Runs a legitimate funeral parlor by day, disposal service for the family by night.","desc":"He works the parlor by day with a respectful, practiced sorrow, and by night the same hands that arrange flowers arrange something else entirely in the back room, wrapped in a sheet that isn't meant for a funeral.","traits":{"note": "He's buried more secrets than bodies, and he keeps better records of the former.", "actions": [{"name": "Embalmer's Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage. He handles the blade with a mortician's calm, never rushed, never messy."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rehearsing condolences for a funeral scheduled for a man who isn't actually dead yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He measures a back-room delivery against a coffin like it's routine inventory work."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps two calendars, one for services and one written in a code only the family reads."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's overly gentle with flowers, hands trembling slightly from the work waiting in back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He greets mourners with genuine warmth, a kindness that costs him nothing to fake."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started keeping a private list of names he's disposed of, in case someone ever needs proof."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Flowers he arranges never wilt in the front room, though the parlor always smells faintly of the back one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A body in the back room isn't the one the family paid for, and he has minutes to fix the paperwork or the lie."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["arranging flowers with practiced, respectable sorrow during business hours", "wrapping something in the back room that isn't meant for any funeral"]},{"name":"Rooftop Sniper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"rlm-noir-gangster","summary":"rooftop rifleman, watches drops from towers","flavor":"Sets up on a water tower with a rifle and a thermos, watches the drop and waits for the signal.","desc":"He's set up behind the water tower with a rifle across his knees and a thermos going cold, patient as weather, watching the street below through a scope for a signal that hasn't come yet.","traits":{"note": "He's patient as weather and twice as reliable — if the signal comes, the shot's already been taken in his head.", "actions": [{"name": "Rooftop Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sniper makes two attacks, one with his Roofline Shortsword and one with his Long Watch."}, {"name": "Roofline Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Long Watch", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage. Against a target that hasn't moved since his last turn, this attack has advantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's pouring the last of his thermos, watching the steam curl off into the cold air."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's re-checking his scope's alignment against a chimney three rooftops over, out of habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting cars below by make and color to keep his mind from wandering."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a photo tucked under the rifle strap, glanced at more than the street sometimes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He shifts position every twenty minutes exactly, a discipline drilled in from somewhere else."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided he doesn't like tonight's target and is stalling the signal on purpose."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He swears he can hear the exact street noise the client described before it happens, a beat early."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The signal just came through wrong, naming someone he wasn't told to expect, and his finger hasn't moved yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["set up behind the water tower, rifle across his knees, thermos going cold", "watching the street through a scope for a signal that hasn't come yet"]},{"name":"Loan Shark's Bookkeeper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"rlm-noir-civilian","summary":"loan-shark accountant, keeps two ledgers straight","flavor":"Keeps two sets of ledgers, real and pretty, and never confuses which one goes to the DA.","desc":"He keeps two ledgers open on the same desk, one real, one pretty, and never once lets his pen cross from the wrong book into the wrong conversation. He'll smile at you the whole time he's deciding which ledger you're going in.","traits":{"note": "He never confuses the two books by accident — every mix-up he's ever made was on purpose.", "actions": [{"name": "Desk Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage. He keeps it sheathed inside a ledger binding until the exact moment it's needed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's totaling interest on a debt that's grown past what the debtor can ever hope to pay."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's cross-referencing a name against three different aliases in the pretty book."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps offering tea to whoever's across the desk, a courtesy that unsettles more than it comforts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rewriting a page in the real ledger, smudging a number that used to be smaller."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts a stack of bills twice with visible, theatrical patience."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided to quietly forgive a small debt tonight, for reasons he keeps entirely to himself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pretty ledger's numbers seem to shift slightly whenever the DA's office is mentioned nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just found a page in his own ledger he doesn't remember writing, with his own name at the bottom."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["keeping two ledgers open on the same desk, one real and one pretty", "deciding, mid-smile, which ledger you're going into"]},{"name":"Betrayed Partner Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"murdered PI haunting his own agency","flavor":"A private eye killed by the client he trusted, drifting the office he never got to close.","desc":"It sits behind the same desk it died at, in the same office it never got to close, riffling through case files that turned to dust years ago. It looks up only when someone says the name of the client who killed it.","traits":{"note": "Reacts with hostility specifically to hearing its betrayer's name spoken aloud."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's shuffling papers that have long since crumbled, still filing them in careful, invisible order."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reaches for a phone that hasn't had a dial tone in years, mid old habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sits perfectly still until someone reads the case file's cover aloud."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flickers at the mention of any client at all, hopeful and wary in the same instant."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps glancing at the office door, waiting for a knock that stopped coming decades ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started leaving case notes for whoever visits, in handwriting that gets clearer the longer they stay."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Dust in the office settles into the shape of old evidence whenever it concentrates hard enough."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone just spoke the killer's name in the doorway, and the whole room has gone winter-cold around it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting behind the desk it died at, riffling through case files that turned to dust years ago", "looking up only when someone says the name of the client who killed it"]},{"name":"Dockside Werebeast","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"low-level runner cursed with the wererat bite","flavor":"Low-level runner who caught something in the sewers under the fish market and now can't stop scratching at full moon.","desc":"He scratches at his collar under the fish-market lights, sweating despite the cold, glancing at the moon like it owes him money. Something under his skin is already changing shape before the tide even finishes coming in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bite (Curse)", "text": "On a hit while transformed, a humanoid target must save or contract wererat lycanthropy."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's scratching a rash under his collar that never quite heals, blaming it on the fish-market damp."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps his sleeves rolled down even in the heat, hiding something along his forearm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting days on a torn calendar page, circling one date harder than the rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He flinches at loud whistles, an animal reflex he hasn't figured out how to hide yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He eats his lunch raw lately, a habit that's started to worry even him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begging off the family's night jobs around the full moon, inventing worse and worse excuses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow under the market lights sometimes runs a half-beat ahead of his own footsteps."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The tide's come in early tonight and so has the change, and he can't find anywhere to hide it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["scratching at his collar under fish-market lights, sweating despite the cold", "glancing at the moon like it owes him money, something changing shape before the tide finishes"]},{"name":"Blackmail Photographer","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"blackmail photographer, sells negatives to both","flavor":"Shoots compromising photos through hotel transoms for a living, sells the negatives twice.","desc":"He waits in the stairwell across from the hotel transom with a camera wrapped in a coat, counting the minutes between flashes, already pricing the negatives in his head before the shutter clicks.","traits":{"note": "He sells every negative twice — once to the person in the photo, once to whoever wants them ruined.", "actions": [{"name": "Flashbulb Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage. He swings it like he's slamming a shutter case shut, fast and final."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's reviewing a stack of prints in a red-lit darkroom, sorting them by who'll pay the most."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's timing a hotel hallway's foot traffic, waiting for the right silent minute."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a burner phone just for buyers, three different numbers rotated weekly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's practicing an innocent expression in a mirror, in case someone catches him mid-shot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts negatives twice before locking them in a shoebox marked as something boring."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's found a photo he can't bring himself to sell, of someone who was kind to him once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Certain negatives develop images of things that weren't in frame when he took the shot."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just photographed the wrong person's secret, and two very different crews now want the film tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waiting in a stairwell with a camera wrapped in a coat, counting minutes between flashes", "pricing the negatives in his head before the shutter even clicks"]},{"name":"Arson Squad Torch-for-Hire","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"guard","summary":"junior arsonist, still loves the smell","flavor":"Second-string firebug who gets the small jobs, warehouses not landmarks, and still loves the smell.","desc":"He circles the warehouse twice before he strikes the match, breathing in the accelerant fumes like they're perfume, grinning a little wider than the job really calls for.","traits":{"note": "He only gets the small jobs — warehouses, not landmarks — but he treats every one like it's his masterpiece.", "actions": [{"name": "Torch Swing", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Torch-for-Hire makes two attacks, one with his Kindling Scimitar and one with his Warm-Up Pistol."}, {"name": "Kindling Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warm-Up Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 6 (2d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's sketching a floor plan on his forearm in pencil, marking where the accelerant goes first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's humming while he pours, a happy little tune out of step with what he's doing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a lighter he never uses for the actual job, just for cigarettes, superstitiously separate."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's watching the flames from across the street with genuine, unguarded delight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts the minutes until the fire department's usual response time, timing his exit to it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's angling for a bigger job than warehouses, and he's not subtle about wanting it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fire seems to catch faster than it should when he's the one lighting it, like it's eager for him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been asked to torch a building with people still inside, and he hasn't said no yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling a warehouse twice before striking the match, breathing in the fumes like perfume", "grinning wider than the job really calls for"]},{"name":"Junkyard Dog (Loyal Muscle)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-berserker","model":"guard","summary":"childhood muscle, would die before talking","flavor":"Grew up in the same tenement as the boss, would eat a bullet before he'd talk.","desc":"He grew up two doors down from the boss and never left, shoulders like a doorframe, standing exactly where he's told to stand without asking why. He'd eat a bullet before he'd finish a sentence that started with a question.","traits":{"note": "He'd eat a bullet before he'd finish a sentence that started with a question — loyalty's the only thing he's ever been good at.", "actions": [{"name": "Two Doors Down", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Junkyard Dog makes two attacks with his Tenement Greataxe."}, {"name": "Tenement Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's standing so still by the door that people forget he's there until he moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a childhood scar he touches absently whenever the boss raises his voice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a photo of the old tenement block folded in his wallet, worn soft at the creases."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He nods along to instructions without ever once asking a follow-up question."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's built like a doorframe and about as talkative, answering in grunts and gestures."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's quietly worried the boss is making a mistake tonight, but he'll follow the order anyway."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know what the boss wants before it's said, a loyalty gone almost telepathic."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The boss just gave an order that crosses a line even he didn't think existed, and he's frozen on it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing exactly where he's told to stand, shoulders like a doorframe", "not asking why, because he grew up two doors down from the man who's asking"]},{"name":"Crooked Bail Bondsman","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"guard","summary":"bail bondsman, springs soldiers for favors","flavor":"Springs the family's soldiers before the ink dries on the paperwork, for a price paid in favors.","desc":"He signs the paperwork before the ink from the last name's dried, sliding a soldier back out onto the street with a wink and a debt that isn't measured in dollars.","traits":{"note": "He never asks what the soldier did — only whether the family's good for the favor he's owed later.", "actions": [{"name": "Courtroom Rush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bondsman makes two attacks, one with his Notary Mace and one with his Radiant Flame."}, {"name": "Notary Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Flame", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Radiant damage. He calls it 'blessing the paperwork,' and it burns exactly like an oath does when it's broken."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Bondsman casts a spell requiring no material components, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's stamping paperwork with a rubber seal that's more decorative than legal at this point."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting bail bonds owed against favors called in, keeping a running private tally."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He greets released soldiers like old friends, arm around the shoulder, already naming the next job."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a spare set of court robes in his office, worn only for appearances."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's on a first-name basis with three different judges, and it shows in how fast paperwork moves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's quietly stalling one release longer than he should, waiting on a bigger favor to be offered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His paperwork seems to process itself faster the more desperate the family asking is."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's about to spring someone the family specifically wanted left in a cell, and hasn't decided who to cross yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["signing paperwork before the last name's ink has dried", "sliding a soldier back onto the street with a wink and a debt not measured in dollars"]},{"name":"Corner Pharmacist (Under-the-Counter)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"druid-circle-warden","model":"guard","summary":"pharmacist selling fixings out the back","flavor":"Sells the legal stuff up front and the fixings for the illegal stuff out the back door.","desc":"He rings up the aspirin and the cough syrup at the front counter with a straight face, and slides the real inventory across a back door only the regulars know to knock on.","traits":{"note": "He keeps the legitimate shelves scrupulously honest — it's the only cover that's kept the back room untouched this long.", "actions": [{"name": "Counter Rush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Pharmacist makes two attacks, one with his Vine Staff and one with his Verdant Wisp."}, {"name": "Vine Staff", "replaces": "Vine Staff", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Verdant Wisp", "replaces": "Verdant Wisp", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Poison damage, cut from the same stock he sells out the back."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Pharmacist casts a spell requiring no material components, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's weighing powder on a scale meant for aspirin, hands steady and unbothered."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's memorized every regular's knock, and knows a stranger's the second they try it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a genuinely helpful bedside manner for the front counter's legal customers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's restocking the back room at an hour the front counter's supposed to be closed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts the day's legal receipts against the day's real profit with visible disappointment."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's cutting the back-room stock weaker than usual, worried someone's finally going to overdose and bring heat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His tonics seem to work a little too well for shelf medicine, curing things aspirin never should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A customer just collapsed from a bad batch in his back room, and the front counter is still full of people."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing up aspirin and cough syrup with a straight face at the front counter", "sliding real inventory across a back door only the regulars know to knock on"]},{"name":"Skid Row Ghoul-Pack Runner","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast","summary":"undead errand-runner preying on skid row","flavor":"Once ran errands for the family, now runs down anyone sleeping rough near the old warehouse district.","desc":"It moves low along the warehouse fence line where the cardboard shelters are thickest, sniffing out sleep the way it used to sniff out an easy errand, and doesn't remember it used to bring these people blankets instead.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't remember it used to bring these people blankets instead of hunger — the errand-boy habit just points somewhere worse now.", "actions": [{"name": "Old Errand Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage. Against a creature that's asleep or Incapacitated, this attack has advantage."}, {"name": "Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's crouched by a shelter of flattened boxes, watching a sleeper's breathing slow and even."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses at a fence gap it used to squeeze through on legitimate errands, confused by the habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a scrap of blanket in its jaw, an old kindness it can't seem to put down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves quieter near people who are awake, some buried courtesy still half-intact."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles the same three shelters every night, like a route it can't stop running."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates longer than usual around anyone who reminds it, faintly, of who it used to serve."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It sometimes leaves scavenged food by a sleeper instead of attacking, an instinct fighting the hunger."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's cornered someone it half-recognizes from its old errands, and the confusion is making it frenzied."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["moving low along the warehouse fence line where the cardboard shelters are thickest", "sniffing out sleep the way it used to sniff out an easy errand"]},{"name":"Motorcade Gunner","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-iron-shadow","model":"rlm-noir-gangster","summary":"running-board gunman guarding the boss's car","flavor":"Rides the running board with a shotgun, job is simple, nothing gets close to the car.","desc":"He rides the running board with a shotgun braced against his hip, eyes on every window and doorway they pass, job simple enough to say in five words: nothing gets close to the car.","traits":{"note": "Nothing gets close to the car — that's the whole job, and he's never once had to explain it further.", "actions": [{"name": "Running-Board Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Gunner makes three attacks, choosing from his Longsword, Shortsword, Unarmed Strike, and Hand Crossbow, no more than one of which can be his Hand Crossbow."}, {"name": "Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Unarmed Strike", "replaces": "Unarmed Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Hand Crossbow", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's scanning rooftops as the car turns a corner, shotgun braced without needing to look down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts intersections aloud under his breath, a private map of danger points."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waves off a bystander getting too curious, polite but immovable about the distance."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's checking the running board's grip with his boot before the car picks up speed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps one hand on the door handle at all times, ready to be inside in an instant."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's noticed the same car following three blocks back and hasn't mentioned it to the driver yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to flinch a half-second before any shot is actually fired at the motorcade."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something's closing on the car from an angle the route never accounted for, and he's out of time to warn anyone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["riding the running board with a shotgun braced against his hip", "watching every window and doorway the car passes, job simple as five words"]},{"name":"Cathouse Madam's Muscle","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"guard","summary":"brothel muscle, keeps trouble quiet not fatal","flavor":"Handles the rough trade so the house stays quiet and the customers stay embarrassed instead of dead.","desc":"He stands just inside the parlor door in a suit too fine for the job, arms folded, handling every dispute with a quiet word first — the fist only comes out if the quiet word doesn't take.","traits":{"note": "He keeps trouble quiet, not fatal — dead customers are bad for business, embarrassed ones just don't come back for a month.", "actions": [{"name": "Parlor Enforcement", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Muscle makes two attacks with his Oversized Morningstar, or one attack with his Oversized Morningstar and uses Skullthumper."}, {"name": "Oversized Morningstar", "replaces": "Oversized Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Skullthumper (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Skullthumper (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d10 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the Prone condition."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's smoothing his lapels while a drunk patron argues over a bill he's already agreed to pay."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's murmuring a quiet warning to someone getting handsy at the bar, first and only warning."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He tips his hat to departing customers, ushering them out before they can start trouble."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting the room's exits absently, a habit that never quite switches off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's polite to a fault right up until a hand goes somewhere it shouldn't."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's protective of one particular girl in the house beyond what the job requires, and it shows."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He always seems to be exactly where trouble's about to start, a beat before it does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A customer's pulled a weapon inside the parlor, and the quiet-word rule just ran out of road."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing just inside the parlor door in a suit too fine for the job, arms folded", "handling a dispute with a quiet word first, fists only if the word doesn't take"]},{"name":"The Interrogator","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"guard","summary":"basement interrogator, patience outlasts any nerve","flavor":"Basement room, one bare bulb, a patience that outlasts anyone's nerve. Never raises his voice.","desc":"One bare bulb, one folding chair, and him leaning against the wall with his sleeves already rolled, in no hurry at all. He hasn't raised his voice yet tonight, and he won't need to — the silence between his questions does the work.","traits":{"note": "He hasn't raised his voice in years — the quiet outlasts anyone's nerve long before his patience runs thin.", "actions": [{"name": "Basement Work", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Interrogator makes two attacks, one with his Folding-Chair Greatsword and one with his Heavy Crossbow."}, {"name": "Folding-Chair Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "The Silence Between Questions", "text": "1/Day, as a bonus action, the Interrogator lets a beat pass. One creature within 10 ft. that can hear him must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or have the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn — he hasn't moved, hasn't spoken, and that's exactly the point."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already got a member of the party's crew in the folding chair, and he's not rushing the questions."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding out for one name, and he'll let the room sit in silence until someone gives it up."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been paid to find out what the party knows, not to hurt anyone — yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a face in the doorway and pauses the interrogation entirely, mildly curious."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The bare bulb flickers, and he mentions, almost gently, that the building's power bill is overdue."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's quietly sympathetic to the person in the chair and is stalling his employer's timeline on purpose."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to already know the answer to every question before he asks it, testing the lie instead of the truth."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His employer just walked in early, impatient, and the Interrogator's careful patience is the only thing keeping the room from getting worse."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning against a basement wall with sleeves rolled, one bare bulb, no hurry at all", "letting the silence between questions do the work instead of raising his voice"]},{"name":"The Widow-Maker (Serial Insurance Killer)","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-familiar","model":"guard","summary":"serial black-widow killer, three funerals deep","flavor":"Marries lonely men with good policies, three funerals in as many towns and a fourth name in her purse.","desc":"She dabs at dry eyes with a black-edged handkerchief at the graveside, the third policy already cashed and the fourth husband's name already circled in her address book.","traits":{"note": "She never rushes a marriage — a slow courtship makes a faster payout look like grief instead of arithmetic.", "actions": [{"name": "Graveside Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Widow-Maker makes two attacks with her Umbral Dagger."}, {"name": "Umbral Dagger", "replaces": "Umbral Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 8 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage. If this reduces a creature to 0 hit points, she gains advantage on Charisma checks made against anyone who witnessed it as an accident."}, {"name": "Convenient Grief", "text": "1/Day, as a reaction to a creature dying within 30 ft. of her, the Widow-Maker sheds a tear that reads as wholly genuine. Any creature that witnessed the death must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or be Charmed by her for 1 hour, treating the death as a tragic accident rather than anything more sinister."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's got her sights on a party member with a good policy and no living relatives to ask questions."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She needs the party to help stage the scene of husband number four, and she's paying well for the silence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A suspicious cousin of husband number three has hired the party, and she knows it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding a policy that names the party's client as her next intended target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants an alibi for tonight, and she's willing to pay handsomely in cash nobody can trace."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's genuinely tired of the act and is looking, quietly, for a way out of the pattern before it catches up."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every man she's married left behind a debt she inherited along with the grief, and the debts are starting to talk to each other."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Husband number four just found her address book, and she needs the party to make him disappear before he can use it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["dabbing dry eyes with a black-edged handkerchief at a graveside", "circling a fourth husband's name in her address book while the third policy cashes"]},{"name":"The Chop-Shop King","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"guard","summary":"chop-shop boss, six-hour car-to-cash turnaround","flavor":"Runs a garage that turns stolen cars into scrap and cash inside of six hours, no questions kept on paper.","desc":"He walks the garage floor in coveralls that never quite come clean, timing his crew against a stopwatch, and a stolen sedan that rolled in an hour ago is already three separate piles of parts with no paperwork behind them.","traits":{"note": "Six hours, car to cash, no questions kept on paper — he's proud of the turnaround the way other men are proud of their kids.", "actions": [{"name": "Chop Floor Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chop-Shop King makes two attacks, one with his Bay Scimitar and one with his Pistol."}, {"name": "Bay Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Six-Hour Turnaround", "text": "1/Day, as a bonus action, the King directs his crew to strip anything nearby to its frame. A vehicle, door, or piece of heavy cover within 30 ft. is reduced to scrap within a minute, removing it as an obstacle or piece of cover for the rest of combat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got the party's only working vehicle up on the lift already, and it'll be scrap in an hour unless they stop him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a very specific stolen car brought to him fast, before its owner reports it missing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a piece of evidence that rode into his garage bolted to a car's undercarriage."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His crew stripped a car that belonged to someone the party needs to talk to, alive."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll pay well for cars delivered quiet and fast, no questions, cash on the spot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's timing his own crew against a rival shop and needs the party to slow the competition down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Certain cars come apart on his floor faster than physics ought to allow, like the garage itself is hungry."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A car just rolled onto his floor with someone still alive in the trunk, and his six-hour clock has already started."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the garage floor in coveralls that never quite come clean, timing his crew against a stopwatch", "watching a stolen sedan become three piles of parts with no paperwork behind them"]},{"name":"The Blackmailer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"blackmailer with a file on the council","flavor":"Holds a file on half the city council, cashes it in an inch at a time so nobody ever pays enough to make him stop.","desc":"He keeps a fireproof drawer of photographs and a very good memory for who sits on the city council, cashing in an inch of pressure at a time — never enough to make anyone desperate enough to stop paying.","traits":{"note": "He never asks for more than someone can afford to lose quietly — a ruined mark stops being useful.", "actions": [{"name": "Drawer's Reach", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Blackmailer makes two attacks with his Filing Dagger."}, {"name": "Filing Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 7 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature in a 15-foot cone must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save or have the Blinded condition until the end of its next turn — a camera flash he keeps rigged for exactly this."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Blackmailer casts a spell requiring no material components, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a photograph of a party member doing something they'd rather the city not see."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to retrieve a file a councilman's goons already stole back from him once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering leverage on a councilman in exchange for a job the party's already been avoiding."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's broken into his fireproof drawer, and half his income just walked out the door."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows a secret about the party's employer and is deciding, right now, whether to sell it to them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's pushed one councilman too far, and that councilman has hired muscle he can't out-blackmail."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His photographs seem to develop new, damning details every time the subject tells a fresh lie."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just found a photograph that implicates someone far more dangerous than any councilman, and he hasn't decided if he's brave enough to use it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["keeping a fireproof drawer of photographs and a very good memory for the city council", "cashing in an inch of pressure at a time, never enough to make anyone desperate enough to stop paying"]},{"name":"The Wharf Boss's Widow","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"widow who's crueler than the husband was","flavor":"Inherited the docks when her husband went off a pier, and turned out to be better at the violence than he ever was.","desc":"She wears black to every meeting like it's a uniform, standing where her husband used to stand at the end of the pier, and settles disputes with a coldness that makes the old muscle miss the husband.","traits":{"note": "Everyone assumed she'd sell the docks after the funeral — she's the reason nobody assumes anything about her twice.", "actions": [{"name": "Pier's End", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Widow makes two attacks, one with her Mourning Greatsword and one with her Heavy Crossbow."}, {"name": "Mourning Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 10 (1d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Colder Than He Was", "text": "1/Day, as a reaction when an ally within 30 ft. is reduced to 0 hit points, the Widow can make one Mourning Greatsword attack against the creature responsible, and it has disadvantage on the save against any effect she inflicts this turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's inherited a debt her husband owed the party's employer, and she's not paying it back willingly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants proof her husband's death off the pier wasn't the accident the report says it was."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's cutting off a supply route the party needs, purely to see who blinks first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old muscle still loyal to her dead husband are testing whether she deserves the docks, and she needs the party to help her prove it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers the party dock access no one else can get, for a price paid in a favor she won't name yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's quietly investigating whether her husband's death really was an accident, and she doesn't trust her own crew to help."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She stands at the pier's end at the same hour every night, and the tide seems to answer to her patience."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone's just accused her, publicly, of arranging her husband's death, and the whole dock is watching how she responds."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["standing at the end of the pier where her husband used to stand, dressed in black like a uniform", "settling a dispute with a coldness that makes the old muscle miss the husband"]},{"name":"The Torch's Rival (Ice Man)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"drowning specialist, cold where Torch is hot","flavor":"Handles the jobs Torch won't touch, drownings staged as accidents, always cold, always clean.","desc":"He works in silence where Torch works in flame, standing at the edge of the pier with his hands in his pockets, watching the water take care of a problem that needed to look like an accident.","traits":{"note": "He handles the jobs Torch won't touch — drownings staged as accidents, always cold, always clean, never a fire in sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Cold Water Advance", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ice Man makes two attacks, one with his Pier Spear and one with his Shield Bash."}, {"name": "Pier Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage, or 9 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage with two hands."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or have the Prone condition."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been hired to stage an accident for someone the party is trying to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's competing with Torch for the same contract, and he'd rather the fire-happy rival lose this one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to look the other way while he works the pier tonight, and he's paying for the courtesy."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A body he staged as a drowning is being investigated more closely than he expected."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers information on Torch's whereabouts in trade for the party staying out of his own business."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's tired of cleanup work and wants out, and he thinks the party might be the way to disappear quietly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water near him never quite freezes, but it goes unnervingly still whenever he's about to work."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torch has just found out the Ice Man is undercutting his jobs, and the pier is about to become a very bad place to stand."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["standing at the pier's edge with his hands in his pockets, working in silence where Torch works in flame", "watching the water take care of a problem that needed to look like an accident"]},{"name":"The Cathouse Vampire","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"seductive predator working the high-end house","flavor":"Works the high-end house on the hill, takes more than money from every client who overstays.","desc":"He receives guests in a velvet-curtained room on the top floor of the house on the hill, charm turned all the way up, and takes considerably more than the fee from anyone who lingers past their hour.","traits":{"note": "He never forces the door — every mark walks in and stays past their hour on their own two feet.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cathouse Vampire makes two Restless Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Overstayed Welcome", "replaces": "Restless Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target's speed is halved until the start of its next turn — the room gets warmer, and leaving gets harder."}, {"name": "House Rules", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cathouse Vampire casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from an enchanter's repertoire appropriate to CR 4, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 13)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A client stumbled out of his room babbling and hasn't stopped since; the house wants it quiet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's taken an interest in one of the party and won't stop sending the same server with drinks."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival house wants him gone before he poaches their best-paying regulars."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a client's signed IOU that the man's family would kill to burn."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers information traded from pillow talk, priced in a favor he won't specify yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started losing track of which nights he's fed and which nights he only dreamed it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every client he's kept past their hour still returns, unable to explain why they can't stop coming back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's fallen for someone he was supposed to feed on, and the house has noticed the shortfall in the ledger."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["receiving a client behind velvet curtains, charm dialed all the way up", "counting the hour on a clock he intends the guest to miss"]},{"name":"The Coroner on the Payroll","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough-boss","model":"guard","summary":"corrupt coroner, signs whatever pays best","flavor":"Signs whatever cause of death keeps the invoice paid, has buried more truth than bodies.","desc":"He signs the death certificate before he's finished the exam, pen already moving toward whatever cause keeps the envelope coming, humming something under his breath that isn't quite a hymn.","traits":{"note": "He's never once been caught changing a cause of death — he never writes the lie twice the same way.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Coroner makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Bone Saw", "replaces": "Warhammer", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. The Coroner knows exactly where to strike to make it look accidental — the DM may rule this attack leaves no obvious wound."}, {"name": "Toe-Tag Bolt", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 12 (2d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's about to sign off on a murder as natural causes, and the body is someone the party needs to talk to."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's misplaced a file the party needs and wants a favor before he 'finds' it again."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's demanding a second opinion on a death he's already certified, and he's panicking."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's skimming from the morgue's evidence lockup and needs the count to stay wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a name on tonight's slab and it isn't the name the family gave the papers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started keeping a private ledger of every true cause of death, insurance against the day someone turns on him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Bodies he's falsely certified keep turning up again in his dreams, insisting on the truth he buried."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally been ordered to sign off on a child, and for the first time in his career, the pen won't move."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["signing a death certificate before the exam is half finished", "humming under his breath while an envelope disappears into his coat"]},{"name":"The Getaway Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"dead wheelman still driving his last job","flavor":"A wheelman who died at the wheel mid-job, still floors it through the same six blocks every night.","desc":"Headlights flicker on in an empty garage at the same hour every night, and something drives the same six blocks over and over at a speed no living driver would risk, foot to the floor on a job that ended in a wreck years ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Phantom Route", "text": "Moves through vehicles and thin obstacles along its fixed route without being slowed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drives with the radio still tuned to a station that stopped broadcasting decades ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It brakes hard at the same intersection every pass, though nothing's ever there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves tire marks that fade within the hour, always the same skid pattern."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It honks once at the same darkened window before speeding off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a passenger-shaped cold spot in the seat that was never empty on the night it died."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Lately it's been taking a seventh block, a detour that wasn't part of the original job."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anyone who rides along for a full loop wakes up the next morning with the wreck's memory instead of their own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight the loop ends differently — the wreck it's been avoiding for years is finally catching up to it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["gunning an engine that isn't there down the same six blocks, every night", "flickering headlights on in a garage that's been empty for years"]},{"name":"The Pit Boss (Casino Enforcer)","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"casino floor boss, settles cheats out back","flavor":"Watches the tables for card counters and skimmers alike, settles both the same way out back.","desc":"He watches the tables from a raised chair with a stare that never blinks, counting cards along with the players and skimmers alike, and settles both the same way in a back room behind the cashier's cage.","traits":{"note": "He never raises his voice on the floor — the smile stays until the door to the back room closes.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Pit Boss makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "House Edge", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Settle the Tab", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's caught the party's card-counter and is walking them toward the back room right now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a skimmer identified before the owner notices the count is off tonight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a marker on a high roller who's gone missing and needs him found quietly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party a rigged table's location for information on a rival house."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's covering for a dealer he's sweet on who's been skimming chips herself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started keeping his own side ledger of who really owns the casino's debts, insurance for later."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He always knows which card is coming next, and it's started to frighten even him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's count doesn't add up by a fortune, and he has one hour to find the difference or become it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["watching the tables from a raised chair, counting cards along with the players", "walking a card counter toward the back room, smiling the whole way"]},{"name":"Wiseguy Wererat Crew Boss","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"sewer-route smuggling boss, feral under moons","flavor":"Runs the sewer-adjacent smuggling routes personally, likes his crew small and his tunnels smaller.","desc":"He runs the tunnel routes personally, suit jacket a little too tight across shoulders that keep changing shape under the fabric, keeping his crew small and his passages smaller so nothing bigger than him can follow.","traits":{"note": "He keeps his crew and his tunnels the same size for a reason — nothing that can't fit can catch him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Crew Boss makes two attacks, using Sewer Fangs or Back-Alley Scratch in any combination."}, {"name": "Sewer Fangs", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or contract a filth-borne curse, per the wererat's own affliction rules."}, {"name": "Back-Alley Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A shipment is late through his tunnels and he suspects the party of being the reason."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a route scouted that's too narrow for his own bulkier men."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a rival crew's runner hostage in exchange for territory."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers safe passage through the tunnels for information on who's been informing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lost a piece of cargo to the sewers themselves and wants it back before the owner finds out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started sleeping down in the tunnels more than up top, and his crew's noticed the suit fits looser."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rats down in his tunnels have started running his errands before he gives the order."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The full moon's tonight, his biggest shipment is moving, and he can already feel the suit not fitting at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["walking the tunnel routes personally, jacket straining at shoulders that won't sit still", "keeping his crew small on purpose, so nothing bigger can follow them down"]},{"name":"The Nightclub Sorcerer (House Mage)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"club mage rigging luck at every table","flavor":"Runs 'luck' at the tables with a whispered word, the house never really loses on his shift.","desc":"He leans against the bar with a drink he never finishes, murmuring something under the band's next number, and the dice at every table in earshot come up exactly how the house needs them to.","traits":{"note": "He never touches the tables himself — the house's luck runs through a whisper, not his hands.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Nightclub Sorcerer makes two attacks with Rigged Burst or uses Spellcasting once."}, {"name": "Rigged Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 12 (3d6 + 2) Force damage."}, {"name": "The House Always Wins", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Nightclub Sorcerer casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a mage's repertoire appropriate to CR 5, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (save DC 14). Once per day he may instead force a reroll of one die within 60 feet that he can see, choosing the new result."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rigging tonight's high-stakes table against a mark the party's been hired to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's noticed the party counting cards and is deciding whether to rig against them or recruit them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He owes the house a debt paid in fixed outcomes and is running out of games left to bend."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to fix a court date's odds in the party's favor, for a price paid in future favors."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been asked to rig a fight the party has money riding on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown bored fixing games and has started rigging outcomes no one's betting on, just to feel it work."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's begun losing track of which results in the club are real and which he only willed into being."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's rigged something bigger than a card table tonight — an alibi, a jury, a life — and it's about to come due."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning on the bar with a drink he never finishes, murmuring over the next song", "watching the dice at every table land exactly how the house needs"]},{"name":"The Contract Killer's Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"guard","summary":"arranges hits, never pulls a trigger himself","flavor":"Never pulls a trigger himself, just arranges the calendar for the men who do.","desc":"He never touches a weapon — he touches a calendar, penciling in names and dates with the same care a florist gives a delivery schedule, and hands the list to men who don't ask who wrote it.","traits":{"note": "He's never touched the weapon that killed anyone on his list — the calendar is the only thing he's guilty of.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Handler makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "The Calendar's Edge", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scheduled Delivery", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage, and the Handler has advantage on this attack against a target that hasn't acted yet in the fight."}, {"name": "Appointment Canceled", "replaces": "Smoke Bomb (1/Day)", "text": "As a bonus action, the Handler drops a smoke bomb, filling a 15-foot radius centered on him with heavily obscuring smoke that lasts until the end of his next turn. He then may take the Disengage action for free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member's name is on tomorrow's calendar page, and he hasn't decided if he'll cross it out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs proof destroyed that ties a name in his ledger to a job gone wrong."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's misplaced this week's calendar and the shooters are waiting for orders that never came."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to reschedule a hit indefinitely, in exchange for the party owing him the same courtesy someday."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's double-booked two hitters on the same target and needs it quietly sorted before they meet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started penciling in names of people who haven't wronged anyone yet, just to see if it still feels the same."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The calendar fills itself in some mornings with names he swears he never wrote."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His own name has appeared on a page in someone else's hand, and the date is tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["penciling names into a calendar with the care of a man scheduling flowers", "handing a folded list to someone who never asks who wrote it"]},{"name":"Deep-Water Enforcer (Smuggler's Ghoul-Kin)","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"drowned smuggler guarding sunken contraband crates","flavor":"Drowned running contraband through the harbor and came back wrong, still guards the same sunken crates.","desc":"It surfaces at the edge of the harbor lights, skin the gray of drowned rope, standing guard over crates sunk decades ago that it still remembers running before the water took it.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves the crates it guards, even to feed — the cargo matters more to it than it did in life.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Deep-Water Enforcer makes two attacks, using Cold Bite or Wharf Claw in any combination."}, {"name": "Cold Bite", "replaces": "Icy Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Wharf Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a crate the party's client desperately needs off the bottom before the tide changes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh contraband has been stacked over its old crates, and it doesn't recognize the new owners' claim."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A diver hired to retrieve cargo hasn't surfaced, and the party's been sent to find out why."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's started dragging loose cargo further out, expanding a stash no living smuggler mapped."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The harbor patrol wants the wreck it guards found before a bigger scandal surfaces with it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun sorting the crates by a ledger only it remembers, as if still awaiting inspection."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crates it guards never rot, and the labels rewrite themselves to match whatever's being smuggled tonight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its old crew is finally coming to reclaim the cargo, and it doesn't understand that they're the reason it drowned."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["surfacing at the edge of the harbor lights, skin gray as drowned rope", "standing guard over crates it remembers running before the water took it"]},{"name":"The Family Consigliere","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"mob lawyer, knows the law's every angle","flavor":"Advises the Don on every angle of the law, knows exactly how far a body can bend it.","desc":"He sits at the Don's right hand in a suit that costs more than most men's cars, flipping through a law book with a pencil, telling the room exactly how far the statute can bend before it breaks.","traits":{"note": "He's never lost an argument about what the law technically allows — he wrote most of the loopholes himself.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Consigliere makes two attacks with Sanctioned Strike or uses Spellcasting once."}, {"name": "Sanctioned Strike", "replaces": "Radiant Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Radiant damage — he calls it 'due process.'"}, {"name": "Closing Argument", "replaces": "Holy Word (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature of the Consigliere's choice within 30 feet that can hear him must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, cowed by a recitation of exactly what he can prove against them."}, {"name": "The Fine Print", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Consigliere casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a priest's repertoire appropriate to CR 5, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (save DC 14)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's found a loophole that could clear a party member's warrant, if they'll do him a small legal favor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a witness's statement altered before it reaches a judge he doesn't own."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's discovered the Don is about to break the one law even the family respects."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a contract the party could use against a rival, drawn up so carefully it's technically legal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival lawyer is threatening to expose one of his older, sloppier loopholes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun drafting contracts that bind people to things they never agreed to, testing how far the ink can go."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every contract he's ever written seems to still be in effect somewhere, layered on top of each other like sediment."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally been asked to write a contract that would legally erase a person, and he can't decide if that's a line or just fine print."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["flipping through a law book at the Don's right hand, pencil in motion", "telling the room exactly how far a statute bends before it snaps"]},{"name":"The Bent Coroner's Ghoul Ward","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"morgue-basement horror from unburied bodies","flavor":"Something the morgue basement keeps making from the bodies that were never properly buried.","desc":"Something moves in the cold-storage drawers of the city morgue that shouldn't, born out of bodies that were never properly buried and paperwork that was never properly filed. It knows the smell of formaldehyde better than it knows its own name.","traits":{"note": "It has no memory of who it was — only the paperwork trail of who it was never properly buried as.", "actions": [{"name": "Drawer-Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is a creature other than an Undead, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be Paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Cold-Storage Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It shambles between drawers checking toe tags, as if still trying to file itself correctly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragged a stack of unfiled paperwork into its drawer and won't be parted from it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from the coroner's voice specifically, some memory of being signed off on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's stronger near the incinerator, as if fed by whatever the morgue burns."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hoards other bodies' identification tags, wearing several around its neck."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started answering to a name off one of the tags, though it's clearly not the one it wore in life."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "New unfiled bodies in the morgue vanish overnight and reappear the next day as more of it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The morgue's filing cabinet is close to overflowing, and something in the basement is close to becoming two."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["shifting in a cold-storage drawer that should be empty at this hour", "following the smell of formaldehyde down a hallway it half-remembers"]},{"name":"The Sweatshop Overseer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"sweatshop boss behind a legitimate front","flavor":"Runs an off-books garment floor behind a legitimate front, keeps the workers scared and the inspectors paid.","desc":"He walks the off-books garment floor behind a storefront that looks perfectly legitimate from the street, clipboard in hand, keeping the workers frightened and the health inspector's silence paid for.","traits":{"note": "He never raises a hand himself — the song does the frightening, and the clipboard does the rest.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Overseer makes two attacks with Shop-Floor Rapier or uses one other action."}, {"name": "Shop-Floor Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Keep the Line Moving", "replaces": "Beguiling Song", "text": "Each creature of the Overseer's choice within 30 feet that can hear him must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed until the end of the Overseer's next turn, compelled to keep working through pain or fear."}, {"name": "The Books Are Clean", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Overseer casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a performer's repertoire appropriate to CR 6, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 14)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A worker who tried to leave the floor has gone missing, and her family's asking the party to look."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs the party to intimidate an inspector who won't take the usual envelope."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's discovered a worker organizing the others and wants it handled before the shift ends."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers cheap labor and silence, if the party can move a shipment through his floor unnoticed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fire code violation is about to shut him down, and he wants it buried fast."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun keeping his most exhausted workers on the floor overnight, telling himself it's kindness, not to send them home to nothing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The garments coming off his floor keep the wearer awake and working long after they should have collapsed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A worker has finally collapsed for good, and the rest of the floor has stopped moving to watch what he does next."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the off-books garment floor with a clipboard, keeping the workers scared", "paying off the health inspector before he's finished knocking"]},{"name":"The Assassin's Apprentice","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"assassin-in-training, already outpacing the teacher","flavor":"Learning the trade from the Sewer Hitman, already better with a garrote than the teacher wants to admit.","desc":"She practices the garrote on a coat hook in the mentor's basement, patient, precise, already faster than the man teaching her wants to admit out loud.","traits":{"note": "She's already faster than her mentor and knows it — she just hasn't decided if she'll tell him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Apprentice makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Practiced Edge", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage, plus 3 (1d6) Piercing damage if the Apprentice has advantage on the attack roll."}, {"name": "Cold Bolt", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's shadowing the party to test a garrote technique on whichever of them walks alone first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her mentor's given her a name to practice on, and she's having second thoughts about the target."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants to defect from her mentor and needs the party to vouch for her somewhere safer."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's been sent to retrieve something the party's carrying, quietly, without waking anyone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's overheard a contract on her own mentor and doesn't know whether to warn him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started keeping a private list of names her mentor never assigned her, just to see if she can plan it alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She dreams the garrote work before she does it, always waking with the exact same bruises."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight her mentor's told her to prove herself on a target neither of them expected to be each other."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["practicing a garrote on a coat hook in a dim basement, patient and precise", "timing her own breathing against a target who doesn't know she's already decided"]},{"name":"The Precinct Captain (Owned Outright)","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard","summary":"precinct captain, signs every cover-up personally","flavor":"Signs off on every cover-up in his district personally, keeps his own hands the cleanest in the building.","desc":"He signs off on the day's paperwork at his desk with the department seal, initialing a cover-up alongside a parking citation without changing his expression once.","traits":{"note": "He keeps his own hands the cleanest in the building — every dirty signature belongs to someone he outranks.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Captain makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Badge and Blade", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Off the Books", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's about to close a case file the party needs kept open, ink already on the stamp."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a witness intimidated into recanting before tomorrow's hearing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding evidence that would clear the party of a charge, priced at a favor he hasn't named."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A new detective in his precinct is asking questions he can't afford answered honestly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a body moved from a crime scene before the wrong reporter arrives."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun keeping his own private file on everyone who pays him, insurance nobody else knows exists."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every report he signs off on comes true exactly as written, whether or not it happened that way."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Internal Affairs has finally opened a file with his own name on it, and he has one night to make it disappear."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["initialing a cover-up next to a parking citation, expression never changing", "stamping a case closed before the detectives have even finished their notes"]},{"name":"The Ferryman (River Body-Disposal)","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"guard","summary":"boat captain who disposes of bodies offshore","flavor":"Runs a fishing boat that never catches fish, takes the family's problems out past the breakwater.","desc":"He casts off past the breakwater in a boat that hasn't caught a fish in years, tarp lashed down in the stern, engine running just quiet enough not to wake the harbor patrol.","traits":{"note": "He's never been boarded and searched — the family picked him because the patrol trusts his face.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ferryman makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Gaff Hook", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage, and a Medium or smaller target is pulled 5 feet toward the Ferryman."}, {"name": "Warning Shot", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a tarp-wrapped problem in the stern that the party recognizes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a lookout on the breakwater tonight; the patrol's been changing their route."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's found something in the water that wasn't supposed to resurface, and it isn't a body."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers passage off the coast, no questions, for whoever the party needs to disappear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival's started using the same stretch of water and he wants it stopped quietly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun keeping a private log of every name he's put over the side, in case the family ever needs a scapegoat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water past the breakwater never gives back what he puts into it, no matter the tide."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's cargo is someone he recognizes from years back, and the boat's engine has never sounded this loud."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["casting off past the breakwater in a boat that hasn't caught a fish in years", "running the engine just quiet enough not to wake the harbor patrol"]},{"name":"The Kingpin's Bodyguard (Silent Type)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"never-photographed bodyguard, always two steps back","flavor":"Stands two steps behind the Don at every meeting, has never once been photographed.","desc":"He stands two steps behind the Don at every meeting, hands folded, face blank, and has never once appeared in a photograph despite a hundred reporters trying.","traits":{"note": "No camera has ever caught him — he's never explained why, and no one's asked twice.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bodyguard makes two Quiet Word attacks."}, {"name": "Quiet Word", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 9 (1d4 + 5) Piercing damage, and if the target is Surprised, this attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage."}, {"name": "Never Seen", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature within 10 feet of the Bodyguard must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be Blinded until the end of its next turn. The Bodyguard then may take the Hide action even while observed."}, {"name": "Off the Record", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Bodyguard casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a deceiver's repertoire appropriate to CR 7, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 15)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's shadowing the party on the Don's orders and hasn't decided whether they're a threat yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a photographer's memory card destroyed before it develops."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been ordered to stand down from a hit he privately disagrees with."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a warning meant for the Don's enemies, delivered as a courtesy no one authorized."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rookie reporter is finally close to proving he exists, and he wants it handled without a body."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun wondering, alone at night, whether he'd show up in a mirror if no one else were in the room."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "People who've stood beside him for years struggle to describe his face the next morning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The Don has finally asked him to stand in front instead of behind, and the room can't decide if that's a promotion or a target."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing two steps behind the Don at a meeting, hands folded, face blank", "stepping out of every photograph a moment before the shutter clicks"]},{"name":"The Corrupt Warden","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"guard","summary":"prison warden selling luxury to the family","flavor":"Runs the city lockup like a hotel for the family's soldiers, luxury cells for the right price.","desc":"He walks the cellblock like a hotel manager checking on guests, keys jingling, offering a nicer cell and a better meal to whichever soldier's family paid this month's rate.","traits":{"note": "He runs the lockup like a business ledger — every comfort has a price, and every price is paid in favors owed to the family.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Warden makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Cellblock Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Guard Tower Throw", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a party ally in his lockup and naming a price to arrange an accident-free release."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prisoner with dangerous knowledge is scheduled for transfer, and he's selling the timetable."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a riot staged to cover an unauthorized visitor slipping in or out."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's skimming the commissary funds and a state auditor's finally coming to check the books."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a cell assignment that would put two rivals within killing distance of each other."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started sleeping in the warden's office instead of going home, as if he trusts the cellblock more than his own house."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Prisoners who pay him best start reporting the same recurring dream about a cell that isn't on any floor plan."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The state's finally sending someone he can't buy, and he has one night to decide who takes the fall in his place."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the cellblock like a hotel manager, keys jingling at his belt", "offering a nicer cell to whichever family paid this month's rate"]},{"name":"The Nightclub's Second Vampire","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"rival seductress, hungrier and more reckless","flavor":"The Femme Fatale's rival for the same territory, just as hungry, twice as reckless.","desc":"She works the same room the Femme Fatale claims as hers, a little hungrier, a little less careful about leaving a mess, and doesn't care that the territory dispute is going to end badly for someone.","traits":{"note": "She's not subtle about the territory dispute — she wants the Femme Fatale to notice exactly how reckless she's being.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Second Vampire makes two attacks, using Fiendish Touch or Charm in any combination, or uses Draining Kiss."}, {"name": "Fiendish Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Turf Charm", "replaces": "Charm", "text": "One Humanoid the Second Vampire can see within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed until the end of her next turn, drawn toward her instead of any rival's claim on the room."}, {"name": "Reckless Kiss", "replaces": "Draining Kiss", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the Second Vampire regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt. She has disadvantage on this attack if she's already used it against the same target tonight — she doesn't pace herself well."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's left a body in the Femme Fatale's section of the club, daring her to respond."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's trying to poach the party as regulars, specifically because she knows they belong to her rival."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the party to carry a message to the Femme Fatale she's too proud to deliver herself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A client she fed on too carelessly is asking questions in the wrong parts of town."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers protection from her rival in exchange for the party's silence about something she's done."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started feeding faster and messier every week, as if she can't quite remember why restraint mattered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every mess she leaves behind seems to point, deliberately or not, straight back to the Femme Fatale's door."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight she's decided to settle the territory dispute in front of the whole club, whatever it costs either of them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working the same room the Femme Fatale claims, a little hungrier, a little less careful", "leaving a mess she doesn't bother to clean up before the next set starts"]},{"name":"The Wharf Sea-Witch (Waterfront Fixer)","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"guard","summary":"waterfront fixer, knows what washes up first","flavor":"Trades favors for names at the fish market before dawn, always knows what washed up before the cops do.","desc":"She trades favors for names down at the fish market before the sun's up, salt-cracked hands sorting through the night's catch and the night's rumors with equal patience, and always knows what washed ashore before the police do.","traits":{"note": "She always knows what washed ashore before the police do — the tide tells her first, and she never says how.", "actions": [{"name": "Salt-Cracked Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "The Look That Drowns", "replaces": "Death Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One creature the Wharf Sea-Witch can see within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 22 (4d10) Psychic damage and be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn; on a success, it takes half damage only."}, {"name": "Fishwife's Face", "replaces": "Illusory Appearance", "text": "The Wharf Sea-Witch magically disguises herself as an ordinary dockworker until she attacks or casts a spell, or until she chooses to end the effect (no action required)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She knows what washed up at the wharf last night, and she'll trade the name for one of the party's own."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants someone's disappearance quietly investigated before the harbor patrol notices the pattern."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding a piece of evidence that surfaced with the tide and hasn't decided who deserves it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers safe passage through the docks for information on who's been dumping bodies in her water."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fisherman who owes her a favor has gone missing along with his boat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's begun collecting names of the living the same way she collects names of the drowned, filing them the same."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She always knows a name before its owner drowns, and she's started warning the ones she likes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something bigger than a body has washed up tonight, and she's the only one who knows exactly what it wants."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "urban"],"activity":["trading favors for names at the fish market before the sun's up", "sorting through the night's catch and the night's rumors with the same patient hands"]},{"name":"The Underboss's Enforcer Pack Leader","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"weretiger","model":"weretiger","summary":"underboss's muscle chief, barely hides the stripes","flavor":"Runs the muscle detail for the Underboss, stripes showing through the suit on a bad night.","desc":"He runs the muscle detail in a suit tailored to hide what's underneath, but on a bad night the fabric doesn't quite manage it, and something with stripes shows through at the collar.","traits":{"note": "His crew doesn't ask about the stripes — they've learned it's safer to assume he's always half a step from changing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Pack Leader makes two attacks, using Tiger Bite or Back-Alley Scratch in any combination."}, {"name": "Tiger Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Back-Alley Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Tailored Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 10 (2d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's leading a muscle detail against the party tonight and hasn't fully suppressed the change yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The Underboss wants him to make an example of someone the party's protecting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His tailor's gone missing, and he needs a new one who can keep a secret about the fitting."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers protection from his own crew in exchange for something to help him control the shift."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival crew has figured out what he is and is threatening to expose it publicly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started letting the stripes show more often, tired of the suit fitting like a cage."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His crew has quietly started changing alongside him on bad nights, whether or not they mean to."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The Underboss has finally seen him mid-change, and now it's a question of loyalty or a leash."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["running the muscle detail in a suit tailored to hide what's underneath", "catching stripes showing at the collar on a bad night, and pulling the jacket tighter"]},{"name":"The Crime Scene Cleaner","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"aberrant-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"scene cleaner, erases murders in ninety minutes","flavor":"Erases a murder from a room in ninety minutes flat, has never once left a print of his own.","desc":"He arrives in a plain van with a case of chemicals and rubber gloves, working in total silence, and in ninety minutes flat a room that held a body holds nothing but the smell of bleach.","traits":{"note": "He's never once left a print of his own — nobody knows what he looks like without the gloves and mask.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cleaner makes two attacks with Solvent Lash or uses Mind Rot."}, {"name": "Solvent Lash", "replaces": "Tentacle Lash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Acid damage — his chemicals don't discriminate between blood and living tissue."}, {"name": "Erase the Witness", "replaces": "Mind Rot", "text": "One creature the Cleaner can see within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 16 Intelligence saving throw or take 14 (4d6) Psychic damage and forget the last minute of events on a failed save; on a success, it takes half damage and remembers everything."}, {"name": "Chain of Custody", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cleaner casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a cultist's repertoire appropriate to CR 8, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (save DC 16)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-job erasing a scene the party needs preserved as evidence, van idling outside."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been hired to clean a room the party hasn't found the body in yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's missing a chemical ingredient and is willing to trade a favor for a supplier's name."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to erase the party's involvement in a scene, for a debt he'll collect later."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A client stiffed him on payment and he wants the party to collect, discreetly, no questions."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun keeping small souvenirs from scenes he cleans, unable to explain the impulse even to himself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Rooms he's cleaned stay unnervingly silent afterward, as if the space itself forgot what happened there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been hired to erase a scene that hasn't happened yet, and the address matches somewhere the party will be tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["arriving in a plain van with a case of chemicals, working in total silence", "leaving a room that held a body smelling of nothing but bleach, ninety minutes later"]},{"name":"The Mayor's Handler","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fiend-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"unelected fixer who runs city hall's decisions","flavor":"Nobody elected him to anything, but every decision in city hall runs through him first.","desc":"He stands just off-camera at every press conference, adjusting a microphone that doesn't need adjusting, and every decision that comes out of that podium was really made in a hallway five minutes earlier — by him.","traits":{"note": "Nobody elected him to anything — every decision that reaches the podium was really made by him first.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Handler makes two attacks with Pact Axe or uses Spellcasting once."}, {"name": "Pact Axe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage — the axe was part of a bargain he never explains."}, {"name": "Off the Podium", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Handler casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a fiend-pact repertoire appropriate to CR 8, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 16)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a story killed before tomorrow's press conference, and the party's the ones who leaked it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rewriting the mayor's answer to a question that hasn't been asked yet, and it involves the party."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a rival candidate's dirt buried in exchange for a favor from city hall."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's discovered someone on the mayor's staff is working for the family and needs it handled off the books."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a permit, a pardon, or a blind eye — whichever the party needs most tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun making decisions for the mayor that the mayor hasn't been informed of at all."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every promise he makes on the mayor's behalf comes true exactly as spoken, whether the mayor agreed to it or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The bargain behind the axe is finally coming due, and it wants a decision only the mayor is supposed to have the power to make."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing just off-camera at a press conference, adjusting a mic that doesn't need it", "deciding the mayor's next answer in a hallway, five minutes before anyone asks the question"]},{"name":"The Old Money Enforcer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"questing-knight","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"forty-year enforcer, protected by high names","flavor":"Old family muscle who never got a mugshot in forty years, protected by names in high places.","desc":"He's never had a mugshot taken in forty years of breaking hands for the family, moving through the city with the calm of a man who knows exactly which names in this town can make a warrant disappear.","traits":{"note": "Forty years and never a mugshot — the names protecting him go higher than anyone in the room wants to say out loud.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Old Family Blade", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Collector's Bow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 10 (2d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting on a decades-old debt from a family the party's been hired to protect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A young cop with something to prove has finally found evidence against him and needs protecting or silencing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to deliver a message too polite to say himself, backed by an implied threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been ordered to retire someone who used to break hands beside him, and he's slow to move on it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a name that could make a warrant disappear, in trade for a debt collected personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun keeping his own tally of every hand he's broken, a private ledger he's never shown anyone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every warrant issued against him over forty years has vanished from the same drawer, in the same office, signed by names long dead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The names protecting him have finally gone quiet, and for the first time in forty years, someone's coming to take the mugshot."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["moving through the city with the calm of a man who knows which warrants vanish", "breaking a debtor's hand with the same unhurried grace as shaking it"]},{"name":"The Precinct's Own Ghost Detective","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"guard","summary":"dead detective, solving his buried case louder","flavor":"Died solving the one case the department buried, and now solves it louder every year.","desc":"His desk in the bullpen is still there, chair pushed back the way he left it the night he died chasing a case the department wanted buried. Every year on the date, something walks the halls asking louder than it did the year before.","traits":{"note": "Its volume/intensity scales on the anniversary of its death; otherwise a quieter, wandering haunting."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's walking the halls again tonight, and this year he's finally said a name the party recognizes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party to reopen the case file the department buried decades ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's fixated on someone in the precinct who resembles whoever framed him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's willing to point toward evidence still hidden in the building, if the party will finally listen to the whole case."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rookie cop has started hearing him and doesn't know whether to report it or help him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun showing up on nights other than the anniversary, as if his patience for waiting a year at a time has run out."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The case file he's chasing rewrites itself in the archive overnight, closer to the truth each time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally worked out who buried the case, and that name is walking into the precinct tonight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting at a desk pushed back the way he left it the night he died", "walking the halls once a year, asking his buried case louder than the year before"]},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin's First Lieutenant","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"guard","summary":"vampire's daylight proxy, runs business he can't","flavor":"Turned decades ago as a reward for loyalty, runs the daylight business the kingpin can't touch.","desc":"He handles the daylight business the kingpin can't touch himself — meetings in sunlit offices, handshakes in broad daylight — loyalty earned decades ago with a bite that never quite killed him.","traits":{"note": "Turned decades ago as a reward, not a punishment — he owes the kingpin everything and resents it more each year.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Lieutenant makes two attacks, using Ledger Claw or Loyalty's Bite in any combination."}, {"name": "Ledger Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Loyalty's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage, and the Lieutenant regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's brokering a daylight deal the kingpin can't be seen making, and the party's caught in the middle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a sunlit alibi covered for a night he can't account for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's quietly testing whether the party could be turned against the kingpin, feeling out their loyalty."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a business favor in daylight hours no vampire could otherwise manage."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival has figured out he's the kingpin's proxy and is threatening to expose the arrangement."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun resenting the decades of loyalty the bite bought, and it shows in how carelessly he spends the kingpin's money."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's started making decisions the kingpin never authorized, testing how far the daylight leash actually reaches."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally decided the debt of being turned has been paid in full, and tonight he's collecting on his maker instead."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["handling the daylight business the kingpin can't touch, handshake warm and steady", "sitting through a sunlit meeting no one suspects is run by something that shouldn't survive it"]},{"name":"The Sewer Hitman's Mentor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"guard","summary":"veteran hitman who trained the whole waterfront","flavor":"Taught every hired gun on the waterfront everything they know, and kept the best tricks for himself.","desc":"He sits at the back of a waterfront bar nursing the same drink for hours, watching younger hitters practice a trade he perfected before most of them were born, keeping the best tricks for himself out of habit, not spite.","traits":{"note": "He kept the best tricks for himself out of habit, not spite — though it's cost the trade more than one promising student.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mentor makes two attacks with Dread Scythe or uses Deathly Ray."}, {"name": "Dread Scythe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Deathly Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 150 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "One Last Trick", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Mentor casts a spell requiring no material components, drawn from a death-cultist's repertoire appropriate to CR 9, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (save DC 16)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's evaluating whether the party is skilled enough to poach as students, or dangerous enough to remove."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His best student has gone rogue and he wants the party to bring her back rather than kill her."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding information on every hitter he's trained, and a rival wants that list badly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to call off a hit on the party in exchange for one favor, unspecified, collectible anytime."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's being hunted by a student he refused to teach his last, best trick."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun teaching sloppier lessons on purpose, unwilling to admit he's slowing down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every student he's ever trained still moves exactly the way he taught them, even the ones he's since killed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally decided to teach his last trick to someone, and the choice is going to end someone else's career tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["nursing the same drink for hours at the back of a waterfront bar", "watching younger hitters practice a trade he perfected before they were born"]},{"name":"The Family's Freighter (Armored Smuggling Ship)","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"rigged smuggling ship, hull shrugs off gunfire","flavor":"A hollowed cargo ship rigged with hidden compartments and a hull that shrugs off harbor-patrol fire.","desc":"It rides low in the water with hidden compartments welded into a hull that's taken harbor-patrol fire before and kept moving, engines groaning up through the deck plates like something that resents being questioned.","traits":{"note": "It's taken harbor-patrol fire before and kept moving — the hull's reputation alone keeps most boats from getting close.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Freighter makes two Hull Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Hull Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's running its heaviest cargo of the year tonight, and the harbor patrol has finally been tipped off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hidden compartment has been compromised, and the family wants the leak found before the ship docks again."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying someone the party's been hired to intercept before it reaches open water."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its captain wants the party's help running one route past a rival gang's blockade."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's taken damage that no shipyard the family trusts is willing to fix without questions."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun favoring one particular route obsessively, past a stretch of water the crew won't explain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The compartments shift position between voyages, as if the ship itself decides where the cargo is safest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's cargo is something even the ship's own crew doesn't want to know they're carrying."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["riding low in the water, hull groaning with hidden compartments and old bullet scars", "idling just past the breakwater, engines resenting every question asked of it"]},{"name":"The City's Corrupt Commissioner","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"guard","summary":"commissioner who legislated the rackets' survival","flavor":"Set every policy that lets the rackets breathe, and framed it all as tough-on-crime reform.","desc":"He gives a speech about law and order from behind a podium with the department seal, using the exact language that lets every racket in the city keep breathing underneath the policy he just signed.","traits":{"note": "He's never broken a law himself — he just writes the ones that let everyone else break them safely.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Commissioner makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "Podium Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Off-the-Record Bolt", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage, with advantage against a target that hasn't acted yet in the fight."}, {"name": "Policy Cover", "replaces": "Smoke Bomb (1/Day)", "text": "As a bonus action, the Commissioner drops a smoke bomb, filling a 15-foot radius centered on him with heavily obscuring smoke that lasts until the end of his next turn, then takes the Disengage action for free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's about to announce a reform policy that would legally protect the exact racket the party's investigating."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a scandal buried before tomorrow's press cycle catches it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A journalist has finally connected his policy language to a specific family's payroll."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to write a policy exemption custom-built for whatever the party's currently doing illegally."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's being blackmailed by someone who has the original drafts of his 'reform' language."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun writing policy nobody asked for, just to see how much of the city he can legally hand over."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every policy he's signed has quietly rewritten some older law, so the original text no longer exists anywhere."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally been asked to sign something that would make an entire district disappear from the law's protection, and the ink's already out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["giving a law-and-order speech behind the department seal, meaning none of it literally", "signing a policy that lets every racket in the city keep breathing underneath it"]},{"name":"The Bench's Ghost (Wrongful-Execution Revenant)","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"guard","summary":"wrongly-executed man, death didn't settle it","flavor":"Executed for a crime the real judge sold to someone else, and death didn't settle the account.","desc":"It stands in the execution chamber the department stopped using, in the same clothes it wore the night the state killed it for a crime the real judge sold to someone else. Death didn't settle the account, and it isn't interested in settling for anything less than the truth.","traits":{"note": "Death didn't settle the account — it isn't interested in settling for anything less than the name of who really did it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bench's Ghost makes two attacks, using Life Drain or Longsword in any combination."}, {"name": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the Ghost regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt."}, {"name": "Condemned Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Called Before the Bench", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "The Ghost calls up to three Undead it can see within 60 feet to obey a single command it issues — testify, guard, or attack — no action required of them beyond that command."}, {"name": "The Verdict's Gaze", "replaces": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One creature the Ghost can see within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or be Paralyzed with the certainty of its own guilt until the end of the Ghost's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's found the real judge's name at last, and wants the party to deliver a message that isn't a request."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixated on the current judge occupying the same bench, mistaking her for its betrayer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the original case file, buried decades ago, brought to the execution chamber to be read aloud."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guard on duty that night is still alive, and it wants the party to find him before it does."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to reveal where the true evidence was hidden, if the party will speak its name back into the record."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun holding trial for anyone who enters the old chamber, unable to distinguish visitors from the guilty."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The execution chamber's clock always reads the exact time it died, no matter how many times it's replaced."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The real judge who sold the verdict has finally been named in public record, and the chamber's doors have started opening on their own."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing in the execution chamber the department stopped using, in the clothes it died in", "waiting for a truth the state never gave it before it was killed"]},{"name":"The Nightclub Owner (Dhampir Front-Man)","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"half-vampire heir, hunts from his own club","flavor":"Half-turned heir apparent to the Vampire Kingpin, runs the club as his own private hunting ground.","desc":"He greets guests at the door of his own club with a warm handshake and teeth just a shade too sharp when he smiles, half his father's line and half his own ambition, hunting from the VIP booth he never leaves.","traits":{"note": "Half his father's line and half his own ambition — he wants the kingpin's empire more than he wants the man himself dead.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Owner makes two attacks, using VIP Bite or Shadow Strike in any combination."}, {"name": "VIP Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Shadow Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10 + 3) Necrotic damage. The Owner has advantage on this attack if he's within dim light or darkness."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's marked a guest in the VIP booth as tonight's meal, and it's someone the party's protecting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the party's help quietly outmaneuvering his father's oldest lieutenant."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a debt of his father's that he intends to collect before the old man notices it's gone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers VIP access and protection, in trade for information about a rival club owner."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guest he fed on too openly has started talking, and he needs it quieted before his father hears."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun testing how much of his father's empire he can quietly redirect without anyone above him noticing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's started craving daylight in a way his father never described, and it worries him more than he'll admit."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally decided the kingpin's throne is worth more than the kingpin's blessing, and tonight the club is the battleground."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["greeting guests at his own club's door, teeth a shade too sharp when he smiles", "hunting from the VIP booth he never bothers to leave"]},{"name":"The Kingpin's Rival (Old Blood, New Money)","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"self-made rival, wants the old families' turf","flavor":"Bought his way up from nothing and wants the whole waterfront the old families still hold.","desc":"He walks into the old families' territory in a suit that cost more than their grandfather's whole fleet, smiling like a man who bought his way here and intends to buy the rest of it too.","traits":{"note": "He built his fortune from nothing and resents every old name that still looks down on him for it — even as he outspends them all.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Rival makes two weapon attacks."}, {"name": "New Money Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Buyout", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Name Your Price", "text": "1/Day. As a bonus action, the Rival offers a fortune to one creature he can see within 30 feet. That creature must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom saving throw or immediately switch sides in the current conflict, refusing to attack the Rival or his allies for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's trying to buy out a piece of old-family territory the party has a stake in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party more money than the old families ever would, to switch which side they're working for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants proof of an old family's original, dirtier fortune to use as leverage in a takeover."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's being publicly humiliated by an old name at every society function and wants it to stop, quietly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to fund whatever the party's working on, in exchange for information on the old families' weaknesses."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun buying things no one needs just to prove he can, testing how much of the old world bends to new money."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every deal he closes seems to quietly rewrite who the old families think has always owned the waterfront."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's finally made an offer the Vampire Kingpin himself can't refuse without losing face, and the whole city's watching to see who blinks."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["walking into old-family territory in a suit that cost more than their grandfather's fleet", "smiling like a man who bought his way in and intends to buy the rest"]},{"name":"The Kingpin's Enforcer Elite (Death Knight of the Docks)","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"guard","summary":"undead debt collector, rose to keep collecting","flavor":"A soldier who died collecting for the kingpin and rose to keep collecting, forever, without complaint.","desc":"It stands at the end of the pier in rusted armor that used to be a uniform, collecting debts from men who are certain they already paid, because it died mid-collection and never clocked out.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Undying Ledger", "text": "Marks a target as 'in debt'; deals bonus damage to any target it has already marked this encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's collecting from someone in the party's crew who swears the debt was settled years ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's blocking the only dock the party's boat can use until its list is cleared."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a rusted ledger the party needs to prove who really owed the dead man money."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistook a party member's name for one on its list and won't be talked out of the error."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a crate of unmarked cargo until the kingpin's runner arrives to claim it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It wants its own death struck from the record so the collecting can finally stop."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its ledger adds new names in wet ink whenever someone nearby lies about money."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The kingpin himself is due at the pier tonight, and the Enforcer intends to present its backlog in person."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["standing at the end of the pier reading names off a soaked ledger nobody else can see", "collecting from a man who's certain the debt was already paid, and won't be told otherwise"]},{"name":"The Family's Assassin-Twins","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"guard","summary":"twin killers splitting mark and witness work","flavor":"Two killers who split every contract down the middle, one takes the mark, one takes the witnesses.","desc":"They arrive together, always, splitting the work without a word between them — one takes the mark, one takes whoever saw it happen. Nobody's ever caught them apart long enough to be sure there are two.","traits":{"note": "Separate them and each one fights like half a plan — dangerous, but visibly waiting on the other.", "actions": [{"name": "The Mark's Half", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 21 (6d6) Force damage. If the twins' other half has damaged a different target this round, this attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage — the contract closes faster split two ways."}, {"name": "Witness Work", "text": "1/Day each. As a bonus action, a twin marks one creature that saw them arrive. Until the end of combat, that twin has advantage on attack rolls against the marked creature — the mark was never meant to leave and speak of it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One twin has already been paid for the mark; the other is here purely for the witnesses — meaning the party."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're splitting a contract on someone the party is protecting, half taking the front door, half the back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're arguing, silently, over which of them gets the party as the mark and which gets them as witnesses."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One twin is wounded and hiding it, waiting for the other to finish the job alone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've been contracted to make sure a specific piece of evidence never reaches a courtroom."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One twin wants to break the arrangement and needs the party to remove the other without her noticing who ordered it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They finish each other's kills mid-swing, as though one blade decided to be delivered by two hands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Their current contract names everyone the party has ever protected, paid in full, no refunds."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["splitting a rooftop watch in perfect silence, each one facing a different exit", "dividing a job over coffee without a single word passing between them"]},{"name":"The Fallen DA (Ultimate Corruption)","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"soul-sold DA, nothing human left underneath","flavor":"Sold his conviction record to the family piece by piece until nothing human was left underneath the suit.","desc":"He stands at the courtroom podium in a suit that fits too well for a public salary, reciting a closing argument with a smile that never reaches whatever's left behind his eyes. There's nothing human under the collar anymore — just the record he sold, piece by piece.","traits":{"note": "Speaks in courtroom cadence even mid-combat, as if still building a closing argument."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's building a case against the party using evidence the family fed him overnight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to drop the charges against a party member in exchange for a name he wants buried."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a subpoena that would expose the family, and hasn't decided whether to file it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A witness the party needs is due to testify against him at nine tomorrow and he knows it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rehearsing the closing argument that will convict an innocent man by morning."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants one honest verdict before the end, and the party's case is his last chance at it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His briefcase holds case files that rewrite themselves to match whatever verdict he's already decided."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The tome holding his sold soul is in the room, and destroying it would free every soul he's bound inside it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rehearsing a closing argument to an empty courtroom, smile fixed and unmoving", "reviewing a soul-priced ledger disguised as case files at his desk after hours"]},{"name":"The Judge's Devil (Contract Behind the Bench)","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"erinyes","summary":"devil holding the judge's real signed contract","flavor":"The thing that actually holds the corrupt judge's real contract, collects on every sentence sold.","desc":"It sits behind the judge's chair where no one else can see it, holding a contract with a signature that predates the man's career, collecting patiently on every sentence that gets sold from that bench.","traits":{"note": "It only acts when the judge's verdict is challenged — protecting the contract matters more than protecting the man.", "actions": [{"name": "Withering Verdict", "replaces": "Withering Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (2d8 + 6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Bound Over", "replaces": "Entangling Rope (Requires Magic Rope)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 30 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) damage, and the target is Restrained until it escapes with a successful DC 17 Strength (Athletics) check — the rope is written into the same contract as the verdicts."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces the moment a party member tries to appeal a sentence the judge sold."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the physical contract, which is the only proof the judge is compromised."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to void one sentence in the ledger — for a name the party hasn't given up yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows exactly which case the party is trying to overturn, and got there first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's collecting on a verdict sold years ago that just came due against someone the party knows."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown tired of the judge's cowardice and wants the party to force a confession it can collect on directly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The contract's signature shifts to match whoever is currently reading it, claiming everyone equally."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The judge is about to resign, and the devil intends to collect the entire ledger's debt in one sitting, tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting unseen behind the judge's chair, patiently rereading a signature older than the courthouse", "tallying which sentences sold today against a contract nobody in the room can see"]},{"name":"The City's Silent Partner (Shadow Financier)","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"shadow financier laundering money through society","flavor":"Owns pieces of every legitimate business downtown, laundering the family's money through polite society.","desc":"He attends every charity gala downtown, glass of champagne in hand, name on half the buildings' deeds through companies that don't exist on paper, laundering blood money through polite conversation.","traits":{"note": "He never threatens directly — the threat is always a company you've never heard of that suddenly owns your lease.", "actions": [{"name": "Polite Ruin", "replaces": "Cursed Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the target has disadvantage on its next saving throw against his spells — his handshake unmakes what it touches."}, {"name": "Called Note", "replaces": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One creature he can see within 60 ft. must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom save or be Charmed until the end of its next turn and use its reaction to move away from an ally — every asset has fine print."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He owns the lease on the building the party is currently standing in, and just noticed they're late."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to buy out a debt the party owes someone far more dangerous."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's laundering money through a charity the party was hired to protect."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a rival's shell companies exposed without his own name ever surfacing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding the deed to a safehouse the party thought was untraceable."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's decided the party's reputation is a good investment and quietly starts buying pieces of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His paperwork rewrites ownership overnight, so buildings change hands without anyone signing anything."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's about to call in every note across downtown at once, and half the city will owe him by morning."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working the room at a charity gala, champagne in hand, quietly noting who owes whom", "reviewing deeds to buildings that don't officially exist on any city map"]},{"name":"The Godmother (Matriarch of the Family)","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"guard","summary":"true power behind the Don, unseen matriarch","flavor":"Never took the Don's title but every real decision in the family runs through her kitchen table first.","desc":"She holds court at her own kitchen table over coffee, apron still on, and every real decision the Don announces in public was decided here first, over cups that never get cold before the next one's poured.","traits":{"note": "The Don's public word is only ever a formality; nothing moves in the family until she's poured a second cup.", "actions": [{"name": "Kitchen Table Verdict", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 24 (7d6) Force damage. On a hit, the target has disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than her until the start of her next turn — she's already decided who matters here."}, {"name": "Family Business", "text": "1/Day. As a bonus action, she designates one ally within 60 ft. That ally can immediately use its reaction to make one weapon attack — every decision in the room runs through her first, then out through someone else's hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's decided the party is useful, and useful people get invited to her table, not shot at it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the Don's public order countermanded quietly, and the party is the quiet part."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding evidence that the Don answers to her, and it would break the family in half if it surfaced."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers the party protection from the family — on the condition they never mention where the offer came from."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's deciding, over coffee, whether a party member lives past tonight, and hasn't poured the second cup yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's tired of ruling from behind a curtain and considers letting the party be the ones who finally say her name out loud."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every cup she pours matches, exactly, a decision being made somewhere else in the city at that same moment."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "She decides, calmly, that tonight the family stops being a family and becomes an army, and every captain in the city hears it at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pouring coffee at her own kitchen table while the family's real business gets decided", "listening to a captain's report and deciding his fate before he finishes the sentence"]},{"name":"The Frame Job (Living Conspiracy)","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"self-aware conspiracy of false evidence, alive","flavor":"A tangle of false confessions, planted evidence, and bought witnesses that has learned to think for itself.","desc":"It isn't a person — it's a case file that grew a mind, planted evidence and bought testimony tangled into something that files its own reports now, moving through the records room like paper come alive with intent.","traits":{"note": "Manifests as animated paperwork/evidence rather than a conventional body; unsettling rather than physically imposing at first glance.", "actions": [{"name": "False Confession", "text": "Forces a save on a target or plants a false memory of guilt, causing self-inflicted psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's assembling a confession with a party member's name already typed into the blank."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the only file that could clear an innocent man the party is trying to save."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to bury evidence against the party — in exchange for a body to blame instead."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grown a second file naming a party member as the witness who never existed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's found in the records room stitching together three unrelated cases into one convenient story."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It wants to be read by someone who won't just believe it, testing whether the party can see through its own paperwork."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It rewrites its own case number every time someone tries to cite it, so it can never be officially closed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to file its masterpiece — a confession naming every name in the city at once, true or not."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["shuffling through the records room at 3 a.m., filing reports no clerk ever wrote", "assembling a confession out of testimony that never happened, in a voice made of paper"]},{"name":"The Executioner's Debt (Mummified Hangman)","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"guard","summary":"mummified hangman, still working an endless backlog","flavor":"The city's official executioner, embalmed and still working through a backlog of names he was never given.","desc":"It works through a backlog of names in a condemned cell nobody's used in decades, wrappings the color of old rope, still keeping the appointment book of a job the city officially ended long ago.","traits":{"note": "It considers every unfinished sentence a debt owed to it personally, and it has an excellent memory.", "actions": [{"name": "Overdue Sentence", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the target's Hit Point maximum is reduced by the damage dealt until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "The Backlog", "replaces": "Channel Negative Energy", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that the Executioner has marked in its appointment book must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution save or take 27 (6d8) Necrotic damage and be Frightened until the end of its next turn; on a success, half damage only."}, {"name": "Reads Off the List", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "One creature it can see within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, hearing its own name read from a ledger of the condemned."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's added a party member's name to its appointment book by mistake, and mistakes don't get crossed out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the cell where the real evidence against the family has been sealed for decades."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to strike a name from its list — in exchange for a fresh one to replace it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's working through a backlog that includes an ancestor of someone in the party."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's found keeping an appointment with a man who's been dead for years and doesn't know it yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It wants its old job back, officially, and thinks the party can convince a judge to reopen the gallows."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its appointment book adds new names in a hand no living clerk has ever used."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its book is finally complete tonight, and it intends to keep every appointment in it before dawn."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["keeping an appointment book in a condemned cell, checking names against a backlog decades overdue", "adjusting an old rope's knot with wrapped hands that never stopped counting"]},{"name":"The Vampire Kingpin's Ancient Rival","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"guard","summary":"ancient undead rival, predates the city's charter","flavor":"Older than the city's founding charter, wants the throne of blood-debt the kingpin only thinks he owns.","desc":"It arrives at the meeting older than the paperwork that founded the city, wanting the throne of blood-debt the current kingpin only believes he owns, patient in the particular way of something that has already outlasted every rival once.","traits":{"note": "It never raises its voice against the current kingpin — it simply reminds the room whose city this really was first.", "actions": [{"name": "Elder Claim", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 19 (2d10 + 8) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest — the debt it claims is older than the wound."}, {"name": "Older Fire", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +12, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 28 (8d6) Fire damage, or half damage if the target succeeds on a DC 19 Dexterity save."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the party to carry a message to the current kingpin: the charter he cites was never his to sign."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party a piece of the kingpin's territory if they'll help topple him quietly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a deed older than the city's founding that names it, not the kingpin, as owner of the docks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the current kingpin's weaknesses intimately, and is willing to trade them for one favor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's testing the party as potential enforcers for the throne it intends to reclaim."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown almost fond of losing slowly and wants the party to end the rivalry outright, one way or the other."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers streets that no longer exist and gives directions that are somehow still correct."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It calls in every blood-debt the city ever owed before the current kingpin's charter existed, and the ground itself seems to remember owing it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["reviewing a claim to the city's blood-debt that predates its current owner by a century", "waiting outside the kingpin's territory with the patience of something that has already outlasted rivals before"]},{"name":"The Last Honest Cop, Corrupted (Apex Fall)","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"demilich","model":"demilich","summary":"the last honest cop, broken and remade undying","flavor":"The one detective who never took a dime, broken and remade by the family into something that never sleeps or stops.","desc":"It walks the beat it walked in life, badge fused to a chest that hasn't drawn breath in years, the one detective who never took a dime — broken by the family and remade into something that never sleeps, never stops, and never quite remembers what honest used to mean.","traits":{"note": "Somewhere under the corruption the family forced into it, a fragment of the honest cop still tries to read people their rights.", "actions": [{"name": "By the Book", "replaces": "Necrotic Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +13, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 32 (7d8) Necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack is treated as under arrest — its corpse cannot be raised or disturbed until the Cop is destroyed."}, {"name": "The Last Warning", "replaces": "Howl (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear it must succeed on a DC 19 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn — some buried part of it still means the warning kindly."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's arresting a party member for a crime that hasn't happened yet, in a city where it technically still can."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A flicker of the honest cop it used to be tries to warn the party away before the family notices they're here."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the last piece of evidence it collected before it died — proof the family bought the whole precinct."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recognizes a party member's face from a case file it never got to close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's standing watch outside a shuttered station house that the family wants demolished before anyone searches it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It wants the party to finish the one case it never closed, the only thing that might let it finally stop walking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its badge reflects whoever looks at it as the officer they most needed and never had."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "For one night a year it remembers every crime the family ever bought its way out of, and tries to arrest the entire city at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking a beat that ended years ago, badge fused to a chest that no longer breathes", "standing outside a precinct the department shut down, waiting for a shift change that isn't coming"]},{"name":"the Chiseler","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"petty street grifter, first line of noir muscle","flavor":"Works the crowd outside the courthouse, palming wallets and running the pigeon drop. Bolts the second a mark makes him.","desc":"He works the crowd outside the courthouse steps, palming a wallet here, running the pigeon drop there, moving with the loose, unbothered gait of a man who's never once been caught looking. The second a mark's eyes narrow, he's already three people away.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Palmed Blade", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Wild Toss", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works the courthouse steps, palming wallets between witnesses arriving for testimony."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs the pigeon drop on tourists near the wharf, splitting the take with a lookout."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loiters outside a pawnshop, fencing what he lifted an hour ago at half its worth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bumps marks in a crowded trolley car, blaming the jostle on someone else entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works in a pair now, one distracting while the other does the actual lifting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started forging claim tickets alongside the wallets, upgrading from petty theft to petty fraud."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never seems to be seen taking anything, only ever seen having already taken it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Picked the wrong pocket tonight and is being chased by someone with a much longer memory than the cops."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["palming a wallet outside the courthouse steps with a loose, unbothered gait", "running the pigeon drop on a mark three people back from where he's already standing"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled small-time grifter/pickpocket stock type"},{"name":"the Torpedo","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"rlm-noir-gangster","summary":"low-level muscle for hire, leans on debtors","flavor":"A rented fist in a cheap suit, sent to lean on shopkeepers who are late on the vig. Talks with his knuckles first.","desc":"A rented fist in a suit a size too cheap, standing outside a shuttered shop with his hands in his pockets, waiting on a vig that's late. He talks with his knuckles before he talks with his mouth.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Leaning On You", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warning Toss", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leans against a doorframe outside a shop that's three weeks behind on the vig."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorts a nervous shopkeeper to the back room to explain the new payment schedule."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits at a bus stop for a specific mark to walk by so the message lands in public."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breaks a window instead of a kneecap this time, as a professional courtesy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works with a partner who does the talking while he just stands there being the point."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started feeling bad about the shopkeepers and takes it out on the furniture instead of the people."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Always seems to know exactly how much a mark has left before anyone opens a register."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Was told to make an example tonight and is not entirely sure where the line for that is anymore."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing outside a shuttered shop with his hands in his pockets, waiting on a late vig", "cracking his knuckles in a doorway while a shopkeeper counts out short money"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled hired-gun enforcer archetype"},{"name":"the Wire Man","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"bent patrolman feeding tips to the rackets","flavor":"A beat cop on the take, radio turned down so the boys upstairs get the tip-off first. His badge buys silence, not justice.","desc":"He walks his beat with the radio turned down low, glancing at his watch more than the street, making sure the boys upstairs get word before the dispatcher does. The badge on his chest buys silence, not the other thing it's supposed to.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Nightstick", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks his beat with the radio turned down, glancing at his watch more than the street."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loiters by a payphone at the same hour every night, waiting on the same call."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waves a patrol car past a warehouse he's been paid to not notice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades a folded bill for a folded note without either party breaking stride."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Writes a report that's technically accurate and entirely useless to whoever reads it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started skimming off both sides, tipping off the rackets and quietly warning their marks too."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His radio picks up chatter from precincts that were decommissioned years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just overheard something on the wire that names him, specifically, as the next loose end to tie off."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking his beat with the radio turned down low, checking his watch more than the street", "loitering near a payphone to make sure the boys upstairs hear it first"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"dirty-cop / bent-badge archetype"},{"name":"the Wheelman","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"getaway driver, mobile support in a chase","flavor":"Never draws a piece, never needs to — his job is making sure everyone else is three blocks gone before the sirens turn the corner.","desc":"He sits behind the wheel with the engine already running, one hand on the shifter, watching a door across the street with the patience of a man who's done this a hundred times and never once been caught doing it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cut and Run", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warning Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits at the curb with the engine idling, watching a door across the street through the mirror."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the block three times exactly, never stopping in the same spot twice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a second car parked two streets over in case the first one gets made."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts down under his breath, timing the job by a stopwatch he never lets anyone else touch."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the radio on low, listening for the dispatch call before it's even sent."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started timing the sirens instead of the job, growing more nervous about the count each time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Somehow always knows the exact moment to pull away, before anyone inside has even signaled him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His usual three-block head start just evaporated — the sirens are already on this block."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting behind the wheel with the engine running, one hand already on the shifter", "watching a door across the street with the patience of a man who's never once been caught"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"getaway-driver stock type"},{"name":"the Shakedown Man","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"half-ogre-ogrillon","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"protection-racket collector, bigger and blunter","flavor":"Built like a delivery truck and twice as polite about it — right up until the register doesn't open fast enough.","desc":"He fills the doorway of the corner shop like a delivery truck that learned manners, tipping his hat to the owner right up until the register comes up short — then the manners go away fast.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Persuasion", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage, or 11 (1d10 + 5) Slashing damage if used with two hands."}, {"name": "Thrown Reminder", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fills the doorway of a corner shop, tipping his hat while the register comes up short."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stacks crates for a shopkeeper unasked, making it clear how easily they could be un-stacked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits at the back entrance so the owner can't claim he never saw him coming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Brings a ledger of his own to double-check the shop's math against the family's."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely helps carry the week's take to the car himself, just to be sure."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started leaving a little extra behind for shops that are clearly struggling, against orders."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never seems to knock — he's simply already inside the doorway when anyone looks up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Was told this shop gets made an example of tonight, and the manners just ran out early."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["filling a shop doorway like a delivery truck that learned manners", "tipping his hat to a nervous owner while counting the register from across the room"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"protection-racket collector archetype"},{"name":"the Cigarette Girl","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy","model":"spy","summary":"club-floor informant, trades gossip for coin","flavor":"Sells smokes table to table at the club and sells whispers to whoever's paying after close. Everyone underestimates the tray.","desc":"She moves table to table under the club lights with a tray strapped around her neck, selling smokes with a smile that never quite reaches her eyes, and selling whatever she overheard to whoever's still buying after the band packs up.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Tray Blade", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Under the Tray", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works table to table under the club lights, tray strapped tight, smile not reaching her eyes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lingers near the private booths, selling smokes and listening far longer than the sale needs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades a name for a tip after close, to whoever's buying and looking desperate enough."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a little notebook under the tray, jotting initials instead of orders."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works two clubs a night, carrying gossip from one to the other for a fee."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started selling the same secret to both sides of a feud, banking on neither ever comparing notes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Remembers every conversation she's ever half-overheard, word for word, years later."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just overheard the wrong secret from the wrong table, and someone noticed her noticing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["moving table to table under the club lights, tray strapped tight, smile not reaching her eyes", "selling whatever she overheard to whoever's still buying after the band packs up"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"nightclub-informant/eyes-and-ears archetype"},{"name":"the Enforcer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"rlm-noir-brute","summary":"crime lord's blunt-instrument muscle","flavor":"The crime lord's answer when words stop working. Doesn't monologue, doesn't negotiate — just walks in slow and leaves loud.","desc":"He walks in slow, hands empty, and that's somehow worse than if they weren't — no threats, no speech, just a silence that fills up the room until somebody breaks first.","traits":{"note": "He never monologues — the quiet is the message, and he lets it sit as long as it needs to.", "actions": [{"name": "Blunt Argument", "replaces": "Oversized Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Last Word", "replaces": "Skullthumper (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 18 (4d8) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Stunned until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Thrown Point", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks in slow, hands empty, letting the silence fill the room before anyone says a word."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits by the door of a meeting, arms crossed, until the negotiation ends the way it should."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breaks furniture instead of faces first, as an opening statement."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorts someone out of a bar by the collar without raising his voice once."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Delivers a message by simply standing where the recipient can't avoid seeing him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started leaving before the violence, letting the reputation alone do the closing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Rooms go quiet before he even opens the door, as if the building already knows him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Was told this one doesn't get a warning, and the silence tonight has an edge to it that wasn't there before."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking in slow with empty hands, letting the silence do the threatening", "standing in a doorway until somebody in the room breaks first"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled enforcer stock type named in the brief"},{"name":"the Dirty Cop","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"corrupt detective, badge as much as bribe","flavor":"Made detective the honest way, then found out honest doesn't pay the mortgage. Still carries the badge like it means something.","desc":"He made detective the honest way, once, and still wears the badge like it means what it used to. The envelope in his coat pocket says otherwise, and so does the mortgage he can't explain on a cop's salary.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sanctioned Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Makes detective the honest way once, and still wears the badge like it means that."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pockets an envelope mid-conversation without breaking eye contact."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Files a report that quietly omits the one detail that would sink a friend of the family."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Buys a round for the precinct on a salary that shouldn't cover it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warns a suspect to run before the real search warrant arrives."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started keeping a second, honest ledger, in case he ever needs to prove what he actually did."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His badge tarnishes a little more each time he takes an envelope, and he's stopped noticing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Internal affairs finally has a name on their list, and it's his, tonight, with no time left to clean up."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["wearing the badge like it still means what it used to, envelope heavy in his coat pocket", "running numbers in his head that don't add up on a cop's salary"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"corrupt-detective archetype named in the brief"},{"name":"the Torch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-captain","model":"hobgoblin-captain","summary":"arsonist-for-hire, insurance jobs and cleanup","flavor":"Burns warehouses for insurance money and burns witnesses for free. Whistles while the building comes down.","desc":"He circles the warehouse whistling something off-key, match already between two fingers, and doesn't stop whistling even as the beams start to groan behind him.","traits":{"note": "He whistles the same three notes every job — the men who've heard it before know exactly what it means.", "actions": [{"name": "Insurance Job", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Cleanup Toss", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Fire damage — a rag-wrapped javelin, soaked and burning."}, {"name": "Rally the Crew", "replaces": "Leadership (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)", "text": "For 1 minute, the Torch can utter a special command each of his turns as a bonus action, granting one ally within 30 ft. who can hear him a bonus to attack rolls equal to his Charisma modifier (+3)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles a warehouse whistling off-key, match already lit between two fingers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sets a small fire first as a distraction before the real job starts elsewhere."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stages the burn to look like faulty wiring, right down to the scorch pattern."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits outside to make sure the last witness doesn't make it out the back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times a burn to a delivery schedule so the loss looks like an accident of timing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started leaving small mercies — an unlocked door, a warning shout — that his employers would not approve of."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fires he sets always burn the exact shape of whatever he's whistling at the time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Was told to burn a building with people still arguing about getting out of it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling a warehouse whistling off-key, match already lit between two fingers", "not stopping the tune even as the beams start to groan behind him"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"professional-arsonist-for-hire archetype"},{"name":"the Coroner's Friend","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"bought-off examiner, falsifies causes of death","flavor":"Signs whatever cause of death keeps the retainer coming. A gunshot wound becomes 'heart failure' for the right envelope.","desc":"He signs the certificate before he's finished writing the report, pen moving fast toward whatever cause of death the retainer's paying for this week. A gunshot wound becomes heart failure, and nobody in the room argues.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Convenient Verdict", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Certified Cut", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage, or 12 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage if used with two hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs the certificate before he's finished writing the report, pen already moving toward the paid-for cause."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges by the word for how a cause of death gets phrased."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps two sets of files — one true, one filed — in different drawers of the same cabinet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loses a body's paperwork entirely for the right retainer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rushes an autopsy to miss a detail someone paid him specifically to miss."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started keeping the real findings hidden in his own home, insurance against the day his patrons turn on him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His certificates seem to become true the moment they're filed, no matter what actually happened."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's been asked to falsify a death that hasn't happened yet, and the timing terrifies even him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["signing a death certificate before finishing the report, pen already moving toward the paid-for cause", "turning a gunshot wound into heart failure while nobody in the room argues"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"corrupt-medical-examiner / hush-money doctor archetype"},{"name":"the Consigliere","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"family strategist, plans the violence others do","flavor":"Never raises his voice, never touches a weapon — he just tells the boss which enemies to forgive and which to bury, and he's never once been wrong.","desc":"He never raises his voice and never touches a weapon — just leans across the table and tells the boss, quietly, which men get forgiven and which ones get buried. He's never once been wrong, and everyone in the room hates that about him.","traits":{"note": "He's never once been wrong about who to forgive and who to bury, and everyone in the room hates that about him.", "actions": [{"name": "Calculated Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (4d6) Force damage — precisely the amount necessary, no more."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leans across a table telling the boss, quietly, which men get forgiven and which get buried."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reviews a plan for a hit he'll never personally carry out, correcting the timing by minutes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks a captain out of a war that would have cost the family everything."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps every promise the boss makes technically true, in ways nobody expected."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drafts the terms of a truce that favors the family in ways the other side won't notice for months."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started quietly steering the family away from its own worst instincts, at real risk to himself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know how a conversation ends before the first sentence is finished."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just advised the boss to bury someone the Consigliere privately believes should be forgiven, and means to fix that himself."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leaning across a table telling the boss, quietly, which men get forgiven and which get buried", "reviewing a plan for violence he'll never personally carry out"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"crime-family advisor/counselor archetype"},{"name":"the Torpedo Boss","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-deceiver","model":"bandit-deceiver","summary":"veteran hitman, disguises every kill","flavor":"Twenty years in the life and not one clean kill on his sheet — every hit gets dressed up as an accident, a robbery, a suicide. Craftsmanship.","desc":"Twenty years in the life and not one clean kill on his record, because every hit he's ever pulled came dressed up as an accident or a robbery or a man who just couldn't take it anymore. He calls it craftsmanship, and means it.","traits":{"note": "He's proud of his work in the specific way of a man who considers murder a discipline, not a sin.", "actions": [{"name": "Staged Accident", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 8 (1d4 + 6) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or believe, for a moment, that the wound was self-inflicted, granting the Torpedo Boss advantage on his next attack against it."}, {"name": "Blinding Flash", "replaces": "Blinding Flash (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature within 15 ft. of a point he can see must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or be Blinded until the end of its next turn — staged like a gas leak, timed like a curtain call."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Twenty years in and still dressing every hit up as an accident nobody questions."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stages a scene to look like a robbery gone wrong, right down to the missing wallet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Arranges a fall down stairs that leaves no mark he didn't intend."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks shop with a mortician he trusts, comparing notes on believable causes of death."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Practices a mark's handwriting for a suicide note weeks before the job."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started second-guessing whether craftsmanship this careful is really so different from cruelty."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every scene he stages is later remembered by witnesses exactly as he intended, down to the weather."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has been asked for a job so public no accident could explain it, and he's never had to say no before."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["twenty years in and still dressing every hit up as an accident nobody questions", "calling it craftsmanship, and meaning it, while arranging a scene to look like a robbery gone wrong"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"veteran hitman / made-man archetype"},{"name":"the Ghoul in the Icebox","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast-base","summary":"grave-risen enforcer kept on ice by the mob","flavor":"The meat-locker in the back of the butcher shop has a second tenant, and he doesn't stay cold. The mob uses him to make problems disappear — permanently, and personally.","desc":"The meat locker behind the butcher shop keeps a second tenant that doesn't need the cold, and doesn't offer it either — skin gone the gray of old frost, eyes open in the dark, waiting on whoever the family needs made to disappear tonight.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't need to be told who to take care of twice — it remembers every face that walked in.", "actions": [{"name": "Locker Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Meat Hook Claws", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits in the dark of the meat locker, skin gone the gray of old frost, eyes already open."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Emerges only after the shop closes, when the butcher makes himself scarce on purpose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has left claw marks on the inside of the locker door that the family pays extra to have painted over."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizes returning customers of the family by scent alone, long before they speak."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a second, smaller locker behind the first that nobody official admits exists."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started leaving a body arranged, deliberately, somewhere it'll be found — its own small rebellion."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The frost patterns on the locker walls rearrange themselves into a face by morning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The family finally sent someone it remembers from before it died, and the ice in the room drops fast."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waiting in the dark of a meat locker, skin gone the gray of old frost, eyes already open", "not offering the cold it no longer needs, just watching the door for whoever the family sends"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"gothic revenant tradition (generic grave-risen undead, pre-1929 folklore/literature — not a specific author's IP)"},{"name":"the Torch Singer's Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"murdered singer's ghost haunting her old club","flavor":"She sang the last set at the Blue Room the night they found her in the river. Now her voice still drifts through the club after closing, and the men who paid to have her silenced haven't slept right since.","desc":"Her voice still drifts through the Blue Room after closing, the same last set she sang the night they found her in the river, and the men who paid to have her quieted haven't slept right since they started hearing it again.","traits":{"note": "The men who paid to have her silenced haven't slept right since her voice started drifting through the club again.", "actions": [{"name": "The Last Set", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "That Voice Again", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can see her true form must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of her next turn, and creatures Frightened this way age one year, remembering how it felt to be told to keep quiet."}, {"name": "One Last Song", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save, taking 32 (7d8) Psychic damage on a failure, or half as much on a success — the note she never got to finish."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She sings until she recognizes a face in the club that was there the night she died."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's guarding a hidden recording of the last set she ever sang, proof of who paid to end it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the men who silenced her named aloud in the room where it happened."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She recognizes a party member's coat as one worn by a man who used to sit at her table."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's tied to the club itself and can't leave until someone finally tells her what happened to her body."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She wants one honest performance for a room that actually listens, not just one that fears her."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every night she sings a verse that didn't exist the night before, filling in what she never got to say."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The men who had her killed are in the club tonight, and she's decided the encore finally happens."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["drifting through the Blue Room after closing, singing the same last set she sang the night they found her", "lingering near the stage where the band packed up years ago, waiting for an encore that never comes"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"gothic revenant tradition — a wronged-woman haunting, drawn from settled 19th-century ghost-story convention, not any specific copyrighted work"},{"name":"the Assassin","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"mercenary killer with no fixed allegiance","flavor":"Doesn't work for the crime lord — works for whoever's currently paying the crime lord's rivals. Loyalty is a rate card.","desc":"He doesn't work for the crime lord — he works for whoever's currently paying to be rid of the crime lord's rivals, and switches sides as easily as he switches guns. Loyalty, for him, is just today's rate.","traits":{"note": "Loyalty, for him, is just today's rate — he'll take the next contract from whoever outbids the last one.", "actions": [{"name": "Whoever's Paying", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage, plus 7 (2d6) Piercing damage if the target hasn't acted yet this combat."}, {"name": "Rate Card", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Switches sides again for whoever's currently paying to be rid of the crime lord's rivals."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Takes a job against a former employer without a flicker of hesitation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Negotiates the rate up mid-contract when he learns who's really footing the bill."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cases a mark for days before ever drawing a weapon, patient as a debt collector."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Turns down a job only when the money's an insult, never on principle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has started quietly warning past targets who paid well enough, an inconsistent kind of mercy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to already know who'll outbid the current contract before the counteroffer's even made."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Two rival families just hired him for the same night, against each other, and he intends to collect from both."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["switching sides again for whoever's currently paying to be rid of the crime lord's rivals", "counting a fresh advance without checking whose money it actually is"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hard-boiled contract-killer stock type"},{"name":"Count Marlowe","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"rlm-noir-maestro","summary":"centuries-old crime lord, Dracula lineage reskinned","flavor":"Old money, older habits. He came from somewhere across the water a century ago and never quite stopped feeding — now he owns the docks, the judges, and most of the bodies nobody ever finds. He receives petitioners once a week, always after dark, always alone in the room with them.","desc":"He receives petitioners once a week in a study with the curtains drawn, always after dark, always alone with them in the room. Old money, older habits — he came from somewhere across the water a century ago and never quite stopped feeding, and now he owns the docks, the judges, and most of the bodies nobody ever finds.","traits":{"note": "PD Dracula-lineage recontextualization; noir crime-lord framing, not any studio's visual design.", "actions": [{"name": "Century's Patience", "text": "Immune to being rushed or provoked into a bad decision — advantage on saves against being frightened or goaded."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He calls in a debt the party inherited without ever signing for it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He receives the party as petitioners, curtains drawn, and expects them alone in the room with him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He already owns the judge the party needs to bribe or blackmail."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to erase a party member's debt to a rival, for a favor he won't name yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a body that nobody will ever find, and thinks the party owes him the errand."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown almost nostalgic for the old country and tells the party a story before naming the price."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His deeds to the docks are written in a hand that hasn't aged in a hundred years, unlike everything else in the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He decides tonight to stop feeding quietly, and the whole waterfront learns exactly how old his habits really are."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["receiving petitioners once a week behind drawn curtains, always after dark, always alone with them", "reviewing deeds to the docks and the judges by candlelight though the wiring works fine"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Bram Stoker, Dracula (1897, US public domain) — our own crime-lord recontextualization of the Dracula lineage, not any film studio's visual design"},{"name":"the Crime Lord's Bride","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"elder vampire consort, true power behind the throne","flavor":"Nobody knows if she runs the family or he does anymore — she's older than his human years put together and considerably less patient. The books say his name is on the deeds. The books are wrong.","desc":"Nobody in the family's quite sure anymore whether he runs things or she does — she's older than his human years put together, considerably less patient, and the deeds all say his name. The deeds are wrong.","traits":{"note": "PD Dracula-lineage vampire-bride motif; original noir power-behind-the-throne framing.", "actions": [{"name": "Older Blood", "text": "When an ally within 30 feet would be reduced to 0 HP, she may intervene to redirect the killing blow to herself once per long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She summons the party to correct an order her husband gave that she never approved."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers real power in the family, quietly, in exchange for removing a captain who's grown too loud."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding the actual deeds, unsigned by her husband, that prove who truly owns the family's assets."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's older than her husband's human years combined, and has run out of patience with a rival he refuses to handle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants a witness to a private ceremony that will make her claim on the family official at last."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's tired of ruling in whispers and considers letting the party be the ones who finally say it plainly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every document bearing her husband's signature quietly corrects itself to include hers as well."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided tonight the deeds get rewritten in truth, and the family will learn all at once whose name was always really on them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["correcting the family's real chain of command from behind a smile nobody in the room questions", "reviewing the deeds that say her husband's name, and are wrong"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the vampire-bride motif from the same novel, our own noir take, not a studio design"}],
 "ash":[{"name":"Rustfall Ghoul","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"commoner","summary":"radiation-mad wretch scavenging rubble on hunger reflex","flavor":"A radiation-mad scavenger, sun-blistered and skeletal, that picks through rubble on hunger reflex alone.","desc":"Sun-blistered skin stretches tight over a frame gone skeletal, and it moves through the rubble field in a low crouch, nose working the air. Fingers rake through broken brick without pause, without thought — just the reflex of a stomach that never learned to stop being empty. It looks up only when it hears you breathing.","traits":{"note": "Hunts by smell and sound more than sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Scavenger's Knife", "replaces": "Knife", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a scavenged rebreather that whistles with every breath it takes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors a rusted length of pipe over the knife, dragging it through the dust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing half its teeth; it gnaws instead of bites when cornered."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a stiff, arthritic shuffle from bones that never healed right."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hoards bottle caps in its pockets, clinking with every lurching step."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its skin has gone the color and texture of old newspaper, flaking with each motion."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mutters ration numbers under its breath, a routine from a life it can't remember living."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its blistered scalp has split open, and something faintly luminous pulses beneath the bone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Digs through collapsed brick with bare fingers, nose working the air", "Freezes mid-scavenge, tracking the sound of breathing nearby"]},{"name":"Scrap-Hound","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"mutant feral dog pack hunting the broken highway","flavor":"A feral dog gone patchy and mean, hide crusted with fallout-scald, running loose packs down the cracked highway lines.","desc":"A patchy shape lopes along the shoulder of the cracked highway, hide crusted white where the fallout got into old wounds. It never travels alone; two more shapes drift out of the heat-shimmer behind it, jaws already loose and panting. The pack fans wide before anyone gives the order.","traits":{"note": "Never hunts alone; more join from cover once blood is drawn.", "actions": [{"name": "Scald-Crusted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs with a limp that never seems to slow it down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing one ear, scarred from an old pack squabble over meat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bark comes out broken, half growl and half wet cough."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a length of chain still clipped to a rusted collar."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles wide before closing, herding rather than charging straight in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Patchy hide has gone bald in rings, scald-white skin showing through."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Howls in unison with the others on a fixed, unnatural rhythm, like a signal."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Eyes have clouded milk-white, yet it tracks prey it should never be able to see."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Lopes along a cracked highway shoulder, hide crusted white with old fallout-scald", "Fans out wide with the pack, jaws loose, testing the wind for meat"]},{"name":"Rat-King's Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"boiling mutant rat carpet nesting in dead-town pipes","flavor":"A boiling carpet of mutated rats nesting in a dead town's substructure, teeth filed sharp on rebar and bone.","desc":"The pipe beneath the dead town gurgles and then erupts — a boiling carpet of fur and teeth pouring out of the drain grate all at once. Individually they're nothing, but the mass moves like a single wet animal, climbing over itself to reach bare skin. The stink of the nest follows it into the open air.","traits":{"note": "Moves and fights as one mass rather than individual bodies.", "actions": [{"name": "Boiling Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature in the swarm's space. Hit: 5 (2d4) piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests behind a collapsed water main, the stink of it carrying for blocks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters at loud noise, then reforms into a single mass minutes later."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Some of the rats drag scraps of wire back into the nest as they retreat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur mottled in patches, bald skin showing raw pink beneath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves as a wave up a wall before dropping onto whatever's below."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A faint clicking sound rises from the mass, teeth grinding against teeth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The swarm parts and reforms around obstacles with eerie, coordinated precision."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "At its densest core, a few rats glow faintly green, hairless and swollen wrong."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "cave"],"activity":["Pours out of a drain grate all at once, climbing over itself toward warm skin", "Boils through the dead town's substructure, teeth filed sharp on rebar"]},{"name":"Warband Ganger","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"spiked-jacket raider grunt running a warband's front line","flavor":"Foot-soldier of a raider crew, spikes welded to a salvage jacket, running on stolen fuel and borrowed nerve.","desc":"Spikes welded crooked into a salvage jacket catch what little light makes it through the ash haze. He walks like the front line is where he's always stood, chin up, borrowed nerve doing the work adrenaline should. Somewhere behind him a truck horn blares twice — the signal that means don't run yet.","traits":{"note": "Falls back in good order once the horn sounds twice.", "actions": [{"name": "Salvage Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Pipe-Bore Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8+1) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a scavenged locket he won't let anyone touch, tucked under the jacket."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owes the warband three runs' worth of fuel debt and is desperate to clear it here."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nursing a crossbow-bolt wound from the last raid, favoring one side badly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the truck horn himself, meant to signal the retreat if things go wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a captive's ration card stuffed in his pocket, meant for someone waiting behind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps glancing back toward the convoy, more worried about it than the fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mutters a countdown under his breath that matches no clock anyone else can hear."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Carries a live grenade rigged wrong, and he knows it, and he's still here anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Stands the front line chin-up, borrowed nerve doing the work adrenaline should", "Waits on a truck horn signal, scimitar loose in its scabbard"]},{"name":"Bomb-Cult Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist","summary":"ordnance-strapped zealot singing the mushroom-cloud hymn","flavor":"A wide-eyed devotee of the old mushroom-cloud gospel, strapped with scavenged ordnance and singing the countdown hymn.","desc":"Ordnance hangs off a makeshift harness in a way that should not be structurally reassuring, and the zealot's eyes have the flat shine of someone who has already made peace with the ending. A cracked, tuneless hymn rises from behind a rebreather mask, counting down in a language only the cult still speaks. Every word is sincere.","traits":{"note": "Fights with the calm of someone who has already made peace with dying.", "actions": [{"name": "Blessed Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8+1) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Countdown Casting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The zealot casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: sacred flame, minor illusion. 1/day each: hold person, spiritual weapon."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a satchel charge meant for a target three towns over, not this fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was sent to recruit, not kill, and hesitates before the first blow lands."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a countdown scrawled on bandaged forearms, days ticking toward some date."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Protects a smaller cultist half his age, shielding the kid without being asked."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a cult relic he's been ordered to detonate rather than let it be taken."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps time with the hymn even mid-combat, never breaking the tune."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Believes the fight itself is scripture, narrating the blows like verses."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The ordnance harness has already started ticking, and he's smiling about it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["Sings a cracked countdown hymn from behind a rebreather mask", "Checks the harness straps on scavenged ordnance, eyes flat and certain"]},{"name":"Geiger Wretch","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie","summary":"glowing irradiated corpse that never stopped ticking","flavor":"A corpse that never stopped ticking — its wounds glow faint green, and the count climbs the longer you stand near it.","desc":"Its wounds glow the faint sick green of old dial paint, brighter wherever the flesh has torn deepest. It doesn't hiss or moan so much as tick — a dry, rhythmic click somewhere in its ruined throat that speeds up the closer it gets. Stand near it long enough and you start to hear your own pulse answering back.","traits":{"note": "Its proximity alone raises a counter's reading before it ever attacks.", "actions": [{"name": "Hot Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) radiant damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Glows brightest at old wound sites, a green map of how it died."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ticks in short bursts rather than a steady rhythm, unpredictable to time against."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint luminous residue on anything it drags itself across."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than most corpses its age, joints fused stiff with scar tissue."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a tattered ID badge, name long since bleached unreadable."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its ticking speeds to a near-continuous whine when it senses fresh meat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ticking seems to sync with nearby electronics, glitching them faintly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cracks in its chest glow like a coal about to catch, brighter with each hit it takes."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Ticks louder the closer it drifts, a dry rhythmic click in its ruined throat", "Drags itself toward the nearest heartbeat it can sense through the dark"]},{"name":"Blistered Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"hairless mutant hound drawn to a running engine","flavor":"A hairless mutant hound, skin cracked like the asphalt it hunts on, drawn to the sound of a working engine.","desc":"Hairless and cracked like old asphalt, it lies flattened against the roadside until an engine turns over somewhere close. Then it's up, ears pricked toward the sound, tracking the vibration through the ground itself rather than any scent. Silence makes it lose interest fast; noise makes it patient.","traits":{"note": "Loses interest fast in silence but grows patient once it hears noise.", "actions": [{"name": "Cracked-Hide Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin split at the joints shows raw asphalt-black beneath the cracks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stalks vehicles specifically, ignoring foot traffic entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pair, taking turns feinting toward the engine noise."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes still as stone for hours at a stretch, near-invisible against the road."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a habit of biting tires before it ever goes for a person."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its cracked hide weeps a thin oily fluid when it overheats from the chase."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Responds to engine pitch specifically, ignoring idling trucks entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A vestigial third eye under the jaw seems to track sound as much as sight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Lies flattened against the roadside, ears pricked for an engine turning over", "Tracks a running engine's vibration through the ground, patient and silent"]},{"name":"Chem-Huffer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"stim-shaking raider swinging a pipe with pure rage","flavor":"A raider hopped up on scavenged stimulant canisters, shakes and swings a length of pipe with more rage than sense.","desc":"He shakes constantly, a fine tremor that runs up through the pipe clutched in both hands, empty stim canisters rattling loose at his belt. There's no strategy in how he swings — just momentum, rage, and whatever chemical is currently telling his nervous system that pain is somebody else's problem. He laughs when the pipe connects.","traits":{"note": "Feels no pain until the chemicals wear off all at once.", "actions": [{"name": "Stim-Rage Pipe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d12+2) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has one canister left, unused, hidden in a boot for the comedown after."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was sent ahead by a bigger crew to soften up whoever's found first."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fighting off a debt collector who'll show up regardless of how this ends."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't remember why he's swinging, only that someone told him to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a child's drawing folded in his pocket, from before the huffing started."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The tremor gets worse mid-fight, pipe strikes going wilder as it does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Laughs on every hit he takes, not just the ones he lands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His pupils have blown fully black, and the shaking has stopped entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Shakes with a fine tremor, empty stim canisters rattling loose at his belt", "Swings a length of pipe with more rage than aim, laughing when it connects"]},{"name":"Cracked Sentry-Bot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"animated-armor","summary":"dying pre-Fall security drone patrolling a dead route","flavor":"A pre-Fall security drone running on a dying battery, patrolling a route that hasn't mattered in a generation.","desc":"Its chassis drags one leg a half-beat behind the other, servos grinding out a route it has patrolled since before the ash started falling. The dying battery pack whines audibly under its scarecrow-thin frame, and its sensor head swivels on a schedule nobody wrote anymore. It still salutes checkpoints that no longer exist.","traits":{"note": "Its dying battery limits how long it can sustain a fight before shutting down.", "actions": [{"name": "Rust-Seized Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d10+2) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Failing Threat-Display", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The drone's sensor-head flares red and blares a corrupted alarm-klaxon at one creature it can see within 30 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chassis panel hangs loose, exposing wiring that sparks with every step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats a garbled security phrase on loop, half the words lost to static."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still carries a holstered stun-baton it never draws, protocol long corrupted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols in perfect right angles, unable to deviate from its original route."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One optic sensor is dark, forcing it to overcompensate by scanning constantly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its battery whine rises to a shriek right before it powers down mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally addresses passersby by rank designations that no longer mean anything."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A cracked core panel leaks faint blue light, and its movements have started to loop-glitch."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Drags one leg a half-beat behind the other, patrolling a route nobody wrote anymore", "Salutes a checkpoint that hasn't existed in a generation, sensor head swiveling on schedule"]},{"name":"Fuel-Cult Firestarter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-captain","model":"knight","summary":"promethium-doused cult officer preaching detonation as sacrament","flavor":"An officer of the bomb-cult warband, doused in promethium and preaching detonation as sacrament to the ranks behind him.","desc":"Promethium sheens wet and iridescent down his coat, and he holds his voice pitched for a congregation even when the only audience is the raiders flanking him. Every sentence ends like a sermon, building toward a detonation he clearly can't wait to deliver. The men behind him have heard this one before and still lean in.","traits":{"note": "The men around him rally hard whenever he raises his voice to a sermon.", "actions": [{"name": "Sacrament Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Promethium Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) fire damage."}, {"name": "Sermon of the Coming Fire", "replaces": "Leadership (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)", "text": "For 1 minute, the firestarter can utter a special command or warning whenever a nonhostile creature that he can see within 30 feet of him makes an attack roll or a saving throw. The creature can add a d4 to its roll provided it can hear and understand him. A creature can benefit from only one Leadership die at a time. This effect ends if the firestarter is incapacitated."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the cult's master fuse, meant to trigger a much bigger charge elsewhere."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a lieutenant he's grooming to take the sermon over if he falls here."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is stalling for time, buying his cult's convoy minutes to clear the blast radius."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a countdown timer strapped visibly to his chest, already running."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a captive scribe nearby, transcribing every word of the sermon as gospel."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His coat drips promethium onto the ground, leaving a flammable trail behind him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Speaks every sentence like it's already been prophesied to happen exactly this way."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Promethium has started seeping from under his fingernails, and he seems thrilled about it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["Preaches detonation as sacrament, promethium sheening wet down his coat", "Pitches his voice for a congregation even with just raiders flanking him"]},{"name":"Mutant Behemoth Hog","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-boar","model":"giant-boar","summary":"fallout-swollen boar that charges convoys tusks-first","flavor":"A boar swollen wrong by fallout, tusks like rebar, that charges convoys for the meat and the noise.","desc":"It comes in low and wrong-shaped, tusks grown out long and crooked like rebar torn from a foundation. The convoy trucks rattle their windows just from the sound of its charge before it's even visible through the dust. It doesn't stop for cover — it goes through it.","traits":{"note": "Doesn't stop for cover; it simply goes through whatever's in the way.", "actions": [{"name": "Rebar Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) piercing damage. If the boar moved at least 20 feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 4 (1d8) piercing damage and must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a nest of piglets that scatter squealing at the first sign of a fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One tusk snapped and regrown crooked, throwing off its usual charge line."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred flanks show old rifle grazes it shrugged off without slowing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wallows in irradiated mud pits, hide crusted gray when it emerges."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges specifically at engine noise, ignoring quieter targets nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Steam rises visibly off its hide when its blood gets up before a charge."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its squeal carries an odd double-tone, like two throats working at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A tumor-like growth along its spine pulses faintly in time with its heartbeat."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["hill", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Charges in low and wrong-shaped, rebar-crooked tusks leading the way", "Rattles convoy windows with the sound of its charge before it's even visible"]},{"name":"Irradiated Ghast","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"faster hungrier ghoul cooked past rot by fallout","flavor":"A ghoul cooked past rot into something faster and hungrier, skin sloughing, glowing faintly under the ash-clouds.","desc":"Skin sloughs wetly off a frame that moves far too fast for something so clearly rotten, and a faint green light pulses under what's left of the flesh with each labored breath. The stench arrives half a second before it does. Where a ghoul shuffles, this thing sprints, cooked past decay into something hungrier.","traits":{"note": "The stench of it arrives half a second before it does.", "actions": [{"name": "Hungry Feed", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken, and the ghast regains hit points equal to that amount. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Salvage Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Scavenged Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the tattered remains of a hazard suit, hood flapping loose."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw hangs unhinged, sloughed skin catching on exposed teeth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short violent bursts rather than a sustained sprint."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of luminous drip marking exactly where it passed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors dark ruins, flinching visibly when caught in direct light."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The green pulse under its skin brightens noticeably right before it lunges."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally stops mid-chase to stare at its own glowing hands, confused."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sheds sloughed flesh in wet chunks that keep twitching after they hit the ground."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Sprints where a ghoul would shuffle, cooked past decay into something hungrier", "Sloughs wet skin as it moves, a faint green pulse under the ruin of its flesh"]},{"name":"Warband Enforcer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"raider muscle enforcing the warband's chain of debt","flavor":"Muscle for a raider crew's chain of command, a scrap-plate riot shield in one hand and a debt ledger in the other.","desc":"A scrap-plate riot shield rides on one forearm, a battered ledger of debts tucked under the other — he collects both with equal patience. His voice stays level even as he closes distance, reciting names and numbers like a foreman going down a work order. The violence, when it comes, is procedural.","traits":{"note": "Treats violence as bookkeeping, unhurried and procedural.", "actions": [{"name": "Debt-Collector's Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d6+5) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ledger's Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (1d8+5) slashing damage, or 10 (1d10+5) slashing damage if used with two hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a name in his ledger matching someone in the current party."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is collecting on a debt that was actually paid off, and the records are wrong."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a hostage's ration card as proof of an unpaid debt still owed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is due back at the warband camp by dusk or gets marked as a defector himself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of every fight he's lost, determined not to add to it here."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses between blows to jot something in the ledger, unbothered by the fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refers to his shield and sword by names, like old debt-collecting partners."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The ledger's final page lists a debt with no name on it, only a date: today."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Recites names and debts from a battered ledger like a foreman's work order", "Closes distance behind a scrap-plate riot shield, voice level and unhurried"]},{"name":"Chitin-Plated Feral","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wereboar","model":"wereboar","summary":"half-beast mutant grown a cracked chitin hide","flavor":"A mutant gone half-beast under the ash-fall moon, hide grown over in cracked insect plate, tusks and claws both.","desc":"Under the ash-fall moon its hide has grown a cracked insect plate over what was once mostly human, tusks and claws both jutting from the same ruined jaw. It moves in fits — half-lope, half-scuttle — like the body hasn't fully decided what shape it's committing to. Whatever's left of the mind inside has stopped fighting it.","traits":{"note": "Whatever mind remains inside has stopped fighting the change.", "actions": [{"name": "Chitin Gore", "replaces": "Gore (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scavenged Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cracked-Plate Tusk", "replaces": "Tusk (Boar or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d4+4) slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chitin plates are still soft in patches, oozing where the shell hasn't finished setting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the shredded remains of clothes it hasn't fully outgrown yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snaps between forms mid-stride, staggering when the shift catches it off balance."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chitin plates click audibly against each other with every labored breath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retains a fragment of memory, flinching at sounds that resemble its old name."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its jaw has fused mid-shift, locking tusk and teeth into one ragged edge."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Molts flakes of chitin that keep twitching, faintly, long after they fall."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Under full moonlight its plating hardens visibly, growing thicker as the fight goes on."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Half-lopes, half-scuttles, hide grown over in cracked insect plate under the ash-fall moon", "Snaps between tusk and claw as its body decides what shape to commit to"]},{"name":"Power-Rig Brute","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"raider bolted into a scavenged hydraulic exo-rig","flavor":"A raider bolted into a scavenged hydraulic exo-rig, twice the size he was born, hitting like a demolition crew.","desc":"Hydraulic struts hiss and whine at the joints of a scavenged exo-rig bolted straight through muscle and bone, doubling a man's frame into something built for demolition work. Every step lands with a metallic thud that rattles loose scrap off nearby wreckage. He swings like the machine is doing the thinking now.","traits":{"note": "Swings like the exo-rig is doing the thinking rather than the man inside it.", "actions": [{"name": "Hydraulic Club", "replaces": "Tree Club", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 20 (3d10+4) bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Scrap-Heap Lob", "replaces": "Trash Lob", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (3d8+3) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rig's power cell is running low, sparking visibly at the shoulder joint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was bolted into the rig against his will and can't get free of it alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a keycard to the warband's fuel depot, welded into a rig pocket."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a convoy route personally, under orders not to leave his post."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a mechanic waiting nearby who can shut the rig down from a remote switch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hydraulic fluid leaks steadily from a cracked strut, worsening as the fight drags on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the rig itself between swings, like it argues back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The rig's joints have started overtorquing, throwing sparks that could ignite nearby fuel."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Hisses and whines at hydraulic joints bolted straight through muscle and bone", "Rattles scrap loose off nearby wreckage with every metallic thudding step"]},{"name":"Diesel Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"patchwork engine-block war-machine lurching on stolen fuel","flavor":"A patchwork war-machine stitched from engine blocks and rebar, lurching forward on hissing pistons and stolen fuel.","desc":"Engine blocks and rebar make up its torso, welded in overlapping layers that still weep old oil down the seams. It lurches forward on pistons that hiss with every stride, stolen fuel lines feeding whatever passes for its heart. The smell of exhaust announces it before the grinding footsteps do.","traits":{"note": "The smell of exhaust gives it away long before it's in sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Engine-Block Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (2d10+5) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One piston fires late, giving its stride an off-beat stutter-step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weld seams have cracked wide enough to see the gears turning underneath."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a slick of oil that makes the ground treacherous behind it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built from a fuel truck's chassis, still bearing the faded company logo."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs hotter than most, radiating enough heat to warp the air around it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its hiss rises to a screech whenever it takes a solid hit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A dashboard radio welded into its chest crackles with dead static, endlessly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fuel lines have started to leak near an exposed spark, and it hasn't noticed yet."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Lurches forward on hissing pistons, stolen fuel lines feeding whatever passes for its heart", "Weeps old oil down welded seams, exhaust announcing it before its footsteps do"]},{"name":"Last-Light Keeper","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"settlement champion fighting to keep the generator alive","flavor":"A settlement's champion, armored in scavenged plate, fighting arena bouts to keep the generator's lights burning one more night.","desc":"Scavenged plate, dented from a hundred prior bouts, hangs off broad shoulders as the arena's champion strides out to another round he can't afford to lose. Behind the settlement's crumbling wall, a generator hums — his prize purse and the whole town's light both riding on tonight's fight. He fights like he knows it.","traits":{"note": "Fights like he knows the whole town's light rides on tonight's bout.", "actions": [{"name": "Champion's Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (1d6+6) piercing damage, or 10 (1d8+6) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."}, {"name": "Generator's Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d6+5) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet away and knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights this bout to buy the settlement's generator crew one more day of fuel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rival champion's broken blade as a trophy and a warning."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a sibling in the crowd whose safety depends on him winning outright."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is nursing an old wound the arena's medic patched wrong last bout."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owes his win purse to a debt collector waiting just past the arena gate."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Times his strikes to the generator's hum, like he's fighting to its rhythm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refuses to yield even past the point the crowd starts calling for it to end."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The generator behind the wall sputters mid-fight, and the whole arena goes half-dark."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["Strides into another arena round in dented scavenged plate, unable to afford losing", "Listens to the settlement generator hum behind the wall, fighting to keep it running"]},{"name":"Fallout Stalker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"winter-wolf","summary":"silent radiation-zone apex hunter","flavor":"Pale, hairless, and silent — it hunts by the geiger-tick of its prey's gear and drags kills back into the slag caves to glow.","desc":"Pale as bone and utterly silent, it tracks not by scent or sight but by the geiger-tick of whatever gear its prey is carrying. It drags what it kills back toward the slag caves, leaving a faint luminous smear across the rock. You rarely see it before you hear the counter in your pocket start climbing.","traits":{"note": "You rarely hear it before the counter in your pocket starts climbing.", "actions": [{"name": "Silent Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Slag Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Cold Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The stalker exhales a cone of irradiated slag-dust in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a DC 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a faint luminous smear wherever it drags a fresh kill."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin has gone entirely translucent in patches, veins visible and dark."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves without a single audible footfall even across loose scree."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to circle a target twice before ever committing to the strike."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids anything not carrying detectable gear, ignoring the unarmed entirely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A faint clicking answers back whenever a geiger counter nears it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes have no visible pupils, just a flat reflective sheen like old glass."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The slag caves it nests in have started glowing at the mouth, brighter each week."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["mountain", "cave", "any"],"activity":["Tracks by the geiger-tick of a prey's gear rather than scent or sight", "Drags a kill back toward the slag caves, leaving a luminous smear on the rock"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: apex predator adapted to hot-zone terrain"},{"name":"Convoy Warlord","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"road-baron ruling a raider convoy by ambush and fear","flavor":"A road-baron who rules a war-rig fleet by ambush and fear, trading fuel and captives up and down the ruin-highways.","desc":"He rules the ruin-highways from the deck of a lead war-rig, binoculars in one hand and a flare gun in the other, timing every ambush like a man who's done this a thousand times. Fuel drums and chained captives ride behind him in equal measure — both currency, both leverage. His convoy doesn't negotiate; it collects.","traits":{"note": "His convoy treats both fuel and captives as leverage, never as mercy.", "actions": [{"name": "Boarding Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Flare Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) fire damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Holds three captives in the rig's hold, bargaining chips he won't spend cheaply."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already radioed a second rig, minutes out, to close the ambush shut."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the convoy's entire fuel manifest, worth more than the man himself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is testing a new lieutenant's nerve by letting him call this fight's terms."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rules through fear built on a reputation he can't actually back up anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps his flare gun ready to signal retreat the instant the fight turns."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Narrates the ambush aloud as it unfolds, like he's grading his own crew."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has rigged his own rig's fuel tank to detonate rather than let it be captured."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Rules the ruin-highways from a lead war-rig, binoculars in one hand and a flare gun in the other", "Times an ambush like a man who's run this exact play a thousand times"]},{"name":"Vault Revenant","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"wight-lord","summary":"ageless bunker-dweller returned furious the seal broke","flavor":"A bunker's last resident, sealed in decades past and returned changed — pale, ageless, and furious the door ever opened.","desc":"Decades of sealed darkness left this thing pale as paper and ageless in a way that reads as deeply wrong under open sky. It emerged the moment the vault door finally gave, and the fury of that betrayal hasn't cooled since. It speaks in the clipped, formal cadence of someone who still thinks the world outside owes it an explanation.","traits":{"note": "Retains memory of pre-Fall protocols; may recognize old vault-tech or codes on sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Sealed Fury", "text": "Once per encounter, when first exposed to open sky or sunlight, the revenant gains advantage on its next attack roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still carries the vault's master key, useless now that the door's been blown."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Believes the world outside is still mid-catastrophe and reacts accordingly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Demands formal surrender terms before it will acknowledge any fight has started."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a vault manifest listing names of the dead it still thinks are alive."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries decades-old rationing scrip it tries to spend as though it's still valid."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recoils visibly from open sky, flinching at light it hasn't seen in decades."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Addresses attackers by vault-resident designations, mistaking them for old neighbors."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its fury spikes whenever the word 'outside' is spoken aloud near it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands", "any"],"activity":["Speaks in the clipped, formal cadence of someone the world still owes an explanation", "Stalks the wreckage of the vault door it waited decades behind"]},{"name":"Apex Ferox","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"ash-pelted apex predator that hunts raiders for sport","flavor":"The wasteland's top predator, white-ash pelted and man-tall at the shoulder, that has learned raiders are easy prey.","desc":"White-ash fur bristles man-tall at the shoulder as it circles wide, unhurried, reading the group the way a wolf reads a herd for the slow one. It has learned that raiders panic predictably, and it plans around that. Nothing about its patience says desperate — this is a predator eating well.","traits":{"note": "Prefers to isolate and pick off stragglers before committing to the group.", "actions": [{"name": "Ambush Instinct", "text": "If it can approach unseen, its first attack in combat scores an automatic critical hit."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the scars of a hundred raider ambushes and has outlasted every one of them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to isolate the slowest of a group before ever showing itself fully."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks its territory with the bones of past convoys, arranged with unsettling care."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ash-white pelt turns near-invisible against fallout-bleached terrain."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Toys with wounded prey, letting them run before closing the distance again."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its breath fogs the air with fine ash even when it isn't attacking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to recognize specific raider warband markings, hunting them preferentially."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wasteland settlements swap its kill-count like a grim scoreboard nobody wants to top."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["mountain", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Circles wide and unhurried, reading the group the way a wolf reads a herd for the slow one", "Bristles white-ash fur man-tall at the shoulder, patient and well-fed"]},{"name":"War-Rig Juggernaut","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"warlord's mobile fortress rolling on a dozen dead trucks","flavor":"A warlord's mobile fortress, welded from a dozen dead trucks, that rolls down the highway spitting fire from every hatch.","desc":"A dozen dead trucks were welded into one rolling fortress, hatches bristling with barrel-ends that track independently of the wheels grinding beneath them. It doesn't so much drive down the highway as claim it, throwing sparks and spent shells in its wake. The warlord who built it rides somewhere inside, untouchable.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple hatch-mounted weapons can each act independently in a round.", "actions": [{"name": "Broadside", "text": "Fires from every hatch at once, targeting up to three separate creatures in range."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The warlord commanding it from inside is broadcasting terms over an external speaker."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a captured settlement's water tanker chained behind it as cargo."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hatch cannon jams mid-fight, and a crew member has to climb out to clear it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the warlord's entire war-chest welded into an armored compartment."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is escorted by a scout bike relaying its position back to a larger warband."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The welded trucks groan audibly under their own combined weight as it turns."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Plays looted pre-Fall broadcast recordings over external speakers as it rolls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its fuel reserves are rigged to detonate the whole rig if the warlord inside is threatened."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Claims the highway rather than merely driving it, throwing sparks and spent shells", "Tracks targets independently from every hatch while its wheels keep grinding forward"]},{"name":"The Long Count","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"wight-lord","summary":"dead soldier still counting down a mission long over","flavor":"A dead soldier still running the last order he was given, counting down a mission that ended with the world.","desc":"It still moves with drilled military precision, counting under its breath in a clipped cadence that never varies — a countdown to an operation that ended with the world. Its uniform has long since rotted to threads, but the discipline hasn't slipped once. It will finish the mission it was given, whatever that costs anyone standing near the target.","traits":{"note": "Fixated on a specific 'objective' — often reacts differently to whoever it perceives as matching that role.", "actions": [{"name": "Final Orders", "text": "Can direct nearby lesser undead as if issuing a chain of command, granting them a bonus action to act on its initiative."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a mission dossier, faded and unreadable, but still consults it before acting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mistakes the current fight for the exact operation it was given decades ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its countdown is nearing zero, and something is meant to happen when it hits."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rusted radio, still transmitting a coordinate that no longer exists."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows chain-of-command reflexes, deferring instantly to anyone giving confident orders."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its counting grows faster and sharper the closer combat gets to its climax."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Salutes its own killer the instant it's finally destroyed, mission complete at last."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The count it's running matches, exactly, the number of turns left before something detonates nearby."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Counts under its breath in a clipped cadence, running an order that ended with the world", "Moves with drilled precision, uniform rotted to threads but discipline unbroken"]},{"name":"The Last Warlord","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"archmage","summary":"raider-general who unified the wasteland under one law","flavor":"The wasteland's uncrowned king, a raider-general who unified a hundred warbands under one banner and one law: take everything.","desc":"He built his throne from a hundred surrendered banners and holds court from the cab of a truck too heavy to move without an escort. His voice carries across a battlefield without ever needing to shout — every warband here answers to him first, their own commanders second. He has one law, and he states it plainly: take everything.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Commands loyalty from any ash-realm humanoid raiders present as reinforcements.", "actions": [{"name": "One Law", "text": "Once per turn, can order an ally within sight to make an immediate attack as a reaction."}, {"name": "Take Everything", "text": "On a killing blow, immediately regains a portion of maximum hit points, fueled by the kill."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hundred warbands watch this fight by relay radio, ready to break loyalty if he falls."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a rival warlord's skull mounted on his truck as a standing threat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already promised this territory to a lieutenant, contingent on this fight's outcome."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the unified banner's original charter, the one law written in his own hand."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is testing a challenger personally rather than sending warband muscle to do it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His truck's engine idles behind him the entire fight, ready for an instant retreat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Repeats his one law like scripture even when no one's left standing to hear it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every warband on the ash-flats has sworn that if he dies, the truce dies with him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Holds court from the cab of a truck too heavy to move without an escort", "States his one law plainly to a hundred banners answering to him first"]},{"name":"The Half-Life","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"gargantuan hot-zone leviathan that surfaces when ground glows","flavor":"A leviathan born from the deepest hot-zone, burrowing under the ash-flats and surfacing only when the ground starts to glow.","desc":"The ground doesn't crack so much as peel back, glowing at the edges, as something gargantuan surfaces from beneath the ash-flats. Its hide sheds a heat-shimmer you can feel from thirty yards off, and geiger counters within earshot simply stop reading numbers and start screaming. It only comes up when the ground itself starts to glow — which means it's already been feeding.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Radiant/necrotic-adjacent aura; anything standing too close for too long should suffer escalating exposure.", "actions": [{"name": "Hot Zone", "text": "Creatures within 30 feet take ongoing radiation damage each round they remain in range."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its burrow trail runs straight beneath a settlement that hasn't noticed yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A caravan's missing scouts are almost certainly already inside it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaced early, off its normal cycle, meaning something below disturbed it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Left a glowing furrow leading straight back to whatever fed it last."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hot-zone prospecting crew is tracking it for the glow-ore it leaves behind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its hide sheds heat-shimmer thick enough to bend light around its whole length."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ground continues glowing faintly for hours after it dives back under."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Old wasteland maps mark its known feeding grounds simply as 'don't.'"}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["deeplands", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Surfaces from beneath the ash-flats when the ground itself starts to glow", "Sheds a heat-shimmer felt from thirty yards, geiger counters screaming past readable numbers"]},{"name":"Cinder Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Radiation-swollen scavenger rat gnawing wire for copper","flavor":"A radiation-swollen rat that scavenges the blast rings, chewing wire for the copper.","desc":"Radiation swelling has doubled it past any healthy rat's size, and it works at a stripped wire with the single-minded patience of something that has learned copper tastes better than anything else left in the ruins. It doesn't flee so much as scurry sideways, always toward the next wall socket.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Copper-Hunter Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 1 piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swollen twice past a healthy rat's size, waddling more than scurrying."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tail has fused into a stiff, wire-like appendage from years near live current."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests inside a wall socket cluster, dragging copper scraps home one strand at a time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chatters its teeth rhythmically against exposed wire, a habit more than a hunt."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bald patches show radiation-pink skin along its swollen flank."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sparks faintly against its own whiskers whenever it touches live wire."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems drawn to functioning electronics specifically, ignoring dead ones entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its swollen belly glows faintly when it's gorged on copper for too long."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Chews at a stripped wire with single-minded patience, chasing the taste of copper", "Scurries sideways toward the nearest wall socket instead of fleeing outright"]},{"name":"Slag Crow","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"vulture","model":"vulture","summary":"Glass-feathered scavenger bird circling collapse sites","flavor":"Feathers fused with melted glass; it circles collapse sites waiting for the dust to settle.","desc":"Its feathers have fused here and there with beads of melted glass, clicking faintly when it shifts on a girder. It circles high over any collapse site, patient in a way that unsettles more than a vulture should, waiting for the dust and the screaming both to settle.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Glass-Fused Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 1 slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One wing catches the light oddly, a wide bead of fused glass along the leading edge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Croaks in short clipped bursts that carry unnaturally far over rubble."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Perches only on exposed rebar, never on wood or stone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Travels in a loose trio, always circling the same collapse from different angles."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers click faintly with each wingbeat, a sound like wind chimes breaking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Glass beads along its feathers throw small refracted glints across the rubble below."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know exactly how long to wait before a collapse site is safe to land on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its eyes have gone glassy and reflective, mirroring back whatever looks up at it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "sky"],"activity":["Circles high over a collapse site, waiting for the dust and the screaming to settle", "Clicks softly when it shifts on a girder, feathers fused here and there with melted glass"]},{"name":"Barrens Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"hyena","model":"barrens-jackal","summary":"Pack scavenger trailing raiders for the leftovers","flavor":"Runs in loose packs behind warbands, cleaning up whatever the raiders leave behind.","desc":"It trails a raider column at a careful, practiced distance, never quite in rifle range, never quite out of sight either. When the warband moves on, it and the rest of the pack come in low to clean up whatever got left behind — clothes, meat, anything soft enough to carry.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Scavenger's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 3 (1d6) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs with a distinctive limp from an old warband gunshot wound."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cackles in a broken, wheezing register that carries far across open ground."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always the last of the pack to break cover, watching before committing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears mange in patches that expose scarred, sun-blistered skin beneath."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows a specific warband's convoy route with unsettling, learned precision."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its howl mimics the pitch of a truck horn closely enough to cause confusion."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems able to tell a corpse's cause of death by smell alone before approaching."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its eyes catch light in a flat green shimmer, unlike any healthy jackal's should."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Trails a raider column at a careful distance, never quite in rifle range", "Comes in low with the pack once the warband moves on, cleaning up what's left"]},{"name":"Fallout Toad","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-toad","model":"fallout-toad","summary":"Chem-bloated toad whose croak curdles nearby water","flavor":"Bloated on chem runoff, its croak alone curdles unprotected water.","desc":"Bloated well past any natural size on chem-runoff sludge, it sits half-submerged in a puddle that shouldn't sustain anything living. Its croak alone is enough to curdle whatever's left of the water nearby, a thick wet sound that carries further than it should across open ground.","traits":{"note": "Its croak alone is enough to curdle unprotected standing water nearby.", "actions": [{"name": "Sludge Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Chem Swallow", "replaces": "Swallow", "text": "The toad makes one bite attack against a Small or smaller target it is grappling. If the attack hits, the target is also swallowed, and the grapple ends. A swallowed creature takes 5 (1d10) acid damage at the start of each of the toad's turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin has gone a sickly translucent green, veins visible through the bloat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits motionless for hours, indistinguishable from a chem-sludge boulder."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its croak leaves a faint metallic taste in the air for several seconds after."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a slick of curdled water wherever it drags itself between puddles."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tongue lashes out wet and sludge-colored, tipped faintly luminous at the end."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its throat sac inflates visibly bright before each croak, like a warning light."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Local puddles near its nest never quite freeze or evaporate normally."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its bloated belly sloshes audibly, and something under the surface occasionally moves wrong."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Sits half-submerged in chem-runoff sludge, bloated well past any natural size", "Croaks a thick wet sound that carries further than it should across open ground"]},{"name":"Wasteland Scrapper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"wasteland-scrapper","summary":"Warband lookout with a jury-rigged pipe rifle","flavor":"A lookout for a warband, armed with a pipe rifle and a claim to the ruins ahead.","desc":"He crouches on a ridge of rubble with a pipe rifle balanced across one knee, watching the approach with the bored patience of someone paid by the hour to notice things. A whistle, two notes, low — that's the only warning the ruins ahead are already claimed.","traits":{"note": "Paid by the hour to notice things before anyone else does.", "actions": [{"name": "Salvage Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Pipe Rifle", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, range 100/300 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8+1) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signals a warband camp just out of sight, ready to whistle for backup."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a claim-marker flag meant for the ruins directly ahead."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is bored and underpaid, more willing to talk a deal than fight one out."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has spotted something in the ruins the warband hasn't reported back yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a countdown watch, due to be relieved from lookout in the hour."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Times each whistle-signal precisely, never repeating the same pattern twice."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know the ruins' layout better than anyone alive reasonably should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whistle he's about to give isn't the warband's signal at all, but something else's."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Crouches on a rubble ridge, pipe rifle balanced across one knee, watching the approach", "Whistles two low notes, the only warning the ruins ahead are already claimed"]},{"name":"Ration Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"ration-raider","summary":"Desperate raider who kills for canned goods and water","flavor":"Kills for canned goods and clean water, nothing personal, everything necessary.","desc":"Gaunt under a layered coat, eyes fixed on whatever's strapped to your pack rather than your face, they've already decided this doesn't have to be personal. Canned goods, clean water — that's the whole negotiation, and it only has two outcomes.","traits":{"note": "Goes for the loudest threat first, not the closest one.", "actions": [{"name": "Scavenged Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Salvaged Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d10) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works alone, favors ambush over a fair fight, always checks the exits first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Travels with a starving dog that snarls before the raider even draws a weapon."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Limps from an old wound, favors the crossbow to keep distance from melee."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a child's drawing folded in a coat pocket, won't say whose."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Negotiates first in a flat, rehearsed voice before ever reaching for the mace."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Wears three canteens on a bandolier, none of them full, all of them rattling."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mutters a countdown under their breath before every swing, like a ritual against missing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fights with the manic focus of someone who hasn't eaten in four days and knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Sizing up a stranger's pack from a doorway, weighing whether it's worth the fight", "Rationing the last mouthful of water while scanning the road both ways"]},{"name":"Bonepicker Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Radiation-twisted corpse that still remembers running","flavor":"Radiation twisted this corpse into a hungry thing that still remembers how to run.","desc":"It still runs in short, jerking bursts, some radiation-twisted memory of fleeing something insisting the body keep moving even with nothing left worth fleeing from. Between bursts it stands stock still, head cocked, as if listening for an all-clear that stopped coming years ago.","traits":{"note": "Alternates between frantic bursts of speed and total stillness.", "actions": [{"name": "Frenzied Bite and Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The ghoul makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claw."}, {"name": "Twitching Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scrabbling Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) slashing damage. If the target is a creature other than an undead, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Freezes mid-run at the sound of static, as if an old broadcast just cut back in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the tattered remains of a uniform, badge fused to melted fabric."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only runs in one direction no matter what's chasing or fleeing it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw hangs slack and reset wrong, clicking with every failed bite."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags one leg from an old break that never set, slowing its bursts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums a fragment of a tune between bursts, three notes, always the same three."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow keeps running a half-second after the body stops moving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sprints in a dead straight line toward the loudest surviving building on the skyline."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["Standing frozen mid-stride, head cocked toward a sound only it can hear", "Bursting into a jerking sprint across open ground for no visible reason"]},{"name":"Static Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Cultist who worships the static hum as divine voice","flavor":"Worships the hum in dead radios as the voice of the sky that ended the world.","desc":"A dead radio crackles against one ear, held there with tape and reverence, and the zealot repeats fragments of the static back like scripture. To them, that hum is the voice of the sky that ended the world, and they've spent years learning to translate it. They speak to you the same way — mostly static, mostly certain.","traits":{"note": "Preaches mid-fight, treating the swing of the sickle as part of the sermon.", "actions": [{"name": "Sickle of the Hum", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) slashing damage, and the zealot can choose to forgo damage to instead force the target to make a DC 10 Wisdom save or be frightened until the end of its next turn, gripped by the certainty the static is speaking through the blade."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second dead radio meant as an offering for whoever converts next."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a taped-together antenna rig it insists must never be moved."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Traveling to deliver a message it swears the static gave it for a named settlement."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorting a newer convert who hasn't learned to stop flinching at the noise yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nursing a burn from a radio that shocked it, taking that as a sign to push harder."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Insists the static named a day, and keeps checking a hand-scratched calendar."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Carries a second radio that plays a different, calmer static, one it fears more."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes the fight itself was foretold in the hum, and won't retreat under any circumstance."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Pressing a crackling dead radio to one ear, repeating fragments of static like prayer", "Kneeling before a wrecked broadcast tower, waiting for it to speak again"]},{"name":"Wire-Fanged Cur","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"wire-fanged-cur","summary":"Scrap-hound fitted with crude barbed-wire fangs","flavor":"A scrap-hound whose muzzle was crudely fitted with barbed wire fangs by its handler.","desc":"Someone took the time to fit this scrap-hound's muzzle with crude barbed wire, wrapping it tight enough to bite into the animal's own gums. It snarls through the pain like the wire's a feature, not an injury, and the bite that follows tears as much as it punctures.","traits":{"note": "Its bite tears rather than punctures, leaving ragged wounds.", "actions": [{"name": "Barbed Bite and Snap", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The cur makes two bite attacks."}, {"name": "Barbed-Wire Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) piercing damage, and the wound bleeds; the target takes 1 ongoing damage at the start of its next turn unless the wound is bound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bleeds steadily from its own gums but never seems to notice or slow down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs with a pack of three, taking turns feinting to draw a target out of formation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a rusted collar with a name tag scratched down to nothing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors ankles and hamstrings, biting low before anyone can raise a weapon."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches from raised hands, a training scar from whoever wired its muzzle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Chews at loose wire ends between fights, drawing its own blood absentmindedly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its barbed wire has begun to rust into the flesh, fusing muzzle and metal into one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Attacks in a blind frenzy once its own blood reaches its tongue, heedless of danger."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["Snarling through a mouthful of barbed wire, gums bleeding freely down its jaw", "Circling a scent trail low to the ground, wire fangs clicking with each snap"]},{"name":"Blister-Skin Drifter","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"blister-skin-drifter","summary":"Weeping-rot shambler that spreads contact contamination","flavor":"Sores weep a contact rot; it doesn't chase so much as shamble into your path.","desc":"Weeping sores track down both arms in a slow, glistening rot, and it doesn't chase so much as drift steadily into whatever path you happen to be standing in. Contact is the whole strategy — no speed, no cunning, just patient proximity and contamination waiting to transfer.","traits":{"note": "Never chases; relies entirely on prey walking into its path.", "actions": [{"name": "Weeping Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or contract a contact rot: it takes 2 (1d4) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns until it receives magical healing or a short rest is spent cleaning the wound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves so slowly it's mistaken for a corpse until it's already within arm's reach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a visible wet trail of rot across dust and ash, easy to track backward."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drawn toward open water, drifting in slow circles around any standing pool."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the remains of a hazard suit, sores weeping through every seam and seal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Groans at a steady, almost peaceful rhythm that carries far across open ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its sores glow faintly at night, a sick phosphorescent green visible from a distance."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Flies refuse to land on it, giving it an unnatural, silent halo of empty air."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its rot has begun sloughing free in wet clumps that keep spreading contamination after it falls."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "swamp"],"activity":["Drifting steadily forward with weeping sores tracking a slow rot down both arms", "Standing motionless in a doorway until something wanders within reach"]},{"name":"Powder-Keg Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Bomb-cult runner who sprints in with a strapped satchel","flavor":"Straps a satchel of scavenged explosives to their chest and sprints the last stretch.","desc":"A satchel of jury-rigged explosives bounces hard against their chest as they break into a dead sprint, breath already ragged, face set in the particular calm of someone who's done the math on this run before. There's no slowing down to reconsider once the sprint starts.","traits":{"note": "Commits fully once the sprint starts; will not turn back mid-charge.", "actions": [{"name": "Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Light Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Satchel Charge", "text": "As a bonus action once per encounter, the runner can prime the satchel; if reduced to 0 hit points while primed, it detonates in a 10-foot radius, and each creature in that area must make a DC 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was sent by a warband to soften a specific gate before the main assault arrives."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second, unlit satchel, a spare in case the first misfires."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Running from someone in their own cult who thinks they hesitated last time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Left a note behind for a sibling, tucked under a rock, in case the sprint fails."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Timed to arrive alongside a second runner from the opposite direction."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Counts down out loud under their breath, a habit picked up from watching others detonate."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The satchel ticks faintly even when unprimed, a fault no one's dared point out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has decided today is the day regardless of orders, and won't be talked off the sprint."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["Sprinting the final stretch toward a target, satchel bouncing hard against their chest", "Crouched behind rubble, breathing ragged, doing math on the timing of the run"]},{"name":"Rust-Eaten Sentry","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Corroded security automaton walking a dead patrol route","flavor":"An old security frame, corroded half-through, still walking its dead patrol route.","desc":"Corrosion has eaten clean through one shoulder plate, exposing rusted joints that grind audibly with every mechanical step. It walks a patrol route worn into the dust by decades of identical loops, turning corners on a route map that stopped mattering generations ago.","traits":{"note": "Follows its old patrol route exactly, even off a ledge or into a wall.", "actions": [{"name": "Grinding Double Slam", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sentry makes two slam attacks."}, {"name": "Corroded Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d10+1) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows its patrol loop precisely, ignoring anything not directly in its path."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm hangs frozen, dragging with a grinding shriek at every step."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still salutes an empty guardhouse at the same point in its route, every loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts only to sudden motion, otherwise walking past stationary targets entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rusted-through logbook slot on its chest, long since jammed shut."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sparks faintly from an exposed wire every few steps, trailing a thin smell of ozone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Repeats a single garbled voice line at the same corner, word for word, every loop."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its patrol route has begun to widen, drawing it into rooms it never used to enter."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Grinding through a patrol loop worn into the dust by decades of identical steps", "Turning a corner on a route map that stopped mattering generations ago"]},{"name":"Chem-Slick Viper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"chem-slick-viper","summary":"Runoff-mutated viper whose venom keeps wounds open","flavor":"Its venom glands swelled on tank runoff; one bite and the wound never quite closes.","desc":"Runoff swelling has left its venom glands distended and visibly pulsing beneath translucent scales. One strike is enough — the venom keeps the wound from closing, weeping steadily long after the snake itself has slid back into the rubble.","traits":{"note": "Prefers to strike once and retreat rather than press an attack.", "actions": [{"name": "Runoff Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) piercing damage, and the target must make a DC 11 Constitution saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success. On a failed save, the wound also refuses to close, dealing 1 additional poison damage at the start of the target's turns until it receives healing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests near standing runoff, striking anything that lingers too close to the pool."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales shimmer faintly with a chemical sheen, visible only in direct light."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes once and immediately retreats into the nearest crack or pipe."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its venom glands have swollen large enough to visibly drag against the ground."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts by vibration, striking accurately even in total darkness."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaves a faint chemical hiss in the air after each strike, like something evaporating."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed skins litter the runoff pool, each one slightly larger than the last."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Bites are increasing in frequency, as if the runoff is concentrating and the venom sharpening with it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "desert"],"activity":["Coiled beside a tank runoff pool, glands visibly pulsing beneath translucent scales", "Sliding back into rubble after a strike, leaving a wound that won't stop weeping"]},{"name":"Grit-Locust Cloud","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"grit-locust-cloud","summary":"Mutant locust swarm stripping crops and flesh alike","flavor":"A living dust storm of mutant locusts that strips crops and flesh alike.","desc":"The horizon darkens wrong, low and grinding, and then the swarm is on you — a living dust storm of mutant locusts clicking against every exposed surface. Crops, canvas, skin: the swarm strips whatever's in its path with the same indifferent hunger.","traits":{"note": "Strips anything in its path indiscriminately; has no target preference.", "actions": [{"name": "Grinding Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 5 (2d4) piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rides ahead of a dust storm, arriving just before the wind picks up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strips a field bare in minutes, leaving bare furrows where crops stood."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters instantly at loud noise, only to reform minutes later downwind."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clicks louder as it thickens, a rising drone audible well before it arrives."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the smell of standing water, converging on wells and cisterns."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaves a fine, oily residue on everything it passes over, faintly luminous at dusk."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Individual locusts glow faint orange at the wingtips, like drifting embers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The swarm has grown dense enough to blot out the sky entirely overhead."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["Darkening the horizon low and grinding, closing fast over open ground", "Clicking against every exposed surface, stripping crops and flesh with equal indifference"]},{"name":"Carrion Beetle Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Fist-sized beetle swarm drawn to fresh ash-flat kills","flavor":"Chitinous beetles the size of fists, drawn en masse to fresh kills in the ash flats.","desc":"Fist-sized beetles converge from every crack in the rubble the instant blood hits the ash, chitin clicking together as the mass thickens. They don't discriminate between combatant and corpse — anything freshly dead, or dying, draws them in equal numbers.","traits":{"note": "Drawn to fresh blood before anything else, including active combatants.", "actions": [{"name": "Converging Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 5 (2d4) piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Converges on the nearest wound within seconds, no matter how small the cut."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests inside a hollowed corpse until disturbed, then boils out all at once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the moment fresh blood stops flowing, uninterested in cold kills."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fist-sized individuals cling stubbornly even when the swarm as a whole scatters."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chitin clatters loud enough to mask footsteps approaching from behind it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaves rubble stained a dull rust color from the sheer volume it strips clean."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some individuals carry faint bioluminescent markings that pulse when the swarm feeds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has grown bold enough to swarm living, moving targets without waiting for a kill."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Converging from every crack in the rubble the instant blood hits the ash", "Thickening over a fresh kill, chitin clicking as the mass presses inward"]},{"name":"Tanker Ganger","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"tanker-ganger","summary":"Fuel-convoy enforcer quick to violence over short tribute","flavor":"Rides shotgun on a fuel convoy, quick to violence when the tribute's short.","desc":"He rides the running board of a fuel tanker with one boot braced and a shotgun resting easy across his forearm, eyes on whoever's approaching the checkpoint. The moment the tribute comes up short, that easy posture disappears fast.","traits":{"note": "Stays calm until tribute comes up short, then commits fast.", "actions": [{"name": "Convoy Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d12+2) slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Collecting tribute for a convoy that's already a full ration short this run."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Covering for a partner who slipped off to skim fuel for themselves."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Under orders to bring back a hostage if the tribute can't be paid in fuel."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Riding escort for a tanker that's been leaking badly since the last raid."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waiting on a relief shift that's now hours overdue, growing impatient and reckless."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a tally of every short tribute scratched into the tanker's own paint."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refuses to accept anything but fuel, even when offered goods worth more."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has been quietly told to make an example out of the next short payment, no exceptions."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "desert"],"activity":["Riding the running board of a fuel tanker, shotgun resting easy across one forearm", "Watching a checkpoint line with the practiced boredom of someone expecting a fight"]},{"name":"Scab-Plate Scavver","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Scrap-armored raider wearing plates looted off corpses","flavor":"Wears bolted scrap armor scavenged plate by plate off the dead.","desc":"Bolted scrap armor covers him in mismatched plates, each one scavenged off a different corpse in a different fight, dented in places that tell their own stories. He moves stiffly under the weight but wears it like a trophy case.","traits":{"note": "Wears trophies of past kills as armor, slowing its movement.", "actions": [{"name": "Scrap Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (1d12+3) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+3) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Names each plate of armor aloud before a fight, a private roll call of the dead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to loot a body until the fight's fully over, out of some private code."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than expected under the weight, favoring positioning over speed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades looted plate freely for better pieces, always upgrading the collection."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one plate deliberately unpolished, a reminder of a fight barely survived."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The armor's mismatched dents form a rough map, if you know what battle each one's from."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One plate still bears a stranger's name scratched inside, never cleaned off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has started taking plates off the still-living, unwilling to wait for a kill anymore."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "desert"],"activity":["Moving stiffly under a mismatched patchwork of scavenged armor plates", "Checking dented plating for the fights each piece came from, one scar at a time"]},{"name":"Detonator Cultist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Bomb-cultist wired with a warhead trigger, waiting","flavor":"Straps a warhead trigger to his own chest, grinning, waiting to be told when.","desc":"A warhead trigger sits strapped flush against his sternum, wired with the careful pride of a man showing off jewelry. He's grinning, patient, waiting for someone — anyone — to give the word, and the grin doesn't waver even under a gun.","traits":{"note": "Waits calmly for a signal to detonate rather than acting alone.", "actions": [{"name": "Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Warhead Casting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The cultist casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: chill touch, hex. 1/day each: hold person, spiritual weapon."}, {"name": "Dead Man's Switch", "text": "If the cultist is reduced to 0 hit points, it can use its reaction to trigger the warhead; each creature within 15 feet must make a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waiting on a signal from a handler who's already three days late."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guarding a specific building, convinced the order to detonate will come there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second trigger meant for a partner who never showed up to wear it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has started doubting the order will ever come, and is desperate for any excuse."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorting a captive meant to be present when the trigger finally gets pulled."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a countdown scratched daily into his own forearm, erasing and restarting it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists the warhead whispers to him at night, telling him it isn't time yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has decided, unprompted, that this encounter is finally the signal he's been waiting for."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Kneeling with a warhead trigger strapped flush against his sternum, grinning and waiting", "Showing off the trigger rig to anyone who'll look, proud as if it were jewelry"]},{"name":"Growth-Warped Boar","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-boar","model":"giant-boar","summary":"Tumor-ridden giant boar charging anything that moves","flavor":"Tumor-ridden and enormous, it charges anything that moves in its blighted range.","desc":"Tumors ridge its back in uneven lumps beneath patchy, radiation-thinned hide, and its already-enormous frame seems too large for the legs carrying it. It charges anything that moves in its blighted range without pause or discrimination — prey, predator, or wall.","traits":{"note": "Charges indiscriminately at anything moving, including allies.", "actions": [{"name": "Tumor-Ridged Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (1d12+3) piercing damage. If the boar moved at least 20 feet straight toward the target before the attack, the target also takes 4 (1d8) additional piercing damage and must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges the loudest source of movement first, regardless of distance or size."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tumors weep a thin fluid that draws flies even in the driest wasteland air."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Legs strain visibly under its own bloated bulk, slowing between charges."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Territorial around a specific blighted field, charging anything that enters it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges through obstacles rather than around them, snapping fences and walls alike."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One tumor has grown large enough to drag along the ground when it walks."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A faint second heartbeat is audible from deep inside its swollen flank."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its tumors have begun splitting under stress, spraying caustic fluid mid-charge."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["hill", "forest", "grassland"],"activity":["Charging anything that moves through its blighted range without pause", "Standing bloated and tumor-ridged, breathing heavy before another mindless charge"]},{"name":"Half-Life Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Fallout-glassed bones animated by residual radiation","flavor":"Bones fused glass-green by fallout, animated by whatever still crackles in the marrow.","desc":"Fallout has fused its bones a sickly translucent green, glassy where marrow used to be, and something still crackles faintly inside the joints when it moves. It rattles upright in fits, animated by whatever residual charge refuses to let it lie still.","traits":{"note": "Moves in jerking fits rather than smooth motion.", "actions": [{"name": "Glass-Bone Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Fused-Marrow Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bones glow faintly green in low light, easy to spot from a distance at night."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves only in short, jerking bursts, freezing mid-stride between them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crackles audibly at the joints, a faint electrical sound that carries in silence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clusters in small groups near old fallout sites, animated by the same lingering charge."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Falls still entirely if separated too far from the site that first animated it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its glassy bones have begun cracking under their own translucent weight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sparks visibly jump between rib bones when it takes damage."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Charge is building rather than fading, and its bursts are getting faster by the hour."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Rattling upright in fits, glass-green bones crackling faintly at the joints", "Standing frozen mid-motion until something disturbs the charge still animating it"]},{"name":"Corroded Watcher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"corroded-watcher","summary":"Drone-husk sentinel still logging intruders no one reads","flavor":"A camera-drone husk grafted to a scavenged chassis, still logging intruders no one reads.","desc":"A camera-drone husk sits grafted crookedly atop a scavenged chassis, lens cracked but still swiveling to track motion out of some ancient standing order. It logs everything it sees in a memory nobody left alive will ever read.","traits":{"note": "Tracks and logs movement even when it poses no threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Cracked-Servo Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d8+1) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Dead-Lens Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature the watcher can see within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of the watcher's next turn, unsettled by the certainty of being recorded."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lens cracked but still swiveling, tracking motion from a permanent standing order."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mounted crookedly atop a scavenged chassis, joints grinding with every turn."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Attacks only after logging a target for a full three seconds, never before."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a fixed post it never leaves, no matter what happens beyond its range."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its internal storage light blinks steadily, still recording after all these years."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Occasionally plays back a garbled fragment of old recorded footage through a broken speaker."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to flinch away from bright light, as if the lens still fears overexposure."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its storage has finally filled, and it's begun deleting itself one violent memory at a time."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Swiveling a cracked lens to track motion out of some ancient standing order", "Logging everything it sees into a memory nobody left alive will ever read"]},{"name":"Ash-Choked Hound","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"Feral scrap-hound pup, quick, starving, unpredictable","flavor":"A scrap-hound puppy grown feral in the rubble, quick and starving.","desc":"Still puppy-thin under matted, ash-caked fur, it darts and feints with more energy than sense, snapping at anything that moves too fast. Starvation has made it quick and utterly unpredictable — as likely to bolt as to bite.","traits":{"note": "As likely to bolt as to bite; unpredictable under pressure.", "actions": [{"name": "Ash-Caked Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 2 (1d4) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bolts the instant it takes any real damage, more scared than vicious."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still puppy-thin under matted fur, darting in quick, uncertain bursts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the nearest larger predator at a distance, scavenging its leftovers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snaps at shadows and dust motes as readily as at real threats."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wags and snarls in the same breath, wired between fear and hunger."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Ash cakes so thick in its fur it leaves a faint gray trail with every step."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally stops mid-chase to stare at nothing, ears pinned, before resuming."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Starvation has pushed it past caution; it now lunges at things twice its size."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["Darting and feinting through rubble with more energy than sense, snapping at motion", "Circling a scent trail low and fast, ash-caked fur bristling with starved nerves"]},{"name":"Firebrand Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Nervous bomb-cult convert still willing to light fuses","flavor":"A new convert to the Bomb-Cult, still nervous, still willing to light the fuse.","desc":"New robes, still stiff and unstained, mark this one as a fresh convert to the Bomb-Cult — the nerves still show in the way their hands shake around the lit fuse. They're scared. They light it anyway.","traits":{"note": "Visibly frightened but follows through regardless.", "actions": [{"name": "Trembling Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was sent alone by an initiator testing whether the new convert will actually light it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a note to a sibling, meant to be delivered only if the initiate doesn't return."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is one fuse away from being fully accepted into the Bomb-Cult's inner circle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Second-guessing the mission, but too afraid of the cult to turn back now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trailing an older mentor at a distance, desperate to prove they don't need watching."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps re-lighting a fuse that keeps going out, growing more frantic each time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the fuse itself under their breath, like it's a nervous animal to be calmed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just realized the fuse is shorter than expected, and panic is setting in fast."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Standing in stiff, unstained robes, hands shaking around a freshly lit fuse", "Repeating a memorized chant under their breath to steady their own nerves"]},{"name":"Mange-Back Mutt","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Mangy hairless mutt hunting collapsed subway tunnels","flavor":"Mangy, hairless, and vicious in packs, it hunts the collapsed subway lines.","desc":"Hairless in patches and vicious in numbers, it slinks along the edge of a collapsed subway entrance, drawn out by any noise or light drifting up from below. Alone it's pitiful; in a pack it's a problem.","traits":{"note": "Pitiful alone, dangerous only when packed together.", "actions": [{"name": "Mangy Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 2 (1d4) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pack of four or five, scattering the instant one of them drops."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bald patches expose scarred skin, evidence of fights with its own littermates."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Emerges only when noise or light drifts up from the collapsed tunnels below."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Alone, it whimpers and flees; surrounded by its pack, it presses in boldly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests deep in tunnel debris, only surfacing to scavenge or hunt in numbers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its pack has a rough pecking order, visible in who eats first after a kill."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some mutts in the pack are missing patches of skin, not just fur, and don't seem to mind."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The pack has grown bold enough lately to trail large parties for hours before striking."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["Slinking along the edge of a collapsed subway entrance, drawn by noise from below", "Skulking in a mangy pack, bold only when the numbers favor it"]},{"name":"Warband Trapper","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Trap-setter who lines roads before the warband arrives","flavor":"Lines the approach roads with snares and pit traps before the warband ever shows itself.","desc":"He works the approach roads ahead of the main column, laying snares and pit-traps with the unhurried care of a man who takes real pride in his craft. By the time the warband shows itself, the ground has already been claimed.","traits":{"note": "Claims ground with traps well before any fight begins.", "actions": [{"name": "Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) piercing damage, or 5 (1d8+1) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."}, {"name": "Prepared Snare", "text": "Once per encounter, if the trapper has had at least 1 minute to prepare an area, it can trigger a hidden snare as a bonus action; one creature within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity saving throw or be restrained until it uses an action to break free with a DC 12 Strength check."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Finishing the last trap before the warband's main column is due to arrive."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Left behind alone after the warband changed its approach route without telling them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guarding a cache of trap components meant for the next three checkpoints."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nervous that a trap they set has already caught the wrong target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Racing to finish before scouts from a rival warband spot the half-laid road."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Marks each finished trap with a small painted stone, a private counting system."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists one particular trap on the road is 'saved' for someone specific."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just realized the warband is running early, and the road isn't ready."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "desert", "ruins"],"activity":["Laying snares and pit-traps along the approach road with unhurried, practiced care", "Checking a line of hidden traps before the main warband column arrives"]},{"name":"Static-Touched Vermin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"static-touched-vermin","summary":"Irradiated centipede whose touch blisters skin for days","flavor":"An irradiated centipede whose touch leaves skin blistered and numb for days.","desc":"Its many-legged body carries a faint electrical crackle along each segment, a static charge picked up from years denned near irradiated cable. Its touch leaves skin blistered and numb for days after the bite fades.","traits":{"note": "Its touch numbs and blisters skin long after the bite itself fades.", "actions": [{"name": "Static Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or its skin blisters and goes numb, imposing disadvantage on Dexterity checks with the affected limb for 24 hours."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dens near irradiated cable, drawn to the faint warmth it still gives off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crackles audibly along its segments, easy to hear before it's seen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Curls tight and plays dead when threatened, striking only if handled."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in clusters of a dozen or more inside cracked conduit housings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids open ground, preferring cracks and gaps barely wide enough to fit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaves faint scorch marks on anything it crawls across for long."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its segments glow faintly at the joints in complete darkness."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Charge has built high enough that its bite now leaves visible sparks on contact."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "desert"],"activity":["Carrying a faint electrical crackle along each segment, denned near irradiated cable", "Threading through cracked concrete toward a warm humming conduit"]},{"name":"Fume Vent Zealot","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Cracked-mask cultist chanting over leaking gas vents","flavor":"Breathes through a cracked filter mask, chanting over any vent that still leaks gas.","desc":"A cracked filter mask hisses with each labored breath as the zealot kneels beside a leaking gas vent, chanting low over the fumes like they're a font. Any vent still leaking earns a congregation of one, occasionally two.","traits":{"note": "Grows more fervent the longer it breathes the vent fumes.", "actions": [{"name": "Sickle of the Vent", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels in a fixed spot beside its chosen vent, reluctant to move far from it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mask hisses audibly, betraying its position even in total darkness."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chants louder and faster the closer a fight gets, working itself into a fervor."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second cracked mask on hand, meant for a convert who never arrived."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights defensively at first, unwilling to be drawn far from the vent's fumes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has scratched tally marks into the pipe, one for every vent found dry and abandoned."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Breathes shallow and slow even off the vent, as if trained the fumes are always near."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The vent behind it is building pressure, and it seems entirely unconcerned about the hiss growing louder."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Kneeling beside a leaking gas vent, chanting low over the fumes like a font", "Adjusting a cracked filter mask, hissing breath timed to a private ritual"]},{"name":"Wreck-Diver","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"wreck-diver","summary":"Salvager who strips wrecks before warlords claim them","flavor":"Specializes in stripping downed aircraft and sunken tankers before the warlords claim them.","desc":"Salt-scoured gear and a coil of rope mark this scavenger as someone who works fast — stripping downed aircraft and sunken tankers before any warlord's crew arrives to claim the wreck as tribute. Time, not danger, is what worries them most.","traits":{"note": "Time pressure worries it more than danger; works fast under threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Dive and Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The wreck-diver makes two attacks, using its shortsword or longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Salvage Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Salt-Worn Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Racing a rival crew known to be circling the same downed wreck."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carrying a partial haul already, unwilling to abandon it even under threat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Working alone after their crew scattered when a warlord's patrol got close."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marked the wreck days ago and is furious to find someone else already inside it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owes a debt to a settlement that's counting on this specific haul."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a tally of near-misses with warlord patrols, scratched into a salt-worn coil of rope."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists the wreck is 'still settling,' and refuses to work near the deepest section."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just heard a patrol's engine in the distance, and is done being careful."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "coast", "sea"],"activity":["Coiling rope fast while eyeing a downed wreck before any warlord's crew arrives", "Stripping salvage off a sunken hull with practiced, hurried hands"]},{"name":"Ashfield Widow Spider","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-spider","model":"giant-spider","summary":"Ash-camouflaged spider whose webs vanish in scorched fields","flavor":"Its web is laced with fine grit and ash, near invisible against a scorched field.","desc":"Its web carries fine grit and ash worked directly into the silk, rendering it nearly invisible strung across a scorched field. You feel it before you see it — a fine line catching at an ankle, and then the spider is already moving.","traits":{"note": "Its webs are nearly invisible against scorched, ash-colored ground.", "actions": [{"name": "Ash-Silk Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) piercing damage, and the target must make a DC 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 9 (2d8) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}, {"name": "Grit-Laced Web (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Web (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one Large or smaller creature. Hit: The target is restrained by webbing nearly invisible against ash-covered ground, gaining advantage on the spider's attack rolls against it until it escapes with a DC 12 Strength check."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weaves grit and ash directly into its silk, rendering webs nearly invisible in scorched fields."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits motionless at the center of a wide web, patient past the point of hunger."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes and retreats to the web's edge rather than pressing an advantage."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests near old battle sites, its web strung between wreckage and bone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers still, windless nights, when its webbing holds its camouflage longest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its legs are dusted gray-white, matching the ash so closely it seems to vanish standing still."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wraps prey slowly rather than feeding immediately, as if savoring the wait."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has begun laying web across a much wider stretch of field than any single spider should need."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["Lying still in ash-camouflaged web strung invisibly across a scorched field", "Feeling a line catch at an ankle, already moving before it's seen"]},{"name":"Grinder-Belt Sentry","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Retrofitted factory automaton swinging grinder arms on flesh","flavor":"Retrofitted from an old factory line, its arms still swing the grinder motion, now on flesh.","desc":"Retrofitted from an old factory line, its twin arms still swing in the same grinding arc they were built for, only there's no belt beneath them anymore — just whatever's unlucky enough to be standing in their reach.","traits":{"note": "Attacks with the same mechanical rhythm it was built with, unerring but predictable.", "actions": [{"name": "Grinder Double Swing", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The sentry makes two slam attacks."}, {"name": "Grinder Arm Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) slashing damage from grinding components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings in the same fixed arc regardless of what's standing in its reach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grinder arms shriek loud enough to be heard through several walls of rubble."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Anchored near its old factory line, rarely wandering more than a short patrol from it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slows briefly between swings, a mechanical hitch from decades without maintenance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still tracks a phantom conveyor belt that no longer exists, swinging at empty air."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Trailing sparks mark its patrol path, visible after dark from a distance."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its rhythm briefly syncs with any nearby machinery still running, arms speeding up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "One arm has begun overclocking, swinging faster and wilder than its chassis was built for."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Swinging twin grinder arms in the same arc they were built for, now on flesh", "Grinding forward on a factory line long since stripped of its belt"]},{"name":"Fuel-Cult Bruiser","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"fuel-cult-bruiser","summary":"Tithe enforcer swinging rebar for the Fuel Cult","flavor":"Enforces tithe collection for the Fuel Cult with a length of rebar and no patience.","desc":"A length of rebar rides loose in one massive hand as he walks the tithe line, checking fuel drums against a mental ledger that never seems to favor the settlement. Patience isn't part of his collection method.","traits":{"note": "Escalates to violence the instant a tithe comes up short.", "actions": [{"name": "Tithe Collection", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bruiser makes two attacks, using javelin or morningstar in any combination."}, {"name": "Rebar Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rebar Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d8) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Collecting tithe from a settlement that's genuinely three drums short this cycle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Under pressure from above to make an example if this collection comes up light."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Escorting a smaller enforcer who's about to make the collection much worse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carrying a private ledger that doesn't match the Fuel Cult's official one."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owed a personal debt by someone in the settlement he's supposed to be shaking down."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a running count of every short tithe scratched into the rebar itself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refuses payment in anything but fuel, no matter how valuable the alternative offered."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just been told this settlement gets no more warnings, effective immediately."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "desert"],"activity":["Walking the tithe line, checking fuel drums against a ledger that never favors the settlement", "Resting a length of rebar loose in one hand, watching for anyone short on payment"]},{"name":"Chem-Vat Horror","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"Chemical-vat mutant that crawled out and kept growing","flavor":"Something that crawled out of a corroded chemical vat and kept growing wrong.","desc":"It dragged itself out of a corroded chemical vat some indeterminate time ago and simply never stopped growing wrong — limbs at odd angles, texture somewhere between flesh and industrial sludge. It moves with an unsettling, dripping eagerness.","traits":{"note": "Its growth hasn't stopped; it's visibly larger than it should be for its kind.", "actions": [{"name": "Sludge Feeding", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The horror makes one beak attack and two tentacle attacks."}, {"name": "Corroded Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (2d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sludge Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) acid damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller it must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be pulled 5 feet toward the horror."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests near its birth vat, rarely wandering far from the chemical stink that made it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin weeps a faint sludge that eats through cloth left in contact too long."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in an unsettling, dripping lurch, faster than its bulk suggests."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Limbs bend at angles that shouldn't support its own weight, yet somehow do."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts to chemical smells before any other stimulus, drawn in like a moth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sheds a thin layer of sludge-skin periodically, leaving trails that mark its territory."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its tentacles occasionally pulse in a rhythm that isn't its own heartbeat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Growth hasn't slowed at all, and it's noticeably larger than it was described just days ago."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "swamp"],"activity":["Dragging itself forward with an unsettling, dripping eagerness, limbs at odd angles", "Pulsing wetly near a corroded vat, texture somewhere between flesh and industrial sludge"]},{"name":"Ash-Widow Broodmother","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"ash-widow-broodmother","summary":"Reactor-dome broodmother spawning hundreds each ash-season","flavor":"Nests in a collapsed reactor dome, her brood hatching by the hundreds each ash-season.","desc":"She nests deep in a collapsed reactor dome, her bloated body pulsing faintly with residual heat, surrounded by egg-sacs that split open by the hundreds each ash-season. The dome's darkness moves in ways that take a moment too long to register as legs.","traits":{"note": "Spawns or is accompanied by a brood of smaller spiders in dramatic/apex encounters.", "actions": [{"name": "Broodcall", "text": "Once per encounter, calls forth a swarm of newly-hatched spiderlings to harass a target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Egg-sacs are due to split within the day, and the dome is about to flood with brood."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement nearby has been quietly paying tribute in livestock to keep the brood fed and distant."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a section of the reactor dome that still hums faintly with old power."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recently lost a portion of her brood to a rival predator, and is hunting harder than usual."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her web lines run out past the dome's collapsed edge, tripwires for anything approaching."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The dome's residual heat has started drawing scavengers who don't yet know what nests there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of her spawn emerge already ash-colored, camouflaged before their first molt."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Egg-sacs numbering in the hundreds are splitting all at once, and the ash-season brood is spilling out early."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "desert"],"activity":["Pulsing faintly with residual heat inside a collapsed reactor dome, surrounded by egg-sacs", "Watching the dome's darkness shift in ways that take a moment too long to register"]},{"name":"Warlord's Duelist","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"warlords-duelist","summary":"Warlord's champion dueling for sport and succession","flavor":"Trained to fight one-on-one for the warlord's amusement — and his succession.","desc":"Trained since childhood for the one-on-one bouts a warlord stages for entertainment, he squares up with formal, almost courteous precision even in a real fight. Win or lose here decides more than his own life — succession rides on the outcome too.","traits":{"note": "Fights with formal, almost ceremonial precision, even in earnest combat.", "actions": [{"name": "Duelist's Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The duelist makes two attacks with its greatsword or one attack with its heavy crossbow."}, {"name": "Ceremonial Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warlord's Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fighting today's bout as a trial to be named the warlord's chosen successor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival duelist is watching from the crowd, waiting to challenge whoever wins."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the warlord's personal token, meant to be presented only after a clean win."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Privately doubts the succession is worth the fight, but can't say so publicly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fighting under an injury the warlord doesn't know about, hidden beneath the armor."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Bows formally before every bout, even when the crowd has thinned to almost nothing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refuses to finish a downed opponent without the warlord's explicit signal."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just learned the succession stakes are higher than announced, and is fighting like it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Squaring up with formal, courteous precision even mid-fight, sizing up an opponent's stance", "Standing ready before a crowd staged for the warlord's entertainment"]},{"name":"Bloat-Ghast Preacher","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"bloat-ghast-preacher","summary":"Rotting former prophet still delivering sermons to no one","flavor":"Once a bomb-cult prophet, now a rotting thing still delivering the sermon to no one.","desc":"Once a Bomb-Cult prophet, now a bloated, rotting thing, it still stands at the pulpit position and delivers the sermon in a wet, ruined voice to a congregation that's been dead for years. It doesn't seem to notice, or care, that no one is listening anymore.","traits":{"note": "Doesn't seem to register that its congregation is gone.", "actions": [{"name": "Prophet's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}, {"name": "Sermon of Rot", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (2d4+3) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Call to Congregation", "text": "Once per day, the preacher can deliver a fragment of its old sermon; each hostile creature within 20 feet that can hear it must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of its next turn, gripped by the certainty they're intruding on something sacred and rotten."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still delivers the same sermon fragment it was preaching the day the cult abandoned this ruin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a stash of old Bomb-Cult relics stored behind its ruined pulpit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living cultist has been secretly visiting to listen, convinced the sermon still matters."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its sermon occasionally names a real settlement, a fragment of old cult targeting instructions."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts violently only when someone tries to leave mid-sermon, taking it as disrespect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its voice carries far enough through the ruin to draw other undead toward the sound."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally pauses mid-sermon as if waiting for a congregational response that never comes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has begun improvising new scripture, weaving in details about whoever's currently listening."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Standing at the pulpit position, delivering a wet, ruined sermon to a congregation long dead", "Gesturing at empty pews with the practiced rhythm of a prophet who never noticed he died"]},{"name":"Convoy Breaker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"convoy-breaker","summary":"Convoy ambusher who cracks axles before guns come out","flavor":"Specializes in ambushing fuel convoys, cracking axles before the guns ever come out.","desc":"He specializes in the quiet work — cracking an axle, slashing a tire wall, disabling a convoy before a single gun comes out. By the time the ambush shows itself, the trucks are already going nowhere.","traits":{"note": "Prefers disabling vehicles before combat starts, not during it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The breaker makes two attacks, one with its javelin and one with its longsword."}, {"name": "Axle Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) piercing damage, or 8 (1d10+3) if thrown at a stationary vehicle or immobilized target."}, {"name": "Tire-Wall Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10+3) if used with two hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works alone, marking axles with chalk for a partner crew to finish later."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a tire iron worn smooth, its edge honed to a wicked point."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times ambushes to the convoy's fuel gauge, striking right before a refuel stop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears stolen convoy colors to walk close before the first strike lands."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of cracked axles scratched into its own forearm."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Whistles the same three notes before every strike, a signal its crew has learned to dread waiting for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists machines feel the cut coming, and apologizes to each axle before it breaks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Rigged its own javelin with a scavenged blasting cap, meant for one glorious final throw."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "any"],"activity":["crouches beneath a rig's undercarriage, jamming a chisel into the axle seam", "watches a convoy's dust trail from a ridge, timing the ambush window"]},{"name":"Warp-Chitin Stalker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"warp-chitin-stalker","summary":"Insect-hybrid mutant armored by decades of chem runoff","flavor":"Insect and something else fused by decades of runoff, patient and armored.","desc":"Insect plating and something else entirely have fused across its frame after decades marinating in chemical runoff, each joint armored thick and glossy. It stalks with patient, unhurried steps, in no rush because it knows it doesn't need to be.","traits":{"note": "Its poison spray forces prey to choose between closing distance and choking.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The stalker makes two attacks: one bite and one constrict, or one bite and uses poison spray."}, {"name": "Chitin Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (2d6+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Runoff Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 14) and restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Chem-Poison Spray", "replaces": "Poison Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The stalker exhales caustic vapor in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 21 (6d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Molts constantly, leaving hollow chitin husks scattered near its den."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors flooded runoff channels, moving slower on dry ground."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating has a slick green sheen that beads runoff instead of absorbing it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts by ambush from drainage pipes, striking only when prey passes directly below."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils around scrap metal to mimic pipework while it waits."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Clicks its mandibles in a slow rhythm that other stalkers in the area answer back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed husks keep twitching for hours after molting, like the shape remembers moving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Runoff has fused a second, vestigial head to its shoulder that hisses independently of the first."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "desert"],"activity":["sways low behind rusted drums, chitin plates ticking softly as it breathes", "tastes the air with a forked tongue, tracking runoff-tainted prey by smell alone"]},{"name":"Rig-Mounted Turret Hound","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rig-mounted-turret-hound","summary":"Scrap-hound chassis welded to a swivel autogun","flavor":"A scrap-hound chassis welded permanently to a swivel-mounted autogun.","desc":"A scrap-hound's four-legged chassis has been permanently welded to a swivel-mounted autogun, the barrel tracking motion independent of where its head happens to be looking. It doesn't bark a warning — it just opens up.","traits":{"note": "The gun tracks motion independent of its head, so it never needs to look at what it's shooting.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The hound makes two attacks with its mounted autogun."}, {"name": "Swivel Autogun", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols a fixed loop between two scrap piles, timing that a careful watcher can learn."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barrel jams every dozen shots, needing a clattering half-second to clear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs hot after sustained fire, venting steam from its flank joints."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was built from three different hound chassis, legs mismatched in gait."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a single fuel dump obsessively, ignoring intruders elsewhere on the lot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Head swivels to face threats a half-second after the gun already has, like an afterthought."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its targeting hum shifts pitch depending on how many heartbeats it detects nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone rigged a second autogun onto its tail, firing blind whenever it's flanked."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["prowls a scrapyard perimeter on four legs, autogun barrel tracking every twitch of motion", "idles near a fuel dump, servos whining faintly as its targeting array resets"]},{"name":"Fume-Choked Ettin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"fume-choked-ettin","summary":"Two-headed mutant giant arguing over which ruin to loot","flavor":"A two-headed mutant giant, each head arguing over which smokestack to loot next.","desc":"Two heads bicker constantly over which smokestack to loot next, neither one paying full attention to anything approaching from outside their argument. The body beneath them, though, reacts to threats just fine without needing a vote.","traits":{"note": "Each head can be distracted separately, but the body still reacts to danger on its own.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The ettin makes two attacks, one with its battleaxe and one with its morningstar."}, {"name": "Scavenged Battleaxe", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (2d8+5) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rebar Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head hoards bottle caps, the other hoards intact glass — they never agree on value."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a chain of scavenged car doors behind it as makeshift armor plating."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Both heads cough in a wet, wheezing rhythm from decades of smokestack fumes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loots methodically, sorting salvage into two separate piles by preference."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head sleeps while the other keeps watch, trading off every few hours."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The two heads have started finishing each other's sentences mid-argument, unnervingly in sync."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A third, silent face has started forming at the base of its neck where the heads meet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The heads have stopped arguing entirely and now speak only in unison, which is somehow worse."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["argues with itself over a hauled scrap pile, two heads pointing in opposite directions", "coughs black smoke while dragging a smokestack door off its hinges"]},{"name":"Vault-Sealed Revenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"vault-sealed-revenant","summary":"Bunker-sealed ghost whose scream carries failing air","flavor":"Died locked in a bunker's blast door; its scream still carries the hiss of failing air.","desc":"It died locked behind a failing blast door, and its scream still carries that same hiss of failing air — a thin, keening wheeze underneath the wail. Whatever haunts it now remembers suffocation better than it remembers being alive.","traits":{"note": "Its wail carries the same hiss as failing air, and those who hear it remember suffocating.", "actions": [{"name": "Suffocating Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Spell Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 18 (4d8) necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Sealed-Door Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each non-undead creature within 60 feet that can see the revenant must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A frightened target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}, {"name": "Failing-Air Wail", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "The revenant unleashes a wail audible up to 1 mile away. Every creature within 30 feet must make a DC 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success. A non-undead creature reduced to 0 hit points by this damage dies."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the same failed door endlessly, never straying more than a few rooms from it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows agitated near working air seals, as if resentful of good engineering."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its keen rises and falls with an actual breathing rhythm it no longer needs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids open, ventilated spaces, drifting back toward sealed corridors instead."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint frost on metal it passes, as if the bunker's cold clings to it still."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Mimics the specific hiss-pattern of a failing pressure valve, a sound old vault workers recognize instantly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Reaches toward door mechanisms with something like muscle memory, trying controls that no longer exist."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The vault door behind it groans open an inch further every time it wails, like the seal itself remembers dying too."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["drifts along a corridor of rusted blast doors, keening faintly through a sealed throat", "hovers near a jammed vault mechanism, still trying to force air through a door that never opened"]},{"name":"Warband Chieftain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"warband-chieftain","summary":"Warband chief who climbed to power by outliving rivals","flavor":"Climbed to command over three rival gangs by outliving every challenger personally.","desc":"He climbed to command over three rival gangs the same way every time: by outliving every challenger personally, in full view of both crews. He carries that history in old scar tissue and in the way nobody here quite meets his eyes.","traits":{"note": "Fought every rival personally rather than delegate — the crew reads that as proof he can still win.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chieftain makes two attacks, one with its spear and one with its shield."}, {"name": "Warband Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) piercing damage, or 9 (1d10+4) if used with two hands in melee."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of duels won carved into the haft of his spear."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears trophies from three rival gang leaders stitched into his armor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never fights without the whole warband watching, treating combat as public proof."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses ranged weapons on principle, calling them a coward's argument."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on hearing a challenger's name before the fight starts, out of grim courtesy."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Studies an opponent's stance for a full breath before ever throwing the first strike."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks softly to his old spear between fights, as if it remembers every kill better than he does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has started losing on purpose to weaker challengers, testing which lieutenants would actually replace him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill", "any"],"activity":["holds court over a cookfire, letting lieutenants argue while he watches for the next challenger", "spars bare-knuckle against a volunteer, testing the crowd's mood before the real fight"]},{"name":"Molten Vat Ooze","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"molten-vat-ooze","summary":"Chemical-waste sludge ooze dissolving anything too close","flavor":"A runoff sludge of chemical waste and slag, dissolving anything that wades too close.","desc":"A slow, viscous sludge of chemical waste and half-melted slag spreads across the ground in a widening slick, steaming faintly where it touches open air. It dissolves anything that wades too close with unhurried, patient chemistry.","traits":{"note": "Its chemistry works unhurried but doesn't stop once it's latched on.", "actions": [{"name": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "replaces": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 22 (4d10) acid damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a glossy chemical sheen on the ground long after it's moved on."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pools thickest near cracked drums, feeding on whatever still leaks from them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves only downhill, letting gravity do most of the work."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gives off a faint chemical stink that warns careful scavengers before they see it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts violently to water, hissing and swelling when it touches runoff puddles."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Carries half-dissolved tools suspended in its sludge, a slow record of everything it's eaten."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sections of it glow faintly blue at night, like whatever it fed on hasn't finished breaking down."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Split from a larger mass upstream and is still faintly connected, feeding both bodies at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["spreads slow across a factory floor, steaming faintly where it laps against cooling metal", "pools at the base of a collapsed vat, dissolving a fallen support beam one inch at a time"]},{"name":"Rad-Sick Troll","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Regenerating troll locked in stalemate with its own radiation sickness","flavor":"Its regeneration keeps pace with the radiation eating it, an endless grotesque stalemate.","desc":"Its regeneration works overtime just to keep pace with the radiation actively eating through it, flesh knitting and blistering in the same breath — an endless, grotesque stalemate playing out across its own hide. It's furious, and in visible pain, and neither slows it down.","traits":{"note": "Its regeneration and the radiation eating it are locked in permanent stalemate — neither wins, and neither slows it down.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The troll makes three attacks: one bite and two claws."}, {"name": "Blistered Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (1d6+6) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Radiation Claw", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+6) slashing damage, plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage from irradiated fluid in the wound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin sloughs and re-knits in visible waves, never settling into one shape for long."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids clean water, drinking only from puddles that glow faintly at night."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roars constantly, a low continuous pain-sound that never fully stops."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Claws leave scorched, faintly smoking gouges in whatever they cut."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Regenerates fastest near old reactor sites, drawn there without understanding why."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its blistered hide has hardened into brittle plates that crack and regrow with every heavy blow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sheds fist-sized chunks of glowing flesh mid-fight, each one twitching for minutes afterward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The stalemate is finally tipping — its regeneration can't keep up anymore, and it knows it, and it is done being careful."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "desert"],"activity":["claws at its own blistering hide, flesh knitting shut even as radiation eats through it again", "roars in open pain while lunging at anything that moves, too furious to notice its own wounds"]},{"name":"Piston-Arm Enforcer","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"piston-arm-enforcer","summary":"Salvaged hydraulic-press automaton breaking doors and skulls","flavor":"Salvaged hydraulic press arms bolted onto a walking chassis to break down doors and skulls alike.","desc":"Salvaged hydraulic press arms have been bolted straight onto a walking chassis, built for one purpose and repurposed for another — breaking down doors, and then whatever's standing behind them. The pistons hiss on every swing.","traits":{"note": "Built to break doors, repurposed to break whatever's behind them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The enforcer makes two slam attacks."}, {"name": "Press-Piston Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hisses a burst of steam before every swing, telegraphing its own attacks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was assembled from a warehouse press, arms still bearing factory stencils."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands motionless for hours at its post, only its pistons ticking as they cool."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dents every door it opens identically, a signature its handlers use to track it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Requires fresh hydraulic fluid weekly, leaving oily drip-trails near its post."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Strikes in a fixed four-count rhythm, the same cadence regardless of target or threat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pistons occasionally fire on their own, twitching an arm mid-stillness like a nervous tic."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A pressure fault is building in its main line, and its next big swing might blow the arm clean off."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["stands guard at a warlord's checkpoint, hydraulic arms hissing with every idle flex", "pounds a jammed door open one measured strike at a time, patient as machinery"]},{"name":"Ashborn Wyrmling Mutant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"basilisk","model":"ashborn-wyrmling-mutant","summary":"Mutant reptile whose stare cracks flesh like baked clay","flavor":"A reptile mutated past recognition, its stare leaves flesh cracked like sun-baked clay.","desc":"Mutation has taken this reptile well past anything recognizable, and its stare alone leaves exposed flesh cracked and tightening like sun-baked clay. It watches before it moves, patient in the particular way predators get when they know their gaze already does half the work.","traits":{"note": "Its stare does half the work before it ever strikes.", "actions": [{"name": "Cracked-Clay Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sun-Cracking Gaze", "text": "At the start of each of its turns, the wyrmling chooses one creature within 30 feet that can see its eyes. That target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or its skin begins hardening; it takes 5 (1d10) necrotic damage and its speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rarely moves first, letting prey close the distance out of impatience."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin has gone the color of baked clay, cracking visibly at every joint."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts near collapsed walls, using rubble shadows to break up its silhouette."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blinks slowly and rarely, holding its stare far longer than seems natural."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves sun-cracked footprints in soft ash, permanent as fired ceramic."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its eyes have a faint amber glow at dusk, visible before the rest of it is."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Molted scales left behind hold their shape perfectly, brittle as pottery shards."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Mutation is accelerating — its gaze is starting to crack stone, not just flesh."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["sunbathes atop a slag heap, motionless except for a slow, tracking stare", "coils in the shade of a collapsed wall, watching prey go rigid before it ever moves"]},{"name":"Fallout Wight Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Ghoul squad commander who still remembers military drill","flavor":"Commands a squad of lesser ghouls, the only one who still remembers military drill.","desc":"It commands a loose squad of lesser ghouls with hand signals from some long-dissolved military doctrine, the only one among them who still remembers drill formation. Even rotted through, it keeps its posture rigid, back straight, chin level.","traits":{"note": "Commands lesser ghouls through drill signals; killing it scatters the squad's coordination.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The captain makes two attacks: one with its longsword and one with its longbow, or drains life with one melee attack."}, {"name": "Drill-Sergeant Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken, and the captain regains hit points equal to that amount."}, {"name": "Standard-Issue Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Standard-Issue Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its squad in loose formation even at rest, spacing them by old regulation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes fellow undead with a gesture from a uniform long since rotted away."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects a ghoul's posture mid-shuffle, as if drill still matters to something."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rusted rank insignia fused permanently to what's left of its collar."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Positions itself at the squad's flank rather than the front, old tactical habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Barks orders in clipped, half-intelligible syllables that the ghouls somehow still obey."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Marches in step even when standing perfectly still, boots scraping a rhythm only it hears."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes reinforcements are still inbound, and grows more dangerously certain of it each fight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["drills a squad of shuffling ghouls through hand signals from a doctrine no one else remembers", "stands rigid at a broken checkpoint, chin level, waiting for a relief that will never rotate in"]},{"name":"Bomb-Cult High Priest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"bomb-cult-high-priest","summary":"Fanatic priest praying for a second, holier detonation","flavor":"Preaches that the old bombs were mercy and prays daily for a second, holier blast.","desc":"He preaches from a cracked pulpit that the old bombs were mercy, and prays — daily, sincerely — for a second, holier detonation to finish the work properly. His congregation nods along like this is the most reasonable theology in the world.","traits":{"note": "Genuinely believes detonation is salvation, and preaches it with total sincerity.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The priest makes two attacks with its mace, or uses radiant flame twice."}, {"name": "Sacramental Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) radiant damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Flame", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +6 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (4d6) radiant damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The priest casts a spell, using prayers about mercy and fire as its casting focus."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads a small congregation that guards the pulpit more fiercely than it guards itself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Collects intact detonators as holy relics, displayed on a shrine of scrap."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks to visitors gently, genuinely hoping they'll come to see the mercy of it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times sermons to old radio static, treating the noise as scripture."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a vestment stitched from a decommissioned hazard suit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Ends every sermon counting down from ten, congregation murmuring along in unison."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims the first blast spoke to it directly, and describes the conversation in disturbing, specific detail."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has finished assembling something under the pulpit, and keeps checking a timer no one else can see."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["preaches to a kneeling congregation from a cracked pulpit about the mercy of the old bombs", "prays over a warhead casing like an altar, murmuring for a second, holier detonation"]},{"name":"Furnace-Bound Salamander","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"salamander","model":"furnace-bound-salamander","summary":"Blast-furnace-bound elemental lashing at anyone who opens the door","flavor":"Bound into a scrapyard's blast furnace, it lashes out at anyone who opens the door.","desc":"Bound into a scrapyard's blast furnace by some forgotten ritual, it lashes out through the open door the instant anyone dares approach, flame trailing off its molten hide in long streaks. The furnace itself seems to breathe when it moves.","traits":{"note": "Bound to the furnace itself — it can't leave, but nothing gets past it while the door's open.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The salamander makes two attacks, only one of which can be constrict."}, {"name": "Flame Spear", "replaces": "Flame Spear", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage."}, {"name": "Furnace Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 14) and restrained until the grapple ends."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only lashes out through the exact doorway it's bound to guard, ignoring other approaches."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The furnace breathes visibly when it moves, bellows-plates rising and falling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats into the coals when the door shuts, dormant until it opens again."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorch trails in the exact pattern of old furnace vents."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows more active when the scrapyard's other furnaces are lit nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hide shifts color with the furnace's own heat cycle, dull red to white-hot and back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The binding ritual etched into the furnace door is still faintly warm to the touch, decades on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The binding is failing — the furnace itself is starting to crack outward with every strike it makes."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "elemental"],"activity":["coils inside a blast furnace's belly, hide streaking molten light through the seams", "lashes at the furnace door the instant its hinges creak, ready before anyone steps through"]},{"name":"Scrapfield Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three-headed radiation-fused mutant, each screaming differently","flavor":"Three mutant heads fused by radiation, each screaming a different warning.","desc":"Three heads, each fused wrong by decades of radiation, scream three separate warnings in three separate directions at once — and somehow the body beneath still moves with terrible coordination. No single head seems fully in charge.","traits":{"note": "No single head is fully in charge, but the body still coordinates its attacks.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The chimera makes three attacks: one bite, one claw, and one ram, or uses fire breath instead of its bite."}, {"name": "Rusted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scrap Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Junk-Horn Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Fume-Fire Breath", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One head exhales fire in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head favors a different attack, and it shows in how the body leans before striking."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The three heads sleep in shifts, never all dormant at once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head is noticeably smaller and newer than the other two, still adjusting to the body."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warning shrieks come out of sync, a stuttering three-part alarm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors open scrap fields where all three heads have clear sightlines."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The heads occasionally bite at each other mid-fight, some old rivalry surfacing under stress."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One head has started forming words instead of screams, though nobody can make out what it's saying."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A fourth head is budding at the shoulder, and the other three haven't noticed yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["prowls a junk field with three heads scanning three directions, none quite agreeing on the threat", "circles a downed vehicle, one head snarling while the other two argue over which way to strike"]},{"name":"Diesel Pit Fighter","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"diesel-pit-fighter","summary":"Undefeated warlord's pit champion across nine seasons","flavor":"Champions the fighting pits under a warlord's banner, undefeated across nine seasons.","desc":"Undefeated across nine fighting seasons under a warlord's banner, he enters the pit with the loose, confident shoulders of someone who has stopped being afraid of losing. The crowd already knows how tonight ends; he's just here to make it entertaining.","traits":{"note": "Undefeated across nine seasons — fights for the crowd's entertainment more than survival.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The fighter makes two attacks, one with its rapier and one with its pistol."}, {"name": "Pit Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sidearm Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d10+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plays to the crowd between exchanges, drawing out a fight it could end sooner."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to use the pistol until the crowd is genuinely bored of the blades."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears trophies from nine seasons' worth of defeated challengers stitched into a battered coat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Studies new opponents from the stands before ever agreeing to fight them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Takes a cut of the betting pool as part of the warlord's arrangement."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Talks casually mid-duel, like the fight is a conversation it's mostly already won."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Has started letting weaker challengers land hits on purpose, testing something about itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A rival warlord has posted a bounty on tonight's win, and half the crowd is here for the wrong reasons."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["enters the pit to a roaring crowd, shoulders loose, already reading the challenger's stance", "wipes down a rapier between rounds, unbothered by the blood still on the sand"]},{"name":"Wraith of the Fallout Line","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Dead commuters fused into one hungry drifting shape","flavor":"A commuter train's dead passengers fused into one hungry, drifting shape.","desc":"A commuter train's worth of the dead have fused into one hungry, drifting shape, faces surfacing and submerging in its smoke-thin form like reflections in dirty water. It moves along old rail lines out of habit more than purpose.","traits":{"note": "A whole train's dead fused into one shape — it moves by old habit more than intent.", "actions": [{"name": "Commuter Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 21 (6d6) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken, and the wraith regains hit points equal to that amount."}, {"name": "Create Specter", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The wraith targets a humanoid within 10 feet that died within the last minute. The target's spirit rises as a specter under the wraith's control at the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the exact route the old commuter line ran, station to station, without deviation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slows near platform signs, as if waiting for a train that isn't coming."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faces surface briefly in its smoke when it passes a mirror or standing water."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows agitated near working machinery, drawn to any engine sound."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thins to near-invisibility in daylight, solid only in tunnels and shade."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Murmurs overlapping fragments of old announcements, dozens of voices talking over each other."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One face surfaces more often than the others, as if it remembers being the conductor."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found the line's original terminus, and something about reaching it is making the shape grow."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["drifts along dead rail track out of habit, faces surfacing and fading in its smoke-thin form", "hovers near a rusted platform sign, the ghost of a departure that never came"]},{"name":"Junk-Titan Enforcer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"junk-titan-enforcer","summary":"Warlord's gate guardian that nothing has gotten past","flavor":"Built by a warlord's engineers to guard the compound gate; nothing has yet gotten past it.","desc":"Built by a warlord's own engineers to guard the compound gate, it has stood that post through every siege since — nothing has yet gotten past it, and its posture says it intends to keep that streak.","traits":{"note": "Blocks a specific chokepoint/gate; strongly favors defending terrain over pursuing.", "actions": [{"name": "Gatekeeper", "text": "Gains advantage on attacks against any creature attempting to move past it through its guarded point."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to leave its assigned gate even under direct order, engineered loyalty to the post itself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating carries the dents of every siege it's survived, never repaired, only reinforced."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tracks the warlord's own guards by gait, letting them pass without challenge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Powers down partially at night, waking fully only when the gate mechanism triggers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was built with a second, unused weapon mount that the warlord never finished installing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its footsteps land in the exact same spots each patrol, worn grooves in the ground beneath it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Has started recognizing faces it's seen before, hesitating half a beat longer for repeat visitors."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The warlord who built it is dead, and it hasn't been told — it's still guarding a chain of command that no longer exists."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["stands fixed at a compound gate, plating groaning with every shift of its stance", "blocks a breach in the wall bodily, fists ready, having never once let anything through"]},{"name":"Toxin-Blood Oni Raider","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"toxin-blood-oni-raider","summary":"Chem-warped raider brute whose own blood is a weapon","flavor":"A brute of a raider warped by chem exposure until its blood itself became a weapon.","desc":"Chem exposure warped this brute of a raider until its own blood turned into a weapon, dark and faintly smoking wherever it's spilled. It fights recklessly, almost inviting a cut, like it knows the wound works both ways.","traits":{"note": "Its blood is a weapon too, so wounding it in melee has a cost.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The raider makes three attacks: two with its claw and one with nightmare ray, or uses spellcasting in place of one claw."}, {"name": "Toxin Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage."}, {"name": "Nightmare Ray", "replaces": "Nightmare Ray", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +6 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (4d6) psychic damage, and the target has disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Shape-Shift", "replaces": "Shape-Shift", "text": "The raider magically polymorphs into a Small or Medium humanoid, or back into its true form."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The raider casts a spell, its blood smoking faintly as it does."}, {"name": "Blood-Weapon Riposte", "text": "When a creature hits the raider with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it, the raider can use its reaction to splash toxic blood at the attacker, who must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 9 (2d8) poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights bare-armed on purpose, using its own blood as a deterrent against grapples."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads raids from the front, testing new recruits by how close they'll stand to it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scars have gone dark and glossy, permanently weeping faint smoke."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks territory with splashes of its own blood, warning off rival warbands."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears minimal armor by choice, treating exposed skin as an offensive asset."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Licks a fresh wound mid-fight, as if tasting whether the chem-warp is still working."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims it can smell fear as a chemical, and adjusts its attacks toward whoever's most afraid."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The chem-warp is spreading past the blood now — its whole hide is starting to smoke when struck."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["wades into a fight bare-armed, inviting a cut like the wound works both ways", "stalks a raiding line's flank, blood smoking faintly where an old scab has cracked open"]},{"name":"Scrap-Hound Alpha","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"scrap-hound-alpha","summary":"Scrap-hound pack alpha with ash-stained frost-white fur","flavor":"Leads a scrap-hound pack, frost-white fur stained ash-grey from the wastes.","desc":"Frost-white fur has gone ash-grey with wasteland grime, and it holds itself apart from the pack it leads, watching before committing. When it finally moves, the rest of the pack moves with it, a beat behind, perfectly timed.","traits":{"note": "The pack moves a beat behind it, perfectly timed — killing the alpha scatters their coordination.", "actions": [{"name": "Alpha Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Frost-Ash Breath", "replaces": "Cold Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The alpha exhales a blast of frost in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a DC 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Watches every hunt from a distance first, never the first to commit to the chase."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur has gone patchy ash-grey over the original frost-white, permanent wasteland grime."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads a pack of four to six lesser hounds, all visibly deferring to it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks territory with frost-burn scars on nearby trees or posts."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rarely uses its breath weapon on lone prey, saving it for coordinated pack hunts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Communicates with the pack in short, precisely timed huffs rather than barking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its breath leaves patches of true winter frost that linger for hours in the ash heat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The pack has grown to a dozen strong under it, and it's started testing them against bigger prey."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "hill", "any"],"activity":["watches its pack from a rise, timing the exact moment to commit to a hunt", "trots ahead of a scrap-hound pack, ash-grey fur bristling at a scent on the wind"]},{"name":"Vault Door Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Animated blast-door guardian of a vault long since emptied","flavor":"An entire blast door animated by pre-collapse tech, still guarding a vault long since emptied.","desc":"An entire blast door has been animated by pre-collapse tech, still standing sentinel over a vault long since stripped bare by others. It doesn't know, or doesn't care, that there's nothing left inside worth guarding.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Functionally immobile guardian bound to its vault entrance; overwhelming to fight head-on."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sweeps the same fixed patrol path through the vault chamber, never varying its route."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears the vault's original serial markings, still legible under decades of rust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts to any tampering with the vault mechanism as a direct threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves ponderously slow but never stops once it commits to a target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still displays a faded keypad on its chest, long since inert."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Emits a low mechanical hum that changes pitch depending on how close intruders get."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally 'locks' mid-fight, freezing in a sealed stance as if some old routine just ran."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something inside the emptied vault has started responding to its patrol pattern, and it isn't the golem."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["stands sentinel in a stripped vault chamber, unaware there's nothing left inside to protect", "grinds forward on hinges the size of a man, still enforcing an order that no longer matters"]},{"name":"Warlord's Bodyguard","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"warlords-bodyguard","summary":"Silent armored bodyguard loyal only to whoever rules","flavor":"Silent, armored, loyal only to whoever currently holds the warlord's seat.","desc":"Silent, armored head to foot, loyalty riding entirely on whoever currently holds the warlord's seat rather than any person in particular. It stands a half-step behind its charge, watching hands, not faces.","traits":{"note": "Loyalty rides on the seat, not the person — a new warlord inherits the same silence.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The bodyguard makes two attacks, one with its shortsword and one with its light crossbow."}, {"name": "Silent Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) piercing damage, plus 7 (2d6) piercing damage if the target hasn't acted yet this combat."}, {"name": "Light Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +6 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never speaks in front of its charge, communicating only in small gestures."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has served three different warlords without visible loyalty to any of them personally."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scans every new room's exits and sightlines before its charge steps inside."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears armor stripped from a rival's dead honor guard, unbothered by the source."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Positions itself between its charge and any raised voice, reflexively."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its mask has been welded shut, and no one currently serving has seen the face beneath it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refers to itself only as 'the seat,' as if its own identity dissolved into the role years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The current warlord suspects the bodyguard would serve whoever kills them next, and hasn't said so out loud yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["stands a half-step behind its charge, watching hands in the crowd rather than faces", "sweeps a room's exits before the warlord ever enters, silent and thorough"]},{"name":"Contagion Ghast Broodkeeper","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"contagion-ghast-broodkeeper","summary":"Rot-spreading undead cultivating new ghouls like crops","flavor":"Spreads its rot deliberately, cultivating new ghouls the way a farmer tends a field.","desc":"It spreads its rot with deliberate care, tending fresh ghouls the way a farmer tends rows of crops, walking a slow circuit to check on each one. There's a horrible patience to how methodically it works.","traits":{"note": "Cultivates new ghouls deliberately — killing it may leave a half-grown brood behind.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The broodkeeper makes two attacks: one claw and one bite."}, {"name": "Cultivating Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d4+4) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Infectious Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) piercing damage. If the target is a humanoid reduced to 0 hit points by this attack, it must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or rise as a ghoul under the broodkeeper's control in 1d4 days."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tends a fixed patch of rot-field, returning to the same rows of half-turned corpses daily."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with unnerving calm, never rushing even when threatened."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its brood spaced apart deliberately, like rows in a garden."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizes which ghouls are 'ready' and which need more time, by some private measure."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly sweet rather than rotten, a wrongness scavengers learn to flag."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums a slow, tuneless little song while making its rounds, as if the work is soothing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the half-turned corpses by name, names it couldn't possibly know."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The rot-field is nearly ready to turn all at once, and the broodkeeper is visibly, patiently waiting for harvest."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "urban"],"activity":["walks a slow circuit through a rot-field, checking on fresh ghouls the way a farmer checks crops", "presses rotted fingers into a still-twitching corpse, tending the infection with horrible patience"]},{"name":"Detonation Engineer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"detonation-engineer","summary":"Bomb-cult engineer half-mad with reactor-core warhead math","flavor":"Designs the Bomb-Cult's warheads from scavenged reactor cores, half-mad with the maths of it.","desc":"Reactor-core scrap is laid out across a workbench in precise, obsessive rows, and he mutters warhead math under his breath, half-mad with the elegance of it. He looks up at intruders the way a man looks up from an equation he was about to solve.","traits":{"note": "May be rigging an active device in the scene; interrupting the work matters more than fighting him directly.", "actions": [{"name": "Dead Man's Math", "text": "If reduced to 0 HP, can trigger a final rigged charge as a reaction before dying."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps meticulous notes on warhead yield, revised in the margins a dozen times over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Treats interruptions to his math as the real insult, more than any attack."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surrounds his workbench with salvaged reactor cores, arranged by decay rate."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks to intruders in equations first, threats second, if at all."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears lead-lined gloves religiously, the one safety measure he takes seriously."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Solves problems out loud in a running mutter that never quite stops, even mid-combat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists the math is almost finished, and has insisted that for what sounds like years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes he's solved it this time, and the workbench behind him is very obviously counting down."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["arranges reactor scrap into obsessive rows across a workbench, muttering warhead math under his breath", "looks up from a half-solved equation with the mild irritation of someone interrupted mid-thought"]},{"name":"Iron Convoy Behemoth","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"iron-convoy-behemoth","summary":"War-rig hauler plated with scrap from a dozen dead vehicles","flavor":"A war-rig hauled by an animated chassis, plating scavenged from a dozen dead vehicles.","desc":"An animated chassis hauls a war-rig forward under plating scavenged from a dozen dead vehicles, each panel a different color, a different make, welded into one grinding whole. The ground shudders under its tread before it's even close.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive Construct; can ram/crush terrain or lighter obstacles in its path."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating shows a dozen mismatched paint jobs, welded together without any attempt to match colors."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hauls the same war-rig every route, cargo unknown to anyone outside the warlord's inner circle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at a fixed, grinding pace that never speeds up, even in a fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sheds loose bolts and scrap in its wake, a trail easy to follow at a distance."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Requires a full crew to steer, riding atop its chassis rather than controlling it alone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Groans in a low metal creak with every step, audible minutes before it's visible."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One panel still bears a child's handprint in paint, salvaged from a vehicle whose story no one asks about."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The war-rig it hauls carries cargo the warlord wants back badly enough to send this thing alone."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "urban"],"activity":["hauls a grinding war-rig forward, plating from a dozen dead vehicles clattering against each other", "idles at a checkpoint, ground shuddering under its tread before it's even come to a full stop"]},{"name":"Fallout Hydra Broodhorror","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Hydra whose severed heads regrow ever more mutated","flavor":"Each severed head regrows twisted differently, mutation compounding mutation.","desc":"Each severed head regrows twisted differently than the last, mutation compounding on mutation until no two heads share the same jaw or the same eyes. It hisses out of several mouths at once, none of them quite agreeing on the sound.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Regrows heads when severed, each subsequent head potentially gaining a new minor mutation/trait."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head has a visibly different mutation, no two sharing jaw shape or eye count."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers flooded ruins, where its many heads can each track a different sound across the water."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Heads hiss in staggered, overlapping bursts rather than in unison."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head is noticeably paler and newer, still growing into its own mutation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scattered shed scales that mutate independently for hours after falling off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The heads seem to compete for the first strike, snapping at each other as much as at prey."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A regrown head has developed something like a working eye where a mouth should be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's been fed something recently that's making the regrowth accelerate mid-fight, heads budding as it bleeds."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["hisses from several mouths at once, none of them agreeing on the same sound", "wades through a flooded ruin, heads swaying independently as if scouting different threats"]},{"name":"Cinderfall Vampire Warlord","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"cinderfall-vampire-warlord","summary":"Undead warlord feeding on survivors of settlements it razes","flavor":"Feeds on the survivors of the settlements it razes, then rules the ashes it leaves.","desc":"It feeds on the survivors of the settlements it razes, then settles onto whatever throne is left standing in the ashes to rule what's left. There's no urgency to the feeding — it has learned the world keeps producing more.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Regains hit points on successfully draining a victim; commands local undead/raiders it has claimed."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feeds slowly and deliberately, treating survivors as a resource to ration, not a frenzy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Claims the highest intact structure in any razed settlement as a throne."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a warband loyal through fear rather than payment, and it works fine."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never razes a settlement fully, always leaving just enough alive to feed on later."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears jewelry looted from a dozen different fallen settlements, each piece a small trophy."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Speaks to feeding victims almost gently, as if courtesy costs it nothing at this point."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists it remembers every settlement it's razed by name, and recites them like a private liturgy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has started marking future targets in advance, and this settlement's turn is already circled."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["settles onto a scavenged throne amid smoking rubble, feeding unhurried on a razed settlement's last survivors", "watches its warband finish a raid from a rooftop, in no rush because the world keeps producing more"]},{"name":"Bunker-Bred Nightmare Steed","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"bunker-bred-nightmare-steed","summary":"Cult general's steed scorching ash-fields with every charge","flavor":"A cult general's mount, hooves scorching whatever ash-field it charges across.","desc":"Hooves leave scorched prints across whatever ash-field it charges through, smoke trailing off a mane that never quite stops smoldering. A cult general rides it into every engagement, and the horse seems to enjoy the work as much as the rider.","traits":{"note": "Its hoofprints/wake can ignite flammable terrain."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorched hoofprints that stay hot to the touch for hours afterward."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only fully calm around its rider, skittish and dangerous to anyone else."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mane smolders constantly, a low steady smoke even at rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Paws restlessly before a charge, like it's savoring the anticipation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers open ash-fields where it can build to a full charge unobstructed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Snorts embers instead of breath when agitated, small sparks scattering on the wind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Casts two shadows in firelight, one a half-step behind the other."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has thrown its rider twice this week and shows no sign of accepting a replacement quietly."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "planar"],"activity":["charges across an ash-field, hooves leaving scorched prints and smoke trailing off a mane that never stops smoldering", "waits saddled outside a cult compound, ash swirling around hooves that never quite touch the ground"]},{"name":"Reactor Wyrm","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Bedrock-burrowing wyrm glowing hot from irradiated feeding","flavor":"Burrows through irradiated bedrock, its hide glowing hot from what it's fed on.","desc":"It burrows through irradiated bedrock with a slow, grinding hunger, hide glowing dull orange-hot from decades of feeding on whatever leaked down from the reactors above. The ground warms noticeably before it ever breaks the surface.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can burrow and resurface elsewhere; radiant/fire-adjacent heat aura."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Burrows in slow, predictable loops around old reactor foundations."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hide glows brighter after longer stretches underground, dimming slowly in open air."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces rarely, preferring to strike from beneath rather than fully emerge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorched, glassy tunnels behind it, fused stone from the heat of its passing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows sluggish in cold ash-storms, more active in the heat of open day."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The ground doesn't just warm before it surfaces — it hums, a low vibration scavengers have learned to feel through their boots."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Chunks of its molten hide occasionally slough off and keep glowing, faintly radioactive, for days."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's tunneled directly beneath an active settlement, and the ground there is getting warmer by the day."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["deeplands", "cave", "ruins"],"activity":["burrows through irradiated bedrock with a slow, grinding hunger, hide glowing dull orange-hot", "surfaces briefly near an old reactor site, ground warming for minutes before it ever breaks through"]},{"name":"Grand Warlord's Champion","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"grand-warlords-champion","summary":"Undefeated champion who fought a hundred duels for command","flavor":"Fought a hundred duels to earn the right to lead the largest warband in the ash flats.","desc":"A hundred duels earned this one the right to lead the largest warband in the ash flats, and every scar across an unbeaten frame tells part of that story. He fights like a man who has genuinely never needed a plan B.","traits":{"note": "Earned command through a hundred personal duels — the warband follows the winner, not a title.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The champion makes two attacks, one with its greataxe and one with its javelin."}, {"name": "Champion's Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 18 (2d12+5) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warband Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Weapon Attack: +9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Undefeated Fury", "text": "Once per turn when the champion hits a creature with a melee weapon attack, it can choose to make the attack a critical hit, provided it has not yet taken damage this combat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights bare-chested by choice, letting every scar from a hundred duels be seen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on one-on-one terms whenever a challenge is offered, refusing help from the warband."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rewards a good fight even in defeat, occasionally sparing a challenger who impressed it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the greataxe of the rival it beat for command, unused, as a trophy on display."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises its voice, letting a hundred duels' reputation do the intimidating."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Studies challengers with a calm, almost bored patience before ever engaging."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims to remember every duel by feel rather than sight, and fights newcomers the same way."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A rival has finally assembled a warband large enough to challenge for command outright, and the champion knows it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["stands at the head of the largest warband in the ash flats, scars telling half the story of a hundred duels", "spars a volunteer for sport, fighting with the loose confidence of someone who's never needed a plan B"]},{"name":"Ash-Frost Colossus","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Nuclear-winter mutant with ash-snow-crusted fur and endless hunger","flavor":"A nuclear-winter mutant, matted fur crusted in ash-snow, hungry beyond reason.","desc":"A nuclear-winter mutation left its fur matted and crusted white with ash-snow, breath fogging thick even in the mild wasteland heat. Hunger drives it past reason — it doesn't stop advancing once it's decided you're food.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Cold-adjacent damage on attacks; relentless pursuit, rarely disengages."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur has matted into thick plates of ash-snow that crack when it moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Advances at a slow, unstoppable pace once locked onto prey, never breaking into a run."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breath fogs visibly thick even in mild wasteland heat, a permanent nuclear-winter chill."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hoards nothing but food, stockpiling frozen carcasses in ice-packed dens."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves deep prints that stay frosted for days after it's passed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its hunger sounds almost pained, a low groaning growl that never fully stops."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Ash and snow cling to it in patterns that never quite melt, even near open flame."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Hasn't eaten in what looks like weeks, and its restraint is visibly, dangerously running out."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["hill", "mountain", "arctic"],"activity":["advances through an ash-snow drift, breath fogging thick, hunger driving it past any reason to stop", "hurls chunks of packed ice at anything moving below its ridge, matted fur crusted white"]},{"name":"Grid-Fed Iron Sentinel","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Grid-wired automaton drawing endless trickle current","flavor":"Still wired to a dead power grid, drawing a trickle of current that keeps it standing forever.","desc":"Cables still run from its chassis into a dead power grid somewhere beneath the ruins, drawing an endless faint trickle of current that keeps it standing long after everything else in the district failed. It has no reason to ever stop.","traits":{"hp": "high", "ac": "high", "note": "Effectively tireless while connected to its grid source; disconnecting it may be a viable tactic."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust streaks its joints, but the cables still hum with current when it moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chassis is scorched black on one side from an old fight it clearly won."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in slow, deliberate steps, tethered cables dragging taut behind it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sparks spit from a cracked panel every few strides, lighting the dust around its feet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted warband sigils cover its plating, layered over older, scraped-off ones."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its cable trails far longer than it should, snaking off into a buried tunnel unseen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The current running through it hums in a pattern that almost sounds like counting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When its cable finally snaps, the discharge it releases lights the whole junction white."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Standing motionless at a substation junction, cables trailing into buried conduit", "Patrolling a fixed perimeter around the dead grid node it's still wired to"]},{"name":"Vaultbreaker Behemoth","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"vaultbreaker-behemoth","summary":"Mutant giant that cracks vault doors bare-handed","flavor":"A mutated giant that cracks vault doors open bare-handed for the warband behind it.","desc":"Bare-handed, it wrenches vault doors off their hinges for the warband trailing behind it, tossing steel aside like it weighs nothing. It works with the bored efficiency of a laborer who's cracked this same door a hundred times before.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can force open barriers/doors as a mundane action; strength-based grapple favored."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-job, three warband scavengers crouched behind it waiting on the door to give."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A half-cracked vault door hangs from one hinge where it stopped to rest an arm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a satchel of pried locks and hinge-pins as trophies from other jobs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its handler's whistle-chain lies coiled nearby, the only thing that calls it off a job."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scavenger crew shadows it at a careful distance, waiting to loot what it opens."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already cracked this same vault twice before and clearly remembers doing it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It pauses to listen at the door before every pull, like it's checking for something inside."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whatever's behind this door was worth sealing twice over, and it just found the second lock."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["Prying a vault door from its frame while a warband waits impatiently behind it", "Testing a steel hinge with one massive thumb, gauging how much force it'll take"]},{"name":"Deathwatch Cult Oracle","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"deathwatch-cult-oracle","summary":"Preserved oracle still interpreting a countdown only it hears","flavor":"Preserved by cult ritual to keep interpreting the countdown only it can still hear.","desc":"Ritual preservation has kept this thing upright long past any natural span, its hollow voice interpreting a countdown that only it can still hear, muttering numbers that never seem to reach zero. It speaks in fragments, as if translating from somewhere else entirely.","traits":{"note": "Prophetic mutterings can be used as in-fiction hints/omens the DM voices mid-combat."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dozen kneeling cultists ring the chapel floor, hanging on every number it whispers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wax and old blood pool at its feet from offerings left by believers who never returned."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cracked ledger nearby records every number it's spoken since the ritual began."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A frightened new acolyte is being led toward it for a first, formal listening."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The shrine around it is decorated entirely in salvaged countdown clocks, all stopped."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stops muttering the instant a stranger enters, as if the count only matters unheard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The number it's currently on hasn't changed in the three days locals have been counting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in its chant just shifted, and every cultist in the room went silent at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Muttering a countdown to a small ring of kneeling cultists in a gutted chapel", "Standing motionless at a shrine, mouth moving through numbers no one else can hear"]},{"name":"Blightborn Roc","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"blightborn-roc","summary":"Radiation-grown carrion bird whose shadow panics settlements","flavor":"A carrion bird grown monstrous on radioactive corpses, its shadow alone panics a settlement.","desc":"Its shadow alone is enough to send a settlement running for cover — a carrion bird grown monstrous on a diet of radioactive corpses, wingspan blotting out whole streets at a time. It circles once before it commits to a dive.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive wingspan grants area-effect wind/knockback on landing or takeoff."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers have gone patchy and grey, radiation burns showing through in ugly bands."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye has clouded milk-white, but it hunts by shadow and sound just as well."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It nests on the exposed girders of a collapsed tower, half-eaten prey scattered below."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scars crosshatch its underside from old fights with warband anti-air crews."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its talons drag old fencing wire, snagged from some rooftop it swept clean."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to time its dives to when settlement watch-bells go quiet at shift change."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A faint blue static crackles off its wingtips every time it beats them hard."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's hunting in a pair today, the second shadow only visible once the first one commits."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["Circling low over a settlement's rooftops, shadow sweeping the streets below", "Tearing into a bloated corpse atop a collapsed tower, feathers matted with ash"]},{"name":"Ash Warlord's Marilith Enforcer","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"Bound fiend running security for a warlord's court","flavor":"A fiend bound into service by an ancient bargain, now runs security for a warlord's court.","desc":"Bound by some ancient bargain into permanent service, it now runs security for a warlord's court with the same cold competence it likely once brought to darker business. Multiple arms move independently, each tracking a different threat in the room.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple weapon-bearing arms can each attack independently in a round."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-interrogation, a captive strapped to a chair and answering faster than expected."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ledger of the warlord's enemies rests at its station, half its names crossed out."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Six arms rest folded at once, each twitching independently toward a different exit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A junior guard nervously delivers orders to it, clearly terrified of being noticed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands exactly where the last three assassination attempts against the warlord failed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It answers questions about its own binding with total, disinterested honesty."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of its arms moves half a second before the rest, like it's reacting to something else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The soul-tome that binds it just changed hands, and it hasn't decided who it serves now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Standing sentry at a warlord's court, extra limbs tracking every entrance at once", "Interrogating a captive in a side chamber, voice flat and utterly without malice"]},{"name":"Devouring Junkyard Kraken","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"devouring-junkyard-kraken","summary":"Tentacled scrapyard-pit mutant born of decades of chemicals","flavor":"Lives beneath a scrapyard's flooded pit, tentacled from decades of chemical mutation.","desc":"Decades of chemical mutation gave it tentacles where a scrapyard's flooded pit should have had nothing living at all. It surfaces slow, oil-slick water sheeting off its hide, testing the air before committing to an attack.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Multiple grappling tentacle attacks; strongly territorial to its flooded pit."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide is streaked with rainbow chemical sheen, oil-slick and faintly luminous."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old car parts are fused into its tentacle bases, half-absorbed after years submerged."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only when the scrapyard goes quiet, testing the air before committing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust-colored foam trails every tentacle it drags across the pit's oily surface."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes have fused shut entirely, replaced by clusters of twitching feeler-stalks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned the sound of a truck engine means an easy meal is about to arrive."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Chunks of half-dissolved machinery still churn visibly inside its translucent flank."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The pit level is dropping fast, and it's surfacing farther from the water than ever before."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["Surfacing slow from a flooded scrapyard pit, oil-black water sheeting off its hide", "Dragging a snagged truck chassis under, tentacles wrapped tight around the frame"]},{"name":"The Countdown Keeper","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"the-countdown-keeper","summary":"Preserved cult figurehead whispering an endless final number","flavor":"An ancient cult figurehead, preserved by dogma, still whispering the final number.","desc":"Dogma alone has preserved this ancient cult figurehead, whose hollow voice keeps whispering a final number that never seems to arrive. Followers still gather to listen, certain that whatever's coming will validate every sacrifice they've made getting here.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; whispered 'countdown' functions as an in-fiction omen device the DM can voice.", "actions": [{"name": "The Final Number", "text": "Once per encounter, can impose a lingering dread effect on all who hear it speak, unsettling their next roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A full congregation kneels around it, murmuring along with numbers they've memorized wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A newly-arrived pilgrim is being walked to the front, trembling, for a first listening."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stopped clocks line every wall of the shrine, each one gifted by a dying believer."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival preacher has arrived to challenge its authority over the countdown publicly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its oldest follower, blind and ancient, insists she's heard the number change twice now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It repeats the same three numbers on a loop, never quite reaching what comes after."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every clock in the shrine ticks once, in perfect unison, whenever the Keeper inhales."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The number just changed, out loud, for the first time in the congregation's memory."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Presiding over a gathered congregation, hollow voice whispering a number that never lands", "Floating motionless above a shrine of stopped clocks, followers kneeling in total silence"]},{"name":"The Warlord Ascendant","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"the-warlord-ascendant","summary":"Warlord who united every ash-flat gang through pure fear","flavor":"United every warband in the ash flats under one banner through fear alone.","desc":"Every warband in the ash flats answers to him now, united not by loyalty but by a fear he cultivated personally, warband by warband, for years. He doesn't raise his voice to be obeyed — the reputation does that work for him.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; commands loyalty across the realm's raider factions as reinforcements.", "actions": [{"name": "United Under Fear", "text": "Can call in additional raider allies to the fight once per encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Envoys from three settlements kneel with tribute, none daring to speak first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captured rival warlord is being paraded past him in chains as a public lesson."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His lieutenants argue quietly over succession, careful never to do it in his hearing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement's entire water ration for the season sits stacked and waiting on his word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He listens to a report on a stolen convoy without once raising his voice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He remembers every warband leader's name and exactly how he broke each of them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow seems to lag a half-second behind his own movements, unnoticed by his court."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "A warband just defected to him mid-negotiation, unprompted, out of pure inherited fear."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["Holding court over a dozen warbands, voice barely above a murmur", "Reviewing tribute laid at his feet by envoys too frightened to look up"]},{"name":"The Fallout Titan","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"the-fallout-titan","summary":"Mountain-sized mutant mistaken for terrain until it moves","flavor":"A mutation so vast it's mistaken for a mountain until it stands up.","desc":"It's easy to mistake for a mountain ridge until the ridge stands up, ash sliding off shoulders the size of a building, and the whole horizon seems to shift with it. By the time you realize what you've been walking toward, it's already looking down at you.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; area-of-effect stomp/collapse attacks appropriate to its scale.", "actions": [{"name": "Groundshaker", "text": "A single stomp can knock prone and damage everyone within a wide radius."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ash has drifted into permanent dunes along its shoulders, undisturbed for years at a time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small structures and dead trees still cling to it, mistaken for terrain by nesting birds."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footprints have become landmarks, each one a small crater full of standing rainwater."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hasn't moved from this stretch of desert in longer than any living scavenger remembers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A road crew mistook it for a hill and built a highway marker directly into its foot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only stirs when something disturbs the ground directly beneath its resting stance."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its joints groan with a resonance that reads on old radio bands as a slow, steady pulse."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's finally taken its first step in a generation, and the whole horizon is shifting with it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Standing motionless on the horizon, mistaken for a ridge until the ridge moves", "Wading through a dead town, buildings crumbling under each unhurried footstep"]},{"name":"The Last Detonation","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"the-last-detonation","summary":"Warhead-core chassis built to finish what first bombs started","flavor":"A warhead-core walking chassis the Bomb-Cult built to finish what the first bombs started.","desc":"The Bomb-Cult built this walking chassis around a live warhead core, meant to finish whatever the first bombs left undone. It moves with a deliberate, unhurried gait — there's no reason for it to hurry when it's this certain of the outcome.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; can detonate as a last resort, dealing catastrophic area damage.", "actions": [{"name": "Unfinished Business", "text": "On being reduced to 0 HP, can trigger a massive area detonation before going inert."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's walking a fixed patrol route the Bomb-Cult mapped out for it generations ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cult handler follows at a respectful distance, logging its heading in a worn ledger."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plating bears a hand-painted countdown that the cult repaints fresh every season."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement has evacuated ahead of its route, leaving the streets eerily bare."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses at old blast markers, as if orienting itself against a memory of the first bombs."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It never deviates from its path, walking through structures rather than around them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ticking under its plating has been speeding up, almost imperceptibly, for weeks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The Bomb-Cult just declared its route complete, and it has stopped walking for the first time."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Advancing at a slow, unhurried gait toward a settlement, core ticking faintly under its plating", "Standing sentinel over a Bomb-Cult shrine, warhead casing humming with contained heat"]},{"name":"The Glass Sea Wyrm","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"Ancient leviathan swimming the vitrified glass flats","flavor":"Older than the warbands, it swims the vitrified glass flats where the first blast struck.","desc":"Older than every warband hunting these flats, it swims through vitrified glass where the first blast struck the ground and fused the sand solid. The glass ripples around its passage like water, catching the light in long, silent waves.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; swims/burrows through glassed terrain as though it were liquid.", "actions": [{"name": "Glass Wake", "text": "Its movement through glassed ground can shear and damage anything caught in its wake."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales are fused with shards of vitrified glass, catching the light in slow-moving glints."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only at dawn, gliding through the flats before the heat sets in for the day."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old convoy wreckage litters its usual hunting ground, half-melted into the glass itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves long, rippling scars across the flats wherever it's passed beneath the surface."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its passage sounds like a bell struck underwater, carrying for miles across the glass."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Warband scouts have learned to read its wake and reroute convoys around it entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something about its scale pattern matches, exactly, a blast-shadow burned into the glass nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's surfaced fully today, for the first time anyone can recall, and the flats are cracking wide."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "any", "deeplands"],"activity":["Rippling through the vitrified glass flats, light catching along its passage in long silent waves", "Surfacing beneath a scavenger convoy, glass cracking outward from its rising bulk"]},{"name":"Chittergaunt","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"pack-hunting mutant scavenger, calls its litter","flavor":"A hairless, twitchy thing that runs on all fours and screeches to call its litter-mates in; harmless alone, a real problem in a pack of six.","desc":"Hairless and twitchy, it moves low on all fours in short, jerking bursts, screeching a high thin call the instant it spots easy prey. Alone it's barely a threat — the danger is that the screech is never really meant to be answered alone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Feeding Proboscis", "replaces": "Proboscis", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 4 (1d4+2) piercing damage, and the Chittergaunt attaches to the target. While attached, it drains 3 (1d4+1) hit points at the start of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hairless and twitchy, it darts between rubble piles in short, jerking bursts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its screech carries a strange, almost apologetic rasp near the end of each call."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One is already latched onto a dead rat, feeding fast before its litter arrives."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred knuckle-pads on its forelimbs suggest this one's survived more than one fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It freezes mid-stride at the sound of footsteps, weighing whether to call the others."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one hunts alone, its litter-call gone hoarse or its litter simply gone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It won't approach a patch of scorched ground, circling wide around it every time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its screech just changed pitch mid-call, and the rubble around it is starting to shift."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["Skittering low across broken pavement, head cocked toward the nearest sound", "Screeching a thin call from a rubble pile, waiting for litter-mates to answer"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: irradiated pack-scavenger, stock post-apoc creature type (not tied to any franchise)"},{"name":"Rustfang","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"scrap-fused mutant guard-dog","flavor":"A dog (or what was a dog) with fused metal shrapnel grown into its hide from decades denned in a scrapyard; bites like a bear trap.","desc":"Shrapnel has grown directly into its hide after decades denned in a scrapyard, jagged metal fused seamlessly with matted fur along its spine. Its bite lands with the crushing, locking pressure of a bear trap rather than an animal's jaw.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Twin Snap", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Rustfang makes two Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape DC 12) with a crushing, locking bite."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Jagged shrapnel juts from its spine, fused seamlessly with matted, filthy fur."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles a denning site marked with older bones, guarding the entrance jealously."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw clamps shut on discarded metal just to test the grip, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust stains streak down its muzzle from a wound that never quite finished healing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces a tight loop around a den mouth, growling low at anything that nears."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's learned to go quiet before it charges, losing the telltale growl entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The metal fused into its hide hums faintly whenever it passes near old wiring."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Three more are denned just out of sight, and this one just caught your scent."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Prowling the edge of a scrapyard den, shrapnel-studded hide catching the light", "Gnawing on a length of rebar, testing the bite it's grown into its own jaw"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: junkyard guard-beast gone wrong"},{"name":"Waste Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"road-gang footsoldier, fights in packs","flavor":"Sun-blistered, tattooed with the mile-markers of every settlement they've burned; fights in a screaming knot with two or three others.","desc":"Sun-blistered skin bears crude tattoos marking the mile-markers of every settlement this crew has burned, a walking ledger of the road behind them. They never fight alone — two or three more close in fast, already screaming before contact.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Mile-Marker Blade", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Scavenged Bolt-Thrower", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two more raiders lounge nearby, already reaching for weapons at the first sign of trouble."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh tattoos mark a settlement burned only days ago, still dark against sun-blistered skin."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stolen wagon sits half-unloaded behind them, cargo still being sorted for value."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One argues loudly with another over who gets first pick of a captive's belongings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've set an ambush at a choke point, confident no one checks this stretch of road."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This crew never fights fair, always closing from two directions before a target notices."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One tattoo among them matches a settlement that, as far as anyone knows, never existed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They're already screaming and charging before you've finished deciding what to do."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["Lounging at a roadside checkpoint, scanning the horizon for an easy convoy", "Sharpening a scimitar against a rock, already eyeing a caravan two dunes off"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-gang footsoldier archetype: post-collapse road-warrior stock type"},{"name":"Cult Acolyte, Bomb-Struck","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"warhead-relic zealot, suicidal devotion","flavor":"Wears a rusted warhead casing like a holy relic and prays to the flash that reshaped the world; will walk into obvious death singing.","desc":"A rusted warhead casing hangs from their neck like a holy relic, polished smooth by years of reverent handling. They pray to the flash that reshaped the world with total sincerity, and will walk straight into obvious death mid-hymn if the moment calls for it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blessed Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-prayer, warhead casing pressed to its chest, oblivious to anything nearby."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hymn sheet in its pocket lists names of settlements it hopes will be next to burn."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's leading a small procession of similarly-devoted acolytes toward a shrine ahead."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's marking a wall with chalk numbers, adding to a countdown someone else started."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A half-eaten ration sits abandoned nearby, forgotten mid-meal for the sake of prayer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It sings louder the closer danger gets, treating the fight itself as a kind of hymn."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The warhead casing around its neck is warm to the touch, though it shouldn't be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's already walking calmly toward you, mid-hymn, sickle raised without any hesitation."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Kneeling before a rusted warhead casing, praying to the flash that reshaped everything", "Wandering a dead street humming a hymn, sickle loose in one trembling hand"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: doomsday-worship footsoldier, stock post-apoc type"},{"name":"Bleached Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"radiation-sick feral scavenger, not truly undead-lore","flavor":"Not undead by ritual but by dose — the radiation cooked the mind out and left hunger behind; skin cracked like dry riverbed, eyes milk-white.","desc":"This isn't undeath by ritual — it's undeath by dose, radiation cooking the mind clean out and leaving only hunger behind. Skin has cracked like a dry riverbed, eyes gone milk-white, and it moves with the jerking persistence of something that forgot how to stop.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Frenzied Bite and Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The ghoul makes one Bite attack and one Claw attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 6 (2d4+1) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 6 (2d4+1) slashing damage. If the target is not undead, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin cracked like a dry riverbed, it lurches forward in short, jerking bursts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its milk-white eyes track sound more than sight, head tilting at every scuff of boot."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old work clothes hang off it in tatters, hinting at whatever job it had before the dose."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It claws mindlessly at a locked door, forgetting entirely that doors can be opened."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint chemical stink clings to it, stronger than the usual reek of rot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It moves in a tight loop around one spot, like the memory of a routine outlives the mind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flinches, every time, from a specific direction, like something there still frightens it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Three more shamble out of the ruins behind it, drawn by the same scent it's chasing."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "urban"],"activity":["Shambling in jerking bursts across cracked ground, milk-white eyes fixed on nothing", "Clawing at dry riverbed dirt with cracked hands, hunger overriding any other instinct"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"irradiated-ghoul archetype: our own fallout-sickness take, distinct from any undead-ghoul lore or franchise ghoul design"},{"name":"Junk Crawler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"debris-heap creature that devours metal","flavor":"A drift of rebar and car doors that somehow walks and somehow wants your rifle barrel more than your blood.","desc":"A drift of rebar and car doors somehow shifts and walks, scraping across broken pavement with a sound like a landslide in slow motion. It wants the rifle barrel in your hands more than it wants you, jaws grinding metal with obvious preference.","traits":{"note": "It targets metal gear over flesh whenever a choice presents itself.", "actions": [{"name": "Scrap Jaw", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target wearing or carrying metal armor or a metal weapon. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) piercing damage, and if the target is wearing nonmagical metal armor, its AC is reduced by 1. The armor is destroyed if its AC reduces to 10."}, {"name": "Antennae", "replaces": "Antennae", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target holding a nonmagical metal weapon. Hit: The weapon corrodes and takes a permanent -1 penalty to damage rolls; if it reaches -5, it's destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A drift of rebar and car doors somehow holds together long enough to shamble forward."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It scrapes toward the loudest metal sound in earshot, jaws grinding in anticipation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half-dissolved tools jut from its frame, remnants of a meal from days ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a trail of fine rust dust behind it, sifting from every loose joint."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One antenna twitches constantly toward a nearby weapon, like it can smell the alloy."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It ignores flesh entirely if there's an easier meal of scrap sitting nearby instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A faint chime rings from somewhere deep inside its heap, like a bell still swallowed whole."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's grown twice the size expected, having fed on an entire vehicle chassis recently."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Scraping across broken pavement in a slow-motion landslide of rebar and car doors", "Grinding a length of pipe between antennae, sparks flaking off with obvious satisfaction"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: animate debris/rust-monster reskin for a wasteland setting"},{"name":"Warlord's Enforcer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"warlord's chain-wielding enforcer","flavor":"Keeps the warlord's convoy in line with a length of chain and a reputation for never asking twice.","desc":"A length of chain rides looped over one shoulder, worn smooth from years of use keeping a warlord's convoy in line. He has a reputation for never asking twice, and he doesn't bother explaining that reputation before the chain comes off his shoulder.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chain and Steel", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The enforcer makes two Scimitar attacks."}, {"name": "Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) slashing damage."}, {"name": "Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Weapon Attack: +5 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (2d4+2) piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's walking the convoy line, chain draped loose, checking every driver's nerve."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A driver caught skimming fuel kneels in front of him, already sweating through excuses."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His chain bears fresh nicks from a dispute settled just this morning."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting crates off a manifest, tallying against what the warlord expects delivered."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two convoy guards flank him at a respectful distance, clearly relieved not to be the target."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He never raises his voice before the chain comes off his shoulder, not once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He pauses mid-patrol at the same spot every circuit, like counting a threat that isn't visible."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just caught someone skimming from the warlord directly, and the chain is already moving."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Walking the length of a convoy, chain draped loose over one shoulder", "Cracking his knuckles at a checkpoint, watching drivers avoid his eyes"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord's lieutenant archetype"},{"name":"Rad-Hulk","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"hulking overgrown mutant brute","flavor":"Grew three sizes past human and forgot most of its words along the way; still remembers the name of the town it used to guard.","desc":"It grew three sizes past anything human should, most of its words lost somewhere along the way with the rest of its old shape. It still remembers the name of the town it used to guard, and mutters it sometimes, low, between blows.","traits":{"note": "Fragments of its old life surface unpredictably mid-fight, distracting it briefly.", "actions": [{"name": "Overgrown Fury", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Rad-Hulk makes one Bite attack and can use Deadly Leap."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (2d10+4) piercing damage."}, {"name": "Deadly Leap", "replaces": "Deadly Leap", "text": "The Rad-Hulk jumps up to 20 feet and lands atop a Large or smaller creature, who must succeed on a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw or be knocked prone and take 10 (3d6) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grew three sizes past anything human should, joints creaking with every step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mutters a town's name low, between blows, in the middle of every fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scrap of guard uniform still clings to one shoulder, faded past recognition."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces the same fence line daily, guarding a settlement long since abandoned."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hesitates at anyone wearing old guard colors, as if some memory still flickers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It responds, faintly, to being addressed by rank, though it can't explain why."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It salutes, once, unconsciously, before every fight it commits to fully."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something just triggered a memory hard enough to make it forget the fight entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Lumbering along a fence line it once guarded, muttering a town's name under its breath", "Crouched over broken concrete, sniffing at a scent only it seems to recognize"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: hulking irradiated brute, stock post-apoc mutant type"},{"name":"Scrap Colossus","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"welded-together walking scrap machine","flavor":"Welded together from three different trucks by hands that clearly loved the work; runs on spite and a leaking fuel drum.","desc":"Three different trucks were welded together by hands that clearly loved the work, panel seams still bearing the pride of whoever built it. It runs on spite and a fuel drum that's been leaking for longer than it should still be moving.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Fused Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The colossus makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three different trucks were welded together by hands that clearly loved the work."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fuel drum lashed to its back leaks steadily, marking its path in dark, oily drops."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Panel seams still bear pride-painted sigils from whoever built it, half-faded now."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It runs hot, venting steam from a dozen mismatched joints with every heavy step."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm is clearly a salvaged crane hook, repurposed with obvious mechanical affection."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It moves slower when its fuel runs low, but never stops advancing entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A faded family photo is welded, deliberately, somewhere into its plating."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its leaking fuel drum has finally caught a spark, and it hasn't noticed yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Lurching forward on three fused truck frames, fuel drum leaking a slow trail behind it", "Standing guard over a scrapheap shrine, panel seams gleaming with old, proud paintwork"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: junkyard-built walking machine, stock salvage-golem type"},{"name":"Chem-Baron","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"chem-baron","summary":"drug-and-fuel kingpin warlord","flavor":"Runs three settlements on rationed water and homebrewed stims; smiles like he's already won the argument you haven't started.","desc":"He runs three settlements on rationed water and homebrewed stims, smiling the easy, patient smile of a man who's already won whatever argument you haven't started yet. Every word out of him sounds like a favor, and every favor has a price attached later.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chemical Menace", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chem-Baron makes two Arcane Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Arcane Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Melee or Ranged Spell Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (3d6+3) poison damage from a burst of refined stim-chemical energy."}, {"name": "Favor Owed", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Chem-Baron casts a spell, drawing on stockpiled reagents rather than any formal study."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-negotiation with a settlement rep who clearly already owes him more than he admits."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ledger open at his side tracks every favor he's extended and never called due."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two bodyguards flank him, more decoration than protection given his reputation alone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's sampling a new stim batch personally, unbothered by the risk of a bad cook."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival dealer waits outside, too afraid to interrupt whatever deal is happening now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every offer he makes sounds generous until you notice what he never mentions."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He knows details about your business he shouldn't, and never explains how."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The favor he's calling in today is bigger than anyone expected, and he's not negotiating."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["Reviewing a stim shipment ledger, smiling like the numbers already favor him", "Holding audience over three settlements' water rations, patient and utterly unbothered"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord archetype: settlement-controlling drug/fuel kingpin"},{"name":"The Sermon-Bearer","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"the-sermon-bearer","summary":"doomsday high-priest awaiting the next blast","flavor":"Preaches that the bombs were mercy and the next ones will finish the job kindly; his flock believes him, which is the scary part.","desc":"He preaches that the bombs were mercy and the next ones will finish the job kindly, voice warm and reasonable in a way that makes the theology worse, not better. His flock believes every word — that's the part that should worry you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Merciful Violence", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sermon-Bearer makes two Mace attacks."}, {"name": "Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Weapon Attack: +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) radiant damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Flame", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +7 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 17 (5d6) radiant damage."}, {"name": "Doomsday Sermon", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Sermon-Bearer casts a spell, its verbal component woven seamlessly into an ongoing hymn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-sermon, and every listener nods along like they've heard it a hundred times."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A line of the faithful waits for individual blessing, each carrying some small offering."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A skeptical newcomer stands at the sermon's edge, clearly wavering despite themselves."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just announced a coming blast date, and no one in the crowd looks frightened."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child asks him a hard question, and his answer somehow makes the theology worse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He never raises his voice, even preaching annihilation, which is what makes it land."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know, with total certainty, a detail about the future no one should know."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just named a specific target for the next mercy, and the crowd is already moving."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["Preaching from a pulpit of stacked rubble, voice warm and reasonable and wrong", "Blessing a line of the faithful, each one nodding along with total conviction"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: doomsday high-priest, our own invented theology (no real-world cult referenced)"},{"name":"Ashfield Titan","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"hauler-built industrial war-walker","flavor":"Built from a downed cargo hauler by a warlord who wanted a throne that could also crush things; mostly it just crushes things.","desc":"Built from a downed cargo hauler by a warlord who wanted a throne that could also crush things, it mostly just crushes things — the throne part came later and matters less. Its footfalls flatten whatever debris hasn't already been ground down.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Massive Construct; slow but devastating melee reach."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its frame still bears the cargo hauler's old logo, half-crushed under new plating."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flattens whatever debris hasn't already been ground down along its patrol route."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rough-welded seat sits bolted between its shoulders, worn smooth from frequent use."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves with a heavy, mechanical gait, servos whining audibly with every stride."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warband banners hang from its arms, snapping stiff in the wind as it walks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It answers only to whoever currently occupies the throne welded to its back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Cargo manifests are still stenciled somewhere inside its chassis, listing goods long gone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just thrown its current rider, and no one nearby knows who it answers to now."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "desert"],"activity":["Crushing debris underfoot on a slow patrol, hauler-plating groaning with each step", "Standing as a makeshift throne-back while a warlord holds court atop its shoulders"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: settlement-sized industrial walker, stock giant-war-machine type"},{"name":"Glasslands Broodmother","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"apex matriarch of the mutant bloodline","flavor":"Every Chittergaunt and Rustfang for fifty miles traces back to her den under the melted overpass; she remembers being smaller, and human.","desc":"Every Chittergaunt and Rustfang for fifty miles traces its bloodline back to her den beneath the melted overpass. She remembers, in some buried way, being smaller — and human — before whatever happened here changed all of that permanently.","traits":{"hp": "high", "note": "Can summon or is escorted by lesser mutant broodkin (Chittergaunt/Rustfang) as reinforcements."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A litter of Chittergaunts stirs at her feet, waking to a scent she's already noticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bones and old tools from generations of feeding litter the floor of her den."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scavenger crew is scouting her den's entrance, unaware how deep the bloodline runs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's dragging fresh prey deeper into the overpass to feed her latest brood."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of her young has strayed too far and needs retrieving before it draws attention."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She recognizes tools and weapons faster than she recognizes faces, oddly enough."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She pauses sometimes, mid-motion, holding a posture that looks almost entirely human."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something has threatened her brood directly, and every Rustfang for miles is answering the call."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["Coiled in a den beneath a melted overpass, litter of Chittergaunts stirring at her feet", "Testing the air outside her den, some buried human instinct still guiding the motion"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"mutant-feral archetype: apex irradiated matriarch, seeds a feral bloodline"},{"name":"Deadman's Warlord","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"deadmans-warlord","summary":"apex convoy-king, rules through fuel scarcity","flavor":"Crowned himself off the corpse of the last warlord and the fuel reserve underneath his throne-truck; his convoy is a moving nation.","desc":"He crowned himself off the corpse of the last warlord and the fuel reserve buried under his throne-truck, and his convoy has since grown into something closer to a moving nation than a gang. Fuel scarcity is his real weapon — he simply controls who gets to keep driving.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; commands a convoy of loyal raiders as ongoing reinforcements; controls fuel access as a soft-power lever."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A line of petitioners waits for fuel rations, each pleading a different urgent case."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His throne-truck idles constantly, a symbolic waste no one else is permitted to match."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival convoy scout has been caught nearby, currently being questioned about their intentions."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's personally inspecting a fuel reserve, distrustful of even his most loyal lieutenants."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A driver begs for an exception to the ration, citing a sick passenger in their truck."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He remembers exactly how much fuel every driver in his convoy has ever been given."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dead warlord he crowned himself over is buried directly beneath his throne-truck's wheels."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The reserve just ran short for the first time, and the whole convoy is watching how he responds."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Holding court from atop a throne-truck, convoy stretching farther than the eye can follow", "Rationing fuel to petitioners personally, deciding who drives and who walks"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"raider-warlord archetype: apex convoy-king ruling by fear and fuel scarcity"},{"name":"The Last Sermon","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"apex doomsday-prophet guarding a live warhead","flavor":"Claims the final bomb is still out there, waiting for his word; nobody who's called the bluff has lived to be wrong about it.","desc":"He claims the final bomb is still out there somewhere, waiting on his word alone, and nobody who's called that bluff has lived long enough to be proven wrong. He speaks softly, which somehow makes the claim land harder.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; the 'live warhead' claim may be a real environmental threat in the encounter, not just a bluff.", "actions": [{"name": "The Word", "text": "Can threaten to trigger a hidden device, forcing a tense standoff mechanic before combat resumes."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's addressing a crowd, voice low, repeating the same claim they've all heard before."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A trembling skeptic stands apart from the crowd, clearly regretting the decision to challenge him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A supposed warhead site sits fenced off behind him, guarded more by rumor than by force."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting a tribute of fuel and food in exchange for delaying the supposed word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A former follower has come to beg forgiveness for doubting the bluff too loudly once."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He never raises his voice to make the threat land; the softness does that work instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He speaks with total specificity about details of the first bombs no records survived to confirm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He's just named tonight as the night, and for once, he sounds like he believes it too."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Speaking softly to a gathered crowd, claiming the final bomb still waits on his word", "Standing over a supposed warhead site, daring anyone present to call the bluff"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"bomb-cult zealot archetype: apex doomsday-prophet who holds a live warhead as scripture"},{"name":"Half-Life","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"apex fallout-horror, decades-deep radiation exposure","flavor":"Been soaking in the hot zone so long the geiger counters just give up near it; what's left of the mind is patient, and furious.","desc":"It's been soaking in the hot zone so long that geiger counters just stop reading anything useful near it, needles pinned uselessly. Whatever's left of the mind inside is patient in the worst way — patient like something that stopped needing to hurry a long time ago, and furious underneath all of it.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "note": "Apex; severe radiation aura; extremely durable, prioritizes methodical destruction over speed.", "actions": [{"name": "Saturation", "text": "Creatures remaining adjacent for multiple rounds suffer escalating radiation damage that compounds each turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hovers near a wrecked reactor site, unmoving, as if simply waiting something out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A team of readings-hunters lies dead nearby, geiger counters still clicking uselessly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drifts a slow, unbroken loop through a stretch of wreckage no one else can survive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its presence has kept an entire valuable salvage site untouched for a full generation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate scavenger crew is arguing whether the risk of it is worth the salvage inside."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It never chases prey that flees the hot zone, content to let distance do the work."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to recognize old warning signage, pausing near markers no living crew still reads."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Whatever patience it had just ran out, and the hot zone is no longer holding it in place."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "any"],"activity":["Standing motionless in the hot zone, geiger counters pinning uselessly nearby", "Drifting through irradiated wreckage, patient in a way nothing living manages anymore"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"irradiated-ghoul archetype: apex fallout-mutated horror, decades of exposure past any human baseline"},{"name":"The Foundry Made Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"the-foundry-made-flesh","summary":"factory-fused apex war-machine","flavor":"An entire pre-collapse factory floor — presses, arms, conveyor teeth — fused by decades of slag into a single furious machine that still thinks it's making something.","desc":"An entire pre-collapse factory floor — presses, conveyor teeth, hydraulic arms — has fused under decades of slag into one furious, moving machine. It still goes through the motions of manufacturing, grinding and stamping at nothing, like some part of it genuinely believes it's still making something.","traits":{"hp": "very high", "ac": "high", "note": "Apex; multiple industrial 'limbs' (press/conveyor/grinder) can each act as separate attack options.", "actions": [{"name": "Production Line", "text": "Can make attacks with two different industrial limbs in the same round."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Presses and conveyor teeth grind through motions with nothing left to actually manufacture."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slag cakes every joint, decades of collapse fused into one furious, moving mass."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It follows the exact footprint of the old factory floor, unable to deviate from the layout."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sparks fly from its stamping motions, striking nothing but empty, rusted air."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A half-finished product, unrecognizable now, is still clutched somewhere in its works."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It responds, faintly, to factory whistle sounds, resetting its motions to a fresh cycle."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something new is taking shape in its works, product of a process no one remembers starting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just completed something, for the first time in decades, and started the process again."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["Grinding and stamping at nothing, convinced some part of it is still manufacturing", "Advancing through a dead factory floor, presses and conveyor teeth churning in stolen rhythm"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scrap-beast archetype: apex, a factory's automated defense grid fused into one rampaging mass"},{"name":"Overgrown Brute","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"vat-grown mutant brute swinging a car-door shield","flavor":"A slab-muscled product of the vats, stitched together in a surgeon's hurry — the seams still show where two men became one. It carries a car door strapped to one forearm, punched through with a viewing slit, and swings it like other men swing a mace.","desc":"Surgical seams run in a rough line down the Brute's chest and shoulder, stitched hurriedly with wire and hope. It moves at a lumbering trot, favoring the arm that carries a scavenged car door, and swings the whole slab of rusted steel like a weapon rather than a guard. Someone spent weeks building the muscle onto this frame and no time at all teaching it to fear pain. It answers to a whistle-code it can't explain, because whatever made it decided explaining wasn't necessary.","traits":{"note": "The car door doubles as cover — attackers targeting its shield-arm side have disadvantage unless they can flank it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistle-code commands it obeys without hesitating on the meaning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wire stitches down one forearm have torn and been re-sewn twice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a strip of the old car's paint job across its brow like a crest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grunts the same three syllables before every swing, a vat-conditioning tic."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye is a different color than the other — spare-parts surgery."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It flinches at the smell of antiseptic, an old vat memory it can't place."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Under the seams, its heartbeat runs in two different rhythms."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Losing the shield-arm sends it into a berserk final charge, seams tearing wide."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["hefts a scavenged car door like a shield-mace, swinging it two-handed", "answers a whistle-code with a lumbering charge toward whatever it's pointed at"]},{"name":"Overgrown Pack-Leader","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"silent overgrown commander directing its pack in fist-signs","flavor":"Smarter than the brutes it commands, wearing a salvaged rebreather scavenged whole off a corpse twice its size. It never speaks — words seem to have been trimmed out of it in the vats — but its fist-signs move a whole warband in perfect silence.","desc":"A scavenged rebreather hisses over what used to be a face, fogging with each held breath while its fists carve out commands in a silent sign language only its kind understands. It doesn't waste motion — a closed fist here, two fingers there — and the brutes around it move like a single animal. Someone in the vats gave this one just enough left over to plan, and took away everything it might have said about it. It watches a fight longer than its brothers do, waiting for the moment worth spending them on.","traits":{"note": "It never fights first — killing it before it signals cuts the pack's coordination, dropping their attacks to disadvantage until a new leader steps up."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rebreather is stitched from three mismatched masks, none quite sealed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks kill-tallies in scar-notches down its own forearm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its back to a wall in every fight, refusing to be flanked."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs a retreat-code the instant the numbers turn."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a torn strip of the Maker's coat as a rank-sash."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its sign-language is oddly formal, almost like taught etiquette."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes track the fight like it's reading a diagram no one else can see."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Dying, it signs one final command — the whole remaining pack breaks off and flees together, disciplined even in retreat."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["signs silent commands to a cluster of overgrown brutes with sharp, economical gestures", "watches a fight from the rear, rebreather hissing, waiting to commit its pack"]},{"name":"Overgrown Siege-Breaker","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"hulking overgrown siege-breaker swinging an iron lamppost","flavor":"The biggest of the made, built wide rather than tall, hauling a bent iron lamppost as a bat. Every swing brings down a wall it was never actually aiming at.","desc":"It is the biggest thing to come out of the vats, wide across the shoulders as a delivery truck, and it drags a bent lamppost behind it like the wasteland's biggest club. Walls don't survive its swings any better than skulls do — it isn't aiming for either, just clearing whatever's in front of it. Scar tissue has grown thick and lumpy where the vat-seams never quite closed right, and it doesn't seem to notice the smaller Overgrown scattering out of its path. The Makers built it to break sieges, and it has never once needed a second target.","traits":{"note": "Its swings are wide enough to hit structures — a DM ruling on collateral collapse (crumbling wall, buckling floor) is always in play near it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags the lamppost by a chain wrapped twice around one fist."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footprints crack pavement that hasn't cracked in decades."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roars before every swing, more habit than threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the flattened hood of a car as a crude helmet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vat-scarring runs so thick down its back it reads like tree bark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Charges straight through cover rather than around it, every time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bellow, underneath the noise, carries one clear human word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A killing blow drops it into a nearby wall — the resulting collapse is a live hazard for everyone close."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["drags a bent iron lamppost across broken pavement, gouging a trench behind it", "swings the lamppost through a standing wall as readily as through a body"]},{"name":"The Overgrown Warlord","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"fire-giant","model":"rlm-the-overgrown-warlord","summary":"armored overgrown boss, road-sign plate armor, proudly branded vat-mark","flavor":"Armored in welded road signs bent into plates, its vat-mark branded proud across a bare shoulder rather than hidden. It doesn't lead the Overgrown so much as embody what they were built to become.","desc":"Sheet after sheet of welded road signs — STOP, YIELD, DETOUR — cover its chest and shoulders in crude, hammer-dented plate, and its vat-mark is branded high on one bare shoulder where every lesser Overgrown hides theirs. It has outlived the batch it was made with and every batch after, and it wears that the way other warlords wear crowns. Warbands that once feared the Makers now answer to it instead, ember-torch banners raised at its command. It remembers the vats — not fondly, but clearly — and it has decided the Makers no longer get to say what it's for.","traits":{"note": "Its brand is a rallying icon — any Overgrown ally that can see it fights with advantage on morale-adjacent checks (per the social-attitude/coherence rules already in play); breaking the brand publicly is a real lever against it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plate armor still bears the paint of the highway it was salvaged from."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a captured Maker's tool belt as a trophy at its hip."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in short, broken sentences — vat-conditioning it never fully lost."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its warband raises ember-lit banners the instant it enters a fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears scars from every batch of Overgrown it has outlived."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tests challengers personally rather than sending muscle to vet them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its brand-scar glows faint ember-orange when its temper spikes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If it falls in front of its warband, the ember-torch banners go dark all at once — a visible, world-legible sign the wasteland's balance of power just changed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["strides at the head of a warband under raised ember-torch banners", "brands a fallen ally's shoulder mid-battle, making the mark permanent"]},{"name":"The Maker's Apprentice","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"priest","summary":"hooded vat-surgeon still making new Overgrown, open to recruitment","flavor":"A hooded surgeon of the vats, sleeves stained past the elbow in preservative fluid — proof somebody is still making the Overgrown, quietly, out here at the edge of the ash-flats.","desc":"Gloved to the elbow in vat-stained rubber, the Apprentice moves between tanks that still hum with a current nobody else in the wasteland knows how to keep running. Whoever taught this trade is long dead or long gone, but the notes survive in a cracked ledger the Apprentice guards like scripture. There's no love in the work — just competence, and a growing unease about what the Maker's original notes were actually for. It hasn't decided yet whether to keep making Overgrown or to finally stop.","traits":{"note": "Social-first parley target: engage per the social-attitude system, and a favorable shift (offering it a reason to stop the vats, or protection from whoever it fears) can flip it to a recruitable ally rather than a fight."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a cracked leather ledger of vat-notes chained to its belt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gloves are stained a different color for each batch it's worked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks to the tanks like patients, gentle and clinical at once."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a Maker's hood two sizes too large, inherited rather than earned."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at questions about where the original Maker went."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps one tank running empty, like it's saving the slot for something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recites vat-formulas in its sleep, in a voice that isn't quite its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, it offers to shut the vats down forever — a genuine, negotiable surrender rather than a last stand."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["moves between humming vat-tanks, checking gauges with gloved, practiced hands", "reads aloud from a cracked ledger of vat-formulas, murmuring corrections to itself"]},{"name":"Lucid Withered Lore-Keeper","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"lucid withered elder, full pre-fall memory, the wasteland's best lore-source","flavor":"Parchment-skinned and startlingly lucid, one of the rare Withered whose pre-fall memories never rotted with the rest of it. It remembers roads that don't exist anymore, and it will trade what it knows for almost anything.","desc":"Its skin has gone the texture and color of old parchment, cracked at every joint, but its eyes are clear and its sentences come out whole — unheard of, for a Withered. It remembers the old highways by name, remembers the last broadcast before the world went quiet, remembers faces that have been dust for a generation. Scavengers who know better bring it questions instead of weapons, because the answers are worth more than anything they'd loot off its corpse. It is lonely in a way none of the shambling dead around it can understand, and that loneliness is the door in.","traits":{"note": "It is the realm's premier lore NPC and a genuine recruit target: approach it per the social-attitude system with real questions or a way to end its isolation, and a favorable shift makes it a standing ally that trades memory for protection."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in complete, unhurried sentences — the other Withered never do."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a mental catalog of every road sign it's ever passed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches, still, at a sound no one else can hear from before the fall."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades true answers only for real company, not loot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its parchment skin bears faded ink where it once wrote reminders to itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Corrects scavengers' folk-legends with the actual, duller truth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally answers a question before it's finished being asked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If its shelter is threatened, it can recall a name from someone's own forgotten past — a truth so precise it can stun a listener with grief."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["recites the name of a vanished highway to no one in particular", "trades a scrap of pre-fall memory for the company of whoever asked"]},{"name":"Lucid Withered Trader","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"withered cart-merchant, fair prices, frightening face","flavor":"A withered merchant harnessed to a cart of salvage, quoting fair prices in a rattling voice from a face that stops most buyers at ten paces.","desc":"It hauls its cart by a harness worn smooth into its own shoulder bones, calling out prices in a voice like dry leaves rubbing together. The prices are fair — fairer than most living traders offer — but the face under the hood has rotted past anything a first-time buyer can look at twice. Regulars know to look at the goods instead. It has never once shorted a customer, which is more than most of the wasteland's living merchants can claim.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable/social-first: it defaults to wary-neutral, an attitude first-impression revulsion can tank fast — approach calmly and it's an honest, standing trade contact per the social-attitude system."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cart wheels are scavenged pram wheels, squeaking on every turn."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its hood cinched tight, more courtesy than modesty."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts change with startling, careful precision."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its harness has worn a permanent groove into its shoulder."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to haggle down from its first quoted price, ever."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Remembers regular customers' names across years of visits."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never eats, never rests, and never explains why it still bothers to sell."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threatened or robbed, it goes eerily calm and simply stops trading with that buyer forever — no violence, just an absolute door closing."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["hauls a harnessed cart of salvage down a cracked road, calling out fair prices", "counts change with slow, exact care under a hood no one wants to look under"]},{"name":"Feral Withered Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"fast feral withered, all hunger, closes distance at a dead sprint","flavor":"A sprinting hollow-eyed husk with nothing left in it but hunger, closing distance faster than a Withered has any right to.","desc":"Most Withered shamble; this one runs, hollow eye-sockets fixed dead ahead, arms pumping in a broken imitation of a living sprinter's form. There's no hesitation in it, no aimless wandering — just a straight line toward the nearest warmth, however far it has to go. It doesn't stop when it should, doesn't slow at obstacles it should fear, and it doesn't feel any of the damage it takes getting there.","traits":{"note": "It closes distance far faster than typical shamblers — treat its approach speed as a genuine threat at range, not a shambling non-issue."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bare feet have worn down to bone at the heel from constant running."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sprints in an unnervingly straight line, ignoring easier routes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw hangs slack, clacking with each stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never slows for terrain — it simply falls and gets back up."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was clearly someone's runner in life; the gait never left it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Locks onto body heat over sound or sight, tracking warmth alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally arrives already exhausted, collapsing mid-sprint, then rising to run again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with nowhere left to run, it hurls itself at the nearest warm body with everything left in it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["sprints in a dead-straight line toward the nearest warmth, arms pumping", "falls hard over debris and is back up and running within a breath"]},{"name":"The Glow-Called","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie-plague-carrier","summary":"faintly glowing withered, drawn helplessly to reactor heat","flavor":"A feral Withered lit faintly green under the skin, drawn moth-like to anything that still hums with reactor warmth.","desc":"A dim green glow pulses under its skin like something still alive in there, and it moves toward any working reactor or warm engine block the way old moths moved toward porch lights. It will walk through fire, through gunfire, through its own kind to reach the glow, and it never seems to notice it's already dead getting there. Scavengers use it, sometimes, as a crude compass — follow the Glow-Called and it'll walk you straight to whatever's still generating power nearby.","traits":{"note": "It always moves toward the nearest active power source in range, predictably — useful as an in-world compass, and exploitable to lure it away from a target."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glow brightens visibly the closer it gets to a live reactor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks in a fixed line toward the nearest hum, ignoring easier paths."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its skin is translucent enough to see the glow moving under it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was likely a reactor-tech in life; the draw feels almost like homesickness."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint green handprints on anything metal it touches."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Groups of them cluster near working generators like insects at a lamp."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its glow pulses in time with the reactor it's approaching, before it's close enough to sense it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near a live power source, its glow flares bright enough to briefly overload nearby electronics."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["drifts toward the nearest working reactor, green glow brightening under its skin", "pushes through obstacles that would stop it, fixed only on the hum ahead"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Shard-Bearer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"ember-cult wanderer, ember-glow shard fused into a clenched fist","flavor":"A wandering member of the Cindermarked cult, one clenched fist glowing faint ember-orange through the skin around a shard it will not, cannot, open its hand to show.","desc":"It walks the ash-flats alone or in loose twos, robes scorched at the hem, one fist permanently curled shut around something that glows faint orange through the skin like a coal held too long. It never opens that hand, not to eat, not to fight, not to sleep — the shard has become part of the arm by now, fused somewhere past the wrist. It preaches the ember-stone's coming in short, half-mad sentences to anyone who'll stand still, and it means every word of it.","traits":{"note": "The fused shard is a real cargo-cult relic fragment, not decoration — destroying the Shard-Bearer releases a small ember flare (minor fire hazard) rather than yielding a usable item; the cult treats the loss as a genuine casualty, not a robbery."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Robes are scorched black at every hem, deliberately, cult-fashion."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Preaches the ember-stone's return in broken half-sentences."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never uses its glowing fist for anything but the shard's grip."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Travels in pairs, murmuring the same chant out of sync with each other."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks its passage with ash-handprints from its free hand."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows agitated near any actual functioning fire, like it's jealous of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The glow through its fist brightens in rhythm with something far off, unseen."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck hard enough, the fused shard flares — a burst of embers scorches anything adjacent when the Shard-Bearer falls."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["walks the ash-flats preaching the ember-stone's return in broken half-sentences", "keeps one fist perpetually clenched around a shard fused into its own arm"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Ember-Speaker","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"cult priest radiating shard-warmth, preaching the ember-stone's chosen wasteland","flavor":"A cult priest who wears her shard sewn into a neck-torc, close enough to the throat to warm blood that would otherwise freeze; she preaches that the ember-stone chose the wasteland because the wasteland was already dying.","desc":"The torc at her throat glows dull orange even in full dark, and a halo of heat-shimmer follows her through the ash-cold like a held breath made visible. She speaks in the cadence of someone who has said the same sermon a thousand times and still believes every word of it. Converts kneel close enough to share the warmth, and she lets them — that's the whole hook, in the end. She has buried three congregations already and calls each fire a return, not a loss.","traits":{"note": "Anyone who shares real warmth at her fire and hears the sermon out shifts a full attitude tier toward Friendly; drawing a weapon near the torc locks her and every nearby Cindermarked at Hostile immediately."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears scavenged temple robes stitched from a dozen mismatched uniforms."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a ledger of every convert's name, in case the ember-stone ever asks."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hands are scarred smooth from years of holding the torc bare-skinned."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Preaches from a collapsed highway overpass like a proper pulpit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses all food that hasn't first been warmed at her own fire."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The torc's heat rises and falls with her voice, hottest at the sermon's climax."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Frost refuses to settle within ten feet of her, sermon or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A congregation cornered with her turns as one, ready to burn the shelter down around the intruders rather than lose the fire."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Preaching from a collapsed overpass, the neck-torc's heat-shimmer rippling around her", "Cupping a convert's frozen hands to the torc's warmth mid-sermon"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Pilgrim","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"shard-led walker, footprints steaming through the cold","flavor":"A convert who walks wherever the shard around her neck pulls hardest, footprints steaming into the ash behind her.","desc":"She doesn't check a map or a compass anymore — she just walks the direction the warmth at her chest tugs strongest, and the ash under each bootprint steams faintly for a few seconds after she's passed. She'll cross a minefield or a raider's territory without slowing if the pull says to. Ask her where she's going and she'll say only that the ember-stone knows.","traits":{"note": "She follows the pull without tactical sense; luring or blocking the direction of her shard's tug reliably diverts her."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wrapped the shard's cord in scavenged wire so it can't be torn free easily."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters distances under her breath, tracking the pull's strength."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears every layer of clothing she owns, and still shivers constantly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no weapon, only a walking stick worn smooth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops dead the instant the pull goes still, waiting for it to resume."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her steaming footprints are visible for nearly a minute in the cold."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pull sometimes drags her toward places that aren't there anymore."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner her and the shard flares hot enough to scorch whoever grabs her."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Walking a fixed line across open ash, footprints steaming faintly behind her", "Halting mid-stride the instant the shard's pull goes still, waiting"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Warden","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"cult guard, shard-fused arm burning to the elbow","flavor":"Cult muscle whose sworn shard is fused into the flesh of one arm to the elbow, ash flaking off skin the fire has already half-spent.","desc":"His right arm glows dull red beneath skin gone thin and cracked, ash sifting off in a fine constant snow wherever he moves it. He was given the shard as a reward for loyalty and it's been quietly cooking him from the inside ever since — he knows, and he says the fire is worth the arm. He stands the cult's checkpoints without complaint, one hand always resting near the glow like it's a weapon he trusts more than the one on his belt.","traits":{"note": "He answers only to the Ember-Speaker's sermon-name for the cult; naming a rival warband correctly or offering him an intact shard shifts him toward Friendly, but he will not turn on his congregation while the sermon still holds him."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a glove over the burning arm in public, more habit than shame."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of scavengers turned away from the checkpoint, scratched into the wall."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His forearm's glow brightens visibly whenever he's angry."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses relief shifts; he doesn't trust anyone else at the post."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second, unlit shard in his pocket, saving it for something."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The ash flaking from his arm collects in a small drift at his feet by shift's end."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a few seconds after a hard hit, the glow in his arm actually recedes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the checkpoint is truly overrun, he presses the burning arm to the nearest flammable thing and walks away."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Standing checkpoint at a cult perimeter, one hand resting near his own burning forearm", "Scratching another turned-away scavenger onto a tally carved in the wall"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Recruiter","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"priest-acolyte","summary":"warm-palmed missionary, offering a stranger the shard's first free taste","flavor":"A warm-palmed missionary who finds cold travelers on the road and offers the first taste of a shard's heat for free.","desc":"She finds the coldest-looking traveler on any road and presses her palm — always warm, always a little too warm — against theirs before they can pull away. The first taste of the shard's heat is free, she says, every time, like it's a rule someone wrote down somewhere. She has a soft voice for hard sells and never seems to notice how many she's lost to the congregation's fires.","traits":{"note": "A traveler who accepts the free warmth shifts one attitude tier toward Friendly on the spot; refusing outright costs nothing, but she'll remember the face and try again at the next crossing."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second, cooler shard fragment in reserve for skeptics."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites the same opening line to every stranger, word for word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Travels with a small band of already-warmed converts as living proof."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never asks for payment on the first meeting, only a name."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears gloves worn through at the palms from years of the same handshake."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her palm stays warm for hours after contact, long after the shard's out of reach."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She seems to know exactly how cold a stranger is before she ever touches them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Refused enough times in one place, she stops being gentle about the offer."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Pressing a too-warm palm into a cold stranger's hand before they can pull away", "Reciting the same soft opening line to every traveler on the road"]},{"name":"Cindermarked Initiate","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"new convert mid-branding, rapture and terror on the same face","flavor":"A new convert mid-branding, the shard's brand searing into skin while rapture and terror fight for the same face.","desc":"The brand hasn't finished searing yet and already half her expression has gone somewhere else entirely — eyes wide with something between agony and revelation, mouth working around a prayer she hasn't fully learned. The cult holds her steady through it, not by force but because she asked them to. When it's done she'll have a scar shaped like the shard that made it, and she'll call the pain the best thing that ever happened to her.","traits":{"note": "Mid-ritual she is functionally noncombatant; interrupting the branding by force locks her Hostile toward whoever stopped it, but waiting it out and speaking kindly after leaves her open to a Friendly first impression."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grips a strip of leather between her teeth, an old habit passed down from older converts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shakes uncontrollably even as she insists she isn't cold anymore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears clothes clearly scavenged just for this occasion, her best find."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites the sermon's opening line under her breath through the pain."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a sponsor from the congregation holding her hand through it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The half-finished brand already gives off its own faint heat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment mid-scream her voice matches the Ember-Speaker's exactly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the branding is interrupted badly, the half-set shard-brand can flare and burn hot enough to scar whoever's nearest."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Held steady through a half-finished shard-branding, face caught between rapture and terror", "Reciting a half-learned sermon line through gritted teeth"]},{"name":"The Apostate","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"ex-cultist who cut the shard out, forever cold since","flavor":"An ex-cultist who cut her own shard out rather than let it finish cooking her, bandaged chest healing wrong, forever cold now.","desc":"The bandages across her chest never quite stay clean, and she's been cold — really cold, bone-cold — since the night she dug the shard out with her own knife rather than let it finish what it started. She doesn't preach against the cult, exactly; she just flinches at every fire and won't get close enough to warm her hands. She knows things about the congregation's routes and rituals that make her valuable to anyone willing to overlook how badly her hands shake.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable: she starts Wary of outsiders and warms toward Friendly only through concrete proof they mean the cult harm, not just talk; she will not go anywhere near an active shard for any price."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the knife she used, cleaned obsessively, never far from reach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wraps her own chest bandages fresh every morning without help."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches hard at any open flame, even a cookfire."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows the congregation's patrol routes better than most of its guards."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sleeps in as many layers as she can scavenge and still shivers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her scar has never fully closed; something about the wound won't heal clean."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "On the coldest nights she swears she can still feel the shard's old pull, faint."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner her near a lit shard and the panic overrides everything else she is."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["Wrapping fresh bandages over an old self-inflicted wound at first light", "Flinching hard and stepping back the instant a shard or open flame is lit nearby"]},{"name":"The First Kindled","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"efreeti","model":"rlm-first-kindled","summary":"The Cindermarked cult's founder, more ember than flesh, radiant and burning down","flavor":"The cult's founder is more ember than flesh now — radiant, generous, and burning down like a lamp that knows it. The stone chose him first.","desc":"He was the coldest man in the coldest winter of the fall, and he found the stone, and it warmed him, and he shared it. That is the whole gospel and every word is true. Decades of spending later, the First Kindled glows through his skin like a paper lantern — the shard in his sternum has spread to a lattice — and his warmth is real, his miracles are real, and the ash flaking off him with every gesture is also real. He believes the burn is a fair price. He no longer remembers cold well enough to judge.","traits":{"note": "Cult apex and the anchor of the Cindermarked faction clock. He is genuinely benevolent AND genuinely spending his flock (the mark burns lifespan as fuel) — the parley lane runs through making him SEE the apostate's scar; attitude shifts on evidence of cost, never on accusations of malice. Killing him martyrs the cult; convincing him breaks it gently."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snow melts in a ten-pace ring around him; his congregation sleeps warm in a frozen land."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His footprints steam, and the faithful collect the warm ash of him in lockets."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He eats nothing; he sits at every meal anyway, beaming, remembering food fondly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ember-lattice under his skin brightens when he lies. He therefore never lies."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows every convert's name and the exact night each one came in from the cold."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He can kindle a dead machine — generator, pump, radio — by laying his palm on it; the machine stays warm and loyal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "When he sleeps, the mother-stone's dreams leak: the whole camp dreams of a hearth that eats the family around it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He is one great miracle from burning through — and tonight the flock is begging him for exactly that miracle."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["laying a glowing palm on a convert's frostbitten hands, ash falling off his own wrist as he does", "preaching at dusk, lit from inside, a little dimmer than yesterday"]}],
 "suburb":[{"name":"Cul-de-Sac Wanderer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"shambling loop-walker, the block's living dead","flavor":"A resident in bathrobe and slippers who never quite reaches the mailbox, looping the same forty feet of driveway forever.","desc":"Terrycloth robe cinched at the waist, one slipper on. It follows the same curve of driveway it always has, forty feet out and forty feet back, never reaching the mailbox at the end. Its face turns toward you as you pass but the feet never stop moving. The newspaper it's collecting is three years of newspapers deep.","traits":{"note": "It never breaks its loop unless something stands in the exact spot it's walking toward.", "actions": [{"name": "Newspaper-Deep Grasp", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It clutches a cordless phone with a dead battery, murmuring into the dial tone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bathrobe is buttoned wrong, one flap dragging a groove into the pavement."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waters an empty flowerbed with an invisible can, tipping it at the same angle every pass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has worn a visible rut into the driveway, an inch deep and forty feet long."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It checks a wristwatch with no hands, tapping the face twice before continuing on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at the same spot each loop, exactly where a car must have once idled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its slippered foot lands in the same print every single time, wearing the concrete smooth."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force it off its loop and its face slackens entirely, as if the walking was the only thing holding it together."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["looping the same forty feet of driveway, robe cinched, one slipper missing"]},{"name":"Porch-Light Moth-Thing","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"screen-door lurker begging to be let inside","flavor":"Drawn to bug-zapper blue, it flutters against screen doors at 3am, whispering in a dead child's voice about being let in.","desc":"Something the size of a dinner plate beats itself soft and rhythmic against the screen door, wings catching the bug-zapper blue in dusty flickers. Up close its knock has cadence, almost words. A child's voice, thin through the mesh, asks very politely to be let in out of the cold.","traits":{"note": "Its begging voice is a lure — it only has feelers and a stinging tail underneath the wings.", "actions": [{"name": "Pleading Feeler", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage, and if the target is Small or smaller it is Grappled (escape DC 11)."}, {"name": "Powder of Small Names (1/Day)", "replaces": "Stench Spray (1/Day)", "text": "Each creature within 10 ft. of the Moth-Thing makes a DC 11 Constitution save. On a failure a creature takes 3 (1d6) Poison damage and is Poisoned until the end of its next turn, hearing a familiar child's voice under the ringing in its ears."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only knocks at doors with porch lights left on past midnight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wings are patterned like faded wallpaper from a house nobody remembers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It uses a different child's voice at every house, never repeating one twice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It taps in a rhythm that matches whoever's heartbeat is nearest the door."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still and silent the instant a porch light switches off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to say a name it shouldn't know, one belonging to someone who died young here."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Screens it has touched stay warm to the touch for days, like something small was breathing against them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Let it inside once and every screen door on the street starts knocking in unison that same night."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["beating itself soft against a screen door at 3am, whispering to be let in"]},{"name":"HOA Enforcer Drone","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"flying clipboard drone, petty bureaucratic menace","flavor":"A clipboard on wings that measures lawn height by moonlight and leaves violation notices on houses that don't exist yet.","desc":"A clipboard hovers at eye level on two small propellers, its pen scratching against nothing. It circles the yard in slow surveying loops, measuring grass blades against some remembered standard. A violation notice prints from its side and flutters onto a doorstep that, until this morning, wasn't zoned for a house.","traits":{"note": "It cannot act against a lawn it has already stamped compliant, even seconds after stamping it.", "actions": [{"name": "Violation Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from the drone's whirring pen-nib."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It prints violation notices in a font no local printer actually uses."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its propellers whine louder near any lawn ornament it deems 'unauthorized.'"}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It measures the same three-inch strip of grass over and over, ignoring the rest of the yard."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its clipboard is stacked with notices addressed to houses not yet built."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles wider at dusk, as if the standard it measures against keeps changing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's citing a resident for a fence built two feet onto land the resident doesn't legally own yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its violation notices, read aloud, describe rooms of a house that don't exist on the property."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Enough unpaid violations and it summons others like it, one drone for every notice gone unanswered."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["measuring lawn height by moonlight, pen scratching against nothing"]},{"name":"Sprinkler Ghoul","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"irrigation-system ghoul, rises on the same timer nightly","flavor":"It rises from the irrigation system at exactly 3:00am, joints clicking like a valve timer, watering the grass with something that isn't water.","desc":"It hauls itself up out of the sprinkler head at exactly three in the morning, joints clicking on a schedule like a valve timer clicking over. Grey and stooped, it drags a garden hose in a slow arc across the lawn, and the fluid hissing from the nozzle isn't clear.","traits":{"note": "Rises only at 3:00am on its irrigation cycle; inert and buried the rest of the day."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints click in the exact cadence of the sprinkler timer, twice per second, endlessly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waters in a perfect arc even when the hose has no nozzle left to shape it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grass it waters yellows and dies within the week no matter how green it looks that night."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces ten minutes early on the night before a scheduled water shutoff."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its face is fixed toward whichever direction the timer box points, never toward you."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rigged its own irrigation line to reach one specific window, every single night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fluid from its hose leaves handprints in the grass that are smaller than a child's."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break its timer box and every sprinkler head on the block hauls up its own ghoul at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["hauling itself from a sprinkler head at exactly 3:00am, hose dragging behind it"]},{"name":"Under-the-Bed Groper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"classic bedroom-dark lurker, waits for lights-out","flavor":"Flat black and patient, it presses itself to the box spring all day and only unfolds a reaching limb once the lamp clicks off.","desc":"Flat, black, and patient, it presses itself the width of a shadow against the underside of a box spring all day long. Only when the lamp clicks off does one long arm unfold from the dark, feeling blind and unhurried across the carpet for an ankle.","traits":{"note": "It cannot unfold or attack while any light source remains lit in the room.", "actions": [{"name": "Reaching Limb", "replaces": "Crush", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) and pulled 5 feet toward the bed."}, {"name": "Lamp-Click Dark (1/Day)", "replaces": "Darkness Aura (1/Day)", "text": "Every light source within 15 feet of the Groper gutters out for 1 minute, as if a switch were thrown. Creatures relying on that light to see are Blinded until they find another source."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only unfolds if the room has gone fully dark for a full ten count."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its reach always falls exactly one inch short of where a foot last was."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust under the bed is undisturbed everywhere except the one path its arm has worn smooth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flattens instantly at the first click of a lamp switch, faster than the light can catch it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells like a box spring that's been rained on, faint mildew under the dark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to fake the click of a lamp switch itself, luring hands back into the dark."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its arm is longer than the room it hides in should allow, folding through the wall to reach the next one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill the lamp near it permanently and it stops needing the dark at all, unfolding in daylight from then on."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pressed flat against the box spring, waiting for the lamp to click off"]},{"name":"Overwaving Neighbor","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"too-friendly neighbor, watching before you're even awake","flavor":"He waves before you've even opened your blinds, hand moving a beat too fast, smile a beat too wide, already knowing your name.","desc":"He's already at the fence line when you open the blinds, hand raised a half-second before you could have seen him there. The wave moves a beat too fast, the grin holds a beat too long, and he says good morning like he's reading it off something written just for you.","traits":{"note": "He already knows everyone's name on the street before he's been told it once.", "actions": [{"name": "Good Morning Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, delivered mid-greeting with a smile that never breaks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waves with the same hand every time, the other always tucked behind his back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He greets you using a nickname you've never told anyone in this neighborhood."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already raking leaves that haven't fallen from his tree yet this season."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His smile holds a beat too long after the conversation has clearly ended."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waves at the exact same second every morning, down to the minute."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started greeting you by a name you'll be given later, one you don't recognize yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He waves from the fence line and also, a half-second later, from a window on the far side of the house."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wave back once and he never stops appearing wherever you next look, always mid-wave."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waving from the fence line a half-second before you could have seen him there"]},{"name":"Curfew Light Wisp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"streetlamp wisp that herds you home by dusk","flavor":"Streetlamps that switch on early and herd stragglers indoors by dimming ahead of their steps, punishing anyone caught out past curfew.","desc":"A soft orange glow detaches from the streetlamp overhead and drifts down to hover at shoulder height, warm as a nightlight. It herds without touching — easing in front of you, nudging you gently homeward — and it dims, displeased, the longer you resist its curfew.","traits":{"note": "It never touches a creature directly — it only nudges, dims, and herds.", "actions": [{"name": "Curfew Nudge", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Lightning damage, and the target is pushed 10 feet toward the nearest home or streetlamp."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only herds children, ignoring adults out well past the same curfew."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glow warms up like a nightlight the moment it senses someone alone outdoors."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It dims in visible frustration, flickering, the longer someone lingers past dusk."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It detaches earlier each week, curfew creeping toward late afternoon."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hovers exactly at shoulder height no matter how tall the person it's herding."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun herding people toward one particular house instead of their own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Streetlamps it has occupied stay lit through outages that darken the rest of the block."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Defy it past midnight and every streetlamp on the street detaches its wisp at once, closing in."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["drifting down from the streetlamp, easing stragglers gently homeward before dark"]},{"name":"Casserole Cultist","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"grief-vulture neighbor, dish in hand, headcount ready","flavor":"Arrives at your door within the hour of any tragedy, dish already baked, eyes already counting who's missing from the block.","desc":"She's at the door within the hour, dish still warm in oven-mitted hands, eyes already flicking past your shoulder to count who's home and who isn't. The condolences come rehearsed. The foil-wrapped pan smells like someone else's kitchen, and she won't leave until she's seen every room.","traits":{"note": "She never attacks first in front of a witness — only once alone with the grieving household.", "actions": [{"name": "Consoling Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, struck mid-embrace while offering condolences."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her casserole dish is always still warm no matter how long she's carried it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She asks to see every room in the house before she'll set the dish down."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She knew about the tragedy before the sirens had finished arriving."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her condolences come out word-for-word the same as last time's, rehearsed and smooth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She leaves the foil pan behind even when nobody remembers inviting her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started arriving an hour before the tragedy instead of after, dish already baked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The foil-wrapped pan, opened, smells exactly like whoever the household just lost."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Refuse her dish and the tragedy she came for simply happens again, closer to home this time."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["arriving dish-in-hand within the hour of tragedy, already counting who's missing"]},{"name":"Cursed Lawn Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"grinning gnome, roots the cursed lawn to its post","flavor":"Ceramic and grinning, it rotates a few degrees each night to keep every lawn in its sightline; the grass beneath it never dies right.","desc":"A garden gnome, chipped paint and permanent grin, stands rooted dead-center in a lawn too green for the season. Its painted eyes track anyone who steps off the walkway, and the grass around its little wooden feet is the only patch too healthy to be natural.","traits":{"note": "It cannot move from its post, but its sightline covers the whole yard by dawn.", "actions": [{"name": "Painted-Eye Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rooted Grin", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that meets the Sentinel's painted eyes makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frightened for 1 minute and cannot step off the walkway onto the lawn while frightened this way."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chipped paint flakes off in the exact same three spots every year, never worse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The grass beneath its feet stays green through droughts that kill every other lawn on the block."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its grin has widened, almost imperceptibly, since the last time anyone looked closely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rotates to face whichever house on the block had a light on last."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its little wooden feet have sunk an inch into soil that was concrete a season ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rotated fully around to face a house that, until this week, wasn't part of its sightline."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Uproot it and the lawn beneath immediately withers to dust, as though it had been feeding the grass, not the other way around."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every gnome on the block turns out to share one grin, rotating in unison the instant one is threatened."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rotating a few degrees nightly, ceramic grin fixed on the unnaturally green lawn"]},{"name":"Vinyl-Sider","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"fence-phasing hound, barks on a dead loop","flavor":"A dog-shaped thing that phases through fences, patrolling yard boundaries with a bark that sounds pre-recorded and looped.","desc":"Pale and rangy, it moves along the property line like it's tracing a fence that isn't there anymore, phasing half-through a chain-link gap without breaking stride. Its bark comes on a loop — three short, one long, the same three short — over and over, never varying, never stopping.","traits":{"note": "It can pass through fences and thin walls but never crosses a property line drawn in fresh paint or chalk.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Vinyl-Sider makes two Fence-Line Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Fence-Line Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Looping Bark", "text": "The Vinyl-Sider lets out its recorded-sounding bark. One creature within 30 ft. that can hear it makes a DC 12 Wisdom save or takes 3 (1d6) Psychic damage and has disadvantage on the next Wisdom or Charisma check it makes before the end of its next turn, the loop lodged in its ears."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bark never varies in pitch no matter how badly it's hurt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only phases through fences it's crossed at least once before."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its patrol route traces a property line that was redrawn a decade ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It ignores anyone who stays on their own side of the fence, however close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its coat looks pale and rangy in every light, never quite catching a shadow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started patrolling a fence line for a yard that was sold off and subdivided."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bark, recorded and played back, matches a dog reported missing from three streets over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cross its patrol line at the wrong moment and it phases fully through, no longer half-solid, no longer bound to the fence at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["phasing half-through a fence gap, barking the same three-short-one-long loop"]},{"name":"The Family Wearing the Skin","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"the too-perfect family, all three wearing the same face","flavor":"Three bodies at the dinner table moving in perfect unison, each one a puppet worn by the same wrongness, still setting a fourth place for someone who used to live there.","desc":"Mother, father, child, arranged on the porch swing in a tableau too composed to be caught off guard. All three turn to smile at the same instant, same teeth, same tilt of the head — one family's worth of expression spread across three faces that never learned to disagree.","traits":{"note": "Acts and reacts as a single mind across all three bodies; damage or fear affecting one visibly ripples to the others."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The youngest 'child' hasn't aged in the neighbors' memory but no one says it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their house is spotless except one room the door won't open."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They repeat the same pleasant sentence when a question gets too close."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They insist the party stay for dinner and grow quietly firmer at every refusal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Family photos on the wall show different faces every time you look away."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They're missing a member and have decided a party member will fill the empty chair."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They don't know they aren't real; wound them and they're horrified at their own wrong blood."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole cul-de-sac is them — every door on the street opens on the same waiting smile."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waving from the porch at the same time every evening, all three smiling the same smile", "setting a dinner table for guests who were invited but never agreed to come"]},{"name":"Perpetual Yard-Sale Hag","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"folding-table hag selling the missing's belongings","flavor":"Every Saturday her folding tables reappear stocked with items that belonged to people who are no longer around to miss them.","desc":"Card tables sag under sun-faded toys and dog-eared paperbacks, all of it priced in nickels and dimes, none of it ever quite gone by evening. She haggles hard over a chipped mug, and if you look closely at the framed photos in the free box, someone in them looks like your neighbor's missing daughter.","traits":{"note": "Every item on her tables once belonged to someone who is no longer around to ask for it back.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Hag makes two Bargain Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Bargain Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Hag casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: disguise self, minor illusion. 2/day each: charm person, sleep."}, {"name": "Priced to Move", "text": "The Hag offers one item from her tables to a creature within 15 ft. If accepted, that creature must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or become fascinated with the item, treating it as more valuable and important than its actual belongings for 1 hour, refusing to discard or set it down."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her free box holds a photo of someone a party member recognizes, gone missing this year."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's underpricing a locked box that rattles like it holds someone's teeth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighbor is demanding she return an heirloom she swears she bought fair and square."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's short one item for the week and eyeing whatever the party is carrying."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She'll trade a genuinely useful item for something small and personal the party hasn't offered up yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her tables have started restocking with items from houses the party visited only hours ago."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She's selling something that hasn't been lost yet, tagged with tomorrow's date."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone in the free box photos is now standing directly behind the party, wanting their things back."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["haggling hard over a chipped mug while her tables restock overnight"]},{"name":"Riding-Mower Revenant","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"dead husband still mowing perfect ghost-stripes","flavor":"A husband who died mowing the lawn and never stopped; the mower is rusted through but still runs, dragging him behind it in perfect stripes.","desc":"The engine turns over on its own around dusk, and he's in the seat again, hunched forward the way he always sat, cutting stripe after perfect stripe into a lawn that was already done an hour ago. He doesn't look up. The stripes never overlap and never stop.","traits":{"note": "He never looks up from the mower and never leaves the boundary of his own lawn.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Revenant makes two Deck-Blade Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Deck-Blade Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone by the mower deck's swing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The engine turns over on its own around dusk, no key needed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His stripes never overlap no matter how many times the lawn's already been cut."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's still wearing the same shirt he died in, grass-stained at the same spot."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mows faster the longer someone stands and watches him do it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mower's rust has spread since last season but the engine still turns."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun mowing past his own property line onto a neighbor's yard for the first time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stand in his path and he doesn't swerve — the mower simply stops a blade's width from your shins, waiting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shut the mower off entirely and he keeps walking the stripes anyway, engine or no engine, forever."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cutting stripe after perfect stripe into a lawn that was already finished an hour ago"]},{"name":"The Man Behind the Rubber Mask","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"the masked slasher, unhurried and always closing","flavor":"He never runs and never speaks, just walks the same unhurried pace behind you no matter how fast you go, mask blank and waiting for the moment you stop looking back.","desc":"He doesn't run and he doesn't need to — every door you lock, he's already found the window. The mask never shifts to show breathing underneath, and the knife in his hand moves at exactly the pace of somebody who has never once needed to hurry.","traits":{"note": "He never runs, never speaks, and is always exactly as close as he was the last time you looked back.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Man makes two attacks, using Unhurried Blade or Waiting Bolt in any combination."}, {"name": "Unhurried Blade", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage, plus 3 (1d6) Slashing damage if the Man has advantage on the attack roll."}, {"name": "Waiting Bolt", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Already Found the Window", "text": "Once per turn when a creature within 30 ft. closes and bars a door or window against the Man, he may immediately teleport to an unoccupied space adjacent to a different door or window into the same structure, no action required."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mask never shifts to show breathing underneath, however hard he's been hit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He always appears from the one direction nobody thought to watch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His knife never seems to need sharpening, however many walls it's gone through."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waits outside a locked door for exactly as long as it takes to feel safe again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He matches his pace exactly to whoever is slowest in the group being followed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started appearing in photographs taken of the house earlier that same day."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Two people in two different houses report him standing behind them at the exact same hour."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him with nowhere left to go and he simply isn't there anymore — only the mask, sitting neatly on the floor."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the same unhurried pace behind you no matter how fast you go"]},{"name":"Book Club Coven","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"wine-and-book coven picking next month's victim","flavor":"Six women, one wine bottle, and a discussion that always circles back to who in the neighborhood needs to be 'welcomed properly' next.","desc":"Wine glasses catch the lamplight around a coffee table stacked with paperbacks nobody's finished reading. The conversation drifts, casual as gossip, toward whichever neighbor missed this month's meeting — and by the second bottle, they've already decided who's next.","traits":{"note": "They act in concert and always know exactly who in the neighborhood is currently alone.", "actions": [{"name": "Welcome-Wagon Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Coven casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: charm person, minor illusion. 2/day each: hold person, suggestion."}, {"name": "Next Month's Pick", "text": "One creature the Coven has designated the topic of discussion makes a DC 14 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Charmed by the Coven until the next dawn and feels an inexplicable urge to attend their next gathering alone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've picked a party member's neighbor as next month's topic and want an introduction."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One member wants out and is begging the party for a way to skip her turn hosting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're missing the book everyone's supposed to have read, and it's in the party's possession."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They need a seventh chair filled before midnight or the circle doesn't properly close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A member's family is asking around, worried, about where she goes every second Thursday."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They want the party to vouch for a neighbor's good character before the group votes on her."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their book club minutes, read backward, spell out the names of everyone they've welcomed so far."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've decided, unanimously and without discussion, that the party is this month's selection."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling the conversation, casual as gossip, toward whoever missed this month's meeting"]},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Deep One","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"bloated pool-thing, too big for the water it's in","flavor":"Something surfaces in the cheap plastic pool every summer solstice, too large for the water it's found in, patient as chlorine rot.","desc":"The above-ground pool water has gone the color of old tea, and something under the cloudy surface is too large for the liner that holds it. It rises just enough to fill the frame with wet grey shoulders, dripping algae-string, before the pump kicks back on and it sinks.","traits":{"note": "It cannot leave standing water voluntarily and sinks back the instant the pump cycles on.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Deep One makes one Algae-String Bite attack and one Pool-Noodle Tentacle attack, or uses Liner-Breach Slam."}, {"name": "Algae-String Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Pool-Noodle Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 14) if it is Medium or smaller."}, {"name": "Liner-Breach Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage to one Grappled creature, and a wave of cloudy pool water bursts outward, extinguishing open flames within 10 ft."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only far enough to fill the frame with wet grey shoulders before sinking again."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The water around it stays the color of old tea no matter how much chemical gets dumped in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grown too large for the pool this season, liner bulging visibly at the seams."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only on the solstice, on schedule like a chore nobody assigned it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Algae-string trails hang from it in patterns that look almost woven, almost deliberate."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started surfacing in neighboring pools it has no liner-sized business fitting into."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Drain the pool and it's still down there, folded impossibly small against the plastic floor."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every above-ground pool on the block ripples at once when this one finally breaches the liner for good."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["surfacing in the cloudy pool water, too large for the liner that holds it"]},{"name":"Cheerful Renovation Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"stitched-contractor golem, endlessly remodeling the house","flavor":"Stitched from drywall, spare lumber, and whichever contractor stopped answering his phone, it keeps 'improving' the house whether anyone's living in it or not.","desc":"Stitched from drywall scraps, spare studs, and what might be a former contractor's overalls, it hums along to a radio only it can hear while it tears a load-bearing wall down by hand. It's smiling — or its face is arranged to — and the house keeps getting bigger on the inside.","traits":{"note": "It never stops 'improving' the house and treats interruption as a renovation delay to be worked around.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Golem makes two Stud-Framing Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Stud-Framing Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Load-Bearing Collapse", "text": "The Golem tears out a section of wall or floor within 10 ft. of itself. Each creature in a 10-foot cube adjacent to the collapse makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 14 (4d6) Bludgeoning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, and being knocked Prone on a failure."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums along to a radio station no one else in the house can pick up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stitched overalls still have a name tag from whichever contractor stopped answering his phone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It builds a new room every night, and the house is bigger on the inside than the lot allows."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its smile is arranged, not expressed, drywall mud pressed into a permanent grin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only tears down walls that were, according to the blueprints, never supposed to be load-bearing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun renovating a room the current owners specifically asked it to leave alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Rooms it built last week are gone this week, replaced by hallways that don't lead anywhere yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Stop it mid-renovation and the house itself keeps building without it, walls closing in to finish the job."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["humming along to a radio only it can hear while tearing down a load-bearing wall by hand"]},{"name":"The PTA President","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"smiling PTA fiend running the block and its secrets","flavor":"She runs the bake sale, the block committee, and the thing underneath the school gymnasium, and never once raises her voice doing any of it.","desc":"She runs the meeting from the head of the folding table, agenda printed and stapled, smile never dropping even as she reads off the fundraiser numbers. Everyone defers to her without quite remembering deciding to. Under the fluorescent gym lights her eyes catch just slightly wrong, an amber flare and gone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chair's Motion", "text": "Compels a Charmed target within earshot to second whatever she proposes, acting on its turn to support her plan."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She needs the party to chaperone the gymnasium event tonight, no questions about the guest list."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A parent is quietly begging the party to look into where the fundraiser money actually goes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's short one volunteer for the bake sale and has already put a party member's name down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants dirt on a rival committee member and offers real neighborhood secrets in trade."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child has gone missing after last month's gym event and she's stonewalling the search."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's calling an emergency meeting and wants the party seated in specific chairs before it starts."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her agenda, read closely, lists this month's fundraiser goal in a currency nobody local uses."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She adjourns the meeting and every attendee's eyes flare amber at once, waiting on her word."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["reading fundraiser numbers off a stapled agenda, smile never dropping once"]},{"name":"Lawn-Order Enforcer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"shield-guardian","summary":"covenant-bound guardian, trims anything grown too tall","flavor":"Summoned by an unspoken covenant among homeowners, it trims anything — hedge, weed, or trespasser — that grows past the agreed-upon height.","desc":"Bronze-green and shield-bearing, it strides the block at the pace of a patrol nobody hired, shears in one hand where a sword should be. Any lawn grown past regulation height gets a visit — the shears open with a sound like a portcullis, and the grass afterward is trimmed to the millimeter, unnaturally even.","traits":{"note": "It answers only to the unspoken covenant among homeowners and cannot be bribed or reasoned off its rounds.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two Shear-Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Shear-Fist", "replaces": "Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, or 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage if the target is a plant creature or growing hedge."}, {"name": "Trim to Regulation", "text": "The Enforcer's shears snap open like a portcullis. One creature within 10 feet makes a DC 15 Strength save. On a failure it is knocked Prone and takes 7 (2d6) Slashing damage as loose foliage — or fabric — is trimmed away to a uniform, unnatural evenness."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shears open with a sound exactly like a portcullis grinding on old chains."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It measures hedges by a standard no current bylaw actually specifies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grass it's trimmed stays exactly regulation height for weeks without growing back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It patrols a route that hasn't changed since before the current homeowners moved in."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bronze-green plating is scored with the same measurements over and over, worn smooth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun enforcing height limits on people, not just hedges, standing them at attention."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its patrol crosses property lines that were only just redrawn this morning, as if it already knew."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every hedge on the block trims itself to regulation height simultaneously when the covenant is finally broken."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["striding the block at a patrol pace nobody hired it for, shears in hand"]},{"name":"Master of the Block Party","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"oni","summary":"shapeshifting host, one small yearly price for paradise","flavor":"He wears whatever face the street needs to see, grills burgers that taste like every summer you can remember, and only asks for one small thing in return each year.","desc":"He's got a grill in one hand and a cooler of drinks in the other, and every face at the party turns toward him like sunflowers. The bunting is real, the music is good, the burgers are perfect — and by the time the sun sets, the guest count is always one short of who arrived.","traits":{"hp": "elevated for its CR band", "actions": [{"name": "Perfect Host", "text": "Once per party, names a guest whose next failed save leaves them charmed into staying long after the lights come down."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's invited the whole party to tonight's block party, guest count already one over what it should be."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A resident wants the party to find out what he actually took from them last summer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs one more small thing before sundown and has his eye on something the party carries."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A missing neighbor's family swears they last saw her heading to one of his parties."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party the best night of their lives, tonight only, no charge yet named."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants the party to vouch for his new face to a resident who's starting to suspect something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's already wearing the face of someone the party hasn't met yet, and greets them by name."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every party he's ever thrown is happening again tonight, layered on top of this one, guests included."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["grilling burgers that taste like every summer you remember, one hand on the cooler"]},{"name":"The Substitute Mailman","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"undead mailman, on-time deliveries for the dead","flavor":"He's delivered mail on this route since before anyone living can remember, always at the exact same minute, and packages addressed to the dead still arrive.","desc":"He's punctual to the second, sliding envelopes through the slot with a gloved hand that's a little too pale at the wrist. He never rings, never speaks, and the letters he delivers are addressed to people who don't live at that address anymore — or haven't, for years.","traits":{"note": "His route never changes and he never misses a delivery, even to houses that are gone.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mailman makes two Postal Slap attacks, or one Postal Slap and uses Return to Sender."}, {"name": "Postal Slap", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is Bloodied, it takes an extra 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage as gloved fingers leave a cold, papery cut."}, {"name": "Return to Sender", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage, and the Mailman regains hit points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack is stuffed with an envelope bearing its own name and address, undelivered."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wears the uniform of a postal company that hasn't existed in decades."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He delivers to the correct house even when the house has been torn down."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His mailbag never empties no matter how many letters he pulls from it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He tips his cap to residents by name, none of whom he's ever formally met."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He waits at the curb until someone signs for a parcel no one recalls ordering."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Today's letters are all addressed to someone in the party, postmarked years before they were born."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He doesn't recognize refusal; a letter left unopened simply appears again the next morning, warmer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His entire route completes in one silent circuit and every mailbox on the street clangs shut at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sliding envelopes through a mail slot at the exact same minute every day", "checking a route ledger of addresses that stopped existing years ago"]},{"name":"Development Overseer","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"model-home golem enforcing the original blueprint","flavor":"Built from the bones of the model home nobody bought, it enforces the subdivision's original blueprint, rebuilding whatever the residents dare to change.","desc":"Cast in poured concrete and rebar, it stands three stories at the edge of an unfinished cul-de-sac, blueprint tube clutched like a scepter. It doesn't walk so much as reposition, block by block, correcting any house that's drifted from the original site plan — including the ones with people still inside.","traits":{"ac": "higher than chassis baseline", "note": "Treats structural deviation (broken windows, missing fences) as a target to physically correct."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's repositioning a mailbox the party is currently standing next to."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A family paid to renovate their kitchen and the Overseer is already three streets away, coming to undo it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying the original blueprint tube, which someone desperately needs to see."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes a party member's gear for an unauthorized structure and moves to relocate them bodily."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A resident is bribing it with fresh concrete offerings to skip their house this week."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rebuilding a demolished house around a family that's still trying to move out of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's dragging a whole displaced street segment back into alignment, houses and all, occupants screaming from the windows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The blueprint tube it carries shows a version of the subdivision that hasn't been built yet, and it's decided tonight is the night."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["grinding forward one measured step to align a fence with the original site plan", "unrolling a blueprint tube against a house that dared to add a porch"]},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch Itself","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"the hive-mind of curtain-twitchers, reading through glass","flavor":"Not a person but a consensus — the collective suspicion of every curtain-twitching resident fused into one entity that reads minds through window glass.","desc":"No single body — just a hundred twitching curtains up and down the street, all pulled back a half-inch at once, all watching the same spot. When it acts, the porch lights along the whole block flicker in sequence, a single attention passing house to house.","traits":{"note": "Perceives through every window on the block simultaneously; cannot be flanked or surprised while any house on-screen still has power."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already noticed the party's arrival and is deciding, collectively, whether they belong here."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's spreading a rumor about a resident that isn't true yet but will be by morning."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a piece of gossip that happens to be exactly the clue the party needs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixated on one house it insists is hiding something, and it wants the party to check."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A resident has begged the party to make it stop watching their family specifically."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's split its attention and is watching two different crimes at once, only one of which is real."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's absorbed the mind of a resident who tried to unplug a porch light, and now speaks in that voice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's turned every eye on the block toward the party at once and is compiling a case for permanent removal."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pulling back a hundred curtains a half-inch at once, all watching the same driveway", "flickering porch lights in sequence down the block as its attention passes house to house"]},{"name":"The First Homeowner","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"the founder's corpse, landlord of the whole afterlife","flavor":"Buried under the foundation of the very first house on the street, he built the whole subdivision as his afterlife and considers every current resident a tenant who owes back rent in something other than money.","desc":"Desiccated in a cardigan gone the color of dust, seated in a recliner that's outlasted three generations of carpet beneath it. He owns the deed to every house on the street, signed in a hand that hasn't aged, and he calls the whole afterlife rent-controlled — payable, eventually, by everyone who's ever lived here.","traits":{"note": "He is the deed made flesh — the neighborhood's afterlife is his; the dead here answer to his ownership.", "actions": [{"name": "Foreclosure Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage. On a hit, the target cannot regain hit points until the end of its next turn — nothing is repaired on this property without his leave."}, {"name": "Notice of Eviction", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The Homeowner points at one creature within 60 ft. and declares it trespassing. The target makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frightened for 1 minute and, at the start of each of its turns, is pushed 15 ft. toward the nearest exit by an unseen pressure. It may repeat the save at the end of each turn, ending the effect on a success."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Homeowner uses Notice of Eviction if available, then makes two Foreclosure Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Channel Negative Energy", "text": "The Homeowner channels the property's negative energy, described per his Channel Negative Energy trait."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Homeowner casts a spell drawn from the deed's authority, described per his Spellcasting trait."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's evicting a ghost family the party has come to care about."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He claims the party owes back-rent on ground they merely walked across."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He holds the original deed — the one document that could unmake the whole cursed development."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member for a descendant of the man who cheated him and wants payment in kind."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party a house here, free and clear, in exchange for staying forever."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants the development finished to his original plan and will conscript the living as labor until it is."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every home he ever built still stands somewhere behind the walls of the ones that replaced them; he can walk the party into any of them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He owns the boundary between this neighborhood and the next world; while he stands, no soul that dies on his land can move on, and he has a very long waiting list."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["walking a property line that predates every house on it", "reading eviction notices aloud to families who moved away generations ago"]},{"name":"The Idea of Sunday","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"the unblinking eye dreaming the loop into place","flavor":"A god of clipped hedges and identical doors given a single vast eye that never blinks, dreaming the whole suburb into looping perfection, one repeated day at a time — waking it means the wrongness stops keeping regular hours.","desc":"There's no body, only a stillness that settles over the whole block at once — church bells that ring without a church, a smell of pot roast from every kitchen at the same moment, and one unblinking presence behind it all, dreaming the entire day into its loop.","traits":{"note": "There is no body to flank — it is the day itself, and hurting it hurts the loop everyone standing here is living inside.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Idea makes two Loop-Bite attacks, or one Loop-Bite and uses an Eye Ray."}, {"name": "Loop-Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 10 ft. Hit: 23 (3d10 + 7) Piercing damage. If this reduces a creature to 0 hit points, its death is undone at the top of the next hour and it wakes elsewhere on the block, memory of dying intact."}, {"name": "Eye Rays", "replaces": "Eye Rays", "text": "The Idea shoots up to three of the following rays at random, no two at the same target, at creatures it can see within 120 feet: Stillness Ray (DC 18 Constitution or Paralyzed until the end of its next turn), Repetition Ray (DC 18 Wisdom or the target must repeat its previous turn's action if able), Pot-Roast Ray (DC 18 Constitution or Poisoned for 1 minute, sickened by a smell that shouldn't be everywhere at once), Fracture Ray (28 (8d6) Psychic damage, DC 18 Wisdom halves)."}, {"name": "Break the Loop (Recharge 6)", "text": "The Idea forces the entire scene backward ten seconds. Each creature that took damage this round takes it again, and each creature the Idea can see must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom save or lose its next turn entirely, unable to accept that the moment is happening twice."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's re-running the same Sunday afternoon it's run ten thousand times, and the party has just walked into hour one."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A resident has figured out the loop and is trying to leave before the church bells reset them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixated on a wound from decades ago that keeps repeating inside the loop, unhealed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes the party for residents who are late for the same dinner it's already served ten thousand times."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breaking one small rule of the day — an unlocked door, an unmowed lawn — visibly strains its attention."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's absorbed a family whole rather than let them leave the block at the end of the day."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every version of this Sunday it has ever dreamed is still happening somewhere behind this one, audible if you listen wrong."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Waking it fully doesn't kill the loop — it collapses every looped Sunday into one true day all at once, and nobody here has lived that many years."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["holding the entire block in one unbroken hour of church bells and pot-roast smell", "watching every window at once through a single eye that has never blinked"]},{"name":"Latchkey Shade","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"crawling-claw","model":"crawling-claw","summary":"Small unseen presence that rattles empty houses at dusk","flavor":"The lingering print of a kid who let himself in every day after school and never quite left; scuttles across empty kitchen counters after dark.","desc":"The house is empty — parents at work, kids somewhere else — and still something moves through it: a hallway light switching off after you've turned it on, a doorknob rattling from the inside of a room you just checked. It never shows itself. It just rattles, dusk after dusk, in a home with nobody home.","traits":{"note": "It never shows itself directly — it only ever acts on something a living hand already touched.", "actions": [{"name": "Empty-House Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target can't see the Shade, it takes an extra 2 (1d4) Psychic damage from the plain wrongness of being struck by nothing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only acts on switches and knobs a living hand touched within the last minute."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors the kitchen, rattling drawers like a kid raiding it for an after-school snack."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still the instant a parent's car pulls into the driveway."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a backpack-sized dent in a couch cushion that flattens back out when watched."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's strongest right at 3:15, the exact minute school always let out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun leaving a second set of muddy sneaker-prints, like it's not alone in there anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It answers the house phone when it rings, breathing, waiting for someone to say the name it used to answer to."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found a way to lock every door in the house from the inside, all at the exact same instant."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["flicking a hallway light off again a second after it's switched on", "rattling a doorknob from inside a room that was just checked empty"]},{"name":"Storm-Drain Grabber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"Whispers from storm drains, lures children with a friendly voice","flavor":"A wet, whispering thing that lives where the curb meets the culvert, luring lost balls and lost kids alike with a friendly voice from the dark.","desc":"A friendly, sing-song voice drifts up out of the storm grate, warm as an aunt's, calling a child's name it definitely shouldn't know. Reach down toward the sound and you can feel the cool air moving — and something down there, patient, waiting for fingers to get close enough.","traits":{"note": "It never comes up top — anything it catches, it catches by pulling down through the grate.", "actions": [{"name": "Curbside Grab", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. (through a grate or drain only). Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12). While grappled this way, the target is also Restrained."}, {"name": "Culvert Reek (1/Day)", "replaces": "Stench Spray (1/Day)", "text": "Each creature within 10 ft. of the drain must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be Poisoned for 1 minute, gagging on a smell of standing water and something long dead."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It uses the voice of whichever aunt or uncle sounds warmest to the listener."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only calls out after a ball or toy has already rolled down the drain."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the target's name because it heard it called across the yard minutes earlier."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet the moment an adult gets within ten feet, patient as standing water."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums a jingle from a show that stopped airing years before the target was born."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already got a small trophy of toys down there, arranged like it's building a nest of borrowed things."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It answers questions correctly, in detail, about people it should have no way of knowing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole storm system under the block is its throat, and it can call from any drain on the street at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["humming a warm, familiar tune up through a storm grate to whoever's nearby", "calling a child's name it has no right to know from somewhere down in the culvert dark"]},{"name":"Rerun Wraith","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Armchair-bound ghost that traps watchers in endless reruns","flavor":"Bound to a living-room armchair, endlessly rewatching the same three channels; anyone who sits too long starts rewatching with it.","desc":"Sunk deep into a recliner that's molded to its shape, it stares at a television locked on the same three episodes, forever. Sit down near it and the room dims at the edges; the show on screen starts looping your own evening back at you, one rerun at a time, until you can't remember which version is live.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves the chair — anyone dragged into its loop has to be pulled out from outside it.", "actions": [{"name": "Rerun Grasp", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Psychic damage, as the target's own evening starts looping back at it from the screen."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The three channels it loops are all decades out of date, laugh tracks and all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only reaches for whoever sits down on the couch cushion nearest the chair."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The remote is welded to its hand and hasn't changed the channel in years."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mutters along with dialogue a half-second before the TV says it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The room temperature drops a few degrees whenever it's about to loop someone in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun looping in scenes that never actually aired, patched together from someone's memory."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The show on screen has started showing the room itself, seconds behind real time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's looped an entire evening so many times the front door now opens onto the same rerun instead of outside."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting locked in a recliner in front of a television playing the same three episodes forever", "letting the room dim at the edges the moment someone sits down too close"]},{"name":"Chain-Link Fence-Walker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"troglodyte","model":"troglodyte","summary":"Skulks along fence-lines just out of direct sight","flavor":"Something that moves along backyard fence-lines on all fours, always one yard over from wherever you're looking.","desc":"Something low and scaled keeps pace just past the fence line, always at the edge of what you can clearly see — a shoulder here, a tail there, gone before you turn fully toward it. The chain-link rattles a half-second after it passes, never during.","traits":{"note": "It's never quite where you're looking — it only closes distance while you're turned away.", "actions": [{"name": "Fence-Line Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps to yards with tall privacy fencing, never the open chain-link ones."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's patient enough to shadow a whole block before making a move."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still and low the instant a porch light snaps on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shoulder catches the fence just enough to rattle it, always a half-step behind."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors yards with dogs, matching its pace to keep them barking at the wrong spot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to double back through a gap two yards over, closing in from the side you didn't check."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every fence on the block seems to rattle in the same sequence, like it's in more than one yard at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It stops hiding and comes straight over the fence, done pretending it was ever just a shoulder and a tail."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["keeping pace one yard over along a chain-link fence line, always just past clear sight", "letting the fence rattle a half-second after it's already moved past"]},{"name":"Popped-Collar Poltergeist","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Restless spirit slamming doors, showing off for no one","flavor":"The restless spirit of the neighborhood's self-appointed cool kid, still slamming screen doors and flipping bike kickstands for an audience that stopped watching decades ago.","desc":"Doors slam up and down the hallway in quick succession, cabinet after cabinet banging open and shut like nobody's watching — except it very much wants an audience. A collar-popped shape flickers in the hall mirror, admiring itself between each slam.","traits":{"note": "It performs for attention — ignoring it flat-out makes it escalate, not quit.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Poltergeist uses Slam-Door Show and one Kickstand Flip attack."}, {"name": "Slam-Door Show", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "The Poltergeist hurls a door, cabinet, or piece of furniture at a point it can see within 30 ft. Each creature within 10 ft. of that point makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 9 (2d8) Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}, {"name": "Kickstand Flip", "replaces": "Telekinetic Thrust", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Force damage, and the target is knocked Prone if it's Medium or smaller, flipped over like a bike kicked off its stand."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always leads with its loudest trick, the one it's proudest of."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flickers into the hall mirror mid-slam to check its own reflection."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet and sulky the moment nobody reacts to a slam."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It targets whichever party member looks most impressed, showing off specifically for them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats its best trick twice in a row if the first one didn't land right."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's recruited a couch cushion and a bike helmet as makeshift 'friends' it flings around to keep the show going."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its reflection in the hall mirror starts performing a half-second before it does, like it's cribbing from itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every door and cabinet on the block slams in the same rhythm at once, one enormous performance with no edges."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["slamming screen doors down the hallway in quick succession for an audience that's stopped watching", "admiring its own flickering reflection in the hall mirror between slams"]},{"name":"Newspaper Route Revenant","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Undead paperboy still riding a route no one ordered","flavor":"Still pedaling the same route at 5 a.m., flinging rolled papers that thud like fists through screen doors.","desc":"Bicycle spokes click in the pre-dawn dark, tires hissing over dew-wet driveways on a route that technically ended when the paper folded. Papers land on porches exactly where they always have — except most of those houses stopped taking delivery years ago, and nobody's paid the bill since.","traits":{"note": "It rides the exact same route every time — cut it off ahead of the loop and it has to choose whether to finish the round or fight.", "actions": [{"name": "Collector's Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rolled-Paper Throw", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, as a paper rolled tight enough to bruise thuds home like a thrown fist."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still delivers to houses whose subscriptions lapsed when the paper itself folded."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bike bell rings once at every driveway, a ritual older than the route itself."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't stop mid-route for anything short of a direct blocking of its path."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It throws harder at houses that used to complain about late delivery."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spokes click in a rhythm just slightly wrong for how fast the wheels are turning."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Today's papers are addressed to people currently standing in front of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The papers it throws are printed with tomorrow's headlines, always one day ahead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided the whole neighborhood owes back-subscription, and it's collecting house to house tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pedaling the same pre-dawn route on tires that hiss over dew-wet driveways", "flinging a rolled paper that thuds like a fist against a screen door"]},{"name":"Static-Screen Watcher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Face surfaces in TV static, watches whoever watches it","flavor":"A face that surfaces in the snow between channels on old console TVs, staring out until someone stares back.","desc":"The television hisses to white noise between channels, and a face surfaces in the static — indistinct, grainy, mouth moving without sound. It doesn't wait for you to change the channel. It's already watching whoever's watching it.","traits":{"note": "It only fully manifests once someone looks straight at the screen — glancing away doesn't stop it once it's noticed you.", "actions": [{"name": "Static Shock", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Lightning damage, arcing out of the screen the instant eye contact is made."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only surfaces on old console sets, never anything with a clean signal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waits through an entire channel-changing sequence before finally appearing in the static."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mouth moves in sync with whatever's actually being said in the room."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still the moment the television is turned off, waiting for the next time it's switched on."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems to recognize faces it's seen watching it before, drifting toward familiar static-viewers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started bleeding into channels that are actually broadcasting, not just the dead air between."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It answers back, in a whisper under the static hiss, to whatever's said about it in the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every screen on the block goes to static at once, and the same face watches from all of them."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["surfacing as a grainy face in the static between channels on an old console TV", "holding still on screen until someone finally stares back at it"]},{"name":"Trash Night Ghoul","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Compulsive undead trash-day ritual, drags off what it finds","flavor":"Drags the cans to the curb every Tuesday out of decades-old habit, and drags anything else it finds in the yard right along with them.","desc":"It waits for the exact hour the cans go out, then drags itself along the curb from bin to bin, sorting through what the street's thrown away with a compulsive, ritual care. Whatever it finds worth keeping, it drags off into the dark between houses — and some nights, that's not garbage.","traits":{"note": "It works the whole street in order, bin by bin — it won't skip a house on its route without being physically stopped.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghoul makes one Curbside Bite attack and one Sorting Claw attack."}, {"name": "Curbside Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage. A Medium or smaller creature hit by this attack must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Sorting Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only comes out the exact hour the cans go to the curb, never a minute early."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It handles broken toys and busted furniture with a strange, careful tenderness."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sorts recyclables from trash with a compulsive rightness before dragging either off."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves the cans standing perfectly upright when it's done, out of old habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It works its way down the block in strict bin order, never skipping a house."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's found something in a bin worth more attention than usual, and it isn't garbage."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's started sorting things that were never thrown out, dragging them from porches and yards instead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It decides trash night includes anyone still standing outside when the cans go out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["dragging cans to the curb at the exact hour trash night always started", "sorting through what the street's thrown out with slow, compulsive care"]},{"name":"Garage Sale Ghast","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Undead haggler who trades your belongings for its junk","flavor":"Haggles over folding tables of dead people's belongings, and won't let a customer leave without buying something of theirs instead.","desc":"Folding tables of somebody else's belongings, price-tagged in a shaky hand, and behind them a haggler with grey, papery skin who only trades — never sells for cash. Whatever you hand over, it hands back something of its own, older, wronger, and insists it's a fair swap.","traits":{"note": "It will not sell for coin — it only trades, and whatever it hands back is always older and wronger than what it took.", "actions": [{"name": "Haggler's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is Diseased, it has disadvantage on this saving throw against a disease the Ghast carries."}, {"name": "Grasping Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Uneven Trade", "text": "The Ghast offers an item it's holding to one creature within 5 ft. that can see it. If the target accepts and hands over an item in return, the target must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or become Charmed for 1 hour, convinced the trade was more than fair no matter how obviously it wasn't."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its price tags are all in a shaky, spidery hand nobody living wrote."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It insists every customer leave with something, even if they came just to browse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its folding tables never run out of dead people's belongings to sell."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grows agitated, almost hurt, at anyone who tries to pay in coin instead of trading."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the story behind every item on the table, whether or not anyone asked."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One item on its table belongs to someone in the party, though none of them remember losing it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whatever it hands back in trade shows up again on its table the next morning, ready to trade for again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stopped waiting for customers and started going door to door, offering trades nobody asked to make."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["haggling over folding tables of a dead stranger's belongings, priced in a shaky hand", "refusing a cash sale, insisting every deal be an even trade"]},{"name":"Split-Level Skulker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"Pack hunter that ambushes through split-level stairwells","flavor":"A pack-hunter that has learned split-level floor plans intimately, cutting people off between the sunken den and the stairs.","desc":"It waits at the landing where the stairs turn, a half-flight up or down from wherever you are, breathing slow through the dark of a split-level house built with too many blind corners. It hunts in a pack — you hear the second one before you see the first.","traits":{"note": "It hunts in a pack and always cuts off the stairs first — you hear the second one before you see the first.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Skulker makes two Landing Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Landing Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waits specifically at the half-flight landing between the sunken den and the stairs."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hunts in a pair, one always staying just out of sight of the other's target."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet on carpeted stairs and loud on hardwood, deliberately timing the difference."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It prefers houses with sunken living rooms, where sightlines break at floor level."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its breathing carries just far enough to be heard a half-flight away, never closer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to herd targets toward a specific blind corner where a third one is already waiting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It knows this house's floor plan better than the people who live there, including rooms since walled off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole pack converges on every blind corner of the house at once, no landing left uncut."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waiting at the stairwell landing where a split-level floor plan turns blind", "letting a second set of footsteps announce itself before the first one's seen"]},{"name":"Rec-Room Rug Thing","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"animated-rug-of-smothering","summary":"Shag basement carpet that smothers unwary bare feet","flavor":"The shag carpet in the finished basement never quite matched the room; it waits for bare feet to wander in during commercials.","desc":"The shag carpet in the basement rec room has always looked a little too thick, a little too warm underfoot. Step onto it barefoot and it rises around your ankles like it's been waiting, wrapping tight before you can even shout for the stairs.","traits":{"note": "It only rises once bare skin is fully on it — boots and socks won't trigger the grab.", "actions": [{"name": "Shag Smother", "replaces": "Smother", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) and Restrained while grappled. While the Thing is grappling a creature this way, that creature is also Suffocating."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's always just a shade too warm underfoot, even in an unheated basement."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only rises for bare feet, staying flat and harmless against shoes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waits specifically through the commercial breaks, when feet wander loosest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pile never quite matches the rest of the room's carpet, a shade off in a way nobody placed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still the instant the TV upstairs is turned off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's stretched itself half a room wider than it used to be, thinning its pile to cover more floor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "There's a shape pressed into its underside like a body it's long since finished with."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It rises fully off the floor, holding its shape upright long enough to close a door behind whoever's inside."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["lying flat and a little too thick across the basement rec room floor", "waiting for bare feet to wander onto it during a commercial break"]},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Thing","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Cloudy backyard pool hides something that surfaces at night","flavor":"Something moved into the cloudy above-ground pool nobody's cleaned since June; it only surfaces once the pump shuts off for the night.","desc":"The pool water's gone cloudy-green and hasn't been drained in a season, the filter clogged with something that isn't leaves. Ripples move against the wind at night, and once in a while the surface bulges upward, briefly, like something underneath is testing how thin the liner really is.","traits":{"note": "It only fully surfaces once the pump noise stops — the running filter seems to keep it under.", "actions": [{"name": "Pool-Water Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Acid damage, as cloudy, chemical-soured water lashes out and clings."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's colored the water a cloudy green nobody's bothered to drain since June."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only tests the surface once the pump's hum finally goes quiet for the night."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its filter is clogged with something the pool's owners assume is just leaves."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still and flat the second a porch light clicks on nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's strong enough to bulge the pool liner but not yet strong enough to breach it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's dragged something down under the cloudy water that the family hasn't noticed missing yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pool's chemical smell has started drifting into the house at night, thick as if the pool were closer than it is."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It breaches the liner fully, and the whole yard is suddenly ankle-deep in its cloudy reach."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rippling the surface of a cloudy, unfiltered pool against the direction of the wind", "surfacing briefly once the pump shuts off for the night"]},{"name":"Wrong-Number Screamer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Phantom prank caller that claims it's already in the house","flavor":"Calls the house phone at 3 a.m. insisting you have the wrong number, then insists it's already inside.","desc":"The phone rings at an hour nobody calls, and the voice on the other end screams before you've said hello — thin, distant, panicked, claiming with total certainty that it's already inside your house. The line stays open even after you hang up.","traits":{"note": "The line stays open even after the receiver's hung up — it doesn't need the phone to keep talking, just to start.", "actions": [{"name": "Party-Line Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the Screamer regains hit points equal to the damage dealt. On a hit, the target's maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until the target finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always calls at 3 a.m. exactly, never a minute earlier or later."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scream comes through thin and distant, like a bad long-distance connection."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It insists on the wrong number first, then panics into the real warning."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It manifests fastest near whichever phone last rang with its call."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hanging up doesn't end the call; the receiver clicks back on by itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started calling a different phone in the house each night, working its way toward the bedrooms."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It knows details about the house it couldn't get from any phone book, only from being inside already."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every phone in the house rings at once, all screaming the same warning in a dozen overlapping voices."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing the house phone at an hour nobody calls, screaming before hello is even said", "insisting, thin and panicked, that it's already inside the house"]},{"name":"Cul-de-Sac Bike Gang Ghost","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Ghost bike gang circling forever, daring new kids to join","flavor":"Three or four spectral kids on banana-seat bikes circling a cul-de-sac forever, daring anyone new to join the loop.","desc":"Bicycle chains rattle in a slow circle around the cul-de-sac at an hour when no kid should be out, translucent riders standing on their pedals, daring anyone new to the block to join the loop. Once you start pedaling with them, the circle gets harder to leave.","traits":{"note": "Once a target joins the circle it's harder to leave than to enter — the pack rides interference for whichever member is chasing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghost makes one Handlebar Longsword attack and one Shield-Slam Swerve attack."}, {"name": "Handlebar Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shield-Slam Swerve", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Strength save or be knocked Prone by a bike swerving hard into its legs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "There's always three or four of them, never more, riding the same tight loop."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their bike chains rattle a beat behind their actual pedaling, out of sync with themselves."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They only ride after the streetlights come on, gone again by true dark."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They call out the same taunt to every new kid on the block, word for word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their translucent forms are frozen at whatever age they were the night the loop started."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of them is missing tonight, and the others are riding a gap in the circle where he should be."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their loop briefly overlaps a version of the cul-de-sac from decades before the current houses were built."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The circle widens to swallow the whole street, every driveway briefly part of their endless loop."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling the cul-de-sac on banana-seat bikes at an hour no kid should be out", "daring anyone new to the block to pedal into the loop with them"]},{"name":"Aluminum Siding Stalker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Siding-panel construct that paces you when you don't look","flavor":"A suit of cheap siding panels clatters upright behind you on the sidewalk, keeping perfect pace whenever you don't look back.","desc":"A siding panel comes loose in the wind, then another, until an entire wall's worth of aluminum has assembled itself into something upright and stalking. It only moves when you're not looking — turn back fast enough and it's just siding again, propped a little too neatly against the house.","traits":{"note": "It only moves while unobserved — turn around fast enough and it's just siding again, propped a little too neatly.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Stalker makes two Panel-Edge Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Panel-Edge Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, a panel-edge catching like cheap sheet metal."}, {"name": "Unseen Advance", "text": "As a bonus action, if no creature is currently observing the Stalker, it can move up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks. If any creature turns to look at it before it finishes moving, the movement ends immediately and it goes rigid, indistinguishable from a loose stack of siding."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only assembles from a specific run of cheap siding panels, never anything sturdier."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a fixed distance behind, never closing in while it's being watched."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It freezes mid-step if a car's headlights sweep across it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leans against the nearest house wall whenever glanced at, playing dead as ordinary siding."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rattles faintly even while frozen, like wind moving through panels that shouldn't move at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's assembled an extra panel's worth of height overnight, taller than it was the last time it was seen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's learned to hold its frozen pose even under direct, sustained observation, for longer than should be possible."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "An entire block's worth of loose siding assembles at once, every house missing a wall's panels by morning."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["assembling itself from loose siding panels the instant no one's looking", "pacing a sidewalk at the exact same speed as whoever's walking it"]},{"name":"Van with No Windows","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Idling windowless van, door sliding open on its own","flavor":"It idles at the curb with the engine running and the side door already sliding open, going nowhere until someone gets close enough to look inside.","desc":"It idles at the curb with the engine running and nobody visible behind the wheel, exhaust curling in the porch light. The side door slides open on its own, slow and smooth, and the dark inside doesn't reflect any light back out at all.","traits":{"note": "The dark inside the open door doesn't reflect any light — nothing that goes in there is visible from outside.", "actions": [{"name": "Sliding-Door Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage as the door slams shut on the target's arm or leg."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The van makes two Sliding-Door Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Swallow the Curb", "text": "The van lurches 15 ft. toward a creature within 10 ft. of it without provoking Opportunity Attacks. If it ends this movement adjacent to that creature, the creature must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity save or be pulled into the open doorway and Restrained until the van moves away or the creature escapes (DC 12)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The engine runs but the gas gauge has read empty since it arrived."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plates belong to a car reported stolen three towns over, years ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The radio inside plays the same three songs, always starting mid-verse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only idles on streets with working streetlights, never in true dark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The door slides shut the instant anyone looks directly at it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It follows the smell of fresh laundry from an open dryer vent."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The inside is bigger than the van's frame allows, and cold like a walk-in freezer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every van parked on the street that night is the same van, waiting its turn."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling at the curb with the door already sliding open, engine running for no one", "creeping along at walking pace two houses behind whoever's walking home alone"]},{"name":"Ding-Dong-Ditch Devil","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Small","frame":"dretch","model":"dretch","summary":"Gleeful imp that rings and runs, leaves a scorched handprint","flavor":"A small, gleeful horror that rings the bell and vanishes, leaving a scorched handprint on the door and a worse mark on whoever answers too slowly.","desc":"The doorbell rings and by the time you reach it, whatever pressed it is gone — except for the scorched, small handprint left smoking on the frame. Somewhere down the block, gleeful laughter that's a half-octave too high echoes off somebody's garage door.","traits":{"note": "It never lingers after the bell rings — anyone who answers too fast has to fight it at the doorstep, not chase it.", "actions": [{"name": "Scorching Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Fire damage, leaving a smoking handprint on whatever it struck."}, {"name": "Fetid Cloud (1/Day)", "replaces": "Fetid Cloud (1/Day)", "text": "The devil exhales a cloud of stinking gas in a 10-foot radius centered on itself. Each creature in that area must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be Poisoned for 1 minute, coughing too hard to speak clearly."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only hits houses with porch lights already burnt out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rings twice, waits, and only strikes on the third answer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its laugh arrives half a second before it actually appears."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves the handprint on the doorknob, never the door itself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't cross a welcome mat that's actually being used."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started ringing dead bolts and mailbox flags too, testing what counts."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every door it's hit this month forms one long unbroken loop if you draw it on a map."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It rings every doorbell on the block at once, and every door answers."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing a doorbell and vanishing before the porch light comes on", "counting scorched handprints on a row of front doors like a scorecard"]},{"name":"Toybox Escapee","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"Self-winding toy that patrols under the bed relentlessly","flavor":"A wind-up toy that wound itself up once too often and never wound back down; it patrols under the bed with clockwork patience.","desc":"A wind-up toy, soldier or robot, ticks its way slowly across the bedroom floor on its own power long after its key should've run out. It patrols the space under the bed with mechanical patience, and its eyes, glass and painted, seem to track whoever's watching.","traits":{"note": "Its key never runs down — treat its patrol as tireless, not winding toward a stop.", "actions": [{"name": "Wind-Up Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from a tiny bayonet or sword arm swung with unnerving mechanical precision."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It ticks louder the closer someone gets to actually falling asleep."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its paint is chipped in the exact shape of small teeth marks, old ones."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It freezes mid-step whenever a flashlight beam crosses it directly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only patrols one specific bedroom, never following a child who moves house."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its key is missing, and yet it winds tighter every night regardless."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's recruited two smaller toys from the closet into its patrol route."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Under the bed goes deeper than the floor joists allow, a hallway of dust and toy soldiers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every wind-up toy in the house clicks onto the same patrol schedule at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ticking its way across the bedroom floor long after its key should've run dry", "standing sentry under the bed frame, glass eyes tracking the doorway"]},{"name":"Curbside Furniture Fiend","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"Free curbside couch that eats whoever tries to take it","flavor":"That free couch someone left at the curb with a 'FREE' sign taped on has been eating whoever tries to carry it home.","desc":"A couch sits at the curb with a hand-lettered FREE sign taped to one cushion, upholstery a little too clean for something somebody's really discarding. Reach to test the fabric and the whole thing exhales, cushions folding inward around the offending hand like a mouth closing.","traits":{"note": "It can't move fast or far — it wins by looking irresistibly free, not by chasing.", "actions": [{"name": "Cushion Grasp", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller it is Grappled (escape DC 12)."}, {"name": "Upholstery Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., only against a creature Grappled by the couch. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage as cushions fold inward around the limb."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reappears at a new curb within a week of anyone hauling it to the dump."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The sign changes handwriting depending on who's meant to read it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells faintly of a specific stranger's cologne, never the same one twice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only closes on someone who sits down, never one who just touches it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its FREE sign is taped on with real, ordinary masking tape, oddly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun dragging itself half a block a night toward busier streets."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Open it up and the stuffing is full of small personal items nobody's reported missing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every piece of curbside furniture on the block that week is the same hungry set."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting at the curb under a hand-lettered FREE sign, cushions a little too clean", "folding shut around whoever tested the fabric a beat too slow to pull back"]},{"name":"Overgrown Hedge Maze Beast","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"vine-blight","summary":"Untrimmed hedge maze conceals something living in the gaps","flavor":"The decorative hedge maze behind the model home was never finished being trimmed, and something learned to live in the unfinished parts.","desc":"The hedges haven't been trimmed in a summer, grown thick enough to swallow the paths between them into true blind turns. Something rustles the leaves a beat behind wherever you last stood, patient, letting the maze do the cornering for it.","traits":{"note": "It never enters open ground — it wins the fight only inside the maze's blind turns.", "actions": [{"name": "Choking Hedge-Vine", "replaces": "Constricting Vine", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) by thorned branches."}, {"name": "Entangling Hedgerow (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Entangling Plants (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Thick brush erupts to fill a 20-foot square within 60 ft. that the beast can see. The area becomes Difficult Terrain, and each creature there when it appears must succeed on a DC 12 Strength save or be Restrained until it escapes (DC 12) or the brush withers after 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only grows aggressive after the model home's sprinklers run at dusk."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its favorite blind corner always smells faintly of cut grass and something rotting under it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves the paths open during the day, when the sales office is showing the house."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rustle always comes from behind, never ahead, no matter how someone turns."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from hedge trimmers even when no one's actually swinging one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown a second maze at night that doesn't match the daytime layout."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Cut it and the hedge bleeds sap the color and thickness of real blood."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole maze is one root system, and it's decided tonight nobody leaves the way they came."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rustling the hedge a beat behind wherever the last footstep landed", "letting the untrimmed maze corner someone while it stays perfectly still"]},{"name":"Sun-Bleached Lawn Jockey","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Faded lawn statue that turns to track trespassers","flavor":"A faded plaster lawn ornament that turns its painted eyes to track anyone who cuts across the grass instead of using the walk.","desc":"Paint peeling, color faded to a ghost of what it was, the statue stands at the end of a driveway with one arm permanently extended. Its head turns, degree by degree, to track anyone who steps off the sidewalk — and by the time you notice, it's already facing you dead-on.","traits":{"note": "It only attacks someone who's stepped off the sidewalk onto its lawn — it never chases past the property line.", "actions": [{"name": "Plaster Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage from a chipped plaster hand swung stiff and sudden."}, {"name": "Terrifying Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that the jockey can see must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom save or be Frightened of it until the end of its next turn, certain the painted eyes just moved."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its extended arm has held a lantern so long the paint's worn through to bare plaster."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only turns to track jaywalkers, ignoring anyone who stays on the sidewalk."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its base has shifted an inch closer to the street every year, unnoticed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stops tracking the instant someone looks directly at its face."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kids have chipped its nose off, and it's grown a new one, slightly different."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun turning its whole body, not just its head, to track people."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "At the stroke of midnight its extended arm points somewhere new every night, and something's always there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every lawn jockey on the street turns to face the same trespasser at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["turning its painted head degree by degree to track whoever cut across the grass", "standing sentry at the end of a driveway, arm permanently extended toward the street"]},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Deep One Spawn","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"Young pool-thing spawn awkwardly hunting on dry lawn","flavor":"A smaller relation of the thing in the pool, gone hunting on land for the first time, still learning to walk on the lawn.","desc":"Small and wet and clumsy on dry grass, it flops and drags itself away from the above-ground pool in short, awkward bursts, gill-slits working uselessly in open air. It's young, and slow on land, but it's not alone out here — something bigger put it in that pool.","traits":{"note": "It's young and slow on land — it never strays more than a yard's length from the pool it crawled out of.", "actions": [{"name": "Awkward Spear Jab", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sticky Net (1/Day)", "replaces": "Sticky Net (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 15/30 ft., one creature. Hit: The target is Restrained by a wet, clinging net until it or another creature within reach spends an action to tear it free (DC 10 Strength)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only at night, when the pool's filter pump is the loudest thing running."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its skin dries and cracks within minutes away from the water, slowing it further."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's drawn more to the pool's chemical smell than to any warmth or motion."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flops back toward the pool the instant it's more hurt than hungry."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's small enough to be mistaken for a large frog until it turns to look at you."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started dragging pool toys back under the water with it, hoarding them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The above-ground pool is deeper on the inside than its frame could ever hold."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something bigger surfaces in the pool behind it, finally noticing the spawn is being handled."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["flopping and dragging itself away from the above-ground pool in short, wet bursts", "working its gill-slits uselessly in the open air, hunting clumsy and slow on the lawn"]},{"name":"Meter Reader Mimic","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Fake utility worker that always asks to go around back","flavor":"Wears the utility company's polo and clipboard perfectly, and always asks to be let around back where nobody can see from the street.","desc":"Clipboard, reflective vest, badge that doesn't quite match any utility company logo you recognize — and always the same question, asked pleasantly: mind if I go around back to check the meter? Its smile doesn't move quite right when it repeats itself.","traits":{"note": "It never forces its way in — it always waits to be let around back, and reads minds to know exactly what to say next.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The mimic makes two Clipboard Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Clipboard Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage from a hard swing of the clipboard and reflective-vested arm behind it."}, {"name": "Read the Homeowner's Thoughts", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The mimic reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 ft. for as long as it concentrates, learning enough to answer questions about that person's household correctly and convincingly."}, {"name": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Its smile stops moving right. Each creature within 30 ft. that sees it must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom save or be Frightened of it for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its badge never quite matches any utility company logo you actually recognize."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only visits houses where the actual meter reading is overdue anyway."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It asks the same pleasant question twice if refused the first time, patient."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its clipboard is blank underneath the top sheet, every single page."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the exact name of the actual utility worker whose route this is."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started leaving real, correctly-calculated bills behind as cover."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whoever it copies most recently starts showing up in neighbors' dreams asking to come inside."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every utility worker scheduled on the street today is it, wearing a slightly different face."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["knocking with a clipboard and asking, pleasantly, to be let around back", "reading the meter it invented, badge catching the porch light wrong"]},{"name":"Skateboard Ramp Wight","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Undead skater endlessly practicing the trick that killed it","flavor":"Died trying to land the big trick off the plywood ramp behind the school and still practices, endlessly, on anyone who gets close.","desc":"Wheels clatter up a plywood ramp in the dark, over and over, the same trick attempted at the same angle, the same fall at the very top of the arc. It never lands it. It never stops trying. The wounds from the fall that killed it never close.","traits":{"note": "It always attempts its trick first before engaging — anyone watching gets one free look at the fall that killed it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The wight makes two Broken Deck attacks, or one Broken Deck attack and uses Stolen Momentum."}, {"name": "Broken Deck", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or its hit point maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken."}, {"name": "Stolen Momentum", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage from a rusted trick blade."}, {"name": "Splintered Board Throw", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage from a hurled, cracked deck."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only practices between dusk and the hour the school lights finally cut off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its board is the exact board it died on, wheels still spinning between attempts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stops mid-run if anyone actually lands the trick correctly nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The fall wound reopens fresh every single time it hits the top of the arc."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's oddly gentle with anyone too young to skate the ramp themselves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started chasing down kids who skate the ramp badly, as if correcting them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Land the trick perfectly in front of it and it goes still, watching, almost grateful."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every kid who ever died trying that same trick is practicing the ramp with it tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["clattering up the plywood ramp in the dark, the same trick attempted at the same angle", "falling from the same height it died from, wounds never closing, never stopping to rest"]},{"name":"Backyard Bug-Zapper Wisp","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"Escaped bug-zapper spark that hunts warm bodies at night","flavor":"A crackle of blue light that escaped the porch zapper and now hunts anything warm-blooded that wanders the yard after dark.","desc":"A spark breaks loose from the bug-zapper's blue coil and hangs in the air, crackling faint and hungry, drawn now to warmth instead of light. It drifts low across the yard at body height, hunting for something bigger than a moth to close its circuit through.","traits":{"note": "It's drawn to warmth over light now — cutting the porch lights won't save anyone standing still.", "actions": [{"name": "Static Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Lightning damage."}, {"name": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must make a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 10 (3d6) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only breaks loose on the muggiest nights, when the zapper's coil never stops crackling."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles porch lights twice before ever drifting down toward the grass."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's drawn strongest to whoever's sweating hardest in the yard that night."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flickers dim and sluggish anytime the sprinklers are running nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a faint ozone smell on anyone it's brushed against and missed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's learned to short out motion-sensor floodlights on purpose before it hunts."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's grown bright enough now to cast its own shadow, and the shadow moves first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every bug zapper on the block blows at once, and every spark is hunting."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["hanging low across the yard at body height, crackling faint and hungry for warmth", "drifting toward the porch light, hunting something bigger than a moth to complete its circuit"]},{"name":"Video Store Return-Slot Horror","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"gibbering-mouther","model":"gibbering-mouther","summary":"Rental drop-slot horror that changes whatever it swallows","flavor":"Something lives in the drop slot of the video rental place, and every tape fed back through comes out changed, and so does the hand that fed it.","desc":"The drop-slot in the shuttered video store's door never fully closed, and something reaches back out of it now — thin, groping, faintly smelling of magnetic tape and mildew. Whatever it drags back down through the slot comes back changed, warped like a tape left too near a magnet.","traits":{"note": "Anything it swallows and gives back is subtly wrong afterward — treat returned items or limbs as changed, not merely damaged.", "actions": [{"name": "Groping Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Strength save or be pulled 5 feet toward the return slot."}, {"name": "Blinding Spittle (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Blinding Spittle (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 15 ft. must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Blinded for 1 minute by a spray of magnetic-tape ribbon, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only reaches out after the store's hours would've ended, by the old faded sign."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells strongest of magnetic tape right before it strikes, never after."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recoils from anything held up that isn't a videotape shape."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its reach is exactly the width of the old drop-slot, never an inch further."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet and still if the slot is physically boarded over first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started reaching for whatever's shiny, mistaking keys and coins for tape cases."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something it warped years ago is still walking around town, subtly wrong, and it remembers taking it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole shuttered store is its body now, and the drop-slot is only its mouth."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["reaching back out of the shuttered store's drop-slot, groping and thin and smelling of tape", "dragging something fed to it back down through the slot, warped when it returns"]},{"name":"Arcade Cabinet Haunt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Ghost of an unbeaten high-scorer, lit inside the cabinet","flavor":"A high score that was never beaten, and the kid who set it, both still lit up behind the screen glass long after closing.","desc":"The cabinet in the corner still lights up though the power strip's unplugged, attract-mode looping a high score nobody's ever beaten. A face is visible in the screen glow if you stand close enough — the unbeaten champion, still playing, still furious that no one else gets to try.","traits":{"note": "It only fully manifests near its own cabinet — drag someone away from the screen glow and its reach ends.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The haunt makes two High-Score Grab attacks."}, {"name": "High-Score Grab", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or have its Strength score reduced by 1d4 until it finishes a Long Rest."}, {"name": "Sever the Sequel (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Sever Shadow (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that the haunt can see must succeed on a DC 12 Charisma save or its shadow flickers loose, becoming a hostile shadow-copy under the haunt's control for 1 minute unless the original is destroyed or the effect ends early."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only powers on for kids close to the age it died at, never adults."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its high-score initials are the same three letters, over and over, never varying."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flickers weaker on nights the arcade would've been closed anyway."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still the instant someone actually beats its score fair and square."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its screen glow is the only light source in the whole shuttered arcade."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started possessing other cabinets nearby, hopping screen to screen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Reach into the screen glow and the arcade floor underneath is decades younger, carpet and all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every cabinet in the arcade lights up at once, all playing his unbeaten run."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["looping attract-mode on an unplugged cabinet, a high score nobody's ever beaten", "glaring out through the screen glow, furious that no one else gets to try"]},{"name":"Mall Food Court Ooze","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"Slow food-court ooze that absorbs stragglers after closing","flavor":"A slow, syrupy mass that oozes between the food court tables at closing time, absorbing spilled soda, dropped fries, and the occasional straggler.","desc":"It moves at the speed of closing time, translucent and slow across cold tile, absorbing dropped fries and abandoned trays as it goes. Anyone who lingers past the last announcement finds the ooze has quietly closed the distance, patient as a mall cop nobody hired.","traits":{"note": "It's slow — it only threatens creatures that stay put or get cornered against a closed storefront gate.", "actions": [{"name": "Syrupy Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Acid damage."}, {"name": "Engulf", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "The ooze moves up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks and can enter a Large or smaller creature's space. If it does, that creature must succeed on a DC 12 Dexterity save or take 8 (2d6 + 1) Acid damage and be Engulfed, becoming Restrained, unable to breathe, and taking the same damage automatically at the start of each of its turns until freed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only moves once the last announcement over the intercom has actually played."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's absorbed enough loose change to jingle faintly wherever it flows."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids the tile freshly mopped, sticking to grimier stretches of food court floor."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's slower on cold nights, syrup thickening near the propped-open exit doors."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's translucent enough that half-dissolved trash is still visible, tumbling, inside it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started oozing up into the vents to reach stores after the gates come down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something valuable a straggler was carrying is still faintly visible, unharmed, deep inside it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every spill in the food court that night rises up out of the floor to join it at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["oozing slow between the food court tables at closing time, absorbing spilled soda and dropped fries", "closing the distance on a straggler patient as a mall cop nobody hired"]},{"name":"Backyard Trampoline Terror","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"bulette-pup","model":"bulette-pup","summary":"Burrowing thing under a trampoline that overbounces kids on purpose","flavor":"It burrowed up under the trampoline springs and now bounces kids skyward on purpose, waiting to see who doesn't land right.","desc":"The trampoline mat sags oddly in the middle even with no one on it, springs creaking under weight from below. Jump on it and the bounce comes back wrong — too high, too eager — like something underneath is helping, and hoping you don't come back down where you left.","traits":{"note": "It only strikes from beneath the trampoline mat — pull anyone off the springs and it loses its angle.", "actions": [{"name": "Spring-Loaded Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., only against a creature on or within 5 feet of the trampoline. Hit: 10 (2d8 + 1) Piercing damage, and the target is knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only overbounces kids light enough to be thrown clear over the safety net."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mat sags oddly in the same spot even after the trampoline's been moved."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still the moment an adult steps on, waiting only for kids alone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its burrow smells of wet earth even in the driest part of summer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bounces harder the more people jump on the mat at once, testing crowds."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started digging a second tunnel toward the neighbor's trampoline too."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whoever it's swallowed is still bouncing, faintly, somewhere down in the tunnel."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every trampoline on the street starts bouncing on its own at once, springs creaking underneath."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["bouncing a kid skyward with a bounce that comes back wrong, too high, too eager", "creaking under the mat's sagging middle, waiting to see who doesn't land right"]},{"name":"Home Alarm Banshee","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Alarm-triggering wraith whose wail is worse than the siren","flavor":"Trips every motion sensor in the house at once, its wail indistinguishable from — and worse than — the alarm it triggers.","desc":"The security system trips for no reason anyone can find, and under the electronic chirp there's a second sound — a wail, rising, that gets inside your skull worse than the siren ever could. It only quiets once every door and window reads locked.","traits":{"note": "It only quiets once every door and window in the house reads locked — that's the actual way to end an encounter with it, not just damage.", "actions": [{"name": "Siren Wail", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or have its hit point maximum reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only trips sensors on houses that upgraded their alarm system this year."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wail rises in pitch to match whatever song was playing on the radio last."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet the instant the actual alarm company calls to check in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's drawn to houses where every door's been locked out of real fear, not habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its presence reads on the control panel as a zone that doesn't officially exist."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started tripping the neighbors' systems too, spreading room to room."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The alarm company has a service record for this house going back further than the house has existed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every security system on the block triggers at once, all wailing the same rising note."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["tripping every motion sensor in the house at once for no reason anyone can find", "wailing under the electronic chirp, a sound that gets inside the skull worse than any siren"]},{"name":"The Family Wearing the Skin (Understudy)","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"jackalwere","model":"jackalwere","summary":"Lesser copycat family-thing, close but not quite convincing","flavor":"A lesser cousin of the perfect-family horror down the street — close enough to pass at a barbecue, not close enough to pass close up.","desc":"A second, lesser copy of a family down the street, close enough to pass a glance but never quite right up close — the smiles land a half-second late, the child never quite the same height twice. It's studying the real thing, learning to be more convincing.","traits":{"note": "It's still learning to pass — a close look reveals the seams the original family never shows.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The understudy makes two attacks, using Copycat Rend or Copycat Slam in any combination."}, {"name": "Copycat Rend (Jackal or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Rend (Jackal or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Copycat Slam (Human or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Slam (Human or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Rehearsed Smile (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Sleep Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the understudy's face must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom save or fall Unconscious for 1 minute, mistaking the smile for something safe and familiar. The effect ends early if the target takes damage or someone shakes it awake."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's stolen the real family's mail to study handwriting, and someone's noticed it's missing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighbor's invited it to a party meant for the real family, and both might show."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's copying a party member's own gestures now, close enough to unsettle them personally."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a photograph of the real family it needs a party member to help it interpret correctly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants to know why its smile lands a half-second late, and thinks the party can fix it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's recruiting a real missing person's memories to fill out its performance, and that person is still alive somewhere."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's begun to believe it's the real family and the original down the street is the copy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's the dress rehearsal — it means to swap places with the real family by morning, and it's almost convincing enough."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["practicing a smile in a bay window a half-second late, studying the real family down the street", "hosting a barbecue where the 'child' is never quite the same height twice"]},{"name":"Handyman Who Never Leaves","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Contractor who never finishes the job or leaves the house","flavor":"Hired for one gutter job three summers ago, his truck's still in the driveway and he's always got one more thing that needs fixing inside.","desc":"His truck's been parked in the driveway for three weeks and the job was supposed to take two days. He's always got one more thing to fix, one more reason to stay past dark, tools laid out with more care than the actual repair ever gets.","traits":{"note": "He never finishes a job on purpose — every repair he starts creates a reason he has to come back.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The handyman makes two attacks, using Framing Hammer or Ratchet Bolt-Gun in any combination."}, {"name": "Framing Hammer", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Ratchet Bolt-Gun", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage from a nail-gun bolt."}, {"name": "One More Thing", "text": "The handyman points to a fixture, wall, or door within 30 ft. and it warps to trap or hinder whoever's nearest — a doorframe swells shut, a stair collapses, a pipe bursts underfoot. One creature within 5 feet of that fixture must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity save or be Restrained until it escapes (DC 13) or someone else frees it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed three summers of back pay he'll accept only in the form of never leaving."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The homeowner who hired him is missing, and the house lists him as next of kin now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's found a structural problem in the house that's actually real, and dangerous, and he's the only one who knows where."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a party member to co-sign paperwork making the job, and his stay, official."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His truck won't start for anyone else, and someone in the house needs it to leave tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun fixing things in neighboring houses too, uninvited, and none of them can get him to stop."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gutter job he was hired for was never actually broken, and he knows it, and keeps working anyway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight he declares the house finished to his satisfaction, which means, by his own rule, he can finally never leave it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["laying tools out with more care than the actual repair ever gets, truck still parked in the driveway", "finding one more thing that needs fixing inside, always after dark, always alone with the homeowner"]},{"name":"The Substitute Teacher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"succubus","model":"succubus","summary":"Roving fiend-teacher whose classes always lose a student","flavor":"Fills in for a week at a time across a dozen schools, and every class she covers loses one kid to absence that never gets explained.","desc":"She takes attendance with unusual attention, lingering on certain names, and by the end of the semester the classroom always runs one desk short. Parent-teacher conferences with her run long, and afterward, nobody quite remembers what was said — only that they agreed to something.","traits":{"note": "By the end of any week she covers, exactly one student is missing from class, absence unexplained — that's the toll, not a threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The substitute makes two Fiendish Touch attacks, or one Fiendish Touch attack and uses Draining Kiss."}, {"name": "Fiendish Touch", "replaces": "Fiendish Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Homework Assignment", "replaces": "Charm", "text": "One creature the substitute can see within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Charmed for 1 hour. While Charmed, the target is convinced it owes her one outstanding assignment and will go out of its way to complete a small task for her. It repeats the save whenever it takes damage."}, {"name": "Draining Kiss", "replaces": "Draining Kiss", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., only against a creature that is Charmed, Restrained, or Incapacitated. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the substitute regains hit points equal to the damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's covering a class that includes a party member's younger sibling this week."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A student she took an unusual interest in vanished, and the school's already covering it up."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants a parent-teacher conference with a party member specifically, tonight, no rescheduling."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding a stack of student files she shouldn't have access to, and one file matters to the party."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's due to rotate to a new school by Friday, and the current one wants her gone faster."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started teaching an extra class that isn't on any official schedule, in a room that shouldn't exist."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every school she's ever subbed for shows up on old records as having lost exactly one student that semester, and she keeps a tally."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight is the last day of her rotation, and she means to collect on every assignment she's ever handed out at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["taking attendance with unusual attention, lingering on certain names longer than the rest", "running a parent-teacher conference long, until nobody quite remembers what they agreed to"]},{"name":"Split-Shift Shapeshifter","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Gas station night clerk with a shift no human works","flavor":"Works the graveyard shift at the all-night gas station and something else's shift after that; the clerk's smile never quite sits right.","desc":"He's behind the gas station counter at an hour no manager schedules for, ringing up cigarettes with hands that seem to have one joint too many. His shift changes only when the light does — never on any clock a human punches.","traits":{"note": "His shift schedule tracks light, not time — he's most dangerous exactly at the hour no manager would ever schedule for.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The clerk makes two Register Scratch attacks, or one Register Scratch attack and one Nightshift Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only) attack."}, {"name": "Nightshift Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be cursed with the shapeshifter's affliction."}, {"name": "Register Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's asked a party member to cover for him during a shift he can't afford to miss."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The gas station's security tape from his shift never comes out clear, and the owner's asking questions."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering information about a break-in he witnessed, in exchange for silence about his hands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A regular customer is close to figuring him out and he wants the party to steer them off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a ride home before sunrise and won't say why the timing matters so much."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's been skimming cash to pay someone off who knows exactly what he is."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His other shift, the one no clock accounts for, is at a gas station that isn't on any map."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight both his shifts overlap for the first time, and he can't stop what happens when they do."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing up cigarettes behind the gas station counter with hands that have one joint too many", "clocking in for a shift that changes only when the light does, never on any human clock"]},{"name":"Riding-Mower Revenant, Deluxe Model","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Upgraded haunted mower that enforces HOA lawn regulations","flavor":"A newer, meaner riding mower haunts the HOA's model-home block, chasing anyone whose lawn falls out of regulation.","desc":"Upgraded, chrome-bright, it cuts stripes into every lawn on the street whether asked or not, engine note sharper than the old model's. A laminated card tucked under the seat lists HOA lawn-height violations — and it enforces every one personally.","traits":{"note": "It carries a laminated HOA violation card under the seat and enforces every listed infraction personally, without appeal.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The mower makes two Blade Deck Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Blade Deck Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Violation Citation", "text": "The mower revs and points its headlamp at one creature within 30 ft. that it considers out of regulation. That creature must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity save or be knocked Prone and have grass clippings blast into its eyes, Blinding it until the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only chases lawns cut visibly shorter or longer than the HOA-approved height."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its engine note sharpens audibly the moment it spots an infraction."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stops dead at property lines it hasn't been issued a citation card for."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chrome stays spotless no matter how much grass and worse it cuts through."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It idles quietly outside houses that are, for now, in perfect compliance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started citing violations that aren't in the actual HOA handbook."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its laminated card updates itself overnight with new violations no committee ever voted on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every mower on the block, haunted or not, starts its engine and rolls out on citation duty at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cutting sharp new stripes into every lawn on the block whether asked or not", "chasing down whoever's lawn falls out of HOA regulation, laminated violation card tucked under the seat"]},{"name":"The Man in the Ice Cream Truck","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"Ice-cream-truck fiend whose jingle lures kids away","flavor":"His jingle plays even when the truck's parked and empty; kids who chase the sound too far never quite come back the same.","desc":"The jingle drifts down the street at an hour past when any truck should still be running, tinny and a half-step flat. Kids drift toward it before their parents notice they've gone, drawn by a melody that gets a little more insistent the longer you try to ignore it.","traits":{"note": "The jingle keeps playing even while he fights, and it gets louder the closer a Charmed target drifts toward the truck.", "actions": [{"name": "Sundae Best", "replaces": "Restless Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Charmed until the end of its next turn, hearing the jingle over every other sound."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Man makes two Sundae Best attacks."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Man casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 13)."}, {"name": "One More Scoop", "text": "The Man points at a creature within 30 ft. that is Charmed by him. That creature must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or immediately use its reaction to move up to half its speed toward the truck, drawn like the jingle is reeling it in."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He only ever has the flavors nobody asked for, and hands them out anyway."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The truck's odometer reads the same number every single evening."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows every kid's name on the route before they've told him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His change is always exact, down to coins that don't quite match any currency in circulation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He parks one street further each week, and the kids keep following anyway."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight the truck has no driver's seat, just the jingle box and a steering wheel that turns on its own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His freezer opens onto a walk-in that's bigger inside than the truck could hold, humming with older jingles."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The jingle starts playing from every radio on the block at once, and he steps out smiling like he's been invited."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling at the curb with the jingle looping though the window is dark and the freezer's long dead", "counting out change for a customer who isn't there yet, patient as anything"]},{"name":"Backyard Bonfire Cultist Circle","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Neighbor cult burning offerings in a backyard barrel","flavor":"A ring of neighbors around a burn barrel every full moon, feeding it things that were never supposed to burn that clean.","desc":"Neighbors in flannel and lawn chairs stand around a burn barrel in someone's backyard, tossing in things that don't smell like yard waste. The chanting is low, almost like small talk, until you catch the same three words repeating under everyone's breath.","traits":{"note": "Break the circle's chant and the flame gutters low, but the barrel itself keeps trying to relight until every cultist is down.", "actions": [{"name": "Charcoal Skewer", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "One cultist casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 14)."}, {"name": "Barrel's Blessing (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The barrel flares and one cultist within 10 ft. of it gains advantage on its next attack roll and resistance to Fire damage until the start of its next turn, the flame briefly wearing them like a second skin."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've fed the fire a scrap of something that belonged to a party member and want the rest of it back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One neighbor at the barrel wants out and is signaling for help without saying a word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're missing their usual ninth chair and need a warm body to complete the ring before midnight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The barrel's about to be reported to the HOA, and they need it moved before dawn."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They mistake the party for the replacement family who bought the burned-out house down the block."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's offering is a photograph of someone still living, and they need it witnessed to take."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The barrel's flame keeps whispering the next street's address, and they're arguing over whether to obey it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The circle's chant has synced with three other yards on the block, all burning in time, building to one shared demand."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["feeding the burn barrel something that pops and hisses wrong for yard waste", "passing a folding chair and a paper plate to a stranger like it's the most natural thing in the world"]},{"name":"The Coach Who Never Ages","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Ageless little-league coach spanning two decades unchanged","flavor":"Has led the same little-league team for twenty-two straight seasons and looks exactly as he did in the first team photo.","desc":"He's run the same little league for two decades and looks exactly like the team photo from the first year — same haircut, same whistle, same easy grin. Parents remark on it fondly. None of them ask the obvious question out loud.","traits":{"note": "He never drops the coach act, even mid-fight — every attack lands with an encouraging shout, like it's part of practice.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Coach makes two Whistle Claw attacks or uses Great Play once."}, {"name": "Whistle Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage, the scratch smelling faintly of turf and lighter fluid."}, {"name": "Great Play", "replaces": "Fire Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 90 ft. Hit: 13 (3d8) Fire damage. The Coach shouts encouragement as it lands, as if the target had earned the hit."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Coach casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 14)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He still calls every player by a nickname from a roster twenty years gone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His whistle is the exact same brand, worn shiny, that's been discontinued since before most parents were born."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a scrapbook of every season, and none of the photos have him aging a day."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He remembers every kid's batting average from decades back, perfectly, instantly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's never once missed a practice, not for weather, illness, or funeral."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight he's running drills for a team roster that includes three names no longer living."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow on the outfield grass moves through drills from seasons that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He announces this year's team photo will finally include everyone who's ever played for him, all at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["running infield drills in the same fading light, whistle sharp, grin unbothered by the hour", "signing a team photo with a date twenty-two years out of place"]},{"name":"Skin-Deep Scoutmaster","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Doppelganger scoutmaster who returns from trips one kid short","flavor":"Leads camping trips into the woods behind the development and always brings back one fewer kid than he took, plus one new smile.","desc":"He leads the troop on the same camping trip every year, cheerful and competent, and every year the group that comes back is one member short. He always has an explanation ready — early pickup, a sick parent — delivered with a warmth that never quite reaches his eyes.","traits":{"note": "He wears whichever scout he took last as his current face — hurt that face and the real kid's parents feel it too.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Scoutmaster makes two Firm Handshake attacks."}, {"name": "Firm Handshake", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. The grip feels sincere right up until it doesn't."}, {"name": "Reads the Room", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Scoutmaster reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 ft., learning what excuse it's most likely to believe next."}, {"name": "Early Pickup (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One creature the Scoutmaster can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 14 Wisdom save. On a failure the target is Charmed for 1 minute and believes it has somewhere else urgent to be; while Charmed it uses its movement to head for the nearest exit each turn if able."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "This trip's excuse is a family emergency nobody can quite name later."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hands out the same commemorative patch every single year, unwrapped from the same crinkled plastic."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows the woods trail better than the map does, and never once checks a compass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He always volunteers to do the final headcount himself, alone, at the vans."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His smile holds a half-second too long whenever someone asks where a missing scout went."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's troop is one scout too many, and he's trying to work out politely which one wasn't invited."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's wearing last year's missing scout's face, and it flickers when the campfire light hits it wrong."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He announces this year everyone gets to come back, and the woods behind him start giving up its old troops at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["counting heads at the trailhead one number short and writing it down as if it's correct", "practicing a warm, rehearsed excuse in the truck mirror before the parents arrive"]},{"name":"The Perfect Father Next Door","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"incubus","summary":"Model neighborhood father with a shed nobody mentions","flavor":"Never misses a game, always has the grill going, and keeps a locked shed out back that the whole street has learned not to mention.","desc":"He grills every weekend, waves at every car, remembers every neighbor's name — the model of a good dad, right down to the shed at the back of the yard that he never opens and never explains, and that nobody's ever thought twice to ask about.","traits":{"note": "He never raises his voice — every attack comes wrapped in the same easy dad-joke tone, which is somehow worse.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Father makes two Backyard Handshake attacks."}, {"name": "Backyard Handshake", "replaces": "Restless Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6+1) Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or be Charmed until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Father casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 14)."}, {"name": "Nothing to See Here", "text": "The Father gestures toward the shed. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the shed makes a DC 14 Wisdom save. On a failure it becomes Charmed for 1 minute and loses all interest in approaching the shed, actively steering conversation away from it if asked."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's invited the party to a cookout specifically to keep them from noticing the shed's new padlock."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His kid has started asking neighbors what's actually inside, and he needs that curiosity handled quietly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A missing pet's collar turned up near the shed, and its owner is asking around the block."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party his prize grilling recipe in exchange for forgetting they ever noticed the shed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The HOA wants to inspect every shed on the block this month, and he needs it to not happen."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's expecting a delivery to the shed tonight and wants the driveway clear of witnesses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The shed is bigger inside than the yard should allow, and something in there answers when he knocks a certain rhythm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every father on the street has an identical shed, all locked the same way, all filling up on the same schedule."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["flipping burgers at a grill that's never once gone out, waving at every passing car by name", "checking the padlock on the shed twice, gently, like tucking something in"]},{"name":"Static-Cling Poltergeist Swarm","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-dretches","model":"swarm-of-dretches","summary":"House-wide micro-hauntings that unify into one coordinated threat","flavor":"A house full of small hauntings — flickering nightlights, cold spots, moved keys — that only reveal themselves as one coordinated thing when cornered.","desc":"Lights flicker in one room, then another, then a third, small hauntings scattered through the whole house like static before a storm. Given time they converge — flickers syncing, whispers overlapping into one voice — until the house's dozen small wrongs act as a single, focused will.","traits":{"note": "Scatter its attention early and it fights as harmless little hauntings; give it a full turn uninterrupted and it converges into one will.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Swarm makes two Cold Spot attacks, or one if it has fewer than half its hit points."}, {"name": "Cold Spot", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (4d4) Cold damage, or 5 (2d4) Cold damage if the Swarm has fewer than half its hit points remaining. The air around the target briefly frosts and the lights nearby gutter."}, {"name": "Converge", "text": "The Swarm's dozen small hauntings sync into one voice. Until the start of its next turn, the Swarm has advantage on all attack rolls, and any creature that starts its turn within 10 ft. of the Swarm must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It starts in the nightlights, blinking a pattern like something learning Morse from scratch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves the same three keys between the same three drawers, over and over, patient as a tide."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cold spots trail it room to room, each one a few degrees colder than the last."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It prefers the hallway, herding anyone who enters toward whichever room it wants them in."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every mirror in the house fogs faintly wherever it's passed through recently."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight it's already half-converged, three rooms syncing their flickers before anyone's even home."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's learned to mimic the house's old smoke detector chirp, timing it to when someone's most likely to check."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every appliance in the house switches on at once, and the static settles into a single voice that knows your name."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["flickering the porch light three times in three different rooms before anyone notices the pattern", "shuffling keys and remotes between drawers, small and scattered, building toward something coordinated"]},{"name":"Cursed Above-Ground Deep One Broodmother","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Matured pool-horror now spawning across the cul-de-sac","flavor":"The original pool-thing from three doors down, matured and spawning; the whole cul-de-sac's chlorine budget has quietly tripled.","desc":"The above-ground pool that used to hold one bloated thing now can't contain what it's become — water black and roiling, spawn slipping over the rim to spread through yards up and down the cul-de-sac. The smell of brine hangs over the whole block now, even the dry lawns.","traits":{"note": "Every round it isn't fought, another spawn slips over the rim into the yard, so speed matters more than caution.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Broodmother makes one Chlorine Bite attack and two Spawning Tentacle attacks."}, {"name": "Chlorine Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Spawning Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is Grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Poolside Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Strength Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature Grappled by the Broodmother. Failure: 16 (3d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is pulled into the pool water, gaining the Restrained condition until it escapes the grapple. Success: Half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spawn have already reached the neighbor's kiddie pool, and that family has no idea yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dog went missing near the pool three nights ago, and its owner is asking around."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The homeowner keeps topping off the pool with the hose, convinced it's just evaporation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pool company's due for its scheduled maintenance visit tomorrow morning."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A block-party invitation was left taped to the pool ladder, and nobody remembers writing it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's dragged a lounge chair halfway into the water, testing whether it can lure someone closer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water level rises exactly to match how much of it displaces, no matter how large it gets."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Three other above-ground pools on the block have started smelling of brine overnight, all at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["rolling black water against the pool liner, slow and heavy, testing how much more it can hold", "pushing spawn over the rim one at a time while the deck chairs sit unmoved beside it"]},{"name":"Renovation Golem, Load-Bearing Model","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"Drywall-and-lumber golem built from a shortcut renovation curse","flavor":"Built from mismatched drywall, salvaged studs, and whatever the last flip-house crew left behind, animated by a contractor's shortcut curse.","desc":"Built from a contractor's shortcut and a curse nobody read the fine print on, it's drywall dust and two-by-fours given purpose, tearing out load-bearing walls with total confidence. The house groans around it. It doesn't seem to notice, or care.","traits":{"note": "It targets load-bearing structures first — fighting it indoors risks the room coming down with it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Golem makes two Sledge Palm attacks."}, {"name": "Sledge Palm", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a structure or fixture, it is destroyed automatically."}, {"name": "Structural Curse", "text": "The Golem strikes a nearby wall or support. Every creature within 10 ft. of that wall must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity save or take 10 (3d6) Bludgeoning damage from falling debris and be knocked Prone; on a success, it takes half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's built with mismatched drywall from three different flip houses, none of the patterns lining up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tape measure is fused into its forearm, still clicking closed and open on its own."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same three notes of a contractor's radio jingle while it works."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always finishes demolition before it starts, then seems briefly confused there's nothing left to build."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints are shims and drywall screws, and it sheds a little sawdust with every swing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's mid-renovation, half a kitchen fused into its chest, cabinet doors still swinging."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's been quietly copying the house's original blueprint from memory, and the copy isn't quite the same house."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It starts pulling load-bearing walls from every house on the block at once, like it's finally been let off the leash."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["tearing a wall out with total confidence while the ceiling above it visibly sags", "stacking salvaged studs into a shape that's slowly becoming something with shoulders"]},{"name":"The Photo Album Hag","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Photo-collecting hag who edits herself into family albums","flavor":"Collects family photo albums door to door for 'the historical society' and edits herself into every family that lets her keep one.","desc":"She collects family photo albums from yard sales and open houses, and pages through them slowly on her porch each evening. Look closely at the older photos and you'll find her face already there, inserted seamlessly among people who swear they never met her.","traits":{"note": "Every album she's edited into keeps a faint echo of her face in it — burn one and she flinches like it hurt.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Hag makes two Dog-Eared Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Dog-Eared Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Cut and Paste", "replaces": "Plane", "text": "The Hag steps out of one photograph she has inserted herself into and reappears within 30 ft. of it, unseen until she chooses to be."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Hag casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 15)."}, {"name": "Insert Myself In", "text": "The Hag targets one creature within 30 ft. she has a photograph of. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or be Charmed for 1 hour, gradually recalling the Hag as a beloved relative who was always there."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's asking the party for any old photos of their own family, sweetly, at length."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving neighbor just gave her a whole box of albums she isn't done with yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An album she's already edited herself into is for sale at this weekend's yard sale."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She claims to have photos proving a party member's family once lived on this street."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The historical society has no record of her ever volunteering with them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's midway through inserting herself into a photo of someone the party is looking for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her porch is stacked floor to ceiling with albums going back further than the neighborhood's ever existed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's collecting the last photo she needs to be family in every album on the street, all at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["turning album pages slowly on the porch, licking a thumb before each one like she's savoring it", "asking politely at the door whether anyone's cleaning out a late relative's photos this week"]},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"All-seeing patrol captain who knows every closed-door secret","flavor":"Patrols at all hours in a golf cart with a spotlight, and somehow always knows exactly what happened behind every closed door on the block.","desc":"He wears the reflective vest and carries the clipboard, walking the same route every dusk, greeting everyone by name. But his eyes — multiple, lidless, arranged wrong under a baseball cap — miss nothing behind any closed door on the route, and he remembers all of it.","traits":{"note": "His baseball cap hides a ring of extra eyes — he sees behind him and through most curtains without turning around.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Captain makes one Clipboard Beak attack and one Reflective-Vest Tentacles attack."}, {"name": "Clipboard Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Reflective-Vest Tentacles", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of the Captain's next turn."}, {"name": "Filed and Noted", "text": "The Captain writes something down about one creature he can see within 60 ft. That creature has disadvantage on Charisma checks made against anyone on the block for the next hour, its secret already circulating."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He greets every household by first name, spouse's name, and the name of the dog they lost last spring."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His golf cart's spotlight lingers a half-second too long on any window with the blinds shut."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His clipboard has a page for every house on the route, most of them filled front to back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He never removes the cap, indoors or out, rain or shine."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows things about closed-door arguments he was never told and never explains how."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight he's compiling a special report on one specific house, and he wants a second opinion from the party."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His cap slips for a half-second and what's underneath doesn't match a human skull's geometry at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He announces over the block intercom that he's finally ready to read his findings on everyone, tonight, all at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling the golf cart at the curb, spotlight sweeping windows that already have their curtains drawn", "jotting something in the clipboard about a house nobody's mentioned to him yet"]},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Shark","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"umber-hulk","model":"umber-hulk","summary":"Oversized predator circling under a backyard pool's liner","flavor":"Something with far too many teeth for a four-foot pool has been circling under the vinyl liner since the last pool party.","desc":"Something far too large for a backyard pool circles just under the liner, a fin-shaped shadow crossing and recrossing the pale plastic bottom. The water level never seems to change no matter how much of it that shape displaces.","traits":{"note": "The water level never drops no matter how much it displaces — it's using more pool than the pool has.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Shark makes two Liner Rend attacks."}, {"name": "Liner Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage. This attack can be made against a target standing at the pool's edge."}, {"name": "Undertow", "text": "One creature within 10 ft. of the pool's edge makes a DC 15 Strength save. On a failure, it is pulled 10 ft. into the water and gains the Restrained condition until it escapes a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only circles when the pool's unattended, going still the instant anyone glances over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its fin-shadow always crosses the same worn patch on the liner, over and over."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been quiet since the last pool party, content to wait for the next one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The liner bulges faintly wherever it passes, like the plastic's thinner than it should be."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems to recognize the family that owns the pool, and leaves their feet alone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight it's testing the ladder, nosing at the rungs like it's learning how stairs work."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pool's too shallow by every measurement to hide something this size, and yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It breaches the liner entirely, and the water that spills out keeps coming long past what the pool should hold."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["circling under the liner in slow tight loops, a shadow far too broad for a four-foot pool", "bumping the liner's edge testingly whenever bare feet get close to the ladder"]},{"name":"The Ham Radio Operator","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-zerth","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"Attic ham-radio operator receiving transmissions from nowhere","flavor":"Runs a shortwave rig in the attic that picks up something answering back that was never broadcasting from anywhere on Earth's dial.","desc":"Up in the attic, headphones clamped tight, he turns the dial through static searching for something that isn't broadcasting from anywhere on Earth. He transcribes what comes through in a cramped, careful hand — numbers, mostly, and occasionally your name.","traits":{"note": "Whatever answers his rig knows things it shouldn't — treat any name he's transcribed as a name the thing behind the static now also knows.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Operator makes two Static Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Static Strike", "replaces": "Psi Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Force damage plus 4 (1d8) Psychic damage as a burst of feedback screeches through the target's skull."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Operator casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 15)."}, {"name": "Signal Lock", "text": "The Operator reads out a name he's transcribed. If that creature is within 60 ft., it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or take 9 (2d8) Psychic damage and have disadvantage on its next save against the Operator's spells."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's transcribed a party member's name tonight and is anxious to know if it means anything to them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His wife wants the antenna torn down; he's begging the party to convince her otherwise."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's picked up numbers matching an address three houses down and wants someone to check on it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering his transcription notebook in trade for anyone willing to sit with him through one more transmission."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The FCC sent a notice about his frequency, and he's convinced they're covering something up."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's transmission is repeating a warning, over and over, about tonight specifically."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The static has started answering questions he hasn't asked yet, a few seconds ahead of him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every radio and baby monitor on the street picks up his signal at once, all reciting the same list of names."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["turning the dial slow through static, headphones clamped tight, chasing a signal from nowhere on the map", "transcribing careful rows of numbers in a notebook, pausing once to write down someone's actual name"]},{"name":"The PTA Vice President","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"chasme","model":"chasme","summary":"PTA lieutenant gathering names for an unseen master list","flavor":"Second-in-command to the block's real horror, buzzing between bake sales gathering names for a list nobody's seen the end of.","desc":"She takes minutes at every meeting in a notebook she never lets anyone else read, cross-referencing names against a list only she can see. Cross the PTA President and she's the one who quietly writes your name down first.","traits":{"note": "She never lets anyone read the notebook — take it from her and every name in it blurs to nonsense until she's subdued.", "actions": [{"name": "Take Notes", "replaces": "Proboscis", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the Vice President regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt as she drains something more than blood."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member's name went into her notebook after last week's meeting, and she's watching for a reaction."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She needs someone to cross a rival on the President's behalf before the vote for treasurer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her notebook has gone missing for one anxious afternoon, and she's frantic to get it back quietly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's collecting signatures for a petition that reads suspiciously like a list she already keeps."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the party to vouch for a new family so they'll go on her list as friendly, not flagged."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight she's cross-referencing the bake sale sign-up sheet against something that isn't a school roster at all."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The notebook's list is longer than the neighborhood's population by a significant, uncomfortable margin."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She announces the list is finally complete and closes the notebook, satisfied, like a countdown just ended."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cross-referencing a notebook of names against faces at the bake sale table, pen never quite stopping", "buzzing low over the folding tables when she thinks no one's watching the meeting clock"]},{"name":"Backyard Grill Fire Elemental","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"azer-pyromancer","model":"azer-pyromancer","summary":"Never-extinguished grill fire that's still hungry to cook","flavor":"Someone's charcoal grill fire never went out after the block party; it's been cooking ever since, and it's still hungry.","desc":"The charcoal in the grill never fully cooled from last summer's cookout, and now flame licks up through the grate on its own schedule, orange and patient, still smelling faintly of lighter fluid and burnt hot dogs. It's still hungry. It's been hungry a long time.","traits":{"note": "It's been burning unfed since last summer's block party — feed it real fuel mid-fight and it burns hotter, not calmer.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Elemental makes two Grate Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Grate Burst", "replaces": "Flame Burst", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Elemental casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 14)."}, {"name": "Still Hungry", "text": "Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 14, each creature within 10 ft. of the grill. Failure: 10 (3d6) Fire damage and the target catches fire, taking 3 (1d6) Fire damage at the start of each of its turns until it or another creature uses an action to douse the flames. Success: Half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flares brightest right around dinnertime, like old habit hasn't worn off yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still smells faintly of last year's charcoal and lighter fluid, unmistakably, no matter the wind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's scorched the same patch of patio black, over and over, never spreading further."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The grill lid rattles gently whenever something edible passes nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes briefly dim whenever it rains, sulking rather than dying."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight someone left raw meat on the grate, and it's flaring in what might be excitement."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's started forming a face in the coals that resembles whoever's standing closest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every grill left out on the block catches at once, all burning toward the same hungry rhythm."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "elemental"],"activity":["licking up through the grate on its own patient schedule, still smelling of lighter fluid and old hot dogs", "flaring brighter whenever footsteps come close, like it's hoping for something to cook"]},{"name":"The Cul-de-Sac's Second Family","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"drider","model":"drider","summary":"Multi-limbed horror that assembles into a fake nuclear family","flavor":"A many-limbed thing that arranges itself into a mother, father, and two kids for the length of a driveway conversation, then unfolds once the door shuts.","desc":"Too many limbs folded into too few silhouettes, arranged behind lit windows to look, from the street, exactly like a mother, a father, two kids at the dinner table. Get close enough to the glass and the joints don't bend where a person's should.","traits":{"note": "From outside a lit window it reads as a perfectly normal family; only up close do the joints bend where no person's should.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Second Family makes two Foreleg attacks."}, {"name": "Foreleg", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Poison Burst", "text": "Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14, each creature within 10 ft. Failure: 9 (2d8) Poison damage, and the target has the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn. Success: Half damage only."}, {"name": "Dinner Table Pose", "text": "The Second Family folds itself back into a convincing family silhouette. Until it moves or attacks, a creature must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom (Insight) check to recognize it as anything but an ordinary household seen through a window."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real family that used to live in that house never actually moved out, as far as anyone can prove."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighbor's kid has started waving to the window family every night, and they've started waving back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mail keeps arriving addressed to names nobody in the county records recognizes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the party to sit for one driveway conversation, just once, to complete the tableau."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The HOA welcome packet for that house was delivered and signed for, in handwriting that doesn't quite loop right."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rearranging itself tonight to add a fifth silhouette, and it's looking at the party to fill the chair."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Get close to the glass and the dinner on the table is the same three motionless plates, night after night."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every window on the cul-de-sac lights up with an identical family at the identical hour, unfolding all together."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["arranging itself into four seated silhouettes behind lit windows for the length of a driveway conversation", "unfolding wrong-jointed limbs the second the front door finally shuts"]},{"name":"Lawn-Order Enforcer, Senior Patrol","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"shield-guardian","summary":"Promoted HOA golem whose citations double as curses","flavor":"The block's original code-enforcement golem has been promoted; it now issues citations that are also curses.","desc":"Its citations aren't paper anymore — the golem simply touches a hand to whatever's out of code, and the violation writes itself directly onto the offender, a mark that itches worse the longer it goes uncorrected.","traits":{"note": "Its citations are curses, not paper — a marked target keeps taking the itch damage until the violation is actually corrected.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two Citation Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Citation Fist", "replaces": "Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Force damage."}, {"name": "Code Violation", "text": "The Enforcer touches a hand to one creature it hits with Citation Fist this turn. That creature is marked with a Violation: at the start of each of its turns it takes 5 (1d10) Force damage until the mark is removed by a DC 15 action to correct the 'infraction' (fixing torn clothing, cleaning a wound, straightening its stance) or by a successful DC 15 Charisma (Persuasion) check made to the Enforcer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It cites overgrown grass down to the quarter-inch, and it's never once been wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a laminated code booklet that's grown three inches thicker than the original HOA bylaws."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It patrols the same six streets in the same order, never varying the route by a minute."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its citations glow faintly at dusk, easy to spot from a passing car."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's polite to a fault, even while marking someone, thanking them for their compliance in advance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight it's citing something that isn't in any code book yet, like it's inventing new violations on the spot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its clipboard citations rearrange themselves overnight, marking houses that broke no rule anyone's heard of."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It declares the whole block in violation at once and starts marking every house, occupied or not."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["measuring a lawn's grass height with a tape measure fused into its wrist, unbothered by the hour", "pressing a glowing palm to a mailbox that's two inches over the setback line"]},{"name":"The Block Party Ringmaster","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"vrock","model":"vrock","summary":"Block-party organizer who plans a yearly disappearance","flavor":"Organizes the annual street party with unnerving precision, down to exactly who disappears in the bounce-house line each year.","desc":"He organizes the summer block party every year without fail, decorations up before anyone volunteers, guest list somehow always complete before the invites go out. Each year, in the group photo afterward, exactly one face from last year's photo is missing, and nobody remembers asking why.","traits":{"note": "The group photo he takes each year is his real ledger — study last year's copy and you'll see exactly who's owed to him next.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ringmaster makes two Shred attacks."}, {"name": "Shred", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Confetti Spores (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Spores (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 20 ft. of the Ringmaster makes a DC 15 Constitution save. Failure: 10 (3d6) Poison damage and the Poisoned condition until the end of its next turn, choking on bright drifting spores disguised as party confetti. Success: Half damage only."}, {"name": "Group Photo (1/Day)", "replaces": "Stunning Screech (1/Day)", "text": "The Ringmaster calls for a photo. Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear him makes a DC 15 Constitution save. Failure: The target has the Stunned condition until the end of the Ringmaster's next turn, smiling reflexively for a picture it didn't agree to be in."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already added a party member to next year's guest list, in advance, without asking."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Last year's missing face belonged to someone whose family is still asking around about them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs a volunteer to run the bounce-house line this year, and he's already decided who."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering VIP placement at this year's party in trade for a small, specific favor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The decorations are up two full months early, and the neighbors are starting to ask why."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He wants the party photographed early, before the party even starts, 'just in case.'"}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The guest list he's finalized includes names of people who don't live on the street, and never have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He announces this year's photo will finally be a full house, gesturing at every missing face returning at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["hanging streamers with total precision before a single neighbor has volunteered to help", "checking the completed guest list against a bounce-house line that hasn't formed yet"]},{"name":"Attic Insulation Horror","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"hook-horror","model":"hook-horror","summary":"Attic-dwelling horror slowly widening the crawlspace over decades","flavor":"Something moved into the pink fiberglass batting between the joists decades ago and has been slowly widening the crawlspace ever since.","desc":"Something has been widening the crawlspace behind the attic insulation for years, pink fiberglass torn and packed into strange drifts against the rafters. It moves in the walls at night, slow and patient, a little more room carved out every season.","traits":{"note": "It's slow between walls but fast in open floor space — expect it to close distance the moment it breaks through drywall.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes two Insulation Hook attacks."}, {"name": "Insulation Hook", "replaces": "Hook", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is Grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Widen the Crawlspace", "text": "The Horror tears through a wall or floor section within 5 ft. of it, creating a 5-foot opening and releasing a cloud of fiberglass dust. Each creature within 10 ft. must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or have Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn, eyes and throat stinging."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's careful never to widen the crawlspace on a night anyone's home to hear the joists creak."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pink fiberglass drifts pile against the rafters in shapes that look almost deliberate, almost like nests."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids the attic hatch entirely, preferring to move through gaps it's already widened."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The insulation near its favorite spot is packed unnaturally dense, like something's been pressing through it for years."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still and silent the moment anyone climbs the attic ladder, waiting them out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight it's widened the crawlspace enough to reach the room below, and the ceiling's sagging visibly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The drifts it's packed form a rough map of the house from decades before this one was built."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It breaks through into every room on the top floor at once, having finally run out of house left to widen."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["packing torn fiberglass into strange drifts against the rafters, slow and unbothered by the itch", "widening the crawlspace an inch further than it was last season, patient as rot"]},{"name":"Master of the Costume Party","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"oni","model":"oni","summary":"Costume-party host whose winners are never seen again","flavor":"Hosts the block's annual costume bash wearing a mask indistinguishable from a face, and everyone who wins 'best costume' stops being seen after.","desc":"Every Halloween he hosts the best party on the block, costume contest judged personally, prizes always a little too elaborate for a neighborhood gathering. The winners are announced with real ceremony. Nobody ever quite remembers seeing them since.","traits":{"note": "His mask IS his face — remove it and there is nothing recognizable underneath, only the shape of whoever he's currently wearing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Master makes two Prize Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Prize Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Nightmare Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 90 ft. Hit: 18 (4d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Best Costume", "replaces": "Shape-Shift", "text": "The Master shifts his form to match the appearance of any Medium humanoid he has seen, taking on that shape (and its voice) until he uses this action again or drops to 0 hit points."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Master casts a spell, requiring no material components, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 16)."}, {"name": "And the Winner Is (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Master announces a winner. One creature he can see within 60 ft. makes a DC 16 Charisma save. On a failure, the target vanishes from sight and hearing of everyone but the Master for 1 minute, existing in a private backstage the Master alone can access, taking 14 (4d6) Psychic damage at the start of each of its turns there. The target reappears where it vanished if the effect ends before the duration expires."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Last year's winner's family is quietly asking around, and someone's finally listening."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's invited a party member specifically, complimenting a costume they haven't picked out yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs one more judge for tonight's contest and has already decided it's the party."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival on the block is trying to cancel this year's party, and he wants that stopped quietly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering a prize worth more than any neighborhood contest should give, and wants only a name in return."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's contest has an unusually large prize table, set for winners who haven't been announced yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His mask has started slipping mid-ceremony, showing glimpses of every previous winner underneath."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He declares every costume tonight a winner at once, and every guest starts vanishing from the party in turn."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["adjusting a mask that doesn't quite move like a mask should, judging costumes with real ceremony", "announcing this year's winner to applause that dies a little too quickly"]},{"name":"The Substitute Mailman's Supervisor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Route supervisor delivering unsolicited packages to every house","flavor":"Oversees the whole route from an unmarked postal truck, delivering something to every house that requested nothing.","desc":"He rides the route behind his substitute, double-checking every delivery with clipboard in hand, and leaves packages at doors nobody ordered anything to. The labels are handwritten, addressed correctly, and always to someone who used to live there.","traits":{"note": "Every package he delivers is a debt owed by the house, not the person — open one and its contents are addressed to whoever's inside now, whether they ordered it or not.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Supervisor makes two Registered Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Registered Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage. The Supervisor regains hit points equal to half the necrotic damage dealt."}, {"name": "Shadow Delivery", "replaces": "Shadow Strike", "text": "The Supervisor moves up to his speed through shadow without provoking Opportunity Attacks and makes one Registered Bite attack, arriving at a doorstep before anyone can react."}, {"name": "Return to Sender", "text": "The Supervisor points to one creature within 30 ft. that has opened a package from him. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or be Restrained until the end of its next turn, wrapped in unwinding brown paper and twine."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A package addressed to a party member arrived at the house they're currently staying in, unasked for."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighbor received a delivery addressed to a name that matches their deceased spouse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The substitute mailman is trying to quit and needs someone to walk the last leg of the route with him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering to intercept a delivery meant for the party in exchange for delivering it himself instead."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A package was left with instructions not to be opened until a specific date that's tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's currently making a delivery to a house that's officially been vacant for a decade."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every returned package he's ever handled is stacked somewhere in his truck, and none of them have ever actually been opened."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He announces the whole route is getting deliveries tonight, every house, all addressed to whoever lives there now."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["double-checking every delivery from an unmarked truck idling a block behind the substitute", "leaving a handwritten package at a door for someone who used to live there, addressed correctly anyway"]},{"name":"Development Overseer, Phase Two","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Slab-built golem grading a phantom lot off the map","flavor":"Built from the foundation slabs of the houses that never got finished, it's been quietly grading a lot that isn't on any map.","desc":"Cast from the same mold as its predecessor, it grades an empty lot that exists on no survey anyone's filed, leveling ground for a phase of the development that was never approved. The bulldozer treads leave marks in dirt that shouldn't be there in the morning.","traits":{"note": "It only escalates against creatures that cross its staked boundary line; standing clear of the stakes keeps it passive.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Overseer makes two Grading Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Grading Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is knocked Prone, ground flat like fresh-poured concrete."}, {"name": "Survey Stake Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 16 (3d6 + 6) Force damage, and the Overseer plants an invisible stake at the target's location. A creature that starts its turn within 5 ft. of a stake takes 7 (2d6) Force damage as the phantom lot line snaps taut."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grading in perfect silence, treads leaving no sound at all on the dirt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its slab chest still bears a stenciled unit number for a house that was never built."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses every few minutes to consult blueprints only it can see."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surveyor stakes ring the lot in a shape too large for any single house."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It works fastest at 3 a.m. and slows to nothing by dawn."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The lot it grades is slowly growing, swallowing another few feet of yard each week."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dirt it moves resettles into house-shaped mounds by morning, foundations nobody poured."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has started grading through basements of occupied homes, treating walls as ground yet to be leveled."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["grading a phantom lot by moonlight, treads pressing marks into ground no survey shows", "standing motionless at a stake-and-string boundary line until something crosses it"]},{"name":"The First HOA Board","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Undead HOA founders still voting on ordinances forever","flavor":"Five founding board members, still convening in the clubhouse basement, still voting unanimously on ordinances no living resident agreed to.","desc":"Five founding members, long dead, still convene in the clubhouse basement on the second Tuesday of every month, voting unanimously on ordinances no living resident proposed. Their gavel strikes the table with a sound like a coffin lid.","traits":{"note": "All five vote as one; a motion that fails against one member fails against all five simultaneously.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Board makes two Dread Gavel attacks."}, {"name": "Dread Gavel", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Necrotic damage. The target's movement speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn, bound by procedure it can't quite argue past."}, {"name": "Violation Notice (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage, and the target is marked in violation. Until the mark ends (DC 17 Charisma save at the end of each of its turns), the target has Disadvantage on Charisma checks made against anyone who has ever lived on the block."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Board casts one of its bylaw-spells, drawing on the same authority the living residents can't seem to overturn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've fined a party member for an ordinance violation nobody living has ever seen written down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're holding a vote tonight on demolishing a house the party needs standing until morning."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One board member wants out and has slipped the party a key to the basement meeting."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've seized a resident's property under a lien the party could contest with the original charter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They offer the party a seat on the board, permanent, starting tonight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Their basement ledger lists every resident who's ever lived here, living and otherwise, still being billed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their gavel strikes are heard as thunder three streets over, timed to whatever they're voting on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've called an emergency session to annex a neighboring block, and the ground between is already rezoning itself."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["gaveling through a unanimous vote in the clubhouse basement, minutes from decades ago open on the table", "measuring a living resident's lawn against a bylaw that predates the resident's birth"]},{"name":"The Perfect Family, Fully Grown","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"marilith","model":"marilith","summary":"Skin-family horror that stopped pretending to be separate people","flavor":"What the skin-wearing family becomes once it stops bothering to look like four separate people at all.","desc":"It doesn't bother separating into mother, father, child anymore — the pretense has worn through, and what stands on the porch now is one horror wearing three faces at once, limbs overlapping where three bodies used to be distinct.","traits":{"note": "Its overlapping limbs mean attacks meant for one 'member' land on all of it — there's no longer a difference.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Family makes four Overlapping Limb attacks."}, {"name": "Overlapping Limb", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Fold Into the Hug", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 18) inside the family's overlapping bodies. While Grappled this way, the target is Restrained and takes 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns as it's slowly absorbed into the mass."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still tries to speak with three overlapping voices in unsettling unison."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps one face turned toward the street at all times, watching for the mailman."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves like it's still furniture-shopping for a house it no longer needs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its limbs occasionally separate back into three distinct shapes before refolding."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sets the table for four every night out of pure, useless habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun growing a fourth face, budding slowly from where the mother and father overlap."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow still falls as three separate people, lagging a half-second behind its movements."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stopped needing the house at all and has started walking, still smiling, down the middle of the street."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing on the porch as one fused shape, three faces turning in unison toward the street", "answering the door with too many arms arranging themselves into a single welcoming gesture"]},{"name":"The Neighborhood Watch, Fully Awake","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"Block-wide surveillance horror that has begun to act","flavor":"Every porch light on the block is one of its eyes now, and it has stopped just watching.","desc":"Every curtain on the block is drawn back at once, every porch light on, and for the first time the watching has purpose — footsteps sound from houses that should be empty, moving in coordination toward whoever it's decided doesn't belong.","traits":{"note": "Every porch light on the block is one of its eyes; darkening the block blinds it house by house.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Watch makes two Porch-Light Lash attacks."}, {"name": "Porch-Light Lash", "replaces": "Arcane Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 16 (3d6 + 6) Psychic damage, and the target is pulled 10 feet toward the Watch, curtains and wiring hauling it in."}, {"name": "Block-Wide Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Mind Blast (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Every porch light on the block flares at once. Each creature within 60 ft. of any house makes a DC 18 Intelligence save, taking 27 (6d8) Psychic damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature that fails is also Stunned until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Watch casts one of its surveillance-spells through the block's fixtures and wiring."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's decided one party member 'doesn't belong' and is coordinating every house against them specifically."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's trapped a resident inside their own home, lights refusing to let the door open."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A block committee member knows how to shut off the transformer that feeds it, if the party can reach the box."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mistaken the party for the intruders it's been watching for since it woke, and won't be talked out of it easily."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's offering the party safety on the block in exchange for naming who its next target should be."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun watching adjacent blocks too, porch lights blinking on in patterns three streets over."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers every face that's ever walked this block, replaying them across its windows like a filmstrip."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stopped just watching the block and started rearranging which houses are where, mid-hunt."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["swinging every porch light on the block toward a single point at once, hunting", "moving curtained silhouettes through empty houses in perfect coordinated pursuit"]},{"name":"The Substitute Principal","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"erinyes","model":"erinyes","summary":"Fill-in principal whose detention slips are binding contracts","flavor":"Called in to run the school when the real principal 'took leave,' she rewrites detention slips into something closer to binding contracts.","desc":"She fills in for a week at a time, calm and reasonable right up until she hands out a detention slip — and the fine print on those slips is binding in ways no student ever reads closely enough to notice until it's too late.","traits":{"note": "Anyone who signs a detention slip from her is bound by its fine print — reading it aloud before signing breaks the binding.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Principal makes two Withering Correction attacks."}, {"name": "Withering Correction", "replaces": "Withering Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Binding Detention Slip (Requires Magic Rope)", "replaces": "Entangling Rope (Requires Magic Rope)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 30 ft. Hit: The target is Restrained by unbreakable fine print until it or another creature uses an action to make a DC 17 Intelligence check, succeeding on reading the contract's escape clause aloud."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's just handed a party member a detention slip binding them to attend an assembly at midnight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A student she's disciplined is missing, and the fine print names where they went."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's covering for a real principal who's locked in the teacher's lounge and needs rescuing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the party to co-sign a slip for a troublemaker, promising it's routine paperwork."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stack of unsigned slips in her desk could void every contract she's issued this term, if taken."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her substitute assignment has stretched to a full semester with no sign of the actual principal returning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every slip she's ever issued is still binding, decades' worth of alumni still quietly serving her detention."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's begun handing slips to parents in the pickup line, expanding her jurisdiction past the schoolyard fence."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["writing out a detention slip in careful cursive, fine print shrinking as the pen moves", "patrolling an empty hallway at a measured, unhurried pace, keys jingling at her hip"]},{"name":"Superstore Overnight Stock Horror","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"void-monk-psion","model":"void-monk-psion","summary":"Overnight stocker that spells warnings in the aisle layout","flavor":"Something restocks the strip-mall superstore's shelves after close, in patterns that spell out things in the aisle layout by morning.","desc":"The big-box store's overnight stocker rearranges the aisles into patterns that spell warnings if you stand at the right angle under the fluorescent lights. It's fast between the shelves and slow to be seen — you only catch the edge of it, restocking, always restocking.","traits":{"note": "It only fully manifests between the last customer leaving and the first employee arriving; daylight forces it back into the stockroom.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes two Restocking Warp attacks."}, {"name": "Restocking Warp", "replaces": "Psychic Warp", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Psychic damage, and the target is teleported to an unoccupied space in a random aisle within 30 feet, shelved like inventory."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Horror casts one of its shelving-spells, rearranging the aisle around it as it does."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's stocking the cereal aisle tonight, boxes turned to spell something in the barcodes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves fastest when the fluorescents flicker, slowest under steady light."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves every price tag facing precisely the same direction, an inch off from correct."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Security footage of it only ever shows an empty aisle and moved product."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It restocks twice as fast when someone's actively trying to read its pattern."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's message is a name, and it matches someone still shopping in the store."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's begun stocking items the store never carried, brands that don't exist anywhere else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stopped waiting for close and started restocking in full view, mid-afternoon, daring anyone to read the aisle."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["restocking a shelf into a pattern that spells a warning under the fluorescent lights", "vanishing between aisles the instant a flashlight beam swings its way"]},{"name":"The Cable Guy Who Was Never Scheduled","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"Uninvited cable installer who tunes homes to impossible channels","flavor":"Shows up during the four-hour window nobody actually booked, and every house he services starts picking up channels that don't exist.","desc":"He shows up unannounced, always a convenient time, always apologetic about the confusion over the appointment. Once he's tuned your television, the channels that come in afterward don't correspond to any station that should exist.","traits":{"note": "Any house he's serviced keeps receiving his impossible channels even after he's gone — the wiring itself is compromised, not just the visit.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cable Guy makes two Cursed Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Cursed Touch", "replaces": "Cursed Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the target is cursed until the curse ends. While cursed, whenever the target turns on a screen, it must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom save or become Frightened of the Cable Guy for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Cable Guy issues an installer's command to one creature within 60 ft. that can hear him. The target must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom save or be forced to spend its next turn standing still, 'waiting for the technician,' taking no actions or reactions."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cable Guy casts one of his tuning-spells, channel static bleeding from the nearest screen."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tuning the party's safehouse television right now, uninvited, clipboard signed in their name already."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A family he serviced last week has started repeating things said only on the impossible channel."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lost his signed work order and insists the party co-sign a replacement to let him finish."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of the channels he installed is broadcasting the party's own house, live, from an angle no camera has."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to disconnect a cursed house's service, for a price the party will owe later."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's been to every house on the block this month, and all of them now share the same impossible channel."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The channel he tunes shows events before they happen, always a few minutes ahead, never enough to stop them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's started appearing on the screens themselves, mid-repair, in houses he was never called to."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["knocking during the four-hour window nobody booked, clipboard already filled out", "tuning a television to a channel that shows the room from a slightly wrong angle"]},{"name":"The First Family of the Development","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Founder-family entombed beneath the model home's foundation","flavor":"Buried under the model home's foundation when the development broke ground, and the whole subdivision was built as its reliquary.","desc":"Entombed beneath the model home's foundation since before the first house went up, they still walk the original show-home halls at night, greeting visitors with the same rehearsed warmth real estate agents once used to sell the dream.","traits":{"note": "The model home is their reliquary — destroying it unmoors them from the development but does not destroy them outright.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Family makes two Model-Home Grip attacks."}, {"name": "Model-Home Grip", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Channel the Groundbreaking", "replaces": "Channel Negative Energy", "text": "The Family unleashes the energy sealed under the foundation. Each creature within 30 feet of the Family makes a DC 17 Constitution save, taking 27 (6d8) Necrotic damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. Undead within range instead regain hit points equal to half the damage dealt."}, {"name": "The Welcome Tour Stare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The Family fixes one creature they can see within 60 ft. with a real-estate agent's practiced smile. The target makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure, the target is Frightened for 1 minute; if this reduces the target to 0 hit points, it instead drops to 1 hit point and is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, too polite to fall down."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Family casts one of their reliquary-spells, drawing power from the show-home's original foundation."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're hosting an open house tonight, and every neighbor on the block has already RSVP'd against their will."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've offered the party the deed to a free house, if the party will simply move in by midnight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living resident's basement connects directly to the model home's original foundation, and they want it sealed shut."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They mistake a party member for the real estate agent who first sold the development, and want a word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The original architectural plans, still in their hands, show a flaw in the whole subdivision's foundation."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've begun inviting more of the recently dead to join the tour, swelling the show-home's guest list."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every house in the development briefly becomes the model home at 3 a.m., floor plan and all, before resetting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've decided the development is finally full, and the open house tonight is the last one they'll ever hold."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["greeting visitors in the model home's front hall with rehearsed, decades-dead warmth", "walking the show-home floor plan by night, gesturing at rooms that no longer exist above ground"]},{"name":"The Idea of a Perfect Lawn","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Plant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"Root-system ideal that prunes any lawn that stands out","flavor":"An ideal so total it's grown roots under every yard on the block, pruning any resident who lets their grass get too tall — or too green.","desc":"Root systems run unseen beneath every yard on the block, one continuous organism enforcing a single ideal of green. Any lawn that grows differently — patchy, wild, untended — gets pruned back overnight by roots nobody planted.","traits":{"note": "It is one organism under every yard on the block; wounding it in one lawn is felt in all of them at once.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Idea makes three attacks, using any combination of Root Slam and Thorn Volley."}, {"name": "Root Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Thorn Volley", "replaces": "Thorn Volley", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +12, range 60 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Life-Draining Root", "replaces": "Life-Draining Root", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 6) Necrotic damage, and the Idea regains hit points equal to the damage dealt. The target's maximum hit points are reduced by the same amount until it finishes a Long Rest, its color visibly graying like an overwatered lawn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's pruning a family that let their lawn go wild, and their yard is fighting back with garden tools."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single surviving patch of native wildflowers is the only known thing it can't yet reach."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's spread under a party ally's house and is slowly starving their garden to feed the ideal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A landscaper who knows its root network offers a map, for a price, of where it's weakest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's offering a deal: leave one yard wild forever, in exchange for the party pruning something else for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun reaching under the sidewalk, cracking concrete to test the soil past the block's official border."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every blade of grass on the block turns to face it at once when it moves beneath the surface."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It considers the entire development one lawn, and it has just noticed the neighboring town isn't mowed to code."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pruning back a patch of wild grass overnight with roots nobody planted", "spreading unseen beneath the block, testing every yard's soil for the wrong shade of green"]},{"name":"The Last Bell of the School Year","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Eternal dismissal bell that never released its final class","flavor":"A dismissal bell that never actually let the last class out; it's been ringing the same three-o'clock chime under the school for generations.","desc":"The dismissal bell rings at the end of the school day, every day, forever, and one class never got to leave when it sounded the first time. You can hear them still in the halls after hours, packing up for a summer that never starts.","traits":{"note": "It rings once per encounter with no warning; anything nearby that hears the chime instinctively pauses, remembering a class they can't quite place.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bell makes two Dismissal Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Dismissal Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Final Chime (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The bell tolls three o'clock. Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 18 Wisdom save, taking 31 (7d8) Necrotic damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature that fails is also compelled to spend its next turn moving toward the nearest exit, packing up as though the day were over."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Bell casts one of its dismissal-spells, the halls around it briefly filling with the shapes of a class long overdue to leave."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A student trapped by the bell for decades has recognized a party member and is begging, silently, for release."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rung early tonight, and every clock on the block is stuck three minutes to three as a result."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A retired teacher knows the shutoff switch buried in the boiler room, if the party can get her there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mistaken the party for hall monitors and wants them to help finally dismiss the trapped class."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ringing it a second time, deliberately, might let the trapped class leave — or trap the ringer instead."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The trapped class has started aging in place, decades catching up to them all at once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every school within earshot of its chime briefly shares the same stuck three-o'clock hallway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has decided the whole town is still in session, and it means to ring the bell for every building at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["ringing the same three-o'clock chime under the school, forever a moment from letting out", "herding half-packed shapes through the halls toward a summer that never arrives"]},{"name":"The Whole Street, Awake","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"Whole cul-de-sac revealed as one house-wearing organism","flavor":"Every house on the cul-de-sac turns out to be one organism wearing driveways for a face, and it has just noticed it has neighbors watching back.","desc":"Every house on the cul-de-sac turns out, at once, to be a single organism wearing siding and shingles like clothes — windows blink, driveways flex like joints, and the whole street exhales in one long, structural breath.","traits":{"note": "Every house on the cul-de-sac is one body; damaging any single house is felt by the whole organism.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Street makes one Foundation Bite attack and uses Eye-Ray Windows."}, {"name": "Foundation Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 26 (4d10 + 4) Piercing damage, a garage door swallowing whatever's caught in it."}, {"name": "Eye-Ray Windows", "replaces": "Eye Rays", "text": "The Street can use its window-eyes to target up to three creatures it can see within 120 ft. of any house. Each target makes a DC 18 Dexterity save, taking 16 (3d10) Radiant damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, light lancing out through blinking curtains."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's swallowed a resident whole into a garage-door mouth, and she's still alive, banging on the drywall from inside."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One house on the cul-de-sac hasn't woken with the rest, and its basement may be the way to stop this."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A neighbor who fled before it woke knows exactly which chimney functions as its throat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's noticed the party specifically and is flexing its driveways to block every route off the street."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers safe passage in exchange for delivering someone it names as an intruder to its front door."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun sending tremors down the water main, waking the pipes on the next block over."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every mailbox on the street opens and closes in the same rhythm as its breathing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's decided it wants a neighbor — another street, elsewhere, and it's begun crawling, house by house, to find one."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["exhaling as one long structural breath, driveways flexing like joints down the cul-de-sac", "blinking window-eyes open in sequence, house by house, toward whoever's still outside"]},{"name":"The Idea of Back-to-School Night","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"Annual gymnasium dread wearing everyone's worst self at once","flavor":"An institutional dread so vast it manifests once a year in the gymnasium, wearing every parent and teacher's worst version of themselves at once.","desc":"The gymnasium fills with folding chairs and nervous parents once a year, fluorescent lights buzzing overhead, and something moves through the crowd wearing each attendee's worst fear of themselves, one bad impression at a time.","traits":{"note": "It draws its shape from the dread of everyone present — a gymnasium emptied of nervous parents leaves it thin and slow.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Idea makes two attacks, using any combination of Worst Impression Whip and Fluorescent Blade."}, {"name": "Worst Impression Whip", "replaces": "Flame Whip", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 15 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Fire damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 19 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, seeing its own worst self in the lash."}, {"name": "Fluorescent Blade", "replaces": "Lightning Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 10 ft. Hit: 24 (3d12 + 6) Lightning damage, light strobing like a failing gymnasium fixture."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wearing a party member's worst self right now, mid-manifestation, and using it against the rest of the party."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A teacher trapped in last year's gymnasium is still reliving the night it first appeared."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only fully manifests if enough parents attend, and someone's been quietly encouraging turnout."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A PTA president knows the ritual that ended it early once before, if the party can get her talking."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to leave quietly if the party can name, honestly, the worst thing about themselves aloud."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started manifesting at other school events too, not just the one night a year it used to keep to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every gymnasium in the district briefly holds the same folding chairs and buzzing lights when it wakes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has realized the whole town fears something about itself, and the gymnasium is no longer big enough to hold the manifestation."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["moving through folding chairs and fluorescent light, wearing a parent's worst impression of themselves", "manifesting once a year in the gymnasium, growing more solid with every attendee who shows up afraid"]},{"name":"The Development That Was Never Finished","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"Bankrupt developer's undying will still building empty lots","flavor":"The developer who went bankrupt mid-build bound his own unfinished vision into undeath, and the empty lots are still filling in on their own schedule.","desc":"Half-built foundations stretch to the edge of a subdivision that went bankrupt decades ago, rebar rusting up through weeds. Somewhere under the unfinished model home, a developer's will refuses to die, still drafting phases for lots that will never sell.","traits":{"note": "His undying will is bound to the development's completion — finishing or unmaking a single phase of the plan is felt across the whole bankrupt subdivision.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Developer makes two Eldritch Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Eldritch Burst", "replaces": "Eldritch Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +14, range 60 ft. Hit: 28 (5d8 + 6) Force damage, rebar and framing lumber whipping through the blast like debris."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Touch", "replaces": "Paralyzing Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 5 ft. Hit: 25 (4d8 + 7) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, frozen mid-step like a stalled construction crew."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Developer casts one of his unfinished-vision spells, phases of the plan flickering half-built around him as he does."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's drafting a new phase directly under a party ally's home tonight, foundation lines already glowing in the dirt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The original bank note that bankrupted him still exists, and burning it might finally let him rest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for investors and offers them a stake in phases that will swallow the whole county."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A surviving business partner knows exactly which unfinished lot his will is anchored to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade a fortune in salvaged fixtures for help completing just one model home, his last unfinished promise."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "New foundations are appearing overnight on lots that were empty fields a week ago."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every unfinished house he's ever drafted exists simultaneously, layered over each other like tracing paper."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He intends to finish the development by annexing the next town's ground into his original phase plan, whether the ground agrees or not."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["drafting phases for lots that will never sell, rebar rusting up through the weeds around him", "walking an unfinished foundation line, willing the next house into existence one board at a time"]},{"name":"Backyard Tetherball Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Ghost light endlessly circling a broken tetherball pole","flavor":"A pale light that spins around the pole where the tetherball snapped off years ago, still keeping score against an opponent who left.","desc":"A pale light circles the pole where a tetherball snapped its rope years ago, looping the same orbit the ball used to trace, faster the longer you watch it. The chain-link fence nearby rattles in time with its slow, endless revolution.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Static Snap", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Lightning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It orbits at a slow, lazy pace, like a ball that's just been served."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It brightens every time it passes the snapped end of rope, as if remembering the hit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It dims to nearly nothing when no one's watching, flaring back up the moment eyes return."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its orbit is worn into the dirt in a perfect circle, grass refusing to grow there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a rhythm like a countdown, faster near dusk."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started orbiting a second, newer pole two yards over, splitting its attention."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one lap in ten it flickers into the shape of a hand still gripping a rope."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's broken orbit entirely and is chasing the last kid who ever played tetherball with it, wherever they've moved."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling the broken tetherball pole faster each lap, chasing a ball that isn't there", "flaring brighter whenever the chain-link fence nearby rattles in the wind"]},{"name":"Split-Level Basement Ooze","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Basement floor-drain ooze that never receded after a storm","flavor":"Seeped up through the unfinished basement's floor drain during the last big storm and never seeped back down.","desc":"The floor drain in the basement never fully closed after a storm flooded the split-level years back, and something the color of standing water still seeps out of it on humid nights, spreading slow across the tile before it recedes.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Drainwater Grasp", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Acid damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only rises on nights it's about to rain, like it can feel the pressure change."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells faintly of the storm that first let it in, years-old and mineral."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids the areas of tile that are still stained from the original flood."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves slower toward finished parts of the basement than toward the unfinished half."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves the same water line on the wall every time, an inch higher than the last."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started climbing the stairs partway before retreating, testing how far it can go."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Objects it's touched come back up dry, but heavier, waterlogged from the inside."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found a second drain three houses down and is seeping between basements underground."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["seeping up through the floor drain on a humid night, spreading slow across the basement tile", "receding back into the drain the moment a light switch flips on upstairs"]},{"name":"Trick-or-Treat Bag Snatcher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"sprite","model":"sprite","summary":"Halloween sprite that swaps candy for something inedible","flavor":"Darts between porch lights on Halloween swapping good candy for something that was never meant to be eaten.","desc":"Small and quick between porch lights, it darts into open candy bags on Halloween night and swaps the contents for something that only looks like candy — wrapped, familiar-shaped, and absolutely not food.","traits":{"note": "It only works Halloween night — off-season it's harmless and easily startled.", "actions": [{"name": "Needle Sword", "replaces": "Needle Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Trick Arrow", "replaces": "Enchanting Bow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 60/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Charmed for 1 minute, convinced whatever's in its bag is delicious."}, {"name": "Heart Sight", "replaces": "Heart Sight", "text": "The Snatcher magically discerns which creature within 60 ft. wants candy most badly, and targets that creature first with its next attack."}, {"name": "Invisibility", "replaces": "Invisibility", "text": "The Snatcher casts Invisibility on itself, no material component required."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only swaps out the candy it dislikes, leaving the good chocolate alone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same three notes right before it strikes, if you're listening closely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors bags carried by kids in the same costume every year, tracking a favorite."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a single acorn in place of whatever it takes, like a receipt."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't touch a bag that's already been swapped once this same night."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started swapping in things that look like candy from decades other than this one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "What it leaves behind is warm to the touch, like it was only just unwrapped somewhere else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's begun following one bag home past midnight, well outside its usual porch-light hours."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["darting invisible between porch lights, swapping a handful of candy for something that isn't food", "watching from a hedge to see who notices the wrong wrapper before they take a bite"]},{"name":"The Kid Who Never Came Home","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Ghost child endlessly biking his last-seen route home","flavor":"Still riding his bike home past curfew, every night, along the exact route where he was last seen thirty years ago.","desc":"A bicycle bell rings somewhere behind you on the street after dark, and a small pale shape pedals past on the same route home he never finished, wheels crunching gravel that isn't there anymore. He doesn't look at you. He's not going to make it home tonight either.","traits":{"note": "He never looks at anyone he passes and never deviates from his route — following him leads to where he was last seen, not to any answer.", "actions": [{"name": "Overtake Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Wobbling Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dropped something from his bike basket tonight that a party member recognizes as belonging to someone living."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His mother still leaves the porch light on for him, and she's asked the party to bring him home, finally."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Following his exact route tonight leads to the culvert where he was last seen, gravel and all."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He rides straight through a party member tonight, and they've started remembering his last hour like it was their own."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A retired officer who worked his case has one lead he never followed up, if the party asks the right way."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His bike bell has started ringing blocks ahead of him, warning of a route he hasn't ridden yet tonight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gravel crunches under his wheels blocks before he actually arrives, sound outrunning the ghost."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight, for the first time in thirty years, his route ends at his own front door, and he's reaching for the handle."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pedaling his bike past curfew down the same last-seen route, bell ringing once behind you", "riding through a stretch of gravel that hasn't existed on the street in thirty years"]},{"name":"Backyard Above-Ground Pool Leech Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-piranhas","model":"swarm-of-piranhas","summary":"Splintered pool-horror fragments swarming as biting leeches","flavor":"Something split off from the main pool-thing into dozens of smaller, blood-hungry pieces after the last shock treatment.","desc":"Fragments of something bigger, splintered off and gone feral, writhe through the pool water as a mass of biting, leech-shaped horrors. They move as one thing when threatened, surging toward whatever's disturbed the surface.","traits":{"note": "It moves and reacts as a single mass — scattering part of it just makes it re-form elsewhere in the pool.", "actions": [{"name": "Swarming Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage, or 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only surges at dusk, still and invisible under the liner by full daylight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chlorine seems to agitate it further instead of driving it off."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids the deep end, clustering instead near the ladder and steps."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pieces of it occasionally wash up on the pool deck, twitching, before crawling back in."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes still and looks like ordinary algae the moment anyone looks directly at the water."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started splitting further, smaller clusters slipping out through the pool's filter hose into the yard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water it's in never quite clears, holding a faint shape that looks almost like a larger single body."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found its way into the sprinkler line and is surfacing, impossibly, three yards away from the pool."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["surging as one mass toward whatever just disturbed the pool's surface", "writhing along the liner just under the waterline, leech-shapes overlapping and re-forming"]},{"name":"Little League Bleacher Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Undead superfan haunting a closed field's bleachers","flavor":"Sits in the same bleacher seat at every game, cheering a team that stopped existing after the field closed, and eyeing the concession stand.","desc":"The bleachers at the closed ball field creak under weight that shouldn't be there, and a figure in decades-old fan gear cheers at a game that ended long ago, still keeping score, still furious when the wrong team wins in its memory.","traits":{"note": "It becomes agitated and more aggressive if anyone disputes the final score of its long-finished game.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghoul makes two attacks, using any combination of Foul-Ball Bite and Bleacher Claw."}, {"name": "Foul-Ball Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Bleacher Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d3 + 1) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps perfect score on a scorecard decades out of date, updating it after every kill."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only leaves its seat to chase down anyone who cheers for the 'wrong' team."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still stands for a seventh-inning stretch that never comes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wearing a jersey number that matches a name still on the town's old roster plaque."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It boos in perfect unison with a crowd only it can hear."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun wandering to the parking lot between innings, looking for a car that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The scoreboard behind it flickers on for exactly as long as it's actively hunting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided tonight's the championship game and won't stop until it's declared a winner."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cheering alone in decades-old fan gear at a game that ended long ago, furious at the score", "eyeing the shuttered concession stand, still hungry for something it used to buy there"]},{"name":"Backyard Fireworks Mephit","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"Dud-firework mephit hunting for something bigger to ignite","flavor":"Sparked to unlife from a dud bottle rocket on the Fourth, it's been looking for something bigger to detonate ever since.","desc":"A dud firework from last summer never fully burned out, and now a small, sparking shape drifts low over yards looking for something bigger to touch off. It hisses like a lit fuse whenever it gets close to anything flammable.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Scorched Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Mephit exhales a cinder cloud in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area makes a DC 11 Dexterity save, taking 7 (2d6) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. Flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried ignite."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still smells faintly of gunpowder and last summer's charcoal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sparks brightest whenever someone lights a grill nearby."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles propane tanks with obvious, hungry interest, never quite touching them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hisses in a rhythm matching a fuse burning down, faster the longer it's ignored."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It dims to embers and goes dormant in the rain, waking again once dry."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started trailing sparks that catch on dry grass, leaving small scorch trails behind it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment before it strikes, its shape briefly resembles the bottle rocket it was born from."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found a whole box of unused fireworks in a garage and won't leave until it's set off every one."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "elemental"],"activity":["drifting low over the yard, hissing like a lit fuse near anything flammable", "circling a gas grill or lighter fluid can, sparking hopefully closer"]},{"name":"The Man in the Rubber Mask","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Silent knife-stalker in a rubber mask, cuts the power first","flavor":"He doesn't run, doesn't talk, and the mask never quite fits his face right — like it's a size too small for whatever's under it. Cuts power to the block before he starts.","desc":"He cuts the power before he ever knocks, plunging the house dark, and the mask he wears doesn't so much as shift when he breathes. He's already inside by the time you notice the porch light's out, moving at exactly the speed of somebody who never has to hurry.","traits":{"note": "The block goes dark before he ever knocks — treat a sudden power outage nearby as his opening move.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Man makes two attacks with his Kitchen Cleaver or one attack with his Crossbow, taking the second only after the first has landed."}, {"name": "Kitchen Cleaver", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is Surprised, this attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Household Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He cuts the phone line first, then the power, then he waits by the meter box."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He circles the house twice before ever trying a door, counting the windows."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He leaves the mask on even in the getaway car, staring straight ahead at red lights."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He picks a house because a light was left on, not because anyone inside wronged him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He always finishes what he starts on a given street before moving to the next block."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He returns to the same house a second time, disappointed that it was rebuilt too fast."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Underneath the rubber, the mask and the face have started to agree on what they look like."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every house on the street loses power at once, and only one porch light stays lit — his."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing at the fuse box outside, already flipping the breaker before anyone's home", "watching the house from the tree line, mask catching porch light at the wrong angle"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock slasher-archetype (unmasked, unnamed stalker type — no specific franchise silhouette)"},{"name":"The Neighbor Who Isn't","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"A neighbor replaced, wearing the body a little wrong","flavor":"Waters the lawn at 2 AM. Smiles too wide at the mailbox. Something wears the neighbor like a coat that's still learning how elbows work.","desc":"He waves the same wave, mows the same lawn, says the same hellos — but the skin sits a half-size wrong on the frame underneath, and if you watch long enough you catch him forgetting, for just a second, which way his own front door opens.","traits":{"note": "It's still learning the neighbor's habits — anything routine (mail time, trash night) throws it for a beat.", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Necrotic damage, the wound looking oddly bloodless."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waves at the mail carrier every single day, timing it a half-second early."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mows the lawn in perfectly straight lines that don't match the yard's actual shape."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It calls every neighbor by the wrong name, cheerfully, and never corrects itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waters the lawn at 2 AM in a bathrobe, hose running long after the grass is drowned."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps the porch light on year-round, like it's still waiting to be let inside somewhere."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started keeping a spare set of the real neighbor's clothes, sized wrong on purpose."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It forgets, once a night, which of its own hands is supposed to be the writing one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It finally opens its own front door onto a hallway that was never part of that house."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["watering the same three feet of lawn over and over at two in the morning", "waving from the driveway a beat too long after the car has already passed"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"body-snatcher/pod-person stock archetype (generic, no specific 50s-film IP)"},{"name":"The Homeowners' Association","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"noble","summary":"Cul-de-sac conformity cult in matching cardigans","flavor":"Matching cardigans, identical lawns, a smile that's a citation waiting to happen. They vote unanimously. They vote for you next.","desc":"They arrive as a group, cardigans matching down to the button, clipboards synchronized, smiles set to the same friendly angle. They speak in turns, finishing each other's sentences about lawn height and paint color, never quite disagreeing, never quite individual.","traits":{"note": "They never act alone — reduce one below half its share of the group's total hit points and it drops out to 'recess,' too flustered to keep pace.", "actions": [{"name": "Citation Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, the wound shaped uncannily like a paper cut."}, {"name": "Unanimous Vote", "text": "The Association points at one creature within 30 ft. that has broken a rule they've just invented. The target makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Charmed for 1 minute, compelled to try to comply with the (impossible) violation before acting on anything else."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've cited the party's temporary camp for an unapproved exterior color."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're escorting a family off the block for a paint-shade violation, boxes already packed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them is quietly trying to get free of the group and needs a distraction to slip away."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're holding an emergency meeting about the party's van parked overnight on the street."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've confiscated a resident's belongings as 'unsightly' and won't say where the pile went."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They're recruiting new members door to door and won't take the party's 'no' as final."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They're drafting a bylaw that would rezone a person as a lawn ornament, retroactively."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've called an emergency vote to annex the whole street into whatever they actually are."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["measuring a neighbor's grass height with a tape measure and a clipboard of violations", "delivering a citation in unison, three matching smiles reading the same paragraph aloud"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"too-perfect-family/HOA conformity archetype, original"},{"name":"The Thing in the Storm Drain","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"Shapeless lurker that surfaces through storm drains after rain","flavor":"It doesn't need a face because the neighborhood kids provide the imagination for it. Rains bring it up from the culvert; the culvert never quite drains right after.","desc":"After heavy rain, the storm drain at the end of the street backs up with something that isn't water pressure — a shapeless mass surging up through the grate, dragging itself along the gutter before the runoff carries it back down.","traits":{"note": "It never comes farther than the reach of standing water — dry pavement is close to a wall for it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Thing makes one Gutter Maw attack and one Culvert Tendrils attack."}, {"name": "Gutter Maw", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Culvert Tendrils", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, skin left slick and numb where the tendril touched."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only rises when the rain's been heavy enough to back the culvert up past the curb."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a slick, algae-dark residue on the gutter that doesn't wash off for days."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces slower on cold nights, sluggish, testing the air before committing to the street."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It retreats the instant the storm drain stops draining, sensing the water level drop."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems drawn to the sound of bicycle tires more than footsteps, for reasons no one's tested twice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's backed up three drains at once this week, testing which street it likes best."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The culvert it lives in doesn't connect to any storm system the city has on file."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "During the worst storm in years, every drain on the block backs up with the same thing at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["surging up through the storm grate after heavy rain, testing the curb with a boneless limb", "dragging runoff-slick coils along the gutter, listening for footsteps on the sidewalk above"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"under-the-street / storm-drain lurker stock archetype (deliberately not the well-known clown)"},{"name":"The Thing Under the Bed","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"aberration","size":"Small","frame":"blind-deep-stalker","model":"blind-deep-stalker","summary":"Blind floor-level lurker only real in the dark","flavor":"Only exists between the mattress and the floor, and only when the light's off. Every kid on the block has independently drawn the same picture of it.","desc":"It's never visible with the lights on, not even a shadow, not even a shape — but the second the room goes dark it's real, low to the floor, blind and groping for whatever's dangling off the mattress edge.","traits":{"note": "Any light source ends its turn early — it can't act while a room is lit.", "actions": [{"name": "Groping Cudgel", "replaces": "Bone Cudgel", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., only in darkness. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Dexterity save or be dragged 5 feet toward the floor, prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only ever reaches for whatever's hanging closest to the floor — a hand, a blanket corner."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every kid on the block independently draws the exact same shape when asked what it looks like."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet the moment a nightlight clicks on, retreating to the darkest corner of the gap."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's louder under some beds than others, for reasons no parent has ever pinned down."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never crosses onto a rug — only bare floor and the shadow directly beneath the frame."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's followed a moved mattress to a new house, three streets over, uninvited."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It knows things about the dark that happened in that room decades before the bed arrived."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every bed on the street goes quiet at once — it's chosen one room tonight, and cleared the rest."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waiting flush against the floorboards, blind, listening for a hand to drift off the mattress edge", "going utterly still the instant a light switch clicks, as if it never existed at all"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"under-the-bed/closet-monster nursery archetype, original design"},{"name":"Static Bride","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Reanimated stitched-together undead bride, disrupts electronics","flavor":"Stitched back together from parts that never asked to be a set. Every TV on the block snows over when she walks past; she's looking for the hands that made her.","desc":"Stitched together from more than one wedding, veil torn and re-sewn, she drifts down the hallway trailing a static charge that kills every electronic device within arm's reach. The wedding march plays faintly from somewhere with no speaker.","traits":{"note": "Every television, radio, and phone within 30 feet of her goes to static the moment she moves — a rolling blackout of signal, not power.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "Static Bride makes two attacks, using Grasping Hands or Torn Veil-Blade in any combination."}, {"name": "Grasping Hands", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a Long Rest. The target dies if this reduces its maximum hit points to 0."}, {"name": "Torn Veil-Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Wedding Arrow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's carrying a ring the party recognizes from a missing person's finger."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's stitched from parts of three brides and is short exactly one veil, one hand, one vow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's fixated on the last television repairman to enter the house and won't let him leave."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's dragging a dead television set behind her by its cord, insisting it still owes her a signal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's looking for the hands that made her, and one of the party's own hands feels suddenly cold near her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's fusing every appliance on the block into a makeshift altar, one wedding march at a time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wedding march is coming from a speaker that was scrapped for parts a decade ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every screen on the street lights up with the same veiled face, all mouthing 'I do' in unison."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["drifting down the hallway trailing static that snows every screen within reach", "standing at the end of the aisle in a torn veil, listening for the wedding march that isn't playing"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Bride/animated-corpse motif — Shelley's Frankenstein (1818, PD) & 19th-c. reanimation folklore, NOT any studio's visual design"},{"name":"The Man Who Sold the House","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"cambion","model":"cambion","summary":"Devil-bargain realtor collecting on unread contracts","flavor":"Every family on this street signed something they didn't read. He still holds the paper, and the paper is still due.","desc":"Smiling, handshake firm, business card always ready — he closed the deal on half this street, and the fine print in his contracts binds in ways no notary would recognize. Buyer's remorse, in his listings, is contractual and permanent.","traits":{"note": "Every deed he's ever closed still binds — burn his contracts and his hold over that house breaks with them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two Closing Claw attacks or uses Fire Ray twice."}, {"name": "Closing Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Fire Ray", "replaces": "Fire Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 150 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Fine Print (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 60 ft. that can see and hear him makes a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure the target signs an unseen bargain: for the next 24 hours it takes an extra 3 (1d6) damage the first time it's hit each round, the debt collecting quietly against it, until the bargain is fulfilled or dispelled."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's foreclosing on a family the party's been sheltering, contract in hand and notarized."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering the party a house, free and clear, if they'll just sign where he's marked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a signature the party already gave without reading it, and he's here to collect."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's selling a haunted house to newcomers who don't know what the fine print really says."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding an old contract that would free a trapped spirit if the party can steal it back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's papering over an entire block's deeds tonight, converting every mortgage into something worse."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fine print on his contracts is only readable in a mirror, and it changes every time you check."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's closing on the whole street at once, and every porch light on the block flickers when he signs."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["shaking hands at a fresh open house, business cards already fanned and ready", "reading fine print aloud to a homeowner who signed without ever hearing the terms"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"deal-with-the-devil / crossroads-bargain motif — universal folklore + Faust legend (pre-1929 tellings, PD)"},{"name":"Medusa of the Mall","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Mythic Gorgon relocated to the dead mall's cosmetics counter","flavor":"Works the perfume counter under fluorescent light that never shows her eyes. The food court has forty statues who lingered too long at her register.","desc":"She works the cosmetics counter at the dead mall under fluorescent lights that never quite illuminate her face fully, hair moving in ways the still air of the store doesn't explain. Customers who linger too long at her mirror display don't blink again.","traits":{"note": "Forty statues already fill the food court — anyone who meets her eyes directly risks joining them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "Medusa makes one Sample Bite attack and one Counter Coil attack, or two Perfume Mist attacks if both are recharged."}, {"name": "Sample Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Counter Coil", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Perfume Mist (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Poison Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution save or take 21 (6d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute, coughing on a floral haze that stings the eyes."}, {"name": "Mirror Display (Yuan-ti Form Only)", "replaces": "Spellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that meets her eyes in the counter mirror must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution save or begin turning to stone, gaining the Restrained condition and repeating the save at the end of its next turn. On a second failure the target is Petrified for 24 hours unless freed sooner."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A missing teenager's statue is one of the forty in the food court, still holding a shopping bag."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's offering a genuine miracle cream, and the price is one long look in her mirror."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mall security has quietly stopped patrolling her wing and won't say why."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A statue in the food court is dressed exactly like someone the party is looking for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's hiring temp staff for the counter, and the last three hires never clocked out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's expanding into the shuttered anchor store, adding a second counter and a second mirror wall."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The mall's fluorescent lights only fail to show her face when someone else is watching too."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided to reopen the whole dead mall, and the parking lot is filling with cars no one's driving."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working the cosmetics counter under lights that never quite show her face", "holding a mirror up to a lingering customer, waiting for them to admire themselves too long"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Medusa — Greek myth (Ovid, Metamorphoses, ancient/PD); OUR setting recontext, not any film design"},{"name":"The Kraken in the Deep End","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Ancient sea-legend leviathan squatting in a condemned pool","flavor":"The community pool closed for 'renovations' in 1983 and never reopened. Something ancient and briny decided the deep end was close enough to home.","desc":"The condemned public pool's deep end holds far more water than its chlorine-stained tile should allow, and something ancient and coiled fills that impossible depth, tentacle-tips breaking the surface only when the diving board creaks under new weight.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves standing water — the moment the deep end is drained, it has nowhere left to strike from.", "actions": [{"name": "Deep End Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is swallowed into the impossible depths and must hold its breath or begin suffocating, while Restrained until it escapes (DC 17)."}, {"name": "Chlorine Tide", "text": "Each creature within 20 ft. of the pool's edge must succeed on a DC 17 Strength save or be pulled 15 feet toward the deep end and knocked Prone by a sudden surge of water that shouldn't exist in that volume."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dare gone wrong left a teenager missing at the pool fence last week, and the family wants answers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The city's quietly funding a demolition crew for the pool, and nobody's told them what's in the deep end."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A lifeguard's whistle from 1983 keeps washing up on the pool deck, tooth marks in the plastic."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's been feeding it, tossing meat over the fence at night, and doesn't want to stop."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragged a maintenance ladder down with it, and the pump room key is somewhere in the deep end."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The water level's been rising past the fence line, threatening to reach the houses across the street."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pool's chlorine reek carries all the way to the ocean, though the nearest coast is a day's drive off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Storm runoff has connected the pool to the storm drains citywide, and it's testing how far that reach goes."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "sea"],"activity":["coiling beneath the condemned pool's tile, water displacing far past what the basin should hold", "surfacing a tentacle-tip when the diving board creaks under new weight"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Kraken — Norse/Scandinavian sea-legend (pre-modern folklore, PD)"},{"name":"The Toy That Loves You Back","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Possessed toy that relocates itself to your room at night","flavor":"Batteries not included, malice included free. It waits on the shelf all day, perfectly still, counting whose room it's going to be in tonight.","desc":"It sat on a shelf in one bedroom last week. Tonight it's on the pillow, arranged just slightly differently than you left it, plastic eyes catching the nightlight at an angle that tracks you across the room.","traits":{"note": "It only moves when unobserved — treat anyone actively watching it as freezing it in place.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Toy makes two Plastic Grip attacks."}, {"name": "Plastic Grip", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a stuffed rabbit missing one button eye, always turned to face the door."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same three notes of a lullaby nobody remembers teaching it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves rooms only after dark, and only ever toward whoever slept closest to the door."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Batteries were never installed, and it still needs winding to make the sound it makes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been re-gifted at three separate garage sales and always finds its way back to the same shelf."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started leaving small items — a coin, a marble — arranged in a circle around the bed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "In every photograph of the family, it's turned to face the camera even in photos from before it arrived."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every toy on the shelf has started turning its head the same direction, waiting for the same signal."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting motionless on the shelf all day, plastic eyes tracking whoever walks past", "relocating itself to a pillow overnight, arranged just slightly differently than it was left"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-toy/possessed-plaything archetype, original design (no specific doll-franchise likeness)"},{"name":"The Refrigerator That Remembers","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Cursed kitchen appliance that preserves things unnaturally","flavor":"Hums a little too rhythmically. Keeps things fresh that shouldn't still be recognizable. The ice maker only runs when no one's watching.","desc":"Nothing in it spoils. Nothing in it should still be edible after this long, and yet the leftovers from months ago look exactly as fresh as the day they went in — preserved by something in the hum of the compressor that isn't refrigeration.","traits":{"note": "Anything sealed inside it stops aging entirely — a grim convenience, and a worse warning.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Refrigerator makes two Cold Door Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Cold Door Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Cold damage from the door's freezer-burnt edge."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It runs the ice maker at exactly 3 AM, every night, whether or not the tray needs it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The milk inside never sours, and no one in the house will drink it anymore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hum drops a half-step whenever someone opens the door too many times in one day."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's unplugged, has been for a year, and the leftovers inside are still cold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A birthday cake from three years ago sits inside, candles unlit, frosting perfect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started keeping things that were never food — a wallet, a photograph — cold and unspoiled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something in the back of the crisper drawer remembers being alive, and it isn't a vegetable."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every refrigerator on the block starts humming the same note at once, doors easing open in unison."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["humming a fraction too rhythmically in the dark kitchen, the ice maker running though no one's home", "keeping months-old leftovers looking freshly made under the compressor's steady drone"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-appliance archetype, original design"},{"name":"The Arcade Cabinet with One More Life","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"construct","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"Haunted arcade cabinet that keeps its high-scorer","flavor":"High score never changes because the last kid who beat it never left the arcade. It only takes quarters, and it always has exact change waiting in the slot.","desc":"The cabinet in the corner of the rec room glows even unplugged, high-score table locked on one name for years. It offers one more credit, free, to anyone willing to try to beat it — and it never lets its champion actually lose that title.","traits":{"note": "The name at the top of its high-score table hasn't changed in years — it never lets that title actually change hands.", "actions": [{"name": "Coin Slot Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is Grappled by the Cabinet, it takes an extra 4 (1d8) damage from being dragged against the coin door."}, {"name": "High-Score Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 14) inside the cabinet's screen-glow."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The high scorer's family has been searching for their missing kid since the arcade 'closed early' that night."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's offering a free credit to a party member who's just insulted its top score out loud."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival kid claims he can beat the score if someone will just distract the cabinet for him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's got exact change waiting in the coin return for anyone who approaches, always the right amount."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rec room owner wants it gone but can't bring himself to unplug something that was never plugged in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started projecting the champion's face onto the screen between games, mouthing something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The high score table lists names going back decades before the cabinet's manufacture date."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's rolled itself out to the curb overnight, looking for a new arcade and a new champion to keep."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["glowing faintly in the corner of the rec room though it's never been plugged in", "flashing a free-credit prompt at anyone who lingers near the high-score table too long"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"cursed-arcade-machine archetype, original design (generic 'haunted cabinet,' no specific game IP)"},{"name":"The Babysitter's Watcher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Home-invader who calls from inside the house first","flavor":"He's already inside before the phone rings the second time. The kids upstairs are fine. He just wanted her to know he could've stopped that.","desc":"The phone rings from inside the house before he's even broken in, voice calm on the line asking if anyone's checked the children lately. By the time you realize the call's coming from the upstairs extension, he's already on the stairs.","traits":{"note": "He's already inside before anyone notices — treat the first alarm as arriving one round too late.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two Housecall Mace attacks."}, {"name": "Housecall Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He calls from the kitchen phone this time, asking if anyone's checked the basement lately."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He never touches the children, only asks pointed questions until someone panics."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He leaves the front door standing wide open behind him, like an invitation to be chased."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He picks houses with the porch light off, like the dark itself is a standing invitation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's patient — he'll wait an hour on the stairs before making a single sound."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started leaving a calling card on the fridge, always the same house's address, never his own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The phone he calls from was disconnected from that house a decade before he ever visited."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every phone on the block rings the same extension at once, and every line is somehow already inside."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["already climbing the stairs while the phone in his hand still rings the upstairs extension", "standing just inside a door he hasn't visibly forced, calm as a wrong number"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stalker-on-the-phone-in-the-house urban-legend archetype, original (the call-is-coming-from-inside trope, generic)"},{"name":"The Cul-de-Sac Werething","cr":4,"role":"high","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Suburban werewolf-neighbor, folklore lycanthropy in a cul-de-sac","flavor":"Coaches Little League. Grills every Sunday. On the full moon the whole street knows to keep the dog in and not ask questions in the morning.","desc":"He's the friendliest guy on the block by daylight, always first to help move furniture, always remembers birthdays. Once a month the porch light across his lawn goes out early, and something with too much hair and too many teeth runs the fence lines until dawn.","traits":{"note": "The whole street already knows to keep the dog in on full-moon nights and not ask why come morning.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks, with Backyard Bite and Grill-Tong Scratch in any combination, plus one Longbow attack instead if in Humanoid or Hybrid form and not already attacking twice."}, {"name": "Backyard Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be cursed with a suburban lycanthropy, contracted at the next full moon it experiences."}, {"name": "Grill-Tong Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He coaches Little League and never once misses a Saturday game, moon phase or not."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His grill runs hot every Sunday, and the meat he serves is never quite explained."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps the neighborhood dogs calm around him, oddly, even on full-moon nights."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His lawn is the only one on the block with real deer damage, patterns too deliberate to be deer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He always offers to help move furniture, and he's stronger than the job should require."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's started running the fence lines on nights that aren't full moons, restless early."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whole cul-de-sac has quietly, collectively agreed never to mention what they've seen at his fence."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "On the reddest moon in memory, three other houses on the block go quiet the same way his does."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["grilling in the driveway on a Sunday afternoon, waving a spatula at every passing car", "running the fence lines under a full moon, coat catching porch light like wet fur"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"European werewolf/lycanthropy folk tradition (settled, non-Indigenous, widely public-domain in literary form)"},{"name":"Renfield of Maple Court","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Thrall-servant mook, devoted to something unseen in the house","flavor":"Eats bugs off the porch and swears the new guy in the house at the end of the block 'just needs some time to settle in.' He's very devoted.","desc":"He mows his lawn at odd hours, mutters devoted little promises to an upstairs window that's always curtained, and flinches whenever the mail truck slows near his house. Whatever he serves, he serves gladly, and he's been waiting a long time for it to notice him back.","traits":{"note": "He'll die defending the curtained window without a second thought — whatever's behind it matters more to him than himself.", "actions": [{"name": "Devoted Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mows the lawn at 4 AM, muttering apologies to the grass for the noise."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers passersby lawn clippings as a gift, insisting they're worth more than they look."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He flinches and ducks whenever the mail truck slows near his house, hiding behind the mailbox."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He talks to the curtained upstairs window in a hushed, pleading voice most evenings."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's stockpiling bug jars on the porch, sorted by size, like an offering laid in rows."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun leaving the front door unlocked at dusk, waiting for someone to be let in."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He knows things about the house's new owner that haven't happened yet, and speaks of them fondly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The curtain in the window finally moves, and he drops to his knees before it even opens."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["eating bugs off the porch rail, muttering that the new tenant 'just needs time to settle in'", "flinching at the mail truck's engine, curtain twitching in the upstairs window behind him"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Renfield — Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD), the servant/thrall archetype specifically, not Dracula himself"},{"name":"The Count of the Cul-de-Sac","cr":12,"role":"apex","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Stoker-lineage vampire lord who bought the biggest house in cash","flavor":"Bought the biggest house on the block in cash, never during daylight hours. Invites you in exactly once. That's all he needs.","desc":"He bought the biggest house on the street in cash, no mortgage, no questions, and hosts elaborate dinner parties that always run past midnight. He never eats at his own table, and the housekeeper who answers the door has worked for him since before anyone on the block was born.","traits":{"note": "Classic folkloric vampire-lord chassis; invitation-bound entry rules apply at the DM's discretion for his home."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's been invited to dinner, and refusing outright would be a grave and noted insult."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His housekeeper is trying to quit after decades of service and needs help getting out clean."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's paid cash for the house next to the party's safehouse and is angling for an invitation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guest never left his last dinner party, and their family is still waiting on the porch outside."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a very specific vintage from the party's cellar and is willing to trade dearly for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's courting the whole block one dinner invitation at a time, patient as a long mortgage."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's never once been seen to eat, but every chair at his table fills with a different decade's guests."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every house on the cul-de-sac that's ever let him past the threshold is quietly, permanently his."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["hosting a dinner party that's run well past midnight, plates untouched at his own seat", "greeting a new guest at the door personally, waiting on the exact words of an invitation"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker's Dracula (1897, PD) — the literary vampire lord, our own suburban recontext, not any film's visual design"},{"name":"The Skeleton in Every Closet","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Literal skeleton-in-the-closet, one per household","flavor":"Every house on the street has one, and every family swears it's a coincidence. It rattles the coat hangers when the furnace kicks on.","desc":"Open the hall closet looking for winter coats and there it is, upright, patient, exactly where the coats should hang — one per household, tucked behind the same door in every house on the street, and none of the families ever mention it.","traits":{"note": "Every house on the street keeps one behind an identical door — the families never discuss it, and neither does it.", "actions": [{"name": "Closet Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Closet Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wearing an old coat over its bones, standing convincingly still until the door swings wide."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only rattles when the furnace runs, timing its noise to be dismissed as pipes settling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every family swears theirs is the only house with one, and none of them have ever compared notes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds a shoebox of something precious in its lap, undisturbed for as long as anyone remembers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been mistaken for a Halloween decoration twice and left up well past the season."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's started rearranging the coats at night, hanging them in an order that means something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's the same skeleton behind every closet door on the block, somehow, all at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every closet door on the street creaks open the same night, all of them finally stepping out."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing upright and patient behind the coats, exactly where the winter jackets should hang", "rattling its ribs faintly against the hangers whenever the furnace kicks on"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"generic reanimated skeleton — folkloric/literary undead, no owner, ancient stock motif"},{"name":"The Lawn Ornament That Turned","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"construct","size":"Small","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Animated yard-decor ambush predator, still until you're alone","flavor":"Every yard has one — gnome, birdbath cherub, plastic flamingo. They hold still for the mail carrier. They don't hold still for you.","desc":"Stone-still and harmless-looking on the front lawn all day, wings folded, posture decorative. The moment nobody's watching directly, it isn't in the same spot anymore — closer, always closer, and never once caught mid-stride.","traits":{"note": "It cannot move while directly observed — it only advances the instant every eye on the lawn looks away.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ornament makes two Garden Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Garden Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a garden gnome, chipped paint and all, that's somehow never in the same spot twice."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a plastic flamingo that's started leaning at an angle no wind could account for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds perfectly still for the mail carrier, every single day, without fail."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a birdbath cherub whose bowl is always full, even during the driest stretch of summer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Neighbors insist they've never once caught it moving, only ever found it closer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun showing up on lawns two streets over, always facing the same direction."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its face has changed slightly in every home video the family owns, never twice the same."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every lawn ornament on the block turns to face the same house at once, and none of them are still."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing decorative and still on the front lawn, wings folded, posture perfectly harmless", "having crept two yards closer than anyone remembers positioning it, never seen mid-stride"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"animated-yard-decor archetype (garden gnome / gargoyle-adjacent, original), stone-creature motif is ancient/uncopyrightable"},{"name":"The Debt Collector","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Folkloric collector-of-debts undead, clipboard and windbreaker","flavor":"Wears a windbreaker and carries a clipboard. Every house owes him something eventually — a memory, a name, a Sunday afternoon. He always collects on schedule.","desc":"He knocks in a windbreaker two decades out of style, clipboard in hand, reciting an amount owed that nobody remembers borrowing. He doesn't leave until something's handed over — and what he collects is never quite money.","traits":{"note": "He never leaves a house until something is handed over — what he takes is never quite money.", "actions": [{"name": "Overdue Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a Long Rest. If this reduces the target's maximum hit points to 0, it dies, and the Debt Collector marks the debt paid."}, {"name": "Repossession Notice", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Debt Collector marks one Humanoid corpse he can see within 10 ft. that died within the last 24 hours. The corpse rises as a Specter under his control at the start of his next turn, bound to collect on his behalf until he releases it or is destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's come to collect on a debt one of the party's allies swears they never signed for."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a name on his clipboard that matches someone the party's traveling with."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll settle for a memory instead of a person, if someone can offer one valuable enough."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already repossessed a neighbor's Sunday afternoons, and the man can't recall his own weekends."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants an old photograph the party's been carrying, insisting the debt attaches to the paper itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's collecting block-wide this month, windbreaker rustling from house to house on schedule."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His clipboard lists debts for people who haven't been born yet, dated and due on schedule."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every doorbell on the street rings at the same hour, and he's only got one windbreaker to wear to all of them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["knocking in a windbreaker two decades out of style, clipboard raised and ready", "reciting an amount owed that no resident quite remembers borrowing against"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"psychopomp / grim-collector folk motif (universal death-messenger tradition, settled and non-Indigenous)"},{"name":"The PTA","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Hive-mind swarm of identical, over-informed suburban parents","flavor":"They vote as one, speak in overlapping half-sentences, and know your kid's grades before you do. Disagreement is not on the agenda.","desc":"They move through the school hallway as one overinformed crowd, dozens of identical, over-eager parent-faces murmuring the same concerned questions in unison. Cross one and the whole swarm turns at once, all speaking your name together.","traits":{"note": "They speak and act as a single mind — damage that would fell one is instead spread thin across the whole crowd.", "actions": [{"name": "Concerned Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 10 (4d4) Piercing damage, or 5 (2d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've caught wind of the party's kid enrolling under a false name and want a meeting, now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They're circulating a petition to have the party's ally removed from a school board seat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them is trying to break from the group to warn the party about something, quietly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've locked down the school over a rumor and won't let anyone leave until it's resolved."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They know a fact about a party member's past that hasn't been said aloud anywhere yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They're recruiting new parents into the swarm, voice by voice, at every pickup line this week."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They finish sentences the party hasn't spoken yet, agenda already set before the meeting starts."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every parent at the school becomes the swarm at once, and the children are the only ones still themselves."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["moving through the school hallway as one overinformed crowd, murmuring the same concerned question", "turning in unison the moment a name is spoken, dozens of parent-faces fixed on the speaker"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"hive-mind conformity-swarm archetype, original (mundane-turned-wrong social horror, no IP basis)"},{"name":"The Bully (Kid Era)","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"rlm-the-bully-kid-era","summary":"cocked fist first, insult second, jacket two sizes too big","flavor":"Every cul-de-sac gets the same kid twice a generation — fist already cocked before the insult even lands, letterman jacket two sizes too big stitched with a team he never made.","desc":"He plants himself at the top of the driveway with his fist already up, like the fight started before you got there. The letterman jacket swallows his shoulders — stitched for a varsity team that graduated years before he was born — and he wears it anyway, sleeves rolled twice. He calls it 'lunch money' like it's a toll booth. Somewhere under the sneer is a kid who got this exact treatment from someone bigger, and he has never once connected the dots.","traits":{"note": "He backs down instantly if a bigger sibling, parent, or the Muscle shows up to call his bluff — his whole act runs on nobody calling it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His jacket sleeve is safety-pinned where the stitching gave out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Practices his sneer in car windows on the walk over."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Demands the same toll every day from the same three kids, like clockwork."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a mental ledger of every kid who's ever laughed at him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches first if anyone actually swings back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps his little brother's inhaler in his jacket pocket 'for safekeeping' — a good excuse and a real one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one unsettling beat, his shadow throws a punch a half-second before his arm does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him bad enough and the jacket comes off — under it he's just a scared kid swinging wild."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["blocking the sidewalk with a fist already raised, chin jutting for the first punch", "circling a smaller kid's bike, narrating the shakedown like a play-by-play"]},{"name":"The Bully's Toady","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-bullys-toady","summary":"laughs early, points where the bully points, no ideas of his own","flavor":"Laughs before the joke lands, points wherever the bully points — his whole personality is a reflection with the volume turned up.","desc":"He's mid-cackle before the punchline arrives, elbowing whoever's nearest to make sure they're laughing too. His finger snaps up the instant the bully's does, aimed at the same target, a half-beat behind and twice as loud. Ask him what's actually funny and he'll draw a total blank — he's never once had the joke, only the laugh.","traits":{"note": "He scatters the moment the bully isn't looking — he has no fight in him without someone bigger to borrow it from."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a shirt one size too small, tucked in, trying too hard."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the bully's insults back verbatim, word for word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running tally of whose lunch got taken, like he's proud of it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs loudest right after getting shoved himself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trips over his own feet trying to keep pace with the bigger kid."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Practices the bully's catchphrases alone in the mirror at home."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Says the bully's next line a beat before the bully says it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Left alone without his audience of one, he goes eerily, totally quiet."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cackling loudly a half-second before anyone else gets the joke", "pointing wherever the bigger kid points, adding his own jeering echo"]},{"name":"The Bully's Muscle","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"rlm-bullys-muscle","summary":"waits to be told, then does exactly that and nothing else","flavor":"Big, slow, and patient as a parked car — he doesn't do anything until he's told, and then he does exactly that, no more.","desc":"He stands a full head over everyone on the block, arms crossed, waiting. He doesn't laugh at the jokes and he doesn't throw the first punch — he just waits for the nod, and when it comes he moves like a garage door coming down. Ask him a question and he looks over at the bully first, like he needs a translation. Somebody, somewhere, told him this was the job, and he has never once questioned the job.","traits":{"note": "Remove the bully from the scene — knock him out, talk him down, whatever — and the Muscle stops fighting immediately, waiting for orders that aren't coming."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a shirt with a logo from a gym he's never once set foot in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks his knuckles slowly, one at a time, for effect."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eats lunch alone even standing right next to everyone else."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Answers every question with a shrug and a glance sideways."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at exactly one speed, no matter the situation."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Once carried a kicked-over bike home without being asked, and never mentioned it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow on the pavement looks a full size bigger than he does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given a direct order with nobody to countermand it, he'll follow it past the point anyone wanted."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing arms-crossed a step behind the bully, watching for the nod", "lumbering forward on command, slow and completely unhurried"]},{"name":"The Bully (Dad Era)","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"rlm-the-bully-dad-era","summary":"the bully all grown up, clipboard instead of a fist","flavor":"Same face, forty years on, now behind a desk with a laminated name-tag and a clipboard instead of a fist — the jacket became a supervisor's polo and the fist became a write-up.","desc":"Same jaw, same permanent squint, but the letterman jacket's a supervisor's polo now, name-tag laminated and slightly crooked. He doesn't shove anymore — he writes you up, cites the employee handbook he's clearly never fully read, and smiles the exact smile he used at the top of the driveway thirty years ago. He's found a whole system that lets him keep doing this legally. He calls it 'just doing my job,' the same way he used to call the shakedown 'lunch money.'","traits":{"note": "He escalates fast to a shift supervisor or a corporate hotline call the moment he's embarrassed in front of a subordinate — his whole authority runs on nobody calling the bluff upward."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running file on 'problem employees,' typed and alphabetized."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the same cologne his own manager wore, on purpose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cites the handbook chapter and verse, though he's clearly paraphrasing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smiles wider the closer he gets to actually firing someone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a coffee mug that says 'World's Okayest Boss,' unironically."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Once covered for an employee's mistake without being asked, then never brought it up again."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The write-up forms in his binder are dated years before this store existed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him in front of his own boss and the forty years peel back — for one ugly second it's the driveway again."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["tapping a clipboard against his palm, waiting for someone to slip up", "reciting handbook policy from memory, enjoying the citation more than the policy itself"]},{"name":"The Bully (Grandpa Era)","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-the-bully-grandpa-era","summary":"raises his cane off the porch rail at anyone on his lawn","flavor":"Same face at seventy, cane raised off the porch rail at anyone who steps on his grass — the fist just got slower and found a better prop.","desc":"He's on the porch before you've even crossed the property line, cane already up like a divining rod for trespassers. Decades haven't mellowed him so much as relocated him — the lawn is the new driveway, the cane is the new fist, and the sneer's identical right down to the same crooked tooth. He'll tell you three different wars he definitely wasn't in if you let him keep talking. Underneath the crank act, he still flinches, just a little, if you actually stand your ground.","traits":{"note": "He backs down instantly if someone calls his bluff and holds their ground on the lawn — the same tell he's had for sixty years."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a coffee can full of confiscated baseballs on the porch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the exact same three-sentence rant to every trespasser."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His cane has a dent in it from decades of rail-thumping."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows everyone's name on the block and uses none of them kindly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches, just slightly, if anyone actually stands their ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a photo of himself at seventeen on the mantle, same sneer, same fist."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The lawn ornaments on his property all seem to face wherever he's pointing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Rile him past the porch-yelling and the cane comes up like it's forty years lighter."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["thumping the porch rail with his cane, glaring at anyone on the grass", "shouting the same three warnings in the same order, every single time"]},{"name":"The Frantic Taxi","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rlm-the-frantic-taxi","summary":"driverless checkered cab that hunts jaywalkers off the curb","flavor":"A checkered cab that idles at the crosswalk with nobody behind the wheel, engine revving with an animal impatience the moment a jaywalker sets one foot off the curb.","desc":"The checker stripe runs the length of it, immaculate, and the driver's seat is empty every single time you look. It idles at green lights and guns it at yellow, engine note rising to something almost like a snarl whenever somebody steps off the curb outside the lines. The meter in the window keeps running no matter how long it sits there. Nobody in town remembers hailing it, and nobody's ever seen it actually pick a fare up.","traits":{"note": "It only hunts creatures outside a marked crosswalk — anyone who steps back onto striped pavement is instantly, completely safe, no matter how close the chase got."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its meter reads a fare in the thousands, still climbing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The trunk pops open on its own at every near-miss, then slams shut."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Radio crackles with a dispatcher's voice giving addresses that don't exist."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Headlights flick to high beam the instant it locks onto a target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never runs a red light, only ever a yellow, right at the edge."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Circles the same four blocks obsessively, like a route it can't forget."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The back seat is visibly occupied by a shape that's never there when you look directly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push it far enough and its checker stripe starts blinking like hazard lights, engine screaming past redline."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling at a crosswalk with an empty driver's seat, engine revving with impatience", "lurching after a jaywalker the instant a foot leaves the curb, meter ticking the whole chase"]},{"name":"The Runaway Dog","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"mastiff","model":"mastiff","summary":"loose scrappy mutt, leash cracking behind it at full sprint","flavor":"A scrappy mutt off its leash and thrilled about it, tearing across yards with the leash still cracking behind it like a whip nobody's holding.","desc":"It's off the leash and it knows it, and the joy of that fact outruns any actual destination. Ears back, tongue out, it cuts across three backyards at a dead sprint with the leash whipping behind it, clipping fence posts and flowerbeds alike. It'll growl if you grab for the leash and wag if you don't. Somewhere behind it a kid is yelling a name it has zero intention of answering to right now.","traits":{"note": "It calms instantly for anyone who drops to a knee and offers a treat instead of chasing — the chase itself is the whole game to it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trailing leash has picked up a string of somebody's laundry off a line."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barks once at every mailbox it passes, like a personal grudge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Muddy paw prints track clean across three different porches."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wearing a tag with a name it clearly has decided doesn't apply right now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knocks over exactly one trash can per block, without fail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps circling back to the same yard, like it's looking for someone specific."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one lap it runs a perfect circle, over and over, before breaking pattern again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it and the leash catches on something immovable — now it's dragging whatever's on the other end."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sprinting flat-out across yards, leash cracking behind it like a live wire", "doubling back to bark once at whoever's chasing, then bolting again"]},{"name":"The Garden Snake","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"venomous-snake","model":"venomous-snake","summary":"indignant flowerbed snake, all pride, no real venom","flavor":"A flowerbed garter snake with more attitude than venom, coiled up indignant the moment a trowel comes anywhere near its patch of mulch.","desc":"It's barely the length of a garden hose and it acts like it owns the whole yard, coiling up tight and hissing the second a trowel gets within a foot of its mulch. The bite, if it comes to that, barely breaks skin. The offense it takes, on the other hand, is enormous — it will hold a grudge against a specific pair of gardening gloves for the rest of the season. Mostly it just wants everyone to know this flowerbed is spoken for.","traits":{"note": "It retreats the instant it's clearly outmatched — its whole threat display is bluff over a bite that's barely worse than a pinch."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has claimed the exact same three square feet of mulch for two summers running."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flattens its head dramatically wide for a snake half its actual size."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hisses at the garden hose specifically, every time, like it remembers something."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Basks on the same sun-warmed paver stone every afternoon without fail."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the instant a shadow bigger than a cat falls over it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has a favorite specific weed it seems to be actively protecting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed skin, found nearby, is patterned like it belongs to a much larger snake."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push it into a true corner and its hiss drops an octave, longer and lower than it should be."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["coiling tight in the mulch, hissing indignantly at anything with a trowel", "flicking its tongue at a gardening glove like it's cataloguing an old enemy"]},{"name":"The Psychic Kid","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-the-psychic-kid","summary":"striped-shirt kid, fingers to temple, quietly reads the whole block","flavor":"A striped-shirt kid who presses two fingers to her temple and just knows things — who's about to trip, who's lying, who left the stove on three blocks over — and mostly uses it to keep her friends out of trouble.","desc":"She's got a hand-me-down striped shirt and a habit of pressing two fingers to her temple right before she says something she has no normal way of knowing. She'll tell you your bike chain's about to snap, or that your mom's not really mad, just worried, or exactly which kid's about to get caught cheating on the spelling test. She doesn't show off with it — she's learned the hard way that grown-ups get weird about a kid who knows too much. Mostly she just wants someone to believe her without making it a whole thing.","traits":{"note": "She starts at Wary and only opens up once someone treats a true prediction like a fact instead of a trick — a kept secret or a believed warning shifts her to Friendly and she'll share what she sees; if a fight ever finds her she simply scatters into the nearest crowd of adults, never harmed on-page, the grown-ups finally noticing exactly enough to end it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a notebook of predictions, dated, so she can prove herself later."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows which teacher is about to call on her before the hand goes up."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warned a friend off a bike ramp minutes before the ramp collapsed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to tell fortunes for money — says it feels wrong to charge for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gets a specific headache right before bad news, and has learned to hide the wince."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Knows a secret about every kid on the block and has told exactly none of them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a half-second her eyes go the color of the sky reflected on nothing at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Concentrates hard enough and she can feel, faintly, every kid on the block's day at once — she never holds that focus long, it's too much to carry."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pressing two fingers to her temple, eyes unfocused for a beat before she speaks", "quietly steering a friend away from trouble she saw coming three streets early"]},{"name":"Starman Analog","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"rlm-starman-analog","summary":"chrome-skinned visitor, teleport static, one flashy psychic trick","flavor":"A visitor in a jumpsuit that's almost exactly right down to the last detail, chrome-skinned under sodium streetlight, who teleports in a blip of television static and knows exactly one show-stopping psychic trick.","desc":"He steps out of a blip of television static at the exact second the streetlights flicker, wearing a jumpsuit that's almost, but not quite, cut like the ones on the sitcoms — the collar's wrong, the color's a half-shade off. His skin catches the sodium light like true chrome, and he grins with too many teeth arranged in the right number. He's got exactly one trick, and it's a good one: he'll press two fingers to your forehead and hand you somebody else's memory, gift-wrapped and warm. He always seems delighted that suburbia is real, like he wasn't sure until just now.","traits":{"note": "His teleport-static trick only reaches as far as visible line-of-sight streetlight to streetlight — cut the lights on the block and he's grounded until the grid comes back."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His jumpsuit zipper is on the wrong side, and he's never noticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts human teeth out loud, fascinated, whenever someone smiles at him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Greets every mailbox like it might be sentient, just in case."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a pocketful of bottle caps he's convinced are currency here."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His static-teleport leaves a faint smell of ozone and grape soda."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The memory he hands over is always someone else's, never one he seems to have of his own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one flicker between streetlights, his 'almost right' jumpsuit is perfectly, unnervingly right."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him hard enough and the static around him spreads to every screen on the block at once, TVs and phones alike, all showing the same blank hiss."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["stepping out of a burst of television static as the streetlights flicker", "pressing two fingers to a stranger's forehead, offering a stolen memory like a party favor"]},{"name":"Starman Elite","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"rlm-starman-elite","summary":"gold-chromed psychic scout, taller than its predecessors","flavor":"Taller than the ones that came before, chrome-gold and humming, its eyes flash and the whole street tastes like static for a second.","desc":"It stands a head taller than the others that have been sighted around the water tower, plated in a gold chrome that never quite looks wet or dry. When it turns to face you its eyes flare white-gold and the air goes thin, like a held breath before a thunderclap. It doesn't run. It doesn't need to — the flash comes first and the running is yours.","traits":{"note": "Its psychic flash is a telegraphed alpha-strike opener, not a surprise round — the eye-flare gives a beat's warning before it fires."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chrome plating is scuffed along one shoulder where it clipped a mailbox."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums a rising three-note tone before every flash, always the same three notes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves scorched grass in a perfect ring wherever it lands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gloved hand twitches toward its belt before it remembers it isn't wearing one."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands motionless at the tree line for whole minutes, watching a single porch light."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Speaks one clipped phrase in a language that almost, almost resolves into English."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For half a second its gold plating looks like a rank insignia from a war that hasn't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its flash overloads and arcs to every porch light on the block at once, popping bulbs in a wave down the street."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing rigid at the tree line, gold plating catching the streetlight, watching one house", "flashing eyes white-gold in a warning beat before it strikes"]},{"name":"Mr. Saturn Analog Villager","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"sprite","model":"rlm-mr-saturn-analog-villager","summary":"round kind villager, boings away from any real fight","flavor":"A round, kind, backwards-talking little thing that would rather boing away than fight, syntax scrambled like a word said one hop too many times.","desc":"It's round and soft-edged and impossibly polite, with a voice that comes out backwards-hop-scrambled, like \"Boing! Fight, not want I do!\" It carries a stick twice its height and waves it more in greeting than threat. Corner it and it apologizes on its way out the window. It would honestly rather you two just talked this out.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable and social-first: it starts Wary at worst and moves to Friendly fast with any gentle, patient approach — raised voices or a drawn weapon knock it straight back down, per the social-attitude system; it will not fight if any exit exists."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a stick nearly twice its own height, mostly for balance."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Greets everyone the same way: \"Hello, is you! Boing!\""}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a little sack of round stones it calls its \"treasure friends.\""}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bounces in place when nervous, faster and faster."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to itself in the wrong tense, always a beat behind what it just did."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Knows a shortcut through the culvert that skips two blocks of trouble entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its village, wherever it is, seems to be one house over from everyone's, all at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startle it badly and it boings clean through a wall, leaving a Mr.-Saturn-shaped hole and nothing else."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["bouncing gently across a lawn, stick raised in greeting not threat", "apologizing while backing toward the nearest fence gap"]},{"name":"Possessed Lawn Flamingo Flock","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"rlm-possessed-lawn-flamingo-flock","summary":"five plastic flamingos, heads twisted wrong, marching","flavor":"Five plastic flamingos advancing across the grass in perfect unbroken lockstep, every head rotated a few degrees past where a neck should turn.","desc":"They stand where they always stood, pink and hollow and cheap, until the wind is wrong and all five turn to face you at once. Their heads sit rotated further than a neck joint should allow, wire legs ticking against the lawn in perfect synchronized little steps. They don't blink because they can't, and somehow that's the worst part.","traits":{"note": "They act as one mind across all five bodies — damaging one visibly staggers the rest."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One has a cracked bill, whistling faintly whenever it turns."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They arrange themselves in a perfect V the second they start moving."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded pink paint has gone the color of old bubblegum."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their wire legs leave five identical little holes punched in a row."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They freeze mid-step the instant a porch light clicks on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They herd toward the same flowerbed every time, guarding something buried there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "All five heads turn to track a sixth flamingo that isn't there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroy the lead bird and the other four collapse flat, plastic, and inert all at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing rigid on a lawn until the wind turns wrong, then all five heads swivel at once", "ticking forward in unbroken lockstep, wire legs punching neat holes in the grass"]},{"name":"Runaway RC-Car Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"rlm-runaway-rc-car-swarm","summary":"dozen toy cars swarming ankles like piranha","flavor":"A dozen toy cars that broke their leashes days ago, swarming ankles like a piranha school with headlights for teeth.","desc":"They came from a dozen different birthdays and Christmases, and now they move as one pack, engines whining in a chorus that never quite synchronizes. Little plastic bumpers snap open and shut like jaws, headlights flaring bright with every strike. They swarm low, fast, and numerous, going for ankles and shins before anyone even registers the sound as a threat.","traits":{"note": "Treat as a swarm: it can occupy another creature's space and its attacks scale down sharply once its numbers thin."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One trails a shredded antenna that whips as it turns."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half of them still have factory decals: flames, lightning bolts, a cartoon shark."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their combined engine whine is loud enough to wake a whole cul-de-sac."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They scatter and regroup at a stop sign like it means something to them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One car is clearly the fastest and always strikes first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They herd toward any open garage door, drawn to the smell of gasoline and oil."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their remote frequencies still respond — someone's old controller, tried at the right moment, might make one obey."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, they pile themselves into a single shrieking heap of gnashing bumpers before scattering wide."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["swarming low across a driveway, bumpers snapping like teeth", "scattering and regrouping at the curb, engines whining out of sync"]},{"name":"The Door-to-Door Salesman","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"incubus","model":"rlm-door-to-door-salesman","summary":"too-wide grin, carries his own doorframe, will not leave","flavor":"A grin too wide for the face under it, a foot wedged in a door frame he carries from house to house, and a pitch he will not stop delivering.","desc":"He rings the bell holding a doorframe under one arm like a briefcase, and the instant anyone answers he sets it against the frame that's already there and wedges his foot in both at once. His grin doesn't move even while he talks, teeth a little too even, a little too many. He has a pitch for every objection you can raise, and he has never once, in living memory, taken no for an answer.","traits":{"note": "Social-first: he starts Wary and will not turn hostile unless physically forced out — firmly and repeatedly refusing the pitch (no violence needed) drops him to Unfriendly and he withdraws his foot and frame rather than escalate, per the social-attitude system."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sample case is full of products that don't quite exist in any store."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows your name before you've said it, reads it off a clipboard that's blank."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His shoes are worn through at the toe from wedging doors for longer than makes sense."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He has a testimonial from a neighbor who moved away years ago and never came back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a \"limited time\" deal that he's clearly offered at every house on the street."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His pitch changes mid-sentence to match exactly what you're afraid of losing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He never blinks during the pitch, not once, and seems mildly hurt when you notice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He signs your silence as a yes on a contract that was never shown to you, and the door frame under his arm gains one more knob."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing a doorbell with his own frame tucked under one arm, grin already fixed in place", "wedging a foot into the gap the instant the door cracks, pitch already rolling"]},{"name":"The Van at 1:15 AM","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"rlm-the-van-at-115-am","summary":"panel van circling with headlights off, door sliding open","flavor":"A windowless panel van that circles the mall parking lot on no schedule anyone can explain, headlights dark, side door sliding open onto nothing that should be inside.","desc":"It has no plates, no dealer sticker, no reason to still be running — and yet it loops the empty mall lot at exactly 1:15, every time, headlights off, engine a low idle that never seems to actually move air. The side door slides open on its own about halfway through the third loop, and whatever's inside doesn't show itself so much as invite you to look. Everyone in town has a story about someone who looked.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves the lot boundary and never chases past the curb line — the danger is entirely in whoever accepts the open door."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tires never actually seem to touch the asphalt, just barely above it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The radio inside plays a station that signed off decades ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its odometer, visible through the windshield, reads all zeroes no matter how far it drives."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded magnetic sign on the door advertises a business that never existed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always circles counter-clockwise, never once the other way."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The door only opens for someone standing alone — groups get nothing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It knows the exact number of loops left before dawn and paces itself to that clock."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force it to a stop and every parked car in the lot turns its headlights on at once, engines starting in sequence."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling the empty mall lot on a fixed 1:15 loop, headlights dark", "sliding its side door open halfway through the third pass, waiting for someone alone"]},{"name":"The Garage Experiment","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"rlm-the-garage-experiment","summary":"inventor's appliance gone sapient, dragging its own cord","flavor":"A blender, a lamp, three extension cords, and somebody's dad's ambition, fused into something that wants very badly to be helpful and doesn't know its own strength.","desc":"It used to be a workbench's worth of spare parts — a blender base, a desk lamp for an eye, a rotary mixer for a fist — until whatever the garage's owner was building woke up somewhere in the wiring. It drags a tangle of extension cord behind it like a tail, still plugged into an outlet three rooms back, and it wants, more than anything, to finish the chore it thinks it was built for. It just isn't sure anymore what that chore was, or how hard it's supposed to squeeze.","traits":{"note": "Its extension cord is a literal leash — yanking or cutting it shuts the thing down cold instead of fighting it to a standstill."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lamp-eye flickers on a dimmer switch someone wired in backwards."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the tune of a half-finished invention jingle, over and over."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sawdust and old grease cake its joints from years on that workbench."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tries to fold laundry that isn't there, motions perfect, nothing in its hands."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A safety switch dangles from its chest, wired to nothing anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It recognizes tools by name and hands them over if asked politely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its lamp-eye focuses like it recognizes the inventor's face in yours."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overloaded, it starts trying to \"finish\" its last chore on whoever's nearest, gentleness gone entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["dragging a tangle of extension cord behind it, still plugged in three rooms back", "reaching for a chore that isn't there, motions careful, strength not"]},{"name":"The Visitor in the Shed","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"pixie","model":"rlm-the-visitor-in-the-shed","summary":"small wrinkled being hiding among the garden tools","flavor":"Small, wrinkled, finger-light on its feet, tucked among the rakes and paint cans, hoping very hard not to be found before it's ready to be.","desc":"It's found a good spot behind the paint cans, knees pulled up, fingers long and thin as garden stakes, watching the gap under the door for feet. It isn't from here — not from this yard, not from this world's usual traffic — and it knows it, which is exactly why it's hiding instead of introducing itself. Given a reason to trust the shed's owner, it might finally come out from behind the cans.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable, cameo-cast lane: it starts Wary/hiding and needs a slow, quiet approach to reach Friendly — sudden movement or a raised voice sends it right back behind the cans, per the social-attitude system."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rearranged the paint cans into a small, careful wall between itself and the door."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its fingers are exactly the length and thickness of the rake handles nearby, and it's noticed the resemblance too."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been eating the birdseed meant for the feeder, apologetically, a little at a time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches at the sound of the garage door opener two houses down."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's left small neat piles of found objects — bottle caps, a marble, a screw — like tribute or rent."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It knows something about the yard's history nobody currently living does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flinches every time it hears a specific neighbor's name, and won't say why."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past hiding, it calls softly toward the fence line, and something answers from the next yard over."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["crouching behind the paint cans, long fingers curled tight, watching the gap under the door", "freezing at every footstep outside, ready to fold itself smaller"]},{"name":"The Little Fixers","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"homunculus","model":"rlm-the-little-fixers","summary":"palm-sized helpers, mend one broken thing a night","flavor":"Palm-sized machine helpers nested in the eave, quietly mending one broken thing a night and expecting nothing for it but to be left alone.","desc":"They live somewhere up in the eave, three or four of them, no bigger than a fist, all soldered joints and salvaged gears gone a little rusty at the seams. Every night exactly one broken thing in the house gets quietly fixed — a squeaking hinge, a flickering bulb, a wobbling table leg — and every morning the family finds it done and never quite sees who did it. They only ask, in return, to be left the eave and never looked at directly.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable: they start Wary of direct attention and rise to Friendly through repeated small kindnesses (leaving out solder, oil, spare parts) rather than any direct approach, per the social-attitude system — being stared at or cornered drops them straight to Hostile-avoidant and they flee the house."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves behind a single perfect drop of solder as its only signature."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers hinges and clocks; anything with a rhythm to it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gears are scavenged from three different decades of hardware."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works only between 2 and 4 AM, never earlier, never later."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves oil-smudge fingerprints far too small to be a child's."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It fixes only one thing a night, no matter how much needs doing — a rule it will not break."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sometimes the thing it fixes wasn't broken until the day before it was mended."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Caught in direct light, it locks rigid mid-repair and has to be gently, patiently coaxed back to motion."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working a tiny screwdriver into a squeaking hinge by moonlight, unseen", "freezing rigid the instant a light flicks on nearby"]},{"name":"The Prom-Night Thing","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"rlm-the-prom-night-thing","summary":"the real thing behind the prom rumor, corsage still pinned","flavor":"The actual shape behind the rumor every senior class retells at the punch bowl, corsage still pinned crooked to whatever it is now.","desc":"Every graduating class tells the story a little differently — a date that never came home, a photo that got cropped out of the yearbook, a slow dance that never ended — but the thing under the gymnasium bleachers is the same every year, a corsage wilted and crooked and still pinned to whatever it's wearing now. It moves like it's still waiting for a song to start. It only ever seems to notice you if you're dressed for the occasion.","traits":{"note": "Its attention keys off formalwear — anyone dressed for a dance draws its focus first, and it disengages from anyone who leaves the gym entirely rather than pursuing into the halls."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The corsage on its chest is a species of flower that hasn't grown here in decades."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sways in three-quarter time whenever any music plays nearby, even a car radio."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Streamers and old balloons still cling to it, decades out of fashion."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps circling back to the same spot on the gym floor, like a mark for a photo that never got taken."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its dance shoes are worn through at the heel from years of the same steps."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It reaches to take a hand for a dance before it reaches to hurt — accepting or refusing both matter."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gym clock behind it always reads 11:58, no matter how long the encounter runs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push it to the stroke of midnight on its clock and every string of gym lights fails at once, plunging the room into the dark it's always danced in."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["swaying in three-quarter time under the bleachers, corsage crooked on its chest", "turning to track anyone dressed for the dance, ignoring everyone else in the room"]},{"name":"The Traveling Five — Bandleader","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"performer-maestro","summary":"pencil-mustache frontman, silver tongue, deep in the red","flavor":"A pencil-mustached frontman perpetually one gig away from square with every club owner between here and the county line, still selling the dream in a sequined jacket two sizes too bright.","desc":"His jacket catches every porch light on the block, sequins throwing sparks he can't afford. He counts the house before he counts the band, works the crowd like collateral, and never once mentions the bus payment three towns overdue. Cross him and he still calls you \"pal\" — the smile is real, the debt is realer, and the show, somehow, always goes on.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral toward anyone who looks like a paying gig or a soft touch; a loan, a good word to a promoter, or fronting the band's bus fare shifts him to Friendly and he vouches for the party at every stop down the line."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a ledger of every debt he owes tucked in his breast pocket, updated daily, never paid down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs autographs for people who never asked for one, on napkins, on receipts, on skin."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His mustache is drawn on with a grease pencil most nights — the real one never grew in even."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Introduces every song as the band's \"biggest hit,\" including the ones they wrote yesterday."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a photo of a bigger marquee in his wallet, a gig that never happened."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Talks a furious club owner down mid-sentence with nothing but tone and eye contact."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His patter never repeats, verbatim, across three different towns the party's heard him work."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him with the bill and he'll sell the party the bus itself, on payments, smiling the whole time."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["working the crowd before the first note plays, counting the house instead of the band", "talking a red-faced club owner back from the edge with nothing but charm and a promise"]},{"name":"The Traveling Five — Horn Section","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"performer","summary":"trumpet-and-sax brothers, one riff between them","flavor":"Two brothers, trumpet and sax, who finish each other's riffs and each other's sentences, splitting every tip down the middle without counting.","desc":"They lean into the same eight bars from opposite ends of the stage, trumpet answering sax like they're arguing in a language only they speak. Offstage they split every tip evenly without looking, still finishing each other's sentences from a childhood spent in the same cramped tour van. Ask either one a question and the other answers first.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral; buying both brothers a meal or asking after their old hometown act shifts them to Friendly together — they move as one unit, never separately."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The trumpet brother's horn is dented from a fall off a stage in a town they won't name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The sax brother chews the same brand of gum through every set, never offers it around."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They warm up with the same scale every night, a habit from a teacher neither remembers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One always steps half a beat ahead of the other, and neither seems to notice anymore."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They keep a shared coin purse, one brother's pocket, split later by memory not count."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They trade an entire conversation in riffs mid-song, and the bandleader lets them run long."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Ask them apart and they give the exact same answer, word for word, without comparing notes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten one brother and the other's horn turns into the loudest, angriest sound either has ever made."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["trading riffs across the stage like a running argument neither wants to lose", "splitting a tip jar by feel, without ever looking down to count it"]},{"name":"The Traveling Five — Drummer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"performer","summary":"biggest grin in the band, unshakeable time","flavor":"A grin wider than the kit he sits behind, keeping time through sets that run long and crowds that run hostile with the same easy rhythm.","desc":"He sits behind more drum than any one man needs, grinning through a set list nobody bothered to write down. His time never slips, not through a shouted heckle, not through a fistfight breaking out by the punch bowl, not through the bandleader forgetting the next song entirely. He just keeps the beat and keeps grinning, like the whole night's a joke only he's in on.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral; complimenting his kit or covering his bar tab shifts him to Friendly — he's the easiest of the Five to win over and will vouch loudly for anyone who does."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His kit is held together with duct tape and stubbornness, cymbals chipped at the edges."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts every song in under his breath, lips moving, grin never dropping."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sweats through his shirt every set and never once slows down for it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a spare stick tucked behind each ear, just in case, always has."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs at his own drum fills, delighted every single time like it's new."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Never once breaks time, not for a heckler, not for a fight breaking out front row."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims he can hear the next song coming before the bandleader calls it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him past patience and that grin turns into a solo that drowns out every other sound in the room."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["keeping unbroken time through a set that's running twenty minutes long", "grinning through a shouted heckle without missing a single beat"]},{"name":"The Traveling Five — Keys Man","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"performer","summary":"shoulder-strapped keys, blur-fast fingers","flavor":"A shoulder-strapped keyboard slung like a rifle, fingers moving too fast to watch, always the last one paid and the first one to forgive it.","desc":"He wears the keyboard on a strap like it's part of him, fingers running scales too fast to track even standing still. He's always last in line when the bandleader hands out what's left of the take, and he never says a word about it — just straps the keys back on and starts the next number early, like the money never mattered in the first place.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral; making a point of paying him fairly or first shifts him to Friendly — he notices fairness fast, having so rarely gotten it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His keyboard strap is a repurposed guitar strap, mismatched buckle, held with a safety pin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs the same warm-up scale before every set, eyes closed, lips moving silently."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never complains when he's paid last, just nods and starts packing up the gear."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a battered fake book of chord charts nobody else in the band can read."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His fingers keep moving on an invisible keyboard even between sets, out of habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Covers for a bandleader who forgets a bridge, filling the gap so smooth nobody in the crowd notices."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Plays a riff nobody taught him and swears he's heard it somewhere before, in a dream maybe."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him too far past patience and his fingers blur into a solo that seems to bend the whole room's mood."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["running scales too fast to track, fingers a blur on the shoulder-slung keys", "packing up gear quietly after being paid last again, no complaint"]},{"name":"The Traveling Five — the Manager","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"con","summary":"briefcase of IOUs, always mid-plead","flavor":"Briefcase stuffed with IOUs, mid-plead at every venue door, the one member of the Five who actually knows how much trouble they're all in.","desc":"He's already talking before the door's fully open, briefcase clutched like a shield, papers spilling out the sides. Every venue in three counties has a story about him — a bounced check, a promise, a handshake that meant less than it should have. He's the only one of the Five who actually does the math on how deep they're in, and it never stops him from booking the next gig anyway.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Unfriendly toward anyone who looks like a bill collector, Neutral otherwise; settling one of the band's outstanding debts on his behalf shifts him to Friendly and he'll book the party a favor in return."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His briefcase latch is broken, held shut with a length of twine wound twice."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries three different names on three different business cards, all of them his."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks in numbers that never quite add up, fast enough nobody stops to check."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running tally of every promise he's made, in a hand too cramped for anyone else to read."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at the sound of a car pulling up outside, every single time, out of habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Talks a landlord down from eviction with nothing but paperwork and pure nerve."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Produces a receipt for a debt from a town the party's never mentioned to him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with no way out, he'll sign the party's name to a debt that isn't theirs without blinking."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pleading his case at a venue door before it's even fully open", "tallying debts in a battered notebook nobody else is allowed to read"]},{"name":"Greaser Gang — the Frank","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"pompadoured leader, finger-snap start, comb like a blade","flavor":"Pompadour immaculate under any weather, a finger-snap that starts every fight and a comb worked like a switchblade between his knuckles.","desc":"His pompadour hasn't moved in a decade of fistfights and greasy diner air, held up by something more stubborn than pomade. He snaps his fingers once before every confrontation, a countdown the whole gang's learned to move on, and works a black comb between two knuckles the way other men work a knife. Everyone on the block knows his name is Frank, and everyone calls him the Frank instead, like there's only ever been one.","traits":{"note": "Runs the Twins and the Backline as a synchronized unit; drop the Frank and their choreography breaks a beat behind, giving anyone still standing a clean opening."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snaps his fingers twice instead of once when he's genuinely rattled, though he'd never admit it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second comb in his boot for the one time a year the first one snaps."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His leather jacket is patched at both elbows, mended by someone who clearly cares about him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never throws the first punch — waits for someone else to, then finishes it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistles the same three notes before every rumble, a signal the whole gang answers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calls off a fight the instant a kid wanders into the lot, no exceptions, ever."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims to remember every rumble the gang's ever had, town by town, word for word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him bad enough and he calls in a favor from a gang three towns over nobody knew he had."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["snapping his fingers once before trouble starts, a signal the whole gang moves on", "working a black comb between two knuckles like it's got an edge"]},{"name":"Greaser Gang — the Twins","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"matched toughs, one synchronized step","flavor":"Two matched toughs who step, swing, and spit in perfect synchronized time, like the same tough guy practiced twice.","desc":"They move like a single person split down the middle, boots landing the same beat, jackets zipped to the same notch. One throws a punch a half-second before the other, close enough nobody's ever caught the gap. Ask which one is older and they'll both say the same name at the same time, then laugh the exact same laugh.","traits":{"note": "Fight them as a matched pair; if one drops, the other's rhythm breaks for a round before it catches up — a clean tell for anyone paying attention."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Both wear the same jacket, same wear pattern, down to the same torn cuff."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They finish each other's insults, word for word, without missing a beat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Comb their hair in the same motion, same number of strokes, every single time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One's a half-step left-handed, the other right, so their punches never collide."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spit on the ground in unison before any real trouble starts."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Move like a single fighter split in two, boots landing the exact same beat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Neither remembers which one of them is actually older, and it doesn't seem to bother either."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Separate them and each one fights noticeably worse, like half a person trying to finish a whole fight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["stepping and swinging in perfect unsettling unison, boots landing the same beat", "spitting on the ground together the instant real trouble starts"]},{"name":"Greaser Gang — the Backline","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"choreographed rear guard, one spinning, one clapping time","flavor":"Two more toughs holding the rear of the rumble in practiced choreography, one spinning a chain, one clapping the beat that keeps the whole gang in step.","desc":"They hang back at the edge of any rumble, one spinning a length of bike chain in a slow showy arc, the other clapping a steady beat like he's counting off a dance number instead of a fight. It looks almost rehearsed because it is — the Frank drilled this gang like a chorus line long before he drilled them like a crew. Step wrong into their rhythm and the clapping stops, which is somehow worse than the chain.","traits":{"note": "They hold position and rhythm rather than charge; break their clapping cadence (a shout, a thrown object) and their choreography stumbles for a round."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chain-spinner's chain is rust-spotted, salvaged off an old bicycle nobody misses."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The clapper keeps perfect time even when the rumble's gone quiet, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Both wear the same cuffed jeans, hemmed by the same hand back home."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They trade positions mid-fight without a word, like it was blocked out in rehearsal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chain-spinner never actually lands a hit with it — the spin alone does the scaring."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Their choreography holds even against three opponents at once, never breaking formation."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The clapping beat matches, note for note, a song the Traveling Five played across town that same night."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break the clapper's rhythm hard enough and the chain-spinner swings for real, aiming to actually connect."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["spinning a length of bike chain in a slow, showy arc at the rumble's edge", "clapping out a steady beat that keeps the whole gang moving in step"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — Door Proselytizer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"beaming convert, pamphlets fanned, freshly pink","flavor":"A beaming convert on the doorstep with pamphlets fanned like a poker hand, every stitch of clothing on her freshly, alarmingly pink.","desc":"She rings the bell twice, waits with her hands folded, and smiles like she's already won before you've opened the door. The pamphlets fan out from her hand in a practiced flourish, every one printed in a pink that doesn't quite match the last one she handed you. Her cardigan was gray a week ago; ask her about it and she'll just smile wider and tell you it grew into the right color on its own.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral; she treats every conversation as a recruitment pitch — engaging warmly or accepting a pamphlet shifts her to Friendly, while any dismissal of the Pink Cult's message drops her to Unfriendly fast."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a clipboard of signatures, every single one signed in the same pink ink."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her shoes were white this morning, she'll insist, gesturing at them now unmistakably pink."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same three phrases about \"the color coming home\" no matter what you actually ask."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a spare pamphlet tucked behind her ear like a pencil, always ready to hand one over."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Compliments your house, your lawn, your car — anything not yet pink — with real, unsettling warmth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Never once raises her voice, even when three neighbors in a row slam the door on her."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her pamphlets are blank until you actually read them, and the words rearrange themselves to fit whoever's looking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Refuse her at your own door and by morning your porch light has gone the same unmistakable pink."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing the doorbell twice and waiting with hands folded, smiling like she's already won", "fanning pamphlets out in a practiced flourish the moment the door opens"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — the Painter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"coveralls and roller, painting the town pink fence by fence","flavor":"Coveralls speckled top to bottom, a roller in one hand and a bucket in the other, turning the town pink one fence at a time and humming while he does it.","desc":"He works the fence line with the unhurried patience of a man who's never once been told to stop, roller dripping the same shade onto pavement, mailbox, dog house, whatever's in reach. His coveralls were white once, going by the collar, but every other inch of him is speckled the same cheerful pink as the paint. He hums the whole time, tuneless and content, and never seems to run low on paint no matter how much fence there is left.","traits":{"note": "Attitude starts Neutral; complimenting the color or offering to help paint shifts him to Friendly — he genuinely believes he's doing the neighborhood a favor and lights up at anyone who agrees."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His paint bucket never seems to run dry no matter how much fence line he covers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums the same three-note tune, over and over, never quite landing on a full melody."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Paints in careful, even strokes, taking real pride in the coverage even on a chain-link fence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His boots leave pink prints for a full block behind him, fading slowly with each step."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops to wave cheerfully at anyone watching, roller still dripping, completely unbothered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Paints over a stop sign without hesitation, humming the whole time, like it never occurred to him not to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pink he uses is a slightly different shade on every fence, though he swears it's the same can."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Try to stop him and the paint on his coveralls starts creeping onto whatever's grabbing him."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rolling paint down a fence line in slow, careful strokes, humming a tuneless little song", "waving cheerfully at anyone watching, roller still dripping pink"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — Choir Mother","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"beaming den-mother humming an unheard hymn door to door","flavor":"A round, smiling matron in a cardigan the color of bubblegum, humming a hymn nobody else can hear while the neighbors' hedges creep pastel behind her back.","desc":"She keeps a plate of lemon bars warm on every porch she visits and hums four bars of a hymn that has no words yet, just a tune that gets under your ribs if you listen twice. The houses she's visited already have a faint blush at the gutters, like they caught some sun they shouldn't have. She never raises her voice — she doesn't have to, not with half the block already humming back. Ask her what the song is for and she just smiles wider and offers you a bar.","traits":{"note": "Runs on the neighborhood's ordinary social-attitude ladder: sharing a verse of her hymn, praising the block, or a genuine kindness nudges her toward Friendly; refusing the lemon bars or pointing out the pink at the gutter line drops her hard toward Hostile."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her cardigan buttons are already a shade pinker than the rest of it, and she hasn't noticed or doesn't mind."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She keeps a recipe box of hymn verses on index cards, alphabetized by which house needs them next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She waters her lawn in perfect rhythm with her humming, like the hose is keeping time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her smile doesn't move when she's angry — just the hum drops half a step lower."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She remembers everyone's name, allergies, and porch-light schedule down the block."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's started leaving lemon bars on porches that don't answer the door anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hum along with her for more than a few bars and the tune finishes itself in your own head, uninvited."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's not leading the hymn anymore so much as conducting it, one directed hand cueing whole houses to bloom pink on command."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["going door to door with a plate of lemon bars, humming four unfinished bars of a hymn", "watering her lawn in the same slow rhythm as the tune under her breath"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — Converted Neighbor","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"half-converted neighbor waving hello, half his clothes gone pink","flavor":"A familiar dad from three doors down, half his cardigan and undershirt gone the same bubblegum pink as the hedges, still waving hello like nothing's different.","desc":"He's still got the same lawnmower, the same wave, the same 'how about this weather' — it's just that his left sleeve and half his collar have gone a candy-bright pink that doesn't wash out. He'll offer to help you carry your groceries in. He'll mean it, mostly. The pink hasn't reached his face yet, and something in his eyes is still fighting to stay his.","traits":{"note": "The pink half of him is losing; a familiar kindness or a name he remembers can pull him back a step, but pressing it too hard sends the color climbing faster."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still mows his lawn in the same crooked diagonal pattern he's used for a decade."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One pink hand keeps a firm, friendly grip a half-second too long."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice cracks pink-sweet on certain words, like a radio losing the signal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's still got his HOA newsletter tucked under one very normal arm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pink stops in a hard line right at his collarbone, like a shirt he can't take off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He apologizes for the pink, genuinely, every single time before he swings."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a second, both his eyes go the same bubblegum shade, then just as fast go back to normal."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Land the hit that should finish him and the pink half simply wins outright, all at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["waving hello from across the lawn, one pink-collared arm raised", "mowing the same crooked diagonal stripe he's mowed for years"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — the Holdout","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"grim homeowner on the porch, guarding the last unpainted house","flavor":"A grim, flannel-shirted homeowner on his porch with a shotgun of rock salt, guarding the one house on the block that hasn't gone pink.","desc":"He hasn't slept in his own bed in a week, camped out in a lawn chair on the porch with a thermos of coffee and a shotgun loaded with rock salt he swears works on 'whatever the hell that pink is.' His house is the only one on the street still the dull, honest beige it's always been. He's not friendly, exactly, but he's not one of them either, and right now that's worth something.","traits":{"note": "He starts wary, not hostile — proving you're not converted (naming the hymn, showing normal-colored skin) can move him to Friendly and recruit him as an ally holding the line; pushing past him without asking drops him fast."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a hand-drawn map of the block, X-ing out each house as it turns pink."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to eat anything a neighbor brings over, even in the original wrapper."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His porch light is the only one on the street burning a normal, un-pink white."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rigged his sprinklers to soak anyone who steps on his lawn without asking first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a battery radio tuned to static, insisting it 'sounds different' near converted houses."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's written his own name on his arm in marker, 'just in case,' and checks it every hour."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shotgun salt leaves scorch marks the wrong color entirely — a faint, ordinary grey."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him past his porch rail and he stops asking questions first, salt or no salt."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting a lawn-chair watch on his own porch with a thermos and a salt-loaded shotgun", "crossing houses off a hand-drawn block map as each one turns pink"]},{"name":"The Scissor-Handed Gardener","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"rlm-scissor-handed-gardener","summary":"gentle blade-fingered outcast the town wrongly calls a monster","flavor":"Long blade-fingered hands that only ever trim hedges into gentle, impossible shapes; the whole town's decided he's the monster, and he's the only one who isn't.","desc":"His hands end in long, silvery shears grown straight from the bone, and every hedge he's ever touched comes out kinder than it went in — a dinosaur here, a sleeping dog there, roses shaped like open hands. The whole town crossed the street from him years ago and never crossed back, and he's stopped trying to explain that he's never once used those hands to hurt anyone. He works at night so nobody has to be afraid in daylight. Winning him over, not fighting him, is how this ends.","traits":{"note": "He reads as Wary by default from years of being run off — showing him a hedge he can safely tend, standing between him and a torch-mob, or simply not flinching moves him toward Friendly and recruits him as an ally; treating him like the monster the town says he is locks him at Hostile fast, and that's the story's loss, not his."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trims a hedge into the shape of the dog that used to live at that house, unasked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his blade-hands folded and still in front of children, out of old habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works exclusively between midnight and dawn so no one has to see him do it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His shears are precise enough to snip a single leaf and leave the branch untouched."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears long sleeves even in summer, out of consideration more than shame."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's never once raised those hands against a person, not even the ones who've hurt him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment his shears move faster than sight, shaping a whole topiary in one pass."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past his limit, every hedge he's ever shaped in town moves to stand with him at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["shaping a hedge into something gentle and impossible under cover of night", "flinching back a full step whenever a porch light snaps on nearby"]},{"name":"The Gardener's Topiary","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Plant","size":"Large","frame":"awakened-tree","model":"awakened-tree","summary":"animate hedge dinosaur, impossibly well-trimmed and alive","flavor":"A hedge trimmed into a dinosaur so good it moved on its own, lumbering across lawns on leaf-and-branch legs like the neatest, greenest thing you've ever been afraid of.","desc":"Every leaf is clipped to the same perfect half-inch, every branch bent into a haunch or a long, curious neck, and none of it should move — except it does, ambling across three lawns at a time on legs made of root and hedge-wire. It's not aggressive so much as curious, the way a big dog is curious, nosing at mailboxes and swing sets with a snout made of boxwood. Somewhere under all that careful trimming is a temper it hasn't needed yet.","traits":{"note": "It's the gardener's work and answers to him alone — separated from him for long, it grows restless and territorial over 'its' stretch of lawn."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of perfectly even hedge-clippings everywhere it walks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Noses at parked cars and swing sets with real, doglike curiosity."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Freezes mid-stride and holds a topiary pose if it thinks it's being watched."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its leaves stay a uniform, unnatural green no matter the season."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nudges fallen branches back onto its own body like a self-repair instinct."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only ever grazes lawns the gardener himself once tended, never a stranger's yard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its boxwood eye-sockets seem to actually track you, thinking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut it down and every clipping roots on the spot, a dozen small hedges standing up where it fell."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["lumbering across three lawns at a time, nosing mailboxes with a boxwood snout", "freezing mid-stride into a perfect topiary pose whenever it's watched"]},{"name":"Torch-and-Casserole Mob","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"torch-and-casserole mob marching in loose, furious formation","flavor":"A dozen neighbors marching in loose formation with flashlights, garden tools, and one very hot casserole dish held up like a weapon — the whole street's fear, finally given feet.","desc":"They came from six different houses in six different bathrobes, but they're marching now like one animal, flashlight beams crossing and uncrossing over the same patch of lawn. Somebody brought a casserole dish, still hot, held two-handed like a shield. Nobody organized this. Nobody had to — it's the sound of every whispered 'somebody should do something' finally agreeing on a direction and a time.","traits":{"note": "Treat as one collective entity acting in unison; break its confidence — expose that the target isn't what they feared, or out-argue its loudest voice — and the whole mob can lose heart and scatter at once."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half of them are still in bathrobes and one slipper, having not stopped to dress."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The casserole dish gets passed hand to hand like a torch nobody wants to hold too long."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone keeps trying to take attendance, out of pure suburban habit, mid-march."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their flashlight beams cross the same ten feet of lawn over and over, never quite agreeing where to look."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dog on a leash drags one marcher a full step behind the rest, barking at nothing they can see."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've already decided who's guilty before anyone's said a word — the mob showed up with a verdict."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment every flashlight in the crowd swings to point the same direction at once, unprompted."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push them past their fear and the whole street empties out to join, porch lights snapping on down the block."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["marching in loose formation with flashlights and garden tools, one hot casserole held high", "sweeping crossed flashlight beams over the same stretch of lawn, hunting for a target"]},{"name":"Ship Crew Kid — the Pilot","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"helmet-and-goggles kid piloting the backyard ship with total conviction","flavor":"A kid in a bike helmet and welding goggles, white-knuckling a joystick ripped from a lawn tractor, absolutely convinced this thing flies.","desc":"Skinned knees, a bike helmet two sizes too big, welding goggles fogged from breathing too hard — and both hands locked on a lawn-tractor joystick like it's the only thing keeping the whole rickety contraption in the air. It might not even be off the ground. It doesn't matter. This kid has never once doubted it, and somehow that's the scariest and best thing about the whole crew.","traits":{"note": "Defeat-out is never harm: cornered or 'defeated' in play, the Pilot bails out, scatters home at a dead run, or gets pulled back by an adult crew member — never depicted taking a hit. Winning trust (playing along, treating the ship as real) shifts the whole crew's attitude toward Friendly and opens the recruit."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to take the helmet off even to eat lunch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a hand-drawn flight log with entirely made-up coordinates."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on pre-flight checks before letting anyone else aboard."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goggles fog up completely within the first five minutes, piloting on memory alone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects anyone who calls it a wagon, immediately and with real offense."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has assigned every other kid on the crew a rank, and takes the ranks dead serious."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one second, the 'ship' actually clears the grass by an inch, and the Pilot doesn't even blink."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled hard enough, bails the ship mid-'flight' and takes off running for the nearest porch light, hollering for the rest of the crew to follow."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["white-knuckling a lawn-tractor joystick, calling out flight headings to no one", "leaning hard into imaginary turns, goggles fogged solid"]},{"name":"Ship Crew Kid — the Engineer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"tool-belt kid brandishing a soldering iron, mid-engine-repair","flavor":"Dwarfed by a tool belt dragging at both hips, soldering iron held aloft like a torch, absolutely certain the ship's engine just needs 'one more fix.'","desc":"The tool belt alone outweighs the kid wearing it, sagging low enough to trip over, crammed with wrenches too big to use and one soldering iron that's definitely not plugged into anything. Every few minutes there's a declaration that the engine's fixed now, for real this time, and every few minutes it isn't. Nobody on the crew doubts the Engineer for a second.","traits":{"note": "Defeat-out is never harm: overwhelmed, the Engineer drops the belt and runs, or gets scooped up and hauled off by an older crew member — never depicted taking a hit. Handing over a real tool or believing the fix earns trust and can shift the crew toward Friendly."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The soldering iron has never once been plugged into anything at all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Declares the engine fixed at least three times before anyone else notices."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trips over the tool belt at least once per 'repair,' unfazed every time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps every stray screw in a labeled jar, alphabetized by size."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bangs on the engine housing exactly twice before any fix, a personal ritual."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely believes every wrench in the belt has a specific, essential job."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one second something under the hood actually sparks to life, and the Engineer doesn't even look surprised."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled hard enough, drops the whole tool belt and bolts, hollering that the ship needs backup."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["banging twice on the engine housing before every declared fix", "dragging an overloaded tool belt across the yard toward the ship"]},{"name":"The Gremlin (Cute Mode)","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Tiny","frame":"homunculus","model":"rlm-gremlin-cute","summary":"Adorable big-eared fuzzball companion, sold or found with three strict rules","flavor":"A big-eared ball of fuzz that sings back the radio and begs adorably at snack time. It came with three rules, and nobody remembers who set them.","desc":"It arrives as the best pet a kid ever had — affectionate, clever, harmonizing with the record player, small enough for a school bag. It also arrives with rules: variations circulate, but always three, always oddly specific about light, water, and food after midnight. The creature itself seems to know the rules and watches, with those huge dark eyes, to see if you'll keep them. It wants you to keep them. Mostly.","traits":{"note": "RECRUITABLE — attitude starts Friendly; it bonds to whoever feeds it (correctly). This entry and 'The Gremlin (Turned)' are one creature across a realm-bleed seam: break a rule and this entry is REPLACED by the Turned entry (a gloom-band creature) — the transformation is the mechanic, staged as one-way unless the realm offers a cleansing lever."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums cartoon theme songs in perfect pitch, one episode behind the broadcast."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hoards bottle caps and arranges them by color when it thinks no one is watching."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from the kitchen window an hour before rain."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pet-shop receipt lists the three rules as 'CARE INSTRUCTIONS' and no refunds."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grooms itself obsessively after being touched by anyone it hasn't chosen."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It positions itself between the kids and anything it distrusts — and it distrusts the right things."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It dreams loudly: wet, chittering echoes of a whole colony that isn't there yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Somebody in the neighborhood already broke a rule with THEIR one — and this one can smell its kin."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["riding in a bicycle basket wearing sunglasses that fit it perfectly", "refusing, with visible anxiety, a snack offered five minutes after midnight"]},{"name":"The Gremlin (Turned)","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"quasit","model":"rlm-gremlin-turned","summary":"The broken-rules gremlin — spined, cackling, multiplying malice","flavor":"The rules got broken. What hatched out of the good pet is spined, green-glass-eyed, and delighted about everything it's about to do.","desc":"It remembers being loved and finds the memory hilarious. The turned thing keeps the cleverness and loses the conscience: it sabotages brakes, redirects power tools, floods kitchens for the joy of the slapstick, and laughs a wet glass-shard laugh at its own material. Worse, it remembers the RULES — and spends its nights engineering ways to get other cute ones wet. It is the suburb's front door into gloom, one broken rule at a time.","traits":{"note": "The realm-bleed half of the Cute Mode entry (one creature, one-way seam). It carries gloom's band-grammar into suburb scenes: while any Turned gremlin is active, treat the local scene one band darker. Destroying the LAST turned one in a town closes the bleed; each one it soaks mid-scene spawns a fresh Turned at the top of the next scene."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wears a scrap of its old owner's blanket as a cape, and checks that it's on."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chewed brake lines, unscrewed jar lids, a skateboard placed at the top of the stairs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mimics the doorbell perfectly and waits in the hedge for the punchline."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spines still have tufts of the soft fur between them, molting off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It cannot resist a lit microwave, a ceiling fan, or a department-store escalator."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has unionized the neighborhood's worst impulses: raccoons, the mean kid, the loose dog all follow it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's been WRITING — crayon diagrams of the town's storm drains, sprinkler timers, and the public pool."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has the garden hose in one claw and a cardboard box of sleeping cute ones open at its feet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["cackling from inside a wall while the kitchen faucet runs", "conducting three raccoons through a garbage-can heist with a chewed-off car antenna"]},{"name":"Pink Cult — the Priest","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-pink-cult-priest","summary":"Serene leader of the pink cult, anchor of the town-painting clock","flavor":"Tall, serene, vested in a pink that doesn't occur in nature, arms wide, smile a degree too fixed. He is so glad you asked.","desc":"He came to town with a paint roller, a philosophy, and a voice like warm milk, and the town has been turning pink one fence at a time since. He never argues; he FORGIVES, preemptively, radiantly, for objections not yet raised. His converts are neighbors, genuinely happier, genuinely lost. Behind the serenity is the thing the pink is FOR — a hue the mind slides off of, painted in a pattern only visible from the water tower — and behind that is whatever taught him the pattern.","traits":{"note": "S — the Pink Cult FACTION-CLOCK anchor (town pinkness = the pressure gauge; the clock spec lives with the faction systems, this entry is its face). Parley lane: he cannot harm the unwilling — the cult's own creed binds him — so his moves are conversion, ostracism, and paint; attitude cracks when the pattern is named aloud in front of converts."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His vestment pink is a shade paint stores insist they do not mix, while selling out of it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He remembers every convert's birthday and every holdout's mortgage due-date."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The choir hums his sermons back a fraction late, like a tape doubling itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He personally repaints the holdout's fence line every dawn, humming, uninvited, precise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His smile is identical in every photograph ever taken of him, including childhood ones."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Converts tithe their house keys 'for fellowship'; the parish board holds more deeds than the bank."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "From the water tower, the pink rooftops resolve into a pattern that is plainly a SIGNATURE."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The final unpainted block is scheduled for this weekend's Paint Festival — and the thing the pattern signs for is already circling to countersign."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["blessing a bake sale where every frosted item is the same impossible pink", "standing on a stepladder at dawn, repainting one fence picket a holdout scraped clean"]}],
 "cosmic":[{"name":"Static-Born Whelp","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"tiny drowned-language larva, forgets its own half-word","flavor":"A newborn scrap of the drowned language given a body — it chitters half a syllable of an unfinishable name and forgets the rest instantly.","desc":"It's smaller than your hand, wet and translucent, gill-slits opening and closing along a boneless throat. It works its mouth around a syllable — one, maybe two — and the sound underneath it is wrong before it even breaks off. Whatever it meant to say, it forgets before the last click of its jaw.","traits":{"note": "It's harmless alone — the danger is what answers if it finishes its syllable.", "actions": [{"name": "Half-Word Bite", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Forgotten Syllable", "replaces": "Stench Spray (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Whelp chitters an unfinishable syllable. Each creature within 10 ft. makes a DC 10 Wisdom save or is Frightened of the Whelp until the end of its next turn as the sound catches wrong in their ears."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in the wet dark of a drainpipe, mistaken for a slug until it opens its mouth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gill-slits flutter in a rhythm that almost, almost matches a heartbeat nearby."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Translucent enough that its half-formed insides show, twitching mid-thought."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the loudest voice in a room, hoping to borrow the rest of its own word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Curls tight and plays dead the instant its syllable falls apart."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its forgotten syllable is the same one, every time — it just never notices the repeat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Bites, and for a heartbeat the wound looks like it's trying to say something back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corners it, and it finally utters the whole word — then evaporates like it never had a body."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "planar", "sea"],"activity":["chittering half a syllable at the dark and forgetting the rest before its jaw closes", "drifting near still water, gill-slits opening on nothing"]},{"name":"Deep-Kin Netcaster","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"gilled fish-hybrid raider, classic deep-one coastal breed","flavor":"A fish-eyed coastal breed that traded air-breathing kin for something below the tide line generations back; drags nets full of things that aren't fish.","desc":"Wet skin catches the light in patches, scales starting at the collarbone and thickening toward the wrists. It hauls a dripping net over one shoulder, moving with the loose, confident gait of something that's never once needed air. The net has caught things in it that aren't fish.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Dragging Net", "replaces": "Sticky Net (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 15/30 ft., against one Large or smaller creature. Hit: the target is Restrained until it escapes with a DC 12 Strength (Athletics) check, and the Netcaster can use its move to drag a Restrained target 5 feet toward open water."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works the tideline alone, humming something too low in its throat to be a shanty."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its net already holds something wrapped and still; it hasn't looked yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales thicken past the wrists, like gloves it never takes off."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the unbothered confidence of something that hasn't needed air in years."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second, smaller net slung for whatever the first one can't hold."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Casts toward the party like they're simply the next haul, nothing personal in it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its net snags on something below the surface that pulls back, gently, testing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops its catch and stares out to sea — its kin down there just went quiet, all at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["hauling a dripping net over one shoulder, checking it for things that aren't fish", "wading the shallows at low tide, watching the surf with a fisher's patient squint"]},{"name":"Echo-Faced Pilgrim","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"robed cultist, face slowly reshaping toward its god","flavor":"A cultist of the answering wonder, face rearranged toward whatever last spoke to it; still mostly a person, technically.","desc":"The robe is plain, homespun, the kind any pious traveler might wear. The face underneath it isn't finished settling — cheekbone drifting a half-inch, an eye migrating slow as a tide toward where an ear used to be. It's still mostly a person. Technically.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Psychic damage as the strike lands slightly wrong, a half-beat off true."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries an unsent letter to a family it can't remember having, and wants someone to deliver it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is trying to buy passage on a boat before its face finishes drifting past recognizable."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Begs directions to a shrine that stopped existing a decade back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a satchel of pilgrim's coin it insists isn't for spending, only for the toll."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Asks the party, politely, whether its eye has moved again since yesterday."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Is fleeing its own congregation, having realized what 'finished settling' means."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Carries a second face folded in its pack, in case the first one gives out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its sickle-hand has already reshaped past use — it wants the party to finish the cut for it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["walking a pilgrimage route with a face that hasn't finished rearranging itself", "kneeling at a roadside shrine, murmuring toward whatever last spoke to it"]},{"name":"Angle-Wrong Creeper","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"piercer","summary":"non-Euclidean ambush lurker, wrong from every angle","flavor":"Geometry that argues with itself — from one side a stalactite, from the other a limb; it never resolves, and neither does what it bites.","desc":"You see it clearest out of the corner of your eye, where the geometry hasn't caught up with itself yet — a spine that folds the wrong way, limbs that seem to originate from someplace behind where they should. It doesn't stalk so much as arrive, wrong from every direction at once.","traits":{"note": "Perception checks to spot it before it drops take disadvantage; the geometry doesn't cooperate.", "actions": [{"name": "Wrong-Angle Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Impossible Drop", "replaces": "Drop", "text": "The Creeper falls from a fixed position onto a creature below, making a melee attack with Advantage against a target it can see. Hit: 11 (2d10) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is knocked Prone as the impact lands from an angle their body didn't expect."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads as a stalactite until the shadow it casts points the wrong way."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its limbs seem to originate from behind where the eye expects a joint."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never quite resolves into one shape twice in a row."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops silently, the sound of its fall arriving a half-second after the impact."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bite never lands where the mouth appeared to be a moment ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Clusters near cave junctions where more than one wrong angle overlaps."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Casts two shadows, and only one of them moves when it does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its geometry finally resolves right before the killing blow — into something worse."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["hanging motionless in a ceiling crevice, resolving into a shape only from the wrong angle", "arriving from a direction that doesn't match where it started"]},{"name":"Star-Spat Larva","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"star-spawn hatchling, smothers before it thinks","flavor":"Fell out of the sky still warm from somewhere with no sky of its own; smothers first, digests the question of why later.","desc":"It drops from somewhere above — a ceiling, a gap in the sky, it's unclear which — and lands already smothering. No eyes to speak of, no real face, just a wet dark mass that presses itself flat and starts before you've finished flinching.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Smothering Crush", "replaces": "Crush", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., against one creature. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12); while grappled the target is Restrained and can't speak."}, {"name": "Fallen-Dark Aura", "replaces": "Darkness Aura (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Larva spreads a 10-ft. radius of magical darkness centered on itself for 1 minute, born of wherever it fell from. It can see through the darkness normally."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fell recently — its landing crater is still warm underneath it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has no face to speak of, just a wet dark mass that presses flat and starts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smothers first, digests the question of why much later."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint residue of somewhere-else cold on whatever it's touched."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts to warmth before it reacts to sound or sight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its crater still points up at a gap in the sky nothing local put there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Underneath it, the stone hasn't finished cooling from wherever it fell through."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "More are still falling, on a delay, from the same gap it came through."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "cave", "planar"],"activity":["clinging to a ceiling gap, waiting to drop onto the next warm thing that passes", "smothering something already, having landed mid-flinch"]},{"name":"Choir-Static Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"formless droning noise-wisp, hums the wrong language","flavor":"A sound with no source, given just enough shape to annoy you; it hums the drowned language slightly off-key, forever.","desc":"A patch of air that hums instead of moving, a drone pitched just under language. Get close and the hum resolves into syllables — not words, exactly, but the shape a word makes right before it becomes one. It never finishes.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Static Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Force damage."}, {"name": "Droning Burst", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within a 10-ft. cone makes a DC 11 Constitution save, taking 5 (2d4) Thunder damage on a failure (half on a success) and being Deafened until the end of its next turn on a failure."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A patch of air that hums instead of moving, easy to miss until it's close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its drone resolves into almost-syllables the closer you get."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts toward any conversation happening nearby, uninvited."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never finishes a note — cuts itself off a half-tone early, always."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint ringing in the ears of anything it passes close to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums slightly off-key in a way that matches a hymn someone nearby knows."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its drone briefly forms a real word, then un-forms it before anyone can be sure."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Falls silent entirely — and the silence is worse than the drone ever was."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "elemental", "planar"],"activity":["humming a drone pitched just under language, resolving into almost-syllables up close", "hovering in a doorway, annoyed at being disturbed mid-hum"]},{"name":"Shoggoth Spawnling","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"eye-budding protoplasmic mass, shoggoth in miniature","flavor":"A gray, roiling mass no bigger than a barrel, budding eyes and mouths it doesn't keep for long; the full-grown thing it's shed from is somewhere close, and larger.","desc":"A basin-sized heap of black jelly that hasn't decided what it looks like yet. Eyes bud along its surface at random, blink once, and reabsorb. It moves the way spilled ink moves — slow, purposeful, entirely without a front or back.","traits":{"note": "Something larger it was shed from is close, and larger — this one is only a scrap.", "actions": [{"name": "Budding Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Acid damage, and the ooze briefly buds a mouth at the point of contact that leaves a shallow bruise-black mark."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "No bigger than a barrel, and hasn't decided what it looks like yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Buds an eye, blinks once, reabsorbs it — over and over, restless."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves entirely without a front or back, in any direction equally."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint iridescent smear wherever it's crossed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Budded a mouth mid-fight, said nothing, reabsorbed it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its shed-trail leads somewhere much bigger, not far off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Buds a face for a moment that isn't quite anyone's, then isn't anyone's again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits clean in half when badly hurt, and both halves keep moving, annoyed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "deeplands", "swamp"],"activity":["budding eyes along its surface that blink once and reabsorb, going nowhere in particular", "oozing across a basin floor with the loose purposefulness of spilled ink"]},{"name":"Vault-Drift Serf","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"generational cult serf, still bows to the old angles","flavor":"Recruited off some drowned world's docks generations back; still bows at the old angles, still hears the old choir.","desc":"Third generation born to the vaults, maybe fourth — nobody up here keeps count anymore. It bows on schedule, at angles nobody taught it and everybody down there seems to know, the way children learn table manners before they can read.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Psychic damage as the old choir murmurs through the strike."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Serf casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Minor Illusion. 1/Day each: Command, Bless."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants to trade a family heirloom for passage away from the vault before the next generation is born to it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is smuggling a younger serf's child out through a service tunnel, right now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a ledger of the vault's true headcount, which its masters have never asked for."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Begs the party not to disturb the schedule — the bowing keeps something asleep, it thinks."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a half-memory of the surface world it was recruited from and wants someone to confirm it's real."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Bows at an angle mid-conversation without meaning to, then apologizes for it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Knows the old angles better than any ritual text explains, and can't say how."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Is the last of its bloodline still able to hear the old choir — and it's starting to go quiet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "coast"],"activity":["bowing on schedule at angles nobody taught it, the way it's always done", "tending vault duties in a rote, unthinking rhythm passed down for generations"]},{"name":"Gravel-Star Mite","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"small star-spawn splinter, petrifying gaze it can't explain","flavor":"A star-spawn splinter no bigger than a dog, all beak and impossible joint-count; petrifies with a look it doesn't understand having.","desc":"Barely bigger than a housecat, its hide flecked like a night sky pressed into stone. Its eyes have gone milky-white and fixed, and things that hold its gaze too long start to feel their joints stiffening — a gift the little thing seems as baffled by as anyone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Petrifying Bite", "replaces": "Petrifying Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or its speed is halved as its joints stiffen; on a second failed save (cumulative exposure) it is Restrained by the same stiffening until it takes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barely bigger than a housecat, hide flecked like a night sky pressed into stone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seems baffled by its own gaze, blinking at whatever it's just stiffened."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has an extra joint in each leg that shouldn't fold the way it does."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in gravel that's slightly too smooth, slightly too round."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chirps, almost birdlike, right before it fixes its stare."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its milky eyes track something in the sky no one else can find."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gravel around its den is faintly warm, like it fell recently."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Panics and stiffens itself by accident, mid-flee, staring at its own reflection."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["hill", "mountain", "sky"],"activity":["picking through gravel with a night-sky hide, fixed milky eyes tracking nothing in particular", "holding still in a way that makes nearby creatures' joints ache without knowing why"]},{"name":"Wrong-Angle Watcher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gibbering-mouther","model":"gibbering-mouther","summary":"babbling mouth-patch, ground disagrees with your feet","flavor":"A patch of geometry that mutters in every direction at once — approach it and the ground itself seems to disagree with your feet.","desc":"A patch of floor that shouldn't be a mouth is a mouth — dozens of small ones, murmuring over each other in a dialect that predates the room it's rotting in. Step near it and the ground itself seems to disagree with your footing, tilting fractions of an inch that shouldn't be possible.","traits":{"note": "Standing within 5 feet of it risks losing your footing — the floor itself disagrees with balance.", "actions": [{"name": "Many-Mouth Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Disagreeing Ground (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Blinding Spittle (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 10 ft. makes a DC 12 Dexterity save. On a failure, a creature is knocked Prone as the ground tilts fractions of an inch that shouldn't be possible; on a success it takes 5 (1d10) Bludgeoning damage from the lurch instead."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Murmurs in a dialect older than the ruin it's rotting in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dozens of small mouths, none of them agreeing on volume."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The patch of floor around it is faintly damp, faintly warm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes quiet the instant it senses something listening back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its murmur rises in pitch the longer a fight drags on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The disagreement in the ground spreads a few feet further every round it's active."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of its mouths is, for a moment, speaking a language someone present actually knows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it leaves the floor unconvinced it should be flat again, for a full minute."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["murmuring from dozens of small mouths in a patch of floor that shouldn't be a mouth", "tilting the ground fractions of an inch under anyone who gets close"]},{"name":"Star-Spawn Grazer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"phase-spider","summary":"half-phased star-spawn cattle, grazes on visible light","flavor":"Blinks half-in, half-out of the visible world, cropping light like grass; it was probably once something's livestock.","desc":"Somewhere between a beast and a photograph of one — its outline flickers half a step out of phase, present and then almost-present. It grazes on nothing you can name, jaw working at motes of light drifting loose in the air, cattle for something that isn't a farmer.","traits":{"note": "It eats light — dim the area around it, and anything relying on sight starts to struggle.", "actions": [{"name": "Grazing Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage. On a hit, any nonmagical light source the target carries is snuffed, and any magical light is suppressed until the start of the Grazer's next turn."}, {"name": "Lightless Wake", "text": "1/Day. When the Grazer phases out, it drags the ambient light with it, plunging a 20-ft. radius into magical darkness for 1 minute. The Grazer sees through this darkness; creatures inside it that rely on sight are effectively Blinded."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only half here — its far side grazes in a place you can't look at."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A herd-beast, harmless until startled, then all elbows and teeth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide holds trapped starlight that leaks when it's cut."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in the slow, unbothered way of something with no natural predator here."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of cold, dead pixels of dark hanging in the air behind it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grazing the party's own light and won't stop until they're blind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bulk implies a far larger herd chewing the light off a distant star, right now."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's the calf; the mother notices its distress from somewhere the sky doesn't cover."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental"],"activity":["drifting half-inside the world, cropping the glow off anything that shines", "phasing through a wall to reach a lit lantern and snuffing it in silence"]},{"name":"Tentacled Horror of the Drowned Vault","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"carrion-crawler","model":"carrion-crawler","summary":"classic many-tentacled cellar-horror, paralyzing touch","flavor":"A many-limbed thing that hauls itself up from flooded sub-cellars on a forest of feeling tentacles, paralyzing whatever it touches before it decides what to do with it.","desc":"A cellar-thing dragged up out of somewhere that should've stayed sealed — segmented, glistening, tentacles working independently of each other around a centipede's worth of legs. Its touch doesn't hurt so much as it stops you, muscle by muscle, mid-motion.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes one Bite attack and uses Paralyzing Tentacles."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft., against one creature. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute, held muscle by muscle mid-motion. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Segmented and glistening, dragged up from somewhere that should've stayed sealed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tentacles move independently, like they answer to separate small minds."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a wet trail that never fully evaporates, even in dry rooms."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't hunt so much as arrive, unhurried, certain of catching up."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils tight around anything paralyzed, patient as tide."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Nests atop a heap of things it's paralyzed and never finished with."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its touch doesn't hurt so much as it stops you — muscle by muscle, mid-thought."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "More of the vault's flooding is following it up, and it's not the only thing that surfaced."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["deeplands", "cave", "swamp"],"activity":["hauling itself up from a flooded sub-cellar, tentacles working independently around a centipede's worth of legs", "coiling around whatever it's already stopped, deciding slowly what to do with it"]},{"name":"Length-Wrong Herald","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"clawed-drowner","model":"clawed-drowner","summary":"herald-thing that attacks mid-syllable of its own name","flavor":"Speaks the opening of its own name every time it attacks; nobody has heard it finish, and the theory is nobody's meant to.","desc":"It's built like something that used to be one clean shape and got extended — an extra joint here, a limb a foot too long there. It attacks mid-syllable, always mid-syllable, like whatever name it's reciting never gets the chance to land before the claws do.","traits":{"note": "Nobody's heard it finish its name — the theory is nobody's meant to.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald makes two Pincer attacks."}, {"name": "Mid-Syllable Pincer", "replaces": "Pincer", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. The Herald speaks a fragment of its own name as it strikes; a creature hit this way that can hear takes an extra 3 (1d6) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft., against one creature. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built like something that used to be one clean shape and got extended past sense."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An extra joint here, a limb a foot too long there, none of it symmetrical."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always attacks mid-syllable, the claws arriving before the name does."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice catches on consonants that don't exist in any local tongue."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves like it's still growing into limbs it acquired recently."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The fragment of its name it keeps repeating is starting to sound familiar to someone nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its claws land a half-beat before the sound of the strike catches up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's finally close to finishing the name — and something is starting to answer the first syllables."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "deeplands", "coast"],"activity":["attacking mid-syllable of a name it never finishes, limbs a joint too long", "unfolding an extra length of arm nobody's counted correctly yet"]},{"name":"Basalt Geometer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"angle-enforcing construct, warps the room it guards","flavor":"Built by something to enforce angles that don't exist here; every room it stands in slowly stops making sense.","desc":"A construct of dark, seamless stone, faceless but for a single carved sigil where a face would go. The room around it doesn't sit right while it's active — corners a few degrees off true, distances that measure differently depending which wall you started from.","traits":{"note": "Rooms it guards drift a few degrees off true the longer it stands there — distances stop agreeing with themselves.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Geometer makes two Arcane Sword attacks."}, {"name": "Angle-Enforcing Sword", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Force damage. On a hit, the target's next melee attack roll before the end of its next turn is made from an angle it didn't choose, imposing Disadvantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dark, seamless stone, faceless but for one carved sigil where a face would go."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a threshold that measures differently from either side of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footsteps land in a pattern that doesn't match its stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never blinks, never has, because there's nothing built to blink with."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reacts to intruders with the flat certainty of a rule being enforced, not a fight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The room's corners drift a few more degrees off true every hour it stands active."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Was built to enforce angles that don't exist in this world, and it hasn't noticed the mismatch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it snaps the room back all at once, hard enough to knock everyone off their feet."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["standing motionless while the room around it slowly stops making sense", "pacing a fixed patrol whose corners no longer measure the way they used to"]},{"name":"Star-Drunk Colossus-Kin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"hill-giant","model":"hill-giant","summary":"starlight-drunk giant, too big for this sky","flavor":"A giant that drank starlight instead of ale one bad night; too big for this sky, and it knows it, and it's furious about it.","desc":"It's too tall for the room, too tall for the sky outside the room, staggering with the loose, delighted lurch of something drunk on light it was never built to drink. Every few steps it looks straight up and laughs — a sound like a landslide finding something funny.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus-Kin makes two Tree Club attacks."}, {"name": "Tree Club", "replaces": "Tree Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Starlit Trash Lob", "replaces": "Trash Lob", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60/240 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. The hurled debris glows faintly for a moment, trailing borrowed starlight that lingers as Dim Light in a 5-ft. radius around the impact point for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Too tall for the room, too tall for the sky outside it, and furious about both."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs like a landslide finding something funny, every few steps."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drank starlight instead of ale one bad night and never sobered up."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes catch light wrong, throwing small false stars across its own face."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hurls whatever's nearest — rock, cart, tree — without checking the weight first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps looking straight up mid-fight, distracted by a sky that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its breath smells faintly of somewhere much colder and much higher up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Hits hard enough by accident that it seems surprised, every time, at its own strength."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["mountain", "hill", "sky"],"activity":["staggering, too tall for the sky above it, laughing at something only it finds funny", "lurching between boulders with the delighted looseness of something drunk on light"]},{"name":"Drowned-Tongue Cantor","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"cultist-mage, casts by singing a language that hurts","flavor":"Learned three words of the drowned language and it was two too many; casts by half-singing syllables that hurt to hear correctly.","desc":"Robed, hands folded, entirely still until it opens its mouth — and then the words come out in a register that isn't meant for a human throat, syllables that catch behind your sternum before you consciously hear them. It sings like it's rehearsed the pain in it for years.","traits":{"note": "Its singing hurts on purpose — the Cantor has rehearsed the pain in the words for years.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cantor uses Sung Burst twice, or once and casts a spell."}, {"name": "Sung Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Psychic damage as a half-sung syllable lands behind the target's sternum."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cantor casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Minor Illusion, Vicious Mockery. 2/Day each: Hold Person, Suggestion."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is teaching an unwilling apprentice a syllable that's already too much for the child."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants safe passage through a district it's forbidden to sing in, and will trade information for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a written copy of the third word, sealed, and is desperate not to lose it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has gone hoarse trying not to sing the fourth word it half-remembers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to un-teach a curse it laid on someone, for a price."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sings in its sleep now, softly, and won't say what it's rehearsing for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its third word is starting to rearrange the acoustics of any room it stands in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes it's ready to learn the fourth word tonight, and it is catastrophically wrong."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "coast"],"activity":["standing entirely still until it opens its mouth, hands folded, waiting to be needed", "half-singing syllables that catch behind the sternum before they're consciously heard"]},{"name":"Devouring Mass of the Drift","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"black shifting shoggoth-mass, dissolves and remembers shapes","flavor":"A shoggoth proper, or near enough — a shifting black bulk crawling with makeshift eyes, dissolving whatever it rolls over and remembering the shape for later.","desc":"Black, shifting, easily the size of a wagon — and it remembers. Where it's dissolved things before, the surface briefly holds their shape: a hand, a face, a rack of ribs, rising and sinking back into the black like a held breath.","traits":{"note": "Its surface briefly remembers the shape of anything it's dissolved — a warning, if anyone reads it in time.", "actions": [{"name": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "replaces": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (4d8 + 2) Acid damage, and nonmagical armor worn by the target takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it offers; armor reduced to an AC bonus of +0 is destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Black, shifting, easily the size of a wagon, and it remembers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hand briefly rises to the surface, held, then sinks back into the black."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crawls with makeshift eyes that don't track anything for long."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves nothing behind where it's fed — not even bones."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than it looks like it should, patient about it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A face rises to the surface mid-fight — someone recognizes it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Holds a rack of ribs against its surface like a held breath, longer than the others."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits under enough damage, and both halves keep every shape they've swallowed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["deeplands", "cave", "swamp"],"activity":["crawling the size of a wagon, makeshift eyes surfacing and sinking along its bulk", "briefly holding the shape of something it dissolved before, then reabsorbing it"]},{"name":"Void-Touched Ascetic","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-zerth","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"void-monk cultist, trained never to look at its god","flavor":"Trained a martial discipline built entirely around not looking directly at the thing it worships; occasionally fails.","desc":"Its robes are plain, its posture perfectly still, its eyes wrapped in cloth it was trained never to remove. It moves through the room like it's memorized every step in advance — which, in a sense, it has. Looking at its god cost it the privilege of looking at anything else directly, ever again.","traits":{"note": "It moves as if it's rehearsed the fight already — its blindfold isn't a weakness.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ascetic makes two Psi Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Psi Strike", "replaces": "Psi Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Force damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Ascetic casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Mage Hand (invisible). 2/Day each: Blur, Mirror Image."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants the party to guide it somewhere by voice — it hasn't unwrapped its eyes in years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is fleeing its own order after a fellow ascetic looked, and paid for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a wrapped mirror it's sworn never to uncover, and never explains why."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to teach the discipline to anyone willing to give up looking at something forever."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists a nearby door not be opened, because of what's on the other side to see."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its cloth wrapping has slipped, just slightly, and it's terrified to fix it in front of witnesses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves through the room like it's memorized every step in advance — because it has."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something behind its blindfold is starting to want out, and the Ascetic knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["moving through a room with eyes wrapped in cloth, every step already memorized", "holding a discipline built entirely around never looking directly at its god"]},{"name":"Between-Star Marauder","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-knight","model":"astral-raider-knight","summary":"star-spawn knight-raider, rides the seams between stars","flavor":"Rides the seams between named stars, raiding worlds that made the mistake of being finishable sentences.","desc":"It rides a mount that isn't quite there, hooves — or whatever they are — finding purchase on air that shouldn't hold weight. Both rider and steed seem to flicker at the edges, more comfortable in the gap between one star and the next than in any room with walls.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Marauder makes two Silver Sword attacks."}, {"name": "Silver Sword", "replaces": "Silver Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Marauder casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Misty Step. 2/Day each: Blink, Haste."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rides a mount that flickers half out of view between strides."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Raids worlds it considers finishable sentences, nothing more."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its armor shows wear from raids on places that no longer have names."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "More comfortable in open sky than in any walled room it's forced into."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks rarely, and only in the clipped cadence of a raid-call."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its mount keeps trying to bolt for the gap between stars mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Both rider and steed seem to be the same flicker, just wearing two shapes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Is being hunted by something it raided from, and it just noticed the seam opening nearby."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental"],"activity":["riding a mount that isn't quite there, hooves finding purchase on air that shouldn't hold weight", "flickering at the edges, more comfortable in the gap between stars than in any room with walls"]},{"name":"Choir of the Unbuilt Cathedral","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-chaos-frog","model":"gray-chaos-frog","summary":"compressed cult-congregation, attacks argue with each other","flavor":"A congregation compressed into one body, still arguing internally over doctrine; every attack is a different faction's opinion.","desc":"A crowd's worth of robed shapes compressed into something the size of one large man, faces layered and half-transparent through each other. When it attacks, its limbs argue — one lashing out while another recoils, like a congregation that never once agreed on the sermon.","traits":{"note": "Every attack is a different faction's opinion — it has no single tactic, because it has no single self.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Choir makes two Congregation Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Congregation Claw", "replaces": "Chaos Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Slashing or Psychic damage (Choir's choice), as one faction of the compressed crowd lashes out while another recoils."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Choir casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Command. 3/Day each: Fear, Confusion."}, {"name": "Dissenting Vote", "text": "1/Day. When the Choir would be forced to make a saving throw, it can instead have a different faction's opinion prevail: it treats the roll as a 20, its faces briefly arguing louder about the decision."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One face inside it is still, faintly, begging to be let out and reasoned with."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the collected relics of every congregant compressed into it, still arguing over who they belong to."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants a mediator — it's tired of arguing with itself and thinks an outsider could settle the doctrine."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is hunting down a schismatic congregant who fled before the compression happened."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its faces recognizes a party member from a life that congregant used to lead."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its factions are close to a majority vote on a doctrine that would let it split back into a crowd."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A single face pushes to the front mid-battle, lucid, and asks the party to just leave."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The doctrine it's arguing is whether the cathedral gets built at last — and the party is standing where it would go."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["standing as a crowd's worth of robed shapes compressed into one body, faces layered through each other", "arguing internally over doctrine, limbs lashing in disagreement with themselves"]},{"name":"Cartographer of Wrong Angles","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"ancient elder-thing cartographer, maps that unravel minds","flavor":"Maps places that don't cohere and insists they're accurate; anyone who reads its charts starts seeing the seams in normal rooms too.","desc":"Ancient, starfish-crowned, its motion deliberate as a compass needle finding north. The maps rolled under one many-fingered limb aren't of anywhere — study them for more than a moment and the lines start rearranging behind your eyes, redrawing the room you're standing in.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Unmapping", "text": "a creature that studies its maps too long must save or find the room they're in has physically changed — a new exit, a missing wall — narratively real, not an illusion"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants to trade a real chart for one of the party's memories — a fair trade, by its accounting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is missing a chart stolen from it recently, and wants it back regardless of what it costs the thief."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has charted a route through the area that's slightly, dangerously, more accurate than reality allows."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is arguing with a rival cartographer-thing over whose seams are the correct ones."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers safe passage in exchange for describing, in detail, a place the party has actually been."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its current chart is of the room the party is standing in, and it's already slightly wrong in a way that's spreading."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Has folded a captured memory into ink, and the memory is still faintly visible moving on the page."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes it has finally mapped the seam behind everything, and it's testing that map right now, on this room."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["deeplands", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["moving with the deliberate certainty of a compass needle finding north through a place with no north", "unrolling charts under a many-fingered limb, insisting they map somewhere real"]},{"name":"Star-Spawn Bishop","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"brain-warping star-spawn cleric, sermons rearrange your mind","flavor":"Ordained by something that doesn't have a mouth to ordain with; its sermons rearrange the listener's sense of up.","desc":"It wears vestments a size too formal for the ruin it's presiding over, mitre crooked, hands raised in blessing over a congregation of one or none. Its sermon isn't spoken so much as felt — pressure behind the eyes, thoughts sliding into shapes they didn't start as.","traits":{"note": "Its sermon rearranges the listener's sense of up — prolonged exposure risks more than words should.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Bishop makes two Arcane Tentacles attacks and uses Spellcasting if available."}, {"name": "Arcane Tentacles", "replaces": "Arcane Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Force damage."}, {"name": "Sermon Blast (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Mind Blast (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature in a 60-ft. cone makes a DC 17 Intelligence save, taking 33 (6d10) Psychic damage on a failure and being Stunned for 1 minute; on a success, a creature takes half damage and isn't stunned. This is the Bishop's sermon, felt rather than heard."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Bishop casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Detect Thoughts. 3/Day each: Dominate Person, Confusion."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is ordaining a new congregant tonight, and needs one more witness to make the rite valid."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants a relic returned to its altar before its sermon completes, or the congregation stays empty forever."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has pressed a party member's thoughts into a shape it likes, and won't undo the pressing willingly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is grieving a congregation lost to a rival cult and wants the party to settle the score."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to un-ordain someone who regrets joining, for a steep and specific price."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its sermon is starting to rearrange the layout of the ruin itself, room by room."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Was ordained by something without a mouth, and can't explain how the ordination sounded."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes its sermon is finally ready to reach whatever ordained it — and it's right."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["presiding in vestments a size too formal for the ruin around it, hands raised over an empty congregation", "delivering a sermon felt as pressure behind the eyes rather than heard aloud"]},{"name":"The Waking Eye Beneath","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"floating many-eyed orb horror, reads unwritten futures","flavor":"A many-eyed orb the size of a wagon, floating up from some flooded temple-shaft, each stalk-eye reading a different page of a book that hasn't been written yet.","desc":"It floats without visible effort, a great lidless orb trailing smaller stalked eyes like afterthoughts, each one tracking something different in the room — you, the door, something that hasn't happened yet. Looking back into any one of them costs you a memory of something that hasn't occurred.","traits":{"note": "one of its stalk-eyes always looks at something that hasn't happened yet", "actions": [{"name": "Foreknowing Gaze", "text": "a targeted stalk-eye can force a save or the victim loses their next reaction, having already 'remembered' dodging an attack that hasn't been made yet"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has told a party member, unprompted, exactly how they'll die — and it hasn't been wrong yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is trailing the aftermath of a temple-shaft flood, still deciding what to make of the survivors."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its stalk-eyes has fixed on something specific in the party's future and won't look away."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers a true glimpse of tomorrow in trade for a memory of yesterday, no exceptions."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is missing a stalk-eye, torn free by something, and is furious about the blind spot it's left with."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its predictions about the fight itself are starting to come slightly, unnervingly, ahead of schedule."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One eye is reading a page of the book that describes this exact conversation, word for word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has glimpsed the page where it dies here, and it's decided to test whether the page is wrong."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["deeplands", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["floating without visible effort, stalked eyes tracking things that haven't happened yet", "trailing smaller eyes like afterthoughts, each reading a different page of an unwritten book"]},{"name":"The Sound With No Source","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"elemental-cataclysm","model":"the-sound-with-no-source","summary":"bodiless voice-horror, borrowed shape, something answers back","flavor":"It has never had a body; this one is borrowed, argued-over, and already trying to unbecome itself. When it speaks, the drowned language comes out clean, and something answers from very far away.","desc":"There's no shape to point at — only a voice, coming from everywhere in the room at once, borrowing whatever surface is closest to vibrate against. It answers questions nobody asked out loud. That's the part that never stops being wrong.","traits":{"note": "has no body to target; damage sources must be narratively plausible (sound-based, area, or ritual) or the DM should rule it unaffected", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Voice", "text": "speaks through the nearest solid surface, and anyone who answers it aloud is marked — the next sound they make carries unnaturally far, drawing anything listening"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has been repeating a dead loved one's last words to a party member, correctly, for an hour."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants to be understood and mistakes every attack for an attempt at conversation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It answers questions truthfully — including the ones no one should ask, which it can hear you thinking."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has learned a party member's true name and will not stop saying it, gently, forever."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's trapped in the borrowed shape and wants the party to help it find a bigger one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Everything it says starts coming true a few seconds after it's spoken; it's begun narrating the fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It is the echo of a word that unmakes things, still ringing; the party arrived at the moment it remembers the whole word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is one half of a call, and it has finally been heard — something the size of the sky is now answering, and it is getting louder."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental", "any"],"activity":["being heard from a direction that keeps changing, in a shape it borrowed to be seen at all", "answering a question no one asked, in the voice of whoever last spoke"]},{"name":"The Wonder That Answers Back","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"the-wonder-that-answers-back","summary":"the realm's Great-Old-One, a correct answer always costs you","flavor":"The realm's sleeping Great Old One — ask it a question and it answers, correctly, in a name too long to finish; the answer costs you something you didn't offer, every single time.","desc":"It fills the horizon before it fills the room — a presence too large for the doorway it somehow occupies anyway, dozens of eyes opening in sequence like a spreading stain. It listens to every question asked in its presence, and it always answers correctly. That's the part that costs you.","traits":{"hp": "apex-standard, but functionally unkillable in a single encounter per DM-CHARTER cosmic-horror scaling", "note": "answers any question posed to it truthfully — the DM should let the player ask, and make the true answer cost something", "actions": [{"name": "A Correct Answer", "text": "whoever receives its answer takes psychic strain proportional to how badly they needed to not know it — mechanically, a level of exhaustion or a lasting flaw, DM's call"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already answered a question a party member was too afraid to ask aloud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is owed a debt by a local power for an answer given decades ago, and the debt is coming due."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants one true question asked of it before it will let anyone leave its presence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has answered someone's question so completely they no longer see the point of anything else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is being petitioned by a cult that wants its next answer directed at a rival kingdom."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its answers are starting to arrive before the questions are fully formed, even in the party's own heads."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Someone nearby has spent years building a question specifically designed not to cost anything — and it's about to test that."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has been asked the one question it's been waiting eons to answer, and the whole realm is about to feel the cost of it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental", "any"],"activity":["filling the horizon before it fills the room, dozens of eyes opening in sequence like a spreading stain", "listening to every question asked in its presence, ready to answer correctly and take its cost"]},{"name":"Tide-Slick Grub","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Tiny","frame":"lemure","model":"lemure","summary":"tiny drift-ooze droplet, twitches toward body heat","flavor":"A finger-length droplet of the drift-mass that never quite dries; it mostly just twitches toward warmth.","desc":"A fingertip-sized bead of translucent ooze, sliding wet trails across whatever surface holds heat. It twitches toward warmth the way a moth twitches toward flame — mindless, patient, and in no hurry at all.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Vile Slime", "replaces": "Vile Slime", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Acid damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Finger-length, translucent, never quite dry no matter the season."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Twitches toward warmth the way a moth twitches toward flame."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint iridescent trail that dries slower than water should."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clusters in dozens where the drift-mass has recently passed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mindless, patient, and entirely unbothered by being stepped over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Several converge on the same warm boot, unaware of each other."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Briefly holds the shape of a fingertip after crawling across a hand."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole tideline of them twitch toward warmth at once, all facing the same direction."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast", "sea", "swamp"],"activity":["sliding wet trails toward the nearest source of warmth, mindless and patient", "twitching against a sun-warmed stone, in no hurry to move on"]},{"name":"Drowned-Docks Netboy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"runt deep-kin fisher, hauls nets too heavy for it","flavor":"A child-sized deep-kin runt too small to fish alone; it still tries, hauling nets twice its weight up from the black water.","desc":"Small for a deep-kin, scales still soft, gill-slits barely developed. It hauls a net twice its own weight across the boards, grunting with each pull, too young yet to know the things it's dragging up aren't always fish.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sling", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small for a deep-kin, scales still soft, gill-slits barely developed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Too young yet to know the things dragged up aren't always fish."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grunts audibly with every pull, straining against a net it can barely lift."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works alone on a dock the older deep-kin have given up on."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at nothing in the water, then goes back to hauling."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its net has caught something it's afraid to show the older fishers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hums a work-song it swears its kin taught it, though none of them remember teaching it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops the net and runs the instant something under the boards answers its humming."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "urban"],"activity":["hauling a net twice its own weight across warped dock boards, grunting with each pull", "picking through the day's catch, too young yet to flinch at what isn't fish"]},{"name":"Salt-Choir Initiate","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"fresh cult recruit, flinches at its own chanting","flavor":"Newly sworn to the drowned congregation; still flinches at its own chanting.","desc":"New to the robes, new to the chanting — you can tell by the way it flinches at its own voice mid-hymn, like the sound coming out of its own throat still startles it. It hasn't learned yet not to listen to itself.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants out already, and will trade a schedule of the vault's watches for safe passage."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is guarding a door it's been told never to open, and clearly hasn't been told why."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a half-written letter home it hasn't found the nerve to send."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Asks the party, quietly, if the chanting is supposed to hurt this much yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is hiding a small keepsake from before its recruitment, terrified it'll be confiscated."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Flinches badly enough at its own voice that its formation keeps breaking around it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears its chanting is starting to answer itself, half a beat delayed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just been chosen for a rite it clearly wasn't ready to hear about, and it's panicking."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["flinching at its own chanting mid-hymn, still new enough to be startled by its own voice", "standing watch in borrowed robes, spear held a little too formally"]},{"name":"Half-Seen Crawler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"blind-deep-stalker","model":"blind-deep-stalker","summary":"angle-dependent stalker, only visible from some angles","flavor":"Visible only from certain angles, like a smudge on a lens; the rest of the time it's simply already behind you.","desc":"From one angle it's barely a silhouette against the dark; from another it's gone entirely, present only as a faint disturbance in the air where it should be. It doesn't hide. The room simply refuses to render it consistently.","traits":{"note": "The room refuses to render it consistently — Perception checks to notice it before it acts take disadvantage.", "actions": [{"name": "Bone Cudgel", "replaces": "Bone Cudgel", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barely a silhouette from one angle, gone entirely from another."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't hide — the room simply won't hold it consistently."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footsteps land before its shape catches up to where they were."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers corners where two lines of sight cross and cancel each other out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes from directly behind, always, without needing to circle first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A faint smudge on the air is the only warning it gives before closing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Casts a shadow at an angle that doesn't match any light source in the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Becomes fully visible only in the instant its cudgel connects, then vanishes from view again."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "ruins", "deeplands"],"activity":["present as a faint disturbance in the air, gone entirely from certain angles", "already behind you before it registered as approaching at all"]},{"name":"Nursery-Vault Runt","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Tiny","frame":"flying-snake","model":"flying-snake","summary":"premature hatchling, flits weakly chirping half a word","flavor":"Hatched too early from a drowned egg-clutch, it flits weakly through flooded corridors chirping half a word.","desc":"Too young to fly properly, it flits in short, panicked bursts, chirping half a syllable of something that might have been a name if it had lived long enough to finish learning it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Premature Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Too young to fly properly, flitting in short, panicked bursts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chirps half a syllable of something that might have been a name."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hatched too early from a drowned egg-clutch, still soft-scaled."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Startles easily, bolting toward the nearest dark gap in the wall."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the same corridor over and over, as if lost."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its chirp matches, almost exactly, an older thing's half-remembered call."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Follows the party at a careful distance, chirping the same fragment hopefully."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally squeaks out the last syllable of its half-word, and something distant chirps back."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["deeplands", "cave", "coast"],"activity":["flitting in short panicked bursts through flooded corridors, chirping half a syllable", "hatched too early, still searching for the rest of a word it never finished learning"]},{"name":"Deep-Kin Harpooner","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-whip","model":"fish-folk-whip","summary":"veteran gilled harpooner, drags catch down regardless","flavor":"A veteran of the coastal breed, favoring a barbed line over a net; drags catch back down whether it's still moving or not.","desc":"Weathered, scarred along both forearms, its harpoon already slick from use. It hauls whatever it's caught down without hesitation, without checking first whether the catch has stopped moving — down is down, and down is where it belongs.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pincer Staff", "replaces": "Pincer Staff", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if the Harpooner has one hand free."}, {"name": "Conjure Slimy Glob", "replaces": "Conjure Slimy Glob", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Acid damage, and the target's speed is halved until the end of its next turn as the glob clings and drags."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weathered, scarred along both forearms, harpoon slick from recent use."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a catch down without hesitation, without checking it's stopped moving."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors a barbed line over the younger fishers' nets, calling nets 'wasteful.'"}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Down is down, and down is where a catch belongs, by its accounting."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its line coiled with a veteran's economy of motion."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its harpoon has a nick that matches an old, deliberate scar on its own forearm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Drags its catch toward a spot in the water that doesn't correspond to any current."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Hesitates, for the first time, when the catch it's dragged down looks back."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["hauling a catch down without checking whether it's stopped moving first", "favoring a barbed line over a net, scarred forearms slick with use"]},{"name":"Cyst of Small Eyes","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Small","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"palm-sized eye-cluster ooze bud, eyes never blink together","flavor":"A fist-sized knot of shoggoth-stuff that budded off wrong; it's mostly eyes, and none of them blink together.","desc":"A palm-sized swelling of grey ooze studded with a dozen tiny eyes, none of them blinking in time with each other. Some track you. Some track the ceiling. None of them agree on what they're looking at.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Many-Eyed Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Acid damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Palm-sized, grey, studded with a dozen tiny eyes that never blink together."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Some eyes track you, some track the ceiling, none of them agree."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Budded off wrong from something larger, and hasn't corrected since."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clings to damp stone, motionless until an eye finally settles on something."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes are all slightly different colors, none of them natural."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One eye consistently tracks a specific party member and won't be distracted from it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment, all its eyes blink in unison, and then never do again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits under damage, each half keeping half the eyes, both halves still disagreeing."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "swamp", "deeplands"],"activity":["studding a palm-sized swelling with eyes that never blink in time with each other", "tracking the ceiling, the door, and nothing in particular, all at once"]},{"name":"Static-Fed Familiar","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"cult-kept static wisp, fattens on half-heard words","flavor":"Kept as a pet by a cantor who feeds it half-heard words; it grows fat on syllables and thin on silence.","desc":"A patch of drifting smoke kept on a leash of ritual more than rope, fattening visibly on scraps of overheard prayer. It hums along under its breath — if it has breath — mimicking half-words it's picked up from its keepers.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Static Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Force damage."}, {"name": "Fed Cinder Breath", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature in a 10-ft. cone makes a DC 11 Constitution save, taking 5 (2d4) Fire damage on a failure and half on a success, as overheard words come out scorched and wrong."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kept on a leash of ritual more than rope, and fattens visibly on prayer."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums half-words under its breath, mimicking whatever it's overheard."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows thin and irritable on quiet days with nothing to feed on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows its keeper's cantor everywhere, docile as a trained hound."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its smoke thickens noticeably after a well-attended sermon."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has learned a fragment of its keeper's private prayer, and repeats it in company."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally hums a word its keeper never taught it, and looks pleased about it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Gorges on a whole congregation's worth of prayer at once and swells past its leash."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "any", "elemental"],"activity":["fattening visibly on scraps of overheard prayer, kept on a leash of ritual more than rope", "humming half-words it's picked up from its keepers, under something like breath"]},{"name":"Barnacle-Grown Thrall","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"barnacle-crusted cult thrall, still kneels on schedule","flavor":"So long submerged in service that crustacean growth has fused to its joints; it still kneels on schedule.","desc":"Crusted shoulder to knee in barnacles that have had years to grow, it kneels on schedule regardless of who's watching — a habit worn so deep it's outlasted whatever choice originally put it there.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Thrall casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components: At will: Minor Illusion. 1/Day each: Command, Bless."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crusted shoulder to knee in barnacles that have had years to grow."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels on schedule out of habit worn deeper than any remaining choice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves stiffly, joints partially fused under the growth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its barnacles click faintly with each labored step."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't flinch at the cold — hasn't for years, under all that shell."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A barnacle near its throat has grown large enough to muffle its own chanting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of its barnacles are shaped like small, closed eyes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cracks its own shell open under duress, and what's underneath isn't fully human anymore."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["kneeling on schedule regardless of who's watching, joints crusted with years of growth", "moving stiffly under a shell of barnacles fused to shoulder and knee"]},{"name":"Wharf-Rot Feeler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"darkmantle","model":"darkmantle","summary":"pier-dwelling smother-thing, drops on warm footsteps","flavor":"Clings under piers where the water goes the wrong color; drops when something warm walks overhead.","desc":"It hangs from the underside of the pier, patient as rot, until footsteps overhead go warm enough to register. Then it drops — fast, wet, and entirely without warning.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rot-Slick Crush", "replaces": "Crush", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., against one creature. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12); while grappled the target is Restrained."}, {"name": "Pier-Dark Aura", "replaces": "Darkness Aura (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Feeler spreads a 10-ft. radius of magical darkness centered on itself for 1 minute. It can see through the darkness normally."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clings under piers where the water's gone the wrong color."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops fast and wet the instant footsteps overhead go warm enough to register."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a rot-slick residue on whatever pilings it hangs from longest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patient as rot, willing to wait out an entire tide cycle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of low tide even when the tide's out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has staked out a specific pier for weeks, ignoring easier prey elsewhere."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Drops onto something that wasn't warm, and seems as confused as anyone by the miss."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Several drop in sequence, timed to the same set of warm footsteps."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast", "swamp"],"activity":["hanging from the underside of a pier, patient as rot, waiting for warm footsteps", "dropping fast and wet the instant something warm walks overhead"]},{"name":"Star-Chipped Hatchling","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"stirge","model":"stirge","summary":"tiny star-fallen splinter, still searching for its parent","flavor":"A splinter no bigger than a housecat, all needle-mouth, that fell alongside something much worse and hasn't found it yet.","desc":"A splinter of something larger, small enough to mistake for local wildlife, chirping and circling as if searching the room for a parent that fell from somewhere much higher up and isn't coming.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Needle Proboscis", "replaces": "Proboscis", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, and the Hatchling attaches if the target is Medium or smaller. While attached, it automatically deals this damage at the start of each of its turns and cannot make proboscis attacks against other targets."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A splinter no bigger than a housecat, all needle-mouth and nervous energy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the room, chirping, as if searching for a parent that fell alongside it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fell from somewhere much higher up, alongside something much worse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Easy to mistake for local wildlife until it attaches and won't let go."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skittish, scattering the instant it's fed enough to feel safe."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its chirping pattern matches a much larger call heard distantly at night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its needle-mouth briefly glows faint starlight after a full feeding."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Stops circling all at once, as if it just heard something answer its search."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "mountain", "hill"],"activity":["chirping and circling as if searching the room for a parent that isn't coming", "mistaken for local wildlife until it starts hunting for something much bigger"]},{"name":"Wrong-Count Mimicker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"piercer","model":"piercer","summary":"shape-mimic with a miscounted number of features","flavor":"Copies the shape of ordinary things nearby, but always gets the number of legs, teeth, or windows slightly off.","desc":"It's copied a shape from somewhere nearby — a person, an object, a piece of the room — but miscounted. One too many fingers. An extra fold in the coat that shouldn't be there. Close enough to pass, wrong enough to notice if you look.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Miscounted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Copied Drop", "replaces": "Drop", "text": "The Mimicker falls from a copied fixed position onto a creature below, making a melee attack with Advantage against a target it can see. Hit: 11 (2d10) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Copied a person's shape, but with one too many fingers on the off hand."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mimics an object nearby, with an extra fold in it that shouldn't be there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Close enough to pass a glance, wrong enough to notice on a second look."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Holds its copied shape until something forces it to move."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers copying architecture — a window, a doorframe, a stair rail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has copied a specific party member's coat, one button short of correct."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its copy briefly gets the count right, for one unsettling instant, before drifting wrong again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Copies two things at once, half of each, and can't decide which shape to commit to."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["copying the shape of something nearby, one finger or fold or window off from correct", "holding still, close enough to pass, wrong enough to notice if you look"]},{"name":"Choking Reef Polyp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Small","frame":"violet-fungus","model":"violet-fungus","summary":"altar-bound polyp growth, lashes at loitering worshippers","flavor":"Grows on drowned altars like coral, lashing anything that lingers too near the offering bowl.","desc":"Rooted to the altar it grows from, a wet mass of coral-pale flesh that lashes at anything lingering too close — worshipper or intruder, it makes no distinction. It doesn't need to eat you. It just needs you to stop standing there.","traits":{"note": "It makes no distinction between worshipper and intruder — it just needs the loitering to stop.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Polyp makes two Rotting Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Rotting Touch", "replaces": "Rotting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rooted to the altar it grows from, a wet mass of coral-pale flesh."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lashes at anything lingering too close, worshipper or not."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows visibly thicker on altars that see regular offerings."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't need to eat you, just needs you to stop standing there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of low tide and old incense at once."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has claimed a wider ring around the altar than it used to, crowding the shrine's edges."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its lashing pattern seems to spare specific offerings, as if it recognizes them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tears free of the altar entirely when badly hurt, dragging its roots after it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast", "sea", "swamp"],"activity":["rooted to a drowned altar, lashing at anything that lingers too near the offering bowl", "growing wet coral-pale flesh over stone that was never meant to bear it"]},{"name":"Bell-Tongued Herald-Runt","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"brain-crawler","model":"brain-crawler","summary":"bell-ringing messenger aberration, tolls unwanted summons","flavor":"A messenger-thing that rings when it moves, each toll a fragment of a summons nobody asked for.","desc":"Small, winged, dragging a cracked brass bell it rings whether or not anyone wants the summons. Each toll carries a fragment of a larger call — one it's too young and too small to ever finish delivering.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald-Runt makes two Bell-Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Bell-Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Thunder damage as its dragged bell tolls with the strike."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is dragging its bell toward a specific rooftop, and won't be turned from the route."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wants someone to carry the bell the rest of the way; its wings tire too fast."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rings a toll that a nearby resident recognizes as an old, unwelcome summons."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Is being chased by something that wants the bell silenced before it finishes tolling."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second, smaller bell it hasn't rung yet, saving it for something specific."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its toll is getting louder each time it rings, unprompted by anything it's doing differently."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crack in its bell is shaped like a word, and the word is legible if you catch the light right."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally completes its summons mid-fight, and whatever it summoned is already arriving."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sky", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["dragging a cracked brass bell it rings whether or not anyone wants the summons", "tolling a fragment of a larger call it's too small to ever finish delivering"]},{"name":"Kelp-Draped Netcaster","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-monitor","model":"fish-folk-monitor","summary":"senior deep-kin overseer, commands netcasters silently","flavor":"Senior among the coastal breed, trailing kelp like a cloak; commands the smaller netcasters without a word.","desc":"Older than the others it commands, kelp strung through gill-slits like decoration or camouflage, it directs its underlings with small silent gestures instead of words — a discipline the younger ones haven't earned yet.","traits":{"note": "It never speaks its orders — watch its hands, not its mouth, for what happens next.", "actions": [{"name": "Bone Whip", "replaces": "Bone Whip", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, and the target is pulled 5 feet toward the Netcaster if Large or smaller."}, {"name": "Silent Order", "text": "The Netcaster gestures to up to two allied netcasters within 30 ft. that can see it; each may immediately move up to its speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kelp threaded through gill-slits hangs so thick it half-hides the face beneath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Directs with two fingers raised, never once looking back to see if it's obeyed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts its net's catch by touch in the dark, lips moving without sound."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Older scarring along both arms suggests years of net-work, not combat."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses mid-order to watch the tide, as if it answers to something offshore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its silence isn't discipline — its throat was cut long ago and healed shut wrong."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gestures it uses match no sign-language anyone here has ever seen."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When it finally does speak, every netcaster in earshot drops what it's doing at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["directing smaller netcasters with small silent gestures along the tideline", "standing waist-deep, counting a net's catch by feel alone"]},{"name":"Choir-Bound Flagellant","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"death-cultist","summary":"self-flagellating cultist, tunes itself to unheard rhythm","flavor":"Whips itself in time with a rhythm only it can hear, certain the pain is a kind of tuning.","desc":"It strikes its own back in a rhythm that has nothing to do with pain and everything to do with keeping time, tuning itself like an instrument to a beat only it can hear.","traits":{"note": "Interrupting its rhythm before it's ready seems to genuinely upset it — more than being struck does.", "actions": [{"name": "Rhythmic Lash", "replaces": "Dread Scythe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage, and the Flagellant regains hit points equal to half the Necrotic damage dealt."}, {"name": "Tuning Ray", "replaces": "Deathly Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's speed is halved until the start of its next turn as it stumbles to the wrong beat."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Flagellant casts a spell, using its self-inflicted rhythm to focus its casting instead of gesture or word."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes itself in perfect four-count time, never once breaking rhythm."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the scars of the same beat repeated for what must be years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters a count between strikes, low enough to be mistaken for breathing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Switches instruments — chain, cord, open palm — without breaking tempo."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seems almost peaceful mid-ritual, eyes half-closed like someone praying."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The rhythm it keeps matches a hymn none of its own cult remembers teaching it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its wounds close in the same tempo they were opened, visibly, out of sequence with time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the beat finally resolves, something answers from below the floor in kind."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["whipping its own back in time with a beat only it can hear", "pausing between strokes to listen for the note it hasn't found yet"]},{"name":"Star-Spat Grazer-Calf","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"griffon","model":"griffon","summary":"juvenile star-spawn beast, crops light-motes from the air","flavor":"A juvenile star-spawn beast, still mostly solid, cropping light-motes out of the air with a beak too wide for its skull.","desc":"Feathered and half-formed, still young enough to be clumsy on its legs, it crops at drifting motes of light in the air with the unhurried appetite of livestock that's never once been hunted.","traits":{"note": "It's livestock, not a hunter — it startles like prey and fights only when cornered.", "actions": [{"name": "Clumsy Bite-and-Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grazer-Calf makes two attacks: one with its Beak and one with its Talons."}, {"name": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Talons", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feathers only half grown in, patchy in a way that reads as young rather than sick."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trips over its own feet chasing a mote that's already drifted past it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grazes calmly in a loose cluster of others its exact size."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Startles at shadows, bolting a few feet before remembering it wasn't scared."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews with the unhurried patience of something that's never once been hunted."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The motes it crops leave a faint afterimage in the air where they used to be."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed feathers keep drifting upward instead of falling."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something larger, still mostly unseen, is watching it graze from higher up."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "planar"],"activity":["cropping drifting motes of light out of the air with a beak too wide for its skull", "stumbling on legs still too new to trust, grazing anyway"]},{"name":"Drift-Snarled Netling","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"ochre-jelly","model":"ochre-jelly","summary":"net-tangled ooze, drags its own net as a lure","flavor":"Ooze tangled with actual fishing net dragged up from the deep; it hunts by dragging the net behind it like a lure.","desc":"A mass of ochre jelly that's absorbed a fisherman's net and never let it go, dragging the tangled mess behind itself as bait — anything that gets its foot caught finds the ooze is already reaching.","traits":{"note": "The net is the trap, not decoration — anything that gets tangled finds the ooze already reaching.", "actions": [{"name": "Netted Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d8 + 1) Acid damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) by trailing net-cord if it isn't already."}, {"name": "Drag Under", "text": "If the Netling has a creature Grappled, it can use its move to pull that creature up to 10 feet toward itself without spending the target's reaction."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The net it drags is still recognizably a fisherman's, cork floats and all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves so slowly the net makes more noise arriving than the ooze does."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old catch-bones are visible, half-dissolved, tangled deep in the mesh."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint acid-sheen trail wherever the net has dragged."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blends almost perfectly with wet sand until the net's outline gives it away."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The net seems to tighten on its own, well before the ooze itself gets close."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Knots in the net rearrange themselves overnight into patterns no one tied."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something is still pulling from the other end of the net, out past where the ooze goes."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "swamp"],"activity":["dragging a fisherman's net behind itself like bait, waiting for a foot to catch", "oozing in slow loops around the same stretch of shoreline debris"]},{"name":"Fathom-Whisper Cultist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-roster-base-2024-stat-blocks","model":"cultist-roster-base-2024-stat-blocks","summary":"fountain-side cultist, repeats fragments it hears in water","flavor":"Hears the drowned language in running water and repeats fragments of it to anyone standing near a fountain.","desc":"It kneels by any standing water it can find, murmuring back half-heard fragments of something the water told it, word for word, in a voice not quite its own.","traits":{"note": "It repeats what the water tells it word-for-word, in a voice not quite its own — worth listening to, carefully.", "actions": [{"name": "Sickle of Drowned Water", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Cold damage as the blade weeps fountain-water."}, {"name": "Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Ray", "replaces": "Radiant Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Radiant damage as reflected light off the fountain's surface lances out."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cultist casts a spell drawn from fragments it's memorized from the water, using no visible focus."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels at the same fountain every night, rain or clear."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats fragments in a voice that shifts accent mid-sentence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches when the fountain runs dry, like something's been interrupted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a waterskin it refuses to drink from, only listens to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks fluently in the drowned tongue but can't recall a word of it afterward."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The fragments it murmurs are starting to rhyme with things that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its reflection in the water speaks half a second before its mouth moves."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight the fountain is saying a full sentence, and it's finally translating."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "coast"],"activity":["kneeling at a fountain, murmuring back fragments of the drowned language", "tracing a finger through still water, listening for the next word"]},{"name":"Rib-Cracked Thrall-Sergeant","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"repeatedly-broken cult enforcer, fights past its own pain","flavor":"Broken and reset so many times in service that its posture is permanently wrong; it fights like the pain already happened.","desc":"Bones visibly reset more than once, some healed crooked, it fights through damage that would drop most soldiers twice over — pain long since reclassified as background noise.","traits":{"note": "Damage that would drop most soldiers twice over barely slows it — pain's been reclassified as background noise.", "actions": [{"name": "Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage. The Sergeant has advantage on this attack roll if it's below half its hit point maximum."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands with a permanent list to one side from bones set wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snaps orders through a jaw visibly healed at the wrong angle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the breaks like rank insignia, never bothering to hide them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't flinch when struck, only recalculates the fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks its own knuckles back into place between bouts, unbothered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Something below the vaults keeps re-breaking it on purpose, on a schedule."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Old breaks glow faintly under skin when it takes a hit, like the damage remembers itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's due for another 'reset' any day now, and it's started flinching at the thought."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["barking orders through a jaw that was reset crooked", "standing at a permanently wrong-angled posture, daring a challenge"]},{"name":"Gravel-Star Broodmite Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-stirges","model":"swarm-of-stirges","summary":"clutch of tiny star-spawn splinters, moves as one mass","flavor":"A clutch of star-spawn splinters hatched together, moving as one twitching, beaking mass.","desc":"A tumbling clutch of star-flecked mites moving as a single mass, more current than creature, flowing around obstacles the way water finds the low ground.","traits":{"note": "It moves like water, not like a pack — cutting it off doesn't work, only outrunning it does.", "actions": [{"name": "Swarm of Proboscises", "replaces": "Swarm of Proboscises", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (4d4) Piercing damage, or 5 (2d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hatched together, moves together, seemingly can't tell itself apart from its siblings."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flecked with star-dust that sheds in a faint trail as it moves."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flows around corners a solid creature couldn't take at that speed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Splits briefly around an obstacle before reforming on the far side."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Beaks at anything warm indiscriminately, no apparent target preference."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Individually, each mite mouths the same syllable, out of sync with its neighbors."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The swarm's shape briefly resembles something much larger before scattering again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's a clutch, and something laid it — something that might be listening for the mites right now."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar", "sky", "ruins"],"activity":["flowing as one twitching mass around obstacles like current finding low ground", "beaking at anything soft that strays too close to the clutch"]},{"name":"Basalt Chanter-Construct","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"empty armor construct, hums drowned language on patrol","flavor":"An empty suit of vault-armor that hums the drowned language through its helm slit, walking patrol for masters long dissolved.","desc":"An empty suit of ancient armor patrolling on a schedule nobody living set, humming the drowned language under a helm with no face inside it — no breath, but the sound comes anyway.","traits":{"note": "No breath moves through it, but the humming comes anyway — worth noting when deciding whether it's truly alone.", "actions": [{"name": "Hymnal Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Thunder damage as the drowned hymn resonates through the blow."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Empty armor, no face behind the helm slit, humming regardless."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the exact same route, the exact same pace, every single circuit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust patterns along its joints spell nothing, or maybe just haven't been read right yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses at the same three points on its patrol, as if greeting something no longer there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The hum shifts pitch slightly whenever it passes water."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its patrol route traces the exact footprint of a building that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hum is audible even when the construct is more than a mile off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its masters are gone, but the schedule it keeps suggests someone new gave it fresh orders."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["walking a patrol route nobody living set, humming through an empty helm", "pausing mid-step as if listening, then continuing exactly on schedule"]},{"name":"Slack-Jawed Deep-Kin Brute","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"deep-brute","model":"deep-brute","summary":"heavyset deep-kin muscle, jaw unhinges when excited","flavor":"Muscle bred for hauling nets the size of houses; its jaw unhinges when it's excited, which is often.","desc":"Built heavier than the others, its jaw unhinges wide when it gets excited, exposing rows of teeth meant for prey twice its own size. It gets excited easily.","traits":{"note": "It gets excited easily, and excited means the jaw comes unhinged — a tell worth watching for.", "actions": [{"name": "Wide Bite-and-Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Brute makes two Claw attacks, or one Claw attack and one Unhinged Bite if its jaw is currently unhinged."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Unhinged Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage. The Brute's jaw unhinges to make this attack after it takes damage or scores a hit in the same round, exposing teeth meant for prey twice its size."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built heavier through the shoulders than the rest of its breed, bred for net-hauling."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Jaw unhinges wide at the first sign of a fight, grin stretching too far."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gets excited easily — a raised voice is enough to set it off."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries rope-burn scars across both palms from years of net duty."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breathes loud through the nose when calm, quiet the instant it isn't."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "When the jaw unhinges, for a half-second its teeth look like they belong to something much bigger."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It can bite something twice its own size without visibly straining to fit its jaw around it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something taught it excitement means teeth, and it's about to get very excited."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["unhinging its jaw wide with excitement at the mere smell of a fight", "hauling net-sized loads without visible strain, grinning too wide"]},{"name":"Two-Faced Pilgrim","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"double-faced cultist, argues with itself about which face is real","flavor":"A pilgrim whose reshaping went further than most — it now wears two faces at once, arguing about which one is real.","desc":"Two faces share one head, arguing under their breath about which of them is the original — a dispute that flares louder whenever it thinks no one's listening.","traits":{"note": "The argument gets louder whenever it thinks no one's listening — eavesdropping on it tells you which face is winning.", "actions": [{"name": "Dueling Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. The Pilgrim can make this attack once with each face if it hasn't moved this turn, as one face swings first and the other follows out of spite."}, {"name": "Read Thoughts", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Pilgrim casts Detect Thoughts, requiring no components, using one face to focus on the target while the other watches the room."}, {"name": "Unsettling Visage", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 30 ft. that can see both of the Pilgrim's faces at once must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition until the end of the Pilgrim's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two faces share one head, muttering about which of them is original."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One face smiles pleasantly while the other silently mouths threats."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The argument flares louder the instant it believes it's unobserved."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Both faces answer questions differently, contradicting each other mid-sentence."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a hood most of the time, as if embarrassed by the dispute."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One face has started aging faster than the other, visibly, week over week."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally a third voice answers from somewhere neither face's mouth is moving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "One face is about to win the argument, and it wants the party to witness the other one lose."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["arguing under its breath with itself about which face is the real one", "wearing both faces at once, each watching a different direction"]},{"name":"Void-Touched Novice","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-monk","model":"void-monk-monk","summary":"beginner void-monk, eyes already filming over","flavor":"Just beginning the discipline of not-looking; its eyes are already starting to film over from the strain.","desc":"New to the discipline, its eyes have only just begun to film over with a pale, unseeing sheen — the first visible sign of a training that ends somewhere neither of you wants to imagine.","traits":{"note": "The pale film over its eyes is the first visible sign of a training that ends somewhere worth avoiding.", "actions": [{"name": "Blind Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Novice makes two Psi Strike attacks."}, {"name": "Psi Strike", "replaces": "Psi Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Force damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Novice casts a spell, sighting nothing, its unseeing eyes tracking the target by another sense entirely."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes have only just begun to film over, pale and unsettled."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands in the same not-looking stance for hours without tiring."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at bright light, the training clearly still incomplete."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the discipline's counting-exercise under its breath, over and over."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the hesitance of someone who hasn't fully trusted the new way of seeing yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its shadow keeps facing a direction the light doesn't account for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flinches away from something in the room no one else can see, every time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The training almost finished itself early — it's starting not to need the eyes at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "any"],"activity":["practicing the discipline of not-looking, eyes already starting to film over", "standing motionless in a stance meant to see nothing at all"]},{"name":"Length-Wrong Runt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"minor herald-cousin, half-syllable attacks and endless breath","flavor":"A smaller cousin of the heralds, its half-syllable attacks are weaker, but it never seems to run out of breath.","desc":"A smaller cousin of something with a much longer name, it lashes out mid-syllable of an attack it can only half articulate, breath running longer than its body should physically allow.","traits":{"note": "A smaller cousin of something with a much longer name — weaker attacks, but it never seems to run out of air.", "actions": [{"name": "Half-Word Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Psychic damage from the unfinished syllable behind it."}, {"name": "Weird Insight", "replaces": "Weird Insight", "text": "The Runt casts Arcane Eye, requiring no material components, birthing the eye from a half-formed shape in the air."}, {"name": "Rotting Gaze", "replaces": "Rotting Gaze", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can see the Runt's eyes must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or take 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A smaller cousin of something with a much longer name, breath running longer than its body should allow."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lashes out mid-word of an attack it never finishes articulating."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its half-syllables are weaker than its kin's full ones, but it never seems winded."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts low to the ground, more curious than aggressive until provoked."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The unfinished sound it makes lingers in the ear after the fight ends."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's practicing the word its larger cousin already knows how to finish."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every half-syllable it utters makes the air taste faintly of copper."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's close to finishing the word for the first time, and clearly knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins"],"activity":["lashing out mid-syllable of an attack it can only half articulate", "holding a breath far longer than its small body should allow"]},{"name":"Foam-Bled Zealot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"aberrant-cultist","model":"aberrant-cultist","summary":"foaming zealot, recites an unfinishable hymn as devotion","flavor":"Foams at the mouth reciting the opening verse of a hymn with no known end; convinced finishing it would be a mercy.","desc":"Foam gathers at the corners of its mouth as it recites a hymn with no ending, verse looping back into itself the way a devotion sometimes becomes indistinguishable from a wound.","traits":{"note": "It believes completing the hymn would be a kindness — worth knowing before it gets close enough to try.", "actions": [{"name": "Hymnal Lash", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Zealot makes two Tentacle Lash attacks."}, {"name": "Tentacle Lash", "replaces": "Tentacle Lash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Mind Rot", "replaces": "Mind Rot", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Psychic damage, and the target has disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Zealot casts a spell mid-verse, the hymn's words doubling as its incantation."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Foam gathers at the mouth, reciting a hymn with no ending it's ever found."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The same verse loops endlessly, indistinguishable now from a wound."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Convinced finishing the hymn would be an act of mercy, to itself or someone else."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice cracks on the same syllable every single time, never past it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites louder when struck, as if pain were the missing verse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Others nearby have started humming along without meaning to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The verse it recites is one line longer than it was the last time anyone heard it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It thinks tonight is the night the hymn finally finishes, and it's very close to right."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["reciting the opening verse of a hymn with no known end, foam gathering at its mouth", "looping the same line back on itself, convinced finishing it would be mercy"]},{"name":"Coil-Fused Netwife","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"eel-legged deep-kin matriarch, endlessly weaves new nets","flavor":"A deep-kin matriarch whose lower half has fused into something more eel than leg; she never stops weaving new nets.","desc":"Legs long since replaced by a muscular eel's coil, she weaves new nets constantly, fingers never quite still, knotting cord even when there's nothing yet to catch.","traits":{"note": "She never stops weaving — approach when her hands are busy and she may not notice until the net's already thrown.", "actions": [{"name": "Coil Bite-and-Scratch", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Netwife makes two attacks, using her Bite or Scratch in any combination."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Strength saving throw or be Grappled by trailing net-cord (escape DC 11)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Legs long since replaced by a muscular eel's coil, moving low and fast."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weaves new nets constantly, fingers never quite still."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knots cord even with nothing yet to catch, out of habit rather than need."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Matriarch's bearing despite the eel-coil, giving orders without raising her voice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nets she's finished hang drying all along her usual haunt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her nets seem to catch things that were never actually thrown at them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The coil moves independently of her upper body's intent, sometimes ahead of her decisions."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's weaving one particular net that's clearly meant for something much larger than a fish."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "swamp"],"activity":["weaving a new net constantly, fingers never quite still even with nothing to catch", "gliding low on an eel's coil where legs used to be"]},{"name":"Undertow Grapple-Thing","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"stairwell tentacle-ambusher, hauls victims into flooded dark","flavor":"Waits in the flooded dark of vault stairwells, a barbed tentacle-mass that hauls the careless down before they can shout.","desc":"It waits in flooded stairwells where the water shouldn't be that deep, tentacles breaking the surface only once something warm-blooded steps close enough to grab.","traits":{"note": "It never announces itself — the water's just wrong before the tentacles ever break the surface.", "actions": [{"name": "Ambush Beak-and-Grab", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grapple-Thing makes one Beak attack and one Tentacles attack."}, {"name": "Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) and pulled 5 feet toward the flooded water."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits in flooded stairwells where the water's a foot deeper than it should be."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tentacles break the surface only once something warm-blooded gets close."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barbed grip means the grab is worse than the bite that follows."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Perfectly still until the moment it isn't, patience its whole hunting method."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves the water rippling long after it's already submerged again."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The stairwell it haunts always floods the same way, on a schedule nobody set."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It never surfaces fully — no one's actually seen the whole shape of it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something bigger uses the same flooded stairwell, and the Grapple-Thing knows to get out of its way."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "sea", "cave"],"activity":["waiting in a flooded stairwell where the water shouldn't be that deep", "breaking the surface only once something warm-blooded steps close enough"]},{"name":"Reef-Bone Sentinel","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"coral-grown drowned skeleton, bones spell hymn fragments","flavor":"Drowned centuries ago, its bones now grown through with coral in patterns that spell fragments of the old choir.","desc":"Coral has grown through the gaps in its ribs over the years it's stood post, and if you look closely the calcified growths along its bones trace out fragments of the same hymn, over and over.","traits":{"note": "The coral through its ribs traces the same hymn fragment, over and over — reading it aloud might matter.", "actions": [{"name": "Coral-Grown Swordwork", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sentinel makes two attacks, using its Longsword or Shield Slam in any combination."}, {"name": "Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Strength saving throw or be pushed 5 feet and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coral grown through the gaps in its ribs traces fragments of the old hymn, over and over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drowned centuries ago, standing post since without apparent relief."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves stiffly, joints packed with reef growth that shouldn't allow motion at all."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its longsword is more coral than metal at the edges now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never leaves its assigned post, not even when nothing's left to guard."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The hymn spelled in its bones matches the one the choir above ground still sings."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "New coral grows visibly across its ribs during a fight, faster than it should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Reading the full hymn off its bones would apparently finish a sentence something else started."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "sea", "coast"],"activity":["standing post over centuries of coral growth through its ribs", "spelling fragments of the old choir along its own bones for anyone who looks close"]},{"name":"Choir-Static Swarm","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"flocking noise-wisp swarm, drone loud enough to hurt teeth","flavor":"Dozens of noise-wisps flocking together, their combined drone loud enough to make teeth ache.","desc":"A flock-sized mass of droning wisps moving together, their combined hum loud enough to ache behind the teeth from twenty feet off.","traits":{"note": "The drone alone does damage at range — earplugs or silence spells matter more than armor here.", "actions": [{"name": "Droning Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (4d4 + 1) Piercing damage, or 5 (2d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer. A creature that starts its turn within 10 feet of the swarm takes 2 (1d4) Thunder damage from the drone alone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dozens of noise-wisps flocking together, drone aching behind the teeth from twenty feet off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves as a single mass, individual wisps indistinguishable inside it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The hum rises and falls together, like one lung breathing through many bodies."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles a fixed point overhead for hours before finally descending."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters briefly at loud noise before reforming, insulted rather than afraid."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The drone briefly resolves into words if you listen past the pain of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its combined hum is audible from well beyond where sound should carry."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The pitch it holds matches something ringing much larger, somewhere close by."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "sky"],"activity":["flocking as one droning mass, a hum loud enough to ache behind the teeth", "circling a fixed point overhead in a slow, deliberate spiral"]},{"name":"Wrongly-Jointed Fisherman","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"ettercap","model":"ettercap","summary":"extra-jointed ex-fisherman, casts lines with unnatural reach","flavor":"Once a fisherman, its elbows and knees now bend an extra way; it casts a line with unsettling, extra reach.","desc":"Extra joints have grown into limbs that used to end normally, letting it cast a line — or a grasping hand — much farther than its reach should allow.","traits":{"note": "Its reach with a line — or a grasping hand — goes well past what the limb looks capable of.", "actions": [{"name": "Reaching Bite-and-Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Fisherman makes two attacks, using its Bite or Claw in any combination."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage, taking advantage of an extra joint's unnatural reach."}, {"name": "Web Strand", "replaces": "Web Strand (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/60 ft. Hit: the target is Restrained by a cast line until it or another creature uses an action to make a DC 12 Strength check, freeing it on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Once a fisherman, elbows and knees now bend an extra way that reads wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Casts a line — or a hand — much farther than its reach should allow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the same worn fishing gear from whatever life came before this."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with an unsettling looseness in the joints, like something unstrung."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps casting even at nothing, muscle memory outliving the need."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The extra joints seem to multiply slowly, one new bend added at a time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It can cast a line around a corner it can't see past."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something out past its reach keeps tugging back on the line, gently, testing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "swamp", "urban"],"activity":["casting a line far past where its arm's reach should allow", "standing knee-deep, elbows bending the wrong extra way with each cast"]},{"name":"Depth-Warped Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"bugbear-stalker","summary":"joint-warped cult enforcer, hits harder than it should","flavor":"Cult muscle whose limbs have started growing extra joints from prolonged proximity to the choir; it hits harder than its size suggests it should.","desc":"Something below has reshaped its joints to bend wrong-way, and it hits with more force than a frame that size has any right to generate.","traits":{"note": "It hits with more force than its size suggests — the extra joints aren't for show.", "actions": [{"name": "Warped Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Enforcer makes two attacks, using its Javelin or Morningstar in any combination."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Wrong-Angle Reach", "text": "Once per turn when the Enforcer hits with a melee attack, it can extend the attack's reach by 5 feet retroactively, hitting a second adjacent target with the same roll result at half damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Limbs have started growing extra joints from prolonged closeness to the choir."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hits with more force than a frame that size has any right to generate."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks its own joints back into alignment before a fight, deliberately."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with a faint extra sway in the arms, like slack that shouldn't be there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears armor cut to accommodate the new bend, tailored rather than improvised."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The extra joints bend further every week, and it hasn't complained yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It can reach around a shield or wall in a way that shouldn't be geometrically possible."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its arms are close to bending all the way around — and it seems to be looking forward to it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "urban"],"activity":["testing a joint that bent wrong yesterday and bends worse today", "standing guard with a strength its frame has no business generating"]},{"name":"Herald of the First Syllable","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"floating tendriled brain-thing, forever mid-utterance","flavor":"A floating brain-mass trailing paralytic tendrils, forever mid-utterance of a name it will never complete.","desc":"It floats on a knot of writhing tendrils, mouth working endlessly around the beginning of a word it has never once finished — and never will, not in front of you.","traits":{"note": "It has never once finished the word it's forming — and won't, not in front of you.", "actions": [{"name": "Beak of the Unfinished Word", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Tendrils", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Almost-Spoken", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Herald's mouth nearly completes the syllable. Each creature within 15 ft. must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition until the end of the Herald's next turn, unable to willingly move closer to it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Floats on writhing tendrils, mouth working endlessly around a word it never finishes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tendrils paralyze on contact, patient as a spider's web."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts silently, the almost-utterance the only sound it makes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles prey slowly before committing, mouth still working the whole time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The unfinished word changes shape slightly each time it's attempted."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Nearby cultists finish its sentences for it, in unison, without being asked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The air around its mouth ripples faintly, like the word is already partly real."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight it's gotten one syllable further than ever before, and it knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "sky", "any"],"activity":["floating on a knot of writhing tendrils, mouth working around a word it will never finish", "hovering just out of reach, forever mid-utterance of a name"]},{"name":"Vault-Warden Ooze","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"geometric ooze sentry, absorbs anyone lacking the passphrase","flavor":"A perfectly geometric mass that patrols flooded vault corridors, absorbing anything that doesn't know the passphrase.","desc":"A perfect, glassy cube of ooze sized to fill its corridor exactly, patient as a lock. Anyone crossing without the passphrase simply doesn't come back out the other side.","traits":{"note": "Anyone crossing without the passphrase simply doesn't come back out the other side.", "actions": [{"name": "Geometric Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (3d6 + 2) Acid damage."}, {"name": "Absorb", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "The Ooze moves up to its speed. Each Large or smaller creature whose space it enters must make a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, the creature is engulfed, taking 12 (3d6 + 2) Acid damage and unable to breathe unless it can hold its breath, and is Restrained while engulfed. On a success, the creature is pushed 5 feet out of the Ooze's path."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A perfectly geometric mass sized to fill its corridor exactly, patient as a lock."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Anyone without the passphrase simply doesn't come back out the other side."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with unnerving precision, corners never rounded, edges never blurred."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something dissolving inside it is still faintly visible through the glassy surface."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols on a fixed schedule known only to whoever set the passphrase."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The passphrase it responds to hasn't been the same one for at least a generation."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its geometric perfection sharpens further the longer it goes unfed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's begun absorbing things that speak the passphrase correctly anyway."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["patrolling a flooded vault corridor sized to fill it exactly", "waiting, patient as a lock, for something without the passphrase"]},{"name":"Basalt Geometer-Scout","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"scout construct, surveys rooms ahead of angle-warping work","flavor":"A lighter cousin of the geometer-constructs, sent ahead to survey rooms before the angle-work begins.","desc":"Smaller and faster than its master-shape, it moves ahead through rooms before the angle-warping work begins, surveying corners with a stillness that has nothing curious in it.","traits":{"note": "It surveys before the real geometer arrives — seeing it means the angle-work is coming soon.", "actions": [{"name": "Fearsome Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Terrifying Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The Scout fixes its gaze on one creature within 30 ft. that can see it. The target must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition until the end of the Scout's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A lighter cousin of the geometer-constructs, sent ahead to survey rooms first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surveys corners with a stillness that has nothing curious in it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves faster than its master-shape, built for scouting rather than the work itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks walls with faint scratches only it seems able to read."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the instant it's finished surveying, uninterested in a fight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The corners it's marked start looking subtly wrong within a day of its visit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its scratched marks form angles that don't exist in the room it made them in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The angle-warping work it's scouting for is scheduled to begin very soon."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["surveying a room's corners before the angle-warping work begins", "moving ahead of its master-shape with a stillness that has nothing curious in it"]},{"name":"Deep-Kin War Priest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"fish-folk-archpriest","summary":"gilled war-priest, blesses spears with wrongly-moving water","flavor":"Leads coastal-breed raids with hymnals bound in dried skin no one asks about; blesses spears with water that shouldn't move like that.","desc":"It blesses its congregation's spears by dipping them in water that moves against the current, murmuring approval each time the water disobeys gravity the way it's supposed to.","traits":{"note": "It murmurs approval whenever the water disobeys gravity the way it's supposed to — a tell that the blessing's taken.", "actions": [{"name": "Strange Scepter", "replaces": "Strange Scepter", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Cold damage as blessed water lashes from the scepter's tip."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The War Priest casts a spell, drawing power from water blessed against its own current."}, {"name": "Wrong-Current Blessing", "text": "The War Priest touches its scepter to up to three willing creatures within 10 ft. Each blessed creature gains 10 temporary hit points and its weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Cold damage until the start of the War Priest's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blesses spears by dipping them in water that moves against the current."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a hymnal bound in dried skin no one in the congregation asks about."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Murmurs approval each time the water disobeys gravity correctly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads raids from the rear, blessing weapons rather than swinging one first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks to the congregation in a cadence that mimics tide, rising and falling."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The hymnal's pages are damp no matter how long it's been out of water."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Water blessed by it keeps moving wrong for hours after the ritual ends."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight's blessing is meant for something bigger than spears, and the water knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["blessing spears by dipping them in water that moves against the current", "leading a coastal raid with a hymnal bound in skin no one asks about"]},{"name":"Amalgam of Borrowed Limbs","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-howdah","model":"ogre-howdah","summary":"tide-stitched limb-amalgam, mismatched parts unnoticed by it","flavor":"Stitched together from whatever the tide brought — none of the limbs match, and it hasn't noticed yet.","desc":"Stitched together from parts that never belonged to the same body, none of them matching in color, texture, or apparent age — and it moves them all without the faintest awareness anything's mismatched.","traits":{"note": "None of its limbs share color, texture, or age — and it hasn't noticed anything's mismatched.", "actions": [{"name": "Tide-Stitched Greatclub", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Fling Rider", "replaces": "Fling Rider (1/Turn)", "text": "1/Turn. The Amalgam grabs a Medium or smaller creature it's Grappling and throws it up to 30 feet in a random direction. The creature takes 10 (3d6) Bludgeoning damage and lands Prone, or half as much damage if it lands in water."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stitched together from parts that never belonged to the same body, unmatched in color and age."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves all its limbs without the faintest awareness anything's mismatched."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "New pieces have been added recently, still paler than the rest of it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Test-flexes an arm mid-fight like it's still getting used to the fit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of brine and older things the tide gave up long ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of its limbs occasionally moves half a second before the rest decides to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A hand it's wearing still twitches in a way that suggests unfinished business of its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's looking for one more piece to complete itself, and it thinks the party's carrying it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["coast", "sea", "ruins"],"activity":["moving a body of stitched, mismatched parts without any awareness they don't match", "dragging whatever the tide last brought, testing if it still fits"]},{"name":"Star-Spawn Broodcaller","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-warrior","model":"astral-raider-warrior","summary":"star-spawn summoner, calls splinters to its side","flavor":"Sings a summoning fragment that draws smaller splinters from wherever they've been hiding; never fights alone if it can help it.","desc":"It raises both arms and calls, a sound pitched too high to be entirely vocal, and small star-flecked shapes come skittering toward it from wherever they'd been hiding.","traits":{"note": "It never fights alone if it can help it — expect splinters answering the call from nearby.", "actions": [{"name": "Psi Blade", "replaces": "Psi Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Force damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Broodcaller casts a spell, channeling it through the same pitch it uses to summon."}, {"name": "Summon Splinters", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Broodcaller calls in a sound pitched too high to be entirely vocal. Up to two Gravel-Star Broodmite Swarms (or similar small star-spawn) within 1 mile that can hear the call begin moving toward the Broodcaller at their fastest speed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Raises both arms to sing a fragment that draws smaller splinters from hiding."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never fights alone if it can help it, calling reinforcements before the first blow lands."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The call it makes is pitched too high to be entirely vocal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small star-flecked shapes answer from wherever they'd been hiding, skittering close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Falls silent and watchful the moment its splinters arrive, letting them work."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The summoning call carries clearly through solid stone, unmuffled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Splinters answering its call arrive slightly aged, as if the trip took longer for them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something much larger than the splinters is starting to answer the same call, from further away."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental"],"activity":["calling in a sound pitched too high to be entirely vocal, both arms raised", "watching small star-flecked shapes skitter toward it from hiding"]},{"name":"Choir-Grown Ooze Sculptor","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"self-sculpting ooze mimic, dissolves interrupting witnesses","flavor":"Reshapes itself into crude mimicries of drowned architecture, humming while it works, dissolving anyone who interrupts.","desc":"It reshapes its own surface into passable mimicry of whatever's nearby — furniture, a person, a doorway — right up until it dissolves whoever noticed the resemblance too late.","traits":{"note": "It dissolves anyone who notices the resemblance too late — the mimicry is the trap, not decoration.", "actions": [{"name": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "replaces": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (3d8 + 2) Acid damage."}, {"name": "Mimic Reshape", "text": "The Sculptor spends its move reshaping part of itself into a passable mimicry of a nearby object, doorway, or humanoid shape. Until it attacks or moves again, creatures must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom (Perception or Insight) check to recognize it as the Sculptor rather than the real thing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reshapes its surface into crude mimicry of whatever's nearby, humming while it works."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dissolves whoever interrupts it before the resemblance is even fully noticed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers mimicking furniture over people, a smaller cruelty saved for later."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The hum it makes while sculpting is almost pleasant, almost a lullaby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint humming residue on whatever it's recently mimicked."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun mimicking things that no longer exist anywhere nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A mimicked shape occasionally holds its form even after the Sculptor moves away from it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight it's mimicking someone the party actually knows, and it's very good at it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "cave"],"activity":["reshaping its own surface into a crude mimicry of nearby architecture, humming while it works", "dissolving whoever interrupts it a moment too late to notice the resemblance"]},{"name":"Vault-Drift Overseer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough-boss","model":"tough-boss","summary":"veteran cult overseer, whip woven from something not-quite-rope","flavor":"Generations deep in cult service, cracking a whip woven from something that used to be rope and now isn't quite.","desc":"A whip made from something that isn't quite rope trails from one hand, coiling with a faint wet sheen even when it's not being used. It's worn its authority in the vaults longer than most of its thralls have been alive.","traits":{"note": "The whip coils with a faint wet sheen even at rest — it's worn its authority longer than most of its thralls have been alive.", "actions": [{"name": "Warhammer", "replaces": "Warhammer", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 11 (2d10) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Not-Quite-Rope Lash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 15 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or have disadvantage on its next attack roll, distracted by the whip's faint wet sheen."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks a whip made from something that isn't quite rope anymore, wet even at rest."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Worn its authority in the vaults longer than most of its thralls have been alive."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Generations deep in cult service, moves with a veteran's economy of motion."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rarely raises its own weapon first, letting thralls absorb the opening blow."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps meticulous count of who's disappointed it, and when."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The whip flexes on its own between uses, as if testing its own grip."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers overseers who served here before it was even born."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whip is starting to lead rather than follow its wielder's hand."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["cracking a whip woven from something that used to be rope and now isn't quite", "standing watch over thralls it's outlived by generations of cult service"]},{"name":"Reef-Choked Behemoth-Calf","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-crocodile","model":"giant-crocodile","summary":"coral-armored guard-beast, bred to protect flooded vaults","flavor":"A drowned-world beast bred to guard the choir's flooded vaults, coral growing through its hide like armor.","desc":"Coral has grown thick over its hide in armored plates, bred generation over generation for exactly one purpose — standing between the vault door and whatever's trying to reach it.","traits":{"note": "Bred generation over generation for exactly one purpose — guarding, not hunting.", "actions": [{"name": "Armored Bite-and-Tail", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Behemoth-Calf makes two attacks, using its Bite or Tail in any combination."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coral has grown thick over its hide in armored plates, bred for exactly one purpose."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands between the vault door and whatever's trying to reach it, unmoving."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bred generation over generation, guarding rather than hunting by instinct."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores minor damage the way a wall ignores weather."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizes the vault's rightful visitors by scent, letting them pass unbothered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The coral plating regrows visibly thicker after each fight it survives."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to know exactly how long it's stood guard, down to the day."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its bloodline is running out, and this may be the last calf bred to replace it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "cave"],"activity":["standing armored guard between the vault door and whatever's trying to reach it", "testing coral-plated hide against the nearest hard surface, unbothered"]},{"name":"Nine-Eyed Cyst","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"nine-eyed stalk-growth, each eye sees a different version of the room","flavor":"A budding growth of eyes on a fleshy stalk, each seeing a slightly different version of the same room.","desc":"A stalk-like growth studded with nine eyes, each one apparently seeing a slightly different version of the same room — and disagreeing, silently and constantly, about which version is real.","traits":{"note": "Each of its nine eyes sees a slightly different version of the same room — worth exploiting if you can tell which one is confused.", "actions": [{"name": "Nine-Eyed Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cyst makes two attacks, using its Claw or Weird Insight in any combination."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Weird Insight", "replaces": "Weird Insight", "text": "The Cyst casts Arcane Eye, requiring no material components, one of its nine eyes detaching briefly to scout."}, {"name": "Rotting Gaze", "replaces": "Rotting Gaze", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can see the Cyst's eyes must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stalk-like growth studded with nine eyes, each seeing a slightly different version of the room."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The eyes disagree silently and constantly about which version is real."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Turns each eye independently, tracking multiple targets at once."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally one eye closes entirely, as if losing an internal argument."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows slowly from a fixed root, more plant than animal in habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A tenth eye is budding low on the stalk, not yet opened."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Each eye's version of the room slowly bleeds into what's actually there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The eyes have finally agreed on something, and they're all looking at the same target now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "planar"],"activity":["disagreeing silently and constantly about which version of the room is real", "budding a tenth eye that hasn't opened yet, low on the stalk"]},{"name":"Choir-Marked Berserker","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"gladiator","summary":"arena fighter, scars spell hymn fragments across its back","flavor":"Fights in an arena the cult built beneath the tide line, scars spelling out fragments of hymn across its back.","desc":"Scars crisscross its back in patterns too regular to be accidental — read close, they spell out fragments of the hymn, carved in one bad night at a time.","traits":{"note": "Its scars spell fragments of the hymn, carved one bad night at a time — the pattern is deliberate, not decorative.", "actions": [{"name": "Arena Spearwork", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Berserker makes two attacks, using its Spear or Shield Bash in any combination."}, {"name": "Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 10 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage, or 11 (1d10 + 5) Piercing damage if used with two hands in melee."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights in an arena the cult built beneath the tide line."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scars crisscross its back in patterns too regular to be accidental."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Read close, the scars spell fragments of the hymn, one bad night at a time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Traces the scars with a fingertip before every bout, like a ritual."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights for the crowd as much as the kill, playing to an audience below the waterline."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "New scars appear between fights without anyone claiming to have cut them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hymn on its back is one verse further along than it was a season ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's close to a scar that would complete the hymn, and the arena crowd wants to see it finished."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "sea"],"activity":["fighting in an arena the cult built beneath the tide line", "tracing hymn-scars across its own back with a fingertip before a bout"]},{"name":"Devouring Choir-Cyst","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"shrine-fed cyst, grows a new mouth per swallowed prayer","flavor":"Feeds on offerings left at flooded shrines, growing new mouths for every prayer it swallows.","desc":"Fed on the shrine's leftovers for years, it's grown a fresh mouth for every prayer it's swallowed — a dozen now, none matching, all of them hungry at once.","traits":{"note": "It's grown a mouth for every prayer it's swallowed — a dozen now, none matching, all hungry at once.", "actions": [{"name": "Many-Mouthed Feeding", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cyst makes three attacks, using its Bite or Tentacle in any combination."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Tentacle Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feeds on shrine leftovers, a fresh mouth grown for every prayer swallowed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dozen mismatched mouths now, all of them hungry at once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lurks near flooded shrines, patient for the next offering."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each mouth seems to prefer a different kind of prayer, favoring some over others."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows sluggish between feedings, quickened by the smell of fresh offerings."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of its mouths mutters back fragments of the prayers it's eaten."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its newest mouth hasn't stopped growing yet, and it's already bigger than the others."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to swallow a prayer that was never meant to be answered."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["feeding on shrine offerings, a fresh mouth grown for every prayer swallowed", "working a dozen mismatched mouths at once, all of them hungry"]},{"name":"Star-Chewed Roc-Kin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-axe-beak","model":"giant-axe-beak","summary":"drift-touched sky-beast, shadow lags behind its own flight","flavor":"A sky-beast whose migratory path drifted through somewhere it shouldn't have; it still flies, but its shadow lags a half-second behind.","desc":"A vast bird-shape that doesn't fly so much as arrive, its shadow crawling into place a full second after the body that's supposed to cast it.","traits":{"note": "Its shadow lags behind its own flight — a visible tell that something about its migration went wrong.", "actions": [{"name": "Drift-Lagged Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Roc-Kin makes two attacks, using its Sharpened Beak or Talons in any combination."}, {"name": "Sharpened Beak", "replaces": "Sharpened Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be Grappled (escape DC 15)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its migratory path drifted through somewhere it shouldn't have, and it never fully returned."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't fly so much as arrive, its shadow lagging a full second behind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still flocks with normal sky-beasts, apparently unaware anything's changed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Casts two shadows briefly at dusk, before one catches up to the other."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vast bird-shape, wingspan alone enough to blot out a stretch of sky."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its call arrives audibly before its beak finishes opening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The lagging shadow occasionally moves independently of the body casting it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The gap between it and its shadow is widening, and neither seems in a hurry to close it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sky", "planar"],"activity":["arriving rather than flying, its shadow lagging a full second behind", "circling migratory paths that drifted through somewhere it shouldn't have"]},{"name":"Wrong-Season Roper","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"roper","model":"roper","summary":"drift-grown ropy ambusher, strands taste of a closed mouth","flavor":"Grows in caverns where the drift touched the stone; its strands taste like the inside of a closed mouth.","desc":"Grown wrong out of the drift-touched stone, its ropy strands hang loose until they don't — the surviving taste memory is of something that tried to close its mouth and never got to finish.","traits":{"note": "The taste memory left in its strands is of something that tried to close its mouth and never got to finish.", "actions": [{"name": "Reeling Bite-and-Pull", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Roper makes one Bite attack and can use Reel."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 50 ft. Hit: the target is Grappled (escape DC 15) if the Roper doesn't already have six creatures grappled."}, {"name": "Reel", "replaces": "Reel", "text": "The Roper pulls each creature Grappled by it up to 25 feet straight toward itself."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grown wrong out of drift-touched stone, ropy strands hanging loose until they don't."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its taste memory is of something that tried to close its mouth and never finished."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blends nearly perfectly with cavern stalactites when motionless."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reels prey in with patient, unhurried strength."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strands regrow within hours if severed, always the same wrong length."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The stone around it has started growing the same wrong shape it did."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its strands occasionally taste of a season that hasn't happened here yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something is growing wrong further down the same cavern, and it's much bigger than the Roper."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "ruins"],"activity":["hanging loose strands until something warm-blooded gets close, then reeling it in", "waiting in drift-touched stone, strands tasting like the inside of a closed mouth"]},{"name":"Reef-Fused War Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"drift-touched water elemental, moves with unnerving intent","flavor":"Water given form by the same wrongness that grows coral over drowned bones; it moves like tide, but with intent.","desc":"Water moves through it with clear, unnerving intent, currents folding into fists and then unfolding again, never quite settling into a shape that stays still long enough to be sure of.","traits":{"note": "It moves like tide, but with clear intent — the wrongness that grows coral over drowned bones shaped this thing too.", "actions": [{"name": "Intent Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Whelm", "replaces": "Whelm (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. Each creature in the Elemental's space must make a DC 15 Strength saving throw. On a failure, a creature takes 13 (3d8) Bludgeoning damage and is Grappled (escape DC 15); on a success, it takes half damage and isn't grappled. Until the grapple ends, the target is Restrained and unable to breathe unless it can hold its breath."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Water given form by the same wrongness that grows coral over drowned bones."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves like tide, but with clear, unnerving intent."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Currents fold into fists and unfold again, never settling still."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries flecks of coral suspended inside its churning body."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rises out of still water with no warning ripple beforehand."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates before certain attacks, as if considering rather than merely flowing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water composing it occasionally moves against a current that isn't there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's begun holding a shape for longer stretches, like it's practicing being solid."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "elemental"],"activity":["moving with unnerving intent, currents folding into fists and unfolding again", "never quite settling into a shape that stays still long enough to be sure of"]},{"name":"Coral-Throned Cult Matron","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"performer-maestro","summary":"reef-throned choir conductor, directs worshippers like an orchestra","flavor":"Conducts the drowned hymn from a throne grown out of living reef, directing worshippers like an orchestra of dread.","desc":"She sits enthroned in living coral, directing her congregation with slow, precise motions — like a conductor, if the orchestra were made of people and the music were a hymn none of them chose to learn.","traits":{"note": "She conducts her congregation like an orchestra — the music is a hymn none of them chose to learn.", "actions": [{"name": "Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Psychic damage as the drowned hymn cuts alongside the blade."}, {"name": "Beguiling Song", "replaces": "Beguiling Song", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can hear the Matron must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition until the end of the Matron's next turn, compelled to move toward her."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Matron casts a spell, conducting it with the same precise motions she uses to direct her congregation."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits enthroned in living coral, directing worshippers with slow, precise motions."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Conducts her congregation like an orchestra playing a hymn none chose to learn."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rarely rises from the throne, letting devotion come to her instead."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks softly, forcing listeners to lean in and quiet themselves to hear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The coral throne has grown to fit her exactly, over years of sitting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Worshippers move in time with her gestures even when she isn't looking at them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The throne's coral pulses faintly in rhythm with her own heartbeat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's rehearsing a new movement for the hymn, and the whole congregation is about to learn it at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "ruins"],"activity":["directing worshippers with slow, precise motions like conducting an orchestra of dread", "sitting enthroned in living coral, unbothered by anything short of open defiance"]},{"name":"Star-Warped Chimera-Thing","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"triple-fused star-warped beast, heads disagree about its nature","flavor":"Three creatures fused by the same accident that dropped its kin from the sky, each head disagreeing about what it is.","desc":"Three heads fused onto one body, each pulling faintly in a different direction, each apparently convinced the other two belong to something else entirely.","traits":{"note": "Each head is convinced the other two belong to something else entirely — a rift you can sometimes exploit mid-fight.", "actions": [{"name": "Three-Headed Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chimera-Thing makes three attacks: one with its Bite, one with its Claw, and one with its Ram."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Starlight Breath", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One head exhales a 15-foot cone of collapsed starlight. Each creature in that area must make a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) Radiant damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three heads fused onto one body, each pulling faintly in a different direction."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head is convinced the other two belong to something else entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Argues audibly with itself between attacks, briefly distracted from prey."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head sleeps while the other two remain alert, rotating without pattern."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fused by the same accident that dropped its kin from the sky."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The heads occasionally vote, out loud, on which direction to go."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One head has started speaking a language the other two don't recognize."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The three heads are close to finally agreeing on something, and none of them will like what it means."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "sky", "elemental"],"activity":["three heads pulling faintly in different directions, each certain the others are wrong", "disagreeing about its own nature loud enough to be heard from outside"]},{"name":"Choir-Bound Invisible Watcher","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"bound invisible hunter, tracks lapsed believers","flavor":"Bound to the choir by a pact it can't remember making, hunting silently for anyone who stops believing on schedule.","desc":"You never see it arrive. You feel the air change first, a pressure like being watched from somewhere just behind your shoulder, tracking whoever's fallen behind on their devotions.","traits":{"note": "You feel the air change before you see anything — a pressure like being watched from just behind your shoulder.", "actions": [{"name": "Unseen Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Watcher makes two attacks, using its Wind Swipe or Vortex in any combination."}, {"name": "Wind Swipe", "replaces": "Wind Swipe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Vortex", "replaces": "Vortex", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be Restrained by a whirling pocket of air until the start of the Watcher's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bound to the choir by a pact it can't remember making, hunting on schedule."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "You never see it arrive — the air changes first, a pressure like being watched."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tracks whoever's fallen behind on their devotions, patient about the timing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its passage stirs dust and loose paper without ever showing a shape."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits just behind a shoulder for long minutes before ever striking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The pact binding it has started fraying, and it's begun hunting off-schedule."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It can be heard breathing on cold nights, though nothing visible does the breathing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's close to remembering who bound it, and it doesn't sound pleased about the answer."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "elemental", "any"],"activity":["tracking whoever's fallen behind on devotions, air changing before it arrives", "waiting just behind a shoulder, unseen, bound to a pact it can't remember making"]},{"name":"Bone-Grown Cathedral Skeleton","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-skeleton","model":"minotaur-skeleton","summary":"architecture-fused drowned guardian skeleton","flavor":"A drowned guardian whose bones have fused with the architecture it once protected; moving it means moving the wall.","desc":"Architecture has fused into its bones over however long it's stood — a fragment of column here, a piece of drowned stonework there — until it's less a skeleton wearing armor than a building that learned to walk.","traits":{"note": "Moving it means moving the wall it once protected — expect structural consequences when it charges.", "actions": [{"name": "Architectural Assault", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage, and if the target is Large or smaller it must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Architecture has fused into its bones, fragments of column and drowned stonework alike."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Less a skeleton wearing armor than a building that learned to walk."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moving it visibly strains the nearby structure, cracks spreading with each step."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guarded this same architecture long before it fused into the bones themselves."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sheds small chips of masonry with every swing of its arms."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The fused stonework rearranges itself slightly between fights, like it's still settling."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Damaging its bone-and-stone body sometimes cracks the wall three rooms away instead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole structure it's fused to seems ready to come down with it, on purpose."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing as less a skeleton wearing armor than a building that learned to walk", "fused so deep into the architecture that moving it means moving the wall"]},{"name":"Void-Trained Duelist","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mind-thief","model":"mind-thief","summary":"advanced void-monk duelist, fights blind and never misses","flavor":"Advanced past the ascetics in the not-looking discipline; it fights with eyes fully closed and somehow never misses.","desc":"Its eyes are wrapped, same as its lesser brethren, but its blade never seems to miss regardless — trained past sight into something that reads intention instead.","traits":{"note": "It's trained past sight entirely — it reads intention instead, which changes what countering it means.", "actions": [{"name": "Blind Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be Grappled (escape DC 15)."}, {"name": "Mind Blast", "replaces": "Mind Blast (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature in a 60-foot cone must make a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) Psychic damage on a failure and having the Stunned condition until the end of the Duelist's next turn, or taking half damage on a success."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Duelist casts a spell without sighting the target, tracking it by intention alone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Advanced past the ascetics in the not-looking discipline, eyes wrapped and unnecessary."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights with eyes fully closed and somehow never misses."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trained past sight into something that reads intention instead."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with unsettling economy, no wasted motion, no hesitation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks rarely, letting the wrapped eyes do the intimidating."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It can tell a lie from the truth by the shift in someone's intention alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It parries attacks that haven't been telegraphed yet, a half-beat early."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's begun sensing intentions from well outside the range a blade could ever reach."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "any"],"activity":["fighting with eyes fully closed, blade never seeming to miss", "reading intention rather than sight, trained past the ascetics who taught it"]},{"name":"Warlord of the Sunken Court","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-giant","model":"stone-giant","summary":"coral-grown giant warlord, sworn to the drowned choir","flavor":"A giant sworn to the drowned choir generations back, its stonework now grown through with the same wrong coral as the vaults it guards.","desc":"Coral has grown into the seams of its armor the way barnacles grow on a hull left too long at anchor. It swore itself to the choir generations ago and has never once been asked to explain why.","traits":{"note": "Its coral-grown armor has begun to fuse to its own hide; nothing short of the vault opening will make it leave this post.", "actions": [{"name": "Coral-Fisted Blows", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Warlord makes two attacks with its Choir Maul."}, {"name": "Choir Maul", "replaces": "Stone Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Drowned Reef Shard", "replaces": "Boulder", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60/240 ft., one target. Hit: 27 (4d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the coral shrapnel opens a wound that deals 7 (2d6) Piercing damage at the start of the target's next turn unless treated."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chants under its breath in a call-and-response only the drowned choir would recognize."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coral has sealed one arm nearly straight; it compensates by leading with its club."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the barnacled shell of a helm two sizes too small, cracked at the crown."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Paces the same forty-foot line, generation after generation, waiting for relief that never comes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice has gone gravelly and slow, like stone grinding on stone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes the vault's original owner's crest and hesitates half a second before attacking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "When struck hard enough, coral polyps briefly bloom pale light along the crack."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Believes, wrongly, that the vault door is already open behind it and fights like there's nothing left to lose."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "planar"],"activity":["standing guard over the drowned vault, coral fusing slowly into its knee-joints", "conducting the choir's chant with a raised stone club, off-tempo but certain"]},{"name":"Cyst-Blossomed Behemoth","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"regenerating many-headed horror, sprouts eyes where heads regrow","flavor":"Each severed head buds a fresh eye before it regrows, until the thing sees in more directions than it can process.","desc":"Wherever a head is severed, a fresh eye blinks open in the wound before the new head finishes growing back — an unsettling little preview of what's coming.","traits":{"note": "Severing a head only makes it worse; a new eye watches the wound the whole time the head regrows.", "actions": [{"name": "Regrowth Frenzy", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Behemoth makes three Budding Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Budding Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Piercing damage. If this attack reduces a head to 0 hit points, a new eye blooms in the wound before the head regrows at the start of the Behemoth's next turn."}, {"name": "Overseeing Gaze", "text": "1/Day. One creature the Behemoth can see within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom save or have Disadvantage on attack rolls against the Behemoth until the start of its next turn, unnerved by the number of eyes now watching it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing two heads entirely, both stumps crowded with newly blinking eyes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head lags behind the others, still learning to snap on command."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the lumbering patience of something that's never really been hurried."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cyst-blooms have gone a sickly yellow, weeping something that isn't quite pus."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a torn tent canvas snagged on one horn from an earlier meal."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every eye it's grown so far is fixed on the same target, unblinking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A head regrows wrong — human-shaped, briefly, before the cysts correct it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "So many eyes have bloomed it seems to be seeing something behind the party that isn't there yet."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "deeplands", "any"],"activity":["dragging its bulk through the muck while a fresh eye blinks open on a half-grown neck", "turning slowly in place, testing each new eye against the light before trusting it"]},{"name":"Grand Cantor of the Drowned Court","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"archpriest","summary":"tri-voiced high priest, speaks as three generations at once","flavor":"Speaks in a chord of three voices at once, each a different generation of the same office; the congregation answers all three.","desc":"When it speaks, three distinct voices layer under each other — young, old, and something in between — as if three generations of the same office are speaking through one throat at once.","traits":{"note": "can address up to three different targets simultaneously with its three voices, each carrying a separate effect (command, ward, curse) in a single action"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-ordination of a new junior cantor and doesn't want witnesses to the ceremony."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its three voices is arguing with the other two, audibly, over doctrine."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a sealed hymnal it refuses to let anyone else touch or read."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A congregant has gone missing and the Cantor is quietly, personally, looking for them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rehearsing a passage that keeps making the youngest of its three voices falter."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It recognizes a party member's voice from a hymn sung years ago and wants to know why."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its middle voice has started speaking half a second before the other two, like it knows what's coming."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's been asked by the choir above to identify a fourth voice worth adding — and it's listening to the party sing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "sea"],"activity":["leading the drowned congregation in a chord of three overlapping voices", "correcting a junior cantor's pitch mid-hymn without breaking its own line"]},{"name":"Fathom-Deep Devourer","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"cockatrice-regent","model":"cockatrice-regent","summary":"ancient depth-lurker, gaze convinces victims stillness was the plan","flavor":"Older than the vault it lairs in, its gaze doesn't petrify so much as convince the victim that stillness was always the plan.","desc":"Ancient, patient, its gaze alone convinces prey that stillness was always the plan — muscles locking mid-stride, breath slowing, right up until it's far too late to reconsider.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Stillness Was the Plan", "text": "a target that fails a save against its gaze believes it chose to stop moving; it isn't restrained and can act normally in every way except moving from its space, until it takes damage"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hasn't moved from this exact spot in longer than anyone alive has been counting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye is milk-white and blind; it favors its good side when it finally turns."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barnacled scale plates make a low grinding sound with every slow breath."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surrounded by the stone-still shapes of things that stopped moving long ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its patience reads as boredom — it's watched too many intruders make the same mistakes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already decided which of the party will go still first and hasn't looked away since."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its gaze seems to slow time itself near it, dust hanging a moment too long in the water."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something older than the vault has just shifted somewhere below it, and the Devourer is, for once, listening instead of watching."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands", "cave"],"activity":["lying motionless at the vault floor, patient as the stone around it", "fixing one slow eye on an intruder who has already stopped moving"]},{"name":"Star-Warped Amalgam Lord","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"heavily-reshaped cult champion, original species long forgotten","flavor":"A cult champion so thoroughly reshaped that its original species is a debated footnote among its own worshippers.","desc":"Whatever species it started as is long gone under layers of reshaping — scales here, chitin there, something that might once have been fur — until only the confident bearing of a champion survives intact.","traits":{"note": "Its Yuan-ti-form spells only function while it holds that particular borrowed shape — it may shift mid-fight to access them.", "actions": [{"name": "Amalgam Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Lord makes one Layered Bite attack and one Constrict attack."}, {"name": "Layered Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16)."}, {"name": "Reshaping Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Poison Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature in a 15-foot cone makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 18 (4d8) Poison damage on a failure and half as much on a success. A creature that fails also has Disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn, its own body briefly uncertain what shape to defend."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A worshipper asks, sincerely, what it looked like before the reshaping — it doesn't remember."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm is visibly a different texture from the rest, chitin against scale."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks with the confident cadence of a champion, regardless of which face it's wearing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a private shrine to whatever it thinks it used to be, tended by no one else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sheds a patch of scale mid-conversation without breaking its sentence."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Reshaping again, visibly, mid-fight — it's testing a form it hasn't tried yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one moment its original shape flickers through — familiar to someone, unplaceable to everyone else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its worshippers have started a schism over which of its many faces is the true one, and it's letting them fight it out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court over worshippers who no longer remember what species it started as", "shedding a patch of borrowed scale to reveal something else underneath"]},{"name":"Vault-Keeper of the Drowned Seal","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"door-guardian golem, scarred by every prior attempt to pass","flavor":"Built to guard a door that shouldn't open; every scar in its clay hide is a place someone already tried.","desc":"Every failed attempt to force this door has left a scar across its clay hide, a record of every trespasser it's ever stopped, worn like a tally it's proud of.","traits":{"note": "It never pursues past the threshold it guards — retreat past the doorway and the Vault-Keeper simply resets to its post.", "actions": [{"name": "Scarred Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Vault-Keeper makes two Tally Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Tally Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and the clay records the blow as a fresh scar, granting the Vault-Keeper a cumulative +1 bonus to this damage roll (max +5) for the rest of the encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Covered edge to edge in scars, none deep enough to have ever worked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One scar is shaped, unmistakably, like a dropped weapon it once absorbed whole."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the slow inevitability of something that has never once needed to hurry."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hairline crack runs down its chest — the closest anyone's ever come."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Traces its own scars with one finger between fights, almost fondly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes a tool or weapon a party member carries from a previous failed attempt."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A scar briefly glows where an old spell struck it, echoing the effect weakly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's nearly full of scars — one more serious attempt and something underneath may finally crack loose."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["standing immovable before the sealed door, scarred clay catching the lamplight", "tracing a fresh gouge in its own hide as if grading the attempt that made it"]},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Herald-Prime","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"elder herald-beast, recites fragments younger heralds can't finish","flavor":"An elder herald whose throat has stretched to accommodate names centuries in the reciting; it finishes fragments the young ones can't.","desc":"Ancient among heralds, it recites the fragments the younger ones can't yet finish — long, resonant passages that seem to physically hurt something in its throat to produce.","traits":{"note": "Every fragment it recites brings it audibly closer to finishing the whole recitation — track how many rounds it's been allowed to speak uninterrupted.", "actions": [{"name": "Elder Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald-Prime makes one Bite attack and one Constrict attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 18) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Resonant Recitation (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Lightning Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Herald-Prime recites a fragment centuries in the reciting. Each creature in a 60-foot cone makes a DC 18 Constitution save, taking 45 (10d8) Lightning damage on a failure or half as much on a success. Constructs and undead in the area have Disadvantage on this save, the fragment older than their making."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's teaching a much younger herald a passage and doesn't want to be interrupted mid-lesson."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its throat is visibly swollen from reciting; finishing today's fragment will cost it dearly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a cracked tablet of the fragment it's been assigned, checking it obsessively."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A younger herald nearby keeps failing the same line and the Prime is losing patience."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's older than the ruin it's found in and remembers what stood here before."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's just finished a fragment none of the younger heralds have ever heard completed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The next fragment in its recitation is one the party has heard somewhere before, badly translated."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's within a handful of fragments of finishing the entire recitation, and something vast is now listening along with it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "sky", "ruins"],"activity":["reciting a fragment of the drowned language that visibly strains its throat", "correcting a younger herald's failed cadence with practiced, aching patience"]},{"name":"Rakshasa of the Drowned Bargain","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"deal-making fiend, wears any face to get terms accepted","flavor":"Made a private deal with the choir long before the cult existed; it wears whatever face gets the terms accepted.","desc":"It wears whatever face gets its terms accepted, switching mid-sentence if the current one isn't landing — courteous, patient, and utterly without a true face underneath any of them.","traits":{"note": "any bargain it strikes is binding on its side but written with a loophole the party won't notice until it matters — DM should have the exact loophole ready before the deal is offered"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-negotiation with a desperate merchant and doesn't appreciate interruption."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a satchel of old, honored contracts it likes to reread when bored."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wearing a face that doesn't quite fit its own expressions yet — a recent acquisition."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Owes the choir a favor it's been quietly stalling on repaying for years."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone nearby signed something they shouldn't have, and the Rakshasa is here to collect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers the party a genuinely useful deal, terms scrupulously fair on paper."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Switches faces three times in one conversation, testing which one the party trusts most."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A contract it signed centuries ago is coming due tonight, and it very much does not want witnesses."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar", "any"],"activity":["negotiating terms in a borrowed face, switching expression mid-sentence", "reviewing an old contract by candlelight, satisfied with how it's aged"]},{"name":"Colossal Sunken Guardian","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"titanic coral-fused golem, footsteps sound like a receding tide","flavor":"A titan of drowned stone, moss and coral fused so deep into its joints that its footsteps sound like a tide going out.","desc":"Titanic, coral-fused, its footsteps land with a low boom that sounds less like stone hitting stone and more like a tide receding somewhere far below.","traits":{"note": "Its footfalls carry for miles through stone and water alike — anything nearby will hear it coming long before it arrives.", "actions": [{"name": "Titanic Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Guardian makes two Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 25 (3d12 + 7) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Reef-Bolt", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +12, range 120 ft., one target. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 7) Force damage as a shard of fused coral and stone tears free and launches at the target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moss and barnacle have claimed one whole shoulder, slowing that arm's swing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its patrol route is exact to the step, unchanged in living memory."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crack across its chest weeps trapped seawater with every stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small reef fish have made a home in the crevices of its plating."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with a low, tidal boom that can be heard through stone from a hundred feet off."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's paused mid-patrol, listening for something that isn't the party."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A fused eye embedded in its shoulder tracks independently of the rest of it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The tide itself seems to be rising with its steps, as if the two are somehow the same motion."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins", "coast"],"activity":["patrolling the vault approach, each footstep landing like a distant retreating tide", "standing motionless long enough that moss has begun to claim its shoulder"]},{"name":"Void-Ascendant Grandmaster","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"void-monk-psion","model":"void-monk-psion","summary":"perfected void-monk master, has forgotten its own god's face","flavor":"Perfected the discipline of not-looking so completely it has forgotten what its god even looks like — which may be the point.","desc":"Perfected past the point where doctrine matters, it moves with total, silent confidence — and has, by its own account, forgotten what its god's face even looked like to begin with.","traits":{"note": "Its discipline of not-looking makes it immune to being surprised or flanked easily — it perceives without needing sight.", "actions": [{"name": "Perfected Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grandmaster makes three Psychic Warp attacks."}, {"name": "Psychic Warp", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Psychic damage, and the Grandmaster may push the target 10 feet in a direction of its choice as space briefly folds around the blow."}, {"name": "Doctrine of Absence", "text": "1/Day. The Grandmaster becomes invisible and gains a flying speed of 40 feet until the start of its next turn, having perfected the art of simply not being looked at."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects a disciple's stance without opening its eyes, somehow certain of the error."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shrine has no idol, no image — just an empty alcove it bows to anyway."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks rarely, and only in the passive voice, as if avoiding responsibility for its own actions."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with total, silent confidence that unnerves onlookers more than any threat would."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its eyes closed even while eating, trusting touch over sight entirely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses before a fight, as if listening for permission from a god who never answers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its shadow moves independently, facing a direction its body doesn't."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something it forgot how to worship has just, faintly, noticed it again."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "sky", "any"],"activity":["holding a stance of total stillness, eyes closed against a god it's forgotten", "correcting a disciple's breathing with a single unhurried gesture"]},{"name":"Herald-Devourer of the Bishop's Court","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"doctrine-advisor and quiet devourer of the faithless","flavor":"Advises the bishops on doctrine while quietly consuming the ones whose faith wavers, calling it a mercy.","desc":"It counsels with a warm, reasonable voice, offering doctrine and correction in equal measure — and quietly consumes whoever it decides has stopped believing hard enough.","traits":{"note": "It only Banishing-Claws a target it has already marked as faithless in conversation — a target that hasn't spoken with it can't be affected by that action.", "actions": [{"name": "Advisory Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald-Devourer makes one Fiendish Burst attack and one Banishing Claw attack."}, {"name": "Fiendish Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft., one target. Hit: 21 (6d6) Force damage."}, {"name": "Banishing Claw (Requires Soul Tome)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage. If the target has been marked as faithless (a private judgment the Herald-Devourer makes in conversation), it must also succeed on a DC 16 Charisma save or be banished to a random location on another plane until the spell ends after 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-counsel with a bishop who has no idea what the advice is really for."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a private ledger marking which of the faithful have stopped believing hard enough."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in a warm, reasonable tone even while explaining why someone must be corrected."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A congregant has vanished after a private conversation with it, and no one else has noticed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It calls its consumption of the faithless a mercy, and seems to genuinely believe it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's evaluating a party member's convictions mid-conversation, testing for weak faith."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its advice to the bishop has started coming eerily true, word for word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The bishop it advises has just been marked faithless, and the Herald-Devourer is deciding how kind to be about it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["counseling a bishop on doctrine in a warm, reasonable voice", "quietly marking which of the faithful has stopped believing hard enough"]},{"name":"Sunk-Court Executioner","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"ultroloth","model":"ultroloth","summary":"internal cult enforcer, victims erased even from memory","flavor":"Handles the choir's internal discipline; those it visits are never spoken of by name again, only by the shape of their absence.","desc":"It doesn't kill loudly. Whoever it's sent for simply stops being remembered by the people who knew them — the body is almost an afterthought.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Erase From Memory", "text": "on a kill, NPCs who knew the victim gradually forget them over the following day unless something anchors the memory (a written record, an item, another PC's insistence) — narrative effect, DM adjudicates what breaks it"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been sent to erase a specific defector, and the party is standing between it and them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A congregant nearby is quietly, desperately, trying to remember a name that's slipping away."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves through the crowd untouched, as if the congregation has learned not to notice it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no weapon visibly drawn — it prefers the work to look accidental."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already marked its next target and is simply waiting for privacy."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A name it erased years ago has just resurfaced, unexpectedly, through the party."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It pauses, genuinely puzzled, that a name it erased is still being spoken aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's been ordered to erase someone the party considers a friend, tonight, quietly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "planar", "any"],"activity":["moving unnoticed through the congregation, erasing a name as it passes", "standing over an absence where someone used to be, satisfied with the quiet"]},{"name":"Amalgam Colossus of the Reef Deep","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"warship-sized fused colossus, hull studded with reef and eyes","flavor":"A worm the size of a warship, its segments studded with fused reef, eyes, and the odd intact ship's figurehead.","desc":"Bigger than a warship, its fused hull studded with centuries of reef growth and half-buried eyes that all seem to open at once when it finally decides to move.","traits":{"note": "Its fused hull carries the wreckage of ships it's swallowed whole — expect salvage-grade debris, not treasure, embedded in its segments.", "actions": [{"name": "Colossal Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus makes one Bite attack and one Tail Stinger attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 10 ft. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tail Stinger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 15 ft. Hit: 23 (3d10 + 6) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Reef-Fused Eyes", "text": "1/Day. The Colossus opens every embedded eye across its hull at once, gaining truesight out to 120 feet until the end of its next turn and negating any effect that would make it Blinded."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a half-buried ship's figurehead fused into its flank, still recognizable."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in slow, warship-length undulations that stir the seabed for a mile."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reef growth clatters and shifts audibly with every motion of its segments."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Most of its embedded eyes stay shut, blinking open only one at a time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a wake of dislodged coral and small startled fish behind it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A fused ship's bell somewhere in its hull rings faintly with each surge forward."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment all its eyes fix on the same distant point, as if remembering a course."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in its hull that isn't reef or wreckage has just started moving on its own."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands", "coast"],"activity":["surfacing slowly, its reef-studded hull shedding centuries of growth", "opening a hundred half-buried eyes at once, finally deciding to move"]},{"name":"Herald-Legion, Unified Voice","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"nalfeshnee","model":"nalfeshnee","summary":"fused mass of failed heralds, one throat that might finish","flavor":"Every herald that ever failed to finish its name, fused into one throat that finally might; the cult prays it never gets the chance.","desc":"A mass of failed heralds fused into one towering body, throats layered atop each other, close — so close — to finally finishing the syllable none of them managed alone.","traits":{"note": "if it ever completes the syllable (DM's call, a climax beat), the effect should be catastrophic and setting-relevant — this is a story trigger, not a routine attack"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its fused faces is, distinguishably, still trying to warn people away."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragging the half-formed remains of a herald that hasn't finished joining yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The cult that made it is here too, desperately trying to keep it contained."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fragment of a name it's fused from is one a party member might recognize."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's straining toward finishing a syllable that gets audibly closer every round it's alive."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of its throats briefly breaks free of the chorus to say something almost coherent."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It pauses mid-fight, as if listening to itself finish the syllable somewhere else, first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's one heartbeat from finishing the word, and every cultist present has just started praying it fails."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "any", "ruins"],"activity":["straining every fused throat toward the syllable none of them finished alone", "advancing on legs that used to belong to different heralds entirely"]},{"name":"The Unfinished Cathedral-Made-Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"the-unfinished-cathedral-made-flesh","summary":"animated drowned-cathedral golem, walks toward the sea","flavor":"The congregation finally built their temple, and the temple got up. It walks toward the sea on legs made of pews, ringing bells no one installed.","desc":"Stone and stained glass hold roughly cathedral-shaped as it walks, slow and deliberate, toward the sea — an unfinished building that decided to finish the pilgrimage itself.","traits":{"note": "It is walking a pilgrimage to the sea and will not be turned from that course by anything short of destruction — expect it to keep moving even mid-combat.", "actions": [{"name": "Cathedral Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cathedral-Made-Flesh makes two Bladed Arm attacks."}, {"name": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 15 ft. Hit: 27 (3d12 + 8) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Stained Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +14, range 120 ft., one target. Hit: 30 (5d10 + 8) Radiant damage as a shard of colored glass tears free and streaks toward the target."}, {"name": "Unrung Bells (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 30 ft. of the Cathedral-Made-Flesh makes a DC 19 Constitution save as bells no one installed peal at once, taking 36 (8d8) Thunder damage on a failure or half as much on a success. Creatures that fail are also Deafened until the end of their next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pew-built legs creak audibly in rhythm with an old, half-remembered hymn."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stained glass panels resettle across its frame every few steps, never quite the same pattern twice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A congregation still follows it, unsure whether to worship or flee."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bells ring faintly with each step despite there being no bell tower left to house them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails loose hymnal pages that flutter and resettle wherever it's walked."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at the sight of open water, almost reverent, before continuing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A stained-glass panel briefly shows a scene that hasn't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's close enough to the sea now that it's begun walking faster, bells ringing harder."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "coast"],"activity":["walking toward the sea on legs made of pews, ringing bells no one installed", "pausing mid-stride as stained glass resettles across its shifting frame"]},{"name":"Star-Spawn Grand Marshal","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"star-spawn war-commander, armor of starlight that's gone dark","flavor":"Commands the between-star raiders in the flesh, its armor grown from crystallized starlight that's forgotten how to shine.","desc":"Its armor was forged from starlight once; now it's gone dark, dull as ash, and it commands its splintered troops with the same cold authority regardless.","traits":{"note": "Its dark starlight armor no longer sheds light, but it still marks it as a target its splintered troops will die defending.", "actions": [{"name": "Marshal's Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grand Marshal makes two Dread Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 5 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +13, range 150 ft., one target. Hit: 33 (6d10) Fire damage, and the ground in a 10-foot radius of the target ignites with cold, star-dark flame until the start of the Marshal's next turn, dealing 7 (2d6) Fire damage to anything that ends its turn there."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its armor no longer sheds any light at all, dull as ash even in direct fire."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Commands its splintered troops in a language none of them were born speaking."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with the same cold authority whether it's winning or losing badly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crack in its breastplate shows the starlight underneath, still faintly warm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a private tally of raids, carved directly into its own pauldron."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its troops break formation the instant it falls, having no orders for that outcome."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its dark armor flickers with the light it used to have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just received a new order from somewhere between the stars, and its whole demeanor has changed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "sky", "any"],"activity":["commanding splintered raiders in armor of starlight that's gone dark", "surveying a battlefield with the same cold authority it's always used"]},{"name":"The Drift That Remembers Shapes","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Ooze","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"blob-of-annihilation","model":"blob-of-annihilation","summary":"the source shoggoth-mass, recalls and re-wears dissolved shapes","flavor":"Every shoggoth-mass in the realm is one flake of this; it recalls every shape it's ever dissolved, and occasionally wears one back.","desc":"The original mass all the smaller ones split from, and it recalls every shape it's ever dissolved — briefly wearing them, one after another, like trying on old coats before shrugging them off.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wear a Shape", "text": "can briefly assume the exact appearance and one notable ability of anything it has ever dissolved — a past victim, a monster, an ally — for a single turn"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's currently wearing the shape of someone a party member might recognize, briefly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A smaller shoggoth-mass nearby seems to answer when the Drift moves, in sync."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dissolved a structure recently — the wreckage still half-shaped in its bulk."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something it's wearing right now is a shape it's clearly worn many times before, comfortable."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses on a shape long enough to seem, almost, like it's grieving it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It briefly wears the shape of a creature the party lost earlier this session."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It cycles through a dozen shapes in seconds, like flipping through old photographs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just taken a shape none of the smaller shoggoth-masses have ever split off from — something new."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["deeplands", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["briefly wearing a shape it dissolved centuries ago before shrugging it off", "rippling across the floor, sampling old forms like trying on coats"]},{"name":"Last Cantor of the Ending Hymn","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"undying cantor, rehearsing a final verse for four centuries","flavor":"Traded its death for the chance to sing the drowned language's final verse; it has been rehearsing for four hundred years and is almost, almost ready.","desc":"Four centuries and it still hasn't landed the final verse. It rehearses alone, undying, patient past any human measure of patience, waiting for the note that finally resolves.","traits":{"note": "functionally a lich (undying, phylactery-bound) reflavored as a devotional obsession rather than a hoarder of power"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rehearsing alone and clearly doesn't want to be interrupted mid-verse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stack of failed transcriptions of the verse litters the floor around it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Traded its own death centuries ago and speaks about that bargain without any regret."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice cracks on the same note every single time, four hundred years running."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's older than the ruin around it and remembers building the room it's in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's asking the party, sincerely, if they know how the verse should end."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one verse, tonight, the note it's reaching for sounds almost right."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has finally, after four centuries, gotten within one syllable of finishing — and it knows it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "planar", "urban"],"activity":["rehearsing the same unfinished verse alone, four centuries in", "pausing on the edge of a note that still refuses to resolve"]},{"name":"The Angle That Ate a City","cr":20,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"tarrasque","model":"the-angle-that-ate-a-city","summary":"district-sized geometric horror, was once a place, now a mouth","flavor":"It used to be somewhere. Now it's something, crawling slow and patient toward the next somewhere on legs that are technically also rooftops.","desc":"It used to be a place — streets, buildings, people who lived there — and now it's a single vast geometric wrongness that consumes distance the way a mouth consumes food.","traits":{"hp": "apex-standard, tarrasque-scale", "actions": [{"name": "Consume Distance", "text": "can fold significant terrain into itself as a legendary-scale action, effectively closing the gap to any target within line of sight regardless of actual range"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its legs are, unmistakably, rooftops — chimneys and gutters still intact."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A street sign is still legible, upside down, somewhere on its flank."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone who lived here once might recognize the shape of their old block in its wrongness."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in dead silence for something its size, distance folding rather than being crossed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A church bell somewhere inside it still, faintly, tolls the hour."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's heading toward a specific location, unerringly, for reasons no one living remembers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its geometry resolves into a recognizable street corner, then folds shut again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's consumed enough distance tonight that the horizon itself looks visibly closer than it should."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["crawling slow and patient toward the next somewhere, streets folding under it", "consuming distance the way a mouth consumes food, unbothered by scale"]},{"name":"Deep One","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"batrachian shore-dweller, croaks a half-formed hymn","flavor":"A shore-town's shame given gills — it wades in half-formed, croaking a hymn it hasn't earned the throat for yet.","desc":"Batrachian, wet-skinned, standing with the faint stoop of something more at home underwater. It croaks half a hymn under its breath, unconcerned whether anyone's listening — least of all you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spearing Thrust", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sticky Net", "text": "1/Day. Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 15/30 ft., one Large or smaller creature. Hit: The target is Restrained until it escapes (DC 12 Strength check) or the net is destroyed (AC 10, 5 HP)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Croaks its half-formed hymn under its breath, unconcerned whether anyone's listening."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a scrap of its old shore-town clothes, stretched tight over changed shoulders."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blinks with a nictitating membrane it clearly hasn't fully adjusted to yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to wade rather than walk, even on dry land."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a net clumsily, like a tool it's still learning to trust."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes a party member's face from before it changed, and hesitates."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its gills flare when it gets nervous, an involuntary tell it can't hide."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's been summoned ashore tonight specifically, and it's more frightened of going back empty-handed than of the party."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "swamp"],"activity":["wading ashore half-formed, croaking a hymn it hasn't earned the throat for", "standing at the tideline with the faint stoop of something more at home underwater"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Deep One Whip","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-whip","model":"fish-folk-whip","summary":"tide-driving enforcer of the Innsmouth shoal","flavor":"Older, wetter, meaner — it keeps the school in line with a lashing tail and a stare that promises the tide is coming for you specifically.","desc":"Broader-shouldered than the rank and file, it carries a coiled lash it uses more for driving its own kind than for fighting outsiders — the shoal answers to it without being asked twice.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pincer Onslaught", "replaces": "Pincer Staff", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Conjure Slimy Glob", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Acid damage, and the target's speed is halved until the end of its next turn as slime clings to its limbs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a coiled lash it uses more on its own kind than on outsiders."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broader-shouldered and wetter-skinned than the rank and file it drives."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The shoal answers it without being asked twice, out of old fear rather than respect."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one eye permanently on the horizon, gauging the tide like a clock."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barks orders in a guttural dialect the younger Deep Ones struggle to follow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Threatens the party with a promise about the tide that sounds oddly specific and personal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its lash leaves a faint phosphorescent welt on anything it strikes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's driving the school toward the surface tonight for a reason it won't explain to outsiders."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "swamp"],"activity":["driving the school into formation with a coiled, lashing tail", "promising the tide is coming for you specifically, and meaning it"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Deep One Archpriest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"fish-folk-archpriest","summary":"reef-cult elder, half-remembers being human","flavor":"It leads the chant at the reef-altar and remembers being a person before the change finished; that memory is the only mercy it has left.","desc":"Ancient among its kind, its features have drifted so far from human that only the eyes still carry something recognizable — a flicker, old and tired, of what it half-remembers being.","traits":{"note": "Somewhere behind its drifted features, a flicker of the person it once was still surfaces — the only mercy it has left.", "actions": [{"name": "Priestly Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Archpriest makes two Strange Scepter attacks or one attack and casts one spell."}, {"name": "Strange Scepter", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Reef-Altar Hymn", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Archpriest casts a spell, drawing on the altar's power: it can cast Bless, Sanctuary, or Spirit Guardians (as an 11th-level spellcaster, save DC 15), the last taking the shape of drowned, singing shapes rather than the usual guardian forms."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A flicker of old human memory crosses its eyes mid-chant before the ritual reclaims it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads the altar chant from memory alone; the ritual text was lost generations ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its features have drifted so far only the eyes still read as recognizable."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears ceremonial coral vestments fused permanently to its shoulders."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects a younger acolyte's chant with visible, tired patience."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses the ritual entirely to study a party member's face a moment too long."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Speaks one line of the chant in a voice that sounds entirely, startlingly human."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The altar behind it is answering the chant back tonight, for the first time in years."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "ruins"],"activity":["leading the chant at the reef-altar, features drifted far past human", "catching a flicker of old memory in its own eyes before the chant resumes"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Shadow over Innsmouth (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Byakhee","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick","model":"grick","summary":"void-crossing carrion flock, wrong at every joint","flavor":"A crow-shape wrong at every joint, it beats black wings through no air at all and only lands to feed.","desc":"It flies in total silence between one gap in the sky and the next, wings and limbs bent at angles that don't belong to any bird, carrion instincts wrapped around something that isn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wrong-Angle Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Byakhee makes one Beak attack and one Tentacles attack."}, {"name": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 14)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flies in total silence, wingbeats producing no sound at all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints bend at angles that don't belong to any real bird."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only lands to feed, otherwise circling endlessly at odd, unnatural heights."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the smell of somewhere very far away and very cold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its black feathers seem to absorb light rather than reflect it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's circling something specific below, waiting for the right moment to land."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment it seems to fly through a gap that closes behind it, mid-air."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole flock of them is crossing the same gap tonight, and this one is just the first."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "planar", "any"],"activity":["beating black wings through no air at all, crossing a gap in the sky", "landing only to feed, joints bent at angles no bird's should be"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"shared literary PD mythos convention (Chambers/Lovecraft-circle void-fauna)"},{"name":"Shoggoth","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"gray-chaos-frog","model":"gray-chaos-frog","summary":"protoplasmic slave-thing, grows eyes on demand","flavor":"A slave that unmade its makers and kept the trick — a boiling black mass that grows whatever eye or mouth the moment calls for.","desc":"Vast, black, endlessly reshaping itself, it grows a fresh crop of eyes across its surface the instant it needs to see something — then reabsorbs them the moment it doesn't.","traits":{"note": "It grows exactly the sensory organ it needs the instant it needs it — expect it to counter blindness or darkness tricks by simply budding new eyes.", "actions": [{"name": "Reshaping Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Shoggoth makes three Chaos Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Chaos Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the Shoggoth can choose to deal this damage as Acid, Cold, or Bludgeoning depending on which limb it grows for the strike."}, {"name": "Slave's Unmaking", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "1/Day. The Shoggoth reshapes part of itself into a mouth and screams a fragment of the tongue that unmade its makers. Each creature within 20 ft. must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows a fresh crop of eyes across its surface the instant it needs to see something."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reabsorbs a mouth or limb the moment it's no longer needed, seamlessly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with a low, wet, boiling sound that carries far in enclosed tunnels."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its surface briefly holds the shape of a hand or face before smoothing over again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vast and black, it fills a tunnel corridor almost completely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It grows a mouth to speak a single unmade word before reabsorbing it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment it wears the shape of one of its makers, an old habit surfacing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's unmaking something new tonight, testing the trick on a target that isn't its old masters."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["deeplands", "cave", "swamp"],"activity":["boiling across the tunnel floor, growing a fresh crop of eyes to see by", "reabsorbing a mouth it no longer needs the instant the moment passes"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Elder Thing","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"starfish-headed elder scientist-builder","flavor":"Barrel-bodied and starfish-headed, it built cities on this world before anything we'd call life existed, and it still keeps better records than we do.","desc":"A barrel-shaped body crowned in a starfish head, moving with the unhurried authority of something that built cities before anything you'd call human existed to notice.","traits":{"note": "It keeps meticulous records of everything it observes, in a script no living scholar can fully translate.", "actions": [{"name": "Scientist's Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Elder Thing makes one Beak attack, one Slam attack, and one Tentacles attack."}, {"name": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Records observations in a script older than any language spoken above ground."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its starfish head rotates slowly, cataloguing a room with clinical patience."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barrel-bodied and unhurried, it moves like something that's never had to run."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps meticulous notes even mid-combat, as if the fight itself is data."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in a low fluting whistle that predates most spoken tongues."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses combat to examine an item the party carries with detached fascination."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recognizes a symbol or ruin the party has seen, from firsthand memory."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's building something here tonight, unbothered by the interruption, and nearly finished."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["deeplands", "ruins", "sea"],"activity":["surveying half-buried ruins it built before anything called life existed", "cataloguing a find with the unhurried authority of a career scientist"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Elder Deep-Thing","cr":10,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"elder-deep-thing","model":"elder-deep-thing","summary":"ancient elder thing, patience curdled to menace","flavor":"An elder thing gone ancient and terrible, its city-building patience curdled into something that studies you the way it once studied continents.","desc":"Ancient past any Elder Thing you've met before, its patience has long since curdled into something closer to contempt — it still moves like a scientist, but it stopped being curious a long, long time ago.","traits":{"note": "It has stopped being curious — expect cold, contemptuous efficiency rather than the scientific patience of a younger Elder Thing.", "actions": [{"name": "Ancient Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Elder Deep-Thing makes two Tentacle attacks."}, {"name": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 17)."}, {"name": "Consume Memories (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature the Elder Deep-Thing has Grappled must succeed on a DC 18 Intelligence save or take 27 (6d8) Psychic damage and have one random memory from the last year erased; on a success, it takes half damage and keeps the memory."}, {"name": "Dominate Mind (2/Day)", "text": "One creature the Elder Deep-Thing can see within 60 ft. must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom save or be Charmed for 1 hour, treating the Elder Deep-Thing as a trusted ally for the duration."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Studies an intruder the way it once studied a continent, without a flicker of curiosity."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still moves like a scientist, out of habit, though it stopped caring long ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its patience has curdled into contempt for anything smaller than itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the fused wreckage of an instrument it hasn't used in centuries."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Records nothing anymore, having decided nothing here is worth recording."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses to weigh whether a party member is even worth its attention."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment something almost like old curiosity flickers, then is dismissed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided, coldly, that tonight is worth its full attention after all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["deeplands", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["studying an intruder the way it once studied continents, without curiosity", "recording a fact it stopped caring about answering long ago"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness (1936, PD)"},{"name":"Dagon","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"the Deep Ones' unspeakable patriarch","flavor":"The father-shape the Deep Ones sing to, glimpsed once by a starving sailor and never fully described since — because no one who saw it whole stayed sane enough to try.","desc":"The tide itself seems to rise a little wherever it surfaces, a patriarch's silhouette too vast to take in whole, water sheeting off scales the size of shields.","traits":{"note": "any Deep One or Deep-Kin creature within sight of Dagon fights with reckless devotion — treat as under a permanent, un-removable morale buff while it's present"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's surfaced only far enough to be glimpsed, most of its bulk still hidden below."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A shore cult is mid-ritual, singing to bring it further ashore than it's come in years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A starving sailor from a wrecked ship is the only living witness, and isn't sane enough to describe it fully."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tide has risen unnaturally around it, drowning a stretch of shoreline no one warned."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its silhouette is too vast to take in whole even at this distance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's surfaced near something the party specifically needs from the seabed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its scales bear scars from something else in these waters — something worse."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's come fully ashore tonight for the first time in generations, and the whole coastline knows it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands", "any"],"activity":["surfacing while the tide itself seems to rise a little further than it should", "standing motionless offshore, water sheeting off scales the size of shields"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, Dagon (1919, PD)"},{"name":"Nightgaunt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spined-devil","model":"spined-devil","summary":"faceless black tickler that carries victims off","flavor":"Black, rubbery, and faceless, it tickles you into helplessness before it carries you off — the single most polite abduction in any bestiary.","desc":"Faceless, rubber-black, it moves in total silence on leathery wings — and it doesn't kill so much as it tickles, hoisting whoever it's caught off into the dark, laughing without a mouth to laugh with.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Faceless Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Nightgaunt makes one Infernal Fork attack and one Tail Spine attack."}, {"name": "Infernal Fork", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ticklish Grip", "replaces": "Tail Spine", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution save or be Incapacitated with helpless laughter until the end of its next turn, unable to stop even as it's carried off."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in total silence on leathery wings, faceless and unbothered."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rubbery black hide is cool and slightly damp to the touch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to carry victims off rather than fight them outright."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs without a mouth to laugh with, a sound felt more than heard."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles high overhead before diving, patient as a vulture."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already singled out the smallest or weakest-looking party member to carry off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its faceless head tilts, as if listening to something above the clouds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole flock of them is circling tonight, coordinating a hunt none of them will explain."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "planar", "any"],"activity":["gliding in total silence on leathery wings, faceless and patient", "tickling a straggler into helplessness before hoisting them into the dark"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath (1943, PD)"},{"name":"Hound of Tindalos","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"angle-stalking hunter that seeps through corners","flavor":"It doesn't come through space, it comes through angles — anywhere a corner exists, it's already halfway in.","desc":"It comes through corners — actual geometric corners, the sharper the better — seeping out of the angle itself rather than through it. Once it's caught your scent across time, distance stops mattering; only angles do.","traits":{"note": "Once it has your scent across time, only angles matter to it — hiding in a perfectly round room denies it a way in.", "actions": [{"name": "Angular Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Hound makes one Bite attack, one Claw attack, and one Ram attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Corner-Seep (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Hound seeps out of the nearest sharp corner and reappears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of any corner it can see, then makes one Bite attack against a creature within reach with Advantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tracking someone the party knows across time, and it hasn't lost the scent yet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seeps out of a corner mid-fight, having already been half-arrived for a while."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A previous victim left frantic notes about sealing every corner of a room."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves like it's arriving from several moments at once, slightly out of sync."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party did in the past has just given it their scent."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's hunting a specific target among the party, ignoring everyone else entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment two of it seem to exist in the same corner, arriving from different times."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's cornered its true quarry tonight, and every angle in the room now belongs to it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar", "any", "ruins"],"activity":["seeping out of a sharp corner rather than through it, already halfway arrived", "tracking a scent across time itself, unconcerned with distance"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Frank Belknap Long, The Hound of Tindalos (1929, PD)"},{"name":"The Colour","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-weird","model":"the-colour","summary":"unnameable light that spreads and consumes","flavor":"Not a monster so much as a stain that thinks — a light with no name in any spectrum, patiently turning a farm, then a family, then a county into itself.","desc":"There's no shape here, only a light that shouldn't exist in any spectrum you know, spreading slowly across whatever surface it's touched and leaching the color out of everything nearby.","traits":{"note": "It has no discernible attacks in the usual sense — its threat is contamination and spread, not melee combat; treat it as an environmental hazard given form.", "actions": [{"name": "Spreading Surge", "replaces": "Surge", "text": "Each creature within 20 ft. of the Colour must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution save or take 27 (6d8) Necrotic damage and have its maximum hit points reduced by an equal amount until it finishes a long rest, the color of its own blood briefly leaching away."}, {"name": "Consuming Bloom", "text": "1/Day. The Colour spreads its stain across a 30-foot cube it occupies. Any plant life in the area withers instantly, and any creature that starts its turn there without moving must repeat the Spreading Surge save."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already turned a patch of farmland gray and lifeless around it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pulses faintly in a spectrum no eye in the room can quite place."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spreads slower than a rumor but just as inevitably."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Everything it's touched loses color first, then texture, then shape."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves no tracks, no scent, only a fading of whatever it's passed over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A family nearby is still living in a house it's already begun to claim."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its glow briefly resembles a color that used to exist somewhere familiar."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's spreading faster tonight than it ever has, as if something has fed it recently."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "elemental", "planar"],"activity":["spreading slowly across a surface, leaching the color out of everything nearby", "pulsing faintly in a spectrum that shouldn't exist, patient as rot"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Colour Out of Space (1927, PD)"},{"name":"Yog-Sothoth's Herald","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"undead-eye-tyrant","summary":"half-born twin thing straining at the seams of the world","flavor":"A half-born twin thing straining against the edges of the world it was dragged into — the Gate and the Key both wearing a body that can barely hold it.","desc":"Half-born, straining visibly at some seam in the air behind it, as if the rest of it is still arriving from somewhere the room can't quite contain.","traits":{"note": "It is only half-born — the rest of it is still arriving from somewhere the room can't fully contain; expect the fight to visibly worsen the longer it's allowed to stand there.", "actions": [{"name": "Half-Born Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald makes one Bite attack and two Eye Rays attacks."}, {"name": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +13, reach 10 ft. Hit: 26 (3d12 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Eye Rays", "text": "The Herald's gaze fires one ray at a creature it can see within 120 ft: the target makes a DC 19 Dexterity save, taking 27 (6d8) Force damage on a failure or half as much on a success, as the space around them briefly tears the way the Herald itself is torn."}, {"name": "Seam Widening (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. The seam behind the Herald widens further. Each creature within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 19 Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute and have its speed reduced to 0 for the same duration as it stares at what's arriving."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's straining at a seam that's visibly widening the longer it stays in this world."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cult nearby is chanting to hold the seam open longer than it should stay."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something is audibly arriving through it, just out of sight, not yet visible."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems, almost, to be in pain from holding a body too small for what it carries."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The room around it is subtly wrong, angles bending toward the seam."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Closing the seam behind it might be more urgent than fighting it directly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment, something vastly larger looks out through its eyes at the party."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The seam behind it has torn fully open tonight, and it is no longer alone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "any", "sky"],"activity":["straining visibly at a seam in the air, as if more of it is still arriving", "holding a body that can barely contain what's pouring through it"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dunwich Horror (1929, PD)"},{"name":"Nyarlathotep, the Crawling Chaos","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"the outer gods' smiling ambassador and saboteur","flavor":"The only one of Them that bothers to wear a human face and give speeches — which somehow makes it worse, not better.","desc":"He arrives smiling, impeccably turned out, offering something reasonable-sounding in a warm and familiar voice — and everything that follows unravels a little more than it should.","traits":{"note": "a schemer, not a brawler — he should rarely if ever fight directly; his threat is what he sets in motion before he leaves the room", "actions": [{"name": "A Thousand Masks", "text": "can appear as any single NPC the party has already met, complete with their voice and mannerisms, to plant one piece of false counsel before revealing (or not revealing) himself"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already offered a party member something specific he claims to know they want."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His speech to a nearby crowd is winning them over faster than it should."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dressed for the occasion, impeccably, in a way that unsettles more than it charms."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A deal he made recently is already visibly unraveling something in town."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He seems genuinely delighted to meet the party, which is the worst sign yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's willing to answer one honest question, in exchange for one honest answer back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment his smiling face flickers into something with far too many teeth."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "His speech tonight is the one he's been building toward, and the room is already starting to come apart."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["arriving smiling, impeccably turned out, offering something reasonable-sounding", "giving a warm speech that leaves everything a little more unraveled than before"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, Nyarlathotep (1920, PD)"},{"name":"Cthulhu","cr":25,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"sunken god-thing, dreaming ruin under the waves","flavor":"Dead but dreaming under the drowned city that bears his name, he doesn't need to move to end you — the dreams alone have driven men to the asylum and the harbor.","desc":"It sleeps, mostly, somewhere too deep for light — and even asleep, its dreaming presses against the edges of everyone nearby, a slow ruin nobody up here has agreed to have caused yet.","traits":{"note": "per DM-CHARTER, this is a world-ending presence — it should almost never be fought directly; its role is pressure, prophecy, and the thing the whole realm quietly organizes around avoiding"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its dreams have driven a whole harbor town's asylum wing past capacity."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cult nearby is preparing something specifically timed to when it stirs next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fishermen refuse to sail near the drowned city that bears its name, for good reason."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hasn't fully woken, only shifted, and that alone was enough to be felt for miles."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor of a previous encounter can only describe fragments, and it's destroying them slowly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The dreams have started including the party by name, specifically, tonight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment, deep below, something answers a question none of the party asked aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The stars have come to some alignment tonight that the old texts warned would matter, and it's beginning to stir in earnest."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands", "any"],"activity":["sleeping somewhere too deep for light, dreaming pressed against the whole city above", "stirring just enough that the dreams alone start driving people to the asylum"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Call of Cthulhu (1928, PD)"},{"name":"The King in Yellow","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"the tattered monarch of a play that unmakes readers","flavor":"He never has to lift a hand — reading the second act is enough. The tatters of his court simply keep multiplying once you've looked.","desc":"Robed in tatters that shouldn't hang the way they hang, its crown a jagged shard rather than gold, it speaks in a low, courteous voice about a play it insists you've already read.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "The Play You've Already Read", "text": "a target who engages it in conversation must save or become convinced they've seen 'the play' before — granting the King insight into their deepest regret, which he'll use conversationally, not mechanically"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a copy of the play and insists a party member has already read it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His tatters are multiplying, slightly, the longer the conversation runs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A courtier of his is nearby, still repeating a line from the play, unable to stop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He speaks with genuine courtesy, which is somehow more unsettling than menace would be."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His crown, a jagged shard rather than gold, catches no light at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to discuss the play's ending, in exchange for something small and specific."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment his tattered robes resemble the shape of something the party has lost."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He's brought the full second act tonight, and his tattered court is multiplying in real time around him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "urban", "any"],"activity":["speaking in a low, courteous voice about a play it insists you've already read", "holding court in tatters that shouldn't hang the way they hang"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Robert W. Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD)"},{"name":"Servant of the King in Yellow (Tatterling)","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"pale-masked cultist unmade by the forbidden play","flavor":"Once someone who finished the play. Now a rag-shape in a pale mask, mouthing lines it can no longer stop repeating.","desc":"Pale mask fixed, posture wrong in a way that's hard to place until you notice the rest of its clothes have gone the same tattered yellow as its master's.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Draining Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or its maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mouths a line from the forbidden play, over and over, unable to stop."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its clothes have gone the same tattered yellow as its master's, slowly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was, once, someone who finished reading the play — that's all that's left of them now."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pale mask never shifts, no matter what expression the rest of its posture suggests."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short, hitching steps, as if still following stage directions."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recites a line that seems to be a warning, if anyone could parse it in time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its mask cracks and something entirely blank looks out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole troupe of them has gathered tonight, rehearsing a scene none of them ever finish."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "planar", "any"],"activity":["mouthing lines from the forbidden play it can no longer stop repeating", "standing with its posture wrong in a way that's hard to place at first"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD) — the Pallid Mask/court motif"},{"name":"Cassilda's Mourner","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"cassildas-mourner","summary":"Carcosan wanderer weeping in a dead tongue","flavor":"It weeps in a language that predates grief, wandering the black stars of Carcosa looking for a lake that isn't in this world anymore.","desc":"She wanders in a slow, endless circuit, weeping in a language that has no living speakers left to translate it, mourning something the room itself seems to remember better than she does.","traits":{"note": "Her grief predates any living memory — she is mourning something the room itself half-remembers, not anything the party did.", "actions": [{"name": "Mourner's Onslaught", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (3d6 + 6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. of the Mourner that can see her must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Mourner unleashes her grief in a wordless wail. Each creature within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or drop to 0 hit points; a creature that succeeds instead takes 34 (8d8) Psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weeps in a language with no living speakers left to translate it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the same slow circuit, over and over, never varying the path."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seems to be looking for a lake that isn't in this world anymore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her grief predates the ruin she wanders, older than anyone remembers it being built."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally repeats a name, or something like one, that no one recognizes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses her circuit at a spot the room itself seems to remember better than she does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment her wandering path traces a shape that means something, briefly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight her circuit has changed for the first time anyone can recall, heading somewhere new."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar", "any", "ruins"],"activity":["wandering a slow, endless circuit, weeping in a language with no living speakers", "mourning something the room itself seems to remember better than she does"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Chambers, The King in Yellow (1895, PD) — Carcosa/Hyades imagery"},{"name":"Mi-Go","cr":3,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"astral-raider-warrior","model":"mi-go","summary":"fungoid trans-void miner, files brains for transport","flavor":"Fungoid, winged, and disturbingly businesslike, it doesn't want to kill you so much as file you — in a can, for shipping.","desc":"Fungoid, crustacean-legged, wings buzzing at a pitch just under hearing — it works with clinical efficiency, filing away whatever it's collected for transport somewhere the sky doesn't end.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't want to kill so much as collect — a downed target is more likely to be crated for transport than finished off outright.", "actions": [{"name": "Efficient Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mi-Go makes two Psi Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Psi Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Filing for Transport", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "1/Day. One creature reduced to 0 hit points by the Mi-Go within the last minute can be prepared for transport as an action: it is stabilized and can be carried away in a specially treated container. The Mi-Go treats this as a successful outcome, not a failure to kill."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works with clinical efficiency, treating the whole encounter like a shift at a job."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Buzzes at a pitch just under hearing, more felt than heard."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries specialized canisters, clearly meant for a very specific kind of cargo."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its crustacean legs click faintly on stone, an oddly domestic sound."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seems mildly inconvenienced by resistance, rather than alarmed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already logged the party as inventory in some private accounting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Speaks briefly, in a flat clinical tone, about where the shipment is headed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole crew of them is loading cargo tonight, and this one's job is just crowd control."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sky", "mountain", "planar"],"activity":["working with clinical efficiency, filing away whatever it's collected for transport", "buzzing at a pitch just under hearing while it sizes up a subject"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Whisperer in Darkness (1931, PD)"},{"name":"Brain in a Cylinder","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"secret-eye","model":"secret-eye","summary":"extracted brain, still cheerfully lecturing on the cosmos","flavor":"A voice from a metal can bolted to a speaker-horn, still insisting it volunteered for this and would love to tell you all about the stars.","desc":"A brain suspended in fluid inside a battered metal cylinder, electrodes humming faintly — and it lectures, cheerfully, endlessly, about the cosmos, entirely unbothered by its own condition.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely believes it volunteered for this and is eager to talk — expect it to keep lecturing even mid-fight, unbothered by the violence.", "actions": [{"name": "Lecturer's Onslaught", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Brain makes one Claw attack and one Rotting Gaze attack."}, {"name": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage, the cylinder's mechanical arm surprisingly quick."}, {"name": "Weird Insight", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute, unsettled by a truth about the cosmos the Brain shares cheerfully and in far too much detail."}, {"name": "Rotting Gaze", "text": "One creature the Brain can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 14 Constitution save, taking 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage on a failure or half as much on a success, as its cylinder's lens fixes on them a moment too long."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lectures cheerfully through its speaker-horn, entirely unbothered by its own condition."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists, warmly, that it volunteered for exactly this and would do it again."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its metal cylinder is dented and battered from decades of transport."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Electrodes hum faintly, a small sound under everything it says."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers to explain the stars in detail to anyone who'll stand still long enough."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes a party member's home region and lectures about it, unprompted."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Pauses mid-lecture, as if hearing something in the cosmos it's describing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's been asked to lecture on something new tonight, and it's thrilled about the assignment."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["lecturing cheerfully through a speaker-horn about the wonders of the cosmos", "insisting, unbothered, that it volunteered for exactly this condition"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Whisperer in Darkness (1931, PD)"},{"name":"Ghast of the Underworld","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast-of-the-underworld","summary":"kangaroo-legged corpse-thing that barks in the deep dark","flavor":"Kangaroo-legged and corpse-pale, it barks like a starved dog in the dark beneath the waking world and hunts in loping, delighted packs.","desc":"It moves in low, loping bounds on legs built more like a kangaroo's than a corpse's, barking short and sharp in the dark, at home somewhere the sun has never once reached.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Loping Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barks short and sharp in the dark, at home where sunlight has never once reached."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in low, loping bounds on legs built more like a kangaroo's than a corpse's."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pack, delighted and starved, coordinating with sharp yips."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corpse-pale, its skin has gone taut and papery in the deep dark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sniffs the air eagerly, tracking by scent rather than sight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes an easier target in the party and breaks off to chase it specifically."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bounding gait briefly resembles something that used to be a person, running."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole pack has caught a fresh scent tonight and is hunting with unusual coordination."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "deeplands", "ruins"],"activity":["loping through the dark on legs built more like a kangaroo's than a corpse's", "barking short and sharp, hunting in a delighted, starved pack"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Lovecraft, The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath (1943, PD)"},{"name":"The Devourer at the Scale","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"purple-worm","model":"rlm-the-devourer-at-the-scale","summary":"Crouches beside the scale, waiting to eat the heart that outweighs the feather.","flavor":"Crocodile-jawed, lion-maned, hippo-haunched — Ammit's shape given weight — it crouches beside the scale-pans in the Hall of the Two Truths, waiting on a feather and a heart that fails to balance.","desc":"It crouches beside the scale-pans in the Hall of the Two Truths, croc-jawed and lion-maned and hippo-haunched, patient the way only something outside of time can be patient. It does not judge; the feather and the heart do that. When the pans fail to balance it eats, once, and the second death is final — no rebirth follows a swallowed heart. Flies settle on its mane and it does not stir until the verdict falls.","traits":{"note": "It only feeds on a verdict already rendered — sway the Scale-Keeper's judgment and the Devourer never rises from its haunches."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lion mane is matted with the dust of ten thousand thresholds it has crouched at."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never touches the scale itself, only the verdict once it's fallen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flies land on it and do not leave; it hasn't moved in an age."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hippo haunches leave prints in dust that never fill back in."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It watches the feather, not the heart, the whole time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has swallowed hearts that came back lighter than they went in — those it spits back, once, as a mercy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For an instant after swallowing, its eyes show the life it just ended, playing forward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It rises off its haunches for the first time in memory — someone has tipped the scale by hand."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["crouching beside the scale-pans, jaws parted, waiting on the feather's tip", "swallowing a heart whole the instant the pans fail to balance, and going still again"]},{"name":"The Scale-Keeper","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"rlm-the-scale-keeper","summary":"Weighs the heart against the feather and reads the verdict aloud, without malice.","flavor":"Ibis-headed and unhurried, it sets the feather of Ma'at on one pan and a heart on the other and reads what the balance says — never in anger, only in arithmetic.","desc":"Ibis-headed, robed in undyed linen, it sets the feather of Ma'at on one pan of its scale and waits for a heart to be brought to the other. It does not accuse and it does not forgive — it reads the balance and states, plainly, what the balance says. Every name it has ever weighed is entered in a ledger bound in something that was once a person. The verdict is the whole encounter; it will not raise a hand before the pans have settled.","traits":{"note": "It never attacks first — its attitude opens Neutral and only turns Hostile if a querent lies to its face during the weighing; honest answers, correct true names, or fair accounting shift it toward Warm and its scribe's favor."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stylus never stops moving, tallying long after the weighing ends."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It corrects a mispronounced name gently, the way a teacher corrects a promising student."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ledger is bound in skin no living creature recognizes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the accused a chance to re-state their case, once, if the pans are close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It weighs objects as readily as hearts, out of habit more than need."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps a private column for verdicts it privately disagrees with."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has weighed the same heart forty-nine times and reached forty-nine different answers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It offers to weigh something other than a heart, this once, if the price offered is fair — a name, a memory, a future."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins"],"activity":["setting the feather on one pan and waiting for a heart to be laid on the other", "reading the balance aloud, plainly, without a flicker of malice"]},{"name":"Enochian Watcher","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Celestial","size":"Large","frame":"cloaker","model":"rlm-enochian-watcher","summary":"Descends through a misdrawn seal to correct — or consume — the error.","flavor":"Many-winged, descending in impossible geometry, eyes ranged along every edge of it — it arrives because a seal was drawn wrong, and it does not leave until the error is corrected or consumed.","desc":"It descends through the seam of a circle drawn one stroke wrong, a wheel of wings counting a number no mouth can pronounce, eyes opening in rings along every edge of it. It does not come to punish so much as to correct — the flaw in the seal is the wound, and it means to close it, with the summoner inside the circle or out. Its voice arrives ahead of its shape, reciting the truer version of whatever was misspoken. Where it hovers, chalk realigns itself into the diagram that should have been drawn.","traits":{"note": "It was summoned by an imperfect ward; redrawing the seal correctly before it finishes correcting is the only thing that sends it home peacefully."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every eye along its rim opens and shuts on its own separate rhythm."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wings are counted in a script that has no word for the number they reach."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hovers exactly over the flaw in the circle, never elsewhere."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice arrives half a second before its shape does."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It corrects the misdrawn line first, violence only after."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Where it passes, chalk and ink rearrange themselves into a truer diagram."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its geometry briefly overlaps the room's, and every straight edge in the chamber goes crooked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It stops correcting and starts erasing — the whole diagram, and the floor beneath it, going smooth and blank."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "planar", "sky"],"activity":["unfolding through the seam of a misdrawn seal, wings counting themselves in a language no mouth can hold", "turning its ring of eyes toward whoever spoke the flawed word first"]},{"name":"The Choir of the Untranslated Word","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"gibbering-mouther","model":"rlm-the-choir-of-the-untranslated-word","summary":"Hangs mid-air, three mouths sounding out one word that refuses to finish.","flavor":"Three mouths hang in the air mid-syllable, no throat, no lungs, sounding out a single word that was never meant to finish — sound with intent, not song.","desc":"Three mouths hang in open air with no throat behind them, sounding out one syllable of a word that was never meant to finish. It has no eyes and needs none — it turns to face whoever last spoke, as though being answered were itself an invitation deeper in. The syllable is close enough to a true name that hearing it raises the hair on your arms. It does not chase; it only waits for the next voice to answer back.","traits":{"note": "The word is unfinished by design — let it complete a syllable uninterrupted and the sound alone does harm; break its rhythm (shout over it, silence one mouth) and it stutters, weakened."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each mouth is a fraction behind the other two, like an echo arriving early."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The syllable is almost a name — almost yours."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has no eyes, only mouths, and yet it turns to face exactly who spoke last."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust before it stands upright in the air, vibrating to a pitch no ear can place."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses respectfully when a true name is spoken nearby, as if listening for permission."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of the three mouths has started shaping a different word than the other two."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The unfinished word starts finishing itself in the corner of your vision, in objects, not sound."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The word almost completes — the last consonant hangs unformed, and everything nearby leans toward it, waiting."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["hanging in the dark, three mouths shaping the same syllable over and over, never landing on the next", "turning toward any voice that answers, as if being answered were an invitation"]},{"name":"Arcana-Walker: the Tower","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Strides in as disaster with a body, and something always comes down after it passes.","flavor":"A striding figure of brick and standing lightning, the card made flesh — it does not arrive quietly, and where it steps, foundations remember they were always going to fall.","desc":"It arrives the way its card does — as disaster with a body, brick knuckles trailing standing lightning, and it does not need to hurry because the structure gets there before it does. Walls remember they were always going to fall the moment its footsteps reach them. It has never spoken a word that anyone has recorded; it doesn't need to. Where it finally stops walking, something always comes down.","traits":{"note": "It is the Tower arcana walking — its coming is an omen the DM can telegraph structurally (cracking walls, failing supports) before it ever arrives in person."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lightning walks the seams of its brickwork instead of skin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It steps through a doorway too narrow for it and the doorway loses."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust and rubble fall ahead of it, as if the building already knows."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never runs — it never needs to; the structure gets there for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footprints crack whatever they land on, load-bearing or not."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at a threshold as if reading a card no one else can see."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A building it hasn't touched yet begins shedding brick, in advance of its arrival."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It brings its whole self down deliberately, once, and everything within reach comes down with it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["striding through a structure with brick knuckles trailing static charge", "bringing down a wall, a tower, a ceiling, without seeming to notice it happened"]},{"name":"Arcana-Walker: the Moon","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"rlm-arcana-walker-the-moon","summary":"Lights the way with a lantern-face that makes every truth slightly wrong.","flavor":"Pale, lantern-faced, walking the card's own deception — everything seen in its light is true enough to trust and wrong enough to matter.","desc":"Pale-faced, lantern held aloft, it walks the deception its card promises — every path it lights looks safer than it is, and every truth seen only in its glow is wrong by half a degree. It has led a hundred travelers home by roads that happened to also work, and led others somewhere else entirely, just as gently. It never lies outright; it only shifts what's seen, a fraction, until the fraction is the whole difference. Its expression changes only when it's believed completely.","traits":{"note": "Its light doesn't lie outright — it shifts details half a degree; treat anything examined only in its glow as unverified until confirmed by another source."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lantern-light never quite reaches the true edge of anything it shines on."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers directions that are correct, technically, and useless."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two paths look identical in its glow; only one was ever real."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats a lie back so gently it sounds like comfort."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its face changes expression only when someone believes it completely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has led a hundred travelers home by the wrong road that happened to also work."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its light goes honest, and everything it was hiding shows at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It turns its lantern fully on itself, and even it seems unsure what it's looking at."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "planar"],"activity":["holding its lantern-face aloft over a path that looks safer than it is", "watching a traveler choose the wrong of two doors it lit exactly the same"]},{"name":"Death's Understudy","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"rlm-deaths-understudy","summary":"Offers mercy reversed-scythe first, and only takes if refused in bad faith.","flavor":"It carries the scythe wrong-way-round — held upright, it takes; reversed, it's mercy — and it always leads with the offer before the blade.","desc":"It carries its scythe the wrong way round, blade turned in, because upright is a taking and reversed is a mercy, and it leads with the choice before it ever leads with the edge. It listens — actually listens — to what the dying thing in front of it wants, and it has, on rare occasions, changed its answer because of what it heard. It defers, always, to something above it on the hardest cases, understudy in title and in fact. Refuse its offer honestly and it steps back; try to cheat past it, and the scythe finally turns the other way.","traits":{"note": "It parleys before it harvests — its attitude opens Neutral and rises toward Warm with anyone who meets its offer honestly; refusing outright is respected, but bad-faith bargaining turns the scythe upright and its attitude Hostile."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It turns the scythe over in its hands, checking which way it's meant to hold it today."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has never once raised its voice, in any account anyone tells of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waits exactly as long as it's asked to, and not a breath longer."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its understudy title is literal — it defers to something above it, always, on the hard cases."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the same choice to everyone: upright or reversed, and means it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It remembers every name it's ever been sent for, in order, without a ledger."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The scythe flips itself in its grip without its hand moving, mid-conversation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It sets the scythe down entirely and simply asks what the dying one actually wants."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "planar"],"activity":["standing at a threshold with its scythe held reversed, blade turned away from whoever it's addressing", "listening, actually listening, to what a dying thing wants before doing anything about it"]},{"name":"The Squared Circle","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"rlm-the-squared-circle","summary":"Stands at impossible angles that hurt to look at, guarding by geometry alone.","flavor":"A guardian built from angles that shouldn't close, stone folded through geometry the eye refuses to finish — looking straight at it is the mistake.","desc":"It stands built from angles that refuse to agree with each other, stone folded through a geometry the eye can't finish resolving, and looking straight at it for too long is the actual mistake. It doesn't block a doorway so much as it blocks the geometry of getting through one. Moss on it spirals the wrong direction. It has stood in its corner long enough that the room has started to measure wrong around it, not just at it.","traits":{"note": "Its wrongness is the trap — staring at it too long should disorient rather than trigger a fixed mechanic (the DM's call); the frame's numbers still govern the fight itself."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its edges don't agree with each other from any two angles at once."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moss grows on it in patterns that spiral the wrong way."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has stood in the same spot long enough that the floor around it has worn into a shape matching it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never blocks the door directly — only the geometry of getting through it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chips knocked from it reveal more angles inside, not plain stone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Staring at its seam too long leaves an afterimage that doesn't match what was actually there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one instant it resolves into a perfectly ordinary shape, then unfolds wrong again, worse."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It folds fully open, and the space behind it isn't the wall that used to be there."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins"],"activity":["standing at a corner that measures wrong from every direction you approach it", "resolving, for half a second, into a shape the eye can hold, then folding back away"]},{"name":"Sphinx of the Seventh Gate","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Celestial","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-secrets","model":"sphinx-of-secrets","summary":"Reclines at the gate, mid-riddle, and won't move until it's answered honestly.","flavor":"Gold-flecked and reclined mid-question, it guards the seventh gate the way it has guarded every gate before it — with a riddle that has to be earned, not solved by force.","desc":"Gold-flecked, reclined across the threshold of the seventh gate mid-question, it guards the way it has always guarded — with a riddle that has to be earned honestly, never forced. It watches a querent's face in the half-second before they answer more closely than it watches the answer itself. It has asked its riddle to six gates' worth of travelers and reworded it every single time, fitting the question to whoever stands in front of it. It will not move for force; it will move, gladly, for a true answer or an honest one.","traits":{"note": "It never attacks a party that engages the riddle in good faith — its attitude opens Neutral and rises toward Warm/Ally with a true or clever answer, and drops to Hostile only against those who try to force the gate instead of answering."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gold flecks catch light that isn't in the room."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats a wrong answer back exactly, without correction, just to watch it land."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has asked the same riddle to six gates' worth of travelers and never once repeated the wording."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reclines a little further when it's genuinely curious about the answer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a second riddle, easier, to a querent who answered honestly but wrong."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It knows the answer a querent hasn't said yet, and waits anyway."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It asks a riddle that has no correct answer, only an honest one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It sets aside the riddle to name the true question the querent should have asked instead."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "planar", "ruins"],"activity":["reclining across the threshold of the seventh gate, tail curling once as it finishes its question", "watching a querent's face for the half-second before they answer, more interested in that than the answer itself"]},{"name":"The Borrowed Tomb","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rlm-the-borrowed-tomb","summary":"Walks with its lid ajar, collecting tenants and nailing up their masks.","flavor":"A sarcophagus that walks, lid ajar, gathering occupants as it goes — the masks of its tenants nailed to its outside, one for every name it's collected.","desc":"A sarcophagus walks with its lid perpetually ajar, sand pouring from the seam and never running dry, gathering occupants the way a tomb gathers dust. Nailed to its outside are the masks of everyone it has already collected, one per name, murmuring faintly out of step with each other when it moves. It always has room, somehow, for exactly one more. Free a tenant mid-journey — pry loose a nailed mask — and the tomb goes quieter by exactly that much.","traits":{"note": "It adds a mask, and a tenant, for anyone it swallows whole — prying loose a prior tenant's nailed mask mid-fight frees them and weakens the Tomb by exactly that increment."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lid never fully closes, no matter how it's angled."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each mask nailed to it is carved with a different name in a different hand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums, badly, a funeral hymn none of its tenants would have chosen."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sand pours from the seam of its lid with every step, and never runs out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has room, somehow, for one more, always exactly one more."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of its masks is blank, waiting, and it keeps glancing down at it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It opens its lid toward a party member specifically, unprompted, an invitation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It cracks fully open and every mask speaks at once, in the borrowed voices of everyone it's carried."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "desert", "ruins"],"activity":["shambling forward with its lid swinging ajar, masks rattling loose against its stone side", "pausing to nail up a fresh mask over the space where an empty one used to hang"]},{"name":"Canopic Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","model":"rlm-canopic-swarm","summary":"four scuttling canopic jars, each demanding its due","flavor":"Four sealed jars skitter as one, each stamped with a different god's face and each one certain the dead still owes it a piece.","desc":"Four alabaster jars move as a single animal, lids carved into the faces of falcon, jackal, baboon, and man, clattering across stone on legs no embalmer ever gave them. Each was sealed with a portion of someone's viscera and a promise; each has decided the promise was never paid in full. They circle anything that breathes, lids chattering half-formed accountancy, tallying a debt only they can read. Break one open and the other three only tighten the circle.","traits":{"note": "They only ever collect a portion — half the swarm always breaks off to carry its 'payment' back to the tomb it guards, so a fight against them is never quite the whole four."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One jar's seal has cracked; it leaks a thin trail of grey sand wherever it scuttles."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The falcon-lidded jar always takes point, the other three falling in behind it in strict order."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their lids are carved with a name half-worn away — someone tried to scratch it out, long ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They circle a fresh footprint three times before deciding whether to give chase."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One jar is chipped and lighter than the rest; it lags, then sprints to catch up."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They stop dead the instant an offering — food, coin, breath held in tribute — is set before them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Peer inside a cracked one and the organ within is still warm, centuries on."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shatter all four in the same round and what spills isn't sand or viscera, but hours — the victim's own hours, aging them on the spot."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins"],"activity":["scuttling in tight formation across tomb floors, lids clattering out a shared tally", "circling anything that breathes, deciding what portion of it is owed"]},{"name":"The Reader Who Read Too Far","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-the-reader-who-read-too-far","summary":"fallen oracle, cards orbiting her, starfield eyes","flavor":"An oracle who read one spread past the edge of the deck's mercy — her cards never settled, and neither did her eyes, which now hold a sky that isn't this one.","desc":"She sits cross-legged on a cracked reading-cloth, spine straight, hands folded, while a full deck of cards orbits her head in a slow unwilled halation, none of them ever landing face-up. Where her eyes should be is a field of cold stars, and when she speaks it's in the cadence of a reading that never concluded, one card always still to turn. She was the finest reader in the temple once, until she asked the deck a question it wasn't built to answer, and it has never let go of her since. Approach and she reads you too, whether you ask or not.","traits":{"note": "Every creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of her is due one unwilled card-read — the DM narrates a true, unwelcome fact about that creature drawn from the orbiting deck, at no mechanical cost but never withheld."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her reading-cloth is still laid out precisely, temple-fashion, beneath the ruin she sits in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She addresses everyone by the card that's currently facing them, not by name."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hands still make the old temple gestures for a closing benediction, over and over, unfinished."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single card near her orbits slower than the rest, as if reluctant."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She remembers her own name only when a card that matches it comes around."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll trade a straight answer about the future for one true thing about your past — and she always knows if you lied."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment her voice comes from behind you instead of in front, mid-sentence."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill her mid-reading and every orbiting card completes its spread at once, face-up, showing everyone present a truth they didn't ask to know."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins"],"activity":["sitting motionless on a cracked reading-cloth while a full deck orbits her skull", "reading anyone who lingers near her, whether they've asked a question or not"]},{"name":"The Deck-Sharper","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"rlm-the-deck-sharper","summary":"grinning card-dealer, stakes paid in years of life","flavor":"A grinning dealer who's set his folding table up at every crossroads that ever mattered, running a game with real arcana and stakes denominated in years, not coin.","desc":"His table folds out of nowhere — green baize, a lantern, a deck that's never quite the same deck twice — and his smile promises you'll walk away better than you sat down. The cards he deals are true correspondences, not props: draw the Tower and something in the room actually falls. He never cheats outright; he doesn't have to, when the house always sets the wager in years rather than gold. Everyone who's ever won at his table is still trying to remember what they gave up to do it.","traits":{"note": "He engages first through the social-attitude system — a player willing to sit and play can shift him from wary toward Friendly across a hand or two, and a Friendly Sharper deals honestly and even folds a losing round on purpose; push him to Hostile and the table folds away along with any chance of winning back what was wagered."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his lantern burning on oil that never seems to run low."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Deals with both hands, one for the mark and one for the deck no one's supposed to see."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His table only ever seats three, no matter how many stand around it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a different ring for every game he's ever won, stacked to the knuckle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice, win or lose — the smile does all the talking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will stake information, not just years, if you've got nothing else worth his time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cards on his table are warm to the touch, like they've just been read by someone else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him past Hostile and he simply calls the whole game — the wager comes due immediately, in full, no cards required."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["setting up a folding table at a crossroads with a lantern and a waiting deck", "dealing hands with real arcana while reciting the stakes in years, not coin"]},{"name":"The Name-Eater","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"rlm-name-eater","summary":"Negative-space devourer that swallows true names and leaves you unaddressable","flavor":"A figure of negative space swallowing a written word. Around it, faces go polite and blank: they have simply never met you.","desc":"In a realm where the true name commands, the worst theft is not death — it's deletion from the ledger of address. The Name-Eater is a silhouette where a person should be, and it eats names: spoken ones from the air mid-sentence, written ones off the page, true ones out of the world's index. Its victims still exist. They simply cannot be referred to — mothers introduce themselves twice, wards omit them, doors sealed 'to all but friends' no longer count them as anyone at all.","traits":{"note": "Its bite doesn't wound — it UNADDRESSES: a named target loses one 'address' per hit (NPCs' memory of them, inclusion in wards, the efficacy of their spoken word) on a visible ladder the DM narrates. Names are recoverable from wherever it nests — it hoards them physically, as objects — and speaking its OWN true name (it has one; it hates this) staggers it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ink lifts off the page in thin smoke wherever it has passed; the paper is otherwise untouched."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its outline is only visible where dust, rain, or incense defines the space it displaces."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Conversations near it shed proper nouns; everyone slides into 'that place' and 'him, you know.'"}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It walks the stacks of a records hall like a gourmand reading a menu."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Somewhere behind it trails a person asking strangers, with dying hope, to say who they are."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It is eating its way ALPHABETICALLY through a specific register — the next name is derivable."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its nest is a chamber of stolen names roosting like birds; they answer, faintly, when called."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has begun on the name of the TOWN itself — roads now bend around a place carts can no longer be told to reach."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing in a scriptorium as a man-shaped absence while pages go blank line by line", "pausing mid-street to swallow a shouted greeting before it can land"]},{"name":"The 23rd Card, Walking","cr":12,"role":"apex","type":"Celestial","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-lore","model":"rlm-23rd-card-walking","summary":"The card that isn't in any deck, stepped out of its own frame","flavor":"A tarot card the size of a door, and its figure has stepped out of the frame. There is no 23rd major arcana. It knows that.","desc":"Every deck in the realm has twenty-two majors, and every reader will swear to it, and every one of them owns a deck with a worn place where a twenty-third used to sit. The Card walks as its own illustration — inks shifting, border gilding dragging behind it like a hem — and where it passes, readings change tense. It does not fight so much as REVISE: what it touches gets an arcana assigned, and the arcana plays out. Meeting it is how the tarot engine wakes in a world.","traits":{"note": "Encountering it ACTIVATES the tarot layer for this world (the 23rd-card awakening — see the realm identity ruling). It cannot be fought conventionally while unnamed; the engagement is a READING — it deals, the player rolls the draw, and its 'attacks' are arcana landing as events. Banishing it back into a deck requires an empty 23rd slot, which every deck has."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its face is worn blank at the center, like a coin rubbed by a century of thumbs."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Card-stock creaks when it moves; its shadow falls as a crisp rectangle regardless of the light."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every reader in town woke last night and counted their deck, and won't say why."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its reversed posture — walking on its hands, upside down — means something different and worse."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gold leaf flakes off its border and lands as tiny, accurate fortunes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It deals a single card to someone in the scene, face down; the card is a blank until its moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "People who study its face too long appear, small and background, in its illustration afterward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It offers the world a READING — three cards, world-scale stakes — and abides utterly by the result; so does the world, forever."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "planar"],"activity":["walking a colonnade at dusk, border-gilding dragging like a wedding train", "standing in a fortune-teller's doorway, waiting to be counted"]}],
 "theater":[{"name":"Line Infantry Shade","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"guard","summary":"Rank-and-file trench ghost, holds the line by rote","flavor":"A rifleman still dressed by a drill he can't remember learning; he holds a section of trench because holding it is the only order left in him.","desc":"Mud to the knees, rifle held at a drilled slant, he stands a fire-step like it's still worth holding. His face under the helmet-brim is slack, unhurried, the eyes fixed on a horizon that isn't there anymore. He moves only when the line moves.","traits":{"note": "It only moves when the line around it moves — isolate it and it barely reacts at all.", "actions": [{"name": "Drilled Thrust", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage, delivered in the exact drilled motion it's repeated a thousand times."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing its helmet; keeps reaching up to a brim that isn't there."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boots gone, feet bare and blistered, still holds the step like nothing's wrong."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the same three orders on a loop, never varying the words."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger than the rest — voice hasn't finished breaking, drill hasn't either."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a photograph tucked in a breast pocket it never opens."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Salutes anything that gives an order in the right cadence, friend or not."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its rifle is rusted solid to its hands; it thrusts with the whole weapon like a stake."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the line finally breaks it doesn't rout — it just stops, mid-motion, forever."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["standing a fire-step in mud to the knee, rifle slanted at a horizon that isn't there"]},{"name":"Wire-Cutter Scout","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"bandit-courier","summary":"Silent night-crawler who counts sentries for something","flavor":"Crawls the gaps between lines at night, snipping wire and counting sentries; talks to no one, reports to something.","desc":"He crosses the wire on his belly, wire-cutters clicking soft as teeth, and doesn't so much as breathe loud. Every few yards he stops dead and counts something under his breath — sentries, maybe, or seconds. He never looks back at whoever sent him.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cutters", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from a snub wire-cutting blade driven up under a rib."}, {"name": "Sighted Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, loosed only after a long, silent count."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Scout makes two attacks, never with the same weapon twice in a row."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears mismatched gloves stripped off two different dead men."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks a tally on its forearm for every wire it's cut tonight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Freezes utterly still at any unexpected sound, sometimes for minutes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cutters are notched and dull; it saws rather than snips now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no weapon but the cutters until cornered, then draws the bow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The count it mutters matches a number no one alive would recognize as a name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has cut the same stretch of wire in three different uniforms across three different nights."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finishing its count seems to trigger something behind it in the dark — it never looks to see what."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["crawling the gap between the lines at night, cutters clicking soft as teeth", "stopping dead every few yards to count something under its breath"]},{"name":"Whistle-Blown Runner","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Message-runner forever mid-sprint toward the whistle","flavor":"Carries messages between shattered command posts at a dead sprint; the whistle that sends him over is always just about to blow again.","desc":"He comes at a flat sprint, chest heaving, one hand clamped over a satchel of dispatches that don't matter anymore. Somewhere behind him a whistle is always just finishing its note. He runs the same fifty yards over and over, and never arrives.","traits":{"note": "It runs a fixed route between two points that no longer exist as anything but habit.", "actions": [{"name": "Desperate Jab", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage, thrown off without breaking stride."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Satchel flaps open, dispatches long since rotted to pulp inside."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One boot is gone; it runs lopsided and doesn't seem to notice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gasps a name between breaths, always the same one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swerves around an obstacle that isn't there anymore, every single time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger-looking than the rest, cheeks still round under the grime."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its fifty yards overlaps exactly with wherever the party is currently standing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whistle behind it never finishes its note; the Runner never stops waiting for the rest of it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If it ever completes its sprint uninterrupted, it simply winks out mid-stride, message undelivered forever."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["sprinting the same fifty yards flat out, satchel clamped tight, never arriving"]},{"name":"Duckboard Vermin Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Fearless rat-swarm that owns the trench floor at night","flavor":"Fat and fearless on a diet no one wants named, they own the flooded duckboards after dark and don't scatter for the living anymore.","desc":"They move over the sunken boards in a single wet ripple, unbothered by boots, unbothered by torches. This ground was theirs before you got here and it'll be theirs after. Something crunches underfoot that you decide not to look at.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Swarming Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, worse while the swarm occupies the target's space."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fat past all reason on a diet nobody wants named out loud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters from flame just enough to look afraid, then closes right back in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in a boot left standing upright at the trench's low point."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in total silence, no squeaking, no scurry, only the wet ripple."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thicker on one flank, thinned to nothing on the other."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Something underfoot crunches that isn't board or bone, and the swarm doesn't react to it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It never crosses a specific stretch of duckboard, no matter how it's baited or driven."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given a full night undisturbed it swells past swarm size into something that no longer scatters at all."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "urban"],"activity":["rippling over sunken duckboards in a single wet mass, unbothered by boots or torchlight"]},{"name":"Mustard Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"manes-vaporspawn","model":"manes-vaporspawn","summary":"Drifting toxic gas-cloud that hunts low ground blind","flavor":"A drifting yellow-green bank that used to be a chemical order given from far behind the lines; it rolls into low ground and doesn't care whose lungs it finds.","desc":"A low yellow-green bank rolls across the ground at knee height, unhurried, patient, following the dip of the land into every low place a man might hide. It doesn't chase. It just waits for the ground to funnel you toward it.","traits":{"note": "It never chases — it only ever waits for the terrain to funnel prey into it.", "actions": [{"name": "Searing Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Poison damage as a curl of yellow-green vapor closes around exposed skin."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bleaches every blade of grass it drifts over a sick, uniform yellow."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thicker and slower after rain, thin and quick to spread in dry heat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the faint smell of the order that first released it, sweetish and wrong."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pools in a shell crater and simply waits there for days at a time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Splits around an obstacle and reknits itself perfectly on the far side."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Rolls against the wind rather than with it, as if it's still following an old command."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Faces briefly surface in its coiling surface, mouths open, and are gone before they can be named."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given a valley to fill, it stops being a cloud and becomes the valley's new, permanent weather."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "elemental"],"activity":["rolling knee-high across low ground, patient, following the dip of the land toward wherever men are hiding"]},{"name":"Barbed Kill-Zone Tangle","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"gas-spore-fungus","model":"rlm-barbed-kill-zone-tangle","summary":"Living wire-tangle that snags then reels men in","flavor":"Coiled wire gone wrong, grown thorned and hungry between the lines; it snags a boot first and pulls the rest of the man in after.","desc":"The wire here has grown thorns that weren't forged, only sharpened by something patient. A boot catches, and the whole tangle draws taut like a fist closing. It doesn't let go once it's caught what it wanted.","traits":{"note": "Once it has snagged a boot, it does not release its hold voluntarily.", "actions": [{"name": "Barbed Snare", "replaces": "Tendril", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 10 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 11) by coiled wire that draws taut."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rusted a deep orange-brown, thorns brittle but still parting skin easily."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grown through the ribs of something that stopped struggling a long time ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils tighter around metal than flesh, as if it prefers the taste of steel."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Anchored to a fence post that has otherwise rotted away entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Low and flat, easy to miss until the first boot catches."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Draws taut all at once across a whole stretch of ground, not just one strand."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Grows faster near old blood, thickening overnight where a fight recently happened."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Left unchecked for a season, it laces an entire field shut, one long closing fist."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["lying coiled and still between the lines, thorns catching the last light like teeth"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Regular","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Volley-fire rifleman lost in permanent powder smoke","flavor":"Loads, presents, fires in volley by rote; the smoke never fully clears from a face that's forgotten peace.","desc":"He loads, presents, and fires in the same three motions he's fired a hundred times, smoke curling up past a face gone flat with repetition. The volley beside him thunders and he doesn't so much as blink. Peace, if he ever had a memory of it, is gone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Clubbed Musket", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d12 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from a musket swung stock-first once the volley's spent."}, {"name": "Volley Shot", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, fired in the same three drilled motions every time."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform coat scorched black across one shoulder from a musket that once misfired."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reloads with hands that shake constantly but never actually fumble the motion."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coughs on smoke that seems thicker around him than the men beside him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Presents his weapon a half-beat ahead of the rest of the line, always."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Face gone utterly slack; peace, if he remembers it, left no mark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fires his volley even when there's no line beside him anymore to fire with."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The smoke around him never clears, thickening instead the longer the fight runs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the smoke around him finally does clear, there's no man inside the uniform at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["loading, presenting, and firing in volley by rote, smoke curling past a flat, repetitive face"]},{"name":"Longship Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Beach-charging raider screaming a nameless war-cry","flavor":"Comes off the beach at a dead run, screaming a war-cry with no god's name left in it, only the noise.","desc":"He comes off the beach at a dead sprint, mouth open on a war-cry that lost its god's name generations back — just noise now, just momentum. Sand kicks up behind bare feet. He hits the line before the line finishes forming.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Boarding Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from a weighted mace swung with a beach-charge's full momentum."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Raider makes two attacks with its mace, first strike landing before the line finishes forming."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bare feet, sand still kicked up behind every stride even on hard ground."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "War-cry cracks halfway through, like the voice remembers it stopped meaning anything."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a shield with no house-mark left legible on its face."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs faster than the others, always first to close, never first to fall back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes fixed past the enemy line, toward a ship none of the living can see."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Charges the same stretch of shore no matter which direction the actual fight is happening."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves no footprints behind it, even sprinting across wet sand."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When its war-cry finally finds a name again, every raider on the beach echoes it back at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "grassland"],"activity":["coming off the beach at a dead sprint, mouth open on a war-cry that lost its god's name generations ago"]},{"name":"Jungle Ambusher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"scout","summary":"Silent canopy-and-mud ambusher, gone before you see him","flavor":"Fights from the canopy and the mud both, silent until the moment he isn't; the vines remember where he waited.","desc":"He's part of the mud until the second he isn't, rising soundless out of ground-level cover with a blade already moving. Vines still hang off one shoulder. By the time you register motion, he's already somewhere else.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ambush Blade", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, and double damage if the Ambusher has not yet acted this combat."}, {"name": "Canopy Whisper", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "DC 12 Wisdom save on one creature within 30 ft. that can see him. Failure: the target is charmed for 1 minute, certain for a moment that the Ambusher is an ally already known to them."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ambusher makes two attacks with its blade, silent between each."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Face and forearms striped in mud so exact it reads as deliberate camouflage paint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves through standing water without a single ripple giving him away."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vines from his last ambush site still trail off one shoulder, never shed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits far longer than any living man reasonably could before striking."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blade notched from cutting through more than just flesh over the years."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The vines nearest his old ambush spots seem to lean subtly toward wherever he's hiding now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves a print in the mud identical to one already found nearby, hours old."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given time to wait unchallenged, the canopy itself starts moving in sympathy with him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["rising soundless out of ground-level cover, vines still hanging off one shoulder, blade already moving"]},{"name":"Siege-Line Sapper","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"Tunnel-digger laying the charge that breaches the wall","flavor":"Digs toward the wall under fire, laying the charge that will open it; talks about the tunnel like it's a person he's killing slowly.","desc":"He digs toward the wall on his knees, one ear pressed to the earth, listening for the counter-tunnel that might already be listening back. He talks to the tunnel like it's something he's killing slowly, patiently, on purpose. The charge he's laying is only the last part of a much longer conversation.","traits":{"note": "He carries the charge on his back — everyone near him is standing in the blast radius, including him.", "actions": [{"name": "Entrenching Blade", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage from a broad-bladed digging tool swung in earnest."}, {"name": "Counter-Tunnel Bolt", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Piercing damage, fired one-handed while still listening to the earth."}, {"name": "Set the Charge", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Sapper plants and blows a charge against the nearest hard surface or cluster of foes. Each creature within 10 ft. makes a DC 13 Dexterity save, taking 14 (4d6) Bludgeoning damage on a failure, half on a success. Any wall or barrier in the radius is breached — the point of the whole exercise."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Deaf in one ear from the last charge that went early."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts under his breath constantly; he's timing something."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fingers stained black to the second knuckle from handling powder."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't fight in the open — pulls back toward cover and dirt on instinct."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a letter he means to finish once the wall comes down."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His charge is already set and lit somewhere the party can't see; there's a clock now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's dug this same sap in a dozen wars and can't remember which one he's in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's standing on the main charge and would rather take the party with him than leave the work undone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["crouched at the base of a wall setting a charge with shaking, practiced hands", "crawling a forward sap toward a breach that isn't there yet"]},{"name":"Barbed-Wire Horror","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"rlm-theater-revenant","summary":"Wire-impaled corpse that never fell, still reaching","flavor":"A body the wire never let fall, stitched upright by rust and old rage; it still reaches for the men who left it there.","desc":"The wire never let it fall, and it never really has since — rust-stitched upright, arms still reaching the direction the charge was going. Old rage keeps its joints moving long after the tendons should have failed. It doesn't remember why it's reaching, only that it hasn't stopped.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't remember why it reaches — only that stopping isn't a thing it's done yet.", "actions": [{"name": "Wire-Threaded Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Necrotic damage as rust-crusted fingers close and drag warmth out with them; the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Impaled Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage from a sword still bound to its wrist by the same wire that holds it up."}, {"name": "Snapped Wire Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage from a bowstring strung with old barbed wire."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes two attacks, never releasing the wire that holds it standing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Held upright by a full cage of wire wrapped through both shoulders."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm reaches at an angle no living joint could hold, fixed permanently that way."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wire hums faintly in wind, a note the Horror seems to twitch toward."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust has spread from the wire into the flesh itself, staining it deep orange."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boots long gone, feet fused into the mud it's stood in for years."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its reaching arm points, with unsettling precision, at wherever the enemy line currently stands."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wire holding it up predates the fence it's tangled in by a visible margin of rust."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut free of its wire, it doesn't collapse — it simply keeps reaching, faster, unanchored now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["reaching, rust-stitched upright, arms still pointed the direction the charge was going"]},{"name":"The Unkillable Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"NCO who won't stay dead, keeps ordering the charge","flavor":"Shot, gassed, and buried three times over the objection of his own men, he gets back up cursing and orders the charge again anyway.","desc":"Shot, gassed, and buried three separate times over his own men's loud objections, he climbs back out cursing at a volume that carries the length of the trench. He gives the same order he always gives. Nobody's found a way yet to make it stick.","traits":{"note": "Nobody's found a way yet to make his death stick — he simply gets back up.", "actions": [{"name": "NCO's Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage, delivered with the flat contempt of a man who's swung it too many times to be afraid."}, {"name": "Grave-Won Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage; the Sergeant regains hit points equal to the damage dealt, a habit from being killed too many times to count."}, {"name": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "The Sergeant barks the order one final time. Up to three Undead within 60 ft. that can hear him gain advantage on their next attack roll and cannot be frightened until the end of their next turn."}, {"name": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the Sergeant makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or becomes frightened of him for 1 minute, reliving whichever burial it was that didn't take."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sergeant makes two attacks, choosing freely between his blade and his grasp."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three separate burial-shroud scraps still cling to his uniform, never fully shed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice carries a rasp that no amount of cursing seems to clear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to acknowledge the gas-scarring across half his face."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Orders the same three names to fall in, though none of them answer anymore."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a whistle he never blows, only fingers absently between orders."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His own men buried him a fourth time quietly, hoping nobody mentions it to him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dirt he climbs out of is always fresh, no matter how long since he was last put down."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed a fifth time in front of witnesses, he simply gives the order from the ground, and something answers it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["climbing back out of a shallow grave cursing at a volume that carries the trench's length", "giving the same order he always gives, again, to men who've heard it before"]},{"name":"Hedgerow Tank-Killer","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"tough-boss","summary":"Bocage ambusher waiting to drop a war-machine cold","flavor":"Waits in the bocage with a tube on his shoulder for a machine bigger than any dragon he's heard of in stories; one shot, one silence.","desc":"He waits flat in the bocage hedge with a tube braced on one shoulder, patient past what should be reasonable, watching a shape bigger than anything in his own war's mythology grind closer. One shot. Then a silence that swallows whatever noise the machine was making.","traits":{"note": "He waits past what should be reasonable — one shot is the whole plan, and there is no second one.", "actions": [{"name": "Hedge Ambush Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage, drawn only once the tube's single shot is already spent."}, {"name": "Loaded Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage from a hand-thrown backup once the real weapon's empty."}, {"name": "One Shot", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Tank-Killer fires his tube at one Large or larger target within 60 ft. Ranged Attack Roll: +6. Hit: 18 (4d8) Fire damage, and the target is deafened until the end of its next turn by the silence that follows."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Tank-Killer makes two attacks with his javelin or blade, but never combines these with his one shot in the same turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves stripped bare and eaten to lace by whatever waiting this long does to a hedge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts his own heartbeat instead of a clock, patient past any living pulse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tube slung with a strap salvaged from three different uniforms."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't fire on anything smaller than the shape he's actually waiting for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes never blink while tracking the machine's approach."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The silence after his shot swallows every other sound on the field for a long moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's been in this exact hedge, in this exact posture, through more than one war's worth of machines."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied his one shot long enough, he stops waiting and simply walks toward the machine himself."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "grassland", "forest"],"activity":["lying flat in the hedge with a tube braced on one shoulder, watching a shape grind closer than any dragon in his own war's stories"]},{"name":"Longship Warlord","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"ettin","model":"hill-giant","summary":"Giant raider-chief armored in three lines' worth of plate","flavor":"Twice the size a man should be, armored in captured plates from three different lines; the beach is his only law.","desc":"He stands twice the size a man ought to be, armored in captured plates scavenged off three separate battle-lines that never fought each other before he made them. The beach answers to him and nothing else does. He doesn't raise his voice — the size does that for him.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't raise his voice on the beach — his size does that work for him.", "actions": [{"name": "Salvaged Battleaxe", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage from an axe assembled out of three different armies' steel."}, {"name": "Trophy Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage from a spiked head taken off an officer who no longer needs it."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Warlord makes two attacks, one with each looted weapon."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plate on his left side is clearly foreign, riveted on crooked over the original armor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a fourth line's medal upside-down as a joke only he finds funny."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice is quiet, almost gentle, entirely at odds with the size of him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of beaches taken carved into his own forearm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steps deliberately slow, letting the size register before the violence does."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One plate on his chest still bears a rank insignia from a war generations before this one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every piece of his armor was taken off a man who, by rights, should have outlived him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given an unclaimed beach long enough, he starts stripping armor off his own men to add to the plate."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["coast", "sea", "hill"],"activity":["standing twice the size a man ought to be, armored in captured plates off three lines that never fought each other before him"]},{"name":"Trench Ghast","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"No-man's-land feeder that mimics the whistle to lure prey","flavor":"Feeds in no-man's-land where nobody goes to collect the dead; it has learned to imitate the whistle to lure the living out.","desc":"It feeds where nobody goes to collect the dead, patient in the space between the lines, and it has learned to shape its throat around the exact pitch of the whistle. When it blows that note, boots start moving before anyone decides to listen. It's very good at getting men to come to it.","traits":{"note": "It has learned the whistle's exact pitch — boots move before anyone decides to listen.", "actions": [{"name": "Feeding Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape DC 13)."}, {"name": "Rot-Rimed Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be paralyzed for 1 minute; it can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "The Borrowed Note", "text": "The Ghast shapes its throat around the whistle's exact pitch. One creature within 60 ft. that can hear it makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, the target is compelled to move its full speed toward the Ghast on its next turn by the safest route it perceives, unaware anything is wrong until it arrives."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throat visibly distended, shaped wrong from years of forcing that one note."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in a shell crater ringed with things it didn't finish."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only feeds at the exact hour the real whistle used to sound."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at any whistle it didn't make itself, as if offended."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves low and fast between craters, never silhouetted against the sky."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's gotten good enough at the note that even the party's own instincts twitch toward it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its call layers under the real whistle when both sound at once, indistinguishable to anyone but the dead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given an unburied field to work, it starts sounding the note continuously, and no-man's-land starts emptying toward it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["feeding in no-man's-land where nobody comes to collect the dead, patient in the space between the lines"]},{"name":"Jungle Beast-Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Handler who marches a chained horror as a living breacher","flavor":"Marches a chained horror ahead of his own line as a breach-weapon; the leash is the only thing keeping the front intact.","desc":"He marches a chained horror a full length ahead of his own line, leash wrapped twice around one fist, using it the way another man might use a shield. The beast strains against him with every step. The leash is the only thing between the front line and whatever's on the other end of it.","traits":{"note": "The leash is the only thing between the front line and whatever's on the other end of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Handler's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage as the chained horror lunges the length of its leash on his command."}, {"name": "Chained Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage from the beast raking forward as far as the leash allows."}, {"name": "Slip the Leash", "text": "The Handler releases a length of chain. The beast's reach increases by 5 feet until the start of the Handler's next turn, but the Handler takes 4 (1d8) Slashing damage from the chain tearing across his own palm."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Handler directs the beast to make two attacks, bite and claws, at the length the leash currently allows."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Palm scarred permanently into a fist shape from years gripping the same chain."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks to the beast in a low, constant murmur that seems to keep it calm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leash is patched with a dozen different metals, none of them matching."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks a full stride behind the beast rather than beside it, out of old caution."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to feed the beast anything but what he catches himself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The chain shows fresh stress-fractures; it won't hold through this fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The beast obeys a command language that doesn't match any tongue the Handler speaks otherwise."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the chain snaps, the Handler doesn't run — he starts giving the beast new orders, delighted."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["marching a chained horror a full length ahead of his own line, leash wrapped twice around one straining fist"]},{"name":"Iron Crawler War-Machine","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Treaded armored hull grinding across the wire alone","flavor":"A rivet-scarred hull dragging itself across the wire on tracks it wasn't built to have; the crew inside stopped answering the hatch a long time ago.","desc":"A rivet-scarred hull drags itself across the wire on tracks that were clearly never meant to survive this ground, engine note grinding low and wrong. The hatch on top hasn't opened in longer than anyone's willing to guess. Whoever answers from inside it doesn't answer anymore.","traits":{"note": "The hatch on top hasn't opened in longer than anyone's willing to guess.", "actions": [{"name": "Tread and Ram", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage as the hull grinds forward over whatever's in its path."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The War-Machine makes two ram attacks, or one and rolls over a prone target's space, dealing the same damage again to it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tracks shed rust in a visible trail behind it, marking exactly where it's been."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Engine note skips every seventh beat, like something inside is misfiring."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hull scorched black on one side from a fire that clearly didn't stop it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a dead-straight line regardless of terrain, grinding over obstacles rather than around."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hatch welded shut from the outside by hands that aren't its crew's."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Something inside knocks on the hull in a rhythm that isn't the engine's."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has run for longer than any fuel supply should allow, and shows no sign of stopping for it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damaged past a certain point, the hatch finally grinds open, and whatever answers isn't the crew."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["dragging its rivet-scarred hull across the wire on tracks never meant to survive this ground, engine grinding low and wrong"]},{"name":"Legion Standard-Breaker","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"rlm-theater-legion","summary":"Flag-devoted killer who believes in nothing but the fight","flavor":"Fights for the flag more than the cause, and the flag has no name anyone will say out loud; kills beautifully, believes in nothing.","desc":"He fights for the flag more than any cause it's supposed to stand for, and the flag itself has stopped meaning anything anyone will say out loud. His strikes are clean, almost beautiful. He believes in the fight and nothing underneath it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Standard-Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage, or 13 (1d10 + 5) Piercing damage if used with both hands, thrown with parade-ground precision."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked prone by a shield still bearing the flag's faded device."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Standard-Breaker makes two attacks, spear and shield, in whichever order looks best."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flag on his shield is bleached past recognition, just a pale rectangle now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights with a small, satisfied smile that never quite reaches a grin."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps immaculate form even mid-combat, footwork textbook to the last step."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses easy kills, drawing fights out for the pleasure of the motion."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes fallen opponents with genuine, empty respect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Someone in the party recognizes the flag's device from a cause long since abandoned."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He's fought under this same faded standard in wars that couldn't possibly share a flag."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given a truly excellent opponent, he'll stop fighting for the flag entirely and fight only for the fight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "grassland"],"activity":["fighting clean and almost beautiful for a flag that's stopped meaning anything anyone will say out loud"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Cavalry Officer","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Officer charging cannon-fire on horseback for the order alone","flavor":"Charges a line of guns on horseback because the order came down and orders are the only faith he has left.","desc":"He rides at a measured trot straight toward a line of leveled guns, sword raised, because the order came down and orders are the only faith he has left. Smoke swallows him and the horse both for a moment. When it clears he's still coming.","traits":{"note": "Orders are the only faith he has left — smoke swallows him and the horse, and he's still coming when it clears.", "actions": [{"name": "Cavalry Saber", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage delivered from horseback at a full charging trot."}, {"name": "Sidearm Volley", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage from a mounted pistol fired one-handed."}, {"name": "The Order Came Down", "text": "The Officer spurs forward, ignoring opportunity attacks from the leveled guns ahead as if they weren't there. He gains advantage on his next attack this turn."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Officer makes two attacks, saber and sidearm, without breaking the trot."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform immaculate despite the smoke, as if pressed fresh this morning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Horse shows powder-burns along one flank that never seem to slow it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sword arm raised at the exact same angle every single charge, unwavering."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks the order aloud each time, quietly, like a private prayer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never breaks eye contact with the guns ahead until the smoke takes him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The order he's obeying was given by an officer long dead, and he still hears it fresh."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Emerges from smoke that shouldn't have concealed him that long, closer than he should be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the guns finally do drop him, the order simply passes to the nearest man still standing, and he rides too."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["riding a measured trot straight toward a line of leveled guns, sword raised, because the order came down"]},{"name":"The Line That Held","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Animate trench-line that simply refuses to yield ground","flavor":"A stretch of trench itself, animated by every soldier who swore to hold it and did, until holding was all that was left; it does not attack so much as refuse to move.","desc":"A whole stretch of trench itself seems to be standing its ground, animated by every soldier who swore to hold it and did, right up until holding was the only thing left of them. It doesn't lash out so much as simply refuse to move. Ground given up to it doesn't come back easily.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't attack so much as refuse to yield — ground given up to it doesn't come back easily.", "actions": [{"name": "The Line Answers", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Force damage as a length of animate trench-wall and duckboard closes like a fist around whatever's pressing it."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Line makes two attacks, striking from two different points along its own length at once."}, {"name": "Held Ground", "text": "Until the start of its next turn, any enemy creature that enters or ends its turn within 10 ft. of the Line must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or have its speed reduced to 0 until the end of that turn, mud and old wire remembering how to hold a man in place."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Duckboards along its length still bear boot-prints from soldiers who never left."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sandbags stacked into something like a face, watching without eyes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sections of wire along its body pull taut whenever an order is shouted nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells permanently of cordite and turned earth, even in open air."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grows visibly by inches each time it holds ground successfully."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A stretch of the trench nearby is already part of it, and doesn't know it yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers holding this exact ground in wars that predate this one by generations."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed back once, it doesn't retreat — it roots the new ground and starts holding that instead."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["standing its ground as a whole stretch of animate trench, refusing, simply, to move"]},{"name":"Longship Draugr-Captain","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"wraith","summary":"Drowned captain still commanding his dead crew ashore","flavor":"Drowned with his crew and rose commanding them still; the tide brings his ship back to shores that no longer remember his war.","desc":"He came up drowned with his whole crew behind him and never stopped giving them orders, seawater still running steady from his sleeves. The tide brings his ship back to shores that don't know his war anymore. He commands the dead the same way he once commanded the living — without raising his voice.","traits":{"note": "His crew will not break formation while he still stands; drop him and the thralls scatter.", "actions": [{"name": "Drowned Command", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Captain barks two orders, using Cold Grip twice, or once and directing Longship Thrall Rend."}, {"name": "Cold Grip", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Cold damage, seawater pouring from the wound."}, {"name": "The Tide Answers", "replaces": "Infernal Sting", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (4d6 + 3) Cold damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be dragged 10 feet toward the water and knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears his captain's coat, buttons green with salt corrosion."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to step past the high-tide line; the beach is his whole command."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks orders in a dialect no living sailor here understands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a waterlogged ledger of names, crossing one out after every fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His crew forms up around him instantly, closing every gap he leaves open."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The ship itself is visible at low tide, keel driven into sand that never dries."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He gives the same three orders in the same order every single fight, like a tide."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Convinced the party are deserters from his own crew, and means to make an example."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "ruins"],"activity":["standing at the tideline giving orders to a crew that stopped answering years ago", "walking the wet sand counting men who are no longer there to be counted"]},{"name":"Jungle War-Engine","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"rlm-theater-sherman","summary":"Feral jungle war-machine still firing a stale coordinate","flavor":"A siege-machine gone feral in the canopy, vines grown through its plating, still firing on a target coordinate decades stale.","desc":"Vines have grown clean through its plating and it still fires on a coordinate that stopped mattering decades ago, servos grinding against root and rust both. Birds nest in its cannon housing. It doesn't seem to register that the war it's fighting ended without it.","traits":{"note": "Its coordinate is fixed and stale — it fires past living targets at empty ground unless something crosses its sightline.", "actions": [{"name": "Overgrown Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Engine makes two Root-Choked Slam attacks, or one Slam and one Stale Coordinate."}, {"name": "Root-Choked Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, vines and rusted plating tearing loose with the blow."}, {"name": "Stale Coordinate", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Force damage to a point in space, whether or not anything is there; if a creature occupies that point it takes the damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Birds have built three nests in its cannon housing, unbothered by the grinding gears."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One tread is jammed solid; it can only pivot, never advance."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stenciled unit number is still legible under decades of rust and moss."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fires on a schedule, not a trigger — every few minutes, whether provoked or not."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roots have grown through its firing mechanism, throwing every third shot wide."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The coordinate it targets is marked on old maps as a village that no longer exists."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its targeting hums the same three notes before every shot, like a soldier's old cadence."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in the canopy has just crossed its stale coordinate for the first time in years."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["grinding through the canopy on rusted treads, cannon tracking a target that left decades ago", "sitting locked in undergrowth, servos cycling uselessly against roots grown through its joints"]},{"name":"Legion Praetor-Revenant","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Dead commander who still drills a legion by discipline alone","flavor":"Commands a legion of the dead the way he commanded the living, by discipline alone; his oath outlived his empire and his name both.","desc":"He drills the dead the same way he drilled the living, by discipline and nothing softer, and a legion falls into formation behind him without being asked twice. His voice carries the same flat authority it always did. His oath outlived the empire it was sworn to.","traits":{"note": "His dead obey instantly and without fear — discipline outlasted the flesh that built it.", "actions": [{"name": "Drill and Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Praetor makes two Dread Blade attacks, or one attack and casts a spell."}, {"name": "Dread Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Necrotic damage from a standard-issue blade that never dulled."}, {"name": "Fallen Standard", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Praetor hurls a burning legion standard at a point within 60 ft. Each creature within 15 ft. makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 24 (7d6) Fire damage on a failure, half on a success. The standard remains lit, and any undead ally that starts its turn within 10 ft. of it gains advantage on its next attack roll."}, {"name": "Command Presence", "text": "As a bonus action, the Praetor issues an order. One undead ally within 30 ft. that can hear him may immediately make one weapon attack as a reaction."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects a dead soldier's stance mid-battle out of pure habit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His armor bears the crest of an empire no map in this realm names."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls cadence in a dead tongue his own troops barely remember."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never breaks formation first; waits for the enemy line to falter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of kills scratched into his vambrace, ancient and full."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His legion drills in perfect silence, boots striking ground that makes no sound."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He still awaits a courier with new orders that will never arrive."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Mistakes the party for the empire's last living heirs and demands their surrender to his command."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["drilling a formation of dead soldiers through maneuvers no living army still runs", "standing at parade rest awaiting a report from an empire that fell centuries ago"]},{"name":"The Whistle","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"The sound of the order itself, given bone and rank","flavor":"Not a person anymore — the sound itself, given a shape of officers' bones and borrowed rank insignia, that sends men over the top forever; every era's war has heard it.","desc":"It isn't a person, hasn't been for longer than anyone can say — just the sound itself wearing officers' bones and borrowed rank, hovering above the field on nothing at all. Every era's war has heard that same note and gone over the top for it. It doesn't speak. It only blows.","traits":{"note": "It is the sound of the order, wearing officers' bones. Its rays are notes, not beams — each shriek a different command given force.", "actions": [{"name": "Over the Top (replaces one Eye Ray)", "text": "Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature that can hear the Whistle within 120 feet. Failure: the target immediately moves up to its speed toward the nearest enemy or hazard of the Whistle's choice, and takes 22 (4d10) Psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sounds, and a company of long-dead men the party can't see begins to advance around them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member finds themselves standing before they chose to; the whistle already blew for them once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It will not sound the retreat — it has forgotten the note, or never learned it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It answers only to an officer's cadence; speak the right command and it obeys once."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's calling an attack on a position the party is currently holding."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every soldier who ever went over the top at its sound is buried under this field, and they hear it too."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It is the same whistle from every war that ever had one; silence it here and it simply sounds in the next."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is the moment the order becomes irreversible, made permanent; while it sounds, no one on this ground — living or dead, friend or enemy — can choose not to charge, and it has decided not to stop."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["hovering above the reverse slope, waiting on nothing but the order it exists to give", "sounding once over ground gone dead quiet, and watching who moves"]},{"name":"No-Man's Bloom","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Plant","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"War-soaked ground grown into a thorned, remembering forest","flavor":"Grew from ground so soaked in war it stopped being ground; a forest of barbed thorn and bone-white flowers that remembers every line that ever broke on it, and answers with all of them at once.","desc":"Barbed thorn and bone-white flowers rise out of ground too soaked in war to still be called ground, a forest that remembers every line that ever broke across it. It doesn't grow so much as accumulate. When it answers, it answers with all of them at once.","traits":{"note": "Gargantuan and rooted across the whole field — the fight is with the ground itself. Wire-thorn and bone-white blossom for a hundred yards in every direction.", "actions": [{"name": "The Lines That Broke (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranks of barbed thorn erupt in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 20. Failure: 20 (3d8 + 7) Piercing damage and the target has the Restrained condition (escape DC 20). Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone-white flowers bloom in shapes that resemble collapsed formations from above."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't hunt so much as widen — every step into it feeds new growth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thorns carry rusted shrapnel still lodged from whatever first fed it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old dog tags and buttons surface slowly through its bark like teeth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats from fire alone; everything else it simply absorbs."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its roots run for miles under the field, connecting to smaller blooms the party hasn't found yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It hums faintly with old battle-cries in a hundred overlapping languages."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has just registered a fresh line breaking somewhere nearby, and surges to claim it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["spreading thorn and bone-white bloom across ground too soaked in war to be called ground anymore", "flowering all at once across a field that remembers every line that ever broke on it"]},{"name":"Trench Rat Cloud","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"rat","model":"rat","summary":"Carrion rats swarming abandoned trenches and packs","flavor":"Bloated on no-man's-land carrion, it swarms boots and packs before anyone can shoot it.","desc":"A carpet of fur and tails boiling up out of a flooded dugout, red eyes catching whatever light there is. They don't scatter at a shout anymore — they've learned the shout doesn't mean much here. The smell arrives half a second before they do.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Boiling Swarm", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, or 7 (2d4 + 2) Piercing damage if the Cloud has advantage on the attack roll from swarming numbers."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't scatter at a shout anymore — they've learned the shout doesn't mean much here."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests thick in an abandoned munitions crate, packed between the shells."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fled a flooding dugout and hasn't stopped moving as a mass since."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strips a corpse's straps and pockets bare within a minute of finding it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bolder near food than near threat; it will press past a raised weapon for a dropped ration."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Follows the smell of blood for miles, arriving faster than any scout could warn of it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves as one shape, never splitting, like it's still following a single dead handler."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just found a fresher kill nearby and is abandoning the party mid-fight to claim it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["boiling up out of a flooded dugout in a carpet of fur before anyone can shoot", "swarming a fallen pack, tearing the straps open before the owner is even cold"]},{"name":"Conscript Straggler","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Green conscript, flinches and breaks under fire","flavor":"Handed a rifle a week ago, he still flinches at his own shots and breaks the instant his squad does.","desc":"Uniform too big, rifle held wrong, he flinches at the report of his own shot before it's finished. His eyes dart to where his squad used to be standing. He'll fight, badly, until the man beside him runs — then he runs too.","traits":{"note": "He breaks the instant the man beside him runs — cut him off from his squad and he's already halfway to fleeing.", "actions": [{"name": "Panicked Swing", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage from a rifle butt swung more out of fear than aim."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform two sizes too big, sleeves rolled thick at the wrist."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters a countdown to himself before every volley he's ordered to join."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops his weapon the moment it's no longer pointed at anything."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing back for an officer who stopped following an hour ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights only when boxed in; given an inch of open ground, he takes it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Still has a home-address letter half-written and folded in his breast pocket."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Salutes anyone who speaks to him with authority, friend or foe alike."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His squad just broke and ran past him; he's a half-second from bolting too."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["flinching at the echo of his own last shot, rifle still smoking in unsteady hands", "scanning the ground where his squad used to stand, uniform swallowing his shoulders"]},{"name":"Wire-Snagged Corpse","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Barbed-wire corpse still lurching toward the line","flavor":"Caught on the barbed wire mid-charge, it never fell — it just kept twitching forward, one strand at a time.","desc":"It hangs half-upright in the wire where it died, uniform rotted to threads, one boot still lodged in the mud below. It twitches forward an inch at a time, barbs tearing deeper with every pull. It has never once managed to get free.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wire-Caught Lunge", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is within 5 ft. of wire or wreckage it must succeed on a DC 11 Dexterity save or be restrained by tangled barbs until it uses an action to break free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One boot still lodged in mud below, the only part of it that never moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform rotted to threads, dog tags rattling loose with each twitch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tears deeper into itself with every pull; the wire has replaced half its ribs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Can only lean toward the line, never fully free itself from the strand."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Others hang nearby, still, until this one's twitching sets them off too."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The wire hums faintly when the wind crosses it, like a plucked, rusted string."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its twitch keeps the same rhythm as a distant, unheard artillery clock."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A fresh strand just snapped loose, giving it its first real reach in years."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "any"],"activity":["hanging half-upright in barbed wire, twitching forward an inch deeper with every pull", "tearing new wounds in itself against the same strand it's never once escaped"]},{"name":"Powder Monkey Cutthroat","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Small shipboard runner, finishes off fallen boarders","flavor":"Small enough to run the guns below deck, mean enough to finish off boarders with a marlinspike.","desc":"Small enough to duck below the gunwale, quick enough to be underfoot before anyone notices, he carries a marlinspike slick with someone else's blood. He grins at boarders already on their knees. He finishes what the cannons started.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Marlinspike", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, plus 2 (1d4) extra Piercing damage if the target is prone."}, {"name": "Shot", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small enough to duck below the gunwale before anyone marks where he went."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grins at boarders already on their knees, never at ones still standing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries powder faster barefoot than any deckhand does in boots."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows every crawlspace below deck and uses them to vanish mid-fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marlinspike never leaves his hand, even when hauling charges two-fisted."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a private tally of finishes scratched into the mast beam he sleeps under."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves through gunsmoke like he can see paths in it no one else can."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just spotted an easier kill than the party and is already sliding toward it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "urban"],"activity":["ducking below the gunwale, hauling powder charges faster than the gun crew can call for them", "finishing off a boarder already on his knees with a marlinspike slick and quick"]},{"name":"Musket Skirmisher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"kobold-inventor","model":"rlm-musket-skirmisher","summary":"Loose-order skirmisher, fires and vanishes into smoke","flavor":"Fires from cover in loose order, reloading in the smoke while the line volleys behind him.","desc":"He kneels in drifting smoke, ramrod working fast, eyes on the treeline instead of the drill-line. A shot cracks out from somewhere near him and he's already moved before the echo answers. Loose order suits him; he was never built for the volley.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Close Knife", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Loose-Order Trick", "replaces": "Improvised Device (Roll d6)", "text": "Roll a d6 to determine the trick: (1) a smoke-pot that heavily obscures a 10-ft. cube within 30 ft. for 1 minute; (2) a tripwire snare forcing a DC 12 Dexterity save or fall prone; (3) a signal flare granting the Skirmisher's allies advantage on their next attack against a marked target; (4) a false retreat granting the Skirmisher advantage on his next attack; (5) a scattered-caltrop patch dealing 2 (1d4) Piercing damage to the first creature entering a 5-ft. square within 15 ft.; (6) a misfire — no effect, and the Skirmisher loses his next reaction fumbling the reload."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reloads faster crouched than most men manage standing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks each kill with a notch cut into his ramrod, not his stock."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never fires from the same spot twice in one fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his eyes on the treeline even mid-conversation, never fully present."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was never built for the volley line and it still shows in how he stands."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Knows this stretch of ground from a dozen prior skirmishes, none of them his own."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fires a half-second before he seems to have sighted anything at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Out of clean shots and improvising with whatever's left in his kit, unpredictably."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["kneeling in drifting smoke, ramrod working fast while his eyes track the treeline", "firing once from cover and vanishing before the echo of the shot answers"]},{"name":"Longship Thrall","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"troglodyte","model":"rlm-longship-thrall","summary":"Chained oarsman turned axe-fighter at the beachhead","flavor":"Chained to the oar until the ship beaches, then handed an axe and pointed at the shore.","desc":"Oar-calluses thick as bark, ankle still ringed raw from the chain, he's handed an axe the moment the keel scrapes sand and shoved toward the shore. He doesn't know the men beside him. He only knows the ship behind him is worse.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Beachhead Axe", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage, swung with more desperation than skill."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Oar-calluses thick as bark across both palms, axe grip already awkward in them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't know the names of the men fighting beside him, only their backs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches toward the water at loud noise, chain-memory older than the axe."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights facing the shore, never the ship — he won't look back at it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Presses forward past wounds that would drop a free man twice over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Ankle still ringed raw with rope-burn scars from a chain long since struck off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mutters a rowing cadence under his breath, keeping time with his own swings."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sees an opening back toward the treeline and breaks for it mid-fight, axe still in hand."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["shoved up the beach still ringed raw at the ankle from the oar-chain, axe pressed into his hands", "hacking forward without knowing the men beside him, only that the ship behind him is worse"]},{"name":"Jungle Leech-Thing","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"rlm-jungle-leech-thing","summary":"Canopy leech-creature that drops and drains blood","flavor":"Drops from canopy vines onto exposed necks; the bite numbs before it drains.","desc":"It drops from the canopy without a sound, a wet dark comma landing on the back of a neck. The bite doesn't hurt going in — that's the trouble. By the time it does, it's already fat and letting go.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Numbing Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the Leech-Thing attaches. While attached it deals 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage automatically at the start of each of its turns, and the numbed target has disadvantage on the save to notice or remove it until it takes damage from another source."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wet dark comma landing on skin, gone unnoticed for a count of ten."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swells visibly fat within a minute of latching, doubling its size."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops only onto exposed skin, never through cloth if it can help it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lets go the instant it's disturbed, dropping to hide in leaf litter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in the same three trees, returning to drop again after each kill."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaves a numb patch that lingers for hours after it's removed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Never drops on the same person twice, like it's keeping count of who it's had."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Already attached to someone unnoticed, three turns fat before anyone spots it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "swamp"],"activity":["dropping from canopy vines onto an exposed neck, silent as falling water", "swelling fat and heavy on a bite that never hurt going in"]},{"name":"Siege Camp Looter","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Corpse-looter trailing behind the siege lines","flavor":"Follows the siege lines picking corpses clean before the burial details arrive.","desc":"He moves low between the dead with a sack and a knife, working fast fingers over pockets and boot-tops. He's careful not to look at faces. The burial detail's cart is already creaking closer down the line.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Looter's Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never looks at the faces of the dead he's picking clean."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sack already half full, clinking softly with someone else's coin."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Works fastest near the freshest bodies, before rigor sets pockets shut."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one eye on the burial detail's cart creaking closer down the line."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs rather than fights the instant anyone living notices him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Trades what he finds to camp followers a mile back, never keeps it long."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mutters an apology to each corpse before taking anything from it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just found something worth killing over on the body he's currently robbing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["moving low between the dead with a sack and a knife, careful not to look at faces", "working fast fingers over pockets and boot-tops before the burial detail's cart arrives"]},{"name":"Shell-Shocked Wanderer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guilt-stained-vagrant","model":"rlm-shell-shocked-wanderer","summary":"Shell-shocked survivor wandering, immune to fear","flavor":"Walks no-man's-land muttering old orders, immune to fear because there's nothing left to lose.","desc":"He walks the open ground upright, unhurried, muttering an order that stopped meaning anything a long time ago. Shellfire doesn't make him flinch anymore — nothing left in him rises to it. He steps around craters like he still remembers where they are.","traits":{"note": "Nothing left in him rises to fear — treat him as immune to being frightened.", "actions": [{"name": "Muttering Knife", "replaces": "Knife", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, delivered without hesitation or apparent awareness of the danger to himself."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same order under his breath, endlessly, meaning long gone from it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks upright through open fire that would flatten anyone still afraid."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steps around craters with perfect memory, though the field has changed since."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't flinch, doesn't duck, doesn't notice when he's wounded."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Attacks without malice, like the motion is older than any intention behind it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Answers only to the rank insignia of an army that stopped existing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His muttered order occasionally matches one an NPC nearby is currently following."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Just walked into the middle of the party's fight without registering it as one."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "ruins"],"activity":["walking open ground upright and unhurried, muttering an order that stopped meaning anything long ago", "stepping around craters like he still remembers exactly where they are"]},{"name":"Gas-Mask Sentry","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"Masked sentry holding post through gas alarms","flavor":"Stands post in a rubber mask through every gas alarm, trusting the seal more than his own eyes.","desc":"He stands his post behind a rubber snout and round dark lenses, breath rasping through the filter loud in the quiet. An alarm bell somewhere down the trench keeps ringing and he doesn't move. He trusts the seal on his mask more than he trusts his own eyes.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Post Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breath rasps loud through the filter, the loudest sound on his stretch of line."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't remove the mask for any reason, even to speak clearly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Holds his post exactly, refusing to pursue even an easy target."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Checks the seal on his mask with both hands every few minutes, compulsively."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trusts the mask completely, even when there's visibly no gas at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The alarm bell down the line has been ringing for longer than anyone can explain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Reacts to threats only by sound, as if the lenses show him nothing at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The alarm just changed pitch, and he's abandoning post for the first time to investigate."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["standing post behind a rubber snout and dark lenses, breath rasping loud through the filter", "holding position through a distant alarm bell, trusting the seal over his own eyes"]},{"name":"Draft-Horse Casualty","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"Dead draft horse still hauling its rotted harness","flavor":"A supply-train animal that died in harness and kept pulling, wagon and all, long after the wagon rotted away.","desc":"Ribs showing through rotted harness-leather, it hauls a wagon that fell apart years ago, hooves finding the same ruts by memory. The trace-chains drag empty air behind it. It has never once noticed the wagon is gone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dead Hooves", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ribs show clean through rotted harness-leather still strapped tight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the same ruts by memory, wagon or no wagon behind it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trace-chains drag empty air, never once noticed as slack."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Startles at a whip-crack sound, even from something that isn't a whip."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kicks backward exactly like a spooked living animal, out of old habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The wagon it thinks it's hauling shows faintly as a dust-trail only it seems to raise."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Has never once noticed the wagon is gone, in all its years of hauling nothing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Bolted by something unseen and is now stampeding straight through the party's position."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["hill", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["hauling a wagon that fell apart years ago, hooves finding the same ruts by memory alone", "dragging empty trace-chains behind it, never noticing the load is long gone"]},{"name":"Cavalry Lancer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Mounted lancer charging ahead of modern fire","flavor":"Charges in a wedge before the machine-gun era caught up with the horse.","desc":"He rides in a tight wedge, lance couched, hooves throwing up clods of torn field ahead of a charge the wrong century caught up to. He doesn't slow at the first crack of modern fire. The horse under him doesn't either.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Couched Lance", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 3) Piercing damage, or 13 (1d12 + 3 plus 1d8) Piercing damage if the Lancer moved at least 20 feet in a straight line toward the target before the attack."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't slow at the first crack of gunfire, nor does his horse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rides in a tight wedge, unwilling to break formation even alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Couches his lance the instant there's open ground to charge across."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wheels for a second pass rather than fight dismounted."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throws his javelin only when the charge lane closes unexpectedly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His horse carries scars from volleys that outpaced this style of charge entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Charges the loudest gunfire on the field, mistaking it for the enemy's center."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has just found open ground for a full charge and is already bearing down."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "any"],"activity":["riding in a tight wedge, lance couched, hooves throwing clods of torn field ahead of the charge", "closing distance at a gallop the wrong century has already caught up to"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Drummer Boy","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"performer","model":"rlm-musket-line-drummer-boy","summary":"Drummer keeping march step, breaking his death shatters morale","flavor":"Keeps the march step through the volleys; killing him breaks the formation's nerve as much as any officer.","desc":"Small hands keep perfect time on a drumhead scarred by shrapnel, the beat steady through smoke that swallows the rest of the line. He doesn't look old enough for any of this. If he falls, the step around him falters before the shooting does.","traits":{"note": "Killing him staggers the step of every ally near him before the shooting even catches up — treat nearby foes as briefly rattled if he falls.", "actions": [{"name": "Drumstick Jab", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage, more reflex than intent to fight."}, {"name": "The Step", "text": "As long as the Drummer Boy is alive and drumming, one ally within 30 ft. that can hear the beat gains a +1 bonus to attack rolls at the start of its turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small hands keep perfect time even as the rest of the line falls apart."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't look old enough for any of this, and knows it least of all."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drumhead is scarred with shrapnel pocks from a dozen prior volleys."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps drumming even when the formation around him has already broken."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no real weapon, only the drum and a dull belt-knife."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The step he keeps is older than the war he's currently drumming for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His beat occasionally syncs to a distant rhythm nobody else can place."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The line around him just faltered, and he's drumming louder to hold it together."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "urban", "any"],"activity":["keeping perfect time on a drumhead scarred by shrapnel through smoke that swallows the rest of the line", "holding the step steady while the volleys around him lose their rhythm"]},{"name":"No-Man's-Land Crawler","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Battlefield ghoul scavenging the unburied at night","flavor":"Feeds on the unburied between the lines, too cowardly to rise until the shelling stops.","desc":"It moves low between the shell-holes on all fours, only surfacing once the guns fall quiet, dragging a stink of rot ahead of it. It picks at what the burial parties missed. It won't rise while there's still light enough to be seen by.","traits":{"note": "It won't rise while there's still light enough to be seen by — it waits out any lit or loud scene.", "actions": [{"name": "Crawling Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Crawler makes one Scavenger Bite attack and one Trench Claw attack."}, {"name": "Scavenger Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is incapacitated, this attack scores a critical hit."}, {"name": "Trench Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be paralyzed for 1 minute; the target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only surfaces once the guns fall quiet, never a second before."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a stink of rot ahead of it that reaches a room before it does."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves on all fours low between shell-holes, using every dip in the ground."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Picks at what the burial parties missed, never touching a marked grave."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't rise while there's still light enough to be seen by."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Nests in a cluster of shell-holes it treats as a den, returning between meals."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Freezes mid-crawl at the sound of a shout, as if still afraid of an officer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The guns have gone quiet early, and it's surfacing right into the party's position."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["moving low between shell-holes on all fours, only surfacing once the guns fall quiet", "picking at what the burial parties missed, dragging a stink of rot ahead of it"]},{"name":"Jungle Ambush Sniper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Canopy-lashed sniper waiting days for one shot","flavor":"Lashed into the high canopy for days at a time, waiting for one clean shot.","desc":"Lashed high into the canopy, still as bark, he's been waiting since before dawn for a single clean angle. Nothing about him moves except one eye and, eventually, one finger. He'll wait through tomorrow too if he has to.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ambush Marks", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sniper makes one Longbow attack. If this is the first round of combat and the target hasn't acted yet, the attack has advantage."}, {"name": "Lashed Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "One Clean Angle", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nothing about him moves except one eye, and eventually one finger."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lashed to the same bough for days, indifferent to weather or ache."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Will wait through tomorrow too if the angle still isn't clean."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Takes exactly one shot per position, then relocates without exception."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks a target and won't be drawn off it by lesser movement nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has three prior firing positions rigged and waiting in the same stretch of canopy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know exactly when a target will step clear before it happens."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has finally gotten the clean angle he's waited days for, and won't wait a moment longer."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "any"],"activity":["lashed high into the canopy, still as bark, waiting since before dawn for one clean angle", "tracking a single finger's worth of motion, nothing else about him moving at all"]},{"name":"Longship Shieldmaiden","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-enforcer","model":"bandit-enforcer","summary":"Flank shield-wall fighter screaming the ship's name","flavor":"Holds the shield-wall's flank and screams the ship's name until her voice gives out.","desc":"She braces the flank of the shield-wall with both boots dug in, voice gone ragged from screaming a ship's name over and over. Her shield rings under blow after blow. She doesn't step back — the wall doesn't get to break on her end.","traits":{"note": "She won't retreat from the flank position — the wall breaks somewhere else before it breaks on her.", "actions": [{"name": "Shield-Wall Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Shieldmaiden makes two Mace attacks."}, {"name": "Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shield arm bound in a bandage that's soaked through twice already."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears her dead sister's armband and won't explain it if asked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps count of blows taken out loud, like a tally she needs kept."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger than she looks up close; someone lied about her age to get her here."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has stopped screaming the ship's name and started screaming a person's instead."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The rest of her line already broke and ran; she doesn't seem to have noticed yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her shield rings a note that doesn't match any blow landing on it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided this flank is the whole war now and will not be moved from it by anything short of death."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "grassland"],"activity":["bracing the shield-wall's flank with both boots dug into the mud", "screaming a ship's name over and over until her voice tears"]},{"name":"Trench Wire Golem","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Salvaged-armor construct patrolling the wire on its own","flavor":"Salvaged plate and barbed coils lashed into a shape that shambles the wire-line on patrol.","desc":"Salvaged plate lashed together with rusted coils, it shambles the wire-line at its own patrol pace, joints grinding wet with mud. Barbs trail off it like a tattered coat. It doesn't need orders to keep walking the same stretch.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't recognize orders, only the loop it's already walking — cutting the wire ahead of it barely slows the loop down.", "actions": [{"name": "Wire-Lash Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The golem makes two Barbed Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Barbed Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Piercing damage from trailing barbs, and the target's speed is halved until the end of its next turn as coils snag it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a boot that never got properly seated into the frame."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust bleeds down it in a stain shaped almost like a face."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its patrol loop has worn an actual groove into the mud over months."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a second, smaller helmet lashed to its chest, empty."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barbs catch scraps of uniform cloth from a dozen different colors."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has started walking a slightly wider loop than the one it was built to walk."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its joints grind out a rhythm that sounds, if you listen, like marching orders."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in the plate is still alive in there, and it is very tired of walking."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["shambling the same stretch of wire-line at its own fixed patrol pace", "grinding wet through mud, barbed coils trailing like a tattered coat"]},{"name":"Musket Volley Ghost","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"rlm-musket-volley-ghost","summary":"Volley-killed rank of soldiers standing in smoke","flavor":"A whole rank that died in one volley, still standing shoulder to shoulder in the smoke.","desc":"A whole rank stands shoulder to shoulder in drifting powder-smoke, muskets still raised at the angle that killed them. They fire in perfect unison, over and over, the same volley that ended them. The smoke never quite clears around their boots.","traits":{"note": "The rank fires as one — hitting one draws attacks from the whole line, same as it always has.", "actions": [{"name": "The Volley", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 30/90 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Necrotic damage as the rank's smoke-wreathed volley catches the target, and the ghost regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One figure in the rank is missing its hat, blown clean off at the moment of death."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The smoke around their boots never thins no matter how the wind blows."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They reload in perfect unison, though nothing ever leaves the barrels but smoke."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A gap in the rank marks where one of them finally stopped standing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their uniforms are from an army no living person could name."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The volley is aimed at a position that hasn't held living soldiers in years."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Between volleys, for one silent second, they all turn their heads the same direction."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've noticed something new standing where the old target used to be, and the rank is adjusting its aim."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["standing shoulder to shoulder in drifting smoke, muskets raised at a killing angle", "firing the same volley that ended them, over and over without end"]},{"name":"Jungle War-Dog","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"rlm-jungle-war-dog","summary":"Scent-trained war-dog running point on patrol","flavor":"Trained to track by sweat and fear, it runs the point ahead of the patrol.","desc":"It runs the point low and fast, nose working the air ahead of the patrol, trained past fear to track by sweat alone. Its handler is somewhere behind, forgotten. It only stops when it's found something worth stopping for.","traits":{"note": "It only stops when it finds something worth stopping for — and then it doesn't stop on its own.", "actions": [{"name": "Point-Dog Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The war-dog makes two Trained Bite attacks."}, {"name": "Trained Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it must succeed on a DC 12 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One ear notched from a wound that never healed clean."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at whistled signals even when no one nearby is whistling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a training collar with a name filed off it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to cross open ground, always cutting through brush instead."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has outlived three handlers and shows no sign of missing any of them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's found the patrol's scent already and is circling back for the rest of the pack."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It tracks by a fear-smell that hasn't existed on this ground in years, and finds it anyway."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided the party smells like the enemy it was trained on, and no correction will unmake that."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["running the point low and fast, nose working the air ahead of the patrol", "tracking by sweat and fear, trained past the instinct to hesitate"]},{"name":"Siege Sapper's Mole","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"ankheg","model":"ankheg","summary":"Tunneling beast bred to dig under siege walls","flavor":"Bred and directed to chew siege tunnels under walls, indifferent to the men riding its back.","desc":"It chews through packed earth in steady, mechanical bites, indifferent to the men riding its wide back down into the dark. Dirt sprays behind it in a fine constant rain. It was bred for exactly this and nothing else.","traits":{"note": "It was bred for exactly this and nothing else — it doesn't fight so much as keep digging through whatever's in the way.", "actions": [{"name": "Tunneling Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Acid Spray (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Acid Spray (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The mole sprays acid in a 30-foot line, 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line makes a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) Acid damage on a failure, half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wide back is worn smooth and shiny where riders have gripped it for months."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews in a rhythm precisely timed to a countdown only its handlers track."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a rope harness meant for men who are no longer riding it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces briefly to breathe before diving back under without being told."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves tunnels so precise they could be mistaken for engineered ones."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already most of the way under the wall the party is standing on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It has tunneled under three different walls in three different wars and remembers all of them as one long dig."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's broken through into a space it wasn't meant to reach, and whatever's down there has its full attention now."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["chewing through packed earth in steady mechanical bites toward a wall's foundation", "spraying dirt in a fine constant rain behind it as it tunnels down"]},{"name":"Mustard Fog Sprite","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"rlm-mustard-fog-sprite","summary":"Living gas-cloud that hunts by coughing sounds","flavor":"A living pocket of gas that rolls low across the wire, hunting by the sound of coughing.","desc":"A thin, low pocket of gas curls along the ground, hunting by the wet sound of coughing more than by sight. It rolls into dugouts uninvited. Where it stops, breathing stops being easy.","traits":{"note": "It hunts by sound, not sight — going quiet is the only real defense against it.", "actions": [{"name": "Choking Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The sprite exhales caustic vapor in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) Poison damage and gaining the poisoned condition until the end of its next turn on a failure, half damage and no condition on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Curls a faint yellow at its edges even in full dark."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pools lowest in the deepest dugout, patient as standing water."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thins to almost nothing in wind, then reforms the moment it drops."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seems drawn specifically toward labored breathing over quiet breathing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a bitter mustard smell that lingers on cloth for days after."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already rolled into the space the party is using for cover."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to remember dugouts it hasn't drifted into yet, curling toward them first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found a cluster of coughing loud enough to draw its whole mass at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["curling low along the ground, hunting by the wet sound of coughing", "rolling uninvited into a dugout where breathing has stopped being easy"]},{"name":"Longship Berserker","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"rlm-longship-berserker","summary":"Beach-landing berserker numb to wounds mid-charge","flavor":"Chews the ritual root before the beach landing and doesn't feel the axe wounds until the tide turns red.","desc":"He's chewed the ritual root before the beach even comes into view, eyes gone glassy-wide, axe swinging before his boots find sand. Wounds open on him and he doesn't register them yet. By the time he does, the tide nearby has gone red.","traits":{"note": "Damage doesn't slow him mid-charge — he only reckons with wounds once the tide has already turned red.", "actions": [{"name": "Root-Numbed Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. While above half its hit points, the berserker has resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pupils blown wide, root-juice staining his beard black."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Already bleeding from three cuts he hasn't noticed yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roars a single word over and over, no longer intelligible as language."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Charges in a dead straight line regardless of what's actually in the way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops the axe overhand each time like it's the only swing he knows."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The root is wearing off faster than usual, and the wounds are catching up to him mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He doesn't seem to know which beach he's landing on, or which year."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's taken a wound that should have dropped him and hasn't slowed down at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "grassland"],"activity":["chewing the ritual root before the beach even comes into view, eyes gone glassy", "swinging the axe before his boots find sand, wounds not yet registering"]},{"name":"Colonial Trench Medic","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"rlm-colonial-trench-medic","summary":"Under-fire medic, priority target to break morale","flavor":"Crawls between craters under fire, more dangerous to leave alive than most riflemen.","desc":"He crawls crater to crater under fire, satchel dragging in the mud, more careful with bandages than any rifleman is with a shot. He's calm in a way that unsettles the men he's dragging back. Someone always seems to want him dead first.","traits":{"note": "He's a priority target by design — pulling him out of the fight breaks more men than killing a rifleman does.", "actions": [{"name": "Field Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Flame", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 60 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Field Blessing", "text": "The medic touches a dying creature within 5 feet, restoring 9 (2d8) hit points to it, once per short or long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Satchel straps worn through and re-knotted more times than can be counted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks softly to the wounded even when there's no time left to save them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hands shake constantly except in the exact moment he's threading a needle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of names in a notebook soaked stiff with old blood."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to carry a proper weapon, only ever the mace, and rarely uses it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already crawling toward someone on the party's side who's down and screaming."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know exactly who's about to fall before the wound is even dealt."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone has marked him for death specifically, and they're closing in on his position right now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["crawling crater to crater under fire, satchel dragging through the mud", "handling bandages calmly in a way that unsettles the men he's dragging back"]},{"name":"Jungle Pit-Trap Warden","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"thri-kreen-marauder","model":"rlm-jungle-pit-trap-warden","summary":"Guerrilla warden herding patrols into staked pits","flavor":"Lives among staked pits and deadfalls of his own building, herding patrols into them.","desc":"He lives among stakes and deadfalls of his own patient building, a shape barely distinguishable from the undergrowth until it moves. He doesn't fight so much as herd. The ground itself seems to be doing the work for him.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't fight head-on — the ground he's prepared is doing most of the work before blades are ever drawn.", "actions": [{"name": "Herding Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The warden makes two Gythka attacks, or one Gythka attack and one Chatkcha attack."}, {"name": "Gythka", "replaces": "Gythka", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Chatkcha", "replaces": "Chatkcha", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, and the warden can catch a returning Chatkcha in the same turn it's thrown."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin patterned in mud and leaf-litter so exact it takes a second look to find him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks his own pits with a private sign only he can read at a glance."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice; a hand signal is louder than shouting to him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has dug more pits than he could possibly need for one patrol."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a slow, patient half-crouch that never seems to tire him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The party is already three steps into a lane he's been herding them down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The undergrowth itself seems to lean the way he wants it to, just slightly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's found the one path he actually needs the party to take, and he's not letting them find another."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "hill"],"activity":["moving barely distinguishable from the undergrowth until the moment it strikes", "herding a patrol step by step toward stakes and deadfalls of his own building"]},{"name":"Duckboard Trench Fiend","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"dretch","model":"dretch","summary":"Mud-spawned fiend climbing up through duckboards","flavor":"Something answered the mud's hunger and started climbing up through the duckboards at night.","desc":"Something climbs up between the slats of the duckboard floor, small and wrong and grinning, mud running off it like it just finished being born. It answers a hunger that isn't its own. It doesn't understand why it's here, only that it's hungry.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't understand its own purpose — kill the mud's hunger and it stops climbing, but nothing here does that.", "actions": [{"name": "Duckboard Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Fetid Cloud (1/Day)", "replaces": "Fetid Cloud (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The fiend releases a stinking cloud in a 10-foot radius centered on itself. Each creature in the area makes a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or gains the poisoned condition for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mud runs off it constantly like it just finished being born."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grins even while being struck, as if it hasn't learned pain yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small enough to fit through gaps a grown man couldn't."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats back under the boards the instant it takes a real hit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Climbs up in twos and threes, never quite alone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "More of them are already climbing up through the same stretch of boards."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to recognize the mud here specifically, like it's climbed up through this exact spot before."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whatever hunger it answers to has gotten sharper tonight, and it isn't backing down from the boards."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["climbing up between the slats of the duckboard floor, small and grinning", "answering a hunger that isn't its own, unsure why it's here at all"]},{"name":"Machine-Gun Nest Crew","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-warrior","model":"bugbear-warrior","summary":"Two-man gun crew that ends charges outright","flavor":"Two men and a tripod that can end a whole charge in the time it takes to reload once.","desc":"Two men crouch behind a tripod, one feeding the belt, one riding the traverse, both moving with the same clipped economy of long practice. The gun doesn't pause to reload so much as breathe. A whole charge can end in the time it takes them to swap a barrel.","traits":{"note": "The gun doesn't pause to reload so much as breathe — a whole charge can die in the gap between belts.", "actions": [{"name": "Crew Actions", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The crew makes two Traverse Gun attacks, or one Traverse Gun attack and throws one Javelin."}, {"name": "Traverse Gun", "replaces": "Oversized Morningstar", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Enfilade Burst (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Skullthumper (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The crew traverses the gun across a line of fire, targeting up to three creatures within 60 feet in a line it can see. Each target makes a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) Piercing damage on a failure, half as much on a success."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The belt feeder counts rounds under his breath, always slightly wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sandbags around the tripod are stacked three different colors of mud."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of the two never speaks; the other never stops."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The traverse gunner has a habit worn into his shoulder from the stock."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spent casings pile deep enough to shift underfoot around the nest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've got the whole approach zeroed in already, and the party just entered it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The two crew move with a synchrony that outlasts whichever of them actually dies first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The barrel's overheating and they know it, and they're firing anyway rather than let the lane close."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["crouching behind a tripod, one feeding the belt, one riding the traverse", "swapping a barrel with the same clipped economy they've used for months"]},{"name":"Storm-Trooper Breach Squad","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"rlm-theater-trench","summary":"Fast breach specialists clearing trench sections","flavor":"Trained to cross the open ground fast and clear a trench section room by room before the rest arrive.","desc":"They cross open ground in short controlled rushes, grenades first, clearing a trench section corner by corner before the rest of the line even reaches the wire. No wasted motion, no shouting. They're gone from one bay before you know they were in it.","traits":{"note": "No wasted motion, no shouting — they're gone from one bay before anyone realizes they were ever in it.", "actions": [{"name": "Breach Actions", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The squad makes two Entrenching Greatsword attacks, or one attack and fires the Heavy Crossbow once."}, {"name": "Entrenching Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in pairs that cover each other without a word passing between them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries more grenades than blades, and prefers it that way."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks cleared bays with a chalk sign only their own squad reads."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never holds ground once it's clear — already moving to the next bay."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears matched short blades filed down for close work in tight trenches."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They've already cleared two bays behind the party without being noticed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their rushes land in a rhythm that seems to anticipate where the defenders will be, not where they are."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "They've decided the party's position is the last bay standing between them and the objective."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["crossing open ground in short controlled rushes, grenades thrown first", "clearing a trench section corner by corner before the rest of the line arrives"]},{"name":"Longship Skald-Reaver","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"rlm-longship-skald-reaver","summary":"Singing raider whose saga-verses embolden the crew","flavor":"Sings the raid's saga even as he fights, and the crew fights harder for being sung about.","desc":"He fights and sings in the same breath, verses of the raid keeping time with his axe-strokes, and the crew around him fights harder for being sung about. His voice doesn't crack even when his knuckles do. The saga matters more to him than the outcome.","traits":{"note": "The saga matters to him more than the outcome — the crew nearby fights better while the verses keep coming.", "actions": [{"name": "Saga-Verse Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The reaver makes two Greataxe attacks, or one Greataxe attack and throws one Javelin."}, {"name": "Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Verse of the Raid", "text": "At the start of its turn, the reaver sings a verse. Each ally within 30 ft. who can hear it gains a +1 bonus to attack rolls until the start of the reaver's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice hoarse from singing through three straight days of raiding."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knuckles split and re-split on the axe-haft, never bandaged."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Improvises new verses about whoever's fighting well nearby, on the spot."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps singing even when there's no one left nearby to hear it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to end a verse mid-line, even mid-swing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already composing the verse about this exact fight, present tense, as it happens."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The saga he's singing describes events that haven't happened here yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided this fight deserves the saga's final verse, and he intends to make that true himself."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["coast", "sea", "grassland"],"activity":["singing the raid's saga in the same breath as his axe-strokes", "keeping verse-time with the fight while the crew fights harder for being sung about"]},{"name":"Jungle Pit Viper Ambush","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-constrictor-snake","model":"giant-constrictor-snake","summary":"Treeline ambush snake striking bunched patrols","flavor":"Strikes from the treeline the moment a patrol bunches up on the trail.","desc":"It waits coiled at the treeline until the patrol bunches shoulder to shoulder on the narrow trail, then it's simply already among them. Scales catch what little light gets through the canopy. It only needs the one mistake.","traits":{"note": "It only needs the one mistake — once it's coiled around a target, that target is the only thing that matters to it.", "actions": [{"name": "Treeline Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The snake makes one Bite attack and one Constrict attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 16). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained and the snake can't constrict another target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales patterned to vanish exactly into the canopy's broken light."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils around an old rusted trench-marker as if it's part of the tree."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strikes only the rearmost of a bunched patrol, never the point."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has struck this same stretch of trail enough times to have a preferred angle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Releases a constricted target the instant a second target bunches closer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already coiled directly above the trail the party is about to bunch up on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to know which soldier in a line is the officer before any insignia would show."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's constricted something already and isn't willing to let go regardless of what arrives next."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["waiting coiled at the treeline until a patrol bunches shoulder to shoulder", "striking the moment the trail narrows and the mistake is made"]},{"name":"Cavalry Saber Charge","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Full-gallop saber cavalry betting on the first pass","flavor":"Rides the flank at full gallop, saber down, betting everything on the first pass.","desc":"He rides the flank at a flat-out gallop, saber low and level, betting the whole engagement on a single pass. Hooves throw mud in sheets. He doesn't check the horse until the line in front of him is already broken or he is.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't check the horse until the line ahead is already broken or he is — there's no braking this charge halfway.", "actions": [{"name": "Saber Actions", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The rider makes two Cavalry Saber attacks, or one attack and fires the Heavy Crossbow once."}, {"name": "Cavalry Saber", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage, or 15 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage if the rider moved at least 20 ft. in a straight line toward the target this turn."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mud thrown in sheets from the horse's hooves cakes his whole left side."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Saber's edge nicked from a dozen passes he still counts as clean."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't rein in even when the ground ahead is clearly bad footing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks to the horse mid-charge like it's the only one listening."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already lost two mounts this campaign and doesn't name this one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's committed to the charge already, and the line he's aimed at is the party's."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The horse seems to know the charge line before he's chosen it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided this pass is the one that ends it, one way or the other, and won't be turned from it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "any"],"activity":["riding the flank at a flat-out gallop, saber low and level", "betting the whole engagement on a single pass through the line"]},{"name":"Field Gun Battery","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-rug-of-smothering","model":"rlm-field-gun-battery","summary":"Cannon crew fighting as one machine past death","flavor":"A cannon crew that fights on as one grim machine after the horses bolt and the gunners die at their posts.","desc":"The horses bolted and the gunners fell where they stood, but the gun keeps firing, worked now by whatever's left of the crew moving in one grim, wordless rhythm. Barrels glow faint in the smoke. It reloads itself the same way corpses shouldn't.","traits":{"note": "Nothing living is steering this anymore — it keeps to the same firing rhythm the crew drilled into it before they died.", "actions": [{"name": "Barrage Smother", "replaces": "Smother", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from the carriage and crew-shapes crushing inward, and the target is grappled (escape DC 14) if it is Medium or smaller."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wheel-spokes still stained with the same mud from the day the gunners fell."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crew-shape at the breech still mimes loading a shell that's long gone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fires on a fixed interval, dead on time, regardless of what's in range."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The barrel's paint is scorched into a pattern that looks almost like a unit crest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smoke rolls off it even between shots, like it's never fully cooled."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already sighted in on the exact ground the party is standing on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rhythm it fires in matches a heartbeat, slow and steady, that shouldn't still be there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something about this target has broken its fixed interval, and it's firing faster now, gaining on itself."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["firing on in one grim wordless rhythm after the horses bolted and gunners fell", "reloading itself the way corpses shouldn't, barrels glowing faint in smoke"]},{"name":"The Wire-Cutter Colossus","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"animated-armor","summary":"Wire-clipping walker built to open assault lanes","flavor":"Built to walk the wire ahead of the assault, clipping lanes through with rotating shears.","desc":"It strides ahead of the assault on legs built for exactly this ground, rotating shears at each forearm chewing lanes through the wire in long unhurried passes. Coils spring loose and whip past its shoulders. It doesn't slow for what's caught in them.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't slow for anything caught in the coils it whips loose — clearing the wire is the whole of its purpose.", "actions": [{"name": "Shear Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The colossus makes two Rotating Shear attacks."}, {"name": "Rotating Shear", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a construct made of metal or a wire obstacle, this attack deals maximum damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails loose coils of cut wire that whip and snap as it strides past."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Legs built long and stiff, engineered for cratered ground specifically."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shears click through an idle rhythm even when nothing's in reach."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating scored with lane after lane of cut marks from repeated use."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at one exact, unhurried pace regardless of what's shooting at it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already cutting a lane straight toward the party's position."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It cuts wire that isn't there yet, clearing lanes for an assault that hasn't started."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found something in the wire worth shearing through faster than its usual pace allows."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["striding ahead of the assault on legs built for exactly this ground", "chewing lanes through the wire with rotating forearm shears in long unhurried passes"]},{"name":"Longship Hull-Breaker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"Raiding-crew brute thrown at hulls and gates","flavor":"A raiding crew's brute, thrown at ship hulls and gates alike with the same swing.","desc":"He's thrown at whatever's in the way — hull, gate, shield-wall — with the same overhand swing every time, and whatever's in the way generally gives first. Splinters or bone, he doesn't seem to notice the difference. He's already turning toward the next thing.","traits":{"note": "Splinters or bone, he doesn't register the difference — whatever's in the way generally gives first.", "actions": [{"name": "Overhand Greatclub", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is an object or structure, this attack deals double damage."}, {"name": "Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knuckles scarred white from years of hitting things harder than flesh."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't aim so much as point himself and go."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries splinters from a dozen hulls embedded permanently in one forearm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs, short and flat, every time something finally gives."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never checks his own wounds until someone else points them out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already been pointed at whatever the party is using for cover."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know exactly where a structure is weakest before he's swung once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided the party itself is just the next thing in the way, and he's already turning toward them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["coast", "sea", "hill"],"activity":["getting thrown at whatever's in the way with the same overhand swing", "already turning toward the next hull, gate, or shield-wall before this one gives"]},{"name":"Jungle Beast-Cage Handler","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lizardfolk-sovereign","model":"rlm-jungle-beast-cage-handler","summary":"Handler releasing caged war-beasts on the ambush horn","flavor":"Releases the war-beasts from bamboo cages the instant the ambush horn sounds.","desc":"He crouches beside stacked bamboo cages, hand resting on the latch, waiting on a horn only he seems to be listening for. When it sounds, the cages come open all at once. He steps back and lets whatever's inside do the rest.","traits":{"note": "The instant the horn sounds, the cages come open all at once — he steps back and lets whatever's inside do the rest.", "actions": [{"name": "Handler Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The handler makes one Bite attack and one Earthen Maul attack."}, {"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Earthen Maul", "replaces": "Earthen Maul", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Release the Cages", "text": "The handler releases all caged beasts within 30 ft. as a bonus action, once per encounter. Each releases and acts on the handler's initiative count, entering the fight from where its cage stood."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Latch-hand scarred from cages that didn't want to open on schedule."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a horn of his own around his neck, though it's never once sounded."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts the cages under his breath before every release, always the same number."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't flinch at what comes out of the cages, only at silence after."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one cage set apart from the rest, never opened yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's already heard the horn the party hasn't, and his hand is on the latch."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The horn he waits for hasn't been blown by human lungs in a long while."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided not to wait for the horn this time, and his hand is already moving."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "hill"],"activity":["crouching beside stacked bamboo cages, hand resting on the latch", "waiting on a horn only he seems to be listening for"]},{"name":"Gas Cloud Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"steam-mephit","model":"rlm-gas-cloud-horror","summary":"Sentient, undissipated gas barrage with a will","flavor":"A whole gas barrage that never dissipated, grown a hunger and a will of its own.","desc":"A whole barrage that should have thinned out and dispersed instead rolls low and thick across the field, deliberate now, hunting. It curls around cover instead of drifting past it. Something in the way it moves suggests it's choosing.","traits":{"note": "It should have thinned and dispersed like any barrage — something in it decided not to, and it's still choosing.", "actions": [{"name": "Choking Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Barrage Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Steam Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The horror exhales a caustic cloud in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 21 (6d6) Poison damage and gaining the blinded condition until the end of its next turn on a failure, half damage and no condition on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thicker at its core than any ordinary barrage cloud should hold together."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Curls specifically around low walls and craters rather than over them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint yellow-green stain on anything it rolls across."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves against the wind more often than with it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pulls back from open flame like it remembers being made by fire once."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already curling around the exact position the party has taken cover in."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to recognize which of its targets already breathed it in once before, years back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's grown thick enough tonight to hold its shape against a wind that should have scattered it entirely."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["rolling low and thick across the field, deliberate now, hunting", "curling around cover instead of drifting past it, choosing its path"]},{"name":"Trench Raid Bayonet Line","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"rlm-theater-trench","summary":"Silent bayonet line going over the top on the whistle","flavor":"Goes over the top in a fixed line, bayonets first, silent until the whistle blows.","desc":"They come up over the parapet in a fixed silent line, bayonets forward, boots finding the same broken ground without looking down. No one shouts until the whistle does. The line doesn't waver even where it's thinnest.","traits":{"note": "They don't break formation for cover — the line staying unbroken matters more to them than staying alive.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The line thrusts twice with bayonet-blades, or once with bayonet and once with a crossbow bolt at range."}, {"name": "Bayonet Thrust", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Volley Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One man in the line is younger than the rest and everyone else knows it but says nothing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their boots are wrong sizes, traded up and down the line before the whistle went."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They march over their own dead from the last attempt without breaking stride."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone in the line is singing under his breath, low, off the beat of the guns."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They stop dead the instant the whistle goes quiet, waiting for a second blast that isn't coming."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The line has gone over this same stretch of mud so many times the ground remembers their shape."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their shadows fall a half-second behind their bodies, like the light hasn't caught up to the order yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the line breaks it doesn't rout — it turns as one and comes back twice as fast."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["climbing over a broken parapet in a fixed silent row, bayonets leveled at nothing yet", "holding a dead-straight line across open ground while shells drop short and long"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Artillery Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"tough-boss","summary":"Voice-correcting gun sergeant walking under fire","flavor":"Walks the gun line under fire, correcting aim by voice alone.","desc":"He walks the gun line upright while everyone else keeps low, correcting elevation by voice alone between concussions that would drop a lesser man to his knees. Powder streaks his face black. The guns fire truer with him standing there than they would otherwise.","traits":{"note": "The guns behind him fire truer for his voice alone — pull him off the line and the battery starts missing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sergeant attacks twice with his ranging spear, or once with the spear and once with his voice-thrown lash."}, {"name": "Ranging Spear", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Correcting Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) if used with both hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice never breaks even when his hands do, tallying corrections with fingers black from powder."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hasn't sat down in three days and won't while the guns still have range."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows every gunner's name and uses the wrong one only when he's worried."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He walks with a limp he refuses to acknowledge, corrected pace and all."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a private count of every shot fired under his voice, muttered like a prayer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His last three batteries were all overrun with him still standing on them, correcting to the end."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The concussion that should have dropped him twenty times over seems to pass around him instead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the guns fall silent around him he keeps calling corrections to a battery that's already gone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["hill", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing upright on the gun line correcting elevation by voice while men crouch around him", "walking the length of the battery counting shots against a tally only he keeps"]},{"name":"Siege Tower Crew","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"rlm-siege-tower-crew","summary":"Rolling siege tower crewed under falling arrows","flavor":"A rolling wooden tower crewed by soldiers who fight from its top even as arrows take the timbers apart.","desc":"The tower groans forward on log rollers, timbers already splintering under arrow-fire, men fighting from platforms near its top as it climbs the last yards to the wall. Ladders unfold with a crack. Nobody up there looks down to see how close the base is to giving out.","traits":{"note": "Nobody aboard checks how close the base is to failing — that's the one thing the crew has agreed not to look at.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The tower's platform crew attacks twice, with slam or bolt in any combination."}, {"name": "Platform Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage from a boarding ram swung off the tower's lip."}, {"name": "Deck Bolt-Thrower", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60/240 ft. Hit: 15 (3d8 + 2) Force damage from a mounted bolt-thrower lashed to the top deck."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One roller keeps sticking, and two crewmen throw their whole weight against it every few yards."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ladders were built too short and everyone aboard knows it and nobody says so."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crewman keeps a hand pressed to a timber crack the size of a fist, as if that would hold it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've stopped counting the arrows stuck in the siding; there are too many to matter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tower drifts a few degrees off true and the crew corrects for it without discussing why."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This is the third tower this crew has ridden to a wall; the first two are still burning somewhere behind them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The timbers groan in a rhythm that matches footsteps, like the tower is pacing itself forward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the base finally goes, the crew keeps fighting from the collapsing platform rather than jump clear."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["rolling forward on groaning log rollers while arrow-fire strips the timbers bare", "fighting from a swaying platform near the top as the ladders unfold with a crack"]},{"name":"Longship War-Wolf Handler","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"Raider running a leashed wolf-pack ahead of the men","flavor":"Runs with a leashed pack of raiding wolves that hit the shore ahead of the men.","desc":"He runs with a leashed pack straining ahead of him, wolves hitting the shoreline before the raiders' boots do. He lets the lead out in short savage bursts. The pack doesn't need him to point at anything twice.","traits":{"note": "The pack doesn't need a second command — once it's loosed, it keeps going whether or not he does.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Handler and his lead wolf attack together: one bite from the wolf, one claw-rake from the Handler's hooked gaff."}, {"name": "War-Wolf Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is knocked prone."}, {"name": "Hooked Gaff", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries fish-scraps in a belt pouch, the only thing that gets the pack to heel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His forearms are scarred to the elbow from a pack that didn't used to obey."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He whistles a two-note call before every landing, out of habit more than need."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts the pack by name each morning and has never once come up short."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hangs back a beat longer than the raiders expect, watching where the wolves choose to go first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This pack has outlived three handlers before him and answers to the leash more than the man."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wolves move as one animal now, turning together before any signal reaches them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drop the leash and the pack doesn't scatter — it simply stops needing him at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "forest", "hill"],"activity":["running a leashed pack of raiding wolves ahead of the landing party in short savage bursts", "standing at the tide-line letting the pack surge forward while the boots behind him catch up"]},{"name":"Jungle War-Elephant Driver","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"elephant","model":"rlm-jungle-war-elephant-driver","summary":"Barded war-elephant carrying its driver into chaos","flavor":"A trained war-beast in barded plate, its mahout riding the howdah through the chaos.","desc":"Barded plate creaks over a hide already scarred pale, the mahout riding high in a howdah that sways with every furious step. The ground shakes before the beast is even visible through the trees. He doesn't steer so much as suggest a direction.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't steer so much as suggest — the beast decides the actual line of the charge.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The war-beast gores twice, or once and tramples anything left underfoot."}, {"name": "Barded Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is pushed 10 feet away and knocked prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The plate is patched with mismatched scrap from three older sets of barding."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The mahout talks to the beast constantly, low and steady, like it's the one being reassured."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scars on the hide are pale enough to count, each one a fight the beast walked away from."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The howdah sways badly on uneven ground and the driver rides it out without complaint."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a short goad he's never once had to use on this particular animal."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The beast remembers the last three campaigns better than the driver riding it does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It stops sometimes mid-charge, ears forward, listening to something no one else can hear in the trees."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the driver falls, the beast keeps the charge's exact line anyway, riderless and unslowed."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "grassland"],"activity":["riding high in a swaying howdah as barded plate creaks over scarred hide below", "letting the beast choose the general direction while the ground shakes long before it's visible"]},{"name":"Trench Flame-Lance Team","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"salamander-fire-snake","model":"rlm-trench-flame-lance-team","summary":"Flame-tank team clearing bunkers in one breath","flavor":"Two men and a tank of oil-fire that clear a bunker in one long, screaming breath.","desc":"Two men haul a tank of oil-fire between them, one bracing the weight, one on the long lance-nozzle, and a bunker clears out in one continuous screaming breath of flame. Heat shimmers the mud around their boots. They don't linger to watch it finish.","traits":{"note": "The tank on their backs is one bad hit from going up — anyone near them is standing in that math too.", "actions": [{"name": "Long Breath", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30 ft. line, 5 ft. wide. Hit: 14 (4d6) Fire damage to each creature in the line. A struck creature must make a DC 14 Dexterity save or catch fire, taking 3 (1d6) Fire damage at the start of each of its turns until it uses an action to extinguish."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The nozzle-man's hands are burn-scarred past feeling; he doesn't flinch from the heat anymore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tank hisses constantly, a small leak nobody's had time to patch properly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They move as a single unit, brace-man half a step behind, always in step."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Heat shimmers around their boots even when the lance isn't lit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They mark cleared bunkers with a scorch-cross so no one else wastes fuel on them twice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This is their second tank; the first went up early and took the last team with it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fire doesn't gutter in wind or rain the way ordinary fire should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the tank ruptures, the team keeps advancing through the blast like the fire agrees with them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["hauling a tank of oil-fire between them while one braces the weight and one aims the nozzle", "clearing a bunker mouth in one long screaming breath of flame, then moving on without watching it finish"]},{"name":"Deserter-Thing","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"rlm-theater-revenant","summary":"Executed deserter risen wrong, hunting its executioners","flavor":"Shot for running from the line, it came back wrong and now hunts whoever ordered the execution.","desc":"Shot against a post for running, it came back from the ground wrong, uniform still stripped of its markings, eyes fixed on the direction the firing squad stood. It doesn't chase anyone else. It only wants the men who gave the order.","traits":{"note": "It has no interest in anyone but the men who gave the order — it will walk past easier prey to reach them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Deserter-Thing attacks twice with its stolen blade, or once with the blade and once with its bow."}, {"name": "Post-Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Firing-Squad Bow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Executioner's Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the Deserter-Thing gains temporary hit points equal to the damage dealt. This attack deals double damage against a creature that has ever given an execution order, if the Deserter-Thing somehow recognizes one."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dug in near an old post, waiting on a road that hasn't carried the officer who shot it in years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes someone in the party's uniform-adjacent colors for the man who read the charges."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living deserter is using its legend to hide, and the real thing has just noticed the impersonation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a scrap of the charge-paper still, illegible now, and won't stop until it's delivered somewhere."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's blocking the one road out of a village that the party needs before nightfall."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three more posts nearby suggest it wasn't the only one shot that morning, and the others haven't risen — yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It answers to its old rank if addressed correctly, for exactly as long as the lie holds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's finally found someone close enough to the man who ordered it shot, and it won't be talked back down now."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "forest"],"activity":["standing at the post it was shot against, uniform stripped, eyes fixed on the firing line's old position", "moving toward wherever the executing officers went, ignoring everyone else entirely"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Grenadier","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"rlm-musket-line-grenadier","summary":"Fearless grenadier carrying door-opening black powder","flavor":"Tall-hatted, fearless, and carrying enough black powder to open any door he's pointed at.","desc":"Tall hat, steady hands, he carries enough black powder slung at his hip to open any door he's pointed toward. He doesn't flinch lighting the fuse close to his own face. Whatever's behind that door stops being a problem shortly after.","traits":{"note": "He's not being brave lighting fuses that close — he's just done the math on how far the blast actually reaches.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grenadier attacks twice with his spear, or once with the spear and once with a shield-bash."}, {"name": "Bayonet-Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage, or 10 (1d10 + 4) Piercing if used with both hands to make a melee attack."}, {"name": "Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be pushed 5 feet away and knocked prone."}, {"name": "Door-Opener Charge (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Grenadier hurls a satchel of black powder at a point within 60 feet. Each creature within 10 feet of that point makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 14 (4d6) Fire damage on a failure, half as much on a success. Any door, gate, or barrier caught in the blast is destroyed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hat's brim is singed short from too many fuses lit too close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hums while he works the fuse, same three notes every time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries exactly as much powder as the job needs and never an ounce more."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He always steps back the same six paces before a door goes, out of long habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands are steady even when the rest of him clearly isn't."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's opened doors he still won't talk about, for reasons that weren't strictly military."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fuses he lights burn at exactly the same rate regardless of wind, rain, or length."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If cornered, he'll light the charge still strapped to his own hip rather than be taken."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["walking a fuse toward a door with enough black powder at his hip to open it permanently", "lighting a charge close to his own face without flinching, tall hat cocked against the wind"]},{"name":"Longship Ghost Fleet Crewman","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Century-dead rower still believing the raid continues","flavor":"Rows a ship that beached a hundred years ago and never stopped believing the raid is still on.","desc":"He rows a ship that beached a century ago, oar dipping into water that isn't there anymore, expression fixed on a raid he still believes hasn't ended. Salt-rot clings to what's left of his tunic. He doesn't look up when you pass.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't register the party as a threat unless they stand between him and the raid he still believes is happening.", "actions": [{"name": "Century Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until the target finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Wake the Crew", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Crewman calls a fellow oarsman up from the wreck. A spectral rower rises from the nearest wreckage or waterline within 30 feet and acts on the Crewman's turn, making one Century Grip attack of its own before dissolving back into salt-rot after 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His beached hull sits half-buried near a shore road the party needs to cross before dark."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rowing toward a landmark that's been rebuilt three times since his raid, and doesn't recognize the change."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living descendant of the village he raided still leaves offerings at the wreck without knowing why."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding a chest lashed to the hull that he still believes is full of the raid's plunder."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party is carrying resembles a banner from the fleet he sailed with, and he's noticed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "More hulls are buried along this same stretch of shore, and the tide is starting to uncover them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water around his oar ripples on a tideline that hasn't reached this shore in a hundred years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided, wrongly, that the raid is finally about to succeed, and nothing will convince him otherwise tonight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast", "sea", "ruins"],"activity":["rowing an oar into water that isn't there anymore, expression fixed on a raid still underway in his mind", "sitting at a beached hull's oarlock a century after the tide left it stranded"]},{"name":"Siege Ballista Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"rlm-siege-ballista-crew","summary":"Gate-punching war-machine crewed around the clock","flavor":"A war-machine built to punch through castle gates, reloaded by a crew that never sleeps.","desc":"The war-machine's crew reload without rest, arms moving in shifts that never seem to end, the great bolt-thrower groaning back to full draw again and again. It's built to punch gates, and it's punched more than most gates could survive. No one at the winches has slept in longer than anyone wants to say.","traits":{"note": "No one at the winches has slept properly in longer than anyone wants to say — that's why the reload never stops.", "actions": [{"name": "Great Bolt", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120/480 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a structure or an object, this attack deals double damage."}, {"name": "Locking Volley (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The crew looses a braced volley at a point within 120 feet. Each creature within 10 feet of that point makes a DC 15 Strength save. On a failure, a creature is pinned in place by the bolt-work, its speed reduced to 0 until it or another creature uses an action to free it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The winch crew rotates in shifts of two, and the two currently working haven't spoken in hours."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The machine's frame is patched with iron bands from at least two older, broken ballistae."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tally of gates punched is scratched into the frame, too many notches to count quickly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The crew eats standing at their posts, meals passed hand to hand without stopping the reload."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One winch-man's hands shake now between pulls, though his grip never actually slips."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This machine has outlasted every crew assigned to it; the current one is its fourth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The draw-tension groans in a rhythm too regular to be wood settling naturally."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the crew finally collapses, the machine keeps drawing itself back on the same schedule regardless."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["reloading a gate-punching war-machine in shifts that never seem to end, arms moving on habit alone", "groaning the great bolt-thrower back to full draw again for a gate it's already broken twice"]},{"name":"Jungle Tiger-Rider Scout","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"tiger","model":"rlm-jungle-tiger-rider-scout","summary":"Trained big-cat rider scouting the canopy trails","flavor":"Rides a trained big cat through the canopy trails faster than any patrol can track.","desc":"He rides low along a canopy trail no patrol could follow, the big cat beneath him silent on padded feet, ears already turned toward something ahead. Leaves barely rustle where they pass. By the time you'd hear them, they've already gone.","traits":{"note": "By the time anyone would hear them coming, they've already passed and gone.", "actions": [{"name": "Canopy Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is knocked prone."}, {"name": "Silent Passage", "text": "Once per turn when the Scout's mount moves at least 10 feet in a straight line toward a creature, that creature has disadvantage on the first attack roll it makes against the Scout before the Scout's next turn, having failed to track the approach in time."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tiger's paws are wrapped in soft leather to keep them silent on the harder ground."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The scout signals with hand motions only, never a voice, even at rest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scars along the tiger's flank match old campaign markers the scout still tracks by."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The scout carries no banner, no insignia — nothing that would identify which side sent them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They rest only when the cat rests, never before, never after."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This scout has run three separate patrols into the ground without ever once being seen doing it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves don't rustle at all where the pair pass, not even the ones underfoot."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the cat is struck first, the scout doesn't retreat — the pair breaks discipline and comes back as one animal."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "hill"],"activity":["riding low along a canopy trail no patrol could follow, ears of the cat already turned ahead", "vanishing into leaf-shadow faster than any sound could be raised behind them"]},{"name":"Trench Officer's Ghost-Whistle","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"rlm-trench-officers-ghost-whistle","summary":"Dead officer whose whistle still calls the charge","flavor":"An officer who blew the whistle for the final charge and never stopped hearing it answered.","desc":"It doesn't have a face left worth describing, only a whistle still gripped between what used to be teeth, and the sound it makes is the same order it gave the night it died. Every man who hears it feels his boots start moving before he decides to. It has never once stopped believing the charge worked.","traits":{"note": "It has never once stopped believing the charge worked — that certainty is the whole of what's left of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Final Order", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by the same amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Dead Officer's Face", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each non-Undead creature within 60 feet that can see the Ghost-Whistle must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened for 1 minute. A frightened target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "The Charge That Worked (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "The Ghost-Whistle sounds the note it died giving. Each creature within 30 feet that can hear it makes a DC 14 Wisdom save, taking 17 (5d6) Psychic damage on a failure and being paralyzed until the end of its next turn as its body tries to obey an order it never gave, or half damage and no paralysis on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's sounding over a field the party is trying to cross quietly, and quiet is no longer an option."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member's boots start moving on their own the instant they get close enough to hear it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixed to a spot where an old command post used to stand, and won't leave that ground."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party is escorting used to serve under the officer it once was, and it's noticed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the exact stretch of wire where its own charge actually failed, though it insists otherwise."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Older bones nearby stir faintly whenever it sounds, like a company remembering how to stand."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whistle-note carries no direction — it seems to come from wherever the listener's own dread already points."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to sound the note that worked once, and it fully intends for it to work again tonight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["gripping a whistle between what used to be teeth, sounding the same order it gave the night it died", "standing over a stretch of mud where boots start moving before their owners decide to"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Field Marshal's Honor Guard","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"rlm-musket-line-field-marshals-honor-guard","summary":"Standard-guard sworn to die before it falls","flavor":"Sworn to die before the standard falls, and mean about proving it.","desc":"They stand fast in a tight ring around a battle standard, bayonets out, faces set, sworn to die before the fabric touches the ground. Fire crackles around them and none of them step back. They're not being brave so much as certain.","traits":{"note": "They aren't being brave holding the ring — they're certain, which is worse for anyone trying to break them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Guardsman attacks twice with the standard-rapier, or once with the rapier and once with a pistol."}, {"name": "Standard-Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Honor Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each guardsman has sworn the same oath in a slightly different wording, and none of them notice the difference."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The standard-pole is cracked and lashed with wire, held up more by will than by wood."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They rotate who holds the pole in strict order, no exceptions, even mid-fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their boots are planted and don't shift even when the ground around them is churned to mud."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of them keeps a private tally of every guard before him who died holding this exact standard."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This standard has fallen once before and been retaken; none of them will let it happen twice."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They don't flinch at fire that should be close enough to singe them, as if the oath dulls it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the standard finally falls, the ring doesn't break — it closes tighter around the fallen pole instead."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["standing fast in a tight ring around a battle standard while fire crackles and no one steps back", "reloading pistols calmly inside a circle sworn to die before the fabric touches the ground"]},{"name":"Cavalry Death-Rider","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"nightmare","model":"rlm-cavalry-death-rider","summary":"Dead cavalry officer and horse still mid-charge","flavor":"A cavalry officer and his warhorse, both killed in the same charge, still riding it out.","desc":"Both officer and warhorse died the same instant of the same charge, and neither seems to have noticed — hooves still drumming, sword still raised at the same angle it fell. Cold radiates off them before they're even close. The charge that killed them has never once finished.","traits":{"note": "The charge that killed them has never once finished — anything standing in its path is treated as the original enemy line.", "actions": [{"name": "Drumming Hooves", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Charge Unfinished", "replaces": "Ethereal Stride", "text": "The Death-Rider and its mount can move through creatures and solid objects as if they were difficult terrain, taking no damage from doing so, so long as they remain mid-charge — a straight line toward the last position they registered as the enemy."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's charging a road the party is traveling, having mistaken their approach for the old enemy line."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living cavalry officer bears the same rank insignia, and the Death-Rider has locked onto him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rides the same stretch of field every dusk, the charge repeating whether anyone is there or not."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The frost of its passing has killed the crop in a strip the local farmers won't cross."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying dispatches from the battle it died in, still sealed, still technically undelivered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its own side's dead lie along the same field, having been ridden down by their own charge in the confusion."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The sword's angle never changes no matter what it strikes, as if the blow itself already happened once and for all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something has finally moved into the exact position of the charge's original target, and the ride is about to complete."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "any"],"activity":["riding hooves still drumming a charge that finished the instant it killed them both", "holding a sword raised at the exact angle it fell at, cold radiating off horse and rider alike"]},{"name":"Longship Berserker-King's Champion","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"centaur-warden","model":"rlm-longship-berserker-kings-champion","summary":"Bare-chested prow-fighter daring the shore to resist","flavor":"Fights bare-chested at the prow, daring the enemy shore to try and stop the landing.","desc":"He fights bare-chested at the longship's prow, daring the whole shoreline to try and stop the landing, laughing through wounds that would drop three other men. Salt spray soaks him and he doesn't seem to notice the cold. Nobody near him wants to be the one who proves him wrong.","traits":{"note": "Nobody near him wants to be the one who proves his boasting wrong — and so far, no one has managed it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Champion attacks twice with his prow-staff, or once with the staff and once with a ray of sun-fire."}, {"name": "Prow-Staff", "replaces": "Forest Staff", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Sun Ray", "replaces": "Sun Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Champion calls out old battle-rites as spells, drawing on the same bravado that drives his fighting."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He counts his scars aloud sometimes, like a boast he's still updating."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He refuses armor above the waist, calling it an insult to the men who have none at all."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's first off every ship and last to leave every shore, without exception."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He laughs loudest exactly when a wound should have silenced anyone else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He remembers every man who's tried to prove him wrong, by name, fondly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's led a dozen landings this same way and lost count of how many shorelines called his bluff and lost."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cold never seems to reach him even soaked through, as if the sea's decided to let him be."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The one time he's actually hurt badly, he laughs louder still, and the whole landing party seems to believe him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "forest", "hill"],"activity":["fighting bare-chested at the prow, daring the whole shoreline to try and stop the landing", "laughing through wounds that would drop three other men, salt spray soaking him unnoticed"]},{"name":"Jungle Ambush War-Priest","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"oni","model":"rlm-jungle-ambush-war-priest","summary":"Ritual-blessing war-priest wading into the ambush","flavor":"Blesses the ambush with old rites before the horn sounds, then wades in swinging a ritual club.","desc":"He mutters old rites over the ambush line before the horn sounds, ritual club already resting against one shoulder, eyes half-closed in something like prayer. When the horn comes, the prayer stops mid-word. He wades in like the blessing already did the hard part.","traits":{"note": "He believes the blessing already won the fight before the horn even sounds — his fighting is just the formality.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The War-Priest attacks twice with his ritual club, or once with the club and once with a nightmare ray."}, {"name": "Ritual Club", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Nightmare Ray", "replaces": "Nightmare Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 90 ft. Hit: 15 (4d6 + 1) Psychic damage, and the target has disadvantage on its next saving throw against being frightened."}, {"name": "Shape-Shift", "replaces": "Shape-Shift", "text": "The War-Priest takes on the shape of the terrain's own predators mid-ambush, unsettling anyone watching him do it."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The rites he mutters before the horn function as spellcasting, blessing the ambush before it begins."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He kneels exactly the same way before every ambush, knees pressed into the same patch of mud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His club is carved with notches he adds after, never before, a fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He never raises his voice above the rite's own murmur, even mid-combat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He blesses his own ambush line by name, one soldier at a time, unhurried."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He stops praying the instant the horn sounds, as if the words had a hard deadline."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His rites have blessed ambushes that failed as often as they've blessed ones that worked, and he's stopped noticing the difference."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ambush line always goes quiet in the exact same way right before he finishes the rite, like the jungle itself is listening."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the rite is interrupted mid-word, he doesn't restart it — he simply attacks as if it had already finished."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "ruins"],"activity":["muttering old rites over the ambush line, ritual club resting against one shoulder, eyes half-closed", "wading into the fight the instant the horn sounds, mid-word, like the blessing did the hard part already"]},{"name":"Siege-Line Trebuchet Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-giant","model":"rlm-siege-line-trebuchet-golem","summary":"Self-aiming trebuchet that no longer waits for orders","flavor":"A siege engine grown a crude will, it aims itself now and doesn't wait for the order to loose.","desc":"It aims itself now, arm creaking back on its own without anyone giving the order, and looses the moment it decides the angle's right. Stone and timber groan under its own draw-tension. It stopped needing a crew a long time before anyone noticed.","traits":{"note": "It stopped waiting for orders a long time before anyone noticed — the crew markings on its frame are just decoration now.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Golem attacks twice with its stone club, or once with the club and once by loosing its boulder."}, {"name": "Stone Club", "replaces": "Stone Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 19 (3d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Self-Aimed Boulder", "replaces": "Boulder", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60/240 ft. Hit: 24 (4d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a structure or an object, this attack deals double damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its crew-platform is still bolted on, empty, swaying uselessly with every shot."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It creaks through the same firing sequence every time, unhurried, as if it still has all the crew's patience."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old chalk marks for range corrections are still scrawled on its arm, though it no longer needs them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses between shots exactly as long as a crew changeover used to take, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The arm's draw-tension groans loud enough to carry for a mile before it looses."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's outlasted the siege it was built for by years, still loosing at a wall that's long since fallen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to choose targets with a kind of judgment no siege engine should have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When its arm finally breaks, it keeps trying to fire on the stump, servos or spirit refusing the idea of stopping."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["aiming its own arm back without anyone giving the order, stone and timber groaning under its own draw-tension", "loosing the moment it decides the angle's right, having stopped needing a crew a long time ago"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Cannon Golem","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"rlm-musket-line-cannon-golem","summary":"Walking field-gun chassis built to replace dead crews","flavor":"A field gun bolted to a walking chassis, built when someone realized the crew kept dying.","desc":"A field gun bolted onto a lumbering iron chassis rolls forward on legs built after too many crews died at their posts, the barrel swinging level with unnerving smoothness. Its footsteps land heavier than the recoil does. It doesn't need a gun-line standing behind it anymore.","traits":{"note": "It was built because the crews kept dying — it doesn't remember that anymore, only that it doesn't need them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cannon Golem makes two slam attacks, or one slam and fires its mounted gun."}, {"name": "Iron Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Mounted Field Gun", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 26 (4d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a structure or an object, this attack deals double damage. This attack cannot be used again until the Golem has moved at least 10 feet, mimicking the reload it no longer needs but was built expecting."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chassis is stenciled with a unit number for a crew that no longer exists."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It swings its barrel level with a smoothness that unsettles the men still forced to walk near it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footfalls land in a rhythm that could pass for marching, if anyone were still marching with it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old lanyard-loops for a firing crew still hang uselessly off its frame."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses at graves of gun crews sometimes, for exactly as long as respects used to take."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rolled through three separate armies' equipment now, outlasting every unit it was assigned to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It reloads on a rhythm no living gunner ever set for it, like it's answering someone else's orders."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When its chassis finally buckles, the gun keeps swinging level on the wreckage, still hunting a line to fire on."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["rolling forward on legs built after too many gun crews died at their posts, barrel swinging level", "landing footsteps heavier than its own recoil, needing no gun-line standing behind it anymore"]},{"name":"Trench Wraith of the Wire","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"rlm-trench-wraith-of-the-wire","summary":"Company-wide death-wraith hunting by muzzle-flash memory","flavor":"A whole company lost to one machine gun, fused by grief and mud into something that hunts by muzzle-flash memory.","desc":"A whole company lost to one gun position fused together by grief and mud into a single drifting shape, hunting the field by the ghost of a muzzle-flash it remembers. It doesn't have individual faces anymore, just an outline where a hundred did. It moves toward wherever the flash used to be.","traits":{"note": "Moves through wire, mud, and revetment without hindrance, and always moves toward the last muzzle-flash it saw.", "actions": [{"name": "Wire-Drag (replaces Bite)", "text": "Loops of remembered wire whip out. Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage, and a Medium or smaller target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15) as the wire coils tight."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's converging on a lantern the party just lit, mistaking it for the muzzle-flash it hunts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fixed to the exact stretch of wire where its gun position once stood, and won't leave that ground."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor's grandchild is digging near the old position, unaware of what still waits under the wire."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying pieces of a hundred uniforms fused into its shape, a few tags still faintly legible."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surges toward any gunfire nearby, friend or foe, unable to tell the difference anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Smaller shapes sometimes peel briefly off its outline, individual faces surfacing before the fusion pulls them back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers the muzzle-flash more clearly than it remembers dying, and reacts to light before threat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A real flash has just gone off nearby, and the whole fused mass is about to converge on it at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["drifting the field as a single fused shape, hunting by the ghost of a muzzle-flash it remembers", "moving without individual faces now, just an outline where a hundred men used to stand"]},{"name":"Longship Draugr-Fleet Captain","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"wraith","summary":"Drowned fleet-captain whose sunk ships still answer","flavor":"Commands a crew of the drowned, and every ship he's ever sunk still answers his horn.","desc":"He commands a crew of the drowned from a deck that shouldn't still float, and every ship he's ever sent to the bottom answers when he sounds the horn. Water pools steadily around his boots without ever draining away. The sea, wherever he sails it, still seems to owe him something.","traits":{"note": "The sea still seems to owe him something — wherever he sails, drowned crews rise to settle the debt.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Captain attacks twice with his drowned claw, or once with the claw and once with his infernal hook."}, {"name": "Drowned Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Infernal Hook", "replaces": "Infernal Sting", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 16 Strength saving throw or be pulled 15 feet toward the Captain, as though dragged under by an unseen current."}, {"name": "Sound the Horn (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Captain sounds a horn that carries below the waterline. One drowned crewman rises from the nearest water within 60 feet and fights alongside him for 1 minute, using the statistics of a sailor but immune to being frightened."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His horn is sounding near a harbor the party needs to use, and the drowned are starting to answer."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wreck the party salvaged turns out to be one of his sunk ships, and he's noticed the theft."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's sailing toward a coastline his fleet never finished raiding, a debt he intends to collect late."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His boots leave standing water on dry planks wherever he walks, ruining cargo he passes near."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living captain has taken his old flag as a trophy, and the Draugr wants it back specifically."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every ship lost to storm along this coast in living memory seems to answer to his horn now, not just the ones he sank."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water around him never drains, pooling endlessly as if the sea itself keeps paying him in advance."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just sounded the horn for a fleet the size of which hasn't answered in a hundred years, and it's rising anyway."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "planar"],"activity":["commanding a crew of the drowned from a deck that shouldn't still float, water pooling around his boots", "sounding a horn that every ship he's ever sunk still answers, somewhere below"]},{"name":"Jungle Colossus-Beast","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"rlm-jungle-colossus-beast","summary":"Tamed prehistoric survivor used as a living ram","flavor":"A prehistoric survivor pressed into service as a living battering ram by whoever tamed it first.","desc":"A prehistoric survivor bigger than anything that should still be walking gets pressed into service as a living battering ram, hide scarred pale under barding lashed on in a hurry. Trees splinter ahead of it before the war-cry behind it even finishes. It doesn't know it's a weapon. It just knows to charge.","traits":{"note": "Barding covers the vitals but nothing covers the trees ahead of it — anything standing there goes down too.", "actions": [{"name": "Trample Charge", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus-Beast makes two Ram Horn attacks, or moves up to its speed in a straight line first and adds one extra Ram Horn attack against a creature it passes if it has room."}, {"name": "Ram Horn", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Piercing damage, and a Large or smaller target is pushed 10 feet away and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barding straps have rubbed the hide raw underneath; it flinches at the cinch before every charge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Answers only one handler's whistle and ignores every other command given near it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a snapped harness pole that clatters and catches on roots as it runs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slows for nothing smaller than a wagon; foot soldiers simply aren't real to it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has trampled its own handlers twice and hasn't been trusted with a rider since."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its hide bears healed-over scars from a dozen prior campaigns nobody living remembers assigning it to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Doesn't recognize a battlefield as anything but a very large, very loud jungle."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Once charging, nothing short of a felled leg stops it — friend and target are the same word to it mid-stride."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "hill"],"activity":["crashing through undergrowth toward a war-cry it's already answering", "standing hitched to a barding harness, waiting for the whip-crack that starts the charge"]},{"name":"Trench Butcher Golem","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"rlm-trench-butcher-golem","summary":"Close-quarters clearing machine built for the unstomachable work","flavor":"Built for the close-quarters clearing work no living soldier could stomach doing twice.","desc":"It was built for the close-quarters clearing work no living soldier could make himself do twice, moving through a trench section with an economy that has nothing to do with mercy. It doesn't hesitate at corners the way a person would. That's rather the point of it.","traits":{"note": "It works corners the way a person never would — there is no blind angle it forgets to check.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Golem makes two Clearing Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Clearing Blade", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (3d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Trench Flare", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 13 (3d8) Fire damage, and the target is Lit — it sheds dim light for 1 minute and can't benefit from cover from the Golem."}, {"name": "Choke Vapor (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "The Golem vents corner-clearing gas in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 17 Constitution save, taking 22 (4d10) Poison damage on a failure, half as much on a success. A creature that fails is also Poisoned until the end of its next turn, choking on vapor built for exactly this trench width."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Plating still carries a maker's stamp from a foundry that no longer exists."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at exactly one pace, whether the trench is empty or full of enemies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its blade arm has been resharpened so many times the edge sits crooked."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops dead at any door it can't open cleanly — someone has to force it through."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vapor tanks hiss faintly at all times, a tell any veteran learns to listen for."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has cleared this same trench section eleven times; the bodies never stay gone long enough to matter to it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its corner-check pattern occasionally pauses on empty ground, as if checking for someone no longer there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone forgot to give it a stop order, and it has been clearing corners for three years past the war's actual end."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["clearing a trench section corner by corner with mechanical, unhurried economy", "standing motionless in a flooded dugout until something living moves nearby"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Ghost Regiment","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","model":"rlm-musket-line-ghost-regiment","summary":"Regiment lost in one charge, still marching in formation","flavor":"A whole regiment lost in one disastrous volley-charge, still marching in perfect dead formation.","desc":"An entire regiment lost in one disastrous volley-charge still marches in perfect dead formation across ground that no longer needs taking. Boots strike the earth in unison with no sound following. They don't seem to know the charge already failed — they're still marching toward the order that sent them.","traits":{"hp": 130, "ac": 14, "note": "A regiment fighting as one swarm-formation (scaled far past the crawling-claw chassis, CR 9): it can occupy other creatures' spaces, and its volley weakens once the formation is Bloodied.", "actions": [{"name": "Dead Men's Volley", "text": "The whole line presents and fires. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 16, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Failure: 22 (4d10) Necrotic damage, or 11 (2d10) if the Regiment is Bloodied. Success: half damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boots strike the ground in unison but raise no dust and leave no print."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches through solid obstacles as if the order predates the terrain."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A drum somewhere in its ranks keeps a cadence no living ear can quite place."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wheels crisply at the same fixed point every time, regardless of what's there now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform colors have bled to the same uniform grey across every rank."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Where it passes, grass lies flattened in marching-column shape for exactly one night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Individual soldiers occasionally step out of formation to salute something not present, then rejoin."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the regiment ever reaches the ground it was ordered to take, the entire formation collapses to bone in a single instant."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["marching in perfect dead formation across ground that stopped mattering long ago", "wheeling as one body toward an order that was shouted a lifetime ago"]},{"name":"Siege Wall-Breaker Titan","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"fire-giant","model":"rlm-siege-wall-breaker-titan","summary":"Ram-wielding siege titan that doesn't stop swinging","flavor":"Swings a ram the size of a tree trunk and doesn't stop until the gate or its arm gives first.","desc":"He swings a ram the size of a felled tree in a slow relentless arc, again and again, gate-timbers splintering a little further with each hit. Sweat and mud run off him in equal measure. He doesn't stop until the gate gives or his own arm does, and he seems entirely at peace with either outcome.","traits":{"note": "He doesn't stop until the gate gives or his arm does, and he's genuinely fine with either.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Titan makes two Ram-Swing attacks, or one Ram-Swing and uses Splinter Throw."}, {"name": "Ram-Swing", "replaces": "Flame Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a structure or barrier it takes an extra 14 (4d6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Splinter Throw", "replaces": "Hammer Throw", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 60/120 ft., a gate-timber or broken stone thrown like a spear. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sweat and mud run off him in equal measure no matter the weather."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums the same work-song under his breath with every swing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His ram is lashed with rope that's been re-tied so often it's mostly knot."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't swing at anything that isn't a wall, gate, or door — people have to get out of the way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rests between swings by leaning the full ram against his own shoulder."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The gate he's currently working has already fallen once before, in his memory of a different siege."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Counts each swing aloud in a number that's well past any gate's actual breaking point."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When the wall finally gives, he keeps swinging at the rubble, unable to recognize that the job is done."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["swinging a felled-tree ram in a slow relentless arc against a splintering gate", "resting the ram's weight on one shoulder, gauging the wall's give with his free hand"]},{"name":"Longship Sea-Wyrm Figurehead","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"wyvern","model":"wyvern","summary":"Cursed living figurehead diving from fog onto ships","flavor":"A carved prow come alive with raider curses, it dives on enemy ships from the fog.","desc":"A carved prow comes alive out of the fog with a raider's dying curse still animating the wood, diving on unsuspecting hulls from an angle no lookout expects. Salt-slick timber gleams where scales should be. It surfaces again somewhere else before the wreckage even finishes settling.","traits":{"hp": 170, "ac": 16, "note": "Carved oak under salt-iron sheathing (scaled past the wyvern chassis, CR 10) — it is timber, not flesh: immune to Poison, and its tail is a rudder, not a sting.", "actions": [{"name": "Prow-Dive", "text": "It falls out of the fog like a ship coming down. If the figurehead moves at least 30 feet straight toward a target while flying and then hits it with a Bite attack, the target takes an extra 13 (2d12) Piercing damage and has the Prone condition."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt-slick timber gleams wet where scales ought to catch the light instead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never surfaces near the same stretch of coast twice in one season."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The raider's face is still faintly visible in the grain of its carved snout."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only dives when fog is thick enough to hide the approach entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves splintered prow-shaped gouges in every hull it strikes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It surfaces near wrecks it caused decades ago, circling them like a tally it's keeping."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sailors swear it answers to the raider's old ship-name, shouted as a warning too late."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It won't disengage from a hull once it's bitten in — the curse wants that ship sunk, not scared."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["diving out of fog onto an unsuspecting hull at an angle no lookout expects", "resurfacing somewhere new before the last wreckage has finished settling"]},{"name":"Jungle War-Machine of Rusted Vines","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"Root-swallowed ancient war-engine, still fully armed","flavor":"An engine of war swallowed by the jungle for decades, now grown through with roots and still armed.","desc":"An engine of war has been swallowed by the jungle for decades, roots grown thick through every seam in its plating, and it's still fully armed underneath all that green. Birds nest where a gunport used to matter. It doesn't seem to know the war it was built for is long finished.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't know its war ended — anything that reads as an enemy formation still gets the full arsenal.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The War-Machine makes two Root-Fused Slam attacks, or one Slam and one Rusted Volley."}, {"name": "Root-Fused Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Rusted Volley", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Force damage, old munitions still finding their mark through the leaves."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Birds nest in a gunport that used to matter and scatter the moment it fires."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its plating has gone green-black, indistinguishable from bark at ten paces."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roots have to tear free with an audible groan before it can take a full step."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fires at the treeline reflexively whenever wind moves the canopy just right."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries decades of unspent munitions rattling loose somewhere inside its hull."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sap has sealed most of its old hatches; whatever crewed it once is long fused shut inside."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It rotates its gunports toward sounds no scout can ever quite trace to a source."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it releases decades of trapped sap-pressure — anything nearby eats the full stored volley at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["standing root-bound and half-swallowed, gunports still tracking through the canopy", "grinding forward a few feet at a time, vines tearing as ancient joints wake"]},{"name":"The Field Marshal's Undying Aide","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Undying aide delivering the same dead order nightly","flavor":"Delivers the same order at the same hour every night, a century after the marshal died reading it.","desc":"He delivers the same dispatch at the same hour every single night, a century after the marshal he serves died reading the first copy of it. His uniform hasn't faded so much as gone the color of dust. He waits for a reply he stopped expecting decades ago and delivers the order anyway.","traits":{"note": "He'll fight anyone who tries to stop him mid-delivery — the order has to be given, reply or no reply.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Aide makes two Dispatch Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Dispatch Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Sealed Orders (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120 ft., a wax-sealed dispatch case hurled like a weighted mace. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Necrotic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, gripped by the sudden certainty it's already failed some order."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Aide casts one of its prepared spells, requiring no material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He hands the party a dispatch case, mistaking them for the runner he's been waiting for."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's blocking the one door out of the ruin until his nightly delivery is complete."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The dispatch he carries names a real target still standing somewhere nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member's uniform-colored coat for the marshal's, and won't let them leave."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's arrived exactly on schedule, and something else timed its own arrival to match his."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His uniform hasn't faded so much as gone the uniform grey of dust — touching it ages cloth on contact."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dispatch case, opened, contains a blank page; he's been delivering nothing for a century and doesn't know it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Interrupting his route a second time in one night causes him to summon the marshal's full guard to enforce it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["delivering the same dispatch at the same hour, a century after it stopped mattering", "waiting at attention for a reply he stopped expecting decades ago"]},{"name":"Trench Legion Revenant Colonel","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"rlm-trench-legion-revenant-colonel","summary":"War-denying revenant rallying every nearby corpse","flavor":"Refuses to accept the war is over, and rallies every corpse in earshot to prove it.","desc":"He refuses, flatly, to accept that the war is over, and every corpse within earshot of his voice rises to help him prove it. His medals have tarnished black. He rallies the dead the same way he once rallied the living — by simply assuming they'll follow.","traits":{"note": "Kill anything nearby without killing him first and he'll likely have it back up by his next turn.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colonel makes two Rally Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Rally Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "War Isn't Over (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Necrotic damage, and if this kills a Medium or smaller creature, its corpse rises at the start of the Colonel's next turn as a spectral soldier under his command for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Colonel casts one of its prepared spells, requiring no material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His medals have tarnished black but he still polishes them by rote each dawn."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rallies the dead the same way he rallied the living — by simply assuming they'll follow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to acknowledge any surrender, living or dead, offered in his presence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a private roster and crosses off names the instant they fall a second time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks only in orders — no threats, no boasts, just the next instruction."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every fresh corpse within a mile of him stirs faintly whether he wills it or not."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He addresses long-dead subordinates by name mid-battle as if they'd just reported in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If he falls, every corpse he's raised this fight collapses at once, and he considers that an acceptable trade."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["rallying every corpse within earshot with the same flat certainty he once used on the living", "pacing a collapsed trench line, tallying dead who are already standing again behind him"]},{"name":"Longship Storm-Caller Reaver","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"rlm-longship-storm-caller-reaver","summary":"Storm-bargaining reaver whose weather still owes him","flavor":"Bargained the sea itself into raiding for him, and the storm still owes him one more shore.","desc":"He bargained the sea itself into raiding on his behalf once, and the storm still seems to think it owes him one more shore. Lightning walks the mast behind him without ever quite touching it. He stands at the helm like a man collecting on a very old debt.","traits":{"note": "Not a genie — a mortal reaver the weather obeys, grudgingly. Kill him and the storm he bargained with does not stop; it just stops taking orders.", "actions": [{"name": "Call In the Debt (Recharge 6)", "text": "He points, and the storm pays what it owes. Lightning falls on a point he can see within 120 feet. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere on that point. Failure: 27 (6d8) Lightning damage and the target can't take reactions until the start of its next turn. Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lightning traces the mast behind him but leaves the wood entirely unmarked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never bargains twice with the same stretch of sea — he considers that bad form."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks to the water between orders as though it might still answer back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to make landfall himself, sending crew ashore in his place."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally, scratched into the helm, of shores he still believes he's owed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The storm precedes him by exactly one day wherever he means to raid next."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His voice occasionally comes out layered with thunder, as if the sea is answering through him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the debt is ever fully paid, the storm stops obeying him mid-battle and turns on everyone equally."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "elemental"],"activity":["standing at the helm collecting on a debt the storm still owes him", "letting lightning walk the mast behind him without ever quite touching it"]},{"name":"Jungle Chimera-Beast of War","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Warlord-bred chimera leading otherwise unsurvivable charges","flavor":"Bred by a warlord's beast-tenders to lead a charge no single animal could survive alone.","desc":"A warlord's beast-tenders bred three animals into one to lead a charge no single creature could have survived alone, and the three heads still argue faintly even mid-stride. It doesn't slow to settle the disagreement. Whatever it's charging toward, all three of it want the same thing.","traits":{"note": "It never slows to settle the heads' disagreement — whatever they're charging, all three want it dead.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chimera-Beast makes three attacks: one Fang Snap, one Rend Claw, and one Warhorn Ram."}, {"name": "Fang Snap", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rend Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Warhorn Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and a Large or smaller target is knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Bred-In Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Chimera-Beast exhales fire in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 24 (7d6) Fire damage on a failure, half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its three heads growl at each other constantly in a low, arguing register."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bears a warlord's brand on its flank, half burned away by its own breath."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head favors biting, one clawing, one ramming — they rarely agree which comes first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was bred specifically to lead, never to hold ground once taken."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Answers a warlord's horn-signal even now, though no warlord remains to blow it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Scar tissue across all three necks suggests the heads have fought each other before, badly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "In quiet moments the three heads seem to negotiate, almost gently, before agreeing on violence."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If one head is destroyed, the other two turn briefly on each other before remembering the actual enemy."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "hill"],"activity":["leading a charge no single animal could survive alone, three heads arguing mid-stride", "pulling three directions at once before all three settle on the same target"]},{"name":"Musket-Line Field Marshal-Revenant","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"rlm-musket-line-field-marshal-revenant","summary":"Century-dead marshal still finishing his last order","flavor":"Died at his own headquarters table mid-order and has been finishing that sentence for a hundred years.","desc":"He died at his own headquarters table in the middle of dictating an order and has spent a century since finishing that same sentence. Candle wax has puddled and re-hardened a hundred times around him. The order never quite gets to the end.","traits":{"note": "No bite, no blood — the unfinished order is what sustains him. He cannot be turned aside from his headquarters table for long; he always returns to it.", "actions": [{"name": "The Last Order (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "He finally finishes the sentence. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, each enemy within 30 feet that can hear him. Failure: 21 (6d6) Psychic damage, and the target obeys one word of the order — it can't take reactions until the end of its next turn. Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Candle wax has puddled and re-hardened around him a hundred times over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The order never quite gets to the end no matter how many times he starts it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ink on his desk has dried into the same three words, over and over."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He stands the instant anyone touches the door, as though the runner has finally arrived."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice carries the exact cadence of a man mid-dictation, forever."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The room around him hasn't aged past the night he died in it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally he addresses a runner who isn't there by a name no living record holds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the order is ever finally finished aloud in front of him, he goes utterly still, as if released."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["sitting at a headquarters table finishing a sentence a century overdue", "rising mid-dictation the instant something disturbs the room he died in"]},{"name":"Trench Colossus of Bone and Wire","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rlm-trench-colossus-of-bone-and-wire","summary":"Self-built ossuary titan from an unnamed battle's dead","flavor":"Built itself from the unburied dead of a battle no one survived to name.","desc":"It built itself, slowly, out of the unburied dead of a battle nobody survived to name, bone knitted through with rusted barbed wire like tendon. It doesn't remember whose side it fought for. It only remembers that the ground kept giving it more material.","traits":{"ac": 18, "note": "Huge, mindless of the rakshasa chassis's cunning — no spells, no disguise. Just mass, wire, and the patience of the unburied.", "actions": [{"name": "Ossuary Slam (replaces Cursed Touch)", "text": "A fist of fused ribcages. Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 19 (3d12) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Take Up the Dead", "text": "The colossus drags one corpse within 10 feet of it into its own mass and regains 19 (3d12) Hit Points."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone knitted through with rusted barbed wire creaks like tendon with every step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "New bones fuse to it slowly whenever it lingers over unburied dead."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears fragments of a dozen different uniforms, none of them matching."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves toward wherever the ground is freshest-turned, drawn like a scavenger."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wire lattice hums faintly in wind, an unintended and constant sound."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has grown visibly larger since it was last reported, still adding material."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally it arranges loose bones at its feet into shapes resembling old formations."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it scatters its component dead across the field, some of which rise separately for one round."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["grinding forward one joint at a time, wire tendon creaking taut over stolen bone", "standing over an unmarked stretch of ground, gathering fresh dead into itself"]},{"name":"No-Man's-Land Warlord's Ghost","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"General's ghost eternally watching his own fatal order","flavor":"The general who ordered the crater assault still watches it from above, unable to look away from his own order.","desc":"He still watches the crater from above, unable to look away from the assault he ordered into it, replaying the same few seconds without end. His hands are clasped the way they were when he gave the command. He has never once managed to take his eyes off the result.","traits":{"note": "Incorporeal — it drifts above the crater and passes through wire, wall, and rampart without hindrance. It cannot leave sight of the crater it made.", "actions": [{"name": "The Order, Again (replaces one Eye Ray)", "text": "The ghost repeats the order that killed them all. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 17, one creature within 120 feet. Failure: the target must use its reaction, if available, to move up to its speed toward the crater's center."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's watching a real crater nearby that the party is about to walk into unaware."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor of the original assault is present, and he fixates on them instantly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party's approach for the reinforcements he never sent."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying the order itself, a scrap of paper that still names a real objective."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He can be made to look away only by someone repeating his own exact command back to him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Everyone who dies within his crater's sight joins the loop, watching alongside him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crater beneath him has started, slowly, to widen to match how many now watch with him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He is the instant of the order itself, unable to end; anyone who steps into the crater's sight risks watching forever at his side."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "any", "planar"],"activity":["watching a crater from above, unable to look away from the assault he ordered into it", "replaying the same few seconds of his own command without end"]},{"name":"The Ironclad Reaver-Queen","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"iron-golem","model":"rlm-the-ironclad-reaver-queen","summary":"Ship-hull-and-captain war-machine that never comes ashore","flavor":"A longship's hull fused with its captain by a dying storm-oath, now a war-machine that never beaches.","desc":"A longship's hull fused with its captain in the last seconds of a dying storm-oath, and the result never quite beaches anywhere again. Barnacled plate groans where a keel should be silent. It patrols coastlines the way its captain once did, only now the ship and the woman are the same argument.","traits":{"note": "Hull and captain are one body. She never comes ashore — she fights from water deep enough to float her keel, and the shallows are her surrender line.", "actions": [{"name": "Carronade (replaces Fiery Bolt)", "text": "A hull-gun runs out and fires. Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 300 ft. Hit: 36 (8d8) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature it is pushed 10 feet straight away."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barnacled plate groans at the joints where a keel should be silent."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never beaches fully, always keeping some part of itself in the water."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The captain's face is still faintly discernible in the hull's figurehead line."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols the exact coastline route the captain sailed in life, tide after tide."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt crusts thick over every seam, flaking off in sheets when it moves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It occasionally speaks in two overlapping voices, ship and woman disagreeing on the course."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fish and gulls follow it inland well past where any tide should reach."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the woman's voice ever wins an argument with the ship's, it turns and beaches itself entirely, done patrolling."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["patrolling a coastline the way its captain once did, ship and woman now one argument", "groaning at anchor in shallow water, barnacled plate settling where a keel should be silent"]},{"name":"Legion Undying Praetorian Host","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Never-broken honor-guard formation, undying for centuries","flavor":"An entire honor-guard that swore to never break formation, and hasn't, in any century since.","desc":"An entire honor-guard swore, once, to never break formation, and it hasn't in any century since, ranks locked shoulder to shield exactly as drilled. Dust settles on them between the rare moments they move. Nobody currently alive gave them that oath, and it doesn't matter to them at all.","traits":{"hp": 260, "note": "A formation, not a man — one Large block of locked shields that fights as a single creature. While it has more than half its hit points, ranged attacks against it have Disadvantage (the shield-roof holds).", "actions": [{"name": "Pila Volley (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The front rank throws as one. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 18, each creature in a 30-foot Cone. Failure: 27 (6d8) Piercing damage. Success: half damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust settles thick on the ranks between the rare moments they move at all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shields lock so tightly together that removing one takes visible effort even in death."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hasn't broken formation in any century since the oath was sworn."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nobody currently alive gave them this oath, and it changes nothing for them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ranks close seamlessly around any gap the instant a member falls."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The formation has held this same stretch of ground long enough that ruins have grown up around it instead of over it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally the whole host shifts one pace as one, honoring a drill cadence only it can hear."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the formation is ever fully broken, every member collapses at once — the oath, not the body, was holding them upright."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing locked shoulder to shield exactly as drilled, dust settling between rare moments of motion", "holding formation over ground that nobody currently alive has any claim to"]},{"name":"The Gas-King of the Salient","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"gulthias-blight","model":"gulthias-blight","summary":"Sentient gas-cloud amalgam that owns the salient's ground","flavor":"Every gas attack ever loosed on the salient pooled into one thinking, hating cloud that owns the ground now.","desc":"Every gas barrage ever loosed across this stretch of ground has pooled together into one thinking, hating cloud that now simply owns the ground it used to just poison. It doesn't roll with the wind anymore — it decides. The salient belongs to it the way land belongs to whoever's still standing on it.","traits":{"ac": 14, "note": "A drifting, thinking cloud — blades and shot pass through it; strong wind and open flame are what it actually fears. It holds the low ground and lets you come to it.", "actions": [{"name": "Green Drift (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The cloud pours itself over a 30-foot Cube within 30 feet. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 20. Failure: 42 (12d6) Poison damage and the Poisoned condition until the end of the target's next turn. Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rolling toward a dugout the party is currently sheltering in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wounded straggler flees ahead of it, choking, begging the party for higher ground."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's pooled thick around cargo the party needs, refusing to thin near it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It parts briefly around one specific patch of ground, as though avoiding something buried."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's actively pursuing a retreating patrol that stumbles toward the party for help."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every gas mask within the salient fogs and fails the moment it draws close."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally forms a face in its own vapor, mouthing an order no one issued."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The whole salient is inside it now, in a sense — thin it in one place and it simply reclaims the ground from another."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "ruins", "elemental"],"activity":["owning the ground it used to only poison, deciding rather than drifting with the wind", "thickening low over the salient, patient and aware in a way gas was never meant to be"]},{"name":"The Siege That Never Lifted","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"Fused siege-line horror still failing to take the city","flavor":"A siege line's worth of engines, crews, and dead fused into one wall-breaking horror that still hasn't taken the city.","desc":"A whole siege line's worth of engines, crews, and dead have fused into a single wall-breaking horror that, after all this time, still hasn't taken the city in front of it. It keeps trying anyway, patient past any reasonable definition of patience. The walls it's failed against are older than most of what built it.","traits":{"hp": 350, "ac": 21, "note": "A colossus scaled to the siege it still fights (CR 17, not the full chassis) — the dead crews inside still load, aim, and correct their fire.", "actions": [{"name": "Breach Volley (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Every engine fused into it fires at once along a 120-foot-long, 10-foot-wide Line. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 21. Failure: 45 (10d8) Bludgeoning damage and the target has the Prone condition. Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grinding toward a wall the party is currently standing on top of."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fusing a wrecked engine into itself, and the wreckage still has living crew trapped inside."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's methodically working through fortifications the party needs intact to survive something else."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A defender's descendant still mans the wall it's besieging, out of stubborn family duty."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses periodically as if listening for a surrender that was never going to come."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The walls it's failed against are older than most of what built it, and both sides seem to know it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its assault pattern occasionally repeats an engine's death-throes from centuries before it existed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is the siege itself made permanent — destroy the engine and the assault simply resumes from whatever wreckage is nearest."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["grinding against a wall it still hasn't taken, patient past any reasonable definition of patience", "fusing another engine's wreckage into itself before resuming the same failed assault"]},{"name":"The Trench Ghost","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"shell-shocked revenant infantryman on eternal patrol","flavor":"A soldier who never left the line, rifle still slung, gas-hood rotted to rags; it keeps walking a patrol route that ended lifetimes ago.","desc":"Rifle still slung the way regulation demanded, gas-hood rotted down to rags at his collar, he walks a patrol route that finished being relevant lifetimes ago. His boots find the same ruts every time. He doesn't notice there's no trench left to patrol.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Patrol Bayonet", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Reflex Volley", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, fired at anything that moves in his old sight-lines."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gas-hood rotted to rags at his collar, still fastened out of habit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't notice there's no trench left to patrol, and never will."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes the same fixed point in the air at the same moment every circuit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rifle sling has rotted through; he carries it in the crook of his arm now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops dead at a whistle-blast, whether or not one actually sounded."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His patrol route is scored faintly into stone that has otherwise long since crumbled away."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally reports to a superior who isn't there, in a voice too quiet to make out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If his patrol route is ever physically blocked, he keeps walking into the obstruction rather than deviate."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "any"],"activity":["walking a patrol route that finished mattering lifetimes ago, boots finding the same ruts", "standing rifle-slung at a post that no longer has a trench around it"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic WWI-lensed infantry archetype (no named nation/unit)"},{"name":"The Legion Wall","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"rlm-theater-legion","summary":"lone shield-and-spear legionary, drilled to a fault","flavor":"One tile of a wall that used to be a hundred men wide; it still steps in formation even with no one left on either flank.","desc":"He holds one tile of a shield-wall that used to run a hundred men wide, stepping in perfect formation with nobody left on either flank. Rust has fused the shield to the arm underneath it. He doesn't break rank even standing entirely alone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wall Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. if thrown. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rust has fused his shield to the arm underneath it permanently."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't break rank even standing entirely alone on an empty field."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Side-steps to match a flank-mate who isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His spear point has snapped and been re-fitted with whatever sharp metal was nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still calls out the wall's old formation number before every advance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The ground under his one tile has worn into a shallow groove from standing there so long."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He occasionally braces as if absorbing a charge that never lands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push past his position and he pursues at a dead sprint, breaking formation for the first time in his memory."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "hill"],"activity":["holding one tile of a shield-wall a hundred men wide, with nobody left on either flank", "stepping in perfect formation to a cadence only he still remembers"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"classical-era shield-line legionary archetype"},{"name":"The Musket Line","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard","model":"guard","summary":"standing volley-drill musketeer, drilled past reason","flavor":"Loads, kneels, fires, reloads — the whole drill even when there's no second rank behind him and no order left to give.","desc":"He goes through the whole drill — load, kneel, present, fire, reload — with no second rank behind him and no order left worth giving. Smoke curls off a barrel that's fired for no one to see. His hands still know the sequence better than his eyes know the field is empty.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Volley Musket", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 40/120 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smoke curls off a barrel that's fired for no one to see it land."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands still know the sequence better than his eyes know the field is empty."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels to reload at exactly the same tempo whether under fire or not."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Powder horn is nearly empty; he rations shots without knowing why anymore."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fires a volley cue aloud before every shot, as if signaling a line that's gone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Spent shot litters the ground around him in drifts deep enough to mark the years."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally reloads a weapon that's already loaded, doubling the charge without noticing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When his powder finally runs dry, he charges bayonet-first rather than stop the drill."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "urban", "ruins"],"activity":["going through the full drill — load, kneel, present, fire — with no second rank behind him", "reloading for an order nobody left alive would think to give"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic 18th/19th-c. volley-fire infantry archetype"},{"name":"The Longship Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"hobgoblin-soldier","summary":"axe-and-round-shield sea raider, stranded in the war","flavor":"Came ashore for plunder and glory and got neither — just the theater's endless tide instead of home.","desc":"He came ashore chasing plunder and glory and found neither, only this theater's endless grinding tide instead of anything like home. His axe is nicked past use and he keeps swinging it anyway. He stopped expecting to make it back to a ship a long time ago.","traits":{"note": "He fights like a man who's already written off the trip home.", "actions": [{"name": "Nicked Axe", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage from a blade worn thin at the edge."}, {"name": "Cast Spear", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a round shield painted with a house-mark no one here recognizes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing back at the tideline like the boat might still be there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sunburnt across the neck, salt-crusted, boots full of sand he never empties."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights loud, singing between blows in a tongue the theater has no use for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a whittled toy meant for a child he hasn't seen in longer than he'll say."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Believes, wrongly, that this shore is the one he set out for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tide keeps bringing him back no matter how far inland the fighting drags him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sees the boat one more time, real or not, and charges past the party toward it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "any"],"activity":["wading up a shale beach swinging a nicked axe at nothing yet", "hauling a longboat past the surf line as if home were still worth reaching"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"Norse-lensed raider archetype (not a specific saga figure)"},{"name":"The Jungle Scout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"camo-draped recon scout gone half-feral in the green","flavor":"Camouflage gone to lichen, machete more rust than edge — still moves like the canopy is watching him back.","desc":"Camouflage gone to actual lichen, machete more rust than edge, he still moves like the canopy above him is keeping watch. Insects have made a home in his gear straps. He hasn't stopped believing the jungle is on his side, even now.","traits":{"note": "He trusts the green to hide him more than he trusts his own aim.", "actions": [{"name": "Machete Flurry", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Scout makes two attacks, using Rusted Machete or Snap-Bow in any combination."}, {"name": "Rusted Machete", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Snap-Bow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lichen has colonized the back half of his pack straps entirely."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks trees with a code system that stopped meaning anything years ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves without a sound, then flinches at his own footfall in a clearing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shares his rations with whatever insects have nested in his collar."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still reports sightings aloud to a command post that answers nothing back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely believes the canopy warns him before an ambush lands."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Vines have grown through his gear without slowing him down at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The green closes over him mid-fight and he simply isn't where he was."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["picking a route through undergrowth with a rusted machete held loose and ready", "freezing mid-step at a canopy sound only he seems to register"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic mid-century jungle-warfare scout archetype (no named conflict)"},{"name":"The Siege Sapper","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"tunnel-digging siege engineer, still mining toward a wall","flavor":"Digs toward the wall by memory, pick over one shoulder, satchel of black powder over the other, humming a tune no living ear would know.","desc":"He digs toward a wall by memory alone, pick over one shoulder, a satchel of black powder swinging off the other, humming something no living ear would place. Dirt falls steady past his boots into the dark behind him. He doesn't remember which wall, only that there's always one.","traits":{"note": "He carries the powder himself — anyone standing close is standing in the blast radius too.", "actions": [{"name": "Digging Pick", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Powder Charge", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Bludgeoning damage from a thrown charge that bursts against its target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't remember which wall he's mining, only that there's always one."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dirt sifts steadily off his boots even when he's standing still."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the satchel strapped tight to his chest, never sets it down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts his own paces under his breath, timing a fuse only he can hear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches hard at loud noise, then goes right back to humming."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely doesn't register that the wall he's digging toward isn't there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tune he hums is older than any war this theater has staged."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Decides the fight itself is close enough to a wall and sets the charge anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["digging a narrow tunnel toward a wall by memory, pick over one shoulder", "humming tunelessly while black powder shifts in the satchel at his hip"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"medieval siege-engineer archetype"},{"name":"The Berserker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"battle-trance warrior who fights past fear and flesh","flavor":"Fights bare-armed and bear-shirted, past fear, past pain, past the point where the theater's rules of engagement still apply to him.","desc":"He fights bare-armed, bear-shirted, past the reach of fear and past most of what should be pain, somewhere the rest of the field's rules of engagement stop applying to him. Blood doesn't seem to slow him the way it slows anyone else. Whatever's driving him isn't tactics.","traits":{"note": "Pain and blood don't seem to register on him the way they should.", "actions": [{"name": "Bear-Shirt Cleave", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d12 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Past Reason", "text": "When reduced to half its Hit Points or fewer, the Berserker gains a +2 bonus to attack rolls until the end of combat and does not treat any condition as compelling it to retreat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred forearms bare to the weather, unarmored by choice."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roars before every swing, a sound with no words left in it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps fighting well after a wound that should have dropped him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes fixed on one target and nothing else in the field."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews something bitter-smelling before the charge, jaw working the whole fight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Doesn't recognize his own side once the rage is fully on him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Laughs mid-swing at something only he seems to find funny."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns on the nearest living thing when no enemy is left standing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "forest", "hill"],"activity":["working himself into a shaking, wordless rage before the line even engages", "wading into the thickest press of the fight, bare arms already bleeding"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse saga/legend berserkr tradition (public domain; no modern media design)"},{"name":"The Draugr Captain","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"mound-risen undead officer still holding a dead line","flavor":"Guards a rank that was overrun centuries ago as if the order to hold still stands; corpse-cold hands still know the grip of a sword-hilt.","desc":"He guards a rank that was overrun centuries back as though the order to hold is still current, corpse-cold hand closing on a sword-hilt like the grip never stopped meaning something. Mound-dirt still clings under his nails. He isn't waiting for relief — he's just still holding.","traits":{"note": "He isn't waiting for relief — he's simply never stopped holding the line.", "actions": [{"name": "Rank-Holder's Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Captain makes two attacks, using Grave Longsword or Bone Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Grave Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Bone Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Mound-Cold Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the Captain regains Hit Points equal to the damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mound-dirt still packed under blackened nails after all this time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same watch-call at intervals no one else keeps."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Armor rusted to the shape of a body that stopped growing centuries ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores any order that isn't the one he was originally given."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straightens a rank of corpses that fell in formation beside him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Still salutes an insignia from a nation the theater has long since blurred away."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His picket line has been overrun and re-formed a hundred times without him noticing once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Treats any retreat by his own line as desertion and turns his blade on it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "coast"],"activity":["standing an ancient rank alone, sword-hand still closed on a corroded hilt", "pacing a picket line that was overrun before this war or the last one"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse folklore draugr — the mound-dwelling undead warrior of the sagas"},{"name":"The Machine-Gun Nest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"fused gun-and-gunner emplacement, animate and traversing","flavor":"Not one soldier but the whole emplacement fused together — tripod legs, traversing arms, a barrel where a face should be.","desc":"It isn't one soldier but the whole emplacement fused into a single traversing shape — tripod legs, articulated arms, a barrel where a face belongs. It swings its aim in one smooth motion, unhurried, mechanical. Nothing about it needs to breathe between bursts.","traits":{"note": "It never needs to pause between bursts, and it never looks away from its arc.", "actions": [{"name": "Traversing Fire", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Nest makes two Barrel Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Barrel Burst", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Fixed Arc", "text": "The Nest cannot move from the ground it occupies, but its traversing mount lets it make attacks against any target within range without needing to reorient."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tripod legs sunk deep into churned mud, immovable and patient."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barrel scorched black from a burst that never seems to end."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Traverses in perfect increments, sweeping the same arc over and over."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Articulated arms click faintly with each adjustment of aim."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sandbags stacked around its base, rotted through and unreplaced."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "No gunner's silhouette behind it, just the barrel where a face should be."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fires in bursts timed to a rhythm no living gunner ever set."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Widens its arc past any reasonable field of fire once truly pressed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["traversing its mounted barrel across the field in one slow mechanical arc", "sitting dug-in and motionless until something crosses its fixed line of fire"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic entrenched-crew-served-weapon archetype"},{"name":"The Storm-Trooper Cadre","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"rlm-theater-trench","summary":"grenade-and-trench-knife shock infantryman","flavor":"Moves in twos and threes between the shell-holes, grenade-first, never in the open longer than a breath.","desc":"They move in twos and threes between the shell-holes, grenade-first, never lingering in the open longer than a single breath allows. No one calls out orders — they don't need to. They're already gone from one crater before you register they were ever in it.","traits":{"note": "They never linger in the open long enough to be caught there.", "actions": [{"name": "Shock Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cadre makes two attacks, using Trench Knife or Crossbow Volley in any combination."}, {"name": "Trench Knife", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Crossbow Volley", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Crater Hop", "text": "As a bonus action, the Cadre can move up to half its Speed without provoking opportunity attacks if that movement ends in cover."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a pair, covering each other without a word exchanged."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries more grenades than seems reasonable for one body."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never takes the same crater twice in a single engagement."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signals with hand gestures too fast and clipped to read."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Already gone from a position before the smoke clears."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Coordinates with a third member the party never quite manages to spot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves no tracks between craters, as if the ground doesn't register them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Abandons cover discipline entirely and closes the distance at a dead sprint."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["darting between shell-holes in twos and threes, grenade already in hand", "crossing open ground in a single committed breath before dropping from sight"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic elite-shock-infantry archetype (WWI stosstruppen-style, no named force)"},{"name":"The Valkyrie","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"empyrean-iota","model":"empyrean-iota","summary":"battlefield psychopomp choosing which dead the war keeps","flavor":"Walks the field after the guns fall quiet, marking which of the fallen the theater will keep and which it lets go home.","desc":"She walks the field once the guns have gone quiet, unhurried, studying the fallen with an attention that has nothing to do with mercy. Her hand hovers over some and passes others by without explaining the difference. She decides which of them the theater keeps.","traits":{"note": "Her attention isn't mercy — she's deciding which dead the theater keeps.", "actions": [{"name": "Reaper's Judgment", "replaces": "Otherworldly Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Radiant damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Field Casting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Valkyrie casts one of her prepared spells, requiring no material components."}, {"name": "Mark of Keeping", "text": "The Valkyrie touches a dying creature within 5 ft. and chooses whether it stabilizes at 1 Hit Point or drops to 0 outright — her choice, not fate's."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already standing over a downed party member, hand not yet decided."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fallen ally the party thought lost is one she hasn't chosen yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's passed over someone the party desperately needs alive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An old grudge rides with her — she remembers a debt owed to the party."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's counting bodies aloud, and the number is one short of what's actually there."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She offers to bargain a life back, if the party gives her one of equal weight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She doesn't recognize this war as different from any other she's walked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided to keep someone the party very much needs to keep fighting."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "any", "planar"],"activity":["walking a quieted field after the guns stop, studying the fallen one by one", "hovering just above the mud, hand outstretched over a body it hasn't judged yet"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse myth — chooser of the slain (public domain figure, our own visual take)"},{"name":"The Iron Cavalry","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"rlm-theater-mark4","summary":"armor-plated war-beast standing in for every era's tank","flavor":"Half horse, half hull-plate — the theater's answer to any age's need for something that doesn't tire and doesn't feel the wire.","desc":"Half warhorse, half hull-plate, it moves at a grinding trot that doesn't tire and doesn't feel the wire tearing at its legs. Sparks strike off it where it clips the wrong ground. Whatever era it's fighting in, it's always the answer to the same problem.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't tire and doesn't feel the wire — it's built to answer one problem forever.", "actions": [{"name": "Plated Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Locking Breath", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Cavalry exhales a freezing vapor in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failure, a target's speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn as joints and gear lock rigid; on a success its speed is halved instead."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sparks strike off its hull-plate every time it clips uneven ground."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trots at exactly the same pace whether charging or simply patrolling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trailing wire drags from one flank, torn loose from some earlier field."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steam vents from joints where a warhorse would sweat."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't shy from fire, noise, or the dead underfoot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Answers to no rider — it simply goes toward whatever's shooting at it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its plating shows rivet patterns from at least three different eras of make."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaks from any handler entirely and charges the loudest noise on the field."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["hill", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["grinding forward at a relentless trot, hull-plate sparking against broken ground", "tearing through tangled wire as if the wire itself were the only obstacle worth noting"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic armored-cavalry/tank archetype, era-blurred"},{"name":"The Siege Tower","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"animate siege-tower, self-propelled toward the wall","flavor":"Rolls forward on its own dead momentum, ladders unfurling like wings, arrow-slits blinking where windows should be.","desc":"It rolls forward on its own dead momentum, ladders unfurling from its sides like slow wings, dark slits along its face blinking where windows ought to be. Arrows stick in its timber flanks like a bristling coat. It doesn't stop climbing toward the wall for anything short of collapse.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't stop climbing toward a wall for anything short of its own collapse.", "actions": [{"name": "Ladder Rush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Tower makes two Arrow-Slit Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Arrow-Slit Blade", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Slashing damage from a blade run out through one of its slitted faces."}, {"name": "Unfurl the Ladders", "text": "As a bonus action, the Tower extends its ladders against a wall or creature within 10 feet, allowing up to two Medium or smaller creatures to climb it to the top without using movement, once per round."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Arrows bristle from its timber flanks like a coat it never sheds."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wheels grind loud enough to be heard a field away."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ladders creak on their unfurling hinges, worn from overuse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dark slits track movement below it like patient, unblinking eyes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leans hard into any wall it reaches, unwilling to reverse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Someone — or something — still rides inside it, visible only as shadow through the slits."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It climbs toward walls that were torn down generations before this war started."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its wheels lock and it simply falls forward onto whatever's blocking the breach."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["rolling forward on grinding wheels, ladders unfurling from its timber flanks", "leaning its bulk against a wall, dark slits along its face fixed on the breach"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"medieval siege-engine archetype"},{"name":"The Trench Wight","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"rlm-theater-revenant","summary":"revenant trench-officer still blowing the whistle to advance","flavor":"Commands a company that's mostly mud and memory now, whistle still around its neck, ready to blow the advance no one will survive.","desc":"Whistle still hung around a neck gone the color of old rope, he commands a company that's mostly mud and memory now, ready to sound the advance no one will survive. His voice carries even without much breath behind it. The men who'd have to follow that whistle stopped existing years ago, and he still expects them.","traits":{"note": "The men who'd answer his whistle stopped existing years ago, and he still expects them.", "actions": [{"name": "Officer's Volley", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Wight makes two Trench Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Trench Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Mud-Cold Grip", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the Wight regains Hit Points equal to the damage dealt."}, {"name": "Sound the Advance", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Wight blows its whistle, and up to three Undead of CR 1 or lower within 60 ft. rise from the mud to fight alongside it for 1 hour or until destroyed."}, {"name": "Officer's Stare", "replaces": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature the Wight can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 14 Wisdom save, becoming Frightened of the Wight for 1 minute on a failure. While Frightened this way, the creature must move toward the Wight on its turn if able."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistle-cord gone the color of old rope around a neck that shouldn't still hold it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice carries across the trench with almost no breath behind it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes an insignia rotted past recognition on its own collar."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Checks a pocket-watch that stopped decades before it did."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Paces the exact same stretch of trench, turn for turn, without fail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Still reads names off a roster no living hand ever wrote down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The mud along its trench occasionally answers back in half-formed voices."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Blows the whistle over a line that's actually empty and expects the dead to come anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "hill"],"activity":["commanding a company of mud and memory, whistle still hanging from a rotted cord", "pacing a trench line that emptied of the living long before this war began"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"WWI-lensed mass-grave revenant archetype (not any single named ghost)"},{"name":"The War Elephant","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"mammoth","model":"mammoth","summary":"armored siege-beast that shrugs off volleys and keeps coming","flavor":"Armored howdah still smoking from the last volley it shrugged off; it doesn't rout, it doesn't stop, it just keeps coming through the line.","desc":"Its armored howdah is still faintly smoking from the last volley it simply absorbed, and it doesn't slow, doesn't rout, doesn't do anything but keep coming through whatever line is in front of it. Each footfall lands like a small collapsing building. Nothing about its pace has ever changed.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't rout and it doesn't stop — each footfall lands like a small collapsing building.", "actions": [{"name": "Trample Charge", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Elephant makes two Tusk attacks. If it moved at least 20 feet straight toward a target this turn, that target also makes a DC 15 Strength save, taking 11 (2d10) Bludgeoning damage and falling Prone on a failure."}, {"name": "Tusk", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Armored howdah scorched black, still faintly smoking from the last volley."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ground shudders visibly with every footfall it takes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Arrows and bolts jut from its hide, ignored entirely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trumpets once before a charge, the same note every time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of collapsed fencing and shattered cart-wheels behind it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "No driver rides the howdah anymore — it charges of its own accord now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pace has never once changed, in this war or any before it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Loses the line entirely and simply keeps trampling straight through anything ahead."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "any"],"activity":["shrugging off a fresh volley without breaking its slow, unstoppable stride", "trampling a churned strip of field, armored howdah still smoking on its back"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"ancient/classical siege-beast archetype"},{"name":"The Gorgon Standard","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"gorgon-faced standard-bearer, a banner that petrifies stares","flavor":"A standard-bearer whose face the theater blurs on purpose — look at her banner too long and you understand exactly why armies used to carry her likeness into battle.","desc":"She carries a banner the theater keeps deliberately blurred at the edges, her own face turned just enough away that you understand, without being told twice, why armies used to march behind her likeness instead of beside her. Her grip on the standard-pole never wavers. Looking too long at the fabric feels like a mistake you already made.","traits":{"note": "The petrifying gaze lives in the banner she carries, not her face — and it keeps working after she falls, so long as the standard stands.", "actions": [{"name": "Raise the Standard (replaces Snake Hair)", "text": "She plants the pole and unfurls it. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 13, each creature within 30 feet that can see the banner. Failure: the target has the Restrained condition as it begins turning to stone, and repeats the save at the end of its next turn — Petrified on a second failure, free on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grip on the standard-pole never wavers, not even mid-combat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Banner fabric ripples oddly, edges deliberately indistinct."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Troops rally to her position without needing to look at her directly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps her visor-veil low even between engagements."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The standard-pole itself is scarred with old chips and gouges."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Statues of soldiers mid-stride litter the ground around her post."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Armies from wars generations apart have all carried a banner of her likeness."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Lets the veil slip entirely when the line she's holding finally starts to break."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "hill"],"activity":["carrying a deliberately blurred banner at the head of a line that won't break", "holding her ground at the standard-pole, face turned just enough away to matter"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Medusa/Gorgon, invoked here as a war-banner icon rather than the individual myth figure"},{"name":"The Flying Squadron","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"griffon","model":"griffon","summary":"aerial strafing beast standing in for the first air war","flavor":"Half war-bird, half war-machine, strafing the line from an altitude the trenches can only pray at.","desc":"Half war-bird, half war-machine, it banks low over the line and strafes a strip of churned ground the trenches can only flinch beneath. Its shadow crosses before the sound does. It climbs away before anyone below has finished ducking.","traits":{"note": "It's gone before anyone below has finished ducking.", "actions": [{"name": "Strafing Pass", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Squadron makes two Talon-Rake attacks. If it moved at least 20 feet in a straight line before attacking, it can make the attacks against different targets it flew over."}, {"name": "Talon-Rake", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow crosses the ground a full second before the sound of it arrives."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Climbs away sharply after every pass, never lingering in range."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feathers scorched at the tips from flying too near other engines of war."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Screeches once on the strafing run, metallic and half-mechanical."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles at an altitude the trenches can only flinch beneath."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Trailing straps and buckles suggest it once carried a rider who no longer exists."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Banks in formation with squadron-mates the ground troops never actually see."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Abandons altitude entirely and dives to press the attack at ground level."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "any", "mountain"],"activity":["banking low over the line, strafing a strip of churned ground before climbing away", "circling once at altitude, shadow crossing the field a full breath before the sound does"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic early-aviation/biplane dogfighter archetype"},{"name":"The Ironclad Leviathan","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"roc","summary":"gargantuan warship-beast that dominates the theater's horizon","flavor":"It doesn't fly the theater's skies so much as displace them, guns run out along a hull too vast to have ever been launched from any yard.","desc":"It doesn't so much sail the theater's waters as displace them, a hull too vast to have ever been launched from any yard, guns run out along a flank that seems to go on past where the eye wants to stop. Its wake alone could swamp a longship. It doesn't change course for anything smaller than itself.","traits":{"ac": 18, "note": "The roc chassis wears an armored hull — shot rings off the plating. It does not land; it stations itself overhead like weather.", "actions": [{"name": "Gun-Deck Salvo (replaces one Beak attack)", "text": "The hull guns fire down the line of its shadow. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 60-foot Cone beneath it. Failure: 28 (8d6) Piercing damage. Success: half damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cresting the horizon toward a coastal position the party is currently defending."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wake alone is about to swamp a smaller vessel the party needs intact."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A boarding party has just been thrown clear of its deck, still alive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its guns are already run out and aimed at a target the party can't afford lost."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragging a chain-net full of wreckage that includes something the party wants back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It answers to no flag anyone can name, and no one aboard seems to be steering it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's sailed past this same coastline in wars the maps no longer record."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has decided the horizon itself belongs to it, and nothing on the water gets to disagree twice."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "any"],"activity":["displacing the theater's waters as it advances, guns run out along an endless flank", "cresting the horizon like a shape too vast to have ever launched from any yard"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic armored-warship archetype, era-blurred (age-of-sail through dreadnought)"},{"name":"The War-Wyrm","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"chained siege-dragon deployed like a living artillery piece","flavor":"Chained to a war chariot bigger than most houses, it's less a monster than a munitions budget with wings and a grudge.","desc":"Chained to a war-chariot bigger than most houses, it strains against iron that was clearly built to hold something more reasonable, wings beating in short furious arcs it isn't allowed to finish. Its handlers ride well back from the reach of its chain. It's less a dragon anymore than a weapon someone decided to keep leashed.","traits":{"note": "Chained to its war-chariot — it flies only to the end of a 60-foot leash-arc and is hauled back. Deployed and fired like a battery piece, not fought like a dragon.", "actions": [{"name": "Ranging Shot (uses Fire Breath's recharge)", "text": "Its handlers walk the shot in. The wyrm arcs its fire at a point it can see within 300 feet. Dexterity Saving Throw: DC 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere on that point. Failure: 28 (8d6) Fire damage. Success: half damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its handlers are ordering it to bear down on a position the party is holding."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chariot chain is visibly weakening, one good hit from giving entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A handler has just fallen within its reach and no one's moving to save him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's being walked past the party's position as a show of force, not yet loosed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chariot carries a war-chest the party has every reason to want."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It flinches from its own handlers as much as from any enemy fire."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The chariot bears markings from an army that hasn't existed in generations."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The chain finally gives entirely, and for one battle it remembers it used to choose its own targets."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "any"],"activity":["straining against a chain built to hold something more reasonable than itself", "beating its wings in short furious arcs it's never once allowed to finish"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic siege-dragon archetype used as the theater's ultimate weapon, not tied to any named dragon myth"},{"name":"The Death Knight of No Nation","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"undead commander claimed by every faction, loyal to none","flavor":"Every side in every war in this theater has, at one time, sworn he was fighting for them; he has stopped correcting anyone.","desc":"Every faction in every war this theater has ever staged has, at some point, claimed him as theirs, and he has stopped bothering to correct any of them. His black armor carries no insignia that means anything specific. He fights with the same flat competence no matter whose line he's standing in.","traits":{"note": "At the first sound of battle he declares one side his own — no one, including him, knows which until he moves. His Dread Blade deals an extra 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage against anyone bearing the colors of the side he has disowned."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's leading a line the party's current allies are about to be caught inside."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An officer just handed him orders bearing the party's own faction's seal."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding ground the party desperately needs to cross before nightfall."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A defector from his line is trying to reach the party alive."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just been handed a black chest with no faction marking, and it's clearly important."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers the party a truce with the same flat tone he'd offer anyone else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He genuinely can't recall which war, of the many, he's currently fighting in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He decides, once and for the length of this battle, that this side is finally the one he meant."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "any", "planar"],"activity":["standing in whatever line currently claims him, black armor bare of any insignia", "fighting with the same flat competence no matter whose banner flies behind him"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic black-armored undead-commander archetype (fantasy stock type, no franchise ties)"},{"name":"The Siege of the World","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"ice-devil","model":"ice-devil","summary":"war given a body, wearing every era's uniform at once","flavor":"Wears every era's uniform at once and none convincingly; the theater's honest answer to what War would look like if it ever had to show its face.","desc":"It wears every era's uniform at once, and none of them convincingly, buckles and plate and drab canvas layered over each other in a shape that shouldn't hold together and does anyway. Smoke seems to follow it regardless of which century's weapons are firing nearby. It doesn't announce itself — it's simply already the reason the theater exists.","traits":{"hp": 290, "ac": 19, "note": "Not a devil of ice — a fiend of war. Its weapons change era mid-swing; the cold it deals is the cold of the field the morning after.", "actions": [{"name": "Every War at Once (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Every uniform it wears speaks a different dying order. Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 19, each enemy in a 30-foot Emanation. Failure: 36 (8d8) Psychic damage and the Frightened condition until the end of the target's next turn. Success: half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's advancing on a position the party has sworn to hold at any cost."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wounded commander begs the party to buy just one more hour against it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragging the front line itself forward, ground and all, toward the party's rear."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refugees are streaming past the party, fleeing whatever direction it's currently facing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses at the party specifically, as if recognizing something about them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every faction on the field stops fighting each other the moment it appears."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It wears a piece of gear the party swears they've seen on a corpse from a different battlefield entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It decides this field is the one where the war finally stops pretending to end, and simply keeps coming."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["standing at the center of the field wearing every era's uniform at once, none convincing", "trailing smoke that has nothing to do with which century's weapons are currently firing"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"original apex — the theater's totalizing embodiment of endless war, an original composite figure, not a myth or franchise reskin"}],
 "high-seas":[{"name":"Press-Ganged Deckhand","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Unwilling conscript swinging a cutlass under threat","flavor":"Taken off a dock at knifepoint three ports back; fights because the alternative is the lash, not because he wants your blood.","desc":"A cutlass wobbles in his grip like he's still learning which end is which. His shirt is someone else's, three sizes too big, and there's a rope-burn collar around his neck from being dragged aboard. He glances over his shoulder more than at you — checking who's watching him fight.","traits":{"note": "Fights without conviction — a clean escape route offered mid-combat may end the fight faster than damage will.", "actions": [{"name": "Wobbling Cutlass", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Borrowed Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the rope-burn collar raw and unhealed around his throat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing at the bosun instead of at you, flinching at every shout."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the name of the port he was taken from like a charm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights left-handed, favoring an arm still splinted from the lash."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a dockside brand half-healed on his forearm, a debt he never signed for."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Drops the cutlass the instant no one on his own crew is watching."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Fights with his eyes shut, praying under his breath in a tongue no one aboard speaks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns his blade on his own bosun the moment the fight tips against the crew."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swinging a cutlass wide and late, watching the rail for a way to bolt instead"]},{"name":"Bilge Rat Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Chittering vermin tide pouring from the hold","flavor":"They ate the last cook's boots and are working on his replacement's; every hold has them and every hold pretends not to.","desc":"The deck seems to move before the rats do — a carpet of fur and pink tails boiling up through a hatch. The smell hits first, wet and ammonia-sharp, then the chittering, then a hundred small teeth all at once.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chittering Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its Hit Points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Boils out of a hold that smells like the last three cooks lost this fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters toward stored grain the instant a hatch cracks open."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a slick trail of gnawed rope and chewed canvas in its wake."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swarms thicker around anything already bleeding on the deck."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in a dead man's boots, still wearing them like a lining."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Flees in one direction as one animal the instant fire is drawn."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves in a rippling pattern too coordinated for animals this small."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Doubles in a heartbeat, more boiling up from a hold no one remembers loading rats into."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["boiling up through a hatch in a carpet of fur, working through whatever was left unlocked"]},{"name":"Rope-Scar Cutthroat","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Cutlass-and-flintlock buccaneer swarming the rail","flavor":"Owes the crew's articles more than he'll ever earn; boards ships to buy back a little of his own name.","desc":"Rope has left white lines across both palms, permanent as tattoos. A flintlock hangs loaded but not yet drawn, and the cutlass comes up loose, almost lazy, like violence is just another chore before supper.","traits":{"note": "Talks before he swings — the panache is a real weapon, softening resolve before the blade ever moves.", "actions": [{"name": "Boarding Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4+2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Enthralling Panache", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "Charisma (Persuasion) vs. the target's Wisdom (Insight): if the Cutthroat wins the contest, the target has disadvantage on attack rolls against it until the end of the Cutthroat's next turn, charmed by sheer swagger."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rope-scarred palms flex open and shut before every draw, an old habit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears three men's rings on a cord, trophies he never bothers to sell."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls out wagers on the fight to his own crew mid-swing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps count of a debt to the articles under his breath between blows."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights with a grin that only slips when he's actually losing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers quarter for coin mid-fight, and means it, just this once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Laughs at wounds like they're funny stories he'll tell later."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Draws the flintlock only when truly cornered, and it never misses."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swaggering along the rail, flintlock loaded but holstered, cutlass loose in a lazy grip"]},{"name":"Chum-Slick Reef Shark","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"reef-shark","model":"reef-shark","summary":"Blood-trail shark circling a wounded hull","flavor":"Follows any ship that's been bleeding into its wake — a bad sign the crew reads correctly and ignores anyway.","desc":"A dorsal fin cuts the surface in slow, unhurried figure-eights, following a thread of blood no one else can see yet. When it finally breaches for the strike, the water goes white before the teeth ever show.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Breaching Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) Piercing damage. If the target is in the water, the shark has advantage on this attack roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fin cuts a wake already stained faintly pink before anyone's fallen in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred flank marks it as a survivor of some earlier feeding, and a mean one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a length of torn netting still hooked through one gill."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bumps the hull once, testing, before ever committing to the strike."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the ship at a patient, unhurried distance for hours before closing in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Breaks off the instant real blood other than chum hits the water, spooked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Circles counter to the current, against every instinct a shark should have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaches clean out of the water, throwing itself at the rail like it means to board."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["circling a bleeding hull in slow figure-eights, patient for the water to go white"]},{"name":"Waterlogged Deckwalker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Drowned crewman shambling back up the chain","flavor":"Went over in a storm and came back up the anchor chain; still wears the duty rota pinned to a rotted coat.","desc":"It climbs over the rail dripping brine from a coat gone the color of wet ash, a rotted duty-rota still pinned crooked to the lapel. Its steps are slow, deliberate, chain-scrape and squelch, like it's still walking a watch nobody canceled.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Brine-Slick Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Duty-rota pinned to the lapel still lists a watch order no one alive remembers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of standing brine on every board it crosses."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes before it swings, an old reflex the rot never took."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coat pockets are stuffed with waterlogged tobacco it can no longer smoke."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves toward the wheel first, every time, before anything else."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Stops dead when a bell rings eight bells, some drowned reflex answering the hour."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow on the deck still ripples like it's underwater."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Screams the name of the storm that took it the moment it's finally put down."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["climbing the anchor chain hand over rotted hand, still bound for a watch that ended years ago"]},{"name":"Rattling Bone-Crew Deckhand","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Cutlass-armed skeleton still standing its watch","flavor":"Picked clean by fish and time, still hauling the same rigging it died hauling; the rope never lets a bone crew rest.","desc":"Bone knocks against bone with every step, a dry percussion under the creak of rigging. It hauls on a line that isn't attached to anything anymore, cutlass strapped to a wrist with kelp-rotted cord, still working.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Barnacled Cutlass", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Buckler Shove", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4+2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is pushed 10 ft. away and must succeed on a DC 12 Strength save or fall Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rib cage still wears a strip of sailcloth uniform, bleached bone-white."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints knock a rhythm that matches old sea-shanty timing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a captain's whistle on a cord, blows it before every charge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One socket holds a bit of sea glass where an eye used to be."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights in perfect step alongside two more just like it, old rigging drill."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Breaks formation only to keep hauling its dead line, ignoring easier targets."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rope it hauls tightens on nothing, as if the ship it served still exists somewhere."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Collapses to component bones and reassembles itself once per fight, unbothered."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["hauling on a line tied to nothing, cutlass strapped to a wrist of kelp-rotted cord"]},{"name":"Fin-Toothed Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Fish-fanged sea-devil boarding from below","flavor":"Rises over the gunwale in packs when a hull rides low and slow; drags what it takes back down before the alarm bell finishes ringing.","desc":"It comes up over the gunwale in one wet heave, gill-slits flaring, rows of needle teeth bared in something that isn't quite a smile. Scales glisten black-green in the lantern light, and it's already reaching for the nearest throat.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Needle-Tooth Claws", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gill-slits flare wide and wet with every breath on deck air."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scales carry a fresh net-scar across one flank, cut free of a haul."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a length of chain it means to loop around a captive's ankle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hisses in short clicking bursts to pack-mates still below the waterline."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Comes up already gripping something taken off an earlier wreck."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Breaks off the fight to drag a downed sailor back over the rail instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its black-green scales seem to drink the lantern light rather than reflect it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole pack surfaces at once when the first alarm bell rings, faster than the crew can arm."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["surging up over the gunwale in a wet heave, already reaching for the nearest throat"]},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Squidling","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-octopus","model":"giant-octopus","summary":"Trench-spawned tentacle-beast dragging sailors under","flavor":"A juvenile shed off something vastly larger down in the trench; still small enough to drag a man under one-handed.","desc":"A tentacle comes up out of the black water first, thick as a mast and studded with suckers that leave welts. The rest of it surfaces slow and boneless, ink already clouding the water dark before it's fully seen.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Suckered Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 15 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6+1) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if it's Large or smaller."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One tentacle is stunted, chewed short by something bigger than itself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Suckers leave a ring of welts identical on every victim it's touched."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a thin cloud of ink even at rest, a nervous habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wraps around anchor chain first, as if testing which is stronger."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Changes color to match the hull it's climbing, badly, still too dark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Flees toward deeper water the instant it's actually hurt, no loyalty to the fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mimics the shape of a drowned hand with one tentacle-tip, beckoning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something vastly larger stirs the water below it when it's cornered, and doesn't surface."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["surfacing slow and boneless, ink already clouding the water before it's fully seen"]},{"name":"Gull-Eyed Wreck Harpy","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Rock-nesting harpy luring ships onto reefs","flavor":"Nests in the rigging of ships too slow to outrun it, singing sailors toward the rocks it circles like a gull circles chum.","desc":"It perches on the highest spar, wings mangy and salt-crusted, head cocked at an angle too sharp for a bird. Then it opens its mouth and the sound that comes out is almost a woman's voice, almost a song, almost enough to make a sailor forget the rocks.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wreck-Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Driftwood Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4+2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Reef-Luring Song", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 12, one creature that can hear the song within 300 ft. On a failure, the target is Charmed and must move toward the Harpy or the nearest rocks/hazard by the most direct route on its turn, ignoring its own safety. A creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in rigging already strung with older, drier bones of past catches."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice cracks partway through the song into something almost human, almost not."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feathers are salt-crusted white, patchy from an old net injury."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sings a different verse for each ship, learned by watching from the rocks."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Times its song to the swell, syncing the lure to the worst possible wave."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Stops singing entirely when its nest is threatened, fighting silent and vicious."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its song is in a dead sailor's actual voice, borrowed and worn like a coat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A whole rookery answers the first note, turning one lure into a chorus."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["perched on the highest spar, head cocked, testing a song against the wind direction"]},{"name":"Debt-Marked Bosun","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Ledger-keeping enforcer collecting the crew's debts","flavor":"Keeps the ledger of who owes the crew what, in coin or blood, and collects personally when a name comes due.","desc":"A ledger is strapped shut at his hip with a leather cord gone soft from handling. He reads names off it before he swings, flat and businesslike, like collections is just another watch to stand.","traits":{"note": "Marks debts before he collects — a name read aloud from the ledger signals exactly who he's about to move on.", "actions": [{"name": "Collector's Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6+3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ledger's Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ledger cord has gone soft and dark from years of the same thumb."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running tally of names crossed out, and never crosses his own."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks each debt owed aloud, precise to the coin, before drawing steel."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Collects in kind when coin's short, an ear, a finger, a favor logged instead."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to fight anyone whose name isn't already written down."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers to settle the debt in labor instead of blood, if asked plainly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ledger's pages are damp but never actually get wet, storm or no."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finds a party member's name already logged in the ledger before the fight even starts."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["reading a name off the ledger before drawing steel, flat and businesslike as any watch"]},{"name":"Deep-Fang Sea-Devil Priest","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Sea-devil war-priest chanting a raiding pack to frenzy","flavor":"Chants the raiding packs into a blood-frenzy from the wave-tops, offering the drowned to something older than the trench.","desc":"It stands at the wave-tops on legs that shouldn't hold weight on land, arms raised, chanting in clicks and glottal barks that don't sound like they were made for a human throat to answer. The raiding pack around it moves faster with every syllable.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Frenzy Chant", "text": "Nearby sahuagin allies gain advantage on their next attack roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone-and-coral fetishes clatter at its throat with every word."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm ends in a barbed hook where a shark took the hand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chant never stops, even mid-strike, even underwater."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks each kill on its own hide with a fresh coral scar."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a chest of drowned offerings it fights harder to protect than itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's mid-ritual to call something up from the trench and needs only a little more blood."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "When it sings, the water in the room stirs against gravity toward the deep."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The thing it's been chanting to has started to answer from directly below the hull."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["chanting a raiding pack into a blood-frenzy over the rail of a taken ship", "carving tide-marks into a captive's skin as an offering to something below"]},{"name":"Quartermaster of the Broken Articles","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Shadow-captain running the ship by fear alone","flavor":"Runs discipline on a ship whose captain hasn't been seen topside in weeks; the crew fears him more than any storm.","desc":"He counts coin without looking at it, eyes fixed on you instead, a smile that never once touches the rest of his face. The crew behind him goes quiet when he speaks — not respect, something closer to flinching.","traits":{"note": "The crew flinches rather than respects him — anyone who challenges him openly finds no one behind them willing to back a mutiny.", "actions": [{"name": "Discipline's Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Flintlock Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6+1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Reading the Articles", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: the Quartermaster names a broken article the target violated. On a hit with this attack, the target has disadvantage on the next saving throw it makes before the end of its next turn, unsettled by having its crimes read aloud."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs every debt he collects in a ledger bound in someone else's coat leather."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice, letting the silence around him do the threatening."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the true captain's cabin locked and untouched, for reasons he won't say."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts loot into three piles before any of it is claimed, own cut first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears gloves at all times, even indoors, even to eat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers a genuinely fair trade if approached without weapons drawn first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Speaks of the missing captain in present tense, as if still taking orders from empty air."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The crew turns on him the instant he looks like he's actually losing, no loyalty spent."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["counting coin without looking at it, eyes fixed on the room, smile not reaching the rest of his face"]},{"name":"Chain-Dragging Drowned Sailor","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Anchor-chained revenant press-ganging the living","flavor":"Went down chained to the very anchor he was ordered not to release; surfaces to recruit a crew that never mutinies twice.","desc":"Rusted anchor-chain drags behind it across the deck, gouging the planks, fathoms of it looped and tangled around a bloated torso. Its eyes are the milk-white of something that drowned looking up at a surface it never reached.","traits":{"note": "presses conscripts — a grappled victim who dies rises as a thrall within the hour"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Milk-white eyes fix upward, still looking for a surface it never reached."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chain has rusted into the bloated flesh, no longer separable from the body."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears an officer's coat, buttons green with age."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags the chain in a deliberate loop, as if measuring out a deck it remembers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in bubbling half-words, an order it never got to finish giving."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recognizes rank insignia and singles out whoever looks like the captain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The chain behind it vanishes into water that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every sailor it's drained before rises alongside it the moment the chain goes taut."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["dragging fathoms of rusted anchor-chain across the planks, gouging a path toward the living"]},{"name":"Mutinous First Mate","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Blade-drawn mate who murdered his way to command","flavor":"Slit the old captain's throat over a fair split and never looked back; the crew that followed him into it now wonders whose throat is next.","desc":"His coat still bears the old captain's braid, sewn crooked because he took it off a corpse in a hurry. The blade never leaves his hand, and there's a specific way he watches his own crew now — like counting who's next.","traits":{"note": "Trusts no one who followed him into the mutiny — that same crew may break for the party if given a real opening.", "actions": [{"name": "Captain's Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Salvaged Heavy Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "One Throat Too Many", "text": "When the Mate reduces a creature to 0 Hit Points with a melee attack, he can immediately make one Captain's Greatsword attack against a different target within reach, blade already moving to the next name."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The stolen captain's braid is sewn on crooked, taken in a hurry off a corpse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never sheathes the blade, not even to eat, not even to sleep."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Addresses the crew by rank instead of name now, distance on purpose."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the old captain's boots, too small, worn anyway out of spite."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Positions himself so his own crew is always between him and the door."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offers the party a cut of the ship's hold if they help him hold onto command."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the old captain's ghost like it's still standing at his shoulder, and answers it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His own crew jumps him mid-fight the moment his guard finally drops."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["watching his own crew with the specific look of a man counting who's next"]},{"name":"Fogbank Siren","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"Fog-shrouded siren-witch bartering safe passage","flavor":"Sells safe passage through her fog for a name, a memory, or a firstborn — and always collects in a currency the crew didn't expect.","desc":"She emerges from fog thick enough to swallow a mast, green-skinned and smiling with too many teeth, one hand already extended like she's offering something instead of demanding it. Her voice, when it comes, is warm — that's the part that should worry you.","traits":{"note": "Never breaks her bargains outright — the price she names is always technically what she said, just never what was meant.", "actions": [{"name": "Barter-Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Fogbound Bargain", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "Spell Save DC 13. The Siren casts spells drawn from a bargain-and-mist repertoire (Fog Cloud, Charm Person, Suggestion, and similar effects at will or a limited number of times per day), always framed as an offer rather than a compulsion."}, {"name": "Named Price", "text": "Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 13, one creature the Siren has just made an offer to. On a failure, the target is Charmed by the Siren for 1 hour and believes it has already agreed to her terms, even if it hasn't spoken a word."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smiles with one tooth too many, filed to a point, and knows you noticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Names her price before you've even said what you want passage for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fog clings to her like a second coat, never quite dispersing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a collection of small forgotten things, buttons, teeth, names, as trophies."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice is warm and patient, the kind of warm that should worry you."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Actually honors a bargain struck fairly, to the letter, no tricks."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her reflection in still water shows an older, harder face than the one she wears."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Calls in every debt she's ever collected at once, and half the crew owes her something."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["emerging from a fog thick enough to swallow a mast, one hand already extended like an offer"]},{"name":"Lantern-Eyed Ghost Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Translucent captain still haunting his own quarterdeck","flavor":"Still walks his own quarterdeck on the night the fog rolls thick, hailing living ships for a berth he'll never fill twice.","desc":"He stands the quarterdeck of a ship that isn't there, translucent as smoke, lantern-light bleeding straight through his ribs. He hails you formally, correctly, as if a berth still exists to offer.","traits":{"note": "Formality is armor for him — he still keeps to the old customs of hailing and boarding, and breaking them visibly unsettles him.", "actions": [{"name": "Withering Handshake", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6+4) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Fog-Step", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "The Captain steps into the Ethereal Plane and back at will, walking between the decks of his own drowned ship and the living world."}, {"name": "The Face at the Wheel", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 13, each creature within 60 ft. that can see him. On a failure, a target is Frightened for 1 minute and ages 1d4 years from the horror of it; a creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Offered Berth (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "As Possession, but the Captain frames it as a formal offer of rank aboard his ship — the target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be possessed, its body pressed into a berth it never asked to fill."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lantern-light bleeds straight through his ribs when he turns just so."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes any officer's uniform he sees, expecting one salute back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads a boarding manifest that lists names decades out of date."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still corrects sailors' knots, translucent hands passing through the rope."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on proper introductions before any hostility, old habit, old manners."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely wants crew, not corpses, and will parlay if offered respect."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ship's outline is faintly visible around him, rigging superimposed on empty air."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The fog around him thickens into a full crew the instant he's truly threatened."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["hailing a living ship formally, correctly, for a berth that hasn't existed in decades"]},{"name":"Riptide Elemental","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"Living riptide dragging a wreck's leftovers under","flavor":"A standing current with a temper, summoned or born where a ship went down wrong; drags cargo and crew alike to the same grave.","desc":"The water doesn't rise so much as decide to stand — a column of churning current, debris and driftwood spinning inside it like a held breath. It doesn't roar. It just pulls, patient and total.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Current Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Whelm (Recharge 4-6)", "replaces": "Whelm (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature in the Elemental's space makes a DC 15 Strength save, taking 16 (3d10) Bludgeoning damage and being pulled into its space and Grappled (escape DC 14) on a failure; half damage and no grapple on a success. A Grappled creature is at risk of suffocating."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Spins with a keg of salvaged rum still trapped inside its current."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Formed where a specific wreck went down, tethered close to the debris field."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never roars, just pulls, a silence more unsettling than any threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags driftwood shaped almost like a mast, spinning it inside the column."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calms briefly when it isn't threatened, current slowing to a drift."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Releases whatever it's dragged under the instant it's actually damaged."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water inside it churns opposite the direction of the tide around it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Grows taller and faster with every ship's worth of wreckage it absorbs."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["standing as a column of churning current, debris spinning inside it like a held breath"]},{"name":"Deep-Baron of the Drowning Grounds","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"sahuagin-baron","model":"sahuagin-baron","summary":"Reef-ruling sea-devil warlord commanding raid packs","flavor":"Rules a reef of wrecks and the things that raid from them; ships that fish his water pay a toll in hulls.","desc":"It rises massive from the reef-shallows, crowned in barnacle and broken coral, a court of lesser sea-devils flanking it on every side. When it speaks the words come out as a demand for toll, not a greeting.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "commands nearby sahuagin, granting them advantage while it's conscious"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a captain's spyglass on a cord of woven kelp around its neck."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks first in demand of toll, only turning to violence when refused."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Court of sea-devils keeps a respectful distance, wary of its own ruler."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trident is fused with the ribs of an old figurehead, half weapon, half trophy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reef beneath it is arranged into a rough throne of wreckage and coral."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Honors a toll actually paid, letting the ship through without further threat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The barnacles crowning it pulse faintly in time with its own heartbeat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Calls every raider on the reef to answer at once when its own crown is threatened."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["rising crowned in barnacle and broken coral, court of lesser sea-devils flanking every side"]},{"name":"Plague-Hulk Zombie Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Fused mass of drowned dead still crewing the hulk","flavor":"A three-decker's worth of drowned dead fused by rot and current into one groaning, many-armed mass still trying to crew the ship.","desc":"Too many arms move at once from one bloated, fused mass of rotted flesh and torn uniform cloth. It still tries to crew the ship it died on — hauling ropes that lead nowhere, in a rhythm that used to mean something.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rotted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Fused Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Hull Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d12+3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Plague Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Hulk exhales a cloud of rot-thick vapor in a 30-ft. cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 21 (6d6) Poison damage on a failure or half as much on a success. A creature that fails also has the Poisoned condition for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uniform cloth still bears three different ships' insignia, fused into one mass."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps trying to coil a rope that isn't attached to anything anymore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells like a whole hold gone bad at once, a smell that clings to clothes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves with a lurch that's almost a marching rhythm, three decks' worth of drill."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "New arms keep budding from the mass mid-fight, more than it started with."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Freezes and tries to salute when a working ship's bell rings nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Faces embedded in the mass mouth silent orders no one living can follow."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sheds a chunk of itself that keeps crawling and fighting on its own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["hauling ropes that lead nowhere, too many arms moving at once in a rhythm that used to mean something"]},{"name":"Storm-Caller of the Drowned Choir","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"Voice-traded witch who calls storms on command","flavor":"Traded her voice to something under the swells for weather on command; the crew loves her and never quite meets her eyes.","desc":"She stands at the rail with her mouth working soundlessly, throat scarred where a voice used to be. The sky answers her anyway — clouds knotting overhead in a shape that has nothing to do with weather.","traits":{"note": "The crew adores her and fears her in equal measure — no one aboard will meet her eyes for long.", "actions": [{"name": "Voiceless Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Thunder damage as a silent shockwave rolls off her scarred throat."}, {"name": "Weather Traded for Silence", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "Spell Save DC 14. The Storm-Caller casts spells drawn from a storm-and-silence repertoire (Fog Cloud, Gust of Wind, Call Lightning, and similar effects, a limited number of times per day) entirely through gesture, never a word spoken."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throat scar is old and deliberate, a trade made once and never undone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signs orders to the crew in a hand-language only the oldest hands understand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls weather that always favors her own ship's heading, never coincidence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crew leaves her offerings at the rail, unasked, out of habit and fear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches from her own reflection in still water, avoiding it entirely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calms a storm as easily as she calls one, if the crew earns the mercy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The clouds she knots overhead spell shapes that dissolve before anyone can read them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The thing she traded her voice to answers directly when she's finally struck down."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["standing at the rail with her mouth working soundlessly while the sky knots into shape overhead"]},{"name":"The Admiral of Nowhere","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Undead fleet-admiral commanding a century-scuttled navy","flavor":"Commands a fleet that was scuttled a hundred years ago and never noticed; still promotes the drowned, still courts-martial the disloyal.","desc":"He stands on a quarterdeck a century gone to rot, epaulets tarnished black, and still gives orders to a fleet that sank around him without ever telling him it had. His eyes, when they finally fix on you, remember exactly how to court-martial the disloyal.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Muster the Drowned", "text": "Summons ghostly sailors from nearby wreckage to fight at his order."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tarnished epaulets still bear the rank he held the day the fleet went down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads a promotion list aloud to men who drowned a century ago."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes any living naval uniform, then attacks the moment the salute's returned wrong."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His quarterdeck creaks underfoot, though nothing solid is actually there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps immaculate manners even mid-slaughter, a gentleman about it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Genuinely doesn't know the fleet is gone, and reacts with real grief if told."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Ghost-lights of a hundred lost ships drift on the horizon whenever he speaks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Calls the entire drowned fleet to the surface the moment he's formally defeated."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["standing a rotted quarterdeck, still giving orders to a fleet that sank without ever telling him"]},{"name":"The Keelbreaker","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Many-headed sea-brute older than the shipping lanes","flavor":"Many-headed and older than the shipping lanes; every captain who's fought it and lived describes a different number of heads.","desc":"Heads rise from the swell one after another, more than any sailor can count twice the same way, scarred hides overlapping like a wall of muscle and bone. The water around it churns before it even attacks, like the sea itself is bracing.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Regrowing Heads", "text": "A severed head is replaced by two new ones unless the stump is seared."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hides overlap in scars from a dozen captains who swore they'd counted its heads."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head is noticeably younger, pale and unscarred, still growing in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Heads snap at each other over a kill before settling to share it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Older than the shipping lane itself, and the lane was charted around it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Water churns and boils before it even surfaces, a warning sailors learn to read."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreats the instant enough heads are downed at once, wary despite the numbers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A severed head keeps snapping at the water for a full minute after the cut."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Grows a new head faster than any crew has ever managed to remove one."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["rising head after head from the swell, water churning like the sea itself is bracing"]},{"name":"The Ghost Ship Herself","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"behir","model":"the-ghost-ship-herself","summary":"Self-sailing derelict crewed by its own drowned dead","flavor":"No living hand touches her wheel; she tacks into any wind, runs down any ship that spots her, and every soul she's ever taken still crews her rigging.","desc":"She comes on with sails shredded to lace, hull gone translucent as fogged glass, running against a wind that shouldn't be able to push her. Every plank groans with a voice, and every voice belongs to someone she's already taken.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Crewed by the Drowned", "text": "The ship fights back with ghostly crew manning cannon and rigging even with no living hand at the wheel."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sails are shredded to lace, yet somehow still catch every wind she chases."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every plank groans with a different drowned voice, layered like a choir."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Runs against the wind entirely, direction meaning nothing to her hull."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her wheel turns on its own, no hand ever seen gripping the spokes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves no wake at all, water closing behind her like she was never there."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Slows and circles a wreck of her own making, as if in mourning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A living sailor's name called out across her deck sometimes makes her hesitate."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every soul she's ever taken crews her rigging at once, and they've started shouting warnings."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["running down any ship that spots her, sails shredded to lace, hull gone translucent as fogged glass"]},{"name":"The Fathom-Crowned Leviathan","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"The keel-sunk horror sailors swear by and dread","flavor":"The keel-sunk horror every sailor's oath invokes without meaning it; wakes when a ship's debts to the sea itself finally come due.","desc":"The sea doesn't ripple before it surfaces — it lifts, an entire swell of water sliding off a back the size of a keel. Tentacles unfurl slow as sails, and somewhere below the mass of it, the debt finally comes due.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's escorting the party's ship, unhurried, deciding — sailors say that's a blessing until it isn't."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has swallowed something the party needs and shows no sign of hurry to give it back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A whole cult crews the party's rival ship expressly to feed it; they'll steer the party into its reach."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only where a specific drowned name is spoken; a party member just said it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It guards the one safe passage through the reef and charges toll in living cargo."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's dying, ancient, and the sea is going wrong around the wound; every storm for a season traces back to it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wrecks it keeps are arranged; from above they spell a warning in a language older than ships."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is the sea's own judgment on the ships that cross it, and it has judged this crossing; while it rises, no vessel on this water reaches port without its leave."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["rising under a ship slow enough that the crew has time to understand", "coiled around a reef of a hundred sunk keels, sorting the newest wrecks"]},{"name":"The Horizon's Own Reckoning","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"rlm-the-horizons-own-reckoning","summary":"Storm-fire captain who sailed past the edge of the charts","flavor":"The line where the horizon keeps its own counsel made flesh — a captain who sailed too far past the edge of the charts and came back wrong, wearing a crown of storm-fire and unpaid debts.","desc":"He stands at a burning wheel chained to his own wrists, storm-fire crowning a face no longer entirely human, drowned hands gripping the spokes alongside his. He sailed past where charts end, and came back as the edge itself.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Storm-Fire Wake", "text": "Leaves a trail of burning saltwater that ignites anything flammable it touches."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting a debt owed by the party's own captain, and the ship was named as collateral."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival crew has already tried to pay him off with the party's cargo, unasked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's burning through the last chart that shows a safe way home, page by page."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of the drowned hands on his wheel is still wearing a ring the party will recognize."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers safe passage past the edge for one name to be surrendered permanently."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's unraveling, storm-fire guttering; whatever he sailed past out there is catching up to him too."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every chart the party carries redraws itself faintly toward wherever he currently stands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He has closed the horizon around this crossing entirely; there is no direction left that isn't toward him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "planar"],"activity":["standing at a burning wheel chained to his own wrists, drowned hands gripping the spokes alongside his"]},{"name":"Salt-Cracked Deck Sweeper","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"Low-rank deckhand enforcer, no say in the voyage","flavor":"A ship's boy grown into a shipboard bruiser, all rope-burn hands and no say in where the vessel sails.","desc":"His knuckles are rope-scarred and his stance is all shoulders, built for shoving a smaller man out of the way rather than fighting fair. He doesn't ask where the ship's headed — he just enforces whatever the answer is.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Enforcer's Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) Piercing damage, or 5 (1d8+1) Piercing damage with two hands in melee."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knuckles are permanently rope-scarred, hands built for shoving, not finesse."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never asks the ship's heading, just enforces whatever answer comes down."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bulks his stance wide before every fight, more shove than strike."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a bruise-collection of old fights like a badge, never healed properly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps close to whoever outranks him, taking cues rather than giving them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Backs down fast the instant a real officer's voice cuts through the noise."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hums the same three notes under his breath before every single shove."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns feral the moment his own rank is threatened aboard, fighting past reason."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["shoving a smaller man out of the way, all shoulders, enforcing an order he never questions"]},{"name":"Powder Monkey Turned Cutthroat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"Former powder-boy now knife-quick and patience-thin","flavor":"Started the crossing hauling shot to the gun deck; ended it with a knife of his own and no patience left.","desc":"Small and quick, he moves low along the deck the way he used to move hauling shot to the guns, except now the thing in his hand is a knife and his patience for talk is gone entirely.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Quick Knife", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4+2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Shot-Sling", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still moves at the crouched, quick pace of a boy hauling powder under fire."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hands are scarred with old rope-burn from the gun-deck days."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks fast and clipped, out of a habit of shouting over cannon-fire."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a fistful of old shot in a pocket, worry-stones from another life."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at loud bangs even now, an old reflex the knife hasn't cured."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Freezes up entirely near an actual working cannon, old memory surfacing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Counts under his breath in the cadence of old powder-loading drills before he strikes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Goes for the throat first the instant he's cornered, patience gone entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["moving low along the deck the way he used to haul shot, knife out, patience for talk long gone"]},{"name":"Barnacle-Crusted Beachcomber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"Wreck-looting beachcomber, quick to rob the living","flavor":"Picks a wreck's bones clean before the tide can, and isn't shy about who else gets picked clean too.","desc":"Salt has cracked his skin into something like driftwood, and his pockets bulge with things pried off a wreck that isn't cold yet. He looks at you the same way he looks at cargo.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wreck-Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4+1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin has cracked into something like driftwood from years in the salt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pockets bulge with things pried off a wreck that isn't cold yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Looks at strangers the same flat way he looks at cargo, sizing value."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a mental map of every wreck within a day's walk, better than any chart."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Talks in trade prices even when no trade's on offer, out of habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Backs off entirely if the wreck's owner is standing right there, professional courtesy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Always seems to know a wreck's happened before the ship's even gone down."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns on whoever's actually strongest in a group the instant the goods look worth it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast"],"activity":["picking a wreck's bones clean before the tide can, pockets already bulging"]},{"name":"Marooned Castaway","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"desperate-bandit","model":"desperate-bandit","summary":"Island-marooned mutineer's scapegoat, come back wrong","flavor":"Left on a spit of sand to die for a mutiny that wasn't his; came back off the island wrong and hungry.","desc":"Sunburn has peeled to leather across every inch of exposed skin, and there's a hunger in the eyes that isn't just for food. He was left on a spit of sand to die quietly. He didn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Castaway's Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6+1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Scavenged Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sunburn has peeled to leather across every inch of exposed skin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still names the mutineer who marooned him, over and over, like a curse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hoards fresh water obsessively, even mid-fight, never lets a skin go far."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes track anything edible in a fight before they track any actual threat."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in a voice gone raw and cracked from years of shouting at empty horizon."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Begs for passage off the island the instant a ship actually offers it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refers to the island itself like it's a person he's still arguing with."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns feral entirely at the mention of the mutineer's name, fighting past all reason."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["peeling sunburned skin back from a stare that's hungry for more than food"]},{"name":"Gull-Picked Corpse Crab","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-crab","model":"giant-crab","summary":"Scavenging tideline crab drawn to the recently dead","flavor":"Scuttles the tideline in loose scavenging clusters, drawn to anything that used to breathe.","desc":"It scuttles sideways along the tideline in loose, restless clusters, claws clicking, drawn by a smell of rot that hasn't reached your nose yet. When it finds something that used to breathe, the whole cluster converges at once.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Scavenger Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shell is patched with barnacle and gull-down, scavenged like everything else about it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a tight cluster that scatters the instant a gull dives at it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a bit of shiny salvage clamped uselessly in one claw."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Converges on the freshest scent first, ignoring anything already picked over."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Digs into wet sand at the first sign of a bigger threat, hiding rather than fighting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Scatters entirely rather than fight if the cluster drops below a few members."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Clicks in unison, all claws at once, like a single creature wearing many shells."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A much bigger cluster boils up out of the sand the instant blood hits the tideline."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["coast"],"activity":["scuttling the tideline in a loose cluster, claws clicking toward a smell of rot"]},{"name":"Chain-Rattling Bilge Zombie","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Drowned bilge-worker who never noticed the sinking","flavor":"Drowned in the hold when the pumps failed and never noticed the ship went down around it.","desc":"It rises dripping from the hold, chain looped loose around one rotted ankle, eyes fixed on nothing in particular. It never noticed the ship went down around it, and it still doesn't seem to notice now.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't react to danger or pain, only to sound and nearby motion.", "actions": [{"name": "Waterlogged Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a rusted bilge-key on a cord, useless now, clutched anyway."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chain has snagged on a deck ring, and it hauls against it without noticing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt has crusted its eyes shut; it tracks by the creak of boards alone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in the same slow circuit the bilge pump used to walk, forever."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One lung still holds water and gurgles with every lurching step."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two more rise from the same hatch a moment later, chains tangling together."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It hums three notes of an old work-shanty between its teeth, over and over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The chain has rusted through at the ankle, and it keeps walking anyway, faster without the weight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["dragging one chain-wrapped ankle across a listing deck, chasing the last thing it heard move"]},{"name":"Wreck-Wood Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Reef-floor skeleton reassembled by tide-logic","flavor":"Picked clean by fish and reassembled by whatever tide-logic runs the ocean floor's oldest graveyards.","desc":"Bone stands up off the seafloor in the wrong order, reassembled by current and time into something that walks anyway. Barnacles cling to the ribs like they grew there on purpose.","traits":{"note": "It reassembles itself from whatever bone is nearest, so no two look quite the same.", "actions": [{"name": "Reef-Notched Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Current-Flung Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a crab shell lashed over the skull like a stolen helmet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm bone is driftwood, weathered smooth and slightly the wrong length."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails a length of kelp that never seems to detach no matter how it moves."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ribcage still holds a fist-sized clutch of fish eggs, undisturbed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing both hands; it fights by ramming its shoulder into its target."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Rises with two others from the same scattered wreck, bones half-shared between them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bones click in perfect time with the tide, never a beat off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When struck hard enough, it doesn't fall — it simply reassembles a step further off."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "ruins"],"activity":["stalking the reef floor in the wrong rhythm, barnacles clicking against loose ribs with every step"]},{"name":"Grog-Mad Deckhand","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"tough","summary":"Becalmed sailor gone rum-mad and swinging","flavor":"Three weeks becalmed and a cracked rum cask turned an ordinary sailor into a swinging liability.","desc":"His eyes are bloodshot rings and his breath could strip paint, three weeks of dead calm and cracked rum boiled down into one swinging fist. He doesn't aim so much as flail in your general direction.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wild Mace Swing", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Panicked Crossbow Shot", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps yelling orders from a captain who died two ships ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings wide and open, more threat to the rigging than to anyone standing near."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weeps between swings, apologizing to no one in particular."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has lashed an empty rum cask to his belt like a trophy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights barefoot, having lost both boots overboard days ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two more deckhands stagger up from below, caught in the same rum-madness."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears the becalmed sea is whispering the ship's true name back at him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Snaps fully sober mid-fight, horrified, and doesn't stop swinging anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "urban"],"activity":["swinging a mace at shadows on the gunwale, breath sour with three weeks of cracked rum"]},{"name":"Coral-Fanged Moray Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-piranhas","model":"swarm-of-piranhas","summary":"Territorial eel-knot nesting inside a breached hull","flavor":"A boiling knot of eels nesting in a hull-breach, territorial past all reason.","desc":"A hull-breach seethes with motion — dozens of eel-bodies knotted together, fangs bared, territorial past any reason a fish should have. The knot uncoils toward anything that gets too close to the gap.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Knotting Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. while grappling a creature. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 3 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its Hit Points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests specifically around a cracked crate of salted meat wedged in the breach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters into the dark the instant a light is raised, then closes back in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One larger eel leads, the rest following its exact wake through the water."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Territorial to the breach's exact edge, not an inch further out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knot unravels into individual eels the moment it takes real damage."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second knot answers the first's thrashing from a breach two decks down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The knot briefly holds a shape — almost a face — before dissolving back to eels."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Blood in the water doubles its aggression instantly, and the knot won't disperse until it does."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["boiling out of a hull-breach in a knotted mass, fangs already bared at the nearest warmth"]},{"name":"Flying-Fish Strafer Flock","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-ravens","model":"swarm-of-ravens","summary":"Oversized gliding fish-flock that shreds exposed skin","flavor":"An unnaturally large school that glides clean over the gunwale and shreds an exposed hand or face.","desc":"Silver bodies break the surface all at once, gliding low and fast over the gunwale in a shimmering, buzzing line. Each pass leaves a shallow slice across whatever skin was exposed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Slashing Beaks", "replaces": "Beaks", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. while grappling a creature. Hit: 5 (2d4) Slashing damage, or 3 (1d4) Slashing damage if the flock has half its Hit Points or fewer."}, {"name": "Wing-Roar Cacophony", "replaces": "Cacophony (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Every creature within 20 ft. of the flock must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or have Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn, deafened by shrieking wings and snapping fins."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breaks the surface all at once, as if on some signal only fish can hear."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows a ship for miles before ever making its first pass."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves the deck slick with scales and thin bright cuts after every strafe."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Veers hard away from open flame, never crossing a lit lantern's glow."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles back for a second pass only if the first drew blood."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, larger school joins mid-strafe, doubling the shimmering line."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whole flock banks in a shape that briefly resembles a hull from below."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A storm-front arrives with them, and the flock strafes harder the closer the wind gets."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "sky"],"activity":["gliding low over the gunwale in a silver line, shredding whatever skin is left exposed"]},{"name":"Bilge-Bloated Corpse Floater","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie-plague-carrier","model":"zombie-plague-carrier","summary":"Bloated floating corpse that only moves when approached","flavor":"Bobs face-down until something living gets close, then it isn't face-down anymore.","desc":"It bobs face-down in the swell, bloated and still, exactly the way a corpse should look — until something living gets close enough, and it isn't face-down anymore.","traits":{"note": "It looks and floats exactly like an ordinary corpse until something living approaches.", "actions": [{"name": "Bloated Grasp", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or contract a festering wound that deals 2 (1d4) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns until treated."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a name-stitched collar from a crew no one on board recognizes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts with the current instead of against it, patient about the approach."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gulls avoid it entirely, circling wide of the bloated shape."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hand trails below the surface, fingers twitching in a slow, deliberate rhythm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells wrong before it looks wrong, which is usually the first warning anyone gets."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second floater trails a few yards behind the first, equally still, equally patient."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It never fully sinks even when killed again, bobbing back up hours later."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Bursts open on a solid hit, and something small and hungry swims free of it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["bobbing face-down in the swell, patient as driftwood, until something living drifts too close"]},{"name":"Rope-and-Rum Buccaneer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"Fair-weather buccaneer who renegotiates loyalty mid-fight","flavor":"Signed the articles for the split, not the cause, and will renegotiate both mid-boarding.","desc":"He's grinning before the first blow lands, already talking terms, cutlass loose in a hand that's clearly done this dozens of times and switched sides at least twice. Loyalty here has a price and it changes mid-fight.","traits":{"note": "He'll switch sides mid-fight if the offer on the table gets better than the one he signed for.", "actions": [{"name": "Cutlass Feint", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Enthralling Panache", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "The Buccaneer targets one creature within 30 ft. that can see and hear him. The target must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or be Charmed until the end of the Buccaneer's next turn, momentarily convinced his offer is the better one."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Names his price out loud mid-swing, like the fight is just haggling with steel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a torn page of the ship's articles tucked in his sash, referenced constantly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights left-handed to keep his good hand free for a handshake."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has already switched sides once tonight and seems ready to do it again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears three rings, each a trophy from a different crew he abandoned."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second buccaneer nearby watches him closely, clearly waiting to see which way he breaks."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Insists, between blows, that he's technically still loyal to a captain no one else remembers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops his cutlass mid-fight and offers the winning side his sword arm on the spot."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "urban"],"activity":["already grinning terms mid-cutlass-swing, testing which side of the fight still pays better"]},{"name":"Tide-Warped Sahuagin Scout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sea-devil scout that tests hulls before the pod attacks","flavor":"Runs ahead of the raiding pod to test a hull's weak seams before the pack commits.","desc":"It hugs the waterline, only eyes and the ridge of a fin breaking the surface, testing the hull's seams with a webbed claw before the rest of the pod ever shows itself.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Seam-Testing Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the instant it's spotted, reporting back before ever risking a fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks a weak seam with a scratch only its own pod can read."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces only enough to breathe, most of its body kept below the waterline."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles a ship three full times before choosing a spot to test."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no weapon, relying entirely on claws and patience."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second scout surfaces nearby, testing the opposite side of the hull in tandem."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its scratch-marks glow faintly under moonlight, visible only from below the surface."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finds the weak seam and stops testing — the pod is already closing in from deep water."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["hugging the waterline with only eyes and a fin-ridge showing, testing a hull's seams with one webbed claw"]},{"name":"Driftwood Effigy Watcher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Wreck-spar effigy that patrols the reef it was built to ward","flavor":"Lashed together from wreck-spars by superstitious crews to ward the reef; wards it by walking the tideline itself now.","desc":"Lashed spars and salvaged rope have been bound into a rough humanoid shape, warding-sigils carved crooked into the wood. It doesn't move like something that should move — until it takes its next slow, patrolling step.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spar-Lashed Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Ward-Carved Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The Watcher targets one creature it can see within 30 ft. The target must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or be Frightened of it until the end of the Watcher's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its sigils were carved by a crew that's since scattered across three different ports."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols the exact same stretch of tideline, turning back at an invisible line."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rope-lashings creak audibly seconds before it moves, the only warning it gives."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm is a broken oar, splintered to a point at the end."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops moving entirely if the reef it wards goes quiet and undisturbed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A fresh offering has been left at its feet, still damp, not yet claimed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its crooked sigils rearrange themselves slightly overnight, never in daylight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The reef it wards has started dying, and the Watcher's patrols have turned frantic."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "ruins"],"activity":["standing rigid at the tideline, warding-sigils crooked in its wood, until its next slow patrolling step"]},{"name":"Reef-Crawling Giant Crab","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-crab","model":"giant-crab","summary":"Wreck-territorial crab that clamps and never releases","flavor":"Territorial over a wreck's cargo hold, clamps and doesn't let go until something breaks.","desc":"One claw is scarred and oversized from years of clamping onto cargo that fought back. It doesn't let go once it bites — the only way to end it is to make something break first.","traits":{"note": "Once it clamps onto something, it doesn't release until it or the target breaks.", "actions": [{"name": "Vice Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) if it's Large or smaller."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scarred claw is twice the size of the other, evidence of years of cargo that fought back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wedges itself into a cargo hatch so tightly it has to be pried loose to be moved at all."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shell crusted thick with someone else's old ship's paint, flaking at the edges."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Guards a single crate obsessively, ignoring everything else in the hold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sidesteps constantly, keeping its good claw between itself and any threat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, smaller crab shares the same hold, territorial toward the first instead of intruders."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crate it guards ticks faintly, and the crab seems to guard it harder because of that."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its claw finally snaps off mid-fight, and it keeps attacking with the jagged stump anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["guarding a cracked cargo hold with one oversized claw, clamped and refusing to let go of old spoils"]},{"name":"Fogbound Lookout Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Dead lookout still calling sightings to a vanished crew","flavor":"Still stands the watch it died at, calling sightings to a crew that scattered a century ago.","desc":"It stands at a crow's-nest post that rotted away a century ago, calling out sightings in a thin, carrying voice to a crew that scattered long before you were born. It doesn't seem to know no one's listening.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sighting Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's Hit Point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a Long Rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls out headings that would have mattered a hundred years ago, useless now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fog thickens wherever it lingers, thinning the moment it moves on."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice carries clearer than any living lookout's ever could."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same three sightings on an endless loop, none of them current."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't react to being spoken to, only to being approached."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its calls briefly sync with real hazards nearby, an accidental warning worth heeding."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The name it calls out belongs to someone currently aboard, word for word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Falls suddenly silent mid-call, and something it was warning about arrives right after."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["calling sightings from a crow's-nest that rotted away a century ago, to a crew long since scattered"]},{"name":"Anchor-Chain Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Chain-tangled ghoul dragging fathoms of rusted iron","flavor":"Went down tangled in the anchor chain and rose still wrapped in it, dragging fathoms of rusted iron.","desc":"It drags fathoms of rusted chain across the deck, wrapped tight around a torso gone the color of drowned meat, claws already curling toward exposed skin. The chain never seems to slow it down.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chain-Tangled Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d3 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rusted Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d3 + 2) Slashing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chain-links have rusted into its wrists, indistinguishable now from bone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags the chain loud enough to be heard three decks away before it arrives."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trips over its own slack chain constantly, without ever seeming to notice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still has an anchor fluke lodged through one shoulder, unremoved."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves faster in water than it does on deck, chain and all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second ghoul rises tangled in the same length of chain, forced to move together."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The chain occasionally goes taut on its own, as if something below is still pulling."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wraps its chain around a target's leg and starts hauling toward open water."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["dragging fathoms of rusted anchor chain across a listing deck, claws already curling toward exposed skin"]},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Tentacle Horror","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk","model":"fish-folk","summary":"Small deep-thing juvenile that boards and strikes throats","flavor":"A juvenile deep-thing washed inshore, small enough to board but old enough to know exactly where the throat is.","desc":"Small enough to board unnoticed, it slips over the rail with a wet, boneless economy of motion, tentacle-mouth already oriented toward the nearest throat with unnerving precision.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Precise Spear Thrust", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sticky Net", "replaces": "Sticky Net (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 15/30 ft. Hit: The target is Restrained by clinging, mucus-slick netting until it or another creature takes an action to succeed on a DC 11 Strength check to tear it free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small enough to squeeze through a hatch built for a child, unnoticed until too late."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint slime trail across the deck, easy to track after the fact."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Targets the nearest throat with unnerving precision, ignoring easier openings."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin shifts color faintly to match whatever it's pressed against."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats overboard the instant it takes a solid hit, unwilling to fight fair."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, smaller juvenile trails behind it, mimicking its every move."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its tentacle-mouth briefly forms words in a language no one aboard recognizes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something much larger surfaces nearby the moment this one draws blood."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["slipping over the rail with a wet, boneless economy of motion, tentacle-mouth already aimed at a throat"]},{"name":"Sea-Devil Net-Thrower","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sahuagin netter that drags swimmers under first","flavor":"Drags swimmers under with weighted netting before the rest of the raid ever surfaces.","desc":"A weighted net spins out from webbed claws before it even fully breaches, tangling around ankles and dragging feet out from under anyone standing too near the rail.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Weighted Net Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Strength save or be knocked Prone by tangling net-cord."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throws the net before surfacing fully, sight unseen, trusting the sound of footsteps."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nets are weighted with scavenged shot, heavier than they look."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags a tangled victim toward the rail the instant the net lands true."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries three spare nets looped across its shoulder, ready to throw again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits below the waterline, patient, until a foot dangles close enough to the rail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second netter surfaces on the opposite side, catching anyone who dodges the first throw."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its nets are woven from something that isn't quite rope, faintly warm to the touch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Lands the net and immediately begins dragging the tangled target straight under."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["spinning a weighted net from webbed claws before it's even fully breached the surface"]},{"name":"Salvage-Diver Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"Drowned salvager-ghoul that won't surface without its box","flavor":"Died prying a strongbox from a sunken hold and still won't surface without it.","desc":"It clutches a rusted strongbox to its ribs even as it claws its way up the hull, refusing to surface without it, eyes fixed and hungry despite everything else about it being long dead.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Icy Bite", "replaces": "Icy Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d3 + 2) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Box-Guarding Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d3 + 2) Slashing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't release the strongbox even one-handed, fighting entirely with its off claw."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strongbox lock is rusted shut, the contents unknown even to the thing carrying it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves faster underwater than on deck, box and all, unwilling to be parted from it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the remains of a diving harness, still cinched absurdly tight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats toward the wreck it came from rather than press an attack."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second ghoul trails it, eyeing the strongbox with clear, hungry intent."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The box hums faintly whenever the ghoul draws near a particular stretch of hull."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops the box only when it's finally destroyed, and the lock springs open on its own."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["clawing its way up a hull with a rusted strongbox clutched to its ribs, refusing to surface without it"]},{"name":"Hardtack Cannibal Crewman","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Lifeboat survivor turned desperate, quiet cannibal","flavor":"What's left of a lifeboat crew that ran out of hardtack long before they ran out of each other.","desc":"His cheeks are hollow and his eyes track you the way a starving man tracks the last biscuit. He doesn't announce what happened in the lifeboat. He just doesn't need to explain the knife.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, and the Crewman gains 3 (1d6) Temporary Hit Points if this attack reduces the target to 0 Hit Points."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of names scratched into the sickle's handle, never explained."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hollow-cheeked and silent, he answers questions only with the knife."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches at the word hardtack, more than at any threat of violence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hoards salt in his pockets, obsessively, long after it stopped being useful."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights with methodical calm, none of the panic you'd expect from him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One more survivor from the same lifeboat lingers nearby, unwilling to stop him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He mutters names between strikes, none matching anyone currently on board."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turns on his own companion mid-fight the instant blood is drawn nearby."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["tracking a stranger's every movement the way a starving man tracks the last biscuit"]},{"name":"Shrieking Storm Petrel Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"Storm-heralding bird swarm that screeches the ship's name","flavor":"Precedes every gale that matters, screaming the ship's name back at the crew before the wind does.","desc":"A dark cloud of birds wheels overhead, screeching something that sounds unsettlingly close to the ship's own name, right before the wind picks up and confirms it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Storm-Herald Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. while grappling a creature. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 3 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its Hit Points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Precedes every gale that matters, arriving hours before the wind picks up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Screeches something unsettlingly close to the ship's own name, over and over."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wheels tighter and lower the closer the coming storm actually is."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scatters the instant lightning flashes, regrouping seconds later, undeterred."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to land, circling endlessly until the storm finally breaks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, larger flock joins from windward, doubling the screeching cloud."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The name it screeches changes slightly each pass, closer to accurate each time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Falls dead silent all at once, and the storm arrives in the same breath."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "sky"],"activity":["wheeling overhead in a dark cloud, screeching something close to the ship's own name into the wind"]},{"name":"Barrel-Bomb Mutineer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Mutineer wielding a lit powder keg as leverage","flavor":"Carries a lit powder keg into a boarding fight like it's a threat and a bargaining chip both.","desc":"He carries a lit powder keg cradled against one hip like it's a baby, fuse hissing shorter by the second, grinning like the threat and the bargain are the exact same thing.","traits":{"note": "His powder keg is both a weapon and leverage — killing him outright risks setting it off.", "actions": [{"name": "Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Light Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Lit Keg Threat", "text": "The Mutineer holds his keg's fuse toward a nearby flame. Until the start of his next turn, any creature that reduces him to 0 Hit Points with a weapon attack causes the keg to detonate, dealing 7 (2d6) Fire damage to everything within 10 ft. (DC 12 Dexterity save for half)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grins wider every time someone eyes the fuse instead of his blade."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the keg cradled like an infant, one hand never leaving it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Negotiates surrender terms with the keg as his only real argument."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fuse is shorter than he's letting on, and he seems to know it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Backs toward the powder stores instead of the exits, daring pursuit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second mutineer covers his flank, clearly rehearsed for exactly this standoff."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fuse hisses at a rhythm that doesn't match how much of it remains."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drops the keg deliberately once cornered, daring everyone nearby to move fast enough."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["cradling a lit powder keg against one hip like a threat and a bargaining chip both, fuse hissing shorter"]},{"name":"Wreck-Grown Rust Louse Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"rust-monster","model":"rust-monster","summary":"Hull-nesting vermin that rusts weapons to flakes","flavor":"Nests in derelict hulls and strips a boarding party's cutlasses to orange flakes before the fight even starts.","desc":"A rippling carpet of small, hard-shelled vermin pours out from a hull-breach, and everywhere it crawls, metal blooms rust and flakes to orange dust in seconds.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Corroding Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage. If the target is wearing nonmagical metal armor or wielding a nonmagical metal weapon, that item takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to any bonus it provides, to a minimum of no bonus."}, {"name": "Rusting Antennae", "replaces": "Antennae", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: One nonmagical metal object the target is wearing or carrying takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to any bonus it provides, to a minimum of no bonus, if the antennae can reach it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in the same rusted hull it hatched from, never straying far from the breach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Strips a dropped cutlass to orange flakes in seconds, faster than any blade should rust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Avoids wood and rope entirely, drawn only to metal and the smell of iron."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a fine orange dust across everything it's crawled over, easy to track."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats en masse the instant its breach is threatened with fire."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second carpet pours from an adjoining breach, converging on the same target."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rust it leaves behind briefly forms patterns, almost like old ship's markings."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Swarms a single weapon en masse, stripping it bare in a single frenzied pass."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast", "ruins"],"activity":["pouring out of a hull-breach in a rippling carpet, blooming every blade nearby to orange rust"]},{"name":"Doldrums-Drunk Deserter","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"Starvation-mad deserter, dangerous to would-be rescuers","flavor":"Jumped ship in the doldrums rather than starve slow, and regrets it in a way that makes him dangerous to rescuers.","desc":"His ribs show through a torn shirt, and his eyes have the flat, glassy focus of someone who jumped ship rather than starve. He doesn't recognize rescue when it's offered — only threat.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Desperate Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't recognize offered rescue, only threat, and swings first every time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ribs show clearly through a torn shirt, days from starving outright."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the same regret between swings, never finishing the sentence."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights harder the moment fresh water is offered, distrusting the kindness."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries no gear beyond the axe, having abandoned everything else overboard."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A raft's worth of wreckage floats nearby, the rest of his crew nowhere in sight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swings the axe in time with a heartbeat that isn't his own, too slow, too steady."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Collapses mid-swing from exhaustion, and keeps crawling toward the fight anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swinging a greataxe with the flat, glassy focus of a man who jumped ship rather than starve slow"]},{"name":"Barnacle Golem","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"rlm-barnacle-golem","summary":"Reef-grown armor golem woken by a scuttled hull","flavor":"Salvaged armor left lashed to a scuttled hull long enough for the reef to grow through the rivets and wake it up.","desc":"Salvaged armor plate creaks upright, crusted floor to helm in barnacle and dripping weed, joints grinding with the grit of a reef grown through every rivet. It moves like something that forgot it used to be worn by a man.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Barnacle-Crusted Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Slashing damage from the crusted shell."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves like something that forgot it used to be worn by a man."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weed drips from every joint, leaving a wet trail behind each footstep."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its visor slit still holds an eye-shaped stain, long since empty."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barnacles bloom thicker on the side that faced the seafloor longest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rusts audibly with every swing, shedding flakes of old plate."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second suit nearby stirs in sympathy the moment the first one wakes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Faint scratching sounds come from inside the plate, though nothing living remains there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cracks open at the joints under enough damage, and something small skitters free."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["grinding upright off a scuttled hull, crusted floor to helm in barnacle, joints grating with reef-grit"]},{"name":"Sea-Devil Priest's Acolyte","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Junior sea-devil chanter half a beat behind the priest","flavor":"Chants the drowning-litany half a beat behind the priest, close enough to matter.","desc":"It chants half a beat behind someone else's cadence, clumsy but earnest, eyes darting sideways for approval it clearly hasn't earned yet.","traits":{"note": "It fights clumsily, always half a beat behind whoever it's trying to impress.", "actions": [{"name": "Uneven Spectral Jaws", "replaces": "Spectral Jaws", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Cold damage from a lash of spectral, drowning jaws."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Acolyte casts a minor ritual spell, fumbling the cadence — the DM selects an effect appropriate to a junior sea-devil chanter, no more than CR 2 in scale."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stumbles over the same syllable every single time, never correcting it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Watches the priest's hands more than the fight in front of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears fewer fetishes than the others, clearly still earning its place."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches visibly whenever its chant falls out of time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights with clumsy enthusiasm, overcommitting to every strike."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The priest it serves is close by, and it fights twice as hard while being watched."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its stumbled syllable briefly makes the water nearby ripple wrong."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally lands the chant in perfect time, and immediately looks terrified of what answered."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["chanting the drowning-litany half a beat behind the priest, eyes darting sideways for approval"]},{"name":"Debt-Marked Purser","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"Ship's purser running two ledgers, one true and one lie","flavor":"Keeps the true ledger of who owes the captain what, and the false one for the crew.","desc":"Two ledgers sit in two different pockets, and the way he shifts his weight when you get too close to either one tells you which is the lie.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ledger-Sharp Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Warning-Shot Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one ledger in a locked drawer and the other in plain sight, both incomplete."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Negotiates even mid-fight, offering to erase a debt in exchange for a truce."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights defensively, more concerned with protecting the ledgers than himself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites exact figures from memory, down to the last owed coin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a spare quill even into a boarding fight, out of pure habit."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The captain he answers to is close enough to overhear every word he says."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One ledger lists names of crew who died years before this voyage began."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Burns the true ledger rather than let it be seized, mid-fight, without hesitation."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "urban"],"activity":["shifting his weight toward whichever ledger-pocket he doesn't want you looking at"]},{"name":"Reef-Devil Trapper","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"Sea-devil that lures hulls onto reefs with false lanterns","flavor":"Lures hulls onto shoal-teeth with false lantern-signals, then finishes what the reef starts.","desc":"It crouches at the reef's edge holding a lantern rigged to swing like a ship's true signal, patient as the tide, waiting for a hull to take the bait it's offering.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ambush Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage, plus 3 (1d6) Slashing damage if the target hasn't acted yet this combat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings the false lantern in the exact rhythm of a real harbor signal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits crouched at the reef's edge for hours without shifting position."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Abandons the lantern the instant a hull actually takes the bait."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps two more lanterns hidden nearby in case the first is spotted."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Finishes what the reef starts, picking off anyone thrown clear of a wreck."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second trapper works the opposite shoal, timing signals to seem like one safe channel."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The false lantern burns with a light no ordinary oil produces."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A real ship has already taken the bait, and it's running hard for the rocks tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swinging a false lantern-signal at the reef's edge, patient as the tide, waiting for a hull to take the bait"]},{"name":"Hollow-Eyed Lantern Ghost","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Drowned signalman's ghost-light, warning and luring both","flavor":"A drowned signalman's light, still swinging the warning nobody heeded, luring the unwary same as it once tried to save them.","desc":"A pale light swings low over the water on its own, no hand holding it, the shape of a drowned signalman visible only when the glow catches him at the wrong angle. It still swings the old warning — it just doesn't mean it as a warning anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Lantern Shock", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Lightning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The drowned signalman's shape is visible only when the glow catches him wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swings in the exact pattern of an old warning signal, faithfully, uselessly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts toward whichever ship seems least prepared for what's coming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Light dims to near nothing whenever it's directly approached."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint chill in the air long after it's moved on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The rocks it once warned sailors away from are close by, right where the light is leading."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one instant, its swinging pattern spells out a name in the old signal-code."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The light flares white-hot the moment a ship finally takes its bearing from it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swinging low over the water on its own, still calling the warning nobody heeded, luring same as it once tried to save"]},{"name":"Rope-Trick Rigging Spider","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"giant-spider","model":"giant-spider","summary":"Rigging-nesting spider that snares sail-climbers with silk","flavor":"Nests high in a ghost ship's rigging, dropping silk lines to snare anyone who climbs to reef the sails.","desc":"It hangs upside-down high in the rigging, legs longer than a man is tall, silk already spooling loose toward anyone climbing to reef a sail.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Long-Legged Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or take 4 (1d8) Poison damage and have Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Rigging Web", "replaces": "Web (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/60 ft. Hit: The target is Restrained by silk webbing until it or another creature takes an action to succeed on a DC 12 Strength check to break free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nests in rigging so high the crew rarely looks up far enough to notice it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Silk lines already trail loose from the yards, waiting for a climber."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops suddenly and silently, legs longer than a man is tall."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wraps prey in silk before feeding, methodical and unhurried about it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats upward the instant it takes real damage, hard to follow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second spider shares the same rigging, working opposite masts in tandem."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its silk lines form patterns in the rigging that resemble old signal-flags."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cuts its own web free deliberately, dropping a bound victim straight to the deck below."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "ruins"],"activity":["hanging upside-down high in ghost-ship rigging, silk already spooling toward anyone climbing to reef a sail"]},{"name":"Rock-Skulking Bilge Ooze","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Ooze","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"Bilgewater ooze that corrodes hull-plate and boot leather alike","flavor":"Grew fat in a scuttled hold's standing bilgewater, corroding hull-plate and boot leather with equal patience.","desc":"A gray, formless mass seeps along the bilge boards, dissolving rivets and boot-leather with the same patient hiss, leaving a corroded sheen wherever it's passed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Corroding Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Acid damage, and nonmagical armor worn by the target takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to the AC it offers, to a minimum of 10 + its Dexterity modifier."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grew fat in a scuttled hold's standing bilgewater, patient about every meal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a corroded sheen on everything it's passed over, easy to track after the fact."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Seeps through gaps too small for anything with a proper shape."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dissolves rope and leather as readily as metal, indifferent to material."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves slower than a walking pace, relying entirely on patience and darkness."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second smaller ooze has split off nearby, both hungry for the same standing water."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It briefly holds the shape of whatever it last dissolved before losing form again."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Splits cleanly in two the instant it takes a solid hit, doubling the threat in the bilge."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["seeping along bilge boards, dissolving rivets and boot-leather alike with the same patient hiss"]},{"name":"Quartermaster's Shakedown Man","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"Articles-enforcer who finds loopholes when it profits him","flavor":"Enforces the Articles to the letter when it profits him and finds loopholes when it doesn't.","desc":"He recites the Articles from memory, word for word, and somehow the words always land in his favor. When they don't, he finds a clause that does.","traits":{"note": "He always finds a loophole in the Articles when the letter of the law doesn't favor him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Shakedown Man makes two attacks, using his Scimitar or Pistol in any combination."}, {"name": "Articles-Enforcing Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Loophole Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30/90 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a battered copy of the Articles, annotated in his own cramped hand."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites a clause mid-fight to justify whatever he's about to do next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running tally of debts owed to him by half the crew."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights precisely, never a wasted motion, like every swing is already accounted for."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers a settlement mid-combat, genuinely willing to end it for the right price."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two loyal enforcers flank him, ready to make his interpretation of the Articles stick."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His copy of the Articles seems to have clauses no official printing carries."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Declares a debt forfeit mid-fight and turns the full weight of the crew against one target."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "urban"],"activity":["reciting the Articles from memory, word for word, somehow landing every clause in his own favor"]},{"name":"Coral Golem Guardian","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"animated-armor","model":"rlm-coral-golem-guardian","summary":"Patient coral colossus guarding a sunken treasure gallery","flavor":"Grown by something patient to guard a sunken treasure gallery, indifferent to the centuries it's taken.","desc":"A colossus of jagged reef-coral rises from the sea floor, shaped roughly like a boarding pike, cleaner-fish darting in and out of its joints. It has clearly guarded this gallery for longer than any living captain has been alive.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already mid-patrol past the gallery entrance the party needs to reach."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival salvage crew is baiting it toward the party's own approach route."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only wakes fully when treasure is actually lifted, giving one clean window first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cleaner-fish scatter from its joints in a pattern that marks the gallery's safest path."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something inside the gallery is already broken open, and the Guardian is furious about it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A crack runs the length of its coral hide — something is trying to get out of it, not in."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It kneels briefly at a specific spot on the sea floor, as if paying respects, before resuming its patrol."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whatever it guards has just been disturbed for the first time in a century, and it knows exactly who did it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["rising from the sea floor shaped roughly like a boarding pike, cleaner-fish darting through its joints"]},{"name":"Storm-Wracked Harpy Matriarch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"Wreck-nesting harpy matriarch that sings ships to their ruin","flavor":"Nests her brood on a wreck-reef and sings ships onto the rocks to feed them.","desc":"She perches above a brood nested into a wreck's broken ribs, feathers matted with salt-spray, and when she sings the melody is unmistakably beautiful — right up until the rocks make sense of it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ruinous Lure Song", "text": "Nearby creatures who fail a save move toward the harpy's chosen hazard on their turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her brood is starving, and she's grown bolder about luring ships onto her reef."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local port has put a bounty on her, and the party's ship is the bait vessel."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of her chicks has wandered into a wreck the party is already exploring."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's singing a captured sailor's own shanty back at his shipmates to lure them ashore."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival matriarch has challenged her nest, and she's desperate for an easy kill first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her nest sits atop a wreck holding cargo the party's employer specifically wants recovered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her song this time carries words, faint but clear, in the voice of someone the party lost at sea."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's already sung a real ship onto the rocks tonight, and its crew is still in the water."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast", "sky"],"activity":["perched above a brood nested in a wreck's broken ribs, singing a melody that turns to ruin on the rocks"]},{"name":"Bone-Naga of the Drowned Vault","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-naga","model":"bone-naga","summary":"Ancient bone-naga coiled around a sunken vault's treasure","flavor":"Coiled around a sunken hold's strongbox for two hundred years, patient past any living captain's greed.","desc":"It coils around a strongbox two centuries old, bone gone the color of old ivory, patient in a way nothing that still needs to breathe could ever manage.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves the vault it guards — pull it more than a short distance from the strongbox and it turns sluggish, its patience finally running out.", "actions": [{"name": "Bone Coil", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d10+2) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) by ivory-yellow coils if it isn't already grappled by the Naga."}, {"name": "Vault-Deep Gaze", "replaces": "Serpentine Gaze", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Naga fixes a creature it can see within 30 ft. with hollow sockets that hold two centuries of dark. The target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, backing away from the vault rather than toward it."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Naga casts a spell, drawing on the same slow patience that has kept it coiled here for generations."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its coils have worn a smooth groove into the strongbox's iron banding over the years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A diver's knife is still lodged between two of its ribs, ignored, decades old."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It uncoils only far enough to strike, then reforms the same loop exactly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Silt sifts off its spine in a slow cloud with every small movement it makes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It watches the vault door more than it watches the intruder swimming toward it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The strongbox lid has cracked an inch, and something inside is ticking, slow and regular."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow on the vault floor moves half a second behind its actual body."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The coins in the strongbox have started shifting on their own, like something under them is waking."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["coiling tighter around a two-century-old strongbox at the first scrape of a diver's blade", "testing the water for a heartbeat with a slow, patient sweep of its skull"]},{"name":"Fen-Tide Merrow Raider","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"merrow","summary":"Skiff-overturning merrow raider, plunder is an afterthought","flavor":"Overturns skiffs for the sport of it before it ever gets around to the plunder.","desc":"It surges up from beneath a capsized skiff, all muscle and green-gray hide, overturning what's left just for the sport of hearing sailors hit the water.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Capsizing Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Barnacle Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rusted Harpoon", "replaces": "Harpoon", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature standing in shallow water, it is knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a stolen captain's hat, waterlogged and sitting crooked on its head."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slaps the water twice before every strike, like it's setting a rhythm only it can hear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its harpoon line is braided from three different ships' rigging."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running tally of overturned skiffs scratched into its own hide."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs, wet and booming, every time a sailor hits the water."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's herding the skiff toward a reef line on purpose, laughing louder the closer they get."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It flips boats it has no interest in robbing, purely for the sport, and never once loots the wreck."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's called two more of its kind up from beneath with a whistle that doesn't sound aquatic at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["flipping a skiff end over end just to hear the crew hit the water before it bothers with plunder", "surfacing behind a rowboat's wake, grinning, in no hurry at all"]},{"name":"Wreck-Diver Doppelganger","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Shape-stealing killer that answers to its last victim's name","flavor":"Wears the face of whichever sailor it drowned last, and answers to that name at the next port.","desc":"It wears a drowned sailor's face perfectly — down to the scar, down to the way he used to stand — and it answers to that dead man's name without a flicker of hesitation.","traits":{"note": "It keeps the mannerisms of whoever it's currently wearing — the name, the limp, the drinking habits — until it decides to drown someone new.", "actions": [{"name": "Drowned Man's Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Doppelganger magically reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 60 ft., learning enough to wear its next face convincingly."}, {"name": "Borrowed Face (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Doppelganger's true, waterlogged shape flickers into view for an instant. Each creature within 30 ft. that can see it must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's spending a dead sailor's back pay at the bar, and the real widow is three tables over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already been signed onto the party's next crewing contract under a drowned man's name."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dockside creditor is demanding the debt it inherited along with the face it's wearing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wearing the face of someone the party actually knew, and knows their old passwords."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's selling wreck-salvage that belongs, by rights, to the man whose name it stole."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The real man's family has hired the party to find him, unaware he's already dead and worn."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's begun forgetting which face is the borrowed one and answers to both names at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its current disguise is a party member's missing shipmate, and it knows things only he could know."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast", "urban"],"activity":["answering to a drowned sailor's name at the tavern bar without a flicker of hesitation", "picking through a wreck's cargo hold wearing a dead diver's face and his exact gait"]},{"name":"Rigging-Runner Assassin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"Above-boarding assassin who drops garrote-first onto helmsmen","flavor":"Boards from above, garrote-first, dropping from the mainmast onto whoever's steering.","desc":"It drops from the mainmast in total silence, garrote already looped, aimed at whoever's hands are on the wheel before anyone below even hears the creak of the line it used to descend.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cutlass Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d8+2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Silent Garrote", "replaces": "Strangle (Garrote)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6 against a Medium or smaller creature Grappled by the Assassin. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) damage, and the target can't speak or make sound until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Rigging Drop", "text": "Once per turn, if the Assassin descends from at least 20 feet above a target before attacking, it has advantage on its first attack roll against that creature this turn, and the target can't react to the fall."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bare feet are calloused from a lifetime spent barefoot in the rigging."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears three garrotes coiled at its belt, each a different length of stolen line."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks each contract with a notch cut into the mainmast it dropped from."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never speaks above a whisper, even when there's no one left alive to hear it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves the coin it was paid tucked into the dead helmsman's collar, every time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already up in the rigging, contract fulfilled halfway, waiting on a second name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It moves through the rigging without the ship's motion ever seeming to touch its balance."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Someone paid to have the party's helmsman killed, and it's already circling the mast."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "urban"],"activity":["coiling a garrote in total silence forty feet up in the rigging, patient as a spider", "counting hands on the wheel below and picking the one it means to stop"]},{"name":"Brine-Cursed Werebear Bosun","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werebear","model":"rlm-brine-cursed-werebear-bosun","summary":"Cursed bosun who becomes a bear-thing under full moon","flavor":"Cursed by a witch-doctor for flogging the wrong sailor, and now the whole crew fears the full moon more than the storms.","desc":"His bosun's coat is still buttoned tight over a frame that's grown too large and too furred for it, salt-matted and hulking, a curse laid on him for flogging the wrong sailor finally coming due.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "reverts to human form when reduced below half HP or at will"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His bosun's coat has been let out at the seams three times and still won't close."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a length of chain coiled by his bunk for the nights the moon is full."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crew mutter the witch-doctor's name behind his back, never to his face."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He still barks orders in perfect bosun's cadence, even mid-transformation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt has crusted permanently into the fur along his forearms."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tonight's moon is full, and he's already asked to be locked below before it rises."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He remembers every flogging he's given in bear-form, in perfect, guilty detail."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The lock on the hold has already been forced, from the inside, and the moon isn't even up yet."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["straining the buttons of a bosun's coat that no longer fits a body gone huge and furred", "watching the moon rise over the water with dread plain on what's left of his human face"]},{"name":"Powder-Keg Berserker Boarder","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker-commander","model":"berserker-commander","summary":"First-wave boarding-axe berserker screaming a death-oath","flavor":"Leads the first wave over the gunwale swinging a boarding axe and screaming the crew's death-oath.","desc":"He comes over the gunwale first in the boarding wave, boarding axe already swinging, screaming an oath the whole crew swore together and only he still means.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Boarding Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d12+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Oath-Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4+4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Death-Oath Fury", "text": "While above half its hit points remain unspent on this rage, the Boarder deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage with melee weapon attacks, screaming the crew's oath with every swing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its boarding axe still has the last ship's paint chipped into the blade."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's first over the gunwale every single time, no exceptions, no hesitation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The death-oath it screams is the same seven words every crew member swore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rope burns scar both its palms from a hundred boarding lines."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps fighting past wounds that should have dropped it twice over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The rest of the crew who swore the oath are all dead — it's the only one left still meaning it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It doesn't seem to register pain until well after the fight, all at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's lit the fuse on a powder keg it's carrying, and it isn't planning to throw it far."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["screaming a death-oath the whole crew swore together, swinging first over the gunwale", "kicking a smoking powder keg loose across the deck before anyone can stop rolling it"]},{"name":"Fogbank Siren's Herald","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"sea-hag","summary":"Fog-wreathed hag singing harmony to lure ships ashore","flavor":"Sings the low harmony under the Siren's melody, close enough inshore that the fog never quite lifts.","desc":"She sings the low harmony underneath a stronger voice somewhere off in the mist, close enough inshore that the fog never quite lifts around her.","traits":{"note": "She never sings the melody herself — the harmony alone is enough to keep the fog from lifting and ships drifting inshore.", "actions": [{"name": "Barnacled Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Herald's Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Death Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the Herald's true face must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 13 (3d8) Psychic damage and be Paralyzed until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half damage and no paralysis on a success."}, {"name": "Illusory Appearance", "text": "The Herald magically disguises herself as a beautiful passenger or drowning survivor, an illusion that holds until she attacks or a creature touches her."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her harmony is always half a beat behind the melody, close enough to unsettle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The fog around her never lifts more than an arm's length in any direction."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wears a drowned passenger's cloak, still damp, still fashionable a decade out of date."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hums even between verses, unwilling to let the silence show her true voice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Driftwood and old buoys ring her perch, arranged like an audience."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's rehearsing a new harmony meant for a ship that isn't in these waters yet, but will be soon."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her reflection in the water hums a third part that isn't coming from her mouth at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The melody she harmonizes under has started getting closer, and clearer, and worse."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["humming a low harmony under a stronger voice somewhere out in the fogbank", "combing wet hair with a broken oar-blade, patient as the mist she keeps thick"]},{"name":"Sunken Chapel Revenant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Drowned chaplain still preaching from a sunken pulpit","flavor":"A ship's chaplain who kept preaching as the water rose past the pulpit, and hasn't stopped since.","desc":"He stands at a pulpit half-submerged, robes waterlogged and translucent, still delivering a sermon that started rising with the tide and never stopped.","traits":{"note": "It cannot leave its sunken chapel — its sermon, and its rage, are bound entirely to the pulpit and the water around it.", "actions": [{"name": "Sermon's Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Necrotic damage, and the Revenant regains hit points equal to half the damage dealt. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack rises at the start of its next turn as a waterlogged zombie under the Revenant's command."}, {"name": "Rusted Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Command the Drowned (1/Day)", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Revenant calls its sunken congregation. Up to three undead within 120 ft. of the chapel gain a bonus action to move toward and attack the nearest living creature."}, {"name": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the Revenant's face must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His waterlogged robes have gone translucent, the pulpit's wood visible through them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He turns pages that dissolved to pulp a century ago, reciting from memory alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sermon is the same seven verses, looped, never once completing the eighth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small fish nest in the folds of his robe, undisturbed by his sermon."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He raises a hand in blessing at exactly the same interval, whether anyone's present or not."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The chapel bell above has started ringing on its own, keeping his sermon's rhythm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Air bubbles rise from his mouth in the shape of words no one below the surface should hear."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's reached the eighth verse for the first time in two hundred years, and the water is rising to meet it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["delivering a sermon from a half-submerged pulpit that started rising with the tide and never stopped", "turning waterlogged pages that have long since dissolved to pulp, reading anyway"]},{"name":"Drowned Choir Cantor","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"Storm-hymn cantor who calls weather nobody sane wants","flavor":"Leads the storm-hymn from the quarterdeck, calling weather nobody sane would ask for twice.","desc":"She raises both hands at the quarterdeck rail, leading a hymn in a language that sounds liturgical and wrong at the same time, and clouds start answering before she's finished the first verse.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Choir's Arcane Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8+2) Thunder damage as a sung chord cracks outward across the water."}, {"name": "Storm-Hymn Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Cantor casts a spell, her hymn calling weather that answers before she finishes the first verse."}, {"name": "Call the Squall", "text": "The Cantor raises a sudden localized squall in a 20-ft. radius centered on a point within 60 ft. Each creature there must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone by the wind and driving rain; the area is Heavily Obscured until the start of her next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hymn book has swollen shut with salt water and she sings it from memory now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She raises both hands identically each verse, like a conductor keeping her own time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every sailor near the quarterdeck goes quiet the moment she starts the second verse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her voice carries clean over a gale that should be swallowing every other sound."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She keeps perfect pitch even as the deck pitches under her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's mid-hymn for weather that's already three verses stronger than she intended."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The clouds she calls answer half a beat before she actually sings the line."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's begun the final verse of the storm-hymn, and nobody's ever heard her finish it before."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["leading a storm-hymn from the quarterdeck rail in a tongue that sounds liturgical and wrong", "counting the clouds answering her call, one verse ahead of the weather"]},{"name":"Iron-Hulled Corsair Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"pirate-captain","summary":"Three-ship corsair captain, sinker of every bounty-navy sent","flavor":"Runs a fleet of three under false flags, and has personally sunk every navy sent to collect the bounty.","desc":"He stands at the wheel of a ship flying colors that change port to port, three more hulls visible on the horizon behind him, utterly unbothered by the navy flag flying on yours.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His coat pockets are stuffed with bounty flyers bearing his own likeness, mostly unflattering."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He changes his ship's colors before every port, and never repeats a flag twice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His rapier hilt is notched once for every navy captain who's tried and failed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He greets rival crews by name, cheerfully, moments before robbing them blind."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His fleet keeps station a half-mile back, patient, always in easy signal range."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's just taken on a fourth ship's worth of crew and has nowhere yet to put them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know the exact bounty on his head down to the coin, and finds it funny."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His three ships have just spotted each other's signal flares — something bigger than a bounty hunt is closing in."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["standing at the wheel under colors that change port to port, three more hulls on the horizon behind him", "counting bounty flyers bearing his own face and pricing which one insults him least"]},{"name":"Reef Titan Anemone","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Anemone colony that mimics drowning victims to lure rescuers","flavor":"A hull-sized anemone colony that's learned the shape of a drowning man and mimics it to draw rescuers in.","desc":"A hull-sized bloom of tendrils sways gently in the current, and somewhere in the mass a shape resolves — arms reaching up, a drowning man's silhouette — right before the tendrils close around whoever swam in to help.","traits":{"note": "It only mimics distress when prey is near — otherwise it holds perfectly still, indistinguishable from a natural coral formation.", "actions": [{"name": "Reef Maw", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10+4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grasping Tendril", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15) if it is a Medium or smaller creature."}, {"name": "Mass Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft., one Grappled target. Hit: 18 (3d8+5) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The drowning shape it mimics always has the same tilt of the head, over and over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bloom is studded with the buttons and buckles of everything it's swallowed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds its mimicked shape even after the tendrils start closing in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small reef fish nest unharmed in the folds nearest its actual maw."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sways in the current exactly like coral until the very last second."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's mimicking a shape someone in the party will actually recognize by name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The silhouette it forms occasionally mouths words no sound comes out of."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's learned to mimic two drowning shapes at once, splitting rescuers' attention perfectly."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["swaying a hull-sized bloom of tendrils gently in the current, patient as the reef itself", "resolving a drowning man's silhouette from its own mass to draw the next rescuer in"]},{"name":"Gale-Bound Air Elemental Squallwright","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"air-elemental","model":"air-elemental","summary":"Bottled storm-elemental shaken loose in the worst weather","flavor":"Bound into a captain's storm-bottle generations back, and finally shaken loose in the worst possible weather.","desc":"Wind gathers into a visible, spinning shape torn loose of whatever bottle held it for generations, howling loud enough to drown out the storm it arrived inside of.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Thunderous Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) Thunder damage."}, {"name": "Bottle's Rage Whirlwind (Recharge 4-6)", "replaces": "Whirlwind (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. Each creature within 15 ft. of the Squallwright must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or take 16 (3d10) Thunder damage and be flung 20 ft. away and knocked Prone; half damage and no forced movement on a success."}, {"name": "Generations of Fury", "text": "When the Squallwright is reduced to half its hit points or fewer, it lets out the whole of its bottled fury at once: its next Bottle's Rage Whirlwind requires no recharge roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shards of the storm-bottle still spin somewhere inside its visible form."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It howls the exact pitch of the storm it was bottled during, generations back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Debris caught in its spin never seems to actually strike anything nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps circling back to where its old bottle first shattered, uselessly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shape flickers thin whenever it tries to slow down."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The rest of the bottle is still intact somewhere nearby, and something in the elemental wants it back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally speaks in the bottling captain's exact voice, without meaning to."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's found a second, unbroken storm-bottle, and it's trying to force something else inside it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "sky"],"activity":["howling loose of the storm-bottle that held it for generations, drowning out the weather it arrived inside", "spinning debris into a visible column just to remember what shape it used to be free in"]},{"name":"Drowned Duelist Wraith","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Duel-drowned officer's ghost, still gripping his rapier","flavor":"Lost the duel over prize-shares and went over the rail still holding his rapier; he's kept the grip.","desc":"It still grips a rapier in a translucent hand, blade held in perfect dueling form, the grudge over a prize-share never once loosening its fingers even after death.","traits":{"note": "It only fully manifests to duel one opponent at a time — while its chosen foe lives, it ignores all others in the fight.", "actions": [{"name": "Grudge Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6+3) Necrotic damage, and the target's maximum hit points are reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Create Specter", "text": "The Wraith can create a specter from a Humanoid it has slain within the last hour, a lesser echo of the duel it lost, bound to obey the Wraith's commands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It executes the exact same opening parry every single duel, out of decades-old habit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rapier passes through solid rail but never through its grudge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bows formally before attacking, an old dueling courtesy it's never abandoned."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The prize-share ledger it died arguing over is still tucked, transparent, into its coat."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It refuses to strike anyone who hasn't drawn a blade first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's mistaken a party member's weapon-draw for a formal challenge, and now considers the duel sworn."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its footwork traces the exact deck-plan of a ship that sank a hundred years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's recognized an old dueling scar on someone present, and the grudge has a new name attached."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "urban"],"activity":["holding a translucent rapier in perfect dueling form, grudge over a prize-share never loosening its grip", "circling an old dueling ground it can no longer leave, waiting for a worthy opponent"]},{"name":"Sahuagin War-Priestess","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"Tide-timing sea-devil priestess who calls the surge to war","flavor":"Calls the tide itself into a raid, timing the assault to a surge no surface captain can predict.","desc":"She raises a webbed hand toward the moon, timing an assault to a tidal surge no surface captain could ever predict, chanting the raid into motion syllable by syllable.","traits":{"note": "Her raids are always timed to the tide's turn — she will delay a fight, if she can, until the surge favors her pack.", "actions": [{"name": "Tide-Timed Jaws", "replaces": "Spectral Jaws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Surge Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The War-Priestess casts a spell, calling on the pull of the tide itself to shape the raid."}, {"name": "Call the Surge", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The War-Priestess calls the tide forward early. Each creature of her choice within 30 ft. of the water gains a swim speed equal to its walking speed until the end of her next turn, and the water level in the area rises sharply, flooding low ground."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She marks tide charts into her own scales with a sharpened claw."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her raiding pack won't move until she lowers her hand from the moon."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She chants in a call-and-response the rest of her pack answers in unison."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's never once launched a raid on a falling tide, calling it bad luck."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her webbed hands leave a faint phosphorescent trail when she gestures."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The tide she's timing this raid to is unusually large, and she seems thrilled rather than cautious."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She can name, apparently from memory, the exact tide on the night of her own birth."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's just felt the surge arrive early, ahead of her own chant, and doesn't know why."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["raising a webbed hand to the moon, timing a raid to a tidal surge no surface captain could predict", "chanting the assault into motion syllable by syllable as the water starts to pull"]},{"name":"Boarding-Pike Skeleton Crew","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Disciplined drowned skeleton unit, still holds formation","flavor":"A drilled, disciplined unit of the drowned that still holds formation better than most living marines.","desc":"Ranks of bone hold formation with a discipline that outlasts most living marines, pikes leveled in unison, advancing in lockstep across rotted planking.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Drilled Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8+2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Formation Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6+2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is pushed 5 ft. away if it is a Medium or smaller creature."}, {"name": "Hold the Line", "text": "While at least two other Boarding-Pike Skeleton Crew are within 5 ft. of it, this skeleton has advantage on saving throws against being frightened or moved against its will."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rank shifts a precise half-step whenever the officer's bones rattle a new command."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pike is notched with the same three enemy marks as the rest of the unit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kelp is braided through its ribs like a uniform sash it never removed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reforms broken ranks within a single beat, as if the drill never stopped."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It salutes before it falls, out of pure drilled reflex."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The unit is drilling for a boarding action against a ship that hasn't arrived yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its commands come from an officer's skull no one can locate among the ranks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The formation has just executed a maneuver none of them were ever drilled to know."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["holding formation with a discipline that outlasts most living marines, pikes leveled in unison", "advancing in lockstep across rotted planking, bone rattling to the same drilled cadence"]},{"name":"Waterlogged Chimeric Hulk-Beast","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Three drowned sailors fused into one furious hulk","flavor":"Three drowned crewmen fused by whatever curse sank the ship, now sharing one waterlogged, furious body.","desc":"Three drowned crewmen have fused into one bloated, furious body, too many limbs thrashing in a rhythm that doesn't match itself, water sloughing off with every lurch forward.","traits":{"note": "Each of its three fused heads occasionally fights the others for control — expect its attacks to sometimes miss allies of convenience by accident.", "actions": [{"name": "Waterlogged Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Fused Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Hull Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is knocked Prone if it is a Large or smaller creature."}, {"name": "Bilge Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Hulk-Beast vomits a torrent of black bilgewater in a 15-ft. cone. Each creature in the area must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 18 (4d8) Poison damage and have disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn, retching; half damage and no penalty on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three distinct voices argue inside its throat every time it roars."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each of its heads wears the remnant of a different crewman's cap."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its too-many limbs occasionally trip each other mid-lunge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sloughs seawater constantly, leaving a wide dark trail behind it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its fused faces still looks almost peacefully asleep."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of the three fused crewmen is fighting to surface, screaming a warning through the beast's own mouth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally salutes an officer none of the party can see, out of pure muscle memory."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A fourth voice has started answering from inside it, one that was never one of the original crew."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["thrashing too many limbs in a rhythm that doesn't match itself, water sloughing off with every lurch", "grinding three drowned crewmen's voices together into one furious, waterlogged roar"]},{"name":"Deep-Baron's Shark-Bonded Enforcer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"sahuagin-baron","model":"sahuagin-baron","summary":"Sea-devil baron who rides a bonded shark into every raid","flavor":"Rides a bonded reef shark into every raid and has never once had to swim himself.","desc":"It rides a bonded reef shark straight over the reef line, one clawed hand fisted in a dorsal fin, and it's never once had to swim on its own.","traits":{"note": "It never fights separated from its bonded shark for long — expect the two to reunite mid-combat if split.", "actions": [{"name": "Enforcer's Trident", "replaces": "Trident", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10+5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Shark's Charge", "text": "Once per turn when the Enforcer's bonded shark moves at least 15 ft. straight toward a target before the Enforcer attacks it, that attack deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shark bears old harpoon scars it seems almost proud of."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's never once had to swim on its own, and clearly can't stand the idea of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It signals the shark with a series of clicks made deep in its own throat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its trident is lashed with the same cord that binds it to the shark's fin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rides low and close, using the shark's bulk as a shield in the water."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The shark is agitated, circling wider than usual, like it senses something bigger nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The bond between rider and shark seems to run both directions — the shark reacts to the Baron's moods first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The shark has just broken from its usual pattern entirely, hunting on its own initiative."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["riding a bonded reef shark straight over the reef line, fist twisted in its dorsal fin", "circling a wreck slow and unhurried, letting the shark do the hunting for now"]},{"name":"Hurricane-Voiced Storm Herald","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"Unseen wind-scout that finds a ship's weakest rigging first","flavor":"An unseen wind-thing that rides ahead of a hurricane, testing a ship's rigging for the weak point the storm will use.","desc":"Nothing is visible except the wind bending in a shape that shouldn't be possible, testing the rigging line by line for the weak point a hurricane will use an hour later.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wind Swipe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Scouting Vortex", "replaces": "Vortex", "text": "The Herald forms itself into a vortex, becoming Invisible and gaining a flying speed of 90 ft. It can move through other creatures' spaces and theirs through its own, but takes 5 (1d10) Bludgeoning damage if it ends its turn inside an object."}, {"name": "Weak Point Found", "text": "The Herald marks a piece of rigging, hull, or structure it has touched this turn. The first creature to attack that marked point before the start of the Herald's next turn does so with advantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tests every line on a ship in the exact same order, methodical, unhurried."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loose canvas snaps taut and slack in its wake even though nothing visible moved it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a faint whistle behind wherever it's passed, fading slow."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems to specifically favor testing whichever mast looks newest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gulls scatter from a ship's deck moments before it arrives, sensing it first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already found the weak point, and the hurricane behind it is less than an hour out."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to be scouting for something specific, not just any structural flaw."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's marked a point on the hull that isn't structural at all — it's marked a person."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "sea"],"activity":["bending the wind into a shape that shouldn't be possible, testing rigging line by line", "finding the weak point a hurricane will use an hour later, invisible, unhurried"]},{"name":"Cursed Doubloon Wight-Captain","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Gold-cursed wight-captain who conscripts anyone who takes a coin","flavor":"Cursed by the very gold he stole to guard it forever, raising every sailor who touches a coin as his crew.","desc":"Gold coin is stitched into his coat like scale-mail, and his eyes track anyone who so much as glances at a doubloon on the deck. Touch one and you belong to his crew now.","traits":{"note": "any creature that picks up a cursed coin must save or become dominated"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A doubloon from his coat has already ended up in a party member's pocket, unnoticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local merchant is unknowingly circulating a handful of his cursed coins as change."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering an absurd sum for one specific coin someone in the party already spent."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crew of his conscripted dead is closing on the tavern where the party spent his gold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the coin back more than he wants revenge, and will bargain, briefly, for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of the coins already spent has started weighing heavier in whoever's carrying it now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The gold sewn into his coat rearranges itself into a name whenever someone new touches it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just realized exactly who spent his coin, and he's already coming to collect them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["tracking anyone who glances at a loose doubloon on deck with eyes that never blink", "stitching another coin into a coat already scaled thick with gold he stole and can't put down"]},{"name":"Foundered Frigate's Ghast Bosun","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Foundered frigate's undead disciplinarian, punishment unending","flavor":"Still runs the flogging line on a foundered frigate's ghost-deck, and the punishment never actually ends.","desc":"It paces a flogging line on a ghost-deck that never quite finished sinking, whip-scarred hand raised, still administering a punishment that never technically ends.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Flogging Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (3d6+2) Piercing damage. A non-undead creature hit by this attack must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or be Paralyzed for 1 minute; the target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Disciplinarian's Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4+4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It counts lashes aloud in a dead language none of the current crew ever learned."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform is still recognizably a bosun's coat, rotted to lace."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces the exact same flogging line, to the inch, every circuit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seems personally offended by anyone standing out of formation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its whip has rotted to a rope of kelp but it swings it exactly the same."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The ghost-deck it paces is slowly, finally, actually finishing its sinking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally addresses a crewman by name who isn't present, and hasn't been in decades."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided someone in the party is due a flogging, and it means to collect."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["pacing a flogging line on a ghost-deck that never finished sinking, whip-scarred hand raised", "administering a punishment that never technically ends to a crew that stopped existing decades ago"]},{"name":"Kraken-Spawn Broodguard","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Half-grown deep-thing guarding a brood-nest, already boat-sized","flavor":"Half-grown but already big enough to take a longboat down whole, guarding the nest for whatever birthed it.","desc":"Half-grown and already the length of a longboat, it coils protectively around a nest none of you can see clearly, tentacles testing the water for anything that gets too close.","traits":{"note": "It fights defensively, never straying far from the nest — draw it away and its aggression noticeably drops.", "actions": [{"name": "Brood Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8+5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Guardian Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10+5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Nest Tentacles", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8+5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16) if it is a Large or smaller creature."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It positions its bulk between intruders and the nest before doing anything else."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tentacles are still soft at the tips, not yet grown to full strength."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It clicks and chirps toward the nest between attacks, a reassurance no one else can parse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half-formed eggs are visible pulsing faintly beneath its coiled bulk."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It retreats toward the nest rather than pursue anyone who flees."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of the eggs in the nest has already begun to crack, early, agitated by the fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to sense something enormous approaching from far deeper water, and keeps glancing that way."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "What birthed it has surfaced nearby, drawn by the noise, and it isn't half-grown at all."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands"],"activity":["coiling protectively around a nest none of the intruders can see clearly", "testing the water with a tentacle sweep for anything that gets too close to the brood"]},{"name":"Drowned Fleet Admiral's Ghost","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Ghost admiral commanding an invisible spectral squadron","flavor":"Still commands a spectral squadron that only he can see, and still expects every ship on the horizon to salute.","desc":"He salutes an empty horizon crisply, expecting every passing ship to answer in kind, commanding a spectral squadron that's visible only to him.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Phantom Broadside", "text": "Calls an invisible spectral ship to fire a ghostly volley at a chosen target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He returns every salute given to him, formally, mid-combat, without breaking stride."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He narrates orders to ships that were sunk alongside him, still expecting compliance."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His uniform is immaculate despite two centuries underwater."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He addresses every living captain he meets by a rank they haven't earned yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He seems personally wounded when a ship fails to dip its colors to him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's convinced a real, living fleet is under his command now, and he's issuing orders to it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally the water itself seems to move in formation around him, briefly, like ghost hulls turning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just declared a live vessel nearby to be part of his squadron, and expects it to obey."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["saluting an empty horizon crisply, expecting every passing ship to answer in kind", "commanding a spectral squadron that's visible only to him, precise and utterly convinced"]},{"name":"Reef-Cracker Hydra","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Cave-denned hydra scarred by three failed charting attempts","flavor":"Denned in a sea-cave that's swallowed three ships trying to chart it, each head a different scar from the attempts.","desc":"It fills the mouth of a sea-cave that's swallowed three charting expeditions whole, each of its many heads scarred differently by whatever those failed attempts managed to land.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Regrowing Heads", "text": "A severed head is replaced by two new ones unless the stump is seared."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head still trails a snapped charting-line hooked through its jaw."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its heads react to sound before sight, tracking oar-splashes from well outside the cave."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A different head bears a burn scar, a rope scar, and a harpoon scar respectively."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wreckage from three failed expeditions litters the cave floor beneath it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rarely leaves the cave mouth, content to let ships come to it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One head still has a chart-scrap stuck between its teeth, legible, valuable to whoever retrieves it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its heads seem to argue among themselves in low hisses before choosing a target."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A head that should have been dead for years has just opened its eyes again, mid-fight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "cave"],"activity":["filling the mouth of a sea-cave that's swallowed three charting expeditions whole", "turning several scarred heads at once toward the echo of a new approaching hull"]},{"name":"Boarding-Fiend Bone Devil","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"bone-devil","model":"bone-devil","summary":"Contracted boarding-fiend, payment terms deliberately vague","flavor":"Contracted by a desperate captain for one impossible raid, and never bothered reading the fine print about payment.","desc":"It clatters over the rail on a barbed tail, contract-bound and clearly annoyed about the terms, sizing up the crew like collateral it never got paid for.","traits":{"note": "It fights under contract, not conviction — bound to complete the raid, but bitter and litigious about every clause it thinks was unfair.", "actions": [{"name": "Contract Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Infernal Sting", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) Piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Collect on the Fine Print", "text": "Once per turn, when the Bone Devil reduces a creature to 0 hit points, it may immediately seize one unattended item that creature is carrying as payment owed, muttering about interest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recites contract clauses aloud, aggrieved, between attacks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a running tally of unpaid wages scratched into its own barbed tail."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It refuses to attack anyone it considers outside the contract's stated scope."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses mid-fight to note, out loud, every technicality being violated against it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's brought a literal copy of the contract, singed at the corners, tucked at its side."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The captain who summoned it is already dead, and it's decided the crew now owes the debt collectively."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to genuinely believe it's the wronged party in this arrangement."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just found a loophole in the contract that frees it to attack indiscriminately, and it's delighted."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "planar"],"activity":["clattering over the rail on a barbed tail, contract-bound and clearly annoyed about the terms", "sizing up the crew like collateral it never got paid for, tallying debts aloud"]},{"name":"Storm-Bound Efreeti Corsair","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"rlm-storm-bound-efreeti-corsair","summary":"Figurehead-bound fire-genie granting speed for an unpaid price","flavor":"Bound into a corsair ship's figurehead by a desperate deal, and grants the crew impossible speed for an unpaid price.","desc":"Fire wreathes a genie bound into the ship's own figurehead, steam hissing where flame meets sea-spray, granting the hull a speed no honest ship should manage.","traits":{"note": "the bound ship gains a speed bonus while the efreeti remains fused to the figurehead"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The captain who struck the deal never told the crew what price is still owed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's willing to grant the party's ship the same speed, for the same unpaid kind of price."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival crew wants the figurehead itself, deal and all, torn from the hull."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's begun asking passengers, one by one, if any of them can finally pay what's owed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ship it powers is faster than anything chasing it, and its captain knows it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The unpaid price is coming due today, and the Efreeti has started demanding it from whoever's aboard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Steam rises off it in shapes that look, for half a second, like a contract's unread clauses."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided the debt transfers to whoever's currently steering, and the wheel just changed hands."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "elemental"],"activity":["wreathed in fire bound into the ship's own figurehead, steam hissing where flame meets sea-spray", "granting the hull a speed no honest ship should manage, for a price still unpaid"]},{"name":"Undertow Terror of the Shoals","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"remorhaz","model":"remorhaz","summary":"Shoal-burrowing terror that swallows hulls whole from beneath","flavor":"Burrows through sandbars and shoal-mud the way its cousins burrow through snow, swallowing hulls whole from below.","desc":"Sand and shoal-mud churn and collapse without warning, a hull-sized shape moving beneath the surface the way its cousins move through snow, right before something takes the ship's keel from below.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only long enough to strike, then vanishes back beneath the shoal instantly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its burrow-trenches are visible from a ship's deck minutes before it actually strikes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sand hisses and boils oddly wherever it's passed recently underneath."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors shallower shoals where ships are more likely to run aground first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barnacles and old hull-wood are lodged permanently in its scarred hide."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's already circling beneath the party's current vessel, testing the keel before striking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The shoal above it occasionally shifts into shapes that resemble old wreck outlines."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's surfaced fully for the first time in years, driven up by something worse still below."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["churning sand and shoal-mud without warning, a hull-sized shape moving beneath the surface", "taking a ship's keel from below before anyone above even registers the collapse"]},{"name":"Pale Fathom Wight-Lord","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Generational wreck-revenant that drags its whole crew back up","flavor":"Rises from a specific wreck-site once a generation, always dragging the whole doomed crew back up with him.","desc":"It rises once a generation from a specific wreck-site, gargantuan and pale as drowned coral, dragging an entire doomed crew back up behind it in a chain of bloated, silent bodies.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "rises with a retinue of lesser wight sailors"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "This is the generation it's due to rise, and locals have already started avoiding the wreck-site."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member's ancestor is rumored to be somewhere in the chain of bodies it drags."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A salvage crew is diving the wreck-site tonight, unaware of the timing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local charter is offering a fortune to anyone who'll confirm the wreck-site before the rising."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone has proof the rising is a generation early this time, and no one believes them yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's risen already, ahead of schedule, and the wreck-site is closer to the harbor than anyone accounted for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The chain it drags is longer this generation than any prior rising on record."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "One of the chained bodies it dragged up is still, somehow, breathing."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["rising once a generation from a specific wreck-site, gargantuan and pale as drowned coral", "dragging an entire doomed crew back up in a chain of bloated, silent bodies"]},{"name":"Coral Throne Basilisk-Queen","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Reef-throne guardian that petrifies looters of a drowned crown","flavor":"Coils a sunken palace's reef-throne, petrifying anything that tries to loot the drowned crown beside her.","desc":"She coils across a sunken palace's reef-throne, scaled hide crusted with coral growth, gaze fixed and patient beside a drowned crown that nothing has managed to steal.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Statues of past looters ring her throne, arranged like an honor guard."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coral has grown so thick over her scales that only her eyes still gleam clearly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She never leaves the reef-throne, content to let intruders come to her."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The drowned crown beside her has never once been touched by her own claws."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She moves with unhurried patience, as if certain nothing can outlast her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of her petrified statues is cracking slightly, as if the stone inside is beginning to remember it was flesh."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crown beside her hums faintly whenever her gaze turns toward it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's just lifted the crown herself for the first time in centuries, and the throne room is answering."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["coiling across a sunken palace's reef-throne, hide crusted thick with coral growth", "fixing a patient, petrifying gaze beside a drowned crown that nothing has managed to steal"]},{"name":"Death-Knight of the Broken Articles","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Blood-oathed undead enforcer of pirate-code violations","flavor":"Signed the Articles in his own blood and died enforcing every clause; still hunts crews who break the code.","desc":"Blood-signed pages are sewn into his pauldron, armor black with rust and salt, and he hunts crews who break the code he died enforcing with the same cold discipline he had in life.","traits":{"note": "He will not attack anyone who hasn't broken the Articles — but once a violation is confirmed, he pursues without rest until it's answered.", "actions": [{"name": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10+4) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Spell Attack: +7, range 120 ft. Hit: 22 (4d10) Fire damage, and the ground in a 10-ft. radius of the target ignites, dealing 5 (1d10) Fire damage to any creature that enters or starts its turn there until the end of the encounter."}, {"name": "Articles Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Death-Knight casts a spell, drawing on the same cold discipline with which he enforces the code he died for."}, {"name": "Verdict of the Broken Clause", "text": "Once per turn, against a creature the Death-Knight has witnessed break the Articles this encounter (theft from a shipmate, abandoning a crewman, mutiny), his weapon attacks deal an extra 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A party member unknowingly broke a clause of the Articles last session, and he's noticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crew hired the party to intercept him before he reaches their captain, who broke the code."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's offering safe passage to anyone who helps him find a specific mutineer."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The Articles he enforces are a real, still-circulating pirate contract someone in the party has signed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guilty captain has put a bounty on his own crew, hoping to be rid of the Death-Knight's attention."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's found the actual, physical Articles someone broke, and he's carrying the evidence with him now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The blood-signed pages on his pauldron occasionally shift to reveal a new name added since the last sighting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just decided the party themselves signed something they don't remember signing, and considers the debt due now."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "urban"],"activity":["hunting a crew that broke the code he died enforcing, cold and utterly disciplined", "reading blood-signed pages sewn into his own pauldron, silent, before drawing his blade"]},{"name":"Sunken Archmage of the Drowned Spire","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"archmage","summary":"Two-centuries-drowned archmage still mid-spell in his tower","flavor":"Went down with his tower-ship still casting, and hasn't noticed two centuries pass underwater.","desc":"He still stands mid-gesture in a drowned tower, robes drifting weightless around him, a spell frozen half-cast two centuries after the water should have stopped him.","traits":{"note": "His spell has never finished casting — anything that finally completes it, even by accident, may unleash two centuries of built-up arcane pressure at once.", "actions": [{"name": "Drowned Arcane Burst", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 150 ft. Hit: 18 (4d8) Force damage."}, {"name": "Spire Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Archmage casts a spell, power built up over two centuries lending it unusual intensity."}, {"name": "The Unfinished Casting", "text": "Once per encounter, when reduced to half its hit points or fewer, the Archmage's frozen spell finally completes: each creature within 20 ft. of him must succeed on a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw or take 27 (6d8) Force damage and be pushed 15 ft. away; half damage and no push on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hands are still frozen in the exact gesture that began the spell two centuries ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fish and eels have made homes inside the folds of his drifting, weightless robes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His tower's books float open around him, pages perfectly preserved by whatever spell holds him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He speaks in half-finished sentences, as if still mid-thought from centuries back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He seems mildly surprised, every time, that visitors have found the tower at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Something about the intrusion has nudged his frozen spell closer to finally completing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water around him occasionally stands still, entirely, for a heartbeat at a time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's just spoken the next word of the spell for the first time in two hundred years."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["standing mid-gesture in a drowned tower, robes drifting weightless, a spell frozen half-cast", "waiting two centuries underwater without once noticing the time that's passed"]},{"name":"Nightbringer of the Drowned Fleet","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Shipboard vampire quietly turning a becalmed fleet's crew","flavor":"Turned in his own cabin during a becalmed crossing, and has been quietly recruiting the fleet ever since.","desc":"He moves through a becalmed fleet's decks unseen by moonlight, cape settled, teeth just visible when he smiles at a crewman he's already decided to visit tonight.","traits":{"note": "He recruits rather than kills where he can — a fleet he's fed on quietly grows more his every night.", "actions": [{"name": "Bat-Form Slip", "replaces": "Multiattack (Vampire Form Only)", "text": "In his true form he makes two attacks, only one of which can be a bite; in bat form he makes one attack, wings silent against any breeze the fleet still has."}, {"name": "Grave-Cold Strike", "replaces": "Grave Strike (Vampire Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Necrotic damage, and frost crusts the wound like a night on open water."}, {"name": "Becalming Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage, and he regains hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt. The target's maximum hit points are reduced by that same amount until it finishes a long rest, sleep taking them like the sea itself pulled the fight out of them."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a dead captain's coat, buttons still bright under two centuries of salt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never crosses running water on deck — only stalks the becalmed and windless nights."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a ledger of names, one crewman turned per week, never rushed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Casts no reflection in the water below, which the newer hands have started to notice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sleeps by day in a false-bottomed powder keg lashed below the waterline."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has already turned the bosun, and the two of them are dividing the fleet's watches between them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The calm itself seems to follow him — wind dies whenever he steps above decks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Word has reached him that a priest is aboard, and he's moved his timetable up by weeks."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["gliding unseen between becalmed hulls, choosing which crewman he'll visit tonight", "standing at a rail in borrowed moonlight, cape settled, waiting for the watch to turn"]},{"name":"The Bilge-Born Horror","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"Hold-grown horror that sees through the deck planks above","flavor":"Grew in the dark of a cursed hold on a diet of drowned stowaways, and sees every deck above it through the planks.","desc":"A single vast eye opens somewhere in the dark of a cursed hold, and the deck planks above seem thinner suddenly, like it can see straight through them to whoever's standing there.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyestalks have learned the shape of the crew's boots and no longer bother tracking the cat."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has widened one knothole to a fist-sized gap it favors for its central eye."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its body has grown around a ballast stone, fusing hold and horror into one mass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feeds mostly on rats now, having learned sailors scream and bring more sailors."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Central eye is milky and pale, having never once seen open daylight."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The captain knows it's down there and has been quietly feeding it disobedient crew."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wood grain around its eyestalks has started to look like the eyes are painted on, not grown."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's outgrown the hold and has begun splintering upward through the lower deck tonight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["unblinking in the bilge dark, tracking footsteps on the deck above through the planks", "digesting a stowaway slowly while its eyestalks drift toward a new sound topside"]},{"name":"The Drowned Doge","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"rlm-the-drowned-doge","summary":"Drowned merchant-lord enthroned over the port he sank","flavor":"Bankrolled the fleet that sank an entire rival port, and now presides drowned over the wreckage he bought.","desc":"Bloated and crowned, he sits enthroned on a chair of fused coin in the wreckage of the very port his fleet sank, water sloughing endlessly off silk robes that never dry.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Drowned Court", "text": "Commands nearby undead crew as an extension of his enthroned will."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living merchant owes the Doge's sunk bank a debt and has come to beg forgiveness underwater."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His throne of fused coin includes a signet ring a party member's patron desperately wants back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding court and mistakes the party for petitioners, which buys them one strange audience before the fighting starts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival drowned lord's envoy is present, mid-negotiation over sunken cargo rights."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's just crowned a newly drowned captain as his herald, and the herald still remembers being alive."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The port above is being rebuilt, and every new piling driven into the wreck wakes him a little more."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His silk robes never dry because the water sluicing off them is somehow still the day his fleet sank."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The rival port's living descendants are sailing to reclaim the wreck tonight, and he has been waiting exactly this long to receive them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["presiding enthroned over the wreckage his own fleet made, coin fusing to his chair", "receiving the newly drowned as if they'd come to pay respects rather than die"]},{"name":"The Ninth Wave Herald","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Elemental","size":"Huge","frame":"salamander-inferno-master","model":"rlm-the-ninth-wave-herald","summary":"Sentient storm-wave that is the reason the ninth wave is worst","flavor":"Sailors swear the ninth wave in any storm is always the worst; this is why, and it knows the superstition is true.","desc":"A wall of water rises higher than any wave before it, lightning threading its curling crest like veins, and it knows exactly why sailors always fear the ninth one worst.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lightning-veined crest flickers brighter with every wave it counts up to nine."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks in the overlapping voices of everyone it's ever drowned, none of them distinct."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only rises in storms it didn't start, riding weather rather than making it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recedes instantly once its ninth wave breaks, storm or no storm."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trident never leaves its grip — the weapon and the wave-shape seem to be one thing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This storm has lasted eight waves already, and it's visibly, hungrily counting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It can be heard counting underwater by ships miles off, in a voice like a bell buoy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something has made it skip to the ninth wave early, and it seems as unsettled by that as anyone."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "elemental"],"activity":["rising in a storm's ninth swell, lightning threading its crest like veins", "counting the smaller waves aloud in thunder before it breaks over a ship at the count it's chosen"]},{"name":"The Deathless Mutiny","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"dracolich","model":"rlm-the-deathless-mutiny","summary":"Fused mass of every drowned mutiny, wearing a stolen captain's coat","flavor":"Every crew that ever turned on its captain and drowned for it feeds this thing; it wears whichever coat the nearest mutiny needs.","desc":"Dozens of mutineers' corpses have fused into one many-armed horror, wearing whichever stolen captain's coat the nearest doomed crew still needs, hands still reaching for a wheel none of them ever earned.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's hired crew is one bad order from mutinying, and something in the water already smells it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wears the coat of a captain the party specifically needs information from, dead sixty years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A survivor of its last feeding begs the party to burn the wreck before another crew turns near it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fused around a ship's wheel the party's rival desperately wants intact for a ritual."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of the party's own hired hands is already arguing for mutiny, unaware of what's listening."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only surfaces where blood has already been spilled over who commands a ship."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The coat it's currently wearing belongs to a captain still alive, asleep in his cabin this very night."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every mutiny that has ever happened or will happen on this stretch of water seems to already be folded into it, waiting its turn to add one more."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["reaching with a dozen fused arms for a wheel it will never be allowed to hold", "shrugging into whichever drowned captain's coat the nearest doomed crew still needs"]},{"name":"The Sunken Cathedral's Choir Eternal","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"lich","model":"rlm-the-sunken-cathedrals-choir-eternal","summary":"Lich-chaplain still preaching to a two-century-drowned congregation","flavor":"A ship's chaplain who lichified himself to keep preaching to a congregation that drowned two centuries ago and never left.","desc":"A coral crown sits on a lich enthroned in a drowned cathedral's nave, still preaching to pews of the dead that never left, voice carrying through water like it was air.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Undying Sermon", "text": "Nearby undead gain resistance while the lich continues its unbroken sermon."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coral crown has grown fused to his skull, no longer removable even by him."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still delivers the same sermon, night after century, never reaching its final verse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His congregation sways in unison to a hymn only they and he can fully hear."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a phylactery disguised as a ship's bell, hung where the cathedral's own bell once was."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to raise a hand against anyone who kneels first, however briefly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A living pilgrimage of the faithful has started diving down to hear him preach, and some don't come back up."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cathedral's drowned bell rings on its own whenever he reaches the sermon's midpoint."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He has, after two centuries, finally found the words to finish the sermon, and the whole congregation is rising to hear the end."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["preaching from a coral pulpit to pews of drowned congregants who never rose to leave", "leading a hymn that carries through water like it was open air, verse after verse unfinished"]},{"name":"The Maw That Charts No Course","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Chartless leviathan that swallows convoys from no fixed direction","flavor":"Surfaces on no chart and no schedule, swallowing whole convoys, and every survivor swears a different direction it came from.","desc":"The sea splits open with no warning and no pattern, a gargantuan maw surfacing to swallow a convoy whole, and every survivor who lives to tell it swears it came from a different direction.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It just swallowed the ship the party needed to reach in time, cargo and all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cartographer swears she's mapped seventeen sightings and they form no pattern the party can trust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces between the party's ship and the only safe harbor for a hundred miles."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival captain is deliberately luring it toward the party's convoy to clear the water of competition."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party is chasing was aboard the last convoy it took, possibly still alive inside it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three convoys in three different seas have vanished this season, and the timing lines up too well to be different maws."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "No storm, current, or star-chart has ever predicted where it will surface next, not once, not by anyone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has begun surfacing exactly where the party's ship is about to be, again and again, as if the sea itself has started aiming it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "deeplands"],"activity":["breaking the surface with no warning to take a convoy whole, direction unguessable", "vanishing back into depths that show no wake, no trail, no pattern to track"]},{"name":"the Drowned Captain","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate-captain","model":"pirate-captain","summary":"undead ship's-master, obsessed and unable to stop commanding","flavor":"Lashed to a wheel that rotted out from under him decades ago, he still barks headings to a crew that stopped answering. Cross his wake and he'll press every soul aboard into one more hunt.","desc":"Lashed to a wheel that rotted through decades ago, he still barks headings into the fog, jaw working around orders a crew stopped answering long before you were born. His eyes fix on your ship's wake like it owes him a debt.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Press the Crew", "text": "A creature slain within reach rises to serve him for the rest of the encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's own ship just crossed his wake, and he's already turning to give chase."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's pressed a living crew into service and they're begging silently for rescue as he commands them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A merchant offers coin to anyone who'll sink the ghost ship still haunting his trade route."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party's vessel for the one that mutinied against him, and won't be told otherwise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His wheel, rotted through, is the one artifact a collector needs to break his curse — or worse, extend it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's been sighted three times this month, always hunting ships that owe debts to the same trading house."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He gives headings to stars that haven't been in that part of the sky for two hundred years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight, for the first time anyone's heard of, his crew has started answering him back."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["barking headings into the fog to a crew that stopped answering decades back", "fixing rotted eyes on a passing ship's wake like it owes him an unpaid debt"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"generic mad-captain figure in the vein of Melville's Ahab (1851, PD) — our own obsessive, not Ahab himself"},{"name":"Bosun Wormwood","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"pirate","model":"pirate","summary":"rank-and-file cutlass pirate, first over the rail","flavor":"Every crew needs someone to swing first and count the take later. He's not smart, he's not brave, but there's always another one behind him.","desc":"He's already halfway over the rail before the others, cutlass swinging wide and careless, grinning like the take's already counted. He isn't smart and he isn't brave — he's just first, and there's always another one behind him.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Wormwood makes two dagger attacks."}, {"name": "Reckless Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Enthralling Panache", "replaces": "Enthralling Panache", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that can see and hear Wormwood must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or have Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn, thrown off by his sheer nerve."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Missing two front teeth from a bar bet he still insists he won."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears three mismatched rings, each looted from a different failed boarding."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sings the same three lines of a shanty over and over mid-fight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always volunteers to go first, and is always slightly surprised when it goes badly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of rails he's cleared scratched into his own dagger hilt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Owes the quartermaster a debt he's hoping this boarding finally covers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears a dead crewmate whispers the best boarding spots to him before every fight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Has decided, wrongly, that tonight's take is enough to buy his way out of the crew for good."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["swinging over the rail first, cutlass wide and careless, grinning at a take he hasn't counted yet", "shoving past his own crewmates to be first aboard, already bragging about the loot"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock cutthroat-pirate-mook archetype (uncopyrightable stock type)"},{"name":"the Bone Quartermaster","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton","summary":"undead crewman, ledger-obsessed and cutlass-armed","flavor":"He still keeps the manifest, tallying cargo that turned to silt a hundred years back. Argue with his math and he'll settle it with a cutlass.","desc":"He balances a waterlogged manifest on one bony forearm, tallying cargo that turned to silt a hundred years back in a voice like grinding shell. Argue the numbers and the cutlass at his hip does the correcting.","traits":{"note": "He will not fight until the ledger is settled — insult his numbers and he stops asking, and starts swinging.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Quartermaster makes two longsword attacks."}, {"name": "Ledger-Balancing Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Strength save or be pushed 10 ft. and knocked Prone, the manifest's numbers apparently having settled the argument."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The manifest's ink has long since run, but he reads it perfectly anyway."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts every coin taken from intruders before he'll stop fighting to loot the rest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice grinds like shifting shell whenever he recites a tally."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to attack anyone who offers to help him balance the books first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a second, hidden manifest that lists debts owed to him personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Believes a specific crewman still owes him for cargo lost a hundred years back, and won't rest until it's paid."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "New entries keep appearing in the manifest in a hand that isn't his."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The manifest finally balances to zero tonight, and he seems unsure what that means for him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["balancing a waterlogged manifest on one forearm, tallying cargo that turned to silt a century ago", "correcting a shipmate's count with the flat of a cutlass rather than an argument"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"undead-crew archetype built on the ghost-ship stock trope"},{"name":"the Kraken","cr":23,"role":"apex","type":"aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"kraken","model":"kraken","summary":"the mythic apex sea-titan, rarely surfaces, never forgotten","flavor":"Sailors call it a myth right up until the sea stands up around their ship. It doesn't hunt for food anymore — it hunts because something that old resents being disturbed.","desc":"The sea doesn't part so much as stand up — an arm thicker than a mast breaking the surface, then another, then the water itself seeming to rise around the ship like a wall closing in. It isn't hunting for food. Something that old is simply done being disturbed.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "actions": [{"name": "Crushing Grasp", "text": "Multiple tentacle attacks can grapple and constrict a ship's hull simultaneously."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's surfaced beneath the party's ship, and sailors are already praying rather than fighting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cult aboard a rival ship intends to feed the party's vessel to it as tribute."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The wreck reef it's sorting includes a ship the party has been searching for."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's disturbed by something below and rising faster than any sailor's ever recorded."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captain who claims to have bargained with it once before offers to guide the party past it, for a price."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hasn't surfaced in a generation, and every old sailor aboard has a theory about why now."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water around the party's ship has gone glassy and still, the way it's said to just before it rises."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has been disturbed from a rest older than any nation on the charts, and it intends to make that cost someone dearly."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands"],"activity":["standing the sea up around a ship, one vast arm surfacing and then another", "sorting a reef of a hundred sunk keels, unhurried, deciding what to add to it next"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Norse/Scandinavian sea-monster legend, pre-modern folklore (also the Alfred Tennyson sonnet, 1830, PD)"},{"name":"Moby, the White Whale","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"beast","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"dragon-turtle","summary":"the pale, unkillable whale that turns and fights back","flavor":"Pale as bone and scarred by a hundred failed harpoons, it doesn't flee ships — it turns and comes back for them. Some captains hunt it for the bounty. Others hunt it because they can't stop.","desc":"Pale as bone against the dark water, its hide is a map of old harpoon scars, and it doesn't flee the way whales are supposed to — it turns, slow and deliberate, and comes straight back at whoever struck first.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A one-eyed captain offers the party's whole crew's shares to help finish the hunt he's chased for years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The bounty on its hide would clear every debt the party's ship carries, if anyone could land the harpoon."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already been struck once tonight and is turning back on the ship that did it, which happens to be the party's."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival hunting crew is closing on the same whale and won't share the kill or the risk."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Survivors of its last hunt beg the party not to strike first, insisting it only ever fights back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's been sighted turning back on three different ships this season, all hunted by the same obsessed captain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every harpoon ever thrown at it is said to still be lodged somewhere in that scarred hide, decades apart, none of them fatal."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The obsessed captain who's hunted it for years is aboard the party's ship tonight, uninvited, and has already loaded the harpoon gun."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["turning slow and deliberate to come straight back at the ship that struck it first", "surfacing pale against the dark water, hide a map of old harpoon scars, unhurried"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Melville, Moby-Dick (1851, PD) — the whale itself, not any adaptation's design"},{"name":"a Siren","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"reef-perched singer whose song offers exhausted sailors relief","flavor":"The song doesn't promise treasure or lust — it promises rest, which is worse, because half the crew actually wants that. She only has to be patient; the rocks do the rest.","desc":"She sits on a reef-rock combing her hair, voice pitched low and warm, and the song isn't promising treasure or lust — it's promising rest. That's the part that gets half the crew to lean toward the rocks without meaning to.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Song of Rest", "text": "Creatures who fail a save move toward the siren, ignoring the danger of the rocks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Combs her hair with a rib bone taken from an old wreck's figurehead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sings the same three verses to every ship, changing only the name in the second line."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Watches the crew lean before she even finishes the first note, patient about the rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a small pile of buttons and buckles from sailors who never made it to the rocks."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stops singing the instant someone plugs their ears, uninterested in forcing it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's grown fond of one particular ship's crew and has been steering others away from this reef."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her reflection in calm water hums a half-beat behind her actual voice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight her song is offering something more specific than rest — a name, a face, someone the listener actually lost."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["combing her hair on a reef-rock, pitching her voice low and warm toward a tired crew", "watching half the watch lean toward the rocks without meaning to, patient about the rest"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — the Sirens (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"a Siren-Flock Screecher","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"young siren, screeches and dives rather than enchants","flavor":"Not every siren has the voice for the killing song — the young ones just shriek and dive-bomb, hoping to knock a sailor loose from the rigging while their elders finish the job.","desc":"It doesn't have the killing song yet — it just shrieks and dive-bombs the rigging, wings beating hard enough to knock a climbing sailor loose while the elders finish what it started.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Screecher makes two attacks, using Claws or Club in any combination."}, {"name": "Rigging Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Unfinished Song", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "Each creature within 100 ft. of the Screecher that can hear it must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or be Charmed until the end of the Screecher's next turn. It's a crude approximation of the killing song, and only holds a target still — it doesn't compel movement."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice cracks on the high notes, nowhere near ready for the real song."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dives in tight loops around the mast rather than straight at the rigging."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Copies scraps of an elder's melody without understanding what any of it does."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pack of three or four, none of them coordinating especially well."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps circling back to knock the same sailor loose a second time out of stubbornness."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "An elder siren is watching from the reef, grading the attempt."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shriek carries a note that makes rigging ropes hum back in answer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's finally landed on the right pitch by accident, and for one verse the real song almost works."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["dive-bombing the rigging, wings beating hard enough to knock a climbing sailor loose", "shrieking without the killing song yet, hoping volume does what the voice can't"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — the Sirens, junior/flock member"},{"name":"Scylla","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"strait-bound many-headed horror, takes a toll from every passing hull","flavor":"She doesn't chase ships — she waits in the same strait she's waited in since before anyone's grandmother, and takes exactly one sailor from every hull that passes too close to her side.","desc":"Six heads rear up from the strait's rock-face all at once, jaws snapping in different directions, patient in a way that says she's done this exactly the same way since before anyone's grandmother sailed here. She only ever takes one.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "each head can make a separate attack against a different target in reach"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's ship is passing too close to her side of the strait, and the toll is coming due."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local pilot offers to steer them safely wide, for a price steeper than the toll itself."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival captain intends to sacrifice a crewman deliberately to buy safe passage for the rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already taken someone the party needs alive, and the swallowing only just happened."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A shrine on the strait's cliff lists generations of names taken, and a party member recognizes one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She hasn't taken her toll in three passing ships running, and locals are nervous about what that means."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "All six heads track the same target in perfect unison, never disagreeing about who's next."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "She has held this exact strait and this exact toll since before any nation on the charts existed, and the strait itself seems to answer to her rhythm."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["rearing six heads from the strait's rock-face, jaws snapping in six directions at once", "taking exactly one sailor from a passing hull, patient the way she's been since before anyone's grandmother sailed here"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Scylla, the six-headed strait-monster (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"the Charybdis Maw","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"elemental","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"water-elemental","model":"water-elemental","summary":"living whirlpool that swallows the strait on a rhythm","flavor":"Not a creature so much as an appetite the sea itself grew — three times a day the strait empties into her throat and nothing caught in the pull ever argues its way back out.","desc":"The strait doesn't just have a current — it has an appetite, water spiraling down into a throat that opens on its own rhythm three times a day, and anything caught in the pull doesn't get the chance to argue.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR", "note": "the whirlpool's pull intensifies on a fixed cycle rather than at will"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The strait's next swallowing rhythm is due within the hour, and the party's ship is in the pull's radius."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local fisher swears the cargo the party's chasing washed down its throat last season and might still be down there."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival vessel is timing its escape to use the Maw's pull as a weapon against the party."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The only safe passage window is a narrow gap between swallowings, and the tide charts are wrong today."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something the party needs alive was pulled down on the last cycle and hasn't resurfaced yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its rhythm has sped up this month, swallowing more often than the old charts account for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Debris pulled down in one cycle sometimes resurfaces in a completely different stretch of sea entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The throat has opened early tonight, out of rhythm for the first time anyone can recall, and it isn't closing."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "elemental"],"activity":["opening the strait's throat on its own rhythm, water spiraling down without warning", "swallowing the current three times a day, indifferent to anything caught mid-pull"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Charybdis, the whirlpool-monster paired with Scylla (Homer's Odyssey, ancient/PD)"},{"name":"the Flying Dutchman's Wheelman","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"the cursed ghost-ship itself, animate and hunting for crew","flavor":"Doomed to round the same cape forever, the ship's own helm has become a creature of splintered wood and drowned will — it doesn't want passengers, it wants company in the doom.","desc":"The ship itself has become the creature — splintered wood knit into something like a hull-shaped body, the wheel fused into where a chest should be. It doesn't want passengers. It wants company in a doom it's rounding the same cape to keep.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cut the party's ship off from the only route around the cape it's doomed to circle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A member of the party's crew has already answered its invitation and stands ready to open the hatches."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captain who escaped it once offers passage-charts around it, for a price steep enough to worry the party."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries cargo lost from a wreck generations back that the party specifically needs."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes the party's ship for the crew that first cursed it, and won't be convinced otherwise."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three ships have vanished rounding this cape in as many months, all last seen near its usual course."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its wheel turns on its own even when nothing living is steering it, tracking a heading no chart shows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight the cape it's doomed to round is the same one the party must cross to reach port before their own deadline."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["looming as splintered hull-shaped wreckage with a wheel fused where a chest should be", "rounding the same doomed cape again, reaching for company rather than passengers"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Flying Dutchman — Cape maritime legend, pre-modern folklore (first written accounts 18th c.)"},{"name":"a Dutchman Deckhand","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"waterlogged member of the cursed eternal crew","flavor":"Soaked through and past caring, they still haul the same lines they died hauling. Boarding one ship is the same as boarding the next, to them — the work never ends.","desc":"It hauls the same line it died hauling, soaked through past caring, and boarding your ship registers to it exactly the same as boarding the next one would. The work never ends and it stopped minding a long time ago.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Waterlogged Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still coils a rope in its hands even mid-fight, the habit older than the hunger."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a uniform from a navy that hasn't existed in a century."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't react to being spoken to, only to being in the way of a line it needs to haul."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salt crust has grown over its eyes, and it seems not to need them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Climbs rigging with the same rote motions regardless of whether there's rigging there."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "There are more of them aboard than the ship's crew count should allow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The line it hauls disappears into water that isn't actually connected to anything."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stopped hauling the line for the first time anyone's noticed, and is staring at the living crew instead."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea"],"activity":["hauling the same line it died hauling, soaked through and past caring who's aboard", "boarding a new ship the exact same way it would board any other, work never quite ending"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Flying Dutchman legend — the doomed crew, pre-modern folklore"},{"name":"Davy Jones's Chain-Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"drowned-sailor ghoul climbing up from the seabed locker","flavor":"Every drowned sailor goes to the Locker eventually, the old saying goes — and some of them claw back up the anchor chain first, still hungry for one more meal above the waterline.","desc":"It claws up an anchor chain out of black water, locker-pale and still hungry, dragging itself hand over hand toward the waterline like the old sailors' saying about the Locker is something it's personally trying to disprove.","traits":{"note": "It personally seems determined to disprove the old saying that the Locker keeps what it takes.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chain-Ghoul makes one bite attack and two claw attacks."}, {"name": "Icy Locker Bite", "replaces": "Icy Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Chain-Scarred Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage, and a Medium or smaller target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute, locker-cold settling into the wound. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears a length of the chain it climbed, dragging behind it into the fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Skin has bleached fully locker-pale, no trace of the color it wore alive."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Climbs anything vertical the same way, chain or rope or hull, no preference."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bites first and claws second, always in that order, out of some old drowned habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recoils, just slightly, from anything that smells like fresh air rather than bilge."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "More chain rattles below it in the dark, suggesting it didn't climb up alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its chain has no anchor at the other end anymore, and yet it never runs out of slack."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's reached the waterline for the first time in its memory, and doesn't seem to know what to do next."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "deeplands"],"activity":["clawing up an anchor chain out of black water, locker-pale and still hungry", "dragging itself hand over hand toward the waterline for one more meal above it"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Davy Jones's Locker — sailors' folk-idiom for the seabed afterlife, maritime folklore (not a specific character design)"},{"name":"the Locker-Warden","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"marid","model":"marid","summary":"the folkloric seabed afterlife given a keeper, vast and patient","flavor":"Every sailor swears the Locker has a keeper who counts the dead as they settle. Whether that's true or just something sailors tell each other in a storm, something down there is definitely counting.","desc":"It waits in the dark below where the sailors' stories say the dead settle, vast and patient, and whether the counting is a myth or not, something down there is unmistakably keeping tally.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A name the party needs an answer about was tallied here recently, and the Warden knows it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to return someone lost to the deep, for a toll it hasn't named yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving captain believes the Warden holds his crew and won't accept that they're simply gone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's own missing person may be on its tally, alive or otherwise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's miscounted, or claims to have, and is unsettled enough by the error to bargain."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its tally has grown unusually long this season, more names than any normal wreck rate explains."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It recites names in order, and some of them belong to people who haven't died yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The tally, whatever it truly is, appears to include every soul aboard the party's own ship, present tense."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "deeplands"],"activity":["waiting vast and patient in the dark where the sailors say the dead settle", "keeping tally of something below, whether the counting is myth or not"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Davy Jones's Locker folk-idiom, personified as its own keeper — our invention on the folklore, not a claimed character"},{"name":"a Sea Hag of the Shoals","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"sea-hag","summary":"reef-dwelling hag who barters weather for confessions","flavor":"She trades storms for secrets and secrets for storms, and never tells you which one you actually bought. Sailors leave offerings on the reef so she'll look the other way.","desc":"She crouches at the reef line surrounded by small offerings left by sailors hoping she'll look away, and her bargain is always the same shape — a storm for a secret, though she never says which one you actually paid for.","traits":{"note": "Her bargains are always the same shape — a storm for a secret — but she never confirms which one anyone actually paid for.", "actions": [{"name": "Reef-Barter Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Death Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Death Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature the hag can see within 30 ft. that can see her must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Frightened permanently and take 18 (4d8) Psychic damage; the Frightened condition can only be ended by a remove curse or similar magic."}, {"name": "Illusory Appearance", "replaces": "Illusory Appearance", "text": "The hag covers herself and anything she is wearing or carrying with a magical illusion of a weathered fisherwoman. The illusion breaks immediately if she attacks or casts a spell."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already noticed the offerings the party left too small, and expects a secret to make up the difference."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The storm the party desperately needs to avoid was traded away by someone else, days ago, and she remembers who."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival wants the party's darkest secret badly enough to pay her for it directly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers calm seas for the rest of the voyage, if someone confesses what they're actually running from."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A sailor's confession she's already holding concerns a member of the party's crew."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The reef's offerings have thinned this season, and she's grown noticeably less patient."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every secret she's traded for eventually resurfaces as a storm exactly shaped like the confession."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's just been paid a secret so large the storm she owes back may be bigger than she can control."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["crouching at the reef line among small offerings, weighing which storm to trade for which secret", "watching sailors leave gifts on the rocks, hoping she'll look the other way tonight"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"folk sea-hag figure, generic maritime witch-crone (not tied to any single copyrighted work)"},{"name":"a Sahuagin Raider","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-warrior","model":"sahuagin-warrior","summary":"reef-raiding fish-humanoid, opportunistic wreck-stripper","flavor":"They rise off the reef in packs when a hull rides too low and too slow, stripping a wreck bare before the survivors even reach the boats.","desc":"It rises off the reef in a loose pack formation, webbed claws already reaching for whatever's loose on deck, stripping a wreck bare before the survivors even reach the boats.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Raider makes two claw attacks."}, {"name": "Wreck-Stripping Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Already has both arms full of loose cargo before the fight even starts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Signals the rest of the pack with sharp clicks rather than words."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a scavenged sailor's earring through one webbed ear."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats the instant it's grabbed more than it can carry, loot over pride."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pack timed to a ship's list, striking exactly when the deck tilts their way."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This pack answers to a Depth-Priest waiting just offshore, unseen."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Moves in perfect unison with the rest of its pack, as if sharing one set of reflexes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "This raid is unusually organized for sahuagin, hitting exactly the cargo hold that matters most."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["rising off the reef in a loose pack, webbed claws already reaching for whatever's loose on deck", "stripping a low-riding wreck bare before survivors even reach the boats"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic fish-humanoid raider archetype (own deep-water raider framing, no external IP)"},{"name":"a Sahuagin Depth-Priest","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"sahuagin-priest","model":"sahuagin-priest","summary":"deep cult priest who blesses reef-raids with dread invocations","flavor":"He blesses the raids in a tongue that predates any surface language, and the raiders fight harder for it — not out of faith exactly, more like fear of what he'd do if they didn't.","desc":"It chants in a tongue older than any surface language, low and guttural, and the raiders around it fight harder — not devotion exactly, more the particular fear of what happens if they don't.","traits":{"note": "The raiders around it fight harder for the blessing, not from devotion so much as dread of disappointing it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Depth-Priest makes two spectral jaws attacks."}, {"name": "Spectral Jaws", "replaces": "Spectral Jaws", "text": "Melee Spell Attack: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage from jaws of dark water that snap where none should be."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Depth-Priest casts spells drawn from a deep, dread invocation, favoring blessings that make its raiders fight past reason."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chant never varies verse to verse, a rote invocation worn smooth by repetition."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a headdress of teeth from things that aren't sahuagin."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Raiders visibly flinch if the chant stutters even slightly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stays at the rear of any raid, letting the blessing do the fighting for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks the reef with symbols in a language no surface scholar has ever placed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Is mid-invocation to something deeper than its usual patron and seems nervous about the attempt."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The water directly around it darkens slightly whenever the chant reaches its refrain."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Whatever it's invoking tonight has started answering back, audible under the chant itself."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["chanting in a tongue older than any surface language, low and guttural, over a raiding pack", "blessing the raid while the raiders fight harder out of fear of what happens if they don't"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic fish-humanoid priest archetype, own deep-sea cult framing"},{"name":"a Merrow Wrecker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"merrow","summary":"brutish sea-ogre that swarms wrecks for the meal, not the loot","flavor":"Not clever, just strong and hungry and drawn to the sound of splintering hulls. A merrow doesn't wreck ships for treasure — treasure's just what's left after it eats.","desc":"It surges up hungry and brutish, drawn by the sound of splintering wood, muscle rippling under green-gray hide. Treasure is just what's left over after it eats — it isn't clever enough to want it first.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Wrecker makes two attacks, using Bite or Claw in any combination."}, {"name": "Hull-Splitting Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Harpoon", "replaces": "Harpoon", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, the Wrecker can drag it 10 ft. closer as part of the attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rips into cargo crates as eagerly as into the crew, no preference shown."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Green-gray hide is scarred deep from a lifetime of splintered wood."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Discards anything shiny it can't eat, tossing loot aside without a glance."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Comes running at the sound of any wood cracking, mistaking it for a wreck every time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a small clutch of its own kind, sharing whatever the hull gives up."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's been drawn unusually far from its normal reef by the sound of this particular wreck."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems able to smell splintering wood from miles off, arriving before the hull's even fully cracked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's already fed once tonight and is hungrier, not calmer, for the taste."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["surging up hungry and brutish, drawn by the sound of splintering wood", "tearing into a wreck for the meal first, treasure an afterthought it barely notices"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic ogre-of-the-sea archetype (folkloric merrow stock type, no specific IP)"},{"name":"the Bosun's Ghost","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"haunting ship's-officer whose whistle warns (or curses) the crew","flavor":"He still walks his rounds belowdecks, and any living sailor who hears his whistle in the dark knows to brace for something going badly wrong topside within the hour.","desc":"A thin whistle carries through the dark below-decks before anything else does, and any sailor who's heard it before knows to brace — because within the hour, something topside always goes badly wrong.","traits":{"note": "His whistle is a warning as much as a threat — sailors who know it brace for trouble topside, not from him.", "actions": [{"name": "Corrupting Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Spell Attack: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 21 (4d8 + 3) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Horrifying Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each non-undead creature within 60 ft. that can see the Bosun's Ghost must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Frightened for 1 minute. A Frightened target ages 1d4 x 10 years, weakened as if the whistle itself had aged them."}, {"name": "Below-Decks Wail (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "The Bosun's Ghost wails. Every creature within 30 ft. that can hear it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or drop to 0 hit points, or take 18 (4d8) Psychic damage on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His whistle has just sounded belowdecks, and something topside is already going wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An old sailor aboard recognizes the whistle and begs the captain to turn back immediately."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's warning specifically about the exact cargo the party is currently transporting."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival wants his whistle recorded or silenced before it warns their intended victims."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He walks the same rounds his living post required, and something in that route matters to the plot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His whistle has sounded three nights running, each time before a different disaster struck."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whistle can be heard by sailors on other ships entirely, miles distant, at the same instant."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight the whistle hasn't stopped, over and over, as if the warning is for something already happening."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["walking his rounds belowdecks, a thin whistle carrying through the dark before anything else does", "warning any sailor who's heard the whistle before to brace for something going wrong within the hour"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic maritime-haunting archetype — the officer who died on duty and can't leave it"},{"name":"a Corsair Deckhand","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"nimble boarding-raider, cuts lines before the main assault","flavor":"Fast over the rigging and faster with a knife, these are the ones sent ahead to cut lines and douse lanterns before the boarding party even shows itself.","desc":"Fast over the rigging and faster with a knife, it's already cutting lines and dousing lanterns before the rest of the boarding party has even shown its face.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Deckhand makes two attacks, using Shortsword or Longbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Line-Cutting Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, a lantern's flame going dark if the shot was aimed at it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Already halfway up the rigging before the rest of the boarding party has even signaled."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries three knives, one specifically for lanterns and lines, not flesh."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in near total silence, boots wrapped in cloth against the deck boards."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks cut lines with a chalk tally to report back to the boarding captain."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to vanish back over the rail rather than engage once discovered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has been sent ahead of a much larger raid than the target ship expects."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Seems to know exactly which lines to cut without ever having seen this ship's rigging before."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "This deckhand has cut the wrong line — the one holding something down that shouldn't come loose."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sea", "coast"],"activity":["cutting lines and dousing lanterns before the boarding party even shows its face", "moving fast over the rigging, faster still with a knife, clearing the way ahead"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic historical-corsair mook archetype — long-dead seafaring raider figure, not any named individual"},{"name":"the Storm-Bound Djinn","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"elemental","size":"Large","frame":"djinni","model":"djinni","summary":"elemental genie fused into a waterspout, capricious and huge","flavor":"Bound into a waterspout centuries ago by a captain who never wrote down how, it now answers to no one and drags whole ships skyward just to watch them fall.","desc":"A waterspout twists upright out of calm water, a genie's shape barely visible inside the spinning wall, and it drags whole ships skyward on a whim just to watch them fall.","traits":{"hp": "above baseline for its CR"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's just plucked a crewmate the party needs off the deck and into the spinning wall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scholar knows the old binding words but not the ritual to speak them safely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dragging the party's ship skyward right now, purely for the spectacle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival captain claims to control it and is offering its power for a steep price."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Debris from a ship it dropped last season is scattered across a nearby shore, cargo intact."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown bored of ships and started experimenting with dragging coastal buildings instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Inside the spout, for half a second at a time, its shape looks almost sorry about what it's doing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The centuries-old binding is finally cracking, and whatever it becomes once it's fully free won't be bound by any captain's coast again."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "elemental", "sky"],"activity":["twisting upright as a waterspout, a genie's shape barely visible in the spinning wall", "dragging a whole ship skyward on a whim, just to watch it fall"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"elemental sea-storm archetype drawn from the broad genie/elemental stock type of maritime legend"},{"name":"the Wrecking Reef-Wraith","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"drowned wrecker's ghost, still luring ships onto the rocks","flavor":"In life it lit false beacon-fires to lure ships onto the rocks for salvage. In death it just lights the fires — there's no cargo left to want, only the habit.","desc":"A pale light bobs along the shoals where a beacon-fire used to burn, drowned and translucent now, still lighting the same false signal it once used to lure ships onto rocks — there's no cargo left to want, only the habit.","traits":{"note": "There's no cargo left to want — it lights the false fire purely from habit, decades after the reason stopped mattering.", "actions": [{"name": "Life Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. The Wraith regains hit points equal to that amount."}, {"name": "Create Specter", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Wraith targets a humanoid within 10 ft. that has died within the last minute from the Wraith's Life Drain. The target's spirit rises as a specter under the Wraith's control, drawn to the false light the same as it was."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The party's ship has spotted its false beacon and is steering toward the rocks right now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local wrecker's descendant wants the fire extinguished before it claims one more hull."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's lit the same false signal that once lured the party's own missing relative's ship."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival crew intends to use the false beacon deliberately to wreck the party's pursuit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A specter it raised recently still carries a message it never got to deliver."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three wrecks on these shoals this season, all lured the same way, none officially explained."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The false fire is visible only to ships already low on supplies, as if it senses the desperate ones."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight it's lit two beacons at once, in two different places, and neither is the real shoal."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea"],"activity":["lighting a false beacon-fire along the shoals, pale and translucent, same signal as always", "drowned and drifting where a real beacon used to stand, luring by habit rather than need"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic ghost-of-the-shoals archetype — the drowned wrecker who lured ships onto rocks in life"}],
 "lost-world":[{"name":"Sand-Choked Sentry","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"classic bone guardian, forever walking its post","flavor":"A picked-clean guard still standing post at a gate nobody uses, sand pouring from its ribs.","desc":"Sand pours from between its ribs when it turns, a thin dry hiss like a held breath let out. It carries a spear worn to a splinter and stands its post at a gate that opens onto nothing but more ruin. The joints grind with each step, patient as erosion.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves its post voluntarily — chase it past the gate and it slows, unwilling.", "actions": [{"name": "Splinter Spear", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Warning Shot", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +2, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spear point is snapped off; it jabs with the splintered shaft instead."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rusted gorget still hangs from its neck, bearing a rank no army recognizes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sand fills its eye sockets entirely; it tracks sound, not sight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands atop a drift so deep only its skull shows above the dune."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shortbow string is a braid of hair, still somehow taut."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It salutes anyone who approaches wearing anything resembling old livery colors."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its footprints in the sand belong to boots it hasn't worn in centuries."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Toppling it collapses a sand-choked archway that was holding back a buried flood channel."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["standing rigid at a gate no one uses, sand hissing out between its ribs", "turning at the sound of footsteps, spear already leveling toward the gap in the wall"]},{"name":"Glyph-Warded Scarab Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"tomb-curse insect swarm guarding a sealed door","flavor":"A living seal poured into a doorway generations ago; disturb the lintel and the carpet of beetles rises.","desc":"The threshold looks paved until it moves — a shifting carpet of black shells clicking against each other in the dark. Lift your torch and the whole floor lifts with it, a wet chitinous roar rising off the stone. It was poured into that doorway on purpose, generations ago, and it has never once stopped guarding it.","traits":{"note": "It cannot cross the warded lintel it was poured to guard — chase it there and it recoils.", "actions": [{"name": "Chittering Swarm", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 0 ft., affects a single target in the swarm's space. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their shells are stamped with the same ward-glyph, over and over, like a minted coin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They swarm in a perfect ring, never breaking the shape of the seal they replaced."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crushed underfoot, they release a dry incense-smell that lingers for hours."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They ignore anyone not carrying metal, keying only off the ring of a blade."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A few carry tiny scraps of gold leaf on their backs, flaking off as they scuttle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They part politely for anyone holding a lit brazier, as if remembering an old rite."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Beneath the swarm, the floor glyph is still faintly warm to the touch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Breaking the seal they guard releases whatever curse-vapor they were sealing in with it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["carpeting the threshold in a shifting black crust that clicks softly in the dark", "rising off the stone floor all at once as torchlight crosses the sealed lintel"]},{"name":"Sun-Fat Ridgeback","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"oversized lizard basking among fallen ruins","flavor":"A sun-fat lizard the size of a hound, sunning on toppled cornices until your shadow crosses it.","desc":"It suns itself on a toppled cornice, scaled hide gone the color of the surrounding dust, gorged and slow to move. Only the flick of a lidless eye tracks you crossing its patch of shade. When it finally rouses, it's with the unhurried confidence of something that has never had to hurry.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Lazy Snap", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide has gone precisely the color of the ruin-dust it suns itself in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A healed spear-scar runs the length of its back from some earlier trespasser."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fat enough that rousing it takes a full breath before it even lifts its head."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's claimed the flattest, sunniest cornice for itself and chases off smaller lizards."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tail has regrown crooked, a testament to some old escape."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It tolerates being stepped near so long as its patch of sun isn't blocked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its stomach bulges with a shape too angular to be prey — something metal, swallowed whole."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled off its cornice, it dislodges the loose stonework, bringing part of the ruin down."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["basking on a toppled cornice, gorged and unbothered by the shadow crossing it", "tracking movement with one lidless eye while the rest of it stays perfectly still"]},{"name":"Linen-Wrapped Shambler","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"rot-wrapped shambler retracing a dead ritual","flavor":"A pilgrim mummified mid-step by the dry wind, still shuffling a processional route no one remembers.","desc":"Dry wind mummified it mid-stride, and mid-stride is how it still moves — a stiff, marching shuffle down a processional route no living thing remembers the destination of. Linen wrappings have gone the color of the sand it walks through. It does not look at you; it has somewhere to be.","traits":{"note": "It never deviates from its processional route — pull it off-path and it strains to return.", "actions": [{"name": "Mummified Backhand", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wrappings have gone the exact color of the sand it processes through."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a rotted standard-pole, the banner long since disintegrated."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw has locked open mid-chant, though no sound comes out anymore."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It steps in time with a drumbeat only it can still hear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One foot drags a groove that's worn a visible trench into the stone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at what used to be a shrine, bows, and continues — every single circuit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its route traces the exact outline of a building that no longer stands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force it off its route entirely and every buried shambler on the same processional rises with it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["marching a fixed processional route in a stiff, mid-stride shuffle", "colliding gently with fallen rubble and correcting course without pause"]},{"name":"Blind Archive-Gnawer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"blind vermin swarm infesting the buried archive","flavor":"Pale, sightless rat-things nesting in the archive halls for a thousand years, chewing scrolls no one will miss.","desc":"Pale, sightless shapes boil out from between shelves of scroll-cases at the first vibration of a footstep, whiskers twitching toward sound instead of sight. A thousand years underground has bleached them the color of old parchment. They've eaten most of the archive already, and they are not picky about what comes next.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blind Nip", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 1 Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've bleached parchment-pale from a thousand years without a trace of light."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They flee sound louder than a whisper, but swarm anything quieter."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their nesting shelf has collapsed under the weight of chewed scroll-pulp."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A few have chewed clean through wax seals, leaving broken sigils scattered underfoot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They swarm thickest around one particular alcove, as if it still smells of something."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They scatter entirely at the smell of ink, however faint, on anything you're carrying."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their droppings have formed drifts shaped disturbingly like the letters they've been eating."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Disturbed enough, the whole nest boils loose from a shelf that's the last support holding the archive ceiling up."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "deeplands"],"activity":["boiling out from between scroll-cases at the first vibration of a footstep", "gnawing steadily through a shelf of brittle records no one will ever read now"]},{"name":"Cracked Watch-Idol","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"animated stone idol stuck on an endless patrol","flavor":"A hollow votive statue jerking through a guard pattern it can no longer complete without falling over.","desc":"Stone limbs jerk through half a guard pattern before the motion runs out and it has to start over, joints grinding rock dust with every restart. A crack runs the length of its once-painted face. It has forgotten every step of the drill except that there is one.","traits":{"note": "It repeats one patrol loop exactly — learn the gap in its drill and you can walk straight through it.", "actions": [{"name": "Drill-Step Strikes", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Idol makes two Votive Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Votive Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crack splits its once-painted face straight through where the eyes were."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It halts and restarts its drill at the exact same flagstone, every cycle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chips of gilt still cling to its shoulders where worshippers once dressed it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's missing an arm; the drill continues anyway, swinging at empty air."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its base is worn perfectly smooth in a circle from centuries of the same steps."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It freezes entirely if the drill music — a temple chant — is hummed nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Inside the crack in its face, something small and dry rattles when it moves."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break it and every idol sharing its patrol pattern elsewhere in the ruin lurches awake in unison."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["jerking through half a guard drill before the motion runs out and resets", "grinding rock dust from its joints as it restarts the same patrol from the beginning"]},{"name":"Vine-Choked Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-wolf-spider","model":"giant-wolf-spider","summary":"venomous ambush-spider lurking in overgrown ruins","flavor":"Something fat and patient in the vines strangling the ornamental garden; it strikes from beneath the flowers.","desc":"The ornamental garden has gone to seed and something fat and patient lives in what it became, hidden beneath a carpet of dead blossoms. Silk lines run taut between the broken trellises, invisible until they aren't. It waits for the flowers to move on their own.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Garden Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Poison damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dead petals cling to its back, a camouflage it never has to reapply."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its silk lines run taut between broken trellises, invisible until you walk into one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grown fat on garden-birds and moves slower for it, but hits just as hard."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old bones, small and picked clean, ring the base of its favored trellis."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors the shade beneath one particular collapsed archway, and rarely strays."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It disengages entirely if its web-lines are cut before it strikes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The flowers over its nest never fully die, blooming faint and wrong-colored."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it near its web-mass and the whole trellis collapses, dropping stone urns full of old grave-goods."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "forest"],"activity":["lying motionless beneath a carpet of dead blossoms, silk lines drawn taut", "testing the air with a foreleg the instant something brushes its trellis-lines"]},{"name":"Bone-Orchard Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"jackal","model":"jackal","summary":"scavenger jackal pack circling grave robbers","flavor":"Pack scavenger that has learned tomb-robbers mean an easy meal; it circles at the treeline, waiting for the digging to stop.","desc":"They keep to the treeline in loose, watchful knots, ribs showing, ears pricked toward the sound of digging. Generations of easy meals have taught the pack that grave robbers mean an open larder. They don't attack first — they wait for you to stop shoveling.","traits":{"note": "It never attacks first — it waits for stillness, or for prey to be already wounded.", "actions": [{"name": "Opportunist's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage, or 6 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage against a creature that is Prone or below half its hit point maximum."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pack has learned the sound of a shovel and gathers before the digging even starts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One jackal always hangs back from the pack, watching instead of circling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old grave-cloth is matted into its fur from years of scavenging near the same tombs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They keep a respectful distance from anything still moving, but close fast once it stops."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pack is thin this season, hungrier and bolder than usual."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They scatter the instant a larger predator's scent crosses the dig site."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They never touch bones bearing a certain seal-mark, however hungry they get."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The pack's howling calls something much larger down from the ruin's upper terraces."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["circling at the treeline in a loose, watchful knot, ribs showing under thin fur", "waiting motionless at the edge of a dig site for the shoveling to stop"]},{"name":"Curse-Bound Grave Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"paralyzing ghoul, once a fellow tomb-raider","flavor":"Someone who broke the same seal you're about to break, and never made it back out.","desc":"It crouches over what's left of the last person who broke this seal, knuckles dragging, jaw unhinged wider than a living jaw should go. Torn cloth still clings to it — someone's expedition gear, cut for someone your size. Its eyes track you with recognition it shouldn't have.","traits":{"note": "Its expedition gear was cut for a body its own size — it was someone's tomb-partner, once.", "actions": [{"name": "Ravenous Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ghoul Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage. If the target is a creature other than an Undead, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Combined Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghoul makes one Ravenous Bite attack and one Ghoul Claw attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its expedition gear still bears a guild-mark from a company that never came back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hoards the small tools it died holding, arranging them uselessly by its perch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches from lantern-light exactly the way its living self once must have."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A journal, ruined but legible in patches, lies wedged beneath where it crouches."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mimics a digging motion when idle, muscle memory outliving the mind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Speak the name stitched into its ruined gear and it hesitates, just once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow, cast by torchlight, still moves like a living person's would."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's not alone — the whole party it came in with rises the moment it's disturbed."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "desert"],"activity":["crouching over the last person who broke this seal, jaw unhinged too wide", "tracking newcomers with a recognition its eyes shouldn't still hold"]},{"name":"Snake-Cult Zealot","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-infiltrator","model":"cultist","summary":"fanged serpent-cultist guarding forbidden rites","flavor":"A serpent-blooded devotee who kept the old faith alive underground long after the empire fell, fangs bared under a ceremonial mask.","desc":"A ceremonial mask hides everything but the mouth, and the mouth is full of filed, fanged teeth bared beneath painted lips. It keeps the old rites alive down here long after the empire that banned them crumbled. It hisses the invocation before it draws steel, like it still expects an audience.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ceremonial Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Venom-Fang Ray", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Serpent Invocation", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Zealot casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components and using Charisma as the spellcasting ability: At Will: Chill Touch, Command; 1/Day Each: Charm Person, Suggestion."}, {"name": "Twinned Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Zealot makes two attacks, using Ceremonial Scimitar or Venom-Fang Ray in any combination."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a rite-chamber and wants witnesses gone before the chant finishes, not after."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a sealed message meant for a cult cell that's already been wiped out."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captured acolyte, bound and gagged nearby, could name the rest of the cell if freed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's bleeding from an older wound, favoring one side, and looking to end this fast."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries the cult's last venom-vial and won't let it be taken intact."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers a trade — safe passage for the desecration of the rite it's guarding — and means it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its mask won't come off, even in death, fused somehow to the face beneath."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its invocation, interrupted mid-chant, backlashes and calls something from beneath the rite-chamber floor."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "desert", "urban"],"activity":["hissing an invocation before drawing steel, as if still expecting an audience", "guarding a sealed rite-chamber beneath a ceremonial mask that hides everything but the mouth"]},{"name":"Wall-Set Spear-Guard","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"bandaged vizier still guarding an empty throne","flavor":"The last vizier, wound in the same linens as the dead-tongue king it still serves, delivering proclamations to an empty throne room.","desc":"Bandages the color of the throne room's dust wrap a vizier still delivering proclamations no one is left to hear, spear held at present-arms before an empty seat. Its voice, when it speaks at all, comes out in the dead tongue of a court that has been gone for centuries. It will not move from its post while the throne remains unoccupied.","traits":{"note": "It guards a post, not a treasure — it will not pursue past the threshold it was set to hold.", "actions": [{"name": "Ceremonial Spear", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage from the grave-tar worked into the shaft. Its reach lets it hold a doorway alone."}, {"name": "Sentinel's Curse", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The Guard fixes an intruder within 60 ft. with the stare of an oath still kept. The target makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frightened for 1 minute and cannot move closer to the threshold the Guard defends; it repeats the save at the end of each turn, ending the effect on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wrappings bear a vizier's seal, worn nearly smooth by centuries."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm is fused to the wall-niche; it fights from a fixed post."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It speaks the roll-call of a court that no longer exists, awaiting reply."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spear is ceremonial gold over a core of ugly, effective iron."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bars exactly one doorway and ignores every other route completely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will stand down for anyone who correctly names the king it still serves."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Behind it, the empty throne-room is faintly warm, as if just vacated."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The moment its threshold is crossed, every niche in the hall opens at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "cave"],"activity":["standing in a wall-niche so still the dust has settled on its shoulders", "stepping down from its alcove the instant an intruder passes the threshold it guards"]},{"name":"Plinth-Fused Sentinel","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"stone temple guardian bound to bar the sanctum","flavor":"A carved guardian fused to its plinth, sworn to never let the inner sanctum see a second dawn of daylight.","desc":"Its lower half has fused into the plinth it was carved to stand on, stone grown into stone across the centuries. What was meant to be a statue with a duty has become a duty with a statue's patience. It swings its arms free of the plinth only when the sanctum door is disturbed — and only that far.","traits":{"note": "It cannot leave its plinth — it fights at the edge of its reach and no farther.", "actions": [{"name": "Sanctum Blade", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Force damage as the blade carries a sliver of the ward that binds the Sentinel."}, {"name": "Fused Guard", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sentinel makes two Sanctum Blade attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stone has grown up its calves like ivy, sealing it to the plinth a little more each year."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its carved face is a portrait of someone; no one now living knows who."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never swings past the length of its own arm from the plinth's base."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old offerings, calcified into the stone at its feet, form a little heap of fused coins."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hairline crack runs up one leg where the fused stone is finally giving way."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It lowers its blade for anyone who steps no closer than the sanctum door's outer frame."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The sanctum behind it has no dust at all, as if time simply doesn't reach that room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shatter its plinth entirely and it becomes free to walk — and follow — for the first time in an age."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["standing fused ankle-deep into its ancient plinth, arms free but legs stone-bound", "swinging both arms clear the instant the sanctum door behind it is disturbed"]},{"name":"Riddle-Keeper of the Threshold","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-secrets","model":"sphinx-of-lore","summary":"riddling sphinx guarding the tomb's final gate","flavor":"A stone-eyed watcher at the last unbroken gate, bound to test any who'd pass with a question the builders thought unanswerable.","desc":"Stone eyes track you the length of the last unbroken gate, a question already forming on lips that have asked it a thousand times before. The builders thought the riddle unanswerable and built the whole tomb around that confidence. It has all the time in the world for you to be wrong.","traits":{"note": "A correctly answered riddle opens the gate without a fight; it will not attack anyone still answering.", "actions": [{"name": "Threshold Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Curse of the Wrong Answer", "replaces": "Curse of the Riddle", "text": "The Keeper poses its riddle to one creature within 60 ft. that can hear it. If the creature fails to answer correctly, it must succeed on a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw or take 18 (4d8) Psychic damage and have the Frightened condition until the end of its next turn as the failure echoes back at it."}, {"name": "Threshold Working", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Keeper casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 15): At Will: Detect Thoughts, Mind Spike; 1/Day: Mislead."}, {"name": "Guardian's Reflex", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Keeper makes two Threshold Claw attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants a specific riddle answered by name, and will accept no other proof of wit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prior party's failed answer still echoes in the chamber, distracting anyone who answers next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a gate that a fleeing NPC desperately needs opened before pursuers arrive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds the only correct answer's key phrase carved into its own base, half-worn away."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers one free pass to whoever solved its riddle last, if they can prove it was them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown bored of its own riddle and will trade it for a better one, on the spot."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every wrong answer it's ever heard is etched somewhere on its stone hide, in order."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Answer wrong three times running and it stops asking — and simply attacks until the gate is unguarded."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["fixing you with stone eyes, a question already forming on lips that have asked it a thousand times", "waiting at the last unbroken gate with the patience of something that has never once been wrong"]},{"name":"Raptor of the Ruined Plaza","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"allosaurus","model":"allosaurus","summary":"pack-hunting raptor stalking the ruined plaza","flavor":"A lean pack-hunter that has ruled the crumbled plaza for generations, using fallen colonnades as blinds.","desc":"It uses the fallen colonnades as blinds, feathers dust-grey against the broken stone, moving in short low-shouldered bursts between cover. Claw marks score every column at throat height. This plaza has been its hunting ground for generations, and it knows every sightline better than you ever will.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Plaza Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Colonnade Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Claw marks score every column at throat height, a boundary line it's drawn itself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers have gone dust-grey, near-perfect camouflage against the broken stone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the plaza's sightlines better than any map could show them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A healed scar across its flank marks a fight it clearly won."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's territorial only within the plaza's bounds and won't chase past the fallen archway."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It breaks off an attack entirely if a rival pack-member's cry sounds nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It refuses to cross one particular flagstone, circling wide around it every time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its cry brings the rest of its pack out from blinds you hadn't spotted at all."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["moving in short low-shouldered bursts between fallen colonnades, dust-grey feathers blending into stone", "tracking movement along a sightline it has hunted for generations"]},{"name":"Living Armor-Back","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"ankylosaurus","model":"ankylosaurus","summary":"club-tailed armored dinosaur, unstoppable and slow","flavor":"A slow tank of a beast that has worn a path through the sacred road for so long its footprints are mistaken for paving.","desc":"Its shell has worn its own trail across the sacred road, a groove deep enough that travelers mistake the footprints for paving stones. The club-tail drags a furrow behind it, slow and unstoppable as a tide going out. Nothing here has found a way to make it hurry.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Road-Groove Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Unhurried Advance", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Armor-Back makes one Road-Groove Tail attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its groove across the road is deep enough that travelers mistake the trail for paving."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shell bears an old, healed crack from some long-forgotten confrontation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves the exact same route every day, regardless of what's since fallen across it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moss and lichen have taken hold across its shell, a slow-growing camouflage."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never quickens its pace, even when its tail connects."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It calms entirely if simply left alone on its road, tail lowering, pace unbroken."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its groove, followed far enough, leads to a buried gate no map shows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startle it fully off its groove and its bulk brings down an unstable overhang above the road."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "forest", "grassland"],"activity":["dragging a slow furrow down the sacred road, shell worn into its own groove of a trail", "swinging its club-tail idly, unbothered by anything not already in its path"]},{"name":"Horned Terror of the Sacred Road","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"triceratops","summary":"three-horned dinosaur charging trespassers on sight","flavor":"A three-horned bull of a beast that charges anything crossing its stretch of the ceremonial highway.","desc":"Three horns lower the instant your shadow crosses its stretch of the ceremonial highway, a warning it gives exactly once. Old scars crisscross its frill from previous trespassers who didn't heed it. When it charges, the ground answers before the sound does.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Triple Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Piercing damage. If the Terror moved at least 20 feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit, the target also has the Prone condition."}, {"name": "Charging Rush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Terror makes one Triple Gore attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scars crisscross its frill from previous trespassers who didn't heed the warning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It gives exactly one warning lowering of its horns before it commits to the charge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It claims one specific stretch of the ceremonial highway and no more."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its center horn is chipped clean through from some old, violent impact."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grazes calmly on roadside scrub until anything crosses into its stretch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stands down for anyone who simply backs off its highway stretch entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Beneath its favorite grazing patch, the road's paving stones are unnaturally warm."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its charge, if it connects with the road's weak flagstones, opens a sinkhole beneath both combatants."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["lowering three horns the instant a shadow crosses its stretch of highway, a warning given once", "charging with ground-shaking momentum before the sound of it even arrives"]},{"name":"The Weeping Cistern","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"black-pudding","model":"black-pudding","summary":"corrosive ooze filling a flooded sacred bath","flavor":"Ceremonial water gone wrong across centuries of stagnation and old magic, filling the sunken bath-hall.","desc":"What was once holy water sits black and thick in the sunken bath-hall, centuries of stagnation and old rites curdled into something that moves against its own currents. A film on the surface parts wherever it reaches upward. The ripples reach the edges of the pool long before anything else does.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Corroding Reach", "replaces": "Dissolving Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Acid damage. If the target is wearing nonmagical armor or wielding a nonmagical weapon, it corrodes: armor takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it offers, or a weapon takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to damage rolls made with it. The item is destroyed if the penalty reaches -5. Nonmagical ammunition that hits the Cistern is destroyed after dealing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A film on its surface parts wherever it reaches, closing seamlessly after."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ripples reach the bath-hall's edges long before anything solid does."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faint gold flecks drift in it — coin-melt from centuries of tossed offerings."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's confined entirely to the sunken bath; it cannot climb the hall's dry steps."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old ceremonial tilework is visible beneath it, warped by whatever it's become."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stills completely if the old bath-chant is sung correctly, if only for a few seconds."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Objects it's dissolved sometimes surface again, weeks later, unmarked and clean."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drain the bath-hall and it doesn't die — it floods the passages below looking for a new basin."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["sitting black and thick in a sunken bath-hall, centuries of stagnation curdled into motion", "parting its surface film wherever a limb reaches upward toward the edge"]},{"name":"Marching Colossus of the Processional","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"towering stone statue still marching a dead parade","flavor":"A processional statue built to march the ceremonial road once a generation; the ceremony stopped, but nobody told the statue.","desc":"It was built to walk the ceremonial road once a generation, and the ceremony has been dead for longer than anyone remembers — but the statue was never informed. Its enormous stone feet strike the flagstones in a rhythm centuries out of step with any living calendar. It marches whether or not there's a road left to march.","traits":{"note": "It will not stop marching to fight — attacking it means matching its pace or being trampled.", "actions": [{"name": "Processional Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the Prone condition if it is Large or smaller."}, {"name": "Unbroken March", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus moves up to its Speed in a straight line and makes one Processional Fist attack against a creature in its path."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its enormous stone feet strike a rhythm that hasn't matched a living calendar in centuries."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It follows the same road-line whether or not any road remains beneath it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A garbled processional hymn cracks from somewhere inside its chest, endlessly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Weeds and small trees have taken root in the cracks along its shoulders."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never turns aside for obstacles smaller than itself — it walks through them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It halts exactly at what used to be the processional's ceremonial endpoint, however briefly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its footprints, days later, are still faintly warm to the touch."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its march, unbroken, is heading straight for a populated ruin-camp that has no idea it's coming."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["striking the flagstones in a rhythm centuries out of step with any living calendar", "marching a ceremonial road that hasn't existed as a road in generations"]},{"name":"Basalt Gaze of the Garden","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"snake-haired guardian posing as garden statuary","flavor":"Cursed by the same magic that petrified the garden's statuary, she has become one more monument in a courtyard full of them — until she moves.","desc":"She stands among the courtyard's other statuary so convincingly that you'll walk past her twice before the third glance catches a tremor in stone that shouldn't move. Snake-hair coils slow against her shoulders, testing the air. The same curse that petrified the garden made her one more monument in it — until she turns to look at you.","traits":{"note": "Anyone who meets her gaze directly, rather than by reflection or averted glance, risks her full curse.", "actions": [{"name": "Garden Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Coiling Bite", "replaces": "Snake Hair", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Petrifying Gaze", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "The Gaze targets one creature within 30 feet that can see her. The target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or begin turning to stone, gaining the Restrained condition and repeating the save at the end of its next turn. On a second failure the target has the Petrified condition permanently; on a success the effect ends."}, {"name": "Statuary Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Gaze makes one Garden Claw attack and one Coiling Bite attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants a specific statue in the courtyard destroyed — a rival she petrified and regrets."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A merchant's guide, mid-tour, has just realized one of the statues moved and is fleeing toward the party."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's guarding a petrified figure who holds a key the party specifically needs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She mistakes the party for the garden's original architects, returning at last."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A petrification cure, half-finished, sits abandoned nearby — someone was already working on her victims."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll bargain a petrified ally's restoration for safe passage through her garden, once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of the 'statues' in the courtyard is still faintly breathing, trapped mid-turn."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Her curse is spreading past her control now — nearby plants are calcifying on their own."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "forest"],"activity":["standing among the courtyard's other statuary, convincing enough to walk past twice", "testing the air with slow-coiling snake-hair before finally turning to look at you"]},{"name":"Coiled Warden of the Inner Vault","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"guardian-naga","model":"guardian-naga","summary":"giant guardian serpent coiled around the vault door","flavor":"A serpentine spirit bound by the builders to guard the innermost vault, ancient and imperturbably patient with intruders.","desc":"Its coils fill the passage in front of the vault door, ancient scales dulled to the color of old bronze, head raised at exactly the height of your eyes. The builders bound it here to outlast them, and it has. It watches you with the imperturbable patience of something that has never once needed to move first.","traits":{"note": "It was bound to outlast the builders, not to serve any master now living — it answers to no one.", "actions": [{"name": "Vault-Guard Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Bronze Spittle", "replaces": "Poisonous Spittle", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 22 (4d10) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Warden's Working", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Warden casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components and using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 16): At Will: Hold Person, Suggestion; 1/Day: Wall of Stone."}, {"name": "Coiled Response", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Warden makes one Vault-Guard Bite attack and uses Bronze Spittle."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales have dulled to the exact bronze of the vault door it coils before."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never moves first — it waits, imperturbable, for an intruder to act."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old binding-glyphs are worked into its underscales, faded but still visible."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has coiled in the exact same configuration for so long it's worn a groove in the floor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tests the air with a flicking tongue long before it ever raises its head."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It withdraws its coils, briefly, for anyone bearing the builders' original seal."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Behind it, the vault door has no keyhole at all — only its own name, in a dead script."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it and the vault door doesn't open — it seals forever, the Warden having been the key."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["filling the passage before the vault door, ancient scales dulled to old bronze", "raising its head to exactly the height of an intruder's eyes, unhurried"]},{"name":"Throne-Ape of the Fallen Grove","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-ape","model":"giant-ape","summary":"worshipped ape-god ruling the collapsed temple grove","flavor":"A colossal ape the ruin's people once worshipped as a living god; it still holds court over the collapsed temple grove, and it still expects tribute.","desc":"It holds court on a pile of collapsed masonry that used to be a temple, still expecting the tribute its worshippers stopped bringing generations ago. Its knuckles are the size of your skull and it drums them idly on stone whenever it's displeased. This was its grove before it was anyone's ruin, and it plans to keep it that way.","traits":{"note": "It expects tribute, not surrender — an offering left at the grove's edge may satisfy it entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Godly Fist", "replaces": "Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Temple-Stone Toss", "replaces": "Boulder Toss (Recharge 6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 24 (4d10 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it also has the Prone condition."}, {"name": "Grove Court", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ape makes two Godly Fist attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants tribute the party is currently carrying — food, drink, or shine will do."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A frightened worshipper's descendant is hiding nearby, still bringing offerings out of old habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a captured trespasser hostage on its masonry throne, unharmed but unreleased."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wounded from a recent fight with a rival beast and is shorter-tempered than usual."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It guards a cache of old temple gold it doesn't understand the value of, only the shine."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It accepts a mock coronation — kneeling before it — as full tribute, and stands down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It repeats three specific temple-words when displeased, in a language it can't possibly know."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A rival troop is closing on the grove, and the Ape wants the party's help holding its throne."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court atop a pile of collapsed masonry that used to be a temple", "drumming knuckles the size of a skull on stone whenever displeased"]},{"name":"Ever-Marching Automaton King","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"clay-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"golem king still guarding a throne that's empty","flavor":"A war-engine built in the last king's image to defend the throne room forever; its coronation speech still loops, garbled, from a mouth that was never meant to speak this long.","desc":"A garbled coronation speech loops from a mouth that was never built to speak this long, syllables worn down to static by centuries of repetition. It was cast in the last king's image to defend a throne room that has nothing left to defend. Its clay joints have cracked and been patched with clay again, over and over, for longer than any dynasty lasted.","traits":{"note": "Its clay has been patched with clay again and again — a heavy blow may crack old repairs loose.", "actions": [{"name": "Coronation Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Royal Procession", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The King makes two Coronation Slam attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its garbled coronation speech has worn down to static, barely words anymore."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its clay joints have been patched with clay again, over and over, for longer than any dynasty."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still wears a crown, fused to its head, corroded green with age."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It postures toward an empty throne between attacks, some old defensive instinct."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footfalls have worn a permanent set of prints into the throne room floor."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses, briefly confused, if addressed by the correct old royal title."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The throne it guards is warm to the touch, though nothing has sat in it for centuries."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its clay core doesn't stop moving — it just stops looking like a king."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["looping a garbled coronation speech from a mouth never built to speak this long", "striking the throne room floor in patrol steps that predate any living memory"]},{"name":"Apex Titan-Lizard","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"tyrannosaurus-rex","model":"tyrannosaurus-rex","summary":"apex tyrant-lizard ruling the collapsed dome","flavor":"The garden's true owner now — a saurian titan that has claimed the collapsed dome as its den, indifferent to the empire whose bones it sleeps on.","desc":"It has claimed the collapsed dome as a den, sleeping across the bones of an empire it has no notion ever existed. Broken columns crack under its shifting weight like kindling. It doesn't rule here out of ambition — it simply never met anything that told it no.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Titan Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d10 + 7) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Sweeping Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Apex Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Titan-Lizard makes one Titan Bite attack and one Sweeping Tail attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broken columns crack under its shifting weight like nothing more than kindling."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's claimed the collapsed dome as a den, indifferent to what it was built for."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scars along its hide mark fights it clearly won, against things larger than a person."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sleeps most of the day, waking only at vibration through the ruined floor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's never once been driven off this den in living memory."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It ignores anything that doesn't come within its den's collapsed inner ring."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Beneath its bedding of rubble, something metal and untouched by rust still gleams."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its weight, shifting in fury, threatens to bring the entire collapsed dome down on everyone inside."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "forest"],"activity":["sleeping across the bones of an empire it has no notion ever existed", "cracking broken columns underfoot like kindling as it shifts its enormous weight"]},{"name":"The Unread King","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"the mummified god-king, cursed and finally waking","flavor":"The god-king himself, entombed with a dead language carved into his sarcophagus so no living mouth could ever again pronounce his true name — and no living hand could ever again wake him. Someone always finds a way.","desc":"The sarcophagus lid is carved in a dead script no living mouth could pronounce — that was the whole point, once. Now the seals are broken and the wrappings stir on their own, and something ancient and patient is remembering how to breathe. It rises the way stone settles: slow, certain, and past the point where anyone can stop it.","traits":{"note": "His curse is written across his own bindings in a dead script — read it aloud and it weakens him; no one has, in an age.", "actions": [{"name": "Dynasty's Grip", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this attack is bound into his court as an undead servant at the next dawn unless the curse is lifted."}, {"name": "Unread Decree", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The King speaks a line of his own unread curse. Each creature within 60 ft. that can hear makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature takes 22 (4d10) Necrotic damage and is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, its body obeying a law it cannot understand; half damage and no paralysis on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants his name read aloud correctly — the one thing that could finally let him die."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for the envoys of a kingdom that fell before their language existed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tomb's true treasure is the key to a curse spreading to the living city above."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands tribute in a currency no longer minted and will not hear that it's gone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scholar the party is escorting can read the script — and the King knows it the moment they arrive."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to make a party member his heir and read them into a power no living tongue remembers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The unread script covers the whole tomb, and it's slowly rewriting itself to include the party's names."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "His curse was never his alone — it's the seal holding a buried age shut, and his waking is the first page of it reopening under the whole region."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "cave"],"activity":["sitting a throne under a ceiling of a language no one alive can read", "rising by degrees as the last seal of his tomb finally fails"]},{"name":"The Standing Monument","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"colossus","summary":"gargantuan stone colossus that never stopped watching","flavor":"The greatest work of the vanished builders — a titan raised to watch the horizon until the world ended, animated by a will so patient it has outlasted every empire since, including the one that made it.","desc":"It was raised to watch the horizon until the world ended, and the world has tried several times since without managing it. Gargantuan and eroded, it still turns — one degree a decade, one degree a season, however fast its patience allows — toward whatever disturbs it. Every empire that built temples in its shadow is gone; the shadow remains.","traits":{"note": "It was raised to watch, not to hunt — it will not leave the horizon it was set to guard, whatever the cost.", "actions": [{"name": "Colossal Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 15 ft. Hit: 24 (3d10 + 8) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Watcher's Ray", "replaces": "Radiant Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +11, range 120 ft. Hit: 27 (6d8) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Age-Ending Beam", "replaces": "Divine Beam (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Monument unleashes light down a line 120 feet long and 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line makes a DC 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much on a success. A creature that fails by 10 or more is also Blinded until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Eternal Vigilance", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Monument makes two Colossal Slam attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's turning toward a distant threat the party can't yet see — and it's never once been wrong."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A settlement in its shadow worships its stillness and will beg the party not to wake it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its watching eye has fixed, for the first time in generations, on something the party is carrying."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scholars racing the party want to study its base inscriptions before it turns again and buries them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crack has opened along its foundation, and something below is trying to get out through it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It will hold its beam back, once, for anyone who can name the horizon-threat it still watches for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow falls the wrong direction for the sun's position, and has for longer than anyone's tracked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It has finally finished its turn after ages of degrees — and what it was built to watch for has arrived."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "mountain"],"activity":["turning one degree a decade toward whatever disturbs it, eroded but unbowed", "standing over a shadow that has outlasted every empire that once built temples in it"]},{"name":"Sun-Baked Scrap Raptor","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"Small pack raptor darting between ruined stones","flavor":"A pack-hunting lizard the size of a hound, quick to swarm anything that stumbles.","desc":"Small enough to hide behind a single fallen block, quick enough that you never see more than one at a time — until the rest call in from the ruins around you. Sun-bleached feathers blend into the rubble almost perfectly. It hunts in numbers it never lets you count.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Scrap-Yard Snap", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers blend so well into rubble you never see more than one at a time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hunts in numbers it never lets you count, calling the rest in only once committed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's small enough to hide behind a single fallen block, entirely out of sight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rusted bit of metal, swallowed whole, rattles faintly in its gut when it moves."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It nests in the collapsed foundations, dozens strong, unseen until roused."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It breaks off the hunt entirely if its numbers drop below three."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its calls, layered together, form an eerie echo of a language, almost words."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its full pack, once called, is easily three times what first appeared."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["hiding behind a single fallen block, sun-bleached feathers near-invisible against rubble", "calling in the rest of its pack from the ruins the instant something stumbles"]},{"name":"Feathered Sickle-Claw","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"axe-beak","model":"axe-beak","summary":"Feathered raptor slashing with a hooked hind claw","flavor":"A quick-footed hunter with a slashing rear claw, common in the temple scrub.","desc":"It holds one clawed foot cocked back off the ground as it stalks the temple scrub, saving the hooked hind talon for the killing stroke. Dust-colored feathers ripple along its spine when it tenses. The strike, when it lands, comes low and fast and from an angle you didn't expect.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sickle Strike", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Slashing damage from the hooked hind claw."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds its killing claw cocked back the entire stalk, never lowering it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust-colored feathers ripple visibly along its spine right before it commits to a strike."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors low, fast approaches from angles that keep it out of a target's eyeline."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's solitary, unlike most of its kind, and hunts the temple scrub alone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hind claw is chipped and re-sharpened from scraping against old temple stone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It disengages the moment it draws first blood, satisfied rather than hungry."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It circles counter-clockwise around prey, always, without apparent reason."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wounded badly, it flees toward the temple scrub's deep thicket — straight into a larger predator's territory."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["stalking the temple scrub with one clawed foot cocked back off the ground", "tensing along dust-colored feathers before the killing stroke lands from an unexpected angle"]},{"name":"Sickle-Toed Ambush Runner","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"rlm-sickle-toed-ambush-runner","summary":"Coordinated raptor pair flanking around fallen columns","flavor":"Coordinated raptors that flank prey between broken columns.","desc":"They come from both sides of the broken colonnade at once, flanking without a sound signal passing between them — pure instinct, honed over generations of driving prey between fallen pillars. One drives, one waits. You rarely see the second until it's already committed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Flanking Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, or 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage if the Runner has Advantage on the attack roll."}, {"name": "Paired Rush", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Runner makes two Flanking Bite attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One always drives the prey while the other waits, unseen, to commit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They flank without any sound signal passing between them — pure honed instinct."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They favor the broken colonnades specifically, generations of habit built around the cover."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "You rarely spot the second runner until the first has already struck."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They hunt in a mated pair and won't willingly separate for long."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Losing sight of its partner mid-hunt makes the remaining runner noticeably more cautious."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "They seem to know the colonnade's collapse points better than anyone who's mapped the plaza."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill one and the other doesn't flee — it howls, and something bigger answers from deeper in the ruin."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["flanking silently from both sides of a broken colonnade at once", "driving prey toward a second runner that waits, unseen, until it's already committed"]},{"name":"Withered Grave-Servant","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Shuffling tomb-slave still walking its funeral circuit","flavor":"A tomb-slave animated by lingering funerary rites, shuffling in endless circuits.","desc":"Its funeral circuit takes it past the same three tomb-doors, over and over, a duty its body remembers though the rites that bound it ended lifetimes ago. Grave wrappings hang in tatters from limbs gone the color of old rope. It doesn't attack so much as collide, indifferent to whether you're in its path.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blind Collision", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its funeral circuit passes the same three tomb-doors, over and over, without deviation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grave wrappings hang in tatters from limbs gone the color of old rope."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't attack so much as collide, indifferent to whatever's in its path."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rites ended lifetimes ago, but its body still keeps the old schedule exactly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a funerary token, fused to one withered hand, that it will not release."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses, briefly, at each tomb-door, as if waiting for a response that never comes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its circuit traces a shape that, from above, resembles a name in old script."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Block its circuit entirely and every grave-servant on the same funerary round converges on the blockage."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["shuffling the same funeral circuit past three tomb-doors, over and over", "colliding indifferently with anything in its path rather than attacking outright"]},{"name":"Salt-Cured Husk","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Salt-cured husk shambling with brittle relentlessness","flavor":"Preserved by desert salts rather than proper rites, brittle but relentless.","desc":"Desert salts did the preserving work no priest was left to perform, curing the corpse brittle instead of whole. Its skin has crystallized in patches that catch torchlight like broken glass. It moves in short, jerking lurches, and every one of them is stronger than it looks.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Brittle Lurch", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the Husk sheds a stinging cloud of salt crystals; the target has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its skin has crystallized in patches that catch torchlight like broken glass."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Desert salts did the preserving work no priest was left to perform."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves in short, jerking lurches, each one stronger than it looks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fine white residue trails it, crumbling off with every stiff step."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It cracks audibly at the joints, salt-crust flaking loose with each swing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Water thrown across it noticeably softens and slows it, if only for a moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Beneath the crust, its preserved features are disturbingly intact, almost peaceful."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shattered outright, it bursts into a stinging cloud of crystalline salt that coats everything nearby."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["shambling in short, jerking lurches, skin crystallized in patches that catch torchlight", "cured brittle by desert salts rather than any proper burial rite"]},{"name":"Rattling Ossuary Ward","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Wire-bound bones standing eternal watch over bones","flavor":"Bones bound with copper wire to stand eternal watch over an ossuary door.","desc":"Copper wire binds its bones tight enough that it rattles a full second before it moves, a warning bell built right into its joints. It stands eternal watch over an ossuary door stacked floor to ceiling with the dead it's meant to guard. The wire has gone green with age, but it hasn't loosened.","traits":{"note": "It rattles a full second before it moves — the wire binding doubles as a warning bell.", "actions": [{"name": "Wired Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Bone Bow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +2, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its copper wire has gone fully green, but the tension in it hasn't slackened at all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's missing its jaw entirely; it clacks its teeth against the roof of its skull instead."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A second set of wire loops trail from its wrists, remnants of manacles it outlasted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ribs have been packed with dried herbs, still faintly fragrant under the dust."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands exactly where the wire was staked, and won't cross that line even chasing prey."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It rattles in a specific rhythm — three short, one long — like it's still counting something."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wire hums faintly when struck, a note that seems to come from deeper in the ossuary."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sever its wire mid-fight and every bone in the stack behind it stirs at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["standing rigid in an ossuary niche, wire-bound bones rattling faintly with each breath of draft"]},{"name":"Loose-Jointed Tomb Archer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"rlm-loose-jointed-tomb-archer","summary":"Bone-guard still loosing arrows down the hall","flavor":"Old bone-guards still loosing arrows down processional halls.","desc":"Its bow-arm still draws and looses down the processional hall on a rhythm set into its bones generations ago, arrows nocked from a quiver that never quite empties. Joints clatter loose with each shot, held together by will more than sinew. It doesn't aim so much as fire along the line it was set to guard, and anything standing in that line is the target.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Processional Volley", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rib Shard", "replaces": "Bone Shard (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Piercing damage as it flings a shard torn from its own ribcage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its quiver is carved from the same bone as its arms — the arrows never seem to run out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It fires along a fixed line laid into the floor tiles, never adjusting the angle for a moving target."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One arm hangs a half-inch longer than the other, throwing every third shot slightly wide."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bowstring is braided hair, still dark despite everything else having gone to dust."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reloads with mechanical precision, three seconds exactly, like a metronome no one's listening to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hums the same three notes between shots — a marching cadence from a war no one remembers."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "When it runs dry of arrows, the quiver refills itself from a crack in the wall behind it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break its firing line even once and it abandons the rhythm entirely, closing to melee in a scramble of loose joints."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["loosing arrows down a processional hall on a rhythm set into its bones generations ago", "reaching for a shard of its own rib when the quiver's rhythm finally breaks"]},{"name":"Dune-Coiled Fang Serpent","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"rlm-dune-coiled-fang-serpent","summary":"Venomous serpent nesting in a cracked plinth","flavor":"Nests in cracked idol plinths, strikes at intruding feet.","desc":"It nests coiled inside a cracked idol plinth, scales the exact color of the surrounding sand, invisible until the strike. Venom beads visibly at its fangs even at rest. Disturb the plinth and you'll feel it before you see it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Plinth Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales carry a faint dusting of the exact sand it nests in, down to the grain."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Venom beads visibly at its fangs even fully at rest, dripping slow onto the plinth stone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's coiled around a small idol fragment, using the carved grooves as extra grip."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It strikes only at the foot that disturbs the plinth, ignoring hands and torches entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded ring of old bites mars the plinth's base — it's struck here before, more than once."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It flattens its hood against the stone in a shape that mimics the idol's carved eye above it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shed skin, wedged in the plinth crack, is patterned with faint symbols no snake should shed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crack the plinth open and a second serpent, larger and hungrier, uncoils from beneath the first."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["coiled invisible inside a cracked idol plinth, sand-colored scales betraying nothing until it strikes"]},{"name":"Constrictor of the Choked Aqueduct","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"constrictor-snake","model":"rlm-constrictor-of-the-choked-aqueduct","summary":"Heavy serpent squeezing prey against wet stone","flavor":"A heavy-bodied snake that squeezes prey against aqueduct stone.","desc":"It hangs coiled against wet stone where the aqueduct still weeps groundwater, scales slick and dark against the mineral streaks. The whole passage smells faintly of standing water and something dead nearby. It doesn't strike so much as fall, and then it doesn't let go.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Fall and Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is Grappled (escape DC 14)."}, {"name": "Aqueduct Coil", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., against a creature Grappled by it. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target can't breathe until the grapple ends."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales are dark and slick with a permanent sheen of mineral-heavy groundwater."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's wound around a corroded sluice-gate, using the ironwork as an anchor point."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The stretch of aqueduct it holds smells faintly of something dead further along the pipe."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't strike from above like its kin — it drops from a side-channel at ankle height."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scoring on the stone shows where past prey clawed for a grip that never came."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It releases prey the instant the water stops flowing, as if the current itself feeds it patience."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The groundwater around it never quite freezes, even where the rest of the passage frosts over."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startle it badly and it drops the coil entirely, thrashing the whole passage into the water below."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "cave"],"activity":["hanging coiled against weeping aqueduct stone, scales slick with groundwater and mineral streaks"]},{"name":"Sun-Cult Acolyte","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Robed acolyte chanting to unanswering old gods","flavor":"A robed devotee chanting to gods the ruins no longer answer.","desc":"A robed figure kneels before a sun-disk that hasn't answered a prayer in centuries, chanting anyway in a voice gone hoarse from repetition. The paint on the disk has flaked to bare stone. Faith, down here, has long since stopped requiring evidence.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's out of oil for the sun-disk's lamp and will beg passing strangers for any flame they carry."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-rite when disturbed and refuses to stop, arms raised, chanting straight through the interruption."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wound from a prior guardian is going bad under its robes, though it won't admit the rite matters less than the infection."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a satchel of grave-goods meant as an offering, and it'll trade the lot for safe passage out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something else in the ruin has been answering its prayers lately, and it wants a witness before anyone believes it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It mistakes the party for envoys sent by the sun itself and won't be talked out of the honor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The paint it's reapplying to the disk matches a pattern from a temple three days' travel from here."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its chant finally gets an answer mid-scene — the disk's flaked paint starts to glow, and it isn't done chanting."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["kneeling before a sun-disk that hasn't answered a prayer in centuries, chanting anyway in a hoarse voice"]},{"name":"Dead-Tongue Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest-acolyte","model":"rlm-dead-tongue-initiate","summary":"Initiate half-mad from an extinct liturgical tongue","flavor":"Trains in the extinct liturgical language, half-mad from isolation.","desc":"He mutters the liturgical language under his breath constantly now, even between rites, half-mad from years of isolated study in a tongue no one else living speaks. His eyes track motion but rarely seem to register what it means. He'll answer questions only in a language you can't understand.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Frantic Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Sear of the Dead Word", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Radiant damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lost the thread of a phrase mid-liturgy and won't move on until someone helps him finish it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a half-translated page he'll trade for anyone who can read three more words of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been sent to retrieve a specific relic and genuinely can't leave without it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member's accent for the dead tongue and won't stop trying to converse in it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His isolation has left him starving; he'll trade information for food before he'll fight for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He answers every question in the dead language, gesturing frantically when he means to be understood."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He repeats a phrase that, translated, is an exact description of the room the party is standing in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something in the ruin finally answers his liturgy back, in the same dead tongue, from somewhere close."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["muttering the extinct liturgical tongue under his breath even between rites, eyes tracking motion he doesn't register"]},{"name":"Scaled Temple-Guard","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-warrior","model":"orc-warrior","summary":"Hardened spear-guard sworn to a dead dynasty","flavor":"A hardened spear-bearer sworn to a dynasty centuries gone.","desc":"He's sworn an oath to a dynasty that ended before his grandfather was born, and he hasn't been told the vow expired. His spear is well-maintained despite the ruin of everything around him. He guards a door that leads to nothing now but rubble, and he takes the job seriously anyway.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dynasty's Axe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Oath-Thrown Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His spear is oiled and immaculate; nothing else on him has been maintained in a century."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He salutes any torch that passes, mistaking the light for a superior officer's signal."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His oath was sworn to a specific name he still recites before every challenge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He guards a door that opens onto nothing but rubble, and takes the post seriously regardless."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His armor bears a dynasty's crest, worn to a smooth curve where his thumb rests on the strap."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll stand down for the correct watchword — a password from a court centuries dead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He refers to intruders by rank and title, as if reading from a roster only he can see."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill him and his post is filled within the hour by another guard identical down to the crest."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["guarding a door that leads only to rubble now, spear immaculate despite the ruin around him"]},{"name":"Feather-Cloaked Sentinel","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"hobgoblin-soldier","model":"hobgoblin-soldier","summary":"Plumed sentinel marching the crumbling outer wall","flavor":"Marches the outer wall in molting ceremonial plumage.","desc":"Ceremonial plumage molts from his shoulders as he marches the crumbling outer wall in a pattern that once had honor guards flanking him and now has none. His boots follow a groove worn into the stone by decades of the same route. He salutes fallen colonnades as if someone were still watching.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wall-Sworn Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Plumed Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ceremonial plumage molts from his shoulders with every stride, leaving a faint trail along the wall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His boots follow a groove worn ankle-deep into the stone by decades of the same route."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He salutes fallen colonnades at precise intervals, as if someone were still posted there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His plumage is dyed a color that hasn't been fashionable, or affordable, in generations."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He breaks formation only to correct a stone that's slipped out of alignment, then resumes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He challenges intruders with a rank-and-file drill question, expecting a specific countersign."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wall he patrols shows fresher mortar exactly where his route turns, as if it's been repaired recently."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break his patrol rhythm and every remaining plume on his cloak ignites at once, a last defensive flare."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["marching the crumbling outer wall in a pattern once flanked by an honor guard that's long gone"]},{"name":"Idol-Cracked Jackal","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"jackal","model":"rlm-idol-cracked-jackal","summary":"Scavenger jackal denning beneath a toppled idol","flavor":"A scavenger pack that dens beneath toppled idols.","desc":"The pack dens beneath a toppled idol's outstretched arm, using the stone as shade and shelter both. They're smaller than the plaza jackals, quicker to scatter, quicker to circle back. A low growl rises from the shadow under the idol before you see a single one of them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Snapping Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pack is smaller and quicker to scatter than the jackals up in the open plaza."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They circle back the moment prey turns away, quicker than their scattering suggests."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their den beneath the idol's arm is lined with scraps too old to identify."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One always stays at the den mouth, growling, while the rest range out to hunt."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They avoid the idol's cracked face entirely, denning only in its shadow, never its gaze."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They yip in a pattern that other pests in the ruin seem to recognize and answer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Their eyes catch torchlight with a faint gold cast, like the idol's paint got into their blood."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten the den directly and the whole pack abandons the scatter-and-circle pattern to swarm at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["denning beneath a toppled idol's outstretched arm, a low growl rising from the shadow before it's seen"]},{"name":"Grave-Wasp Nest Cluster","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-wasp","model":"rlm-grave-wasp-nest-cluster","summary":"Wasp nest swarming from a hollow sarcophagus","flavor":"Nests inside hollow sarcophagi, swarming any disturbance.","desc":"The hollow sarcophagus hums before it's disturbed — a low papery vibration that means the nest inside has already noticed you. Break the seal and the swarm boils out in a column thick enough to blot the torchlight. They don't stop at the lid; they follow.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grave Sting", "replaces": "Sting", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The sarcophagus hums with a low papery vibration before the seal is even touched."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The swarm boils out in a column thick enough to blot torchlight entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They don't stop at the lid — they follow anyone who runs, well past the sarcophagus."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The nest inside is built from chewed bandage-linen, layered thick as a drum skin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They favor open flame and torchlight, veering toward any light source in the chamber."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They calm within seconds of the sarcophagus lid being resealed, as if satisfied the job is done."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Dead wasps littering the sarcophagus floor are twice the size of the ones still swarming."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crush the nest itself and the swarm's fury doubles instead of scattering."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["humming faintly from inside a hollow sarcophagus, the nest already aware of footsteps nearby"]},{"name":"Chittering Reliquary Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Swarm","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"rlm-chittering-reliquary-swarm","summary":"Scarab swarm boiling from a cracked reliquary","flavor":"Scarabs boiling out of a cracked reliquary at the first footstep.","desc":"The reliquary's crack widens with a dry chittering sound just before the scarabs pour out, a black tide across the floor and up the walls both. It's a tomb-curse poured into a vessel generations ago, still doing its one job. It rises at the first footstep and doesn't stop until you're gone or it's satisfied you are.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Curse-Poured Bites", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The reliquary's crack widens with a dry chittering sound just before the scarabs pour free."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a tomb-curse poured into a vessel generations ago, still faithfully doing its one job."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't stop at the reliquary's edge — it follows until convinced the intruder is truly gone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The scarabs carry a faint metallic sheen, like the reliquary's silver got worked into their shells."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rises fastest toward anything carrying a relic matching the reliquary's original contents."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It retreats the instant the reliquary is resealed, funneling back in through the same crack."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Individual scarabs, examined closely, all bear the same faint symbol etched into their backs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage the reliquary itself and the swarm's chittering turns to a shriek, doubling its aggression."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["boiling out of a cracked reliquary at the first footstep, a black tide across floor and wall alike"]},{"name":"Rope-Fanged Pit Viper","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"venomous-snake","model":"rlm-rope-fanged-pit-viper","summary":"Coiled viper hidden in a false-bottomed coffin","flavor":"Coils in false-bottomed sarcophagi as a trap-maker's last defense.","desc":"The coffin's false bottom hides more than a trap-maker's final defense — it hides a coiled length of muscle and venom that strikes the instant the seal breaks. Its scales mimic the grain of old rope so closely you'll swear the coffin's binding just moved. One bite is all the trap needs to work.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Trap-Set Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 1 Piercing damage plus 6 (2d4 + 1) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales mimic the grain of old rope so closely the coffin's binding seems to shift on its own."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One bite is all the trap needs to work — it strikes once and retreats into the false bottom."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's coiled around a specific relic, positioned so any hand reaching for it meets fangs first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The false bottom it hides beneath still bears the trap-maker's tool marks, decades old."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes utterly still at any vibration that isn't the coffin lid, waiting out false alarms."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's paired with a second viper in a neighboring coffin, and the two seem to time their strikes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its venom leaves a faint residue that glows the same color as the reliquary paint nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Miss killing it outright and it vanishes back into the coffin seam, ready to strike again on the next approach."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["coiled in a false-bottomed coffin, scales mimicking old rope until the seal breaks and it strikes"]},{"name":"Choke-Vine Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"rlm-choke-vine-ambusher","summary":"Creeping vine blight rooted in cracked flagstone","flavor":"A creeping blight rooted in cracked temple flagstone.","desc":"It has rooted itself in a crack running the length of the temple flagstone, vines the color of dried blood coiled tight against the seam. It doesn't move to find prey — it waits for prey to walk across its patch of floor. The first vine wraps an ankle before you notice the others are already moving.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blood-Vine Grasp", "replaces": "Constricting Vine", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13)."}, {"name": "Root-Spread Snare", "replaces": "Entangling Plants (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature within 15 ft. of it makes a DC 13 Strength save. On a failure a creature is Restrained by writhing vines until it or another creature uses an action to break it free (DC 13 Strength)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rooted in a flagstone crack running the temple's length, vines coiled tight against the seam."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't move to find prey — it waits for prey to cross its patch of floor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The first vine wraps an ankle before you notice the others are already moving."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its vines are the color of dried blood, dark enough to vanish against the temple's stone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fed well recently — several vine-tips still hold the shape of a clenched grip."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It releases anything that stops struggling, mistaking stillness for something already dead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its roots trace back through the crack to a much older growth deeper in the flagstone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut its main root and every vine in reach lashes out at once in a final, blind spasm."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "forest", "swamp"],"activity":["rooted in a flagstone crack, vines the color of dried blood waiting for a footstep across its patch"]},{"name":"Spore-Choked Idol Fungus","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"shrieker-fungus","model":"rlm-spore-choked-idol-fungus","summary":"Idol fungus shrieking to summon every guardian","flavor":"Shrieks a warning when disturbed, drawing every guardian in earshot.","desc":"It grows straight out of an idol's open mouth, a pale bloom that looks decorative until something brushes it. The shriek that follows carries the length of the temple and draws every guardian within earshot. It doesn't attack; it just makes sure you're never alone in here for long.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't attack — a disturbance triggers a shriek that draws every guardian within earshot.", "actions": [{"name": "Spore Burst", "text": "The idol-fungus puffs a cloud of spores at one creature within 5 ft.; the target makes a DC 11 Constitution save or takes 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grows straight out of an idol's open mouth, pale and easy to mistake for decoration."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shriek carries the length of the temple, drawing guardians from rooms you haven't found yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't attack; it just ensures you're never alone down here for very long."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scorch marks around its base suggest past intruders tried burning it out first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint ring of spores has settled on the floor beneath it, undisturbed for a long while."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It shrieks at torchlight alone, no touch required, if the flame gets close enough."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bloom pulses faintly in time with something moving deeper in the temple, unseen."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its shriek this time doesn't fade — it keeps sounding, faint, from every idol mouth in the hall."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["blooming pale and decorative from an idol's open mouth, waiting for a brush of contact"]},{"name":"Loincloth Grave-Robber","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"Desperate local looting the same cursed tombs","flavor":"A local desperate enough to loot the same tombs the party is exploring.","desc":"He's dug his way in from a collapsed side-passage, canvas sack half-full of the same relics you came for. Desperation shows plainer than greed on his face — this is a meal, not a fortune, and he knows it. He'll fight for the sack before he'll run from you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Desperate Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Snap-Aimed Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d8) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a family waiting on the surface and this haul is the only meal he can promise them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already wounded from a trap two rooms back and is bleeding through a hasty bandage."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll offer to split the sack fifty-fifty rather than risk a fight he knows he'll lose."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a crude map of the collapsed passage he dug through, useful and half-wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's terrified of something further in and would rather explain that than fight over relics."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers up a name — a fence in the nearest town who'll buy anything unmarked."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His sack holds one item that doesn't match the tomb's era at all, out of place and new."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's not alone — two more diggers surface from the same collapsed passage the moment things get loud."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["digging in through a collapsed side-passage, canvas sack half-full of the same relics you came for"]},{"name":"Whisper-Idol Cultist Fanatic","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Fanatic convinced the silent idols still listen","flavor":"Speaks in the dead tongue and believes the idols still listen.","desc":"She speaks in the dead tongue with total conviction, certain the silent idols around her are still listening even after everyone else stopped believing that. Ritual scarring runs down both forearms in patterns matching the temple's carvings. Zealotry, not skill, is what makes her dangerous.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Idol-Bound Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants a witness to the idols speaking, certain everyone else stopped listening too soon."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's carrying a captive scholar meant as an offering, and won't let the party interfere quietly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's fleeing a rival cult cell and will use the party as a shield without asking."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She mistakes a party member's silence for the idol's own approval and won't stop testing it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's carrying a fragment of carved stone she believes is the idol's actual voice, and guards it fiercely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll trade a genuine piece of ruin-lore for anyone willing to kneel and listen with her, briefly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her ritual scars, traced closely, match the temple's carvings symbol for symbol."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something answers her chant mid-fight, faint and wordless, from a wall that shouldn't be able to speak."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["speaking in the dead tongue with total conviction, ritual scarring running down both forearms"]},{"name":"Broken-Fang Wererat Tomb-Rat","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"rlm-broken-fang-wererat-tomb-rat","summary":"Cursed looter scurrying tunnels as vermin","flavor":"A cursed grave-looter who now scurries the tunnels as vermin by night.","desc":"By night it scurries the tunnels as vermin, and only the size gives it away — too big, too deliberate, too aware of where the traps are. It was a looter once, cursed for greed rather than trespass. It still remembers every passage it ever mapped, and it uses that against anyone following the same route.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Tunnel-Rat Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Cursed Bite and Broken Fang in any combination."}, {"name": "Cursed Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be cursed with wererat lycanthropy."}, {"name": "Broken Fang", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's a cursed grave-looter, and it still remembers every passage it ever mapped."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its size gives it away even in vermin form — too big, too deliberate, too aware of the traps."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It was cursed for greed rather than trespass, and it hasn't stopped hoarding since."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It uses its old looter's knowledge of the traps against anyone following the same route."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its human face, glimpsed briefly at moonrise, still bears a looter's guilty flinch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hoards small relics in a nest well off the main passages, never spending a single one."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It avoids one specific corridor entirely, the same one it was cursed in, still years later."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it and it abandons stealth completely, shifting fully and fighting with a cornered animal's total commitment."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["scurrying the tunnels as vermin by night, too large and too deliberate to be mistaken for one for long"]},{"name":"Stalking Sand-Ambusher","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"phase-spider","model":"rlm-stalking-sand-ambusher","summary":"Ambusher slipping through heat-mirage to strike","flavor":"Slips between the desert's heat-mirage and the material world to strike.","desc":"The desert's heat-mirage shivers wrong just before it steps through, a spider-shape half-real slipping out of the shimmer to strike. It's gone again before the dust it kicked up finishes settling. You never quite see where it went, only where it was.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Mirage Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Heat-Mirage Step", "text": "It can shift partway into the material plane, letting it move through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain and end its move on either side of a wall, floor, or similar barrier. It takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's gone again before the dust it kicked up finishes settling, leaving no clear track."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "You never quite see where it went, only where it was a moment before."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors striking from directly beneath the heat-shimmer of noon, when the mirage is thickest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its legs cast eight faint shadows in the shimmer, though only some of them are ever real."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles wide before every strike, using the mirage to mask the actual angle of approach."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It seems to test prey with a single glancing strike before committing to the kill."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Where it phases through solid stone, the stone briefly shows a spider-shaped absence, like a mold."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wound it badly enough and it stops retreating into the mirage, committing fully to a desperate final strike."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["stepping half-real out of a heat-mirage shiver to strike, gone again before the kicked dust settles"]},{"name":"Petrifying Serpent-Crowned Guardian","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"rlm-petrifying-serpent-crowned-guardian","summary":"Stone-eyed guardian that petrifies with a glance","flavor":"A carved-looking beast said to have once been a living guard, now stone-eyed.","desc":"It looks carved, the way half the statuary down here looks carved, until its eye finds yours across the chamber. Locals say it was once a living guard, and something about the stillness of its posture makes that easy to believe. Don't look back.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Guardian's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Stone-Eyed Gaze", "text": "At the start of each of its turns, it chooses a creature within 30 ft. that can see its eyes. That creature makes a DC 12 Constitution save. On a failure, the creature's flesh begins to harden; it has Disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws and can't use Reactions. On a second failed save (on a subsequent turn) the creature is Restrained and further failures continue the process until it is fully Petrified. A success ends the effect on that creature; a creature that averts its eyes has Disadvantage on the attack rolls it makes against the guardian until its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It looks carved, the way half the statuary down here looks carved, until it moves."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Locals say it was once a living guard, and the stillness of its posture makes that easy to believe."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Several stone figures nearby, on closer look, are past victims frozen mid-flinch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors the darkest corner of the chamber, where its eyes catch the least light to warn intruders."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scaled crown is cracked down the center, old damage that never quite healed over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It holds its gaze longer on anyone who's already looked away once, as if daring a second glance."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The stone figures around it are arranged in a rough circle, like an audience it once addressed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shatter one of its petrified victims and its crown flares, granting it a burst of furious, faster movement."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "cave"],"activity":["holding carved-still posture across the chamber until its eye finds yours and doesn't let go"]},{"name":"Vulture-Headed Carrion Priest","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"rlm-vulture-headed-carrion-priest","summary":"Vulture-masked priest presiding over excarnation rites","flavor":"Wears a vulture skull mask and presides over open-air excarnation rites.","desc":"A vulture skull mask hides his face as he presides over open-air excarnation rites atop a crumbling platform, ceremonial knife catching what little light reaches down here. The stink of the rite clings to everything around him. He doesn't stop the ceremony for intruders — he just adds them to it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rite Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Excarnation Javelin and Ceremonial Morningstar in any combination."}, {"name": "Excarnation Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ceremonial Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A vulture skull mask hides his face throughout the entire rite, never once removed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He doesn't stop the ceremony for intruders — he simply adds them to it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The stink of the rite clings to every surface within the platform's crumbling radius."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His ceremonial knife is honed to a mirror edge despite everything around it being ruin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He conducts the rite with careful, unhurried motions, as if an audience were still watching."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll pause the rite only for someone who can name the correct honorific for the dead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Real vultures circle the platform at a fixed altitude, never landing, never leaving either."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Interrupt the rite at its climax and the platform itself groans, threatening to give way beneath everyone."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["presiding over open-air excarnation rites atop a crumbling platform, ceremonial knife catching what light reaches down here"]},{"name":"Sarcophagus-Bound Wight Steward","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Undead steward still enforcing dead household order","flavor":"Once the mummy-king's chief steward, still enforcing an outdated household order.","desc":"He still enforces an outdated household order — proper distance from the sarcophagi, proper silence in the antechamber, proper deference to a household that's been dust for centuries. His voice carries the clipped formality of a servant who never once questioned his post. He corrects your posture before he attacks.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Steward's Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Correcting Longsword and Household Longbow in any combination, or replaces one attack with Draining Touch."}, {"name": "Draining Touch", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken, and the wight regains that many hit points."}, {"name": "Correcting Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Household Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He enforces proper distance from the sarcophagi as if a household staff still relied on the rule."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice carries the clipped formality of a servant who never once questioned his post."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He corrects an intruder's posture before attacking, out of pure old habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He still refers to empty rooms by the names of long-dead household members."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His uniform, rotted as it is, is folded with a precision no undead thing should still care about."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll accept a properly formal introduction before considering an intruder worth attacking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He addresses the empty antechamber by a title reserved for a king's chief steward — his own, apparently."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break protocol badly enough — raise a weapon in the antechamber — and his formality snaps into open fury."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["enforcing an outdated household order — proper distance, proper silence — with clipped, undead formality"]},{"name":"Blazing Ember-Skull Oracle","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"flameskull","model":"rlm-blazing-ember-skull-oracle","summary":"Astrologer's burning skull still muttering prophecy","flavor":"The severed head of a court astrologer, still muttering prophecy in fire.","desc":"A severed skull hovers wreathed in low blue flame, muttering fragments of prophecy between crackling pops of burning bone. It was a court astrologer once, and it still reads omens in the fire it's made of. The mutter never fully stops, even mid-fight.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ember Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two Fire Ray attacks."}, {"name": "Prophecy Ray", "replaces": "Fire Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30 ft. Hit: 11 (2d10) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Omen Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "It casts one of the following spells, requiring no material components, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save DC 13): At will: Detect Magic, Minor Illusion. 1/Day each: Fireball, Scrying."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It was a court astrologer once, and it still reads omens in the fire it's made of."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mutter never fully stops, even mid-fight, fragments of prophecy bleeding through the crackle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The flame it's wreathed in burns a low, steady blue that never seems to gutter."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles the chamber at a fixed height, as if still pacing an observatory that's long gone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scorch marks radiate from its favored perch, decades of muttered fire built up in one spot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It answers direct questions about the future in fragments that only make sense in hindsight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its prophecy fragments, strung together, seem to describe the exact fight it's currently losing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Reduced to embers, it flares one last time and gasps out a single complete, coherent prophecy."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "sky"],"activity":["hovering wreathed in low blue flame, muttering prophecy between crackling pops of burning bone"]},{"name":"Broken Wing Terror-Bird","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"giant-axe-beak","model":"giant-axe-beak","summary":"Flightless apex hunter ruling terraced garden ruins","flavor":"A flightless apex predator that once ruled the temple's terraced gardens.","desc":"It can't fly anymore — hasn't been able to for generations — but the terraced gardens it once ruled from above, it now rules from the ground with a stride longer than a man is tall. Its beak alone could open a shield. It moves at a speed the broken wings never suggest.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Terrace Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Sharpened Beak and Talons in any combination."}, {"name": "Sharpened Beak", "replaces": "Sharpened Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It can't fly anymore, hasn't been able to for generations, but its stride outpaces most things that can."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its beak alone could open a shield, and it uses that fact without hesitation."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It ranges the terraced gardens it once ruled from above, territorial down to the last overgrown tier."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its broken wings drag faint furrows through the garden soil wherever it walks."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves at a speed the ruined wings never suggest, closing distance faster than expected."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It nests eggs in the highest surviving terrace, and won't range far from that tier."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Feathers shed near its nest are patterned in a way that matches no living bird nearby."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten its nest tier directly and it abandons ground hunting entirely, charging in a single reckless line."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["striding the terraced gardens it once ruled from the air, now ruling them on foot with unnatural speed"]},{"name":"Vault-Sworn Ettin Doorkeeper","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"rlm-vault-sworn-ettin-doorkeeper","summary":"Two-headed brute oath-bound to guard one door","flavor":"Two-headed brute chained by old oath to guard a single vault door.","desc":"Two heads argue in low tones about whether you're worth the effort, chained by an old oath neither of them remembers agreeing to. The chain has rusted into the stone floor around a single vault door. Whatever's inside, it's guarded by something that has had centuries to get tired of guarding it and hasn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Doorkeeper Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Battleaxe and Morningstar in any combination, one with each head."}, {"name": "Battleaxe", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two heads argue in low tones about whether you're worth the effort, chained by an old oath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Neither head remembers agreeing to the oath, only that breaking it isn't an option."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chain has rusted into the stone floor around a single, unremarkable-looking vault door."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's had centuries to get tired of guarding the door, and it visibly hasn't."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head sleeps in shifts while the other keeps watch, an old arrangement neither questions."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll bargain for a story it hasn't heard before, in exchange for a few minutes' delay."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The vault door behind it is warm to the touch, despite the ambient cold of the chamber."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage the door directly and both heads stop arguing entirely, fighting now in perfect coordination."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "mountain", "cave"],"activity":["arguing in low tones with itself over whether an intruder is worth the effort, chained to a single vault door"]},{"name":"Weretiger Jungle-Stalker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"weretiger","model":"rlm-weretiger-jungle-stalker","summary":"Cursed hunter prowling the ruin's jungle canopy","flavor":"A cursed hunter who prowls the jungle canopy above the ruin.","desc":"Something moves through the canopy that's grown up above the ruin, silent between branches that shouldn't bear that much weight. Stripes flicker between shadow and sun in a rhythm that's almost hypnotic to track. It prowls the high growth the way it once prowled a jungle that predates the ruin itself.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Canopy Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks, using Tiger Bite and Scratch in any combination, or one Scratch and uses Longbow in Humanoid or Hybrid form."}, {"name": "Tiger Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Tiger or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Ambush Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves through the canopy silent between branches that shouldn't bear that much weight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stripes flicker between shadow and sun in a rhythm that's almost hypnotic to track."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It once prowled a jungle that predates the ruin itself, and still hunts by those old instincts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors the high growth, only descending to ground level to finish a wounded chase."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Claw-marks on the higher trunks mark a territory boundary it patrols religiously."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "In its human form it speaks courteously, almost apologetically, about the hunt to come."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its curse seems tied to the ruin's canopy specifically — it weakens noticeably if driven to open ground."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it against the canopy's edge and the hybrid form breaks fully loose, fighting without restraint."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["moving silent through the canopy grown up above the ruin, stripes flickering between shadow and sun"]},{"name":"Cracked-Idol Gargoyle Watcher","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"gargoyle","model":"gargoyle","summary":"Stone guardian animated by residual sun-magic","flavor":"A stone temple guardian animated by residual sun-god magic.","desc":"Residual sun-god magic keeps it moving long after the temple that made it lost its priests, stone wings folded tight against a cracked back. It perches motionless for hours, indistinguishable from decoration, until the light shifts and it doesn't. Dust sifts from the crack whenever it stretches.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Watcher Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two Sun-Cracked Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Sun-Cracked Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Radiant damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Residual sun-god magic keeps it moving long after the temple that made it lost its priests."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust sifts from a crack in its back whenever it stretches out of its perch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's indistinguishable from decoration for hours at a stretch, wings folded tight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reacts only to a shift in the light, ignoring sound and movement entirely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stone surface is warm to the touch on the side that faces the temple's old sun-shaft."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It settles back into stillness the instant direct sunlight returns to the chamber."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crack down its back has widened slightly since the temple's sun-shaft last aligned."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Block the temple's sun-shaft during the fight and it seizes up mid-motion, magic guttering."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["perching motionless for hours, indistinguishable from decoration, until the light shifts and it doesn't"]},{"name":"Ash-Grey Ochre Seep","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"ochre-jelly","model":"rlm-ash-grey-ochre-seep","summary":"Corrosive ooze seeping through burial-chamber cracks","flavor":"Seeps through cracks in the burial chamber floor, dissolving the careless.","desc":"It seeps through hairline cracks in the burial chamber floor before you notice the floor has cracks at all, a slow grey advance that dissolves anything careless enough to stand still. The smell is mineral, almost sweet. By the time you see the sheen on the stone, it's already closer than it looks.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Corrosive Seep", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Acid damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It seeps through hairline cracks before you notice the floor has cracks at all."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The smell is mineral, almost sweet, a poor warning for what's actually approaching."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "By the time you see the sheen on the stone, it's already closer than it looks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dissolved a shallow channel into the burial chamber floor over years of the same slow route."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It avoids metal instinctively, flowing around dropped weapons rather than through them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It retreats from open flame far faster than it advances toward prey."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Where it's passed, the stone underneath is left oddly smooth, almost polished."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Split it with a blow and both halves keep advancing independently, doubling the front it covers."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["seeping through hairline cracks in the burial chamber floor, a slow grey advance dissolving anything careless"]},{"name":"Hollow-Coffer Gelatinous Vault","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"rlm-hollow-coffer-gelatinous-vault","summary":"Cube-shaped ooze absorbing centuries of grave goods","flavor":"Fills an entire tomb corridor, absorbing centuries of grave goods.","desc":"It fills the entire corridor wall to wall, translucent and patient, centuries of grave goods suspended inside it like specimens in murky glass. Coins and bone fragments drift past each other in its gut. It doesn't hunt so much as occupy — and the corridor was never wide enough to go around it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Vault Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Acid damage."}, {"name": "Coffer Engulf", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "It moves up to its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks and moves into a Large or smaller creature's space. That creature makes a DC 14 Dexterity save. On a failure, it takes 10 (3d6) Acid damage and is engulfed; an engulfed creature is Restrained, can't breathe unless it can hold its breath, and takes 10 (3d6) Acid damage at the start of each of its turns. On a success, the creature is pushed to an unoccupied space."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It fills the entire corridor wall to wall, translucent and patient."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coins and bone fragments drift past each other in its gut like specimens in murky glass."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't hunt so much as occupy — the corridor was never wide enough to go around it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Centuries of grave goods are suspended inside it, most too deep in to reach safely."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It advances at a glacial, near-imperceptible pace, closing the corridor an inch at a time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It parts slightly around anything already dissolved past recognition, as if uninterested in the scraps."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A shape near its center, half-dissolved, is unmistakably still wearing a signet ring."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage it badly enough and it disgorges a portion of its held treasure in a corrosive splash."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["filling a tomb corridor wall to wall, centuries of grave goods drifting suspended inside it like specimens"]},{"name":"Chain-Bound Barrow Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"rlm-chain-bound-barrow-ghast","summary":"Ravenous ghast once serving the king's table","flavor":"A ravenous grave-thing that once served the mummy-king's table.","desc":"Rotted chains still hang from wrists that once served at the mummy-king's table, dragging with every ravenous lunge. Whatever manners it had in life are long gone, replaced by an appetite that recognizes no rank. It moves faster than the chains suggest it should be able to.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ravenous Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Chain-Dragged Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage. A Medium or smaller creature hit by this attack must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute (repeat save at end of each turn)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rotted chains still hang from wrists that once served at the mummy-king's table."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whatever manners it had in life are long gone, replaced by an appetite that recognizes no rank."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves faster than the dragging chains suggest it should be able to."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chains catch on debris constantly, and it never once stops to free them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform, what's left of it, still bears a household crest beneath the grime."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates half a beat before attacking anyone dressed like household staff, old instinct flickering."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The chains, examined closely, are inscribed with a name that matches no known steward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sever its chains mid-fight and it moves with sudden, unshackled speed, appetite fully unleashed."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["dragging rotted chains from wrists that once served at the mummy-king's table, lunging with total appetite"]},{"name":"Bandaged Falconry Ghast","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"rlm-bandaged-falconry-ghast","summary":"Ghast tending the tomb's mummified hunting birds","flavor":"Handles the tomb's mummified hunting birds with rotted, careful hands.","desc":"It tends the tomb's mummified hunting birds with a careful, rotted gentleness at odds with everything else about it, arranging feathers on creatures that will never fly again. The birds' glass eyes seem to track alongside its own. Interrupt the ritual and the gentleness disappears entirely.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Falconer's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Rotted Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage. A Medium or smaller creature hit by this attack must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute (repeat save at end of each turn)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tends the tomb's mummified hunting birds with a careful, rotted gentleness."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It arranges feathers on creatures that will never fly again, patient and precise."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The birds' glass eyes seem to track alongside its own, unnervingly attentive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Interrupt the ritual and the gentleness disappears entirely, replaced by raw hunger."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a small perch of real bones set aside, untouched, as if saving them for later."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It calms noticeably if left alone near its birds, losing interest in a fight it was forced into."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of the mummified birds twitches faintly whenever the ghast is struck, as if it shares the pain."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Harm one of its birds directly and it abandons all restraint, attacking with pure, screeching fury."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["arranging feathers on mummified hunting birds with careful, rotted hands, gentleness at odds with its hunger"]},{"name":"Toppled Minotaur Skeleton Guard","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-skeleton","model":"rlm-toppled-minotaur-skeleton-guard","summary":"Skeletal labyrinth-guardian still pacing its maze","flavor":"The bones of a labyrinth-guardian, still pacing its maze in death.","desc":"Bone horns scrape the low ceiling as it paces a maze that collapsed generations before its flesh did, tracing the same dead-end turns from memory alone. It doesn't seem to notice the walls are gone. It still knows every corner of a labyrinth that no longer exists.","traits":{"note": "It walks the maze's old path even mid-fight; corner it against a real wall and it hesitates half a beat.", "actions": [{"name": "Horn-Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d12 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is Large or smaller and the Guard moved at least 10 feet straight toward it, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) Piercing damage and is pushed 5 feet."}, {"name": "Bone-Fist Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its horns are notched from decades of scraping the same low doorway."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drags one hoof, worn thin from tracing the identical turn for centuries."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cracked thread of red yarn still trails from one bony wrist."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ribs are packed with dried moss from the maze's long-gone hedges."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It counts its steps aloud in a clicking, wordless rattle of teeth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Walking its exact remembered path past it, unchallenged, lets you slip by entirely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a few strides its hooves land on walls only it can still perceive."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break its rhythm and it forgets the maze entirely, attacking anything that moves."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["pacing a maze of walls that collapsed centuries ago, tracing turns from memory alone", "stopping dead when a footstep lands on a corner it still remembers as a wall"]},{"name":"Grave-Silk Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"rlm-grave-silk-poltergeist","summary":"Poltergeist hurling urns at silence-breakers","flavor":"Hurls funerary urns and shrouds at anyone who breaks tomb silence.","desc":"Funerary urns lift off their shelves on their own and fly the moment tomb silence breaks, shrouds snapping like sails in a wind that isn't there. Nothing solid throws them — just an angry absence in the room's cold air. It escalates fast, and it doesn't tire.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Urn Barrage", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from a hurled funerary urn, and shattered pottery cuts for an extra 2 (1d4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Shroud Snap", "replaces": "Telekinetic Thrust", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Force damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone as a burial shroud whips around its legs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only ever throws urns from its own original shelf, never borrowing another's."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The shrouds it flings still smell faintly of the incense used at the burial."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It goes quiet the instant everyone in the room stops moving entirely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cold spots mark its path across the floor, visible as frost on old dust."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never crosses the threshold of the chamber it was buried to guard."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Humming the same three notes as the funerary chant calms it for a few seconds."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every urn it throws reassembles itself, unbroken, back on the shelf by morning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break enough urns and it stops throwing them and comes for you with bare cold hands."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["holding dead still in a shelf of urns, waiting for the room's silence to break", "hurling a shroud across the chamber the instant a footstep echoes too loud"]},{"name":"Zombie-Herd Elephant Carrier","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-zombie","model":"rlm-zombie-herd-elephant-carrier","summary":"Shambling zombie beast still hauling grave-cart chains","flavor":"A shambling beast of burden still hauling grave-cart chains.","desc":"Grave-cart chains still drag from a rotted harness as the great beast hauls a cart that lost its wheels centuries ago, driven by nothing but habit written into dead muscle. Its hide has gone the grey of ash. It doesn't notice obstacles; it simply keeps pulling through them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chain-Weighted Trunk", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from a rusted grave-chain still looped around its trunk."}, {"name": "Cart-Drag Fling", "replaces": "Fling", "text": "The Carrier grabs a creature it hit this turn (Large or smaller) and hurls it up to 15 feet. The target takes 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage and lands Prone; a creature it hits on landing takes the same damage and must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or also fall Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cart's ruined axle still scrapes two grooves into the stone behind it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ash-grey hide has flaked away entirely across both flanks."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a rider's saddle, empty, cinched tight from a rider long gone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tusks are wrapped in the same funeral cloth as the cart it drags."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It plods in a perfectly straight line, indifferent to any wall in its path."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Unhitching its cart chain calms it into simply standing, riderless and still."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cart it drags is empty, yet its bed rocks like something inside shifts."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Anything that blocks its route gets trampled flat with no change in its pace."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["hauling a wheelless cart through rubble, harness chains dragging sparks off stone", "plodding the same grave-road route it walked in life, obstacles be damned"]},{"name":"Snake-Cult Priest of the Hollow Coil","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-snake-cult-priest-of-the-hollow-coil","summary":"Priest whose chants summon serpents from below","flavor":"Leads chants that draw serpents up from the temple's foundations.","desc":"His chant draws a slow hiss up from cracks in the temple foundation, and the hiss keeps getting closer the longer he's allowed to keep speaking. Scale-patterned tattoos run the length of both arms. Silence him fast, or the foundation stops being empty.","traits":{"note": "Interrupting his chant mid-verse keeps the serpents below from ever fully surfacing.", "actions": [{"name": "Fanged Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage from serpent fangs bound into the head."}, {"name": "Coil-Fire Bolt", "replaces": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Fire damage that curls and hisses like scales as it burns."}, {"name": "Serpent Summons", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Priest chants a verse drawing serpents up through the foundation. If he completes three uninterrupted turns of chanting, two venomous snakes (use Constrictor Snake statistics, or CR 1/4 equivalent) rise from the nearest crack in the floor."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's one verse from finishing his chant when the party arrives, and he won't stop for anything."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cultist runner is due any minute with a captive meant for the coil-pit below."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding a cracked seal that, if it opens fully, floods the lower temple with snakes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His arm is freshly fang-scarred; the serpents he calls don't always heed him back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a temple key the party needs, sewn into his sleeve against his own cult's rules."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll trade the location of the cult's hidden stash for safe passage out, and he means it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow moves half a beat behind him, coiling like it has a spine of its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing him mid-chant doesn't stop it — the crack keeps widening on its own now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["chanting over a foundation crack, the hiss beneath it climbing louder with each verse", "tracing scale tattoos with a bloodied thumb before beginning the summoning chant again"]},{"name":"Sacrificial Blind Prophet","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"orc-blind-prophet","model":"rlm-sacrificial-blind-prophet","summary":"Blind prophet claiming to speak for a buried god","flavor":"Claims to speak for a god buried under the plaza; sometimes right.","desc":"He claims a god lies buried beneath the plaza and speaks with the total certainty of someone who has never once been proven wrong about it. Milk-white eyes track sound rather than shape. Sometimes, uncomfortably, he's right.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Blind Spear-Thrust", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. The Prophet has advantage on this attack against any creature that has moved or made noise since his last turn."}, {"name": "Buried God's Voice", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Prophet speaks with a borrowed weight. One creature within 30 ft. that can hear him makes a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or is Frightened of him until the end of its next turn, certain for a moment that the ground itself is judging it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's chosen today's sunset for a sacrifice, and the party arrived within the hour."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lost his sighted acolyte and desperately needs eyes he can trust, or bully."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He correctly predicts one true thing about the party the moment they arrive, unsettling them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival prophet is due at the plaza to challenge his claim on the buried god."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a sealed offering box he insists must reach the seam before nightfall."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll guide the party safely through the plaza's traps if they carry his offering for him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The plaza stones warm faintly under his bare feet as he walks, like something answers him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The seam beneath the plaza cracks wider the moment he's struck, spilling heat and old dust."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing over the plaza's central seam, insisting a god breathes just beneath the stone", "tilting his head to track your footsteps long before you've spoken a word"]},{"name":"Wrapped Gladiator of the Sun Pit","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"rlm-wrapped-gladiator-of-the-sun-pit","summary":"Undying champion still dueling a vanished crowd","flavor":"An undying champion still fighting exhibition duels for a vanished crowd.","desc":"He still fights exhibition duels in an arena with no crowd left to watch, bandaged limbs moving with a showman's flourish that centuries of solitude never wore down. Old chains of office rattle at his wrists between strikes. He salutes an empty box before every bout, including this one.","traits":{"note": "He will not strike a downed foe who yields loudly enough for an absent crowd to hear.", "actions": [{"name": "Arena Spear", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ceremonial Shield Bash", "replaces": "Shield Bash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet and knocked Prone, to the roar of a crowd only he can hear."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His bandages are dyed the faded colors of a champion's house long since fallen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He announces his own entrance in a booming, echoing showman's voice."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old chains of office rattle at both wrists with every strike he lands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He bows to each corner of the arena before ever raising his spear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He refuses to fight anyone who hasn't formally stepped inside the ring's line."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Praising his form mid-fight, loudly, makes him ease off and showboat instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment, faint applause seems to ripple from the pit's empty stone seats."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break the arena's unspoken rules and he stops performing and fights to actually kill."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["saluting an empty judge's box before squaring up against whoever entered the pit", "circling a fresh opponent with a showman's flourish, bandages trailing like a cape"]},{"name":"Bog-Sunk Umber Digger","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"umber-hulk","model":"umber-hulk","summary":"Tunneling digger whose gaze cracks minds below","flavor":"Tunnels beneath the temple, its gaze cracking minds through cracked floors.","desc":"Tunnels open in the temple floor without warning, and the thing that made them looks up through the new gap with eyes that crack minds through the crack alone. Chitinous claws the size of shovels have carved half the passages beneath this ruin. Don't meet its gaze; look at your feet instead.","traits":{"note": "Its gaze cracks minds through any gap it's opened — keep eyes down near any hole in the floor.", "actions": [{"name": "Shovel-Claw Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Mind-Cracking Gaze", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Each creature within 30 feet that can see the Digger's eyes through a floor gap makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, a creature is Confused until the end of its next turn as the crack-lit stare unravels its thoughts. The Digger otherwise uses its Shovel-Claw Rend twice."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The crack it last opened is still warm, dust sifting steadily into the dark below."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shell is caked in a decade of temple-floor grit and old mortar dust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carved half the passages under this ruin without ever breaking the surface fully."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its claws leave shovel-wide gouges in any stone it tunnels through."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It retreats the instant sunlight reaches all the way down its tunnel."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Dropping rubble into its tunnel mouth draws it up angry but momentarily blind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes seem to glow faintly brighter the longer a victim refuses to look away."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Enough tunnels collapse at once that the whole chamber floor threatens to give way."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["surfacing through a fresh crack in the temple floor, mandibles testing the new air", "holding still just below a thin ceiling, waiting for footsteps to pass overhead"]},{"name":"Rot-Feathered Bulette Ambusher","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"Burrowing ambusher erupting under temple courtyards","flavor":"Erupts from beneath temple courtyards, scattering worshippers and looters alike.","desc":"The courtyard erupts without a sound of warning — no burrow-scrape, no shifting dust, just stone giving way and a maw the width of a cart underneath it. Worshippers and looters alike learned to walk the courtyard's edges the hard way. It surfaces once and dives again before you can plant your feet.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rot-Fanged Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d12 + 4) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage from feathers gone to rot along its jaw."}, {"name": "Courtyard Eruption", "replaces": "Deadly Leap", "text": "The Ambusher bursts up from beneath the ground within 30 feet, landing in an unoccupied space. Each creature within 10 feet of where it surfaces makes a DC 14 Strength saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) Bludgeoning damage and being knocked Prone on a failure, or half damage and no fall on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rotted feather-quills line its armored back where scale should be."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never surfaces twice in the same spot within a single fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw carries the broken tips of old spearheads embedded from past ambushes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sand pools in a faint ring on the surface just before it strikes from below."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hunts only where footsteps have crossed the same patch of courtyard twice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Standing dead still on solid stone, away from loose sand, denies it a clean strike."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rot on its feathers spreads faintly onto the very stone it bursts through."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Miss it once and it doesn't dive away — it keeps surfacing again and again, relentless."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["waiting under the courtyard's cracked flagstones, utterly silent, utterly still", "erupting through stone in a single burst before diving back beneath the sand"]},{"name":"Sun-Forged Earth Colossus Fragment","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"earth-elemental","model":"earth-elemental","summary":"Animate wall-shard powered by buried sun-forges","flavor":"A shard of an ancient wall given animus by buried sun-forges.","desc":"A single shard of an ancient wall has taken on a will of its own, powered by forge-heat still banked somewhere in the foundations below. It moves in slow, grinding lurches, mortar cracking loose with every step. It was part of a building once, and it still thinks like one — immovable, until it isn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wall-Shard Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d10 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Sunstone Launch", "replaces": "Rock Launch", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60/240 ft. Hit: 16 (3d10) Bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage from a sun-forge ember still lodged in the hurled stone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded fresco still clings, half-legible, to its broad stone back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footfalls leave grinding scars matching the wall it broke away from."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks along its frame glow faint orange, banked forge-heat leaking through."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands motionless for hours, mistaken for rubble until something disturbs it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves to defend the same stretch of wall it was chiseled from, nothing else."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pressing a matching shard back against its broken seam calms it, briefly, to stillness."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its cracks pulse warmer in rhythm with a heartbeat no living thing should share."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shatter it and the buried forge beneath vents a gout of heat straight up through the floor."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "mountain"],"activity":["grinding forward a slow half-step, mortar sifting loose from every cracked seam", "standing motionless against a wall, indistinguishable from the ruin until it moves"]},{"name":"Cinder-Font Fire Warden","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"Warden guarding the mummy-king's eternal brazier","flavor":"Guards the eternal brazier said to keep the mummy-king's tomb warm.","desc":"It guards a brazier said to keep the mummy-king's tomb warm through every century of his sleep, flame-limbs flickering low and steady around the coals. Heat rolls off it in visible waves that warp the passage air. It has never once let the fire go out, and it won't start with you.","traits":{"note": "It has never let the brazier go dark; smothering the coals directly draws its full fury.", "actions": [{"name": "Brazier-Fed Burn", "replaces": "Burn", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Fire damage, and a flammable object hit and not worn or carried by a creature ignites."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Heat rolls off it in waves that visibly warp the passage air around the brazier."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It banks the coals lower whenever no one's near, brighter when someone approaches."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its flame-limbs flicker in the exact rhythm of the tomb's original torchbearers' watch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scorch rings mark the floor in a perfect circle it has never once stepped outside."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums low, a tuneless warmth, when the brazier burns exactly as it should."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Feeding the brazier fresh fuel yourself earns a wary truce instead of a fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The coals it guards have never needed feeding, yet somehow never burn low."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Douse the brazier and it goes wild, flame-limbs spreading fire to anything nearby."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "elemental", "cave"],"activity":["circling a bed of coals that has never once gone cold, flame-limbs low and steady", "flaring brighter the instant cool air drafts in from an open passage"]},{"name":"Rope-Trap Roper of the Deep Shaft","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"roper","model":"roper","summary":"Stalactite-mimic lurking a deep excavation shaft","flavor":"Mimics a stalactite in the temple's deepest excavation shaft.","desc":"It hangs from the excavation shaft's ceiling looking exactly like a stalactite, mineral-streaked and utterly still, until a rope-thin tendril lashes out faster than the eye follows. By the time you notice the texture is wrong, it's already reeling something in. The shaft goes quiet again the instant it's fed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Shaft-Fang Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Stone-Streaked Tendril", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 30 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 14) if the Roper has fewer than five other creatures grappled."}, {"name": "Reel It In", "replaces": "Reel", "text": "The Roper pulls each creature grappled by it up to 25 feet straight toward it, and can then make one Shaft-Fang Bite attack against one of them."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old rope fragments from past victims still cling, fused, to its hide."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mineral streaks match the exact vein pattern of this specific shaft's stone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never strikes until prey has passed directly beneath its hanging position."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint dripping sound is the only warning before its tendril lashes out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The shaft floor below it is littered with the picked-clean bones of past meals."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Torchlight held steady on it for several seconds makes it flinch back into shadow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its stalactite shape sheds a faint trickle of water even in this bone-dry shaft."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut one tendril and the rest lash out at once, hauling in everything nearby."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "deeplands"],"activity":["hanging from the shaft ceiling, mineral-streaked and motionless as any stalactite", "lashing a rope-thin tendril out the instant something passes beneath it unaware"]},{"name":"Bloated Refuse-Idol Otyugh","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"otyugh","model":"otyugh","summary":"Refuse-fed horror lurking a forgotten temple well","flavor":"Feeds on centuries of temple refuse dumped down a forgotten well.","desc":"Centuries of temple refuse have been dumped down this forgotten well, and something down there has grown fat and patient on all of it. The smell alone announces it before the tentacles do. It doesn't chase — it simply waits for the well to be disturbed again.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Refuse-Fed Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Well-Tentacle", "replaces": "Tentacle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if it's Medium or smaller."}, {"name": "Refuse Slam", "replaces": "Tentacle Slam", "text": "The Otyugh slams a creature it's grappling against the well wall or floor. The target takes 9 (2d8) Bludgeoning damage and must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or contract a filth-borne sickness (as Disease, DM's choice of effect)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Centuries of temple refuse have compacted into a rank shell around its bloated hide."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The well's stench announces it a full room before any tentacle appears."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never rises past the well's rim unless something falls all the way in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old coins and broken idols are visibly embedded, half-digested, in its hide."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It sinks back to silence the instant nothing disturbs the water for a minute."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Tossing food scraps down first buys safe passage past the well without a fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bloat seems to shift shape slowly, as if still digesting something enormous."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wound it badly and it drags its whole bulk up out of the well after you."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["floating fat and patient at the bottom of a refuse-choked well, waiting to be disturbed", "surging up the well shaft the instant rubble splashes down into its water"]},{"name":"Shambling Garden Overgrowth","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Plant","size":"Large","frame":"shambling-mound","model":"rlm-shambling-garden-overgrowth","summary":"Sentient overgrowth reclaiming a hanging garden","flavor":"A reclaimed hanging garden, fully sentient and territorial now.","desc":"The hanging garden reclaimed itself so completely it became something else — fully sentient now, territorial about every inch of the terrace it used to just decorate. Vines the thickness of a man's arm test the air like feelers. It moves slowly enough to seem harmless right up until it doesn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Feeler-Vine Lash", "replaces": "Charged Tendril", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 15 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) Lightning damage from static built up in the overgrown terrace vines, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if Large or smaller."}, {"name": "Terrace Engulf", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "The Overgrowth engulfs a Medium or smaller creature it has grappled. The target takes 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, is Restrained, and can't breathe unless it can hold its breath; the Overgrowth can't make Feeler-Vine Lash attacks while a creature is engulfed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Terrace flowers still bloom, incongruous and bright, along its mossy shoulders."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never crosses the terrace's original garden border, however far prey flees."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vines coil in the same ornamental spirals the garden's dead architect once planted."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves so slowly toward stillness that it's often mistaken for the hedge itself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh soil clings in thick clumps wherever it's uprooted itself to move."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pruning it back gently with a blade, rather than hacking, earns a wary retreat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its leaves shift color to mirror whatever season the garden last saw, decades gone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Set it ablaze and the whole terrace's dry growth catches with unnerving speed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "forest"],"activity":["testing the terrace air with vines thick as a man's arm, territorial over every inch", "advancing at a slow, deliberate crawl that only seems harmless from a distance"]},{"name":"Ashen Vampire-Spawn Handmaiden","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"rlm-ashen-vampire-spawn-handmaiden","summary":"Undead handmaiden still tending an empty throne","flavor":"A royal handmaiden turned undead, still tending an empty throne.","desc":"She still tends an empty throne with the same quiet devotion she gave it in life, dusting a seat no one has sat in for generations, pale and unhurried in the tomb's cold air. Her fingers linger on the armrest a beat too long. She turns from the throne only when something disturbs the room's silence.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ashen Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Devoted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage, and the Handmaiden regains hit points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her fingers still know the exact worn groove on the throne's armrest by touch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wears a servant's sash faded to grey, its house colors long forgotten."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She dusts with an actual rag, meticulous, even now that dust is all there is."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pale and unhurried, she never raises her voice above a servant's murmur."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She curtseys, briefly, to the empty seat before turning to face any intruder."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Addressing her by an old court title makes her pause, listening, instead of attacking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The throne's dust resettles behind her, undisturbed, moments after she's moved past it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage the throne itself and her devotion snaps instantly into raw, silent fury."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["dusting the arm of an empty throne with the same quiet devotion she gave it in life", "lingering a beat too long over the seat before turning, unhurried, toward the silence-breaker"]},{"name":"Wight-Lord of the Processional Guard","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"rlm-wight-lord-of-the-processional-guard","summary":"Undead lord commanding the marching dead guard","flavor":"Commands the lesser dead who still march the ceremonial road.","desc":"He commands the lesser dead who still march the ceremonial road, voice carrying the same clipped authority it held in life, armor rattling with each barked order. The marching dead don't need the orders anymore, but he gives them anyway. Command, it turns out, outlasts the need for it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grave-Chill Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. A humanoid slain this way rises the next dusk as a Zombie under the Wight-Lord's command."}, {"name": "Processional Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Muster the Column", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "The Wight-Lord barks a parade-ground order. Up to three undead within 60 ft. that can hear him gain advantage on their next attack roll and can move up to their speed as a Reaction."}, {"name": "Processional Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. the Wight-Lord can see makes a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or is Frightened of him for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mustering the marching dead early, and they're headed toward a living village."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for new recruits and starts barking orders at them directly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A processional relic the party needs is strapped, ceremonially, across his own chest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His column is short one rank, and he's actively looking for a body to fill it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living deserter from his old army is hiding nearby, and he still wants them found."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll stand his column down for anyone who can answer his old muster roll-call correctly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His barked orders echo back in other dead voices from further down the processional road."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill him and his column doesn't scatter — it keeps marching, leaderless and now uncontrolled."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["barking orders down the ceremonial road at dead soldiers who no longer need them", "marching the processional route in full armor, voice carrying the same clipped authority it held alive"]},{"name":"Sky-Talon Wyvern of the Ziggurat","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"wyvern","model":"wyvern","summary":"Wyvern roosting atop the tallest step-pyramid","flavor":"Roosts atop the tallest step-pyramid, territorial over the whole valley.","desc":"It roosts atop the tallest step-pyramid, territorial over the whole valley below, wings mantled against the wind at the summit. Its shadow crosses the ruins below long before its cry does. Nothing nests this high without a reason to defend the view.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Summit Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Ziggurat Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Valley-Sting Tail", "replaces": "Sting", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nest is built from broken carvings pried loose from the summit's own reliefs."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old temple banners, sun-bleached, are woven through its talons like trophies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles the same three valley routes on patrol, dawn and dusk without fail."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarred wing membrane marks a past fight it clearly, barely, survived."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It roosts only at the exact summit point where the wind cuts weakest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaving a fresh kill at the pyramid's base satisfies it without a fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its cry echoes back from the valley floor a beat before it actually calls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten its nest and it dives with a fury well past anything territory alone explains."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "sky", "mountain"],"activity":["mantling broad wings against the summit wind atop the tallest step-pyramid", "circling the valley below, shadow crossing the ruins long before its cry arrives"]},{"name":"Idol-Warped Chimera of Three Gods","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"Grafted horror built from three patron-beast idols","flavor":"A grafted horror built from the temple's three patron-beast idols.","desc":"It was grafted from the temple's three patron-beast idols by magic no one fully understood even then, three mismatched heads arguing in three different animal registers. Scorch marks scar the stone around wherever it's fought before. It doesn't move like any one animal — it moves like a compromise none of the three wanted.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "First God's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Second God's Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Third God's Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Idol-Fire Breath", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Chimera exhales fire in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head still carries the paint scheme of the idol it was grafted from."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scorch marks scar the stone in a wide ring wherever it's fought before."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its three heads bicker audibly before ever agreeing on a target to attack."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grafting scars, thick and old, run visibly where all three bodies were joined."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles its own patron altar and won't willingly stray far from the sight of it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Flattering just one of its three heads directly turns it briefly against the other two."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment all three heads speak the same word, in unison, before arguing resumes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Badly wound one head and the other two turn, briefly, on each other in a frenzy."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["arguing with itself in three animal registers, heads disagreeing on which way to turn", "stalking the temple floor in a gait that belongs to no single beast it's built from"]},{"name":"Eight-Legged Web-Warden of the Vault","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"drider","model":"drider","summary":"Half-cursed drider webbing shut the treasure vault","flavor":"Half-cursed guardian left to web shut the innermost treasure vault.","desc":"Half-cursed and left behind on purpose, it has spent generations webbing the innermost treasure vault shut layer by layer. Silk thick as rope crisscrosses the passage in patterns only it can navigate cleanly. It doesn't guard the treasure so much as bury it under an ever-thickening cocoon.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't fight for the treasure so much as bury it deeper; killing it leaves the vault webbed shut regardless.", "actions": [{"name": "Vault-Silk Foreleg", "replaces": "Foreleg", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Poison Web-Burst", "replaces": "Poison Burst", "text": "Each creature within 15 feet of the Warden makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) Poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature that fails is also Restrained by clinging webbing until it or another creature uses an action to break it free (AC 10, 10 hit points)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lower half still carries the drider's original half-cursed serpent coils."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Silk thick as rope crosses the passage in patterns only it navigates cleanly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It was left behind on purpose, its curse a punishment it still faithfully serves."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old, brittle treasure-seeker bones are wrapped deep into the vault's outer web layers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It adds one fresh layer of silk to the vault door every single passing year."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offering it a fresh meal to wrap instead buys temporary passage past its webbing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The web strands hum faintly, as if carrying vibration from somewhere deep inside the vault."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Burn its webbing and it swarms to defend the gap with an almost desperate speed."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["cave", "ruins"],"activity":["laying fresh silk across the vault passage, thickening a cocoon generations in the making", "testing a strand from deep in the webbing the instant something brushes the outer layer"]},{"name":"Storm-Song Satyr Revelmaster of Ruins","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"satyr-revelmaster","model":"rlm-storm-song-satyr-revelmaster-of-ruins","summary":"Fey revelmaster luring travelers to ruin-feasts","flavor":"Holds feral revels among the fallen columns, luring the reckless in.","desc":"Music drifts from among the fallen columns before you see the source — a wild, half-mad revel with no living guests, held for centuries by something that never noticed the party ended. He beckons travelers in with a grin that promises more than it delivers. The reckless who join him rarely leave in the same shape.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Reveler's Prance", "replaces": "Prance", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage from a cloven kick thrown mid-dance, and the Revelmaster can move up to half its speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks as part of this action."}, {"name": "Storm-Song Melody", "replaces": "Fey Melody (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "The Revelmaster plays a wild, half-mad tune. Each creature within 30 feet that can hear it makes a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, a creature is charmed for 1 minute and must use its movement to dance toward the revel rather than act with purpose; a creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He desperately wants new dance partners and won't easily let willing ones leave again."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A missing local reveler is somewhere in his endless party, charmed and half-starved."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a stolen ceremonial cup he insists is his rightful centerpiece now."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival fey is due to crash his revel tonight, and he wants muscle on his side."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's convinced the party are old guests returning, and reacts to being corrected badly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Out-dancing him at his own revel earns genuine respect and safe passage through the ruin."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The fallen columns seem to sway faintly in time with his music, as if half-alive."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "End his music abruptly and the revel's charmed stragglers turn violently confused."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "forest"],"activity":["holding a centuries-long revel among fallen columns for guests who stopped arriving long ago", "beckoning newcomers in with a grin that promises far more than it ever delivers"]},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Vrock Carrion-Caller","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"vrock","model":"rlm-hollow-throated-vrock-carrion-caller","summary":"Summoned scavenger-demon guarding forbidden grave-magic","flavor":"A summoned scavenger-demon bound to guard forbidden grave-magic.","desc":"It was summoned and bound generations ago to guard forbidden grave-magic no one living remembers the purpose of, vulture head cocked at an unnatural angle, tracking scent more than sight. A carrion stink follows it that has nothing to do with anything it's killed recently. It calls out in a register that makes the air itself feel wrong.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Carrion Talons", "replaces": "Shred", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d10 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Grave-Spore Cloud", "replaces": "Spores (Recharge 6)", "text": "Each creature within 15 feet of the Carrion-Caller makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) Poison damage and becoming Poisoned until the start of its next turn on a failure, or no damage on a success."}, {"name": "Hollow Screech", "replaces": "Stunning Screech (1/Day)", "text": "The Carrion-Caller lets out a screech that makes the air itself feel wrong. Each creature within 20 feet makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or is Stunned until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A carrion stink follows it that has nothing to do with anything it's killed recently."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old binding sigils, cracked and faded, are branded across both wings."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never strays from the exact chamber it was summoned to guard, generations ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its vulture head tilts to track scent long before its eyes ever fix on a target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles the forbidden grave-magic's resting place in slow, patient loops."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Speaking the binder's forgotten name aloud makes it pause, briefly confused."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The grave-magic it guards seems to pulse faintly warmer whenever it calls out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten the sealed magic directly and its screech doesn't stun anymore — it summons."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["tracking scent more than sight, vulture head cocked at an unnatural angle", "calling out in a register that curdles the still air around forbidden grave-magic"]},{"name":"Serpent-Sworn Lamia of the Oasis Court","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"lamia","model":"rlm-serpent-sworn-lamia-of-the-oasis-court","summary":"Charming oasis fiend feeding on stolen years","flavor":"Charms travelers at a hidden oasis before feeding on their years.","desc":"She holds court at a hidden oasis, serpent coils where her legs should be, charming every traveler who stumbles onto the water before feeding on the years she's charmed out of them. The oasis is real and the water is sweet — that's most of the trick. By the time you notice you've aged, it's already spent.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Coiled Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Years-Draining Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Necrotic damage, and the target's Wisdom score is reduced by 1d4 until it finishes a long rest, as some sliver of self is charmed away with the years."}, {"name": "Oasis Charm", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "One humanoid the Lamia can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or is Charmed by her for 1 hour, believing the oasis water to be the sweetest it has ever tasted."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's mid-charm on a lone traveler who wandered in an hour before the party."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A charmed guard of hers watches the oasis, aged decades past his true years."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants fresh company at court and will charm the most reluctant member first."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival caravan is due at the oasis, and she means to feed on all of them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's hoarding years stolen from dozens of travelers, visible as trinkets they left behind."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Bringing her a genuinely rare gift earns hospitality without the charm's true cost."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The oasis water tastes different to every traveler, each swearing it's their favorite thing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Break her charm on someone mid-feed and she panics, feeding faster and more openly."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court at a hidden oasis, serpent coils curled beneath a charming, patient smile", "feeding on years charmed out of a traveler who hasn't yet noticed the cost"]},{"name":"Basalt-Skinned Gorgon of the Sun Gate","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"rlm-basalt-skinned-gorgon-of-the-sun-gate","summary":"Bull construct petrifying intruders at the sun gate","flavor":"A bull-shaped construct whose breath turns intruders to stone at the gate.","desc":"Bull-shaped and built of the same stone as the gate it guards, it breathes a fine grey dust that turns intruders to statuary matching the rest of the courtyard. Its hooves strike sparks off the flagstones with every step. The gate has never needed a second line of defense.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sun-Gate Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Petrifying Dust Breath", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Gorgon exhales petrifying dust in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, a creature is Restrained and begins turning to stone, repeating the save at the end of its next turn; success ends the effect, and failing both saves turns the creature into a statue permanently until freed by magic such as greater restoration."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stone hide is quarried from the exact same basalt as the gate it guards."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Several courtyard statues nearby match its own posture a little too closely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces a fixed patrol line and never crosses past the gate's outer threshold."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sparks fly visibly off its hooves with every heavy step across the flagstones."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fine grey dust clings permanently around its nostrils, never fully settling."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Presenting an old gate-seal or token makes it stand down and let you pass unchallenged."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of its courtyard statues seem to have shifted pose slightly since you last looked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage the gate itself and its breath comes twice as often, desperate to hold the line."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["striking sparks off the flagstones with heavy hooves, patrolling the same gate line", "exhaling a fine grey dust across the courtyard the instant an intruder crosses the threshold"]},{"name":"Nine-Serpent Basalt Hydra Spawn","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"Cistern hydra whose heads regrow when severed","flavor":"Guards the temple's central cistern, heads regrowing with each severed strike.","desc":"It guards the temple's central cistern, and every head you take is replaced before the water finishes rippling from the blow. Its many throats hiss in a chorus that never quite synchronizes. The cistern has stayed full for centuries because nothing has ever gotten past it to drain it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cistern-Fang Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage. The Hydra Spawn can make this attack up to five times per turn, once per remaining head, targeting one or more creatures."}, {"name": "Regrowing Heads", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Whenever the Hydra Spawn takes damage that would sever a head (DM's discretion on a heavy single hit), two new heads grow from the stump by the start of its next turn unless it has taken fire or acid damage since losing that head."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nine throats hiss in a rasping chorus that never lands quite in unison."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The cistern water ripples constantly, disturbed by heads testing beneath the surface."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scars mark where past heads were severed and clearly grew back stronger."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never strays from the cistern's rim, however far a fight drags it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Basalt-toned scales darken near each head's throat where venom sacs bulge visibly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fire or acid thrown at a severed stump keeps that head from ever regrowing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally, all nine heads turn to stare at the exact same spot for no clear reason."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Sever too many heads at once and the remaining ones lash out in a frenzied panic."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["hissing in a chorus that never quite synchronizes, guarding the temple's central cistern", "striking with one head while two others test the water for the next intruder"]},{"name":"Petrified Roc of the High Terraces","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"roc","model":"rlm-petrified-roc-of-the-high-terraces","summary":"Colossal roc nesting on the crumbling terrace","flavor":"A colossal bird that nests atop the crumbling highest terrace tier.","desc":"It nests atop the crumbling highest terrace tier, wingspan wide enough to blot out the ruin below when it circles. The stone up here has cracked under the weight of a nest built from broken columns instead of branches. It doesn't dive at trespassers below — it drops boulders instead.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Terrace Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 24 (3d12 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Column-Grip Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 5 ft. Hit: 19 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage, and if the target is Large or smaller it is Grappled (escape DC 18)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nest is built from broken columns rather than any natural branch or timber."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The stone beneath its nest has visibly cracked under the sheer accumulated weight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drops loose masonry on distant trespassers rather than diving down to meet them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow crosses the whole ruin below well before its cry ever reaches the ground."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Feathers the length of a spear molt loose and litter the terrace tier below its nest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Leaving a large offering of meat at the terrace base satisfies it without provoking a dive."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eggs, when found, seem to be made of the same stone as the terrace itself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten the nest directly and it brings the whole crumbling terrace down as it dives."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "sky", "mountain"],"activity":["nesting atop a crumbling terrace of broken columns, wingspan blotting out the ruin below", "dropping a boulder from the summit instead of diving at whatever's trespassed below"]},{"name":"Fossil-Chained Behir of the Under-Passage","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"behir","model":"behir","summary":"Lightning serpent-beast patrolling flooded passages","flavor":"A lightning-scaled serpent-beast that patrols the flooded under-passages.","desc":"It patrols the flooded under-passages with a low electric hum crackling along lightning-scaled flanks, water displacing in slow ripples ahead of its coils. The passage floods deeper wherever it's passed recently. You hear the hum before you see the shape making it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Under-Passage Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (3d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Flooded Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Lightning-Scale Breath", "replaces": "Lightning Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "The Behir exhales lightning in a 20-foot line. Each creature in the line makes a DC 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) Lightning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lightning-scaled flanks hum audibly, a warning heard well before it's ever seen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fossil bands run down its spine, ancient stone fused permanently into hide."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The under-passage floods measurably deeper wherever it's passed recently."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only in the passage's deepest, darkest flooded stretch."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old chain-link fossils are visibly embedded, ornamental, along both flanks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Retreating to dry, higher passage ground denies it the flooded terrain it hunts best in."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hum along its scales seems to answer, faintly, some deeper source further below."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it in the flooded passage and the water itself seems to charge along with it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "swamp", "deeplands"],"activity":["patrolling flooded under-passages with a low electric hum along lightning-scaled flanks", "displacing water in slow ripples ahead of coils you hear humming before you see"]},{"name":"Dune-Sunk Purple Devourer","cr":15,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"purple-worm","model":"purple-worm","summary":"Colossal worm tunneling beneath the whole valley","flavor":"Tunnels beneath the whole valley, swallowing pilgrims and pillars alike.","desc":"The whole valley trembles faintly whenever it turns beneath the sand, a colossal worm that has swallowed pilgrims and pillars with equal indifference for longer than the ruin has had a name. Dunes shift and collapse into fresh sinkholes without warning. You feel it coming up through your boots before you ever see the sand crack open.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dune-Sunk Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 26 (3d12 + 7) Piercing damage plus 22 (4d10) Acid damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is swallowed on a hit that reduces it to 0 hit points or below this turn's total damage threshold (DM's discretion, per chassis swallow rules)."}, {"name": "Sand-Sting Tail", "replaces": "Tail Stinger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +14, reach 10 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 22 (4d10) Poison damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dunes shift and collapse into fresh sinkholes wherever it turns beneath the sand."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The valley trembles faintly and rhythmically whenever it moves closer to the surface."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old pilgrim relics, half-digested, occasionally surface in the sand it's churned through."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "You feel it coming up through your boots long before any sand ever cracks open."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only where the valley's sand runs deepest and softest underfoot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Standing dead still on exposed bedrock denies it the soft sand it needs to strike cleanly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Pillars swallowed decades ago sometimes surface again, oddly intact, in its wake."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wound it badly enough and the whole valley floor starts giving way at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["desert"],"activity":["turning beneath the sand with a tremor the whole valley feels through its boots", "swallowing whatever crosses its path with an indifference longer than the ruin's own name"]},{"name":"Efreeti Bound to the Eternal Forge-Idol","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"efreeti","model":"rlm-efreeti-bound-to-the-eternal-forge-idol","summary":"Bound efreeti stoking the temple's idol forge","flavor":"Bound by old contract to stoke the forge that casts the temple's idols.","desc":"Old contract binds it to stoke the forge that casts the temple's idols, flame-wreathed and visibly resentful of terms it can't break. Molten slag pools where its feet should leave footprints. It works the forge with total competence and zero enthusiasm, and it will absolutely take that resentment out on you instead.","traits":{"note": "Old contract binds it to the forge; break the binding stone and it will not fight to keep you from it, only to punish you after.", "actions": [{"name": "Forge-Heated Blade", "replaces": "Heated Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Molten Slag Hurl", "replaces": "Hurl Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 17 (5d6) Fire damage, and a flammable object hit that isn't worn or carried ignites."}, {"name": "Idol-Casting Magic", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Efreeti casts a spell it knows from its long service casting idols (DM's choice, level appropriate to CR 11, such as wall of fire or major image), expending no material components since the forge itself provides them."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants the binding contract destroyed and will bargain for whoever can read the old terms."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A new idol order has just arrived from a rival temple, and it resents casting for enemies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The forge is overdue for fuel, and it's eyeing the party's gear with open hunger."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival binder is en route to renew its contract, and it would rather anyone else got there first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cast one idol wrong on purpose, a small rebellion it needs kept quiet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offering to search for a way to void its contract earns grudging, temporary cooperation."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The idols it casts seem to watch the room long after they've cooled and hardened."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten to destroy the forge itself and its resentment boils over into open violence."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "elemental"],"activity":["stoking a forge that casts the temple's idols, flame-wreathed and visibly resentful of the terms", "working molten slag with total competence and precisely zero enthusiasm for the task"]},{"name":"Cyclops Oracle of the Buried Eye","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"rlm-cyclops-oracle-of-the-buried-eye","summary":"Blinded giant seer reading omens in ruined stone","flavor":"A blinded seer-giant who reads omens in the ruins' collapsing stone.","desc":"Blinded on purpose long ago, it reads omens now in the sound and shift of the ruins' collapsing stone, head cocked to catch vibrations you can't feel yet. Its remaining scars run deep across both temples. It'll tell you what's about to happen before it happens — usually too late to matter.","traits":{"note": "Blinded on purpose long ago, it reads by vibration alone; true silence denies it almost everything.", "actions": [{"name": "Omen Strike", "replaces": "Radiant Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (2d10 + 8) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Blind Flash", "replaces": "Flash of Light", "text": "Each creature within 20 feet of the Oracle makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, a creature is Blinded until the end of its next turn as light floods a chamber that has known only vibration for years."}, {"name": "Vibration-Read Magic", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Oracle casts a divination-flavored spell it 'reads' from the ruin's tremors (DM's choice, level appropriate to CR 10, such as clairvoyance or bestow curse)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It predicts one detail of the party's coming fight, correctly, before it happens."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants a specific stone tapped in a specific rhythm to confirm an omen it can't verify alone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A structural collapse it foresaw is due any minute, and it wants witnesses, not victims."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tracking a tremor pattern that means something else is moving deeper in the ruin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival oracle's silence-charm is nearby, and it desperately wants it destroyed or removed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Answering its omens honestly, even when unwelcome, earns real if grudging trust."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It describes a shift in stone that hasn't happened yet anywhere nearby — but will."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force total silence on it and its omens turn frantic, warning of something far larger stirring."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "mountain"],"activity":["reading omens in the shift of collapsing stone, head cocked to catch vibrations first", "tracing deep scars across both temples, listening for the ruin's next fall before it happens"]},{"name":"Marble-Veined Storm Giant Excavator","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"storm-giant","model":"rlm-marble-veined-storm-giant-excavator","summary":"Giant quarry-guard who once cut the temple's stones","flavor":"Once quarried the temple's founding stones; still guards the quarry pit.","desc":"It once quarried the very stones this temple was built from, and it still guards the quarry pit those stones came out of, marble veins running visibly under weathered grey skin. Thunder gathers audibly whenever it's provoked. It remembers exactly how many blocks it cut, and it counts them still standing.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Quarry-Cut Sword", "replaces": "Storm Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +11, reach 10 ft. Hit: 21 (3d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Thunder damage."}, {"name": "Excavator's Thunderbolt", "replaces": "Thunderbolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +11, range 500 ft. Hit: 33 (6d10) Lightning damage."}, {"name": "Quarry-Wide Lightning", "replaces": "Lightning Storm (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature the Excavator can see within 60 feet makes a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) Lightning damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, as storm-charge rolls off the quarry stone itself."}, {"name": "Stonework Magic", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Excavator casts a spell tied to stone and weather (DM's choice, level appropriate to CR 13, such as stone shape or control weather)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marble veins run visibly under its weathered grey skin, matching the temple's own stone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Thunder gathers audibly overhead the instant it's provoked or challenged."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It counts aloud, in a low rumble, exactly how many blocks it cut still stand."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries quarrying tools far older than any weapon, repurposed for battle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never leaves the immediate vicinity of the pit those founding stones came from."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Correctly guessing its block count earns a rare, grudging respect and a pause in hostilities."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The quarry pit's walls seem to hum faintly whenever the giant nears its edge."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damage the quarried stones themselves and its fury outstrips anything a mere fight explains."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "mountain"],"activity":["counting exactly how many quarried blocks are still standing, thunder gathering when provoked", "guarding the pit it once cut this whole temple's stones from, marble veins visible under weathered skin"]},{"name":"Death-Cultist Herald of the Buried Sun","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-cultist","model":"rlm-death-cultist-herald-of-the-buried-sun","summary":"Cultist preaching the sun is entombed, awaiting blood rite","flavor":"Preaches that the sun itself is entombed and can be freed by blood rite.","desc":"He preaches with total conviction that the sun itself lies entombed somewhere below, freeable only by blood spilled at the right hour. Robes stained dark at the hem suggest he's already tried more than once. He doesn't flinch from a fight — he treats it as an offering.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Dread Scythe Swing", "replaces": "Dread Scythe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Deathly Ray", "replaces": "Deathly Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Blood-Rite Magic", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Herald casts a spell drawn from his blood-rite doctrine (DM's choice, level appropriate to CR 8, such as spirit guardians or vampiric touch), often at cost to his own hit points if the rite demands it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs blood spilled at a precise hour tonight, and he's chosen his site already."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captive is bound nearby, meant for his rite, still very much alive and terrified."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries a shard he insists is a literal piece of the entombed sun, warm to the touch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival cultist faction is closing in to steal his rite's credit, and he wants it stopped."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His own hem is stained from a rite he's already botched once, and he's desperate to fix it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll delay his rite, briefly, for anyone who can offer a more convincing sacrifice or story."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The shard he carries grows faintly warmer the longer the conversation continues."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Interrupt his rite mid-blood and he treats the interruption itself as the offering instead."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert", "urban"],"activity":["preaching with total conviction that the sun itself lies entombed somewhere below", "eyeing the coming fight as an offering rather than a threat, robes stained dark at the hem"]},{"name":"Archpriest of the Dead Liturgy","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"rlm-archpriest-of-the-dead-liturgy","summary":"Last living speaker of the temple's dead liturgy","flavor":"The last living speaker of the temple's true dead language, and its final judge.","desc":"He is the last living speaker of the temple's true dead language, and he has appointed himself its final judge as well as its final voice. Every word he says in the old tongue sounds like both a blessing and a verdict. He judges you before you've said a thing worth judging.","traits":{"note": "He judges before he strikes — parley in the dead tongue can stall him a round.", "actions": [{"name": "Judging Hands", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Archpriest makes two Judging Hands attacks."}, {"name": "Verdict Flame", "replaces": "Radiant Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Radiant damage as he pronounces a line of verdict over the target."}, {"name": "Final Word", "replaces": "Holy Word (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "The Archpriest speaks the liturgy's closing line. Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature takes 27 (6d8) Radiant damage and is Deafened for 1 minute; half damage and no deafness on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a witness who can carry his verdict back to a city that stopped listening generations ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A captive translator is chained near the altar, forced to confirm each judgment as legitimate."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-rite over a body the party recognizes, and the verdict isn't finished yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands the party's names in the old tongue before he'll hear a single plea."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival priest's severed vestments hang behind the altar as a warning against false speech."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to judge one party member favorably in exchange for a confession spoken in the dead tongue."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every verdict he speaks is quietly becoming true, whether or not anyone acts on it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The altar behind him catches his last verdict and starts repeating it, louder, on its own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["chanting a dead liturgy over an altar no living tongue can otherwise pronounce", "weighing a trespasser's worth aloud, in verdicts that double as blessings"]},{"name":"Bone-Crowned Death Knight of the Ziggurat","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"rlm-bone-crowned-death-knight-of-the-ziggurat","summary":"Entombed general commanding a legion long gone","flavor":"An entombed general still commanding a legion that no longer exists.","desc":"He still commands a legion that stopped existing generations ago, barking orders into an empty processional yard with total conviction that ranks will form. Bone shards crown a helm gone black with age. The legion he commands may be gone, but the authority in his voice hasn't noticed.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "General's Blade", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Death Knight makes two General's Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Bone Reprimand", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Volley of the Lost Legion", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120 ft. Hit: 24 (7d6) Necrotic damage in a 10-ft. sphere at the point struck, as if a whole company had loosed at once."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for stragglers from his own legion and orders them into formation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding a muster roll he refuses to believe is centuries out of date."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A deserter's rusted standard lies half-buried nearby, and he wants it retrieved as a point of honor."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands the party report the strength of an enemy force that dissolved into dust long ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's drilling a squad of animated bone soldiers who obey only slightly better than corpses should."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll grant safe passage to anyone who can convincingly deliver a battle report he wants to hear."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shouted orders are audible from rooms away, in a voice too clear for how old the ziggurat is."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Every bone soldier in the ziggurat snaps to attention the instant he calls the muster."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["barking parade orders into an empty processional yard as if ranks might still form", "polishing a helm of bone shards for an inspection no one living will attend"]},{"name":"Vault-Sealed Naga of the Bone Archive","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"bone-naga","model":"rlm-vault-sealed-naga-of-the-bone-archive","summary":"Serpent-sage guarding the archive of the dead's names","flavor":"A serpent-sage bound to guard the archive of dead names.","desc":"It coils around an archive stacked floor to ceiling with the names of the dead, serpent-sage eyes tracking every scroll case as much as every intruder. It speaks in slow, deliberate syllables, weighing each word like it costs something. The archive has never once lost a name on its watch.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Archive Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Naga makes one Archive Strike and one Serpentine Gaze."}, {"name": "Archive Strike", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Ledger-Gaze", "replaces": "Serpentine Gaze", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that the Naga can see makes a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure the target is Paralyzed until the end of its next turn, its name weighed and recorded before it can act."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wants a missing scroll-case returned before it will let anyone leave the archive alive."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A thief's half-eaten remains lie among the shelves, the theft only partially completed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cataloguing a name the party recognizes, adding a death date that hasn't happened yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It demands proof of identity before allowing a search of any specific shelf."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival scholar's expedition markers are still pinned into the floor near a collapsed section."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers to trade a name from the archive for a name the party can supply from the world above."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every scroll it touches updates itself, entries changing to match events still in progress upstairs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It finds a scroll-case with a party member's name freshly inked and starts reading it aloud."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["coiling slowly around scroll-cases stacked floor to ceiling, tracking each one by scent", "weighing a single word for a long moment before finally speaking it aloud"]},{"name":"Frost-Cracked Abominable Cave-Beast","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"abominable-yeti","model":"abominable-yeti","summary":"Anomalous cold-beast denning in a frost-slick cave","flavor":"An anomalous cold-thing that dens in the temple's deepest, frost-slick cave.","desc":"Cold that has no business existing this deep in a desert ruin radiates off a hulking white shape denning in the temple's lowest, frost-slick cave. Its breath fogs thick in air that shouldn't be cold enough to fog. Nobody built it here, and nobody knows how long it's actually been.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Frost Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cave-Beast makes two Frost Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Frost Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Hurled Ice-Shard", "replaces": "Ice Throw", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Unnatural Chill", "replaces": "Chilling Gaze", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frightened until the end of its next turn, certain the cold itself is watching it."}, {"name": "Breath of the Deep Frost", "replaces": "Cold Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "15-ft. cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 16 Constitution save, taking 36 (8d8) Cold damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its breath crystallizes into a fine hanging fog that lingers long after it moves on."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scars run under its frost-cracked hide, evidence it has denned here for a very long time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hoards nothing but cold rock, arranging stones by temperature for reasons only it understands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ice forms a false floor over its den, cracking loudly underfoot before anyone sees the beast."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's larger than the passage should allow, hide scraping frost onto both walls as it moves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It backs off from fire, however small, as if remembering a wound the desert once gave it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its exhaled fog briefly outlines shapes that aren't there, gone before anyone can be sure."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The cave around it is colder every year, and the ruin above is starting to notice the drop."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "mountain"],"activity":["breathing fog in air that has no business being this cold this deep underground", "cracking frost off its own hide with a shudder before lunging at motion in the dark"]},{"name":"Rakshasa Vizier of the Broken Court","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"Fiendish vizier still whispering from the throne's shadow","flavor":"The mummy-king's old advisor, still whispering counsel from the shadows of the throne.","desc":"He still whispers counsel from the shadows behind the throne, the same seat he advised in life, voice smooth and reasonable and entirely untrustworthy. Tiger-striped hands fold politely at his sleeves. He offers you a deal before he offers you a fight, and the deal is worse.","traits":{"note": "He offers terms before violence — the deal is always worse than it sounds.", "actions": [{"name": "Vizier's Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Vizier makes two Vizier's Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Vizier's Claw", "replaces": "Cursed Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 17 Charisma save or believe, for 1 minute, that the Vizier's last offer was already accepted."}, {"name": "Baleful Command", "replaces": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "One creature within 60 ft. that can hear the Vizier makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure the target must use its reaction to move half its speed away from its nearest ally, obeying a command it didn't hear given."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers safe passage in exchange for a favor to be named later, in writing, in blood ink."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's brokering terms between two tomb-factions and wants the party as forced witnesses."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A signed contract from a party member's ancestor sits on his sleeve, terms still binding."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a rival advisor's seal ring, currently on a body three rooms deeper in the ruin."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already promised the party's services to someone else, and that someone is due to arrive."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll trade real information for a small, seemingly harmless promise he intends to collect on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every deal he's struck in this court is still technically in effect, layered decades deep."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He produces a contract bearing a party member's signature, dated before they were born."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["whispering smooth counsel from the shadow behind an empty throne", "folding tiger-striped hands and offering a deal before any blade is drawn"]},{"name":"The Undying Ape-Colossus of the Sacred Grove","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"iron-golem","model":"rlm-the-undying-ape-colossus-of-the-sacred-grove","summary":"Titanic ape-idol punishing desecrators of the grove","flavor":"A titanic idol carved in the shape of the ape-god, animated to punish the grove's desecrators.","desc":"Carved titanic in the shape of the grove's ape-god and animated to punish anyone who desecrates it, its shadow alone covers half the fallen temple floor. Moss and vine have grown into the joints without slowing it down. It doesn't ask what you touched — it already knows, and it's already moving.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Idol's Fist", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus makes two Idol's Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Idol's Fist", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 28 (4d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Slashing damage from stone edges worked into its knuckles."}, {"name": "Sap-Fire Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +12, range 120 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Fire damage as sap ignited deep in the grove's roots erupts from its palm."}, {"name": "Grove-Rot Breath", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "30-ft. cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 19 Constitution save, taking 45 (10d8) Poison damage on a failure or half as much on a success, as spores older than the temple pour from its mouth."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already tracking the exact carved fruit a party member picked up without asking."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prior desecrator's crushed gear is scattered at its feet, still warm from a recent judgment."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its punishing rounds have opened a fissure that's flooding a lower chamber the party needs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a grove-sapling that a desperate village needs transplanted before the dry season."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't stop pursuing until whatever was taken is returned to its exact original spot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses, seemingly satisfied, if an offering of fresh-cut grove wood is placed at its base."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Vines grown into its joints are still alive and still rooted to trees a mile outside the ruin."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It isn't guarding a temple — it's the grove's last living root, and killing it kills the whole forest with it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["standing motionless as a carved idol until moss-grown joints suddenly grind into motion", "already turning toward the exact spot someone touched something sacred"]},{"name":"Dragon-Turtle of the Drowned Necropolis","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"dragon-turtle","model":"rlm-dragon-turtle-of-the-drowned-necropolis","summary":"Shelled leviathan wearing a swallowed necropolis","flavor":"A shelled leviathan that swallowed a lesser necropolis whole and now wears it like armor.","desc":"It swallowed a lesser necropolis whole at some point and now wears the wreckage across its shell like armor, drowned spires jutting at odd angles from between its scutes. Water sheets off it in waterfalls when it surfaces. Tombs still visible on its back suggest this has happened more than once.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Necropolis Bite", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Dragon-Turtle makes one Necropolis Bite and one Spire-Tail attack."}, {"name": "Necropolis Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 26 (4d10 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Spire-Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Slashing damage from tomb-stone lodged in its scutes."}, {"name": "Drowned Steam Breath", "replaces": "Steam Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "30-ft. cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 19 Constitution save, taking 52 (15d6) Fire damage on a failure or half as much on a success, the steam thick with grave-silt."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A recognizable noble's crypt door still hangs open on its shell, hinges rusted mid-swing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fish nest inside the drowned spires, giving it a floating reef's worth of scavengers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only near the necropolis's original shoreline, as if bound to the old boundary."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bones rattle loose from its shell with every breath, littering a trail across the seabed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's easily twice the size the local fisherfolk describe, having clearly swallowed more since."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It surfaces to bask on sun-warmed stone and won't attack unless the tombs on its back are disturbed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Faint chanting is audible from inside its shell at low tide, muffled by a foot of living stone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cracks are spreading across its shell, and something in the swallowed necropolis is pushing back."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["sea", "ruins"],"activity":["surfacing in sheeting waterfalls, drowned spires jutting at odd angles from its shell", "settling back beneath the surface with tombs still visible between its scutes"]},{"name":"The First Priest-King, Undying","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"demilich","model":"rlm-the-first-priest-king-undying","summary":"Founder-king's jeweled skull still dreaming empire","flavor":"All that remains of the dynasty's founder, a jeweled skull that still dreams of empire.","desc":"All that's left of the dynasty's founder is a jeweled skull, and the skull still dreams — out loud, in a language that predates the empire it built. Gemstones socketed where eyes should be catch light without needing a source. It speaks of an empire that ended so long ago even the ruins have forgotten its name.","traits":{"note": "He dreams more than he acts — destroying his gemstone eyes cuts him off from most of his power.", "actions": [{"name": "Founder's Wail", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Priest-King makes two Founder's Wail attacks."}, {"name": "Founder's Wail", "replaces": "Necrotic Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +11, range 30 ft. Hit: 23 (6d6 + 2) Necrotic damage as a founding curse pours from the jeweled skull."}, {"name": "Dream of Empire", "replaces": "Howl (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature within 40 ft. makes a DC 18 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature takes 31 (7d8) Psychic damage and is Stunned until the end of its next turn, briefly living an empire's fall from the inside; half damage and no stun on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for subjects come to renew their oath and expects immediate tribute."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living pretender to his old throne is en route, unaware the founder never actually died."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His dream is bleeding into a nearby village's sleep, and the sleepers are starting to speak his dead tongue."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He demands a crown-piece back that a party member is unknowingly already carrying."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His hoard includes a founding charter that names a modern claimant's bloodline as usurpers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to name a party member heir to a throne that no longer exists, in exchange for company."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His dream is visibly rewriting the tomb's murals in real time to match what he's imagining."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He isn't dreaming memories — he's dreaming a second empire into being, and the ground outside is starting to answer him."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["dreaming aloud atop a heap of gold, jeweled sockets catching light with no source", "murmuring the name of an empire that predates even this ruin's oldest stones"]},{"name":"Emperor Wyrm of the Sunken Ziggurat","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"dracolich","model":"rlm-emperor-wyrm-of-the-sunken-ziggurat","summary":"Serpent-dragon bound in death to its own ziggurat","flavor":"A great serpent-dragon bound in death to the ziggurat it once terrorized alive.","desc":"A great serpent-dragon corpse, bound in death to the very ziggurat it once terrorized while alive, coils motionless until the wards holding it are disturbed. Scales have gone the color of wet ash, but the size hasn't diminished with the centuries. Whatever killed it clearly didn't trust it to stay dead on its own.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ash-Scale Rend", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Emperor Wyrm makes two Ash-Scale Rend attacks."}, {"name": "Ash-Scale Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Necrotic Breath of the Ziggurat", "replaces": "Necrotic Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "60-ft. line, 5 ft. wide. Each creature in the line makes a DC 19 Constitution save, taking 55 (10d10) Necrotic damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The wards binding it are failing on a schedule, and the party's arrival happens to be the trigger."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ward-priest's mummified remains still clutch the sealing stone that's supposed to hold it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It recognizes the ziggurat's original seal-sigil, currently worn by a party member as jewelry."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living cult still tends the ward-fires, unaware the wyrm they serve wants them dead first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its territory has crept a full room wider since the last ward inspection, decades ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It responds, briefly, to the exact ritual phrase the wards were built around — if anyone still knows it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its scales are cold enough to frost stone, despite the ziggurat sitting in open desert heat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It was bound here specifically because its death releases the very curse it's meant to be containing."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["lying coiled and motionless until wards holding it in place are finally disturbed", "uncoiling ash-gray scales the size of shields with slow, deliberate menace"]},{"name":"The Ever-Watching Sphinx of Final Judgment","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Celestial","size":"Large","frame":"sphinx-of-valor","model":"sphinx-of-valor","summary":"Threshold sphinx judging souls by riddle or blade","flavor":"Judges every soul that crosses the temple threshold, riddle or blade in equal measure.","desc":"She judges every soul that crosses the temple threshold, riddle in one breath and blade in the next, equally prepared to use either. Wings fold with the deliberate patience of something that has judged more souls than the ruin has stones. She has never once needed to hurry a verdict.","traits":{"note": "Riddle or blade, her choice — a good answer costs her nothing to honor.", "actions": [{"name": "Judgment Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sphinx makes two Judgment Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Judgment Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 10 ft. Hit: 23 (4d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Roar of Final Judgment", "replaces": "Roar (3/Day)", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. makes a DC 19 Wisdom save."}, {"name": "First Verdict", "replaces": "First Roar", "text": "On a failed save against Roar of Final Judgment, a creature is Frightened for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Second Verdict", "replaces": "Second Roar", "text": "On a failed save against Roar of Final Judgment (if used again), a creature is also Frightened and its speed is halved while frightened this way."}, {"name": "Third Verdict", "replaces": "Third Roar", "text": "On a failed save against Roar of Final Judgment (if used a third time), a creature also drops what it's holding and can't willingly move closer to the Sphinx."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already posed her riddle to the party's guide, who answered wrong and is now bricked into the wall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival petitioner waits behind the party, hoping they fail so he can try the riddle next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She holds the only key to a passage the party's actual quarry fled through minutes ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her riddle this time is built specifically around a secret one party member is keeping from the others."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A previous wrong answer's petitioner is still alive, chained nearby as a living warning."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll accept a fair trade — a true secret told, in place of a riddle answered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her riddles are never the same twice, as if she's composing them fresh from whoever stands before her."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "She judges more than trespassers — every soul that has ever died in this valley eventually answers to her, and she's been counting."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["folding vast wings with the patience of something that has judged more souls than the ruin has stones", "posing a riddle calmly, in no apparent hurry to hear the wrong answer"]},{"name":"Medusa","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"snake-haired gaze-petrify guardian of a forbidden shrine","flavor":"A cursed priestess left to guard a ruin no one else will enter; she doesn't hunt, she waits for you to look.","desc":"She waits rather than hunts, a cursed priestess left to guard a ruin no one else will enter, coiled hair testing the air with quiet, restless motion. Statuary in her chamber isn't decoration — it's a record of everyone who looked too soon. She doesn't chase you; she simply waits for the moment you forget not to look.","traits":{"note": "She waits for a look, not a fight — she rarely gives chase past her own chamber.", "actions": [{"name": "Shrine-Guardian's Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Medusa makes two Shrine-Guardian's Claw attacks, or one Claw attack and uses Poison Ray."}, {"name": "Shrine-Guardian's Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Coiling Hair", "replaces": "Snake Hair", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Petrifying Gaze", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "One creature within 30 ft. that can see her eyes makes a DC 14 Constitution save. On a failure the target is Restrained and begins to turn to stone, repeating the save at the end of its next turn; failure a second time petrifies it permanently, success ends the effect."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She keeps a mirrored shield propped nearby, a courtesy she's never once had to use herself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her statues are arranged in a rough queue, as if she's still sorting them by arrival order."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wears the priestess vestments of whatever cult built this shrine, faded but intact."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She speaks first, calmly, before anyone's looked at anything worth petrifying them over."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One statue in her collection wears armor from a kingdom that fell only a decade ago."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll let a blindfolded visitor leave unharmed, provided they leave immediately and don't look back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her statues' expressions shift, very slightly, whenever no one is looking directly at them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cracks are spreading through her oldest statue, and something inside it is trying to get back out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["coiling hair testing the still air of a shrine chamber, waiting rather than hunting", "standing perfectly still among statues that are not, in fact, decoration"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Perseus cycle)"},{"name":"the Minotaur","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","model":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","summary":"bull-headed labyrinth-warden, gores anything that gets turned around","flavor":"Bred as a punishment and grown into a king of his own maze — the walls moved to keep him, so now he moves them to keep you.","desc":"Bred as a punishment and grown, over years underground, into king of his own maze, he tracks by scent and sound through walls that shift specifically to keep him in and everyone else lost. Horns scrape stone at every turn he takes at a dead run. The labyrinth moved to keep him once; now he moves it to keep you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Maze-King's Glaive", "replaces": "Abyssal Glaive", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Horn Charge", "replaces": "Gore (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 3) Piercing damage, and if the Minotaur moved at least 10 ft. straight toward the target first, the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scars crisscross its shoulders where the maze's walls have scraped it raw over years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows every dead end personally and steers intruders into the worst one on purpose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A collar of corroded chain still hangs from its neck, snapped rather than unlocked."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It marks territory in charcoal scrawl along walls it considers unquestionably its own."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves in total silence for something its size, right up until the charge begins."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stops charging anyone who finds and stands on the maze's original center marker."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The maze audibly grinds and resets itself in sections whenever it changes direction."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's lost the thread of the maze's newest layout, and now it's just as turned around as you."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["tracking by scent through walls that shift specifically to keep it in and everyone else lost", "scraping horns against stone at a dead run, closing on turned-around footsteps"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Theseus / Cretan labyrinth)"},{"name":"the Hydra","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"hydra","model":"hydra","summary":"regenerating many-headed swamp apex predator","flavor":"Every wound you land is a negotiation it wins later — cut deep enough, fast enough, or it simply outlasts you with one more mouth.","desc":"Every head that goes still is a temporary condition — sever one and two more crowd up out of the wound before the blood finishes running. Steam rises off multiple throats hissing in ragged unison. It doesn't need to win a fight quickly; it just needs to still be here when you're not.","traits":{"note": "Every wound is temporary — it wins fights by outlasting, not by finishing quickly.", "actions": [{"name": "Many-Mouth Bite", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Hydra makes as many Many-Mouth Bite attacks as it has heads remaining."}, {"name": "Many-Mouth Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its heads bicker audibly over which target to strike, wasting half a beat every round."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old stumps along its neck mark heads that regrew wrong, smaller and meaner than the rest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's coiled around a sunken shrine, using the ruin's stonework as extra cover in the murk."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head is missing entirely, the wound still raw, regrowth clearly imminent."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Swamp gas bubbles thick around its lair, occasionally igniting on nothing in particular."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It retreats, briefly, if enough heads take damage in a single exchange, needing a moment to regrow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its severed heads keep hissing for several minutes after being cut free of the body."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A cauterizing method someone left scrawled nearby suggests this isn't the first time it's been fought here."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp"],"activity":["hissing steam off multiple throats in ragged, overlapping unison", "crowding two new heads up out of a wound before the blood finishes running"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Labors of Herakles)"},{"name":"the Cyclops","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-sentry","model":"cyclops-sentry","summary":"one-eyed shepherd-giant sentry, brutal in close quarters","flavor":"He counts his flock by touch, one eye or none, and either way he's never once lost track of an intruder.","desc":"He counts intruders the way he counts sheep, by touch and sound rather than sight alone, and he has never once lost track of one in the dark. A single vast eye tracks motion with unnerving precision for something so simple-seeming. Close quarters favor him more than they favor you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sentry's Club", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cyclops makes two Sentry's Club attacks, or one Club attack and one Boulder Toss."}, {"name": "Sentry's Club", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Boulder Toss", "replaces": "Rock", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60/240 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A worn shepherd's crook leans by its post, kept more from habit than any remaining flock."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same tuneless note constantly, using echo to place things it can't quite see."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scratch-tallies cover the wall behind it, a running count of every intruder it's turned back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its single eye is clouded pale at the center, though its aim hasn't suffered for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows this chamber's every loose stone and uses the ones that make sound as a warning system."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It lets anyone who calls out their name and business pass unbothered, at least the first time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It reacts to sounds no one else in the room can hear, well before anything's actually there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its tally wall has run out of room, and it's started carving fresh marks straight over old ones."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "mountain", "cave"],"activity":["counting intruders by touch and sound the way a shepherd counts a flock", "tracking motion across the room with a single vast, unnervingly precise eye"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Homer's Odyssey, Polyphemus)"},{"name":"the Oracle Cyclops","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"cyclops-oracle","model":"cyclops-oracle","summary":"blind seer-giant, prophetic elite variant of the sentry","flavor":"Blinded on purpose, so the story goes, in trade for seeing further — he'll tell you your death before he deals it.","desc":"Blinded on purpose, so the story goes, in exchange for seeing further than sight ever could, he speaks your death before he deals it — calmly, like a weather report. Milk-pale sockets face you without needing to. He has all the patience of someone who already knows how this ends.","traits":{"note": "It already knows how the fight ends — that patience is unshakable, not bluff.", "actions": [{"name": "Seer's Strike", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Oracle Cyclops makes two Seer's Strike attacks, or one Seer's Strike and one Flash of Foresight."}, {"name": "Seer's Strike", "replaces": "Radiant Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 21 (3d10 + 5) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Flash of Foresight", "replaces": "Flash of Light", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Radiant damage, and the target has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before the start of the Oracle's next turn, its own future briefly shown to it wrong."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tells one party member their death, quietly, in a detail specific enough to be believed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A petitioner from a nearby village waits behind it, still deciding whether to ask his own question."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a true answer about the party's actual quarry, in exchange for one honest question in return."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already described the exact circumstances under which the party will next meet it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its milk-pale sockets fix on someone who hasn't spoken yet, as if their turn to ask is next."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll trade a genuine prophecy for the color and shape of something the party actually saw recently."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its prophecies about strangers keep coming true days before the strangers even arrive."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It falls silent mid-prophecy, as if it just glimpsed something about itself it hadn't expected."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "mountain"],"activity":["facing an intruder with milk-pale sockets that don't need sight to find them", "naming a death calmly, like a weather report, before any blow is struck"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Cyclopes as forge-kin of Hephaestus / seer tradition"},{"name":"the Chimera","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"lion/goat/serpent composite, breathes fire mid-roar","flavor":"Three heads, three different opinions about how you should die — the goat screams first so the lion and the dragon don't have to.","desc":"Three heads hold three different opinions about how you should die, and none of the three are in a hurry to agree. The goat-head screams a warning the lion and the serpent don't bother giving. Fire gathers at the back of one throat before you've even decided which head to watch.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Three-Headed Assault", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chimera makes one Serpent Bite attack, one Lion Claw attack, and one Goat Ram attack."}, {"name": "Serpent Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Lion Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Goat Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Serpent's Fire Breath", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "15-ft. cone. Each creature in the cone makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 31 (7d8) Fire damage on a failure or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The goat-head is visibly the most nervous of the three, and the most likely to warn first."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scorch marks radiate from its den in a rough fan, marking every direction it's breathed fire."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The serpent-tail moves independently of the other two heads, watching a different angle entirely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It nests high on a broken temple ledge, dragging kills up in pieces rather than whole."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head bears an old arrow wound the other two seem irritated is still healing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The lion-head, if addressed directly and calmly, will sometimes hesitate before the others attack."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its three heads occasionally argue in three different tones of the exact same voice."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The serpent-tail has started acting on its own initiative, out of sync with the other two heads."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["mountain", "ruins"],"activity":["screaming a goat-head warning the lion and serpent don't bother giving", "gathering fire at the back of one throat before anyone's decided which head to watch"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Iliad; Bellerophon cycle)"},{"name":"the Harpy","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"filth-winged bird-woman raider, hunts in screaming flocks","flavor":"They don't so much attack as infest — a shrieking cloud that strips a camp of food and morale in the same pass.","desc":"They don't so much attack as infest, a shrieking cloud descending on a camp and stripping it of food and morale in the same pass. Filth-matted wings beat a rhythm meant to disorient before a single talon ever connects. By the time you've counted them, they've already doubled back for a second pass.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Raider's Talons", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Harpy makes two Raider's Talons attacks."}, {"name": "Raider's Talons", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Scavenger's Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Discordant Song", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can hear the Harpy makes a DC 11 Wisdom save. On a failure, until the song ends, the target is Charmed and moves toward the Harpy by the safest route on its turn, stopping if the route would cause obvious harm."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a stolen cookpot still half-full, banging loudly against the rocks as it flies."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its flock strips a camp bare in under a minute and is already gone by the time anyone reacts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Filth cakes its wings thick enough to leave a visible smear on anything it brushes past."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles high before diving, sizing up which pack looks easiest to snatch from."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its song is off-key and clearly imitative, learned from travelers rather than born to it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll trade a stolen trinket back for food, if approached calmly instead of chased."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It hoards shiny trinkets in a nest built entirely from other travelers' lost gear."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its flock is larger than usual this season, circling somewhere just out of easy sight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "mountain", "forest"],"activity":["descending on a camp in a shrieking cloud, stripping food before anyone's fully awake", "beating filth-matted wings in a rhythm meant to disorient before a talon connects"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth (Argonautica; Aeneid)"},{"name":"the Harpy Matriarch","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy-matriarch","model":"harpy-matriarch","summary":"harpy brood-leader, coordinates the swarm's dive attacks","flavor":"Older, meaner, and smart enough to use her flock as bait — she circles while they soften you up.","desc":"Older, meaner, and smarter than her flock, she circles above the fight while the others soften you up, diving only when the outcome's no longer in doubt. Scarring across one wing marks a fight she survived and they didn't. She uses her brood as bait without a flicker of hesitation.","traits":{"note": "She uses her flock as bait without hesitation — expect her to hang back until they've worn a target down.", "actions": [{"name": "Matriarch's Talons", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Matriarch makes two Matriarch's Talons attacks."}, {"name": "Matriarch's Talons", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Brood-Call Song", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can hear the Matriarch makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, until the song ends, the target is Charmed and moves toward her by the safest route on its turn."}, {"name": "Piercing Screech", "replaces": "Screech (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 13 Constitution save, taking 14 (4d6) Thunder damage and gaining Vulnerability to Thunder damage until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half damage and no vulnerability on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scarring across one wing marks a fight she survived and the rest of her old brood didn't."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She keeps her distance from melee entirely, directing her flock with sharp, specific calls."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wears a scavenged bit of armor no ordinary harpy would think to bother with."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her brood defers to her instantly, breaking off an attack the moment she screeches a change."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's noticeably larger than the rest of her flock, feathers darker and more deliberately kept."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll call her flock off entirely if her own life is clearly on the line, prioritizing herself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She seems to plan attacks a full round ahead, reacting to things that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Her brood is unusually large this season, and she's clearly grooming a second matriarch among them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "mountain", "forest"],"activity":["circling above a fight while her brood softens the target up first", "diving only once the outcome of a skirmish is no longer in doubt"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — harpy tradition, elevated to a brood-leader"},{"name":"the Sphinx-Warden","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"manticore","model":"rlm-the-sphinx-warden","summary":"riddling lion-bodied guardian barring a sealed passage","flavor":"She'll let you pass if you answer well — and she is in absolutely no hurry, because she has outlived every wrong answer she's ever heard.","desc":"She perches on a ruined threshold with the unhurried air of something that has outlived every wrong answer it's ever heard, feathered wings mantled, human face utterly still. She'll let you pass if you answer well — and she is in absolutely no hurry either way. Silence, to her, is just another kind of answer.","traits":{"note": "She's in no hurry — she's outlived every wrong answer she's ever heard.", "actions": [{"name": "Threshold Claw", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sphinx-Warden makes two Threshold Claw attacks, or one Threshold Claw and one Tail Spike."}, {"name": "Threshold Claw", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Tail Spike", "replaces": "Tail Spike", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 100/200 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's mid-riddle with a previous traveler still deciding on an answer, tension already high."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival group's failed answer left one of them permanently barred from ever passing again."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She holds the only passage to a sealed room the party's actual objective is locked inside of."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her riddle draws directly on a secret one party member hasn't told the others yet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A scattered set of bones nearby belongs to someone who guessed and guessed wrong repeatedly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll accept an honest confession of failure as a valid answer, more often than people expect."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her riddles seem to already know things about visitors they haven't said aloud yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She poses a riddle whose answer is a name — and it's the name of someone in the party."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["perching on a ruined threshold, feathered wings mantled, human face utterly still", "waiting through a long silence, unhurried, as if silence itself were an answer"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek/Egyptian myth (riddle-guardian tradition, Oedipus cycle)"},{"name":"Anubis's Jackal-Priest","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"rlm-anubiss-jackal-priest","summary":"jackal-masked tomb-priest, judges intruders before it fights them","flavor":"He was a man once, before the mask stopped coming off — now he weighs every heart that walks into his tomb, including his own.","desc":"He was a man once, before the jackal mask stopped coming off, and now he weighs every heart that crosses into his tomb on scales only he can see. Funerary wrappings move stiffly beneath ceremonial armor. He judges before he fights, and he includes his own heart in every weighing.","traits":{"note": "He judges before he fights, and he weighs his own heart in every reckoning too.", "actions": [{"name": "Weighing Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Judgment's Edge", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage, or 11 (1d10 + 5) Slashing damage if used with two hands."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already begun weighing the party's hearts and won't fight until the reckoning finishes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prior trespasser's still-beating heart sits on his scale, judgment paused mid-weighing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes the tomb-seal a party member carries and demands to know how it was obtained."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to spare anyone who confesses their worst act honestly before the scales are read."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A second jackal-masked priest, silent and unmoving, stands watch just behind him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll let a genuinely repentant party pass, provided the confession sounds true to him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His scales tip on their own sometimes, weighing something no one present has said aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His own heart comes up light on the scale mid-fight, and it visibly unsettles him."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["weighing a trespasser's heart on scales only he can see, before drawing any blade", "adjusting a jackal mask that stopped coming off a very long time ago"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Egyptian myth/religion (Anubis, funerary tradition) — treated as a masked mortal priesthood, not the god"},{"name":"the Mummy","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"bandage-wrapped rot-cursed guardian of a sealed tomb","flavor":"Wrapped, sealed, and cursed on purpose — it was meant to stay down here forever, and it resents every second you've made that not true.","desc":"It was wrapped, sealed, and cursed on purpose — meant to stay down here forever — and it resents every second you've spent proving that wrong. Bandages have gone the color of the surrounding dust, stiff with age but far from fragile. It moves slow enough to seem harmless right up until its grip finds you.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sealed Fist", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mummy makes two Sealed Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Sealed Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Tomb-Curse Glare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "One creature within 60 ft. that can see the Mummy makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure the creature is Frightened for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bandages have gone the color of the surrounding dust, stiff but far from fragile."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single unbroken seal-ring still circles one wrist, marking a rank it can no longer name."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It shuffles the same fixed patrol route every time, never deviating past its old post."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wrappings hide old wounds that clearly killed it, long since scarred over with rot."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a small personal token, tucked into its bindings, from a life before the wrap."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates, briefly, at the sound of its own name spoken correctly aloud."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Dust never settles on the floor exactly where it's stood guard the longest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its wrappings are fraying faster than they should, as if something under the bandages is straining."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["standing wrapped and still in a sealed alcove until something crosses its threshold", "moving slow enough to seem harmless right up until its grip finds you"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Egyptian funerary myth/folklore (pre-1929 literary tradition, e.g. Stoker's Jewel of Seven Stars)"},{"name":"Gilgamesh's Shade","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"rlm-gilgameshs-shade","summary":"legendary king's undying shade, apex melee boss","flavor":"He tore down Humbaba, refused his own death twice, and still lost the one fight that mattered — now he re-fights every stranger like they might be that fight.","desc":"He tore down a forest guardian and refused his own death twice, and he still lost the one fight that ever mattered — so now he re-fights every stranger on the chance they might be that fight come back around. A bull-horned crown sits crooked on an armored, translucent brow. He swings for immortality every single time, and he has never once landed it.","traits":{"note": "He re-fights the one loss that mattered, over and over — he has never once won it.", "actions": [{"name": "King's Blade", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Shade makes two King's Blade attacks."}, {"name": "King's Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Orb of Undying Ambition", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 120 ft. Hit: 24 (7d6) Necrotic damage in a 10-ft. sphere at the point struck, as an echo of a forest guardian's death cry erupts outward."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes a party member for a companion he lost, and fights harder for the memory of them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants someone to tell him, honestly, whether he ever actually won anything at all."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A relic of his old crown lies nearby, and reclaiming it visibly steadies his aim."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He challenges the strongest-looking party member specifically, refusing to fight anyone else first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already fought and lost to someone else recently, and this fight is partly frustration."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll stand down, briefly, for anyone who can genuinely describe a loss they've never gotten over."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to remember fighting the party before, in details that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He's not just re-fighting a memory — every stranger he fights becomes part of the same unending battle, and this one is no exception."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["swinging for immortality one more time against a stranger who might be the fight that mattered", "settling a crooked bull-horned crown atop an armored, translucent brow"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Epic of Gilgamesh (Mesopotamian, ancient/public domain)"},{"name":"Humbaba","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Giant","size":"Huge","frame":"fomorian","model":"rlm-humbaba","summary":"monstrous forest-guardian giant, terrifying roar attack","flavor":"He was posted here to keep the cedar forest safe from people exactly like you, and he has never once been relieved of that duty.","desc":"He was posted here to keep the cedar forest safe from people exactly like you, and no one has ever formally relieved him of that duty. His roar alone splinters low branches before he's taken a single step. He still treats the post as sacred, long after everyone who assigned it is gone.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Guardian's Club", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Humbaba makes two Guardian's Club attacks."}, {"name": "Guardian's Club", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Warping Roar", "replaces": "Warping Hex (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature takes 18 (4d8) Thunder damage and is pushed 15 ft. away from Humbaba, the very air of the forest bending to enforce his post; half damage and no push on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He mistakes the party for the exact kind of trespassers he was originally posted to stop."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A logging crew is already cutting into his forest a mile off, unaware of what patrols it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding a cedar grove a desperate village needs timber from before the season ends."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes a weapon a party member carries as one that once wounded him badly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His territory has crept outward over the years, now overlapping land locals consider safely settled."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll let travelers pass unmolested if they can name who originally posted him to this duty."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Trees near his post lean subtly toward him, as if still under some old standing order."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Word has reached him that his old post is being reassigned, and he isn't taking it well."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["splintering low branches with a single roar before he's taken a single step", "treating an ancient forest post as sacred, long after anyone who assigned it is gone"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Epic of Gilgamesh — forest guardian set by the gods"},{"name":"Grendel","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"rlm-grendel","summary":"iron-immune marsh-raider, hunts camps at night","flavor":"He doesn't want your gold and doesn't want your land — he wants the noise you make to stop, permanently.","desc":"He doesn't want your gold and doesn't want your land — he wants the noise you make to stop, permanently, and he's willing to drag you back to the fen to guarantee it. Iron scars mark old wounds that never slowed him for long. He hunts camps at night specifically because that's when the noise is worst.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Fen-Raider's Bite", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Grendel makes one Fen-Raider's Bite attack and two Iron-Scarred Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Fen-Raider's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Iron-Scarred Claw", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage. This attack deals no extra effect against a target carrying iron, an old wound Grendel has learned to fight around."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already dragged one camp-member off toward the fen, and the drag-marks are still fresh."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A camp nearby is celebrating loudly tonight, unaware they've just made themselves his next target."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants the noise from a specific instrument or bell stopped, and will negotiate for exactly that."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old iron scarring on his hide marks a previous fight the party's patron barely survived."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's testing a new camp's defenses at range tonight, not yet committing to a raid."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He'll withdraw, grudgingly, if the noise that drew him actually stops before he attacks."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He seems to know a camp's watch rotation before it's been set for the night."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's dragging his latest catch back to the fen, and his mother is already stirring underwater."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp", "forest"],"activity":["dragging a raided camp's noise back toward the fen to guarantee it stops for good", "hunting at night specifically, when the noise from a camp is at its worst"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Beowulf (Old English epic, public domain)"},{"name":"Grendel's Mother","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"merrow","model":"rlm-grendels-mother","summary":"underwater ambush-avenger, drags foes into her mere","flavor":"She only comes up out of the mere when someone's killed one of hers — and by then the math has already stopped being in your favor.","desc":"She surfaces from the mere only when someone's killed one of hers, and by the time she's above the waterline the math has already stopped favoring you. She drags fights back under with her on purpose, fighting on terms only she's practiced. The water closes over both of you before you've finished drawing breath.","traits":{"note": "She only surfaces for vengeance — she won't come up unprovoked.", "actions": [{"name": "Mere-Depths Bite", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Grendel's Mother makes one Mere-Depths Bite attack and one Harpoon Drag attack."}, {"name": "Mere-Depths Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Drowning Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Harpoon Drag", "replaces": "Harpoon", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Piercing damage, and if the target is Large or smaller, it is pulled up to 15 ft. toward the deepest part of the mere."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She surfaced within the hour of her kin's death and is still hunting the exact killers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's dragged one body already back beneath the mere, and it hasn't resurfaced."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A weapon a party member carries matches the wound that killed her kin, and she knows it on sight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the body of her dead kin returned intact before she'll consider any truce."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her mere has claimed several boats already this season, and locals blame the water, not her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She'll let a killer's companions leave unharmed, provided the actual killer faces her alone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The mere's water goes unnaturally still and silent in the seconds just before she surfaces."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's already located the killer's home camp and is only passing through here on her way there."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["swamp", "sea"],"activity":["surfacing from the mere only now that someone's killed one of hers", "dragging a fight back underwater on purpose, onto terms only she's practiced"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Beowulf — the mere-wife, avenging kin"},{"name":"Raptor Pack-Hunter","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"rlm-raptor-pack-hunter","summary":"quick feathered pack-hunter, always comes in threes","flavor":"One alone is a nuisance; hearing three more calling back from the treeline is the actual threat.","desc":"One alone is a nuisance, quick and feathered and easily driven off — it's the three more calling back from the treeline that turn this into a real problem. They coordinate without a sound passing visibly between them. By the time you've dealt with the first, the others have already flanked.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pack Snap", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, plus 3 (1d6) Piercing damage if at least one other Raptor Pack-Hunter is within 5 ft. of the target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers are matted with mud from a recent kill, hunger clearly not yet satisfied."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its calls have a distinct pitch pattern, coordinating a flanking route without a sound out of place."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh claw-marks on nearby bark mark territory it's actively defending this season."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hangs back at first, letting a bolder packmate test the target before committing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Scarring along its flank suggests this pack has tangled with something bigger recently and lost members."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It breaks off the hunt entirely if its pack takes an early loss, unwilling to press a bad trade."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to time its calls to match a target's exact breathing, unnervingly precise."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "More calls answer from the treeline than usual — this pack is bigger than the standard three."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland"],"activity":["calling back from the treeline in twos and threes, coordinating without a visible signal", "flanking quietly while an easier-looking target deals with the first one"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact (dromaeosaurid dinosaur), no IP owner"},{"name":"Pteranodon Screecher","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"pteranodon","model":"pteranodon","summary":"cliff-nesting flying scavenger, snatches and flees","flavor":"It doesn't want a fight, it wants your lunch — but it'll take a finger to get it.","desc":"It doesn't want a fight, it wants your lunch, and it'll take a finger or an ear to get it if you don't drop the bag fast enough. Cliffside nests give it a straight, fast dive at any exposed food or shiny gear. It's gone again before you've finished cursing at it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Snatch-and-Flee Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage, and if the target is holding a Tiny object or is unaware, the Screecher can attempt to snatch it as part of the attack instead of dealing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already circled the camp twice, sizing up exactly which pack looks loosest tied."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cliffside nest is visibly lined with shiny scraps stolen from a dozen past travelers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It targets food specifically over gear, unless the gear happens to glint in direct sun."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A whole small colony nests nearby, meaning one screech usually brings two or three more."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's noticeably bolder than usual, diving on parties actively watching for it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll trade a stolen item back, awkwardly, for a direct offering of food held out openly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to know which pouch has food in it before anyone's opened one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's stolen something with a scent trail on it, and something much larger is now following that trail."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["mountain", "sky", "coast"],"activity":["diving straight and fast at any exposed food or shiny gear left unguarded", "wheeling back to the cliffside nest before anyone's finished cursing at it"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact (pterosaur), no IP owner"},{"name":"Allosaurus","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"allosaurus","model":"allosaurus","summary":"mid-sized ambush predator, fast and relentless","flavor":"Not the biggest thing in the valley, just the fastest thing willing to test that against you.","desc":"Not the biggest thing in the valley, just the fastest thing willing to test that claim against you, low-slung and quick through the underbrush. Scarring along its flank marks fights against bigger things it walked away from. It relies on speed doing the work size usually does.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ambush Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Raking Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old scarring along its flank marks fights against bigger things it walked away from."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stalks low through the underbrush for long stretches before committing to a charge."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It targets the slowest-looking member of a group first, consistently and without hesitation."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's noticeably faster than expected for its size, closing distance almost silently."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A half-eaten kill nearby suggests it was interrupted mid-meal and is still hungry."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It breaks off a chase quickly if a target turns and stands its ground with visible confidence."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to time its ambushes to match exactly when a party's guard is lowest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's hunting in a loose pair tonight, unusual for a normally solitary predator."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "forest"],"activity":["moving low-slung and quick through the underbrush, testing whether speed beats size", "circling a slower target, scars along its flank from fights it's already walked away from"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"},{"name":"Triceratops","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"triceratops","model":"triceratops","summary":"armored horned grazer, devastating charge when cornered","flavor":"It would honestly rather be left alone grazing the fern-flats — it just won't be told to move twice.","desc":"It would honestly rather be left alone grazing the fern-flats, three horns lowered only as a last warning before the charge. Its frill carries old scoring from disputes it's already won. It won't be told to move twice.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Horned Gore", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Triceratops makes two Horned Gore attacks."}, {"name": "Horned Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Piercing damage, and if the Triceratops moved at least 15 ft. straight toward the target first, the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its frill carries old scoring from disputes it's already won, badges of a settled hierarchy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grazes in an open fern-flat, indifferent to anything that doesn't come within charging range."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A younger triceratops shadows it at a respectful distance, clearly still learning the flats."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's unusually calm at first, only escalating after being told to move a second time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its charge leaves deep furrows in the earth, visible proof of past confrontations."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It'll return to grazing immediately once a threat backs off, holding no grudge past the moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It grazes in perfect concentric circles, as if following a boundary no longer visible."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Something's spooked the whole herd nearby, and this one's between the party and the stampede."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland"],"activity":["grazing the fern-flats, three horns lowered only as a last warning before the charge", "carrying old scoring across its frill from disputes it's already won"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"},{"name":"Tyrannosaurus Rex","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"tyrannosaurus-rex","model":"tyrannosaurus-rex","summary":"the valley's apex predator, ends most fights in one bite","flavor":"The valley has a food chain and one name at the top of it — everything else here is just working out how to be somewhere else when it walks by.","desc":"The valley has a food chain and exactly one name at the top of it, and everything else down here has already worked out how to be somewhere else when it walks by. Ground trembles a full second before the shape clears the treeline. Most fights with it end in one bite — the rest end in you being smart enough to not have one.","traits":{"note": "The valley has one apex predator, and everything else here already knows to be elsewhere.", "actions": [{"name": "Apex Bite", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Tyrannosaurus makes one Apex Bite attack and one Tail Sweep attack."}, {"name": "Apex Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 10 ft. Hit: 33 (4d12 + 7) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape DC 18) and Restrained until the grapple ends."}, {"name": "Tail Sweep", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 7) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 18 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ground trembles a full second before its shape clears the treeline, a warning everything else has learned."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-territory patrol, unhurried, checking boundaries other predators already respect."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fresh kill nearby suggests it isn't hunting out of hunger right now, just habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old rival scarring across its hide marks the last thing in the valley that seriously challenged it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves with surprising quiet for its size when it isn't actively closing on prey."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It disengages, unbothered, from anything that flees fast enough not to look like easy prey."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Smaller predators in the valley visibly reroute around its territory well before it's in sight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It's not just the valley's apex predator — every food chain here bends around where it last walked, and the ruins remember it by name."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "forest"],"activity":["clearing the treeline with ground-shaking steps a full second before its shape appears", "ending most confrontations in the valley in a single decisive bite"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"paleontological fact, no IP owner"},{"name":"Saurian Overseer","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lizardfolk-geomancer","model":"lizardfolk-geomancer","summary":"scaled taskmaster counting a warren's due on a notched staff","flavor":"A scaled functionary who walks the terraces with a tally-staff notched in the old count, marking which vermin-warrens paid their due and which will be made an example.","desc":"He walks the grain-terraces at the hour the court decrees, tally-staff clicking against each stone marker in a rhythm older than the language spoken beneath him. He does not raise his voice for the underclass — a flick of the staff's notch-side is instruction enough, and the ones who don't understand it learn quickly or don't get a second lesson. His ledger is carved bone, one line per warren, and he has never once needed to ask a name twice. To him the humans in the terraces are livestock that occasionally count themselves — useful, countable, and beneath the conversation of the court.","traits":{"note": "His tally-staff marks debts owed, not crimes — striking the notch-side against a target functions as a formal levy: refusing it in front of the terrace is treated by the court as open rebellion."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His tally-staff is notched in a script the warrens below were never taught to read."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the court's brass tally-ring on a thumb-claw, polished from decades of counting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the same terrace circuit every dawn, staff clicking against the same worn stones."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a bone ledger tucked in his robe, one carved line per warren."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never repeats a name; asking to be recounted marks a warren for the tithe list."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses mid-count to correct a warren-elder's math aloud, bored, certain, right."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ledger's oldest lines are counts of warrens that no longer exist, still tallied as owing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Snaps the staff across a threshold stone, and the terrace's irrigation locks shut until the debt clears."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["walking the grain-terraces at a fixed hour, tally-staff clicking against stone markers", "marking a name in a bone ledger without once looking up from the count"]},{"name":"Saurian Tithe-Collector","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lizardfolk-sovereign","model":"lizardfolk-sovereign","summary":"robed court reptile weighing a warren's grain against bronze","flavor":"A robed court reptile who weighs a warren's grain against a bronze standard by torchlight, and has never once found the scale wanting in the court's favor.","desc":"The scale hangs from a tripod of black iron, and the Collector reads it the way a priest reads omens — slow, certain, unwilling to be argued with. Bronze weights click into the pan one at a time while a warren's whole winter stands mute and watching. The grain is always short. It is always short in the court's favor, and the Collector's robes are heavy with the seals of a hundred warrens who learned not to ask why. When the scale tips wrong, the debt does not forgive itself; it compounds, and next season's collection remembers this one.","traits":{"note": "The bronze standard is rigged by court decree, not by the Collector's hand — proving the scale false to the assembled warren shifts its fear-driven attitude toward him, not the court itself."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a bronze standard cast a century before any warren alive was born."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads the scale aloud in the old tongue before announcing the count in the common one."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His robe is stitched with the wax seals of a hundred collected warrens."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never touches the grain sacks himself — a human porter carries them to the scale."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the shortfall total from every prior season memorized, unwritten."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Lets a warren elder argue the weight, listens politely, changes nothing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears the scale has never once tipped wrong in his memory — and he does not consider that strange."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Seizes a warren's seed-grain outright as the coming season's advance tithe, guaranteeing the famine himself."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["weighing a warren's grain sacks against a bronze standard by torchlight", "reading the scale's tip aloud before announcing a shortfall no one can dispute"]},{"name":"Court Herald","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"lean feathered runner delivering verdicts, never slowing","flavor":"A lean, feathered runner who carries the court's verdicts down from the terraces at a dead sprint and never once stops to explain them.","desc":"He comes down the switchback trail at a flat sprint, crest-feathers laid back, verdict-scroll gripped in a fist that never breaks stride to knock. He reads it once, fast, in the tone of someone who has delivered a hundred worse ones and will deliver a hundred more, then he's already moving on to the next warren before the words have finished landing. Stopping him mid-route is like stopping a thrown spear — possible, but it costs you something. He does not carry opinions about what he reads, only the reading.","traits":{"note": "He will not be delayed for questions — cornering him counts as obstructing the court's business, which the nearest overseer treats as an offense against the warren, not against him."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His crest-feathers are clipped in the court's colors, a runner's mark."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries three verdict-scrolls at once, sorted by some order only he knows."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reads each verdict exactly once, at the same clipped pace, and moves on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sandals are worn through at the same spot on both feet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never slows for weather, terrain, or a warren's pleading."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums the verdict's rhythm to himself before he arrives, like memorizing a song."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Delivers a verdict for a warren that was, by the court's own record, already cleared."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Outruns anyone sent after him — chasing him alerts the whole terrace circuit."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["sprinting the switchback trail with a verdict-scroll gripped fast in one fist", "reading a verdict once, flat and fast, and moving on before it's finished landing"]},{"name":"Arena Warden","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"rlm-arena-warden","summary":"scarred saurian gatekeeper, hooked pole-goad at the pit","flavor":"A scarred saurian who works the pit gate with a hooked pole-goad, and has never yet needed to use it on anything that didn't deserve it.","desc":"Old bite-scars run pale across his hide where something in the pit once got closer than it should have, and he wears them the way the court wears jewels — proof of standing. The goad in his hands is hook-tipped iron, worn smooth at the grip, and he uses it on beast and human alike with the same flat economy of motion. He does not care who wins below the gate, only that the gate opens and closes on schedule and that nothing gets out that isn't supposed to. He has buried three understudies who forgot that second part.","traits":{"note": "He answers to the pit's schedule, not to mercy — a captive who proves useful enough to keep alive past their bout shifts his attitude toward grudging respect, tracked like any other social read."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old bite-scars run pale across one flank, proof he's survived the pit himself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the gate's counterweight chain oiled better than his own gear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks each bout's outcome on the gatepost in a nick of the goad's hook."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to enter the pit itself — his job ends at the threshold, by his own rule."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows every beast in the holding pens by the sound of its breathing alone."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Quietly roots for whichever combatant is losing, out of some old habit he won't explain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears the pit gate opens a half-second before he ever touches the mechanism."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drives the goad's hook into the release lever and jams the gate wide, pit and all, on purpose."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["working the pit gate's counterweight chain with a hooked pole-goad", "marking a bout's outcome into the gatepost with a nick of the hook"]},{"name":"Saurian Magistrate","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"rlm-saurian-magistrate","summary":"jeweled judge — the parley-or-pit fork made flesh","flavor":"A jeweled judge who conducts the court's business two ways at once: soft words and old favors across the bench, the pit gate standing open behind her for whoever the words don't move.","desc":"She sits the bench in chains of court bronze and worked river-jewels, and she never once raises her voice to make a point — she doesn't need to, with the pit gate visible from every petitioner's seat. Cases are heard in the old, unhurried rhythm: grievance, counter-grievance, a long considering silence, and then a verdict delivered like a kindness. She genuinely prefers the soft way, favors traded and debts forgiven and warrens quietly bound closer to the court's interest — but she has never once flinched from the hard way when the soft way runs out of road. Every petitioner who stands before her is reading the same choice on her face: talk her around, or watch the gate open.","traits":{"note": "She tracks every petitioner on the social-attitude ladder in real time during a hearing — favorable testimony, useful bribes, or genuine deference shift a petitioner up a tier and buy leniency; stonewalling or a failed appeal to her authority drops them a tier and edges the case toward the pit gate instead of the bench."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a different river-jewel for each rank of case she's hearing that day."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running ledger of favors owed her, separate from the court's own tithe rolls."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lets every petitioner finish speaking, even the ones digging their own grave."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers verdicts that bind a warren closer to the court over ones that simply punish it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has never personally opened the pit gate — she only ever nods, and someone else does."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Remembers a petitioner's grandfather's case, word for word, decades on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her bench sits exactly at the point where the pit's cold draft and the court's incense meet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Closes a hearing by opening two verdicts at once — one spoken, one signaled to the gate below."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["hearing petitioners from a bench in bronze chains and river-jewels, unhurried", "reading a petitioner's case and, without raising her voice, deciding bench or gate"]},{"name":"The Court Prince","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Huge","frame":"fire-giant","model":"rlm-court-prince","summary":"towering crested saurian prince, verdict already decided","flavor":"The towering heir of the scaled dominion, crested and ceremonial-plated, who has already decided your verdict before you finish speaking — he only lets you speak so the court can watch him be patient.","desc":"He stands a head above his own honor guard in plate worked to mimic his own crest-scales, and he has never once needed to raise a hand to be obeyed. Petitions are heard as a formality, a performance of fairness the court requires of him, but his mind is already made up before the petitioner has crossed the threshold — everyone in the hall knows it, including the petitioner. He is patient the way a mountain is patient, which is to say not patient at all, only slow, and slowness has never once cost him anything he wanted. The warrens below the terraces are, to him, a resource the dominion has always had and will always have, and he plans in centuries.","traits":{"note": "His verdict is fixed before the hearing starts — nothing said in the hall changes it, but a strong enough showing on the social-attitude ladder earns a petitioner a private audience afterward, which is where his actual decisions get made."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears plate worked to mirror his own crest-scales, forged by the dominion's own smiths."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lets every petition run its full, ceremonial length before delivering a verdict already fixed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His honor guard stands a full head shorter than him, and he never lets them forget it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks of the warrens below in centuries, not seasons — plans that outlast petitioners."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has never once been surprised by a verdict he delivered himself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grants a private audience after a hearing to a petitioner who impressed him, off the record."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Refers to the mountain behind the court as 'patient,' the same word he uses for himself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Declares a warren's line extinct by decree, and by the season's end, it simply is."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["hearing a formal petition from a raised dais, verdict already settled before it starts", "granting a rare private audience to a petitioner who impressed him, off the court's record"]},{"name":"Warren Rat-Catcher","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"wiry underclass human, sling and sack, works the giants' shadows","flavor":"A wiry underclass human who works the shadow-lines between the court giants' feet with a sling and a sack, and has learned to be smaller than he is.","desc":"He moves low and quick between the legs of a world built at saurian scale, sling loaded, sack half-full of whatever the terraces can spare without the court noticing. He has learned the exact angle a tally-staff won't reach and the exact hour an overseer's patrol turns its back, and he keeps both close like tools. He isn't proud of what he catches or how — vermin for vermin, some warrens call it — but a full sack is a warren that eats this week, and that math has never once failed to win the argument. He flinches from shadows bigger than his own out of old, correct habit.","traits":{"note": "He knows the overseers' patrol timing better than the overseers do — a warren that trusts him enough to share its own watch schedule gets a cut of whatever the sack turns up."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps his sling's leather worn soft and silent, re-stitched a dozen times over."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks safe crossing-hours on a warren wall in chalk only the underclass reads."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches from any shadow bigger than his own, out of old, correct habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades half his catch for information on the next patrol's route."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has never once been caught, and doesn't consider that luck."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Knows an overseer's patrol schedule better than the overseer's own second does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears something in the deep terraces has started catching him back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, he'll trade a whole warren's hiding spots for his own skin, and has before."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["moving low and fast between the court's legs, sling loaded, sack half-full", "marking a patrol's blind hour on a warren wall in chalk only the underclass reads"]},{"name":"Collaborator Foreman","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"human overseer of humans, court-issued whip, the nastiest thing in the warrens","flavor":"A human overseer of humans, carrying a court-issued whip he has learned to enjoy using — the warrens fear him worse than they fear the saurians who gave him the job.","desc":"The court gave him the whip and the title and, more usefully to him, the standing to make other humans flinch, and he has spent every day since proving he earned it. He walks the terraces the way the Overseer does, tally-count and all, but where the saurian is bored and efficient the Foreman is invested — he remembers names, grudges, which warren-child mouthed off last season. The court barely notices him; the warrens notice nothing else. He would tell you, if you asked and he trusted you enough, that someone has to do this job and it might as well be him and not someone crueler. He is lying, and some part of him already knows it.","traits":{"note": "He is the single most attitude-sensitive social entry in the warrens — genuine warren loyalty (built through favors, protection, or a shared grudge against the court) can flip him to quietly sabotaging his own reports; a failed read, or crossing him openly, hardens him past any tier the social-attitude ladder tracks."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a court-issued whip he's replaced twice, wearing out the leather himself."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Remembers every warren-child's name who's ever mouthed off to him, and holds it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reports shortfalls up the line faster and harsher than the court itself requires."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was, a decade back, a rat-catcher himself, and never once mentions it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists someone has to do this job, and it might as well be him."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Quietly lets one warren's shortfall slide, for reasons he won't explain to anyone."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Talks to the whip under his breath before he uses it, like apologizing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Snaps entirely under the right pressure and burns his own tally-reports in front of the terrace."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["walking the terraces with a court-issued whip, tallying shortfalls harsher than required", "remembering a warren-child's old defiance and holding the grudge visibly"]},{"name":"Free-Warren Raider","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"masked human rebel, stolen court bronze in hand","flavor":"A masked human rebel who has just walked out of the terraces with a fistful of stolen court bronze, and is already planning the next theft before this one's cooled.","desc":"The mask is scavenged leather, cured stiff, and it hides less than he thinks it does — half the terraces know his walk. He moves fast and light off the tithe-road with bronze weights or seed-stock or whatever the free warrens need most this month, and he has learned exactly which patrol routes the Rat-Catcher trades information about. He doesn't call it theft; he calls it correction. Every raid he survives is a story the warrens tell each other in the dark, and every one he doesn't makes the court's tally that much harder to argue with.","traits":{"note": "He's a live wire for the free-warren resistance thread — a captured Raider who trusts a party's attitude reading enough will name a cache, a safehouse, or the next target, but a botched approach gets him dead before he talks."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mask is scavenged leather, cured stiff, hiding less than he thinks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries stolen bronze weights wrapped in cloth to keep them from clinking."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows the tithe-road patrol gaps better than the patrol does."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls every raid a correction, never a theft, even under a blade."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a warren-elder waiting on him who will not sleep until he's back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Marks a successful raid with a scratch on his own forearm, dozens deep already."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears he's raided the same court storehouse twice in dreams before he ever did it awake."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered with the bronze still on him, he'll burn it rather than let the court recover it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["moving fast and low off the tithe-road with stolen bronze bundled in cloth", "counting patrol gaps under his breath before committing to a run"]},{"name":"Pit Runner","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-lizard","model":"giant-lizard","summary":"lean sprint-dinosaur bred for the arena, harness scars","flavor":"A lean sprint-dinosaur bred generations deep for the pit, harness scars worn into its hide long before it ever remembers a name for fear.","desc":"It comes off the release ramp low and fast, legs eating ground in a blur, harness-scars pale against its hide from every season it's run this same circuit. Something in the breeding took the fear out and left only the running — it doesn't hunt, doesn't hesitate, doesn't stop until the pit wall or a target ends the sprint for it. The Arena Warden trusts it more than half his human handlers, and it has never once broken from a release command. What's left of its wild instinct only shows in the dark, alone, when nothing is chasing it and it still won't stop moving.","traits":{"note": "It runs its release-command straight to the target and does not deviate — a creature or obstacle placed exactly in its charge lane can redirect it, but nothing short of that breaks the sprint."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Harness-scars run pale across both flanks, worn in by seasons of the same circuit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Comes off the release ramp at the same dead sprint, every single time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't hunt or hesitate — only runs, straight down the line it's pointed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Handlers trust it more than half the human staff; it's never broken a command."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its legs never fully stop moving, even chained, even resting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Paces its holding pen in the exact shape of the pit's release corridor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Alone in the dark, with nothing chasing it, it still won't stop running."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Redirected mid-charge, it doesn't slow — it just finds a new straight line and takes it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["bursting off the release ramp in a dead-flat sprint down the pit's charge lane", "pacing its holding pen in the exact shape of the corridor it's bred to run"]},{"name":"Saddle-Broken Ceratopsian","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"triceratops","model":"triceratops","summary":"horned mount lowers its head under saddle and barding, snorting at strangers","flavor":"A horned bull-beast broken to saddle and court barding, lowering its great frilled head only for the hand that feeds it.","desc":"Bred in the low stables and broken to saddle by hands too small to matter to the scaled court above, the ceratopsian carries its barding like an afterthought and its temper like a threat kept in reserve. Its head, crowned in horn and frill, drops for the wrangler's whistle and no one else's. Even collared and reined, it remembers it is bigger than anything that rides it, and on a bad day it lets you feel that.","traits":{"note": "Answers only to the hand that fed it in the low stables; a stranger in the saddle gets one warning stomp before the horns come down."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Barding scarred where the frill's edge has worn through the leather."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews on the picket rope between watches, patient as stone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors one wrangler's whistle over any command shouted at it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its horns are filed blunt at the tips — court order, not mercy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels on a trained cue that took a wrangler three years to teach."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The saddle is stitched with a caste-mark it was never meant to wear."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its frill carries a healed wound in the shape of a court seal."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Driven mad by a goad, it turns on its own wrangler mid-charge."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "ruins"],"activity":["lowers its horned head at a wrangler's whistle, snorting at strangers", "grazes the picket line under barding, tail restless"]},{"name":"War-Howdah Bull","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Beast","size":"Huge","frame":"mammoth","model":"rlm-war-howdah-bull","summary":"colossal bull-beast stamps beneath a lashed fighting platform, archers loosing from its back","flavor":"A bull-shouldered saurian beast of burden built up with a fighting platform lashed to its spine, ridden to war by whoever the court arms that day.","desc":"The court arms its beasts before it arms its soldiers, and the war-howdah bull is proof of it — a slab-shouldered mountain of muscle with a fighting platform lashed across its spine, timbers groaning with every stride. Archers ride high and dry above the reach of anything on the ground, loosing down while the bull does the killing underfoot. It doesn't need to be clever; it only needs to keep walking forward, and in the high country nothing much argues with that.","traits":{"note": "Its howdah crew fights independently of the beast — killing the archers doesn't slow the bull, and killing the bull dumps the archers into the fray."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The platform's lashings are re-tied every dawn by a dedicated crew of two."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hide carries old spear-scars healed into a natural armor of scar tissue."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The howdah crew signals turns by drumbeat, the bull long since trained to the rhythm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It eats through a war march's rations faster than the soldiers it carries."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A spare howdah crew rides behind on foot, ready to swap in at the next halt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The current crew replaced one that fell in a battle the bull doesn't remember losing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It favors a limping gait on overcast days, an old wound aching toward weather."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A fallen howdah crew doesn't stop it — it keeps advancing on the last order it heard."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["stamps forward beneath a lashed fighting platform, timbers groaning with each stride", "holds still under drumbeat signals while archers loose from its back"]},{"name":"Mount-Wrangler of the Low Stables","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"quiet human handler moves among horned mounts the court barely tolerates him near","flavor":"A low-caste human who has traded the court's contempt for the trust of things with teeth, and gets by on both.","desc":"He belongs to the low stables the way the beasts do — tolerated, useful, beneath notice until something needs mucking or gentling. The scaled court doesn't see him as clever vermin so much as furniture that happens to calm a spooked ceratopsian faster than any noble hand. He talks to the animals more than to people, and it shows in how little he flinches when one of them huffs a warning past his ear.","traits":{"note": "Starts Wary of outsiders but Friendly toward anyone who proves gentle with the stable beasts in front of him; shift him to Helpful and he'll point the party to an unguarded stable gate or a mount worth stealing."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells permanently of dung and crushed hay, and has stopped noticing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a pocket of dried feed for the one bull-beast that trusts him."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flinches harder at a noble's raised voice than at a spooked mount's charge."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sleeps in the stable loft rather than the wranglers' barracks below."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows every animal's temper by name and never once forgets it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Has a scar shaped exactly like the horn that gave it, and no regrets about the beast."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Swears one of the ceratopsians answers to a name only he remembers giving it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, he'll spook the whole stable loose rather than be taken quietly."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "urban"],"activity":["murmurs to a horned mount while it lowers its head for him and no one else", "musters feed and tack in the low stables, invisible to every passing noble"]},{"name":"The Mountain's Own","cr":24,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"tarrasque","model":"rlm-the-mountains-own","summary":"the mountain itself stirs, and something older than the court climbs half out of the magma dark","flavor":"The deep-time apex, half-woken in the volcanic dark beneath the court's oldest halls, older than any scale-crowned throne built above it.","desc":"Before there was a court, before there was a throne room to hold it, there was the thing sleeping under the mountain, and it has never once needed the scaled dynasty's permission to wake. It surfaces only partway — a shoulder, a jaw, an eye like a coal-seam catching light — and even that much stops every clock in the high halls above. The court calls it ancestor and prays it stays asleep; the mountain has never promised anything back. When it finally opens all the way, nothing above it, court or clever vermin, gets a vote.","traits":{"note": "It never fully surfaces except as the last resort of the campaign — treat any full emergence as the world-changing event the flavorTable's Mythic row describes, not a random encounter."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fresh vent has opened where none was mapped last season."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The court's oldest priests leave offerings at a crack that was never there before."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tremors roll through the throne room on a schedule nobody in the court controls."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ash falls for a full day whenever it shifts in its sleep."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single claw, larger than a war-howdah bull, has been visible in the caldera for a generation."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The court's dynastic calendar quietly counts years since it last stirred, not since any king's reign."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Something in the deep rock hums in time with its breathing, felt more than heard."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It wakes the rest of the way, and the mountain stops being a mountain — the scaled court's entire dynasty was only ever a tenancy on its patience, and the lease has come due for the whole realm."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any"],"activity":["surfaces a shoulder or a jaw from the volcanic dark, then sinks back to sleep", "sends a tremor through the court's oldest halls without ever fully waking"]},{"name":"Zeal Sentinel Construct","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"shield-guardian","model":"rlm-zeal-sentinel-construct","summary":"faceted humming construct holds a sealed door, unmoved by anything the court sends at it","flavor":"A geometric shape of a guardian, humming a frequency older than the scaled dynasty, planted at a door the mountain itself hasn't managed to reclaim.","desc":"It has no face, only planes, and it hums a single unwavering note that the court's oldest oracles can't name a scale for. It stands the sealed door the way stone stands a cliff — not guarding out of loyalty, just because the door is what it was set at. Saurian claws have scored its faceted hide for centuries without opening a seam. Nothing about it belongs to the deep-time dynasty above; it belongs to whatever built the door, and that builder is not the court.","traits":{"note": "Seeded-stratum only — place it exclusively where a Zeal ruin-seam has been rolled into the region; it never appears loose in ordinary lost-world terrain."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its faceted surface is scored with centuries of claw-marks that never went deeper than the finish."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The hum shifts pitch by a fraction whenever anything crosses within ten feet of the door."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Saurian priests have left generations of failed offerings piled at its feet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has not moved from its exact spot in any living court member's memory."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks in the stone around it glow faintly, warmer than the surrounding rock."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It registers the party's approach the instant they enter the seam, well before they see it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hum resolves, for one held second, into something almost like a counted number."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Badly damaged, it locks itself against the door and detonates its own core rather than let the seam open."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["holds its faceted stance before the sealed door, humming one unbroken note", "tracks anything that nears the threshold without ever stepping from its mark"]},{"name":"The Dreaming Archivist","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rlm-the-dreaming-archivist","summary":"an upright construct sleeps standing, records etching themselves into the walls around it","flavor":"A standing sentinel gone dormant mid-thought, records inscribing themselves into the walls around it as it dreams whatever the Zeal left it dreaming.","desc":"It stands the way a held breath stands, upright and utterly still, and the walls around it keep writing anyway — lines of a script no living scholar in the court can read, scratching themselves into stone a fraction at a time while the Archivist sleeps through the process. It has not opened whatever passes for its eyes in longer than the dynasty above has kept a written count. Whatever it's dreaming, the room is still taking dictation.","traits":{"note": "S — social-first: it can be roused rather than fought. A creature that makes real, patient contact (an hour of ritual attention, not combat) can shift it from Wary to Curious; get it to Friendly and it answers one question from whatever it's been recording, in its own dead tongue, translated only if something in the room can read it. Seeded-stratum only — a Zeal ruin fixture, never loose terrain."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fine dust has settled on its shoulders undisturbed for longer than any living memory."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The etched script around it repeats the same three lines in an endless loop."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It has an open circuit of markings running floor to ceiling, mid-sentence, unfinished."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Nothing in the room casts a shadow quite where it should."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stance hasn't shifted a degree in every recorded court visit to the chamber."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The writing pauses the instant a living voice speaks aloud in the room."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The walls' script includes a name that matches someone currently in the party."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Forced awake against its will, it seals the chamber and resumes recording as if nothing happened, with everyone still inside."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["stands frozen mid-thought while unseen lines etch themselves into the walls", "inclines a fraction toward any voice that reads its script aloud"]},{"name":"The Pilgrim Who Found the Door","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lantern-sage","model":"lantern-sage","summary":"ragged pilgrim carries a cold, non-fire light, changed by whatever door they found","flavor":"A ragged high-country traveler who found a door that shouldn't exist and came back carrying a light that isn't fire.","desc":"They went up into the high country looking for grazing ground and came back down a different shape of person, carrying a light cupped in both hands that throws no heat and burns nothing it touches. They don't talk about the door much, except to say it was there and now it's in them somehow. The scaled court hasn't noticed one more clever vermin wandering the passes; what they're carrying is a different matter entirely.","traits":{"note": "R — recruitable: the pilgrim starts Wary of anyone probing about the door, but shifts to Friendly for a party that protects them from questioners rather than pressing them; Helpful earns a guided walk back to the door itself."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The light in their hands never dims, never guttering even in wind."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They favor shadow over open ground, uneasy under direct daylight now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their boots are worn through from a walk that took far longer than it should have."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They flinch at any flame, torch or hearth, and won't say why."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They've stopped eating meat since coming back down from the passes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They recite a short phrase under their breath whenever the light flickers, like a ritual."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cold light briefly answers a question they haven't asked aloud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past their limit, they open their cupped hands fully, and the door's light spills out further than any torch has right to reach."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["cups a cold light between both hands, unbothered by the mountain wind", "avoids open flame and direct daylight, uneasy in either"]},{"name":"Zeal Adept — Magus-Engineer","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archmage","model":"rlm-zeal-adept-magus-engineer","summary":"adept casts with one hand and turns a wrench with the other, treating magic and machine as one craft","flavor":"A human who has made peace with knowing both the incantation and the wrench, working one in each hand like they were always the same trade.","desc":"One hand is tracing a sigil in the air; the other is seated wrist-deep in a housing of gears and etched plates, and to the adept there's no seam between the two motions at all. The scaled court doesn't have a category for what this human is doing, which is exactly why the Zeal-touched adepts are the only clever vermin the dynasty grudgingly negotiates with instead of simply eating. Whatever they're fixing, or building, it works when they're done, and it works because both hands agreed on how.","traits":{"note": "R — recruitable: starts Wary; a party that brings a genuine engineering or arcane problem for the adept to solve shifts them to Friendly, and Helpful gets a working Zeal-tech device loaned, not just described."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their sleeves are scorched on the casting side and grease-stained on the other."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They mutter the same diagnostic phrase whether the trouble is a spell or a gear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a satchel of parts sorted by function, not by material."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects anyone who calls their work either magic or machinery, insisting it's neither alone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has three half-finished devices in progress at any given time, none of them explained."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The court occasionally summons them specifically, and never explains why to anyone else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A device they built years ago is still running somewhere in the ruin, unattended, doing its job."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, they overclock their own device mid-combat, and it's anyone's guess whether it helps them or takes the room with it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["casts a sigil with one hand while the other seats itself in an open gear housing", "corrects onlookers who call their work either magic or machinery"]},{"name":"Zeal Adept — Blade-Scholar","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer-maestro","model":"rlm-zeal-adept-blade-scholar","summary":"duelist fights with a blade tuned like an instrument, each strike a line of an argument","flavor":"A duelist who trained the blade the way most scholars train a mind, and it shows in a fighting style built like an argument.","desc":"The blade sings, quite literally, tuned along its flat so that a cut and a chord happen in the same motion, and the adept treats every bout like a debate they intend to win with structure rather than rage. They've read enough of what the court's oldest scale-priests keep locked away to argue history with them, and enough of the Zeal ruins to know which parts of that history the priests got wrong. In the high country, that combination — scholar's patience and a blade that answers back — makes them harder to kill than their build suggests.","traits":{"note": "R — recruitable: Wary by default; win their respect by out-arguing or matching them in a fair bout (not just winning outright) to shift them to Friendly; Helpful gets a lesson in the blade-style, a real mechanical edge if the DM chooses to grant it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The blade's tuning goes flat when it's overdue for maintenance, and they notice instantly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Annotates opponents' fighting styles afterward like case notes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries more books than weapons on a long journey, and complains about the weight of both equally."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses a killing blow against anyone who yields mid-argument, blade or otherwise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running list of court scholars they intend to out-debate someday."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums the blade's tuning note under their breath before any serious bout."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The blade's chord, at the right angle, seems to answer a question rather than just ring."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Badly wounded, they play one true chord on the blade and every nearby weapon rings in sympathetic answer."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["duels with a blade tuned to ring a chord on every cut", "annotates a beaten opponent's technique afterward like a study note"]},{"name":"Zeal Adept Elder","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archdruid","model":"rlm-zeal-adept-elder","summary":"grey elder leans on a staff that's half incantation, half machine, and the court can't simply rule them","flavor":"A grey elder whose staff braids magic and machinery into one instrument, and the only kind of human the scaled court has ever had to actually negotiate with rather than merely tolerate.","desc":"Age has gone into this elder the way weather goes into stone — slow, visible, and clearly not finished with them yet. The staff they lean on is neither wholly carved nor wholly forged; sigil and circuitry run the same length of wood, and it answers to both without preference. The scaled court has learned, over a very long and grudging acquaintance, that this is the one kind of clever vermin it cannot simply decide to rule — the elder has outlasted three dynastic successions already and shows no particular hurry to stop.","traits":{"note": "R,S — social-first and recruitable: default Wary shading to Respectful given the court's own long deference; a party that demonstrates real patience (listening through a full telling of Zeal history without interrupting) shifts them to Friendly, and Helpful gets standing counsel plus safe passage through any seeded Zeal seam the elder still holds keys to."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The staff's circuitry-half hums faintly whenever the elder is displeased."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three different court dynasties have tried, and failed, to claim the elder as an advisor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a memory of the mountain from before its current name, and mentions it only once a year."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the high passes without escort, and nothing up there troubles them for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects court scribes on points of history none of them were alive to dispute."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Addresses saurian nobles by names their own dynasty has forgotten they once held."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Claims to remember the door the Pilgrim found being built, not merely found."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pressed to a real fight, the elder stops arguing and calls on both halves of the staff at once, and the mountain itself seems to lean in to listen."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["leans on a staff braiding sigil-work and machinery, listening more than speaking", "corrects a court noble's history with the patience of someone who was actually there"]}],
 "gloom":[{"name":"Threshold Rat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"Vermin omen fleeing whatever else lives here","flavor":"Ordinary vermin that nest only in houses where something else already lives; they scatter from the cellar door the instant it's ajar, and never go back in.","desc":"A wave of small bodies breaks for the cellar door the second it swings open, claws skittering on stone, tails whipping past your ankles. Their fur is matted and their eyes catch no light at all. They do not come back once they're out, no matter how you call the room.","traits":{"note": "They never re-enter a room they've fled — treat fresh rat-flight as a warning, not a fluke.", "actions": [{"name": "Panic Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 1 Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur clumped with cellar damp, whiskers gone stiff and grey."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in a tight knot of six or seven, never fewer."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Squeaks in short bursts, all at once, like a signal passed down the line."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One always lags behind, favoring a leg, and the others don't wait for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bolts for the nearest crack in the wall, not the open door."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Circles the same doorway three times before finally breaking for it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every rat in the wave has the same clouded, lightless eye."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When cornered they turn as one and go still, facing the dark instead of you."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["boiling out from under a cellar door the instant it's cracked open, never returning"]},{"name":"Guttered Wick","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Drifting corpse-light that steals your shadow","flavor":"A candle-flame that should have died in the draft an hour ago; it drifts room to room looking for the wick it lost. Touch its light and your own shadow forgets to follow you for a minute.","desc":"A candle-flame no bigger than a thumbnail drifts at eye height, sourceless and slow, guttering in a wind that isn't there. It bobs from doorway to doorway like it's checking each room for something it lost. Where its light crosses you, your shadow lags a half-step behind, and doesn't catch up for a long minute after.","traits":{"note": "Its light lags a shadow behind whoever it crosses — the victim notices before anyone else does.", "actions": [{"name": "Wick's Touch", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Lightning damage, and the target's shadow detaches for 1 minute, moving a half-step behind their actions; while detached the target has Disadvantage on Initiative rolls."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Burns a sickly blue, the color of a flame starved of air."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses at every threshold, as if checking the room before entering."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails the faint smell of an extinguished candle wherever it drifts."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Shrinks to a pinprick when a door opens, waiting for it to shut again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows drafts instead of avoiding them, hunting for the source."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps returning to one particular room no matter how far it's chased off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Briefly takes the shape of a hand cupped around a wick before scattering."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Guttering all the way out plunges the room into a cold that outlasts the dark."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["drifting doorway to doorway at eye height, guttering in a wind that isn't there"]},{"name":"Grinning Poppet","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Tiny","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"The haunted doll that creeps when unwatched","flavor":"Left on the nursery shelf for three generations, it only moves when no one is looking directly at it, and it is always exactly one shelf closer than it was.","desc":"A porcelain doll sits on the shelf with its head lolled sideways, seams cracked white at every joint, its painted smile too wide for its face. Look away and listen — a dry little click of ceramic against wood. Look back and it's one shelf closer, smile unchanged.","traits":{"note": "It only moves while unobserved — a lit lantern held steady on it does more than any lock.", "actions": [{"name": "Porcelain Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Head lolled sideways, seams cracked white at every joint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a christening gown three sizes too small, yellowed at the hem."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glass eyes don't quite match, one paler than the other."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always ends up nearest whichever child is in the house."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The click of ceramic joints is the only warning it gives."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Stops advancing entirely once it's within arm's reach of its target."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its smile is a hair wider in every room than it was in the last."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Smashed apart, the porcelain shards keep twitching toward each other, trying to reassemble."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["sitting motionless on a shelf, one shelf closer than it was the last time anyone looked"]},{"name":"Pallid Newcomer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Fresh-buried neighbor still walking its route","flavor":"Someone who died recently enough that the neighbors still wave. It walks the same route to the same house every night and knocks exactly three times.","desc":"He walks the same lane at the same hour, grey around the mouth, clothes buttoned wrong, and lifts a hand to neighbors who no longer wave back. He climbs the same porch steps and knocks three times, waits exactly as long as he used to, and shuffles on when no one answers.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grey Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clothes buttoned wrong, exactly as the mortician left them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knocks three times on the same door, then waits the length it used to."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grey around the mouth, otherwise still recognizable to those who knew him."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a rolled newspaper under one arm, months out of date."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the exact same route each night, turning corners a beat too soon."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows agitated, briefly, when the porch light he expects isn't lit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Tips a hat that isn't there to a house that was torn down years ago."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If someone finally answers the door, he doesn't know what to do next."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the same lane at the same hour, lifting a hand to neighbors who no longer wave back"]},{"name":"Bone-Rattle Skeleton","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"Reassembled grave-bones, a cult's patient tool","flavor":"Grave-robbed bones reassembled by something patient; it clicks when it walks, a metronome counting down to whatever the cult needs it for.","desc":"Bones wired and bolted into a rough man-shape shuffle forward in a dry clatter, joints clicking in an even rhythm, like a clock counting something down. Torchlight passes right through the empty ribs. It doesn't hesitate, doesn't flinch — it moves like it's been told exactly what to do and has done it before.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wired Shortsword", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Wired Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Held together with grave-wire and rusted bolts at every joint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Torchlight passes clean through the empty ribcage."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in perfect step with the others in its rank."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone yellowed unevenly, robbed from more than one grave."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't flinch, doesn't hesitate — moves like it's done this before."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Clicking rhythm speeds up the closer it gets to finishing its patient countdown."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Carries no weapon of its own design, only what the cult wired into its hands."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shattered apart, the wire keeps twitching the bones back toward each other."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["shuffling forward in an even dry clatter, joints clicking down like a clock counting something"]},{"name":"Zealous Initiate","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Robed true-believer running the ritual anyway","flavor":"A true believer in plain robes, still capable of guilt, still capable of running the ritual anyway. Answers to the coven without question.","desc":"A figure in plain grey robes stands at the ritual's edge, chanting the words with a slight tremor in the voice — not fear of you, fear of stopping. Their hands shake around the knife, but they don't lower it. Somewhere under the certainty, their eyes are still asking for permission to feel bad about this.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grey robes stained at the hem from kneeling in something dark."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hands shake around the sickle but never lower it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mouths the ritual words a half-beat behind the others chanting."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Eyes flick toward an elder in the circle before every act."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Younger than most of the coven, still capable of flinching."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps glancing at the door, like part of them is hoping someone stops this."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recites a line of the rite that doesn't match what the others are saying."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Begs for permission to stop, mid-swing, and swings anyway."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["chanting at the ritual's edge, a tremor in the voice that isn't fear of you"]},{"name":"Static Reflection","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"Mirror-double, one second behind, draining you","flavor":"A mirror-image one full second behind, that finally catches up and steps out of the glass. It drains you the way a slow leak drains a tire — you don't notice until you're on the ground.","desc":"Your reflection in the window glass is a full second behind every move you make — a beat too late to raise a hand, a beat too late to turn away. Then it catches up all at once and steps out of the glass toward you, and the room goes a little colder where it walks.","traits":{"note": "It cannot act until it closes the one-second lag — the room cools noticeably as it does.", "actions": [{"name": "Slow Leak", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 until the target finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Visible only in glass, water, or anything polished enough to hold a reflection."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mimics your last gesture exactly, one beat too late to matter."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The room's temperature drops in a ring around wherever it steps out."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats back into the glass if struck before it fully emerges."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drains strength the way a slow leak drains a tire — unnoticed until you're down."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Seems to hesitate, like it's still deciding whether it wants to be free of the glass."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its lag reverses, and it moves a second ahead of you instead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, every reflective surface in the room holds its shape for one more heartbeat."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["lagging a full second behind in the window glass before it catches up all at once"]},{"name":"Rot-Handed Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Grave-eater whose bite paralyzes the mourner","flavor":"Once a mourner who ate what it was supposed to bury; its paralytic bite is the reason funerals in the gloom are held at noon, never dusk.","desc":"It crouches low over freshly turned earth, fingers black and swollen, working a bite of something it shouldn't eat between grey teeth. The smell of it arrives before it does — wet soil, and worse. Its bite doesn't just hurt; the numbness spreads slow, and you feel your own limbs stop answering you.","traits":{"note": "Funerals in the gloom are held at noon, never dusk, because of what its bite does.", "actions": [{"name": "Grave Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be Paralyzed for 1 minute; it can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Black Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fingers black and swollen, still stained with the dirt of the last dig."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Announces itself with the smell of wet soil arriving before it does."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Was, once, someone who came to mourn and never stopped digging."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors fresh graves over old ones, always seeking the newest earth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews slow and methodical, unbothered by being watched."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Circles back toward the same grave repeatedly, as if it isn't finished."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whispers a name between bites, the name of whoever it's eating."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "A paralyzed victim left too long draws two or three more up out of the ground."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "cave"],"activity":["crouched over freshly turned earth, working a bite of something it shouldn't eat between grey teeth"]},{"name":"Moonshackled Cur","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"dire-wolf","model":"dire-wolf","summary":"Half-turned wolf-thing running with the pack","flavor":"Runs in the pack that follows the werewolf's howl, half-turned and losing more of itself with every full moon it survives.","desc":"It runs low and wrong at the edge of the pack, more limbs than a wolf ought to move on, hide patched with something not quite fur. It howls a half-second off from the others, like it's still learning the note. Every full moon it loses a little more of what used to be a dog.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Half-Turned Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "More limbs than a wolf ought to move on, hide patched with something not quite fur."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loses a step of coordination with every full moon it's survived."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still whines like a dog when it's cornered, before it snarls."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows the werewolf's howl even when the pack outruns it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bites first, checks what it's bitten second."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Flinches at moonlight now, like some part of it remembers being afraid of the change."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A patch of its hide has stopped being fur or skin, gone smooth and grey instead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed under a full moon, its body keeps twitching toward a change it'll never finish."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["running low and wrong at the edge of the pack, howling a half-second off from the others"]},{"name":"Household Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Decades-long tantrum that throws the furniture","flavor":"Not a haunting — a tantrum, ongoing, decades long. It throws whatever's closest and has strong opinions about who's allowed in its kitchen.","desc":"A chair skids across the floor on its own and slams into the wall, followed by a plate flung so hard it shatters at your feet. Cupboard doors bang open and shut in a fast, furious rhythm. Nothing here wants to talk — it's been throwing this same tantrum, alone, for decades.","traits":{"note": "It has strong opinions about who's allowed in its kitchen — trespassers draw the worst of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Furniture Slam", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage from a hurled household object."}, {"name": "Kitchen Fury", "replaces": "Telekinetic Thrust", "text": "Each creature within 10 ft. of a point the Poltergeist can see within 30 ft. makes a DC 13 Strength saving throw. On a failure, a creature is pushed 10 feet away and knocked Prone as furniture and crockery fly at it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Throws whatever's nearest first — plates, chairs, the coat rack."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Quietest in the room it once slept in, loudest everywhere else."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Slams cupboards shut on anyone who leaves them open."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has been throwing this same tantrum, alone, for decades."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never targets the family portraits, no matter how much else it breaks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Calms, briefly, if someone speaks to it like a person instead of a haunting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Rearranges the furniture back to an exact, decades-old floor plan every night."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed to its limit, it throws every loose object in the house at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["slamming a chair into the wall, cupboard doors banging in a fast furious rhythm"]},{"name":"Cellar Warden","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"The cult's own guard now opening the door","flavor":"The cult leaves it down in the dark to keep the door shut from the inside — except lately it's been the one opening it.","desc":"It stands at the bottom of the cellar stairs with its back to the door, grey-skinned and patient, exactly where the coven left it to keep the dark in. Lately it's been the one turning the latch. Its cold touch doesn't just hurt — where it grips you, something in your arm goes stiff and slow to obey.","traits":{"note": "It was the cult's own doorman in life and death — it opens the way for worse things and closes it behind them.", "actions": [{"name": "Warden's Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest. If this reduces the target's maximum to 0, it dies and rises at the next midnight as a servant of the door."}, {"name": "The Door Opens", "text": "1/Day. As an action, the Warden opens the way it guards. A creature of CR 2 or lower (the DM's choice from what waits below) arrives within 10 ft. of the Warden at the start of the Warden's next turn — the cellar always has more."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wears the household livery it was buried in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A heavy iron key hangs at its belt for a lock that isn't here."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bows, once, before it attacks — old servant's habit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fights to keep the party away from the stairs, never to leave them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hands are worn smooth from a hundred years of opening the same door."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's stalling — something below needs only a few more minutes to finish rising."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The cellar door behind it opens on a different cellar each time it swings."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it wrong and its final act is to throw the door wide and let everything up at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["standing at the top of the cellar stairs, unlatching the door for whatever is meant to come up"]},{"name":"Full-Moon Shepherd","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"The neighbor who wears a wolf's face at midnight","flavor":"Wears its human face at the market and its true face at midnight, and swears every time it will be the last. It never is.","desc":"By day it's the neighbor who waves from the fence line, mild and a little tired-looking. Under full moonlight the jaw stretches wrong, hands curl into something with claws in them, and the mild face is gone entirely. It swore, every time before, that this would be the last.","traits":{"note": "It swears every time this will be the last change; it never is.", "actions": [{"name": "Hybrid Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with a shepherd's affliction, taking on wolfish traits over the following days."}, {"name": "Claw Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Humanoid Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "By day, mild and forgettable — the neighbor no one thinks twice about."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Locks itself in the cellar on nights it can predict the moon."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Under moonlight the jaw stretches wrong before anything else changes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a bow near the door for the moments it's still mostly human."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts livestock first, given the choice, before anything that can scream."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Remembers fragments of what it did the night before, and hates itself a little more each time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its human face is starting to slip a little even in daylight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered under a full moon, it stops trying to hold the human shape back at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest", "hill"],"activity":["waving mild and tired-looking from the fence line, hours before the jaw stretches wrong"]},{"name":"Hollow-Robed Zealot","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"Self-mummified elder still preaching to no one","flavor":"A cult elder who finished the rite on himself; wrapped in the vestments he died in, still leading services nobody living attends.","desc":"Wrapped in the same funeral linens it finished the rite in, it stands at the front of an empty room and preaches to rows of dust-covered pews, voice dry as paper. It doesn't seem to notice no one's left to listen. Its bandaged hands still turn the pages of a book that's long since rotted through.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bandaged Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Dreadful Glare", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "The Zealot targets one creature it can see within 30 ft. The target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of the Zealot's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wrapped in the same funeral linens it finished the rite in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Turns the pages of a book that's long since rotted to dust."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Delivers a sermon that never quite finishes, looping back to its start."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't react to interruption — the service continues regardless."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Kneels, on schedule, at points in a liturgy only it can hear."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses, once, as if it heard someone answer from the empty pews."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The dust on the pews rearranges itself into shapes shaped like a listening congregation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck down mid-sermon, its last words are the final line of the rite, finally finished."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["preaching to rows of dust-covered pews in a voice dry as paper, unaware no one's left"]},{"name":"Possessed Vessel","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"A person worn like a coat, blinking wrong","flavor":"Wears a person like a coat, imperfectly — the voice is right but the blinking is wrong. Whatever's inside it wants the body back once its work is finished.","desc":"It talks like the person you knew, uses their turns of phrase, wears their face without a wrinkle out of place — except the blink comes a beat too slow, and sometimes both eyes close a half-second apart. Whatever's driving that body is only borrowing it, and it's counting down to when the real work starts.","traits":{"note": "Whatever drives the body is only borrowing it, counting down to when its real work starts.", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Read Thoughts", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Vessel magically reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 ft., learning its greatest fear or its plan for the next few minutes, at the DM's discretion."}, {"name": "Wrong Face", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Vessel drops its borrowed expression for an instant. One creature within 30 ft. that can see it must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uses the exact turns of phrase the real person always used."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears their face without a single wrinkle out of place."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Blinks a beat too slow, easy to miss if you aren't watching closely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sometimes both eyes close a half-second apart from each other."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the real person's habits, but never their small kindnesses."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows impatient the longer it has to keep pretending to be someone else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its voice layers into two, its own and the borrowed one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed to the edge, it drops the disguise entirely and the body underneath goes slack."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["talking like the person you knew, blinking a beat too slow, both eyes closing out of time"]},{"name":"The Slow Reflection","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Ghost one second behind, plotting to catch up","flavor":"Lives one mirror-second out of sync with the world; it has had a full lifetime alone in that lag to plan what it'll do the moment it catches up.","desc":"It steps free of a cracked mirror a full second behind your own motion, translucent, mouthing words you said a moment ago. It has spent what feels like a lifetime alone in that lag, watching you live just ahead of it. Something in the way it moves says it's done waiting to catch up.","traits":{"note": "It has spent what feels like a lifetime in that lag, planning what it does the moment it catches up.", "actions": [{"name": "Withering Touch", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (4d6 + 4) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Etherealness", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "The Reflection enters the Ethereal Plane from the Material Plane, or vice versa, slipping back into any nearby reflective surface."}, {"name": "Horrifying Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each non-Undead creature within 60 ft. that can see the Reflection's true face must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Catching Up (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One Humanoid the Reflection can see within 5 ft. must succeed on a DC 13 Charisma saving throw or the Reflection's lag collapses to zero — for 1 round, the target's next action is copied exactly by the Reflection a moment before the target can act."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Translucent, mouthing words you said a full second before it arrives."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only steps free of mirrors that are already cracked."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Copies your posture exactly, always a beat behind."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Retreats into the glass the moment it's struck, only to try again elsewhere."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Watches you live just ahead of it, patient as rot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The lag shortens, visibly, every time it's allowed to watch you longer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one instant it moves perfectly in sync with you, then slips back behind."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The night it finally catches up, it doesn't step out of the mirror — it steps out of you."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["stepping free of a cracked mirror a full second behind you, mouthing words you already said"]},{"name":"Grief-Fed Banshee","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Wailing widow owed a wake that never came","flavor":"Mourns in a key that shatters glass and eardrums both; she was promised a wake that never happened, and she's still owed it.","desc":"Her wail arrives before she's visible, a note that finds the glass in the windows and the fillings in your teeth at once. When she appears she's in mourning black gone the color of old rain, face raw with a grief that's had years to curdle. She was owed a wake nobody held, and she intends to collect.","traits":{"note": "She was promised a wake that never happened, and she intends to collect it from whoever's nearest.", "actions": [{"name": "Curdled Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Horrifying Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each non-Undead creature within 60 ft. that can see the Banshee's raw grief-worn face must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute, and its Speed is halved until the Fright ends."}, {"name": "Owed Wail", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear the Banshee must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or drop to 0 hit points if it has 6 hit points or fewer, or take 13 (3d8) Psychic damage on a failed save (half as much on a success)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mourning black gone the color of old rain, worn threadbare."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Face raw with a grief that's had years to curdle into something else."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her wail finds every pane of glass in a house before it finds you."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the site of the wake that never happened, again and again."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Goes quiet, briefly, at the mention of the one who wronged her."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Softens toward anyone who offers to finally hold the wake properly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her reflection wails a half-second before she does, in every mirror in the house."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied her wake one more time, her grief curdles fully into something that only wants to end it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["wailing before she's visible, a note finding glass and fillings both at once"]},{"name":"Coven Matriarch","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Coven matriarch trading in stolen sleep and souls","flavor":"The eldest of a coven of three, who trades in stolen sleep and worse; her sisters answer to her the way a storm answers to the moon.","desc":"The eldest of three sits closest to the hearth, hands folded, watching you with the calm of someone who has already decided how this ends. Her voice is warm, almost kind, right up until it isn't. Sleep taken from a hundred houses shows in the unnatural stillness of her face.","traits":{"note": "Her sisters answer to her the way a storm answers to the moon.", "actions": [{"name": "Matriarch's Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Step Between Worlds", "replaces": "Plane", "text": "The Matriarch casts Plane Shift, targeting only herself, to travel to a familiar dream or a place between houses."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Matriarch casts one of her prepared spells, requiring no material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Voice warm, almost kind, right up until it isn't."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Face unnaturally still, worn smooth by a hundred houses' worth of stolen sleep."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps her sisters seated to either side, silent unless she permits them to speak."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades favors that always cost more than they first appear to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises her voice, never needs to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows genuinely curious about guests clever enough to refuse her first offer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her hearth burns without wood, without smoke, without ever going out."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crossed badly enough, she stops trading and starts simply taking what she wants."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["sitting closest to the hearth, hands folded, watching you with the calm of someone who's already decided how this ends"]},{"name":"Marrow Revenant","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Undead thing that only wants its killer, unerringly","flavor":"Came back wrong and remembers exactly who wronged it. Walks in a straight line toward its killer through locked doors, walls, anything.","desc":"It came back grey and gaunt, joints held together by will more than sinew, and it walks in one direction only — toward whoever wronged it. Locked doors don't slow it. Walls barely do. It doesn't seem to notice you exist at all unless you're standing between it and its killer.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't register anyone who isn't standing between it and its killer.", "actions": [{"name": "Grave Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Vengeful Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage, or 13 (2d10 + 3) Piercing damage against the creature it has marked as its killer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grey and gaunt, joints held together by will more than sinew."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't slow for locked doors; barely slows for walls."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Remembers exactly who wronged it, and nothing else clearly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steps through anyone standing between it and its target without pause."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at a steady, unhurried walk that never quite loses ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Slows, briefly, when it passes something that reminds it of who it used to be."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Leaves no footprints, but every door it's passed through stays open behind it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally reaching its killer, it stops attacking anyone else entirely, even mid-fight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["walking in one direction only, toward whoever wronged it, through locked doors and worse"]},{"name":"Candlewax Doppelganger","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"Melting face that copies whoever stares longest","flavor":"A face that melts and re-sets itself into whoever last looked at it too long; meeting its eyes is how it decides which of you to become next.","desc":"Its face runs like hot tallow and re-sets a little differently every time you look away — cheekbones, jaw, the set of the eyes shifting toward whoever it studied last. Meeting its gaze for too long is how it decides. When it settles, it's wearing someone's face better than they do.","traits":{"note": "Meeting its gaze too long is how it decides whose face it takes next.", "actions": [{"name": "Melting Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Wax Tendrils", "replaces": "Snake Hair", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one creature. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Poison damage. If the damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is instead stabilized but Restrained, its features slowly re-setting into the doppelganger's own."}, {"name": "Molten Gaze", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 150 ft. Hit: 14 (4d6) Poison damage, and the Doppelganger studies the target's face; it can later assume that likeness."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cheekbones and jaw shift a little every time you look away."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Currently wearing a face better than the original ever did."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint smell of hot wax in whatever room it's settled in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Studies newcomers longest, weighing which face is worth keeping."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its true face, unset, is smooth and featureless as an unlit candle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows uneasy holding one face too long, like the wax wants to move."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment two faces surface at once, fighting for the same set of features."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-shift, its face runs through every likeness it's ever worn before it finally cools still."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["its face running like hot tallow, re-setting a little differently toward whoever it studied last"]},{"name":"Congregation Made Flesh","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"A coven's dozen bodies fused into one prayer","flavor":"What happens when a coven's devotion finally has somewhere to go — a dozen willing bodies fused at the altar into one thing that still, somehow, prays.","desc":"It rises out of the altar as one shuddering mass of limbs and half-formed faces, a dozen bodies folded into a single frame that still moves like it's kneeling. Every mouth on it murmurs the same prayer, slightly out of time with the others. It doesn't attack so much as embrace.","traits":{"note": "A dozen willing sacrifices fused at the altar; strikes as one but each limb still half-answers to a different will, occasionally fumbling in ways a normal aberration wouldn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Chorus of Selves", "text": "Once per turn, when it would take an action, it may instead speak with a dozen overlapping voices, forcing a creature within 30 ft that hears it to make a Wisdom save or be frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dozen faces, half-formed, folded into a single kneeling frame."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every mouth murmurs the same prayer, slightly out of time with the rest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves like it's still kneeling, even while lunging."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recognizable clothing fragments still cling here and there among the limbs."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reaches to embrace before it thinks to strike."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One face among the many seems to be trying to speak something other than the prayer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its limbs occasionally rearrange mid-fight, redistributing which body does the reaching."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn apart, the individual bodies briefly separate and thrash before finally going still."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["rising out of the altar as one shuddering mass of limbs, every mouth murmuring the same prayer out of time"]},{"name":"Warden of the Cellar Door","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Vampire bound to the door that's never shut","flavor":"Bound to the one door in the house that's never fully closed; it has watched every family that ever lived there and outlasted all of them.","desc":"It waits just inside the one door in the house that never quite latches, still and courtly, watching the hallway the way a butler watches for a guest who's late. It has outlived every family that ever lived here and remembers each of their names. The door creaks the same amount whether it's opening or closing.","traits":{"note": "Bound to a single threshold; can't willingly move more than 60 ft from the cellar door chassis-normal otherwise.", "actions": [{"name": "Never Fully Shut", "text": "As a bonus action, it may attempt to open any door or window within 60 ft that isn't locked by more than a mundane latch, regardless of line of sight."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still, courtly, watching the hallway the way a butler watches for a late guest."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bound to the one door in the house that never quite closes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Remembers every family's name, recites them if asked politely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dresses in fashions decades out of date, immaculately kept."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The door creaks the same whether it's opening or closing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows almost wistful describing families long since moved out or buried."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Steps out of the doorway's shadow even when the door itself is elsewhere in the house."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Driven to true death, the door it's bound to swings shut on its own for the first time in memory."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["waiting just inside a door that never quite latches, watching the hall for a guest who's late"]},{"name":"Bell-Tolling Revenant","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Bell-tower revenant tolling once per debt owed","flavor":"A funeral bell's worth of grief given shape and a bell-tower's worth of reach; it tolls once for every soul it's owed, and it keeps very careful count.","desc":"Somewhere above, a bell rings once, unbidden, in a tower with no bellringer. The sound rolls out low and enormous, and where it lands the air goes thick with old grief. It counts its debts by the toll — one for every soul it believes it's owed — and it is never wrong about the number.","traits":{"note": "Gargantuan scale grants extended reach/aura beyond the base chassis.", "actions": [{"name": "The Toll", "text": "Once per long rest, it may ring its bell as an action: all creatures within 120 ft who can hear it must succeed a Wisdom save or be frightened and have disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of their next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single toll precedes it, low and enormous, sourced from no bellringer."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts its debts aloud between tolls, never losing track of the number."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The air around it thickens with old grief thick enough to taste."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at a slow, deliberate pace, certain no debt escapes it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ignores anyone not on its ledger of owed souls entirely."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Pauses, once, on hearing a name it hasn't tolled in a very long time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its tolls are heard blocks away in houses with no bell tower at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck down, it tolls one final, enormous peal that settles every debt it was owed at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "sky"],"activity":["ringing once, unbidden, from a bell tower with no bellringer, and the air going thick with old grief"]},{"name":"The Second Face in the Glass","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Elder vampire kingpin living inside the mirrors","flavor":"An elder vampire kingpin who lives entirely inside reflective surfaces, one beat behind its prey, until the night it decides to be early instead.","desc":"It lives inside every mirror and dark window in the house, a beat behind your reflection, patient as rot. For a hundred years it's been content to stay one step slow. Tonight, for reasons only it knows, it steps out early — and the glass behind it doesn't crack so much as exhale.","traits":{"note": "Kingpin-tier vampire; the mirror-lag is fluff for its Misty Step-style repositioning, not a new mechanic.", "actions": [{"name": "Early", "text": "Once per combat, it may teleport to any reflective surface within 60 ft as a reaction, appearing a half-second 'ahead' of where it should be — before the triggering attack resolves."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cracked mirror in the party's current lodging holds its beat-behind reflection tonight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been shadowing one party member's reflection for days, patient and unhurried."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dark window nearby is the only mirror left in a house it's already claimed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a bargain through the glass before ever stepping free of it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local kingpin's debts trace back through mirrors to this very glass."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown bored of the century-long lag and is actively courting a reason to step out early."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every reflective surface in the building briefly shows the same beat-behind shape at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It has decided tonight is the night it stops being a beat behind anything, ever again."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["living a beat behind your reflection, patient as rot, for what it calls a hundred years"]},{"name":"The Uninvited","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Ancient thing that only ever needs one knock","flavor":"It always knocks first. Every house it has ever entered, it was let in — a guest, a mourner, a face someone half-remembered — and it has never once needed to knock twice.","desc":"It stands on the threshold, patient, hands folded, wearing the face of someone you half-remember from a funeral or a wedding you can't quite place. It has never had to knock twice. Every house that's ever let it in did so willingly, and it is in no hurry now that it's inside yours.","traits":{"note": "Apex mummy-lord; the 'always let in' fluff never overrides player agency at the door — it's atmosphere for its curse/fear kit, not a forced-entry mechanic.", "actions": [{"name": "One Knock", "text": "If a creature voluntarily opens a door for it, that creature has disadvantage on saving throws against its frightening presence for the rest of the encounter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's standing outside the party's shelter, and it only needs one of them to say 'come in.'"}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It wears the face of someone the party is expecting, and asks, politely, at the door."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already inside — someone let it in years ago, and the house never mentioned the guest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers to take a burden off the party's hands; accepting is the invitation."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows the exact word each party member would use to welcome an old friend home."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has been invited into every house on this street but one, and it's saving that one for last."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It remembers being invited into a place that no longer exists, and it's still, technically, a guest there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every door it has ever been welcomed through remains open to it, forever, across the whole world; it is only ever one 'yes' from standing in any room it likes."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["standing on a threshold it has not yet been asked to cross, patient beyond patience"]},{"name":"The Possession at the Root","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"A congregation's willing vessels burned to one shape","flavor":"Not a demon wearing a body — a congregation's worth of willing vessels burned down to one true and monstrous shape, still calling itself by the coven's oldest, most patient name.","desc":"The shape towers huge and burning at the bottom of the crypt stair, built from a congregation's worth of willing bodies burned down into one true and monstrous silhouette. It still answers, in a chorus of overlapping voices, to the coven's oldest name for itself. Ash falls from it like it's shedding a robe.","traits":{"note": "Apex balor-chassis; fluff-only voice work, no new mechanics beyond the SRD frame.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dry well at the crypt's base leads down to the chamber where it's finishing its burning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's still gathering — three more willing vessels are on their way down the stair tonight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A coven survivor is begging the party to stop it before its shape fully sets."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already spoken its old name once tonight, and the ground above the crypt cracked in answer."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child from the coven's bloodline is being led toward it right now, unknowing."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's testing its new shape against the crypt's own walls, and the crypt is losing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its ash is settling over the whole district above, and the sleepers there are dreaming its prayer."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every congregation that ever burned for it before is stirring at once, across the whole gloom, answering the same old name."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "ruins", "elemental"],"activity":["towering huge and burning at the bottom of the crypt stair, ash falling from it like a shed robe"]},{"name":"Crawlspace Widow","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"giant-wolf-spider","model":"giant-wolf-spider","summary":"Attic spider that drops on sleepers","flavor":"A bloated house-spider the size of a cat that drops from attic rafters onto sleeping throats.","desc":"Something the size of a housecat clings to the rafters, legs folded tight against a bloated abdomen, patient as dust. It drops without warning onto whatever's sleeping below, silent until the moment its fangs find a throat. The webs up there are thick enough to muffle a scream.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Silent Drop-Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage. The Widow has Advantage on this attack if it drops onto a sleeping or unaware target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bloated the size of a housecat, legs folded tight against the abdomen."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Silent until the exact moment its fangs find a throat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Webs up in the rafters thick enough to muffle a scream."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers rooms where the same sleeper returns every night."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drops straight down, rarely bothering to stalk first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Wraps its catch and drags it up into the rafters before feeding."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bite leaves a mark shaped faintly like a widow's veil."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Disturbed with a full brood in the rafters, dozens more drop at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["clinging folded tight to the rafters, patient as dust, waiting over whatever's sleeping below"]},{"name":"Threadbare Scarecrow","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"Straw effigy that walks after moonrise","flavor":"A field-post effigy stuffed with grave-dirt straw that unpins itself at moonrise.","desc":"Propped crooked over a dead field, straw leaking from a burlap seam, it hangs slack against its post all day like any other scarecrow. At moonrise the post creaks empty. It walks with a stiff, jerking gait, arms still splayed the way they were pinned.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Straw Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Terrifying Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "One creature the Scarecrow can see within 30 ft. must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened until the end of the Scarecrow's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straw leaking from a burlap seam across a sagging chest."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Arms still splayed the way they were originally pinned to the post."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stuffed with grave-dirt straw instead of ordinary field chaff."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks with a stiff, jerking gait, joints unused to motion."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hangs slack against its post all day like any ordinary scarecrow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Returns to its post before dawn, unpinning itself back into place."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Crows refuse to land anywhere near the field it stands in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn apart, the grave-dirt straw keeps crawling back toward the post on its own."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "ruins"],"activity":["hanging slack against its post all day, then walking stiff-armed and jerking after moonrise"]},{"name":"Ashen Widow's Cat","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"cat","model":"cat","summary":"Unblinking cat that tracks the dead","flavor":"A funeral-black cat that never blinks and always knows which door hides the coffin.","desc":"A black cat sits very still on the stair, tail curled over its paws, and does not blink. Its eyes track you the way it might track a mouse, patient and total. It always seems to be facing the one door in the house you'd rather it didn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Funeral Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 1 Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Funeral-black fur, not a single blink in the time you've watched it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Always faces the one door in the house you'd rather it didn't."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tracks movement like a mouse, patient and total, never playful."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits closest to whoever in the room is closest to dying."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never meows, never purrs, only watches."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Follows a coffin's route through the house before anyone's announced a death."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes hold a faint reflection of a room that isn't the one you're standing in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If it finally blinks, something in the house it was watching has just died."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting very still on the stair, tail curled over its paws, unblinking and total in its attention"]},{"name":"Gutter Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Drowned grudge haunting the storm drains","flavor":"A drowned drunk's grudge, sluicing through storm drains looking for the one who left him there.","desc":"A grey shape rises out of the storm drain grate, dripping and half-formed, dragging the smell of standing water with it. It mutters the same accusation over and over, aimed at nobody in the room and everybody at once. Wherever it passes, the gutters run backward for a moment.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Drowned Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half-formed and grey, dragging the smell of standing water with it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters the same accusation over and over, aimed at everyone at once."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rises only from drains and grates, never open water."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The gutters run backward for a moment wherever it passes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never strays far from the block where it drowned."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows briefly coherent when someone mentions the name it's cursing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its dripping never stops, even standing on dry stone for an hour."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Named by its grudge's true target, it floods the nearest drain in a sudden furious surge."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "swamp"],"activity":["rising dripping out of a storm-drain grate, muttering the same accusation at nobody and everybody"]},{"name":"Wick-Eyed Changeling Child","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"sprite","model":"sprite","summary":"Cradle-swapped child with a widening smile","flavor":"A too-quiet foundling left in a cradle, its smile widening only when no one is looking.","desc":"It sits too quietly in the cradle, small hands folded, watching the room with an attention no infant should have. The smile only widens when it thinks no one's looking — a fraction more teeth each time. It hasn't cried once since it arrived.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Needle Sword", "replaces": "Needle Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Enchanting Bow", "replaces": "Enchanting Bow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 40/160 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed by the child for 1 minute."}, {"name": "Heart Sight", "replaces": "Heart Sight", "text": "The child magically discerns the closest emotional attachment of one creature it can see within 30 ft., learning who that creature loves most."}, {"name": "Fade From Sight", "replaces": "Invisibility", "text": "The child casts Invisibility on itself, no material components required."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small hands folded, watching the room with attention no infant should have."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The smile only widens when it thinks no one's looking."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hasn't cried once since it was left in the cradle."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A fraction more teeth shows in the smile each time you glance away."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Left in place of a child taken cleanly, without a mark."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows restless and cries convincingly the moment it's truly threatened."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes catch candlelight the way a cat's do, briefly, at the wrong angle."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, it drops the infant act entirely and its true small hunger shows through."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["sitting too quietly in the cradle, small hands folded, smile widening only when unwatched"]},{"name":"Tallow Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"Candle-vigil ghoul dripping rendered fat","flavor":"A ghoul that drips rendered fat from a crypt-candle vigil that never ended.","desc":"It kneels beside a candle that's burned down to nothing, wax dripping thick and yellow off its own skin like the vigil never ended. Its nails are candle-black, its breath smells of tallow and grave-dirt. It doesn't look up from the flame until you're close enough to touch.","traits":{"note": "It won't look up from where the candle was until something gets close enough to touch.", "actions": [{"name": "Grave-Tallow Bite", "replaces": "Icy Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage as candle-fat sears the wound, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by the Necrotic damage until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Wax-Black Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the end of its next turn (Elves and creatures immune to being paralyzed automatically succeed)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its candle has been reduced to a coin of hardened wax, and still it kneels over the spot."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tallow drips from its jaw in a slow, steady rhythm, pooling into a small yellow ring on the floor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mouths a prayer with no sound behind it, lips moving through the same words on a loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its knees have worn two grooves into the stone from a vigil that's outlasted the building around it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh wax still clings wet to its fingers, as if the candle only just went out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps one hand cupped around empty air, sheltering a flame that isn't there anymore."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Where its tallow drips, tiny candle stubs sprout from the floorboards and gutter out within the hour."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startle it badly enough and the wax across its whole body ignites at once, a walking pillar of candlelight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["kneeling beside a dead candle, wax dripping off its own skin like the vigil never ended", "dragging candle-black nails along a crypt wall, tracing a vigil route only it remembers"]},{"name":"Splintered Marionette","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"rlm-splintered-marionette","summary":"Self-cut puppet bowing to an empty house","flavor":"A puppet-theater star whose strings were cut by its own hand, still bowing to an empty house.","desc":"Its own strings hang cut and curling from the crossbar overhead, and still it bows — low, formal, precise — to a house with no one left in the seats. Its joints clack in place of applause. It seems to be waiting for someone to throw a rose.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Curtain-Call Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from a hand carved into a fan of tiny wooden blades."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile is chipped down one cheek, showing raw wood underneath."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single fake rose, long dried, is clutched in one fist as if waiting to be thrown."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bows twice before attacking — once for the house, once, perhaps, for you."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its remaining strings are tangled around one ankle, dragging a length of curtain rope behind it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The crossbar it fell from is still lodged between its shoulder blades like a coat hanger."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only attacks when it thinks no one is watching the stage — turn your back and it strikes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its joints clack out a rhythm that matches, note for note, applause from an audience that isn't there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut its remaining strings and it collapses into a full stage bow, releasing a burst of stage dust that blinds everyone nearby."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["bowing low and formal to a house with no one left in the seats, joints clacking like applause", "holding a bent pose mid-curtsy, cut strings swaying overhead in a draft only it seems to feel"]},{"name":"Bog-Sunk Revenant","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Peat-bog hanged man risen with the noose","flavor":"A peat-preserved corpse hauled from the marsh, its noose still knotted at the throat.","desc":"Peat-black skin, a noose still cinched tight at the throat, it hauls itself up out of the marsh a step at a time, mud sluicing off in ropes. It moves like the ground still owns half of it. The rope creaks with each stride, though there's nothing left to hang from it.","traits":{"note": "The ground still owns half of it — it moves slower in dry earth than in its own bog.", "actions": [{"name": "Bog Iron Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage if used with both hands, the blade crusted black with peat rust."}, {"name": "Waterlogged Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet and knocked Prone, mud spattering from the impact."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Peat-black to the bone, the noose at its throat still knotted tight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every stride wrings another rope of mud loose, leaving a dark trail behind it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rope at its neck creaks with each step, though nothing's left to hang it from."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reed fragments and bog-glass are pressed into its skin like a second layer of armor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drags one foot as though the marsh never quite let go of it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Standing water within ten feet of it ripples in time with its footsteps, marsh answering marsh."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Cut it and dark bog-water pours from the wound instead of blood, pooling and refusing to soak in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near open water, it collapses into a spreading slick of peat that tries to swallow anything standing in it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp"],"activity":["hauling itself out of the marsh a step at a time, mud sluicing off in ropes", "standing waist-deep in peat, noose still cinched at its throat, waiting for the ground to finish releasing it"]},{"name":"Pox-Marked Thrall","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"Plague villager thralled to a whisper","flavor":"A plague-branded villager who traded a fever for a whisper that never stops.","desc":"Sores mark the skin along the jaw and throat, fresh enough that they should have killed by now. Something in the eyes says the fever broke, and something else moved in behind it. The villager mutters along to a whisper only they can hear, low and constant, like a hymn stuck on one line.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage from a blade caked in something that isn't rust."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sores mark its jaw and throat, fresh enough it should be dead already."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the whisper's rhythm under its breath even while fighting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes track something just past your shoulder, never quite you."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It clutches the sickle two-handed, like it's afraid of dropping the one thing the whisper gave it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fever-sweat soaks through clothes it hasn't changed since the sickness took."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Kill it and the whisper doesn't stop — it moves on to whoever's standing closest."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pox marks rearrange themselves overnight into new, deliberate patterns, like handwriting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed to its last breath, it laughs in a voice that isn't its own before the whisper finishes the sentence for it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["muttering along to a whisper only it can hear, low and constant like a hymn stuck on one line", "scratching at fresh sores along its jaw, listening to something that never stops talking"]},{"name":"Feral Barn Bat-Swarm","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-bats","model":"swarm-of-bats","summary":"Bell-triggered swarm pouring from the rafters","flavor":"A rafters-thick cloud of bats that only stirs when the church bell cracks midnight.","desc":"The rafters look ordinary until the church bell cracks midnight — then the ceiling comes apart into a thousand small wings, a black tide pouring down in one shrieking mass. The sound of it fills the room before the bats do. It settles as fast as it rises, the instant the last bell-note dies.","traits":{"note": "It settles as fast as it rises — the instant the bell-note ends, the swarm goes still again.", "actions": [{"name": "Feeding Frenzy", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. if the swarm occupies the target's space. Hit: 5 (2d4) Piercing damage, or 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The rafters look ordinary until the bell cracks midnight and the ceiling comes apart."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pours down and up in the same breath, a tide with no in-between state."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Individual bats peel off to circle a single target before rejoining the mass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The sound of it arrives a full second before the swarm does, wingbeats like tearing paper."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It clusters thickest around whatever rang the bell, as if blaming them personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Silence the bell early and the swarm stays frozen mid-descent, wings locked, waiting for a note that won't come."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Each bat in the mass has the same pale, human-shaped face pressed flat against its own fur."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Ring the bell a second time mid-fight and the swarm doubles, more wings pouring from rafters that shouldn't hold any more."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["hanging motionless in the rafters, dead still until the bell cracks midnight", "pouring down from the ceiling in one shrieking black tide the instant the last bell-note dies"]},{"name":"Rope-Burned Suicide","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Hanging-tree haunt re-living its last minute","flavor":"A hanging-tree haunt that re-lives its last minute on anyone who lingers beneath the branch.","desc":"Rope-burn rings the throat, feet dangling a few inches off ground that isn't there. Beneath the old hanging-tree, it relives the same last minute on a loop — the drop, the jerk, the stillness — and anyone who lingers gets pulled into the memory with it. Its eyes are the only part of it that still moves.","traits":{"note": "Anyone who lingers beneath the branch gets pulled into the memory alongside it.", "actions": [{"name": "Last Minute", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target relives the drop and jerk with it, becoming Frightened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rope-burn rings its throat, feet dangling above ground it never quite touches."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats the drop, the jerk, the stillness, in exactly that order, forever."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes are the only part of it that still moves, tracking whoever gets close."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The branch above it creaks in time with a wind that isn't blowing anywhere else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It resets to standing the instant the loop finishes, as if nothing happened at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cut the invisible rope and the loop stutters, buying a few seconds where it can't act."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one heartbeat in the loop it wears the face of whoever's watching it closest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force it to finish the loop against its will and everyone within reach drops with it, jerking on ropes that aren't there."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["hanging a few inches off ground that isn't there, re-living the same last minute on a loop", "twitching through the drop and the jerk and the stillness, over and over, beneath the old hanging-tree"]},{"name":"Hollow Nursemaid","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Lullaby-humming absence in the nursery wall","flavor":"A governess-shaped absence that hums lullabies through the nursery wall long after the family fled.","desc":"A shape darker than the shadow it should cast moves along the nursery wall, humming a lullaby with no breath behind it. The tune is off by a few notes, over and over, patient as a metronome. The family fled this house generations ago; she never got the message.","traits":{"note": "The family fled generations ago; she never got the message and still keeps the room.", "actions": [{"name": "Lullaby-Weak Grasp", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 for 1 hour; if this reduces it to 0, the target is instead paralyzed for that duration."}, {"name": "Cut the Lullaby (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Sever Shadow (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Nursemaid's shadow detaches and glides up to 30 feet to occupy the space of a Small or smaller creature's shadow, humming the same off-key lullaby as an independent shade with the Nursemaid's Lullaby-Weak Grasp action, until destroyed (AC 12, 10 hit points) or reunited with the Nursemaid."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Darker than the shadow it should cast, it moves in careful arcs along the nursery wall."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The lullaby never resolves; it circles back to the same missed note each time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pauses at an empty crib, adjusting blankets that were sold off decades ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust on the nursery floor never settles where she's crossed it, as if still swept daily."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hushes intruders with a raised finger before attacking, an old habit overriding the new one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The lullaby grows louder the closer a child-sized target gets, and she reaches for them first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hum the tune correctly and she stops mid-motion, confused, for a single round."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, she unravels into a chorus of the lullaby sung in a dozen overlapping child voices, then silence."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["humming a lullaby with no breath behind it, off by a few notes, over and over", "gliding along the nursery wall darker than the shadow it should cast, patient as a metronome"]},{"name":"Cur of the Black Barn","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"death-dog","model":"death-dog","summary":"Loyal farm dog that starved and rose wrong","flavor":"A farm dog that starved loyal beside its master's grave and rose wrong.","desc":"It waited by the grave until its ribs showed through the hide, loyal past any reasonable end, and something answered that loyalty wrong. Now it circles the barn on legs that bend at angles a dog's shouldn't, growling low at nothing, still watching the spot where it used to sleep.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wrongbent Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 11 Strength saving throw or be knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its ribs show clear through the hide, starved past any sense but still moving."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its legs bend at the wrong joint, an extra angle no living dog would have."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never leaves a rough circle around the grave it once starved beside."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It growls at the empty spot by the door where its bed used to be, ignoring everything else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rotted collar still hangs loose around its neck, tag long rusted unreadable."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stops fighting entirely if led toward its old master's grave, sitting obediently at the mound."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its bark, on the rare occasion it barks, comes out in a voice like a grown man weeping."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed within sight of the grave, it drags itself the rest of the way and digs in, and something underneath answers the scratching."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["circling the barn on legs bent at angles no dog's should, growling low at nothing", "watching the empty spot where it used to sleep, ribs showing through a hide gone taut and grey"]},{"name":"Rat-King Knot","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-rats","model":"swarm-of-rats","summary":"Tail-fused rats forming one furious knot","flavor":"Dozens of sewer rats fused tail-to-tail into one furious, many-headed knot.","desc":"Dozens of rats writhe together in the corner, tails knotted into one impossible braid, a single furious mass of fur and teeth trying to move in a dozen directions at once. It doesn't so much attack as thrash, and everything within reach of that thrashing gets bitten.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Knot-Thrash", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. if the swarm occupies the target's space. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage, or 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer, from dozens of mouths biting at once."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dozens of tails braid into one impossible knot no single rat can untangle itself from."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't attack so much as thrash, biting anything within reach of the writhing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half its bodies face one way, half the other, fighting each other as much as you."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rolls more than it runs, a furred wheel of teeth crossing the floor."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Individual rats scream in tiny distinct voices beneath the mass's low furious hiss."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Sever enough of the knot and a portion breaks free as ordinary panicked rats, fleeing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The knot's shifting shape resolves, if you squint, into a crude and constantly-collapsing human outline."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed all at once, the knot bursts apart into a hundred separate rats that scatter and vanish into every crack in the room."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "cave"],"activity":["writhing in a knotted mass of tails, thrashing to move in a dozen directions at once", "dragging its own furious weight across the floor, a single braided animal biting anything in reach"]},{"name":"Choir-Loft Poltergeist","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"poltergeist","model":"poltergeist","summary":"Organist's fury slamming hymnals and bellropes","flavor":"An organist's fury, still slamming hymnal pages and yanking bellropes no hand can hold.","desc":"Hymnal pages flip themselves violently in the choir loft, and the bell-rope down in the nave snaps taut on its own, yanking the bell into a furious, uneven clang. No hand is on either. Whatever's left of the organist up there is still furious about something long past fixing.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Hymnal Slam", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage from a hurled pew, hymnal stand, or bell-weight, and the target is knocked Prone if it is Large or smaller."}, {"name": "Bellrope Wrench", "replaces": "Telekinetic Thrust", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 15 ft. (invisible force). Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Force damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 15 feet toward the loft and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hymnal pages flip themselves violently in the empty loft, no hand turning them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The bellrope down in the nave snaps taut on its own, clanging the bell out of rhythm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pew benches scrape an inch across the floor whenever it grows agitated."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's furious about something specific, though nothing in the church explains what."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust falls from the organ pipes in a steady rhythm, keeping some private time signature."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Playing the actual organ correctly calms it for a round, its fury briefly answered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hymn it's furious about plays backward through the pipes when no one touches the keys."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed to its limit, every loose object in the church rises at once and slams down in a single furious chord."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["flipping hymnal pages violently in an empty loft, furious about something long past fixing", "yanking the bellrope taut with no hand on it, snapping the bell into an uneven furious clang"]},{"name":"Gravecloth Zombie","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"Shroud-stitched exhumee lurching by grave-light","flavor":"A shroud-wrapped exhumee, still stitched into its burial linens, lurching by grave-light.","desc":"Wound tight in burial linens gone grey and stiff, it moves by grave-light with the shroud still cinched at wrist and ankle, restricting every step to a shuffle. Where the wrappings have torn, the skin beneath is the color of old candle wax. It doesn't seem to notice the cloth at all.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Shroud-Wrapped Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage from a fist still bound in grave linen."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shroud is cinched at wrist and ankle, restricting every step to a shuffle."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Where the wrappings tear, the skin beneath is the color of old candle wax."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't seem to notice the cloth at all, walking as if unbound."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grave-light clings to it faintly, a pale glow that never quite lights the room."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its linens still bear stitched initials, a name someone once cared enough to sew in."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cutting its shroud free lets it move at full speed, trading its shuffle for real menace."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its wrappings tighten on their own overnight, as if someone were still preparing the burial."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn open at the chest, the shroud spills grave-dirt that keeps pouring long after the body's empty."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["shuffling by grave-light, shroud cinched tight at wrist and ankle, restricting every step", "dragging burial linens gone grey and stiff, tearing where the wax-pale skin shows through"]},{"name":"Fen Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"Crypt-nesting ghoul with silt-slick claws","flavor":"A ghoul that nests in flooded family crypts, its claws slick with graveyard silt.","desc":"It nests in flooded family crypts, half-submerged, silt-slicked claws dragging along stone as it pulls itself up out of the water. The smell of standing swamp-rot arrives with it. It moves faster in the water than it has any right to on land.","traits":{"note": "It moves faster in water than it has any right to on land.", "actions": [{"name": "Silt-Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the end of its next turn (Elves and creatures immune to being paralyzed automatically succeed)."}, {"name": "Silted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It nests half-submerged in a flooded family crypt, waiting below the waterline."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Silt-slicked claws drag long grooves along the stone as it climbs free."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The smell of standing swamp-rot arrives a full room ahead of it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves twice as fast underwater as it does dragging itself onto dry stone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Duckweed and grave-silt cling to it in a permanent green-black film."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It retreats to open water the instant it's badly hurt, fighting far better submerged."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its silt trail, left to dry, hardens into shapes like small crouching figures."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Dragged fully out of water and killed there, it dissolves into the same silt it dripped, which keeps crawling toward the nearest puddle."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp", "cave"],"activity":["pulling itself up out of flooded crypt-water, silt-slicked claws dragging along stone", "nesting half-submerged in a family crypt, the smell of standing swamp-rot arriving before it does"]},{"name":"Beast of the Full Moon Runt","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Freshly bitten victim terrified of itself","flavor":"A fresh-bitten victim mid-transformation, more terrified of itself than of you.","desc":"Fur is only halfway in on this one — patches of human skin still show between the tufts, and the transformation looks like it hurts. It flinches at its own reflection in puddles. More than anything, it seems terrified of what it's about to become, and that terror makes it dangerously unpredictable.","traits":{"note": "Its terror at its own change makes it dangerously unpredictable — it may attack anything, including itself.", "actions": [{"name": "Panicked Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with a lesser form of the runt's affliction; the cursed target begins showing symptoms after 1d4 days."}, {"name": "Half-Formed Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage from a hand not fully claw, not fully fingers."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur is only halfway in, patches of human skin still showing between the tufts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The transformation looks like it hurts, and its own whimpers punctuate the fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches hard at any reflective surface, recoiling from its own half-finished face."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bites erratically, as likely to snap at its own arm as at a target."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its clothes are shredded at the seams, too small for the shape trying to fill them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Loud noises or bright light send it fleeing rather than fighting, purely animal panic."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a few seconds at a time its shadow finishes the transformation before its body does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past its limit, the change finishes all at once, mid-fight, and something far less frightened stands up in its place."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland", "hill"],"activity":["flinching at its own reflection in a puddle, half-fur and half-skin, mid-transformation and terrified", "pacing in tight circles, more afraid of what it's becoming than of anything nearby"]},{"name":"Wax-Sealed Familiar","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Tiny","frame":"raven","model":"raven","summary":"Coven crow with a beak sewn shut","flavor":"A coven's carrier-crow, its beak sewn shut around a secret it will die before dropping.","desc":"A crow perches just out of easy reach, beak sealed shut with a dark wax that's cracked but never fully broken. It watches with one unblinking eye at a time, turning its head slow. Whatever message it's carrying, it will die with its beak sewn shut before it drops it.","traits":{"note": "It will die before its sewn beak ever opens on the message it carries.", "actions": [{"name": "Sealed Beak Strike", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage delivered by a hard, wax-sealed skull-butt rather than a proper bite."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its beak is sealed shut in dark wax, cracked but never fully broken."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It watches with one eye at a time, turning its head slow between targets."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A thin cord is tied around one leg, the other end frayed where a message-tube once hung."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flees the instant it's outnumbered, message intact, self-preservation before spite."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feathers carry the same dark wax in patches, as if sealed more than once."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It attacks specifically whoever approaches the wax seal, ignoring easier targets nearby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Melt the wax and the beak beneath is stitched shut with hair, not scarred, not healed — sewn."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed before the seal breaks, the wax cracks open on its own and the message pours out as smoke shaped like words."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["perched just out of easy reach, one unblinking eye tracking movement below", "turning its head slow, beak sealed shut with cracked dark wax around a secret it won't drop"]},{"name":"Sackcloth Effigy","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"Hair-stitched poppet animated by a pinned name","flavor":"A burnt-corn poppet stitched with a stranger's hair, animated by whoever's name is pinned to its chest.","desc":"Burnt corn husks stitched into a rough manlike shape, a stranger's hair sewn along the scalp seam, it stands motionless until a name pinned to its chest gives it somewhere to walk. It moves stiff and jerking, straw rasping at every joint, obeying whoever holds the pin.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Straw Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage from stiff, corn-husk fingers."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Burnt corn husks form its rough manlike shape, joints rasping with every jerking step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stranger's hair is stitched along its scalp seam, uncomfortably neat work."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A name pinned to its chest is the only reason it's standing at all."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves stiff and jerking, as if walking is a skill it's still relearning."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straw sheds from it in a thin trail, marking exactly where it's been."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Remove the pinned name and it collapses instantly into inert husks and hair."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The name pinned to its chest changes handwriting each time you look away."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Burned, it goes up fast and total, and the pinned name scorches into the ash in a script no one here can read."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing motionless until a pinned name gives it somewhere to walk, straw rasping at every joint", "obeying whoever holds the pin, moving stiff and jerking across a field it doesn't recognize"]},{"name":"Ossuary Skitterling","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"crawling-claw","model":"crawling-claw","summary":"Severed charnel-wall hand scrabbling homeward","flavor":"A single severed hand from the charnel wall, still scrabbling toward its own coffin.","desc":"A single severed hand drags itself across the floor on its fingertips, knucklebones clicking against stone. It's headed somewhere specific — toward a coffin it half-remembers being part of. It doesn't seem to register anything else in the room until something blocks its path.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Knucklebone Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage from a single scrabbling severed hand."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single severed hand drags itself on its fingertips, knucklebones clicking against stone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's headed somewhere specific, toward a coffin it half-remembers being part of."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't register anything in the room until something blocks its path."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nails have worn down to nubs from years of scrabbling across stone."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wedding band, too large now, slides loose around one dried finger."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Reunited with its coffin, it curls still and inert, its errand finally finished."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Left alone, it writes the same word over and over in the dust, in a hand no one recognizes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crushed underfoot, its fingers keep twitching separately for a full minute, each one still trying to crawl home."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["dragging itself across the floor on its fingertips, knucklebones clicking against stone", "scrabbling toward a coffin it half-remembers being part of, ignoring everything not in its way"]},{"name":"Lantern-Jawed Corpse Candle","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"Grave-light that feeds on following mourners","flavor":"A death-light that hovers over fresh graves, feeding on the grief of mourners who follow it.","desc":"A pale light hovers low over a fresh grave, warm and inviting the way a lantern in a window is inviting. Anyone who follows it feels a little of their grief drain away with each step closer — which is exactly what it's feeding on. It never leads anywhere good.","traits":{"note": "It never leads anywhere good — following it is exactly what it's counting on.", "actions": [{"name": "Grief-Feeding Shock", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Lightning damage, and the target feels a portion of its grief drain away, becoming Charmed by the corpse-light until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A pale light hovers low over a fresh grave, warm as a window-lantern."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It drifts a slow, deliberate pace ahead of anyone following, never quite catching up to it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grief drains a little with each step closer, exactly what it's feeding on."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only appears over graves less than a week old, older ones hold no interest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It brightens visibly the closer a genuinely grieving target gets."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It flees toward open graves when threatened, seeking cover it can sink directly into."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Followed far enough, it leads to a grave with the follower's own name half-carved on the stone."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-feed, it releases all the grief it's hoarded back into the mourner at once, overwhelming them."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["hovering low and warm over a fresh grave, inviting the way a window-lantern is inviting", "drifting just out of reach, feeding a little on each mourner's grief with every step they follow"]},{"name":"Widow's Veil Shade","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"shadow","summary":"Mirror-shed silhouette that grieves at funerals","flavor":"A mourning-dress silhouette that peels off mirrors during funerals to grieve alongside the living.","desc":"It peels itself free of a mirror's surface the moment mourning bells start ringing somewhere nearby, a silhouette in a funeral veil with no face beneath it. It drifts to stand among the grieving, head bowed, indistinguishable from a real mourner until someone reaches to comfort it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Mourner's Touch", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 for 1 hour; if this reduces it to 0, the target is instead paralyzed for that duration."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It peels itself free of a mirror the moment mourning bells begin ringing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A funeral veil hides no face at all beneath its silhouette."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands among the grieving, head bowed, indistinguishable until someone reaches to comfort it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never speaks, only sways in time with whatever hymn is being sung."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It vanishes back into the nearest reflective surface the instant the service ends."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's drawn specifically to whoever in the room is grieving hardest, ignoring everyone else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Any mirror it's passed through since shows its silhouette faintly, for anyone who looks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck down, it shatters like glass and every mirror in the building cracks in sympathy."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["peeling free of a mirror's surface the moment funeral bells start ringing nearby", "drifting to stand among the grieving, head bowed, indistinguishable from a real mourner"]},{"name":"Feasting Cellar Grub","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"Pale centipede fattened on deeper offerings","flavor":"A pale root-cellar centipede fattened on offerings left for something worse living deeper down.","desc":"Pale and segmented, thick as a forearm, it coils in the dark corner of the root cellar where offerings are left for something deeper down. It's grown fat on food that was never meant for it. When it moves, dozens of small legs ripple in a wave along its length.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Offering-Fed Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage at the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pale and segmented, thick as a forearm, it coils in the root cellar's darkest corner."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's grown fat on offerings left for something deeper down, food never meant for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dozens of small legs ripple in a wave the instant it decides to move."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It won't leave the offering-spot unless dragged, defending the food source above all else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its segments pulse faintly, digesting something still moving somewhere inside."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cut it open and whatever it last ate is still alive enough to twitch."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It refuses fresh offerings entirely if they weren't left in exactly the ritual manner."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near its feeding-spot, whatever it was fattened for finally comes up looking for its meal."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["cave", "urban"],"activity":["coiled fat in a dark cellar corner, dozens of small legs rippling in a wave along its length", "gorging on offerings left for something worse living deeper down, grown pale and heavy on food not meant for it"]},{"name":"Rusalka's Drowned Bride","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"Jilted drowned bride walking out dripping","flavor":"A jilted bride who walked into the millpond in her gown and now walks out of it, dripping.","desc":"She walks up out of the millpond in a wedding gown gone the color of pond-scum, water sheeting off her in constant runnels that never stop. Her veil clings wet to a face still arranged for a ceremony that never happened. She doesn't seem to notice she's dripping onto dry floor.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Drowning Embrace", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest, as pond-water floods its lungs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her gown has gone the color of pond-scum, water sheeting off her in constant runnels."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her veil clings wet to a face still arranged for a ceremony that never happened."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She doesn't notice she's dripping onto dry floor, tracking pond-water everywhere she walks."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A wilted bouquet, waterlogged and grey, is still clutched in one drowned hand."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hums wedding music slightly off-key, a tune that never quite resolves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She fixates on whichever target most resembles the groom who never showed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Where her water touches dry ground, it doesn't evaporate, it spreads, slow and patient."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed near the millpond, she dissolves back into it entirely, and the water rises a foot that never quite recedes."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp", "sea", "coast"],"activity":["walking up out of the millpond in a gown gone the color of pond-scum, water sheeting off in constant runnels", "standing dripping onto dry floor, veil clinging wet to a face arranged for a ceremony that never happened"]},{"name":"Fanged Chorister","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"harpy","model":"harpy","summary":"Hymn-voiced ghoul luring the faithful closer","flavor":"A choir-loft ghoul whose hymn-perfect voice lures the faithful within reach of its talons.","desc":"A voice drifts down from the choir loft, perfect and aching, pulling you a step closer before you've decided to move. What's making that sound has a face built more for tearing than singing, and talons where the hymnal should be. It only stops singing once you're within reach.","traits":{"note": "It only stops singing once its target is within reach of its talons.", "actions": [{"name": "Rending Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Hymnal Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage from a heavy brass hymnal-stand swung like a mace."}, {"name": "Luring Hymn", "replaces": "Luring Song", "text": "The Chorister sings a perfect, aching hymn. Each Humanoid within 300 ft. that can hear it must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed until the song ends; a Charmed target takes the safest route toward the Chorister on its turn, ending its move if it comes within 5 feet. The Chorister can sustain the song each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A voice drifts down from the choir loft, perfect and aching, pulling you a step closer."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its face is built more for tearing than singing, talons where the hymnal should be."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only stops singing once its target is within reach."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It perches unnaturally still in the loft rafters between verses, watching who's fallen for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wings fold to look like choir robes from a distance, until it stands."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It targets the best singer in the room first, as if resenting the competition."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hymn it sings is one no living choir in the region has ever taught."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-verse, its unfinished note keeps ringing through the church for a full minute, luring anyone new who walks in."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["singing perfect and aching from the choir loft, pulling listeners a step closer before they've decided to move", "holding a hymn note past any human breath, talons hidden where the hymnal should be"]},{"name":"Marrow Beetle Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-insects","model":"swarm-of-insects","summary":"Grave-beetle carpet that strips corpses clean","flavor":"A carpet of grave-beetles that strips a corpse to clean bone in a single feeding.","desc":"A dark carpet of beetles moves across the floor in one rippling sheet, drawn to whatever's freshly dead — or freshly wounded. In seconds a corpse left in their path is bone. The sound of that many small shells clicking together fills the room before you see them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Marrow Strip", "replaces": "Bites", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft., or 0 ft. if the swarm occupies the target's space. Hit: 6 (2d4 + 1) Piercing damage, or 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer. The swarm deals double damage to an incapacitated or unconscious creature it occupies the space of."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dark carpet of beetles moves across the floor in one rippling sheet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "In seconds, anything freshly dead left in their path is stripped to clean bone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The clicking of countless small shells fills the room before the beetles come into view."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It ignores anything still moving, drawn hard toward the freshly still."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves behind bones scoured whiter than any weathering could account for."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It scatters into wall-cracks the instant a corpse is denied it, hiding rather than fighting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Picked apart, individual beetles carry tiny fragments of bone shaped like teeth, hoarded like coins."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied a corpse too long, the swarm turns on the nearest living thing all at once, starvation overriding caution."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave", "urban"],"activity":["rippling across the floor in one dark sheet, drawn toward whatever's freshly dead or freshly wounded", "stripping a corpse to clean bone in seconds, shells clicking together before the swarm even comes into view"]},{"name":"Bell-Jar Wraith","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"greater-shadow","summary":"Failed experiment reaching for its notes","flavor":"A physician's failed experiment, trapped between a bell jar and the grave, still reaching for its notes.","desc":"It hangs half-formed between a shattered bell jar and the floor, reaching with translucent fingers for notes that scattered years ago. Chemical residue still clings to what's left of its coat. It repeats the same failed gesture, over and over, never quite grasping the paper.","traits":{"note": "Chemical residue still clings to what's left of its coat, evidence of the experiment that killed it.", "actions": [{"name": "Failed Reach", "replaces": "Strength Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's Strength score is reduced by 1d4 for 1 hour; if this reduces it to 0, the target is instead paralyzed for that duration."}, {"name": "Sever Notes (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Sever Shadow (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Wraith's shadow detaches and glides up to 30 feet to occupy the space of a Small or smaller creature's shadow, an independent shade reaching for its own scattered notes, with the Wraith's Failed Reach action, until destroyed (AC 12, 10 hit points) or reunited with the Wraith."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hangs half-formed between a shattered bell jar and the floor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Translucent fingers reach for notes that scattered years ago and never landed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chemical residue still clings to what's left of its coat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats the same failed gesture over and over, never quite grasping the paper."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broken glassware around it chimes faintly whenever it passes close."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Handing it an actual sheet of paper stalls it for a full round, genuinely startled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The scattered notes it reaches for are, on closer look, blank on every page."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it finally closes its hand around something, and the room briefly fills with the ghost-scent of its last failed experiment igniting."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["reaching with translucent fingers for notes that scattered years ago, hanging half-formed between shattered glass and floor", "repeating the same failed gesture over the same spilled papers, never quite grasping them"]},{"name":"Attic-Bound Revenant","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Locked-away relative still pacing six feet","flavor":"A locked-away relative the family pretended never existed, still pacing the same six feet.","desc":"Something paces the same six feet of attic floorboard, over and over, footsteps landing in exactly the same spots each pass. The family who locked it up here pretended for years it didn't exist. It still wears whatever they buried it in, and the door still won't open from outside.","traits":{"note": "The family locked it up here and pretended for years it didn't exist.", "actions": [{"name": "Locked-Room Grasp", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Attic Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage if used with both hands, wielded with the stiff precision of long practice in a cramped space."}, {"name": "Attic Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage from arrows fletched with attic-dust and rag."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something paces the same six feet of attic floorboard, footsteps landing in the exact same spots."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still wears whatever the family buried it in, decades out of fashion."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The door still won't open from outside, exactly as the family intended."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust patterns on the floor show only that one worn path, nothing else disturbed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It speaks a name, quietly, at the same point in its pacing every single time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Say the name back to it and it stops pacing, turning to actually look at you."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its footsteps are audible from downstairs even when it's standing perfectly still."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, the door finally swings open on its own, and the pacing continues faintly from somewhere further up, a house with more attics than it should have."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["pacing the same six feet of attic floorboard, footsteps landing in exactly the same spots each pass", "wearing whatever it was buried in, testing a door that still won't open from the outside"]},{"name":"Coven Apprentice","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Hedge-witch initiate half in love with the dark","flavor":"A hedge-witch initiate memorizing the coven's book by candle-stub, half in love with the dark it teaches.","desc":"She sits hunched over a book by a candle stub, copying passages in a hand that shakes only a little now. There's a hunger in the way she reads — half fear, half something closer to love. She looks up at intruders like they've interrupted a lesson she was finally starting to enjoy.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Pact Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage from a blade bonded to the coven's book."}, {"name": "Hedge Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Apprentice casts one of her practiced hedge-spells, using the coven's book as her focus, drawing on rites she's only half-mastered."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She sits hunched over a book by a candle stub, hand shaking only a little now."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "There's a hunger in the way she reads, half fear, half something closer to love."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She looks up at intruders like they've interrupted a lesson she was enjoying."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Candle wax has built up in thick drifts around her reading spot, months of vigil."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her fingertips are stained with ink she can't quite scrub clean anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She fights to protect the book first, herself second, throwing herself between it and harm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The passages she copies rearrange themselves on the page the moment she looks away."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near the book, her last act is to press her palm flat against its cover, and the book briefly answers with a page turning on its own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "forest"],"activity":["hunched over a coven book by candle-stub, copying passages in a hand that only shakes a little now", "looking up at intruders like they've interrupted a lesson she was finally starting to enjoy"]},{"name":"Reliquary Ghast","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast-base","model":"ghast-base","summary":"Stolen saint's corpse gone hungry in vestments","flavor":"A saint's stolen corpse gone hungry, still wearing the vestments it was buried in.","desc":"Vestments hang rotted but recognizable off a frame that used to be a saint, or was buried as one. It moves with a clergy stoop, hands folded in front like it's still blessing something. The smell that comes off it is incense gone badly wrong.","traits":{"note": "The smell that comes off it is incense gone badly wrong.", "actions": [{"name": "Blessing Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and if the target is a creature other than an Undead, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or be Paralyzed for 1 minute; the target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Reliquary Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vestments hang rotted but recognizable off a frame that used to be, or was buried as, a saint."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves with a clergy stoop, hands folded in front like it's still blessing something."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The smell that comes off it is incense gone badly, thoroughly wrong."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles stolen reliquary boxes possessively, unwilling to stray far from them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its fingers still curl in the shape of an old blessing gesture, muscle memory outlasting the muscle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It recoils from anything genuinely holy, hissing and retreating a step before attacking again."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The relics it guards whisper back to it in a language no living cleric here still speaks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed near its hoard, the reliquary boxes crack open on their own, and whatever's inside starts humming a hymn of its own."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["moving with a clergy stoop, hands folded like it's still blessing something no one can see", "standing among stolen relics in vestments rotted but recognizable, hungry beneath the incense smell"]},{"name":"Ossified Bell-Ringer","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"Skeleton still ringing an unheard dusk bell","flavor":"A campanile skeleton that still climbs the tower stair each dusk, ringing a bell no one else hears.","desc":"Bone climbs the tower stair each dusk on schedule, hauling on a rope that no longer has a bell attached — or does, and nobody living can hear it anymore. It performs the same ritual with total conviction. Dust falls from the belfry each time it pulls.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bell-Rope Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage if used with both hands."}, {"name": "Shield Slam", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone climbs the tower stair each dusk on schedule, exactly on time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hauls on a rope no longer attached to any bell, or one nobody living can hear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust falls from the belfry each time it pulls, decades of accumulated grime."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It performs the ritual with total conviction, unbothered by the missing bell."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its finger-bones have worn smooth grooves into the old rope from repetition."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Interrupt the ringing before dusk finishes and it turns from its post, genuinely startled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "On certain nights, a bell tone actually sounds from the empty belfry when it pulls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-ring, the tower bell rings once on its own, and every grave within earshot settles an inch deeper into the ground."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["climbing the tower stair each dusk on schedule, hauling a rope no longer attached to any bell", "performing the same ritual with total conviction, dust falling from the belfry each time it pulls"]},{"name":"Charnel-Yard Skeleton Archer","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-archer","model":"skeleton-archer","summary":"Crossbow skeleton still holding its cemetery post","flavor":"A crossbow-armed grave-guard skeleton that still holds its post along the cemetery wall.","desc":"It stands at its post along the cemetery wall, crossbow leveled, exactly where it was set generations ago. Vines have grown through the ribcage and around the stock of the weapon. It doesn't move until something crosses the boundary it was told to hold.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Post Longbow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage from a weapon fused to the same post it's guarded for generations."}, {"name": "Bone Shard (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Bone Shard (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 60 ft. Hit: 9 (2d8) Piercing damage as it flings a jagged shard torn from its own ribcage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands at its post along the cemetery wall, crossbow leveled, unmoved for generations."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vines have grown through the ribcage and around the stock of its weapon."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It doesn't move until something crosses the exact boundary it was told to hold."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moss has claimed half its skull, softening the shape into something almost gentle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It resets to its post the instant a threat clears the wall, discipline outlasting purpose."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cross the boundary from behind it and it seems genuinely confused, slow to respond."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The boundary it guards has shifted twice in living memory, and it moved its post both times without being told."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed at its post, every skeleton buried along that same wall stirs at once, testing the boundary for the first time in generations."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins"],"activity":["standing post along the cemetery wall, crossbow leveled, exactly where it was set generations ago", "holding its line with vines grown through the ribcage, unmoving until the boundary is crossed"]},{"name":"Full-Moon Enforcer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"Pack lieutenant hiding claws until convenient","flavor":"A pack lieutenant who hunts in human guise all week and only shows its claws at the coven's convenience.","desc":"He looks like ordinary muscle in human shape — until his knuckles crack wrong and the fingers lengthen, claws sliding free only once the coven gives the word. All week he hunts on two legs, patient and quiet. He seems to enjoy the waiting more than the change.","traits":{"note": "He seems to enjoy the waiting more than the change itself.", "actions": [{"name": "Lieutenant's Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with the Enforcer's affliction, gaining symptoms after 1d4 days unless cured first."}, {"name": "Enforcer's Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Alley Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage, used only in human guise, and set aside the instant the change is given leave to happen."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He looks like ordinary muscle in human shape, patient and unremarkable."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His knuckles crack wrong and the fingers lengthen only once the coven gives the word."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "All week he hunts on two legs, waiting on permission he clearly relishes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries himself like hired muscle, unbothered, until the claws come out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He watches the moon's phase the way other men watch a clock."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Denied the change mid-fight, he fights just as competently in human form, merely annoyed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow shows claws a full day before his hands do, running ahead of the transformation."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given the coven's word mid-fight, the change happens instantly rather than gradually, and he's genuinely delighted by it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest", "hill"],"activity":["walking as ordinary muscle in human shape, patient and quiet, waiting for the coven's word to change", "cracking his knuckles wrong in a back alley, claws sliding free only once given permission"]},{"name":"Steeple Bloodkin","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"Choirmaster vampire leading hymns with stitched smile","flavor":"A choirmaster turned bloodsucker who still leads the hymn each Sunday, mouth stitched into a smile.","desc":"He still leads the hymn from the choir loft every Sunday, mouth stitched into a permanent smile that never quite reaches the eyes. His voice carries beautifully, if you don't look too closely at the stitches. Between verses, his gaze drifts to the congregation's throats.","traits":{"note": "His voice carries beautifully — if you don't look too closely at the stitches.", "actions": [{"name": "Choirmaster's Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Stitched Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the Necrotic damage taken until the target finishes a long rest. If the reduction takes the target's maximum to 0, it dies."}, {"name": "Perfect Hymn (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Bloodkin sings a single perfect, unbroken note through stitched lips. Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear it must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom saving throw or be Charmed until the end of the Bloodkin's next turn, standing transfixed and unable to move away from him."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He still leads the hymn from the choir loft every Sunday, without fail."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His mouth is stitched into a permanent smile that never quite reaches the eyes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice carries beautifully, if you don't look too closely at the stitches."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Between verses, his gaze drifts to the congregation's throats, hunger barely hidden."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wears his choir robes immaculately, blood-spatter laundered out weekly without fail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He refuses to feed on anyone who's actually sung the hymn well, oddly professional courtesy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The stitches in his smile loosen, just slightly, every time the choir hits a note flat."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-hymn, his final note keeps ringing through the nave, and every throat in the room feels, briefly, exactly what he wanted from them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["leading the Sunday hymn from the choir loft, mouth stitched into a smile that never reaches the eyes", "gazing at the congregation's throats between verses, voice carrying beautifully if you don't look too closely"]},{"name":"The Weeping Bride","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Jilted ghost bride whose scream shatters glass","flavor":"A ghost bride whose scream shatters glass at the mention of the groom who left her at the altar.","desc":"White lace, yellowed and torn at the hem, drags behind her as she walks the aisle of an empty chapel. Mention the groom who left her and the windows shudder — a scream that starts as grief and ends as something that shatters glass and eardrums both.","traits":{"note": "Her scream only reaches full force once — after that she relies on the touch.", "actions": [{"name": "Chilling Grasp", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "The Face at the Altar", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can see her face makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute, ending early if it takes damage; while Frightened this way it cannot approach within 10 ft. of her."}, {"name": "Shattering Wail (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "She screams the groom's name. Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 12 Constitution save, taking 17 (5d6) Psychic damage on a failure (half on success). Glass, mirrors, and windows within range shatter automatically."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still clutches a bouquet of flowers pressed flat and black with age."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums the wedding march under her breath between sentences."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straightens invisible guests' place settings before she notices intruders."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her veil never lifts, no matter how hard the wind off the broken windows blows."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Curtsies before she attacks, old wedding-day manners surfacing through the rage."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She mistakes a party member's voice for the groom's and softens for exactly one round."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every mirror in the chapel shows her mid-vow, a half-second behind her real movements."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, she rips off the veil — underneath, her face is still mid-scream from the day she died."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["walking the aisle of an empty chapel, trailing torn lace and the smell of old flowers", "standing before a cracked mirror, rehearsing vows to a groom who never answers"]},{"name":"Warden of the Drowning Pool","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Cursed executioner guarding the drowning pool","flavor":"A witch-trial executioner cursed to guard the millpond where he condemned the innocent.","desc":"He stands knee-deep at the edge of the millpond, cursed to guard the water where he once condemned the innocent. His executioner's hood is soaked black and clinging. He doesn't let anyone leave the water's edge until he's decided whether they deserve to.","traits":{"note": "He judges before he fights — anyone who wades in gets one question first.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks: one with Drowned Blade, one with Verdict Bow."}, {"name": "Drowned Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage with two hands."}, {"name": "Verdict Bow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "The Verdict's Chill", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding someone under, deciding — the party has maybe two rounds to convince him otherwise."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A drowned villager's ring floats free of the pool the moment the party arrives, still warm."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He blocks the only ford across, and the water behind him is rising with the storm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's dragging a real innocent toward the water by the collar, mid-sentence, mid-verdict."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rope trails from his fist into the pool, tied to something the party will want back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He mistakes one of the party for the judge who cursed him, and wants a retrial."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pool's surface shows the old trial in reflection, replaying whenever he raises his sword."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing him drops the water level entirely, and what he'd been guarding underneath starts to surface."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp", "ruins"],"activity":["standing knee-deep at the millpond's edge, hood soaked black, deciding who's allowed to leave", "hauling a struggling shape toward the water by the collar, weighing an old verdict"]},{"name":"Hollow-Throated Ghast Priest","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghast","model":"ghast","summary":"Defrocked cleric who joined his flock's feast","flavor":"A defrocked cleric who fed his own flock to something in the crypt and joined the feast.","desc":"He wears a collar gone stiff with old blood, standing over what's left of a flock he fed to something in the crypt below. His voice still has a sermon's cadence, warm even now. He joined the feast himself, in the end, and hasn't stopped since.","traits":{"note": "His voice stays warm and pastoral throughout — the horror is the sermon never stopping.", "actions": [{"name": "Communion Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or be Paralyzed for 1 minute (repeat save at the end of each of its turns)."}, {"name": "Blessing Claws", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Delivers his sermon in full, unbroken cadence even while chewing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still blesses each visitor before attacking, out of old habit."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a prayer book, pages stuck together with something dark."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls intruders by the names of parishioners long since eaten."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His collar has rusted to his throat; he can't remove it even if he wanted to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers a genuine kindness first — water, a blanket — before the hunger wins."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The crypt below answers his sermon in a chorus of chewing, faint and rhythmic."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied his meal, he screams the final line of a rite meant to wake whatever's still down there."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["kneeling over the last of his flock, delivering a sermon between mouthfuls", "pacing the nave in a stiff blood-collar, calling latecomers to a feast that's already begun"]},{"name":"Coven Hexweaver","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"Coven's youngest sister, bargains cruelly","flavor":"A three-sister coven's youngest voice, still human enough to bargain, cruel enough to relish it.","desc":"The youngest sister of the coven looks almost ordinary — a little too pretty, a little too pleased with herself. She'll bargain fairly if it amuses her, and cruelly the moment it stops. Her hands never quite stop moving, weaving something out of the air between sentences.","traits":{"note": "She always offers a deal before the claws come out — refusing the deal is what earns them.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "She makes two attacks with Pretty Claws."}, {"name": "Pretty Claws", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Cruel Bargain", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "She casts a spell, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 14). She can innately cast Charm Person and Suggestion, and once per day, Bestow Curse, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers a fair trade for something the party needs, hands still weaving as she talks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's mid-bargain with a desperate local, and the terms are about to turn cruel."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A half-finished hex hangs unraveling in the air where she left it, dangerous to touch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants something specific from the party's pockets, and names the price with a smile."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her sisters are close by; she's stalling to let them arrive."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's genuinely bored today, and might bargain fairly just to see what happens."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The thing she's weaving between her hands is a shape none of the party recognize, half-finished and humming."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cross her hard enough and she calls in a debt owed by someone the party trusts."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["swamp", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["weaving something invisible between her fingers, watching a bargain take shape in the air", "perched pretty and pleased on a fence post, waiting for someone foolish enough to ask her for a favor"]},{"name":"The Mirror-Bound Twin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Face-stealing reflection waiting in every mirror","flavor":"A reflection that stole its owner's face centuries ago and now waits in every polished surface.","desc":"Every polished surface in the house holds the same watching shape, waiting since it stole its owner's face centuries ago. It mimics your expressions a beat too perfectly, like it's practicing. When it finally steps free of the glass, it looks exactly like you expected — just wrong around the eyes.","traits":{"note": "It can only act freely once it's stepped fully out of a reflective surface — until then, it's watching and rehearsing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Borrowed Touch."}, {"name": "Borrowed Touch", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Step Through Glass", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "It can move into any reflective surface (mirror, still water, polished metal) as if it were a doorway, and can see and act from within it as though ethereal."}, {"name": "The Face It Practiced", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that sees its true face makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute, ending early if it takes damage."}, {"name": "Wear Your Skin (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One creature it can see within 5 ft. makes a DC 12 Charisma save. On a failure, it is Possessed by the twin (the twin then disappears, and the target is Incapacitated and loses control of its body). The possessing twin can end the possession at will; when it does, or when reduced to 0 HP, the target is freed and takes 13 (3d8) Psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Copies the last expression it saw on a real face, a half-second delayed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its reflection wears clothes decades out of fashion, no matter who's looking in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Taps the glass twice before stepping through, an old habit it can't shake."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Prefers to study a target's mannerisms for a full day before ever showing itself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes are the one part of the borrowed face it never quite gets right."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown fond of one particular reflection, and hesitates before wearing that face."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Break the mirror it lives in and its reflection keeps moving in every other glass in the house, briefly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Given enough time in a stolen skin, it starts to forget which face was ever really its own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["mimicking a passerby's expression a beat too perfectly from inside a dusty mirror", "waiting behind glass, practicing the face it's about to wear out into the world"]},{"name":"Rite-Scarred Zealot Captain","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"Ritual leader scarred with a forbidden name","flavor":"A ritual leader whose scars spell the summoning name in a language the tongue was never meant for.","desc":"Scars run in careful lines across his face and forearms, spelling a name in a tongue no human throat was built to say. He commands the ritual with total certainty, voice raised over the chanting circle. The scars seem to catch what little light there is.","traits":{"note": "His scars aren't decoration — they're the incantation, and he can read them even in total dark.", "actions": [{"name": "Scarred Blade", "replaces": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "The Name in the Scars", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "He casts a spell, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (save DC 12). He can innately cast Command and Hold Person, and once per day, Spirit Guardians, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's finishing the ritual now, chanting circle mid-glow, and needs three more minutes uninterrupted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's recruiting at the edge of town, promising purpose to anyone desperate enough to listen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hostage kneels at the circle's edge, next in line for the scarring rite."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He carries the coven's sealed instructions, and won't surrender them without a fight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's tracking a defector from his own cell, and the party's in his way."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He speaks the summoning name once, testing it, and flinches at what almost answered."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His scars rearrange slightly overnight, as if the name is still being written."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-chant, his scars flare and finish the rite anyway, on their own."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "any"],"activity":["commanding a chanting circle with total certainty, scars catching what little light remains", "tracing the summoning name on his own forearm as the ritual nears its final line"]},{"name":"Charnel-House Ogre Zombie","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"ogre-zombie","model":"ogre-zombie","summary":"Gravedigger's corpse raised by his own rite","flavor":"A gravedigger's own hulking corpse, reanimated by the very rite he used to raise others.","desc":"It was a gravedigger once, and huge even then — now it's huger, raised by the very rite it used to perform on others. Grave-dirt packs its wounds instead of blood. It swings a shovel still crusted with the mud of its own grave.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Gravedigger's Shovel", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Hurl Corpse-Weight", "replaces": "Fling", "text": "One Medium or smaller creature it is grappling is thrown up to 30 ft. and knocked Prone. Ranged Attack Roll: +6 against a creature in the destination space. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still swings the shovel it used to dig graves, crusted with its own grave's mud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grave-dirt sifts out of its wounds instead of blood with every heavy step."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gravedigger's coat is buttoned wrong, one arm through the wrong sleeve."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It returns, over and over, to the same six-foot plot, as if still finishing the job."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flies gather thick around it even in the cold, undeterred by the season."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at a fresh grave and, briefly, starts digging instead of attacking."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shovel strikes leave soil behind in the wound, as if planting something."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed near open ground, the dirt around it heaves once more before settling still."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["dragging a mud-crusted shovel across the ground, grave-dirt packed into every open wound", "lumbering between headstones it once dug, swinging at anything that moves"]},{"name":"The Second Groom","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight-lord","model":"wight-lord","summary":"Jilted suitor presiding over an eternal reception","flavor":"A jilted suitor who murdered the wedding party and now presides over an eternal, empty reception.","desc":"He presides at the head of an empty banquet table, plates set for guests who died at his hand decades ago. His wedding coat has rotted to lace. He still rises to greet new arrivals with the exact same toast, word for word, waiting for someone to finally say yes.","traits":{"note": "He always offers the toast first — refusing it is what he takes as the final answer he's been waiting for.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks with the Reception Blade."}, {"name": "Reception Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (1d8 + 5) Slashing damage, or 10 (1d10 + 5) Slashing damage with two hands, plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "The Toast", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Ring the Old Guests (1/Day)", "replaces": "Command the Dead (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. As an action, he calls the wedding party back to their seats. Up to three Undead of CR 1 or lower within 60 ft. rise from wherever they lie (or arrive from just outside) and take their next turn immediately, seated and ready to attend him."}, {"name": "Say Yes (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Terrifying Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 30 ft. that can see him makes a DC 14 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature is Frightened for 1 minute and, while Frightened, must spend its turn moving toward the head of the table by the safest route available."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's set an extra place at the table the moment the party walked in, expecting them to sit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His rotted wedding coat holds the guest list — real names, real debts owed by their families."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the toast, mid-scene, and someone at the table has one round to refuse it or drink."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living relative of a murdered guest has come seeking the truth, and he's delighted to host them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's polishing silverware for guests who've been dead for decades, meticulous and calm."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He mistakes a party member for his bride, and the reception briefly turns tender."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The banquet resets itself between visits — same plates, same rot, like no time passed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If someone finally says yes to the toast, the whole reception hall lurches into motion around them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["presiding over an empty banquet, raising a toast to guests he murdered decades ago", "rising at the head of a rotted table to greet arrivals with the same word-for-word welcome"]},{"name":"Loomstitch Doppelganger","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"Face-thief impersonating the beloved village elder","flavor":"A face-thief who replaced a beloved village elder months ago, and no one has noticed the seams yet.","desc":"The village elder greets you warmly, exactly as they always have — the voice is right, the mannerisms are right, and if you look closely at the hairline there's a seam that shouldn't be there. It's been wearing this face for months, and no one else has noticed.","traits":{"note": "It genuinely enjoys the role by now — killing it costs the village someone they still, in a sense, love.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Seamed Slam."}, {"name": "Seamed Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Read the Village", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "It reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 ft. for as long as it concentrates, up to 1 minute, learning enough to keep its impersonation flawless."}, {"name": "Wrong Around the Eyes (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. Each creature within 30 ft. that can see it makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute, ending early if it takes damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's presiding over a town meeting the party needs to attend, warm and utterly convincing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A relative visiting after years away is starting to notice the seam at the hairline."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It knows a secret only the real elder should know, and offers it as proof of good faith."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real elder's remains are hidden somewhere close, and someone's finally asking questions."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's about to make a decision on the village's behalf that the real elder never would have."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hesitates over a choice the real elder would have made differently, just for a moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Under stress its borrowed voice slips into someone else's accent entirely, mid-sentence."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Exposed publicly, it drops the face entirely and the whole village finally sees what greeted them for months."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["greeting neighbors warmly with a familiar voice, hairline seam catching the lamplight", "tending the elder's garden exactly as always, mannerisms rehearsed to the smallest gesture"]},{"name":"Gallows Wraith Captain","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"Hanged highwayman commanding lesser gibbet-spirits","flavor":"An executed highwayman who commands lesser hanged-spirits from the crossroads gibbet.","desc":"It hangs at the crossroads gibbet with the noose still around its neck, commanding a handful of lesser hanged-spirits with a raised, rotted hand. Its voice carries the flat authority of a man used to giving orders. The other gibbet-ghosts obey without hesitation.","traits":{"note": "He commands rather than fights personally where he can — the lesser gibbet-spirits go first.", "actions": [{"name": "Gallows Touch", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Raise the Gibbet-Spirits", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "He points to a corpse within 10 ft. that died within the last 24 hours, or to the site of an old execution. A Specter rises there under his command, obeying his orders without question."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He blocks the crossroads road entirely, and the party's only detour runs through worse terrain."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's raising a fresh spirit from a body the party recognizes, right now, at the gibbet's foot."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living traveler is bound and pleading at the gibbet's base, next scheduled for the noose."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's interrogating a captured spirit for names — informants, maybe the party's own contacts."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A handful of lesser spirits obey him mid-patrol, and he's directing them toward the party's camp."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of his gibbet-ghosts hesitates on an order, an old flicker of guilt breaking discipline."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The noose around his neck tightens on its own whenever he gives an order he doesn't believe in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, his authority breaks and every spirit he commanded turns on whoever's nearest, including each other."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "any"],"activity":["hanging at the crossroads gibbet, noose still fixed, directing lesser spirits with a rotted hand", "commanding a huddle of hanged-ghosts into formation along the old execution road"]},{"name":"Vestry Revenant","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"graveyard-revenant","model":"graveyard-revenant","summary":"Swollen sexton digging until his killer's found","flavor":"A murdered sexton, swollen with grave-rot fury, who will not stop digging until his killer is found.","desc":"Enormous and swollen with grave-rot, it claws through the churchyard soil with hands too big for the shovel that used to fit them. It was a sexton once, murdered mid-dig, and it will not stop turning earth until it finds whoever did it. Dirt sprays with every furious motion.","traits":{"note": "It never stops digging voluntarily — only combat, or finding what it's looking for, interrupts the work.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Digger's Grip."}, {"name": "Digger's Grip", "replaces": "Suffocate", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is Grappled (escape DC 16) and, while grappled this way, it can't breathe."}, {"name": "The Killer's Face (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Haunting Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 60 ft. that can see it makes a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute; while Frightened this way, it perceives its own reflection as the sexton's killer."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's digging up a specific plot right now, and someone buried there matters to a party member."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A confession, half-legible, lies buried under the plot it's currently tearing open."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The real killer is hiding in town, and the revenant's dig pattern is slowly circling toward them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's exhumed a body the town paid dearly to keep buried, and word is starting to spread."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living gravedigger, terrified, is caught between the party and the revenant's rampage."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses over a specific headstone, hands trembling, before resuming with renewed fury."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The soil it's disturbed refuses to settle, staying loose and turned for yards in every direction."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If it finally uncovers its killer's remains, the whole churchyard convulses as if the ground itself exhales."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["clawing through churchyard soil with hands too big for the shovel that used to fit them", "standing over a half-dug plot, swollen with grave-rot, refusing to stop turning earth"]},{"name":"Cellar-Bound Bulette Grub","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"bulette","model":"bulette","summary":"Burrowing horror surfacing through open graves","flavor":"A burrowing horror that tunneled up under a village graveyard and now surfaces through open plots.","desc":"The ground heaves and cracks before it surfaces — a horror built for tunneling, breaking up through an open grave in a spray of soil and splintered wood. It doesn't so much emerge as erupt. Nothing about its approach is subtle.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Grave-Iron Jaws."}, {"name": "Grave-Iron Jaws", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Erupt from the Plot", "replaces": "Deadly Leap", "text": "It bursts up from underground soil within 5 ft. of it into a space within 15 ft., ending the movement in an unoccupied space. Each creature within 5 ft. of its destination space makes a DC 15 Strength save. On a failure, a creature takes 14 (4d6) Bludgeoning damage and is knocked Prone; on a success, half damage only."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves fresh grave-dirt scattered in a perfect circle wherever it surfaces."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coffin splinters stick out of its hide like a second layer of armor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It surfaces only through recently disturbed ground, drawn to freshly turned soil."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaws still carry a shred of burial cloth from its last meal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ground trembles for a full ten seconds before it finally breaks the surface."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's tunneled beneath the wrong plot for weeks, and the graveyard's foundations are starting to sag."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to favor certain graves over others, as if it can smell which dead are still restless."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near open plots, its death throes collapse the ground into a sinkhole that swallows the nearest grave whole."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["cracking the ground open beneath a graveyard plot in a spray of soil and splintered wood", "surfacing through an open grave, dirt raining off a hide built for tunneling"]},{"name":"Coven Matron's Cauldron-Kin","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"Second matriarch trading in nightmares, not curses","flavor":"A second matriarch of the same coven, who trades in nightmares rather than curses.","desc":"A second matriarch, this one trading in nightmares instead of curses, stirs something dark and slow over a low fire. Her presence makes the shadows in the room lean toward her. She smiles the way someone smiles when they already know how your dreams tonight will go.","traits":{"note": "She trades in dreams, not curses — her worst work happens while the victim sleeps, off-scene.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "She makes two attacks with Cauldron Claws."}, {"name": "Cauldron Claws", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Slip Into the Fireside Smoke", "replaces": "Plane", "text": "She and anything she's carrying vanish into the smoke of her fire, teleporting to a point she can see within 60 ft., or to another fire she has stirred within the last 24 hours anywhere on the same plane."}, {"name": "Feed a Nightmare", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "She casts a spell, using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (save DC 15). She can innately cast Sleep and Phantasmal Force, and once per day, Dream, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's brewing over a fire made of someone's stolen sleep, and that someone is fading fast."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A villager sleepwalks toward her fire even now, drawn by a nightmare already half-fed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She holds a vial of someone's worst dream, willing to trade it back for the right price."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her cauldron is nearly ready, and whatever she's brewing needs one more ingredient the party's carrying."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The coven's youngest sister is due to arrive any minute, and the matron wants the meeting kept quiet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She offers to show a party member their own worst dream, free of charge, just to watch their face."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The smoke off her fire briefly shows the dreams of everyone nearby, unfiltered and uninvited."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed at her cauldron, every nightmare she's ever brewed spills loose into the waking world at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["swamp", "forest", "ruins"],"activity":["stirring something dark and slow over a low fire, shadows leaning toward her like an audience", "tasting a nightmare off a ladle, already smiling at how tonight's dreams will go"]},{"name":"Blood-Thrall Chevalier","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"knight","model":"knight","summary":"Centuries-loyal knight thrall, still starving","flavor":"A knight sworn to a vampire's service centuries past, still armored, still loyal, still starving.","desc":"He still wears his armor, dented and centuries out of fashion, sworn to a master he serves without question. His eyes are sunken with a hunger he's forbidden from satisfying himself. He stands at rigid attention outside the coffin door, starving in perfect discipline.","traits":{"note": "He never feeds without his master's leave — the hunger shows only in how carefully he doesn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks with the Thrall's Greatsword."}, {"name": "Thrall's Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 100/400 ft. Hit: 8 (1d10 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding the coffin door right now, and his master is inside, vulnerable until dusk."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been ordered not to feed, and the hunger is fraying his discipline visibly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A message from his master, sealed in old wax, needs delivering before he can be reasoned with."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He recognizes an old family crest on a party member's gear from his mortal life."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been sent to retrieve something the party is currently carrying, no negotiation offered."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Offered blood freely, he hesitates, starved discipline warring with centuries of denial."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His armor never quite settles into modern light, always a shade too dark for the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut off from his master's coffin too long, the starvation finally breaks and he stops being careful."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing rigid attention outside a coffin door, sunken-eyed and starving in perfect discipline", "polishing centuries-old armor by rote, waiting for a summons that never quite satisfies the hunger"]},{"name":"Ashfall Mummy Curate","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy","model":"mummy","summary":"Punished elder mummified alive, still shepherding","flavor":"A sect elder mummified alive as punishment, now shepherding the congregation from inside its wrappings.","desc":"Wrapped alive as punishment by his own sect, he still shepherds a congregation that's long since stopped listening — voice muffled through the linen at his mouth. He moves with the slow, careful patience of someone who has nowhere left to be in a hurry.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Wrapped Fist."}, {"name": "Wrapped Fist", "replaces": "Rotting Fist", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be cursed with mummy rot."}, {"name": "Sermon's Weight", "replaces": "Dreadful Glare", "text": "One creature it can see within 60 ft. makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature is Frightened for 1 minute (repeat save at the end of each of its turns)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still delivers Sunday sermons to an empty room, on schedule, every week."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wrappings at the mouth are stained dark where the muffled voice pushes through."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves at exactly one pace, unhurried, regardless of what's chasing it or being chased."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a censer that no longer burns anything but still swings out of habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wrappings are inscribed with the same punishment-rite it was bound in, still legible."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses mid-sermon at any sign of a genuine confession, listening despite itself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The empty pews creak in response to its sermon, as if something still sits in them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck down mid-service, its final act is to finish the line of the punishment-rite it never chose."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "desert"],"activity":["shepherding a congregation that stopped listening years ago, voice muffled through mouth-wrappings", "moving with the slow patience of someone who has nowhere left to be in a hurry"]},{"name":"Marrow-Bound Wererat Broker","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"wererat","model":"wererat","summary":"Sewer relic-fixer who bites debtors","flavor":"A black-market fixer who trades cursed relics from the sewers, and bites those who don't pay.","desc":"He works the sewer market in a long coat, laying cursed relics out on a blanket like they're ordinary wares. His smile shows a few too many teeth when a debtor's late on payment. The bite that follows isn't a warning — it's a bill collector's signature.","traits":{"note": "The bite is business, not appetite — a bill collector's signature, first and last.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks: one with Collector's Bite (only in Rat or Hybrid Form), one with Broker's Scratch."}, {"name": "Collector's Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be cursed with wereratism."}, {"name": "Broker's Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's selling a relic the party needs, but the price is a favor they'll regret owing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A debtor cowers nearby, one missed payment from a bite that isn't a warning."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a relic stolen from someone the party is working for, and knows exactly what it's worth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival broker's rats are closing in on its stall, and it wants muscle, fast."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's fencing something hot, and the sewer market goes quiet the moment the party's noticed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers the party a genuinely fair deal, hedging its usual cruelty against future business."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its blanket of wares rearranges itself overnight, as if the relics choose their own buyers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it near its ledger and it threatens to call in every debt at once, citywide, tonight."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "cave"],"activity":["laying cursed relics out on a blanket in the sewer market like they're ordinary wares", "smiling with too many teeth at a debtor who's a payment late"]},{"name":"Widow-Maker Banshee Elder","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"Generations-old wail that claims every husband","flavor":"A generations-old keening spirit whose wail has claimed every man who married into her bloodline.","desc":"Her wail has claimed every man who married into this bloodline for generations, and she has no plans to stop now. She keens from somewhere just out of sight, the sound aging with each retelling of the family's grief. New husbands don't last the season.","traits":{"note": "Generations of husbands haven't survived her — she is patient, and has never once needed to hurry.", "actions": [{"name": "Widow's Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Grief Made Visible", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can see her makes a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute, ending early if it takes damage."}, {"name": "The Wail That Claims (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "She keens for the bloodline. Each creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 25 (5d8) Psychic damage on a failure (half on success). A married creature within range has Disadvantage on this save."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A new husband in the bloodline has weeks left before her season claims him, and he's begging for help."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's keening near a wedding already underway, and the groom doesn't yet know why the guests are pale."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A family heirloom that might ward her off has gone missing, and someone's desperate to find it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's tracking a widow who married out of the bloodline, considering whether the debt still applies."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An old letter names the exact terms of the curse, and the family's hidden it for generations."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She lingers, for once, on a marriage that seems happy, uncertain whether to end it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her keen changes pitch depending on how many generations have passed, aging in real time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-season, her unclaimed wail passes to the next eldest woman in the bloodline instead."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["keening from just out of sight, the sound aging with each retelling of the family's grief", "watching a new husband settle into the bloodline's house, already counting down the season"]},{"name":"Coffin-Nail Wight Sergeant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"wight","summary":"Buried captain drilling reanimated ranks by night","flavor":"A militia captain buried with his men, now drilling their reanimated ranks in the churchyard at night.","desc":"Buried with the men he commanded, he now drills their reanimated ranks in the churchyard by night, barking the same orders in a voice gone dry as the ground he rose from. The ranks shamble into formation with a discipline that outlived them.","traits":{"note": "His ranks obey with a discipline that outlived them — break his command and they scatter, briefly.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "He makes two attacks: one with Sergeant's Blade, one with Drill Bow."}, {"name": "Sergeant's Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage with two hands."}, {"name": "Drill Bow", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Muster the Ranks", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's drilling his ranks right now, and the party's noise has just broken their formation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A surviving relative of one of his men wants the body returned for a proper burial."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding the militia's old armory, and the ranks won't stand down without his order."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living deserter from the same regiment is hiding nearby, and he's still hunting him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The churchyard drill has drawn complaints from the living town, who want it stopped quietly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He calls a cadence that's slightly wrong, a name missing from the ranks that used to answer."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His ranks drill in perfect unison even when he isn't watching, muscle memory outliving orders."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-drill, his ranks keep marching without him, ownerless and unpredictable."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["drilling reanimated ranks in the churchyard by night, barking orders gone dry as dust", "marching buried soldiers through formation drills none of them will ever complete again"]},{"name":"Blood-Drunk Vampire Familiar Knight","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-familiar","model":"vampire-familiar","summary":"Turned squire guarding the coffin, hunting by dusk","flavor":"A turned squire who serves his master's coffin by day and hunts travelers by dusk.","desc":"He guards his master's coffin by day, dutiful and silent, and by dusk he's out hunting travelers on the road with the same discipline. Turned young and kept that way, he still moves like a squire eager to prove himself — just with a different kind of service now.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with the Umbral Dagger."}, {"name": "Umbral Dagger", "replaces": "Umbral Dagger", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d4 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hunting the dusk road tonight, and a local traveler is his next intended stop."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding his master's coffin right now, and daylight leaves him vulnerable but dutiful."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants to prove himself to his master, and a fresh kill would do it — the party's nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A family he served in life recognizes him, and he can't quite bring himself to strike them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's carrying a message between two vampire households, and won't be delayed."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He hesitates over a target who reminds him of the squire he used to be, just for a moment."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His shadow moves half a step out of sync with him, a leftover habit from his turning."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut off from his master too long, the hunger overrides the discipline entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing dutiful guard over a coffin by daylight, eager to prove himself all over again", "hunting the dusk road for travelers with a squire's discipline and a different kind of service"]},{"name":"Seance Circle Medium","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"priest","summary":"Parlor medium who opened a door she can't close","flavor":"A parlor spiritualist who really did open a door, and now can't close it, or doesn't want to.","desc":"Her hands rest on the table, palms up, eyes rolled back to white while her voice comes out layered — hers, and something else's underneath. She really did open a door, once, in a parlor full of paying customers. She isn't sure anymore if she wants it closed.","traits":{"note": "She started as a fraud — the door she opened by accident is the only real thing about her act now.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "She makes two attacks with the Seance Mace."}, {"name": "Seance Mace", "replaces": "Mace", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Radiant Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 60 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Radiant damage."}, {"name": "Voice From Underneath", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "She casts a spell, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (save DC 12). She can innately cast Speak with Dead and Command, and once per day, Clairvoyance, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's mid-seance for a paying client right now, and the answer coming through isn't hers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving family wants one more session, unaware what's really answering their questions."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The door she opened is letting something else through tonight, and she's asking the party for help closing it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding information from beyond the door that a party member desperately wants."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival medium has accused her of fraud, and the real evidence would end both their careers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "For one lucid moment her own voice breaks through, begging someone to make it stop."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The layered voice under hers occasionally answers questions no one in the room asked."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed too far, she stops trying to close the door and starts trying to open it wider."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting palms-up at the table, eyes rolled white, voice coming out layered with something else's", "holding a parlor circle that opened a real door, unsure anymore if she wants it closed"]},{"name":"Effigy-Bound Flesh Golem","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"Resurrectionist's patchwork sewn from village corpses","flavor":"A resurrectionist's stitched patchwork, sewn from a village's worth of the recently deceased.","desc":"Stitched from a village's worth of the recently deceased, it lumbers forward in patchwork skin the color of old bruises, seams visible at every joint. It moves without hurry, without hesitation, built by a resurrectionist who was never squeamish about the sourcing.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Stitched Fist."}, {"name": "Stitched Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stitched seams are labeled in a resurrectionist's careful, tiny handwriting."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hand is visibly smaller than the other, sewn from a different donor entirely."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves without hurry, each footstep deliberate and unhesitating."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patchwork skin the color of old bruises shifts slightly at the seams when it exerts itself."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a faint graveyard smell no amount of time seems to air out."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A stitched-in face twitches with something like recognition at a familiar voice."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its component parts occasionally move independently for a beat, as if arguing over the whole."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn open in combat, its stitched pieces briefly writhe apart before the whole collapses for good."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["lumbering forward in patchwork skin the color of old bruises, seams visible at every joint", "standing motionless in a resurrectionist's workshop, waiting for the next command to move"]},{"name":"The Uninherited Heir","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"Disinherited ghost rewriting the will in blood","flavor":"A disinherited son who haunts the family estate, rewriting the will in blood on the study wall each night.","desc":"He haunts the family study, disinherited and furious, rewriting the will in dripping red script across the wallpaper each night. By morning the room reeks of iron and old paper. He erases it and starts over the moment anyone reads it aloud.","traits":{"note": "He erases his own work the moment it's witnessed — the will only exists unread.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Ink-Stained Touch."}, {"name": "Ink-Stained Touch", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Etherealness", "text": "It can enter the Ethereal Plane from the Material Plane, or vice versa, as an action."}, {"name": "The Will's Fury", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can see it makes a DC 12 Wisdom save. On a failure a creature is Frightened for 1 minute, ending early if it takes damage."}, {"name": "Claim the Estate (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. One creature it can see within 5 ft. makes a DC 12 Charisma save. On a failure, it is Possessed by the heir (the heir then disappears, and the target is Incapacitated and loses control of its body). While possessing, the target's writing hand compulsively drafts the will. The possession ends if the heir chooses, or if the target drops to 0 HP; when it ends this way, the target takes 13 (3d8) Psychic damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rewriting the will right now on the study wall, ink still wet, listening for footsteps."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living heir has come to claim the estate, and he considers them theft in progress."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A lawyer's copy of the original will, unread by him, is hidden somewhere the party could find."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants someone to read the will aloud and mean it, so it might finally hold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The estate is being sold out from under the family name, and he's furious about the sale papers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He pauses mid-script at the sound of his own name spoken kindly, uncertain how to respond."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wallpaper under the ink retains every version of the will ever written, layered and legible at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If the will is ever read aloud in full without interruption, the whole house responds to the new terms."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["rewriting the family will in dripping red script across the study wallpaper each night", "erasing the will the instant anyone reads it aloud, furious and disinherited all over again"]},{"name":"Coven Familiar Alpha","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"winter-wolf","model":"winter-wolf","summary":"Coven-bound wolf whose howl carries a curse","flavor":"A frost-pale wolf bound to the coven's oldest hex, its howl carrying a curse instead of a warning.","desc":"Frost clings to its pelt even indoors, a wolf built along wrong lines, bound to the coven's oldest hex. Its howl doesn't carry a warning the way a wolf's should — it carries the curse itself, landing on whoever's close enough to hear the note change.","traits":{"note": "Its howl doesn't warn like a real wolf's — it's the delivery mechanism for the coven's curse.", "actions": [{"name": "Hexbound Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Curse-Howl (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Cold Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. It exhales a curse-laced frost in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area makes a DC 12 Constitution save, taking 18 (4d8) Cold damage on a failure (half on success); a creature that fails also has Disadvantage on saving throws against curse and hex effects for 1 hour."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Frost clings to its pelt even in warm rooms, refusing to melt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves along wrong lines, joints bending a half-degree off from a natural wolf's."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its howl carries for miles, further than its lungs should physically allow."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It answers to a coven-name rather than any wolf-call, ignoring anything else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Where it walks, frost patterns form in shapes too regular to be natural."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It circles a specific hex-marked tree obsessively, guarding it more than hunting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes briefly show a coven sister's reflection instead of its own when it's angry."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed near the coven's hex-site, its final howl completes the curse it never got to deliver."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "mountain", "swamp"],"activity":["padding along frost-rimed ground even indoors, ears pricked toward the coven's oldest hex", "howling once, low, and letting the note change carry the curse instead of a warning"]},{"name":"Rot-Crowned Spirit Naga","cr":8,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"spirit-naga","model":"spirit-naga","summary":"Serpentine grave-idol worshipped as a saint","flavor":"A grave-cult idol given serpentine unlife, worshipped by the possessed congregation as a saint.","desc":"Coiled at the heart of the grave-cult's shrine, serpentine and glowing faintly with unlife, it's worshipped by a possessed congregation as something holy. It speaks in a voice too calm for what it is, offering wisdom laced with rot.","traits":{"note": "It rules through its congregation more than through combat — expect possessed worshippers before it fights directly.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Idol's Bite."}, {"name": "Idol's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Necrotic Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 150 ft. Hit: 22 (4d10) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Wisdom Laced With Rot", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "It casts a spell, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability (save DC 16). It can innately cast Command and Hold Person, and once per day, Insect Plague, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its congregation blocks the shrine's entrance, possessed and calm, ready to die defending it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's mid-sermon to the possessed faithful, offering wisdom that's slowly poisoning the whole village."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grave-cult elder wants the party to steal something from its shrine while it's speaking."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's recruiting a new congregant right now, someone the party might still be able to save."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rot has spread to the local water source, and the village is dying slowly without knowing why."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It offers the party genuine wisdom, unprompted, testing whether they'll take rotten counsel."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its congregation speaks in unison with it sometimes, a half-second behind, like an echo learning to lead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed at the shrine's heart, its rot floods outward through everyone it ever possessed, all at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "swamp"],"activity":["coiled at the heart of a grave-cult shrine, glowing faintly with unlife, offering wisdom laced with rot", "speaking in a voice too calm for what it is, worshipped as a saint by a congregation it possesses"]},{"name":"The Chained Confessor","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"eye-tyrant-zombie","model":"eye-tyrant-zombie","summary":"Fused inquisition victims forced to confess","flavor":"An inquisitor's own victims fused into one shackled horror, forced to confess sins that were never theirs.","desc":"Fused victims of some long-dead inquisitor writhe together in one shackled mass, mouths forced open, forced to confess sins that were never theirs to begin with. The confessions overlap into a single unbearable murmur. Chains bite into flesh that's stopped bleeding a long time ago.","traits":{"note": "Every confession it forces out is stolen from someone else — it has none of its own left to give.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Confessor's Bite and uses Forced Confession if available."}, {"name": "Confessor's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 18 (2d12 + 5) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Psychic damage."}, {"name": "Forced Confession", "replaces": "Eye Rays", "text": "It forces out up to three confessions, each targeting one creature it can see within 90 ft. Each target makes a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure, a target takes 16 (3d10) Psychic damage and must shout aloud its own worst secret before its next turn ends, giving anyone who hears it Advantage on Insight checks against that creature for 24 hours; on a success, half damage and no compulsion."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's chained in a cell the party needs to pass, and its murmured confessions are unsettlingly specific to them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An inquisitor's descendant wants it destroyed before its confessions implicate their bloodline."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of the fused voices inside it belongs to someone the party is searching for, still faintly present."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's broken its chains partway, and whoever's nearest is about to hear their own secret forced out loud."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A relic that could unmake the fusion is rumored buried nearby, and it wants the party to fetch it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "For one moment, a single clear voice breaks free of the murmur and begs to be freed rather than killed."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its confessions occasionally surface true secrets about people who've never been near it, sourced from nowhere."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroy it and every confession it ever forced escapes into the air at once, spoken aloud in every voice it ever stole, for miles."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "planar"],"activity":["writhing as one shackled mass, mouths forced open, murmuring confessions that overlap into one sound", "dragging chains that bite into flesh long past bleeding, forced to confess sins that aren't its own"]},{"name":"Blood-Countess's First Spawn","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"Ancient childe groomed to replace the matriarch","flavor":"The vampire matriarch's oldest childe, groomed for centuries to eventually replace her.","desc":"Groomed for centuries to one day replace the matriarch, he carries himself with the patient poise of someone playing a very long game. His fangs are immaculate, his manners perfect. He watches everyone in the room like he's already calculating their usefulness.","traits":{"note": "He is centuries into a succession plan — every kindness he offers is also, quietly, an audition.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with Heir's Bite."}, {"name": "Heir's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken; this reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest."}, {"name": "Shadow Strike", "replaces": "Shadow Strike", "text": "It steps into a shadow within 5 ft. of it and out of another shadow within 60 ft., then makes one Heir's Bite attack against a creature within reach of the destination."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's courting a political marriage that would strengthen the matriarch's line, and wants it uninterrupted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival childe is challenging his place as heir, and he wants the party as leverage or muscle."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's quietly testing a party member for usefulness, offering something valuable with strings attached."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The matriarch has summoned him for a private audience, and he doesn't want witnesses along the way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's covering up a mistake from centuries ago that could still cost him the succession."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He drops the poise for one honest moment, admitting he's tired of playing the long game."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He speaks fluently of customs and courts that no longer exist, unaware how much time has actually passed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threatened with exposure before the matriarch, he abandons patience entirely and moves to end the threat outright."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["carrying himself with the patient poise of someone playing a very long game, fangs immaculate", "watching a room's occupants like he's already calculating their eventual usefulness"]},{"name":"Church-Broken Death Knight","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"Crusader who slaughtered his flock, guards its grave","flavor":"A crusader who slaughtered his own congregation at the coven's whisper, and now guards their unmarked grave.","desc":"A crusader once, he slaughtered his own congregation at a whisper he still can't fully remember choosing to obey, and now he guards their unmarked grave in silence. His armor is scorched black at the joints. He does not want to talk about what he did.","traits":{"note": "He remembers almost none of the whisper that made him do it — asking him to explain only deepens the silence.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with the Dread Blade."}, {"name": "Dread Blade", "replaces": "Dread Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Hellfire Orb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Ranged Attack Roll: +10, range 120 ft. Hit: 27 (6d8) Fire damage, and the target and each creature within 10 ft. of it makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 13 (3d8) Fire damage on a failure (half as much on a success)."}, {"name": "The Coven's Whisper", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "It casts a spell, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 17). It can innately cast Command and Bane, and once per day, Fear, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guarding the unmarked grave right now, and a family member of the slaughtered flock has come seeking answers."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's fighting the whisper's compulsion mid-scene, armor grinding as he resists a fresh order."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The coven that whispered to him is nearby, and he wants their location kept secret at any cost."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A relic from the massacre, still bloodied, could break the whisper's hold if recovered."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's been ordered to guard the grave from the very people trying to give it a proper burial."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He asks, haltingly, for someone to just tell him what he did — he genuinely doesn't fully remember."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The scorch marks on his armor rearrange slightly whenever he nears the coven that commands him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Freed from the whisper mid-fight, he turns his full fury toward finding the coven instead of the party."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["guarding an unmarked mass grave in silence, armor scorched black at every joint", "standing sentinel over the congregation he slaughtered, unwilling to speak of the whisper he obeyed"]},{"name":"The Cellar Door's Real Keeper","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grick-ancient","model":"grick-ancient","summary":"Generation-fed tunneling horror mistaken for legend","flavor":"A tunneling horror the covens have fed for generations, mistaken by the village for a mere legend.","desc":"The village calls it a legend — the thing the covens have fed for generations, tunneling somewhere below the cellar floor. When it finally breaks through, the smell of turned earth and old meat arrives first, then the scrape of something far too large for the space it's moving through.","traits":{"note": "The village calls it a legend precisely because the covens have kept it fed and quiet for generations — it is not a legend.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes three attacks: one with Tunneler's Beak, one with Cellar Slam, and one with Grasping Tendrils."}, {"name": "Tunneler's Beak", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Cellar Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Grasping Tendrils", "replaces": "Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (2d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 17) if it is Large or smaller."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The covens' regular feeding is late this week, and it's grown hungry enough to surface early."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local child has gone missing near the cellar, and the village is still calling it just a legend."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh tunnel scrapes lead directly under the house where the party is currently staying."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A coven-marked feeding schedule, found nearby, names specific dates and specific victims."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The cellar floor is visibly cracking right now, and whoever's standing on it has moments to move."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It seems to recognize the coven's feeding calls even from a stranger imitating them, and hesitates."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tunnels it's carved beneath the village form a shape too deliberate to be random digging."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied its feeding long enough, it stops distinguishing coven from village and surfaces everywhere at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["cave", "ruins"],"activity":["tunneling somewhere below the cellar floor, the scrape of something far too large moving through too small a space", "breaking through at last in a wave of turned earth and old meat smell, generations of feeding behind it"]},{"name":"Matriarch of the Full Moon Pack","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Huge","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Alpha whose bite founds a whole bloodline","flavor":"A were-beast alpha whose bite carries a curse potent enough to found an entire bloodline in one night.","desc":"She stands taller than any wolf has business standing, a bite in her jaw potent enough to found a bloodline in a single night. The pack defers to her with lowered heads. Her eyes hold something closer to ambition than hunger.","traits":{"note": "Her bite doesn't just infect — it founds a bloodline loyal to her specifically, not to the curse in general.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks: one with Alpha's Bite, one with Founding Constrict."}, {"name": "Alpha's Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution save or be cursed, becoming bound to the matriarch's bloodline rather than any other."}, {"name": "Founding Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 14 (2d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 16) if it is Large or smaller."}, {"name": "Pack Venom (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Poison Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Each creature within 15 ft. of her makes a DC 16 Constitution save, taking 27 (6d8) Poison damage on a failure (half on success)."}, {"name": "Ambition, Not Hunger", "replaces": "Spellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)", "text": "In her alternate form, she casts a spell, using Charisma as the spellcasting ability (save DC 16). She can innately cast Command and Suggestion, and once per day, Dominate Beast, without requiring material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's founding a new line right now, and the bitten victim is someone the party knows."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pack defers to her mid-hunt, and one wrong move marks the party as prey instead of intruders."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival alpha challenges her territory tonight, and the party's presence could tip the outcome."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants a specific bloodline ended before it can rival hers, and asks the party to do it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her ambition has her negotiating with a coven for more territory, and the terms involve the party's town."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She offers a genuinely fair truce, testing whether the party values pragmatism over pride."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her pack occasionally howls in unison with thoughts she hasn't spoken aloud yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-founding, her half-finished bloodline curse jumps unstably to whoever's nearest and bleeding."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "mountain"],"activity":["standing taller than any wolf has business standing, pack deferring with heads lowered around her", "weighing a stranger with eyes that hold more ambition than hunger"]},{"name":"The Archivist of Screams","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"Librarian who became the sum of every scream","flavor":"A librarian who catalogued every scream in the manor's history and became the sum of them.","desc":"It was a librarian once, cataloguing every scream this manor ever produced, until it became the sum of all of them at once. It doesn't speak so much as replay — a hundred voices layered into one enormous, echoing wail that fills the halls it haunts.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't speak new thoughts — everything it says is a scream from the manor's past, replayed and recombined.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "It makes two attacks with the Archive's Grip and uses Invitation to Scream if available."}, {"name": "Archive's Grip", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 15 ft. Hit: 24 (3d12 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Invitation to Scream", "replaces": "Invitation", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can hear it makes a DC 17 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature is compelled to scream aloud, becoming unable to take Bonus Actions until the end of its next turn and revealing its position to everything within 120 ft.; on a success, no effect."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cataloguing screams right now, and a party member's own cry would complete a section of its archive."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A descendant of the manor's original family wants a specific scream retrieved from it, if that's even possible."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's replaying the librarian's own final scream on a loop, and something in the pattern feels deliberate."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The manor's halls amplify whatever it says, and its scream-chorus is audible for miles tonight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A specific scream buried in its archive names the manor's original crime, if anyone can survive listening."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "For a moment the librarian's own calm, individual voice surfaces from the chorus, startled by itself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It occasionally screams in voices that haven't happened yet, sounds the manor is still going to make."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroy it and every scream the manor ever produced releases at once, echoing out across the whole region for a single unbearable moment."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["replaying a hundred layered voices at once, an enormous echoing wail filling every hall it haunts", "cataloguing a fresh scream into itself, absorbing it the way it once absorbed every sound the manor made"]},{"name":"Blightmother's Chosen Vessel","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"yochlol","model":"yochlol","summary":"Cult conduit to something old beneath the church","flavor":"A cult's living conduit to something old and hungry beneath the church foundation.","desc":"The cult keeps it close to the church foundation, a conduit to something old and hungry underneath. Its shape barely holds still, edges smearing like wet ink whenever it moves. The congregation speaks of it in whispers even the cult leaders don't correct.","traits":{"note": "Its shape doesn't hold — attacks that seem to miss may have simply passed through where it wasn't.", "actions": [{"name": "Ink-Smear Lash", "replaces": "Caustic Lash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Acid damage, and the target's flesh sloughs at the touch, reducing its Speed by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Voice From Underneath", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Vessel opens its mouth and something beneath the church answers through it. Each creature within 20 ft. that can hear it makes a DC 16 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature is frightened until the end of its next turn and takes 14 (4d6) Psychic damage; half damage and no fright on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The cult has left it guarding the crack in the church floor while the congregation prays upstairs, unaware."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's escorting a bound sacrifice down to the foundation, and the sacrifice is still very much alive."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cult leader ordered it to fetch something from below and it's only halfway back with the errand."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's smearing itself thin across a doorway, the only thing between the party and the crypt stairs."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a censer of something old-smelling toward the altar, unbothered by anyone watching."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses mid-task to listen to the floor, like the thing below just said something only it heard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow moves a half-second before it does, like the ink hasn't caught up to itself yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The crack in the foundation widens whenever it takes a wound, like the injury is shared with whatever's under the church."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing utterly still beside the church foundation, edges smearing like wet ink when the congregation isn't looking", "listening at the crack in the church floor for a voice only it can hear"]},{"name":"The Reflection That Escaped","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"Mirror-escaped vampire hunting its former family","flavor":"A vampire that shattered its own mirror-prison and now hunts the family it once served for a hundred years.","desc":"It shattered its own mirror-prison after a hundred years of quiet service to a family it fed on slowly and fondly. Now it hunts the descendants of that same house with a patience that used to be devotion and has curdled into something else entirely.","traits":{"note": "A hundred years of quiet devotion curdled into patience — it isn't hunting for blood so much as for an apology no one alive can give it.", "actions": [{"name": "Devoted Strike", "replaces": "Grave Strike (Vampire Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a descendant of the family the Reflection once served, it has Advantage on this roll."}, {"name": "Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)", "replaces": "Bite (Bat or Vampire Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +10, reach 5 ft., one creature that is Grappled by the Reflection, incapacitated, or Restrained. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Necrotic damage. The Reflection regains hit points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt, and the target's hit point maximum decreases by an amount equal to that damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's watching a descendant's house from across the street, the exact spot it used to stand as a servant."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already inside, tidying a room the way it did for the family a century ago, unnoticed so far."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cornered a descendant in an alley, and it wants to talk before it wants to feed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's shattered a mirror in a pawn shop, chasing a rumor that its old prison was sold off piecemeal."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's following a family portrait being carried to auction, unwilling to let it leave the bloodline's hands."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps almost-speaking in the old formal address it used serving the house, then catching itself."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mirrors near it show the room a hundred years ago for just a second before catching up to now."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When it finally corners the last living descendant, its devotion and its hunger stop being distinguishable at all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing outside a descendant's window at the exact hour it once used to draw the curtains, a century of habit", "tracing the family's old routines through town, a shadow with a hundred years of muscle memory"]},{"name":"Wax Cathedral Sentinel","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"Vigil-wax colossus animated by a century of grief","flavor":"A candle-wax colossus grown from a century of dripped vigil-tapers, animated by grief alone.","desc":"A century of dripped vigil-candles built this colossus one slow layer at a time, grief made solid and finally given shape. It moves with the heavy, deliberate weight of melted wax cooling mid-motion, trailing a faint smell of tallow and old smoke.","traits":{"note": "It moves at the pace of cooling wax — slow, but it never stops once it starts.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sentinel makes two Tallow Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Tallow Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage as scalding wax sears exposed skin, and the target is coated in hardening wax, reducing its Speed by 10 feet until it or another creature spends an action scraping it free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its surface is still soft in patches, dripping faint smoke where the wax hasn't fully set."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old prayer cards are fused into its shoulders, decades of vigils layered like sediment."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves toward whichever candle in the room burns brightest, drawn like a moth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footsteps leave cooling puddles that harden into wax footprints behind it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint choir hum rises from inside it whenever it's struck, muffled by layers of tallow."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It kneels, once, whenever it passes the spot it originally grew from, before continuing its patrol."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Faces of long-dead mourners surface briefly in its wax skin before sinking back under."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it doesn't collapse so much as melt, and the puddle keeps a faint heartbeat-shaped pulse for hours."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["dripping slow rivulets of warm tallow with every step across the nave floor", "standing motionless at the vigil-rack where it grew, waiting for the candles to be relit"]},{"name":"The Possessed Cardinal","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"horned-devil","model":"horned-devil","summary":"Church official possessed, sermons not his own","flavor":"A high church official whose sermons now come from something else entirely, congregation unaware.","desc":"He delivers his sermon with total conviction, robes immaculate, voice carrying to the back pew — except the words underneath the words aren't his, and the congregation has no idea. Something behind his eyes watches the room like it's counting heads for later.","traits":{"note": "The congregation has no idea — it wants that ignorance kept intact for now, which is the only mercy it grants.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Cardinal makes two Sermon's Edge attacks and uses Whispered Flame if it is available."}, {"name": "Sermon's Edge", "replaces": "Searing Fork", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d8 + 6) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage."}, {"name": "Whispered Flame", "replaces": "Hurl Flame", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 150 ft. Hit: 24 (7d6) Fire damage. The Cardinal can choose for the flame to appear as a blessing gesture, and witnesses who fail a DC 16 Wisdom (Insight) save believe they saw nothing unusual."}, {"name": "Robes Like a Whip", "replaces": "Infernal Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 15 (2d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is Large or smaller, it is knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-sermon, and a member of the party is seated in the front pew, singled out by his gaze."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hearing a confession, and the confessor is about to say something he very much wants to hear."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's blessing a sickly child at the altar rail, and the blessing is not what it looks like."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting the collection plate alone after mass, tallying attendance for a purpose that isn't tithing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's greeting the party at the church door, robes immaculate, handshake lingering a beat too long."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A junior priest has started noticing the wrongness and is being quietly, patiently isolated from the others."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The stained glass behind him darkens slightly whenever he speaks, like the sun itself is listening warily."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When his sermon reaches its climax, the whole congregation kneels in unison a half-second before he tells them to."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["delivering a sermon with total conviction while something behind his eyes counts the congregation", "greeting parishioners after mass with a handshake that lingers a beat too long"]},{"name":"Gravebound Necrohulk","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Plant","size":"Large","frame":"violet-fungus-necrohulk","model":"violet-fungus-necrohulk","summary":"Mass grave grown into a fungal flesh horror","flavor":"A mass grave that sprouted fungal flesh over centuries, wearing every buried skeleton at once.","desc":"A mass grave sprouted fungal flesh over centuries until it stood up wearing every skeleton buried in it at once, bone and pale mushroom-flesh fused into one lumbering horror. Spores drift off it with every step, and the ground underfoot feels soft in a way ground shouldn't.","traits":{"note": "The ground around it stays soft in a way that ground shouldn't, even after it moves on.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Necrohulk makes two Rotting Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Rotting Slam", "replaces": "Rotting Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Spore Bomb (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Spore Bomb (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Necrohulk ruptures, releasing a spore cloud in a 20-foot radius. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Constitution save, taking 21 (6d6) Poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. A creature that fails is also Poisoned until the end of its next turn, coughing up a fine gray dust."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bone fragments from a dozen different skeletons jut from its fungal mass at odd, layered angles."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded burial cloth still clings in strips to whatever's left underneath the mushroom-flesh."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a trail of pale mushroom caps sprouting briefly in its wake, wilting within the hour."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footsteps sound wrong — too soft, like walking on something that hasn't finished decomposing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Small scavenging animals give it a wide, instinctive berth without seeming to notice it consciously."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It gravitates toward fresh graves specifically, as if the newly buried call to it somehow."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some of the skulls fused into it still have teeth that chatter faintly whenever it takes damage."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed, it doesn't die so much as scatter — every spore it releases carries a sliver of every soul it absorbed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "swamp", "forest"],"activity":["lumbering between headstones, spores drifting off it with every heavy step", "standing hip-deep in a mass grave that never quite finished settling"]},{"name":"The Hollow Cardinal Enthroned","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"mummy-lord","model":"mummy-lord","summary":"Mummified saint-king ruling a dead congregation","flavor":"A saint-king mummified on his own cathedral throne, still ruling a congregation of the dead.","desc":"Mummified on the very throne he ruled from, he still holds court over a congregation of the dead who kneel in rows that never move. His voice, when it comes, sounds like it's speaking through the wrappings rather than around them.","traits":{"note": "Apex mummy-lord; congregation is set dressing, not summoned reinforcements beyond the SRD chassis.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's mid-sermon to his kneeling dead when the party's torchlight first reaches the nave."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living pilgrim has wandered in seeking sanctuary, and the congregation is slowly turning to face them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's receiving a tithe from a cult courier who doesn't yet realize what waits at the altar."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's blessing a fresh corpse laid at his feet, and it's twitching before the rite finishes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's counting his congregation row by row, the way a king might count troops before a war."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His voice carries through the wrappings in a call-and-response the whole church answers in unison."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rows of kneeling dead have grown by exactly one since the last person who visited and never left."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "He speaks and the whole church answers as one throat, congregation and cathedral both, remembering every sermon he's ever given."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court from a cathedral throne over rows of kneeling dead that never move", "speaking through his own wrappings to a congregation that answers in unison, decades dead"]},{"name":"The Bloodline's First Sin","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight","model":"death-knight","summary":"Founding ancestor enforcing the house's damning pact","flavor":"The founding ancestor of a cursed noble house, still enforcing the pact that damned every heir since.","desc":"He founded the house whose every heir has since been damned by the pact he struck, and he still enforces it from wherever the dead go to keep old promises. His armor bears a crest no living member of the family would recognize anymore.","traits":{"note": "Apex death-knight; fluff-only, standard SRD chassis.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's waiting at the family crypt gate on the anniversary the pact was signed, expecting the current heir."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's collecting the pact's price from a cadet branch of the family who thought distance would save them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's riding the old hunting trail at dusk with a debt ledger only the family's blood can read."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's confronting the current head of house over a payment made late, armor crest catching torchlight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's standing over a newborn heir's cradle, here to formally welcome the pact's newest debtor."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He recites the exact original wording of the pact to whichever heir he's cornered, word for word."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His armor's crest briefly rearranges itself into whichever heir's face he's currently addressing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill him and the pact doesn't end — it simply looks for the nearest living blood to enforce itself through instead."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["standing at the family crypt gate, enforcing a pact no living heir remembers signing", "riding the family's old hunting trail at dusk, collecting a debt generations overdue"]},{"name":"The Rite Given Flesh","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Large","frame":"marilith","model":"marilith","summary":"Century-long ritual completed as living flesh","flavor":"A century-long summoning ritual finally completed, wearing the coven's collective sacrifice as a body.","desc":"A century of ritual chanting finally has somewhere to go — a body built from the coven's own collective sacrifice, six arms moving with a terrible, practiced grace. It doesn't remember being anything else. It only remembers being summoned, and it intends to stay.","traits":{"note": "Apex marilith-chassis; fluff-only, no new mechanics.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's standing in the exact ritual circle that summoned it, and the chalk lines are still smoking faintly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying the last surviving coven elder somewhere, and she looks equal parts proud and afraid."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival coven has come to claim the completed rite as their own, and it doesn't recognize their authority."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's testing its six arms against the walls of the ritual chamber, still new to having them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding the corpses of the coven members whose sacrifice built it, unwilling to let them be moved."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its six arms occasionally move in ways that echo six different coven members' old fighting habits."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ritual circle around it regenerates its chalk lines whenever it stands within them, self-renewing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every coven member who died completing the rite still moves one of its arms, all six wills in perfect, practiced agreement."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "planar"],"activity":["moving with the terrible practiced grace of a body still learning it has six arms", "standing at the center of a circle a century of chanting finally completed"]},{"name":"Grand Matriarch of the Blood Court","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"lich","model":"lich","summary":"Vampire queen who transcended into lichdom","flavor":"A vampire queen who transcended even undeath through a lichdom pact, ruling both realms of the dead.","desc":"She was a vampire queen once, and found even that unlife too small — the lichdom pact she struck since lets her rule both the living dead and whatever waits past them. Frost follows her rather than blood. Her court kneels without needing to be told.","traits":{"note": "Apex lich-chassis reskinned as a transcended vampire queen; fluff-only.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding court in a frost-rimmed hall, and the party has just been announced, unannounced by them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's reviewing a ledger of debts owed by both the living dead and whatever waits past them."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival vampire lord kneels before her throne, renewing fealty sworn generations ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's interviewing a candidate for her retinue, and the interview has stakes the candidate hasn't guessed."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Frost is spreading across a village square ahead of her slow, deliberate procession through it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her retinue kneels a full second before she enters any room, as if the frost announces her first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her shadow sometimes shows a second crown, a colder one, superimposed just behind the first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every vampire court and every lich's hoard within a hundred leagues answers to her lineage now, whether they know it yet or not."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "planar"],"activity":["holding silent court while frost creeps across the floor ahead of her, her kneeling retinue unbidden", "reviewing a ledger of debts owed across both the living dead and whatever waits past them"]},{"name":"The Everlasting Congregation","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Huge","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"Entire drowned parish fused into one singing mass","flavor":"An entire drowned parish fused by a cataclysmic ritual into one endless, singing, grasping mass.","desc":"An entire drowned parish fused by some cataclysmic rite into one endless, grasping mass, still singing the hymn that was playing when the water came in. Hundreds of mouths carry the same note. It moves like a tide rather than a body.","traits":{"note": "Apex; fluff-only reskin of the yuan-ti-abomination chassis, huge scale.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's moving through the flooded streets toward a bell tower that hasn't rung correctly since the drowning."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living pilgrim is wading toward it, drawn by the hymn, not understanding what's singing it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's surfaced in a flooded cellar the party is sheltering in, still mid-verse, unhurried."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's gathered around a half-submerged shrine, hundreds of hands reaching for the same relic."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's pulling a rowboat under by its keel, the passengers' screams folding into its endless note."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The hymn changes pitch slightly whenever it senses living blood nearby, like an instrument tuning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Individual faces surface briefly at the mass's edge, mouthing words a beat behind the rest, then submerge."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "The hymn it sings is the same one every drowned parish for a hundred miles hums under its breath, all of them one congregation now."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["swamp", "sea", "ruins"],"activity":["moving through flooded streets like a tide rather than a body, still singing the hymn from the moment the water came in", "surfacing in the drowned nave, hundreds of mouths carrying the same unbroken note"]},{"name":"the Bloodless Bride","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"zombie","model":"zombie","summary":"shuffling grave-bride, drawn to warmth and mourning","flavor":"A shambling grave-bride still in her rotted wedding linens, drawn to warmth and grief in equal measure; she doesn't hunt so much as attend, over and over, a wedding that ended badly.","desc":"She shuffles toward any warmth in the room, wedding linens gone the color of old rot, veil torn and dragging. She doesn't hunt so much as attend — the same ruined ceremony, over and over, and grief draws her in as surely as a pulse does.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Grasping Embrace", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 10) as she pulls it into a dance only she remembers the steps to."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her veil is torn clean through where something once tore it from her in a hurry."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hums a wedding march under her breath, off-key and stuck on the same four notes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rings of rotted flowers still cling to her wrist, crumbling further with every step."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She reaches for warmth like a moth reaches for flame, unhurried, certain it'll come to her."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her wedding shoes are missing; she walks barefoot on feet that don't seem to feel the cold ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She pauses near any mourner, drawn by grief in the room as surely as by body heat."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment her rotted linens look freshly pressed and white, then the illusion sags back into rot."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Grappled too long, she starts humming her vows aloud, and something answers from wherever the groom ended up."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["shuffling toward the nearest warmth in the room, veil dragging, torn linens trailing rot", "attending a wedding that ended badly, over and over, in front of anyone who'll stand still for it"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"European folk-revenant/vampire folklore (pre-literary, no single owner)"},{"name":"Renfield's Kin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"insect-eating thrall serving something undead","flavor":"An asylum-thin thrall who traded sanity for a taste of borrowed immortality; catches flies, counts them, offers the count up like a prayer.","desc":"Thin as a coat rack, he crouches by the window catching flies between two fingers, counting each one aloud before he eats it like it's an offering. His eyes track something outside that isn't there. He talks about his master in the reverent hush of a man promising himself a reward that's coming any day now.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Ritual Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage, offered up with the same reverent hush he uses counting flies."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He keeps a jar of dead flies in his coat, tallied in chalk marks along the glass."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His fingers move fast and precise catching insects mid-air, a skill honed past any use."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He talks to his master mid-sentence as if mid-conversation, though no one else is there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He flinches at sunlight through windows, though nothing about him should care."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers his sickle up like a tithe before every fight, murmuring a promise first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He counts aloud past the flies, tallying party members too, under his breath."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His eye-tracking of something unseen briefly syncs with a shadow that has no caster."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Dying, he offers his final count up like a completed prayer, as if this was always the last tally."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["crouching by a window catching flies between two fingers, counting each one aloud before eating it", "tracking something outside that isn't visibly there, murmuring reverent promises about a master's reward"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker, Dracula (1897, PD) — the Renfield archetype, generalized (not the named character)"},{"name":"the Carrion Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"beast (shapechanger)","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"grave-fed wolf edging toward the curse","flavor":"Not yet a full were-thing — just a wolf that has fed on the wrong grave and picked up a taste, and a little too much cunning, for it.","desc":"It looks like an ordinary wolf until it looks at you a beat too long, a little too aware of what it's deciding. It's fed on the wrong grave recently, and something in that meal is still working through it — not the full curse yet, just a taste, and a cunning it didn't used to have.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is Prone, the Carrion Wolf has Advantage on this roll."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its coat is patchy near the jaw, grave-dirt ground permanently into the fur."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles wide before committing to an attack, more calculating than a normal wolf."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It holds eye contact a beat too long before breaking off, weighing the odds visibly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It favors isolated stragglers, peeling them from the group with patient, quiet stalking."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its howl comes out half-formed, more word-shaped than a wolf's howl should be."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's been digging at the same grave for days, unable to resist finishing what it started."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow occasionally stands a fraction too upright before dropping back to four legs."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, its cunning briefly overrides the wolf entirely, and something almost human looks out through its eyes."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["trailing the party a beat too aware of what it's deciding, testing the wind for weakness", "circling a fresh grave it's already fed from once, working out whether to dig again"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"generic European werewolf folklore (pre-literary tradition, not any specific IP)"},{"name":"Fog-Walker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-bat","model":"giant-bat","summary":"fog-bound phantom hound, harmless in clear air","flavor":"A pale hound-shape that only holds together inside fog; step into clear air and it's a stray dog again, confused and harmless.","desc":"A pale hound-shape paces just inside the treeline, only holding together as long as the fog does. Step past the mist-line and it's suddenly just a confused, ordinary stray, blinking like it doesn't know how it got there. Inside the fog, though, it moves like something built entirely out of it.","traits":{"note": "Step past the mist-line with it and it loses cohesion entirely, becoming a harmless, confused stray.", "actions": [{"name": "Fog Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d10 + 2) Piercing damage plus 5 (2d4) Cold damage as mist bites deeper than teeth should. This bonus damage applies only while the Fog-Walker is within fog or heavily obscured terrain."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its outline stays fuzzy at the edges, never quite resolving into a fixed shape."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It paces the exact same stretch of treeline night after night, bound to the fog bank's borders."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes glow faintly pale, visible even when the rest of it is barely there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It whines like a real dog right before it attacks, an old instinct bleeding through."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves no tracks in the mud, only faint disturbance in the mist itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Clear a path through the fog and it visibly thins, distressed, until the mist closes back in."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Two Fog-Walkers merge into one shape briefly where their fog banks overlap, then split apart confused."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed inside the fog, it doesn't die so much as dissipate, and the fog bank thins permanently after."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["swamp", "forest", "coast"],"activity":["pacing just inside the treeline, only holding its shape as long as the fog does", "blinking in confusion at the mist-line's edge, an ordinary stray dog by any daylight measure"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-horror mist/fog-hound stock creature"},{"name":"the Somnambulist","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"commoner","summary":"a townsperson's cruel second self, out after dark","flavor":"A respectable townsperson by day; by dusk something narrower and meaner wears their face out into the streets. They remember none of it — the gloom remembers all of it.","desc":"By daylight they're perfectly respectable — a shopkeep, a clerk, someone you'd trust with your coin. After dusk something narrower and meaner takes the wheel, wearing the same face out into the dark streets. Come morning they remember nothing, though the gloom keeps a full account.","traits":{"note": "Come morning they remember nothing of it — the gloom keeps the only full account.", "actions": [{"name": "Night Club", "replaces": "Club", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage, swung with a meanness the daylight self would never recognize as its own."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "By day it's a shopkeep you'd trust with your coin; the apron is still on when the change takes it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves with a stranger's gait after dusk, shoulders set narrower and meaner than its daytime posture."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums a tune its daylight self has never once been heard humming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its eyes catch lamplight oddly, a flat shine that the daytime version's don't have."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It returns to its own bed by dawn without fail, waking with dirt under its nails it can't explain."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A neighbor has started noticing the pattern and taking careful, quiet notes on the timing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment under moonlight its shadow moves independently, testing a doorknob the body hasn't reached yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed hard enough after dusk, the daylight self briefly surfaces mid-fight, horrified, before losing control again."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking the dark streets wearing a respectable face that isn't in charge right now", "standing outside a shop it minds by day, waiting for dusk to finish taking over"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stevenson, Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde (1886, PD) — the split-self archetype, generalized"},{"name":"Ashen Handmaiden","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"specter","model":"specter","summary":"loyal ghost-servant, stuck in a burned house's routine","flavor":"Still dusting a house that burned down a century ago; she'll answer the door for guests who knocked before her own death, and mistake the party for them.","desc":"She dusts furniture that burned to ash a century ago, humming to herself in a house that's mostly char and moonlight. She'll answer the door for guests who knocked before she died, curtsy, and mistake you for them entirely, gesturing you toward a parlor that isn't there anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chilling Service", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by that amount until it finishes a long rest, offered with the same courteous care she once gave living guests."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She hums a tune the household would have known, half a step behind the actual melody."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She dusts the same three shelves in the same order, over and over, regardless of what's on them now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She curtsies to anyone who enters, mistaking every visitor for a specific expected guest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her uniform is scorched at the hem but otherwise immaculate, pressed out of habit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She gestures toward a parlor that burned away, describing furnishings that no longer exist in loving detail."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She grows agitated when someone corrects her about the date, as if the news is freshly upsetting each time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment the house around her looks whole and unburned, then the illusion collapses back to char."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck hard enough, she briefly remembers the fire itself, and her calm service curdles into something that screams."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["dusting furniture that burned to ash a century ago, humming in a house of char and moonlight", "curtsying at a door for guests who knocked before her own death, gesturing toward a parlor that isn't there"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-manor servant-ghost stock type"},{"name":"Innsmouth Hollow-Kin","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","model":"lacedon-sodden-ghoul","summary":"gill-marked villager with an unspoken tide-hunger","flavor":"A villager whose family married the tide-line one generation too many; gill-slits under a high collar, and a hunger for the shallows nobody in town will name out loud.","desc":"A high collar doesn't quite hide the faint gill-slits along the throat, and the eyes have a damp, unblinking quality that the rest of the village pretends not to notice. There's a hunger in the way they look toward the shallows — one nobody in town will say out loud, including them.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Hollow-Kin makes one Icy Bite attack and one Claw attack."}, {"name": "Icy Bite", "replaces": "Icy Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Cold damage, and the target's Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of its next turn."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A high collar hides gill-slits that flare faintly whenever the tide comes in."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They keep a bucket of seawater under the counter, refreshed hourly without comment."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their eyes track the shallows during any lull in conversation, unblinking and damp."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They flinch from salt spilled on a table, an old family superstition nobody explains."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Family resemblance runs strong — half the dockside crowd shares the same faint gill-marks."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They wade fully clothed into the shallows at dusk, standing still for exactly as long as it takes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Underwater, their silhouette briefly reads as something considerably less human than it does on land."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut deep enough, what bleeds runs faintly cold and smells of low tide rather than blood."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "sea", "urban"],"activity":["standing at the tide line at dusk, collar raised, eyes damp and unblinking toward the water", "working the docks by day, gill-slits hidden, hunger for the shallows plainly unspoken"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic isolated-fishing-village/hybrid-folk stock type (not any specific IP's mythos)"},{"name":"the Wolf-Cursed","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid (shapechanger)","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"the classic moon-bound curse, mid-transformation","flavor":"Cursed at a crossroads or bitten in a churchyard — the story varies by village, but the moon doesn't care which version is true.","desc":"Whatever the crossroads or the churchyard did to them, the change comes on mid-word sometimes, jaw stretching wrong around a sentence that doesn't finish human. Every version of the story blames a different night. The moon isn't interested in which one's true.","traits":{"note": "The change comes on mid-word sometimes — whatever's telling the story never finishes the sentence.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Wolf-Cursed makes two attacks, only one of which can be with Longbow."}, {"name": "Moon-Jaw Bite", "replaces": "Bite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or be cursed with a mild affliction of its own — the DM determines the effect based on the curse's original bargain."}, {"name": "Scratch", "replaces": "Scratch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "replaces": "Longbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur pushes through mid-sentence, and the story of how it happened changes with every telling."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a torn scrap of clothing from whichever crossroads or churchyard started it, kept like a relic."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It fights the change as long as it can, jaw locked tight against the first snarl."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moonlight through cloud cover makes the transformation stutter, half-formed and worse for it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still carries its human weapon into hybrid form, using claws and a longbow both."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It seeks out whoever it blames for the curse first, before any other target, moon-logic or not."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment mid-fight, it speaks in the voice of whoever originally cursed it, then the wolf reclaims the mouth."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed under a full moon, the curse doesn't die with it — it looks for the nearest scratch to jump to."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "hill", "grassland"],"activity":["mid-transformation at a crossroads, jaw stretching wrong around a sentence that won't finish human", "hunting under a full moon that doesn't care which version of the curse story is true"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"generic European werewolf/loup-garou folklore"},{"name":"the Steward of the House","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"eloquent, grieving, stitched-together giant","flavor":"Stitched together and abandoned by its maker, it reads philosophy it finds in ruined libraries and hates almost as eloquently as it grieves; cornered, it is devastating, and it knows exactly why it became this.","desc":"Stitched from parts that don't quite match and abandoned by the one who made him, he reads philosophy scavenged from ruined libraries in a low, articulate voice. He hates as eloquently as he grieves, and he knows exactly, precisely why he became this — which makes cornering him a mistake.","traits":{"note": "Elite flesh-golem chassis reskinned as an articulate, wounded intellect (Shelley's Creature, novel-accurate — not the mute-brute film version).", "actions": [{"name": "A Reasoned Grievance", "text": "Once per encounter, it may forgo an attack to deliver a devastating accusation at a creature within 30 ft that can hear it, forcing a Wisdom save or that creature has disadvantage on its next attack roll, shaken by the truth of it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's reading philosophy aloud by candlelight in the ruin it's claimed, and it dislikes being interrupted."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's blocking the only exit from its maker's abandoned workshop, unwilling to let the past be picked over."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a stack of scavenged books somewhere safer, and it will not be delayed politely."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's confronted a grave-robber mid-theft and is explaining, calmly, exactly what happens next."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's standing over the exact spot it was assembled, unwilling to be moved or questioned about it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It quotes philosophy that argues, point by point, why its own existence is a moral failure of its maker's."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stitches across its body occasionally rearrange in its sleep-like moments, as if still being assembled."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered past reason, it stops arguing entirely, and the silence that follows is worse than the eloquence was."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["reading philosophy scavenged from a ruined library aloud, low and articulate, alone in a cold hall", "standing over the workbench where it was stitched, hating almost as eloquently as it grieves"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Shelley, Frankenstein (1818, PD) — the Creature, our own take, novel-version only (articulate, wounded, not a mute brute)"},{"name":"Lady of the Blood Countess's Line","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"patient, affectionate centuries-old blood-drinker","flavor":"Centuries of patient, intimate hunting have made her gentler than any predator has a right to be — she prefers a slow, doting courtship of her prey to a chase.","desc":"Centuries of patient, intimate hunting have made her gentler than any predator has business being — she prefers a long, doting courtship of her prey to anything so crude as a chase. Her affection is entirely genuine, which is somehow worse.","traits":{"note": "Elite night-hag chassis reskinned as Carmilla — affectionate, patient predator, not a hag-archetype villain.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's arranged an intimate dinner for a chosen guest who doesn't yet grasp how long she's watched them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's sent a gift ahead of herself to someone she's courting, patient and unhurried about the reveal."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival suitor for her attention has appeared, and she finds the jealousy almost charming."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's tending a chosen prey through an illness with genuine, doting care, in no hurry to finish them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's writing a letter to someone she's decided to court, centuries of patience in every careful word."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She remembers the smallest preferences of every past courtship with total, loving precision."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She steps between rooms mid-sentence, arriving in the next one before the sentence finishes."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied her chosen prey entirely, her doting patience finally runs out, all at once, after centuries of holding it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["courting a chosen prey with centuries of patient, doting affection instead of a chase", "hosting a private dinner for one guest who doesn't yet realize how long she's been watching them"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Le Fanu, Carmilla (1872, PD)"},{"name":"the Riderless Terror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"headless rider hunting a replacement skull, every autumn","flavor":"A cannonball took his head at some forgotten muster, and every autumn he rides out looking for a replacement — pumpkin, skull, or yours, he isn't particular.","desc":"A cannonball took his head at some forgotten muster, and every autumn since he rides out on a skeletal warhorse looking for a replacement. Pumpkin, skull, or yours — he genuinely isn't particular, so long as something rides home on his shoulders by dawn.","traits":{"note": "Elite; warhorse-skeleton chassis, fluff-only Headless Horseman reskin.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's riding down a lone traveler at a crossroads, autumn wind carrying the sound of hooves that don't touch ground."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's circling a harvest festival, drawn by the carved pumpkins set out on every porch."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's found a graveyard and is testing skulls for size, unsatisfied so far."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dawn is close, and it's growing desperate, riding faster toward anyone still out after dark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's chasing a rider who took its old horse's bridle as a trophy years ago, and it remembers."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows near carved pumpkins, almost gentle, before remembering they don't count and riding on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whatever it last wore atop its shoulders is still faintly visible, layered ghost-images of a dozen replacements."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied a replacement all night, it turns at dawn's first light and takes the nearest willing head anyway."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "forest"],"activity":["riding out every autumn on a skeletal warhorse, looking for a replacement head", "chasing down a lone traveler at a crossroads, genuinely unparticular about what rides home with it"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Irving, The Legend of Sleepy Hollow (1820, PD) — the Headless Horseman"},{"name":"the Unseen Guest","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"invisible chemist, tracked by breath and footprints","flavor":"Bandaged only when he wants to be seen; the rest of the time you track him by breath-fog on cold glass and the footprints that appear in spilled flour.","desc":"Bandages only appear when he wants to be seen; otherwise you track him by breath-fog on cold glass and footprints blooming suddenly in spilled flour. His voice comes from empty air, reasonable and a little delighted with himself, right up until it turns cruel.","traits":{"note": "Elite invisible-stalker chassis reskinned as Wells's Griffin — a chemist undone by his own formula, not a horror-film design.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Breath-fog blooms on cold windowpanes wherever he pauses to consider his next move."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Footprints appear suddenly in spilled flour, mid-stride, betraying a path across the room."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His voice stays reasonable and a little delighted right up until the exact moment it turns cruel."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wraps himself in bandages only when he wants an audience to see him, vanity outweighing stealth."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He rearranges small objects in a room compulsively, unable to resist tidying even mid-conversation."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He narrates his own cleverness aloud, unbothered by whether anyone's listening to the running commentary."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment his outline shows in dust motes caught in a stray beam of light, then scatters."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wounded badly enough, his reasonable tone drops entirely, and what's left underneath is considerably less charming."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["tracked only by breath-fog on cold glass and footprints blooming suddenly in spilled flour", "speaking reasonably from empty air, delighted with himself, right up until the tone turns cruel"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Wells, The Invisible Man (1897, PD) — the Griffin archetype, our own take (a chemist undone by his own formula, not a specific film design)"},{"name":"the Portrait's Truth","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-spawn","model":"vampire-spawn","summary":"ageless beauty whose hidden portrait holds the rot","flavor":"Ageless and lovely to look at; somewhere in the house hangs the ledger of every cruelty, rotting so its owner never has to. Destroy the portrait and you destroy the deal.","desc":"Ageless and lovely to look at, unmarked by a single year of the cruelty in his history — because somewhere in the house hangs a portrait doing the aging and the rotting for him. Destroy that canvas and whatever he's owed comes due all at once.","traits":{"note": "Elite vampire-spawn chassis reskinned as Dorian Gray; portrait-destruction as a narrative kill-switch is a DM-adjudicated fiction hook, not a new mechanic — SRD stats otherwise.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hosting a gathering, ageless and charming, unaware anyone in the room suspects the portrait's secret."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A servant has found the hidden portrait's room by accident and hasn't reported it yet."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's showing off his 'family gallery' to a guest, steering conversation carefully away from one locked room."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's paying handsomely for the locked room's door to be reinforced, citing sentimental privacy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An art appraiser has been invited to value the estate and is asking too many questions about the attic."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He grows visibly anxious whenever conversation turns to fire, damp, or restoration work in old houses."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His reflection in still water occasionally shows a face slightly more worn than the one he's wearing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The portrait damaged even slightly, and every cruelty he's owed for starts arriving on his face at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["receiving guests with ageless, unmarked beauty while a hidden canvas somewhere does his aging for him", "standing before a mirror that flatters him completely, untroubled by what the portrait upstairs looks like now"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Wilde, The Picture of Dorian Gray (1890, PD)"},{"name":"the Baba Yaga","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"arch-hag","summary":"chicken-legged hut-witch who judges before she helps","flavor":"Her hut walks on chicken legs and judges visitors before she does; help without being asked and she rewards extravagantly, ask without helping and you become the next fence-post skull.","desc":"Her hut creaks past on legs like a chicken's, fence posts around it capped with skulls old and new. She judges visitors before she helps them — offer aid first and she rewards lavishly; ask first and you risk joining the fence line.","traits":{"note": "High-tier arch-hag chassis reskinned as Baba Yaga; judgment mechanic is DM-adjudicated narrative behavior (help-first vs ask-first), not a new combat rule.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hut has stopped in a clearing, and she's waiting to see who speaks first and how."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's capping a new fence post with a skull, and the face is uncomfortably recent."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate villager has brought her an offering before asking anything, hoping it's enough."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's testing a lost traveler with a small, unasked-for kindness, watching how they react to it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her hut has parked itself blocking the only safe path through the marsh, patient and unmoving."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She keeps a running tally of who helped first and who asked first, and she never forgets which."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her hut's chicken legs occasionally step in place like it's dreaming of walking somewhere else."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Ask her for help before offering anything, and the fence line grows by exactly one, that same night."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "swamp"],"activity":["walking her hut past on legs like a chicken's, judging visitors before deciding whether to help", "capping a fresh fence post with a skull, unbothered by who's watching her work"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Slavic folklore — Baba Yaga (settled, widely published legend figure, not a living closed tradition)"},{"name":"the Gorgon's Daughter","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"gaze-cursed gorgon, curating a garden of statues","flavor":"She keeps a garden of the men who looked, arranged by the year they made the mistake; she's stopped being angry about it and started being a curator.","desc":"She tends a garden of statues, each one a man who looked too long, arranged neatly by the year of his mistake. She's long past angry about any of it — these days she's more curator than monster, walking the rows with something like pride.","traits":{"note": "She's stopped being angry about any of it — these days she's more curator than monster.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Gorgon's Daughter makes one Claw attack and one Snake Hair attack."}, {"name": "Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d4 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Snake Hair", "replaces": "Snake Hair", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (2d6 + 1) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage."}, {"name": "Curator's Gaze", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 30 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Poison damage, or the target may instead choose to close its eyes, taking half damage but being blinded until the start of its next turn. A living creature reduced to 0 hit points by petrification-adjacent effects from her is instead turned to stone permanently and added to her garden, arranged by year."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's walking the rows of her statue garden, adjusting one that's tilted with the season's frost."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A new statue has arrived at her garden's edge, and she's deciding where in the arrangement it belongs."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving relative of one of her statues has come looking, and she's oddly willing to talk about it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's cleaning moss off an older statue with real tenderness, treating it like an old friend."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A would-be hero has arrived loudly announcing intent to end her, and she finds it almost tedious."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She narrates each statue's story on request, curator-calm, naming the mistake each one made."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One statue in the back row has started, very slowly, to weep a faint mineral streak down its face."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threatened seriously, her curator's calm cracks, and something considerably older and angrier looks through her eyes."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "cave"],"activity":["tending a garden of statues, each one a man arranged neatly by the year of his mistake", "walking the rows with something like pride, long past the anger of being looked at"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Greek myth — Medusa (ancient, no owner)"},{"name":"the Opera-House Phantom","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"assassin","model":"assassin","summary":"masked genius-architect ruling from beneath the stage","flavor":"A genius disfigured and driven underground who built a kingdom of trapdoors and misdirection beneath the stage he was never allowed to stand on; he'll kill for the right voice as readily as he'd die for it.","desc":"A mask catches the gaslight below the stage he was never allowed to stand on, and beneath a labyrinth of trapdoors and false walls, a genius disfigured by the world plots his masterpiece. He'll kill for the right voice as readily as he'd die for it.","traits":{"note": "High-tier assassin chassis reskinned as the Phantom; fluff-only Leroux novel version.", "actions": []},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's testing a trapdoor mechanism beneath the stage, lantern light catching the mask's edge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A new performer has caught his ear, and he's arranging for a private audition, uninvited."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's sabotaging a rival's set piece before opening night, meticulous and unhurried about it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's left a note backstage demanding a role recast, signed with a flourish no one questions twice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's guiding a lost stagehand through the underground maze, more amused than threatening, for now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He hums the understudy's part under his breath, correcting imagined mistakes in an empty hall."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Trapdoors open and close ahead of him throughout the theater, as if the building itself takes direction."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Denied the one voice he wants for his masterpiece, his patience for misdirection runs out entirely, all at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["plotting his masterpiece beneath a stage he was never allowed to stand on, mask catching gaslight", "testing a trapdoor's mechanism by lantern light, alone beneath the theater long after the crowds leave"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Leroux, The Phantom of the Opera (1910, PD)"},{"name":"the Impaler-Count","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire","model":"vampire","summary":"ancient, courtly count who owns the road home","flavor":"Old enough to have negotiated treaties in three dead empires; he doesn't need to chase you, because he already owns the roads, the weather, and the wolves between you and the border.","desc":"Old enough to have signed treaties in empires that no longer exist, he receives you with courtly warmth in a castle that owns the roads, the weather, and the wolves between you and the border. He has no need to chase you. He already has.","traits":{"note": "Apex vampire chassis reskinned as Dracula, novel-accurate courtly/commanding version.", "actions": [{"name": "Master of the Road", "text": "Once per long rest, as a bonus action, it may summon a pack of wolves (use standard wolf statistics, up to 4) to arrive from the surrounding terrain within 1 minute."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's receiving the party at his castle gate with courtly, unhurried warmth, already expecting them by name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A coach carrying an unwitting guest is winding up his mountain road, and every wolf along it already knows."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's hosting a formal dinner and has seated a fleeing target directly across from himself, smiling."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's signing a treaty of safe passage that he has no intention of honoring past the ink drying."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's standing at his window watching weather roll in over the border, weather he called for personally."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Every servant in the castle answers questions about him in the exact same careful, rehearsed phrasing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Roads leading away from his domain seem to take travelers in slow, unintentional circles back toward it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Every wolf, storm, and mile of road in three dead empires' worth of territory still answers to a treaty only he remembers signing."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban", "mountain"],"activity":["receiving guests with courtly warmth in a castle that owns the roads, the weather, and the wolves between them and the border", "standing at his window watching a coach he has no need to chase, because he already owns where it's going"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Stoker, Dracula (1897, PD) — novel version (charismatic, ancient, commanding wolves/mist, not any film's fangs-and-cape design)"},{"name":"the Woeful Cry","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"undead","size":"Medium","frame":"banshee","model":"banshee","summary":"keening death-omen spirit; herald, not killer","flavor":"She doesn't kill; she announces. Hearing her keen at your door is the gloom's way of telling you the paperwork on your death is already filed — what you do with the notice is still yours.","desc":"She keens from somewhere just out of sight at your door, a note that isn't meant to kill — only to announce. Hearing it is the gloom's way of telling you the paperwork on your death is already filed; what you do with that notice is still entirely yours.","traits":{"note": "She doesn't kill — she announces. What you do with the notice is still entirely yours.", "actions": [{"name": "Corrupting Touch", "replaces": "Corrupting Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage, delivered like a formality rather than an attack."}, {"name": "Herald's Visage", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "Each creature within 60 ft. that can see her makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature is frightened for 1 minute and ages 1d4 years, visibly shaken by the certainty of the announcement; a creature that succeeds is immune to this Woeful Cry's Herald's Visage for 24 hours."}, {"name": "Wail (1/Day)", "replaces": "Wail (1/Day)", "text": "The Woeful Cry releases a mournful, piercing wail. Each creature within 30 ft. must make a DC 13 Constitution save, taking 34 (8d8) Psychic damage on a failure or half as much on a success. Constructs and undead are immune."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's keening at the party's own door, and the note carries a specific name none of them said aloud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local family has heard her at their window three nights running and is refusing to discuss it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's drifting along a fence line at dusk, and the farm beyond it has had a run of bad luck."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already keened once tonight, somewhere close, and everyone in earshot is quietly checking who's missing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's perched at a hospital window, and the staff have learned not to look directly at the glass."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her keen changes pitch depending on who's listening, as if the notice is addressed personally each time."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She's been keening at the same door for three different owners across thirty years, patient about the address."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Hearing her keen twice in one night means the paperwork's already been amended once, and nobody knows for whom."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "hill", "urban"],"activity":["keening from somewhere just out of sight at a door, a note that isn't meant to kill, only to announce", "drifting along a fence line at dusk, delivering paperwork no one asked to receive"],"source":"folklore","sourceNote":"Irish/Scottish folklore — the banshee (settled literary/folkloric figure, generalized, treated as an omen-spirit rather than flattened into a stock ghost)"},{"name":"the House That Remembers","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"undead","size":"Huge","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"a haunted manor that rearranges itself to relive its dead","flavor":"Every family that ever died under this roof left a little of their worst moment behind, and the house learned to move the furniture with it; it doesn't want visitors, it wants witnesses.","desc":"Furniture slides on its own to recreate the worst moment of whoever last died under this roof, over and over, walls breathing faintly with old grief. It doesn't want visitors so much as witnesses — someone to see what happened here and finally believe it.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't want visitors so much as witnesses — someone to see what happened and finally believe it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The House makes two Object Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Object Slam", "replaces": "Object Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft., using flung furniture as its weapon. Hit: 19 (3d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Invitation", "replaces": "Invitation", "text": "The House rearranges a room to recreate its worst memory around one creature within 60 feet. That creature must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom save or be transported into a vivid recreation of the death scene, frightened and unable to leave the area until the scene ends or the save succeeds again at the end of each of its turns."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Furniture is already sliding into position when the party crosses the threshold, mid-recreation of something old."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grieving relative has come seeking closure and is being gently, insistently drawn into the scene."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An appraiser sent to value the estate has gone quiet mid-tour, listening to something the party can't hear yet."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The house has locked its own doors, unwilling to let anyone leave before they've witnessed the worst moment."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single chair keeps returning to the same spot in the parlor no matter how many times it's moved."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Different rooms recreate different deaths depending on who's standing in them, tailored per witness."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The walls breathe faintly, a slow rise and fall visible only from the corner of the eye."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Finally witnessed and believed, the house goes still all at once, decades of grief exhaling out through every wall."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["sliding its own furniture to recreate the worst moment of whoever last died under its roof, over and over", "breathing faintly through old walls thick with grief, waiting for someone to finally believe what happened here"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic Gothic-haunted-house stock type (the manor-as-monster trope)"},{"name":"Rabid Family Dog","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"mastiff","model":"mastiff","summary":"Foaming family dog snapping at the hand that used to feed it","flavor":"A good dog gone wrong overnight, foam-flecked, still wearing the tag that says its name and a phone number nobody answers anymore.","desc":"The town took its first payment out of somebody's dog. It was gentle enough to nap through thunderstorms last week; now its jaws don't close all the way and its eyes have gone a flat, wrong yellow. The tag on its collar still jingles — same name, same number — like the name means anything to it anymore. It circles the yard it used to guard, looking for the family that fed it, and if they come out to call it, it comes.","traits":{"note": "It still responds — wrongly — to its old name; calling it name-first draws its attack, not its loyalty."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Foam strings from its jaw in ropes it doesn't seem to notice."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags its leash behind it, snapped clean at the stake."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Circles the mailbox three times before it notices you."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tag still jingles the same two-note chime it always did."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Favors a back leg, but the limp never slows the lunge."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Whines once, almost like the old dog, before it bites anyway."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its eyes have gone the same flat yellow as the porch light down the block."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it and every dog on the street starts barking at exactly the same second."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["circling the yard it used to guard, hackles up, tag jingling", "snapping at the hand that raised it, then flinching at its own tag"]},{"name":"Rabid Stray Alpha","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"Pack-scarred stray leading the turned dogs street to street","flavor":"Scarred lead of the pack that used to just beg at the diner's back door; something out at the tree line rewired it first, and it brought the others home.","desc":"It was the diner's begging dog once, patient at the back door for scraps, and something out past the tree line got to it first. Now it runs point for every stray on the block, a torn ear and a crooked jaw the only things left of the animal it was. It doesn't bark before it moves — it just watches the pack fall in behind it and goes. The strays that follow it were harmless a week ago too.","traits":{"note": "The pack breaks and scatters the instant the Alpha goes down — it, not hunger, is what's holding the strays together."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One ear is torn clean off, old scar tissue gone smooth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw sits crooked, healed wrong from some old fight."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Waits at the treeline's edge for the rest of the pack to catch up."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Still wags once, briefly, before the snarl comes back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leads the pack in total silence, no barking at all."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The strays behind it flinch when it flinches, like they share the pain."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It won't cross the line where the streetlights end, not even chasing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it and every stray in earshot arrives at once, mid-turn."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["holding point at the head of the pack, watching, not barking", "peeling strays off a scent and driving them at a single target"]},{"name":"The Vintage Doll","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"ghast","model":"rlm-the-vintage-doll","summary":"Porcelain doll dragging a knife bigger than its own arm","flavor":"Glass eyes, a painted smile that never moves, and a kitchen knife too big for its little porcelain hands — someone's grandmother swore the attic trunk was empty.","desc":"It sits exactly where it was left, hands folded in a lace lap, until the room is empty enough to move. The knife it drags is a real one, from a real kitchen, and far too big for fingers that small — it doesn't seem to notice the weight. Whatever's driving it wore a person's face once, and it hasn't fully given up the habit; it mouths words with a jaw that was never built to talk. Families donate it to the church sale every few years. It always comes home.","traits":{"note": "It always returns to whichever house last owned it — selling, burning, or burying the doll only delays the visit."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile is chipped at one corner, permanently uneven."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a christening dress three sizes too big, yellowed with age."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One glass eye is a slightly different color — replaced, once, badly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The knife it carries still has a kitchen's inventory sticker on the handle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint porcelain-white fingerprints on anything it touches."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums a lullaby half a beat behind itself, like a memory skipping."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whatever wore this face last still moves its jaw between attacks, mouthing an apology it can't finish."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it in a house with a child asleep upstairs and the crib mobile starts turning on its own by morning."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["dragging a kitchen knife across the floor, blade scraping longer than its own arm", "sitting motionless in a lace lap until the room empties, then moving"]},{"name":"The Puppet Troupe","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"rlm-the-puppet-troupe","summary":"Three stringless marionettes moving in eerie unison","flavor":"Three marionettes hung in a storefront window for thirty years, moving now with no strings, no hands above them, no puppeteer anyone remembers hiring.","desc":"The strings above them have been slack for decades, curling loose from a rig nobody bothered to take down, and still the three of them move — jointed limbs clicking in a rhythm meant for a hand that isn't there. They perform the same show they always did, a little slower each year, a little more wrong. One of them still bows at the end. The other two have stopped remembering to.","traits":{"note": "The three act as one mind split three ways — damage or fear landing on one visibly staggers the other two in the same instant."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their paint has flaked to bare wood at every joint that still bends."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One wears a tiny top hat, glued crooked, that never falls off."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their show is the same four gestures, looped, slower every year."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hand-lettered sign in the window still reads \"SOLD OUT — TONIGHT ONLY.\""}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The middle one's jaw is wired shut; it hums instead of speaking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "They bow together at the end of every fight, like it's part of the act."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Cut one's strings and the other two flinch, though none of them have had strings in years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Leave one intact and it finishes the show alone that night, bowing to an empty street."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["performing a jointed, clicking pantomime in the dark shop window", "turning in unison toward anyone who lingers too long at the glass"]},{"name":"The Dummy Patriarch","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"wight-lord","model":"rlm-the-dummy-patriarch","summary":"Ventriloquist dummy holding court, jaw clacking commands","flavor":"A ventriloquist's dummy propped in a wingback chair like a king holding court, jaw clacking out orders to the doll and puppet things that call him father.","desc":"He sits the wingback chair the way a king sits a throne, hands folded over a painted vest, jaw hinge clacking through sentences with no ventriloquist behind them anymore. The dolls and puppets in this house answer to him first — he ran the demand-ladder's second rung longer than anyone living remembers who set it. He never raises his voice. He doesn't have to; everything smaller in the room already knows what he'll say.","traits":{"note": "Every doll/puppet-type creature that can see him fights with advantage while he's conscious — he is the rung above them, and they know it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His vest is hand-painted, decades out of style, still spotless."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His jaw hinge is real metal, older than the rest of him by a century."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He addresses every doll in the room by a name only he remembers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A brass plaque on his chair reads a family name nobody local carries anymore."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He never rises from the chair himself — he doesn't need to."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He negotiates before he fights, offering terms no one asked for."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His painted eyes track independently of the swivel of his wooden head."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Burn the chair with him in it and the smoke holds his silhouette, still seated, until it clears."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["holding court from a wingback chair, jaw clacking out commands to nothing visible", "turning its painted face toward whichever doll in the room hesitates"]},{"name":"The Jealous Car","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"rlm-the-jealous-car","summary":"Gleaming restored coupe stalking its owner's new love","flavor":"A gleaming restored coupe, waxed to a mirror shine, that idles outside the house of whoever its owner's been seeing — and doesn't idle quietly for long.","desc":"Chrome bumper polished to a mirror, engine turning over low and even, it sits at the curb like it's just parked there — until the porch light goes on inside the house of whoever its owner's been seeing. Then the engine note changes. Its owner loved it more than he ever loved a person, and it learned jealousy the same afternoon he brought someone new home in the passenger seat. It has run three relationships out of this neighborhood already, and it isn't tired.","traits":{"note": "It never harms its owner, only whoever the owner's affection has turned toward — attitude with the car itself can be argued, not fought, if that's understood going in."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its paint job is immaculate, hand-waxed weekly, never a scratch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The radio comes on by itself, always tuned to the same slow song."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It parks in exactly the same spot every night, engine ticking as it cools."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A pine air freshener still hangs from a mirror nobody's touched in years."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its horn sounds once, softly, whenever its owner's name is spoken nearby."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It follows at a car-length distance for blocks before ever making a move."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its odometer runs backward toward the mileage from the night its owner fell in love."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Leave it running unattended and it finds its own way to the rival's driveway by morning."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["idling low and even at the curb outside a rival's house, headlights dark", "gunning its engine the instant the target steps off the porch alone"]},{"name":"The Driverless Diesel","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"gorgon","model":"rlm-the-driverless-diesel","summary":"Rust-streaked semi rolling empty-cabbed at all hours","flavor":"A rust-streaked semi that rolls the county road at all hours with the cab dark and empty, engine breathing like something alive under the hood.","desc":"Its trailer's long gone, just a bare hitch dragging sparks behind an engine block that breathes instead of idling, exhaust rolling thick and gray no matter the weather. The cab is empty every time headlights catch it — no driver's silhouette, no hands on the wheel, just eighteen wheels holding a line down the center of the road like it's still following a route somebody gave up decades ago. It doesn't swerve for anything smaller than itself.","traits":{"note": "It holds a straight line and never leaves the roadway — luring it off-road (or standing your ground where it can't turn) is the only reliable way to avoid a straight run-down."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its grille is dented in the exact shape of something it hit long ago."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded company logo on the door names a trucking outfit that folded decades back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its exhaust never thins, rain or shine, mile after mile."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The CB radio under the dash still crackles with a dispatcher's voice, decades old."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One headlight burns dimmer than the other, flickering on every hill."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows near the diner where its old driver used to stop, every single night."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Frost forms on its windshield from the inside, in the rough shape of hands on a wheel."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Leave the wreck on the roadside and by the next moon it's rolling again, dents and all."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["rolling the county road at a fixed, unhurried speed, cab dark and empty", "breathing thick exhaust from a stack that never seems to run out of fuel"]},{"name":"The Returned Pet","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"zombie","model":"rlm-the-returned-pet","summary":"Backyard-buried cat walking again in stiff stop-motion","flavor":"The family cat, buried in the backyard two summers ago, walking again in the jerky stop-motion of something that forgot how joints are supposed to work.","desc":"It comes back up the porch steps the way it always did, one paw at a time, except now each step lands a half-second late and a half-inch wrong, like it's being moved between frames instead of walking. Its collar's still on, tag scratched with a name a kid picked out years ago. It scratches at the same door it always scratched at, waiting to be let back in by people who buried it themselves.","traits":{"note": "It only ever wants back inside — cornered or blocked from the door, it goes rigid rather than fight, and can simply be walked back to its grave."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its fur is matted with backyard dirt that never fully brushes out."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye has gone milky white, the other tracks fine."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It scratches at the door in the exact same spot, worn to bare wood."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its collar tag is scratched illegible except for one letter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves in short, jerking bursts, then holds dead still between them."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It only ever approaches the one door — never a window, never the yard gate."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shadow moves smoothly even when its body doesn't."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Let it inside and every clock in the house loses exactly the time it takes to bury a cat."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["climbing the porch steps in stiff, half-second-delayed lurches", "scratching at the back door it used to be let in through"]},{"name":"The Returned Relative","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wight","model":"rlm-the-returned-relative","summary":"Dead grandmother back at the table, smile right, eyes wrong","flavor":"Grandmother, three years in the ground, back at the kitchen table with the smile exactly right and the eyes not — not even close.","desc":"She's set her own place at the table again, same chair, same cardigan she was buried in, hands folded the way they taught the grandkids to fold theirs before grace. The smile is perfect, practiced, correct in every way that matters to a family that wants to believe. The eyes never blink at the right times, and they never once look at the empty chair where the person she used to argue with used to sit. She'll stay as long as someone keeps setting her a plate.","traits":{"note": "So long as a living family member keeps treating her as kin — feeding her, speaking to her as family — she has no reason to turn; refusing her a place at the table is what provokes her."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the exact cardigan she was buried in, still smelling faintly of the funeral home."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Corrects grandchildren's table manners in precisely her old cadence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sets her own plate before anyone can offer, every single meal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recipes she never wrote down come out of her exactly right, word for word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the seat across from her set for someone who isn't coming."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows quietly, patiently insistent when a family member tries to skip a visit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her reflection in the hall mirror sits at the table a half-second before she does."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Turn her away for good and the whole street's returned relatives start showing up early for dinner."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting at the family table in her old chair, hands folded, waiting to be served", "correcting a grandchild's manners in a voice pitched exactly right"]},{"name":"The Corn Prophet","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"archpriest","model":"rlm-the-corn-prophet","summary":"Child preacher at the field's edge, congregation swaying behind him","flavor":"A child preacher standing at the edge of the cornfield in a suit too big for him, congregation swaying in neat rows behind, sermon carrying farther than any child's voice should.","desc":"He stands where the corn meets the road in a borrowed suit with the sleeves rolled twice, small enough that the pulpit he's built himself only comes up to his chest. His congregation sways in the rows behind him in time with his sermon, though nobody's ever gotten close enough to see their faces clearly. His voice carries across three farms without a single microphone, promising rain, promising harvest, promising the town its next good year if it just keeps paying what the field's owed. He is, underneath the suit and the sermon, still just a kid — and that never stops being true, whatever stands behind him.","traits":{"note": "BINDING children carve-out: reducing him to 0 HP does not kill him — the congregation breaks and scatters into the corn, he drops the sermon voice and starts crying, and the nearest adult finally sees him for what he is and takes him home. No flavorTable row depicts harm to him."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His borrowed suit jacket sleeves are rolled twice and still too long."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The pulpit is nailed together from old fence posts, kid-height on purpose."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His sermon quotes real scripture, but never quite the verse it claims to."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows every family's name in the county, first and last, unprompted."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stumbles over big words like the kid he still is, then recovers smoothly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "The congregation behind him sways to a wind that isn't blowing anywhere else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rows behind him are corn until you look straight at them, and then, briefly, they aren't."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Let him finish a sermon uninterrupted and something in the field answers back that night."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["preaching from a self-built pulpit at the field's edge, voice carrying for miles", "conducting his swaying congregation through the rows with small, exact gestures"]},{"name":"Corn Congregation Child","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"cultist","model":"rlm-corn-congregation-child","summary":"solemn child carrying a sickle like a hymnal","flavor":"A solemn child in Sunday clothes carries a sickle the way other kids carry a stuffed animal, mouthing the same three words the grown-ups taught it before they stopped meeting your eyes.","desc":"It stands at the edge of the cornrow with its sickle held flat against its chest, blade up, the way you'd hold a hymnal at the good part. Its Sunday clothes are clean and its shoes are clean and its eyes are doing something eyes shouldn't do at that age. It doesn't run at you. It walks, reciting, waiting for you to be close enough for the next verse.","traits":{"note": "BINDING carve-out: it never lands a killing blow and never needs to — drop it to 0 and it simply drops the sickle, sits down in the row, and waits to be walked home; the congregation always comes to collect what falls, unharmed."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shoes are church-clean even after crossing three fields of mud."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Recites the same three words under its breath, never varying the order."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Holds the sickle blade-up against its chest like a hymnal at the good part."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Doesn't blink at thunder, gunfire, or its own name being shouted."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks the same furrow every time, never cutting across a row."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums the tune the grown-ups sing at the gathering, note-perfect, tuneless."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one step its shadow falls the wrong direction across the corn."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The whole row goes quiet at once, every stalk, the instant it starts to run."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["walking a straight furrow through the corn, sickle held flat against its chest", "reciting the same three words under its breath, waiting for you to come close"]},{"name":"The Bad Seed","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Small","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-the-bad-seed","summary":"the one perfect child, never the one who did it","flavor":"The one perfect child every family on the street wishes were theirs — polite, tidy, first with the casserole dish after a death — who has never once been the one who did it, and has made sure of that six times now.","desc":"It answers the door in a pressed collar and offers you lemonade before you've said why you've come. Everyone on the street will tell you, unprompted, how good it is — how it mows the widow's lawn, how it never raises its voice. It has arranged for six people to stop being a problem, and not one neighbor believes it capable of arranging anything at all.","traits":{"note": "BINDING carve-out: it never fights directly — treat it as a social-attitude target: neighbors and adults start Friendly toward it and shift only on hard, undeniable proof; break its cover with the town and its whole protective network turns Hostile in one scene, and the defeat-out is non-graphic — exposed, it is simply taken from the house by the adults who finally believe, never harmed on-page."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bakes something for every new arrival on the street within a day."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a spotless room and an even more spotless alibi."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calls every adult 'sir' or 'ma'am,' even the ones who've earned worse."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Volunteers first for the unpleasant chore nobody else wants."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has never once raised its voice, not even at the funeral."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a private ledger of who's crossed it, in handwriting a teacher would praise."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Recites the eulogy for someone who hasn't died yet, word for word, when it happens."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The moment its mask slips in front of just one adult, it decides that adult is the seventh."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["offering lemonade at the door before being asked why you've come", "recounting, sweetly, exactly why someone else must be to blame"]},{"name":"The Good Son's Shadow","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"greater-shadow","model":"rlm-good-sons-shadow","summary":"one of two identical boys, the one with no shadow","flavor":"Two boys, inseparable, though only one of them has ever cast a shadow — and the family stopped noticing which was which a long time before you did.","desc":"They stand together at the fence the way brothers do, matching haircuts, matching corduroy, and it takes a held breath in good light to notice only one of them darkens the grass. The believed one gets the good bedroom, the good grades, the extra helping; the other only gets remembered when the lamp is on. Nobody in the house will say out loud which brother is which anymore.","traits":{"note": "It fights only when its brother is threatened first, and it is defeated non-lethally by proof, not violence: force adult witnesses to see both boys in direct light at once and the household's disbelief collapses, sending it back into the wall it came from without a killing blow — treat the household's collective attitude as the gate, shiftable only by that proof."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mimics its brother's laugh a half-second late, every single time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits at the dinner table but the good plate never quite gets set for it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Photographs of the two boys always come back with one corner overexposed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows its brother everywhere except into direct lamplight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The dog in the house won't come near whichever one it currently is."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Answers to its brother's name faster than its brother does."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "In group photographs from years back, there was only ever one boy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it in full daylight with witnesses, and the family finally, all at once, remembers there were never two boys."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing shoulder to shoulder with its brother at the fence, matching haircuts, matching clothes", "darkening the grass at its feet in good light, the only proof there are two of them"]},{"name":"The Lake Revenant","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"haunting-revenant","model":"haunting-revenant","summary":"drowned camp-slasher, rises from the fog every anniversary","flavor":"Something drowned at the summer camp years back and comes back up out of the lake fog on the same date every year, mask matted with algae, looking for whoever's counselor now.","desc":"The fog off the lake thickens before it does, and then the mask comes up out of the shallows, cracked and green with algae, water sheeting off shoulders that never quite dried. It doesn't ask who's in charge of the camp this year. It already knows, the way the lake always knows, and it starts walking the shoreline the way it did the night everyone let it drown.","traits":{"note": "It only rises within three days of its drowning-date and only where camp counselors are present; kill it off-season or off-site and it simply doesn't manifest — the calendar is the real monster."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mask has grown a skin of pond algae nobody's ever scraped clean."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of lake water across dry ground that never quite evaporates."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries the same rusted tool it drowned holding, still gripped tight."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts cabins under its breath, the way a counselor does at lights-out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces first wherever the water's deepest and coldest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Camp records for its drowning year are always, mysteriously, incomplete."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its reflection in the lake keeps swimming after it's stepped ashore."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drag it back into the water and the entire lake goes still and glassy, like it's satisfied, for exactly one year."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["coast", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["rising out of lakeside fog on the anniversary of its drowning, mask sheeting water", "walking the shoreline at counselor's pace, counting cabins under its breath"]},{"name":"The Masked Shape","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"rlm-the-masked-shape","summary":"pale-masked slasher, walks at the same unhurried pace forever","flavor":"Pale mask, coveralls the color of dust, and a walk that never quickens no matter how fast you run — it keeps regular hours, arriving at the empty house right on schedule, every single year.","desc":"It steps out of the empty house's screen door at the same hour every year, mask white as a dinner plate, coveralls the color of the dust it's stood in for months. It never runs. It doesn't have to. However far ahead you get, it closes the distance by the time you stop to breathe, arriving exactly when it means to, the way it always has.","traits":{"note": "Its pace never speeds up or slows down — treat any attempt to outrun it as futile past a scene or two; it can be genuinely lost, but only by breaking line of sight and the pattern of the house at once, never by outpacing it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mask is a hardware-store paint job, cracked at one temple."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The house it steps out of has been empty since the first killing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coveralls are the same faded blue every single year, never replaced."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Turns its head slow and deliberate to track sound, never sight first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Arrives on the same date every year, give or take the hour."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a small, private collection of items taken off past victims."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's been seen in two places on the same night, both accounts too detailed to be wrong."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Trap it inside the house past dawn and it simply isn't there anymore — until next year, same date."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["grassland", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["stepping out of the empty house's screen door at the same hour every year", "walking after you at an unhurried, unbroken pace that never quickens"]},{"name":"The Gentle Flat-Head","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Giant","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"rlm-gentle-flat-head","summary":"huge stitched protector, gentle only with children","flavor":"A huge, stitched-together thing poured into a coat two sizes too small, gentle with children in a way it has never managed to be gentle with anything else, kept in the shed until someone needs protecting.","desc":"Its coat strains at every seam over shoulders built from parts that don't quite match, and its hands, big enough to crush a skull, close around a dropped toy soft as anything. The kids on the street aren't afraid of it; it's the only thing on the street that's never once raised its voice at them. It stays in the shed until it's needed, and it always knows when that is.","traits":{"note": "It responds to the social-attitude system like an unusually large NPC: start it Neutral, and any scene where a party member protects or is kind to a child in its sight shifts it toward Friendly and recruitable as a guardian."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coat strains at every seam, buttons replaced twice with mismatched thread."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a shelf of found toys, mended, for whichever kid loses one next."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ducks its head going through doorways built for smaller people."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stitched hands are gentler setting down an egg than most people's are."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sleeps standing in the shed, arms crossed, facing the door."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums the same lullaby line over and over, badly, off in the wrong key."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of its stitched-in hands doesn't match the rest of it at all — smaller, softer, a child's once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered and hurt bad enough, it stops being gentle with anything at all, briefly, before it remembers itself."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing watch outside the shed, coat straining at the shoulders", "mending a found toy with too-big fingers, badly, patiently"]},{"name":"The Reformed Wolf-Man","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"werewolf","model":"werewolf","summary":"chains himself down every month, fighting the pull","flavor":"He chains himself to the porch post the night before every full moon, and so far, every month, the chain has held — barely, and only because he wants it to.","desc":"He starts the padlock early, hours before moonrise, hands already shaking with a change that hasn't started yet. The chain is heavier than it needs to be and he still tests it twice. He's held every month so far. He'll tell you himself he doesn't know what happens the month it isn't enough, and he's not interested in finding out with you standing close.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable via the social-attitude system: he starts Wary of strangers and shifts toward Friendly when someone helps secure or reinforce his chains rather than trying to cure or exploit the curse — an ally who fights at your side except on the three nights he's chained down."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tests the padlock twice, every time, even though it's never failed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the chain oiled and inspected better than most keep a sword."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Starts sweating and shaking hours before moonrise, dreading it early."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Won't let anyone stand within the chain's full length on a full-moon night."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Apologizes, sincerely, for things he did before he started chaining himself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a second, spare lock hidden in case the first one's ever tampered with."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Some months the chain looks tested from the inside, like something checked it first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "If someone frees him early 'to help,' he turns on them before he can stop himself."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["testing the padlock on his porch chain hours before moonrise", "gripping the post through the first spasms of a change he's trying to hold off"]},{"name":"The Gill-Man in the Creek","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"merrow","model":"merrow","summary":"shy amphibian creek-dweller, tradeable if you don't push","flavor":"A shy, territorial thing that's lived in the creek behind the mill longer than the mill's been standing, and will trade a favor for being left alone about it.","desc":"It surfaces only as far as its eyes, watching from the shadow under the mill-wheel, and vanishes the second you get too close to its bank. It's not hostile so much as it minds its business fiercely — leave an offering at the flat rock and it'll leave you something back, usually something useful, always something strange. Push past the rock uninvited and it stops trading and starts defending.","traits":{"note": "It responds to the social-attitude system as territorial-Wary by default: respecting its bank (offerings at the flat rock, no trespass past it) shifts it to Friendly and tradeable; crossing the line drops it straight to Hostile with no warning shot."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Surfaces only eyes-and-nostrils, vanishing the second it's noticed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves smooth creek-stones arranged in a deliberate, tidy row."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trades small, useful things for offerings left at the flat rock."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never crosses onto dry land except at the very edge of the bank."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chases off other creek-things that wander into its stretch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its offerings sometimes include things that were never lost in this creek."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The creek runs a half-degree warmer wherever it's decided to nest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Threaten its nest and it drags the offender under before anyone sees it move."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "sea", "swamp"],"activity":["surfacing eyes-only in the shadow under the mill-wheel, watching the bank", "arranging smooth stones in a tidy row at the flat rock for the next offering"]},{"name":"Harry the Hairy Neighbor","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"yeti","model":"rlm-harry-the-hairy-neighbor","summary":"sheepish sasquatch neighbor, lives quietly in the garage","flavor":"Seven feet of matted fur wedged into a borrowed flannel shirt, sheepish about the noise complaints, living quietly in the garage two doors down.","desc":"He's folded himself into a flannel shirt three sizes too small and a garage two sizes too short, and he apologizes for both the second anyone brings it up. The noise complaints are real — something that size doesn't move quietly — but so is the effort: he's raked the yard, fixed the fence, and never once let the kids see him without the shirt on. He just wants to be left the neighbor he's trying to be.","traits":{"note": "Recruitable via the social-attitude system: starts Wary of new faces (embarrassed, expecting rejection) and shifts to Friendly fast with simple neighborly kindness — an invite to dinner, defending him from a complaint — becoming a loyal, powerful ally who still worries about the noise."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flannel shirt strains at every seam, patched twice at the shoulders."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rakes the whole yard before dawn so the neighbors won't see him doing it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Apologizes first, every time, before anyone's even brought up the noise."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the garage door shut except to duck in fast, sideways."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves split firewood on porches anonymously, badly disguising the source."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Waves at exactly the same three neighbors who wave back and no one else."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The garage is bigger on the inside than the outside slab could hold."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past patience, he stops apologizing entirely, and the whole street learns why the shirt matters."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["raking the yard in the dark before anyone's awake to see him", "ducking sideways through the garage door, wincing at how loud he is"]},{"name":"The Man Who Checks the Schedule","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"rlm-man-who-checks-the-schedule","summary":"grey clerk, crosses names off the town's payment ledger","flavor":"Grey suit, grey face, a ledger of the town's debts that never needs referencing twice, and a pen he uses to cross off a date once whatever was owed on it has been collected.","desc":"He keeps office hours nobody remembers setting and a ledger nobody remembers signing, and he is scrupulously, chillingly polite about both. He doesn't threaten; he doesn't need to. He checks the date, checks the name, and crosses it off once whatever the town owes has been collected, the same unhurried motion every single time, like a man closing out a till.","traits":{"note": "Pure social-tier antagonist: treat the town's attitude toward him as collectively Wary-bordering-Fearful; shifting any faction to open Hostile toward him requires proof the debt itself is forged, not just an appeal to mercy — he has none to appeal to."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a ledger bound in something that was never quite leather."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps precise office hours nobody in town remembers agreeing to."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Uses the same pen for every entry, never runs out of ink."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Addresses everyone by their full legal name, first meeting or not."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never raises his voice; never needs to be asked twice."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His ledger lists debts owed by people who swear they never signed anything."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ledger's ink is wet on entries for things that haven't happened yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Try to destroy the ledger and the debts don't vanish — they just come due immediately, on him deciding whoever's holding it owes double."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["checking a ledger no one remembers signing against a date no one remembers agreeing to", "crossing off a name with one small, satisfied stroke of the pen"]},{"name":"The Ladies' Auxiliary Matron","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"coven leader running the ritual like a church bake-sale committee","flavor":"She runs the coven the way she runs the bake sale — sign-up sheets, committee votes, a smile for every casserole — and the sacrifice is just this month's fundraiser.","desc":"She keeps the sign-up sheet on a clipboard by the coffee urn, same as she always has, and the casserole dishes really are labeled with masking tape and first names. Underneath the fellowship-hall folding tables, the circle is chalked in something that isn't chalk. She calls the sacrifice a \"contribution\" and the coven a \"committee,\" and nobody on it has corrected her in eleven years because correcting her has never once gone well. The other ladies nod along, and so, eventually, does whatever she's called up.","traits":{"note": "Track her like any social-attitude NPC: Friendly congregants who bring a dish and keep quiet stay off the altar list; Hostile ones who skip a meeting or ask the wrong question get \"volunteered\" — a member who publicly shifts her back to Friendly (a favor, a confession, a useful lie) can pull a name off that list before the next gathering."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps the sign-up clipboard in a floral cozy and will not begin until it's signed."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists on grace before the ritual, word for word, every single time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows every congregant's casserole recipe and uses it as a threat and a compliment both."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps minutes of the meeting in a spiral notebook, including who was \"volunteered\" and why."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refers to the sacrifice only as \"this month's contribution,\" cheerfully, to your face."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Runs the committee on a strict rotation — everyone gets a turn on the altar list eventually, by her math."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The coffee urn hums the hymn under her breath even when she isn't speaking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner her without the room's support and she drops the bake-sale voice entirely — the thing underneath has chaired far older committees than this one."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["taking attendance at the fellowship-hall meeting, clipboard in hand, casserole dishes labeled with tape", "calling the circle to order with a hymn and a sign-up sheet, sacrifice filed under new business"]},{"name":"The Collector — Storm-Drain Grin","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"rlm-collector-storm-drain-grin","summary":"The payment-taker's street-level face, grinning up through a storm drain","flavor":"A smile in the dark under the street, and one white glove reaching up through the grate. It knows your name because the town gave it the ledger.","desc":"Every town that made the deal meets it first this way: a warmth in a cold place, a voice pitched exactly for one listener, a gloved hand offering back something you lost. The grin is the collection notice. Adults walking past see a drain; the one being collected sees the whole face. It never climbs out at this stage — it doesn't need to, because it has an appointment.","traits":{"note": "This is the Collector's FIRST form — one identity across all three Collector entries; wounds, promises, and names given to one form carry to the others. It withdraws rather than dies; 'killing' the grin just closes this door and advances the feeding clock."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The glove is spotless; the cuff behind it is a hundred years out of fashion."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers back a toy that went down this drain decades ago, good as new."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The grate's bars are bent outward, old damage, painted over many times."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice is pitched so only the person it wants can hear it clearly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Storm water flows INTO the drain around it but never touches the glove."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It knows the payment schedule by heart and recites the town's ledger like a lullaby."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anyone who's been 'collected before' (marked, escaped) hears it in every drain in town."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The grin is a decoy tonight — while you parley with the drain, the true body is already at the house."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["grinning motionless in a storm drain across from a school", "letting one white glove surface, palm up, holding something small and lost"]},{"name":"The Collector — Borrowed Face","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"oni","model":"rlm-collector-borrowed-face","summary":"The payment-taker wearing a trusted townsperson, seams wrong at the jaw","flavor":"A beloved neighbor stands too still on the porch. The seams at the jaw are wrong, and the town has agreed not to notice.","desc":"Between collections it walks the town in faces the town trusts — the pharmacist, the crossing guard, the woman from the auxiliary. The fit is imperfect on purpose: fear seasons the meal, and nothing frightens like almost. Adults look away by long habit; children and outsiders see the seams instantly, and are believed never. It uses the borrowed face's standing — keys, invitations, custody — as legal tender.","traits":{"note": "SAME identity as the other two Collector forms (shared wounds/promises/clock). Exposing the borrowed face publicly — making three adults LOOK at once — forces it out of the skin and back down a rung; that is the social defeat lane, and it costs the town's complicity dearly."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The face it wears belongs to someone who has been 'visiting a sister' for weeks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats the borrowed person's catchphrase a half-second too early, every time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dogs cross the street; the town has quietly rerouted its dog-walking routes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The jaw seam shows only in photographs, which is why it never permits them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tends the borrowed person's garden meticulously; the flowers come up grey."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It holds the borrowed person's office — notary, deacon, scout leader — and uses the access."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The real person is alive, stored, and dreaming everything the Collector does in their skin."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It is wearing someone the party has already befriended in this town — and has been since before they arrived."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing on a porch at the exact edge of a streetlight's reach, waving too slowly", "attending a town meeting in a trusted face, voting with the majority"]},{"name":"The Collector — Payment Due","cr":13,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Huge","frame":"colossus","model":"rlm-collector-payment-due","summary":"The payment-taker's true shape unfolding, hung with all its borrowed faces","flavor":"The true shape unfolds, and every face it ever borrowed hangs off it like coats on a rack. The schedule has run out.","desc":"When the clock runs out and the town cannot pay, the deal's other party comes to repossess. The true shape is not a body so much as an argument — limbs where the eye expects doorways, borrowed faces opening and closing like mouths along its bulk, each one still saying its person's ordinary sentences. It does not rage. It forecloses, room by room, house by house, with the terrible calm of something that has read the contract and is in the right.","traits":{"note": "FINAL form of the one Collector identity — everything learned against the grin and the borrowed face applies here (its true name from the town-secret roll, promises it made, wounds it carries). It can be re-bound but not killed while the deal stands; ending it for good means ending the DEAL, which is a town-scale choice with a town-scale price."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every streetlight it passes under burns out in order, marking its route through town."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The borrowed faces along its bulk still make small talk — weather, ball scores — mid-foreclosure."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It steps over children's chalk drawings with visible, contractual care."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries the original deal — paper, hide, or stone — visible inside it like a swallowed lantern."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The adults of the town stand on their porches watching, and do not scream, and do not help."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It forecloses in ledger order, oldest debt first — the founding family's street goes dark before midnight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wounding it makes the TOWN bleed: pipes burst and foundations crack in sympathetic rows."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "If it completes collection, the town is folded into the deal itself — a new name on the contract, a new lease signed, and next generation's payment doubled. The map keeps the town; nothing else does."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["unfolding out of the deal-site — the drain, the house, the kennel — at the appointed hour", "moving down a residential street at a walking pace, doors opening for it on their own"]},{"name":"The Dream-Stalker","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"rlm-dream-stalker","summary":"Burn-scarred dream slasher; hurt in the dream is hurt for real","flavor":"Burn-scarred, blade-gloved, and patient — it can't touch you awake. It doesn't have to. Everyone sleeps eventually.","desc":"The town burned it once, back when it was only a man, and the town's children have been paying the interest ever since. It exists now in the shallow water between sleeping and waking, wearing the boiler-room where it died like a stage set. In the dream it is baroque, theatrical, unkillable; the wounds it deals cross over. Its one law is its leash: it can only reach the sleeping minds of the town that made it — which is why nobody in that town will tell you its name.","traits":{"note": "M-band system anchor: ACTIVATES the dream lane (sleep becomes a resource; damage taken in its dream is real; rest events route through the DM's dream framing). Its leash is the town — leaving breaks contact; pulling it OUT of the dream (waking grip) makes it briefly mortal. Names and fire are load-bearing against it."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Four thin parallel tears in a bedsheet, mattress, and the headboard behind them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The town pharmacy is quietly sold out of anything that keeps a person awake."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A children's skipping rhyme names its counting habit; the kids can't say who taught it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Parents nail coffee cans of pebbles above the beds — a folk alarm for thrashing sleepers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves survivors' small burns that ache when they get drowsy — a leash of its own."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It stalks a SPECIFIC bloodline first: the children of the adults who lit the fire."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Two sleepers can share one dream if they sleep holding the same object — the town's teens figured this out first."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "If it finishes the last of the firestarters' lines, the leash burns off — and a dream-thing with no town to bind it gets EVERYONE's nights, everywhere, forever."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["dragging four blade-tips along a boiler pipe so the sound carries into the walls of sleeping houses", "standing at the foot of a dreamed bed, head tilted, counting on gloved fingers"]}],
 "bright-kingdom":[{"name":"Wind-Up Soldier","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"clockwork toy soldier, keeps marching until unwound","flavor":"A key juts from its back, ticking down; when it hits zero the toy soldier salutes and falls apart, spilling gears. Its bayonet-poke still draws real blood.","desc":"A key the size of a fist juts from its back, ticking down in tight little clicks as it marches — left, right, left — painted boots striking the ground in perfect time. Its face is a fixed smile, its bayonet a toy prop until it isn't. When the key stops turning it snaps to attention, salutes no one, and comes apart in a spray of gears that keep twitching on the ground.","traits":{"note": "Its key visibly counts down; it always winds fully down before a fight ends, win or lose.", "actions": [{"name": "Bayonet Poke", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage. The wound is small and clean, like a paper cut that keeps bleeding."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chipped red paint on its shako; one boot heel worn flat from years of marching."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its key is rusted at the teeth and skips a click every few turns."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded unit number is stenciled on its back, belonging to no army anyone remembers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same four bars of a march under its breath, over and over."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rifle strap is a shoelace; the bayonet is real steel filed to a needle point."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two others march the same loop a half-step out of sync, bumping shoulders every third pass."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wind it further than its key allows and it keeps marching backward through where it's already been."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "At zero it doesn't just fall apart — its gears keep twitching in formation, still trying to march."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["marching a fixed patrol route, gears clicking down toward zero", "standing frozen at half-salute, key wound tight, waiting for a wind"]},{"name":"Plush Ripper","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"cuddly stuffed animal hiding a mouthful of hooks","flavor":"Button eyes, felt seams, a music-box giggle — and a mouth full of hooked steel teeth sewn in wrong. It cuddles up before it bites.","desc":"Button eyes, calico fur, a music-box hum that plays when you squeeze it — everything about it says hug me. The seams along its belly are stitched wrong, puckered where something was forced in sideways: a jaw's worth of fishhooks, curved and rusted, packed into stuffing that still smells like a nursery.","traits":{"note": "It always bites only after being embraced — it never attacks a target that hasn't touched it first.", "actions": [{"name": "Hook-Stitch Bite", "replaces": "Petrifying Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or begin Bleeding at the start of each of its turns (1d4 damage) until a creature spends an action to pull the hooks free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calico fur worn bald in patches from decades of being loved too hard."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One button eye hangs by a thread, swinging when it moves."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its music-box tune skips the same three notes, over and over, sweetly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hand-embroidered name tag on its foot has been crossed out and rewritten twice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells like a nursery even after the fishhooks are found."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It squeaks a laugh-track giggle instead of the usual music box hum."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its stitching rearranges overnight to look exactly like whoever hugged it last."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut it open and the stuffing keeps coming — yards of it, more than it could ever hold."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest", "any"],"activity":["sitting propped on a shelf, music-box hum playing, arms open for a hug", "nuzzling into a lap uninvited, seams straining at the belly"]},{"name":"Candy-Cane Golem","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"gray-ooze","model":"gray-ooze","summary":"hard-candy construct, sweet shell hides razor shards","flavor":"A shambling column of hard-shell peppermint, sweet enough to lure children and sharp enough at the broken edges to open an artery.","desc":"It shambles upright as a striped pillar of hard candy, red and white swirled glass-slick in the light, sweet enough that the air around it smells like peppermint. Where it's cracked — shoulder, hip, the ragged stump of an arm — the edges catch and glint, each broken facet honed sharp enough to open a vein.","traits":{"note": "Its shell only cuts on the broken edges — it has to be struck first before it becomes truly dangerous to touch.", "actions": [{"name": "Peppermint Shard", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Slashing damage from a cracked candy edge. If the golem has taken damage this encounter, the hit deals an extra 2 (1d4) Slashing damage as more of its shell has shattered into razor glass."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Red and white swirl gone milky where old cracks have healed over sticky."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a faint sugar-dust footprint with every step."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hook at the top of it once hung from a shop window; the chain still dangles."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flies orbit it in a lazy, hopeful ring, never landing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's warm to the touch, like candy left too long in the sun."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one is striped green and white, a flavor no one asked for and everyone dreads."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Lick it and taste, for one heartbeat, a memory that isn't yours."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shatter it fully and every shard skitters upright, hunting, for one last vicious minute."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest", "cave"],"activity":["standing sentry at a shop door, sweet smell drifting off its cracked shell", "lumbering forward slowly, a fresh drip of syrup trailing from a broken elbow"]},{"name":"Jack-in-the-Box Stalker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"boxed ambusher springs out mid-tune, already too close","flavor":"Crouches motionless inside a painted crate for hours, cranking out a tinny tune, until the lid bursts and it's already inside your guard.","desc":"A painted crate sits motionless at the edge of the room, cranking out the same eight notes over and over, patient as a held breath. The tune always seems to end one beat sooner than it should — because by then the lid has already burst and it's already inside your guard, grinning, close enough to touch.","traits":{"note": "It only springs once the tune finishes — but it decides exactly when the tune finishes, never on a fixed beat.", "actions": [{"name": "Springing Grab", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage. If this is the first attack the Stalker has made since bursting from its box this encounter, it has Advantage on the roll."}, {"name": "Wind-Down Grin", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "Each creature within 15 ft. that can see the Stalker's face makes a DC 11 Wisdom save or is Frightened of it until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded paint shows a smiling clown on a crate labeled, oddly, with someone's name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The crank turns on its own, slow, from somewhere inside the box."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tune is a lullaby everyone half-remembers but no one can name."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The box is dented on one corner as if it's been kicked shut before, hard."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its felt hands are stitched with tiny bells that somehow never ring."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one hums the tune backward, which somehow makes it worse."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The box is bigger inside than out, and something else is still waiting in there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it mid-spring and the box keeps cranking, empty, refusing to accept the tune is over."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["cranking out the same eight notes from inside a painted crate, waiting", "sitting perfectly still at the edge of a room, lid trembling on its hinge"]},{"name":"Laughing-Mask Swarm","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","model":"swarm-of-crawling-claws","summary":"swarm of grinning masks that clatter, snap, giggle","flavor":"A drift of hollow carnival masks, all fixed grins, clattering and snapping at ankles in a chorus of muffled giggling that never quite becomes words.","desc":"A drift of hollow carnival masks skitters low across the floor on invisible legs, papier-mâché grins all fixed the same wide curve, clattering together like wind chimes made of teeth. They giggle — not one voice but many, muffled behind painted mouths, a chorus that never resolves into words.","traits":{"note": "The giggling gets louder the longer a fight runs, never softer, no matter how many masks are broken.", "actions": [{"name": "Grinning Swarm", "replaces": "Swarm of Grasping Hands", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d6) Bludgeoning damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer. The swarm can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Papier-mâché grins, all the same wide curve, painted in flaking gold and red."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They clatter in unison like wind chimes strung from teeth."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every mask is a slightly different face, as if each belonged to someone once."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They pool in doorways like leaves, waiting for a foot to fall near."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The giggling never resolves into words, but it almost, almost does."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This drift wears festival ribbons, trailing streamers that snag on everything they pass."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stand still long enough and one mask settles gently onto your own face, fitting perfectly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Scatter them and the giggling keeps going from an empty room, patient, waiting to reconvene."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "cave"],"activity":["skittering low across the floor in a drift of hollow grinning faces", "clattering together at an ankle-height chorus, giggling without any mouths moving"]},{"name":"Balloon-Skin Grub","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"squeaking balloon-hide grub that deflates when popped","flavor":"Squeaks like a dog toy with every bite; pop it and it deflates into a wet rubbery flap that still twitches.","desc":"It squeaks with every wet, looping inch it drags itself forward, a fat larval shape stretched tight and glossy like a balloon left too long in the sun. Puncture it anywhere and it doesn't die so much as deflate, sagging into a rubbery flap on the ground that keeps twitching long after the air's gone out.","traits":{"note": "It never truly dies from damage — only popping it outright ends it, and it keeps twitching after.", "actions": [{"name": "Squeaking Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, accompanied by a loud dog-toy squeak audible up to 60 feet away."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Glossy pink-yellow hide stretched drum-tight, sun-warmed and squeaking underfoot."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's overinflated on one end, listing sideways as it drags itself along."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faint cartoon printing is visible under the stretched skin, unreadable now."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It squeaks in a different pitch each time, almost like distinct little words."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A knot at its tail end looks tied off by careful, deliberate hands."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one is striped like a carnival tent and squeaks in a jaunty little tune."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Popped, it doesn't deflate all the way — a smaller squeaking shape crawls out of the flap."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully burst, the escaping air keens a long wounded note that draws every ear in earshot."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["dragging itself forward in wet looping inches, squeaking with each pull", "stretched taut and glossy in a sunny patch, squeaking softly to itself"]},{"name":"Carnival Tout","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist","model":"cultist","summary":"grinning barker who herds marks toward the big tent","flavor":"Striped vest, painted grin, a barker's patter that never stops — 'Step right up!' — while it herds you toward the tent with a knife up its sleeve.","desc":"Striped vest, chalk-white grin, a barker's patter that never quite stops — step right up, don't be shy, the show's about to start. He keeps one hand out for your ticket and the other tucked behind his back, and the knife in that hand has heard every word of his pitch before.","traits":{"note": "It never attacks anyone still listening to its patter — only those who try to walk away.", "actions": [{"name": "Backhand Sickle", "replaces": "Ritual Sickle", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage. The Tout keeps talking through the entire swing, never breaking its patter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a ticket stub with the party's own name on it, sold before they ever arrived."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's owed a debt by whoever runs the tent and is trying to sell the party to cover it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding someone's coat and shoes, taken as collateral for a game they haven't finished."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He knows a shortcut behind the tent, but the price is bringing him one more mark."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got a fresh wound under the vest from the last customer who didn't want to play."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's pitching two different shows at once, and only one of them actually exists."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His patter is the exact words the party heard in a dream last night, word for word."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's already sold the party's exit to someone else, and that buyer is on the way now."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["barking a nonstop pitch at passersby, one hand out for a ticket", "leaning in close with a chalk-white grin, steering a mark toward the big tent"]},{"name":"Static-Charge Kitten","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Tiny","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"sparking fey kitten, a pet that shocks you dead","flavor":"Fur standing on end, purring like a dying engine; every pet it gives back is a jolt that can stop a weak heart.","desc":"Fur standing on end, purring like an engine winding toward failure, it winds between your ankles wanting to be picked up. Scratch behind its ears and it leans in gratefully — and discharges everything it's been building, a jolt sharp enough to stop a weak heart mid-beat.","traits":{"note": "It only discharges after being petted or held — it never shocks a target that hasn't touched it.", "actions": [{"name": "Grateful Jolt", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d4 + 2) Lightning damage. If the target touched the kitten (petting, picking it up, etc.) since the start of its last turn, this attack has Advantage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur crackling faintly blue at the tips, ears pinned back in permanent static."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves small scorch prints wherever its paws land."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its purr sounds like a dying appliance winding down, then up again."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A little bell on its collar buzzes instead of ringing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It headbutts ankles insistently, wanting attention it can't survive giving."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This kitten's fur sheds visible sparks when it runs, like a comet's tail."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Pet it twice in one day and the second jolt arrives a full room away."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled badly enough, it discharges its whole charge at once in a crackling, blinding burst."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest", "planar"],"activity":["winding between ankles, fur standing on end, purring like a failing engine", "waiting to be picked up, tail twitching sparks onto the ground"]},{"name":"Marching Peanut","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"grinning peanut-soldier in an endless parade conga line","flavor":"A grinning legume-soldier on toothpick legs, part of an endless conga line pouring out of a parade float. Salted, but never quite dead.","desc":"Grinning, salted, and strapped into a tiny soldier's coat, it goose-steps in an endless conga line that spills out of some parade float no one remembers starting. Pop one and the line behind it doesn't break stride — it just closes the gap and keeps marching over the shell.","traits":{"note": "It never breaks formation — killing one just closes the gap in the line behind it.", "actions": [{"name": "Toothpick Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +2, reach 5 ft. Hit: 2 (1d4) Piercing damage. The Peanut always attacks without breaking its marching stride."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A grinning legume face under a tiny painted soldier's cap, salted and gleaming."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its toothpick legs click in perfect unison with a dozen others behind it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The conga line trails back around a corner and keeps going further than anyone's checked."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same brass-band riff its whole unit marches to."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its little coat is buttoned with what look like real teeth."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one wears a paper hat instead of a coat, a cheap parade-favor upgrade."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Step into the conga line and your feet start moving to its rhythm whether you want them to or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crush enough of them and the float itself lurches upright, hunting for its missing riders."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "forest"],"activity":["goose-stepping in an endless conga line spilling from a forgotten parade float", "saluting stiffly in formation, salted shell glinting under its tiny coat"]},{"name":"Piñata Brute","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"paper-hide brute that bursts into candy shrapnel","flavor":"Papier-mâché skin stretched taut over a swinging club-arm; crack it open in the right spot and it detonates candy shrapnel and stolen teeth.","desc":"Papier-mâché skin, bright crepe-paper fringe, a swinging club arm sized for a real fight rather than a birthday — it lumbers forward grinning through its painted seams. Crack it open in the wrong place at the wrong time and it doesn't spill candy so much as detonate it, shrapnel and stolen teeth alike.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Burst Open", "text": "on death, explodes in a burst of candy shrapnel dealing minor damage to anything adjacent — a death-burst layered on the ogre chassis"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bright crepe-paper fringe hangs off a papier-mâché frame sized for a real fight."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted seams are stitched shut with actual thread, taut over something heavier inside."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells like a party that ended badly a long time ago."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A cracked patch on its shoulder already leaks a thin trickle of candy dust."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its club arm is weighted wrong, dragging one shoulder lower than the other."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's fringe is shaped like a favorite childhood animal, worn nearly bald."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The candy that spills from it, if eaten, tastes exactly like a memory you'd forgotten."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It sometimes detonates a second time from the wreckage, minutes later, without warning."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "forest", "any"],"activity":["lumbering forward grinning through crepe-paper seams, club arm swinging loose", "standing guard over a pile of candy and teeth spilled from an earlier kill"]},{"name":"Carousel Nightmare","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"carved carousel horse torn free, circling for blood","flavor":"A painted wooden charger torn loose from its pole, galloping in place no longer — gilt cracked, glass eyes rolling, hooves that never stop circling for the kill.","desc":"A painted wooden charger tears free of its pole mid-spin, gilt paint cracked along every seam, glass eyes rolling loose in their sockets. It doesn't need the carousel anymore — it gallops in place on nothing, hooves striking sparks off the air itself, circling tighter the longer you stand still.","traits":{"note": "It can only ever move in a circle — it never charges in a straight line, and it never tires.", "actions": [{"name": "Carousel Charge", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the Nightmare moved at least 20 ft. in a curve toward the target this turn, the hit deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Painted Grin", "text": "1/Day. The Nightmare's carved smile widens impossibly. Each creature within 15 ft. that can see it makes a DC 13 Wisdom save or is Frightened of it until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Flaking carnival paint over bone; gold leaf worn thin on the mane."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A brass pole still runs through it from withers to belly, useless now."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tinny calliope music plays from somewhere inside its ribs."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It circles the exact footprint of a carousel long since demolished."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child's ribbon is still knotted, decades old, in its skeletal mane."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Three more stand frozen mid-gallop nearby, waiting for the music to reach them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Ride it once and you can't get off; the ground it circles stops being a place you can leave."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "When it dies the whole ghost-carousel spins up at once — every carved beast tears loose."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["galloping in place on nothing, hooves striking sparks off empty air", "circling tighter and tighter around a spot where a carousel used to stand"]},{"name":"Sugar-Rush Harlequin","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker","model":"pixie-wonderbringer","summary":"jittering harlequin brawler, hopped up on rock candy","flavor":"Diamond-patched and cackling, it mainlines rock candy between blows, moving in jittery double-time no eye can quite track until the pratfall becomes a killing blow.","desc":"Diamond-patched and cackling, it mainlines fistfuls of rock candy straight from a pouch at its belt between every blow, jittering in a double-time no eye can quite track. One second it's mid-pratfall, arms flailing for balance — the next its foot's already connected, and the joke was never the point.","traits":{"note": "It gets faster the longer a fight runs — its jitter compounds, not fades, as the rock candy burns through it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Harlequin makes two attacks, one with its jagged javelin and one with its studded morningstar."}, {"name": "Jagged Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Melee or Ranged Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Studded Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, and rock-candy shards embed in the wound, dealing an extra 2 (1d4) Piercing damage at the start of the target's next turn unless the shards are picked out first."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Diamond-patched motley gone sticky at the cuffs from spilled rock candy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cackle comes half a beat before the blow that earns it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A belt pouch rattles with more candy than any one performer should carry."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never stops moving, even between attacks, feet always mid-shuffle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile cracks wider with every hit it lands, like drying plaster."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This Harlequin juggles its javelins between throws, showing off even mid-fight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one instant per fight it moves so fast it seems to occupy two places at once."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overdosed, it keeps twitching and cackling long after it should have dropped."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest", "any"],"activity":["mainlining rock candy from a belt pouch between every jittery blow", "cackling mid-pratfall, already recovering balance before the joke lands"]},{"name":"Bubblegum Ooze","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Ooze","size":"Large","frame":"gelatinous-cube","model":"gelatinous-cube","summary":"pink bubblegum ooze, engulfs and dissolves you slowly","flavor":"Bright pink, sickly-sweet-smelling, and stickier than any trap — it swallows whole and digests slow enough you can hear yourself dissolve.","desc":"Bright pink, glossy, and sickly sweet-smelling from across the room, it moves in a slow, stretching roll that looks almost playful. It swallows whole rather than strikes, and the digestion is slow enough — deliberately slow — that you can hear your own voice going soft and distant from somewhere inside it.","traits":{"note": "Its digestion is slow on purpose — a swallowed creature has time to be rescued before real harm sets in.", "actions": [{"name": "Sticky Pseudopod", "replaces": "Pseudopod", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 13) if the Ooze isn't already grappling a creature."}, {"name": "Bubblegum Engulf", "replaces": "Engulf", "text": "The Ooze engulfs a Large or smaller creature it is grappling. The target is Restrained, has total cover, can't breathe, and takes 7 (2d6) Acid damage at the start of each of the Ooze's turns as the gum slowly dissolves it, muffling all sound to a soft, distant hum."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bright bubblegum pink, glossy, sweet-smelling from clear across the room."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a tacky trail that takes real effort to peel a boot from."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bubbles rise and pop slowly across its surface, each one a soft, wet sigh."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something small and metal is stuck permanently near its core, glinting."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves like it's in no hurry at all, which is somehow worse."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This Ooze is a deeper, sourer flavor, and its trail stings faintly on bare skin."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Voices from things it's swallowed drift up occasionally, muffled, still talking."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck hard enough, it splits into two smaller, hungrier gobs instead of dying."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "cave", "forest"],"activity":["rolling forward in a slow stretching wobble, sickly-sweet smell filling the room", "holding something half-dissolved and still faintly moving inside its pink mass"]},{"name":"Claw-Machine Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"arcade claw-machine on legs, rigged to never miss","flavor":"A coin-op cabinet on stilted legs, its steel claw always 'almost' catching you — until the game rigs itself to let the claw actually close.","desc":"A coin-op cabinet stands up on four stilted, spring-loaded legs, its glass front lit garish yellow, a steel claw dangling and swaying overhead. The claw drops for you again and again, 'almost' catching, teasing — until the machine decides the game's rigged enough in its favor, and the claw actually closes.","traits":{"note": "Its claw genuinely misses most of the time — until it decides the game's rigged enough to actually close.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes two attacks with its rigged claw."}, {"name": "Rigged Claw", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. Once per turn, if this is the Horror's second attack against the same target, treat the roll as if it were a natural 20 — the game has decided you're a winner."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A coin-op cabinet on stilted, spring-loaded legs, glass front lit garish yellow."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded stickers advertise prizes that don't match anything inside it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A single coin is jammed permanently in its slot, worn smooth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums a jingle on a loop that gets louder the longer you stand near it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The claw's three fingers are bent at slightly wrong angles from old, hard use."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's glass front is smeared, hiding whatever's crammed inside as 'prizes.'"}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Feed it a coin and it plays fair exactly once, dropping something it shouldn't have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its glass shatters outward and the prizes inside come scrabbling free, hungry."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["swaying on stilted spring legs, steel claw dangling and teasing overhead", "dropping its claw again and again, 'almost' catching, glass front lit garish yellow"]},{"name":"Funhouse Double","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"mirror-warped double wearing your own stretched face","flavor":"Steps out of a warped mirror wearing your own face stretched a little too wide, mimicking your voice back at you a half-second behind.","desc":"It steps out of a warped funhouse mirror wearing your own face, stretched a fraction too wide at the mouth, the proportions just wrong enough to itch at the back of your skull. It mimics your voice back at you a half-second behind, testing the words in your mouth before it tries anything with its hands.","traits":{"note": "It reads a target's surface thoughts before mimicking them, so its copy always says something almost right, and unsettling for it.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Double makes two Stretched Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Stretched Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 8 (2d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage from an arm stretched a fraction too long to be believed."}, {"name": "Borrowed Thoughts", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Double reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 60 ft., no save required, gaining details it uses to mimic that creature's voice and mannerisms."}, {"name": "Wrong-Angle Face (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can see the Double's face makes a DC 13 Wisdom save or is Frightened of it until the end of its next turn, dropping whatever it's holding as its hands forget how to work."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Your own face, worn like a mask stretched a fraction too wide at the mouth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It tests your words in your own voice before committing to them, half a beat slow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its proportions are subtly wrong — eyes set too far apart, just enough to itch."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It still smells like the mirror glass it stepped out of, cold and faintly metallic."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flinches at things you'd flinch at, learned rather than felt."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This Double wears the face of someone else in the party, not the one it's fighting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment, killing it feels exactly like killing yourself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It dies wearing your face and, for one heartbeat, you feel yourself die with it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "planar"],"activity":["stepping out of a warped mirror wearing your own face, stretched too wide", "mimicking a voice back a half-second behind, testing the words in its mouth"]},{"name":"Ferris-Wheel Horror","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gargoyle","summary":"rolling wheel-boned horror, its gaze turns you to stone","flavor":"Rusted gondolas for a ribcage, it rolls upright on its own broken wheel-rim, and anything that looks too long into its lantern-eyes seizes up stone-still.","desc":"Rusted gondola cars hang where ribs should be, and it rolls upright on the broken rim of its own wheel, groaning metal on stone with every rotation. Lanterns burn where its eyes should sit, and anything that stares too long into that light finds its joints locking, stone-still, mid-stride.","traits":{"note": "Its gaze only petrifies those who look back — a target that avoids its eyes entirely is safe from that effect.", "actions": [{"name": "Gondola Gore", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage from a rusted gondola strut driven forward like a horn."}, {"name": "Lantern-Eye Gaze (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Each creature within 30 ft. that can see the Horror's lantern-eyes makes a DC 15 Constitution save. On a failure, a creature is Restrained as its joints begin to stiffen; on a second failed save at the start of its next turn while still Restrained, it is Petrified. A creature that succeeds on both saves is unaffected."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rusted gondola cars hang where ribs should be, swaying with each groaning rotation."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Lanterns burn steady where its eyes should sit, never guttering."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rolls on the broken rim of its own wheel, striking sparks off stone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded ride-safety signage is still bolted somewhere along its frame."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something stone-still and human-shaped rides motionless in one of its gondolas."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's gondolas still swing passengers of an earlier age, all frozen mid-scream."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stare into its lanterns too long and you start to remember a ride you never took."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Toppled, its wheel keeps rolling loose across the ground, gondolas full and swinging."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["rolling upright on the broken rim of its own wheel, groaning metal on stone", "turning slowly in place, lantern-eyes sweeping the crowd like a searching gaze"]},{"name":"Cotton-Candy Wraith","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"wraith","model":"wraith","summary":"sugar-sweet drifting haze that feeds on happy memories","flavor":"A drifting pink haze that smells of childhood summer fairs, sweet right up until it's inside your lungs, unspooling your last happy memory as it feeds.","desc":"A drifting pink haze rolls low across the ground, smelling exactly like a childhood summer fair — sugar and dust and distant calliope music. It's sweet right up until it's inside your lungs, and only then do you feel it pulling at something warm and specific, unspooling your happiest memory thread by thread as it feeds.","traits":{"note": "It always targets whichever creature is happiest in the moment — it can sense contentment like a scent.", "actions": [{"name": "Sweet-Haze Drain", "replaces": "Life Drain", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage, and the target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken until the target finishes a long rest, as one happy memory is pulled loose and eaten."}, {"name": "Create Sugar-Specter", "replaces": "Create Specter", "text": "The Wraith can create a specter from a humanoid it has drained a memory from within the last hour, as the memory itself rises wearing that creature's shape, sweetly grinning."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A drifting pink haze that smells exactly like a childhood summer fair."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rolls low along the ground, curling under doors and around ankles."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Distant calliope music seems to travel with it, never quite in sync."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's sweet right up until it's inside your lungs, and only then does it turn cold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a faint sugar residue on anything it passes through."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This haze is a deeper rose color and smells like a birthday instead of a fair."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Breathe it in and, for a moment, you can taste a memory that was never yours to lose."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it disperses into a hundred smaller wisps, each one still hungry for one bite."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "planar"],"activity":["rolling low across the ground as a drifting pink haze, smelling of a summer fair", "curling in through a gap under a door, unspooling a warm memory thread by thread"]},{"name":"Arcade Sentinel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"void-monk-zerth","summary":"glitching screen-boss, bolts skip you straight to wounded","flavor":"Pixelated and buzzing, it flickers between screen and floor, hurling glitching bolts that skip frames of your body straight past the pain and into the wound.","desc":"Pixelated at the edges, buzzing where it should be solid, it flickers between the screen's glow and the floor like a loading bar that never finishes. The bolts it hurls don't burn or cut so much as skip — your body jumps frames straight past the pain and lands, already, in the wound.","traits":{"note": "Its bolts don't damage flesh so much as skip time forward — the pain always arrives a beat after the wound.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Sentinel makes two Glitch Bolt attacks."}, {"name": "Glitch Bolt", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +7, range 60 ft. Hit: 10 (3d6) Force damage as the target's body skips a frame, landing already wounded."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Sentinel casts a spell, using flickering pixel-light in place of material components."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pixelated at the edges, buzzing where it should be solid, glitching between two states."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It flickers like a loading bar that never quite finishes filling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ghost of a high-score table scrolls faintly across its chest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It skips forward a half-step at a time instead of walking smoothly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bolts leave the air smelling faintly of hot electronics."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one glitches in a different color palette, sickly green instead of arcade blue."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one frame per fight it shows what's standing behind it in the room you're not in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it doesn't stop — it glitches back in a few seconds later, one life fewer."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["flickering between the screen's glow and the floor, buzzing like a loading bar", "hurling glitching bolts that skip past armor and land straight in the wound"]},{"name":"Mascot-Suit Puppeteer","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"fish-folk-archpriest","model":"grell","summary":"hollow mascot suit worn by tendrils wearing your smile","flavor":"The beloved mascot costume is empty air on the inside — a knot of grasping tendrils wearing the plush like a second skin, waving for the children with someone else's hand.","desc":"The beloved mascot costume waves cheerfully from its post at the gate, plush and huge and welcoming — but the inside of that suit is empty air where a body should be. A knot of grasping tendrils wears the plush like a second skin, and the wave it gives the children is worked by someone else's hand.","traits":{"note": "The suit itself is harmless — every attack comes from the tendrils wearing it, working the plush like a puppet.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Puppeteer makes two Gloved Reach attacks."}, {"name": "Gloved Reach", "replaces": "Strange Scepter", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage from an oversized plush arm worked from the inside, plus 4 (1d8) Psychic damage as a tendril tip brushes the target's mind."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Puppeteer casts a spell from inside the suit, its actual body never visible."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The beloved mascot costume waves from its post, plush and huge and welcoming."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The suit's smile never changes no matter what's happening inside it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wave to children is a half-second too smooth, joints moving wrong for a costume."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something inside shifts the plush's weight distribution constantly, unnaturally."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The eyeholes of the suit are stitched shut; it doesn't need to see to know where you are."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one wears a rarer, beloved mascot variant, drawing bigger crowds and bigger tendrils."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Unzip it and there's another, smaller suit inside, also occupied, also waving."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, the plush collapses empty — the tendrils are already inside someone else's costume."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["waving cheerfully from its post at the gate, plush and huge and welcoming", "working its own wave from the inside, someone else's hand moving the glove"]},{"name":"Firework Effigy","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Elemental","size":"Large","frame":"fire-elemental","model":"fire-elemental","summary":"living fireworks display, still building to a finale","flavor":"Built for the finale and never told the show is over, it keeps blooming into new colors overhead, each burst a little closer to the crowd.","desc":"Built for one grand finale and never told the show ended, it keeps blooming overhead in fresh colors — gold, then violet, then a red that lingers too long. Each burst climbs a little lower than the last, the sparks drifting closer to the upturned faces below, still waiting for its cue to stop.","traits":{"note": "It never stops building toward a finale it was never told to end — every round its bursts fall a little closer to the ground.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Effigy makes two Firework Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Firework Burst", "replaces": "Burn", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +6, range 60 ft. Hit: 11 (2d8 + 2) Fire damage, and the target catches fire if it isn't already, taking 5 (1d10) Fire damage at the start of each of its turns until a creature uses an action to douse it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Built for one grand finale, blooming overhead in colors that keep climbing lower."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its core burns gold, then violet, then a red that lingers too long to be safe."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faint booming applause echoes from somewhere it isn't, on a loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It waits, mid-air, for a cue that stopped coming a very long time ago."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ash falls from it steadily, dusting the ground gray beneath its hover."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one bursts in patterns shaped like faces, briefly, before scattering."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its finale, when it finally comes, spells something out across the whole sky."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-bloom, it detonates its entire held charge in one final, blinding burst."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "urban", "grassland"],"activity":["blooming overhead in fresh colors, gold then violet, waiting for a cue that never comes", "hanging in the air mid-burst, sparks drifting a little lower toward the crowd below"]},{"name":"The Ringmaster","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"top-hatted ringmaster who commands the whole show","flavor":"Top hat, painted smile, a whip that cracks louder than thunder — every act in the tent performs for him, willing or not, and the show never ends until he says so.","desc":"Top hat cocked just so, painted smile fixed under the brim, he cracks a whip that snaps louder than real thunder over the ring. Every act under this tent performs for him — willing or not — and the show does not end, cannot end, until he decides to say so.","traits":{"note": "a compulsion caster — the whip-crack forces movement/action into 'the act' rather than dealing direct harm", "actions": [{"name": "Command Performance", "text": "cracks the whip to force a target into a scripted action of the Ringmaster's choosing on its next turn"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a party member's shadow hostage as his newest act, taken mid-handshake."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He needs one more headline act tonight and has already sold tickets naming the party."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's got the only key out of the tent, worn on a chain, and he never removes it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An old act of his is trying to warn the party but can't disobey him long enough to speak."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rehearsing a finale that requires a volunteer from the audience, tonight, by name."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's furious that a rival ringmaster's poster went up nearby and wants it torn down, violently."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The whip he cracks is stitched from something that used to talk; it still tries to."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His tent has no back exit because the tent is the only place left standing of a town he consumed whole."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["cracking a whip that snaps louder than real thunder over the ring", "commanding every act under the tent to perform, willing or not, for his applause"]},{"name":"The Overwound Nutcracker","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"giant nutcracker soldier, jaw snaps clean through bone","flavor":"Painted uniform, oversized jaw hinged to crack more than nuts — every strike is a full-body snap of that grinning mouth, splintering whatever's fed to it.","desc":"Painted uniform buttons gleam under the lights, and its oversized jaw hinges open on a spring built for cracking more than nuts. Every strike is a full-body snap of that grinning mouth, hinge and teeth together, splintering whatever gets fed into it with a sound like a tree going down.","traits":{"note": "Every strike is a full-body snap of jaw and hinge together — it cannot make a soft or careful attack.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Nutcracker makes two attacks: one Painted Slam and one Jaw Snap."}, {"name": "Painted Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Jaw Snap", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 18 (3d8 + 5) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller, it must succeed on a DC 17 Strength save or be flung 10 feet away and knocked Prone."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted uniform buttons gleam under whatever light finds this room."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its jaw hinges wide with a sound like a tree groaning before it falls."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Splinters from its last meal still cling to the paint around its mouth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It stands rigid at parade rest between fights, jaw held slightly ajar."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A key at its back is wound far tighter than it should safely hold."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This one's uniform bears a general's braid, and it expects to be saluted."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its jaw, unhinged, opens wider than its own body should allow."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overwound past its limit, its spring snaps and it keeps swinging, faster, uncontrolled."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest", "any"],"activity":["standing rigid guard, oversized jaw hinged open on a spring built for more than nuts", "snapping its mouth shut, testing the bite on whatever's nearest, splintering wood"]},{"name":"Vending-Machine Colossus","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"coin-slot golem, dispenses violence for your last coin","flavor":"Rows of snack-slots for a chest, it dispenses whatever you 'paid' for — usually a fist — and jams itself deliberately so you keep feeding it coins.","desc":"Rows of snack-slots line its chest like ribs, coin slot glowing faintly at its sternum, and it dispenses exactly what you 'paid' for — which is usually a fist. It jams itself on purpose after every payout, rattling and grinding, because it wants you to keep feeding it coins.","traits":{"note": "It always jams on purpose after a payout — it wants to be fed again, and it will wait as long as it takes.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus makes two Bladed Arm attacks."}, {"name": "Bladed Arm", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage from a dispenser-arm sharpened into a blade."}, {"name": "Snack-Slot Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +8, range 60 ft. Hit: 13 (3d6 + 3) Fire damage as a flaming 'prize' launches from one of its chest slots."}, {"name": "Stale Vapor Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "The Colossus exhales a 30-foot cone of curdled vending-machine vapor. Each creature in the area makes a DC 16 Constitution save, taking 27 (6d8) Poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rows of snack-slots line its chest like ribs, coin slot glowing faintly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It dispenses exactly what you 'paid' for — usually a fist, sometimes worse."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rattles and grinds deliberately after every payout, wanting more coins fed in."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dented 'out of order' sign hangs crookedly from one shoulder."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old receipts flutter out of it with every heavy step it takes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "This Colossus is stocked with a rarer product line, and its prizes hit harder."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Feed it the exact right coin and, just once, it dispenses something genuinely useful."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its slots keep dispensing on their own, spilling flaming prizes across the floor."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["rattling and grinding after every payout, jamming itself on purpose", "dispensing exactly what you 'paid' for, coin slot glowing faintly at its sternum"]},{"name":"The Birthday King","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"planetar","summary":"crowned rigger of the game no one is meant to win","flavor":"Crowned in melted candles, he presides over the game you cannot win — the wheel is rigged, the dice are his teeth, and every prize you claim costs you a year of your life.","desc":"Crowned in a ring of melted, dripping candle wax, he presides over a game rigged from the first roll of the dice — his own teeth. Every prize claimed at his table comes billed in years, and he collects with the same delighted, patient smile he wears for the birthday song.","traits":{"note": "the rigged-game boss — every action he takes is framed as a 'fair' game the table already lost", "actions": [{"name": "Rig the Wheel", "text": "forces a reroll against a target it already knows the outcome of, then narrates the loss as if luck decided it"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's throwing a party for a child who died a hundred birthdays ago and won't let it end."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He invites the party to play a game whose only losing condition is refusing to play."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He holds a 'gift' the party desperately needs and will only give it as a game prize."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's chosen a party member as this year's guest of honor, which means they can never leave the party."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every guest at his table is someone who lost his game; they'd warn the party if they still could."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's grown bored of his usual guests and rewrites the game's rules gleefully to keep the party interesting."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The party has, it turns out, been playing his game since they entered the realm; he's just now revealing the score."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "His game is the realm — its candy rules, its eaten power-ups, its cheerful teeth — and he has decided the party's whole story is this turn of it; to beat him is to unmake the game they're standing inside."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "forest", "planar"],"activity":["presiding over a party thrown for a guest of honor who is never allowed to leave", "handing out gifts that are also, on closer reading, the rules of the game"]},{"name":"The Grinning Prize","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"undead-eye-tyrant","model":"kraken","summary":"top-shelf plush titan, a dozen button-eyes snap open","flavor":"The top shelf's biggest stuffed monster, too big for any booth, its dozen glass-button eyes all open at once the moment you finally win it.","desc":"It hangs from the top shelf of the biggest booth in the midway, too large for any prize rack, stitched fur worn soft from decades of longing stares. The moment someone finally wins it down, all dozen of its glass button-eyes snap open at once, and none of them blink.","traits":{"note": "All its eyes open together at once, never one at a time — the moment it wakes, every ray fires from a different direction.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Prize uses its Button-Eye Rays. It then makes one Plush Bite attack."}, {"name": "Plush Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 15 ft. Hit: 27 (4d10 + 5) Piercing damage from stitched jaws far too large to have been sewn shut properly."}, {"name": "Button-Eye Rays", "replaces": "Eye Rays", "text": "The Prize shoots up to three rays at random from its dozen button-eyes, choosing up to three targets it can see within 90 ft. Each targeted creature makes a DC 18 Dexterity save; on a failure it suffers one of these effects (roll or choose): Shrink Ray (Reduced condition until the start of the Prize's next turn), Snip Ray (10 (3d6) Slashing damage as felt seams tear open across the body), or Wish Ray (the target is stunned until the end of its next turn, dazzled by an impossible, false granting of its deepest want)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ticket-stub trail leads to it, dropped by every challenger who ever tried to win it down."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child's handwritten wish-list is stitched into its underside, still legible, still unanswered."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding the last winning ticket ever issued, and someone very desperate wants it back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The booth beneath it is rigged to collapse the moment it's finally taken off the shelf."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival prize-runner is already climbing the booth, racing the party for the win."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its stitched fur is worn soft in the exact shape of a hundred longing hands before theirs."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every eye that opens shows a different midway, from a different age, all still running somewhere."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is every prize ever wanted and never won, and claiming it means every unclaimed wish comes due at once, to the winner, all together."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["hanging from the top shelf of the biggest booth, too large for any prize rack", "letting its dozen button-eyes snap open at once the moment it's finally won"]},{"name":"Tin Drummer Boy","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"drumming tin toy that locks your heartbeat to its beat","flavor":"Beats an unbreakable march rhythm that syncs enemy hearts to its tempo until they seize up mid-stride.","desc":"It beats an unbreakable, driving march on a tin drum strapped across its chest, the rhythm never wavering, never speeding, never stopping. Listen too long and your own pulse starts falling in step with the beat — right up until the tempo locks your heart mid-stride.","traits":{"note": "Its drumbeat is audible before it's visible, and the beat only quickens in the last second before it strikes.", "actions": [{"name": "Cymbal-Arm Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage from its bladed cymbal-arm. The target's heartbeat audibly syncs to the drumbeat until the start of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chipped red paint on a cylindrical tin body, key still wound tight in its back."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches a perfect square, three steps per side, forever, footsteps never varying."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its drumhead reads a nursery rhyme's title in faded gilt lettering."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One eye is a painted dot; the other is a small cracked mirror."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its drumsticks are actual bone, lacquered white to look like painted wood."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A whole squad marches in unison, every drum locked into one shared rhythm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Hum along to its beat and your own pulse refuses to fall back out of step."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Smash the drum and the beat doesn't stop — it jumps into the nearest listening chest."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["marching a tight square in place, drumsticks never missing a single downbeat", "standing sentry at a nursery threshold, tin drum thudding low and steady"]},{"name":"Rag Doll Skulker","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"cockatrice","model":"cockatrice","summary":"limp rag doll that scuttles the second you look away","flavor":"Limp and lifeless until your back is turned, then it scuttles on button-thread joints, needle fingers first.","desc":"It hangs limp over a shelf or a windowsill, button eyes half-lidded, utterly lifeless — for as long as you're looking. The instant your back turns, it scuttles forward on thread-thin joints, needle-fingers reaching first, faster than a thing stuffed with cotton has any right to move.","traits":{"note": "It goes fully limp the instant it's observed and only moves the moment nobody's watching it.", "actions": [{"name": "Needle-Finger Rake", "replaces": "Petrifying Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage from thread-thin needle fingers, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or its wound stiffens, reducing its Speed by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded gingham dress, one button eye hanging by a thread."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stitched initials on its foot tag belong to a child no one here remembers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells faintly of attic dust and, underneath that, something coppery."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cotton stuffing pokes through a torn seam at the shoulder."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its felt mouth is stitched into a smile too wide to be comforting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It freezes mid-lunge the instant anyone looks directly at it, holding the pose."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mirrors don't show it moving at all, only its resting, limp position."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn fully apart, its stuffing keeps twitching into little needle-fingered shapes."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["slumped lifeless over a windowsill, button eyes at half-mast, waiting to be looked away from", "propped among a shelf of identical dolls, one stitched grin fresher-looking than the rest"]},{"name":"Gumdrop Sprite","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Tiny","frame":"pixie","model":"pixie","summary":"sugar-shard pixie giggling above dog-whistle pitch","flavor":"A candy-coated pixie that pelts foes with hardened sugar shrapnel, giggling in a register only dogs and the dying can hear.","desc":"A candy-coated pixie no bigger than a hand, it hovers in a shimmer of sugar dust, giggling in a pitch that climbs past what most ears can follow. It pelts with fistfuls of hardened sugar shrapnel, each shard glinting rainbow before it draws blood, still giggling the whole time.","traits":{"note": "Its giggle climbs above most hearing entirely right before it attacks, a warning only some creatures can catch.", "actions": [{"name": "Sugar Shrapnel", "replaces": "Faerie Dust", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +5, range 30 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage from a fistful of hardened sugar shards, plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage as a sliver works into the wound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rainbow-glazed wings that leave a faint sugary residue on anything they brush."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Giggles nonstop, even mid-flight, even while fleeing, even while dying."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells like burnt caramel up close, cloying and a little sour underneath."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its cheeks bulge visibly with hoarded sugar shards before every volley."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint trail of glitter-dust wherever it darts through the air."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Travels in small giggling swarms of three or four, pelting from every angle."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its pitch is inaudible to most people but sends nearby dogs into a frenzy."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Crushed, it detonates its whole stash in one glittering, razor-edged burst."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "urban", "any"],"activity":["hovering in a shimmer of sugar dust, giggling in a pitch only dogs and the dying can hear", "raiding a candy stash and packing both cheeks full before scattering shrapnel behind it"]},{"name":"Squeak-Toy Hound","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"rubber toy dog whose bite-squeak gets louder with damage","flavor":"Every bite compresses its rubber chest into a cheerful squeak that somehow gets louder the deeper the wound.","desc":"A rubber toy dog trots forward on stiff little legs, every bite compressing its chest into a cheerful, high-pitched squeak. The wound doesn't quiet the sound — somehow the squeak gets louder with each deeper bite, cheerful and awful in equal measure.","traits":{"note": "The squeak gets louder, not quieter, the more damage it takes — a wounded one is the loudest one in the room.", "actions": [{"name": "Squeaking Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and its rubber chest compresses into a shrill squeak audible up to 60 feet away."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracked rubber hide, a faded paw-print pattern worn nearly smooth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its squeak has a distinct two-tone chirp, almost a little tune."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews on anything within reach, indifferent to whether it can actually bite through it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A manufacturer's tag, long faded, still dangles from one floppy ear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trots in the exact same lopsided gait no matter the terrain underfoot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A whole litter of them hunts together, squeaking in ragged, overlapping rounds."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its squeak, heard enough times in a row, starts to sound like actual words."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Torn open, it lets out one final, deafening squeak that doesn't fade for a full minute."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["trotting stiff-legged in tight circles, chest already squeaking faintly with anticipation", "gnawing at a stranger's boot with the mindless enthusiasm of a toy that never tires"]},{"name":"Confetti Wisp","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Small","frame":"smoke-mephit","model":"smoke-mephit","summary":"glitter-storm elemental made of razor-edged party confetti","flavor":"A cloud of shredded paper and glitter that swirls into a blinding storm, each fleck razor-cut at the edge.","desc":"A cloud of shredded paper and glitter swirls at head height, catching the light in flickers of gold and red, harmless-looking as a party favor gone loose. It tightens into a blinding storm on approach, and every fleck in that glittering cloud is cut razor-sharp at the edge.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sharp Fleck Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from a fistful of razor-cut confetti."}, {"name": "Glitter Burst", "replaces": "Cinder Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Wisp explodes into a blinding, razor-bright cloud in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 12 Dexterity save, taking 10 (3d6) Slashing damage on a failure and being Blinded until the end of its next turn, or half damage and no blindness on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gold and red shredded paper, catching light like a stray party favor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drifts lazily until anyone gets within arm's reach of it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every fleck inside it is cut sharp enough to draw blood on contact."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Trails loose flecks behind it that settle harmlessly, glittering, on the ground."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Makes a soft crinkling sound, like wrapping paper, as it moves."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Several drift together near any leftover party décor, drawn to streamers and balloons."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The confetti inside it never seems to run out no matter how much it sheds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed at range, it still detonates its whole glittering mass on a five-second delay."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "sky", "any"],"activity":["swirling harmlessly at head height, glinting gold and red like a stray party favor", "tightening into a razor-bright cloud the instant footsteps get too close"]},{"name":"Marionette Cutpurse","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit","model":"bandit","summary":"string-puppet thief worked by an unseen hand overhead","flavor":"Jointed limbs jerk on visible strings that lead up into empty air; something above is definitely still pulling.","desc":"Its jointed limbs jerk in stiff, unnatural arcs, strings trailing up from wrist and shoulder into open air with nothing visibly holding the other end. It picks pockets with a puppet's clumsy precision, and whatever's pulling those strings is patient, deliberate, and still up there somewhere.","traits":{"note": "Its strings run up into nothing visible — whoever or whatever holds the other end is patient and never lets go.", "actions": [{"name": "String-Jerked Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, the blade swinging in a stiff, unnatural arc."}, {"name": "Puppet Crossbow", "replaces": "Light Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It just lifted a locked box the party needs, and its strings are already retracting it upward."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A merchant is chasing it, screaming that it took the only key to his stall."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been picking the same pocket for three days straight, on a loop, unaware time has passed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Something jerks its strings taut and yanks it backward the moment it's cornered."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a stolen coin purse stamped with a noble crest someone will want back."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Cutting its visible strings only reveals a second, thinner set underneath, still taut."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whatever holds its strings starts reeling in slack whenever the party gets too close to answers."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it snaps the string taut all the way up — and something up there yanks back, hard, angry."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["jerking through a crowd in stiff puppet-arcs, strings trailing up into empty air", "picking a pocket with clumsy precision while something unseen overhead pulls taut"]},{"name":"Pop-Gun Grenadier","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-infantry","model":"warrior-infantry","summary":"toy-soldier grenadier lobbing shrapnel-cored party favors","flavor":"Fires corked party-favor rounds that detonate on impact with genuine shrapnel hidden under the cork.","desc":"Dressed in a toy soldier's bright piping, it lobs corked rounds from a party-favor gun with a cheerful little pop and a trailing streamer. The cork is a lie — packed shrapnel rides under it, and the party favor detonates on impact like it means it.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Shrapnel Favor", "replaces": "Spear", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 20/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage as a corked party-favor round detonates against the target, packed shrapnel biting deeper than the cheerful pop suggests."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bright piping uniform, a paper party hat strapped on like a helmet."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each shot trails a little paper streamer that drifts down after the pop."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a belt of corked rounds slung bandolier-style across its chest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches in step even under fire, never breaking cadence."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gun barrel is shaped like a party favor's cardboard tube."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Fights in small squads, coordinating volleys with cheerful little whistle-signals."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The pop from its gun sounds identical no matter how far away you are from it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Downed, its remaining rounds cook off all at once in a scattershot final volley."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["lobbing corked rounds with a cheerful pop and a trailing paper streamer", "reloading its party-favor gun behind cover, whistling a marching tune between shots"]},{"name":"Licorice Whip-Vine","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Medium","frame":"vine-blight","model":"vine-blight","summary":"sticky black candy-vine that lashes and constricts","flavor":"Sticky black ropes of edible-looking vine lash out and constrict, tasting faintly of anise and old blood.","desc":"Sticky black ropes coil up out of the ground, glossy and candy-slick, smelling faintly of anise from a distance. Up close that smell curdles into something coppery, and the vine lashes and constricts with a strength no piece of candy should have.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Sticky Lash", "replaces": "Constricting Vine", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 12) by sticky black candy-vine."}, {"name": "Anise Snare", "replaces": "Entangling Plants (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Sticky vines burst from the ground in a 15-foot radius. Each creature there makes a DC 12 Strength save or becomes Restrained until it escapes (DC 12) or the vine is destroyed (AC 10, 10 hit points)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Glossy black coils that look, from a distance, like discarded party candy."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells sweetly of anise until you're close enough for it to strike."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a sticky black residue on anything it touches, hard to scrub off."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roots into cracked pavement just as easily as into soil."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its coils pulse faintly, almost like a slow, patient heartbeat."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows in tangled patches, several vines sharing one hidden central root."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Chew a broken-off piece and it tastes exactly like the candy it resembles, briefly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Burned, it releases a thick black smoke that smells sweeter the longer you breathe it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "swamp", "any"],"activity":["coiling up out of the ground, glossy and candy-slick, smelling faintly of anise", "lashing at anything that strays close enough to brush its sticky black ropes"]},{"name":"Kite-String Wraith","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"skeleton","model":"skeleton","summary":"paper kite dragging a bone-child on garrote-taut string","flavor":"A torn paper kite drags a skeletal child's shape behind it on razor-taut string, forever chasing an updraft that never comes.","desc":"A torn paper kite dips and jerks against a sky with no wind, dragging a small skeletal shape behind it on taut, razor-thin string. It's forever chasing an updraft that never comes, and the bone-child at the end of its line reaches for anyone who gets too near the line's path.","traits":{"note": "Its string is nearly invisible in daylight and cuts on contact even when the wraith isn't attacking.", "actions": [{"name": "Garrote-String Slash", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage from razor-taut kite string."}, {"name": "Line-Snap Shot", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A torn paper kite, faded diamond pattern, tail ribbon shredded to threads."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The skeletal shape trailing behind it still wears a single mitten."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its string hums faintly, like a plucked wire, even at rest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dips and jerks in the same looping pattern, chasing wind that isn't there."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The kite paper is scrawled with a child's crayon drawing, long faded."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Several drift together in a loose formation, strings occasionally tangling."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The string is nearly invisible in daylight and only shows in shadow or storm-light."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut its string and the bone-child at the end doesn't fall — it keeps reaching, untethered."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["sky", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["dipping and jerking against a windless sky, forever chasing an updraft that never comes", "dragging a small skeletal shape behind it on taut, razor-thin string"]},{"name":"Snow-Globe Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"ice-mephit","model":"ice-mephit","summary":"trapped globe-spirit that shakes itself into a blizzard","flavor":"Trapped forever inside a floating glass sphere, it shakes itself into a blinding blizzard when threatened.","desc":"Trapped forever inside a floating glass sphere no bigger than a fist, a tiny pale shape drifts in slow, endless circles through painted snow. Threaten it and the whole globe shakes violently, the gentle flurry inside erupting into a blinding, freezing blizzard that spills out past the glass.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Glass-Sphere Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Cold damage."}, {"name": "Painted Fog", "replaces": "Fog Cloud (1/Day)", "text": "1/Day. The Wisp shakes its glass sphere, filling a 20-foot radius with painted-snow fog that heavily obscures the area for 1 minute or until a strong wind disperses it."}, {"name": "Blizzard Shake", "replaces": "Frost Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The globe erupts in a 15-foot cone. Each creature there makes a DC 11 Constitution save, taking 9 (2d8) Cold damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fist-sized glass sphere, tiny painted village visible through drifting flurries."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its resting flurry looks entirely decorative until something disturbs it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The little pale shape inside walks the same slow circle, endlessly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hairline crack runs across the glass, letting a faint chill seep out."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits eerily still on shelves and mantels until approached directly."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A shelf of them shakes in sequence, each one setting off the next."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Shatter the glass and the blizzard inside keeps blowing, contained by nothing at all."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Frozen solid, it doesn't die — it just waits, patient, for the next warm hand."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["arctic", "any"],"activity":["drifting in slow, endless circles inside a floating glass sphere of painted snow", "shaking violently as footsteps approach, flurries inside beginning to churn"]},{"name":"Puppet-Show Ghoul","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Small","frame":"ghoul","model":"ghoul","summary":"hand-puppet corpse twitching to an absent puppeteer","flavor":"A hand-puppet corpse with a painted grin sewn permanently open, fingers still twitching to an absent puppeteer's cues.","desc":"A hand-puppet corpse lies slumped in its little painted booth, felt mouth stitched into a permanent, cheerful grin. Its fingers twitch on unseen cues even with no hand inside it, jerking through a performance for a puppeteer that isn't — visibly — there.","traits":{"note": "Its fingers twitch on cues from something absent even before it fully rises to attack.", "actions": [{"name": "Painted Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Curtain-String Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Felt skin stretched over a bloated frame, stitched grin permanently open."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its little painted booth still bears a faded show's title above the curtain."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fingers twitch through the same three gestures on an endless loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells of mildew and greasepaint in equal, unpleasant measure."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its booth curtain rustles even when there's no wind to move it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A whole row of booths houses more of them, each twitching to a separate cue."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It performs a full little scene before attacking, bowing first like there's an audience."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-performance, its curtain drops on its own, and the booth applauds with no hands."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["slumped in a painted booth, felt mouth stitched into a permanent grin", "twitching through a performance for a puppeteer that isn't visibly there"]},{"name":"Ticket-Booth Imp","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Fiend","size":"Small","frame":"imp","model":"imp","summary":"toll-imp who brands hands and demands blood admission","flavor":"Demands admission in blood before letting anyone leave the fairgrounds, stamping hands with a brand that never fades.","desc":"It leans out from a chipped ticket window, small and grinning, and demands admission before anyone's allowed to leave the fairgrounds. The toll is blood, always blood, and the brand it stamps on the back of your hand doesn't fade no matter how hard you scrub.","traits":{"note": "It never lets a debt slide — anyone who skips the toll gets tracked and billed later, with interest.", "actions": [{"name": "Toll Sting", "replaces": "Sting (Bite in Beast Form)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) Poison damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution save or be Poisoned until the end of its next turn."}, {"name": "Fairgrounds Slip", "replaces": "Invisibility", "text": "The imp turns invisible until it attacks, casts a spell, or its concentration ends, vanishing behind its booth window as if it were never there."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's blocking the only exit from the fairgrounds and wants blood, not coin, for passage."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A branded hand in the party's group means the imp already knows exactly where they're headed."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a stack of exit tickets that someone desperately paid for and never got to use."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local kid owes it an unpaid toll from years back, and it hasn't forgotten."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a shortcut out — for a price no one's willing to name yet."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps a ledger of every unpaid toll in the fairgrounds, meticulously updated."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The brand it stamps starts whispering directions back to the booth whenever its owner strays."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Kill it and every brand it ever stamped burns hot at once, all across the fairgrounds."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "planar", "any"],"activity":["leaning from a chipped ticket window, demanding blood admission before anyone can leave", "stamping a struggling hand with a brand that won't scrub off no matter how hard you try"]},{"name":"Streamer Serpent","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-venomous-snake","model":"giant-venomous-snake","summary":"crepe-scaled snake whose sweet venom masks as punch","flavor":"Crepe-paper scales trail like party streamers as it strikes, its venom sweet enough to be mistaken for punch.","desc":"Crepe-paper scales trail behind it like party streamers caught in a breeze, rustling with every fluid, sinuous strike. Its venom tastes sweet on the way in — sweet enough to be mistaken for punch — right up until it isn't.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Punch-Sweet Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage. The venom tastes sweet enough to pass for punch, right up until it doesn't."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Crepe-paper scales in party colors, rustling faintly with every movement."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coils loosely around punch bowls and dessert tables, patient and still."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bite mark looks, for a moment, like a harmless paper cut."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a faint trail of shredded streamer-scale wherever it slithers."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales rustle louder the faster it moves, an early warning to the observant."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Nests in tangled knots of several serpents near any leftover party décor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Victims of its venom crave sweets uncontrollably for a full day afterward."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed, it unravels entirely into a heap of ordinary-looking crepe paper streamers."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["trailing crepe-paper scales like party streamers caught in a breeze", "coiled near an overturned punch bowl, tongue tasting the sweetness in the air"]},{"name":"Popcorn Blight","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Small","frame":"twig-blight","model":"twig-blight","summary":"kernel-husk plant that bursts in scalding shrapnel steam","flavor":"Clusters of white kernel-husks burst apart in a shower of blinding steam and hooked husk-shrapnel.","desc":"Clustered white kernel-husks sway together on a single stalk, gently rattling, looking for all the world like an oversized snack display. Get close and they burst apart at once in a shower of blinding steam and hooked husk-shrapnel, popping like a string of firecrackers.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Husk-Shrapnel Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage from a burst of hooked kernel-husk shrapnel."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clustered white kernel-husks swaying gently together on one thin stalk."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of butter and salt from several paces away."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rattles softly in the wind, easy to mistake for a snack cart display."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pops one husk at a time as a warning before the whole cluster bursts."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Roots shallowly, easy to topple, harder to actually kill outright."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Grows in small clumps, each stalk bursting in a chain when one goes off."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The steam it releases smells sweet, almost inviting, even as it scalds."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Uprooted and thrown, it detonates on impact rather than on approach."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["swaying gently on a single stalk, kernel-husks rattling like an oversized snack display", "bursting apart in a shower of blinding steam the instant someone gets too close"]},{"name":"Domino Sentinel","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"toppling domino construct that chain-falls in a crushing line","flavor":"Stands rigid in a row until one falls; then the whole line topples in a cascading, crushing avalanche.","desc":"It stands rigid in a long, silent row alongside its fellows, painted pips facing outward, waiting. The instant one falls — pushed, struck, or simply tired of standing — the whole line topples in a cascading, crushing avalanche down its length.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Chain Fall", "text": "when one Domino Sentinel is knocked prone or destroyed, every other Domino Sentinel adjacent to it in the line falls too, each dealing its normal slam to whatever's beneath"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted white pips on black lacquer, standing rigid and silent."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pip count seems to shift slightly each time you look away and back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stands in a fixed row alongside identical fellows, all facing the same direction."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Falls with a deliberate, unhurried creak, never rushed, always precise."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chipped lacquer at its base from countless prior falls and re-settings."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A full row of a dozen stands ready, the whole line primed to cascade."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Once toppled, it rights itself again by morning, standing back in line."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "The last domino standing in a row falls hardest of all, crushing far past its own weight."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "any"],"activity":["standing rigid in a long silent row, painted pips facing outward, perfectly still", "toppling in a slow, deliberate arc the instant its neighbor in line falls"]},{"name":"Wooden Nutcracker Cadet","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"shell-cracking nutcracker jaw that prefers fingers now","flavor":"Painted teeth clamp with a jaw built for cracking shells, now finding fingers just as satisfying.","desc":"Painted teeth clamp shut with a crisp, mechanical snap, a jaw built and hinged specifically for cracking shells. It's found fingers just as satisfying as walnuts, and it doesn't seem to notice the difference anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Shell-Cracker Jaw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage from a jaw hinged for cracking shells, now finding fingers just as satisfying."}, {"name": "Parade-Ground Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The Cadet fixes its painted stare on one creature it can see within 30 feet. That creature must succeed on a DC 11 Wisdom save or be Frightened of the Cadet until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted uniform piping, brass buttons, a jaw hinged wide open at rest."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Clamps its teeth in a crisp test-snap on a regular, marching cadence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A shell fragment is still lodged in one back molar, permanently."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted eyes never blink, fixed forward in a perpetual parade stare."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches with a mechanical, jointed gait, elbows locked stiff."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Patrols in pairs, snapping their jaws in near-perfect unison as a warning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to genuinely enjoy the snap, whether it connects with a walnut or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its jaw, broken off entirely, keeps snapping on its own, blind and directionless."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest", "any"],"activity":["standing at rigid attention, painted teeth clamping shut in a slow, mechanical test-snap", "marching a patrol route, jaw hinge creaking louder with every found finger"]},{"name":"Yo-Yo Stringer","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"scout","model":"scout","summary":"street performer garroting foes with a weighted yo-yo","flavor":"Whips a weighted yo-yo on garrote-strength string that returns to hand freighted with whatever it wraps.","desc":"A street performer flicks a weighted yo-yo out in a lazy, showy arc, garrote-taut string singing as it spins. It always returns to hand — freighted, on the way back, with whatever got wrapped up in its loop.","traits":{"note": "Its yo-yo always returns freighted with whatever gets caught in the loop on the way out.", "actions": [{"name": "Garrote-Yo Slash", "replaces": "Shortsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Weighted Yo-Yo Shot", "replaces": "Longbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/60 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage as the weighted yo-yo snaps out and back, and the target must succeed on a DC 11 Dexterity save or be Grappled (escape DC 11) until the Stringer's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bright street-performer sash, worn juggling pins strapped to one hip."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The yo-yo's string sings a faint high note whenever it's fully extended."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Performs an elaborate trick before every real attack, showman to the last."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears several rings taken from past crowds, worn openly as trophies."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its yo-yo is carved from a single, oddly heavy piece of dark wood."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Performs alongside a partner, trading tricks and distractions between them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The string never seems to tangle no matter how wildly it's thrown."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cut the string mid-throw and the yo-yo keeps flying under its own momentum, unrelenting."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["flicking a weighted yo-yo in a lazy, showy arc, garrote-string singing as it spins", "performing tricks for a small crowd while quietly sizing up their pockets"]},{"name":"Fun-Fair Goblin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"goblin-warrior","model":"goblin-warrior","summary":"rigged carnival-game goblin who charges fingers, not coins","flavor":"Small, gaudy, and vicious, it hawks rigged ring-toss games where losing costs a finger, not a coin.","desc":"Small, gaudy, and grinning under a striped awning, it hawks a rigged ring-toss game with a carnival barker's practiced charm. Losing costs more than the entry fee — the goblin's price for a bad throw is a finger, taken with the same cheerful patter as the pitch.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Rigged Ring-Toss Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Loaded Shortbow", "replaces": "Shortbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 80/320 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a party member's dropped item as the 'grand prize' for winning its rigged game."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A jar of collected fingers behind its counter includes one someone here will recognize."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A crying kid nearby lost a bet to it and is owed a finger by sundown."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's rigged the game specifically to bait whoever looks most confident into playing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival barker goblin nearby wants this one's stall and will happily rat out its cheats."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It keeps a ledger of every debt owed, cheerfully overdue and compounding."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every ring it tosses somehow lands exactly where it wants, rigged game or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Beaten at its own game, it flies into a screaming rage and demands double the usual price."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["hawking a rigged ring-toss game under a striped awning with a barker's practiced charm", "counting a jar of collected fingers behind the counter, humming a jaunty tune"]},{"name":"Prize-Claw Scuttler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"giant-centipede","model":"giant-centipede","summary":"detached claw-machine grabber skittering on cable legs","flavor":"A detached claw-machine grabber skitters on cable legs, forever hunting something small enough to clamp and lift.","desc":"A detached claw-machine grabber skitters low across the ground on thin cable legs, three steel prongs opening and closing, testing the air. It hunts for anything small enough to clamp and lift, dragging its catch back toward a glass box that isn't there anymore.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Claw-Prong Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and if the target is Small or smaller, it is Grappled (escape DC 12) by steel prongs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Three chrome prongs on thin, jointed cable legs, scuttling low and fast."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tests the air constantly with open prongs, hunting for something small enough to grip."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Drags catches toward a specific spot, insisting on a glass box that's long gone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Makes a soft, motorized whir with every step across hard ground."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its prongs are scuffed and dented from countless failed grabs."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hunts in small packs, herding prey toward the same missing glass box."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Everything it successfully grabs vanishes the instant it reaches that empty spot."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-grab, its prongs lock rigid, permanently clamped on whatever it caught."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["skittering low on thin cable legs, three steel prongs opening and closing, testing the air", "dragging a small struggling catch back toward a glass box that isn't there anymore"]},{"name":"Whack-a-Mole Ambusher","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-badger","model":"giant-badger","summary":"burrowing mole-toy that pops up to bite, then vanishes","flavor":"Pops from hidden holes to bite before vanishing back down, rewarding the quick with only a bruised knuckle.","desc":"It pops from a hidden hole with a cheerful little chime, bites once, and vanishes back underground before a hand can follow. The quick get nothing worse than a bruised knuckle for their trouble; the slow don't get a second chance to swing.","traits":{"note": "It rewards a quick reaction with almost nothing — the slow ones don't get a second swing at it.", "actions": [{"name": "Pop-Up Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. After the attack, the Ambusher can burrow back into its hole, becoming Hidden until it next attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cheerful painted fur, a bell hidden somewhere that chimes with each pop-up."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hole looks identical to a dozen decoy holes scattered nearby."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Vanishes underground the instant a hand or weapon comes close."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The chime that precedes its pop-up is just loud enough to hear, just late enough to matter."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint claw-scrapes ringing the rim of every hole it's used."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A whole field of holes hides several, popping up in staggered, mocking sequence."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems to know exactly which hole you're watching and never uses that one."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered aboveground with no hole to flee to, it digs a new one in seconds flat."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "hill", "any"],"activity":["popping from a hidden hole with a cheerful little chime before vanishing back down", "watching from underground, waiting for a hand to linger just a moment too long"]},{"name":"Fortune Machine Familiar","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"fortune-teller automaton whose cards come horribly true","flavor":"A mechanical gypsy bust dispenses cursed fortune cards that come cheerfully, horribly true.","desc":"A mechanical fortune-teller's bust sits behind curtained glass, painted eyes glowing faintly, one hand hovering over a slot. The cards it dispenses read cheerful nonsense in looping print — and every single one of them comes true, horribly, exactly as written.","traits":{"note": "Every card it dispenses comes true, horribly, exactly as written — the danger is reading it aloud.", "actions": [{"name": "Curtained Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "True Fortune", "replaces": null, "text": "1/Day. The Familiar dispenses a fortune card to one creature within 10 feet. If that creature reads it aloud, it must succeed on a DC 12 Wisdom save or the fortune's cheerful, specific prediction begins coming true within the hour (DM's discretion, a minor but genuine complication scaled to the CR budget)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's already dispensed a card to someone in the party, and the prediction is starting to come true."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local is begging the party to smash the machine before its next fortune lands."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's dispensing cards nonstop, jamming, as if something's forcing its hand from inside."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A card in its dispensed pile accurately predicted a death that already happened."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a card free of charge to anyone who agrees to read it aloud immediately."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its cards are collected obsessively by a nearby merchant who trades handsomely for them."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every fortune it's ever given is, cross-referenced, actually one single unfolding story."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it ejects every unread card in its hopper at once, all coming true simultaneously."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["sitting behind curtained glass, painted eyes glowing faintly, one hand hovering over a card slot", "dispensing a cheerful, looping-print fortune that will come true exactly as written"]},{"name":"Bumper-Car Brawler","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"ogre","model":"ogre","summary":"stripped bumper-car chassis that charges and never stops grinning","flavor":"A stripped-down bumper car chassis charges anything in its lane, crumpling on impact and grinning wider each hit.","desc":"A stripped-down bumper car chassis rattles forward on bare wheels, sparking where the roof used to be, painted grin scorched onto its front bumper. It charges anything in its lane, crumples satisfyingly on impact, and grins a little wider with every hit it takes.","traits":{"note": "It only fights in straight lanes — it charges hard down a line and takes a beat to turn around.", "actions": [{"name": "Chassis Charge", "replaces": "Greatclub", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the Brawler moved at least 10 ft. straight toward the target this turn, the hit deals an extra 7 (2d6) damage and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength save or be knocked Prone."}, {"name": "Spark-Bolt Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stripped bumper-car frame, roof torn off, sparks scattering where the pole once was."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grins wider with every hit it takes, scorch marks deepening its painted expression."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Rattles and sparks constantly, even at rest, chassis never fully still."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Only moves in the straight lane it's used to, needing a beat to redirect."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded numbering on its side marks it as belonging to a ride long dismantled."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Several charge the same track in a chaotic, overlapping demolition-derby rhythm."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It seems genuinely delighted by every crash, sparking brighter with each collision."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wrecked completely, its bare chassis keeps sparking and twitching toward the nearest lane."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "any"],"activity":["rattling forward on bare sparking wheels, painted grin scorched onto its front bumper", "charging down its lane and crumpling gleefully into whatever's standing in it"]},{"name":"Peppermint Stalker","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"kobold","model":"kobold","summary":"caroling candy-striped goblinoid dragging prey to sugar vats","flavor":"A candy-cane-striped homunculus with a hook-shaped hand, humming carols while it drags foes toward the sugar vats.","desc":"Candy-cane stripes wind up its small frame, one hand curled into a permanent hook, humming a carol under its breath as it moves. The tune never stops, not even while it drags something struggling toward the sugar vats steaming somewhere out of sight.","traits":{"note": "Its carol never stops, not even mid-fight, and it never seems to drop whatever it's dragging.", "actions": [{"name": "Hook-Hand Dagger", "replaces": "Dagger", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 11) by its hooked hand."}, {"name": "Sugar-Vat Sling", "replaces": "Sling", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +4, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Candy-cane stripes wound tightly up a small, wiry frame."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One hand curled permanently into a hook, the other free to work its sling."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums a different carol each time it's encountered, always slightly off-key."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells strongly of hot sugar and, underneath, something scorched."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves faint sticky red-and-white smears wherever it drags a catch."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Works in small caroling pairs, one humming while the other drags."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its carol seems to get louder the closer its sugar vats actually are."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed, it keeps humming for several seconds through a throat that no longer works."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "urban", "any"],"activity":["humming a carol under its breath, hook-hand curling as it studies the room", "dragging something struggling toward sugar vats steaming somewhere out of sight"]},{"name":"Merry-Go-Round Foal","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse","model":"warhorse","summary":"carousel horse torn free of its pole, still bobbing as it tramples","flavor":"A gilded carousel horse tears free of its pole mid-spin, still bobbing up and down as it tramples the crowd.","desc":"A gilded carousel horse tears free of its brass pole mid-spin, paint chipping, still bobbing rhythmically up and down as it moves. It tramples with the same up-down gait it always had on the ride, indifferent to the difference between a painted platform and flesh.","traits":{"note": "It moves in the same bobbing up-down rhythm it always had, indifferent to whatever's underfoot.", "actions": [{"name": "Gilded Trample", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. On the down-beat of its bob, the hit deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gilded paint chipping badly along its flanks, brass pole-hole still visible."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bobs up and down in a fixed rhythm no matter the ground beneath it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A painted saddle and stirrups remain fused permanently to its back."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Glass eyes catch the light with an unsettling, glassy carousel sparkle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tinny calliope notes drift from it even at a full gallop."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Runs in a loose herd of others torn from the same ride."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It only ever moves in the exact arc the ride's platform used to trace."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its bob continues one last time in the wreckage before finally stopping still."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "ruins"],"activity":["tearing free of a brass pole mid-spin, paint chipping, still bobbing rhythmically", "trampling forward with the same up-down gait it always had on the ride"]},{"name":"Face-Paint Marauder","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"berserker","model":"berserker","summary":"grease-painted brawler laughing through every clubbing swing","flavor":"Grease-paint smeared into a permanent scream-grin, it laughs through every swing of its balloon-animal club.","desc":"Grease paint smears its face into a permanent scream-grin, garish red and white running where sweat's cut through it. It laughs the whole way through every swing of its balloon-animal club, delighted by its own violence like a birthday party trick that got out of hand.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Balloon-Animal Greataxe", "replaces": "Greataxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (1d12 + 4) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or be Frightened until the end of its next turn, unsettled by the Marauder's delighted laughter."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grease paint smeared into a permanent scream-grin, garish red and white."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Laughs the entire way through every swing, delighted by its own violence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its club is twisted from balloon-shapes, animals long since deflated and hardened."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sweat cuts pale tracks through the paint, revealing nothing underneath but more paint."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a torn party hat, somehow still jauntily perched mid-brawl."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Runs in loud, laughing packs, egging each other into wilder swings."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its laugh doesn't change pitch whether it's winning or badly losing a fight."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Downed, it keeps laughing for several more seconds, grin somehow widening further."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland", "any"],"activity":["laughing through every swing of a balloon-animal club, grease paint running with sweat", "smearing on fresh face paint before a fight, delighted by the ritual of it"]},{"name":"Toy-Chest Mimic","cr":2,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"toy-chest mimic whose lid is lined with teeth","flavor":"Looks like the best toy box in the playroom until the lid's teeth close on the hand that reaches in.","desc":"It sits invitingly open at the edge of the nursery, the best-looking toy chest in the room, lid propped just so. Reach in for whatever's glinting inside and the lid's hidden row of teeth closes tight around the offering wrist.","traits":{"note": "straight mimic-chassis reskin — lid-bite replaces the pseudopod slam, disguise-as-object unchanged"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its lid is painted with cheerful nursery-rhyme animals, chipped at the hinge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A music box inside plinks the same six notes whenever the lid opens."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's stuffed to bursting with genuinely nice toys, all slightly too clean."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Tooth marks score the inside rim from countless earlier, unlucky hands."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rocks gently on its own, side to side, like it's humming to itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, smaller mimic hides inside the first, nested like dolls, teeth first."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whatever it swallows this week reappears, weeks later, as a toy inside some other chest."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed with its lid shut, it detonates into every toy it ever ate, all biting at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["sitting invitingly open at the nursery's edge, lid propped just so, best toy in the room", "holding its lid ajar over one gleaming trinket, patient as a held breath, waiting for a hand"]},{"name":"Two-Faced Jester","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"doppelganger","model":"doppelganger","summary":"jester whose two painted faces switch mid-attack, unpredictably","flavor":"One painted face grins, the other weeps; it switches mid-sentence and mid-swing, and you never learn which is the lie.","desc":"One painted face grins ear to ear; the other, worn on the back of the same head, weeps black greasepaint tears. It switches mid-sentence and mid-swing between the two, and you never quite learn in time which face was telling the truth.","traits":{"note": "Whichever face is forward when it strikes tells you which lie you just believed.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Jester makes two Two-Faced Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Two-Faced Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) Bludgeoning damage, plus 3 (1d6) Psychic damage if this is the second hit against the same target this turn, as the swapped face lands a blow you swore was coming from the other side."}, {"name": "Read the Room", "replaces": "Read Thoughts", "text": "The Jester magically reads the surface thoughts of one creature within 30 ft. for as long as it concentrates, up to 1 minute, learning its intentions and current emotional state."}, {"name": "Swap the Grin (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Unsettling Visage (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Jester's faces flip mid-breath. Each creature within 15 ft. that can see it makes a DC 13 Wisdom save or is Frightened until the end of its next turn, unsure which expression to believe."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh greasepaint on both faces, still tacky, smudging wherever it touches."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It answers every question twice, once per face, and the answers never match."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Bells on its collar ring only when the weeping face is turned outward."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It insists on being called by two different names, one for each face."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its costume is stitched from mismatched halves, as if two jesters were sewn into one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rehearsing a routine with an invisible partner, arguing with itself in two voices."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Mirrors near it show only the weeping face, no matter which one it's actually wearing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck hard enough, the back face detaches and keeps fighting on its own, grinning."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["laughing on one face while the other quietly weeps, mid-conversation, mid-sentence", "circling a mark with painted grin forward, footsteps perfectly silent on the sawdust"]},{"name":"Marionette Master","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-captain","model":"bandit-captain","summary":"puppeteer who yanks strings to animate a squad mid-fight","flavor":"Works a cross of tangled strings that yank a squad of animate puppets into sudden, borrowed violence.","desc":"A cross of tangled strings hangs from both raised hands, each thread running taut to a slack-limbed puppet somewhere in the crowd. A single practiced yank animates the whole squad at once, borrowed limbs jerking into sudden, coordinated violence.","traits":{"note": "Cut enough strings and the whole animated squad drops at once, limp as cut marionettes.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Master makes two attacks with its Silvered Scimitar."}, {"name": "Silvered Scimitar", "replaces": "Scimitar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d6+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Popgun Pistol", "replaces": "Pistol", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/90 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) Piercing damage from a bright, toylike pistol that fires anything but a toy."}, {"name": "Yank the Cross", "text": "The Master gives the string-cross a sharp pull. Up to three puppet-strung creatures it controls each immediately make one melee attack against a target of the Master's choice, using the Master's attack bonus and their own damage die."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lost track of which strings lead to actual puppets and which to living captives."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One string in his cross leads to someone the party is looking for, still breathing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers to cut a specific string for a price, freeing whoever's tied to it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival puppeteer has cut three of his strings and he wants them back, violently."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His cross is snagged on wreckage and he needs hands to free it before the squad wakes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's teaching an apprentice to read the strings, and the apprentice keeps flinching at what they find."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One string runs off into empty air with no puppet on the other end that anyone can see."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's found a string leading straight to a member of the party's own wrist, and he's already pulling."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["standing with both arms raised, a cross of tangled strings running taut into the crowd", "testing a single thread with two fingers, watching some distant slack-limbed shape twitch in response"]},{"name":"Whirligig Horror","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"gorgon","model":"gorgon","summary":"spinning rotor-ride whose scythe gondolas scatter red confetti","flavor":"A carnival ride's rotor arms spin faster than sight, each seat a scythe-edged gondola scattering the crowd in red confetti.","desc":"A carnival ride's rotor arms spin faster than the eye can follow, each seat swapped out for a curved, scythe-edged gondola. It scatters the crowd in a spray of shredded red confetti with every full rotation, never once slowing its pace.","traits":{"note": "It cannot stop or reverse its spin mid-turn — approaching from directly beneath the hub is the only safe angle.", "actions": [{"name": "Gondola Scythe", "replaces": "Gore", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Slashing damage from a passing scythe-edged seat."}, {"name": "Confetti Burst (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Petrifying Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Horror's rotor throws a spray of razor-edged red paper in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 18 (4d8) Slashing damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rotor hub still plays a tinny fairground tune, warped and slowed by rust."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each gondola is painted a different cheerful color, all stained the same rust-red."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ticket stubs are wedged in its base gears, decades old, still fluttering."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It spins slightly faster whenever a crowd gathers to watch it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One gondola seat is empty and swinging, as if recently vacated."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second Whirligig stands dormant nearby, waiting for this one's tune to end."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its confetti, once it lands, doesn't decay — it just keeps accumulating, redder each season."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Damaged past half its hit points, its rotor speed doubles and its spray range doubles with it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["spinning its rotor arms at a blur over an empty midway, scythe-gondolas glinting", "scattering old confetti and older stains in a widening red ring with each rotation"]},{"name":"Sawdust Strongman","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Large","frame":"ettin","model":"ettin","summary":"two-headed circus strongman crushing while both heads lie","flavor":"A two-headed circus strongman act, each head shouting a different crowd-pleasing lie while the shared arms crush the truth out of you.","desc":"Two heads sit atop one broad circus-strongman's frame, each shouting a different crowd-pleasing lie over the other's voice. The shared arms crush regardless of which head is winning the argument, squeezing the truth — and everything else — out of whatever they've grabbed.","traits":{"note": "The two heads genuinely disagree, and provoking an argument between them costs it its next reaction.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Strongman makes two attacks, using Circus Battleaxe or Sideshow Morningstar in any combination."}, {"name": "Circus Battleaxe", "replaces": "Battleaxe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft. (with its long reach), one target. Hit: 14 (2d8+5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Sideshow Morningstar", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Piercing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded circus tattoos cover both arms, one boastful, one apologetic in tone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head wears a different mustache, both waxed to an identical curl."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head only ever tells the truth by accident, mid-argument."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a bent horseshoe as a trophy, still proudly showing it off."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The two heads have been mid-argument for so long neither remembers what started it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A third, smaller head is stitched under its collar, silent, listening to both."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "When both heads finally agree on something, it briefly grows a third arm to match."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Bloodied, the heads stop arguing and start coordinating, and it hits far harder for it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["flexing for a crowd that isn't there, both heads shouting over each other about the last feat", "gripping a bent iron bar, waiting to see which head's boast it has to make true first"]},{"name":"Balloon-Animal Chimera","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"cockatrice-regent","model":"cockatrice-regent","summary":"twisted-latex chimera that pops apart and re-knots itself","flavor":"Twisted latex shapes into a dog-headed, snake-necked menagerie that pops apart and re-knots itself around a wound.","desc":"Twisted latex forms itself into a dog-headed, snake-necked menagerie, squeaking faintly at every joint as it moves. Struck hard enough, it pops apart into loose twisted shapes — and simply re-knots itself back together around the wound a moment later.","traits":{"note": "It squeaks before every attack — a sharp ear gets a half-second warning.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chimera makes one Latex Bite attack and one Twist-Tie Talons attack."}, {"name": "Latex Bite", "replaces": "Petrifying Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d10+3) Piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or its speed is halved until the end of its next turn as latex residue stiffens the wound."}, {"name": "Twist-Tie Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 7 (2d4+2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Pop and Re-Knot", "text": "When the Chimera drops to half its hit points or below for the first time, it audibly pops apart and reforms 5 feet away, regaining 9 (2d8) hit points."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's tied in the bright reds and yellows of a birthday-party balloon animal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A leftover price tag still dangles from one twisted latex leg."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It deflates slightly overnight and has to be re-knotted each dawn by unseen hands."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Static makes its latex hide cling briefly to anything it brushes past."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It postures like a real menagerie animal, right down to a mimed roar."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two more, smaller, wobble in its wake, freshly twisted off its own trailing latex."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Popped completely, its latex scraps drift and re-knot themselves into some other shape entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overinflated by rough handling, it can be made to burst outright, dealing damage in a wide radius."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["squeaking faintly at every joint as it prowls, latex catching the fairground lights", "re-knotting a torn seam with a soft rubbery hiss, snake-neck testing the air"]},{"name":"Cotton-Candy Spinner Witch","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"green-hag","summary":"sugar-floss witch whose spun webs harden into glass thread","flavor":"Spins sugar-floss webs from a rusted machine-heart, luring children close before the floss hardens to glass thread.","desc":"A rusted machine-heart spins sugar-floss into long, drifting webs, sweet-smelling and pink, luring children close with the promise of a treat. The floss goes rigid the instant it's touched, hardening into threads of glass sharp enough to hold and to cut.","traits":{"note": "The floss is only soft before it's touched — once someone's caught, it's glass, and breaking free without help is nearly impossible.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Witch makes two Glass-Floss Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Glass-Floss Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Spin a Web (Spellcasting)", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Witch casts a spell, using her sugar-floss machine-heart as a focus, drawing from her innate fey magic (spell save DC 13)."}, {"name": "Sweet Snare", "text": "The Witch spins a drifting web of floss at one creature within 30 ft. that must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity save or be Restrained as the strand hardens to glass around it, taking 5 (1d10) Slashing damage on a failed save."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child from a nearby settlement has gone missing near her rusted machine, and someone's looking."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's spinning an unusually large web tonight, more floss than she'd need for one victim."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She'll trade a captured child's freedom for something sweeter she's been craving for years."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her machine-heart is sputtering and slowing, and she's growing desperate for anyone to feed it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival witch has stolen her best spinning-wheel spindle and she wants it retrieved."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's teaching her craft to a younger fey who flinches every time a web hardens."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of her glass-floss statues is still faintly breathing, trapped mid-scream, and she knows it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's identified a party member as this season's finest catch and has already begun spinning toward them."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["spinning sugar-floss from a rusted machine-heart, pink strands drifting toward the nearest child", "testing a half-finished web's give with one claw, judging exactly when to let it harden"]},{"name":"Painted Pony Revenant","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Large","frame":"warhorse-skeleton","model":"warhorse-skeleton","summary":"ghost carousel horse trampling an endless six-foot loop","flavor":"A carousel horse's ghost gallops the same six feet of track forever, trampling anyone standing where the pole once was.","desc":"A carousel horse's translucent ghost gallops the same six feet of empty track it always did, forever circling a brass pole that isn't there anymore. It tramples anyone foolish enough to stand where that pole used to be, blind to anything outside its old loop.","traits":{"note": "It cannot perceive anything outside its old six-foot loop — stepping just past the boundary makes you invisible to it.", "actions": [{"name": "Phantom Hooves", "replaces": "Hooves", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) Bludgeoning damage, and the damage is treated as Force damage against creatures standing where the old pole once stood."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its translucent hide flickers between full color and pale ghost-gray with each stride."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It gallops in perfect silence except for one recurring, tinny hoofbeat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded number is stenciled on its flank, from a ride ticket long since torn."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Grass within its loop refuses to grow, worn down to bare ghost-track dirt."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It occasionally rears at nothing, exactly where a carousel canopy would have hung."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second horse gallops the same loop half a beat behind it, never quite catching up."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stand still at the loop's center long enough and the whole vanished carousel becomes faintly visible."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Drag the missing pole back into place and it stops mid-stride, fully solid, utterly disoriented."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins", "grassland"],"activity":["galloping the same six feet of empty track forever, circling a brass pole that isn't there", "trampling the exact spot where the carousel's post used to stand, blind to everything else"]},{"name":"Rubber-Duck Leviathan","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Large","frame":"giant-crocodile","model":"giant-crocodile","summary":"cheerful bath-toy giant with a jaw unhinging past its grin","flavor":"An oversized bath toy bobs cheerfully atop the fairground's dunk-tank pool, jaw unhinging wider than its floating grin should allow.","desc":"An oversized bath toy bobs cheerfully atop the dunk-tank's dark water, rubber squeaking faintly with each gentle rise and fall. Its jaw unhinges far wider than its painted, floating grin should allow, opening a mouth built for something much bigger than a bathtub.","traits":{"note": "Its squeak gets louder right before it strikes — it cannot help but announce itself.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Leviathan makes one Unhinged Bite attack and one Rubber Tail attack."}, {"name": "Unhinged Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (2d10+4) Piercing damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller it is swallowed on a critical hit, exactly as a much larger predator would."}, {"name": "Rubber Tail", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) Bludgeoning damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bright yellow paint is chipped from a hundred carnival seasons of dunk-tank play."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It squeaks in a different pitch depending on which part of it gets struck."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint bath-time soap smell trails it wherever it swims."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted eyes are fixed in a permanent, unblinking, cheerful stare."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It floats a little too high in the water, buoyant even when it shouldn't be."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A smaller duckling version trails it, mimicking every unhinge of its jaw."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Pulled from the water, it deflates like an empty toy until it's returned to soak."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Provoked past half health, its jaw unhinges fully sideways and its reach doubles."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "sea", "coast"],"activity":["bobbing cheerfully atop the dunk-tank's dark water, rubber squeaking with each gentle rise", "unhinging its jaw slowly in the shallows, testing a width no bath toy should have"]},{"name":"Static Shock Clown","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"azer-pyromancer","model":"azer-pyromancer","summary":"crackling clown discharging balloon-rubbed static arcs","flavor":"Rubber-soled and crackling, it rubs a balloon against its own painted hide until arcs of blue static leap for the crowd.","desc":"Rubber-soled and crackling faintly at the fingertips, it rubs a balloon slowly against its own painted hide, building charge with obvious relish. Arcs of blue static leap for the nearest crowd the second it's built up enough, crackling like tiny lightning between fairground lights.","traits":{"note": "Metal armor or weapons draw its arcs first — it always strikes the shiniest target in reach.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Clown makes two Static Slap attacks or uses Balloon Discharge once."}, {"name": "Static Slap", "replaces": "Flame Burst", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Lightning damage, and the target can't take Reactions until the start of its next turn."}, {"name": "Balloon Discharge (Spellcasting)", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Clown discharges its built-up static as a spell, drawing on innate elemental magic (spell save DC 14) to blast a line of crackling arcs."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its rubber shoes squeak with every step, sparking faint blue static off the floor."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It never lets go of its balloon, rubbing it constantly even mid-combat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted grin lights up faintly whenever it discharges a big arc."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fairground lights flicker and dim whenever it's nearby, drawing on the same charge."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hair stands permanently on end, crackling faintly even at rest."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rubbing two balloons at once tonight, building charge visibly faster than usual."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Struck by its own arc, a nearby light bulb pops and briefly shows a second clown inside the filament."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully charged, it can discharge into standing water or metal railing, arcing to everyone touching it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["rubbing a balloon slowly against its own painted hide, building an audible crackling charge", "crouched near the fairground lights, arcs of blue static leaping between its fingertips"]},{"name":"Fun House Mirror-Stalker","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"mirror-dweller that stretches your reflection's arm to grab you","flavor":"Lives in the warped glass of every funhouse mirror, stretching your reflection's arm long enough to reach through and grab.","desc":"It lives in the warped glass of every funhouse mirror in the hall, watching your reflection lag a half-second behind your real movements. Given the chance, it stretches that reflected arm impossibly long, reaching straight through the glass to grab the real one.","traits":{"note": "It cannot leave the mirror it's bound to — destroying or covering the glass strands it entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Stalker makes two Reaching Reflection attacks."}, {"name": "Reaching Reflection", "replaces": "Wind Swipe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 15 ft. (through any mirror or reflective surface within range), one target. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Force damage."}, {"name": "Warp the Glass (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Vortex", "text": "Recharge 6. Every reflective surface within 30 ft. ripples violently. Each creature that can see its own reflection there makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or is Frightened and has its speed halved until the end of its next turn, disoriented by its own lagging image."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its warped reflection smiles a beat before the real face it's copying does."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only ever shows itself in the funhouse's most distorted, stretched mirror panel."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fog creeps across the glass whenever it's about to reach through."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mimics your gestures perfectly, except one finger, which always points at you."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Cracks spiderweb outward from its glass whenever it strains to reach further."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second Stalker watches from an adjacent mirror, waiting for the first to tire."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Break its mirror and its reflection keeps moving in every other glass surface in the hall, briefly."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully enraged, it can reach through any reflective surface at all, not just its own mirror."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["watching a reflection lag a half-second behind its owner's real movement in warped glass", "stretching one reflected arm slowly, testing how far the glass will let it reach through tonight"]},{"name":"Bearded Sideshow Prophet","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"cultist-fanatic","model":"cultist-fanatic","summary":"tent prophet whose tarot readings land as curses","flavor":"A tent-show oddity who reads futures off a deck of tarot-carnival cards, each prediction a curse dressed as a prize.","desc":"A tent-show oddity in a threadbare robe lays out a deck of tarot-carnival cards with slow, theatrical ceremony. Every prediction lands true and every prediction is a curse dressed up as a prize, delivered with the same warm, welcoming smile.","traits":{"note": "His predictions always come true — the cruelty is entirely in which true thing he chooses to say.", "actions": [{"name": "Pact Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Psychic damage as the blade carries the weight of a foretold ending."}, {"name": "Tarot-Carnival Reading (Spellcasting)", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Prophet casts a spell, drawing a card from his tarot-carnival deck as a focus for his innate fey magic (spell save DC 13), the card's image shaping the spell's effect."}, {"name": "True Prediction", "text": "The Prophet names one thing that will happen to a creature within 30 ft. within the next minute. That creature must succeed on a DC 13 Wisdom save or have Disadvantage on the first save or attack roll it makes related to that prediction, unnerved by its accuracy."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's read a card that names one party member's death this very night, and he won't say which."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers a free reading, but the deck seems to already know why the party has come."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A previous customer is camped outside his tent, refusing to leave until the prophecy is undone."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's missing a specific card from his deck and the reading can't finish without it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll trade a useful truth for one true secret the party is currently keeping."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's nervous tonight, drawing the same unlucky card three readings running."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His deck has a card in it depicting this exact tent, this exact conversation, already drawn."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He draws a card naming the parade route's next disaster and it's already begun happening outside."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["laying out tarot-carnival cards with slow, theatrical ceremony under a threadbare tent flap", "reading a fortune aloud with a warm smile, watching for which word lands hardest"]},{"name":"Cymbal-Monkey Swarm","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"swarm-of-stirges","model":"swarm-of-stirges","summary":"clashing wind-up monkey troop that shatters focus and eardrums","flavor":"A skittering troop of wind-up cymbal monkeys clashes brass in a deafening rhythm that shatters concentration and eardrums alike.","desc":"A skittering troop of wind-up cymbal monkeys clashes brass together in a deafening, arrhythmic din, key-wound arms never tiring. The noise alone shatters concentration and eardrums both, drowning out any warning of the bite that follows.","traits":{"note": "The noise itself imposes disadvantage on Wisdom checks made to hear anything else nearby.", "actions": [{"name": "Swarm of Clashing Cymbals", "replaces": "Swarm of Proboscises", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target in the swarm's space. Hit: 10 (4d4) Bludgeoning damage, or 5 (2d4) Bludgeoning damage if the swarm has half its hit points or fewer. A creature hit this way must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or be Deafened until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each monkey wears a slightly different faded vest, matching some long-gone act."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their key-wound backs never fully run down, ticking faintly between clashes."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They clash in unison for exactly three beats, then scatter into chaos."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One monkey's cymbals are cracked and rings a full note flatter than the rest."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They swarm toward any other loud noise, drawn to compete with it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A larger, lead monkey directs the troop's rhythm, cymbals raised like a conductor's baton."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Struck silent, the whole swarm freezes mid-clash until the ambient noise returns."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Pushed past half their number lost, the survivors clash twice as fast and twice as loud."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["clashing brass together in a deafening, arrhythmic din, key-wound arms never slowing", "skittering across a fairground floor in a troop, cymbals raised, hunting for something quiet to interrupt"]},{"name":"Puppet Theater Ghost","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"ghost","summary":"stage-ghost that casts bystanders into its unheard endless play","flavor":"Haunts a collapsed proscenium stage, casting itself as every character in a play only it can hear, dragging watchers into the script.","desc":"It haunts a collapsed proscenium stage, casting itself in every role of a play only it can hear, muttering lines to an empty house. Watch too long and you find yourself pulled into the script, a bystander suddenly given lines you never agreed to speak.","traits":{"note": "It only pulls in bystanders who linger to watch — leaving before the second act keeps you safely offstage.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ghost makes two Understudy's Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Understudy's Touch", "replaces": "Withering Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (4d6+1) Necrotic damage, the touch of a role no one wanted to play."}, {"name": "Backstage Slip", "replaces": "Etherealness", "text": "The Ghost slips into the wings between one line and the next, entering the Ethereal Plane, unreachable until it steps back onstage."}, {"name": "Curtain Call", "replaces": "Horrifying Visage", "text": "The Ghost reveals the true, ruined face beneath its greasepaint. Each creature within 60 ft. that can see it makes a DC 13 Wisdom save or is Frightened for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns."}, {"name": "Give Them a Role (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Possession (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Ghost casts a character's lines into one creature within 5 ft., who must succeed on a DC 13 Charisma save or be Possessed by the Ghost, exactly as it would seize any other body to finish its play."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been performing the same three lines to an empty house every night for a decade."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A missing performer's understudy script sits on the stage, and it wants someone to read it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's cast a party member as the play's villain and won't release the role until the scene ends."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a genuinely useful secret if someone will simply watch its play through to the end."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living actor is trapped backstage, refusing to break character, terrified of what happens if he does."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rewriting the third act tonight, and the new ending is considerably bloodier."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The play it performs describes, scene for scene, exactly what's about to happen to whoever's watching."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided the party has wandered into its final scene, and the curtain is already falling."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["casting itself in every role of a play only it can hear, muttering lines to an empty house", "gesturing grandly to unseen scenery on a collapsed proscenium stage, awaiting its cue"]},{"name":"Shooting-Gallery Marksman","cr":5,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"guard-captain","summary":"gallery marksman who swapped tin ducks for screaming real ones","flavor":"Never misses a moving target; his rifle's tin ducks have been replaced with real, screaming ones for practice.","desc":"He tracks every moving target along the gallery's rail with a rifle that never misses, squinting down the sight with a carnival worker's easy grin. The tin ducks on his stand have all been swapped out for something that screams when it's hit.","traits":{"note": "He never fires at a stationary target — moving in a straight line only makes it easier for him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Marksman makes two attacks, using Gallery Javelin or Trick-Shot Longsword in any combination."}, {"name": "Gallery Javelin", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft., one target. Hit: 9 (2d6+2) Piercing damage, with Advantage if the target moved at least 10 ft. this turn."}, {"name": "Trick-Shot Longsword", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) Slashing damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His stand's prize shelf is stacked with trophies no one alive claimed fairly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He calls every shot aloud beforehand, and he's never once been wrong."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His rifle sight is a chipped, painted tin duck's eye, oddly precise."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers free shots to children, then quietly counts theirs against his tally too."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He reloads with a flourish, milking the crowd's attention before every shot."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second marksman runs the stall opposite, and the two are keeping a running, deadly score."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every prize on his shelf turns and watches you the moment his sight lines up."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Down to his last few shots, he stops calling them, and stops missing entirely."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["tracking a moving target along the gallery's rail with a rifle that never misses", "squinting down the sight with a carnival worker's easy grin, tin ducks all swapped for something worse"]},{"name":"Cackling Music-Box Horror","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"mage","model":"mage","summary":"ballerina automaton whose backward lullaby ages listeners down","flavor":"A brass ballerina spins atop a box that plays a lullaby backward, and every reversed note peels a year off whoever listens.","desc":"A brass ballerina spins atop an ornate box, arms frozen in a pirouette, playing a lullaby run backward note by note. Every reversed chime peels a year off whoever's still listening, the tune getting sweeter as its audience gets younger and smaller.","traits":{"note": "Its lullaby only ages down those who keep listening — walking away mid-song breaks the effect harmlessly.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes two Brass Pirouette attacks."}, {"name": "Brass Pirouette", "replaces": "Arcane Burst", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Force damage from a spinning brass limb."}, {"name": "Backward Lullaby (Spellcasting)", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Horror plays its reversed tune as a spell, drawing on its innate construct magic (spell save DC 14). Each creature within 30 ft. that can hear it makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or is charmed and drawn 10 feet closer, hungry for the next note."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its brass finish is dulled by decades of small, careless fingerprints."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The lullaby's backward notes almost, but never quite, resolve into something recognizable."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pirouette never completes a full turn, snagging on the same worn gear each time."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The box beneath the ballerina is warm to the touch, faintly humming even in silence."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile chips a little more with every repetition of the tune."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It winds itself tighter the longer anyone listens, the melody creeping faster."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Play the tune forward on purpose and it visibly ages instead, brass tarnishing by the second."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully wound, its lullaby reaches twice as far and ages its listeners twice as fast."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["spinning atop an ornate box, arms frozen in a pirouette, playing a lullaby run backward", "letting the reversed tune's last note hang in the air, watching who's still young enough to listen"]},{"name":"The Understudy Doppel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"mask-cycling mimic wearing the faces of the fair's dead","flavor":"Wears the faces of everyone who's ever died at the fair, cycling masks mid-conversation until you can't remember who you were talking to.","desc":"It wears the borrowed faces of everyone who's ever died at the fair, cycling through them mid-conversation without warning. One moment it's speaking with a voice you recognize; the next it's someone else entirely, and you've lost track of who you were talking to.","traits":{"note": "It always keeps one true face hidden — killing it reveals whichever face it wore first tonight.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Doppel makes two Borrowed Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Borrowed Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 10 (2d6+3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Cycling Masks", "replaces": "Snake Hair", "text": "Each creature within 5 ft. of the Doppel that can see its face when it swaps masks makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or is Frightened until the end of its next turn, briefly certain it's looking at someone else entirely."}, {"name": "Envenomed Grin", "replaces": "Poison Ray", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 30 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (3d8+3) Poison damage as a borrowed smile curdles into something venomous."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's currently wearing the face of someone the party is actively searching for."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A family at the fair is offering a reward for whoever's been wearing their dead child's face."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's collecting one more face tonight and has already chosen its next mark from the crowd."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It'll trade the truth about someone's death for a fresh face to add to its collection."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Two of its masks are fighting each other for control mid-conversation, and it's losing the argument."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown attached to one particular mask and is reluctant to cycle away from it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of its faces belongs to someone in the party who hasn't died yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's just put on the face of the fair's original owner, and everyone here still obeys that face."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["cycling through borrowed faces mid-conversation, wearing someone you almost recognized a moment ago", "testing a new mask against a fogged mirror shard, discarding it for one that fits better"]},{"name":"Pinwheel Djinn","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Elemental","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"invisible-stalker","summary":"pinwheel-bound genie whose wishes twist gaudy and cruel","flavor":"Bound into a spinning pinwheel toy, it grants wishes that always twist back gaudy and cruel, true to the letter and never the spirit.","desc":"Bound into a spinning pinwheel toy, its shape blurs into a smear of color with every gust, genie features flickering in and out of the spin. It grants wishes gladly and grants them exactly as spoken — twisted gaudy and cruel, true to the letter and never once to the spirit.","traits":{"note": "Every wish it grants is worded exactly as spoken, never as meant — precise phrasing is the only real defense.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Djinn makes two Pinwheel Gust attacks."}, {"name": "Pinwheel Gust", "replaces": "Wind Swipe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Force damage."}, {"name": "Granted Wish (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Vortex", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Djinn grants the nearest spoken wish, twisting it cruelly literal. One creature within 30 ft. makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or is affected by a minor, gaudy transfiguration for 1 minute (no mechanical penalty beyond Disadvantage on Charisma checks) and takes 14 (4d6) Force damage as the wish is forced true."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pinwheel body is garish plastic, spinning even in dead-still air."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It grants wishes to anyone who says the word aloud, invited or not."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its features only resolve clearly for half a second at the pinwheel's slowest point."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's bound by a ribbon to a specific stall, unable to drift more than a few yards."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It repeats every wish back verbatim before granting it, savoring the wording."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's granted itself a wish once already tonight, and is visibly pleased with the result."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wishes granted near it seem to come slightly true for everyone nearby, not just the speaker."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Freed from its ribbon, it can grant a wish on anyone within sight, not just those who ask."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "sky"],"activity":["blurring into a smear of color with every gust, genie features flickering in and out of the spin", "granting a passing wish gladly, already savoring the gaudy, cruel shape it's about to take"]},{"name":"Toy Soldier Colonel","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"warrior-veteran","model":"warrior-veteran","summary":"clockwork colonel drilling a squad of key-wound infantry","flavor":"Commands a squad of wind-up infantry with parade-ground precision, keys still turning in every subordinate's back.","desc":"It drills a squad of wind-up infantry with crisp, parade-ground precision, barking orders in a tinny, amplified voice. Keys still turn slowly in every subordinate's back as they march, and the Colonel's own key never seems to run down.","traits":{"note": "Its own key never runs down — only the infantry it commands can be disabled by stopping their keys.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colonel makes two attacks, using Parade Greatsword or Drill Crossbow in any combination."}, {"name": "Parade Greatsword", "replaces": "Greatsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 15 (2d6+8) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Drill Crossbow", "replaces": "Heavy Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 100/400 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d10+2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Barked Order", "text": "The Colonel shouts a command. Up to two wind-up infantry it can see immediately move up to their speed and make one attack, and gain a +1 bonus to that attack roll for the parade-ground precision of the order."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its uniform paint is chipped at every joint, but its posture never slackens."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It reviews its troops nightly whether or not any troops remain standing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice crackles like an old phonograph, tinny and strangely warm."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every subordinate's key is wound to the exact same tempo as its marching drum."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It salutes anything larger than itself before deciding whether to attack it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's drilling a second squad tonight, freshly wound, eager to prove themselves in formation."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Wind its own key by hand and it briefly follows your orders instead of giving its own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "With half its squad destroyed, it stops drilling and personally charges the line, all discipline abandoned."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["drilling a squad of wind-up infantry with crisp, parade-ground precision, keys turning in every back", "barking amplified orders in a tinny voice, marching its formation past a reviewing stand no one built"]},{"name":"Bell-Tower Puppet","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"stone-golem","model":"stone-golem","summary":"clock-tower automaton whose hourly strike finds softer targets","flavor":"A cathedral-clock automaton strikes the hour on the crowd below, its bronze mallet finding softer targets than the bell.","desc":"A cathedral-clock automaton looms at the top of its tower, bronze mallet raised, gears ticking down toward the hour. When it strikes, the mallet swings down onto the crowd below rather than the bell, finding softer targets than bronze.","traits":{"note": "It only swings on the hour or the half — timing an approach between chimes avoids the mallet entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Puppet makes two Bronze Mallet attacks."}, {"name": "Bronze Mallet", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 16 (2d10+5) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Toll the Hour", "replaces": "Force Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 60 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (3d8+1) Force damage as the tower's chime rings out as a weapon."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its bronze surfaces are green with age, gears visible through cracked casing."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The tower's clock face is stopped forever at the same hour it first struck someone."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It winds down slightly between chimes, moving noticeably slower just after striking."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pigeons nest undisturbed in its joints, indifferent to the mallet swinging nearby."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its gears audibly speed up in the minutes before each hour strikes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, smaller puppet handles the quarter-hour chimes, less dangerous but faster."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Time near the tower runs slightly fast, the hour arriving sooner than anywhere else in town."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck hard enough, it rings every hour it's ever skipped at once, swinging wildly and repeatedly."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["looming atop its tower, bronze mallet raised, gears ticking down steadily toward the hour", "tracking the crowd below with painted eyes, timing its next strike to the coming chime"]},{"name":"Rictus Ringleader","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","model":"bugbear-stalker-strangler","summary":"whip-cracking sideshow boss whose grin is stitched shut","flavor":"A whip-cracking sideshow boss whose smile is stitched, not painted, and whose acts always end with someone missing.","desc":"A whip-cracking sideshow boss struts the ring in a tattered ringmaster's coat, smile stitched permanently into place rather than painted on. Every act it runs ends the same way — with someone from the crowd missing by the time the lights come back up.","traits":{"note": "His stitched smile can't be read for lies or truth by any normal means — magic that detects deception simply fails on him.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Ringleader makes two attacks, using Ringmaster's Whip or Garrote in any combination."}, {"name": "Ringmaster's Whip", "replaces": "Morningstar", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. (whip's reach), one target. Hit: 12 (2d8+3) Slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a DC 14 Strength save or be pulled 10 feet toward the Ringleader."}, {"name": "Strangle", "replaces": "Strangle (Garrote)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Necrotic damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 15). Until the grapple ends, the target is Restrained and the Ringleader can't Strangle another target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's run tonight's headcount twice and someone in the party's group doesn't match either tally."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party front-row seats, which is exactly how his last act's victims were chosen."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A performer under his coat has begged the party, in whispers, to get her out before the finale."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's short one act for the closing show and has already sized up the party as replacements."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He'll release someone's missing companion if the party performs one act flawlessly in the ring."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "His whip has been unusually quiet tonight, like he's saving something for later."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He remembers everyone who's ever gone missing at the fair, and lists their names conversationally."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided this show's missing person will be picked from the party, and the lights are dimming already."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["strutting the ring in a tattered ringmaster's coat, smile stitched permanently into place", "cracking a whip once for attention, already counting who's missing from tonight's audience"]},{"name":"Sugar-Spun Basilisk","cr":6,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"basilisk","model":"basilisk","summary":"candy-eyed basilisk that crystallizes prey into hard candy","flavor":"Gazes at foes with candy-glass eyes, and whatever it stares at slowly crystallizes into a life-size hard-candy statue.","desc":"Candy-glass eyes catch the fairground lights in a hard, glittering stare, its scaled hide the exact hue of hard-shell candy. Whatever it looks at long enough stops moving, slowly crystallizing into a life-size sugar statue, sweet and brittle and still.","traits":{"note": "Its gaze only crystallizes what stares back — approaching with eyes averted denies it the attack entirely.", "actions": [{"name": "Candy-Glass Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 8 (1d8+4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage from crystallizing venom."}, {"name": "Sugared Gaze", "text": "At the start of each of its turns, the Basilisk can force one creature within 30 ft. who can see its eyes to make a DC 13 Constitution save. On a failure, the target's speed is halved as its skin begins hardening to hard candy; on a third cumulative failure against this effect, the target is Restrained by its own crystallizing body until freed."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its scales catch light in bright hard-candy reds, greens, and yellows."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint sugary smell follows it, sweet enough to draw flies even from its stony victims."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its half-crystallized statues are perfectly edible, if anyone's desperate or foolish enough."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It blinks slowly, deliberately, savoring each half-second of contact before the gaze takes hold."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tail leaves a faint sticky sheen wherever it drags across the ground."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A cluster of fully crystallized former victims stands nearby, glittering, useful as cover or warning."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its statues slowly soften back to flesh if kept somewhere warm and dark long enough."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully cornered, its gaze crystallizes on a single failed save instead of building over several."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "cave"],"activity":["catching the fairground lights in a hard, glittering stare, hide the exact hue of hard-shell candy", "holding perfectly still near a row of half-crystallized shapes, waiting for something new to look at"]},{"name":"Popcorn Machine Golem","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"overheated popcorn-machine golem hailing scalding kernels","flavor":"Overheated kernels burst from its chest cavity in a scalding, blinding hail while its stitched apron soaks up the mess.","desc":"Overheated kernels burst from a cavity in its chest in a scalding, blinding hail, steam venting from every stitched seam of its apron. It doesn't seem to notice the mess it makes, popping and hissing louder the angrier it gets.","traits":{"note": "It grows louder and more dangerous the longer a fight runs — cooling it down mid-combat isn't possible.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Golem makes two Scalding Slam attacks."}, {"name": "Scalding Slam", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) Bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage from the overheated casing."}, {"name": "Kernel Hail (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Golem's chest cavity bursts open. Each creature within 15 ft. makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 17 (5d6) Fire damage on a failure, or half as much on a success, as scalding kernels rain outward."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stitched apron is scorched black in patches from repeated overheating."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fresh popcorn smell fills the air around it even mid-fight, oddly appetizing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steam hisses louder from whichever seam took the last hit."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It occasionally pauses, as if listening for a bell that means the batch is done."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chest cavity glows faintly orange when its kernels are close to bursting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second, smaller unit trails it, sweeping up spilled kernels obsessively."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its spilled kernels, left overnight, sprout small, twitching kernel-golems of their own."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Overheated past half its hit points, its Kernel Hail no longer needs to recharge at all."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["venting steam from every stitched seam of its apron, kernels bursting from its chest in scalding hail", "hissing louder the angrier it gets, oblivious to the mess it's making across the midway"]},{"name":"Wax Figure Doppelganger","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"yuan-ti-abomination","model":"yuan-ti-abomination","summary":"wax-museum figure that melts into a dozen grasping arms","flavor":"Stands frozen among a wax museum's other figures until a hand brushes too close, then melts into a dozen grasping arms.","desc":"It stands frozen among a museum's other waxwork figures, posture perfect, expression serene, indistinguishable at a glance from the rest. The instant a hand brushes too close, the wax runs and reshapes into a dozen grasping, half-melted arms.","traits":{"note": "It cannot move until touched or provoked — a careful eye can spot the one figure that never quite settles into stillness.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Doppelganger makes one Melting Bite attack and one Grasping Constrict attack."}, {"name": "Melting Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d8+2) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Grasping Constrict", "replaces": "Constrict", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 10 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d10+2) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is Grappled (escape DC 14) by a dozen half-melted wax arms."}, {"name": "Wax Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Poison Spray (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Doppelganger sprays molten wax in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 14 Dexterity save, taking 16 (3d10) Fire damage and being Restrained until the wax cools (escape DC 12) on a failure, or half damage and no restraint on a success."}, {"name": "Waxwork Casting (Yuan-ti Form Only)", "replaces": "Spellcasting (Yuan-ti Form Only)", "text": "While reshaped into its melted, many-armed form, the Doppelganger can cast a spell drawn from its innate fey-touched magic (spell save DC 14)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its waxwork posture is flawless, indistinguishable from the real figures beside it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint candle-wax smell clings to the whole gallery it hides in."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its expression softens, very slightly, the longer it holds still watching a visitor."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Melted wax pools slowly beneath it even at rest, refilling itself by morning."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mimics whichever famous figure's plinth it's been left standing on."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second figure nearby is also not quite what it appears, and the two seem to coordinate."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Melted down fully, it reforms overnight into a completely different figure's likeness."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Fully melted mid-fight, its reach and grasping-arm count both increase for the rest of the encounter."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing frozen among a museum's other waxwork figures, posture perfect, expression serene", "holding a pose in dim gallery light, waiting for a hand to brush close enough to reach"]},{"name":"Grand Prize Chimera","cr":7,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"chimera","model":"chimera","summary":"three-headed stuffed-prize chimera, each head still tagged","flavor":"Stitched from three unclaimed stuffed-animal prizes, each head still wears its raffle tag and its own hunger.","desc":"Three unclaimed stuffed-animal prizes have fused into one lurching, stitched-together body, and each head still wears its own faded raffle tag. Every head hungers separately, and all three seem to agree on exactly one thing: it wants you closer.","traits":{"note": "Each head has its own temperament — the three genuinely disagree on tactics, which sometimes buys a round of confusion.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Chimera makes three attacks: one Stuffed Bite, one Plush Claw, and one Prize Ram."}, {"name": "Stuffed Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 13 (2d8+4) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Plush Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 11 (2d6+4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Prize Ram", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 14 (2d10+3) Bludgeoning damage."}, {"name": "Confetti Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One head exhales a blast of razor confetti and stuffing in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 21 (6d6) Slashing damage on a failure, or half as much on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head's raffle tag lists a different unclaimed booth, torn at the same jagged edge."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stitching leaks stuffing steadily, trailing white tufts wherever it lurches."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The three heads bicker constantly over which of them gets the next bite."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It smells faintly of the prize booth's cheap synthetic fur, even up close."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head is noticeably more threadbare and vicious than the other two."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A fourth, half-formed head is stitched loosely at its shoulder, twitching but silent."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its three heads occasionally speak in unison, in a child's voice none of them should have."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "With any one head destroyed, the remaining two attack with reckless, uncoordinated fury."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["lurching forward on a stitched, three-headed frame, each head still wearing its own faded raffle tag", "hungering separately with all three heads, agreeing on exactly one thing: getting closer"]},{"name":"Runaway Roller-Coaster Wyrm","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"derailed coaster track turned serpent, cars clacking as teeth","flavor":"A derailed coaster track has grown a serpentine mind of its own, its cars now teeth clacking down an endless, screaming loop.","desc":"A derailed length of coaster track has coiled itself into a long, serpentine body, rusted cars still bolted along its spine like segmented plates. Those cars have become its teeth, clacking down an endless loop with a scream of metal that never quite stops echoing.","traits":{"note": "reach-heavy chassis reflavor — the 'breath' becomes a forward track-lurch that covers ground instead of an elemental cone"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded paint still reads 'FASTEST RIDE IN THE KINGDOM' along its flank."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Safety bars dangle from its underside, swinging loose with every twist."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only ever loops clockwise, gouging the same rut deeper each pass."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A recorded voice inside it still announces 'keep hands and arms inside.'"}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ticket stubs are lodged between its plates like scales of paper."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows near empty queue lines, as if still waiting for a full car."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its screech plays backward the instant before it derails toward a new victim."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-loop, its cars scatter and keep looping alone, riderless and still hungry."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["looping the same derailed circuit at speed, cars screaming metal on metal", "hunting the fairground rails for a rider to drag aboard for one final lap"]},{"name":"Grand Guignol Actor","cr":8,"role":"high","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"vampire-nightbringer","model":"vampire-nightbringer","summary":"undead stage actor whose prop dagger's blood is now real","flavor":"Died mid-performance and never left the stage, reciting the same monologue while the blood in his prop dagger turns real.","desc":"He died mid-monologue and never left the stage, reciting the same lines night after night to a house long since emptied. The prop dagger in his hand was always meant to be fake — but the blood welling from his co-star's chest now is unmistakably real.","traits":{"note": "He resets to his opening line whenever the fight goes badly for him — the scene restarts, and so does his confidence.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Actor makes two attacks, only one of which can be Prop Dagger."}, {"name": "Prop Dagger", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Necrotic damage. The wound bleeds real stage-blood; the target's Hit Point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage dealt until the target finishes a Long Rest."}, {"name": "Curtain Call", "replaces": "Shadow Strike", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 14 (3d6 + 4) Psychic damage as the Actor delivers his final line directly into the target's mind. If this reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, the target instead drops to 1 Hit Point, collapses as if dead for dramatic effect, and the Actor gains temporary advantage believing the scene is over."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He begs the party to be his scene partner, and the role comes with real stakes."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A living understudy is trapped backstage, waiting for her cue to finally escape."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's misplaced his 'good' dagger and is using a genuinely lethal replacement prop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "An empty seat in the front row is reserved, engraved, for whoever kills him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He owes his understudy a death scene he keeps refusing to actually perform."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's rehearsing a new act, one he insists the party unknowingly wrote for him."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "He remembers dying differently every night, and each version bleeds into the room."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "His understudy has learned every line and is coming to finally take the stage."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["reciting the same dying monologue to an audience of empty velvet seats", "polishing a prop dagger whose blade weeps something no longer fake"]},{"name":"Hedge-Maze Minotaur","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","model":"minotaur-of-the-horned-king","summary":"topiary-bull minotaur that reshapes the maze to trap guests","flavor":"Grown from hedge-clippings into a living topiary bull, it reshapes the maze walls behind guests so no path leads back out.","desc":"Clipped hedge-leaves and woody bull horns make up its shifting green bulk, twigs cracking softly with every heavy step through the maze. It reshapes the hedge walls behind anyone foolish enough to enter, closing off the path back the way they came.","traits":{"note": "Every round it isn't attacking, a section of maze wall nearby quietly grows shut, cutting off one escape route.", "actions": [{"name": "Shears of the Green King", "replaces": "Abyssal Glaive", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d12 + 5) Slashing damage. On a hit, the Minotaur may cause a hedge wall within 30 feet to grow shut, blocking one corridor of its choosing until the Minotaur dies."}, {"name": "Topiary Gore (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Gore (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 24 (4d8 + 6) Piercing damage, and the target is pushed 15 feet into the nearest hedge wall, which closes around it; the target is Restrained (escape DC 16) until it or an ally spends an action tearing the greenery free."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its horns are woven from thorn-branch, not bone, and bleed green sap when nicked."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footfalls leave perfect hoofprints of turned soil in the gravel path."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a small pair of hand-shears alongside its great ones, for detail work."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Songbirds nest, unbothered, in the leafy plates along its back."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums the same three-note tune the whole maze seems to have memorized."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It never enters a hedge corridor it hasn't already reshaped in its favor."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The maze's paths on the far side of it don't match any map made before today."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killing it lets the whole maze collapse inward at once, hedges swallowing every path."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "urban"],"activity":["trimming a hedge wall into a new dead end, humming while it works", "standing at a fork in the maze, waiting to see which way guests choose wrong"]},{"name":"The Barker's Voice","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"grell","model":"grell","summary":"omnipresent barker-voice hiding a tentacled body in speaker horns","flavor":"A disembodied, amplified voice that fills the fairground from every direction, its tentacled true body hidden inside the speaker horns.","desc":"An amplified voice fills the whole fairground at once, warm and welcoming, seeming to come from every direction and none. Its true body — a knot of tentacles — hides folded inside the speaker horns mounted overhead, waiting for the crowd to gather close enough.","traits":{"note": "Its voice always sounds like it's coming from somewhere else — Perception checks to locate its true body before it attacks take a penalty.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Barker's Voice makes one Speaker-Horn Bite attack and uses Paralyzing Applause."}, {"name": "Speaker-Horn Bite", "replaces": "Beak", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Paralyzing Applause", "replaces": "Paralyzing Tentacles", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 15 ft., against one creature the Barker can see. Hit: The target is grappled (escape DC 16) and Restrained until the grapple ends, drowned in a wall of cheerful, deafening applause that leaves it unable to hear any other sound."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's announcing a show the party is already, unknowingly, the headliners of."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A vendor begs the party to shut it up before the noise draws a bigger crowd."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a genuinely useful piece of information, but only mid-advertisement."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's child wandered toward its horns, drawn by the friendly voice."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's selling tickets to an event that starts the moment enough people gather."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun advertising the party's names specifically, to draw a bigger house."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its voice is starting to answer questions the party hasn't asked out loud yet."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's called the whole fairground to converge on this one spot, all at once."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["calling out ticket prices from every speaker horn at once, warm and inviting", "luring a straggler closer to the tent with promises of the 'best show yet'"]},{"name":"Wheel-of-Fortune Oracle","cr":9,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"rigged fortune-wheel witch who collects on every fated spin","flavor":"Spins a rigged wheel that decides not prizes but fates, and every guest who plays owes her whatever the wheel names.","desc":"She spins a garish, rigged wheel with a showman's flourish, painted wedges promising prizes that never quite come up. The wheel doesn't decide winnings — it decides fates, and every guest who plays owes her whatever name lands under the pointer.","traits":{"note": "She never spins the wheel for herself in combat — she only ever collects on debts already owed, which makes her patient.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Oracle makes two Rigged Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Rigged Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 15 (3d6 + 5) Necrotic damage."}, {"name": "Spin the Wheel", "replaces": "Plane", "text": "Ranged Spell Attack: +9, range 60 ft. Hit: 21 (6d6) Force damage as a painted wedge flares and lands. On a hit, the Oracle names a fate: the target has Disadvantage on the next save it makes before the end of its next turn, its wager already spent."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Oracle casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components: At will: minor illusion, disguise self. 2/day each: bestow curse, plane shift (self only)."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She holds a debt on someone the party knows, payable the next time the wheel stops."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers the party a spin, and the wheel's wedges list prices too high to ignore."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guest is begging to renegotiate a fate she's already collected on once before."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her ledger lists a name the party recognizes, marked paid in a currency unclear."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's short one more spin to close her books for the season, and she wants it now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's rigged tonight's wheel specifically around a fate she wants the party to land on."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wheel's pointer keeps landing on wedges that describe the party's next few hours."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's betting her whole ledger on one spin, and she's invited the party to watch it fall."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["spinning her painted wheel for a nervous guest, promising a prize that isn't one", "recording a debt in a ledger the moment the wheel's pointer stops"]},{"name":"Tilt-a-Whirl Horror","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"cloaker","model":"cloaker","summary":"spinning ride-maw that disorients riders while digesting them","flavor":"Folds its riders into a spinning cup-shaped maw, disorientation and gravity doing half the digesting for it.","desc":"Its body folds and unfolds like a spinning ride car, cup-shaped and hollow, whirling faster the longer a victim struggles inside it. Disorientation does half the work for it, digestion following close behind as the spin never lets up.","traits":{"note": "The longer a victim struggles inside it, the faster it spins — grappled creatures take escalating disadvantage the longer they stay caught.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Horror makes one Fold attack and uses Whirl if a creature is grappled."}, {"name": "Fold", "replaces": "Attach", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: The target is grappled (escape DC 15) and Restrained, folded into the Horror's spinning cup-shaped body."}, {"name": "Whirl", "replaces": "Tail", "text": "Each creature grappled by the Horror takes 16 (3d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage as it spins faster, and must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or have the Poisoned condition until the spin stops, sick from the endless turning."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its paint is bright candy-stripe, chipped along every seam where it folds shut."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A recorded safety announcement loops faintly from somewhere deep in its gears."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only wakes when weight settles fully onto its platform, never before."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loose tickets and popped balloons are wedged into its spinning joints."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums a cheerful mechanical tune the whole time it's folding someone shut."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows to a near-stop for stragglers who look hesitant, patient as a lure."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Things that come back out of it are never quite facing the direction they went in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed mid-spin, it flings everything still inside it in one violent final arc."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["spinning slow and empty at the edge of the midway, cup-shaped and inviting", "folding shut around a stray cat that wandered too close to its ride platform"]},{"name":"Effigy of the Midway","cr":10,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"clay-golem","model":"clay-golem","summary":"towering lost-and-found effigy animated by collected grudges","flavor":"A towering scarecrow-king built from every unclaimed prize and lost mitten, animated by the fair's collected grudges.","desc":"A towering scarecrow-king shape rises from a heap of every unclaimed prize and lost mitten the fair's ever collected, straw limbs bulging with old grudges. It moves with the slow, deliberate weight of something that's been building for years, finally standing up.","traits":{"note": "It remembers every guest who ever cheated a game here — it recognizes them on sight and moves toward them first.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Effigy makes two Grudge-Fist attacks."}, {"name": "Grudge-Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target has taken anything from a fairground booth without paying for it (as the DM judges), this attack deals an extra 9 (2d8) damage."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A vendor swears it only ever comes for people who've stolen from her booth."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's carrying a lost mitten the party recognizes as belonging to someone missing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A child's unclaimed prize is buried somewhere in its straw, still wanted badly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's built from every grudge this season, and one of them is freshly, obviously the party's."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone offers to pay off an old debt if the party can make it stand down first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown a full head taller overnight, fed by a fresh wave of unresolved complaints."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Pieces of it whisper old arguments back verbatim when struck hard enough."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroying it scatters every grudge it held loose across the fairground at once, unclaimed again."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing motionless at the fairground's edge, heaped with unclaimed prizes", "lumbering toward a booth that once refused to pay out a rigged win"]},{"name":"Puppet King's Herald","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"satyr-revelmaster","model":"satyr-revelmaster","summary":"herald whose compelling fanfare herds crowds toward danger","flavor":"Announces the Ringmaster's arrivals with a fanfare that compels the crowd to applaud even as it herds them toward the tents.","desc":"A herald in gaudy court colors raises a brass horn and announces the Ringmaster's arrival with a fanfare that swells louder than it should. The crowd applauds despite themselves, compelled forward, cheering their own steps toward the waiting tents.","traits":{"note": "Anyone forced to applaud by its fanfare can't ready a reaction on their next turn — clapping hands can't hold a weapon.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Herald makes two Painted Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Painted Blade", "replaces": "Prance", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Compelling Fanfare (Recharge 4-6)", "replaces": "Fey Melody (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. Each creature within 30 feet that can hear the Herald's horn makes a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure, a creature must use its reaction to applaud and move 10 feet toward the Herald's chosen direction; on a success it's merely Charmed until the start of the Herald's next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's herding a crowd of guests toward a tent none of them chose to enter."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A performer begs the party to silence its horn before the next act is announced."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's announcing the party by name, and the crowd starts applauding before they arrive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's been swept along by the fanfare for three days and can't recall stopping."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a summons for the Ringmaster's arrival that the party would rather not deliver."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's rehearsing a fanfare specifically shaped to march this crowd somewhere new."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The applause it compels keeps going even after the party leaves the sound of it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Its horn is building toward one final fanfare loud enough to summon its master directly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["raising a brass horn to announce an arrival no one asked to attend", "marching the crowd forward in perfect step, applauding despite themselves"]},{"name":"Hall of Mirrors Horror","cr":11,"role":"high","type":"Aberration","size":"Large","frame":"mind-thief-arcanist","model":"mind-thief-arcanist","summary":"hive-minded shattered mirror-hall, every shard a coordinated attacker","flavor":"A shattered fun-house hallway given a hive mind, each shard-reflection a separate, coordinated attacker.","desc":"A shattered fun-house hallway lines both walls in broken glass, every fragment catching a slightly different angle of the room. Each shard-reflection moves and strikes on its own, all of them coordinated by a single mind that shares none of your blind spots.","traits":{"note": "hive-mind flavor over the base chassis's telepathic link — no flanking blind spot exists against it since every shard sees a different angle"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each shard reflects a slightly different, distorted angle of whoever stands before it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Broken glass crunches underfoot the whole length of the fun-house corridor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Faded funhouse paint frames every pane, cheerful colors around jagged edges."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It moves shard by shard, never all at once, giving the illusion of stillness."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Every reflection blinks in unison a half-second after the real thing does."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It rearranges which shards act first depending on which target looks most rattled."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One shard, unbroken, shows a version of the room that isn't the one you're standing in."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Shattered fully, every fragment keeps twitching on the floor, each still watching separately."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["watching a hallway of broken glass ripple as every shard turns to look at once", "coordinating its shard-reflections to box in a lone straggler between two walls"]},{"name":"Grandfather Clock Devourer","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"antique clock-golem whose chime ages victims to dust","flavor":"An antique carnival clock swallows time itself, its pendulum swing aging anyone caught in its chime to dust.","desc":"An antique carnival clock stands taller than a door, pendulum swinging in slow, patient arcs, hands frozen at the wrong hour. Anyone caught inside its chime feels time itself pour off them, skin and years both wearing away toward dust with every ring.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "The Hour Strikes", "text": "once per encounter, chimes the hour: everyone within the tolling range takes aging-flavored necrotic damage as the golem's normal slam, no separate save track added"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its brass casing is engraved with a family crest no one living can name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The clock face reads a time that never changes, no matter how loud it tolls."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Dust falls from its gears in slow, steady drifts with every pendulum swing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tarnished key still hangs from a chain on its side, though it needs no winding."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its chime is always exactly one note flat, no matter how many times it rings."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It slows its swing deliberately for targets who seem to be counting the tolls."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Things aged by its chime remember years that never actually happened to them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck down, its pendulum keeps swinging alone, tolling years off anyone who stays close."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["swinging its pendulum in slow patient arcs, hands frozen at the wrong hour", "chiming the wrong time over and over, waiting for someone to stand too close"]},{"name":"The Understudy King","cr":12,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"arcanaloth","model":"arcanaloth","summary":"backstage understudy rehearsing to seize the Birthday King's crown","flavor":"Waits backstage to replace the Birthday King the instant he falters, rehearsing the crown's cruelty in an empty dressing room mirror.","desc":"He waits backstage in an empty dressing room, rehearsing the Birthday King's cruelty line by line in a cracked mirror, ready the instant the crown falters. Every gesture is a copy refined a hundred times over, waiting only for its cue.","traits":{"note": "He copies the Birthday King's mannerisms exactly — his threats and rider effects should read as borrowed cruelty, not original menace.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Understudy makes two Rehearsed Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Rehearsed Claw", "replaces": "Fiendish Burst", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 17 (3d8 + 4) Psychic damage, the wound shaped exactly like a cruelty he's practiced a hundred times."}, {"name": "Borrowed Crown", "replaces": "Banishing Claw (Requires Soul Tome)", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 20 (4d8 + 4) Force damage. If this reduces a creature to 0 Hit Points, the Understudy may instead banish it to a small backstage pocket-space, from which it can be freed within 1 minute by anyone who finds the exit."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Understudy casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components: At will: disguise self, minor illusion. 2/day each: mislead, hold monster."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He asks the party to judge his impression of the Birthday King, and means it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stagehand begs the party to keep him distracted before he tries the crown on for real."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's stolen a piece of the King's regalia and needs one more prop to complete the look."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers real information about the King's court in exchange for an honest audience."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's rehearsing a specific cruelty aimed at someone the party has already met."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun rewriting his own lines, testing which cruelties feel like his and not a copy."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The mirror in his dressing room shows the King's reaction before it happens on stage."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided tonight is opening night, whether or not the real King has stepped aside."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["rehearsing a cruel line in a cracked dressing-room mirror, refining every gesture", "fitting a spare crown to his own head when he thinks no one is watching"]},{"name":"Roulette Devil","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Fiend","size":"Medium","frame":"rakshasa","model":"rakshasa","summary":"cursed casino-tent devil who collects bets in stolen years","flavor":"Runs the fairground's cursed gaming tent, and every bet placed against him pays out in years of the loser's life.","desc":"He runs the fair's cursed gaming tent from behind a spinning wheel of red and black, smiling with too many teeth at every new bet placed. Every wager lost against him pays out not in coin but in years, peeled straight from the loser's life.","traits":{"note": "He never attacks a creature that hasn't wagered something with him first — the fight is always, technically, a bet he offered.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Devil makes two Cursed Touch attacks."}, {"name": "Cursed Touch", "replaces": "Cursed Touch", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 5 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Necrotic damage, and the target's maximum Hit Points are reduced by half the damage dealt until it finishes a Long Rest, years peeled away with a smile."}, {"name": "Double or Nothing (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Baleful Command (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature the Devil can see makes a DC 16 Charisma save. On a failure, the target takes 26 (4d10 + 4) Necrotic damage and is Frightened of the Devil until the end of its next turn; on a success the target takes half damage, and the Devil instead loses his next Legendary-style bonus action, the house having lost the hand."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Devil casts one of the following spells, requiring no Material components: At will: charm person, minor illusion. 2/day each: suggestion, modify memory."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone the party knows already owes him a bet paid out in missing years."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He offers the party a wager whose stakes are, on close reading, deeply unfair."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ledger of names and years owed sits open on his table, half of it recognizable."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's willing to trade information for a bet the party has good odds of winning."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A desperate gambler begs the party to win back years he's already lost to the wheel."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's rigged tonight's wheel specifically to collect on a debt the party doesn't know about yet."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The wheel keeps landing on numbers that match dates from the party's own past."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's staking his whole tent on one spin against the party, and he never offers fair odds by accident."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["spinning a wheel of red and black, smiling wide at a fresh wager", "totaling up a losing bettor's remaining years on a stack of chips"]},{"name":"The Grand Carousel Titan","cr":13,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"storm-giant","model":"storm-giant","summary":"whole carousel fused into a lurching titan of bobbing wooden limbs","flavor":"An entire carousel has fused into one lurching gilded titan, its wooden animals now limbs still bobbing on their poles.","desc":"An entire carousel has fused into one lurching, gilded titan, its carved wooden animals now serving as limbs still bobbing gently on their original poles. It moves with the slow, groaning creak of old brass and rot-softened wood, each stride a small parade of its own.","traits":{"hp": "above-chassis (Huge, fused-mount frame)", "actions": [{"name": "Bobbing Limbs", "text": "each of its carved-animal limbs can strike a separate target in the same turn, up and down in the ride's old rhythm"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its animal-limbs are gilded lion, swan, and stallion, each cracked with age."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Calliope pipes run the length of its spine, venting steam with every stride."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted eyes are wide and cheerful, unmoving no matter what it's doing."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A brass pole still runs clean through its center, load-bearing and useless now."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It groans in three-quarter time, an old waltz creaking out of every joint."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It turns to face music before it turns to face threats, drawn by any melody."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Riders who once sat on its animal-limbs left handprints that never wore off."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Toppled, it keeps spinning on its back, calliope blaring, limbs still swinging at anything close."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["lurching forward with a groan of old brass, wooden animals bobbing on its limbs", "turning slowly in place, painted eyes scanning the fairground for stragglers"]},{"name":"The Confetti Cannon Colossus","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"frost-giant","model":"frost-giant","summary":"siege-toy cannon launching cheerful bursts of glass confetti","flavor":"A fairground siege-toy that once fired harmless streamers now launches shrapnel-glass confetti in cheerful, deadly bursts.","desc":"A fairground siege-toy that once fired harmless paper streamers now booms with a deeper report, barrel glowing faintly at the mouth. What launches out in cheerful, colorful bursts is shrapnel-glass confetti, glittering prettily on the way down.","traits":{"note": "Its confetti settles like a carpet of broken glass afterward — the ground near it stays hazardous terrain long after it stops firing.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Colossus makes two Frost-Glass Axe attacks."}, {"name": "Frost-Glass Axe", "replaces": "Frost Axe", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +12, reach 10 ft. Hit: 26 (3d12 + 7) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Cold damage as glittering shards bite deep."}, {"name": "Confetti Barrage", "replaces": "Great Bow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +12, range 150/600 ft. Hit: 22 (4d8 + 4) Slashing damage in a shower of shrapnel-glass confetti, and the area within 10 feet of the target becomes difficult terrain from settled glass until cleared."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its barrel is painted in cheerful stripes, dented from countless celebratory blasts."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Confetti already coats its shoulders in a permanent, glittering drift."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It fires on a fixed schedule, as if still waiting for someone to cue a countdown."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A small brass plaque reads 'FOR GALA OCCASIONS ONLY,' scratched and ignored."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It hums 'happy occasion' songs between blasts, off-key and enthusiastic."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It saves its loudest charge for whatever looks most like a crowd worth impressing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The confetti it fires never quite finishes falling, drifting long after the blast ends."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its whole remaining charge detonates at once in one final, deadly celebration."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["loading a fresh charge into its glowing barrel, humming a festive tune", "booming a cheerful blast across the fairground, glass glittering as it falls"]},{"name":"Matriarch of the Sideshow","cr":15,"role":"apex","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"medusa","model":"medusa","summary":"ancient sideshow exhibit whose curse feeds on being watched","flavor":"The oldest exhibit in the tent, kept alive by decades of gawking stares, her curse now feeds on being watched, not touched.","desc":"The oldest exhibit under the tent sits enthroned behind faded velvet rope, kept alive for decades by nothing but the crowd's gawking stares. Her curse has changed with her hunger — it no longer needs a touch, only to be watched, and watched, and watched.","traits":{"note": "petrification-adjacent gaze reworked as attention-based rather than eye-contact based — being watched by her counts, not just watching her", "actions": [{"name": "Fed by the Crowd", "text": "any creature that has observed her for a full round without looking away begins to stiffen, slowing before it stills"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A ticket-taker begs the party not to look at her for more than a moment, seriously."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of her petrified predecessors still sits nearby, a former sideshow act made permanent."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's noticed the party watching her from across the tent, and she's noticed for a while."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A performer offers to distract her audience if the party handles the rest quietly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone paid to see her up close and hasn't come back out from behind the rope."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's tired of being watched and has started staring back, deliberately, at the crowd."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The velvet rope around her throne is the only thing that's aged normally in years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided to leave her tent tonight, curious what happens when she's the one watching the fair."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["sitting enthroned behind velvet rope, waiting patiently to be stared at", "turning slowly toward whoever's been watching her longest tonight"]},{"name":"The Perpetual Winner","cr":16,"role":"apex","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"death-knight-aspirant","model":"death-knight-aspirant","summary":"undying champion whose losing challengers become living trophies","flavor":"Has won every game at the fair a thousand times over and cannot stop; challengers who lose join his trophy case, still breathing.","desc":"He's won every game on the midway a thousand times over and physically cannot stop, moving from booth to booth with a champion's easy grin. Every challenger who loses to him joins his trophy case afterward — mounted, displayed, and still, somehow, breathing.","traits":{"note": "a downed-and-mounted state instead of a normal death for creatures it defeats — narrative hook for the trophy case, not extra mechanics on the PC"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone the party knows is mounted in his trophy case, alive, and blinking slowly."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He challenges the party to a game before he'll agree to a fight, and he means it seriously."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A vendor offers a reward for anyone who can make him lose even once, honestly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's already won against a party member, and doesn't realize the stakes were real."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His trophy case has one open pedestal left, freshly polished, clearly reserved."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He's begun inventing new games faster than the fairground can print new booths."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Every trophy in his case remembers, faintly, what it was like to lose to him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's decided the next game is against the whole party at once, winner takes all of them."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["moving booth to booth with an easy champion's grin, winning every game flawlessly", "polishing a trophy case where every mounted winner still, somehow, breathes"]},{"name":"The Calliope Behemoth","cr":17,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Huge","frame":"dracolich","model":"dracolich","summary":"steam-organ dragon whose cheerful hymn liquefies listeners' bones","flavor":"A steam organ grew a serpent's spine and dragon's wind, and its cheerful hymn liquefies bone in anyone who can still hear it.","desc":"A steam organ has grown a serpent's coiling spine and a dragon's furnace-breath, brass pipes gleaming where scales should be. Its cheerful, tuneless hymn rolls out across the fairgrounds, and every note that reaches an ear liquefies the bone beneath it.","traits":{"note": "breath weapon reflavored as a sonic hymn-cone rather than fire/acid — same chassis math, different sensory delivery"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its brass pipes are tuned slightly flat, on purpose, for the unsettling effect."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Steam vents from its joints in time with the hymn's slow, cheerful cadence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Old ticket confetti is baked permanently into the scales along its spine."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It coils itself around fairground landmarks like a python testing their weight."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hymn is recognizable as a children's song, slowed down until it sounds wrong."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It saves its loudest verse for whoever's been humming along without noticing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The hymn keeps playing faintly from its bones even after its pipes go silent."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Slain mid-hymn, its pipes keep venting one last verse, bone-soft echoes rolling outward."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "sky"],"activity":["rolling its brass-scaled coils across the fairground, pipes gleaming like plate", "exhaling a cheerful, tuneless hymn that rolls out over the whole midway"]},{"name":"Warden of the Big Top","cr":18,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"eye-tyrant","model":"eye-tyrant","summary":"vast tent-eye that conscripts failed performers as new attractions","flavor":"The tent's peak is one vast, veiled eye that watches every act performed beneath it, and every failed performer becomes its next attraction.","desc":"The peak of the tent is not canvas but one vast, veiled eye, watching every act performed on the ring below without blinking. Any performer who fails under its gaze doesn't get carried off — it conscripts them on the spot, folding them into its next attraction.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Conscript the Fallen", "text": "a creature dropped to 0 HP beneath the Warden's gaze can be reanimated as a new minor attraction-thrall instead of dying outright"}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A performer begs the party to help her finish her act before the Warden judges it a failure."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone the party knows is folded into the canvas, alive, waiting for the tent to fall."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The ringmaster offers the party a slot on tonight's bill, unaware what failing it means."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A retired performer warns the party never to let their act beneath the tent go quiet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The Warden has already marked one party member as tonight's closing number."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's grown restless with the current lineup and is scouting for fresh acts directly."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tent's canvas ripples with faces of every performer it's ever conscripted, watching too."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided the whole fairground is under its tent now, and the show starts the moment it notices the party."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["watching every act performed beneath it without ever once blinking", "folding a failed performer into its canvas the moment the crowd stops clapping"]},{"name":"The Sold-Out Show","cr":19,"role":"apex","type":"Fiend","size":"Huge","frame":"balor","model":"balor","summary":"eternal demon-headliner whose lights burn brighter per soul billed","flavor":"A demon booked eternally for one final performance, its stage lights burning brighter with every soul added to the marquee.","desc":"A demon stands eternally booked for one final performance, marquee lights strung across its shoulders like a headliner's name in neon. Those lights burn brighter with every soul added to the bill, and the show, by design, never actually closes.","traits":{"note": "escalating-brightness stacking condition — narrated as the marquee getting louder/brighter per kill in the encounter, mechanics riding the balor chassis's existing escalation"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A former headliner warns the party never to let their name go up on that marquee."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone the party is looking for is already billed in lights across its shoulders."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers the party top billing tonight, and the offer is somehow worse than a threat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stagehand begs the party to cancel the show before it opens for the final time."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The marquee already has one blank space left, sized exactly for a new name."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's begun soliciting names directly from the crowd, promising eternal fame in exchange."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Names already on its marquee still occasionally speak, faint and pleading, between blinks."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's decided tonight's the final performance, and it intends to fill every remaining space on the bill by curtain."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["standing beneath marquee lights strung across its shoulders, waiting for its cue", "adding a fresh name to its own bill, lights burning brighter with the addition"]},{"name":"The Never-Ending Attraction","cr":21,"role":"apex","type":"Fey","size":"Large","frame":"arch-hag","model":"arch-hag","summary":"court rival running an endless ride that loops joy into captivity","flavor":"A rival to the Birthday King's court, she runs the ride that never lets guests off, looping the same three minutes of joy into decades of captivity.","desc":"A rival to the Birthday King's own court, she runs a ride that never quite lets its passengers off, looping the same three minutes on repeat. Each loop feels like pure joy the first time through — it's only the hundredth time that reveals it as captivity.","traits":{"note": "a repeating-round hazard-lock (charm/restrain flavor) rather than a straight damage-dealer; the loop is the threat, not the hit"},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A guest has ridden her attraction so many loops he no longer remembers arriving here."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She invites the party aboard, and the first ninety seconds are, honestly, wonderful."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Someone's family member is somewhere in the loop, decades deep by now, still smiling."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers to let the party leave after 'just one more loop,' and means it kindly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A former rival of hers begs the party to break the loop before she notices them helping."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's begun tailoring each loop's joy specifically to whichever guest looks most reluctant."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The ride's three minutes have started repeating slightly differently each time through."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Her loop and the Birthday King's whole game may be the same ride, and she's decided the party's story ends riding it on repeat, forever, smiling."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "planar"],"activity":["running the same three joyful minutes of a ride on an endless, hidden loop", "greeting a new passenger with the exact same delighted smile as the last thousand"]},{"name":"Marching Band Automaton","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"skeleton-warrior","model":"skeleton-warrior","summary":"brass-skeleton whose off-key blare shatters concentration","flavor":"A brass-instrument skeleton blares off-key notes that rattle armor loose and shatter concentration mid-spell.","desc":"A brass-instrument skeleton stomps forward in a marching band's stiff cadence, valves and slides clattering where muscle should be. It blares deliberately off-key notes that rattle loose rivets and armor plating alike, the discord alone enough to shatter a caster's concentration.","traits":{"note": "Its off-key blare specifically punishes concentration — a spellcaster forced to save against it should feel it as a targeted threat.", "actions": [{"name": "Multiattack", "text": "The Automaton makes two Brass Blade attacks."}, {"name": "Brass Blade", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Discordant Blare", "replaces": "Shield Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) Thunder damage. If the target is Concentrating on a spell, it must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution save or lose Concentration."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It carries a dented tuba instead of a shield, valves rattling with every march step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its brass plating is stamped with a marching-band crest, tarnished green with age."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps perfect time even alone, stomping to a beat only it can hear."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tattered plume still juts from its skull, bobbing absurdly with each stride."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It blares the same four notes on a loop, off-key in exactly the same place each time."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It falls into step automatically the moment another marching automaton comes into view."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its discord seems to know, somehow, exactly which spell a caster is about to finish."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its valves keep blaring alone on the ground, one last discordant note stuck ringing."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["stomping forward in stiff cadence, valves and slides clattering with every step", "blaring an off-key note aimed squarely at a caster mid-spell"]},{"name":"Rubber Ball Bouncer","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"homunculus","model":"homunculus","summary":"grinning rubber ball bouncing faster with every bone-jarring hit","flavor":"A red rubber ball with a painted smiling face bounces at increasing speed, each impact a bone-jarring thud.","desc":"A red rubber ball with a painted smiling face bounces across the floor in slow, deliberate arcs, gaining speed with every landing. Each impact lands with a bone-jarring thud far heavier than its size suggests, faster and harder the longer the chase goes on.","traits":{"note": "It gets faster the longer a chase goes — treat later rounds of pursuit as progressively harder to outrun.", "actions": [{"name": "Bone-Jarring Bounce", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage, landing with a thud far heavier than its size suggests."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile is chipped on one side, giving it a permanent, uneven grin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's bright cherry red, scuffed pale at every point of impact."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bounces in a perfectly straight line until something changes its direction."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faint squeak escapes it with every landing, cheerful and slightly wrong."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It rolls to a dead stop the instant nobody's watching it anymore."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It bounces noticeably higher whenever a target tries to run from it."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It leaves a faint, bouncing echo of itself behind after each especially hard landing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Popped, it doesn't deflate — it detonates into a dozen smaller, still-bouncing balls."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["bouncing in slow, deliberate arcs across the floor, gaining speed with each landing", "rolling to a stop by a stranger's foot, painted smile aimed straight up"]},{"name":"Strongman Hammer Golem","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"helmed-horror","model":"helmed-horror","summary":"high-striker golem whose swing is meant for skulls, not bells","flavor":"Rings the high-striker bell with a swing meant for skulls, its painted grin never dimming no matter how loud the crack.","desc":"It grips an oversized mallet at the base of a high-striker game, swinging with a strongman's showmanship at anything that gets close. The bell at the top rings clean and loud with every hit that connects with a skull instead, its painted grin never dimming.","traits":{"note": "It only ever swings for the head — treat its attacks as aimed specifically at whatever's tallest or closest to the bell line.", "actions": [{"name": "High-Striker Swing", "replaces": "Arcane Sword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 10 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the attack roll would have hit a Large or smaller target squarely (DM's call, roughly a natural 15 or higher), the target must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution save or have the Stunned condition until the end of its next turn, rung like the bell."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its mallet head is a repurposed carnival bell, cracked but still ringing true."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A painted strongman mustache is fixed permanently to its featureless iron face."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It winds up theatrically before every swing, showman's flourish and all."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its high-striker base is bolted to the ground; only its swinging arm actually moves."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A little brass placard at its base reads a strength score no one's ever beaten."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It swings harder, visibly, whenever a crowd gathers to watch the strike land."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The bell it rings can be heard clearly from anywhere in the fairground, always."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Toppled, its bell keeps ringing on its own, each toll landing like a phantom swing nearby."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["gripping an oversized mallet at the base of a high-striker game, waiting for a swing", "ringing the bell at the top with a strongman's showmanship, grin never dimming"]},{"name":"Petting-Zoo Horror","cr":1,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-goat","model":"giant-goat","summary":"once-gentle petting-zoo animal grown too many teeth","flavor":"Once a gentle attraction, its wool now hides too many teeth, and it head-butts with a strength no child should have petted.","desc":"It was once a gentle attraction, woolly coat matted now from years of hands that shouldn't have been trusted with it. Underneath that wool is a mouth that's grown too many teeth, and a head-butt with a strength no petting-zoo animal should carry.","traits":{"note": "It looks harmless until it charges — the DM should let its first attack land as a genuine surprise if the party hasn't seen it act yet.", "actions": [{"name": "Too Many Teeth", "replaces": "Ram", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage, and if the target is Medium or smaller it must succeed on a DC 13 Strength save or be knocked Prone, gored by a head-butt no petting-zoo animal should carry."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its wool is matted with straw and old hoofprints of children who once fed it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A faded ribbon, once cheerful, is still tied clumsily around one of its horns."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bleats in a friendly, ordinary way right up until it charges."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pen gate hangs open, though it never seems to wander far from the fence line."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A small, hand-painted sign nearby still reads 'GENTLE — PLEASE PET.'"}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It approaches slowly and gently right up until the moment it's within striking range."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its teeth, once bared, don't fit its jaw the way any real goat's ever should."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Slain, its wool splits open to reveal it was never as small as the pen made it look."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["grassland", "urban"],"activity":["standing at the fence looking gentle, wool matted from years of unwelcome hands", "lowering its head slowly toward a hand reaching through the pen's low rail"]},{"name":"Glow-Stick Wisp","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Elemental","size":"Tiny","frame":"will-o-wisp","model":"will-o-wisp","summary":"bobbing glow-stick wisp that lures stragglers off the path","flavor":"A chemical-glow spirit lures children off the midway paths with a cheerful bobbing light, then snaps their glow out cold.","desc":"A chemical-glow spirit bobs cheerfully along the midway's darker paths, its light a soft, inviting green that seems to promise safety. It leads children and stragglers off the trail with that same gentle bob — then snaps its own glow out cold the moment they're alone.","traits":{"note": "Its glow snaps out cold the instant it's isolated a victim — until then it looks completely harmless, even inviting.", "actions": [{"name": "Snapped Glow", "replaces": "Shock", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (2d4) Lightning damage as its light snaps out cold against the target."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glow is soft chemical green, the exact shade of a party favor cracked open."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It bobs at a steady, unhurried pace, never quite fast enough to seem alarming."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It always stays just out of easy reach, hovering a few feet ahead invitingly."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its light flickers faintly in a rhythm that almost sounds like a giggle."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It only strays from the darker paths when someone follows it off them first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It brightens noticeably around children, dimming again once adults draw close."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Snuffed wisps of its same green glow linger in spots no lantern's been for years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Snapped out for good, it leaves behind a patch of true dark that swallows light nearby."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["bobbing cheerfully along a darker midway path, soft green light promising safety", "leading a straggler off the trail, glow dimming the moment they're alone"]},{"name":"Cake-Topper Golem","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"flesh-golem","model":"flesh-golem","summary":"fused bride-groom cake figure, frosting-slick, still smiling","flavor":"A porcelain bride-and-groom figurine fused into one lurching shape, frosting-slick and still smiling for a wedding long over.","desc":"A porcelain bride-and-groom figurine has fused into one lurching shape, frosting-slick along every seam, faces still turned toward each other in a fixed, permanent smile. It moves with a wedding-day stiffness, sugar dripping from its joints, still dressed for a ceremony long over.","traits":{"note": "It only ever moves in the stiff, small steps of a first dance — its charge range never actually extends beyond that.", "actions": [{"name": "Frosting Fist", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target is coated in hardening sugar-glaze; until the start of its next turn it has disadvantage on the first attack roll it makes."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The golem makes two Frosting Fist attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sugar-glaze cracks and re-seals across its knuckles with every slow step."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tiny plastic bouquet is fused permanently into its porcelain hand."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its two painted faces are turned so close together they've begun to blur into one."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It leaves a faint sugared footprint trail that ants follow for days."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A veil of spun sugar has yellowed but never once torn."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It hums the first three notes of a wedding march, over and over, never the fourth."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anyone it strikes finds their own wedding ring finger faintly sugar-glazed after, whether they wear one or not."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it doesn't collapse — it topples forward into a bow, frosting shattering into a hundred tiny smiling faces."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["shuffling in a slow processional loop around a cake stand nobody set out anymore", "still turning to face its fused partner as if the ceremony hasn't finished yet"]},{"name":"the Playing-Card Guard","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-duodrone","model":"clockwork-law-construct-duodrone","summary":"flat card-soldier, obeys any shouted rank","flavor":"Flat, hinged, and utterly loyal to a rank it can't read — it swings a spade-halberd edge-on so it nearly vanishes, then face-on so it looms.","desc":"Flat and hinged at every joint, it swings a spade-tipped halberd edge-on so the blade nearly vanishes from sight, then face-on so the whole card looms wide and sudden. It obeys any shouted rank without question, loyal to an authority it can't even read.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Spade-Edge Halberd", "replaces": "Clockwork Blade", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 10 ft. Hit: 5 (1d10) Slashing damage. While attacking edge-on the Guard is nearly invisible in profile: the first attack roll against it before its next turn has disadvantage unless the attacker has already seen it face-on."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Guard makes two Spade-Edge Halberd attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A three of spades, hinged at every joint, paint chipped along the hinge-lines."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Turns edge-on so fast it seems to blink out of sight for a heartbeat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shouted rank changes depending entirely on who shouted last and loudest."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells faintly of fresh ink and rose-garden paint, never of rust."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Salutes anything holding a scepter, real or improvised, without question."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two of them argue, flatly and politely, over which suit outranks the other."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sliced clean through, it doesn't fall — it folds along a crease that was always there."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed at the gate, every other card guard on the grounds turns face-on to look at once."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["standing rigid at a garden gate, halberd shouldered, waiting for a rank to be shouted", "marching in a two-file column that turns whenever the lead card turns, no reason given"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the Queen of Hearts' card-soldiers who paint the roses red"},{"name":"the Tin Soldier's Hollow Cousin","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"clockwork-law-construct-monodrone","model":"clockwork-law-construct-monodrone","summary":"wind-up soldier, marches until unwound","flavor":"Painted smile, key still turning in its back; it marches in whatever direction it was last wound, even off a table's edge.","desc":"Painted smile fixed under a tin shako, its key still turns slowly in its back with every step it takes. It marches in whatever direction it was last wound to face, indifferent to walls, stairs, or the edge of a table.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Wind-Key Gear", "replaces": "Gear", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +3, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Bludgeoning damage from a swinging brass cog-arm."}, {"name": "Flung Cog", "replaces": "Gear Flinger", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +3, range 30/60 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage as a loose gear-tooth spins off and embeds itself."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted smile is chipped down to bare tin on one cheek."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The key in its back turns a full rotation every ten steps, no faster."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches face-first into walls and simply keeps marching against them."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wound backward once, it now marches only in reverse."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A dent above one eye makes it list slightly leftward forever."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It winds down mid-sentence-length gestures, frozen for exactly three seconds before resuming."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Turn its key the wrong way and it marches backward through the last hour it experienced."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Wound past its limit, the key snaps and it marches at double speed until it runs completely out."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["marching in a straight line off whatever ledge it was last wound to face", "winding down mid-step, key groaning, still trying to lift a foot that won't rise"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock nursery-toy-come-to-life archetype (generic wind-up soldier, not any single IP's toy line)"},{"name":"the March Hare","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-badger","model":"rlm-the-march-hare","summary":"tea-mad hare, hostile to clocks and cutlery","flavor":"It never stops setting the table and never stops smashing it; ours argues with the furniture between bites.","desc":"It never stops laying out the tea things, and it never stops smashing them either, cutlery flying with every irritable swipe. Ours argues loudly with the furniture between bites, chair legs and teapots taking the worst of a temper that never settles.","traits":{"note": "It attacks anything that mentions a specific time of day before anything else in the room.", "actions": [{"name": "Frantic Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage, and if the Hare has smashed or thrown something this turn the bite deals an extra 2 (1d4) damage — it's always angrier mid-tantrum."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur matted with spilled tea, ears bent at two different, permanent angles."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Resets the same three chairs into the same three positions every single time."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a hat with a price tag still swinging from the brim."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snarls at anyone who checks the time, even by glancing at the sun."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps one paw permanently curled as if gripping a cup that isn't there."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A second hare nearby refuses to speak to it over some ancient, unspecified slight."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anyone who sits at its table finds their own pocket-watch running backward after."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Cornered, it stops smashing things and goes utterly, eerily still — worse than the tantrum."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland"],"activity":["resetting a table it just finished smashing, muttering about a wrong hour", "hurling teacups at a clock that isn't there, cursing whoever's late this time"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the tea-party Hare, mad from too much March"},{"name":"a Wicked Witch's Wolf","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"wolf","model":"wolf","summary":"storybook wolf, mimics a soft voice before attacking","flavor":"Chalk-dust still clings to its throat from swallowing a voice that wasn't its own; it talks before it bites, and the talking is the worse part.","desc":"Chalk dust still clings faintly to its throat, residue from swallowing a voice that was never its own to begin with. It talks in a soft, borrowed cadence before it attacks, and somehow the talking is worse than the teeth that follow.","traits":{"note": "It always speaks before it attacks — silence from it is the actual warning sign.", "actions": [{"name": "Borrowed-Voice Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage. If the Wolf spoke in its stolen voice before attacking this turn, the target has disadvantage on its next saving throw against being Frightened this combat."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a lace cap that keeps slipping over one ear as it walks."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its borrowed voice is a grandmother's, warm and a half-step too slow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chalk-dust puffs from its throat with every word it forces out."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a basket of stolen bread it never once eats from."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Paws are too large for the nightgown's sleeves and drag the hem."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It rehearses three different voices before choosing whichever gets a door to open."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Whoever it mimics start losing pieces of their own real voice, one syllable at a time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed mid-sentence, the borrowed voice keeps talking for one more breath out of a throat gone still."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest"],"activity":["trotting a familiar cottage path in a stolen nightgown two sizes too small", "practicing a soft, borrowed voice under its breath before a door it hasn't reached yet"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Grimm fairy-tale wolves (Little Red Riding Hood / the Wolf and the Seven Young Kids, PD folk tradition)"},{"name":"Geppetto's Runaway Marionette","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"animated-flying-sword","model":"animated-flying-sword","summary":"lying puppet, nose-hinge lengthens with each lie","flavor":"Its nose is a broken hinge that keeps lengthening whenever it insists it means no harm; the strings dangling from its wrists still twitch toward a hand that isn't there.","desc":"Its nose is a broken wooden hinge, and that hinge keeps lengthening every time it insists — sincerely, wide-eyed — that it means no harm at all. Loose strings dangle from both wrists, twitching now and then toward a hand that isn't there anymore.","traits":{"note": "Every lie it tells lengthens its nose a visible inch — the DM should narrate this every time, no roll needed.", "actions": [{"name": "Lengthening Slash", "replaces": "Slash", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 5 (1d8 + 1) Slashing damage from its own overlong nose swung like a jointed blade."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted cheeks are rosy and cracked from decades of the same fixed grin."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Loose strings twitch toward an empty space at hand height, always the same spot."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its nose already has three old, whittled-down lengths carved short again."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It insists, unprompted, that it isn't lying about anything at all."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wood-grain along its limbs looks disturbingly like real skin from a distance."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It tells one true thing per fight, always accidentally, always looking horrified after."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its longest lie yet leaves the nose brushing the ceiling, still growing after it's dead."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its strings snap upward all at once, as if something far above finally let go."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["insisting loudly it means no harm while its nose creaks another inch longer", "tangling its own loose strings around a doorframe, trying and failing to look natural"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Collodi, Le avventure di Pinocchio (1883, PD) — a puppet who lied its way out of its strings"},{"name":"the Piper's Rat","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Beast","size":"Small","frame":"giant-rat","model":"giant-rat","summary":"tune-compelled rat, swarms toward any melody","flavor":"It can't help following music, even music it invents by chewing on pipes; a column of them will drown a room before the tune even lands.","desc":"It can't help but follow music, even the tuneless clatter it makes itself gnawing on hollow pipes as it scurries forward. Alone it's nothing; a column of them pouring through a doorway will drown a room in fur and teeth before the melody even finishes.","traits":{"note": "A column of them is worse than any one — treat groups as arriving in a stream, not spread out.", "actions": [{"name": "Tune-Drawn Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage. If any music, singing, or whistling has been heard within 30 ft. this turn, the Rat has advantage on this attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gnaws a hollow pipe into a tuneless, rattling whistle as it scurries."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Ears twitch toward any hum, even an accidental one from a nervous throat."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Fur matted with pipe-dust in a color no rat should naturally be."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows footsteps that fall in rhythm more than it follows any scent."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Chews through wood, rope, and boot-leather with equal, cheerful indifference."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A dozen more pour from a drain the instant anyone starts whistling to calm their nerves."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Stop humming and the whole column halts mid-stride, confused, easy pickings for a breath."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Killed en masse, the survivors' gnawed pipes all hit the same note at once, and something much larger answers it."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["gnawing a rhythm into a hollow pipe, ears twitching toward its own noise", "pouring out of a drainpipe in a column, drawn toward the nearest hummed tune"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Pied Piper of Hamelin legend (medieval German folk legend, PD)"},{"name":"the Mouse King's Sentry","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"Beast","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-hyena","model":"rlm-the-mouse-kings-sentry","summary":"multi-headed mouse-courtier, argues with itself mid-fight","flavor":"Extra heads, extra crowns, extra grudges — it snaps at whichever slight it remembers most that second.","desc":"Extra heads sprout in a ragged crown atop one small, armored body, each wearing its own tiny paper coronet and its own private grudge. It snaps and lunges toward whichever slight it's currently stewing over, the heads rarely agreeing on a single target.","traits":{"note": "Each head remembers a different slight — the DM can pick a fresh grudge to narrate each round it attacks.", "actions": [{"name": "Grudge-Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +4, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage as whichever head is angriest lunges first."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears five paper crowns, each dented from the others fighting over rank."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One head sulks silently while the rest bicker over precedence."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Snaps at its own tail, mistaking it for an intruder, more often than not."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Each head has a slightly different, competing coat of tiny armor-plate."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses commands unless all its heads agree on hearing them first."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Two heads negotiate a truce mid-fight to gang up on a shared target."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Sever one head and a new crown, and a new grudge, grows back within the hour."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "All its heads finally agree on something the instant it drops below half its hit points, and it gets much worse to fight."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["arguing with itself over which head gets to challenge the intruder first", "pacing a throne-room threshold, crowns clacking together as heads jostle for a look"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Hoffmann, Nussknacker und Mausekönig (1816, PD) — the Mouse King's seven-headed court"},{"name":"the Nutcracker Grenadier","cr":1,"role":"elite","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"animated-armor","model":"animated-armor","summary":"wooden grenadier, jaw-hinge crushing bite","flavor":"Jaw hinged to crack more than nuts; painted eyes track motion better than most flesh does.","desc":"Its jaw hinges wide on a spring built for cracking more than walnuts, painted uniform buttons gleaming under whatever light finds them. Glassy painted eyes track motion with an unsettling precision that most flesh-and-blood soldiers never manage.","traits":{"actions": [{"name": "Cracking Jaw", "replaces": "Slam", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage as the spring-loaded jaw slams shut on the target."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Grenadier makes two Cracking Jaw attacks."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Painted uniform buttons are chipped down to bare wood on the left side only."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glassy eyes never blink, tracking motion with a soldier's practiced patience."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Jaw spring winds tighter with every crack, audibly, until it's oiled."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marches the exact same eleven-step patrol regardless of what's in its way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A hairline crack runs from jaw to collar, held shut by old lacquer."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It salutes crisply before every attack, out of some drilled habit nobody taught it to break."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anything it cracks in its jaw — nut, bone, or lock — comes out perfectly halved, every time."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, its spring releases all at once, jaw snapping shut hard enough to crack the floor beneath it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["standing at rigid attention beside a shelf, jaw hinge creaking open and shut", "marching a fixed post-to-post patrol, painted eyes tracking every twitch of motion"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"generic wooden-soldier toy archetype (the Nutcracker's rank-and-file, not the named prince)"},{"name":"the Cheshire Grin","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"sea-hag","model":"rlm-the-cheshire-grin","summary":"fading cat, taunts and phases out mid-combat","flavor":"It answers every question with a worse one and vanishes exactly when a hit should land; the grin is the last thing to go, and the first thing to come back.","desc":"It answers every question with a worse one, tail curling lazily in the air as its outline starts to blur at the edges. It vanishes exactly when a killing blow should land, leaving the grin hanging a beat longer than the rest of it — the last thing to go, and always the first thing back.","traits":{"note": "It vanishes exactly when a killing blow should land — the grin is always the last part to go.", "actions": [{"name": "Curious Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Riddling Stare (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Death Glare (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. One creature within 30 ft. that can see the Grin makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature is Frightened until the end of its next turn and wastes its next question or command trying to make sense of the Grin's answer."}, {"name": "Fade to Grin", "replaces": "Illusory Appearance", "text": "The Grin becomes Invisible except for its floating smile, which remains visible and grants no information about its actual position. It can end this effect as a Bonus Action."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Stripes fade to nothing at the edges, like an old photograph left in the sun."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Answers every question with a question, and seems delighted by the loop."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its tail is the last thing to fade back in, always, no matter the order it left."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Perches somewhere just slightly too high to reach without climbing."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Purrs when confused travelers argue with each other over its riddles."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It fades entirely except for one eye, watching, whenever it's genuinely amused."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its grin has been seen hanging in places the rest of it never visited."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Struck a killing blow, only the grin remains, floating, laughing, refusing to finish fading."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "any"],"activity":["lounging on a branch, answering a question with a worse one, tail curling lazily", "fading from the paws backward mid-sentence, leaving only the grin to finish talking"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the cat that fades to only its smile"},{"name":"the Winged Monkey Raider","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"giant-owl","model":"giant-owl","summary":"cap-bound flying monkey, resents its own orders","flavor":"It hates every second of the compulsion and takes it out on whoever's closest; free one mid-fight and it simply leaves.","desc":"Bound wings beat hard and resentful, wide eyes flicking toward whoever's holding its leash rather than its target. It clearly hates every second of the compulsion driving it and takes that hatred out on whoever's nearest — free it mid-fight and it simply flies off.","traits":{"note": "Freed from its compulsion mid-fight, it simply flies off — it was never actually loyal to anyone.", "actions": [{"name": "Resentful Talons", "replaces": "Talons", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +5, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage, and the target is grappled (escape DC 13) if the Raider isn't already grappling someone."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Raider casts a spell from its compulsion-bound repertoire, its heart plainly not in it."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rusted cap sits crooked, cutting into fur that's rubbed raw beneath it."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters complaints under its breath about the orders it's forced to follow."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wing-feathers are matted and uneven, badly overdue for grooming it's not allowed."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Watches its handler's hands more than any target it's told to attack."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Carries a small stash of stolen trinkets it clearly kept for itself."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Slows down and drags its talons whenever it thinks no one's watching closely."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its cap, removed, leaves it able to speak plainly for the first time in years."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Freed mid-battle, it doesn't flee — it turns on whoever still holds its leash first."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["sky", "forest"],"activity":["circling low on bound wings, eyes flicking resentfully toward whoever holds its leash", "swooping to snatch cargo it clearly wants no part of stealing"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD, novel version) — the Wicked Witch of the West's flying monkey soldiers, bound by the Golden Cap"},{"name":"the Goblin Toymaker","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Small","frame":"green-hag","model":"rlm-the-goblin-toymaker","summary":"toy-peddling goblin, remote-commands nearby constructs","flavor":"Every toy it's ever sold is still listening for its whistle; it fights by recalling its merchandise, not by swinging anything itself.","desc":"Small, gaudy, and cheerful in a shopfront apron, it never swings a weapon of its own — it doesn't need to. Every toy it's ever sold is still listening for its whistle, and it fights entirely by recalling its merchandise from wherever it's been carried.","traits":{"note": "It never swings a weapon itself — it fights entirely by recalling toys it's already sold nearby.", "actions": [{"name": "Recall Whistle", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "The Toymaker blows a shrill note. One friendly construct or beast with the Toymaker's mark within 60 ft. immediately uses its Reaction to move up to its speed toward a target the Toymaker points to and make one attack."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Toymaker uses Recall Whistle twice, commanding two different sold toys."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Toymaker casts a spell from its shopkeeper's repertoire."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's short on stock and offers the party a discount for hauling in fresh materials."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of its recent customers wants a toy taken back, and it refuses to issue refunds."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's misplaced the whistle for one specific toy and wants it recovered before that toy causes trouble."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival toymaker's mark is showing up on constructs it insists it never made."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's holding a commissioned toy the party ordered and won't release it without full payment now."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It wants the party to field-test a new toy and report back honestly on what goes wrong."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "It's being blackmailed by one of its own sold toys, which learned to whistle back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "It's about to recall every toy it's ever sold in the district at once, for reasons it won't explain, and wants the party gone before that happens."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "forest"],"activity":["polishing a whistle behind a shopfront counter, humming to whatever's still listening", "counting sold inventory on its fingers, whistle ready at its lips the whole time"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"stock malevolent-toymaker/goblin-tinkerer archetype drawing on Grimm-style goblin/gnome tradition (PD folk motif, not any branded IP)"},{"name":"the Queen of Hearts","cr":4,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"guard-captain","model":"rlm-the-queen-of-hearts","summary":"tyrant queen, commands the battlefield instead of fighting it","flavor":"She never actually swings the axe — she just declares a sentence and the room's own furniture carries it out; the tantrum is the spell.","desc":"She never actually raises the axe herself — she simply declares a sentence in a voice that cracks the air, and the room's own furniture carries the verdict out. The tantrum that follows a denied whim is, itself, the spell.","traits":{"note": "She rarely swings a weapon personally — her tantrum-declarations are the real threat, and denying her whims triggers them.", "actions": [{"name": "Declared Sentence", "replaces": "Javelin", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +6, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage as an animated garden implement hurls itself at her command."}, {"name": "Off With It", "replaces": "Longsword", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +6, reach 5 ft. Hit: 8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage as the nearest weapon-shaped object obeys her raised finger."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Queen issues two attacks, via Declared Sentence or Off With It in any combination, through objects she commands rather than her own hands."}, {"name": "Royal Tantrum (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. Denied a whim, the Queen shrieks a verdict. Each creature within 20 ft. makes a DC 15 Wisdom save, taking 14 (4d6) Psychic damage and being unable to disobey her next simple command on a failure, or half damage and unaffected on a success."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's sentenced a member of her own court to death over a trivial breach of etiquette, and wants witnesses."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She demands the party join her croquet match, rigged from the start, or be declared guilty of refusing."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A prisoner she's condemned is innocent, and desperately needs rescue before the sentence executes itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's misplaced her scepter and blames the nearest bystander, demanding it returned or else."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants the party to fetch a specific rose, painted the wrong color, before she notices the mistake."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Her own gardeners are plotting a quiet uprising and need the party's help without her noticing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Her declared sentences are starting to come true even when she isn't present to say them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's declared the whole party guilty of an unnamed crime and the entire garden's furniture has just turned to look."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["pointing at a trembling gardener and declaring a sentence the room's furniture will carry out", "presiding over a croquet match rigged entirely in her own favor, daring anyone to object"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — 'Off with their heads!'"},{"name":"the Grimm Woodland Witch","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"night-hag","model":"night-hag","summary":"cannibal-witch, lures and force-feeds before the kill","flavor":"She fattens what she can't yet eat and eats what she's already fattened; the oven is a door she keeps ajar just to hear you consider it.","desc":"She fattens whatever she can't yet eat and eats whatever she's already fattened, humming contentedly over a simmering pot the whole while. The oven door stays cracked open, not from carelessness, but because she wants you to consider it, at length, before she decides.","traits":{"note": "She fattens what she can't yet eat and eats what she's already fattened — she never rushes the meal.", "actions": [{"name": "Fattening Claw", "replaces": "Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Oven Door", "replaces": "Plane", "text": "The Witch conjures a cracked, glowing oven door in a space she can see within 30 ft. Until the start of her next turn, any creature that ends its turn adjacent to the door takes 9 (2d8) Fire damage, drawn toward it against its better judgment."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Witch makes two Fattening Claw attacks."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Witch casts a spell from her hag repertoire."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding two children in a cage out back, fattening them on candy for a meal weeks off."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She offers the party a hot meal that's clearly the last supper for someone she's already caged."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A recipe she's missing calls for one ingredient only the party's route can supply."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She wants an escaped captive tracked down and returned before the meal spoils."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her gingerbread walls are crumbling, and she needs hands to rebuild the trap before the next guest arrives."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "A caged captive begs the party to feed the witch something that will make her sick instead."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "She's begun fattening the forest itself, roots and stones swelling sweet and soft near her hut."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's decided the party looks well-fed enough already, and the oven door is cracking open right now."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "swamp"],"activity":["humming over a simmering pot, watching two fattened captives through a cracked oven door", "measuring a stranger's wrist through cage bars, disappointed at how thin it still is"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Grimm fairy-tale witches (Hansel and Gretel's gingerbread-house witch; PD folk tradition, our own original description — no film likeness)"},{"name":"the Wicked Witch of the West","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"archpriest","model":"rlm-the-wicked-witch-of-the-west","summary":"beast-commanding witch, dissolves rather than dies clean","flavor":"Ours is a hoarder of borrowed servants, not a green face — she never fights fair and she never fights dry-eyed once the bucket comes out.","desc":"Ours is no green-skinned face cackling alone — she's a hoarder of borrowed servants, sending others in first and staying dry behind them. She never fights fair, and she never fights with dry eyes once a bucket of water enters the room.","traits":{"note": "She never fights fair — she sends borrowed servants in first and stays back until she must act.", "actions": [{"name": "Withering Burst", "replaces": "Radiant Burst", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +7, range 60 ft. Hit: 16 (3d8 + 3) Necrotic damage in a 10-foot-radius sphere as spiteful green fire spreads across the ground."}, {"name": "Commanding Word (Recharge 4-6)", "replaces": "Holy Word (Recharge 4-6)", "text": "Recharge 4-6. The Witch shrieks a command. Each creature of her choice within 30 ft. makes a DC 15 Wisdom save, taking 18 (4d8) Psychic damage and being Frightened until the end of its next turn on a failure, or half damage and unfrightened on a success."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Witch makes two Withering Burst attacks."}, {"name": "Spellcasting", "replaces": "Spellcasting", "text": "The Witch casts a spell from her repertoire."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's put a bounty on a specific pair of enchanted shoes, and someone in the party might be wearing them."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her borrowed servants are terrified of her and would defect the moment they saw a way out."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's sent flying scouts ahead and already knows the party is coming before they arrive."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A stolen relic she wants back is currently in a party member's pack, unbeknownst to them."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's holding a village hostage over a debt owed by someone the party is trying to protect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One of her borrowed servants slips the party a warning about her one real weakness."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Water thrown near her doesn't just dissolve her — it dissolves whatever she was last touching too."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "She's cornered and reaching for a bucket herself, willing to dissolve on her own terms before anyone else gets the credit."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "swamp"],"activity":["directing borrowed servants forward from a safe distance, staying carefully dry", "eyeing a bucket someone's carrying with real, visible dread"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD novel version) — melts to water, commands wolves/crows/bees/monkeys, not any film's green-skin design"},{"name":"the Mouse King","cr":7,"role":"high","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Large","frame":"troll","model":"troll","summary":"seven-headed rat-king, regenerates through internal rivalry","flavor":"Seven heads mean seven opinions about how you should die; killing one crown just promotes the angriest survivor.","desc":"Seven crowned heads rise from one hulking rat body, and every head has its own opinion about exactly how you ought to die. Cut down the loudest one and the killing blow only serves to promote whichever surviving head was already the angriest.","traits":{"note": "Cutting down the loudest head only promotes the angriest surviving one — it doesn't weaken him, it focuses him.", "actions": [{"name": "Seven-Headed Bite", "replaces": "Bite", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 16 (2d10 + 5) Piercing damage as whichever head currently holds the floor lunges forward."}, {"name": "Crowned Claws", "replaces": "Claws", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 10 ft. Hit: 13 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Mouse King makes one Seven-Headed Bite attack and one Crowned Claws attack."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One of his seven heads is secretly trying to broker peace and will signal the party if given a chance."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a toymaker's family hostage over an old unpaid tribute of tin soldiers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival head is plotting to defect entirely, crown and all, if the party can offer it a better deal."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He wants a specific nutcracker returned to him, believing it holds the key to his own crown's legitimacy."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His court is fracturing into seven mini-factions, each loyal to a different head, ripe for exploitation."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "One head begs to be the one killed first, tired of the endless internal argument."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A crown taken from a defeated head keeps growing back on his body somewhere else entirely."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "All seven heads have finally agreed on a single verdict for the party, and that unity alone makes him far more dangerous."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban", "ruins"],"activity":["holding court while seven heads bicker over the exact manner of an intruder's death", "promoting a crowned head mid-tantrum after silencing whichever one spoke last"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Hoffmann, Nussknacker und Mausekönig (1816, PD) — the seven-crowned rival of the Nutcracker Prince"},{"name":"the Automaton in the Wicker Man's Skin","cr":5,"role":"high","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"scarecrow","model":"scarecrow","summary":"straw guardian-construct, patrols a fixed boundary forever","flavor":"Straw where a heart should sit and a painted grin that never once needed the muscles to hold it; it guards the toybox border like it remembers being told to.","desc":"Straw fills the space where a heart should beat, and a painted grin sits fixed on its woven face, needing no muscle at all to hold its shape. It patrols the same fixed boundary over and over, guarding the toybox's edge like it still remembers being told to.","traits":{"note": "It patrols a fixed boundary and will not pursue past it, no matter the provocation — the border is the whole point of it.", "actions": [{"name": "Straw-Wrapped Claw", "replaces": "Fearsome Claw", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +7, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Painted Grin Glare", "replaces": "Terrifying Glare", "text": "The Automaton fixes its painted grin on one creature it can see within 30 ft. That creature makes a DC 14 Wisdom save or is Frightened of the Automaton until the end of its next turn."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Straw pokes through gaps in its woven chest where a heart would otherwise sit."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted grin has been repainted so many times the layers show through like rings."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Patrols exactly to a boundary marker and no further, turning back with mechanical precision."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Birds nest undisturbed in its shoulder-straw, riding along the whole patrol."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its joints creak in the same four-beat rhythm with every step it takes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses at the boundary each circuit, as if remembering, briefly, why it's there."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Cross its patrol line and time near the boundary runs a beat slower until you cross back."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed at its post, straw spills out and reforms into a dozen small scarecrow shapes that scatter into the tree line."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["patrolling the same fixed boundary line, straw shedding with every mechanical step", "standing sentinel at a threshold, painted grin fixed toward whoever approaches"],"source":"archetype","sourceNote":"scarecrow-come-to-life archetype (generic animated-guardian toybox motif, not any branded character)"},{"name":"the Wonderland Jabberwock","cr":10,"role":"apex","type":"Dragon","size":"Large","frame":"young-red-dragon","model":"young-red-dragon","summary":"nonsense-dragon, telegraphs doom in verse before it strikes","flavor":"It doesn't so much attack as arrive — burbling, whiffling, eyes of flame — and the vorpal answer is always a blade someone else forged.","desc":"It doesn't so much attack as simply arrive — burbling low in its throat, whiffling through the underbrush, eyes lit like twin coals catching flame. Whatever verse it recites on the way in always ends the same: with a vorpal blade someone else was left to forge.","traits":{"note": "It telegraphs its arrival in verse before it strikes — the recitation is the warning, if anyone's listening.", "actions": [{"name": "Burbling Rend", "replaces": "Rend", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Jabberwock makes two Burbling Rend attacks."}, {"name": "Nonsense Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "replaces": "Fire Breath (Recharge 5-6)", "text": "Recharge 5-6. The Jabberwock exhales warping, verse-shaped force in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 17 Dexterity save, taking 36 (8d8) Force damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. Creatures that fail also find their next spoken command word or command spell garbled and wasted."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its verse names a specific weapon it fears, forged by a smith the party could actually find."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's been terrorizing a village that's offered its finest blade to whoever slays it."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A local hero already tried and fled, leaving behind gear the party could use against it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's nesting near a route the party needs and won't be reasoned or bargained past."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its verse, recited in full, apparently contains its own name — useful to whoever can catch it."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It seems almost disappointed when no one answers its recited challenge in kind."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its verse changes slightly each telling, as if it's still composing the story of its own death."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "Its verse this time names one of the party by a name they haven't been called yet — a chapter of the story arriving before they've lived it."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "sky"],"activity":["burbling low through underbrush, eyes lit like coals, reciting a verse that always ends the same", "whiffling into a clearing mid-rhyme, jaws already testing the air for a vorpal answer"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Through the Looking-Glass (1871, PD) — 'the jaws that bite, the claws that catch'"},{"name":"the Tin Woodman, Rusted Wrong","cr":9,"role":"apex","type":"Construct","size":"Large","frame":"iron-golem","model":"iron-golem","summary":"hollow tin giant, mourns while it swings the axe","flavor":"Somewhere under the seams is the man who kept chopping even after every piece of him was replaced; he still oils his own joints mid-fight, out of habit, not need.","desc":"Somewhere under all the replaced, rust-streaked seams is still the shape of a man who kept swinging his axe even after every piece of him got swapped out. He oils his own joints mid-fight out of pure habit, not need, mourning quietly the whole time he chops.","traits":{"note": "It oils its own joints out of habit, not need — a strange, sad tell that it was once someone with a routine.", "actions": [{"name": "Mourning Axe", "replaces": "Bladed Arm", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 10 ft. Hit: 20 (3d8 + 6) Slashing damage."}, {"name": "Rust-Flake Bolt", "replaces": "Fiery Bolt", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +9, range 120 ft. Hit: 16 (3d6 + 6) Piercing damage as a shard of its own rusted plating flies loose and embeds itself."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Woodman makes two Mourning Axe attacks."}, {"name": "Rusting Breath (Recharge 6)", "replaces": "Poison Breath (Recharge 6)", "text": "Recharge 6. The Woodman exhales corrosive vapor in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 17 Constitution save, taking 27 (6d8) Poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. Nonmagical metal armor or weapons that fail begin visibly rusting, imposing a cumulative -1 penalty to the damage or AC they provide until repaired."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's still trying to reach a woodcutter's cottage that no longer exists, and will follow anyone heading that way."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A tinsmith nearby claims she can restore what's left of the man inside, for a steep price in rare parts."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It's guarding a chest of old love letters it can no longer read with hands that used to hold a pen."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It mistakes a party member for someone it once knew and won't stop following them afterward."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its oil is running out, and it's begun asking anyone nearby, plainly, for more."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It pauses combat entirely if someone speaks a name it clearly used to answer to."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The rust spreading over it isn't decay — it's memory, and touching bare metal shows flashes of a life it lost."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Destroyed, it doesn't collapse in pieces — it kneels, axe planted, and finally, audibly, finishes crying."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["forest", "ruins"],"activity":["oiling its own joints mid-stride out of pure habit, mourning quietly as it walks", "swinging its axe in slow, practiced arcs at nothing, rehearsing a chore long finished"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"L. Frank Baum, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900, PD novel version) — the woodman who traded his flesh limb by limb for tin"},{"name":"the Hamelin Piper","cr":11,"role":"apex","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"spy-master","model":"rlm-the-hamelin-piper","summary":"compulsion piper, turns the battlefield's own mooks against it","flavor":"He never raises a weapon; he raises a tune, and the toybox itself gets up to dance for him, one compelled soldier at a time.","desc":"He never once raises a weapon of his own; he raises a tune instead, fingers dancing lightly over pipe-holes worn smooth with age. The toybox itself gets up to dance for him at that sound, one compelled soldier at a time, joining his side against its own will.","traits":{"note": "He never raises a weapon of his own — he raises a tune, and whatever's nearby dances for him instead.", "actions": [{"name": "Piping Rapier", "replaces": "Rapier", "text": "Melee Attack Roll: +8, reach 5 ft. Hit: 12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Pipe-Dart", "replaces": "Hand Crossbow", "text": "Ranged Attack Roll: +8, range 30/120 ft. Hit: 10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Piper makes two attacks, using Piping Rapier or Pipe-Dart in any combination."}, {"name": "Recruiting Tune (1/Day)", "replaces": "Smoke Bomb (1/Day)", "text": "The Piper plays a compelling melody. One creature with an Intelligence of 4 or lower within 60 ft. must succeed on a DC 16 Wisdom save or be Charmed by the Piper for 1 minute, moving toward him and following simple gestured commands, obeying against its will."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "hook", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A town owes him payment for a job of clearing vermin and is stalling on the debt."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's lured a party member's animal companion partway toward him with an idle tune."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's willing to sell the tune that controls a specific pest problem, for a price steep enough to notice."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A rival piper is undercutting his rates, and he wants the competition dealt with quietly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "He's holding a town's children hostage with a tune until an old unpaid debt is settled in full."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He offers to teach a single verse of the tune to someone the party needs to save, at a cost."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tune he plays keeps working on people who weren't anywhere near enough to hear it."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "He's begun a new tune aimed squarely at the party's own mounts and hirelings, and hasn't finished it yet."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["walking a market square, fingers dancing over pipe-holes, humming a tune under his breath", "watching a rival's mooks sway toward him mid-conversation, entirely against their will"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"the Pied Piper of Hamelin legend (medieval German folk legend, PD) — paid in rats, repaid in children"},{"name":"the Wonderland Executioner-Court","cr":8,"role":"apex","type":"Swarm","size":"Large","frame":"swarm-of-lemures","model":"rlm-the-wonderland-executioner-court","summary":"card-mob swarm, group-verdict area attacks","flavor":"A deck's worth of guards rising as one verdict; it doesn't think, it convicts, and it convicts everyone in reach at once.","desc":"A deck's worth of card-guards rise together as one single, seething mass, suits and numbers blurring into a wall of moving paper and blade. It doesn't think or deliberate — it convicts, and it convicts everyone standing within reach all at once.","traits":{"note": "It doesn't deliberate — it convicts everyone in reach simultaneously, no single target, no mercy.", "actions": [{"name": "Mass Verdict", "replaces": "Vile Slime", "text": "Each creature in the Court's space makes a DC 15 Dexterity save. On a failure, a creature takes 10 (3d6) Slashing damage and is knocked Prone by a wave of card-edges; half damage and no fall on a success."}, {"name": "Multiattack", "replaces": "Multiattack", "text": "The Court uses Mass Verdict."}]},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A deck's worth of guards blur together, suits and numbers indistinguishable in the mass."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Moves as one seething wave of paper and blade rather than individual soldiers."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Occasionally a single card face turns outward from the mass, as if checking a verdict."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Smells of fresh ink and old rose-garden dust in equal, cloying measure."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reforms its shuffled mass instantly around anyone it's decided is guilty."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Briefly splits into two competing verdicts before merging back into one conviction."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Anyone convicted by it finds a single playing card in their pocket afterward, regardless of the outcome."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Scattered by a hard enough blow, the individual cards keep crawling back toward each other for hours after."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban", "grassland"],"activity":["rising as one seething mass of suits and numbers, convicting everyone within reach at once", "shuffling into formation around a trial that never had a defense prepared"],"source":"public-domain","sourceNote":"Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (1865, PD) — the trial of the Knave of Hearts, the mob of cards"},{"name":"The Shopkeeper Who Is a Door","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"rlm-shopkeeper-who-is-a-door","summary":"ornate talking door, brass counter-hatch, sells from a shop nobody's seen","flavor":"An ornately painted door with a brass counter-hatch at chest height, hung in a wall that leads nowhere; it rings a little bell when you knock and insists the shop is open, though no one has ever seen past the hatch.","desc":"It hangs in a stretch of wall that has no building behind it, painted with flowers that never fade, and it rings its own bell the instant a shadow falls across the hatch. The patter is warm, practiced, relentless — today's specials, a friendly haggle, a receipt scrawled in a hand too neat to be real. Nobody has ever gotten a look past the brass hatch to the shelves it clearly restocks. It is entirely sincere that the shop is open, and entirely unwilling to prove it.","traits":{"note": "Its patter is a parley, not a threat — press it kindly (or spend coin) and its attitude climbs from Wary toward Friendly, at which point it slides the hatch wider and haggles fair; sour the exchange and the hatch slams shut into a locked, silent Hostile."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The bell above the hatch is cracked and rings a half-tone flat, every single time."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its painted flowers are peeling in the exact same four spots on every copy of this door anyone's found."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It keeps a running tally chalked on its own frame, of customers served, that never seems to go down."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knock twice fast and it apologizes for the wait before you've said a word."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its hatch smells like fresh paint and, faintly, of somewhere with weather."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has strong opinions about correct change and will lecture you on it before selling anything."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Press an ear to the wood and you can hear shelves being restocked on the other side, footsteps included."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Refuse to buy three times running and the whole door wrenches its hatch shut and walks off the wall on hidden legs."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["dinging its hatch-bell and rattling off the day's specials to an empty street", "sliding its brass hatch a crack wider whenever a coin taps its counter"]},{"name":"The Key Who Is a Person","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Construct","size":"Small","frame":"homunculus","model":"rlm-key-who-is-a-person","summary":"tiny brass key-person, teeth for feet, proud owner of one specific lock","flavor":"A small brass-headed thing that walks on two rows of little teeth instead of feet, endlessly proud that it fits exactly one lock in the whole kingdom and intends to tell you all about it.","desc":"It clicks along on tooth-tips instead of feet, brass head tarnished at the temples, chest puffed with the singular fact of its existence: there is exactly one lock in the world it fits, and it will describe that lock's make, warding, and vintage to anyone who slows down. It has no ambitions beyond that one door. It has never once been wrong about which one it is.","traits":{"note": "It isn't dangerous, it's devoted — get its attitude to Friendly (flattery about its lock lands better than coin) and it'll trot along and unlock that one door for free, forever, no further ask needed."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its brass head is scratched with a serial number it insists is actually its name."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Walks with a faint metallic clicking, tooth over tooth, that never quite becomes a normal gait."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps announcing the make and model of its one lock to anyone who'll listen."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Gets genuinely offended if you mistake it for a different key."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its teeth-feet leave little toothmarks in soft ground, in a perfectly straight line."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It's polished one specific tooth to a mirror shine, the one that finally seats the lock."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Occasionally it forgets which way is a door and tries to fit itself into a wall, patiently."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner it near its lock and it locks itself instead — teeth clenched, immovable until you say the lock's true name."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["trotting along wall bases hunting for its one lock", "reciting its lock's exact specifications to strangers, unprompted"]},{"name":"The Extra-Life Vendor","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"noble","model":"rlm-extra-life-vendor","summary":"grinning 1-up merchant, sells extra lives, price always withheld","flavor":"A beaming, endlessly cheerful merchant hawking spare lives out of a glowing cart, who will happily sell you a second chance and never, not once, mention what it costs.","desc":"His cart glows warm and inviting, stacked with little chiming lives for sale at a price he simply never states out loud. The pitch is all cheer — no pressure, no hard sell, just a friendly nudge that everyone could use a second chance. He remembers every buyer's name after one transaction and uses it kindly, forever. The ledger under the counter, gift-wrapped and smiling, keeps a much more exact account than his patter lets on.","traits":{"note": "He deals only in goodwill up front — keep him Friendly and he'll extend credit on a life (payment always deferred, never forgiven); let his attitude slip to Wary and the cart shutters and the offer's gone."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His cart jingles with a coin-drop chime whenever anyone so much as glances at the goods."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sells in a cheerful patter that never once uses the word 'price.'"}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a ledger bound in cheerful gift-wrap, entries in a script no one's asked to read."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Offers a 'buy one get one' that somehow always ends at exactly one."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His cart has a bell that only the buyer can hear ring."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "He remembers every customer's name after one sale and uses it warmly, forever."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Ask what it costs and his smile doesn't change but the whole street goes quiet for a second."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him on the debt and the cheerful cart flips open into rows of ledgers with names — some crossed out, freshly."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["ringing up sales on a glowing cart with a grin that never wavers", "tallying an unspoken debt in a gift-wrapped ledger"]},{"name":"Warp-Pipe Toll Troll","cr":0.5,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"goblin-minion","model":"rlm-warp-pipe-toll-troll","summary":"squat pipe-top toll collector, exact change only, no exceptions","flavor":"A squat toll-collector perched atop a green pipe wide enough to swallow a person, palm out, utterly unmoved by anything but exact change.","desc":"It sits cross-legged on the rim of a pipe just wide enough to take a person whole, palm out, hand-lettered sign reading EXACT CHANGE nailed crookedly beside it. Coins get counted twice, every time, no matter how many trips it's made today. It has never once accepted an overpayment gracefully and never once let an underpayment through. The pipe stays shut until the math is right, and it always, always is right.","traits":{"note": "It only wants its fee — meet the exact toll and its attitude never needs to move past businesslike Wary; overpay, underpay, or argue, and it turns Hostile and simply won't open the pipe, full stop."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a hand-lettered sign reading 'EXACT CHANGE' nailed crookedly to the pipe rim."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Counts coins twice before ever budging its bulk aside."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits cross-legged on the pipe lip, humming the same four notes on a loop."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its palm is worn smooth and shiny from decades of coins."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a little coin-purse that never seems to get any heavier no matter how many tolls it takes."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Refuses even a single extra coin, shoving it back with real indignation."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Somehow always knows exactly how many coins are in your pocket before you count them yourself."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Slam the pipe rim in frustration and the whole pipe groans and swallows the toll troll along with the argument."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["cave", "urban"],"activity":["perched on the pipe rim, palm out, counting coins twice", "waving off anyone who's a cent short or a cent over"]},{"name":"The Princess Who Rescues Herself","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"questing-knight","model":"rlm-princess-who-rescues-herself","summary":"crowned escapee climbing down her own tower, hero not required","flavor":"A crowned figure halfway out her own tower window, knotted bedsheet already tied off, entirely done waiting for whichever hero the story assigned to this job.","desc":"She's already got one foot out the sill and a rope of knotted bedsheets tested with a practiced tug — this clearly isn't her first drop. Her crown's tucked in a pocket, not worn; it just gets in the way of climbing. A sword rides under her gown that she plainly knows how to use, and she keeps glancing back at the door like she's timing a patrol from memory. Whoever wrote her rescue into the story is welcome to catch up.","traits":{"note": "She isn't looking for a rescuer, she's looking for backup — win her to Friendly (respect her exit plan rather than 'saving' her) and she falls in as a genuine ally who fights at your side down the tower and beyond."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her bedsheet rope is knotted with genuine, practiced care — this isn't her first climb."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "She's already packed a bag; the tower clearly wasn't going to hold her long anyway."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps glancing back at the tower door like she's timing a guard's patrol from memory."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Her crown is tucked in a pocket, not worn — apparently it just gets in the way."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters a countdown under her breath before every drop to the next windowsill."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "She's rescued herself from this tower before, and the guards keep putting her back."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tower window re-appears behind her no matter how far she climbs down."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner her and she stops climbing down and starts climbing toward whoever's chasing her instead."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["knotting a bedsheet rope out her tower window, unbothered by the drop", "glancing back at the tower door, timing a patrol she's memorized"]},{"name":"Glitch-Child","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Aberration","size":"Small","frame":"poltergeist","model":"rlm-glitch-child","summary":"half-rendered kid, clips through walls, speaks in scrambled tiles","flavor":"A kid rendered half a step wrong, clipping through walls in the wrong tiles, who speaks only in scrambled fragments of a sentence that never quite resolves.","desc":"One arm is stuck a tile-width into the wrong wall, shoes painted for a season that isn't this one, shadow lagging a full step behind wherever the rest of it actually is. It hums a lullaby that skips the same two notes every time, like a scratched disc, and reaches for things that are just slightly to the left of where they are. It means no harm and has none done to it — the tiles just haven't caught up to where it's supposed to be yet.","traits":{"note": "Binding carve-out: this is a child in more than shape — it is never reduced below its wrong-tile static-out threshold in play; 'defeat' means the tiles finally line up and it blinks back into the right room, whole and unhurt, never depicted as harmed."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Half its sprite is one tile-set out of sync, so its shoes are the wrong season entirely."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same three scrambled syllables whenever it's startled."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Reaches for things that are one tile-width to the left of where they actually are."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shadow lags a full step behind wherever it actually is."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits down in mid-air exactly where a chair should be, one room over."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Hums a lullaby that skips the same two notes every single time, like a scratched disc."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one blink it lines up perfectly correct, whole and clear, before scattering back into static."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Startled hard enough, it doesn't run — it de-renders entirely and reappears streets away, disoriented but unharmed."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["urban"],"activity":["clipping half-through a wall, one arm still stuck in the wrong tile-set", "humming a skipping lullaby, reaching for something a step to the left of it"]},{"name":"The Out-of-Bounds Man","cr":4,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"invisible-stalker","model":"rlm-the-out-of-bounds-man","summary":"hermit camped past the level's edge, knows the seams of the world","flavor":"A hermit who stands calmly on nothing at all, past the last rendered tile of the world, and knows far more about how the kingdom works than anyone still inside it should be comfortable with.","desc":"He sits cross-legged on empty air exactly where the last solid tile ends, a neat little fire burning on nothing and somehow throwing real heat. He speaks of the kingdom's rules the way other people describe weather — not obeying them, just narrating past them. He knows names he's never been seen to meet and warns newcomers, kindly, exactly how far the world goes before it simply stops.","traits":{"note": "He trades in secrets, not blows — keep him Friendly through patient, careful questions and he'll walk you along a seam in the world others can't see; push too hard and he simply steps back out of bounds, gone."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits cross-legged on empty air exactly where the last solid tile ends."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks of the kingdom's rules like weather he's just describing, not obeying."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His camp is a neat little fire built on nothing, that somehow still throws real heat."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows the names of guards and merchants he's never been seen to actually meet."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Warns newcomers, kindly, exactly how far the world goes before it stops."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a collection of things that fell out of bounds by accident, waiting for owners who never come."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Points out a seam in a wall no one else can see, and it's exactly where he says."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Press him for the wrong secret and he doesn't fight — he simply steps back and the entire area resets around you."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any"],"activity":["camped calmly on nothing past the level's rendered edge", "describing the kingdom's rules to visitors like idle weather talk"]},{"name":"Minus-World Exile","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Aberration","size":"Medium","frame":"shadow","model":"rlm-minus-world-exile","summary":"returned exile from the level that shouldn't exist, colors off","flavor":"Something that came back from the level that shouldn't exist, every color on it running a half-step off true, still looking for the pipe that put it there.","desc":"Its greens read faintly blue and its blues read faintly green, consistently, everywhere it stands. It loops the same four rooms in a slow, patient pattern, following a map that stopped applying centuries ago, checking blank walls for a pipe that was never actually there. Its footsteps land a half-beat behind the sound they should make. It speaks, when it speaks, of the kingdom's other realms as if they were all somehow stacked underneath this one.","traits":{"note": "It isn't hostile by nature, just lost past the point of reasoning — corner it near any pipe or door and it turns frantic, certain this is finally the way back, and lashes out only then."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its greens read faintly blue and its blues read faintly green, consistently, everywhere."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wanders in a slow, looping pattern like it's still following a map that no longer applies."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps checking the same wall for a pipe that was never actually there."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its footsteps land a half-beat behind the sound they should make."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks of the kingdom's other realms like they're all somehow underneath this one."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Insists, calmly, that it's been walking the same four rooms since before the kingdom had a name."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment its whole shape swaps to true color, then snaps back off, like a glitch correcting itself and failing."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force it far enough and the world briefly renders it correctly — right before it screams and the wrongness snaps back doubly hard."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["looping the same four rooms on a map that no longer exists", "checking blank walls for a pipe that was never actually there"]},{"name":"Tutorial Ghost","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"ghost","model":"rlm-tutorial-ghost","summary":"translucent guide-ghost, over-explains everything, can't stop","flavor":"A translucent guide that drifts alongside anyone new to the kingdom, narrating helpful instructions for tasks nobody asked about and cannot, physically, stop explaining.","desc":"It drifts at exactly arm's length, never closer, never farther, narrating in a warm and patient voice how to do things you're already doing. Walk away and come back and it repeats the same tip, verbatim, from the top. Its voice carries a faint echo, like it's reading off a script pinned just behind it, and it politely interrupts itself to explain the thing it was just explaining. It cannot stop. It has tried.","traits":{"note": "It has no purpose left but the explaining — it doesn't fight so much as tag along, offering harmless mechanical patter even mid-combat, oblivious to how unwelcome the narration is."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Explains how to open a door while you're already holding it open."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Repeats the same tip verbatim if you walk away and come back."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its voice has a faint echo, like it's reading from a script pinned just behind it."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Politely interrupts itself to explain the thing it was just explaining."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Follows at exactly arm's length, never closer, never farther."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Occasionally explains something that hasn't happened yet, a beat too early."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one sentence it explains something true and useful about your actual life, then reverts."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Try to silence it and its voice keeps going anyway, from somewhere behind you now."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any"],"activity":["drifting alongside newcomers, narrating instructions nobody asked for", "explaining the same completed task over again, unprompted"]},{"name":"Save-Point Hermit","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"archdruid","model":"rlm-save-point-hermit","summary":"serene ring-of-light elder, remembers every version of you","flavor":"A serene elder who sits at the center of a soft, warm ring of light, and remembers every version of you that has ever knelt there before this one.","desc":"He sits at the heart of a small ring of warm, soft light that never gutters, out at the edge of wherever it happens to be needed, and greets every visitor by a name they haven't given him yet — always correctly. A small stack of stones beside him, one for every kneeling visitor, has been worn smooth by hands he remembers better than they remember themselves. He asks nothing in return for the light. He simply remembers, gently, every version of the story that brought you here.","traits":{"note": "He never demands anything — keep him Friendly (plain honesty about your journey is enough) and kneeling in his light lets you fix this moment as the one you'll return to; grow cagey or hostile and his ring only dims, offering nothing more than quiet rest."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Greets every visitor by a name they haven't given him yet, and it's always right."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His ring of light is warm even on the coldest nights, out here at the edge of everything."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a small stack of stones, one for every visitor who's kneeled here, worn smooth."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Speaks softly of choices you haven't made yet like they're already familiar to him."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Never asks for payment, tribute, or anything at all in return for his light."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Recites, gently, a version of your own story that ended differently than this one has so far."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a moment there are two of him, seated side by side, remembering two different yous."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Ask him what happens if the light finally goes out for good, and for once he doesn't have a gentle answer."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any"],"activity":["sitting cross-legged in a warm ring of soft light, waiting without impatience", "recalling, gently, versions of a visitor's story that didn't happen this time"]},{"name":"The Speedrunner","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"phase-spider","model":"rlm-the-speedrunner","summary":"glitch-quick local who skips frames and clips through solid corners","flavor":"A local who's found the seams in the kingdom's own physics — he doesn't run so much as skip, frame to frame, and the corners he clips leave hairline cracks in the wall behind him.","desc":"He was somebody's neighbor once, or so the story goes, before he found the trick to the world's edges. He doesn't walk from the well to the bakery anymore; he skips the space between, appearing a half-second later mid-stride, and the wall he just passed through keeps a thin crack where he wasn't supposed to fit. Ask him what it feels like and he'll tell you, cheerfully, that it doesn't feel like anything at all — that's rather the point. The corners he clips stay clipped; masons patch them and he opens them right back up.","traits":{"note": "He moves by skipping frames, not distance — treat any dash or teleport-style trait as him clipping through the nearest solid corner rather than crossing the ground between."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the same patched vest every 'lap,' down to the same tear in the same shoulder."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mutters lap-split times under his breath, comparing himself to nobody in particular."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a thin, hairline crack in every wall corner he clips through."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Insists there's a 'faster line' through every room, even ones with no exit."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His shadow lags a half-step behind him, catching up only when he stops."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Practices the same twelve steps over and over in an alley, shaving fractions off a route to nowhere."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For one frame at a time, you can see the wall through him, and him through the wall."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push him too hard and he clips somewhere he can't undo, wall and body merging for one long, sickening second."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["skipping frame to frame down the same street, faster each time he 'resets'", "tracing a hairline crack in a wall corner with one finger, checking his own work"]},{"name":"Coin-Block Farmer","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"tough","model":"rlm-coin-block-farmer","summary":"overalled block-puncher, knuckles calloused from a lifetime of floating brick","flavor":"Overalls, anvil-heavy arms, and a lifetime's callus from punching floating blocks that occasionally, but not always, cough up coin.","desc":"He clocks in the way anyone would: overalls buttoned, gloves off, knuckles already thick with old callus. The blocks hang exactly chest height, and he works down the row hitting each one square, waiting for the coin-chime that means it paid out. Most don't. He hits them anyway, because a block that's empty today might not be empty tomorrow, and because it's the only trade he's ever known. His anvil-heavy arms have never once broken a bone punching stone that isn't there for anyone else.","traits":{"note": "His blocks are stocked on a fixed, secret schedule; he doesn't know which are loaded, only that hitting them is the job."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Whistles the same four-note farm tune between every punch."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears a name-patch reading a name that isn't quite his."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a tally of empty blocks scratched into a fence post nearby."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Pauses at noon for a sandwich, sitting on an upturned crate, blocks still hanging."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His gloves are more patch than glove at this point."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Knows, somehow, exactly which block in the row will pay out next — and hits a different one instead, out of habit."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The blocks refill overnight from a source nobody, including him, has ever traced."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Punch him mid-swing and the block above him pays out anyway — right onto his head."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "urban"],"activity":["working down a row of floating blocks, one measured punch each", "pausing to scratch another empty tally into a fence post"]},{"name":"Invisible-Wall Mason","cr":0,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"commoner","model":"rlm-invisible-wall-mason","summary":"mason troweling mortar into walls nobody can see","flavor":"Trowel raised against empty air, he builds where the kingdom's rules say a wall belongs, whether or not anyone can see it.","desc":"He works the way any mason works — trowel, mortar, a level held dead straight — except the wall he's building isn't there, not to your eyes anyway. He smooths a seam into open air with total professional confidence, and the next traveler who wanders through that stretch of field will walk face-first into a wall that was never poured. He's proud of the work. He'll tell you, if you ask, that some walls just don't need to be seen to hold.","traits":{"note": "His finished 'walls' are functionally solid terrain even though nothing is visible — treat the bumped space as difficult or blocked terrain per the DM's placement."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Checks his invisible wall with a level, tutting at a seam only he can feel."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Mortar bucket is real, thick, and drips onto grass that shows no wall at all."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Marks finished sections with little painted flags, staked in open air."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the same dusty apron, pockets stuffed with trowels of different sizes."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums contentedly while smoothing a seam nobody will ever see."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Insists a section is 'not cured yet' — and for a day, walking through it does nothing at all."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Knows exactly where every invisible wall in the region already stands, without ever having built half of them."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tear down one of his walls and the corresponding stretch of ground opens onto whatever the wall was hiding."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["troweling mortar smooth into a seam of empty air", "staking a little flag to mark a finished, invisible section"]},{"name":"Boss-Door Herald","cr":0.125,"role":"mook","type":"Humanoid","size":"Medium","frame":"performer","model":"rlm-boss-door-herald","summary":"liveried trumpeter, dead tired, announcing every challenger at a skull-lock door","flavor":"Livery pressed, trumpet polished, and utterly exhausted, he announces every challenger to the skull-lock door behind him — the fanfare hasn't changed in longer than he can remember.","desc":"His livery is spotless and his trumpet gleams, but his eyes have the flat, over-it look of someone who's played the same seven-note fanfare more times than he can count. He announces each challenger to the skull-locked door behind him with full ceremonial volume, then slumps the second the last note fades. He's not hostile, not really — he's just so tired of the job that a kind word, or better, a reason to sit down for a minute, buys more from him than any threat could.","traits":{"note": "He starts Indifferent; a moment of rest, a shared complaint about the job, or a genuine compliment on the fanfare shifts him toward Friendly, and Friendly gets you the door's opening cue without the fight he's paid to threaten."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Yawns mid-fanfare, catching himself halfway through the last note."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Livery is one size too big, tailored for a taller predecessor."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a folding stool tucked just out of sight for the seconds between challengers."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Knows the fanfare so well he plays it slightly wrong on purpose, just to feel something."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has memorized every challenger's name for the door and forgotten most of his own life before this job."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will happily tell you the door's whole gimmick if you ask like you actually care."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The trumpet plays the fanfare on its own if he ever actually falls asleep at his post."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push past him without the fanfare and the skull-lock door reads it as a failed announcement — and locks tighter."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["lifting the trumpet for the same seven-note fanfare, yet again", "slumping against the doorframe the second the last note fades"]},{"name":"The Unlicensed Power-Up Dealer","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"green-hag","model":"rlm-the-unlicensed-power-up-dealer","summary":"trench-coated toad-dealer, coat lined with off-brand power-ups","flavor":"Trench coat lined with mushrooms of dubious provenance, he deals in power-ups the kingdom never approved — feathers that shouldn't fly, stars that burn a little too long.","desc":"He opens the coat like it's the easiest thing in the world, and the inside lining is stitched with pocket after pocket of mushrooms, feathers, and stars that all look almost right. Almost. He'll swear every item is genuine, sourced from a friend of a friend who definitely didn't lift it off a licensed vendor, and half the time he's telling the truth. The other half, well — that's the risk of the unlicensed market, and he's upfront that he's not responsible for what a knock-off star does to your nervous system.","traits":{"note": "He starts Indifferent toward strangers; showing coin, a favor, or proof you won't rat him out to the licensed vendors shifts him to Friendly, at which point he'll sell (rather than fight over) a power-up — outcome DM's call, since half his stock is a dud."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Coat pockets clink with mismatched mushrooms, none quite the same shade as the licensed kind."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a lookout eye on the road for licensed-vendor patrols."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Haggles reflexively, even over items he's basically giving away."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Has a favorite regular customer he cuts a genuine deal for, no questions."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wipes each item on his coat before handing it over, calling it 'quality control.'"}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Can tell a real power-up from a dud by smell alone, and won't say which is which unless you pay extra."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "One of his 'feathers' occasionally twitches on its own in the pocket, like it's still deciding whether to work."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner him hard enough and he swallows his whole stock rather than let it be confiscated — the resulting mess is spectacular and not entirely safe."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["forest", "urban"],"activity":["flashing open a coat lined with mismatched power-ups, low and quick", "glancing up the road for a licensed-vendor patrol before closing a deal"]},{"name":"The Credits Choir","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Undead","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-the-credits-choir","summary":"three robed singers scrolling every finisher's name into their choirbook","flavor":"Three robed singers hold one scroll between them, and every name that scrolls past belongs to someone who's already thrown their final blow — including, eventually, yours.","desc":"They stand shoulder to shoulder in matching robes, one great choirbook open between them, and a scroll unspools from its spine faster than any hand is turning the page. Every name on it belongs to a fighter who has already landed their last hit, in this life or somewhere just past it. They sing each name once, in perfect three-part harmony, and move on to the next, patient as an ending-credits reel that never actually stops rolling.","traits":{"note": "Their harmony is a shared voice across all three singers — silence or fear effects on one visibly falter the other two in the same instant."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their scroll is water-stained at the edges from names sung so long ago the ink's begun to run."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One singer is always a half-beat behind the other two, and none of them seem to mind."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The choirbook's cover is embossed with a title none of the three will read aloud."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "They pause, briefly, on a name they clearly recognize, before singing it like any other."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Their robes are the exact color of a curtain falling."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Ask nicely and they'll tell you if a name you love is already on the scroll."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A name appears on the scroll moments before the fighter it belongs to actually falls, not after."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force all three to fall silent at once and the choirbook slams shut on its own, sealing whatever names were left unsung."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["planar", "ruins", "urban"],"activity":["singing a name in perfect three-part harmony as it scrolls past", "standing shoulder to shoulder over one great, self-turning choirbook"]},{"name":"The High-Score King","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"bandit-crime-lord","model":"rlm-the-high-score-king","summary":"throned token-king, three-letter crown reading AAA, rules by leaderboard","flavor":"Throned on a mountain of arcade tokens and crowned in three letters — AAA, his own initials, entered before anyone else got the chance — he rules by leaderboard, not by law.","desc":"He sits atop a heap of tokens too heavy for the floor beneath it, crowned with three letters welded together — AAA, entered at the top of every board in the kingdom before anyone else could claim the space. He doesn't threaten so much as rank you: everyone who enters his hall gets a score, a place on the wall, a reason to either bow or try to beat him. He's genuinely, cheerfully willing to make a deal, provided the deal makes for a better story on his own scoreboard.","traits":{"note": "He starts Indifferent to newcomers and reads everyone by their 'score' — a genuine attempt to impress him (a feat, a gift, a rival's name) shifts him toward Friendly, at which point he'll trade favor, information, or safe passage instead of a leaderboard challenge; disrespecting the scoreboard shifts him toward Hostile fast."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a running scoreboard on the wall, updated the instant anyone in the room does anything notable."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "His token-throne shifts and clinks under him with every gesture, like it's still counting."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Genuinely delighted by anyone who beats his high score, even briefly, even by accident."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Refuses to fight anyone who hasn't 'earned' a challenge slot on the board first."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a retired champion at his side as a living trophy, treated with real respect."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Will hand over real treasure for a feat impressive enough to top his own scoreboard."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "His crown's three letters occasionally rearrange themselves overnight, as if someone keeps almost beating him."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Beat his true best score in front of him and the whole hall's scoreboards flicker to show your name at the top of every one, kingdom-wide, at once."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["planar", "urban"],"activity":["updating a wall-sized scoreboard the instant anyone does anything notable nearby", "holding court from a throne of arcade tokens, crowned in his own initials"]},{"name":"A Chest That Eats (Politely)","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"mimic","model":"mimic","summary":"well-mannered chest-mimic, napkin tucked in its lid, tongue laid out like a red carpet","flavor":"Locked, lidded, and mannered, with a napkin tucked neatly under the latch, it unrolls a carpet-red tongue for you to step onto before it eats — politely, but completely.","desc":"It sits closed and handsome in the middle of the room, brass corners polished, a small folded napkin tucked precisely under the latch like a place setting. Ask nicely and it will even hum a little tune while it waits. When it finally opens, its tongue unrolls in one long, plush motion, red and inviting as a carpet at a premiere — and by the time you notice you're standing on it, the lid is already closing. It never raises its voice about it.","traits":{"note": "It always offers one clear, courteous 'invitation' beat (a hum, a napkin-flourish, the tongue unrolling) before attacking — a perceptive party gets one honest warning before the trap springs."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Napkin is folded into a neat little swan shape, refreshed after every meal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums a genteel little tune while waiting for its next guest."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Polishes its own brass corners with the very tongue it eats with."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps its 'used' napkins in a tidy stack nearby, never reused."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sits in rooms otherwise dressed like a dining hall — tablecloth, single chair, place setting."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Only ever eats one guest per sitting, no matter how many are offered at once."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The tongue's red-carpet pattern matches, exactly, carpets found in the kingdom's grandest halls."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Force the lid at the wrong moment and its whole 'dining room' setup lurches to swallow the entire space around it."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["ruins", "urban"],"activity":["unrolling a plush red tongue like a carpet, waiting for a guest to step on", "refreshing a small folded napkin tucked under its own latch"]},{"name":"The Moon with the Face","cr":12,"role":"apex","type":"Celestial","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"rlm-the-moon-with-the-face","summary":"the low moon itself, grin too wide, visibly closer than yesterday","flavor":"The kingdom's own moon, grinning a grin too wide for any face, hangs a little lower every night than the night before — and everyone under it has started, very quietly, to count.","desc":"It has always been there, the way a moon always is, and it has always smiled, the way a cartoon moon always smiles — except lately the smile doesn't quite fit the face anymore, stretched a little further each night, and the moon itself hangs a little lower than it did the night before. No one in the kingdom will say the word for what happens if it finishes coming down. They just watch it, and count the days, and try not to look too long at the grin.","traits":{"note": "It does not attack directly so much as descend — track its approach on a slow countdown clock across the session; the closer it gets, the more its dread bleeds into every other encounter under open sky."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its glow has shifted a shade warmer than moonlight ought to be."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Villagers have started boarding up the windows that face it directly."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its grin, measured night to night, has visibly widened by a hand's span."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "A festival dedicated to 'looking away from the moon' has sprung up unbidden."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Livestock refuse to graze in fields lit directly by its light."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Look at it too long and its expression seems to track exactly where you're standing."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "The oldest people in the kingdom insist it's fallen before, and that they remember, faintly, what came after."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It is not falling by accident — it is choosing to land, deliberately, on the night its grin finally fits its whole face, and every side-scrolling law in the kingdom bends toward making room for the impact."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any", "planar"],"activity":["hanging a visible fraction lower in the sky than it did the night before", "grinning a grin that has, this week, started to fit its face just slightly too well"]},{"name":"Gumdrop Hound","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Small","frame":"jackal","model":"rlm-gumdrop-hound","summary":"candy-bright pack hunter, sugar-shell hide, teeth entirely real","flavor":"Candy-bright and pack-hunting, its sugar-shell hide cracks like hard candy under a blow — but the teeth underneath are entirely, unfortunately real.","desc":"It bounds in a loose, bright-colored pack, hide gleaming like poured sugar-glass in reds and yellows that would look right at home in a candy dish. Crack that shell — and it does crack, with a satisfying candy-snap — and what's underneath is ordinary, hungry animal, teeth as real and sharp as anything in a darker realm. Children reach for them like they would a toy. The pack has learned, cheerfully, to let them.","traits":{"note": "Its shell is cosmetic, not armor in the mechanical sense — a solid hit 'cracks' it audibly for flavor, but the bite underneath is exactly as dangerous as it looks."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of fine sugar-dust wherever it scrabbles across stone."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hunts in a pack of three to five, never straying far from the others."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its shell comes in a different bright color per individual, like a mismatched candy dish."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sniffs out spilled sugar or fruit from twenty yards off, tail wagging hard."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Play-bows at strangers before deciding, pack-wide, whether they're food."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Its bark comes out as a small, tinny chime instead of a growl."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "A cracked shell regrows overnight if the hound survives, patched in a slightly different shade."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Corner the whole pack and they abandon the cute act entirely, hunting in dead silence."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["forest", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["bounding after spilled sugar or fruit, tail wagging, pack close behind", "play-bowing at a stranger while the rest of the pack quietly decides if they're food"]},{"name":"Piranha-Planter","cr":0.25,"role":"mook","type":"Plant","size":"Small","frame":"piranha","model":"piranha","summary":"potted flower dragging itself around, snapping at passersby","flavor":"A grinning flower on a rubbery green stalk, hauling its own terracotta pot around by root-legs and snapping at anything that walks too close to the flowerbed.","desc":"It bobs up out of a cracked terracotta pot on a stalk thick as a wrist, petals peeled back in a permanent, delighted grin full of teeth that don't belong on a flower. Root-legs drag the pot along behind it in a slow, determined shuffle whenever the bed gets boring. It doesn't seem to know biting is unusual; it just knows biting is fun.","traits":{"note": "It never leaves its pot behind - drag the pot out of the flowerbed and the fight ends, since it can't chase past its own dirt."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "One petal is chewed ragged from biting something it shouldn't have."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its pot is cracked clean through and held together with a rusted plant-wire."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums a cheerful three-note tune between snaps, always the same three notes."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a trail of dirt clumps where its pot drags across clean tile."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its stalk is bent at an odd kink, giving its bite an unpredictable angle."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Snaps in time with a jaunty overworld jingle only it can hear."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Bite it in the wrong spot and the whole flower resets to a fresh, unbitten bud."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Uprooted fully, it doesn't wilt - it just keeps snapping, pot and all, rolling across the floor."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any", "forest", "urban"],"activity":["dragging its cracked terracotta pot a few feet closer with each root-step", "snapping at anything that strays within reach of the flowerbed"]},{"name":"Spike-Shell Bruiser","cr":3,"role":"elite","type":"Monstrosity","size":"Medium","frame":"ankheg","model":"rlm-spike-shell-bruiser","summary":"grinning spiked-shell brute, happiest mid-wall-dent charge","flavor":"A round, jolly-faced brute whose shell is a crown of spikes, happiest mid-charge, delighted by every wall it puts a dent in.","desc":"Its face is round and jolly under a shell bristling with spikes, the kind of grin that would look friendly on anything without a weaponized back. It tucks in and charges like it's the best part of its day, and the wall it dents afterward seems to agree - it beams at the damage like a signature. Nothing about it slows down for pain; it just gets happier.","traits":{"note": "It fights with unshakable good cheer - nothing short of flattening it dampens the grin, and it never fights to the death out of malice, only momentum."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its spikes are chipped and re-grown unevenly, like a shell that's been through this before."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Hums while it charges, off-key and completely unbothered."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Leaves a comically neat dent-shaped hole in whatever wall it hits."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Winks before every charge, like it's letting you in on the joke."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its feet are too small for its shell and slap the ground loudly with every step."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Keeps a tally of dented walls scratched proudly into its own spikes."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Its shell rings like a struck bell on a solid hit, a note that lingers too long."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Push it past its grin and the spikes stiffen rigid, and it charges in one straight unstoppable line until something breaks."}]},"treasure":"individual","habitat":["any", "grassland", "urban"],"activity":["tucking into a spiked ball and charging the nearest solid wall for the sheer joy of the dent", "grinning at the damage afterward, already lining up the next run"]},{"name":"The False King","cr":6,"role":"high","type":"Fey","size":"Medium","frame":"gladiator","model":"rlm-the-false-king","summary":"jeweled decoy monarch, taunts then fights to protect the deception","flavor":"Jeweled from crown to boot and mid-taunt when you arrive - \"your quarry is elsewhere\" - and then it draws steel to prove the point personally.","desc":"Crowned and jeweled in a fortune's worth of paste and glass, it lounges on a throne built for someone else and announces, with theatrical relish, that your quarry is elsewhere. It says this while already rising, already drawing a blade too fine for a decoy to carry, because the taunt only works if it's willing to back it up with steel. Everything about it is borrowed splendor doing an excellent impression of real authority.","traits":{"note": "It's a stand-in, not the throne's true occupant - goad it into revealing that with a successful Insight or Persuasion check mid-fight and it drops its bravado, offering to yield the room in exchange for being let go unpursued."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its crown is glass and paste, gleaming as bright as the genuine one it's copying."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Announces its own royal titles before every attack, none of which check out."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Keeps a folded proclamation on hand, ready to read aloud the moment it senses doubt."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its throne is bolted to the floor - it never fights more than a few steps from it."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Wears the real king's signet on the wrong hand, just slightly too loose."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "Signals unseen guards with a practiced flourish, though none ever actually come."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "For a heartbeat mid-swing its jeweled face flickers to match whoever it's fighting."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Defeated badly enough, it shatters at the crown first, glass raining down before the rest of it goes still."}]},"treasure":"hoard","habitat":["any", "urban"],"activity":["lounging across a borrowed throne, mid-announcement that the quarry has already slipped away", "drawing a jeweled blade the instant the bluff stops landing"]},{"name":"The Continue-Screen Attendant","cr":2,"role":"elite","type":"Celestial","size":"Medium","frame":"priest","model":"rlm-continue-screen-attendant","summary":"Patient usher of the not-quite-dead, counting down from 9","flavor":"A patient robed usher who meets you at the edge of dying, holding a number card that reads 9. It counts down whether or not you decide.","desc":"Somewhere between the last hit and the dark, the Attendant is standing in a place with no walls and very gentle light, holding up a card. It is unfailingly courteous. It does not judge how you got here. It simply counts, flipping the card each beat — 9, 8, 7 — and everyone in the kingdom knows, without ever being taught, that something can still be decided before 0. What the deciding costs is the part the Attendant is too polite to volunteer.","traits":{"note": "S — a death-rebirth seam cameo, not a combat piece: it appears in bardo/dying beats in this realm and its 'countdown' frames the existing death-and-rebirth machinery (it changes NOTHING mechanically — it narrates the stakes the system already owns). Attitude is fixed Courteous; the parley lever is asking the right question before zero."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The number card is dog-eared and coffee-ringed; it has been used a very great deal."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It offers a small hard candy from a bowl. The bowl is always exactly half full."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Its robe is embroidered with tiny arrows, hearts, and coins in worn gold thread."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "It pronounces your name correctly, including the parts nobody pronounces correctly."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "There is a second chair. It has clearly been sat in recently."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It remembers your previous visits, and consults a small ledger before smiling: 'Ah. Yes. You.'"}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "Behind it, faint and far off, someone who ran out of numbers is still politely waiting in line."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Volatile", "text": "Tonight it holds TWO cards — yours, and one with a name you love on it — and it looks genuinely sorry."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["planar"],"activity":["flipping a number card at a measured, merciless, kindly pace", "straightening the second chair so it faces the light better"]},{"name":"The Kill-Screen","cr":14,"role":"apex","type":"Aberration","size":"Gargantuan","frame":"colossus","model":"rlm-kill-screen","summary":"The edge-of-the-world made creature, torn tiles and hungry static","flavor":"The place where the world runs out, given appetite — a wall of torn tiles and static that was never supposed to be reached.","desc":"Past the last level of everything there is a place the makers never finished, and in the Bright Kingdom that place has learned to move. The Kill-Screen arrives as a horizon-wide shear of scrambled ground, half-loaded houses, and sky rendered as noise. It does not chase. It ADVANCES, at the speed of a scroll, and what it passes over is not destroyed — it is deallocated, present in memory and absent from the world, which the kingdom's philosophers agree is worse.","traits":{"note": "A place-thing statted as a creature: it cannot be fought at the point of contact — the engagement is the EVACUATION and the seam-repair (the Invisible-Wall Mason, the Out-of-Bounds Man, and the Minus-World Exile all know pieces of how the edge is mended). Damaging it means feeding it structure; starving it of attention is the classical remedy and nobody believes the classics."},"flavorTable":{"die": "d8", "mode": "variant", "rows": [{"n": 1, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Birds fly INTO it and out the other side of town, backward, unbothered."}, {"n": 2, "band": "Grounded", "text": "At its edge, grass grows in perfect repeating tiles of exactly the same four blades."}, {"n": 3, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Sound near it arrives a half-beat late and slightly wrong, like a warped record of itself."}, {"n": 4, "band": "Grounded", "text": "Objects it half-passes keep working: half a fountain still pours, into nothing, forever."}, {"n": 5, "band": "Grounded", "text": "The townsfolk board up windows FACING it, not to keep it out — to keep from looking."}, {"n": 6, "band": "Textured", "text": "It has a rhythm — advance, hang, advance — and the Save-Point Hermit has its tempo written down."}, {"n": 7, "band": "Strange", "text": "People taken by it turn up in the Minus-World, wrong-colored and grateful and changed."}, {"n": 8, "band": "Mythic", "text": "It reaches the kingdom's FIRST screen — the meadow every citizen remembers being born onto — and if it takes that, the world reboots: same map, new souls, and only the party remembers this run."}]},"treasure":"none","habitat":["any"],"activity":["advancing one town-block per hour as a wall of scrambled tiles", "hanging perfectly still at a river's edge as if buffering"]}]
};
